window.EXAM_DATA=window.EXAM_DATA||{};window.EXAM_DATA["dop-c02"]=[{"id":1,"question_en":"A company has a mobile application that makes HTTP API calls to an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The ALB routes requests to an AWS Lambda function. Many different versions of the application are in use at any given time, including versions that are in testing by a subset of users. The version of the application is defined in the user-agent header that is sent with all requests to the API. After a series of recent changes to the API, the company has observed issues with the application. The company needs to gather a metric for each API operation by response code for each version of the application that is in use. A DevOps engineer has modified the Lambda function to extract the API operation name, version information from the user-agent header and response code. Which additional set of actions should the DevOps engineer take to gather the required metrics?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款移动应用程序，该程序通过 HTTP API 调用应用负载均衡器（ALB）。ALB 将请求路 由到 AWS Lambda 函数。在任何给定时间，都有许多不同版本的应用程序在使用，其中包括由部分用户 进行测试的版本。应用程序的版本在发送给 API 的所有请求的用户代理标头中定义。 在对 API 进行了一系列近期更改之后，该公司发现应用程序出现了问题。公司需要为每个版本的应 用程序中每个 API 操作按响应代码收集一个指标。一位 DevOps 工程师修改了 Lambda 函数，以从用 户代理标头中提取 API 操作名称、版本信息和响应代码。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪一组额外的操作来收集所需的指标？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the Lambda function to write the API operation name, response code, and version number as a log line to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Configure a CloudWatch Logs metric filter that increments a metric for each API operation name. Specify response code and application version as dimensions for the metric.","B":"Modify the Lambda function to write the API operation name, response code, and version number as a log line to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Configure a CloudWatch Logs Insights query to populate CloudWatch metrics from the log lines. Specify response code and application version as dimensions for the metric.","C":"Configure the ALB access logs to write to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Modify the Lambda function to respond to the ALB with the API operation name, response code, and version number as response metadata. Configure a CloudWatch Logs metric filter that increments a metric for each API operation name. Specify response code and application version as dimensions for the metric.","D":"Configure AWS X-Ray integration on the Lambda function. Modify the Lambda function to create an X- Ray subsegment with the API operation name, response code, and version number. Configure X-Ray insights to extract an aggregated metric for each API operation name and to publish the metric to Amazon CloudWatch. Specify response code and application version as dimensions for the metric."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 Lambda 函数，将 API 操作名称、响应代码和版本号作为一条日志行写入 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。配置一个 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器，为每个 API 操作名称递增一个指标。将响应 代码和应用程序版本指定为该指标的维度。","B":"修改 Lambda 函数，将 API 操作名称、响应代码和版本号作为一条日志行写入 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。配置 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询，从日志行中填充 CloudWatch 指标。将响应代码 和应用程序版本指定为指标的维度。","C":"将应用负载均衡器（ALB）的访问日志配置为写入 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。修改 Lambda 函数，使其以 API 操作名称、响应代码和版本号作为响应元数据来响应 ALB。配置 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器，为每个 API 操作名称递增一个指标。将响应代码和应用程序版本指定为该指标 的维度。","D":"在 Lambda 函数上配置 AWS X-Ray 集成。修改 Lambda 函数以使用 API 操作名称、响应代码和版本 号创建 X-Ray 子段。配置 X-Ray 洞察以提取每个 API 操作名称的聚合指标，并将该指标发布到 Amazon CloudWatch。将响应代码和应用程序版本指定为指标的维度。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The Lambda function already extracts the API operation name, version (from the user-agent header), and response code. The native, documented way to turn these into a per-operation metric broken down by response code and version is to write them as a structured (JSON or space-delimited) log line to CloudWatch Logs and attach a CloudWatch Logs metric filter. The docs state a metric filter 'increments the metric's count by a specified numerical value' each time a matching log event is found, and that for JSON/space-delimited patterns 'You can create JSON and space-delimited metric filters with up to three dimensions' extracted from log fields. Publishing response code and application version as two of the allowed three dimensions on a per-operation metric exactly satisfies the requirement, which is why option A is correct.","explanation_zh":"Lambda function 已從 user-agent header 中擷取出 API operation name、版本資訊與 response code。要把這些資料轉成『依 response code 與版本細分的每個 API operation 指標』，AWS 原生且有文件支援的做法是：把它們以結構化(JSON 或空白分隔)的 log line 寫入 CloudWatch Logs，再設定 CloudWatch Logs metric filter。文件指出 metric filter 在每次比對到符合的 log event 時就會將指標計數依指定數值遞增；對於 JSON/空白分隔的 pattern，可從 log 欄位擷取並發佈最多三個 dimensions。將 response code 與 application version 作為其中兩個 dimension 附加到每個 operation 的指標上，正好符合需求，因此選項 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs Insights is an interactive ad hoc query/analysis engine. AWS docs explicitly contrast the two: 'Metric filters differ from CloudWatch Logs Insights queries in that a specified numerical value is added to a metric filter each time a matching log is found.' Logs Insights does not continuously 'populate CloudWatch metrics' nor emit custom metrics with dimensions; the described mechanism does not exist.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs Insights 是互動式的臨時查詢/分析引擎。AWS 文件明確將兩者區分：『metric filter 與 Logs Insights 查詢不同，metric filter 在每次比對到符合 log 時就為指標加值』。Logs Insights 不會持續『產生 CloudWatch 指標』，也不會發佈帶 dimensions 的自訂指標；題目描述的機制並不存在。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ALB access logs are delivered to Amazon S3, not to a CloudWatch Logs log group, and they record network/HTTP-level fields rather than Lambda-computed application data. A Lambda behind an ALB cannot inject custom 'response metadata' (application operation name, user-agent version, application response code) into ALB access logs, so a metric filter over those logs cannot produce the required dimensioned metrics.","why_zh":"ALB access logs 是送到 Amazon S3，而非 CloudWatch Logs log group，且記錄的是網路/HTTP 層級欄位，並非 Lambda 計算出的應用層資料。ALB 後的 Lambda 無法把自訂的『response metadata』(應用 operation name、user-agent 版本、應用回應碼) 注入 ALB access logs，因此對這些 log 套用 metric filter 無法產生所需的帶 dimension 指標。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"X-Ray subsegments support annotations/metadata, but X-Ray Insights detects anomalies/incidents in traces (e.g., anomalous services, latency spikes) and emits incident notifications via EventBridge. It does not 'extract an aggregated metric for each API operation name' and publish a custom CloudWatch metric with user-defined dimensions such as response code and application version. That capability is fabricated and adds unnecessary overhead.","why_zh":"X-Ray subsegment 可帶 annotation/metadata，但 X-Ray Insights 是偵測追蹤資料中的異常/事件(例如異常服務、延遲飆升)，並透過 EventBridge 發出事件通知。它不會『為每個 API operation name 擷取彙整指標』並以 response code、application version 等自訂 dimensions 發佈自訂 CloudWatch 指標；該功能屬虛構且增加不必要的維運負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntaxForMetricFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CountOccurrencesExample.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/ExtractBytesExample.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-logs-metricfilter-dimension.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/aws-xray.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":2,"question_en":"A company provides an application to customers. The application has an Amazon API Gateway REST API that invokes an AWS Lambda function. On initialization, the Lambda function loads a large amount of data from an Amazon DynamoDB table. The data load process results in long cold-start times of 8-10 seconds. The DynamoDB table has DynamoDB Accelerator (DAX) configured. Customers report that the application intermittently takes a long time to respond to requests. The application receives thousands of requests throughout the day. In the middle of the day, the application experiences 10 times more requests than at any other time of the day. Near the end of the day, the application's request volume decreases to 10% of its normal total. A DevOps engineer needs to reduce the latency of the Lambda function at all times of the day. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司向客户提供一款应用程序。该应用程序有一个通过亚马逊 API 网关的 REST API 调用 AWS Lambda 函数的接口。在初始化时，Lambda 函数会从一个亚马逊 DynamoDB 表中加载大量数据。数据 加载过程导致冷启动时间长达 8 到 10 秒。DynamoDB 表已配置了 DynamoDB 加速器（DAX）。 客户报告称，该应用程序间歇性地对请求作出响应的时间过长。该应用程序全天会收到数千个请求。 在一天的中间时段，其收到的请求量是一天中其他任何时段的 10 倍。临近一天结束时，该应用程序 的请求量会降至正常总量的 10%。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要在一天中的任何时候都降低 Lambda 函数的延迟。哪种解决方案能 满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure provisioned concurrency on the Lambda function with a concurrency value of 1. Delete the DAX cluster for the DynamoDB table.","B":"Configure reserved concurrency on the Lambda function with a concurrency value of 0.","C":"Configure provisioned concurrency on the Lambda function. Configure AWS Application Auto Scaling on the Lambda function with provisioned concurrency values set to a minimum of 1 and a maximum of 100.","D":"Configure reserved concurrency on the Lambda function. Configure AWS Application Auto Scaling on the API Gateway API with a reserved concurrency maximum value of 100."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Lambda 函数的预配置并发设置为 1。删除 DynamoDB 表的 DAX 集群。","B":"在 Lambda 函数上配置预留并发量，将并发量值设为 0。","C":"在 Lambda 函数上配置预置并发。在 Lambda 函数上配置 AWS 应用程序自动扩展，将预置并发值设 置为最小值 1 和最大值 100。","D":"在 Lambda 函数上配置预留并发量。在 API Gateway API 上配置 AWS 应用程序自动扩展，预留并发 量的最大值设为 100。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The 8-10 second latency comes from the Lambda function loading a large amount of DynamoDB data during the Init phase, which only occurs on a cold start. Provisioned concurrency pre-initializes execution environments so they are ready to respond immediately with double-digit-millisecond response times; AWS docs state a function using provisioned concurrency does not exhibit cold start behavior because the environment is prepared ahead of invocation. Because traffic is highly variable (10x at the mid-day peak, dropping to 10% near end of day), a single fixed value cannot keep latency low at all times: too low brings back cold starts at peak, too high over-provisions otherwise. AWS docs explicitly recommend using Application Auto Scaling target tracking to automate provisioned concurrency for workloads without predictable traffic patterns, and the documented CLI example registers the scalable target with exactly --min-capacity 1 --max-capacity 100, matching option C. DAX accelerates DynamoDB reads, not the Lambda Init-phase load, so it should not be deleted.","explanation_zh":"8-10 秒的延遲來自 Lambda function 在 Init 階段從 DynamoDB 載入大量資料，而這只在 cold start 時發生。Provisioned concurrency 會預先初始化執行環境，使其能立即以雙位數毫秒的回應時間提供服務；AWS 文件指出使用 provisioned concurrency 的 function 不會出現 cold start，因為環境已在叫用前準備好。由於流量變化極大（中午尖峰是平時的 10 倍，傍晚降到 10%），單一固定值無法在所有時段維持低延遲：值太低尖峰時 cold start 會回來，值太高其餘時段又過度配置。AWS 文件明確建議對沒有可預測流量模式的工作負載使用 Application Auto Scaling target tracking 來自動化 provisioned concurrency，且文件中的 CLI 範例註冊 scalable target 時正好使用 --min-capacity 1 --max-capacity 100，與選項 C 完全吻合。DAX 加速的是 DynamoDB 讀取，而非 Lambda Init 階段的載入，因此不應刪除。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A single fixed provisioned concurrency of 1 cannot absorb the 10x mid-day spike, so cold starts and high latency return at peak. Deleting the DAX cluster also harms DynamoDB read performance; DAX is unrelated to the Lambda Init-phase cold start, so removing it provides no latency benefit and is counterproductive.","why_zh":"固定為 1 的 provisioned concurrency 無法吸收中午 10 倍的尖峰，尖峰時 cold start 與高延遲會回來。刪除 DAX cluster 還會損害 DynamoDB 讀取效能；DAX 與 Lambda Init 階段的 cold start 無關，移除它毫無延遲上的好處且適得其反。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Reserved concurrency is a max/min cap on concurrent instances and does not pre-initialize environments, so it never reduces cold starts. Worse, AWS docs state that setting reserved concurrency to 0 intentionally throttles the function and stops it from processing any events entirely, which breaks the application.","why_zh":"Reserved concurrency 是對並發實例數的上/下限，並不會預先初始化環境，因此完全無法降低 cold start。更糟的是，AWS 文件指出將 reserved concurrency 設為 0 等於刻意限流，會讓 function 完全停止處理任何事件，直接讓應用程式中斷。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Reserved concurrency does not pre-warm execution environments and therefore does not eliminate the cold-start latency. In addition, API Gateway is not an Application Auto Scaling scalable target and 'reserved concurrency on the API Gateway API' is not a valid configuration, so the option is technically invalid.","why_zh":"Reserved concurrency 不會預先暖機執行環境，因此無法消除 cold start 延遲。此外，API Gateway 不是 Application Auto Scaling 的 scalable target，「在 API Gateway API 上設定 reserved concurrency」並非有效設定，因此此選項在技術上不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/provisioned-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/lambda-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/application/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-lambda.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":3,"question_en":"A company is adopting AWS CodeDeploy to automate its application deployments for a Java-Apache Tomcat application with an Apache Webserver. The development team started with a proof of concept, created a deployment group for a developer environment, and performed functional tests within the application. After completion, the team will create additional deployment groups for staging and production. The current log level is configured within the Apache settings, but the team wants to change this configuration dynamically when the deployment occurs, so that they can set different log level configurations depending on the deployment group without having a different application revision for each group. How can these requirements be met with the LEAST management overhead and without requiring different script versions for each deployment group?","question_zh":"一家公司正在采用 AWS CodeDeploy 来实现其 Java - Apache Tomcat 应用程序（搭配 Apache Web 服务器） 的自动化部署。开发团队首先进行了概念验证，为开发环境创建了一个部署组，并在应用程序内部进行 了功能测试。完成后，团队将为预发布和生产环境创建更多的部署组。 当前的日志级别是在 Apache 设置中配置的，但团队希望在部署时动态更改此配置，以便他们可以根据 部署组设置不同的日志级别配置，而无需为每个组都使用不同的应用程序版本。 如何以最小的管理开销满足这些要求，同时又无需为每个部署组准备不同的脚本版本？","options_en":{"A":"Tag the Amazon EC2 instances depending on the deployment group. Then place a script into the application revision that calls the metadata service and the EC2 API to identify which deployment group the instance is part of. Use this information to configure the log level settings. Reference the script as part of the AfterInstall lifecycle hook in the appspec.yml file.","B":"Create a script that uses the CodeDeploy environment variable DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ NAME to identify which deployment group the instance is part of. Use this information to configure the log level settings. Reference this script as part of the BeforeInstall lifecycle hook in the appspec.yml file.","C":"Create a CodeDeploy custom environment variable for each environment. Then place a script into the application revision that checks this environment variable to identify which deployment group the instance is part of. Use this information to configure the log level settings. Reference this script as part of the ValidateService lifecycle hook in the appspec.yml file.","D":"Create a script that uses the CodeDeploy environment variable DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID to identify which deployment group the instance is part of to configure the log level settings. Reference this script as part of the Install lifecycle hook in the appspec.yml file."},"options_zh":{"A":"根据部署组对 Amazon EC2 实例进行标记。然后在应用程序修订版中放入一个脚本，该脚本调用元数 据服务和 EC2 API 以确定实例所属的部署组。使用此信息来配置日志级别设置。在 appspec.yml 文件 的 AfterInstall 生命周期挂钩中引用该脚本。","B":"创建一个脚本，该脚本使用 CodeDeploy 环境变量 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 来确定实例所属 的部署组。利用此信息来配置日志级别设置。在 appspec.yml 文件的 BeforeInstall 生命周期挂钩中 引用此脚本。","C":"为每个环境创建一个 CodeDeploy 自定义环境变量。然后在应用程序修订版中放入一个脚本，该脚本 检查此环境变量以确定实例属于哪个部署组。使用此信息来配置日志级别设置。在 appspec.yml 文 件的 ValidateService 生命周期挂钩中引用此脚本。","D":"创建一个脚本，该脚本使用 CodeDeploy 环境变量 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID 来识别实例所属的部署 组，以配置日志级别设置。在 appspec.yml 文件的 Install 生命周期挂钩中引用此脚本。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeDeploy automatically exposes built-in environment variables to every EC2/On-Premises lifecycle hook script, including DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME, DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID, APPLICATION_NAME, DEPLOYMENT_ID, and LIFECYCLE_EVENT. A single script in one application revision can branch on DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME to set per-environment Apache log levels, so no per-group revision and no per-group script version are needed, giving the lowest management overhead. The AWS 'AppSpec hooks section' doc gives this exact scenario verbatim: a script that runs 'sed -i -e s/LogLevel warn/LogLevel debug/g /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf' when DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME equals Staging, and states it 'must be invoked during the BeforeInstall deployment lifecycle event.' BeforeInstall is the documented hook for preinstall configuration changes such as editing httpd.conf before the new files are installed, which makes option B both technically correct and the documented best practice.","explanation_zh":"CodeDeploy 會自動將內建環境變數提供給每個 EC2/On-Premises lifecycle hook 腳本，包括 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME、DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID、APPLICATION_NAME、DEPLOYMENT_ID 與 LIFECYCLE_EVENT。單一 application revision 內的單一腳本可依 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 分支來設定各環境的 Apache log level，因此不需要為每個 deployment group 建立不同 revision，也不需要不同腳本版本，管理負擔最低。AWS 'AppSpec hooks section' 文件正好逐字提供此情境的範例：當 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 等於 Staging 時執行 'sed -i -e s/LogLevel warn/LogLevel debug/g /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf' 的腳本，並明確說明此腳本必須在 BeforeInstall lifecycle event 執行。BeforeInstall 是文件指定用於安裝前設定變更（例如在安裝新檔案前修改 httpd.conf）的 hook，因此選項 B 在技術上正確且為文件記載的最佳實務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Tagging EC2 instances and calling the metadata/EC2 API to derive the deployment group is far more management overhead than simply reading the built-in DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME variable that CodeDeploy already injects into every hook. It also adds IAM permissions and API-call complexity for no benefit, and AfterInstall would change config only after the files are already installed.","why_zh":"為 EC2 instance 加標籤並呼叫 metadata/EC2 API 來判斷 deployment group，比直接讀取 CodeDeploy 已自動注入每個 hook 的內建 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 變數負擔大得多，還需額外 IAM 權限與 API 呼叫，毫無好處；且 AfterInstall 是在檔案安裝之後才修改設定。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating CodeDeploy custom environment variables per environment is unnecessary because DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME is already built in, adding setup overhead. Worse, ValidateService is documented as 'the last deployment lifecycle event... used to verify the deployment was completed successfully,' not to configure the application before install, so it is the wrong hook for changing log config.","why_zh":"為每個環境建立 CodeDeploy 自訂環境變數沒有必要，因為 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 已是內建，反而增加設定負擔。更糟的是文件明確指出 ValidateService 是『最後一個 lifecycle event，用於驗證部署是否成功完成』，並非在安裝前設定應用程式，因此是修改 log 設定的錯誤 hook。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The AWS doc states the Install event 'is reserved for the CodeDeploy agent and cannot be used to run scripts' (the agent copies revision files from the temporary location to the destination), so referencing a script under the Install hook is invalid. DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID is a real built-in variable but is a less readable identifier than DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME; the fatal flaw is the unusable Install hook.","why_zh":"AWS 文件指出 Install 事件『保留給 CodeDeploy agent，不能用來執行腳本』（由 agent 將 revision 檔案從暫存位置複製到目的地），因此在 Install hook 下引用腳本是無效的。DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_ID 確實是內建變數，但比 DEPLOYMENT_GROUP_NAME 不易閱讀；致命缺陷是 Install hook 根本無法執行腳本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":4,"question_en":"A company requires its developers to tag all Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes in an account to indicate a desired backup frequency. This requirement Includes EBS volumes that do not require backups. The company uses custom tags named Backup_Frequency that have values of none, daily, or weekly that correspond to the desired backup frequency. An audit finds that developers are occasionally not tagging the EBS volumes. A DevOps engineer needs to ensure that all EBS volumes always have the Backup_Frequency tag so that the company can perform backups at least weekly unless a different value is specified. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司要求其开发人员为账户中的所有亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷添加标签，以表明所 需的备份频率。此要求包括那些不需要备份的 EBS 卷。该公司使用名为“Backup_Frequency”的自 定义标签，其值为“none”（无）、“daily”（每日）或“weekly”（每周），分别对应所需的备份 频率。一次审计发现，开发人员偶尔会忘记为 EBS 卷添加标签。 DevOps 工程师需要确保所有 EBS 卷始终具有“Backup_Frequency”标签，以便公司至少每周执行一次 备份，除非指定了不同的值。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up AWS Config in the account. Create a custom rule that returns a compliance failure for all Amazon EC2 resources that do not have a Backup_Frequency tag applied. Configure a remediation action that uses a custom AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to apply the Backup_Frequency tag with a value of weekly.","B":"Set up AWS Config in the account. Use a managed rule that returns a compliance failure for EC2::Volume resources that do not have a Backup_Frequency tag applied. Configure a remediation action that uses a custom AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to apply the Backup_Frequency tag with a value of weekly.","C":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail in the account. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to EBS CreateVolume events. Configure a custom AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to apply the Backup_Frequency tag with a value of weekly. Specify the runbook as the target of the rule.","D":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail in the account. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to EBS CreateVolume events or EBS ModifyVolume events. Configure a custom AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to apply the Backup_Frequency tag with a value of weekly. Specify the runbook as the target of the rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"在账户中设置 AWS Config。创建一条自定义规则，对于所有未应用“Backup_Frequency”标签的 Amazon EC2 资源返回合规性失败。配置一个修复操作，使用自定义的 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册来应用“Backup_Frequency”标签，其值为“每周”。","B":"在账户中设置 AWS Config。使用一个托管规则，对于未应用“Backup_Frequency”标签的 EC2:: Volume 资源返回合规性失败。配置一个修复操作，使用自定义的 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册来应用“Backup_Frequency”标签，其值为“weekly”。","C":"在账户中启用 AWS CloudTrail。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 EBS 作出反应。 创建卷事件。配置一个自定义的 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，将“Backup_Frequency” 标签的值设置为“weekly”。将该运行手册指定为规则的目标。","D":"在账户中启用 AWS CloudTrail。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 EBS CreateVolume 事件或 EBS ModifyVolume 事件做出反应。配置一个自定义的 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，将 Backup_Frequency 标签的值设置为 weekly。将该运行手册指定为规则的目标。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is that all EBS volumes ALWAYS carry the Backup_Frequency tag, defaulting to weekly when none is specified. The AWS Config managed rule required-tags (identifier REQUIRED_TAGS) explicitly lists AWS::EC2::Volume among its supported resource types and uses a 'Configuration changes' trigger, so it continuously evaluates every volume and flags any that lack the tag - both at creation and if the tag is later removed (because tag removal is itself a recorded configuration change). The required-tags doc page also states verbatim that the AWS-managed AWS-SetRequiredTags automation document does NOT work as remediation for this rule and that you must create your own custom Systems Manager Automation document - which is exactly what option B specifies (a custom runbook applying Backup_Frequency=weekly). Because the rule only flags volumes missing the tag, developers who already specified none/daily/weekly keep their chosen value, while untagged volumes get the safe weekly default. Options C and D are event-driven on CreateVolume (and ModifyVolume for D), firing only at creation/attribute-change time, so they never re-tag a volume whose tag was later deleted; per the EC2 API reference, ModifyVolume changes size, type, and IOPS (not tags), so D's addition closes no gap. Option A needlessly defines a custom rule scoped to all EC2 resources when the purpose-built managed rule already exists and supports volumes.","explanation_zh":"需求是所有 EBS 磁碟區「永遠」都要帶有 Backup_Frequency 標籤，未指定時預設為 weekly。AWS Config 受管規則 required-tags（識別碼 REQUIRED_TAGS）的支援資源類型清單中明確包含 AWS::EC2::Volume，並採用「組態變更（Configuration changes）」觸發，因此會持續評估每個磁碟區並標記任何缺少標籤者，包含建立時未加標籤，以及標籤之後被移除的情形（因為移除標籤本身就是一筆會被記錄的組態變更）。required-tags 文件頁面亦逐字載明：AWS 受管的 AWS-SetRequiredTags 自動化文件無法作為此規則的修復動作，必須自行建立自訂的 Systems Manager Automation 文件，這正是選項 B 所述（自訂 runbook 套用 Backup_Frequency=weekly）。由於規則只標記缺少標籤的磁碟區，已自行指定 none/daily/weekly 的開發者會保留其選擇的值，未加標籤者則套用安全的 weekly 預設值。選項 C、D 以 CreateVolume（D 另含 ModifyVolume）事件驅動，僅在建立或屬性變更時觸發，無法為之後被刪除標籤的磁碟區重新加標；依 EC2 API 參考，ModifyVolume 變更的是大小、類型與 IOPS（而非標籤），故 D 的新增並未補上任何缺口。選項 A 在已有專用受管規則且支援磁碟區的情況下，多此一舉地定義範圍涵蓋所有 EC2 資源的自訂規則。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses an unnecessary custom AWS Config rule scoped to ALL EC2 resources (instances, security groups, ENIs, etc.) when the purpose-built managed rule required-tags already exists and explicitly supports AWS::EC2::Volume. Wrong scope and far more custom effort than needed.","why_zh":"在已有專用受管規則 required-tags 且明確支援 AWS::EC2::Volume 的情況下，使用範圍涵蓋所有 EC2 資源（執行個體、安全群組、ENI 等）的自訂 AWS Config 規則，範圍錯誤且自訂工作量遠高於所需。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EventBridge reacting only to CreateVolume events tags volumes at creation only; it does not re-apply the tag if a developer later removes it, so it fails the 'all EBS volumes always have the tag' requirement.","why_zh":"EventBridge 僅對 CreateVolume 事件反應，只在建立時加標籤；若開發者之後移除標籤不會重新套用，無法滿足『所有 EBS 磁碟區永遠都要有標籤』的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Adding ModifyVolume does not help: per the EC2 API reference, ModifyVolume changes size, type, and IOPS, not tags (tag removal is done via DeleteTags). So this still only triggers at creation/attribute-change and never re-tags volumes whose tag was deleted, failing the 'always' requirement.","why_zh":"加入 ModifyVolume 無濟於事：依 EC2 API 參考，ModifyVolume 變更的是大小、類型與 IOPS 而非標籤（移除標籤是透過 DeleteTags）。因此仍只在建立或屬性變更時觸發，無法為被刪標籤的磁碟區重新加標，不符『永遠』要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/required-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/APIReference/API_ModifyVolume.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":5,"question_en":"A company is using an Amazon Aurora cluster as the data store for its application. The Aurora cluster is configured with a single DB instance. The application performs read and write operations on the database by using the cluster's instance endpoint. The company has scheduled an update to be applied to the cluster during an upcoming maintenance window. The cluster must remain available with the least possible interruption during the maintenance window. What should a DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其应用程序的数据存储设置为亚马逊 Aurora 集群。该 Aurora 集群配置了一个单一的数据库 实例。应用程序通过使用集群的实例端点对数据库执行读写操作。 该公司已安排在即将到来的维护窗口期间对集群进行更新。在维护窗口期间，集群必须保持可用状态， 且中断时间应尽可能短。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add a reader instance to the Aurora cluster. Update the application to use the Aurora cluster endpoint for write operations. Update the Aurora cluster's reader endpoint for reads.","B":"Add a reader instance to the Aurora cluster. Create a custom ANY endpoint for the cluster. Update the application to use the Aurora cluster's custom ANY endpoint for read and write operations.","C":"Turn on the Multi-AZ option on the Aurora cluster. Update the application to use the Aurora cluster endpoint for write operations. Update the Aurora cluster’s reader endpoint for reads.","D":"Turn on the Multi-AZ option on the Aurora cluster. Create a custom ANY endpoint for the cluster. Update the application to use the Aurora cluster's custom ANY endpoint for read and write operations"},"options_zh":{"A":"向 Aurora 集群添加一个读取器实例。更新应用程序，使其在写入操作时使用 Aurora 集群端点。更新 Aurora 集群的读取器端点以用于读取操作。","B":"向 Aurora 集群添加一个读取器实例。为该集群创建一个自定义的 ANY 端点。更新应用程序，使其使用 Aurora 集群的自定义 ANY 端点来执行读写操作。","C":"在 Aurora 集群上启用多可用区选项。更新应用程序，使其在写入操作时使用 Aurora 集群端点。更新 Aurora 集群的只读端点以用于读取操作。","D":"在 Aurora 集群上启用多可用区选项。为该集群创建自定义的 ANY 端点。更新应用程序，使其使用 Aurora 集群的自定义 ANY 端点来执行读写操作。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The cluster has a single DB instance, so a maintenance/failure event forces Aurora to recreate the primary instance, which the AWS HA docs say typically takes less than 10 minutes (read and write operations fail during that window). Converting the cluster to Multi-AZ by adding a reader (Aurora Replica) in a different AZ gives Aurora a promotion target, and the docs state that promoting an Aurora Replica is 'much faster than creating a new primary instance' — service is typically restored in less than 60 seconds and often less than 30 seconds, which is the least possible interruption. The cluster (writer) endpoint always represents the current primary instance and provides automatic failover support, so the application should keep using the cluster endpoint for writes and the reader endpoint for reads. Option A matches both the correct mechanism (add a reader in another AZ) and the correct endpoint usage, so it is the right answer.","explanation_zh":"此叢集只有單一 DB instance，因此維護或故障事件會迫使 Aurora 重新建立 primary instance，AWS 高可用文件指出這通常需時少於 10 分鐘（期間讀寫操作會失敗）。在另一個 AZ 新增 reader（Aurora Replica）以將叢集轉為 Multi-AZ，會提供可供 Aurora 提升的目標，文件指出提升 Aurora Replica「遠快於重新建立新 primary instance」——服務通常於少於 60 秒、且常少於 30 秒內恢復，達到最小中斷。cluster（writer）endpoint 永遠代表目前的 primary instance 並提供自動 failover 支援，因此應用程式應繼續以 cluster endpoint 進行寫入、以 reader endpoint 進行讀取。選項 A 同時符合正確的機制（在另一個 AZ 新增 reader）與正確的 endpoint 用法，因此是正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Adding a reader is correct, but using a custom ANY endpoint for both reads and writes is broken. AWS docs state Aurora directs connections on an ANY-type endpoint to any associated DB instance with equal probability, so writes/DDL can land on a read-only reader instance and fail. The cluster endpoint, not a custom ANY endpoint, is the construct that always tracks the writer.","why_zh":"新增 reader 是正確的，但對讀取與寫入都使用 custom ANY endpoint 是錯的。AWS 文件指出 Aurora 會以相同機率將 ANY 型 endpoint 的連線導向任一相關 DB instance，因此寫入/DDL 可能落到唯讀的 reader instance 而失敗。永遠追蹤 writer 的是 cluster endpoint，而非 custom ANY endpoint。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The endpoint usage (cluster for writes, reader for reads) is correct, but provisioned Aurora has no simple 'Turn on Multi-AZ' toggle the way Amazon RDS does. AWS docs say you convert an existing Aurora cluster to Multi-AZ by adding a new reader DB instance in a different AZ — exactly what option A does, not what C describes.","why_zh":"endpoint 用法（cluster 寫、reader 讀）正確，但 provisioned Aurora 並不像 Amazon RDS 那樣有簡單的「開啟 Multi-AZ」開關。AWS 文件指出，將既有 Aurora 叢集轉為 Multi-AZ 的方式是在不同 AZ 新增 reader DB instance——正是選項 A 的做法，而非 C 所述。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines two errors: provisioned Aurora has no 'Turn on Multi-AZ' option (you add a reader in another AZ instead), and a custom ANY endpoint cannot be relied on for writes because connections are distributed to any instance with equal probability, including read-only replicas.","why_zh":"結合兩個錯誤：provisioned Aurora 沒有「開啟 Multi-AZ」選項（而是在另一個 AZ 新增 reader），且 custom ANY endpoint 不能用於寫入，因為連線會以相同機率分散到任一 instance，包含唯讀 replica。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Concepts.AuroraHighAvailability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Overview.Endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Endpoints.Cluster.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Endpoints.Custom.Considerations.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":6,"question_en":"A company must encrypt all AMIs that the company shares across accounts. A DevOps engineer has access to a source account where an unencrypted custom AMI has been built. The DevOps engineer also has access to a target account where an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group will launch EC2 instances from the AMI. The DevOps engineer must share the AMI with the target account. The company has created an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key in the source account. Which additional steps should the DevOps engineer perform to meet the requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"公司必须对其跨账户共享的所有 AMI 进行加密。一位 DevOps 工程师能够访问源账户，在该账户中已构建 了一个未加密的自定义 AMI。该 DevOps 工程师还能够访问目标账户，在该账户中，Amazon EC2 自动扩展 组将从该 AMI 启动 EC2 实例。DevOps 工程师必须将 AMI 与目标账户共享。 该公司已在源账户中创建了一个 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥。 为了满足要求，DevOps 工程师还应执行哪些额外步骤？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"In the source account, copy the unencrypted AMI to an encrypted AMI. Specify the KMS key in the copy action.","B":"In the source account, copy the unencrypted AMI to an encrypted AMI. Specify the default Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) encryption key in the copy action.","C":"In the source account, create a KMS grant that delegates permissions to the Auto Scaling group service-linked role in the target account.","D":"In the source account, modify the key policy to give the target account permissions to create a grant. In the target account, create a KMS grant that delegates permissions to the Auto Scaling group service- linked role.","E":"In the source account, share the unencrypted AMI with the target account.","F":"In the source account, share the encrypted AMI with the target account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在源账户中，将未加密的 AMI 复制为加密的 AMI。在复制操作中指定 KMS 密钥。","B":"在源账户中，将未加密的 AMI 复制为加密的 AMI。在复制操作中指定默认的 Amazon 弹性块存储 （Amazon EBS）加密密钥。","C":"在源账户中，创建一个 KMS 授予，将权限委托给目标账户中的 Auto Scaling 组服务相关角色。","D":"在源账户中，修改密钥策略以授予目标账户创建授权的权限。在目标账户中，创建一个 KMS 授权，将权 限委托给 Auto Scaling 组服务相关角色。","E":"在源账户中，与目标账户共享未加密的 AMI。","F":"在源账户中，与目标账户共享加密的 AMI。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The goal is to share an AMI encrypted with a customer managed KMS key cross-account and let an Auto Scaling group in the target account launch from it. You cannot encrypt an AMI in place, so you copy the unencrypted AMI to an encrypted AMI and specify the source-account customer managed key in the CopyImage action; AWS documents exactly this 'Copy an unencrypted source AMI to an encrypted target AMI' scenario (A). You cannot use the default AWS managed EBS key because AMIs backed by snapshots encrypted with the default AWS managed key cannot be shared across accounts (eliminates B). For the target account's Auto Scaling group to launch instances with EBS volumes encrypted by a CMK that lives in a different account, AWS requires the two-step cross-account flow in 'Required AWS KMS key policy for use with encrypted volumes', Example 2: first the source account (the key owner) modifies the key policy to let the target account root call kms:CreateGrant, then from the target account you create a KMS grant whose grantee principal is the AWSServiceRoleForAutoScaling service-linked role (D). Finally you must share the encrypted AMI (not the unencrypted original) with the target account using modify-image-attribute (F).","explanation_zh":"目標是用 customer managed KMS key 加密 AMI 並跨帳號分享，讓目標帳號的 Auto Scaling group 從中啟動執行個體。AMI 無法原地加密，因此需將未加密 AMI 複製為加密 AMI，並在 CopyImage 動作中指定來源帳號的 customer managed key；AWS 文件正是記載此『Copy an unencrypted source AMI to an encrypted target AMI』情境（A）。不能用預設 AWS managed EBS key，因為以預設 AWS managed key 加密快照所支援的 AMI 無法跨帳號分享（排除 B）。要讓目標帳號的 Auto Scaling group 以位於另一帳號的 CMK 加密 EBS 磁碟區啟動執行個體，AWS 在『Required AWS KMS key policy for use with encrypted volumes』Example 2 規定了兩步驟跨帳號流程：先由來源帳號（key 擁有者）修改 key policy 允許目標帳號 root 呼叫 kms:CreateGrant，再從目標帳號建立 KMS grant，其 grantee principal 為 AWSServiceRoleForAutoScaling service-linked role（D）。最後必須以 modify-image-attribute 將加密後的 AMI（而非未加密的原始 AMI）分享給目標帳號（F）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Specifying the default EBS encryption key (the AWS managed key aws/ebs) is wrong: the AMI sharing documentation states explicitly that you cannot share AMIs backed by snapshots encrypted with the default AWS managed key. A customer managed key is required for cross-account sharing.","why_zh":"指定預設 EBS 加密金鑰（AWS 受管金鑰 aws/ebs）是錯的：AMI 分享文件明確指出，以預設 AWS managed key 加密快照所支援的 AMI 無法跨帳號分享。跨帳號分享必須使用 customer managed key。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The grant must be created FROM the target account (where the Auto Scaling group lives), not from the source account. Per Example 2, the source account only modifies the key policy to permit the target account root to call kms:CreateGrant; the target account then issues the grant to the AWSServiceRoleForAutoScaling service-linked role.","why_zh":"grant 必須由目標帳號（Auto Scaling group 所在帳號）建立，而非來源帳號。依 Example 2，來源帳號僅修改 key policy 允許目標帳號 root 呼叫 kms:CreateGrant；接著由目標帳號對 AWSServiceRoleForAutoScaling service-linked role 建立 grant。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Sharing the unencrypted AMI directly violates the explicit requirement that all AMIs shared across accounts must be encrypted; you must share the encrypted copy instead (F).","why_zh":"直接分享未加密 AMI 違反了所有跨帳號分享的 AMI 都必須加密的明確需求；應改為分享加密後的副本（F）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/key-policy-requirements-EBS-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/how-ami-copy-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/sharingamis-explicit.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":7,"question_en":"A company uses AWS CodePipeline pipelines to automate releases of its application A typical pipeline consists of three stages build, test, and deployment. The company has been using a separate AWS CodeBuild project to run scripts for each stage. However, the company now wants to use AWS CodeDeploy to handle the deployment stage of the pipelines. The company has packaged the application as an RPM package and must deploy the application to a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances are in an EC2 Auto Scaling group and are launched from a common AMI. Which combination of steps should a DevOps engineer perform to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 管道来自动化其应用程序的发布。典型的管道包含三个阶段：构建、测 试和部署。该公司此前一直使用单独的 AWS CodeBuild 项目来运行每个阶段的脚本。然而，该公司现 在希望使用 AWS CodeDeploy 来处理管道的部署阶段。 该公司已将应用程序打包为 RPM 软件包，并且必须将该应用程序部署到一组亚马逊 EC2 实例上。这些 EC2 实例位于一个 EC2 自动扩展组中，并且是从一个通用的 AMI 启动的。 DevOps 工程师应执行哪些步骤组合才能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new version of the common AMI with the CodeDeploy agent installed. Update the IAM role of the EC2 instances to allow access to CodeDeploy.","B":"Create a new version of the common AMI with the CodeDeploy agent installed. Create an AppSpec file that contains application deployment scripts and grants access to CodeDeploy.","C":"Create an application in CodeDeploy. Configure an in-place deployment type. Specify the Auto Scaling group as the deployment target. Add a step to the CodePipeline pipeline to use EC2 Image Builder to create a new AMI. Configure CodeDeploy to deploy the newly created AMI.","D":"Create an application in CodeDeploy. Configure an in-place deployment type. Specify the Auto Scaling group as the deployment target. Update the CodePipeline pipeline to use the CodeDeploy action to deploy the application.","E":"Create an application in CodeDeploy. Configure an in-place deployment type. Specify the EC2 instances that are launched from the common AMI as the deployment target. Update the CodePipeline pipeline to use the CodeDeploy action to deploy the application."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个安装了 CodeDeploy 代理的新通用 AMI 版本。更新 EC2 实例的 IAM 角色，以允许其访问 CodeDeploy。","B":"创建一个安装了 CodeDeploy 代理的新版本通用 AMI。创建一个包含应用程序部署脚本并授予 CodeDeploy 访问权限的 AppSpec 文件。","C":"在 CodeDeploy 中创建一个应用程序。配置为原地部署类型。指定 Auto Scaling 组作为部署目标。在 CodePipeline 管道中添加一个步骤，使用 EC2 Image Builder 创建新的 AMI。配置 CodeDeploy 以部署新 创建的 AMI。","D":"在 CodeDeploy 中创建一个应用程序。配置原地部署类型。指定 Auto Scaling 组作为部署目标。更新 CodePipeline 管道以使用 CodeDeploy 操作来部署应用程序。","E":"在 CodeDeploy 中创建一个应用程序。配置原地部署类型。指定从通用 AMI 启动的 EC2 实例作为部署目 标。更新 CodePipeline 管道以使用 CodeDeploy 操作来部署应用程序。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two prerequisites are required to use CodeDeploy for the deployment stage when targeting an EC2 Auto Scaling group of instances launched from a common AMI. (A) The CodeDeploy agent must run on every instance; because the instances boot from a shared AMI in an ASG, the documented method is to bake the agent into a new version of that AMI ('Using a custom AMI with CodeDeploy and Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling'), and the EC2 instance IAM role/instance profile must grant access to S3/CodeDeploy so the agent can poll for and download revisions (step 1 of 'Deploying CodeDeploy applications to Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling groups' is to create an IAM instance profile that lets the instances work with S3). (D) You create a CodeDeploy application, choose the in-place deployment type, and specify the Auto Scaling group name as the deployment target, then add the CodeDeploy action to the CodePipeline deployment stage. Targeting the ASG (not individual instances) is essential because CodeDeploy installs Auto Scaling launch lifecycle hooks so that instances added by future scale-out events automatically receive the latest deployed revision. CodeDeploy deploys application revisions (the RPM/files described by appspec.yml), not AMIs, so no EC2 Image Builder step is needed.","explanation_zh":"若要使用 CodeDeploy 對由共用 AMI 啟動、位於 EC2 Auto Scaling group 中的 instances 執行部署階段，需要兩項前置作業。（A）每台 instance 上都必須運行 CodeDeploy agent；由於這些 instances 從共用 AMI 在 ASG 中啟動，官方文件建議的做法是將 agent 預先烘焙進新版的該 AMI（'Using a custom AMI with CodeDeploy and Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling'），且 EC2 instance 的 IAM role / instance profile 必須授予存取 S3/CodeDeploy 的權限，agent 才能輪詢並下載 revision（'Deploying CodeDeploy applications to Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling groups' 的第 1 步即為建立讓 instances 能與 S3 協作的 IAM instance profile）。（D）建立 CodeDeploy application，選擇 in-place 部署類型，將 Auto Scaling group 名稱指定為部署目標，再於 CodePipeline 的部署階段加入 CodeDeploy action。以 ASG（而非個別 instances）為目標至關重要，因為 CodeDeploy 會安裝 Auto Scaling launch lifecycle hook，使未來 scale-out 事件新增的 instances 自動收到最新部署的 revision。CodeDeploy 部署的是 application revision（由 appspec.yml 描述的 RPM/檔案），而非 AMI，因此不需要 EC2 Image Builder 步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Baking the agent into the AMI is fine, but the AppSpec file does not 'grant access to CodeDeploy.' Access is granted through IAM roles/instance profiles; appspec.yml only declares what files to install and which lifecycle event hooks to run. The IAM instance profile (covered by A) is the actual missing prerequisite, so this option's second clause is technically false.","why_zh":"將 agent 烘焙進 AMI 沒問題，但 AppSpec 檔案並不會『授予存取 CodeDeploy 的權限』。權限是透過 IAM role / instance profile 授予；appspec.yml 僅宣告要安裝哪些檔案以及執行哪些 lifecycle event hook。實際缺少的前置作業是 IAM instance profile（由 A 涵蓋），因此本選項的第二個子句在技術上是錯誤的。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeDeploy deploys application revisions (the RPM and files defined by appspec.yml), not AMIs. Adding an EC2 Image Builder step to build a new AMI and have CodeDeploy 'deploy the AMI' is the wrong mechanism for CodeDeploy and adds unnecessary operational overhead; replacing instances via a new AMI is an Auto Scaling/instance-refresh pattern, not a CodeDeploy revision deployment.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 部署的是 application revision（RPM 及 appspec.yml 定義的檔案），而非 AMI。加入 EC2 Image Builder 步驟建立新 AMI 並讓 CodeDeploy『部署該 AMI』對 CodeDeploy 而言是錯誤的機制，也帶來不必要的維運負擔；透過新 AMI 替換 instances 屬於 Auto Scaling / instance refresh 模式，而非 CodeDeploy 的 revision 部署。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Targeting the individual EC2 instances launched from the common AMI instead of the Auto Scaling group breaks the ASG integration. The deployment group must reference the Auto Scaling group name so CodeDeploy can install the launch lifecycle hook that auto-deploys to newly scaled-out instances; tag/instance targeting leaves future instances without the application.","why_zh":"以從共用 AMI 啟動的個別 EC2 instances 為目標，而非 Auto Scaling group，會破壞 ASG 整合。deployment group 必須引用 Auto Scaling group 名稱，CodeDeploy 才能安裝 launch lifecycle hook 以自動部署到新擴展出的 instances；以 tag/instance 為目標會使未來新增的 instances 缺少應用程式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/tutorials-auto-scaling-group.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/getting-started-create-iam-instance-profile.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":8,"question_en":"A company’s security team requires that all external Application Load Balancers (ALBs) and Amazon API Gateway APIs are associated with AWS WAF web ACLs. The company has hundreds of AWS accounts, all of which are included in a single organization in AWS Organizations. The company has configured AWS Config for the organization. During an audit, the company finds some externally facing ALBs that are not associated with AWS WAF web ACLs. Which combination of steps should a DevOps engineer take to prevent future violations? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"该公司安全团队要求所有面向外部的应用程序负载均衡器（ALB）和 Amazon API Gateway API 都要与 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（web ACL）相关联。该公司拥有数百个 AWS 账户，所有这些账户都包含在 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织内。该公司已为该组织配置了 AWS Config。在一次审计中，该公司发现了一些 面向外部的 ALB 未与 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表相关联。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪两种步骤组合来防止未来出现违规行为？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Delegate AWS Firewall Manager to a security account.","B":"Delegate Amazon GuardDuty to a security account.","C":"Create an AWS Firewall Manager policy to attach AWS WAF web ACLs to any newly created ALBs and API Gateway APIs.","D":"Create an Amazon GuardDuty policy to attach AWS WAF web ACLs to any newly created ALBs and API Gateway APIs.","E":"Configure an AWS Config managed rule to attach AWS WAF web ACLs to any newly created ALBs and API Gateway APIs."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AWS Firewall Manager 委托给一个安全账户。","B":"将 Amazon GuardDuty 委托给安全账户。","C":"创建一个 AWS Firewall Manager 策略，将 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（web ACL）附加到任何新创 建的应用负载均衡器（ALB）和 API 网关 API 上。","D":"创建一个 Amazon GuardDuty 策略，将 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（ACL）附加到任何新创建的应 用负载均衡器（ALB）和 API 网关 API 上。","E":"配置 AWS Config 管理规则，将 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（web ACL）附加到任何新创建的应用 负载均衡器（ALB）和 API 网关 API 上。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Firewall Manager is the purpose-built service for centrally and continuously enforcing AWS WAF web ACL associations across hundreds of accounts in an AWS Organization, which is exactly what 'prevent future violations' requires. Firewall Manager must run from a delegated administrator account: per the docs, 'only an organization's management account can create Firewall Manager administrator accounts,' so it designates a member (security) account as the Firewall Manager administrator (A) as the required prerequisite. You then create an AWS WAF Firewall Manager policy (C): the docs state Firewall Manager 'creates and manages web ACLs for in-scope resources,' automatically associating them, continuously remediating newly created or noncompliant resources, and even overriding a customer-attached web ACL. In-scope AWS WAF policy resource types include Application Load Balancers and Amazon API Gateway stages. By contrast, the AWS Config managed rule alb-waf-enabled only checks association and marks resources NON_COMPLIANT (detective only) and cannot attach web ACLs, and GuardDuty is a threat-detection service with no WAF-association capability and no such policy, so B, D, and E do not proactively prevent violations.","explanation_zh":"AWS Firewall Manager 是專為在 AWS Organizations 中跨數百個帳戶集中且持續強制套用 AWS WAF web ACL 關聯而設計的服務，正符合題目「防止未來違規」的需求。Firewall Manager 必須由委派管理員帳戶執行：文件指出「只有組織的 management account 才能建立 Firewall Manager 管理員帳戶」，由它指定某個成員（安全）帳戶作為 Firewall Manager 管理員（A），這是必要的前置步驟。接著建立 AWS WAF Firewall Manager 政策（C）：文件說明 Firewall Manager 會「為範圍內資源建立並管理 web ACL」，自動進行關聯並持續對新建立或不合規的資源進行修復，甚至會覆寫客戶手動關聯的 web ACL。AWS WAF 政策的範圍內資源類型包含 Application Load Balancers 與 Amazon API Gateway 階段。相對地，AWS Config 受管規則 alb-waf-enabled 只會檢查關聯並將資源標記為 NON_COMPLIANT（僅偵測），無法附加 web ACL；GuardDuty 則是威脅偵測服務，沒有 WAF 關聯能力，也不存在此類政策，因此 B、D、E 都無法主動防止違規。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that analyzes logs for malicious activity; it has no capability to associate AWS WAF web ACLs with ALBs or API Gateway, so delegating it does nothing for this requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是分析日誌以偵測惡意活動的威脅偵測服務，無法將 AWS WAF web ACL 關聯到 ALB 或 API Gateway，因此委派它對此需求毫無幫助。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no 'GuardDuty policy' that attaches AWS WAF web ACLs. GuardDuty does not create, manage, or associate web ACLs; this option describes a non-existent capability. WAF association policies are a Firewall Manager function.","why_zh":"並不存在會附加 AWS WAF web ACL 的「GuardDuty 政策」。GuardDuty 不會建立、管理或關聯 web ACL；此選項描述的是不存在的功能。WAF 關聯政策是 Firewall Manager 的功能。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"The AWS Config managed rule alb-waf-enabled only evaluates whether WAF is enabled and marks resources NON_COMPLIANT; Config managed rules are detective and cannot attach/associate web ACLs. They detect violations rather than proactively prevent them, and any remediation would require separate SSM Automation, not the rule itself.","why_zh":"AWS Config 受管規則 alb-waf-enabled 只會評估是否啟用 WAF 並將資源標記為 NON_COMPLIANT；Config 受管規則屬偵測性質，無法附加/關聯 web ACL，只能偵測違規而非主動防止，任何修復都需另行透過 SSM Automation 完成，而非規則本身。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/fms-creating-administrators.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/how-fms-manages-web-acls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/getting-started-fms-waf.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/alb-waf-enabled.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":9,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) keys and manual key rotation to meet regulatory compliance requirements. The security team wants to be notified when any keys have not been rotated after 90 days. Which solution will accomplish this?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥和手动密钥轮换来满足监管合规要求。安全团队希望 在任何密钥 90 天未轮换时收到通知。 哪种解决方案能实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS KMS to publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when keys are more than 90 days old.","B":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge event to launch an AWS Lambda function to call the AWS Trusted Advisor API and publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","C":"Develop an AWS Config custom rule that publishes to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when keys are more than 90 days old.","D":"Configure AWS Security Hub to publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when keys are more than 90 days old."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS KMS，使其在密钥超过 90 天时向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发布通知。","B":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件以启动一个 AWS Lambda 函数来调用 AWS Trusted Advisor API 并发 布到一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。","C":"创建一个 AWS Config 自定义规则，当密钥超过 90 天时向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发 布通知。","D":"配置 AWS 安全中心，使其在密钥超过 90 天时向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发布通知。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The company performs MANUAL KMS key rotation, which means replacing an existing KMS key with a brand-new key (with different cryptographic material) rather than letting KMS automatically rotate the backing key material. No native KMS feature, Trusted Advisor check, or Security Hub control evaluates whether a manually rotated key is older than 90 days and then notifies. The correct approach is an AWS Config CUSTOM rule (a periodic Lambda or Guard rule). AWS Config records AWS::KMS::Key as a supported resource type, so a custom rule can evaluate each key's creation date/age, flag keys older than 90 days as NON_COMPLIANT, and AWS Config natively sends a notification to an Amazon SNS topic when a resource's compliance status changes. The only AWS managed Config rule for KMS rotation (cmk-backing-key-rotation-enabled) merely checks whether AUTOMATIC rotation is enabled, which does not apply to manual rotation, so a custom rule is required.","explanation_zh":"此公司執行的是 MANUAL（手動）KMS key rotation，意即用一把全新的 KMS key（具有不同的密碼學金鑰材料）來取代既有的 key，而非讓 KMS 自動輪替底層金鑰材料。KMS 本身、Trusted Advisor 檢查項或 Security Hub 控制項都沒有原生功能可評估「手動輪替的 key 是否已超過 90 天」並發出通知。正確做法是使用 AWS Config 的 CUSTOM rule（定期觸發的 Lambda 或 Guard 規則）。AWS Config 將 AWS::KMS::Key 列為支援的 resource type，因此 custom rule 可評估每把 key 的建立日期/存在天數，將超過 90 天的 key 標記為 NON_COMPLIANT；當資源的 compliance 狀態改變時，AWS Config 原生會向 Amazon SNS topic 發送通知。唯一與 KMS 輪替相關的 AWS managed Config rule（cmk-backing-key-rotation-enabled）只檢查是否啟用 AUTOMATIC rotation，對手動輪替並不適用，因此必須使用 custom rule。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS KMS has no native feature to evaluate a key's age and publish to SNS when keys are more than 90 days old. KMS emits CloudTrail events and can integrate with EventBridge for rotation events, but it does not natively track a 90-day age threshold or push notifications based on key age. The capability is fabricated.","why_zh":"AWS KMS 沒有原生功能可評估 key 的存在天數並在超過 90 天時發布到 SNS。KMS 會產生 CloudTrail 事件並可透過 EventBridge 整合輪替事件，但不會原生追蹤 90 天的存在天數門檻或依 key 年齡推送通知，此能力為杜撰。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor has no check that evaluates KMS key age or manual-rotation status against a 90-day threshold. Its security checks cover items like exposed IAM access keys, MFA on root, S3 bucket permissions, and security groups, not custom KMS key-age compliance, so the Lambda calling the Trusted Advisor API would have no relevant data to act on.","why_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 沒有任何檢查項可依 90 天門檻評估 KMS key 的存在天數或手動輪替狀態。其安全檢查涵蓋如外洩的 IAM access key、root MFA、S3 bucket 權限與 security group 等，並不包含自訂的 KMS key 年齡合規檢查，因此呼叫 Trusted Advisor API 的 Lambda 取不到相關資料。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Security Hub does not have a control that flags manually rotated KMS keys older than 90 days. Its KMS-related control (KMS.4) only checks whether AUTOMATIC key rotation is enabled, which is irrelevant to manual rotation. Security Hub also does not publish to SNS based on its own custom logic; routing findings to SNS is done via EventBridge, and there is no such 90-day-age finding to begin with.","why_zh":"AWS Security Hub 沒有可標記「手動輪替且超過 90 天」KMS key 的控制項。其與 KMS 相關的控制項（KMS.4）僅檢查是否啟用 AUTOMATIC key rotation，與手動輪替無關。Security Hub 也不會依自身自訂邏輯直接發布到 SNS；將 findings 路由到 SNS 需透過 EventBridge，且根本不存在這種以 90 天年齡為基礎的 finding。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/rotate-keys-manually.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_develop-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/how-does-config-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/resource-config-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/cmk-backing-key-rotation-enabled.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":10,"question_en":"A security review has identified that an AWS CodeBuild project is downloading a database population script from an Amazon S3 bucket using an unauthenticated request. The security team does not allow unauthenticated requests to S3 buckets for this project. How can this issue be corrected in the MOST secure manner?","question_zh":"安全审查发现，一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目正在使用未认证的请求从 Amazon S3 存储桶下载数据库填充 脚本。安全团队不允许此项目对 S3 存储桶发出未认证的请求。 如何以最安全的方式纠正这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Add the bucket name to the AllowedBuckets section of the CodeBuild project settings. Update the build spec to use the AWS CLI to download the database population script.","B":"Modify the S3 bucket settings to enable HTTPS basic authentication and specify a token. Update the build spec to use cURL to pass the token and download the database population script.","C":"Remove unauthenticated access from the S3 bucket with a bucket policy. Modify the service role for the CodeBuild project to include Amazon S3 access. Use the AWS CLI to download the database population script.","D":"Remove unauthenticated access from the S3 bucket with a bucket policy. Use the AWS CLI to download the database population script using an IAM access key and a secret access key."},"options_zh":{"A":"将存储桶名称添加到 CodeBuild 项目设置的“AllowedBuckets”部分。更新构建规范以使用 AWS CLI 下 载数据库填充脚本。","B":"修改 S3 存储桶设置以启用 HTTPS 基本身份验证并指定一个令牌。更新构建规范以使用 cURL 传递令 牌并下载数据库填充脚本。","C":"使用存储桶策略从 S3 存储桶中移除未认证访问权限。修改 CodeBuild 项目的服务角色以包含对 Amazon S3 的访问权限。使用 AWS CLI 下载数据库填充脚本。","D":"使用存储桶策略从 S3 存储桶中移除未认证访问权限。使用 AWS 命令行界面（AWS CLI），通 过 IAM 访问密钥和秘密访问密钥下载数据库填充脚本。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeBuild interacts with other AWS services through its IAM service role, which supplies temporary credentials that the AWS CLI automatically uses to make SigV4-signed (authenticated) requests. The most secure fix has two parts: (1) remove anonymous/unauthenticated read access from the S3 bucket with a bucket policy, since all S3 resources are private by default and a bucket policy is the tool to control who can read objects; and (2) grant the CodeBuild service role s3:GetObject (Amazon S3 access) so the build can authenticate using the role's temporary credentials. The build spec then uses the AWS CLI, which signs requests with those role credentials. This matches the AWS IAM best practice 'Require workloads to use temporary credentials with IAM roles to access AWS,' which states there is no need to distribute long-lived credentials to workloads running on AWS. Option C does exactly this. Option D also removes anonymous access, but it embeds long-term IAM access keys and a secret access key, which AWS explicitly discourages and is therefore less secure than reusing the existing service role.","explanation_zh":"CodeBuild 透過其 IAM service role 與其他 AWS 服務互動，該 role 提供臨時憑證 (temporary credentials)，而 AWS CLI 會自動使用這些憑證發出經過 SigV4 簽署的 (已驗證) 請求。最安全的修正分為兩部分：(1) 使用 bucket policy 移除 S3 bucket 的匿名／未驗證讀取存取，因為所有 S3 資源預設皆為私有，而 bucket policy 正是控制誰可讀取物件的工具；(2) 為 CodeBuild service role 授予 s3:GetObject (Amazon S3 存取權)，讓建置程序能以 role 的臨時憑證進行驗證。build spec 接著使用 AWS CLI，AWS CLI 會以這些 role 憑證簽署請求。這符合 AWS IAM 最佳實務「Require workloads to use temporary credentials with IAM roles to access AWS」，其明確指出在 AWS 上執行的工作負載無需散布長期憑證。選項 C 正是如此做。選項 D 雖然也移除了匿名存取，但卻嵌入長期 IAM access key 與 secret access key，這是 AWS 明確不建議的做法，因此比重用既有 service role 更不安全。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no 'AllowedBuckets' section in CodeBuild project settings; CodeBuild controls S3 access through its IAM service role, not a project-level bucket allowlist. The feature is fabricated, and nothing here makes the request authenticated, so it does not solve the security finding.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 專案設定中並沒有「AllowedBuckets」區段；CodeBuild 透過其 IAM service role 控制 S3 存取，而非專案層級的 bucket 允許清單。此功能屬虛構，且沒有任何機制讓請求變成已驗證，因此無法解決此安全問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon S3 does not support 'HTTPS basic authentication' with a token. S3 authenticates requests using AWS Signature Version 4 with IAM credentials. Passing a token via cURL is not a valid S3 authentication method, so this option describes a nonexistent feature and is not secure.","why_zh":"Amazon S3 不支援使用 token 的「HTTPS basic authentication」。S3 是以 AWS Signature Version 4 搭配 IAM 憑證驗證請求。透過 cURL 傳遞 token 並非有效的 S3 驗證方式，因此此選項描述一個不存在的功能，且並不安全。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This correctly removes anonymous access, but it authenticates with a long-term IAM access key and secret access key, which requires storing static credentials in the build. AWS IAM best practices direct workloads on AWS to use IAM role temporary credentials instead of distributing long-lived keys, so D is functional but less secure than reusing the CodeBuild service role in option C. The question asks for the MOST secure approach.","why_zh":"此選項正確地移除了匿名存取，但卻以長期 IAM access key 與 secret access key 進行驗證，這需要在建置中儲存靜態憑證。AWS IAM 最佳實務指出在 AWS 上的工作負載應使用 IAM role 的臨時憑證，而非散布長期金鑰，因此 D 雖可運作，但比選項 C 重用 CodeBuild service role 更不安全。題目要求「最安全」的做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/setting-up-service-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/access-management.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-bucket-policies.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":11,"question_en":"An ecommerce company has chosen AWS to host its new platform. The company's DevOps team has started building an AWS Control Tower landing zone. The DevOps team has set the identity store within AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) to external identity provider (IdP) and has configured SAML 2.0. The DevOps team wants a robust permission model that applies the principle of least privilege. The model must allow the team to build and manage only the team's own resources. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家电子商务公司已选择 AWS 来托管其新平台。该公司的 DevOps 团队已开始构建 AWS 控制塔着陆区。 DevOps 团队已将身份存储设置为 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）中的外部身份提供程序（IdP）， 并已配置 SAML 2.0。 DevOps 团队希望采用一种强大的权限模型，遵循最小权限原则。该模型必须允许团队仅构建和管理团队自 身的资源。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create IAM policies that include the required permissions. Include the aws:PrincipalTag condition key.","B":"Create permission sets. Attach an inline policy that includes the required permissions and uses the aws:PrincipalTag condition key to scope the permissions.","C":"Create a group in the IdP. Place users in the group. Assign the group to accounts and the permission sets in IAM Identity Center.","D":"Create a group in the IdP. Place users in the group. Assign the group to OUs and IAM policies.","E":"Enable attributes for access control in IAM Identity Center. Apply tags to users. Map the tags as key- value pairs.","F":"Enable attributes for access control in IAM Identity Center. Map attributes from the IdP as key-value pairs."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建包含所需权限的 IAM 策略。包含 aws:PrincipalTag 条件键。","B":"创建权限集。附加一个内联策略，其中包含所需的权限并使用 AWS：用于限定权限范围的 PrincipalTag 条件键。","C":"在身份提供方（IdP）中创建一个组。将用户放入该组。在 IAM 身份中心中将该组分配给账户 和权限集。","D":"在身份提供方（IdP）中创建一个组。将用户放入该组。将该组分配给组织单位（OU）和 IAM 策略。","E":"在 IAM 身份中心启用用于访问控制的属性。为用户应用标签。将标签映射为键值对。","F":"在 IAM 身份中心启用用于访问控制的属性。将来自身份提供方的属性映射为键值对。"},"answer":["B","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical IAM Identity Center attribute-based access control (ABAC) pattern with an external SAML 2.0 IdP. (B) In IAM Identity Center, permissions are delivered through permission sets, which contain IAM policies (managed or inline) that Identity Center deploys as IAM roles in each assigned account. To enforce least privilege so the team manages only its own resources, the permission set's inline policy uses the aws:PrincipalTag condition key (e.g., \"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\") to scope access to resources tagged for that team. (C) Access is granted by assigning a group (AWS recommends groups over individual users) to AWS accounts together with one or more permission sets on the AWS accounts page; you cannot assign to OUs and you do not attach raw IAM policies in the assignment, which eliminates D. (F) Because the identity source is an external IdP using SAML 2.0, you enable Attributes for access control and source the attributes from the IdP (passed through SAML assertions or mapped from synchronized IdP attributes); Identity Center then passes them as session tags referenced by aws:PrincipalTag. The decisive contrast is E vs F: both begin with 'Enable attributes for access control,' but E ('Apply tags to users') describes the Identity Store / IAM Identity Center-as-identity-source flow where you manually set user attributes, which does not match an external SAML IdP, whereas F ('Map attributes from the IdP') correctly reflects sourcing attributes from the external IdP.","explanation_zh":"這是搭配外部 SAML 2.0 IdP 的 IAM Identity Center 屬性型存取控制 (ABAC) 標準模式。(B) 在 IAM Identity Center 中，權限是透過 permission sets 交付；permission set 包含 IAM 政策（受管或內嵌），Identity Center 會在每個被指派的帳戶中部署為 IAM 角色。為落實最小權限、讓團隊只管理自己的資源，permission set 的內嵌政策會使用 aws:PrincipalTag 條件鍵（例如 \"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\"），把存取範圍限縮到標記給該團隊的資源。(C) 存取是在 AWS accounts 頁面把群組（AWS 建議用群組而非個別使用者）指派給 AWS 帳戶並搭配一或多個 permission sets 來授予；無法指派給 OU，指派時也不會附加原始 IAM 政策，因此排除 D。(F) 由於身分來源是使用 SAML 2.0 的外部 IdP，你需啟用 Attributes for access control，並從 IdP 取得屬性（透過 SAML 斷言傳遞，或對應已同步的 IdP 屬性）；Identity Center 接著會把它們以 session tags 傳遞，供 aws:PrincipalTag 引用。關鍵對比在於 E 與 F：兩者都以「Enable attributes for access control」開頭，但 E（對使用者套用標籤）描述的是 Identity Store／IAM Identity Center 作為身分來源的流程，需手動設定使用者屬性，與外部 SAML IdP 情境不符；F（對應來自 IdP 的屬性）才正確反映從外部 IdP 取得屬性。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IAM Identity Center grants access through permission sets, not standalone IAM identity policies. While the aws:PrincipalTag condition key idea is correct, creating plain IAM policies is the wrong delivery mechanism for an IAM Identity Center landing zone; the policy belongs inside a permission set (B).","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 是透過 permission sets 授權，而非獨立的 IAM 身分政策。雖然使用 aws:PrincipalTag 條件鍵的概念正確，但在 IAM Identity Center landing zone 中建立純 IAM policy 是錯誤的交付機制；該政策應放在 permission set 內（即 B）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"In IAM Identity Center you assign groups/users to AWS accounts paired with permission sets, not to OUs, and you do not attach raw IAM policies to assignments. OU-level targeting and IAM-policy attachment are not how IAM Identity Center assignments work, so this step is technically invalid.","why_zh":"在 IAM Identity Center 中是將 group/user 指派到搭配 permission set 的 AWS accounts，而非指派到 OU，也不會將原生 IAM policy 掛在指派上。以 OU 為對象、掛載 IAM policy 並非 IAM Identity Center 的指派運作方式，故此步驟技術上無效。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"'Apply tags to users' and mapping those tags applies when IAM Identity Center (or its Identity Store) is the identity source and you set user attributes manually. With an external SAML 2.0 IdP, attributes are sourced from the IdP and passed via SAML assertions, so you map IdP attributes (F), not user-applied tags. F is the precise external-IdP choice.","why_zh":"「Apply tags to users」（為使用者套用標籤）並對應這些標籤，適用於以 IAM Identity Center（或其 Identity Store）作為身分來源、手動設定使用者屬性的情境。使用外部 SAML 2.0 IdP 時，屬性來自 IdP 並透過 SAML 斷言傳遞，因此應對應 IdP 屬性（F），而非由使用者套用的標籤。F 才是針對外部 IdP 的精確選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/attributesforaccesscontrol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/permissionsetsconcept.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/assignusers.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":12,"question_en":"An ecommerce company is receiving reports that its order history page is experiencing delays in reflecting the processing status of orders. The order processing system consists of an AWS Lambda function that uses reserved concurrency. The Lambda function processes order messages from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue and inserts processed orders into an Amazon DynamoDB table. The DynamoDB table has auto scaling enabled for read and write capacity. Which actions should a DevOps engineer take to resolve this delay? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家电子商务公司收到报告称，其订单历史页面在反映订单处理状态时出现延迟。该公司的订单处 理系统由一个使用预留并发量的 AWS Lambda 函数组成。该 Lambda 函数从 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列中处理订单消息，并将处理后的订单插入到一个启用了读写容量自动扩 展的 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些行动来解决此延误？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Check the ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage metric for the SQS queue. Increase the Lambda function concurrency limit.","B":"Check the ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage metric for the SQS queue Configure a redrive policy on the SQS queue.","C":"Check the NumberOfMessagesSent metric for the SQS queue. Increase the SQS queue visibility timeout.","D":"Check the WriteThrottleEvents metric for the DynamoDB table. Increase the maximum write capacity units (WCUs) for the table's scaling policy.","E":"Check the Throttles metric for the Lambda function. Increase the Lambda function timeout."},"options_zh":{"A":"检查 SQS 队列的“ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage”指标。提高 Lambda 函数的并发限制。","B":"检查 SQS 队列的“ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage”指标。为 SQS 队列配置重传策略。","C":"检查 SQS 队列的“已发送消息数”指标。增加 SQS 队列的可见性超时时间。","D":"检查 DynamoDB 表的 WriteThrottleEvents 指标。增加表的自动扩展策略的最大写入容量单位 （WCUs）。","E":"检查 Lambda 函数的节流指标。增加 Lambda 函数的超时时间。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The delay has two independent causes — a queue-side throughput bottleneck and a database-side throttling bottleneck — so two distinct fixes are required. (A) The Lambda function uses reserved concurrency, which AWS documents as acting 'as both a lower and upper bound', preventing the function from scaling beyond that limit. When messages arrive faster than the capped concurrency can drain them, the Lambda event-source-mapping troubleshooting guide states the symptom is backpressure with 'the age of the oldest message growing linearly' (the ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage metric), and a listed resolution is to raise the function's concurrency. (D) Even with Auto Scaling enabled, the DynamoDB provisioned-throughput documentation explicitly states 'Throttling can occur regardless of whether Auto Scaling is enabled... it does not respond instantly and it is constrained by the maximum capacity limits you configure.' Because the Lambda inserts (writes) processed orders, you detect this with the WriteThrottleEvents metric ('Watch for requests that exceed the provisioned WCU') and remediate sustained traffic that hits the ceiling by raising the maximum WCU in the scaling policy. Together A and D clear both bottlenecks delaying order-status updates.","explanation_zh":"延遲有兩個獨立成因——佇列端的吞吐量瓶頸與資料庫端的節流瓶頸——因此需要兩個不同的修正。(A) 此 Lambda 使用 reserved concurrency，AWS 文件說明其「同時作為下限與上限」，會阻止函式擴展超過該上限。當訊息湧入速度快於受上限限制的並行度所能消化的速度時，Lambda event source mapping 疑難排解指南指出症狀為 backpressure，亦即「最舊訊息的存留時間呈線性成長」（即 ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage 指標），其列出的解法之一即為提高函式的並行度上限。(D) 即使已啟用 Auto Scaling，DynamoDB provisioned throughput 文件明確指出「節流不論是否啟用 Auto Scaling 都可能發生……它不會即時反應，且受限於你設定的最大容量上限。」由於 Lambda 將處理後的訂單寫入資料表，你可用 WriteThrottleEvents 指標偵測（『監看超過已佈建 WCU 的請求』），並透過提高 scaling policy 的最大 WCU 來緩解持續觸頂的流量。A 與 D 一併清除兩個導致訂單狀態更新延遲的瓶頸。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage is the correct diagnostic metric, but a redrive policy only sends repeatedly failed messages to a dead-letter queue. It handles poison/failing messages, not a throughput backlog, so it adds no processing capacity and does not relieve the backpressure causing the delay.","why_zh":"ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage 是正確的診斷指標，但 redrive policy 只會把反覆失敗的訊息送往 dead-letter queue，處理的是毒丸/失敗訊息而非吞吐量積壓，並不會增加處理能力，也無法紓解造成延遲的 backpressure。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"NumberOfMessagesSent measures the producer's send rate, not the consumer backlog, so it does not diagnose the delay. Worse, increasing the visibility timeout keeps in-flight messages invisible longer, which does not add throughput and can make the delay appear worse rather than resolving it.","why_zh":"NumberOfMessagesSent 衡量的是生產者送出速率，而非消費端積壓，無法診斷延遲。更糟的是，增加 visibility timeout 會讓處理中的訊息隱形更久，既不增加吞吐量，反而可能加重延遲表現而非解決問題。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Throttles is a valid Lambda metric, but the proposed fix is wrong: throttling stems from hitting the reserved-concurrency cap, not from short durations. Increasing the function timeout makes each invocation hold a concurrency slot longer, reducing effective throughput and worsening both throttling and the backlog.","why_zh":"Throttles 是合理的 Lambda 指標，但所提修正錯誤：節流源自觸及 reserved concurrency 上限，而非執行時間過短。增加函式 timeout 會讓每次調用占用並行槽更久，降低有效吞吐量，反而加重節流與積壓。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/troubleshooting-event-source-mapping.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/throttling-provisioned-capacity-exceeded-mitigation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/TroubleshootingThrottling-cloudwatch.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":13,"question_en":"A company has a single AWS account that runs hundreds of Amazon EC2 instances in a single AWS Region. New EC2 instances are launched and terminated each hour in the account. The account also includes existing EC2 instances that have been running for longer than a week. The company's security policy requires all running EC2 instances to use an EC2 instance profile. If an EC2 instance does not have an instance profile attached, the EC2 instance must use a default instance profile that has no IAM permissions assigned. A DevOps engineer reviews the account and discovers EC2 instances that are running without an instance profile. During the review, the DevOps engineer also observes that new EC2 instances are being launched without an instance profile. Which solution will ensure that an instance profile is attached to all existing and future EC2 instances in the Region?","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 AWS 账户中运行着数百个位于单个 AWS 区域的亚马逊 EC2 实例。该账户每 小时都会启动和终止新的 EC2 实例，同时还包含运行时间超过一周的现有 EC2 实例。 该公司的安全策略要求所有正在运行的 EC2 实例都使用 EC2 实例配置文件。如果某个 EC2 实例未 附加实例配置文件，则该 EC2 实例必须使用默认的实例配置文件，且该默认配置文件未分配任何 IAM 权限。 一位 DevOps 工程师审查了账户，发现有 EC2 实例在没有实例配置文件的情况下运行。在审查过程 中，该 DevOps 工程师还注意到新启动的 EC2 实例也没有配置实例配置文件。 哪种解决方案能确保将实例配置文件附加到该区域内的所有现有和未来的 EC2 实例？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to EC2 RunInstances API calls. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances.","B":"Configure the ec2-instance-profile-attached AWS Config managed rule with a trigger type of configuration changes. Configure an automatic remediation action that invokes an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances.","C":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to EC2 StartInstances API calls. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances","D":"Configure the iam-role-managed-policy-check AWS Config managed rule with a trigger type of configuration changes. Configure an automatic remediation action that invokes an AWS Lambda function to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 EC2 的 RunInstances API 调用做出反应。将该规则 配置为调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例上。","B":"配置带有配置更改触发类型的“ec2 实例配置文件附加”AWS Config 管理规则。配置一个 自动修复操作，调用 AWS Systems。 用于将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例的经理自动化运行手册。","C":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 EC2 的 StartInstances API 调用做出反应。将该规则配置为 调用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例上。","D":"配置 AWS Config 管理规则 iam-role-managed-policy-check，触发类型为配置更改。配置自动修复操 作，调用 AWS Lambda 函数将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to attach an instance profile to ALL existing AND future EC2 instances. AWS Config's managed rule ec2-instance-profile-attached (identifier EC2_INSTANCE_PROFILE_ATTACHED) evaluates resource type AWS::EC2::Instance and is NON_COMPLIANT when no IAM profile is attached; its documented trigger type is exactly 'Configuration changes'. Because AWS Config records and evaluates the full inventory of EC2 instances, the long-running existing instances and every newly launched instance are all evaluated. Pairing the rule with an automatic remediation action that runs an SSM Automation runbook fixes the violations: the AWS Config docs state that enabling auto remediation 'initiates the remediation process for all noncompliant resources for that specific rule,' which covers the existing noncompliant instances, while the configuration-change trigger evaluates and remediates each new instance as it is created. Option B is the only choice that uses the correct rule, correct resource type, and a mechanism that reaches both the existing and future populations.","explanation_zh":"需求是要為「所有現有與未來」的 EC2 instances 附加 instance profile。AWS Config 的 managed rule ec2-instance-profile-attached（識別碼 EC2_INSTANCE_PROFILE_ATTACHED）評估資源類型 AWS::EC2::Instance，當沒有附加 IAM profile 時判定為 NON_COMPLIANT；其文件記載的 trigger type 正好是「Configuration changes」。由於 AWS Config 會記錄並評估完整的 EC2 instance 清單，因此既能涵蓋長期運行的現有 instances，也能涵蓋每個新啟動的 instance。將此 rule 搭配自動修復動作（automatic remediation action）執行 SSM Automation runbook，即可修正違規：AWS Config 文件明確指出啟用 auto remediation 會「對該 rule 的所有 noncompliant 資源啟動修復流程」，涵蓋現有不合規的 instances；而 configuration-change 觸發則會在每個新 instance 建立時加以評估並修復。選項 B 是唯一使用正確 rule、正確資源類型，並能同時觸及現有與未來兩類 instances 的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An EventBridge rule reacting to the RunInstances API only catches NEW instance launches and does nothing for the existing instances that have already been running for over a week, so it fails the 'all existing' part of the requirement.","why_zh":"對 RunInstances API 反應的 EventBridge rule 只能捕捉「新啟動」的 instance，對已運行超過一週的現有 instances 完全無作為，因此無法滿足「所有現有」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An EventBridge rule on StartInstances fires only when a stopped instance is started; it does not catch newly launched (RunInstances) instances nor already-running existing instances, so neither future launches nor existing running instances are reliably covered.","why_zh":"針對 StartInstances 的 EventBridge rule 僅在已停止的 instance 被重新啟動時觸發；它無法捕捉新啟動（屬於 RunInstances）的 instance，也無法處理已在運行的現有 instances，因此未來啟動與現有運行中的 instances 都無法可靠涵蓋。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The iam-role-managed-policy-check rule (IAM_ROLE_MANAGED_POLICY_CHECK) evaluates AWS::IAM::Role resources to verify that specified managed policies are attached to a role. It has nothing to do with whether an EC2 instance has an instance profile attached, so it cannot detect or remediate the actual non-compliance.","why_zh":"iam-role-managed-policy-check rule（IAM_ROLE_MANAGED_POLICY_CHECK）評估的是 AWS::IAM::Role 資源，確認指定的 managed policies 是否附加到 role，與 EC2 instance 是否附加 instance profile 完全無關，因此無法偵測或修復實際的不合規狀況。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/ec2-instance-profile-attached.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/iam-role-managed-policy-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":14,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is building a continuous deployment pipeline for a serverless application that uses AWS Lambda functions. The company wants to reduce the customer impact of an unsuccessful deployment. The company also wants to monitor for issues. Which deploy stage configuration will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在为一个使用 AWS Lambda 函数的无服务器应用程序构建持续部署流水线。该公 司希望将不成功的部署对客户造成的影响降到最低。同时，该公司还希望对问题进行监控。 哪种部署阶段配置能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) template to define the serverless application. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the Lambda functions with the Canary10Percent15Minutes Deployment Preference Type. Use Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor the health of the functions.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation to publish a new stack update, and include Amazon CloudWatch alarms on all resources. Set up an AWS CodePipeline approval action for a developer to verify and approve the AWS CloudFormation change set.","C":"Use AWS CloudFormation to publish a new version on every stack update, and include Amazon CloudWatch alarms on all resources. Use the RoutingConfig property of the AWS::Lambda::Alias resource to update the traffic routing during the stack update.","D":"Use AWS CodeBuild to add sample event payloads for testing to the Lambda functions. Publish a new version of the functions, and include Amazon CloudWatch alarms. Update the production alias to point to the new version. Configure rollbacks to occur when an alarm is in the ALARM state."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 无服务器应用程序模型（AWS SAM）模板来定义无服务器应用程序。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 以“金丝雀 10% 15 分钟”部署偏好类型部署 Lambda 函数。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控函数 的运行状况。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 发布新的堆栈更新，并在所有资源上设置 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。为开发 人员设置一个 AWS CodePipeline 批准操作，以验证并批准 AWS CloudFormation 更改集。","C":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 在每次堆栈更新时发布新版本，并在所有资源上包含 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。使用 AWS::Lambda::Alias 资源的 RoutingConfig 属性在堆栈更新期间更新流量 路由。","D":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 为 Lambda 函数添加用于测试的示例事件负载。发布函数的新版本，并包含 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。将生产别名更新为指向新版本。配置在警报处于 ALARM 状态时执行回滚。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are to reduce customer impact of an unsuccessful deployment (gradual traffic shifting with automatic rollback) and to monitor for issues (CloudWatch alarms). AWS SAM has built-in CodeDeploy integration for gradual Lambda deployments: by adding AutoPublishAlias and a DeploymentPreference containing a Type and Alarms, SAM automatically creates a CodeDeploy resource that publishes a new version, creates/updates an alias, and gradually shifts traffic. Canary10Percent15Minutes is an officially listed Deployment Preference Type that shifts 10% of traffic to the new version and the remaining 90% after 15 minutes, limiting blast radius. The Alarms property tells CodeDeploy to automatically roll back the deployment when a CloudWatch alarm enters the ALARM state, satisfying both the monitoring and the safe-deployment requirements. This is the AWS-prescribed safe-deployment pattern for serverless Lambda, so A is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是降低部署失敗對客戶的影響（漸進式流量轉移並自動回滾），以及監控問題（CloudWatch alarms）。AWS SAM 內建與 CodeDeploy 整合以提供 Lambda 漸進式部署：在範本中加入 AutoPublishAlias 以及包含 Type 與 Alarms 的 DeploymentPreference 後，SAM 會自動建立一個 CodeDeploy 資源，發佈新版本、建立或更新 alias，並逐步轉移流量。Canary10Percent15Minutes 是官方列出的 Deployment Preference Type，會先將 10% 流量導向新版本，15 分鐘後再轉移剩餘 90%，藉此限制影響範圍。Alarms 屬性會讓 CodeDeploy 在 CloudWatch alarm 進入 ALARM 狀態時自動回滾部署，同時滿足監控與安全部署的需求。這正是 AWS 為 serverless Lambda 規定的安全部署模式，因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A plain CloudFormation stack update is an all-at-once cutover, so a faulty change immediately affects 100% of customers. A manual CodePipeline approval action only gates the change set before deployment; it provides no gradual traffic shifting and the alarms are not wired into any automatic rollback, so it does not reduce customer impact of an unsuccessful deployment.","why_zh":"單純的 CloudFormation stack update 是一次性全量切換，有問題的變更會立即影響 100% 客戶。手動 CodePipeline approval action 只是在部署前對 change set 設關卡，並未提供漸進式流量轉移，且 alarms 未串接任何自動回滾，因此無法降低部署失敗對客戶的影響。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Setting the RoutingConfig (VersionWeight) on AWS::Lambda::Alias gives a static, manually defined weight applied during the stack update; it is not an automated time-based canary, and CloudFormation does not automatically roll back the alias weighting based on those CloudWatch alarms the way CodeDeploy does. The alarms are merely included on resources, not part of an orchestrated alarm-driven rollback, so it is a clunky approximation rather than the prescribed safe-deployment mechanism.","why_zh":"在 AWS::Lambda::Alias 上設定 RoutingConfig（VersionWeight）只是在 stack update 時套用靜態、手動定義的權重，並非自動的時間式 canary，且 CloudFormation 不會像 CodeDeploy 那樣依據這些 CloudWatch alarms 自動回滾別名權重。alarms 只是被包含在資源上，並非協調式 alarm 回滾的一部分，因此是笨拙的近似做法，而非標準的安全部署機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Updating the production alias to point directly to the new version is a 100% all-at-once cutover, immediately exposing all customers to the new code, so it does not reduce customer impact. Rolling back only after an alarm fires happens after full exposure, and the CodeBuild sample-payload testing plus hand-built alias-flip/rollback do not provide the native, time-incremented canary shifting the requirement calls for.","why_zh":"將 production alias 直接指向新版本是 100% 一次性全量切換，會立即將所有客戶暴露於新程式碼，無法降低客戶影響。僅在 alarm 觸發後才回滾是在全量暴露之後才動作，且 CodeBuild 的範例 payload 測試加上手動的 alias 切換/回滾並未提供需求所要求的原生、按時間漸進的 canary 轉移。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/automating-updates-to-serverless-apps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/sam-property-function-deploymentpreference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/tutorial-lambda-sam-template.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuring-alias-routing.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":15,"question_en":"To run an application, a DevOps engineer launches an Amazon EC2 instance with public IP addresses in a public subnet. A user data script obtains the application artifacts and installs them on the instances upon launch. A change to the security classification of the application now requires the instances to run with no access to the internet. While the instances launch successfully and show as healthy, the application does not seem to be installed. Which of the following should successfully install the application while complying with the new rule?","question_zh":"要运行应用程序，DevOps 工程师会在公共子网中启动具有公共 IP 地址的 Amazon EC2 实例。用户数据脚本 在实例启动时获取应用程序构件并将其安装在实例上。现在，由于应用程序的安全分类发生变化，要求这些 实例在运行时不能访问互联网。虽然实例成功启动并显示为正常运行，但应用程序似乎并未安装。 以下哪一项在符合新规则的情况下应能成功安装该应用程序？","options_en":{"A":"Launch the instances in a public subnet with Elastic IP addresses attached. Once the application is installed and running, run a script to disassociate the Elastic IP addresses afterwards.","B":"Set up a NAT gateway. Deploy the EC2 instances to a private subnet. Update the private subnet's route table to use the NAT gateway as the default route.","C":"Publish the application artifacts to an Amazon S3 bucket and create a VPC endpoint for S3. Assign an IAM instance profile to the EC2 instances so they can read the application artifacts from the S3 bucket.","D":"Create a security group for the application instances and allow only outbound traffic to the artifact repository. Remove the security group rule once the install is complete."},"options_zh":{"A":"在带有弹性 IP 地址的公共子网中启动实例。应用程序安装并运行后，运行一个脚本将弹性 IP 地址解 除关联。","B":"设置一个 NAT 网关。将 EC2 实例部署到私有子网。更新私有子网的路由表，将 NAT 网关设置为默 认路由。","C":"将应用程序构件发布到 Amazon S3 存储桶，并为 S3 创建一个 VPC 端点。为 EC2 实例分配一个 IAM 实 例配置文件，以便它们可以从 S3 存储桶读取应用程序构件。","D":"为应用程序实例创建一个安全组，并仅允许向工件存储库发送出站流量。安装完成后删除该安全组 规则。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The new security classification requires the instances to have NO access to the internet, yet the user data script must still be able to fetch and install the application artifacts. A gateway VPC endpoint for Amazon S3 satisfies both constraints. The AWS documentation states explicitly that with a gateway endpoint 'you can access Amazon S3 from your VPC, without requiring an internet gateway or NAT device for your VPC' - the traffic stays on the AWS network and never touches the internet. By publishing the artifacts to an S3 bucket, creating an S3 gateway endpoint (and adding it as a route table target), and attaching an IAM instance profile that grants s3:GetObject, the instances can privately download and install the artifacts with zero internet exposure. This is the only option that both installs the application and fully complies with the no-internet rule.","explanation_zh":"新的安全分類要求這些 instance 完全沒有 internet 存取權，但 user data script 仍必須能取得並安裝應用程式 artifacts。Amazon S3 的 gateway VPC endpoint 同時滿足這兩個條件。AWS 文件明確指出，使用 gateway endpoint 時「可在不需要 internet gateway 或 NAT device 的情況下從 VPC 存取 Amazon S3」，流量保留在 AWS 網路內，完全不會經過 internet。將 artifacts 發布到 S3 bucket、建立 S3 gateway endpoint（並將其加入 route table 作為目標），再為 instance 附加授予 s3:GetObject 的 IAM instance profile，instance 即可在零 internet 暴露的情況下私密地下載並安裝 artifacts。這是唯一既能安裝應用程式又完全符合無 internet 規則的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Elastic IP addresses in a public subnet require an internet gateway and give the instances direct internet access during installation, which violates the no-internet requirement. Disassociating the EIPs afterward does not undo the internet access already used, and it is operationally fragile - relying on a timing race to detach the EIPs.","why_zh":"public subnet 中的 Elastic IP 需要 internet gateway，並在安裝期間讓 instance 擁有直接的 internet 存取，違反無 internet 要求。事後解除 EIP 關聯並無法改變已使用 internet 存取的事實，且此做法很脆弱，依賴時序競態來卸除 EIP。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A public NAT gateway is explicitly designed to enable instances in a private subnet to send outbound traffic to the internet. The AWS docs describe its primary use case as 'Access the internet from a private subnet,' so adding it as the default route grants internet access and directly violates the 'no access to the internet' requirement.","why_zh":"public NAT gateway 的設計目的正是讓 private subnet 中的 instance 將出站流量傳送至 internet。AWS 文件將其主要用途描述為「從 private subnet 存取 internet」，因此將其設為預設路由會授予 internet 存取權，直接違反「無 internet 存取」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A security group only filters traffic; it does not provide a network path to a repository that lives on the internet. Reaching an internet-hosted artifact repository still requires an internet gateway or NAT (and thus internet access, violating the rule), and without that route the instances cannot connect at all. This neither complies with the rule nor reliably installs the application.","why_zh":"security group 只能過濾流量，並不會為位於 internet 上的 repository 提供網路路徑。要存取 internet 上的 artifact repository 仍需要 internet gateway 或 NAT（因此屬於 internet 存取，違反規則），而在沒有該路由的情況下 instance 根本無法連線。這既不符合規則，也無法可靠地安裝應用程式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/vpc-endpoints-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/gateway-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nat-gateway-scenarios.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-nat-gateway.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":16,"question_en":"A development team is using AWS CodeCommit to version control application code and AWS CodePipeline to orchestrate software deployments. The team has decided to use a remote main branch as the trigger for the pipeline to integrate code changes. A developer has pushed code changes to the CodeCommit repository, but noticed that the pipeline had no reaction, even after 10 minutes. Which of the following actions should be taken to troubleshoot this issue?","question_zh":"一个开发团队正在使用 AWS CodeCommit 来对应用程序代码进行版本控制，并使用 AWS CodePipeline 来编 排软件部署。该团队决定使用远程主分支作为触发管道以集成代码更改的触发器。一名开发人员已将代码更 改推送到 CodeCommit 存储库，但注意到即使过了 10 分钟，管道也没有任何反应。 为解决此问题，应采取以下哪项措施？","options_en":{"A":"Check that an Amazon EventBridge rule has been created for the main branch to trigger the pipeline.","B":"Check that the CodePipeline service role has permission to access the CodeCommit repository.","C":"Check that the developer’s IAM role has permission to push to the CodeCommit repository.","D":"Check to see if the pipeline failed to start because of CodeCommit errors in Amazon CloudWatch Logs."},"options_zh":{"A":"检查是否为主分支创建了 Amazon EventBridge 规则以触发管道。","B":"检查 CodePipeline 服务角色是否具有访问 CodeCommit 代码库的权限。","C":"检查开发人员的 IAM 角色是否有权向 CodeCommit 存储库推送内容。","D":"检查一下是否 管道启动失败，原因是 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中出现了 CodeCommit 错误。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"For a CodeCommit source action, CodePipeline uses an Amazon EventBridge rule as the default and recommended change-detection mechanism (created by the console wizard). When code is pushed to the monitored branch, that rule fires and starts the pipeline. The AWS troubleshooting topic 'Pipelines with an Amazon S3, Amazon ECR, or CodeCommit source no longer start automatically' states that when the event rule is not created/updated, 'the pipeline no longer starts automatically' - precisely the 'no reaction' symptom here, and it specifically lists Repository name + Branch name as the CodeCommit trigger identifiers. So verifying that an EventBridge rule exists and is scoped to the main branch (Option A) is the correct first troubleshooting step. The decisive qualifier is the symptom: the pipeline never started at all, which points to the change-detection trigger rather than a permissions failure that would let the pipeline start and then surface a visible error.","explanation_zh":"對於 CodeCommit source action，CodePipeline 預設且建議使用 Amazon EventBridge rule 作為變更偵測機制（由 console 精靈建立）。當程式碼推送到受監控的分支時，該 rule 會觸發並啟動 pipeline。AWS 疑難排解主題『Pipelines with an Amazon S3, Amazon ECR, or CodeCommit source no longer start automatically』指出，當 event rule 未被建立或更新時，『the pipeline no longer starts automatically（pipeline 不再自動啟動）』，正是本題『毫無反應』的症狀，且該主題明確列出 Repository name + Branch name 為 CodeCommit 的觸發識別碼。因此檢查是否存在且指向 main 分支的 EventBridge rule（選項 A）是正確的第一個排錯步驟。決定性的判斷依據是症狀：pipeline 完全沒有啟動，這指向變更偵測觸發機制，而非會讓 pipeline 啟動後才顯示可見錯誤的權限問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A missing CodePipeline service-role permission for CodeCommit produces a different, documented symptom: the pipeline DOES start (the trigger fires) and the source action then FAILS with 'Could not access the CodeCommit repository... Make sure that the pipeline IAM role has sufficient permissions to access the repository.' The question states there was no reaction at all, so this is not the cause.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 服務角色缺少 CodeCommit 權限會產生另一種有文件記載的症狀：pipeline 仍會啟動（觸發成功），但 source action 隨後失敗並顯示『Could not access the CodeCommit repository... Make sure that the pipeline IAM role has sufficient permissions to access the repository.』題目說 pipeline 完全沒反應，故此非主因。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The scenario states the developer already successfully pushed code. If the developer's IAM role lacked push permission, the git push itself would have failed and the code would never have landed in the repository. This option is contradicted by the facts of the scenario.","why_zh":"題目已說明開發者成功推送了程式碼。若開發者的 IAM 角色缺少推送權限，git push 本身就會失敗，程式碼根本不會進入儲存庫。此選項與題目情境矛盾。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodePipeline does not emit a 'pipeline failed to start because of CodeCommit errors' diagnostic to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The change-detection path is EventBridge; a missing or misconfigured rule simply produces no event and therefore no pipeline execution at all - there is no CloudWatch Logs start-failure entry to find. This is a fabricated troubleshooting path.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 不會將『因 CodeCommit 錯誤導致 pipeline 無法啟動』這類診斷寫入 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。變更偵測路徑是 EventBridge；rule 遺失或設定錯誤只會導致沒有事件、因而完全沒有 pipeline 執行，根本不會有 CloudWatch Logs 的啟動失敗記錄可查。此為虛構的排錯路徑。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/change-detection-methods.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/triggering.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":17,"question_en":"A company's developers use Amazon EC2 instances as remote workstations. The company is concerned that users can create or modify EC2 security groups to allow unrestricted inbound access. A DevOps engineer needs to develop a solution to detect when users create unrestricted security group rules. The solution must detect changes to security group rules in near real time, remove unrestricted rules, and send email notifications to the security team. The DevOps engineer has created an AWS Lambda function that checks for security group ID from input, removes rules that grant unrestricted access, and sends notifications through Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). What should the DevOps engineer do next to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"该公司开发人员使用亚马逊 EC2 实例作为远程工作站。公司担心用户能够创建或修改 EC2 安全组，从而允 许不受限制的入站访问。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要开发一种解决方案，用于检测用户创建无限制的安全组规则的情况。该解决方案必 须能够近乎实时地检测安全组规则的变更，移除无限制的规则，并向安全团队发送电子邮件通知。该 DevOps 工程师已创建了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会从输入中获取安全组 ID，移除授予无限制访问权 限的规则，并通过亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）发送通知。 为了满足要求，开发运维工程师接下来应该做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Lambda function to be invoked by the SNS topic. Create an AWS CloudTrail subscription for the SNS topic. Configure a subscription filter for security group modification events.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to invoke the Lambda function. Define a schedule pattern that runs the Lambda function every hour.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge event rule that has the default event bus as the source. Define the rule’s event pattern to match EC2 security group creation and modification events. Configure the rule to invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge custom event bus that subscribes to events from all AWS services. Configure the Lambda function to be invoked by the custom event bus."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Lambda 函数配置为由 SNS 主题调用。为 SNS 主题创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 订阅。为安全组修改事件 配置订阅筛选器。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则以调用 Lambda 函数。定义一个每小时运行一次 Lambda 函 数的计划模式。","C":"创建一个以默认事件总线作为源的 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则。定义规则的事件模式以匹配 EC2 安全 组的创建和修改事件。配置规则以调用 Lambda 函数。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 自定义事件总线，使其订阅来自所有 AWS 服务的事件。配置 Lambda 函数，使其由自定义事件总线触发。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"EC2 security group changes are made through public AWS API calls such as AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress, AuthorizeSecurityGroupEgress, and RevokeSecurityGroupIngress. AWS CloudTrail records these calls and delivers them to the default EventBridge event bus as events with detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' (the EventBridge docs use an EC2 API call as the canonical example, and state these events are delivered to the default event bus only). Creating an EventBridge rule on the default event bus whose event pattern matches EC2 security group creation/modification events invokes the existing Lambda function as a native target the instant a change occurs, satisfying the near-real-time requirement and passing the event detail (including the security group ID) so the Lambda can revoke the unrestricted rules and publish to SNS. This is the standard event-driven remediation pattern for security group changes.","explanation_zh":"EC2 security group 的變更是透過公開的 AWS API 呼叫完成，例如 AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress、AuthorizeSecurityGroupEgress 與 RevokeSecurityGroupIngress。AWS CloudTrail 會記錄這些呼叫，並以 detail-type 為「AWS API Call via CloudTrail」的事件傳送到 default EventBridge event bus（EventBridge 文件以 EC2 API 呼叫作為標準範例，並明確指出這類事件只會送到 default event bus）。在 default event bus 上建立一條 EventBridge rule，並設定 event pattern 比對 EC2 security group 的建立/修改事件，即可在變更發生的當下將既有 Lambda function 作為原生 target 觸發，滿足近即時需求，並把事件細節（含 security group ID）傳入 Lambda，讓它移除不受限制的規則並發佈到 SNS。這正是針對 security group 變更的標準事件驅動修復模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This is backwards and not a real feature. There is no 'CloudTrail subscription for an SNS topic' with a 'subscription filter for security group modification events.' CloudTrail can publish an SNS notification when it delivers a new log file, but it cannot filter per event type, and having SNS invoke the Lambda provides no security group ID as input. This flow does not detect changes correctly in near real time.","why_zh":"此選項方向相反且非真實功能。並不存在「為 SNS topic 建立 CloudTrail subscription」搭配「security group 修改事件的 subscription filter」。CloudTrail 只能在遞送新 log 檔時發 SNS 通知，無法依事件類型過濾，且由 SNS 觸發 Lambda 也無法提供 security group ID。此流程無法正確近即時偵測變更。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A scheduled EventBridge rule that runs the Lambda every hour is periodic polling, not near-real-time detection, so it directly violates the explicit near-real-time requirement. A scheduled invocation also does not carry the specific security group ID from a change event that the Lambda needs as input.","why_zh":"每小時執行一次 Lambda 的排程 EventBridge rule 屬於週期性輪詢，並非近即時偵測，直接違反明確的近即時需求。排程觸發也不會帶入 Lambda 所需的特定 security group ID（來自變更事件）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom event buses do not natively subscribe to events from all AWS services. CloudTrail-delivered events ('AWS API Call via CloudTrail') and AWS service events are delivered to the default event bus only; to process them on a custom bus you must create a rule on the default bus that forwards them. As described, this setup would not receive the EC2 security group change events.","why_zh":"Custom event bus 無法原生「訂閱所有 AWS 服務的事件」。CloudTrail 傳遞的事件（「AWS API Call via CloudTrail」）與 AWS 服務事件只會送到 default event bus；要在 custom bus 上處理，必須在 default bus 建立 rule 來轉發。如題所述，此設定收不到 EC2 security group 變更事件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-create-pattern.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":18,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is creating an AWS CloudFormation template to deploy a web service. The web service will run on Amazon EC2 instances in a private subnet behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The DevOps engineer must ensure that the service can accept requests from clients that have IPv6 addresses. What should the DevOps engineer do with the CloudFormation template so that IPv6 clients can access the web service?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板以部署一个网络服务。该网络服务将在位于应 用负载均衡器（ALB）后面的私有子网中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。DevOps 工程师必须确保该服务能够 接受来自具有 IPv6 地址的客户端的请求。 DevOps 工程师应该如何处理 CloudFormation 模板，以便 IPv6 客户端能够访问该网络服务？","options_en":{"A":"Add an IPv6 CIDR block to the VPC and the private subnet for the EC2 instances. Create route table entries for the IPv6 network, use EC2 instance types that support IPv6, and assign IPv6 addresses to each EC2 instance.","B":"Assign each EC2 instance an IPv6 Elastic IP address. Create a target group, and add the EC2 instances as targets. Create a listener on port 443 of the ALB, and associate the target group with the ALB.","C":"Replace the ALB with a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Add an IPv6 CIDR block to the VPC and subnets for the NLB, and assign the NLB an IPv6 Elastic IP address.","D":"Add an IPv6 CIDR block to the VPC and subnets for the ALB. Create a listener on port 443, and specify the dualstack IP address type on the ALB. Create a target group, and add the EC2 instances as targets. Associate the target group with the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"向 VPC 和用于 EC2 实例的私有子网添加 IPv6 CIDR 块。为 IPv6 网络创建路由表条目，使用支持 IPv6 的 EC2 实例类型，并为这些实例分配 IPv6 地址。 每个 EC2 实例。","B":"为每个 EC2 实例分配一个 IPv6 弹性 IP 地址。创建一个目标组，并将 EC2 实例添加为目标。在 ALB 的 443 端口上创建一个监听器，并将目标组与 ALB 关联。","C":"用网络负载均衡器（NLB）替换 ALB。为 VPC 和 NLB 的子网添加一个 IPv6 CIDR 块，并为 NLB 分配一个 IPv6 弹性 IP 地址。","D":"向 VPC 和 ALB 的子网添加 IPv6 CIDR 块。在端口 443 上创建一个监听器，并在 ALB 上指定双栈 IP 地址 类型。创建一个目标组，并将 EC2 实例添加为目标。将目标组与 ALB 关联。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"To let IPv6 clients reach a web service behind an Application Load Balancer, you make the ALB dualstack. Per AWS docs, you can configure an ALB so clients communicate using IPv4 only or using both IPv4 and IPv6 (dualstack); the dualstack endpoint resolves to both A and AAAA DNS records, so IPv6 clients connect over IPv6 while IPv4 clients still use IPv4. The dualstack type requires the VPC and the load balancer's subnets to have associated IPv6 CIDR blocks (and the subnet route tables, security groups, and network ACLs must allow IPv6 traffic). Critically, the load balancer communicates with its targets based on the target group's IP address type, so the EC2 instances can remain IPv4-only in the private subnet; you just register them in a target group and associate it with the port 443 listener. Option D captures exactly this design: add an IPv6 CIDR to the VPC and ALB subnets, create the port 443 listener, set the ALB IP address type to dualstack, create a target group with the EC2 instances, and associate it with the ALB.","explanation_zh":"要讓 IPv6 用戶端透過 Application Load Balancer 存取 web 服務，需將 ALB 設為 dualstack。根據 AWS 文件，可將 ALB 設定為僅以 IPv4 與用戶端通訊，或同時以 IPv4 與 IPv6（dualstack）通訊；dualstack 端點會解析為 A 與 AAAA DNS 記錄，使 IPv6 用戶端能以 IPv6 連線，IPv4 用戶端仍使用 IPv4。dualstack 類型要求 VPC 與 ALB 所在的 subnet 都關聯 IPv6 CIDR block（且 subnet 的 route table、security group 與 network ACL 須允許 IPv6 流量）。關鍵在於：ALB 與其 target 的通訊是依 target group 的 IP address type，因此私有子網內的 EC2 instance 可維持僅 IPv4；只需把它們註冊到 target group 並關聯到 443 埠的 listener 即可。選項 D 正是此設計：為 VPC 與 ALB 的 subnet 加上 IPv6 CIDR、建立 443 listener、將 ALB 的 IP address type 設為 dualstack、建立含 EC2 的 target group 並關聯到 ALB。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Assigning IPv6 to the EC2 instances and adding IPv6 routing to the private subnet does not make external IPv6 clients able to reach the service, because clients connect to the ALB (via its DNS name), not to the instances directly. The ALB itself must be dualstack to accept IPv6 from clients; making the private backend IPv6 is unnecessary and never creates an IPv6 client-facing entry point.","why_zh":"為 EC2 instance 指派 IPv6 並為私有子網加入 IPv6 路由，無法讓外部 IPv6 用戶端存取服務，因為用戶端是連到 ALB（透過其 DNS 名稱），而非直接連到 instance。必須讓 ALB 本身為 dualstack 才能接受用戶端的 IPv6；讓私有後端使用 IPv6 並非必要，也從未建立面向用戶端的 IPv6 入口。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"There is no such thing as an 'IPv6 Elastic IP address'; Elastic IP addresses are IPv4-only. ALBs also do not use Elastic IPs (they use service-managed addresses), and this option never enables dualstack/IPv6 on the ALB, so IPv6 clients still cannot connect. It is technically invalid.","why_zh":"並不存在「IPv6 Elastic IP」；Elastic IP 僅支援 IPv4。ALB 也不使用 Elastic IP（它使用服務代管位址），且此選項從未在 ALB 上啟用 dualstack/IPv6，因此 IPv6 用戶端仍無法連線。在技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Replacing the ALB with an NLB is an unnecessary architectural change, and NLBs do not use 'IPv6 Elastic IP addresses' (Elastic IPs are IPv4-only). The requirement is simply to accept IPv6 client requests, which the existing ALB can do natively via the dualstack IP address type without swapping load balancer types.","why_zh":"把 ALB 換成 NLB 是不必要的架構變更，且 NLB 不使用「IPv6 Elastic IP」（Elastic IP 僅 IPv4）。需求只是接受 IPv6 用戶端請求，現有的 ALB 透過 dualstack IP address type 即可原生達成，無需更換負載平衡器類型。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-ip-address-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/application-load-balancers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/userguide/how-elastic-load-balancing-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-elasticloadbalancingv2-loadbalancer.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":19,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations and AWS Control Tower to manage all the company's AWS accounts. The company uses the Enterprise Support plan. A DevOps engineer is using Account Factory for Terraform (AFT) to provision new accounts. When new accounts are provisioned, the DevOps engineer notices that the support plan for the new accounts is set to the Basic Support plan. The DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to provision the new accounts with the Enterprise Support plan. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS 组织和 AWS 控制塔来管理公司所有的 AWS 账户。该公司采用企业支持计划。 一位 DevOps 工程师正在使用 Terraform 账户工厂（AFT）来创建新账户。在创建新账户时，该 DevOps 工程 师注意到新账户的支持计划被设置为基本支持计划。该 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，以便为新账 户配置企业支持计划。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an AWS Config conformance pack to deploy the account-part-of-organizations AWS Config rule and to automatically remediate any noncompliant accounts.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function to create a ticket for AWS Support to add the account to the Enterprise Support plan. Grant the Lambda function the support:ResolveCase permission.","C":"Add an additional value to the control_tower_parameters input to set the AWSEnterpriseSupport parameter as the organization's management account number.","D":"Set the aft_feature_enterprise_support feature flag to True in the AFT deployment input configuration. Redeploy AFT and apply the changes."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Config 合规性包部署“账户属于组织”AWS Config 规则，并自动修复任何不符合要求的账 户。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为 AWS 支持服务创建工单，将账户添加到企业支持计划中。 授予该 Lambda 函数 support:ResolveCase 权限。","C":"在 control_tower_parameters 输入中添加一个额外的值，将 AWSEnterpriseSupport 参数设置为组织 的管理账户编号。","D":"在 AFT 部署输入配置中将 aft_feature_enterprise_support 特性标志设置为 True。重新部署 AFT 并应用更 改。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Control Tower Account Factory for Terraform (AFT) ships with optional feature flags that you set in the AFT deployment input configuration (the terraform-aws-control_tower_account_factory module). The official 'Enable feature options' page documents an 'AWS Enterprise Support plan' feature: 'When this option is enabled, the AFT pipeline turns on the AWS Enterprise Support plan for accounts provisioned by AFT... AFT provides automated enrollment into the enterprise support level... The provisioning process opens a support ticket for the account, requesting it to be added to the AWS Enterprise Support plan. To enable the Enterprise Support option, set the following feature flag to True in your AFT deployment input configuration: aft_feature_enterprise_support.' This is exactly the native, supported mechanism for the described scenario (new AFT accounts defaulting to Basic Support). The documented prerequisite ('you must enroll the payer account into the Enterprise Support plan') is satisfied because the company already uses the Enterprise Support plan. After changing the flag you redeploy AFT to apply the change, matching option D verbatim.","explanation_zh":"AWS Control Tower Account Factory for Terraform (AFT) 在 AFT deployment input configuration（即 terraform-aws-control_tower_account_factory 模組）中提供可選的 feature flags。官方「Enable feature options」頁面記載了「AWS Enterprise Support plan」這個功能：啟用後，AFT pipeline 會為 AFT 所佈建的帳戶開啟 AWS Enterprise Support plan，AFT 會自動將帳戶登記到 enterprise support 等級，佈建流程會開立一張 support ticket 要求把該帳戶加入 AWS Enterprise Support plan。要啟用此選項，需在 AFT deployment input configuration 中將 feature flag aft_feature_enterprise_support 設為 True。這正是題目情境（AFT 新帳戶預設為 Basic Support）的原生支援解法。文件中要求的先決條件（payer account 必須已加入 Enterprise Support plan）已被滿足，因為該公司本身就使用 Enterprise Support plan。修改 flag 後重新部署 AFT 以套用變更，完全符合選項 D。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no 'account-part-of-organizations' AWS Config rule that manages support plans, and AWS Config conformance packs evaluate/remediate resource configuration, not AWS Support plan enrollment. Support plan level is a billing/account-level setting not represented as a Config-evaluable resource, so this cannot set Enterprise Support.","why_zh":"不存在能管理支援方案的 'account-part-of-organizations' AWS Config 規則，且 AWS Config conformance pack 是評估/修復資源組態，而非 AWS Support 方案的登記。支援方案等級屬於帳單/帳戶層級設定，無法用 Config 規則評估或修復，因此無法設定 Enterprise Support。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building a custom Lambda to open support cases reinvents functionality AFT already provides natively, adding unnecessary operational overhead. Worse, support:ResolveCase only closes/resolves a case; it does not create a case or change the support plan. The correct API would be support:CreateCase, so the permission is wrong and the approach is not the AWS-recommended solution.","why_zh":"自建 Lambda 開立支援案件等於重造 AFT 已內建的功能，增加不必要的運維負擔。更糟的是 support:ResolveCase 只能關閉/解決案件，無法建立案件或變更支援方案；正確 API 應為 support:CreateCase，因此權限錯誤，且非 AWS 建議的做法。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"control_tower_parameters drives Control Tower setup inputs, and there is no 'AWSEnterpriseSupport' parameter; setting a management account number as a support parameter is fabricated. Enterprise Support enrollment for AFT accounts is controlled by the aft_feature_enterprise_support feature flag, not by control_tower_parameters.","why_zh":"control_tower_parameters 提供 Control Tower 設定輸入，且不存在 'AWSEnterpriseSupport' 這個參數；把管理帳戶號碼當成支援參數是虛構的。AFT 帳戶的 Enterprise Support 登記由 aft_feature_enterprise_support feature flag 控制，而非 control_tower_parameters。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/aft-feature-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/aft-overview.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":20,"question_en":"A company's DevOps engineer uses AWS Systems Manager to perform maintenance tasks during maintenance windows. The company has a few Amazon EC2 instances that require a restart after notifications from AWS Health. The DevOps engineer needs to implement an automated solution to remediate these notifications. The DevOps engineer creates an Amazon EventBridge rule. How should the DevOps engineer configure the EventBridge rule to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS 系统管理器在维护窗口期间执行维护任务。该公司有几台 Amazon EC2 实例，在收到 AWS 健康通知后需要重启。DevOps 工程师需要实施一个自动化解决方 案来解决这些通知。DevOps 工程师创建了一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。 DevOps 工程师应如何配置 EventBridge 规则以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an event source of AWS Health, a service of EC2, and an event type that indicates instance maintenance. Target a Systems Manager document to restart the EC2 instance.","B":"Configure an event source of Systems Manager and an event type that indicates a maintenance window. Target a Systems Manager document to restart the EC2 instance.","C":"Configure an event source of AWS Health, a service of EC2, and an event type that indicates instance maintenance. Target a newly created AWS Lambda function that registers an automation task to restart the EC2 instance during a maintenance window.","D":"Configure an event source of EC2 and an event type that indicates instance maintenance. Target a newly created AWS Lambda function that registers an automation task to restart the EC2 instance during a maintenance window."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Health（EC2 的一项服务）作为事件源，并指定表示实例维护的事件类型。将目标设置为 Systems Manager 文档以重启 EC2 实例。","B":"配置一个 Systems Manager 事件源以及表示维护窗口的事件类型。将 Systems Manager 文档作为目 标以重启 EC2 实例。","C":"配置 AWS Health（EC2 的一项服务）作为事件源，并指定表示实例维护的事件类型。将目标设置为新创 建的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数在维护窗口期间注册自动化任务以重启 EC2 实例。","D":"配置一个 EC2 事件源和一种表示实例维护的事件类型。将目标指向新创建的 AWS Lambda 函数，该 函数在维护窗口期间注册一个自动化任务以重启 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The remediation must be triggered by an AWS Health notification, so the EventBridge event source must be AWS Health (source: aws.health). AWS's own documented runbook 'Running operations on EC2 instances automatically in response to events in AWS Health' specifies exactly this configuration: in the EventBridge rule choose Service name = Health, Specific service = EC2, and an event-type category of scheduledChange (the instance retirement/maintenance event code). The rule's target is set directly to an SSM Automation document (AWS-RestartEC2Instance) using an existing role; no intermediate Lambda function is required. Option A captures this pattern precisely (AWS Health source, EC2 service, instance-maintenance event type, SSM document target) and has the lowest operational overhead. A documented prerequisite is that the instances must be managed by Systems Manager.","explanation_zh":"此自動修復必須由 AWS Health 通知觸發，因此 EventBridge 的事件來源必須是 AWS Health（source: aws.health）。AWS 官方文件「Running operations on EC2 instances automatically in response to events in AWS Health」明確說明了正確設定：在 EventBridge 規則中選擇 Service name = Health、Specific service = EC2，並使用 scheduledChange 事件類型類別（即 instance retirement/maintenance 的事件代碼）。規則的 target 直接設定為 SSM Automation document（AWS-RestartEC2Instance）並使用 existing role，不需要任何中介的 Lambda function。選項 A 精準符合此模式（AWS Health 來源、EC2 service、instance-maintenance 事件類型、SSM document target），且營運負擔最低。文件中的前提是這些 EC2 instance 必須由 Systems Manager 管理。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Wrong event source. The trigger is an AWS Health notification, not a Systems Manager maintenance-window event. An event source of Systems Manager with a maintenance-window event type does not capture AWS Health scheduledChange notifications, so the rule would never fire on the Health event.","why_zh":"事件來源錯誤。觸發來源是 AWS Health 通知，而非 Systems Manager 維護視窗事件。以 Systems Manager 並搭配 maintenance window 事件類型作為事件來源無法擷取 AWS Health 的 scheduledChange 通知，規則永遠不會因 Health 事件被觸發。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Correct event source but unnecessary architecture. AWS documents targeting the SSM Automation document (AWS-RestartEC2Instance) directly from the EventBridge rule. Inserting a Lambda function to register the automation adds development and operational overhead with no benefit, making A the better, lower-overhead answer.","why_zh":"事件來源正確但架構多餘。AWS 文件是讓 EventBridge 規則直接以 SSM Automation document（AWS-RestartEC2Instance）為 target。額外加入一個 Lambda function 去註冊 automation 會增加開發與營運負擔且無益處，因此 A 是更佳、負擔更低的答案。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Wrong event source. The notification originates from AWS Health (source: aws.health), not from a native EC2 service event. Using EC2 as the source would miss the AWS Health scheduledChange/maintenance notifications, and it also adds an unnecessary Lambda function.","why_zh":"事件來源錯誤。通知來自 AWS Health（source: aws.health），而非原生 EC2 服務事件。以 EC2 作為來源會漏接 AWS Health 的 scheduledChange/maintenance 通知，且同樣多了一個不必要的 Lambda function。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/automating-instance-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/cloudwatch-events-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/aws-health-events-eventbridge-schema.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":21,"question_en":"A company has containerized all of its in-house quality control applications. The company is running Jenkins on Amazon EC2 instances, which require patching and upgrading. The compliance officer has requested a DevOps engineer begin encrypting build artifacts since they contain company intellectual property. What should the DevOps engineer do to accomplish this in the MOST maintainable manner?","question_zh":"一家公司已将其所有内部质量控制应用程序进行了容器化处理。该公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行 Jenkins，这些实例需要打补丁和升级。合规官要求一名 DevOps 工程师开始对构建工件进行加密， 因为这些工件包含公司的知识产权。 为了以最易于维护的方式实现这一目标，开发运维工程师应该怎么做？","options_en":{"A":"Automate patching and upgrading using AWS Systems Manager on EC2 instances and encrypt Amazon EBS volumes by default.","B":"Deploy Jenkins to an Amazon ECS cluster and copy build artifacts to an Amazon S3 bucket with default encryption enabled.","C":"Leverage AWS CodePipeline with a build action and encrypt the artifacts using AWS Secrets Manager.","D":"Use AWS CodeBuild with artifact encryption to replace the Jenkins instance running on EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 对 EC2 实例进行自动补丁安装和升级，并默认加密 Amazon EBS 卷。","B":"将 Jenkins 部署到 Amazon ECS 集群，并将构建工件复制到启用默认加密的 Amazon S3 存储桶 中。","C":"利用 AWS CodePipeline 中的构建操作，并使用 AWS Secrets Manager 对构建工件进行加密。","D":"使用带有工件加密功能的 AWS CodeBuild 来替代在 EC2 实例上运行的 Jenkins 实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario has two pain points to solve at once with the MOST maintainable approach: a self-managed Jenkins fleet on EC2 that 'requires patching and upgrading,' and a compliance requirement to encrypt build artifacts. AWS CodeBuild is a fully managed build service that, per the AWS docs, 'eliminates the need to set up, patch, update, and manage your own build servers' and scales automatically, so replacing Jenkins/EC2 with CodeBuild removes the patching/upgrading burden entirely. CodeBuild also natively encrypts its build output artifacts: by default it uses the AWS managed KMS key for Amazon S3, and you can optionally supply a customer managed key, satisfying the compliance officer with no bolt-on components. Because the applications are already containerized and CodeBuild runs containerized build environments, the migration is a clean fit. Option D is therefore the only choice that addresses BOTH pain points while minimizing ongoing operational maintenance.","explanation_zh":"本題要以「最易維護 (MOST maintainable)」的方式同時解決兩個痛點：EC2 上自管的 Jenkins 機群「需要修補與升級」，以及合規上必須加密建置產物的需求。AWS CodeBuild 是全託管的建置服務，依 AWS 文件可「免除設定、修補、更新與管理自有建置伺服器的需求」並自動擴展，因此以 CodeBuild 取代 Jenkins/EC2 即可完全消除修補與升級負擔。CodeBuild 也原生加密其建置輸出產物：預設使用 Amazon S3 的 AWS 受管 KMS key，亦可選用客戶受管 key，無須額外元件即可滿足合規官需求。由於應用程式已容器化、CodeBuild 本身即以容器化建置環境執行，遷移相當契合。因此 D 是唯一能同時解決兩個痛點、且將持續營運維護降到最低的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Automating patching with Systems Manager and enabling EBS default encryption keeps the self-managed Jenkins-on-EC2 fleet alive, so you still own the server lifecycle, OS/Jenkins upgrades, and scaling. EBS default encryption only protects the underlying volume, not the build artifacts as a deliverable, and it does not eliminate the build-server maintenance burden the question wants removed.","why_zh":"用 Systems Manager 自動修補並啟用 EBS 預設加密，仍保留自管的 Jenkins/EC2 機群，因此你依舊要負責伺服器生命週期、OS/Jenkins 升級與擴展。EBS 預設加密只保護底層磁碟區，並非針對建置產物本身，也無法消除題目想去除的建置伺服器維運負擔。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Moving Jenkins to an ECS cluster still means you maintain Jenkins itself (plugins, configuration, controller/agent images and upgrades) and, on the EC2 launch type, the container instances too. S3 default encryption would protect the artifacts, but you still carry Jenkins maintenance, so this has more moving parts and is less maintainable than fully replacing Jenkins with a managed build service.","why_zh":"把 Jenkins 搬到 ECS 叢集仍需自行維護 Jenkins 本身（外掛、設定、controller/agent 映像與升級），若採 EC2 啟動類型還要管理容器執行個體。S3 預設加密雖能保護產物，但你仍背負 Jenkins 維護，元件更多、維護性不如以全託管建置服務完全取代 Jenkins。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Secrets Manager stores and rotates secrets such as credentials, API keys, and OAuth tokens; it is not a service for encrypting build artifacts, so 'encrypt the artifacts using Secrets Manager' is a technical misuse. CodePipeline is only an orchestrator and still needs an underlying build provider, so this option also fails to remove the Jenkins patching/upgrading problem.","why_zh":"AWS Secrets Manager 用於儲存與輪替憑證、API 金鑰、OAuth token 等機密，並非用來加密建置產物的服務，因此「用 Secrets Manager 加密產物」屬技術誤用。CodePipeline 僅為編排服務，仍需底層的建置供應者，故此選項也無法去除 Jenkins 的修補/升級問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/setting-up-kms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":22,"question_en":"An IT team has built an AWS CloudFormation template so others in the company can quickly and reliably deploy and terminate an application. The template creates an Amazon EC2 instance with a user data script to install the application and an Amazon S3 bucket that the application uses to serve static webpages while it is running. All resources should be removed when the CloudFormation stack is deleted. However, the team observes that CloudFormation reports an error during stack deletion, and the S3 bucket created by the stack is not deleted. How can the team resolve the error in the MOST efficient manner to ensure that all resources are deleted without errors?","question_zh":"一个 IT 团队构建了一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，以便公司内的其他人能够快速且可靠地部署和终 止应用程序。该模板创建了一个带有用户数据脚本的 Amazon EC2 实例，用于安装应用程序，还创建了 一个 Amazon S3 存储桶，应用程序在运行时用于提供静态网页。 在删除 CloudFormation 堆栈时，所有资源都应被移除。然而，团队发现 CloudFormation 在删除堆栈期 间报告错误，并且由该堆栈创建的 S3 存储桶未被删除。 团队如何以最高效的方式解决错误，以确保所有资源都能无误地被删除？","options_en":{"A":"Add a DelelionPolicy attribute to the S3 bucket resource, with the value Delete forcing the bucket to be removed when the stack is deleted.","B":"Add a custom resource with an AWS Lambda function with the DependsOn attribute specifying the S3 bucket, and an IAM role. Write the Lambda function to delete all objects from the bucket when RequestType is Delete.","C":"Identify the resource that was not deleted. Manually empty the S3 bucket and then delete it.","D":"Replace the EC2 and S3 bucket resources with a single AWS OpsWorks Stacks resource. Define a custom recipe for the stack to create and delete the EC2 instance and the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"向 S3 存储桶资源添加一个 DeletionPolicy 属性，其值为 Delete，这样在删除堆栈时会强制删除该存 储桶。","B":"添加一个自定义资源，该资源包含一个 AWS Lambda 函数，使用 DependsOn 属性指定 S3 存储桶和 一个 IAM 角色。编写 Lambda 函数，当 RequestType 为 Delete 时，从存储桶中删除所有对象。","C":"确定未被删除的资源。手动清空 S3 存储桶，然后将其删除。","D":"用单个 AWS OpsWorks Stacks 资源替换 EC2 和 S3 存储桶资源。为堆栈定义一个自定义配方，以 创建和删除 EC2 实例和 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application serves static webpages out of the S3 bucket, so the bucket holds objects when the stack is deleted. CloudFormation cannot delete a non-empty S3 bucket: the DeletionPolicy reference explicitly states 'For Amazon S3 buckets, you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed,' which is exactly the deletion error the team sees. The most efficient, repeatable, fully template-based fix is a Lambda-backed custom resource (with an IAM execution role) that empties the bucket when RequestType is Delete. Custom resources support Create, Update, and Delete operations, and CloudFormation waits for the custom resource's response before continuing the stack operation. The DependsOn attribute documentation confirms the deletion ordering rule: when resource A depends on resource B, 'Resource A is deleted before resource B.' So putting DependsOn the S3 bucket on the custom resource forces the Lambda to run (RequestType=Delete) and empty the bucket BEFORE CloudFormation deletes the bucket itself. This keeps the entire deploy/terminate lifecycle inside the template so others can run it reliably without any manual steps.","explanation_zh":"應用程式從 S3 bucket 提供靜態網頁，因此刪除堆疊時 bucket 內含有物件。CloudFormation 無法刪除非空的 S3 bucket：DeletionPolicy 參考文件明確指出『對於 Amazon S3 buckets，必須先刪除 bucket 內所有物件才能成功刪除』，這正是團隊看到的刪除錯誤。最有效率、可重複且完全寫在範本內的解法，是使用由 Lambda 支援的 custom resource（搭配 IAM 執行角色），當 RequestType 為 Delete 時清空 bucket。Custom resource 支援 Create、Update、Delete 操作，且 CloudFormation 會等待 custom resource 回應後才繼續堆疊操作。DependsOn 屬性文件確認了刪除順序規則：當資源 A 相依於資源 B 時，『資源 A 會在資源 B 之前被刪除』。因此對 custom resource 加上 DependsOn 指向該 S3 bucket，會強制 Lambda 先執行（RequestType=Delete）並清空 bucket，CloudFormation 才會接著刪除該 bucket。如此整個部署/終止生命週期都在範本內，讓其他人能可靠地執行而無需任何手動步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DeletionPolicy: Delete is already the default behavior and does NOT empty a bucket. The DeletionPolicy reference explicitly states that for S3 buckets you must delete all objects for deletion to succeed, so a non-empty bucket still fails exactly as observed. The option's claim that Delete 'forces' removal of a non-empty bucket is technically false (and it even misspells the attribute as 'DelelionPolicy').","why_zh":"DeletionPolicy: Delete 本來就是預設行為，並不會清空 bucket。DeletionPolicy 參考文件明確指出 S3 bucket 必須刪除所有物件才能成功刪除，因此非空 bucket 仍會如所觀察到的失敗。此選項聲稱 Delete 會『強制』移除非空 bucket 在技術上是錯的（且還把屬性拼成 'DelelionPolicy'）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Manually emptying and deleting the bucket is a one-time fix and contradicts the stated goal that others must be able to quickly and reliably deploy AND terminate the stack without errors. It is not automated or repeatable, so it is not the most efficient solution.","why_zh":"手動清空並刪除 bucket 只是一次性修補，與『讓其他人能快速且可靠地部署與終止堆疊且無錯誤』的目標相違。它無法自動化或重複執行，因此不是最有效率的解法。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Replacing EC2 and S3 with a single OpsWorks Stacks resource is a massive over-engineered rewrite, not the 'most efficient' change, and OpsWorks Stacks is a legacy service slated for end of life. It also would not natively solve emptying a non-empty bucket any more simply than a custom resource.","why_zh":"把 EC2 與 S3 改成單一 OpsWorks Stacks 資源是大規模、過度設計的重寫，並非『最有效率』的變更，且 OpsWorks Stacks 已是即將終止服務的舊版服務。它也無法比 custom resource 更簡單地原生解決清空非空 bucket 的問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-attribute-deletionpolicy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-custom-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-attribute-dependson.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/troubleshooting.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":23,"question_en":"A company has an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that is configured with an Amazon S3 bucket in the eu- west-1 Region. The pipeline deploys an AWS Lambda application to the same Region. The pipeline consists of an AWS CodeBuild project build action and an AWS CloudFormation deploy action. The CodeBuild project uses the aws cloudformation package AWS CLI command to build an artifact that contains the Lambda function code’s .zip file and the CloudFormation template. The CloudFormation deploy action references the CloudFormation template from the output artifact of the CodeBuild project’s build action. The company wants to also deploy the Lambda application to the us-east-1 Region by using the pipeline in eu-west-1. A DevOps engineer has already updated the CodeBuild project to use the aws cloudformation package command to produce an additional output artifact for us-east-1. Which combination of additional steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道配置了位于 euwest-1 区域的 Amazon S3 存储桶。 该管道将一个 AWS Lambda 应用程序部署到同一区域。该管道由一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目构建操 作和一个 AWS CloudFormation 部署操作组成。 CodeBuild 项目使用 AWS CLI 命令 `aws cloudformation package` 来构建一个包含 Lambda 函数代码的 `.zip` 文件和 CloudFormation 模板的工件。CloudFormation 部署操作从 CodeBuild 项目构建操作的输出工件中引 用 CloudFormation 模板。 该公司还希望利用位于 eu-west-1 区域的管道将 Lambda 应用程序部署到 us-east-1 区域。一位 DevOps 工程师 已更新 CodeBuild 项目，使用 aws cloudformation package 命令为 us-east-1 区域生成额外的输出工件。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些额外步骤的组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Modify the CloudFormation template to include a parameter for the Lambda function code’s zip file location. Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to pass in the us-east-1 artifact location as a parameter override.","B":"Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to use the CloudFormation template from the us-east-1 output artifact.","C":"Create an S3 bucket in us-east-1. Configure the S3 bucket policy to allow CodePipeline to have read and write access.","D":"Create an S3 bucket in us-east-1. Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) from the S3 bucket in eu-west-1 to the S3 bucket in us-east-1.","E":"Modify the pipeline to include the S3 bucket for us-east-1 as an artifact store. Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to use the CloudFormation template from the us-east-1 output artifact."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 CloudFormation 模板，添加一个用于 Lambda 函数代码压缩文件位置的参数。在管道中为 us-east-1 创建一个新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。配置新的部署操作，将 us-east-1 的工件位置作为参数覆盖 传入。","B":"在管道中为 us-east-1 创建一个新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。将新的部署操作配置为使用来自 us- east-1 输出工件的 CloudFormation 模板。","C":"在 us-east-1 区域创建一个 S3 存储桶。配置 S3 存储桶策略，允许 CodePipeline 具有读写访问权限。","D":"在 us-east-1 区域创建一个 S3 存储桶。配置从 eu-west-1 区域的 S3 存储桶到 us-east-1 区域的 S3 存储桶的 S3 跨区域复制（CRR）。","E":"修改管道，将 us-east-1 的 S3 存储桶作为工件存储包含进来。在管道中为 us-east-1 创建一个新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。配置新的部署操作，使其使用来自 us-east-1 输出工件的 CloudFormation 模 板。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Adding a CloudFormation deploy action that executes in us-east-1 makes it a CodePipeline cross-Region action. AWS documentation states that for a cross-Region action you must have one artifact bucket in the pipeline Region (eu-west-1) and one artifact bucket in every Region where an action runs (us-east-1). When the pipeline is managed via the CLI, CloudFormation, or an SDK (as here), CodePipeline does NOT auto-provision that bucket; you must create it yourself and then register it in the pipeline's artifactStores map (the docs are explicit: 'If you create a cross-region action in your pipeline, you must use artifactStores' and 'there must be an artifact store for the pipeline Region and for each cross-region action'). Therefore you must (C) create the us-east-1 S3 bucket and grant CodePipeline read/write access to it, and (E) add the us-east-1 bucket to the pipeline as an artifact store while creating the new CloudFormation deploy action that consumes the us-east-1 output artifact (whose template the engineer already produced with 'aws cloudformation package', so the Lambda .zip location is already baked in and references a us-east-1 location). CodePipeline automatically copies the input artifacts from eu-west-1 into the us-east-1 bucket, so no manual replication is needed. C supplies the physical per-Region bucket; E wires it into the pipeline and adds the deploy action, making them the complete, minimal pair.","explanation_zh":"新增一個在 us-east-1 執行的 CloudFormation deploy action,等於建立了 CodePipeline 的 cross-Region action。AWS 官方文件指出:cross-Region action 需要在 pipeline 所在 Region(eu-west-1)有一個 artifact bucket,並且在每一個會執行 action 的 Region(us-east-1)也各有一個 artifact bucket。當使用 CLI、CloudFormation 或 SDK 管理 pipeline(如本題情境)時,CodePipeline 不會自動建立該 bucket,你必須自行建立並把它登錄到 pipeline 的 artifactStores map(文件明確寫道:'If you create a cross-region action in your pipeline, you must use artifactStores',以及 'there must be an artifact store for the pipeline Region and for each cross-region action')。因此必須 (C) 在 us-east-1 建立 S3 bucket 並授予 CodePipeline 讀寫權限,以及 (E) 把 us-east-1 bucket 加入 pipeline 作為 artifact store,同時新增使用 us-east-1 output artifact 的 CloudFormation deploy action(工程師已用 'aws cloudformation package' 產生該模板,Lambda .zip 位置已內嵌且指向 us-east-1 位置)。CodePipeline 會自動把 input artifacts 從 eu-west-1 複製到 us-east-1 bucket,因此不需要手動複製。C 提供實體的 per-Region bucket;E 將其接入 pipeline 並建立 deploy action,兩者組成完整且最精簡的答案組合。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Parameterizing the .zip location and passing a parameter override is an alternative packaging pattern that contradicts the stated premise: the engineer already ran 'aws cloudformation package' for us-east-1, which rewrites the template to hard-code the us-east-1 .zip S3 location, so no parameter override is needed. Crucially, A still does not provide the mandatory us-east-1 artifact store that a cross-Region action requires, so it cannot complete the set.","why_zh":"把 .zip 位置參數化並用 parameter override 是另一種封裝方式,與題目前提矛盾:工程師已對 us-east-1 執行 'aws cloudformation package',模板中已硬寫入 us-east-1 的 .zip S3 位置,因此不需要 parameter override。最關鍵的是,A 仍未提供 cross-Region action 必備的 us-east-1 artifact store,因此無法構成完整答案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Creating the deploy action that uses the us-east-1 template is correct but incomplete: it omits registering the required us-east-1 artifact store (the docs require artifactStores for any cross-region action). Option E is a strict superset of B (it adds the artifact store as well), so B is redundant and inferior to E.","why_zh":"建立使用 us-east-1 模板的 deploy action 雖正確但不完整:它遺漏了登錄必要的 us-east-1 artifact store(文件規定任何 cross-region action 都必須使用 artifactStores)。選項 E 是 B 的嚴格超集(同時也加入 artifact store),因此 B 相對於 E 多餘且較差。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Cross-Region Replication is unnecessary and does not meet the requirement. CodePipeline itself copies the cross-Region action's input artifacts from the pipeline Region into the action's Region; CRR is asynchronous and eventually consistent, and it does not register a bucket as an artifact store, so it cannot drive the cross-Region deploy action.","why_zh":"S3 Cross-Region Replication 並非必要,也無法滿足需求。CodePipeline 本身會把 cross-Region action 的 input artifacts 從 pipeline Region 複製到 action 所在 Region;CRR 為非同步且最終一致,且不會把 bucket 登錄為 artifact store,因此無法驅動 cross-Region deploy action。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-create-cross-region.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-codepipeline-pipeline-artifactstoremap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/reference-pipeline-structure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/continuous-delivery-codepipeline-cfn-artifacts.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":24,"question_en":"A company runs an application on one Amazon EC2 instance. Application metadata is stored in Amazon S3 and must be retrieved if the instance is restarted. The instance must restart or relaunch automatically if the instance becomes unresponsive. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在一台亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行应用程序。应用程序的元数据存储在亚马逊 S3 中，如果实例重启， 必须能够获取这些元数据。如果实例无响应，必须自动重启或重新启动。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for the StatusCheckFailed metric. Use the recover action to stop and start the instance. Use an S3 event notification to push the metadata to the instance when the instance is back up and running.","B":"Configure AWS OpsWorks, and use the auto healing feature to stop and start the instance. Use a lifecycle event in OpsWorks to pull the metadata from Amazon S3 and update it on the instance.","C":"Use EC2 Auto Recovery to automatically stop and start the instance in case of a failure. Use an S3 event notification to push the metadata to the instance when the instance is back up and running.","D":"Use AWS CloudFormation to create an EC2 instance that includes the UserData property for the EC2 resource. Add a command in UserData to retrieve the application metadata from Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"为“StatusCheckFailed”指标创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。使用恢复操作来停止并重新启动实例。 使用 S3 事件通知在实例重新启动并运行时将元数据推送到实例。","B":"配置 AWS OpsWorks，并使用自动恢复功能停止和启动实例。在 OpsWorks 中使用生命周期事件从 Amazon S3 拉取元数据并在实例上进行更新。","C":"使用 EC2 自动恢复功能，在实例出现故障时自动停止并重新启动实例。使用 S3 事件通知，在实例恢 复运行时将元数据推送到实例。","D":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 创建一个包含 EC2 资源的 UserData 属性的 EC2 实例。在 UserData 中添加一 条命令，从 Amazon S3 获取应用程序元数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must BOTH be met: (1) the instance must automatically restart or relaunch when it becomes unresponsive, and (2) the application metadata in S3 must be retrieved after the instance comes back. Only option B satisfies both with valid mechanisms. AWS OpsWorks Stacks auto healing detects an unresponsive instance (the OpsWorks agent stops sending its heartbeat) and automatically restarts or replaces it, meeting requirement 1. When the instance returns, OpsWorks runs lifecycle events (Setup, Configure, Deploy) whose Chef recipes can PULL the metadata from Amazon S3 and apply it on the instance, meeting requirement 2. Options A and C both rely on an 'S3 event notification to push the metadata to the instance,' which is impossible: per the S3 Event Notifications documentation, S3 can only send notifications to Amazon SNS, Amazon SQS, AWS Lambda, or Amazon EventBridge — never directly to an EC2 instance — and there is no S3 event that fires 'when the instance is back up.' Option D's CloudFormation UserData runs only at first launch and provides no automatic restart-on-failure mechanism, so it fails requirement 1 entirely. Therefore B is the only technically valid solution.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個必須同時滿足的需求:(1) 當執行個體無回應時自動重啟或重新啟動;(2) 執行個體恢復後從 S3 取回應用程式 metadata。只有選項 B 能以有效機制同時滿足這兩點。AWS OpsWorks Stacks 的 auto healing(自動修復)會偵測無回應的執行個體(OpsWorks agent 停止傳送 heartbeat),並自動重啟或替換該執行個體,滿足需求一。執行個體恢復後,OpsWorks 會觸發 lifecycle events(Setup、Configure、Deploy),其 Chef recipe 可以從 Amazon S3 主動拉取(pull) metadata 並套用到執行個體上,滿足需求二。選項 A 與 C 都依賴 S3 event notification 將 metadata『推送(push)』到 EC2 執行個體,這在技術上不可能:依據 S3 Event Notifications 文件,S3 只能將通知發送到 Amazon SNS、Amazon SQS、AWS Lambda 或 Amazon EventBridge,絕不能直接送到 EC2 執行個體,而且也沒有『執行個體恢復時』觸發的 S3 事件。選項 D 的 CloudFormation UserData 只在首次啟動時執行,且完全不提供故障時的自動重啟,因此完全不滿足需求一。所以 B 是唯一技術上可行的解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The fatal flaw is that an S3 event notification cannot 'push metadata to the instance' — S3 notifications only target SNS, SQS, Lambda, or EventBridge, never an EC2 instance, and no S3 event fires when an instance comes back up. Separately, the CloudWatch 'recover' action does not 'stop and start'; it moves the instance to new hardware. The metadata requirement is unmet.","why_zh":"致命缺陷在於 S3 event notification 無法『將 metadata push 到實例』——S3 通知只能以 SNS、SQS、Lambda 或 EventBridge 為目標,絕不能直接送到 EC2 執行個體,且沒有在執行個體恢復時觸發的 S3 事件。另外 CloudWatch 的 recover 動作並非『stop and start』,而是將執行個體移到新硬體。metadata 需求未被滿足。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Shares A's broken mechanism: S3 event notifications cannot push metadata directly to an EC2 instance (destinations limited to SNS/SQS/Lambda/EventBridge), so the metadata-retrieval requirement is not met. Also, EC2 auto recovery recovers the instance onto new hardware rather than literally 'stop and start.'","why_zh":"與 A 同樣有錯誤機制:S3 事件通知無法直接把 metadata 推送到 EC2 執行個體(目的地僅限 SNS/SQS/Lambda/EventBridge),因此無法滿足取回 metadata 的需求。此外 EC2 auto recovery 是把執行個體恢復到新硬體,而非字面上的『stop and start』。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFormation UserData fetches metadata from S3 only at the instance's first launch (boot), and CloudFormation provides no mechanism to automatically restart or relaunch an instance when it becomes unresponsive, so it fails the auto-recovery requirement entirely.","why_zh":"CloudFormation UserData 只在執行個體首次啟動(開機)時從 S3 取回 metadata,而 CloudFormation 不提供任何在執行個體無回應時自動重啟或重新啟動的機制,因此完全無法滿足自動復原需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventNotifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/notification-how-to-event-types-and-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/cloudwatch-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/UsingAlarmActions.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":25,"question_en":"A company has multiple AWS accounts. The company uses AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign- On) that is integrated with AWS Toolkit for Microsoft Azure DevOps. The attributes for access control feature is enabled in IAM Identity Center. The attribute mapping list contains two entries. The department key is mapped to ${path:enterprise.department}. The costCenter key is mapped to ${path:enterprise.costCenter}. All existing Amazon EC2 instances have a department tag that corresponds to three company departments (d1, d2, d3). A DevOps engineer must create policies based on the matching attributes. The policies must minimize administrative effort and must grant each Azure AD user access to only the EC2 instances that are tagged with the user’s respective department name. Which condition key should the DevOps engineer include in the custom permissions policies to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司拥有多个 AWS 账户。该公司使用与 Microsoft Azure DevOps 的 AWS 工具包集成的 AWS IAM 身份 中心（AWS 单点登录）。IAM 身份中心的访问控制属性功能已启用。 属性映射列表包含两个条目。部门键映射到 ${path:enterprise.department}。成本中心键映射到 $ {path:enterprise.costCenter}。 所有现有的亚马逊 EC2 实例都有一个部门标签，对应于公司的三个部门（d1、d2、d3）。一位 DevOps 工 程师必须基于匹配的属性创建策略。这些策略必须将管理工作的量减至最少，并且必须仅授予每个 Azure AD 用户访问其所在部门名称标记的 EC2 实例的权限。 DevOps 工程师应在自定义权限策略中包含哪个条件键才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"","B":"","C":"","D":""},"options_zh":{},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical IAM Identity Center attribute-based access control (ABAC) scenario. AWS docs confirm: when ABAC ('Attributes for access control') is enabled and attribute mappings are configured (department -> ${path:enterprise.department}), IAM Identity Center passes the authenticated user's attribute value into IAM as a SESSION TAG, and you reference that session tag in permission policies with the aws:PrincipalTag/tag-key condition key, where tag-key must match the mapped key name exactly. The official EC2 example is identical in form: \"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\". Here the EC2 instances carry a 'department' tag (d1/d2/d3) and access must be granted by the user's department, so the policy compares the resource department tag against the user's department session tag using aws:PrincipalTag/department. This single dynamic permission set minimizes administrative effort: no per-department policies are needed; adding users/instances only requires correct tagging. The correct condition key is aws:PrincipalTag/department, which in the canonical published version of this question is option C. NOTE: the option text supplied in this dump is blank for all four letters; the C mapping relies on the standard published option ordering (A: aws:PrincipalTag/costCenter, B: ec2:ResourceTag/costCenter, C: aws:PrincipalTag/department, D: ec2:ResourceTag/department), hence medium confidence on the letter even though the underlying technical answer (aws:PrincipalTag/department) is certain.","explanation_zh":"這是 IAM Identity Center 屬性型存取控制 (ABAC) 的標準情境。AWS 文件確認：當啟用 ABAC（Attributes for access control）並設定屬性對應（department -> ${path:enterprise.department}）時，IAM Identity Center 會將已驗證使用者的屬性值以 SESSION TAG（工作階段標籤）形式傳入 IAM；在權限政策中以 aws:PrincipalTag/tag-key 條件鍵參照該工作階段標籤，tag-key 必須與對應的 key 名稱完全一致。官方 EC2 範例形式完全相同：\"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\"。此題中 EC2 執行個體帶有 department 標籤（d1/d2/d3），且需依使用者的 department 授予存取，因此政策用 aws:PrincipalTag/department 將資源的 department 標籤與使用者的 department 工作階段標籤比對。此單一動態 permission set 可最小化管理工作：不需為每個部門建立政策，新增使用者或執行個體只需正確標記。正確條件鍵為 aws:PrincipalTag/department，在本題標準公開版本中對應選項 C。注意：本 dump 提供的四個選項文字皆為空白；C 的對應是依標準公開選項排序推定（A: aws:PrincipalTag/costCenter、B: ec2:ResourceTag/costCenter、C: aws:PrincipalTag/department、D: ec2:ResourceTag/department），故對「字母」給予 medium 信心，但底層技術答案（aws:PrincipalTag/department）為確定。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A costCenter-based principal tag (aws:PrincipalTag/costCenter) does not satisfy the requirement. EC2 instances are tagged by department (d1/d2/d3) and access must be granted by department, not cost center, so matching the costCenter session tag would not align users to their department's instances.","why_zh":"以 costCenter 為基礎的 principal tag（aws:PrincipalTag/costCenter）不符需求。EC2 執行個體以 department（d1/d2/d3）標記，且存取需依 department 授予而非 cost center，因此用 costCenter 工作階段標籤比對無法將使用者對應到其部門的執行個體。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"ec2:ResourceTag/costCenter is a resource-side key on the wrong attribute. It describes the resource's cost center, not the user's department, and a resource tag key alone is not the condition key that carries the federated user's attribute; the user attribute is exposed via aws:PrincipalTag and must be the value compared against the resource's department tag.","why_zh":"ec2:ResourceTag/costCenter 是錯誤屬性上的資源端鍵。它描述資源的 cost center 而非使用者的 department，且資源標籤鍵本身並非承載聯合身分使用者屬性的條件鍵；使用者屬性是透過 aws:PrincipalTag 呈現，必須以該值與資源的 department 標籤比對。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ec2:ResourceTag/department describes the EC2 instance's department tag, not the user's attribute. While the policy does reference this resource tag, the condition KEY that injects the user's department value (the thing the question asks for) is aws:PrincipalTag/department; ResourceTag is the left side of the comparison, the PrincipalTag is the dynamic user attribute being supplied.","why_zh":"ec2:ResourceTag/department 描述 EC2 執行個體的 department 標籤，而非使用者屬性。雖然政策確實會參照此資源標籤，但注入使用者 department 值的條件鍵（即本題詢問者）是 aws:PrincipalTag/department；ResourceTag 是比較式的左側，PrincipalTag 才是被提供的動態使用者屬性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/attributesforaccesscontrol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_ec2-start-stop-match-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":26,"question_en":"A company hosts a security auditing application in an AWS account. The auditing application uses an IAM role to access other AWS accounts. All the accounts are in the same organization in AWS Organizations. A recent security audit revealed that users in the audited AWS accounts could modify or delete the auditing application's IAM role. The company needs to prevent any modification to the auditing application's IAM role by any entity other than a trusted administrator IAM role. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 账户中托管了一个安全审计应用程序。该审计应用程序使用一个 IAM 角色来访问其他 AWS 账户。所有账户都在 AWS Organizations 中的同一个组织内。 最近的一次安全审计发现，被审计的 AWS 账户中的用户能够修改或删除审计记录。 应用程序的 IAM 角色。该公司需要防止除受信任的管理员 IAM 角色之外的任何实体对审计应用程序 的 IAM 角色进行任何修改。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that includes a Deny statement for changes to the auditing application's IAM role. Include a condition that allows the trusted administrator IAM role to make changes. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","B":"Create an SCP that includes an Allow statement for changes to the auditing application's IAM role by the trusted administrator IAM role. Include a Deny statement for changes by all other IAM principals. Attach the SCP to the IAM service in each AWS account where the auditing application has an IAM role.","C":"Create an IAM permissions boundary that includes a Deny statement for changes to the auditing application's IAM role. Include a condition that allows the trusted administrator IAM role to make changes. Attach the permissions boundary to the audited AWS accounts.","D":"Create an IAM permissions boundary that includes a Deny statement for changes to the auditing application’s IAM role. Include a condition that allows the trusted administrator IAM role to make changes. Attach the permissions boundary to the auditing application's IAM role in the AWS accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），其中包含拒绝更改审计应用程序的 IAM 角色的语句。添加一个条 件，允许受信任的管理员 IAM 角色进行更改。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","B":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），其中包含允许受信任管理员 IAM 角色对审计应用程序的 IAM 角 色进行更改的“允许”语句，以及拒绝所有其他 IAM 实体进行更改的“拒绝”语句。将该 SCP 附加到每个拥有审计应用程序 IAM 角色的 AWS 账户中的 IAM 服务。","C":"创建一个包含拒绝更改审计应用程序 IAM 角色语句的 IAM 权限边界。包含一个允许受信任的 管理员 IAM 角色进行更改的条件。将权限边界附加到被审计的 AWS 账户。","D":"创建一个包含拒绝更改审计应用程序 IAM 角色语句的 IAM 权限边界。包含一个允许受信任的管理 员 IAM 角色进行更改的条件。将权限边界附加到 AWS 账户中审计应用程序的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to centrally prevent any principal in the member accounts, other than a trusted administrator role, from modifying or deleting the auditing application's IAM role. A Service Control Policy (SCP) is the correct mechanism: SCPs set maximum-permission guardrails for IAM users and roles in member accounts and support the recommended deny-list strategy. A Deny statement on the role's modify/delete actions (e.g. iam:DeleteRole, iam:UpdateRole, iam:UpdateAssumeRolePolicy, iam:AttachRolePolicy, iam:PutRolePolicy) scoped to the role's ARN, plus a condition that exempts the trusted admin (ArnNotLike/ArnNotEquals on aws:PrincipalARN), blocks everyone else. AWS publishes a near-identical real example in Control Tower control CT.IAM.PV.1, which uses exactly this SCP shape to disallow modification of a managed IAM role. SCPs can be attached to the organization root, where the guardrail applies to all member accounts, and a Deny at any level in the path applies to every account beneath it. Permissions boundaries (C and D) are the wrong tool because a boundary only caps the maximum permissions of the entity it is attached to and never governs what OTHER principals may do TO that entity, and a boundary cannot be attached to an account at all.","explanation_zh":"需求是要集中性地阻止成員帳戶中除受信任的管理員角色之外的任何主體修改或刪除稽核應用程式的 IAM role。正確的機制是 Service Control Policy (SCP)：SCP 為成員帳戶中的 IAM users 與 roles 設定最大權限護欄，並支援建議的「拒絕清單 (deny list)」策略。以 Deny 陳述式針對該 role 的修改/刪除動作（例如 iam:DeleteRole、iam:UpdateRole、iam:UpdateAssumeRolePolicy、iam:AttachRolePolicy、iam:PutRolePolicy），將 Resource 限定為該 role 的 ARN，再加上一個條件以放行受信任的管理員（對 aws:PrincipalARN 使用 ArnNotLike/ArnNotEquals），即可封鎖其他所有人。AWS 在 Control Tower 控制項 CT.IAM.PV.1 中發布了幾乎相同的真實範例，正是用這種 SCP 形式來禁止修改受管的 IAM role。SCP 可附加到組織 root，使護欄套用到所有成員帳戶；路徑上任何層級的 Deny 都會套用到其下的每個帳戶。Permissions boundaries（C 與 D）是錯誤工具，因為 boundary 只限制其所附加實體本身的最大權限，從不規範「其他主體」可以對「該實體」做什麼，而且 boundary 根本無法附加到帳戶。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"SCPs cannot be attached to 'the IAM service in each AWS account'; they attach only to the organization root, an OU, or an account. SCPs also never grant permissions, so the described Allow-plus-Deny structure plus the invalid attachment target make this option technically impossible (the recommended approach is a deny list relying on the default FullAWSAccess).","why_zh":"SCP 無法附加到「每個帳戶中的 IAM 服務」；它只能附加到組織 root、OU 或帳戶。SCP 也從不授予權限，因此所述的 Allow 加 Deny 結構與無效的附加目標使此選項在技術上不可行（建議方式是依賴預設 FullAWSAccess 的拒絕清單）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A permissions boundary is an IAM feature attached to an IAM entity (user or role), not to an account, so it cannot be 'attached to the audited AWS accounts'. A boundary also only caps the attached entity's own permissions and does not control what other principals can do to the auditing role.","why_zh":"Permissions boundary 是附加到 IAM 實體（user 或 role）的 IAM 功能，而非附加到帳戶，因此無法「附加到受稽核的 AWS 帳戶」。boundary 也僅限制所附加實體本身的權限，無法控制其他主體對稽核 role 能做什麼。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Attaching a permissions boundary to the auditing role only limits what that role itself can do; it does NOT prevent other IAM principals from calling iam:DeleteRole/UpdateRole on it. Boundaries govern the holder's outbound permissions, not inbound modification by others, so it fails the requirement.","why_zh":"將 permissions boundary 附加到稽核 role 只會限制該 role 本身能做什麼；它「不會」阻止其他 IAM 主體對其呼叫 iam:DeleteRole/UpdateRole。boundary 規範的是持有者的對外權限，而非他人對其的修改，因此無法滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/ct-iam-pv-1.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":27,"question_en":"A company has an on-premises application that is written in Go. A DevOps engineer must move the application to AWS. The company's development team wants to enable blue/green deployments and perform A/B testing. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个用 Go 语言编写的本地应用程序。一位 DevOps 工程师必须将该应用程序迁移到 AWS。公司的开发团队希望启用蓝/绿部署并进行 A/B 测试。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application on an Amazon EC2 instance, and create an AMI of the instance. Use the AMI to create an automatic scaling launch configuration that is used in an Auto Scaling group. Use Elastic Load Balancing to distribute traffic. When changes are made to the application, a new AMI will be created, which will initiate an EC2 instance refresh.","B":"Use Amazon Lightsail to deploy the application. Store the application in a zipped format in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use this zipped version to deploy new versions of the application to Lightsail. Use Lightsail deployment options to manage the deployment.","C":"Use AWS CodeArtifact to store the application code. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the application to a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. Use Elastic Load Balancing to distribute the traffic to the EC2 instances. When making changes to the application, upload a new version to CodeArtifact and create a new CodeDeploy deployment.","D":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to host the application. Store a zipped version of the application in Amazon S3. Use that location to deploy new versions of the application. Use Elastic Beanstalk to manage the deployment options."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon EC2 实例上部署应用程序，并创建该实例的 AMI。使用该 AMI 创建自动扩展启动配置， 该配置用于自动扩展组。使用弹性负载均衡来分配流量。当对应用程序进行更改时，将创建新的 AMI，从而启动 EC2 实例刷新。","B":"使用 Amazon Lightsail 部署应用程序。将应用程序以压缩格式存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用此 压缩版本将应用程序的新版本部署到 Lightsail。使用 Lightsail 部署选项来管理部署。","C":"使用 AWS CodeArtifact 存储应用程序代码。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将应用程序部署到一组 Amazon EC2 实例。使用弹性负载均衡将流量分发到 EC2 实例。在对应用程序进行更改时，将新版本上传到 CodeArtifact 并创建新的 CodeDeploy 部署。","D":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 来托管应用程序。将应用程序的压缩版本存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用该位 置来部署应用程序的新版本。使用 Elastic Beanstalk 来管理部署选项。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk natively supports the Go platform, so the on-premises Go application can be rehosted with minimal operational overhead: package it as a source bundle, upload the zipped version to Amazon S3, and deploy it as a new application version. Elastic Beanstalk provides built-in blue/green deployments by launching a separate clone environment with the new version and swapping the environment CNAMEs to redirect traffic instantly (and to swap back for fast rollback). For A/B testing it offers the Traffic splitting deployment policy on load-balanced environments using an Application Load Balancer; it launches a full set of new instances and forwards a specified percentage of incoming client traffic to the new version for an evaluation period (canary / A-B testing), per the May 18, 2020 release. This single managed service satisfies every requirement (Go support, blue/green, A/B traffic-splitting) without manually assembling EC2, Auto Scaling, ELB, and deployment orchestration.","explanation_zh":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk 原生支援 Go 平台，因此可以將內部部署的 Go 應用程式以最小的營運負擔重新託管：將其打包為 source bundle，把壓縮版本上傳至 Amazon S3，再部署為新的應用程式版本。Elastic Beanstalk 提供內建的 blue/green 部署，方式是另外建立一個帶有新版本的複製環境，再交換環境的 CNAME 以立即將流量導向新版本（並可換回以快速回滾）。對於 A/B 測試，Elastic Beanstalk 在使用 Application Load Balancer 的負載平衡環境上提供 Traffic splitting 部署原則；它會啟動一整組新執行個體，並在評估期間將指定百分比的進入用戶端流量轉送到新版本（金絲雀／A-B 測試），此功能於 2020 年 5 月 18 日發布。這個單一的受管服務一次滿足所有需求（Go 支援、blue/green、A/B 流量分流），無需手動組合 EC2、Auto Scaling、ELB 與部署協作。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Baking an AMI, launch configuration, Auto Scaling group, ELB, and triggering an EC2 instance refresh performs a rolling in-place instance replacement, not a true blue/green deployment, and provides no native A/B traffic-splitting capability. It also carries far higher operational overhead than a managed platform and uses the deprecated launch configuration concept.","why_zh":"烘焙 AMI、launch configuration、Auto Scaling group、ELB 並觸發 EC2 instance refresh 屬於滾動式就地執行個體替換，並非真正的 blue/green 部署，也沒有原生的 A/B 流量分流能力；其營運負擔遠高於受管平台，且使用了已淘汰的 launch configuration。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Lightsail is a simplified VPS service aimed at simple workloads; it does not offer managed blue/green deployments or A/B traffic-splitting as built-in deployment options, so it cannot meet the A/B testing and blue/green requirements.","why_zh":"Amazon Lightsail 是針對簡單工作負載的簡化 VPS 服務，沒有內建的受管 blue/green 部署或 A/B 流量分流部署選項，因此無法滿足 A/B 測試與 blue/green 的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS CodeArtifact is a software package/dependency repository (npm, Maven, PyPI, NuGet, etc.), not a deployment-artifact (application revision) store consumed by CodeDeploy. CodeDeploy pulls application revisions from Amazon S3 or GitHub, not from CodeArtifact, so this architecture is misconfigured. Although CodeDeploy itself can perform blue/green deployments, the stated CodeArtifact usage is incorrect.","why_zh":"AWS CodeArtifact 是軟體套件／相依性儲存庫（npm、Maven、PyPI、NuGet 等），並非供 CodeDeploy 使用的部署成品（應用程式修訂版）儲存庫。CodeDeploy 從 Amazon S3 或 GitHub 取得應用程式修訂版，而非 CodeArtifact，因此此架構配置錯誤。雖然 CodeDeploy 本身可執行 blue/green 部署，但題目中描述的 CodeArtifact 用法不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/create_deploy_go.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.CNAMESwap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.rolling-version-deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.deploy-existing-version.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/relnotes/release-2020-05-18-ts-deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/welcome.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":28,"question_en":"A developer is maintaining a fleet of 50 Amazon EC2 Linux servers. The servers are part of an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group, and also use Elastic Load Balancing for load balancing. Occasionally, some application servers are being terminated after failing ELB HTTP health checks. The developer would like to perform a root cause analysis on the issue, but before being able to access application logs, the server is terminated. How can log collection be automated?","question_zh":"一位开发人员正在维护一个由 50 台亚马逊 EC2 Linux 服务器组成的集群。这些服务器属于一个亚马 逊 EC2 自动扩展组，并且还使用弹性负载均衡来进行负载均衡。 有时，一些应用服务器在未能通过 ELB HTTP 健康检查后会被终止。开发人员希望对这一问题进行 根本原因分析，但在能够访问应用日志之前，服务器已被终止。 如何实现日志收集的自动化？","options_en":{"A":"Use Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks to put instances in a Pending:Wait state. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for EC2 Instance Terminate Successful and trigger an AWS Lambda function that invokes an SSM Run Command script to collect logs, push them to Amazon S3, and complete the lifecycle action once logs are collected.","B":"Use Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks to put instances in a Terminating:Wait state. Create an AWS Config rule for EC2 Instance-terminate Lifecycle Action and trigger a step function that invokes a script to collect logs, push them to Amazon S3, and complete the lifecycle action once logs are collected.","C":"Use Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks to put instances in a Terminating:Wait state. Create an Amazon CloudWatch subscription filter for EC2 Instance Terminate Successful and trigger a CloudWatch agent that invokes a script to collect logs, push them to Amazon S3, and complete the lifecycle action once logs are collected.","D":"Use Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks to put instances in a Terminating:Wait state. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for EC2 Instance-terminate Lifecycle Action and trigger an AWS Lambda function that invokes an SSM Run Command script to collect logs, push them to Amazon S3, and complete the lifecycle action once logs are collected."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩将实例置于“待处理：等待”状态。为“EC2 实例终止成功”创 建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，并触发一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 SSM 运行命令 脚本以收集日志，将它们推送到 Amazon S3，并在收集日志后完成生命周期操作。","B":"使用 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩将实例置于“Terminating:Wait”状态。创建一个针对 EC2 实例终止 生命周期操作的 AWS Config 规则，并触发一个步骤函数，该函数调用一个脚本以收集日志，将 它们推送到 Amazon S3，并在收集完日志后完成生命周期操作。","C":"使用 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩将实例置于“终止：等待”状态。为 EC2 实例终止成功的事件创建 一个 Amazon CloudWatch 订阅过滤器，并触发 CloudWatch 代理，该代理会调用一个脚本收集日志， 将它们推送到 Amazon S3，然后在收集完日志后完成生命周期操作。","D":"使用 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩将实例置于“终止：等待”状态。创建一个针对 EC2 实例终止生命周 期操作的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，并触发一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 SSM 运行命令脚 本以收集日志，将它们推送到 Amazon S3，并在收集完日志后完成生命周期操作。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"To capture logs before an Auto Scaling group fully terminates an instance, you add a termination lifecycle hook. When it fires, EC2 Auto Scaling moves the instance to the Terminating:Wait state and emits the EventBridge event with detail-type 'EC2 Instance-terminate Lifecycle Action' (source aws.autoscaling), giving you a window (one hour by default) before termination completes. An EventBridge rule matching that event invokes a Lambda function that uses SSM Run Command to collect the logs, push them to Amazon S3, and then call CompleteLifecycleAction so termination can proceed. Option D is the only choice with all four elements correct: the Terminating:Wait state, the real lifecycle-action event, the right service to react to it (EventBridge, not AWS Config or a CloudWatch subscription filter), and a correctly ordered callback. The 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful' event used by A and C is a post-termination 'successful scaling event' that fires after the instance is already gone, so it is useless for pre-termination log collection.","explanation_zh":"要在 Auto Scaling group 完全終止執行個體之前擷取日誌，需新增終止 (termination) lifecycle hook。當它觸發時，EC2 Auto Scaling 會將執行個體移入 Terminating:Wait 狀態，並透過 EventBridge 發出 detail-type 為 'EC2 Instance-terminate Lifecycle Action'（source 為 aws.autoscaling）的事件，提供一段等待時間（預設一小時）讓終止暫停。比對該事件的 EventBridge rule 觸發一個 Lambda function，由它呼叫 SSM Run Command 收集日誌、推送到 Amazon S3，最後呼叫 CompleteLifecycleAction 讓終止繼續進行。選項 D 是唯一四個要素全部正確的答案：Terminating:Wait 狀態、真正的 lifecycle-action 事件、正確的反應服務（EventBridge，而非 AWS Config 或 CloudWatch subscription filter），以及順序正確的回呼。A 與 C 使用的 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful' 是終止之後才發出的『成功擴縮事件』，執行個體早已消失，無法用於終止前的日誌收集。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Two errors: Pending:Wait is a launch (scale-out) wait state, not a termination state, and 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful' is a post-termination success event that fires after the instance is already gone, too late to collect logs. Using a CloudWatch alarm to react to that event is also the wrong trigger model.","why_zh":"兩處錯誤：Pending:Wait 是啟動（scale-out）等待狀態而非終止狀態；且 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful' 是終止後才發出的成功事件，此時執行個體早已不存在，無法收集日誌。以 CloudWatch alarm 反應該事件的方式也屬錯誤的觸發模型。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The Terminating:Wait state is correct, but AWS Config rules evaluate resource-configuration compliance over time; they do not trigger on Auto Scaling lifecycle-action events. The lifecycle action is delivered through Amazon EventBridge, not AWS Config, so this trigger mechanism cannot reliably capture logs during the wait window.","why_zh":"Terminating:Wait 狀態正確，但 AWS Config rule 是用來持續評估資源組態合規性，並不會因 Auto Scaling lifecycle-action 事件而觸發。該 lifecycle 動作是透過 Amazon EventBridge 傳遞而非 AWS Config，因此此觸發機制無法在等待期間可靠地擷取日誌。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A CloudWatch Logs subscription filter routes log-stream data, not Auto Scaling lifecycle events, so it cannot match a lifecycle-action event; and a CloudWatch agent cannot be 'triggered' by a subscription filter to run a script. It also keys on 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful', the post-termination event that is too late for log collection.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 作用於日誌串流資料，而非 Auto Scaling lifecycle 事件，因此無法比對 lifecycle-action 事件；CloudWatch agent 也無法由 subscription filter『觸發』執行腳本。同時它引用 'EC2 Instance Terminate Successful'，這是終止後事件，對收集日誌而言為時已晚。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-event-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/lifecycle-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/tutorial-lifecycle-hook-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-autoscaling.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":29,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations. The organization includes workload accounts that contain enterprise applications. The company centrally manages users from an operations account. No users can be created in the workload accounts. The company recently added an operations team and must provide the operations team members with administrator access to each workload account. Which combination of actions will provide this access? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中拥有一个组织架构。该组织架构包含有企业应用程序的工作负载账户。公司从 运营账户集中管理用户。工作负载账户中不能创建用户。该公司最近新增了一个运营团队，必须为运 营团队成员提供对每个工作负载账户的管理员访问权限。 哪些操作组合将提供此访问权限？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a SysAdmin role in the operations account. Attach the AdministratorAccess policy to the role. Modify the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRole action from the workload accounts.","B":"Create a SysAdmin role in each workload account. Attach the AdministratorAccess policy to the role. Modify the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRole action from the operations account.","C":"Create an Amazon Cognito identity pool in the operations account. Attach the SysAdmin role as an authenticated role.","D":"In the operations account, create an IAM user for each operations team member.","E":"In the operations account, create an IAM user group that is named SysAdmins. Add an IAM policy that allows the sts:AssumeRole action for the SysAdmin role in each workload account. Add all operations team members to the group.","F":"Create an Amazon Cognito user pool in the operations account. Create an Amazon Cognito user for each operations team member."},"options_zh":{"A":"在运营账户中创建一个系统管理员角色。将管理员访问策略附加到该角色。修改信任关系，允许工 作负载账户执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。","B":"在每个工作负载账户中创建一个系统管理员角色。将 AdministratorAccess 策略附加到该角色。修改 信任关系，允许操作账户执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。","C":"在运营账户中创建一个 Amazon Cognito 身份池。将 SysAdmin 角色作为已认证角色进行关联。","D":"在操作账户中，为每个操作团队成员创建一个 IAM 用户。","E":"在操作账户中，创建一个名为 SysAdmins 的 IAM 用户组。添加一个 IAM 策略，允许该组成员执行每 个工作负载账户中的 SysAdmin 角色的 sts:AssumeRole 操作。将所有操作团队成员添加到该组。","F":"在运营账户中创建一个 Amazon Cognito 用户池。为每个运营团队成员创建一个 Amazon Cognito 用 户。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical IAM cross-account role-delegation pattern from the AWS tutorial 'Delegate access across AWS accounts using IAM roles.' In that pattern the trusting (Destination) account is the account being accessed, so it creates the role with the needed permissions and a trust policy that names the trusted (Originating) account; users in the trusted account are then given sts:AssumeRole permission. Mapping to this scenario: (B) create a SysAdmin role in EACH workload account, attach AdministratorAccess, and set the trust relationship to allow sts:AssumeRole from the operations account - the privileged role must live in the account being administered (the trusting account). (D) because users are centrally managed only in the operations account and cannot be created in the workload accounts, create an IAM user for each operations team member in the operations account. (E) create a SysAdmins IAM user group in the operations account whose policy allows sts:AssumeRole on the SysAdmin role in each workload account, and add all team members to it - this grants the trusted-side permission to assume the cross-account role and follows the best practice of granting permissions through groups. Together B+D+E deliver administrator access to every workload account without creating any users in those accounts.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS 教學文件「Delegate access across AWS accounts using IAM roles」所描述的標準 IAM 跨帳戶角色委派模式。在此模式中,被存取的帳戶即受信任 (trusting / Destination) 帳戶,由它建立具備所需權限的角色,並在信任政策中指定信任 (trusted / Originating) 帳戶;接著該受信任帳戶中的使用者才被授予 sts:AssumeRole 權限。對應本題情境:(B) 在「每一個」workload 帳戶中建立 SysAdmin 角色、附加 AdministratorAccess 政策,並設定信任關係以允許來自 operations 帳戶的 sts:AssumeRole - 具特權的角色必須位於被管理的帳戶 (即 trusting 帳戶)。(D) 由於使用者僅集中於 operations 帳戶管理且無法在 workload 帳戶建立,故在 operations 帳戶為每位運維團隊成員建立一個 IAM user。(E) 在 operations 帳戶建立名為 SysAdmins 的 IAM user group,其政策允許對各 workload 帳戶的 SysAdmin 角色執行 sts:AssumeRole,並將所有成員加入該群組 - 這賦予受信任端承擔跨帳戶角色的權限,同時符合透過群組授權的最佳實務。B+D+E 三者結合即可在不於 workload 帳戶建立任何使用者的前提下,提供對每個 workload 帳戶的管理員存取。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creates the SysAdmin role with AdministratorAccess in the operations account, which inverts the trust direction. The privileged role must be created in each workload account (the trusting account that is accessed), with a trust policy that points to the operations account - not a role in the operations account that trusts the workload accounts. As written it would let workload accounts assume into operations, the opposite of what is required, and grants no access to the workload accounts.","why_zh":"在 operations 帳戶建立帶有 AdministratorAccess 的 SysAdmin 角色,使信任方向顛倒。具特權的角色必須建立於各 workload 帳戶 (被存取的 trusting 帳戶),且其信任政策應指向 operations 帳戶,而非在 operations 帳戶建立並信任 workload 帳戶的角色。如此設定反而會讓 workload 帳戶假設進 operations,與需求相反,且無法授予對 workload 帳戶的存取。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Cognito identity pools provide temporary AWS credentials to end users of web and mobile applications via federation; they are not the mechanism for delegating administrator access to internal operations staff across AWS Organizations accounts. The documented cross-account console/CLI role-switching pattern relies on IAM roles and sts:AssumeRole, not Cognito.","why_zh":"Amazon Cognito identity pool 是透過聯合身分為 Web/行動應用程式的終端使用者提供臨時 AWS 憑證,並非用來在 AWS Organizations 帳戶間為內部運維人員委派管理員存取的機制。文件所述的跨帳戶 console/CLI 角色切換採用 IAM 角色與 sts:AssumeRole,而非 Cognito。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Amazon Cognito user pools are a user directory for application sign-up/sign-in (authentication for app end users), not a means of managing IAM principals that assume cross-account AWS roles or of granting administrator access to workload accounts. It does not implement the sts:AssumeRole cross-account delegation required here.","why_zh":"Amazon Cognito user pool 是供應用程式註冊/登入使用的使用者目錄 (為應用終端使用者做驗證),並非用於管理假設跨帳戶 AWS 角色的 IAM 主體,也無法賦予對 workload 帳戶的管理員存取,無法實作本題所需的 sts:AssumeRole 跨帳戶委派。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/tutorial_cross-account-with-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies-cross-account-resource-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create_for-user.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":30,"question_en":"A company has multiple accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company's SecOps team needs to receive an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notification if any account in the organization turns off the Block Public Access feature on an Amazon S3 bucket. A DevOps engineer must implement this change without affecting the operation of any AWS accounts. The implementation must ensure that individual member accounts in the organization cannot turn off the notification. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中拥有多个账户。该公司的安全运维团队需要在组织中的任何账户关闭 Amazon S3 存储桶的“阻止公共访问”功能时收到 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）的通知。一位 DevOps 工程师必须在不影响任何 AWS 账户运行的情况下实施此变更。该实施必须确保组织中的各个 成员账户无法关闭此通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Designate an account to be the delegated Amazon GuardDuty administrator account. Turn on GuardDuty for all accounts across the organization. In the GuardDuty administrator account, create an SNS topic. Subscribe the SecOps team's email address to the SNS topic. In the same account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses an event pattern for GuardDuty findings and a target of the SNS topic.","B":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that creates an SNS topic and subscribes the SecOps team’s email address to the SNS topic. In the template, include an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses an event pattern of CloudTrail activity for s3:PutBucketPublicAccessBlock and a target of the SNS topic. Deploy the stack to every account in the organization by using CloudFormation StackSets.","C":"Turn on AWS Config across the organization. In the delegated administrator account, create an SNS topic. Subscribe the SecOps team's email address to the SNS topic. Deploy a conformance pack that uses the s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited AWS Config managed rule in each account and uses an AWS Systems Manager document to publish an event to the SNS topic to notify the SecOps team.","D":"Turn on Amazon Inspector across the organization. In the Amazon Inspector delegated administrator account, create an SNS topic. Subscribe the SecOps team’s email address to the SNS topic. In the same account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses an event pattern for public network exposure of the S3 bucket and publishes an event to the SNS topic to notify the SecOps team."},"options_zh":{"A":"指定一个账户作为委托的 Amazon GuardDuty 管理员账户。为组织内的所有账户开启 GuardDuty 服务。在 GuardDuty 管理员账户中，创建一个 SNS 主题。将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该 SNS 主题。在 同一个账户中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则使用 GuardDuty 发现结果的事件模式，并将 SNS 主题作为目标。","B":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，用于创建一个 SNS 主题，并将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地址订阅到 该 SNS 主题。在模板中，包含一个使用 CloudTrail 活动事件模式（针对 s3:PutBucketPublicAccessBlock） 的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，其目标为 SNS 主题。通过使用 CloudFormation StackSets 将该堆栈部署到 组织中的每个账户。","C":"在整个组织内启用 AWS Config。在委托管理员账户中创建一个 SNS 主题。将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地 址订阅到该 SNS 主题。在每个账户中部署一个一致性包，该包使用 AWS Config 管理规则 s3-bucket- level-public-access-prohibited，并使用 AWS Systems Manager 文档向 SNS 主题发布事件以通知 SecOps 团 队。","D":"在整个组织内启用 Amazon Inspector。在 Amazon Inspector 委托管理员账户中，创建一个 SNS 主题。将 SecOps 团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该 SNS 主题。在同一个账户中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规 则，该规则使用 S3 存储桶公共网络暴露的事件模式，并将事件发布到 SNS 主题以通知 SecOps 团队。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Amazon GuardDuty has a purpose-built finding type for exactly this event: Policy:S3/BucketBlockPublicAccessDisabled - 'An IAM entity invoked an API used to disable S3 Block Public Access on a bucket' (with Policy:S3/AccountBlockPublicAccessDisabled at the account level), sourced from CloudTrail management events. Designating a delegated GuardDuty administrator and auto-enabling GuardDuty for ALL accounts (including new ones) means member accounts have no control over the detection. The SNS topic, the email subscription, and the EventBridge rule all live in the GuardDuty administrator account, which receives finding events for every member account in a multi-account organization, so individual member accounts cannot turn off the notification. The pipeline is notify-only (EventBridge to SNS), so it does not affect account operations. Option C is the strongest distractor and the dump answer, but it is technically weaker: the named rule s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited evaluates whether a bucket is effectively publicly accessible, not whether the Block Public Access toggle was turned off (the rule that watches the BPA setting itself is s3-account-level-public-access-blocks), so disabling BPA on a bucket with no public policy would leave it COMPLIANT and produce no notification; additionally, using a Config remediation action (an SSM Automation document, designed to change/fix resources) merely to publish an SNS message is a contrived misuse - the idiomatic notify path is EventBridge on a compliance-change event, not a remediation runbook.","explanation_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 有一個專為此事件設計的 finding 類型：Policy:S3/BucketBlockPublicAccessDisabled，原文為「An IAM entity invoked an API used to disable S3 Block Public Access on a bucket」（帳戶層級則為 Policy:S3/AccountBlockPublicAccessDisabled），資料來源為 CloudTrail management events。指定委派的 GuardDuty administrator 並對 ALL 帳戶（含新加入帳戶）自動啟用 GuardDuty，使成員帳戶無法控制偵測機制。SNS topic、email 訂閱與 EventBridge rule 全都建立在 GuardDuty administrator 帳戶內，而該帳戶在多帳戶組織中會收到每個成員帳戶的 finding 事件，因此個別成員帳戶無法關閉通知。整條管線僅為通知用途（EventBridge 到 SNS），不影響帳戶運作。選項 C 是最強干擾項，也是題庫給的答案，但技術上較弱：所指的規則 s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited 評估的是 bucket 是否實際對外公開，而非 Block Public Access 開關是否被關閉（真正監看 BPA 設定的規則是 s3-account-level-public-access-blocks）；因此若在沒有公開政策的 bucket 上關閉 BPA，該規則仍維持 COMPLIANT 而不會發出通知。此外，用 Config remediation action（即用來變更/修復資源的 SSM Automation document）僅僅去發送 SNS 訊息屬於非慣用的誤用，慣用的通知路徑是針對 compliance-change 事件的 EventBridge，而非 remediation runbook。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The SNS topic, EventBridge rule, and email subscription are deployed into each member account via CloudFormation StackSets, so the notification resources are owned by the member account. A sufficiently privileged member-account administrator can delete or disable the local EventBridge rule or SNS subscription, turning off the notification. StackSets (even service-managed) does not make those member-account resources immutable against local admins, so this fails the requirement that members cannot turn off the notification.","why_zh":"SNS topic、EventBridge rule 與 email 訂閱透過 CloudFormation StackSets 部署到每個成員帳戶內，這些通知資源由成員帳戶擁有。具足夠權限的成員帳戶管理員可刪除或停用本地 EventBridge rule 或 SNS 訂閱而關閉通知。即使是 service-managed StackSets，也不會使這些成員帳戶資源對本地管理員不可變更，故未滿足成員無法關閉通知的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Two technical weaknesses make this inferior to A. First, the chosen managed rule s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited checks whether a bucket is effectively publicly accessible, not whether the Block Public Access setting was turned off; turning BPA off on a bucket that has no public policy/ACL leaves it COMPLIANT, so SecOps would not be notified for the exact event the question describes (the setting-watching rule is s3-account-level-public-access-blocks). Second, a Config remediation action is an SSM Automation document meant to modify/fix noncompliant resources; repurposing it only to publish an SNS message is contrived versus the standard EventBridge-on-compliance-change notification path. The governance/non-modifiable claim is true for org conformance packs, but the detection-and-notify mechanism itself is the weaker fit.","why_zh":"兩個技術弱點使其不如 A。第一，所選受管規則 s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited 檢查的是 bucket 是否實際對外公開，而非 Block Public Access 設定是否被關閉；在沒有公開 policy/ACL 的 bucket 上關閉 BPA 會維持 COMPLIANT，因此對題目描述的確切事件不會通知 SecOps（監看設定本身的規則是 s3-account-level-public-access-blocks）。第二，Config remediation action 是用來修改/修復不合規資源的 SSM Automation document，將其重新用途化為僅發送 SNS 訊息，相較於標準的 EventBridge compliance-change 通知路徑顯得牽強。組織 conformance pack 不可被成員修改的治理說法確實成立，但其偵測與通知機制本身較不貼合需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector scans EC2 instances, ECR container images, and Lambda functions for software vulnerabilities and network reachability; it does not monitor S3 bucket Block Public Access configuration. There is no Inspector 'public network exposure of the S3 bucket' finding, so it cannot detect BPA being turned off and cannot meet the requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 掃描 EC2 執行個體、ECR 容器映像與 Lambda 函式的軟體弱點與網路可達性，並不監控 S3 bucket 的 Block Public Access 設定。Inspector 沒有所謂「S3 bucket 公開網路暴露」的 finding，因此無法偵測 BPA 被關閉，也無法滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/set-guardduty-auto-enable-preferences.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-level-public-access-prohibited.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-account-level-public-access-blocks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-pack-organization-apis.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":31,"question_en":"A company has migrated its container-based applications to Amazon EKS and want to establish automated email notifications. The notifications sent to each email address are for specific activities related to EKS components. The solution will include Amazon SNS topics and an AWS Lambda function to evaluate incoming log events and publish messages to the correct SNS topic. Which logging solution will support these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已将其基于容器的应用程序迁移到了亚马逊 EKS，并希望建立自动化的电子邮件通知机制。发送到 每个电子邮件地址的通知是针对与 EKS 组件相关的特定活动。该解决方案将包括亚马逊 SNS 主题和一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于评估传入的日志事件并向正确的 SNS 主题发布消息。 哪种日志记录解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon CloudWatch Logs to log the EKS components. Create a CloudWatch subscription filter for each component with Lambda as the subscription feed destination.","B":"Enable Amazon CloudWatch Logs to log the EKS components. Create CloudWatch Logs Insights queries linked to Amazon EventBridge events that invoke Lambda.","C":"Enable Amazon S3 logging for the EKS components. Configure an Amazon CloudWatch subscription filter for each component with Lambda as the subscription feed destination.","D":"Enable Amazon S3 logging for the EKS components. Configure S3 PUT Object event notifications with AWS Lambda as the destination."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 来记录 EKS 组件。为每个组件创建一个 CloudWatch 订阅过滤器，并将 Lambda 作为订阅源的目的地。","B":"启用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 来记录 EKS 组件。创建与 Amazon EventBridge 事件关联的 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询，这些事件会调用 Lambda。","C":"为 EKS 组件启用 Amazon S3 日志记录。为每个组件配置一个 Amazon CloudWatch 订阅过滤器，将 Lambda 作为订阅源的目的地。","D":"为 EKS 组件启用 Amazon S3 日志记录。将 S3 PUT 对象事件通知配置为以 AWS Lambda 作为目标。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amazon EKS control plane logging sends audit and diagnostic logs from the Kubernetes control plane directly to CloudWatch Logs. Each enabled log type (api, audit, authenticator, controllerManager, scheduler) corresponds to a control plane component and is delivered as a separate log stream within a log group for the cluster. The EKS doc explicitly states you can use CloudWatch subscription filters to do real-time analysis on these logs or forward them to other services, and the CloudWatch Logs subscription filter doc lists AWS Lambda as a supported destination. Therefore creating a per-component subscription filter that invokes a Lambda function lets the function evaluate each incoming log event in real time and publish to the correct SNS topic for the matching email subscribers, satisfying the requirement. Option A is correct.","explanation_zh":"Amazon EKS control plane logging 會把 Kubernetes 控制平面的稽核與診斷日誌直接送到 CloudWatch Logs。每個啟用的日誌類型 (api、audit、authenticator、controllerManager、scheduler) 對應一個控制平面元件，並以個別的 log stream 形式送進該叢集的 log group。EKS 文件明確說明可使用 CloudWatch subscription filters 對這些日誌進行即時分析或轉發到其他服務，而 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 文件也列出 AWS Lambda 為支援的目的地。因此為每個元件建立一個 subscription filter 並以 Lambda 作為訂閱目的地，Lambda 即可即時評估每筆傳入的 log event，並發布到對應的 SNS topic 給相符的 email 訂閱者，符合需求。選項 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs Insights is an interactive, on-demand query tool for ad hoc analysis; you cannot 'link' a Logs Insights query to EventBridge events to invoke Lambda as a continuous, per-log-event evaluation pipeline. This is not a supported real-time forwarding pattern.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs Insights 是互動式、隨選的查詢工具，用於臨時分析；無法把 Logs Insights 查詢「連結」到 EventBridge 事件以觸發 Lambda 來持續逐筆評估日誌。這不是支援的即時轉發模式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EKS control plane logging delivers to CloudWatch Logs, not to S3 directly, so 'enable Amazon S3 logging for the EKS components' is not a native EKS capability. It also incoherently applies a CloudWatch subscription filter, which operates on a CloudWatch Logs log group, to S3 logging.","why_zh":"EKS control plane logging 是送到 CloudWatch Logs，而非直接送到 S3，所以「為 EKS 元件啟用 Amazon S3 logging」不是 EKS 原生能力。它還矛盾地把作用於 CloudWatch Logs log group 的 subscription filter 套用在 S3 logging 上。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EKS does not natively export control plane component logs to S3; control plane logging targets CloudWatch Logs. Even if logs landed in S3, S3 PUT Object event notifications fire per object/batch, not per individual log event, so they cannot evaluate each log event for real-time routing to the correct SNS topic.","why_zh":"EKS 不會原生地把控制平面元件日誌匯出到 S3；控制平面日誌的目的地是 CloudWatch Logs。即使日誌落到 S3，S3 PUT Object 事件通知是以物件/批次層級觸發，而非逐筆 log event，因此無法即時評估每筆 log event 以路由到正確的 SNS topic。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/control-plane-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":32,"question_en":"A company is implementing an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster to run its workload. The company architecture will run multiple ECS services on the cluster. The architecture includes an Application Load Balancer on the front end and uses multiple target groups to route traffic. A DevOps engineer must collect application and access logs. The DevOps engineer then needs to send the logs to an Amazon S3 bucket for near-real-time analysis. Which combination of steps must the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在部署亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）集群以运行其工作负载。该公司的架构将在集 群上运行多个 ECS 服务。架构前端包含一个应用负载均衡器，并使用多个目标组来路由流量。 DevOps 工程师必须收集应用程序和访问日志。然后，该工程师需要将这些日志发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶， 以便进行近乎实时的分析。 DevOps 工程师必须采取哪些步骤组合才能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Download the Amazon CloudWatch Logs container instance from AWS. Configure this instance as a task. Update the application service definitions to include the logging task.","B":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch Logs agent on the ECS instances. Change the logging driver in the ECS task definition to awslogs.","C":"Use Amazon EventBridge to schedule an AWS Lambda function that will run every 60 seconds and will run the Amazon CloudWatch Logs create-export-task command. Then point the output to the logging S3 bucket.","D":"Activate access logging on the ALB. Then point the ALB directly to the logging S3 bucket.","E":"Activate access logging on the target groups that the ECS services use. Then send the logs directly to the logging S3 bucket.","F":"Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream that has a destination of the logging S3 bucket. Then create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs subscription filter for Kinesis Data Firehose."},"options_zh":{"A":"从 AWS 下载 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 容器实例。将此实例配置为任务。更新应用程序服务定义以包 含日志记录任务。","B":"在 ECS 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 代理。更改日志驱动程序在 ECS 任务定义到 awslogs。","C":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 安排一个每 60 秒运行一次的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数将运行 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 的 create-export-task 命令。然后将输出指向日志 S3 存储桶。","D":"在应用负载均衡器（ALB）上启用访问日志记录。然后将 ALB 直接指向日志记录的 S3 存储桶。","E":"在 ECS 服务所使用的目标组上启用访问日志记录功能。然后将日志直接发送到日志记录 S3 存储桶。","F":"创建一个将日志 S3 存储桶作为目的地的 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 交付流。然后为 Kinesis Data Firehose 创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 订阅筛选器。"},"answer":["B","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The task is to collect both ECS application logs and ALB access logs and land them in S3 for near-real-time analysis. (B) Setting the awslogs log driver in the ECS task definition logConfiguration ships container STDOUT/STDERR to CloudWatch Logs, the documented way to centralize ECS application logs and the prerequisite for the near-real-time S3 path. (D) Access logging is an attribute of the Application Load Balancer itself; when enabled it writes access logs directly to a specified S3 bucket, satisfying the access-log requirement. (F) Creating a Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream with an S3 destination and attaching a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to it is AWS's documented near-real-time pipeline from CloudWatch Logs to S3 - the CloudWatch Logs S3-export docs explicitly recommend subscriptions over create-export-task for near-real-time, continuous delivery. Together, D handles access logs and B->F handles application logs, both reaching S3 near-real-time.","explanation_zh":"需求是同時收集 ECS 應用程式日誌與 ALB 存取日誌，並送到 S3 進行近即時分析。(B) 在 ECS task definition 的 logConfiguration 設定 awslogs log driver，可將容器的 STDOUT/STDERR 傳送至 CloudWatch Logs，這是集中化 ECS 應用程式日誌的官方做法，也是近即時送入 S3 路徑的前置條件。(D) 存取日誌（access logging）是 Application Load Balancer 本身的屬性；啟用後會直接將存取日誌寫入指定的 S3 bucket，滿足存取日誌需求。(F) 建立以 S3 為目的地的 Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream，並對其建立 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter，是 AWS 官方文件記載的「CloudWatch Logs 到 S3 的近即時管線」；CloudWatch Logs 的 S3 匯出文件明確建議近即時與持續傳遞應使用 subscriptions 而非 create-export-task。綜合來看，D 處理存取日誌，B->F 處理應用程式日誌，兩者都能近即時抵達 S3。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no downloadable 'CloudWatch Logs container instance' artifact that you configure as a task and attach to service definitions; this is a fabricated mechanism. ECS application logs are shipped via the awslogs (or FireLens/awsfirelens) log driver, not a separate logging task image.","why_zh":"不存在可下載並設定為 task、再掛到 service 定義上的「CloudWatch Logs container instance」；這是杜撰的機制。ECS 應用程式日誌是透過 awslogs（或 FireLens/awsfirelens）log driver 傳送，而非另起一個 logging task 映像。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs create-export-task is a batch export: data can take up to 12 hours to become available, and the docs explicitly advise against using it for continuous/near-real-time delivery, recommending subscriptions instead. Scheduling it every 60 seconds is unworkable (one active export task per account) and is not near-real-time.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs create-export-task 是批次匯出：資料最多可能需 12 小時才可匯出，且文件明確不建議用於持續/近即時傳遞，而建議改用 subscriptions。每 60 秒排程執行不可行（每帳戶僅能有一個進行中的匯出任務），也不是近即時。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Access logging is an attribute of the load balancer, not of target groups. Target groups do not emit access logs, so 'activate access logging on the target groups' is not a real configuration; the correct option is D (enable it on the ALB).","why_zh":"存取日誌是負載平衡器（load balancer）的屬性，而非 target group 的屬性。Target group 不會產生存取日誌，因此「在 target group 啟用 access logging」並非真實設定；正確選項是 D（在 ALB 上啟用）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/using_awslogs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/specify-log-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-access-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/enable-access-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/writing-with-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/S3Export.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":33,"question_en":"A company that uses electronic health records is running a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances with an Amazon Linux operating system. As part of patient privacy requirements, the company must ensure continuous compliance for patches for operating system and applications running on the EC2 instances. How can the deployments of the operating system and application patches be automated using a default and custom repository?","question_zh":"一家使用电子健康记录的公司正在运行一批搭载亚马逊 Linux 操作系统的亚马逊 EC2 实例。作为患者隐 私要求的一部分，该公司必须确保其 EC2 实例上运行的操作系统和应用程序的补丁能够持续合规。 如何使用默认和自定义存储库来自动部署操作系统和应用程序补丁？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager to create a new patch baseline including the custom repository. Run the AWS-RunPatchBaseline document using the run command to verify and install patches.","B":"Use AWS Direct Connect to integrate the corporate repository and deploy the patches using Amazon CloudWatch scheduled events, then use the CloudWatch dashboard to create reports.","C":"Use yum-config-manager to add the custom repository under /etc/yum.repos.d and run yum- config-manager-enable to activate the repository.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager to create a new patch baseline including the corporate repository. Run the AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline document using the run command to verify and install patches."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 创建一个新的补丁基准，包括自定义存储库。使用 run 命令运行 AWS- RunPatchBaseline 文档以验证并安装补丁。","B":"使用 AWS Direct Connect 集成企业存储库，并通过 Amazon CloudWatch 定期事件部署补丁，然后使 用 CloudWatch 控制面板创建报告。","C":"使用 yum-config-manager 在 /etc/yum.repos.d 下添加自定义存储库，并运行 yum-config-manager -- enable 来激活该存储库。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 创建一个新的补丁基准，包括企业存储库。使用 run 命令运行 AWS- AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline 文档以验证并安装补丁。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager automates OS and application patching for EC2 fleets and continuously tracks patch compliance, which satisfies the continuous-compliance requirement. To patch from a source other than the node's default repositories (such as a corporate/custom repo) while still using the defaults, you specify alternative patch source repositories when you CREATE A CUSTOM PATCH BASELINE; the AWS docs note that to keep applying default-repo updates you also list the default repositories in the alternative source configuration, so both default and custom repositories are used. You then run patching by executing the AWS-RunPatchBaseline SSM document via Run Command, which scans (verifies) and installs both operating-system and application patches on Amazon Linux/Linux nodes and reports compliance back to Patch Manager. This matches option A exactly. Option D is wrong because AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline is the name of a PREDEFINED PATCH BASELINE resource, not a runnable SSM document; the recommended runnable patch documents are AWS-RunPatchBaseline, AWS-RunPatchBaselineAssociation, AWS-RunPatchBaselineWithHooks, AWS-ConfigureWindowsUpdate, and AWS-InstallWindowsUpdates, so you cannot 'run' AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline via Run Command.","explanation_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Patch Manager 可自動化 EC2 機群的作業系統與應用程式修補，並持續追蹤修補合規狀態，符合題目所要求的持續合規。若要從節點預設儲存庫以外的來源（例如企業/自訂 repo）進行修補，同時仍套用預設儲存庫，您需在「建立自訂 patch baseline」時指定替代的修補來源儲存庫；AWS 文件指出，若要持續套用預設 repo 的更新，必須在替代來源設定中一併列出預設儲存庫，如此預設與自訂儲存庫皆會被使用。接著透過 Run Command 執行 AWS-RunPatchBaseline SSM document 來進行修補，它會掃描（驗證）並安裝 Amazon Linux/Linux 節點上的作業系統與應用程式修補，並將合規結果回報給 Patch Manager。這完全對應選項 A。選項 D 錯誤，因為 AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline 是「預先定義的 patch baseline」資源名稱，並非可執行的 SSM document；建議用於修補的可執行 document 為 AWS-RunPatchBaseline、AWS-RunPatchBaselineAssociation、AWS-RunPatchBaselineWithHooks、AWS-ConfigureWindowsUpdate 與 AWS-InstallWindowsUpdates，因此無法以 Run Command 執行 AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Direct Connect is a dedicated network connectivity service, not a patch-distribution or automation mechanism, and CloudWatch scheduled events plus a dashboard do not scan, install, or report OS/application patch compliance. This ignores the purpose-built Patch Manager and cannot deliver continuous patch compliance.","why_zh":"AWS Direct Connect 是專用網路連線服務，並非修補散佈或自動化機制；CloudWatch 排程事件加儀表板無法掃描、安裝或回報作業系統/應用程式的修補合規。此選項忽略專為修補設計的 Patch Manager，也無法達成持續修補合規。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Manually editing /etc/yum.repos.d and running yum-config-manager on each instance is a per-node manual step, not centralized AWS automation, and provides no fleet-wide baseline approval rules or continuous compliance tracking/reporting. It bypasses Systems Manager Patch Manager entirely.","why_zh":"在每台執行個體手動編輯 /etc/yum.repos.d 並執行 yum-config-manager 屬於逐台手動操作，並非集中式 AWS 自動化，且無法跨機群提供 baseline 核准規則或持續合規追蹤/回報，完全略過 Systems Manager Patch Manager。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline is a predefined patch baseline resource (it resolves to a patchbaseline/pb-... ARN), not an SSM Run Command document you can 'run.' The runnable patching document that scans and installs patches is AWS-RunPatchBaseline. So although the custom-baseline idea is partly right, the execution action described is technically invalid.","why_zh":"AWS-AmazonLinuxDefaultPatchBaseline 是「預先定義的 patch baseline」資源（會對應到 patchbaseline/pb-... ARN），並非可被「執行」的 SSM Run Command document。可掃描並安裝修補的可執行 document 是 AWS-RunPatchBaseline。因此即使自訂 baseline 的概念部分正確，此處描述的執行動作在技術上並不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-alternative-source-repository.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-aws-runpatchbaseline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-ssm-documents.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-predefined-and-custom-patch-baselines.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":34,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CodePipeline to automate its release pipeline. AWS CodeDeploy is being used in the pipeline to deploy an application to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) using the blue/ green deployment model. The company wants to implement scripts to test the green version of the application before shifting traffic. These scripts will complete in 5 minutes or less. If errors are discovered during these tests, the application must be rolled back. Which strategy will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 来自动化其发布流程。在该流程中，AWS CodeDeploy 用于将应用 程序部署到 Amazon Elastic Container Service （Amazon ECS），采用蓝/绿部署模式。该公司希望在切换 流量之前实施脚本对绿色版本的应用程序进行测试，这些脚本将在 5 分钟内完成。如果在这些测试中发 现错误，必须回滚应用程序。 哪种策略能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add a stage to the CodePipeline pipeline between the source and deploy stages. Use AWS CodeBuild to create a runtime environment and build commands in the buildspec file to invoke test scripts. If errors are found, use the aws deploy stop-deployment command to stop the deployment.","B":"Add a stage to the CodePipeline pipeline between the source and deploy stages. Use this stage to invoke an AWS Lambda function that will run the test scripts. If errors are found, use the aws deploy stop-deployment command to stop the deployment.","C":"Add a hooks section to the CodeDeploy AppSpec file. Use the AfterAllowTestTraffic lifecycle event to invoke an AWS Lambda function to run the test scripts. If errors are found, exit the Lambda function with an error to initiate rollback.","D":"Add a hooks section to the CodeDeploy AppSpec file. Use the AfterAllowTraffic lifecycle event to invoke the test scripts. If errors are found, use the aws deploy stop-deployment CLI command to stop the deployment."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CodePipeline 管道的源代码和部署阶段之间添加一个阶段。使用 AWS CodeBuild 创建运行时环境， 并在 buildspec 文件中编写构建命令以调用测试脚本。如果发现错误，请使用 aws deploy stop- deployment 命令停止部署。","B":"在 CodePipeline 管道的源代码和部署阶段之间添加一个阶段。使用此阶段调用一个 AWS Lambda 函 数来运行测试脚本。如果发现错误，请使用 aws deploy stop-deployment 命令停止部署。","C":"在 CodeDeploy AppSpec 文件中添加一个钩子部分。使用 AfterAllowTestTraffic 生命周期事件来调用 一个 AWS Lambda 函数以运行测试脚本。如果发现错误，让 Lambda 函数以错误退出，从而启动 回滚。","D":"在 CodeDeploy AppSpec 文件中添加一个钩子部分。使用 AfterAllowTraffic 生命周期事件来调用测试 脚本。如果发现错误，请使用 aws deploy stop-deployment CLI 命令停止部署。 部署。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"For a CodeDeploy ECS blue/green deployment, the AppSpec 'hooks' section is the native mechanism to validate the green (replacement) task set before production traffic is shifted. The AfterAllowTestTraffic lifecycle event runs after the test listener serves traffic to the replacement task set but before production traffic is shifted, which exactly matches the requirement to test the green version first. ECS deployment hooks invoke a Lambda function, and AWS documentation explicitly states that the results of a hook function at this point can trigger a rollback. The Lambda reports Succeeded or Failed via putLifecycleEventHookExecutionStatus; a Failed result (exiting the function with an error) causes CodeDeploy to roll back automatically. The 5-minute test scripts are well within the 1-hour hook timeout, so option C meets every requirement.","explanation_zh":"對於 CodeDeploy ECS blue/green 部署，AppSpec 的 'hooks' 區段是在切換正式流量前驗證 green（replacement）task set 的原生機制。AfterAllowTestTraffic 生命週期事件會在 test listener 將流量送往 replacement task set 之後、但在正式流量切換之前執行，正好符合「先測試 green 版本」的需求。ECS 部署 hooks 會呼叫 AWS Lambda function，且 AWS 文件明確指出此事件的 hook function 結果可觸發 rollback。Lambda 透過 putLifecycleEventHookExecutionStatus 回報 Succeeded 或 Failed；回報 Failed（以錯誤結束 function）會讓 CodeDeploy 自動 rollback。5 分鐘的測試指令碼遠低於 1 小時的 hook 逾時上限，因此選項 C 完全滿足所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Placing a CodeBuild test stage between the source and deploy stages runs the tests before the green task set is even deployed, so there is no green version to validate yet. Also, aws deploy stop-deployment merely halts a deployment; at this point in the pipeline the CodeDeploy deployment has not started, and stop-deployment is not the documented rollback mechanism.","why_zh":"在 source 與 deploy 階段之間放一個 CodeBuild 測試階段，會在 green task set 尚未部署前就執行測試，根本沒有 green 版本可驗證。此外 aws deploy stop-deployment 只是停止部署，而此時 pipeline 中 CodeDeploy 部署尚未開始，stop-deployment 也不是文件所載的 rollback 機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same timing flaw as A: a Lambda test stage between source and deploy executes before the green task set is created, so it cannot test the running green application before traffic shift. stop-deployment also does not roll back to the prior version, and there is no in-progress deployment to stop at this stage.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的時序缺陷：在 source 與 deploy 之間的 Lambda 測試階段會在 green task set 建立前執行，因此無法在流量切換前測試正在運行的 green 應用程式。stop-deployment 也不會回滾到舊版本，且此階段並無進行中的部署可停止。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The AfterAllowTraffic lifecycle event runs after production traffic has already been shifted to the green task set, so real users would hit the new version before testing completes, violating 'test before shifting traffic.' It also relies on the aws deploy stop-deployment CLI command rather than the hook's Succeeded/Failed result, which is not the documented rollback mechanism for ECS hooks.","why_zh":"AfterAllowTraffic 生命週期事件是在正式流量已切換到 green task set 之後才執行，真實使用者在測試完成前就已存取新版本，違反「在切換流量前測試」的要求。它還依賴 aws deploy stop-deployment CLI 指令，而非 hook 的 Succeeded/Failed 結果，這並非 ECS hooks 文件所載的 rollback 機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/tutorial-ecs-deployment-with-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-steps-ecs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":35,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Storage Gateway in file gateway mode in front of an Amazon S3 bucket that is used by multiple resources. In the morning when business begins, users do not see the objects processed by a third party the previous evening. When a DevOps engineer looks directly at the S3 bucket, the data is there, but it is missing in Storage Gateway. Which solution ensures that all the updated third-party files are available in the morning?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 存储网关的文件网关模式置于一个由多个资源使用的 Amazon S3 存储桶之前。每天早上 业务开始时，用户看不到前一天晚上由第三方处理的对象。当一名 DevOps 工程师直接查看 S3 存储桶时， 数据在那里，但在存储网关中却不见了。 哪种解决方案能确保所有更新的第三方文件在早上都可用？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a nightly Amazon EventBridge event to invoke an AWS Lambda function to run the RefreshCache command for Storage Gateway.","B":"Instruct the third party to put data into the S3 bucket using AWS Transfer for SFTP.","C":"Modify Storage Gateway to run in volume gateway mode.","D":"Use S3 Same-Region Replication to replicate any changes made directly in the S3 bucket to Storage Gateway."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个每晚触发的 Amazon EventBridge 事件，以调用 AWS Lambda 函数来运行 Storage Gateway 的刷新缓存命令。","B":"指示第三方使用 AWS Transfer for SFTP 将数据放入 S3 存储桶。","C":"将存储网关修改为卷网关模式运行。","D":"使用 S3 同区域复制功能，将直接在 S3 存储桶中所做的任何更改复制到存储网关。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"An S3 File Gateway (file gateway mode) maintains a cached inventory of the objects in its backing S3 bucket so it can serve NFS/SMB clients with low latency. When a third party writes objects directly into the S3 bucket (outside the file-share workflow between the gateway and S3), the gateway's cached inventory is not automatically aware of them, so users do not see the new files even though they exist in S3. The RefreshCache API finds objects that were added, removed, or replaced in the bucket since the gateway last listed it and updates the cached inventory accordingly. AWS documentation explicitly describes configuring an automated cache refresh schedule by having a scheduled Amazon EventBridge/CloudWatch rule invoke an AWS Lambda function that calls RefreshCache, which is exactly the recommended pattern when bucket contents are updated directly outside the gateway. A nightly EventBridge-scheduled Lambda running RefreshCache therefore ensures the third party's evening uploads are reflected in the gateway by morning.","explanation_zh":"S3 File Gateway (file gateway mode) 會為其後端 S3 bucket 維護一份物件的快取清單 (cached inventory)，以低延遲地為 NFS/SMB 用戶端提供服務。當第三方直接將物件寫入 S3 bucket (繞過 gateway 與 S3 之間的 file-share 工作流程) 時，gateway 的快取清單不會自動得知這些物件，因此即使檔案已存在於 S3，使用者仍看不到。RefreshCache API 會找出自 gateway 上次列出 bucket 以來新增、移除或替換的物件，並據此更新快取清單。AWS 官方文件明確說明可透過排程的 Amazon EventBridge/CloudWatch rule 來觸發 AWS Lambda function 呼叫 RefreshCache，以設定自動快取重新整理排程，這正是當 bucket 內容在 gateway 之外被直接更新時的建議做法。因此，使用 EventBridge 每晚排程觸發執行 RefreshCache 的 Lambda，即可確保第三方傍晚上傳的檔案在隔天早上能在 gateway 中呈現。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Switching the third party to AWS Transfer for SFTP still results in objects being written directly into the S3 bucket, bypassing the gateway's NFS/SMB workflow. The gateway's cached inventory would remain stale, so the new files would still not appear to gateway users. It changes the upload mechanism but does not refresh the cache.","why_zh":"改用 AWS Transfer for SFTP 仍然是將物件直接寫入 S3 bucket，繞過 gateway 的 NFS/SMB 工作流程。gateway 的快取清單仍會過時，新檔案對 gateway 使用者依然不會出現。它只改變上傳機制，並未重新整理快取。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Volume Gateway presents iSCSI block storage backed by S3 (stored/cached volumes), not a file interface that maps S3 bucket objects to readable files. It is a different gateway type with a different data model, would break the existing file-based access pattern, and still would not surface objects written directly into the S3 bucket as files.","why_zh":"Volume Gateway 提供的是由 S3 支援的 iSCSI 區塊儲存 (stored/cached volumes)，而非將 S3 bucket 物件對應為可讀檔案的檔案介面。它是不同的 gateway 類型、採用不同的資料模型，會破壞既有的以檔案為基礎的存取方式，也無法把直接寫入 S3 bucket 的物件以檔案形式呈現。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Same-Region Replication replicates objects between two S3 buckets; a File Gateway is not an S3 replication destination. You cannot 'replicate changes into Storage Gateway' via SRR, and it would not refresh the gateway's cached inventory, so the files would remain invisible to gateway users. This is not a valid mechanism for the problem.","why_zh":"S3 Same-Region Replication 是在兩個 S3 bucket 之間複製物件；File Gateway 並非 S3 複寫目的地。無法透過 SRR 將變更「複寫到 Storage Gateway」，它也不會重新整理 gateway 的快取清單，因此檔案仍對 gateway 使用者不可見。這並不是解決此問題的有效機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/filegateway/latest/files3/refresh-cache.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/APIReference/API_RefreshCache.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":36,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to back up sensitive Amazon S3 objects that are stored within an S3 bucket with a private bucket policy using S3 cross-Region replication functionality. The objects need to be copied to a target bucket in a different AWS Region and account. Which combination of actions should be performed to enable this replication? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要使用 S3 跨区域复制功能，将存储在具有私有存储桶策略的 S3 存储桶中的敏感对 象进行备份。这些对象需要复制到不同 AWS 区域和账户中的目标存储桶。 应执行哪些操作组合才能启用此复制？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a replication IAM role in the source account","B":"Create a replication IAM role in the target account.","C":"Add statements to the source bucket policy allowing the replication IAM role to replicate objects.","D":"Add statements to the target bucket policy allowing the replication IAM role to replicate objects.","E":"Create a replication rule in the source bucket to enable the replication.","F":"Create a replication rule in the target bucket to enable the replication."},"options_zh":{"A":"在源账户中创建一个复制 IAM 角色","B":"在目标账户中创建一个用于复制的 IAM 角色。","C":"向源存储桶策略添加语句，允许复制 IAM 角色复制对象。","D":"向目标存储桶策略添加语句，允许复制 IAM 角色复制对象。","E":"在源存储桶中创建一个复制规则以启用复制功能。","F":"在目标存储桶中创建一个复制规则以启用复制。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"For S3 cross-Region, cross-account replication, AWS docs prescribe exactly three actions. (A) The IAM role that Amazon S3 assumes to read and replicate objects is created in the SOURCE account and referenced in the source bucket's replication configuration; the cross-account walkthrough explicitly uses the source-account profile (acctA) to create this role. (E) Replication rules are always added to the SOURCE bucket ('When you configure replication, you add replication rules to the source bucket') to define what gets replicated and the destination. (D) Because the destination bucket is owned by a different account, the destination/target bucket owner must add a bucket policy on the TARGET bucket granting the source account's replication IAM role permission to perform s3:ReplicateObject and s3:ReplicateDelete (plus s3:GetBucketVersioning / s3:PutBucketVersioning). The 'private bucket policy' on the source is a red herring: the source bucket needs no replication-specific bucket-policy statements because the IAM role itself carries the read/list permissions.","explanation_zh":"對於 S3 跨區域且跨帳戶的 replication，AWS 文件明確規定三個動作。(A) Amazon S3 用來讀取並複寫物件而擔任 (assume) 的 IAM role 建立於「來源 (source) 帳戶」，並在來源 bucket 的 replication configuration 中被引用；跨帳戶逐步教學明確使用來源帳戶設定檔 (acctA) 來建立此 role。(E) Replication rule 一律加在「來源 bucket」上（「When you configure replication, you add replication rules to the source bucket」），用以定義要複寫哪些物件及目的地。(D) 由於目的 bucket 屬於不同帳戶，目的/目標 bucket 擁有者必須在「目標 (target) bucket」上加入 bucket policy，授予來源帳戶的 replication IAM role 執行 s3:ReplicateObject 與 s3:ReplicateDelete（以及 s3:GetBucketVersioning / s3:PutBucketVersioning）的權限。題目中對來源「private bucket policy」的描述是干擾項：來源 bucket 不需要任何 replication 專屬的 bucket policy 陳述句，因為 IAM role 本身已帶有讀取/列出權限。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The replication IAM role must be created in the SOURCE account (Amazon S3 in the source account assumes it to read source objects and write replicas), not in the target account. The cross-account walkthrough uses the acctA (source) profile to create the role.","why_zh":"Replication IAM role 必須建立在「來源帳戶」（來源帳戶的 Amazon S3 擔任此 role 以讀取來源物件並寫入複本），而非目標帳戶。跨帳戶教學使用 acctA（來源）設定檔來建立 role。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"No replication-specific statements are needed on the SOURCE bucket policy. Amazon S3's read/list/replicate permissions come from the IAM role's permissions policy, not from a source bucket policy. The cross-account grant is required only on the destination bucket.","why_zh":"「來源」bucket policy 不需要任何 replication 專屬陳述句。Amazon S3 的讀取/列出/複寫權限來自 IAM role 的權限政策，而非來源 bucket policy。跨帳戶授權僅需加在目的 bucket 上。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Replication rules are configured on the SOURCE bucket only, never on the target/destination bucket. The destination bucket only needs a bucket policy granting cross-account access, not a replication rule.","why_zh":"Replication rule 只設定在「來源」bucket，絕不設在目標/目的 bucket。目的 bucket 只需要一個授予跨帳戶存取的 bucket policy，而非 replication rule。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-walkthrough-2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/setting-repl-config-perm-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-walkthrough1.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":37,"question_en":"A company has multiple member accounts that are part of an organization in AWS Organizations. The security team needs to review every Amazon EC2 security group and their inbound and outbound rules. The security team wants to programmatically retrieve this information from the member accounts using an AWS Lambda function in the management account of the organization. Which combination of access changes will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中拥有多个成员账户，这些账户属于同一个组织。安全团队需要审查每个 Amazon EC2 安全组及其入站和出站规则。安全团队希望使用组织管理账户中的 AWS Lambda 函数从成员 账户中以编程方式检索此信息。 哪些访问更改的组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a trust relationship that allows users in the member accounts to assume the management account IAM role.","B":"Create a trust relationship that allows users in the management account to assume the IAM roles of the member accounts.","C":"Create an IAM role in each member account that has access to the AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess managed policy.","D":"Create an IAM role in each member account to allow the sts:AssumeRole action against the management account IAM role's ARN.","E":"Create an IAM role in the management account that allows the sts:AssumeRole action against the member account IAM role's ARN.","F":"Create an IAM role in the management account that has access to the AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess managed policy."},"options_zh":{"A":"建立一种信任关系，使成员账户中的用户能够承担管理账户的 IAM 角色。","B":"建立一种信任关系，使管理账户中的用户能够承担目标账户中的 IAM 角色。 会员账户。","C":"在每个成员账户中创建一个具有访问 AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess 管理策略权限的 IAM 角色。","D":"在每个成员账户中创建一个 IAM 角色，以允许针对管理账户 IAM 角色的 ARN 执行 sts: AssumeRole 操作。","E":"在管理账户中创建一个 IAM 角色，该角色允许对成员账户 IAM 角色的 ARN 执行 sts: AssumeRole 操作。","F":"在管理账户中创建一个具有访问 AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess 管理策略权限的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"This is the canonical cross-account IAM role delegation pattern described in the AWS 'Originating / Destination' tutorial. The EC2 security groups live in the member accounts, so each member account is the Destination (trusting/resource) account and the management account that runs the Lambda function is the Originating (trusted/calling) account. Three changes are required. (C) In each member account, create an IAM role and attach AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess, because the DescribeSecurityGroups permissions must reside where the EC2 resources actually are. (B) That member-account role needs a trust policy that names the management account as a trusted entity, so management-account principals are allowed to assume it. (E) In the management account, create the Lambda execution role with an identity-based policy granting sts:AssumeRole on the member-account role ARNs; AssumeRole succeeds only when BOTH the target role's trust policy permits the caller AND the calling principal has an sts:AssumeRole permission. The AWS delegation tutorial shows exactly this split: the Destination account creates the role with a permissions policy plus a trust policy naming the Originating account, and the Originating-account principal gets an inline Allow of sts:AssumeRole on the Destination role ARN.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS 官方「Originating / Destination」教學所描述的標準跨帳戶 IAM role 委派模式。EC2 security groups 位於 member accounts，因此每個 member account 是 Destination（受信任、擁有資源/trusting）帳戶，而執行 Lambda function 的 management account 是 Originating（被信任的呼叫端/trusted）帳戶。需要三項變更。(C) 在每個 member account 建立 IAM role 並附加 AmazonEC2ReadOnlyAccess，因為 DescribeSecurityGroups 權限必須位於 EC2 資源實際所在的帳戶。(B) 該 member-account role 需要 trust policy，將 management account 指定為受信任實體，才能允許 management account 的 principal 去 assume 它。(E) 在 management account 建立 Lambda execution role，並以 identity-based policy 授予對 member-account role ARN 的 sts:AssumeRole 權限；AssumeRole 必須同時滿足目標 role 的 trust policy 允許呼叫者，以及呼叫端 principal 擁有 sts:AssumeRole 權限，兩者缺一不可。AWS 委派教學正是這樣分工：Destination 帳戶建立帶有 permissions policy 與指定 Originating 帳戶之 trust policy 的 role，而 Originating 帳戶的 principal 取得對 Destination role ARN 的 Allow sts:AssumeRole。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Direction is reversed. This would let member-account users assume a role in the management account, but the Lambda runs IN the management account and must reach INTO the member accounts. The trust relationship must let the management account assume the member-account role, not the other way around.","why_zh":"方向相反。此選項讓 member-account 使用者去 assume management account 的 role，但 Lambda 是在 management account 執行，必須反向進入 member accounts。trust relationship 應允許 management account assume member-account 的 role，而非相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Backwards and redundant. The sts:AssumeRole identity-based permission belongs on the calling principal in the management (Originating) account, targeting the member-account role ARN. The member account is the resource side and does not need permission to call AssumeRole against the management account.","why_zh":"方向錯誤且多餘。sts:AssumeRole 的 identity-based 權限應放在 management（Originating）帳戶的呼叫 principal 上，並以 member-account role ARN 為目標。member account 是資源端，不需要取得對 management account 呼叫 AssumeRole 的權限。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"An EC2 read-only role in the management account only grants visibility into the management account's own EC2 resources. It cannot read security groups in the member accounts, which is the actual requirement. The read permissions must live in each member account (option C).","why_zh":"在 management account 建立 EC2 唯讀 role 只能看見 management account 自身的 EC2 資源，無法讀取 member accounts 的 security groups，而後者才是真正需求。讀取權限必須位於各 member account（即選項 C）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/tutorial_cross-account-with-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies-cross-account-resource-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_update-role-trust-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/lambda-intro-execution-role.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":38,"question_en":"A space exploration company receives telemetry data from multiple satellites. Small packets of data are received through Amazon API Gateway and are placed directly into an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queue. A custom application is subscribed to the queue and transforms the data into a standard format. Because of inconsistencies in the data that the satellites produce, the application is occasionally unable to transform the data. In these cases, the messages remain in the SQS queue. A DevOps engineer must develop a solution that retains the failed messages and makes them available to scientists for review and future processing. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家太空探索公司从多颗卫星接收遥测数据。通过亚马逊 API 网关接收到的小数据包直接放入亚马逊 简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）标准队列中。一个自定义应用程序订阅该队列，并将数据转换为标准格 式。 由于卫星生成的数据存在不一致的情况，应用程序有时无法转换这些数据。在这种情况下，消息会留 在 SQS 队列中。DevOps 工程师必须开发一个解决方案，将失败的消息保留下来，并提供给科学家进行 审查和未来的处理。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Lambda to poll the SQS queue and invoke a Lambda function to check whether the queue messages are valid. If validation fails, send a copy of the data that is not valid to an Amazon S3 bucket so that the scientists can review and correct the data. When the data is corrected, amend the message in the SQS queue by using a replay Lambda function with the corrected data.","B":"Convert the SQS standard queue to an SQS FIFO queue. Configure AWS Lambda to poll the SQS queue every 10 minutes by using an Amazon EventBridge schedule. Invoke the Lambda function to identify any messages with a SentTimestamp value that is older than 5 minutes, push the data to the same location as the application's output location, and remove the messages from the queue.","C":"Create an SQS dead-letter queue. Modify the existing queue by including a redrive policy that sets the Maximum Receives setting to 1 and sets the dead-letter queue ARN to the ARN of the newly created queue. Instruct the scientists to use the dead-letter queue to review the data that is not valid. Reprocess this data at a later time.","D":"Configure API Gateway to send messages to different SQS virtual queues that are named for each of the satellites. Update the application to use a new virtual queue for any data that it cannot transform, and send the message to the new virtual queue. Instruct the scientists to use the virtual queue to review the data that is not valid. Reprocess this data at a later time."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Lambda 以轮询 SQS 队列，并调用一个 Lambda 函数来检查队列消息是否有效。如果验证 失败，将无效的数据副本发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶，以便科学家进行审查和更正。当数据更正后， 使用带有更正数据的重放 Lambda 函数修改 SQS 队列中的消息。","B":"将 SQS 标准队列转换为 SQS FIFO 队列。使用 Amazon EventBridge 计划配置 AWS Lambda 每 10 分钟轮询一次 SQS 队列。调用 Lambda 函数以识别任何 SentTimestamp 值超过 5 分钟的消息，将 数据推送到与应用程序输出位置相同的位置，并从队列中删除这些消息。","C":"创建一个 SQS 死信队列。修改现有队列，添加重定向策略，将“最大接收次数”设置为 1，并将死 信队列的 ARN 设置为新创建队列的 ARN。指示科学家使用死信队列来审查无效的数据。稍后重 新处理这些数据。","D":"配置 API 网关，使其将消息发送到以每颗卫星命名的不同 SQS 虚拟队列。更新应用程序，使其对 于无法转换的任何数据使用新的虚拟队列，并将消息发送到该新虚拟队列。指示科学家使用该虚 拟队列来审查无效的数据。稍后重新处理这些数据。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon SQS dead-letter queues (DLQs) are the AWS-native, purpose-built feature for retaining messages a consumer cannot process so they can be isolated for later review and reprocessing. You first create a new queue, then add a redrive policy to the source queue that names the DLQ ARN and sets maxReceiveCount (the console's 'Maximum Receives'). When the custom transform repeatedly fails on malformed telemetry, the message is received but never deleted; once the receive count exceeds maxReceiveCount, SQS automatically moves it to the DLQ, where scientists can inspect the bad data and later redrive it. The AWS docs explicitly state that setting maxReceiveCount to a low value such as 1 moves a message to the DLQ after a single failed attempt, and that DLQs exist precisely to isolate unconsumed messages for diagnosis and redrive. This is configuration-only with no custom code. The other options either invent a non-existent ability to edit an SQS message in place (A), are technically impossible/incorrect (B: you cannot convert a standard queue to FIFO in place, and selecting by SentTimestamp would also discard valid messages), or misuse the client-side Temporary Queue Client 'virtual queues' that API Gateway cannot natively target (D).","explanation_zh":"Amazon SQS dead-letter queue (DLQ) 是 AWS 原生、專門用來保留消費者無法處理之訊息的功能，將其隔離以供日後檢視與重新處理。做法是先建立一個新佇列，再於來源佇列加上 redrive policy，指定該 DLQ 的 ARN 並設定 maxReceiveCount（主控台中的 'Maximum Receives'）。當自訂轉換程式對格式錯誤的遙測資料反覆失敗時，訊息會被接收但不會被刪除；一旦接收次數超過 maxReceiveCount，SQS 會自動將其移至 DLQ，科學家可在此檢視壞資料並日後 redrive 重新處理。AWS 文件明確指出將 maxReceiveCount 設為像 1 這樣的低值，會在單次失敗後即把訊息移到 DLQ，且 DLQ 的存在正是為了隔離未消費訊息以利診斷與 redrive。此方案僅需設定、無需自訂程式碼。其他選項不是杜撰了原地編輯 SQS 訊息的能力（A），就是技術上不可行/錯誤（B：無法原地將 standard queue 轉成 FIFO，且以 SentTimestamp 篩選會連有效訊息一併丟棄），或誤用了 API Gateway 無法原生指向的用戶端 Temporary Queue Client『virtual queues』（D）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This rebuilds DLQ behavior with a custom Lambda poller, an S3 bucket, and a replay Lambda — far more code and operational overhead than the native DLQ feature. It is also technically muddled: SQS messages are immutable, so you cannot 'amend the message in the SQS queue' in place, and polling SQS with a Lambda to validate reinvents what an event source mapping plus a DLQ already do natively.","why_zh":"此方案用自訂 Lambda 輪詢器、S3 儲存桶與 replay Lambda 重新打造 DLQ 行為，程式碼與營運負擔遠高於原生 DLQ。技術上也含糊：SQS 訊息不可變，無法就地『修改 SQS 佇列中的訊息』，而用 Lambda 輪詢 SQS 驗證等於重新發明事件來源映射加 DLQ 已原生提供的功能。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"You cannot convert an existing standard queue into a FIFO queue in place; FIFO requires creating a new queue. Worse, it selects messages purely by SentTimestamp age rather than by transform failure, so it would move every message older than 5 minutes — including valid, still-processable ones — to the output location. It does not distinguish failed messages at all.","why_zh":"無法原地將現有 standard queue 轉成 FIFO queue；FIFO 需新建佇列。更糟的是它僅以 SentTimestamp 的時間篩選訊息，而非依轉換失敗，會把所有超過 5 分鐘的訊息（含仍可處理的有效訊息）都移到輸出位置，完全無法辨別失敗訊息。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SQS 'virtual queues' are a client-side construct of the awslabs Amazon SQS Temporary Queue Client (a Java library for request-response messaging over a single host queue), not a server-side feature that API Gateway can route to, and not a mechanism for capturing transform failures. It misuses an unrelated library feature and provides none of the durable, native failed-message retention/redrive a DLQ does.","why_zh":"SQS『virtual queues』是 awslabs Amazon SQS Temporary Queue Client（用於在單一主機佇列上做請求-回應的 Java 函式庫）的用戶端構造，並非 API Gateway 可路由的伺服器端功能，也不是捕捉轉換失敗的機制。此方案誤用了不相關的函式庫功能，無法提供 DLQ 那種持久、原生的失敗訊息保留/redrive。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-dead-letter-queues.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-configure-dead-letter-queue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-temporary-queues.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":39,"question_en":"A company wants to use AWS CloudFormation for infrastructure deployment. The company has strict tagging and resource requirements and wants to limit the deployment to two Regions. Developers will need to deploy multiple versions of the same application. Which solution ensures resources are deployed in accordance with company policy?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用 AWS CloudFormation 进行基础设施部署。该公司有严格的标签和资源要求，并希望 将部署限制在两个区域。开发人员需要部署同一应用程序的多个版本。 哪种解决方案能确保资源的部署符合公司政策？","options_en":{"A":"Create AWS Trusted Advisor checks to find and remediate unapproved CloudFormation StackSets.","B":"Create a CloudFormation drift detection operation to find and remediate unapproved CloudFormation StackSets.","C":"Create CloudFormation StackSets with approved CloudFormation templates.","D":"Create AWS Service Catalog products with approved CloudFormation templates."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建 AWS Trusted Advisor 检查，以查找并修复未经批准的 CloudFormation StackSets。","B":"创建一个 CloudFormation 漂移检测操作，以查找并修复未经批准的 CloudFormation 资源。 堆栈集","C":"使用经批准的 CloudFormation 模板创建 CloudFormation 栈集。","D":"使用经批准的 CloudFormation 模板创建 AWS 服务目录产品。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Service Catalog is purpose-built for this scenario. Administrators create products by importing approved CloudFormation templates ('standardized and pre-approved templates'), so only sanctioned infrastructure can be launched. Governance controls enforce company policy: TagOptions and template/launch constraints enforce strict tagging and resource requirements that propagate to provisioned resources, and a Stack Set constraint lets admins specify exactly which Regions a product deploys to ('In Region settings, choose the geographic regions to deploy products'), satisfying the 'limit to two Regions' requirement. Service Catalog also provides built-in versioning: 'Service Catalog allows you to manage multiple versions of the products in your catalog,' and each new version is automatically distributed to entitled users who choose which version to launch, satisfying 'deploy multiple versions of the same application.' This single service simultaneously meets every requirement, which the other options cannot.","explanation_zh":"AWS Service Catalog 正是為此情境設計。管理員透過匯入已核准的 CloudFormation 範本（『標準化且預先核准的範本』）來建立 product，因此只能啟動經核准的基礎設施。治理控制可強制執行公司政策：TagOptions 與 template/launch constraints 可強制套用嚴格的標記與資源需求並傳播至佈建的資源，而 Stack Set constraint 讓管理員精確指定 product 部署到哪些 Region（『在 Region settings 選擇要部署 product 的地理區域』），滿足『限制兩個 Region』的需求。Service Catalog 也內建版本管理：『Service Catalog 允許你管理目錄中 product 的多個版本』，每個新版本會自動發布給有權限的使用者，由使用者自行選擇要啟動哪個版本，滿足『部署同一應用程式的多個版本』。此單一服務同時滿足所有需求，其他選項皆無法做到。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor has no check for 'unapproved CloudFormation StackSets' and cannot remediate them. Trusted Advisor provides best-practice checks (cost optimization, security, fault tolerance, service limits, performance), not governance enforcement of CloudFormation deployments. This is a reactive, non-existent control and addresses none of tagging, resource limits, region restriction, or versioning.","why_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 並沒有針對『未核准的 CloudFormation StackSets』的檢查，也無法修復它們。Trusted Advisor 提供最佳實務檢查（成本最佳化、安全、容錯、服務配額、效能），而非對 CloudFormation 部署的治理強制。這是一個反應式且不存在的控制，無法處理標記、資源限制、Region 限制或版本管理。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFormation drift detection finds differences between a stack's actual resource configuration and its template; it does not detect or remediate 'unapproved StackSets,' and it has no automatic remediation engine. It is a reactive, detective control, not a preventive governance mechanism, and addresses none of the policy requirements (approved templates, tagging, resource limits, regions, versions).","why_zh":"CloudFormation drift detection 用於找出 stack 實際資源組態與其範本之間的差異；它無法偵測或修復『未核准的 StackSets』，也沒有自動修復引擎。它是反應式的偵測控制，而非預防性的治理機制，且無法滿足任何政策需求（已核准範本、標記、資源限制、Region、版本）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudFormation StackSets deploy a stack across multiple accounts/Regions in a single operation, but they provide no self-service product catalog, no built-in version management for developers to launch multiple application versions, and no constraint-based enforcement of tagging/resource governance (a StackSet simply deploys whatever template is supplied). It addresses the multi-region piece but fails the 'multiple versions of the same application' and 'strict tagging/resource requirements' governance needs that Service Catalog provides (Service Catalog can itself use a Stack Set constraint to reach the two Regions).","why_zh":"CloudFormation StackSets 可在單一操作中跨多個帳戶/Region 部署 stack，但它不提供自助式 product catalog、不提供讓開發者啟動多個應用程式版本的內建版本管理，也不以 constraint 強制執行標記/資源治理（StackSet 只會部署所提供的範本）。它能處理多 Region 部分，但無法滿足『同一應用程式的多個版本』與『嚴格標記/資源需求』的治理需求，而 Service Catalog 能提供這些（Service Catalog 本身可使用 Stack Set constraint 部署到那兩個 Region）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/what-is_concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/constraints-stackset.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/managing-versions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/constraints-launch.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":40,"question_en":"A company requires that its internally facing web application be highly available. The architecture is made up of one Amazon EC2 web server instance and one NAT instance that provides outbound internet access for updates and accessing public data. Which combination of architecture adjustments should the company implement to achieve high availability? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司要求其内部使用的网络应用程序具有高可用性。其架构由一台亚马逊 EC2 网络服务器实例和 一台提供互联网出站访问以进行更新和访问公共数据的 NAT 实例组成。 公司应实施哪两种架构调整组合来实现高可用性？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add the NAT instance to an EC2 Auto Scaling group that spans multiple Availability Zones. Update the route tables.","B":"Create additional EC2 instances spanning multiple Availability Zones. Add an Application Load Balancer to split the load between them.","C":"Configure an Application Load Balancer in front of the EC2 instance. Configure Amazon CloudWatch alarms to recover the EC2 instance upon host failure.","D":"Replace the NAT instance with a NAT gateway in each Availability Zone. Update the route tables.","E":"Replace the NAT instance with a NAT gateway that spans multiple Availability Zones. Update the route tables."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 NAT 实例添加到跨越多个可用区的 EC2 自动扩展组中。更新路由表。","B":"创建跨越多个可用区的额外 EC2 实例。添加一个应用负载均衡器在它们之间分配负载。","C":"在 EC2 实例前配置应用负载均衡器。配置 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，在主机出现故障时恢复 EC2 实例。","D":"在每个可用区中用 NAT 网关替换 NAT 实例。更新路由表。","E":"用一个跨越多个可用区的 NAT 网关替换 NAT 实例。更新路由表。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The architecture has two single points of failure: one EC2 web server and one NAT instance. To make the web tier highly available, option B adds multiple EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones behind an Application Load Balancer, so traffic is distributed and the application survives an instance or AZ failure. To make outbound internet access highly available, option D replaces the single NAT instance with a NAT gateway in each Availability Zone and updates the route tables so each AZ's resources egress through their local NAT gateway. AWS documentation states 'Each NAT gateway is created in a specific Availability Zone and implemented with redundancy in that zone' and explicitly recommends 'create a NAT gateway in each Availability Zone' for a zone-independent, highly available design; it also recommends replacing a NAT instance with a NAT gateway. A single NAT gateway is zonal and does not span multiple AZs, so option E is technically inaccurate, and option C leaves a single EC2 instance (CloudWatch recover only restarts it in the same AZ), which is not multi-AZ HA.","explanation_zh":"此架構有兩個單點故障：一個 EC2 web 伺服器和一個 NAT instance。要讓 web 層高可用，選項 B 在多個 Availability Zone 部署多個 EC2 instance 並置於 Application Load Balancer 之後，可分散流量並在 instance 或 AZ 故障時繼續運作。要讓對外網路存取高可用，選項 D 以每個 Availability Zone 各一個 NAT gateway 取代單一 NAT instance，並更新 route table 讓各 AZ 的資源透過該 AZ 本地的 NAT gateway 出網。AWS 文件指出『每個 NAT gateway 建立在特定 Availability Zone 且在該 zone 內實作備援』，並明確建議『在每個 Availability Zone 建立一個 NAT gateway』以達成 zone-independent 的高可用設計，同時建議以 NAT gateway 取代 NAT instance。單一 NAT gateway 屬 zonal 不會跨多個 AZ，因此選項 E 在技術上不正確；選項 C 仍只有一個 EC2 instance（CloudWatch recover 僅在相同 AZ 重啟），並非跨多 AZ 的高可用。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS explicitly recommends replacing NAT instances with NAT gateways because gateways provide better availability with no administrative effort. Running a NAT instance in an Auto Scaling group across AZs does not automatically update VPC route tables on failover (it requires custom scripting/Lambda), so it is high-overhead and not the AWS-recommended HA pattern.","why_zh":"AWS 明確建議以 NAT gateway 取代 NAT instance，因為 gateway 提供更佳可用性且無需維運。將 NAT instance 放進跨 AZ 的 Auto Scaling group 在故障切換時無法自動更新 VPC route table（需自訂腳本/Lambda），屬高維運負擔且非 AWS 建議的 HA 模式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Putting an ALB in front of a single EC2 instance and using a CloudWatch recover alarm still leaves one instance as a single point of failure. Instance recovery (StatusCheckFailed_System) restarts the instance in the same Availability Zone on new hardware and does not provide multi-AZ high availability.","why_zh":"在單一 EC2 instance 前放 ALB 並用 CloudWatch recover 警報，仍只有一個 instance 為單點故障。Instance recovery（StatusCheckFailed_System）在相同 Availability Zone 以新硬體重啟 instance，並非跨多 AZ 的高可用。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A NAT gateway is created in a single specified Availability Zone and is implemented with redundancy only within that zone; it does not span multiple AZs. AWS guidance is to create one NAT gateway per AZ, so this option misdescribes how NAT gateways work.","why_zh":"NAT gateway 建立於單一指定的 Availability Zone，且僅在該 zone 內具備備援，並不會跨多個 AZ。AWS 的指引是每個 AZ 建立一個 NAT gateway，因此此選項錯誤描述了 NAT gateway 的運作方式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/nat-gateway-basics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/vpc-nat-comparison.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/cloudwatch-recovery.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":41,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is building a multistage pipeline with AWS CodePipeline to build, verify, stage, test, and deploy an application. A manual approval stage is required between the test stage and the deploy stage. The development team uses a custom chat tool with webhook support that requires near-real-time notifications. How should the DevOps engineer configure status updates for pipeline activity and approval requests to post to the chat tool?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 构建一个多阶段流水线，用于构建、验证、暂存、 测试和部署应用程序。在测试阶段和部署阶段之间需要一个手动审批阶段。开发团队使用一个具有 Webhook 支持的自定义聊天工具，该工具需要近乎实时的通知。 DevOps 工程师应如何配置管道活动和审批请求的状态更新，以便将其发布到聊天工具？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs subscription that filters on CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change. Publish subscription events to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the chat webhook URL to the SNS topic, and complete the subscription validation.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by AWS CloudTrail events. When a CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change event is detected, send the event details to the chat webhook URL.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that filters on CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change. Publish the events to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Create an AWS Lambda function that sends event details to the chat webhook URL. Subscribe the function to the SNS topic.","D":"Modify the pipeline code to send the event details to the chat webhook URL at the end of each stage. Parameterize the URL so that each pipeline can send to a different URL based on the pipeline environment."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 订阅，筛选条件为 CodePipeline 管道执行状态更改。将订阅事 件发布到 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题。将聊天网络钩子 URL 订阅 到 SNS 主题，并完成订阅验证。","B":"创建一个由 AWS CloudTrail 事件触发的 AWS Lambda 函数。当检测到 CodePipeline 管道执行状 态更改事件时，将事件详情发送至聊天网络钩子 URL。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，筛选 CodePipeline 管道执行状态更改事件。将事件发布到 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将事件详情发送到 聊天网络钩子 URL。将该函数订阅到 SNS 主题。","D":"修改管道代码，在每个阶段结束时将事件详情发送到聊天网络钩子 URL。对 URL 进行参数化， 以便每个管道都能根据管道环境发送到不同的 URL。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodePipeline sends 'CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change' events directly to Amazon EventBridge (source: aws.codepipeline) as a near-real-time stream, so an EventBridge rule is the correct, native trigger. EventBridge routes those events to targets such as Amazon SNS and AWS Lambda. Because a custom chat webhook cannot be a direct SNS subscriber (an HTTP/HTTPS subscription must answer the SNS SubscriptionConfirmation handshake, and SNS would deliver its own envelope rather than the JSON the chat tool expects), an AWS Lambda function subscribed to the SNS topic transforms the event into the webhook's expected payload and POSTs it over HTTPS. This decoupled EventBridge -> SNS -> Lambda -> webhook pattern handles both general pipeline activity and approval requests with low operational overhead and near-real-time delivery, which is exactly option C.","explanation_zh":"CodePipeline 會將「CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change」事件以近即時方式直接傳送到 Amazon EventBridge（source 為 aws.codepipeline），因此以 EventBridge rule 作為觸發來源才是原生且正確的做法。EventBridge 可將事件路由到 Amazon SNS、AWS Lambda 等目標。由於自訂聊天工具的 webhook 無法直接成為 SNS 訂閱者（HTTP/HTTPS 訂閱必須回應 SNS 的 SubscriptionConfirmation 確認握手，且 SNS 會送出自己的訊息封裝格式，而非聊天工具預期的 JSON），因此需要一個訂閱該 SNS topic 的 AWS Lambda 函式，將事件轉換為 webhook 預期的格式並透過 HTTPS POST 出去。此解耦的 EventBridge -> SNS -> Lambda -> webhook 模式能以低營運負擔、近即時方式同時處理一般管線活動與核准請求，正是選項 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no CloudWatch Logs subscription that filters on 'CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change'; that is an EventBridge service detail-type. CloudWatch Logs subscription filters operate on log events in a log group, not on CodePipeline state-change events. Also, subscribing the raw chat webhook URL directly to SNS fails because the webhook will not complete the SNS HTTP/HTTPS subscription-confirmation handshake and would receive the SNS envelope, not the chat tool's expected format.","why_zh":"並不存在可針對「CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change」過濾的 CloudWatch Logs 訂閱；那是 EventBridge 的服務 detail-type。CloudWatch Logs 訂閱篩選器作用於 log group 中的日誌事件，而非 CodePipeline 的狀態變更事件。此外，將聊天 webhook URL 直接訂閱到 SNS 會失敗，因為 webhook 無法完成 SNS 的 HTTP/HTTPS 訂閱確認握手，且只會收到 SNS 封裝格式而非聊天工具預期的格式。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The 'Pipeline Execution State Change' detail-type is emitted directly by CodePipeline to EventBridge; CloudTrail carries API-call events and its delivery is best-effort and not near-real-time. Lambda is also not directly invoked by CloudTrail. This uses the wrong, slower detection mechanism for a near-real-time requirement.","why_zh":"「Pipeline Execution State Change」detail-type 是由 CodePipeline 直接送到 EventBridge；CloudTrail 承載的是 API 呼叫事件，其傳遞屬於 best-effort 且非近即時。Lambda 也無法由 CloudTrail 直接調用。對於近即時需求而言，此做法採用了錯誤且較慢的偵測機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Embedding notification code in the pipeline to POST at the end of each stage is high operational overhead and brittle; it couples notification logic to every pipeline definition and does not cleanly capture the manual-approval-request notification, which is a CodePipeline-managed approval event (delivered via SNS) rather than something custom stage-end code emits. AWS favors decoupled, event-driven notifications over hardcoded webhook calls.","why_zh":"在管線中內嵌通知程式碼，於每個階段結束時 POST，營運負擔高且脆弱；它將通知邏輯耦合到每個管線定義，也無法乾淨地捕捉手動核准請求通知，因為核准事件是由 CodePipeline 託管（透過 SNS 傳遞），並非自訂的階段結束程式碼所發出。AWS 偏好解耦、事件驅動的通知，而非硬編碼 webhook 呼叫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/detect-state-changes-cloudwatch-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codepipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/SendMessageToHttp.confirm.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/http-subscription-confirmation-json.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":42,"question_en":"A company's application development team uses Linux-based Amazon EC2 instances as bastion hosts. Inbound SSH access to the bastion hosts is restricted to specific IP addresses, as defined in the associated security groups. The company's security team wants to receive a notification if the security group rules are modified to allow SSH access from any IP address. What should a DevOps engineer do to meet this requirement?","question_zh":"该公司的应用程序开发团队使用基于 Linux 的 Amazon EC2 实例作为堡垒主机。堡垒主机的入站 SSH 访问仅限于特定的 IP 地址，这些地址在关联的安全组中定义。该公司的安全团队希望在安全组规则被 修改为允许从任何 IP 地址进行 SSH 访问时收到通知。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule with a source of aws.cloudtrail and the event name AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress. Define an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as the target.","B":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty and check the findings for security groups in AWS Security Hub. Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule with a custom pattern that matches GuardDuty events with an output of NON_COMPLIANT. Define an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as the target.","C":"Create an AWS Config rule by using the restricted-ssh managed rule to check whether security groups disallow unrestricted incoming SSH traffic. Configure automatic remediation to publish a message to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","D":"Enable Amazon Inspector. Include the Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures-1.1 rules package to check the security groups that are associated with the bastion hosts. Configure Amazon Inspector to publish a message to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，其来源为 aws.cloudtrail，事件名称为 AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngre ss。将 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题定义为目标。","B":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 并在 AWS Security Hub 中检查安全组的发现结果。配置一个带有自定义模式 的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该模式匹配输出为“不符合”的 GuardDuty 事件。将 Amazon 简单通 知服务（Amazon SNS）主题定义为目标。","C":"使用受限 SSH 管理规则创建一个 AWS Config 规则，以检查安全组是否禁止不受限制的入站 SSH 流量。 配置自动修复功能，将消息发布到 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。","D":"启用 Amazon Inspector。包含通用漏洞和暴露 - 1.1 规则包以检查与堡垒主机关联的安全组。配置 Amazon Inspector 向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发布消息。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to be notified when a security group rule is changed to allow SSH (port 22) from any IP address (0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0). AWS Config provides the managed rule restricted-ssh (rule identifier INCOMING_SSH_DISABLED), which is COMPLIANT only when the incoming SSH CIDR is restricted (other than 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0) and NON_COMPLIANT otherwise; its trigger type is Configuration changes and Periodic, so it re-evaluates whenever the security group is modified. AWS Config auto-remediation runs an SSM Automation document, and the AWS-managed runbook AWS-PublishSNSNotification publishes a message to an SNS topic, so configuring automatic remediation to publish to SNS is a fully supported, standard pattern that delivers the notification. Option A is the closest alternative but is too coarse as written: an EventBridge pattern of just eventName AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress matches every ingress-rule addition regardless of port or CIDR (and the source for a CloudTrail-recorded EC2 API call is aws.ec2, not aws.cloudtrail), so it would over-notify and would not specifically detect SSH-from-any-IP. Therefore C is the genuinely correct answer.","explanation_zh":"需求是當 security group 規則被修改為允許從任何 IP (0.0.0.0/0 或 ::/0) 進行 SSH (port 22) 存取時收到通知。AWS Config 提供受管規則 restricted-ssh (規則識別碼 INCOMING_SSH_DISABLED),只有當入站 SSH 的 CIDR 受限制 (非 0.0.0.0/0 或 ::/0) 時才為 COMPLIANT,否則為 NON_COMPLIANT;其觸發類型為 Configuration changes 與 Periodic,因此只要 security group 被修改就會重新評估。AWS Config 的 auto-remediation 會執行 SSM Automation document,而 AWS 受管 runbook AWS-PublishSNSNotification 會將訊息發佈到 SNS topic,因此設定自動修復以發佈到 SNS 是完全受支援的標準模式,可送達通知。選項 A 是最接近的替代方案,但寫法過於粗略:僅以 eventName AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress 的 EventBridge 模式會比對到每一次入站規則新增,不論 port 或 CIDR (而且 CloudTrail 記錄的 EC2 API 呼叫其 source 是 aws.ec2,而非 aws.cloudtrail),因此會過度通知,也無法明確偵測 SSH-from-any-IP。所以 C 才是真正正確的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An EventBridge pattern with only source aws.cloudtrail and eventName AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress matches every ingress-rule addition regardless of port or source CIDR, so it does not specifically detect SSH from any IP and would fire on unrelated changes. The source for a CloudTrail-recorded EC2 API call is also aws.ec2, not aws.cloudtrail, so the pattern as written is technically off as well.","why_zh":"僅以 source aws.cloudtrail 和 eventName AuthorizeSecurityGroupIngress 的 EventBridge 模式會比對到每一次入站規則新增,不論 port 或來源 CIDR,因此無法明確偵測 SSH-from-any-IP,且會對不相關的變更觸發。此外,CloudTrail 記錄的 EC2 API 呼叫其 source 是 aws.ec2 而非 aws.cloudtrail,所以此寫法在技術上也不正確。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty detects threats from logs (VPC Flow Logs, DNS, CloudTrail) and does not evaluate security group configuration compliance; it has no finding for 'SG allows SSH from any IP'. NON_COMPLIANT is AWS Config/Security Hub control terminology, not a GuardDuty finding output, so this pipeline would never match the intended event.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是從日誌 (VPC Flow Logs、DNS、CloudTrail) 偵測威脅,並不會評估 security group 設定的合規性,也沒有針對「SG 允許從任何 IP 進行 SSH」的 finding。NON_COMPLIANT 是 AWS Config/Security Hub 控制項的用語,並非 GuardDuty 的 finding 輸出,因此此流程永遠不會比對到目標事件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector assesses EC2/ECR/Lambda for software vulnerabilities (CVEs) and network reachability; it does not monitor security group rule modifications. The 'Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures' rules package is from the deprecated Inspector Classic and addresses host CVEs, not changes to SG ingress rules, so it cannot satisfy the requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是評估 EC2/ECR/Lambda 的軟體弱點 (CVE) 與網路可達性,它不會監控 security group 規則的修改。「Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures」規則套件來自已淘汰的 Inspector Classic,針對的是主機 CVE,而非 SG 入站規則的變更,因此無法滿足此需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/restricted-ssh.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-aws-publishsnsnotification.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-create-pattern.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":43,"question_en":"A DevOps team manages an API running on-premises that serves as a backend for an Amazon API Gateway endpoint. Customers have been complaining about high response latencies, which the development team has verified using the API Gateway latency metrics in Amazon CloudWatch. To identify the cause, the team needs to collect relevant data without introducing additional latency. Which actions should be taken to accomplish this? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队管理着一个在本地运行的 API，该 API 作为 Amazon API Gateway 端点的后端。客户一 直在抱怨响应延迟过高，开发团队已通过 Amazon CloudWatch 中的 API Gateway 延迟指标进行了验证。 为了找出原因，该团队需要收集相关数据，同时又不能引入额外的延迟。 应采取哪些行动来完成此任务？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Install the CloudWatch agent server side and configure the agent to upload relevant logs to CloudWatch.","B":"Enable AWS X-Ray tracing in API Gateway, modify the application to capture request segments, and upload those segments to X-Ray during each request.","C":"Enable AWS X-Ray tracing in API Gateway, modify the application to capture request segments, and use the X-Ray daemon to upload segments to X-Ray.","D":"Modify the on-premises application to send log information back to API Gateway with each request.","E":"Modify the on-premises application to calculate and upload statistical data relevant to the API service requests to CloudWatch metrics."},"options_zh":{"A":"在服务器端安装 CloudWatch 代理，并配置代理将相关日志上传到 CloudWatch。","B":"在 API 网关中启用 AWS X-Ray 跟踪，修改应用程序以捕获请求段，并在每次请求期间将这些段上 传到 X-Ray。","C":"在 API 网关中启用 AWS X-Ray 跟踪，修改应用程序以捕获请求段，并使用 X-Ray 守护进程将段上 传到 X-Ray。","D":"修改本地应用程序，使其在每次请求时都将日志信息发送回 API 网关。","E":"修改本地应用程序，使其能够计算与 API 服务请求相关的统计信息，并将其上传到 CloudWatch 指标。"},"answer":["A","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is collecting diagnostic data 'without introducing additional latency'. Option C is correct: enabling X-Ray active tracing on the API Gateway stage gives an end-to-end view of request latency including the on-premises backend (AWS docs: 'Because X-Ray gives you an end-to-end view of an entire request, you can analyze latencies in your APIs and their backend services'), and using the X-Ray daemon means the instrumented application emits segments to the local daemon over UDP port 2000 in a fire-and-forget manner. The daemon 'listens for traffic on UDP port 2000, gathers raw segment data, and relays it to the AWS X-Ray API' asynchronously and can be run on-premises, so no latency is added to the request path. Option A is also correct: the CloudWatch agent collects logs from on-premises servers and ships them to CloudWatch Logs out-of-band, providing additional server-side diagnostic data without affecting request latency. Together they let the team correlate API Gateway latency with backend behavior and pinpoint the source. Option B is the trap because uploading segments to X-Ray 'during each request' means synchronous API calls in the request path, which adds latency and is exactly what the daemon is designed to avoid.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是收集診斷資料時『不可引入額外延遲』。選項 C 正確：在 API Gateway 階段啟用 X-Ray active tracing 可獲得包含地端後端在內的端對端請求延遲視圖（AWS 文件：『Because X-Ray gives you an end-to-end view of an entire request, you can analyze latencies in your APIs and their backend services』），而使用 X-Ray daemon 表示經過 instrumentation 的應用程式透過 UDP port 2000 以 fire-and-forget 方式把 segment 送給本機 daemon。daemon 會『listens for traffic on UDP port 2000, gathers raw segment data, and relays it to the AWS X-Ray API』，以非同步方式上傳且可在地端執行，因此不會對請求路徑增加延遲。選項 A 也正確：CloudWatch agent 可從地端伺服器收集 logs 並以 out-of-band 方式送到 CloudWatch Logs，提供額外的伺服器端診斷資料而不影響請求延遲。兩者結合可讓團隊將 API Gateway 延遲與後端行為關聯起來並找出根因。選項 B 是陷阱，因為在『during each request』時上傳 segment 到 X-Ray 代表在請求路徑中執行同步 API 呼叫，會增加延遲，而這正是 daemon 被設計用來避免的問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uploading segments to X-Ray 'during each request' performs synchronous PutTraceSegments API calls inside the request path, which adds latency. The X-Ray daemon (Option C) exists precisely to decouple segment transmission via local UDP so it happens asynchronously and out-of-band, contradicting the 'without introducing additional latency' requirement.","why_zh":"在『during each request』時上傳 segment 到 X-Ray 會在請求路徑中執行同步的 PutTraceSegments API 呼叫，因而增加延遲。X-Ray daemon（選項 C）的存在正是為了透過本機 UDP 將 segment 傳輸解耦，使其以非同步、out-of-band 的方式進行，因此此選項違反『不增加額外延遲』的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Sending log information back to API Gateway with each request bloats the response payload and adds processing inside the request path, increasing latency. API Gateway is not a logging or diagnostic store, so this provides no useful place to collect or analyze the data and is not a supported mechanism.","why_zh":"在每個請求中把 log 資訊回傳給 API Gateway 會使回應 payload 變大並在請求路徑中增加處理，導致延遲上升。API Gateway 並非 logging 或診斷儲存系統，因此無法提供有用的收集或分析資料之處，且並非支援的機制。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Having the application calculate and upload statistical data to CloudWatch metrics during request processing introduces synchronous PutMetricData calls in the request path, adding latency. CloudWatch already exposes API Gateway latency metrics; app-computed aggregate statistics would not pinpoint where backend latency originates the way per-request X-Ray traces do.","why_zh":"讓應用程式在處理請求時計算並上傳統計資料到 CloudWatch metrics，會在請求路徑中引入同步的 PutMetricData 呼叫而增加延遲。CloudWatch 已提供 API Gateway 延遲 metrics；應用程式自行計算的彙總統計無法像逐請求的 X-Ray trace 那樣定位後端延遲的來源。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/xray-daemon.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-xray.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/xray-services-apigateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Install-CloudWatch-Agent.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":44,"question_en":"A company has an application that is using a MySQL-compatible Amazon Aurora Multi-AZ DB cluster as the database. A cross-Region read replica has been created for disaster recovery purposes. A DevOps engineer wants to automate the promotion of the replica so it becomes the primary database instance in the event of a failure. Which solution will accomplish this?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，该程序使用与 MySQL 兼容的 Amazon Aurora 多可用区数据库集群作为数据 库。为了实现灾难恢复，已创建了一个跨区域读取副本。一位 DevOps 工程师希望在出现故障时自动 将该副本提升为主数据库实例。 哪种解决方案能实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a latency-based Amazon Route 53 CNAME with health checks so it points to both the primary and replica endpoints. Subscribe an Amazon SNS topic to Amazon RDS failure notifications from AWS CloudTrail and use that topic to invoke an AWS Lambda function that will promote the replica instance as the primary.","B":"Create an Aurora custom endpoint to point to the primary database instance. Configure the application to use this endpoint. Configure AWS CloudTrail to run an AWS Lambda function to promote the replica instance and modify the custom endpoint to point to the newly promoted instance.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to modify the application's AWS CloudFormation template to promote the replica, apply the template to update the stack, and point the application to the newly promoted instance. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to invoke this Lambda function after the failure event occurs.","D":"Store the Aurora endpoint in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Create an Amazon EventBridge event that detects the database failure and runs an AWS Lambda function to promote the replica instance and update the endpoint URL stored in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Code the application to reload the endpoint from Parameter Store if a database connection fails."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个基于延迟的 Amazon Route 53 CNAME 并设置健康检查，使其指向主实例和副本实例 的端点。订阅 AWS CloudTrail 发出的 Amazon RDS 故障通知的 Amazon SNS 主题，并使用该 主题调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将副本实例提升为主实例。","B":"创建一个 Aurora 自定义端点以指向主数据库实例。将应用程序配置为使用此端点。配置 AWS CloudTrail 以运行一个 AWS Lambda 函数来提升副本实例，并修改自定义端点以指向新提升的实 例。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于修改应用程序的 AWS CloudFormation 模板以提升副本，应用 该模板以更新堆栈，并将应用程序指向新提升的实例。创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，在 故障事件发生后调用此 Lambda 函数。","D":"将 Aurora 端点存储在 AWS 系统管理器参数存储中。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件，用于检 测数据库故障，并运行一个 AWS Lambda 函数来提升副本实例并更新存储在 AWS 系统管理器参 数存储中的端点 URL。编写应用程序代码，使其在数据库连接失败时从参数存储中重新加载端 点。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS prescribes this exact DR procedure for an Aurora MySQL cross-Region read replica: monitor the source DB cluster for failures, then (1) promote the read replica, (2) direct database traffic to the promoted DB cluster, and (3) create a replacement replica. Option D implements every step with documented building blocks. Amazon RDS sends service events (including RDS DB Cluster Event and RDS DB Instance Event) directly to Amazon EventBridge, so an EventBridge rule can detect the database failure and invoke an AWS Lambda function as a target. The Lambda promotes the replica via the PromoteReadReplicaDBCluster API (promote-read-replica-db-cluster CLI) and updates the endpoint in Systems Manager Parameter Store; the application then reloads the endpoint when its connection fails, satisfying the 'direct traffic to the promoted cluster' step. This is a complete, supported, fully automated solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS 對 Aurora MySQL 跨區域 read replica 的災難復原程序明確規定：監控來源 DB cluster 是否故障，然後 (1) 提升 read replica、(2) 將資料庫流量導向被提升的 DB cluster、(3) 建立替代 replica。選項 D 以官方文件中的元件實作了每一個步驟。Amazon RDS 會將服務事件（包含 RDS DB Cluster Event 與 RDS DB Instance Event）直接傳送到 Amazon EventBridge，因此 EventBridge rule 可偵測資料庫故障並以 AWS Lambda function 作為 target 觸發之。該 Lambda 透過 PromoteReadReplicaDBCluster API（promote-read-replica-db-cluster CLI）提升 replica，並更新 Systems Manager Parameter Store 中的 endpoint；當應用程式連線失敗時即重新讀取 endpoint，符合「將流量導向被提升的 cluster」這一步。這是一個完整、受支援且全自動化的解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Technically incoherent. A latency-based Route 53 CNAME pointing at both the primary and the cross-Region replica is not failover routing and would not correctly redirect after promotion (the replica is not writable until promoted). Moreover, RDS failure notifications are not obtained by 'subscribing an SNS topic to RDS failure notifications from AWS CloudTrail' — CloudTrail logs API activity and does not emit RDS infrastructure-failure event notifications to SNS; RDS event delivery is via RDS event subscriptions/EventBridge.","why_zh":"技術上不通。latency-based Route 53 CNAME 同時指向 primary 與跨區域 replica 並非 failover routing，提升後也無法正確重導流量（replica 在提升前無法寫入）。更關鍵的是，RDS 故障通知並非透過「將 SNS topic 訂閱到來自 AWS CloudTrail 的 RDS 故障通知」取得 — CloudTrail 記錄 API 活動，不會向 SNS 發出 RDS 基礎設施故障事件通知；RDS 事件是經由 RDS event subscription / EventBridge 傳遞。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An Aurora custom endpoint groups instances within a single DB cluster for load balancing and cannot span a cross-Region replica that lives in a separate cluster, so it cannot be repointed to the newly promoted standalone cluster. Also, AWS CloudTrail does not 'run a Lambda function' or detect failures — CloudTrail only records API calls; the detection/invocation mechanism is invalid.","why_zh":"Aurora custom endpoint 是在單一 DB cluster 內將執行個體分組以做負載平衡，無法涵蓋位於另一個 cluster 的跨區域 replica，因此無法重新指向新提升的獨立 cluster。此外 AWS CloudTrail 並不會「執行 Lambda function」或偵測故障 — CloudTrail 只記錄 API 呼叫；其偵測/觸發機制無效。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Promotion is a runtime data-recovery operation, not a CloudFormation template property change; there is no CloudFormation promote action and rewriting/applying a CFN template to promote a cross-Region replica is unsupported, slow, and fragile compared with calling the PromoteReadReplicaDBCluster API directly. The approach is convoluted and not an actual promotion mechanism.","why_zh":"提升是執行時的資料復原操作，並非 CloudFormation template 的屬性變更；CloudFormation 並無對應的 promote 動作，改寫並套用 CFN template 來提升跨區域 replica 不受支援，相較於直接呼叫 PromoteReadReplicaDBCluster API 既緩慢又脆弱。此作法迂迴且不是真正的提升機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/AuroraMySQL.Replication.CrossRegion.Promote.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-rds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-cloud-watch-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/APIReference/API_PromoteReadReplicaDBCluster.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":45,"question_en":"A company hosts its staging website using an Amazon EC2 instance backed with Amazon EBS storage. The company wants to recover quickly with minimal data losses in the event of network connectivity issues or power failures on the EC2 instance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用由亚马逊 EBS 存储支持的亚马逊 EC2 实例来托管其预发布网站。该公司希望在出现网 络连接问题或 EC2 实例断电的情况下能够快速恢复，并将数据丢失降至最低。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add the instance to an EC2 Auto Scaling group with the minimum, maximum, and desired capacity set to 1.","B":"Add the instance to an EC2 Auto Scaling group with a lifecycle hook to detach the EBS volume when the EC2 instance shuts down or terminates.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for the StatusCheckFailed_System metric and select the EC2 action to recover the instance.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for the StatusCheckFailed_Instance metric and select the EC2 action to reboot the instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"将该实例添加到一个 EC2 自动扩展组中，将最小容量、最大容量和期望容量均设置为 1。","B":"将实例添加到具有生命周期挂钩的 EC2 自动扩展组中，以便在 EC2 实例关闭或终止时分离 EBS 卷。","C":"为“StatusCheckFailed_System”指标创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，并选择 EC2 操作以恢 复实例。","D":"为“StatusCheckFailed_Instance”指标创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，并选择 EC2 操作以重 启实例。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario explicitly names network connectivity issues and power failures on the EC2 instance. AWS documentation lists exactly these as examples that cause a System status check to fail: 'Loss of network connectivity' and 'Loss of system power' (plus host hardware/software issues), and a failed system status check increments the StatusCheckFailed_System CloudWatch metric. CloudWatch action based recovery works with the StatusCheckFailed_System metric, and when triggered with the EC2 recover action it migrates the instance to a new healthy host while retaining its instance ID, private/Elastic IP, and its EBS volumes. Because the instance is EBS-backed, persistent data on EBS is preserved (only RAM contents are lost), giving fast recovery with minimal data loss. Option C is therefore correct.","explanation_zh":"題目明確指出 EC2 instance 發生網路連線問題與電源故障。AWS 文件正好把這些列為導致 System status check 失敗的範例：'Loss of network connectivity'（網路連線中斷）與 'Loss of system power'（系統電源中斷），以及實體主機的硬體/軟體問題；當 system status check 失敗時會遞增 StatusCheckFailed_System 這個 CloudWatch 指標。CloudWatch action based recovery 是搭配 StatusCheckFailed_System 指標運作，當以 EC2 recover 動作觸發時，會將 instance 遷移到新的健康主機，同時保留其 instance ID、private/Elastic IP 以及 EBS volumes。由於此 instance 為 EBS-backed，EBS 上的持久資料會被保留（僅遺失 RAM 內容），因此能快速復原且資料遺失最少。故選 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An Auto Scaling group with min/max/desired all set to 1 replaces (terminates and relaunches) an unhealthy instance rather than recovering the running one. A replacement loses the original instance ID and typically destroys the staging website's data on the root EBS volume, so it causes data loss instead of minimal data loss, and is heavier than a recovery alarm.","why_zh":"將 Auto Scaling group 的最小/最大/期望容量都設為 1，會在 instance 不健康時替換（終止並重新啟動）它，而非復原正在執行的 instance。替換會失去原本的 instance ID，且通常會銷毀 staging 網站在根 EBS volume 上的資料，造成資料損失而非最小資料損失，設定也比復原警示繁重。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A lifecycle hook that detaches the EBS volume on shutdown/termination does not detect or remediate host-level power or network failures and does not recover instance availability; it only manages volume detachment during scale-in. It adds operational complexity without restoring the instance.","why_zh":"在關機/終止時卸離 EBS volume 的 lifecycle hook，並不會偵測或修復主機層級的電源或網路故障，也無法復原 instance 的可用性；它只是在縮減時管理 volume 卸離。這增加操作複雜度卻無法還原 instance。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"StatusCheckFailed_Instance reflects Instance status checks, which detect in-guest issues such as incorrect networking/startup config, exhausted memory, corrupted file system, or incompatible kernel — not host power or network failures. Additionally the chosen 'reboot' action keeps the instance on the same impaired physical host, so it cannot resolve a loss of system power or host network connectivity.","why_zh":"StatusCheckFailed_Instance 對應 Instance status checks，偵測的是 instance 內部問題，例如錯誤的網路/啟動設定、記憶體耗盡、檔案系統損毀或不相容的 kernel，而非主機電源或網路故障。此外所選的 'reboot' 動作會讓 instance 留在同一台受損的實體主機上，無法解決系統電源中斷或主機網路連線中斷。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/monitoring-system-instance-status-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ec2-instance-recover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/cloudwatch-recovery.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":46,"question_en":"A company wants to use AWS development tools to replace its current bash deployment scripts. The company currently deploys a LAMP application to a group of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). During the deployments, the company unit tests the committed application, stops and starts services, unregisters and re-registers instances with the load balancer, and updates file permissions. The company wants to maintain the same deployment functionality through the shift to using AWS services. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用 AWS 开发工具来取代其当前的 bash 部署脚本。该公司目前将一个 LAMP 应用程 序部署到一组位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）后面的 Amazon EC2 实例上。在部署过程中，该公司会对 提交的应用程序进行单元测试，停止和启动服务，从负载均衡器中注销并重新注册实例，并更新文件 权限。该公司希望在转向使用 AWS 服务的过程中保持相同的部署功能。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CodeBuild to test the application. Use bash scripts invoked by AWS CodeDeploy's appspec.yml file to restart services, and deregister and register instances with the ALB. Use the appspec.yml file to update file permissions without a custom script.","B":"Use AWS CodePipeline to move the application from the AWS CodeCommit repository to AWS CodeDeploy. Use CodeDeploy's deployment group to test the application, unregister and re-register instances with the ALB. and restart services. Use the appspec.yml file to update file permissions without a custom script.","C":"Use AWS CodePipeline to move the application source code from the AWS CodeCommit repository to AWS CodeDeploy. Use CodeDeploy to test the application. Use CodeDeploy's appspec.yml file to restart services and update permissions without a custom script. Use AWS CodeBuild to unregister and re-register instances with the ALB.","D":"Use AWS CodePipeline to trigger AWS CodeBuild to test the application. Use bash scripts invoked by AWS CodeDeploy's appspec.yml file to restart services. Unregister and re-register the instances in the AWS CodeDeploy deployment group with the ALB. Update the appspec.yml file to update file permissions without a custom script."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 对应用程序进行测试。使用由 AWS CodeDeploy 的 appspec.yml 文件 调用的 bash 脚本重启服务，并从应用负载均衡器（ALB）中注销和注册实例。使用 appspec.yml 文件更新文件权限，无需自定义脚本。","B":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 将应用程序从 AWS CodeCommit 存储库迁移到 AWS CodeDeploy。使用 CodeDeploy 的部署组来测试应用程序，从应用负载均衡器（ALB）中注销并重新注册实例， 并重新启动服务。使用 appspec.yml 文件更新文件权限，而无需自定义脚本。","C":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 将应用程序源代码从 AWS CodeCommit 存储库移动到 AWS CodeDeploy。使用 CodeDeploy 测试应用程序。使用 CodeDeploy 的 appspec.yml 文件重启服务并更新权限，无需自定义脚 本。使用 AWS CodeBuild 从应用负载均衡器（ALB）注销并重新注册实例。","D":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 触发 AWS CodeBuild 对应用程序进行测试。使用由 AWS CodeDeploy 的 appspec. yml 文件调用的 bash 脚本重启服务。在 AWS CodeDeploy 部署组中注销并重新注册实例与 ALB 的关联。 更新 appspec.yml 文件以更改文件权限，无需自定义脚本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Map each of the four deployment tasks to the correct AWS service or mechanism. (1) Unit testing the committed application is a build/test concern handled by AWS CodeBuild, which runs the test commands in its buildspec build phases; neither CodeDeploy nor a CodeDeploy deployment group runs unit tests on committed source. (2) Stopping and starting services is done by bash scripts invoked from the CodeDeploy appspec.yml ApplicationStop and ApplicationStart EC2/On-Premises lifecycle hooks. (3) Deregistering and re-registering instances with the ALB is performed automatically by the CodeDeploy deployment group when an Elastic Load Balancing load balancer is associated with it: the AWS docs state that during an in-place deployment, 'instances in a deployment group are deregistered from the load balancer, updated with the latest application revision, and then reregistered with the load balancer as part of the same deployment group after the deployment is successful' (via the reserved BlockTraffic/AllowTraffic events). (4) Updating file permissions is done natively by the appspec.yml 'permissions' section (EC2/On-Premises only), which sets owner, group, and mode with no custom script. Option D assigns all four tasks correctly: CodePipeline triggers CodeBuild to test, appspec.yml bash scripts restart services, the CodeDeploy deployment group handles ALB deregister/register, and the appspec.yml permissions section updates file permissions.","explanation_zh":"把四項部署任務分別對應到正確的 AWS 服務或機制。(1) 對已提交的應用程式做單元測試屬於 build/test 範疇，由 AWS CodeBuild 在其 buildspec 的 build 階段執行測試指令；CodeDeploy 或 CodeDeploy deployment group 都不會對提交的原始碼跑單元測試。(2) 停止與啟動服務是由 CodeDeploy appspec.yml 的 ApplicationStop 與 ApplicationStart EC2/On-Premises 生命週期 hook 所呼叫的 bash 指令稿完成。(3) 與 ALB 取消註冊及重新註冊執行個體，是在 deployment group 關聯了 Elastic Load Balancing 負載平衡器時由 CodeDeploy deployment group 自動執行：AWS 文件指出在 in-place deployment 期間，deployment group 中的執行個體會從負載平衡器取消註冊、更新為最新的應用程式修訂版，並在部署成功後重新註冊回同一個 deployment group 的負載平衡器（透過保留的 BlockTraffic/AllowTraffic 事件）。(4) 更新檔案權限由 appspec.yml 的 'permissions' 區段原生完成（僅限 EC2/On-Premises），可設定 owner、group 與 mode，無需自訂指令稿。選項 D 把全部四項任務對應到正確機制：CodePipeline 觸發 CodeBuild 測試、appspec.yml 的 bash 指令稿重啟服務、CodeDeploy deployment group 處理 ALB 取消/重新註冊、appspec.yml permissions 區段更新檔案權限。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"It correctly uses CodeBuild to test, but it claims bash scripts invoked by appspec.yml must deregister and register instances with the ALB. When an ALB is associated with the deployment group, CodeDeploy performs that deregister/register automatically as part of the deployment group via the reserved BlockTraffic/AllowTraffic events (custom scripts are only an optional alternative). The option also omits the CodePipeline orchestration the company wants, making it a poorer fit than D.","why_zh":"它正確地用 CodeBuild 測試，但宣稱必須用 appspec.yml 呼叫的 bash 指令稿來與 ALB 取消/重新註冊執行個體。當 ALB 關聯到 deployment group 時，CodeDeploy 會透過保留的 BlockTraffic/AllowTraffic 事件作為 deployment group 的一部分自動完成取消/重新註冊（自訂指令稿只是可選的替代方案）。此選項也省略了公司想要的 CodePipeline 流程編排，比 D 不理想。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It states the CodeDeploy deployment group tests the application. A deployment group is only configuration (Auto Scaling groups, ALB association, deployment config) and does not run unit tests on committed source code; testing is a build-phase task for AWS CodeBuild. This misassignment makes B incorrect.","why_zh":"它說由 CodeDeploy deployment group 來測試應用程式。deployment group 僅是設定（Auto Scaling 群組、ALB 關聯、部署設定），並不會對提交的原始碼執行單元測試；測試是 AWS CodeBuild 的 build 階段任務。此錯誤對應使 B 不正確。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It contains two errors: it says CodeDeploy tests the application (CodeDeploy does not run unit tests on source code; that is CodeBuild's role) and it says CodeBuild unregisters and re-registers instances with the ALB. CodeBuild is a build/test service and does not manage ALB target registration during a deployment; that is handled natively by the CodeDeploy deployment group.","why_zh":"它有兩處錯誤：它說由 CodeDeploy 測試應用程式（CodeDeploy 不會對原始碼跑單元測試，那是 CodeBuild 的工作），又說由 CodeBuild 與 ALB 取消/重新註冊執行個體。CodeBuild 是 build/test 服務，不負責部署期間的 ALB target 註冊；那是由 CodeDeploy deployment group 原生處理。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-elastic-load-balancing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":47,"question_en":"A company runs an application with an Amazon EC2 and on-premises configuration. A DevOps engineer needs to standardize patching across both environments. Company policy dictates that patching only happens during non-business hours. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司运行着一个采用亚马逊 EC2 和本地配置的应用程序。一位 DevOps 工程师需要在两个环境中统一 打补丁的标准。公司政策规定，打补丁只能在非工作时间进行。 哪些操作组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add the physical machines into AWS Systems Manager using Systems Manager Hybrid Activations.","B":"Attach an IAM role to the EC2 instances, allowing them to be managed by AWS Systems Manager.","C":"Create IAM access keys for the on-premises machines to interact with AWS Systems Manager.","D":"Run an AWS Systems Manager Automation document to patch the systems every hour","E":"Use Amazon EventBridge scheduled events to schedule a patch window.","F":"Use AWS Systems Manager Maintenance Windows to schedule a patch window."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 混合激活功能将物理机添加到 AWS Systems Manager 中。","B":"附加一个 IAM 角 色 连接到 EC2 实例，使它们能够通过 AWS Systems Manager 进行管理。","C":"为本地机器创建 IAM 访问密钥，以便其与 AWS 系统管理器进行交互。","D":"每小时运行一次 AWS Systems Manager Automation 文档以修补系统","E":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 定期事件来安排补丁更新窗口。","F":"使用 AWS 系统管理器维护窗口来安排补丁更新窗口。"},"answer":["A","B","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Standardizing patching across EC2 and on-premises machines with AWS Systems Manager requires registering both environments and scheduling patching for non-business hours. (A) Non-EC2 / on-premises machines become Systems Manager managed nodes through a Hybrid Activation: you run create-activation to obtain an Activation Code and Activation ID, then install SSM Agent with them. (B) EC2 instances need an IAM instance profile/role attached so SSM Agent can communicate with and be managed by Systems Manager. (F) Maintenance Windows defines a schedule (cron/rate with a time zone and active periods) for potentially disruptive actions like patching, so patching runs only during the specified non-business hours, and it targets both EC2 and hybrid managed nodes. C is the trap: hybrid activations exist precisely so on-premises machines do NOT use long-lived IAM access keys; the activation code/ID plus an ssm.amazonaws.com service role provide secure access. D fails the policy because patching every hour would run during business hours. E (EventBridge scheduled events) is not the purpose-built Systems Manager mechanism for patch windows; Maintenance Windows is.","explanation_zh":"要使用 AWS Systems Manager 在 EC2 與地端機器之間統一修補，需要先把兩種環境都註冊為受管節點，並把修補排程在非營業時段。(A) 非 EC2／地端機器透過 Hybrid Activation 成為 Systems Manager managed node：執行 create-activation 取得 Activation Code 與 Activation ID，再用它們安裝 SSM Agent。(B) EC2 執行個體需附加 IAM instance profile/role，SSM Agent 才能與 Systems Manager 通訊並被其管理。(F) Maintenance Windows 可定義排程（cron/rate，含時區與作用期間）來執行像修補這類可能造成中斷的動作，因此修補只會在指定的非營業時段執行，且能同時針對 EC2 與 hybrid managed node。C 是陷阱：Hybrid Activations 的存在正是為了讓地端機器「不需」使用長期 IAM access keys；安全存取由 activation code/ID 加上 ssm.amazonaws.com service role 提供。D 不符合政策，因為每小時修補會落在營業時段。E（EventBridge scheduled events）並非 Systems Manager 專為修補視窗設計的機制，Maintenance Windows 才是。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Hybrid Activations are designed specifically to avoid long-lived IAM access keys on on-premises machines; secure access is provided by the activation code/ID plus an ssm.amazonaws.com service role, not IAM access keys. Distributing static access keys to each server would be insecure and is not the documented method (option A is the correct registration path).","why_zh":"Hybrid Activations 的設計正是要避免在地端機器上使用長期 IAM access keys；安全存取由 activation code/ID 加上 ssm.amazonaws.com service role 提供，而非 IAM access keys。在每台伺服器放靜態金鑰既不安全也非官方做法（選項 A 才是正確的註冊方式）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running an Automation document to patch every hour would patch during business hours, directly violating the policy that patching happens only during non-business hours; a fixed hourly interval is not how scheduled patch windows are implemented.","why_zh":"每小時執行 Automation document 進行修補會在營業時段進行修補，直接違反只能在非營業時段修補的政策；固定每小時執行並非排程修補視窗的實作方式。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Although EventBridge can trigger actions on a schedule, the native, documented Systems Manager mechanism for scheduling disruptive patch windows (with duration, time zone, targets, and registered patch tasks such as AWS-RunPatchBaseline) is Maintenance Windows. Option F is the purpose-built correct fit; E is the weaker distractor against F.","why_zh":"雖然 EventBridge 可依排程觸發動作，但 Systems Manager 原生且官方文件中用於排程具干擾性修補視窗（含持續時間、時區、目標與註冊的 AWS-RunPatchBaseline 等修補任務）的機制是 Maintenance Windows。選項 F 才是專為此設計的正確選項，E 是相對較弱的干擾項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-activation-managed-nodes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-hybrid-multicloud.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-setting-up-nodes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/maintenance-windows.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/maintenance-window-tutorial-patching.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/sysman-patch-scheduletasks.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":48,"question_en":"A company has chosen AWS to host a new application. The company needs to implement a multi-account strategy. A DevOps engineer creates a new AWS account and an organization in AWS Organizations. The DevOps engineer also creates the OU structure for the organization and sets up a landing zone by using AWS Control Tower. The DevOps engineer must implement a solution that automatically deploys resources for new accounts that users create through AWS Control Tower Account Factory. When a user creates a new account, the solution must apply AWS CloudFormation templates and SCPs that are customized for the OU or the account to automatically deploy all the resources that are attached to the account. All the OUs are enrolled in AWS Control Tower. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST automated way?","question_zh":"一家公司已选择 AWS 来托管新的应用程序。该公司需要实施多账户策略。一位 DevOps 工程师创建了一个 新的 AWS 账户和一个 AWS Organizations 组织。该 DevOps 工程师还为该组织创建了组织单元（OU）结构， 并使用 AWS Control Tower 设置了着陆区。 DevOps 工程师必须实现一个解决方案，该方案能够自动为用户通过 AWS Control Tower 账户工厂创建的新 账户部署资源。当用户创建新账户时，该解决方案必须应用针对组织单元（OU）或账户定制的 AWS CloudFormation 模板和 SCP，以自动部署与该账户关联的所有资源。所有组织单元均已注册到 AWS Control Tower。 哪种解决方案能以最自动化的方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Service Catalog with AWS Control Tower. Create portfolios and products in AWS Service Catalog. Grant granular permissions to provision these resources. Deploy SCPs by using the AWS CLI and JSON documents.","B":"Deploy CloudFormation stack sets by using the required templates. Enable automatic deployment. Deploy stack instances to the required accounts. Deploy a CloudFormation stack set to the organization’s management account to deploy SCPs.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to detect the CreateManagedAccount event. Configure AWS Service Catalog as the target to deploy resources to any new accounts. Deploy SCPs by using the AWS CLI and JSON documents.","D":"Deploy the Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) solution. Use an AWS CodeCommit repository as the source. In the repository, create a custom package that includes the CloudFormation templates and the SCP JSON documents."},"options_zh":{"A":"结合 AWS Control Tower 使用 AWS 服务目录。在 AWS 服务目录中创建组合和产品。授予精细的权限以 配置这些资源。使用 AWS CLI 和 JSON 文档部署 SCP。","B":"使用所需的模板部署 CloudFormation 堆栈集。启用自动部署。将堆栈实例部署到所需的账户。将 CloudFormation 堆栈集部署到组织的管理账户以部署 SCP。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以检测 CreateManagedAccount 事件。将 AWS 服务目录配置为目 标，以便向任何新账户部署资源。使用 AWS CLI 和 JSON 文档部署 SCP。","D":"部署 AWS Control Tower 自定义解决方案（CfCT）。使用 AWS CodeCommit 存储库作为源。在该存储 库中，创建一个自定义包，其中包含 CloudFormation。 模板和 SCP JSON 文档。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical use case for Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT). The CfCT overview documentation states almost verbatim that customizations are implemented with AWS CloudFormation templates and service control policies (SCPs), that CfCT is integrated with AWS Control Tower lifecycle events, and that 'when a new account is created through account factory, all resources attached to the account are deployed automatically,' with the ability to deploy custom templates and policies to individual accounts and OUs. CfCT uses an AWS CodeCommit repository (or an Amazon S3 bucket) as the configuration source, where a custom package and manifest.yaml define which CloudFormation templates and SCP JSON documents apply to which accounts and OUs. Because both resource deployment and SCP application are triggered automatically by Account Factory lifecycle events with no manual per-account action, option D is the MOST automated solution that satisfies every requirement (CloudFormation + SCPs, customized per OU/account, on Account Factory account creation).","explanation_zh":"這是 Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) 的標準使用情境。CfCT 概觀文件幾乎逐字說明：customizations 以 AWS CloudFormation 範本與 service control policies (SCPs) 實作，CfCT 與 AWS Control Tower lifecycle events 整合，且「當透過 account factory 建立新帳戶時，所有附加至該帳戶的資源會自動部署」，並可將自訂範本與政策部署至個別帳戶與 OUs。CfCT 使用 AWS CodeCommit 儲存庫（或 Amazon S3 儲存貯體）作為設定來源，其中的 custom package 與 manifest.yaml 定義哪些 CloudFormation 範本與 SCP JSON 文件套用至哪些帳戶與 OUs。由於資源部署與 SCP 套用都由 Account Factory lifecycle events 自動觸發，無需逐帳戶手動操作，因此選項 D 是滿足所有需求（CloudFormation + SCPs、依 OU/帳戶自訂、在 Account Factory 建立帳戶時觸發）且最自動化的解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Service Catalog requires users to provision products from a portfolio; granting granular provisioning permissions does not auto-deploy resources when Account Factory creates an account. Deploying SCPs via the AWS CLI and JSON documents is a manual step, so this is far less automated than the lifecycle-event-driven CfCT.","why_zh":"AWS Service Catalog 需要使用者從 portfolio 佈建產品，授予細粒度佈建權限並不會在 Account Factory 建立帳戶時自動部署資源。以 AWS CLI 與 JSON 文件部署 SCPs 是手動步驟，因此自動化程度遠低於由 lifecycle event 驅動的 CfCT。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFormation StackSets auto-deployment triggers on AWS Organizations OU membership rather than the native Control Tower Account Factory customization path, and centrally managing per-OU/per-account SCPs is not what StackSets is designed for (even though an AWS::Organizations::Policy resource exists, that is a management-account-only construct and not the integrated pattern here). CfCT is the purpose-built, lifecycle-integrated solution that bundles both CloudFormation templates and SCP application, so it is more automated and better aligned with the requirement.","why_zh":"CloudFormation StackSets 的自動部署是依 AWS Organizations 的 OU 成員資格觸發，而非原生的 Control Tower Account Factory 自訂路徑，且集中管理依 OU/帳戶的 SCPs 並非 StackSets 的設計用途（雖然存在 AWS::Organizations::Policy 資源，但那是僅限管理帳戶的構件，並非此處的整合模式）。CfCT 是專為此打造、與 lifecycle 整合的解決方案，同時封裝 CloudFormation 範本與 SCP 套用，因此更自動化且更符合需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Although CreateManagedAccount is a real Control Tower lifecycle event, AWS Service Catalog is not a directly supported EventBridge target for auto-provisioning resources into a brand-new account, and deploying SCPs via the AWS CLI remains manual. This is a brittle, partially manual design compared with CfCT, which already provides the lifecycle integration natively.","why_zh":"雖然 CreateManagedAccount 是真實的 Control Tower lifecycle event，但 AWS Service Catalog 並非直接支援的 EventBridge 目標來自動將資源佈建至全新帳戶，且以 AWS CLI 部署 SCPs 仍是手動。相較於原生提供 lifecycle 整合的 CfCT，這是脆弱且部分手動的設計。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/cfct-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/automate-customizations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/the-manifest-file.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":49,"question_en":"An online retail company based in the United States plans to expand its operations to Europe and Asia in the next six months. Its product currently runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. The instances run in an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. All data is stored in an Amazon Aurora database instance. When the product is deployed in multiple regions, the company wants a single product catalog across all regions, but for compliance purposes, its customer information and purchases must be kept in each region. How should the company meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of application changes?","question_zh":"一家总部位于美国的在线零售公司计划在未来六个月内将其业务拓展至欧洲和亚洲。该公司目前的产品 运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器之后。这些实例在多个可用区的亚马逊 EC2 自动扩展组中运行。所有数据都存储在亚马逊 Aurora 数据库实例中。 当产品部署在多个地区时，该公司希望在所有地区拥有一个统一的产品目录，但出于合规性考虑，其客 户信息和购买记录必须保存在各自所在的地区。 公司应如何以最少的应用程序变更来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Redshift for the product catalog and Amazon DynamoDB tables for the customer information and purchases.","B":"Use Amazon DynamoDB global tables for the product catalog and regional tables for the customer information and purchases.","C":"Use Aurora with read replicas for the product catalog and additional local Aurora instances in each region for the customer information and purchases.","D":"Use Aurora for the product catalog and Amazon DynamoDB global tables for the customer information and purchases."},"options_zh":{"A":"产品目录使用亚马逊 Redshift，客户信息和购买记录使用亚马逊 DynamoDB 表。","B":"对于产品目录使用亚马逊 DynamoDB 全球表，对于客户信息和购买记录使用区域表。","C":"对于产品目录，使用带有只读副本的 Aurora，对于每个区域的客户信息和购买记录，则使用额外 的本地 Aurora 实例。","D":"使用 Aurora 作为产品目录，使用亚马逊 DynamoDB 全球表来存储客户信息和购买记录。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application already runs entirely on Amazon Aurora (a relational engine), and the deciding qualifier is LEAST amount of application changes. Option C keeps everything relational: a single product catalog served globally via Aurora cross-Region read replicas (one writer in the primary Region, read-only replicas in Europe and Asia), plus separate local Aurora instances in each Region for customer information and purchases so that regulated data never leaves its Region (data residency/compliance). Because the relational data model and SQL access layer are unchanged, the code barely changes. Aurora MySQL supports up to five cross-Region read replicas (Aurora global database is the managed alternative, and the only cross-Region option for Aurora PostgreSQL), so a read-mostly catalog replicated across Regions is fully supported. Option B (DynamoDB global tables + regional tables) maps the global-vs-regional split correctly but would force a full migration of the Aurora relational schema and all query/data-access code to a NoSQL key-value model, which is the MOST application change, not the least.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式目前完全運行在 Amazon Aurora（關聯式引擎）上，而決定性條件是「最少的應用程式變更（LEAST application changes）」。選項 C 全部維持關聯式架構：產品目錄透過 Aurora cross-Region read replicas 在全球提供單一目錄（主要 Region 一個 writer，歐洲與亞洲各有唯讀 replica），並在每個 Region 各自設置本地的 Aurora 執行個體存放客戶資訊與購買紀錄，使受規範的資料不會離開所屬 Region（資料落地/合規）。由於關聯式資料模型與 SQL 存取層不變，程式碼幾乎無需改動。Aurora MySQL 最多支援五個 cross-Region read replicas（Aurora global database 是受管的替代方案，也是 Aurora PostgreSQL 唯一的跨 Region 選項），因此以讀取為主的目錄跨 Region 複寫完全可行。選項 B（DynamoDB global tables + regional tables）雖然正確對應了全域與區域的切分，但會迫使將 Aurora 關聯式 schema 與所有查詢/資料存取程式碼整體遷移到 NoSQL key-value 模型，這是最大的應用程式變更，而非最少。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Redshift is an OLAP data warehouse, not an operational transactional store for a live product catalog, and it has no native multi-active cross-Region replication for serving the catalog. Moving customer/purchase data to DynamoDB also abandons the existing Aurora relational app, requiring extensive rewrites and not addressing per-Region residency well — far from the least change.","why_zh":"Amazon Redshift 是 OLAP 資料倉儲，不適合作為線上產品目錄的交易型資料存放，也沒有原生的多主動跨 Region 複寫來服務目錄。同時把客戶/購買資料改用 DynamoDB 也等於放棄現有 Aurora 關聯式應用，需要大量改寫，且未妥善處理各 Region 的資料落地，遠非最少變更。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Global tables for the catalog and regional DynamoDB tables for customer data correctly model the global-vs-regional requirement, but the existing app is built on relational Aurora. Re-platforming all data and access code from SQL to a NoSQL key-value model is the MOST application change, directly violating the LEAST-changes qualifier.","why_zh":"用 global tables 放目錄、各 Region DynamoDB tables 放客戶資料，雖然正確對應全域與區域需求，但現有應用建構於關聯式 Aurora。把所有資料與存取程式碼從 SQL 改寫成 NoSQL key-value 模型是最大的應用程式變更，直接違反「最少變更」的限定條件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This inverts the requirement. DynamoDB global tables replicate data across all Regions, so using them for customer information and purchases would spread that data globally — exactly what compliance forbids (it must stay per-Region). Meanwhile a single Aurora cluster does not serve a globally distributed catalog well. The global/regional mapping is backwards.","why_zh":"此選項把需求顛倒了。DynamoDB global tables 會把資料跨所有 Region 複寫，因此用於客戶資訊與購買紀錄會讓這些資料散布到全球，正是合規所禁止的（必須保留在各自 Region）。同時單一 Aurora cluster 也不適合服務全球分散的目錄。全域/區域的對應關係完全相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/aurora-replication-options/cross-region-aurora-replicas.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":50,"question_en":"A company is implementing a well-architected design for its globally accessible API stack. The design needs to ensure both high reliability and fast response times for users located in North America and Europe. The API stack contains the following three tiers: Amazon API Gateway AWS Lambda Amazon DynamoDB Which solution will meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在为其全球可访问的 API 堆栈实施架构良好的设计。该设计需要确保位于北美和欧洲的 用户都能获得高可靠性和快速响应时间。 该 API 堆栈包含以下三个层级： 亚马逊 API 网关 AWS Lambda 亚马逊 DynamoDB 哪种解决方案能满足要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure Amazon Route 53 to point to API Gateway APIs in North America and Europe using health checks. Configure the APIs to forward requests to a Lambda function in that Region. Configure the Lambda functions to retrieve and update the data in a DynamoDB table in the same Region as the Lambda function.","B":"Configure Amazon Route 53 to point to API Gateway APIs in North America and Europe using latency- based routing and health checks. Configure the APIs to forward requests to a Lambda function in that Region. Configure the Lambda functions to retrieve and update the data in a DynamoDB global table.","C":"Configure Amazon Route 53 to point to API Gateway in North America, create a disaster recovery API in Europe, and configure both APIs to forward requests to the Lambda functions in that Region. Retrieve the data from a DynamoDB global table. Deploy a Lambda function to check the North America API health every 5 minutes. In the event of a failure, update Route 53 to point to the disaster recovery API.","D":"Configure Amazon Route 53 to point to API Gateway API in North America using latency-based routing. Configure the API to forward requests to the Lambda function in the Region nearest to the user. Configure the Lambda function to retrieve and update the data in a DynamoDB table."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用健康检查将 Amazon Route 53 配置为指向北美和欧洲的 API Gateway API。将这些 API 配置为将 请求转发到该区域内的 Lambda 函数。将 Lambda 函数配置为从与该 Lambda 函数位于同一区域的 DynamoDB 表中检索和更新数据。","B":"使用基于延迟的路由和健康检查配置 Amazon Route 53，使其指向北美和欧洲的 API Gateway API。配 置这些 API 将请求转发到该区域的 Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数从 DynamoDB 全局表中检索和 更新数据。","C":"配置亚马逊 Route 53 指向北美的 API 网关，在欧洲创建一个灾难恢复 API，并将这两个 API 配置为 将请求转发到该区域的 Lambda 函数。从 DynamoDB 全球表中检索数据。部署一个 Lambda 函数， 每 5 分钟检查一次北美 API 的运行状况。如果出现故障，更新 Route 53 使其指向灾难恢复 API。","D":"使用基于延迟的路由配置 Amazon Route 53 指向北美的 API Gateway API。配置 API 将请求转发至 距离最近区域的 Lambda 函数。 用户。配置 Lambda 函数以从 DynamoDB 表中检索和更新数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The design must deliver BOTH fast response times and high reliability for users in North America and Europe across an API Gateway -> Lambda -> DynamoDB stack. Option B uses Route 53 latency-based routing to send each user to the Region that provides the lowest latency (fast response times), and pairs it with health checks so Route 53 stops resolving to an unhealthy Region (high reliability) at the API tier. It backs this with a DynamoDB global table, which AWS documents as a multi-active, multi-Region feature that 'provides easy to use data replication and fast local read and write performance' and where 'any global table replica can serve reads and writes,' giving each Region's Lambda local data access and a low/zero-RPO failover path. Together, latency-based routing + health checks + global table is the well-architected active-active pattern that satisfies both qualifiers at every tier. The decisive distinction is that only Option B provides BOTH per-user latency optimization AND multi-Region replicated, highly available data; every other option drops one or both.","explanation_zh":"此設計必須同時為北美與歐洲使用者提供「快速回應」與「高可靠性」，且涵蓋 API Gateway -> Lambda -> DynamoDB 三層。選項 B 使用 Route 53 latency-based routing 將每位使用者導向延遲最低的 Region（快速回應），並搭配 health checks，讓 Route 53 在某 Region 不健康時停止解析至該 Region（API 層的高可靠性）。資料層則使用 DynamoDB global table；AWS 文件指出 global table 是 multi-active、multi-Region 功能，提供「易於使用的資料複寫與快速的在地讀寫效能」，且「任一 global table 副本皆可服務讀寫」，使各 Region 的 Lambda 能就近存取資料並具備低或零 RPO 的故障移轉路徑。latency-based routing + health checks + global table 共同構成 well-architected 的 active-active 架構，在每一層都滿足兩項需求。關鍵差異在於：只有選項 B 同時提供「依使用者的延遲最佳化」與「跨 Region 複寫且高可用的資料」，其他選項皆缺其一或兩者。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses health checks but NO latency-based routing, so there is no mechanism to direct each user to the lowest-latency Region (fails 'fast response times' at the DNS tier). It also uses a separate standalone DynamoDB table per Region with no replication, so North America and Europe hold divergent, unsynchronized data rather than a unified, highly available global dataset.","why_zh":"雖有 health checks 但沒有 latency-based routing，缺乏將每位使用者導向延遲最低 Region 的機制（在 DNS 層未滿足『快速回應時間』）。此外各 Region 使用獨立未複寫的 DynamoDB table，導致北美與歐洲資料各自分歧、無法同步，而非統一且高可用的全球資料集。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An active-passive DR design with a single active Region (North America), so European users hit North America in normal operation and do not get fast response times. The custom Lambda polling health every 5 minutes plus manually updating Route 53 adds high operational overhead and gives much slower, more fragile failover than native Route 53 health checks. Not well-architected.","why_zh":"這是 active-passive 災難復原設計，僅有單一作用中 Region（北美），正常運作下歐洲使用者會連到北美而無法獲得快速回應。每 5 分鐘自訂 Lambda 輪詢健康狀態再手動更新 Route 53 帶來高營運負擔，且故障移轉遠比原生 Route 53 health checks 緩慢且脆弱，不符合 Well-Architected。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Latency-based routing pointing to only a single API in North America is meaningless (latency routing needs multiple regional records). It also claims the API forwards to a Lambda 'in the Region nearest to the user', which is not how API Gateway/Lambda works—an API invokes Lambda in its own Region. It uses a single non-global DynamoDB table, so it is neither multi-Region nor reliable, and provides no fast response for Europe.","why_zh":"latency-based routing 只指向北美單一 API 毫無意義（延遲路由需要多個 Region 記錄）。它還宣稱 API 會轉發到『離使用者最近 Region』的 Lambda，這並非 API Gateway/Lambda 的運作方式——API 只會呼叫同 Region 的 Lambda。並且使用單一非全球的 DynamoDB table，既非多 Region 也不可靠，且無法為歐洲提供快速回應。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-latency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":51,"question_en":"A rapidly growing company wants to scale for developer demand for AWS development environments. Development environments are created manually in the AWS Management Console. The networking team uses AWS CloudFormation to manage the networking infrastructure, exporting stack output values for the Amazon VPC and all subnets. The development environments have common standards, such as Application Load Balancers, Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling groups, security groups, and Amazon DynamoDB tables. To keep up with demand, the DevOps engineer wants to automate the creation of development environments. Because the infrastructure required to support the application is expected to grow, there must be a way to easily update the deployed infrastructure. CloudFormation will be used to create a template for the development environments. Which approach will meet these requirements and quickly provide consistent AWS environments for developers?","question_zh":"一家发展迅速的公司希望扩大其 AWS 开发环境以满足开发人员的需求。开发环境目前是在 AWS 管理 控制台中手动创建的。网络团队使用 AWS CloudFormation 来管理网络基础设施，并导出 Amazon VPC 及所有子网的堆栈输出值。开发环境具有通用标准，例如应用负载均衡器、Amazon EC2 自动扩展组、 安全组和 Amazon DynamoDB 表。 为了满足需求，DevOps 工程师希望实现开发环境创建的自动化。由于支持应用程序所需的基础设 施预计会不断扩展，因此必须有一种简便的方式来更新已部署的基础设施。将使用 CloudFormation 来为开发环境创建模板。 哪种方法能满足这些要求，并能迅速为开发人员提供一致的 AWS 环境？","options_en":{"A":"Use Fn::ImportValue intrinsic functions in the Resources section of the template to retrieve Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and subnet values. Use CloudFormation StackSets for the development environments, using the Count input parameter to indicate the number of environments needed. Use the UpdateStackSet command to update existing development environments.","B":"Use nested stacks to define common infrastructure components. To access the exported values, use TemplateURL to reference the networking team’s template. To retrieve Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and subnet values, use Fn::ImportValue intrinsic functions in the Parameters section of the root template. Use the CreateChangeSet and ExecuteChangeSet commands to update existing development environments.","C":"Use nested stacks to define common infrastructure components. Use Fn::ImportValue intrinsic functions with the resources of the nested stack to retrieve Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and subnet values. Use the CreateChangeSet and ExecuteChangeSet commands to update existing development environments.","D":"Use Fn::ImportValue intrinsic functions in the Parameters section of the root template to retrieve Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) and subnet values. Define the development resources in the order they need to be created in the CloudFormation nested stacks. Use the CreateChangeSet and ExecuteChangeSet commands to update existing development environments."},"options_zh":{"A":"在模板的“资源”部分使用 Fn::ImportValue 内置函数来获取虚拟私有云（VPC）和子网的值。使用 CloudFormation StackSets 来创建开发环境，通过“Count”输入参数来指定所需的环境数量。使用 UpdateStackSet 命令来更新现有的开发环境。","B":"使用嵌套堆栈来定义常见的基础架构组件。要访问导出的值，请使用 TemplateURL 引用网络团队 的模板。要在根模板的参数部分获取虚拟私有云（VPC）和子网的值，请使用 Fn::ImportValue 内 置函数。使用 CreateChangeSet 和 ExecuteChangeSet 命令来更新现有的开发环境。","C":"使用嵌套堆栈来定义常见的基础设施组件。使用 Fn::ImportValue 内置函数以及嵌套堆栈中的资 源来获取虚拟私有云（VPC）和子网的值。使用 CreateChangeSet 和 ExecuteChangeSet 命令来 更新现有的开发环境。","D":"在根模板的参数部分使用 Fn::ImportValue 内置函数来获取虚拟私有云（VPC）和子网的值。按照 创建顺序在 CloudFormation 嵌套堆栈中定义开发资源。使用 CreateChangeSet 和 ExecuteChangeSet 命令来更新现有的开发环境。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The scenario needs reusable common components (ALBs, Auto Scaling groups, security groups, DynamoDB tables) shared across many identical dev environments, consumption of the networking team's exported VPC/subnet outputs, and an easy way to update deployed infrastructure as it grows. Nested stacks are AWS's recommended way to package repeatedly-used resource configurations into dedicated reusable templates referenced via AWS::CloudFormation::Stack. Fn::ImportValue consumes another stack's exported Outputs (same account and Region), and the canonical AWS example shows it placed inside a resource property (for example SubnetId: Fn::ImportValue ...), i.e. with the resources of the (nested) stack. Change sets for nested stacks let you preview and then apply updates across the entire stack hierarchy via CreateChangeSet/ExecuteChangeSet, satisfying the 'easily update' requirement. Option C is the only choice that gets all three pieces right. The decisive flaw in B and D is that they place Fn::ImportValue in the Parameters section, where only static attributes (Type, Default, AllowedValues, etc.) are valid and intrinsic functions are not resolved; A invents a non-existent StackSets 'Count' input parameter and uses StackSets (cross-account/Region orchestration) instead of nested stacks.","explanation_zh":"此情境需要在多個相同的開發環境間共用可重用的共通元件 (Application Load Balancers、EC2 Auto Scaling groups、security groups、DynamoDB tables)、取用 networking 團隊匯出的 VPC/subnet outputs，並能隨著基礎設施成長輕鬆更新已部署的資源。Nested stacks 是 AWS 建議用來把重複使用的資源組態封裝成專屬可重用範本 (透過 AWS::CloudFormation::Stack 引用) 的方式。Fn::ImportValue 用來取用另一個 stack 匯出的 Outputs (限同一 account 與 Region)，且 AWS 官方範例顯示它應放在資源屬性中 (例如 SubnetId: Fn::ImportValue ...)，也就是放在 (nested) stack 的 resources 內。Change sets for nested stacks 可透過 CreateChangeSet/ExecuteChangeSet 預覽並套用整個 stack 階層的更新，滿足『輕鬆更新』需求。Option C 是唯一三個要件都正確的選項。B 與 D 的決定性錯誤在於把 Fn::ImportValue 放在 Parameters section，而該 section 只接受靜態屬性 (Type、Default、AllowedValues 等)，intrinsic functions 不會在此被解析；A 則杜撰了不存在的 StackSets 'Count' 輸入參數，且改用 StackSets (跨 account/Region 編排) 而非 nested stacks。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"StackSets has no 'Count' input parameter; StackSets is designed to deploy a stack across multiple accounts/Regions, not to spin up N copies in one account via a count. It also abandons the requested nested-stack reuse model. While UpdateStackSet is real, the invented Count premise makes the option invalid, and Fn::ImportValue is limited to the same account and Region.","why_zh":"StackSets 沒有 'Count' 輸入參數；StackSets 是用來跨多個 account/Region 部署 stack，而非以計數方式在單一 account 建立 N 份副本，且放棄了題目要求的 nested-stack 重用模型。雖然 UpdateStackSet 確實存在，但杜撰的 Count 前提使此選項無效，且 Fn::ImportValue 僅限同一 account 與 Region。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Places Fn::ImportValue in the Parameters section, where intrinsic functions are not evaluated (only static attributes like Type/Default/AllowedValues are valid). It also misframes TemplateURL as a way to 'access exported values'; TemplateURL points to a child template to nest as its own stack, not a mechanism to read another stack's exported outputs.","why_zh":"把 Fn::ImportValue 放在 Parameters section，而該處不會解析 intrinsic functions (僅接受 Type/Default/AllowedValues 等靜態屬性)。並錯誤地把 TemplateURL 描述為『取用匯出值』的方式；TemplateURL 指向要當成 nested stack 部署的子範本，並非讀取另一個 stack 已匯出 outputs 的機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as B: Fn::ImportValue is not valid in the Parameters section of the root template because that section does not resolve intrinsic functions. CloudFormation also resolves resource creation order automatically via dependency references (Ref/GetAtt) and DependsOn, so manually 'defining resources in the order they need to be created' is unnecessary and is not how nested-stack ordering is expressed.","why_zh":"與 B 相同的致命缺陷：Fn::ImportValue 不能用於 root template 的 Parameters section，因該處不解析 intrinsic functions。CloudFormation 也會透過相依參照 (Ref/GetAtt) 與 DependsOn 自動決定資源建立順序，故手動『依建立順序定義資源』既非必要，也非 nested-stack 排序的表達方式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/intrinsic-function-reference-importvalue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/parameters-section-structure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-nested-stacks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/change-sets-for-nested-stacks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-stack-exports.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":52,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage multiple accounts. Information security policies require that all unencrypted Amazon EBS volumes be marked as non-compliant. A DevOps engineer needs to automatically deploy the solution and ensure that this compliance check is always present. Which solution will accomplish this?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理多个账户。信息安全政策要求将所有未加密的 Amazon EBS 卷标记为不符合规定。一位 DevOps 工程师需要自动部署解决方案，并确保始终执行此合规性检查。 哪种解决方案能实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that defines an AWS Inspector rule to check whether EBS encryption is enabled. Save the template to an Amazon S3 bucket that has been shared with all accounts within the company. Update the account creation script pointing to the CloudFormation template in Amazon S3.","B":"Create an AWS Config organizational rule to check whether EBS encryption is enabled and deploy the rule using the AWS CLI. Create and apply an SCP to prohibit stopping and deleting AWS Config across the organization.","C":"Create an SCP in Organizations. Set the policy to prevent the launch of Amazon EC2 instances without encryption on the EBS volumes using a conditional expression. Apply the SCP to all AWS accounts. Use Amazon Athena to analyze the AWS CloudTrail output, looking for events that deny an ec2:RunInstances action.","D":"Deploy an IAM role to all accounts from a single trusted account. Build a pipeline with AWS CodePipeline with a stage in AWS Lambda to assume the IAM role, and list all EBS volumes in the account. Publish a report to Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，定义一个 AWS Inspector 规则以检查 EBS 加密是否已启用。 将该模板保存到已与公司内所有账户共享的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。更新账户创建脚本，使其指 向 Amazon S3 中的 CloudFormation 模板。","B":"使用 AWS CLI 创建一条 AWS Config 组织规则，以检查 EBS 加密是否已启用，并部署该规则。创建 并应用一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止停止和删除 AWS Config 资源。 该组织。","C":"在组织中创建一个服务控制策略（SCP）。使用条件表达式设置策略，以防止在未对 EBS 卷进行加密 的情况下启动 Amazon EC2 实例。将该 SCP 应用于所有 AWS 账户。使用 Amazon Athena 分析 AWS CloudTrail 输出，查找拒绝 ec2:RunInstances 操作的事件。","D":"从一个受信任的账户向所有账户部署一个 IAM 角色。使用 AWS CodePipeline 构建一个管道，在 AWS Lambda 中设置一个阶段以承担该 IAM 角色，并列出该账户中的所有 EBS 卷。将报告发 布到 Amazon S3。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is detective: mark all unencrypted EBS volumes as NON_COMPLIANT across an AWS Organizations multi-account environment, deploy it automatically, and ensure the check is always present. AWS Config provides the managed rule 'encrypted-volumes' (identifier ENCRYPTED_VOLUMES) which checks attached AWS::EC2::Volume resources and reports NON_COMPLIANT when a volume is unencrypted, exactly matching the requirement wording. AWS Config organization rules are created with PutOrganizationConfigRule and, per AWS docs, can only be created via the API or CLI (the console is not supported), which is why option B specifies the AWS CLI; they deploy the rule across all member accounts, auto-deploy to any new account that joins (and remove it when an account leaves), and let the management/delegated administrator account enforce governance so member accounts cannot modify the rule. Applying an SCP that prohibits stopping/deleting AWS Config (e.g., config:StopConfigurationRecorder, config:DeleteConfigurationRecorder) prevents member accounts from disabling the recorder, satisfying the 'always present' requirement. Option B is the only choice that delivers detective compliance marking, organization-wide automatic deployment, and persistence.","explanation_zh":"需求屬於偵測型 (detective)：在 AWS Organizations 多帳戶環境中，將所有未加密的 EBS volume 標記為 NON_COMPLIANT，自動部署，並確保此合規檢查始終存在。AWS Config 提供受管規則 'encrypted-volumes'（識別碼 ENCRYPTED_VOLUMES），會檢查已掛載的 AWS::EC2::Volume 資源，volume 未加密時回報 NON_COMPLIANT，與需求字面完全相符。AWS Config 的 organization rule 透過 PutOrganizationConfigRule 建立，依官方文件只能透過 API 或 CLI 建立（不支援主控台），這正是選項 B 指定使用 AWS CLI 的原因；它會將規則部署到所有成員帳戶、對新加入的帳戶自動部署（帳戶離開時自動移除），並讓管理帳戶/委派管理員帳戶強制治理，使成員帳戶無法修改規則。再套用一個禁止停止/刪除 AWS Config（例如 config:StopConfigurationRecorder、config:DeleteConfigurationRecorder）的 SCP，可防止成員帳戶停用 recorder，滿足『始終存在』的要求。選項 B 是唯一同時達成偵測型合規標記、組織範圍自動部署與持久性的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability and network-reachability assessment service; it has no 'rule' that evaluates whether EBS encryption is enabled and produces a NON_COMPLIANT compliance marking - that capability belongs to AWS Config, not Inspector. Distributing a CloudFormation template via S3 and an account-creation script is also brittle and does not guarantee the check is 'always present' (nothing prevents deletion or skipping it).","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是漏洞與網路可達性評估服務，並沒有判斷 EBS 加密是否啟用並產生 NON_COMPLIANT 合規標記的『規則』——該能力屬於 AWS Config，而非 Inspector。透過 S3 散佈 CloudFormation 範本並依賴帳戶建立腳本既脆弱，也無法保證檢查『始終存在』（無法防止刪除或略過）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP with a conditional expression is preventive: it blocks launching EC2 with unencrypted volumes, but it does not 'mark unencrypted EBS volumes as non-compliant' (no compliance reporting) and cannot flag pre-existing unencrypted volumes. Using Athena over CloudTrail to find denied ec2:RunInstances events audits blocked launch attempts, not the compliance state of existing volumes, so it fails the stated detective requirement and adds high operational overhead.","why_zh":"帶條件運算式的 SCP 屬於預防型：它阻擋啟動帶有未加密 volume 的 EC2，但不會『將未加密的 EBS volume 標記為 non-compliant』（沒有合規回報），也無法標記既有的未加密 volume。用 Athena 分析 CloudTrail 尋找被拒絕的 ec2:RunInstances 事件，是稽核被擋下的啟動嘗試，而非既有 volume 的合規狀態，因此不符合偵測型需求且營運負擔高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A custom CodePipeline + Lambda solution that assumes a role, lists EBS volumes, and publishes a report to S3 is a hand-built, point-in-time inventory job. It does not produce a managed continuous NON_COMPLIANT compliance state, does not automatically apply to new accounts, is not guaranteed to be 'always present', and reinvents functionality AWS Config provides natively - over-engineered and fragile.","why_zh":"自建的 CodePipeline + Lambda 方案（assume role、列出 EBS volume、寫報告到 S3）是手工、時間點式的盤點作業。它不會產生受管的持續性 NON_COMPLIANT 合規狀態，不會自動套用到新帳戶，也無法保證『始終存在』，且重新發明了 AWS Config 原生提供的功能——過度設計且脆弱。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/encrypted-volumes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/config-rule-multi-account-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/APIReference/API_PutOrganizationConfigRule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":53,"question_en":"A company is performing vulnerability scanning for all Amazon EC2 instances across many accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. Each account's VPCs are attached to a shared transit gateway. The VPCs send traffic to the internet through a central egress VPC. The company has enabled Amazon Inspector in a delegated administrator account and has enabled scanning for all member accounts. A DevOps engineer discovers that some EC2 instances are listed in the \"not scanning\" tab in Amazon Inspector. Which combination of actions should the DevOps engineer take to resolve this issue? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在对多个账户中的所有亚马逊 EC2 实例执行漏洞扫描。这些账户位于 AWS 组织中的一个组 织内。每个账户的 VPC 都连接到一个共享的中转网关。VPC 通过一个中央出口 VPC 访问互联网。该公 司已在委托管理员账户中启用了 Amazon Inspector，并为所有成员账户启用了扫描功能。 一位 DevOps 工程师发现，亚马逊 Inspector 中的“未扫描”选项卡里列出了部分 EC2 实例。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些行动组合来解决此问题？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Verify that AWS Systems Manager Agent is installed and is running on the EC2 instances that Amazon Inspector is not scanning.","B":"Associate the target EC2 instances with security groups that allow outbound communication on port 443 to the AWS Systems Manager service endpoint.","C":"Grant inspector:StartAssessmentRun permissions to the IAM role that the DevOps engineer is using.","D":"Configure EC2 Instance Connect for the EC2 instances that Amazon Inspector is not scanning.","E":"Associate the target EC2 instances with instance profiles that grant permissions to communicate with AWS Systems Manager.","F":"Create a managed-instance activation. Use the Activation Code and the Activation ID to register the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"确认 AWS 系统管理器代理已安装并正在运行在亚马逊 Inspector 未扫描的 EC2 实例上。","B":"将目标 EC2 实例与允许通过端口 443 向 AWS Systems Manager 服务端点进行出站通信的安全组相 关联。","C":"授予检查员：启动评估运行权限给开发运维工程师正在使用的 IAM 角色。","D":"为 Amazon Inspector 不扫描的 EC2 实例配置 EC2 实例连接。","E":"将目标 EC2 实例与授予其与 AWS Systems Manager 通信权限的实例配置文件相关联。","F":"创建托管实例激活。使用激活码和激活 ID 注册 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A","B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Inspector's Enhanced EC2 (VM) Scanning installs and runs the scanner via AWS Systems Manager (SSM). For an instance to be scanned (and not appear in the 'not scanning' tab), the official requirements are: (1) the SSM Agent is installed and running on the instance (Option A); (2) the instance has an IAM instance profile that allows SSM to manage it (Option E); and (3) the instance has network connectivity to the SSM service endpoints, which requires SSM Agent to reach the SSM/ssmmessages endpoints over HTTPS port 443 outbound (Option B). These three requirements are explicitly listed on the Inspector 'Enabling Inspector VM Scanner / Requirements' page and the SSM Agent troubleshooting page (port 443 to ssm/ssmmessages). Together they directly resolve why instances show as 'not scanning'.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Inspector 的 Enhanced EC2 (VM) Scanning 透過 AWS Systems Manager (SSM) 安裝並執行掃描器。要讓執行個體能被掃描（不出現在 'not scanning' 分頁），官方需求為：(1) 執行個體上已安裝並執行 SSM Agent（選項 A）；(2) 執行個體具有允許 SSM 管理它的 IAM instance profile（選項 E）；(3) 執行個體可連線到 SSM service endpoints，亦即 SSM Agent 需透過 HTTPS port 443 對外連到 ssm/ssmmessages endpoints（選項 B）。這三項需求明確列於 Inspector 'Enabling Inspector VM Scanner / Requirements' 頁面及 SSM Agent 疑難排解頁面（port 443 連到 ssm/ssmmessages），共同解決執行個體顯示為 'not scanning' 的問題。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"inspector:StartAssessmentRun is an Inspector Classic (v1) API and is unrelated to Inspector v2 continuous VM scanning. The 'not scanning' status is caused by SSM eligibility on the instances, not by the engineer's IAM permission to start an assessment run. The DevOps engineer's permissions do not affect whether an instance is scannable.","why_zh":"inspector:StartAssessmentRun 屬於 Inspector Classic (v1) API，與 Inspector v2 的持續性 VM 掃描無關。'not scanning' 狀態是由執行個體的 SSM 適格性造成，而非工程師啟動評估的 IAM 權限；工程師的權限不影響執行個體是否可被掃描。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EC2 Instance Connect provides SSH browser access to instances; it has nothing to do with Inspector scanning, which relies on SSM Agent connectivity to AWS endpoints, not interactive SSH sessions.","why_zh":"EC2 Instance Connect 提供瀏覽器 SSH 連線存取，與 Inspector 掃描無關。Inspector 掃描依賴 SSM Agent 連線到 AWS endpoints，而非互動式 SSH 工作階段。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Managed-instance (hybrid) activation using an Activation Code and Activation ID is the registration method for non-EC2 / on-premises servers and VMs. EC2 instances must NOT be registered this way; they use an attached IAM instance profile (Option E) instead. Using hybrid activation on EC2 is incorrect and unsupported for this use case.","why_zh":"使用 Activation Code 與 Activation ID 的 managed-instance（hybrid）activation 是用於非 EC2／地端伺服器與 VM 的註冊方式。EC2 執行個體不應以此方式註冊，而應改用附加的 IAM instance profile（選項 E）。對 EC2 使用 hybrid activation 在此情境屬錯誤且不受支援。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/inspector-vm-scanner-enabling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-ssm-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/setup-instance-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-activation-managed-nodes.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":54,"question_en":"A development team uses AWS CodeCommit for version control for applications. The development team uses AWS CodePipeline, AWS CodeBuild. and AWS CodeDeploy for CI/CD infrastructure. In CodeCommit, the development team recently merged pull requests that did not pass long-running tests in the code base. The development team needed to perform rollbacks to branches in the codebase, resulting in lost time and wasted effort. A DevOps engineer must automate testing of pull requests in CodeCommit to ensure that reviewers more easily see the results of automated tests as part of the pull request review. What should the DevOps engineer do to meet this requirement?","question_zh":"开发团队使用 AWS CodeCommit 对应用程序进行版本控制。该团队使用 AWS CodePipeline、AWS CodeBuild 和 AWS CodeDeploy 构建持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）基础设施。在 CodeCommit 中，开发 团队最近合并了一些未通过代码库中长期运行测试的拉取请求。开发团队需要对代码库中的分支执行回 滚操作，导致浪费了时间和精力。 DevOps 工程师必须在 CodeCommit 中实现对拉取请求的自动化测试，以便审阅者在审查拉取请求时能 更轻松地查看自动化测试的结果。 开发运维工程师应该怎么做才能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to the pullRequestStatusChanged event. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes a CodePipeline pipeline with a CodeBuild action that runs the tests for the application. Program the Lambda function to post the CodeBuild badge as a comment on the pull request so that developers will see the badge in their code review.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to the pullRequestCreated event. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes a CodePipeline pipeline with a CodeBuild action that runs the tests for the application. Program the Lambda function to post the CodeBuild test results as a comment on the pull request when the test results are complete.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to pullRequestCreated and pullRequestSourceBranchUpdated events. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes a CodePipeline pipeline with a CodeBuild action that runs the tests for the application. Program the Lambda function to post the CodeBuild badge as a comment on the pull request so that developers will see the badge in their code review.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to the pullRequestStatusChanged event. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes a CodePipeline pipeline with a CodeBuild action that runs the tests for the application. Program the Lambda function to post the CodeBuild test results as a comment on the pull request when the test results are complete."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 pullRequestStatusChanged 事件做出响应。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用具有 CodeBuild 操作的 CodePipeline 管道，以运行应用程序的测试。编写 Lambda 函数，使其将 CodeBuild 徽章作为评论发布在拉取请求上，以便开发人员在代码审查时能看 到该徽章。","B":"创建一个亚马逊账 户 对“pullRequestCreated”事件作出响应的 EventBridge 规则。创建一个 AWS 一个 Lambda 函数，用于调用具有 CodeBuild 操作的 CodePipeline 管道，该操作会运行应用程序 的测试。编写该 Lambda 函数，使其在测试结果完成后将 CodeBuild 测试结果作为评论发布到拉 取请求中。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 pullRequestCreated 和 pullRequestSourceBranchUpdated 事件做出响应。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用具有 CodeBuild 操作的 CodePipeline 管 道，以运行应用程序的测试。编写 Lambda 函数，使其将 CodeBuild 徽章作为评论发布到拉取请求 中，以便开发人员在代码审查时能看到该徽章。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 pullRequestStatusChanged 事件做出响应。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用具有 CodeBuild 操作的 CodePipeline 管道，以运行应用程序的测 试。编写 Lambda 函数，使其在测试结果完成后将 CodeBuild 测试结果作为评论发布到拉取请求 中。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The recurring problem is that code which failed long-running tests kept getting merged, including commits pushed to a pull request AFTER it was opened, forcing rollbacks. To prevent this, the tests must run both when a PR is first created and every time the source branch receives new commits. Per the CodeCommit EventBridge events reference, pullRequestCreated fires once at PR creation, and pullRequestSourceBranchUpdated fires when 'one or more commits' are added to the source branch of an open PR. Only option C subscribes to BOTH events, giving full coverage so later commits are re-tested before merge. pullRequestStatusChanged (A and D) is the wrong trigger: the doc example shows it firing on a status transition such as Open to Closed, so it does not run tests on creation or on new commits before review/merge. Option B triggers only on pullRequestCreated, so commits pushed after the PR is opened are never re-tested, leaving the exact described failure mode open. C's CodeBuild build badge (PASSING/FAILING/IN_PROGRESS/UNKNOWN for the most recent branch build) is an AWS-documented way to surface automated build/test status in the source repository, so reviewers can see pass/fail as part of the review. Because the primary business problem is untested code being merged, correct event coverage is the load-bearing, non-negotiable factor, making C the best single answer.","explanation_zh":"反覆出現的問題是未通過長時間測試的程式碼一直被合併，且包含在 pull request 開啟之後才推送的 commit，導致必須回滾。要避免這種情況，測試必須在 PR 建立時、以及每次 source branch 收到新 commit 時都執行。根據 CodeCommit 的 EventBridge events 參考文件，pullRequestCreated 只在 PR 建立時觸發一次，而 pullRequestSourceBranchUpdated 會在開啟中的 PR 其 source branch 被加入「一個或多個 commit」時觸發。只有選項 C 同時訂閱這兩個事件，提供完整覆蓋，使後續 commit 在合併前都被重新測試。pullRequestStatusChanged（A 與 D）是錯誤的觸發器：文件範例顯示它在狀態轉換（例如 Open 變為 Closed）時觸發，因此不會在建立時或新 commit 時於審查/合併前執行測試。選項 B 只在 pullRequestCreated 時觸發，因此 PR 開啟之後推送的 commit 永遠不會被重新測試，正好留下題目所述的失敗情境。C 使用的 CodeBuild build badge（顯示最近一次分支建置的 PASSING/FAILING/IN_PROGRESS/UNKNOWN）是 AWS 文件記載、用於在 source repository 中呈現自動化建置/測試狀態的方式，讓審查者能在審查中看到通過或失敗。由於主要的業務問題是未測試的程式碼被合併，正確的事件覆蓋是關鍵且不可妥協的因素，因此 C 是最佳的單一答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Reacts only to pullRequestStatusChanged, which the CodeCommit events doc shows firing on status transitions such as Open to Closed/Merged. It would not run tests when a PR is created or when new commits are added, so failing code would not be caught before review or merge.","why_zh":"只回應 pullRequestStatusChanged，CodeCommit 事件文件顯示它在狀態轉換（如 Open 變為 Closed/Merged）時觸發。它不會在 PR 建立時或加入新 commit 時執行測試，因此無法在審查或合併前攔截失敗的程式碼。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Triggers only on pullRequestCreated, so commits pushed to the source branch after the PR is opened are never re-tested. This leaves the exact described failure mode (later commits that fail tests getting merged) unaddressed, even though posting actual test results is otherwise a good approach.","why_zh":"只在 pullRequestCreated 時觸發，因此 PR 開啟後推送到 source branch 的 commit 永遠不會被重新測試。雖然張貼實際測試結果是不錯的做法，但這仍未解決題目所述的失敗情境（之後加入且未通過測試的 commit 被合併）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses pullRequestStatusChanged as the trigger, which fires on status transitions (e.g., Open to Closed) rather than at creation or on new commits. Tests would run at the wrong time and not before review/merge, so it fails to prevent merging code that did not pass tests, despite posting test results.","why_zh":"使用 pullRequestStatusChanged 作為觸發器，它在狀態轉換（例如 Open 變為 Closed）時觸發，而非在建立或新 commit 時。測試會在錯誤的時間執行，且不在審查/合併之前，因此即使有張貼測試結果，仍無法避免合併未通過測試的程式碼。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/monitoring-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codecommit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/badge-statuses.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/publish-badges.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/v1/reference/codecommit/post-comment-for-pull-request.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":55,"question_en":"A company has deployed an application in a production VPC in a single AWS account. The application is popular and is experiencing heavy usage. The company’s security team wants to add additional security, such as AWS WAF, to the application deployment. However, the application's product manager is concerned about cost and does not want to approve the change unless the security team can prove that additional security is necessary. The security team believes that some of the application's demand might come from users that have IP addresses that are on a deny list. The security team provides the deny list to a DevOps engineer. If any of the IP addresses on the deny list access the application, the security team wants to receive automated notification in near real time so that the security team can document that the application needs additional security. The DevOps engineer creates a VPC flow log for the production VPC. Which set of additional steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements MOST cost- effectively?","question_zh":"一家公司在其单个 AWS 账户中的生产 VPC 中部署了一个应用程序。该应用程序很受欢迎，使用量 很大。公司的安全团队希望为应用程序部署添加额外的安全措施，例如 AWS WAF。然而，该应用程 序的产品经理担心成本问题，除非安全团队能够证明额外的安全措施是必要的，否则不会批准这一 变更。 安全团队认为，该应用程序的部分请求可能来自被列入拒绝访问列表的用户。安全团队将拒绝访问列 表提供给了一位 DevOps 工程师。如果拒绝访问列表中的任何 IP 地址访问该应用程序，安全团队希望 在近乎实时的情况下收到自动通知，以便安全团队能够记录该应用程序需要额外的安全措施。DevOps 工程师为生产 VPC 创建了 VPC 流日志。 为了以最经济高效的方式满足这些要求，DevOps 工程师应采取哪一组额外步骤？","options_en":{"A":"Create a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Configure the VPC flow log to capture accepted traffic and to send the data to the log group. Create an Amazon CloudWatch metric filter for IP addresses on the deny list. Create a CloudWatch alarm with the metric filter as input. Set the period to 5 minutes and the datapoints to alarm to 1. Use an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to send alarm notices to the security team.","B":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket for log files. Configure the VPC flow log to capture all traffic and to send the data to the S3 bucket. Configure Amazon Athena to return all log files in the S3 bucket for IP addresses on the deny list. Configure Amazon QuickSight to accept data from Athena and to publish the data as a dashboard that the security team can access. Create a threshold alert of 1 for successful access. Configure the alert to automatically notify the security team as frequently as possible when the alert threshold is met.","C":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket for log files. Configure the VPC flow log to capture accepted traffic and to send the data to the S3 bucket. Configure an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster and domain for the log files. Create an AWS Lambda function to retrieve the logs from the S3 bucket, format the logs, and load the logs into the OpenSearch Service cluster. Schedule the Lambda function to run every 5 minutes. Configure an alert and condition in OpenSearch Service to send alerts to the security team through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when access from the IP addresses on the deny list is detected.","D":"Create a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to hold query results. Configure the VPC flow log to capture all traffic and to send the data to the log group. Deploy an Amazon Athena CloudWatch connector in AWS Lambda. Connect the connector to the log group. Configure Athena to periodically query for all accepted traffic from the IP addresses on the deny list and to store the results in the S3 bucket. Configure an S3 event notification to automatically notify the security team through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when new objects are added to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中创建一个日志组。配置 VPC 流日志以捕获已接受的流量，并将数据 发送到该日志组。为拒绝列表中的 IP 地址创建一个 CloudWatch 指标过滤器。使用该指标过滤器 作为输入创建一个 CloudWatch 警报。将周期设置为 5 分钟，将触发警报的数据点设置为 1。使用 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题向安全团队发送警报通知。","B":"创建一个用于日志文件的 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 VPC 流日志以捕获所有流量，并将数据发送到 该 S3 存储桶。配置 Amazon Athena 以返回 S3 存储桶中所有列入拒绝列表的 IP 地址的日志文件。 配置 Amazon QuickSight 以接受来自 Athena 的数据，并将数据发布为安全团队可访问的仪表板。 设置成功访问的阈值警报为 1。配置警报，使其在达到警报阈值时尽可能频繁地自动通知安全团 队。","C":"创建一个用于日志文件的 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 VPC 流日志以捕获已接受的流量，并将数据发 送到 S3 存储桶。配置一个用于日志文件的 Amazon OpenSearch Service 集群和域。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于从 S3 存储桶中检索日志，格式化日志，并将日志加载到 OpenSearch Service 集 群中。安排该 Lambda 函数每 5 分钟运行一次。在 OpenSearch Service 中配置警报和条件，当检测 到来自拒绝列表中的 IP 地址的访问时，通过 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题向安全团队发送警报。","D":"在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中创建一个日志组。创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶来保存查询结果。配置 VPC 流日志以捕获所有流量，并将数据发送到日志组。在 AWS Lambda 中部署一个 Amazon Athena CloudWatch 连接器。将连接器连接到日志组。配置 Athena 定期查询拒绝列表中 IP 地址的 所有已接受流量，并将结果存储在 S3 存储桶中。配置 S3 事件通知，当有新对象添加到 S3 存储桶 时，通过 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题自动通知安全团队。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is near-real-time, automated notification when deny-list IPs access the application, done MOST cost-effectively. Option A is exactly the pattern AWS documents in 'Process flow log records in CloudWatch Logs': publish VPC flow logs to a CloudWatch Logs log group, create a metric filter that matches the target traffic pattern (the AWS example matches REJECT SSH; here it matches the deny-list IPs in the source field), create a CloudWatch alarm on that metric, and notify via an SNS topic. Metric filters convert log data into metrics as the logs arrive, and a 5-minute period with datapoints-to-alarm of 1 fires on a single matching event, giving near-real-time alerting. Capturing accepted traffic is correct because, with no WAF yet, deny-list users actually reach the application, so the team must prove that access on accepted traffic. This solution is fully serverless and uses only a CloudWatch Logs metric filter, a CloudWatch alarm, and an SNS topic, making it the cheapest of the four options. The other options layer on Athena, QuickSight, or an always-on OpenSearch cluster, which add cost and reduce timeliness.","explanation_zh":"需求是當拒絕清單上的 IP 存取應用程式時，以最具成本效益的方式提供近即時的自動通知。選項 A 正是 AWS 文件「Process flow log records in CloudWatch Logs」所記載的模式：將 VPC flow logs 發佈到 CloudWatch Logs log group，建立比對目標流量模式的 metric filter（AWS 範例比對 REJECT SSH，本題比對 source 欄位中拒絕清單的 IP），對該 metric 建立 CloudWatch alarm，並透過 SNS topic 通知。Metric filter 會在日誌送達時即時將日誌資料轉為 metric，搭配週期 5 分鐘、datapoints to alarm 設為 1，可在單一符合事件時近即時告警。擷取已接受 (accepted) 流量是正確的，因為目前尚未有 WAF，拒絕清單的使用者確實會抵達應用程式，因此團隊必須證明這些已接受流量上的存取行為。此方案完全 serverless，只用到 CloudWatch Logs metric filter、CloudWatch alarm 與 SNS topic，是四個選項中最便宜的。其他選項加上了 Athena、QuickSight 或常駐的 OpenSearch 叢集，既增加成本又降低即時性。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Athena + QuickSight is a batch analytics / BI dashboard pipeline, not near-real-time alerting. QuickSight threshold alerts are not designed for near-real-time security notifications, and QuickSight is an expensive BI service requiring user subscriptions. This is neither timely nor cost-effective.","why_zh":"Athena + QuickSight 是批次分析/BI 儀表板管線，並非近即時告警。QuickSight 閾值警示並非為近即時安全通知設計，且 QuickSight 是需要使用者訂閱的昂貴 BI 服務。既不即時也不具成本效益。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster runs 24/7 and is the most expensive option here; adding a Lambda that runs every 5 minutes to pull logs from S3, format them, and load them into the cluster adds operational overhead and latency. This contradicts the MOST cost-effective requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon OpenSearch Service 叢集需 24/7 持續運行，是此處最昂貴的選項；再加上每 5 分鐘從 S3 拉取、格式化並載入日誌的 Lambda，增加維運負擔與延遲。這違背最具成本效益的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using the Athena CloudWatch (federated query) connector via Lambda, periodic Athena queries, an S3 results bucket, and S3 event notifications is far more complex and costly than a native metric filter. Periodic Athena queries are batch, not near real time, and capturing all traffic increases ingestion cost.","why_zh":"透過 Lambda 使用 Athena CloudWatch（聯合查詢）連接器、定期 Athena 查詢、S3 結果儲存桶與 S3 事件通知，遠比原生 metric filter 更複雜且昂貴。定期 Athena 查詢屬批次處理，並非近即時，且擷取所有流量會增加擷取成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/process-records-cwl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs-cwl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":56,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer has automated a web service deployment by using AWS CodePipeline with the following steps: 1. An AWS CodeBuild project compiles the deployment artifact and runs unit tests. 2. An AWS CodeDeploy deployment group deploys the web service to Amazon EC2 instances in the staging environment. 3. A CodeDeploy deployment group deploys the web service to EC2 instances in the production environment. The quality assurance (QA) team requests permission to inspect the build artifact before the deployment to the production environment occurs. The QA team wants to run an internal penetration testing tool to conduct manual tests. The tool will be invoked by a REST API call. Which combination of actions should the DevOps engineer take to fulfill this request? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师通过使用 AWS CodePipeline 自动化了一个 Web 服务的部署，具体步骤如下： 1. 一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目会编译部署工件并运行单元测试。 2. AWS CodeDeploy 部署组将 Web 服务部署到预生产环境中的 Amazon EC2 实例上。 3. 一个 CodeDeploy 部署组将网络服务部署到生产环境中的 EC2 实例上。 质量保证（QA）团队请求在部署到生产环境之前检查构建工件。QA 团队希望运行一个内部渗透测试工 具来进行手动测试。该工具将通过 REST API 调用进行调用。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪两种组合操作来满足此请求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Insert a manual approval action between the test actions and deployment actions of the pipeline.","B":"Modify the buildspec.yml file for the compilation stage to require manual approval before completion.","C":"Update the CodeDeploy deployment groups so that they require manual approval to proceed.","D":"Update the pipeline to directly call the REST API for the penetration testing tool.","E":"Update the pipeline to invoke an AWS Lambda function that calls the REST API for the penetration testing tool."},"options_zh":{"A":"在流水线的测试操作和部署操作之间插入一个手动审批操作。","B":"修改用于编译阶段的 buildspec.yml 文件，使其在完成前需要人工审批。","C":"更新 CodeDeploy 部署组，使其在继续执行前需要手动审批。","D":"更新管道，使其直接调用渗透测试工具的 REST API。","E":"更新管道以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会调用渗透测试工具的 REST API。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must be met: pause the pipeline before production so the QA team can inspect the build artifact, and trigger an external penetration-testing tool via a REST API call. A manual approval action (A) is the exact CodePipeline construct for this; AWS docs state you use manual approvals when 'you want someone to perform manual quality assurance testing on the latest version of an application, or to confirm the integrity of a build artifact, before it is released.' Placed between the staging actions and the production deploy action, it stops execution until an authorized IAM approver approves. CodePipeline's built-in action categories are only Source, Build, Test, Deploy, Approval, and Invoke, so there is no native action that directly calls an arbitrary external REST API; the documented pattern is a Lambda invoke action (E), since the docs say Lambda lets you 'perform almost any task' and explicitly list 'To add integration with third-party products to your pipeline' as a use case. The Lambda function calls the pen-testing tool's REST API. Together, the approval gate plus the Lambda-invoked REST call satisfy both requirements.","explanation_zh":"需滿足兩項需求：在進入 production 前暫停 pipeline，讓 QA 團隊檢查 build artifact；以及透過 REST API 觸發外部滲透測試工具。Manual approval action (A) 正是 CodePipeline 為此設計的機制；AWS 文件指出，當你希望有人『對應用程式最新版本執行手動品質保證測試，或在發行前確認 build artifact 的完整性』時即可使用 manual approval。把它放在 staging 動作與 production 部署動作之間，會讓執行暫停直到授權的 IAM 核准者核准。CodePipeline 的內建 action 類別僅有 Source、Build、Test、Deploy、Approval 與 Invoke，故沒有可直接呼叫任意外部 REST API 的原生 action；文件記載的標準做法是使用 Lambda invoke action (E)，因為文件說明 Lambda 可『執行幾乎任何任務』，並明列『為 pipeline 加入與第三方產品的整合』作為用途。由 Lambda function 呼叫滲透測試工具的 REST API。核准關卡加上由 Lambda 觸發的 REST 呼叫，正好滿足兩項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeBuild's buildspec.yml has no manual-approval mechanism. Buildspec only defines build phases (install, pre_build, build, post_build) and commands; pausing for human approval is a pipeline-level construct (manual approval action), not a build-phase feature. It is also at the wrong place (compilation stage, not before production), and it does not invoke the pen-testing REST API.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 的 buildspec.yml 沒有手動核准機制。Buildspec 僅定義 build 階段（install、pre_build、build、post_build）與指令；等待人工核准是 pipeline 層級的 manual approval action，而非 build 階段功能。位置也不對（在編譯階段，而非 production 前），且不會呼叫滲透測試的 REST API。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeDeploy deployment groups have no 'require manual approval to proceed' setting. Deployment group settings cover deployment type, target instances/tags, traffic shifting, CloudWatch alarms, load balancers, and Auto Scaling groups. Human approval gating is provided by CodePipeline manual approval actions, not by a deployment group property, and this option does nothing to invoke the pen-testing tool.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy deployment group 沒有『需手動核准才能繼續』的設定。Deployment group 設定涵蓋部署類型、目標執行個體/標籤、流量轉移、CloudWatch 警示、負載平衡器與 Auto Scaling group。人工核准關卡由 CodePipeline 的 manual approval action 提供，而非 deployment group 屬性，且此選項也無法觸發滲透測試工具。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodePipeline has no native action type that directly calls an arbitrary external REST API. Built-in action categories are only Source, Build, Test, Deploy, Approval, and Invoke. To call a third-party REST API you must wrap it in a Lambda invoke action (E) or a custom action with a job worker, so a 'direct' call from the pipeline is not possible.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 沒有可直接呼叫任意外部 REST API 的原生 action type。內建 action 類別僅有 Source、Build、Test、Deploy、Approval 與 Invoke。要呼叫第三方 REST API 必須用 Lambda invoke action (E) 或自訂 action 搭配 job worker 包裝，故無法從 pipeline『直接』呼叫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-invoke-lambda-function.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-edit.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":57,"question_en":"A company is hosting a web application in an AWS Region. For disaster recovery purposes, a second region is being used as a standby. Disaster recovery requirements state that session data must be replicated between regions in near-real time and 1% of requests should route to the secondary region to continuously verify system functionality. Additionally, if there is a disruption in service in the main region, traffic should be automatically routed to the secondary region, and the secondary region must be able to scale up to handle all traffic. How should a DevOps engineer meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 区域中托管一个网络应用程序。出于灾难恢复的目的，另一个区域被用作备用区 域。灾难恢复要求规定会话数据必须在近实时状态下在两个区域之间进行复制，并且 1% 的请求应路 由到备用区域以持续验证系统功能。此外，如果主区域的服务出现中断，流量应自动路由到备用区域， 并且备用区域必须能够扩展以处理所有流量。 DevOps 工程师应如何满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In both regions, deploy the application on AWS Elastic Beanstalk and use Amazon DynamoDB global tables for session data. Use an Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy with health checks to distribute the traffic across the regions.","B":"In both regions, launch the application in Auto Scaling groups and use DynamoDB for session data. Use a Route 53 failover routing policy with health checks to distribute the traffic across the regions.","C":"In both regions, deploy the application in AWS Lambda, exposed by Amazon API Gateway, and use Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL with cross-region replication for session data. Deploy the web application with client-side logic to call the API Gateway directly.","D":"In both regions, launch the application in Auto Scaling groups and use DynamoDB global tables for session data. Enable an Amazon CloudFront weighted distribution across regions. Point the Amazon Route 53 DNS record at the CloudFront distribution."},"options_zh":{"A":"在两个区域中，均在 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 上部署应用程序，并使用 Amazon DynamoDB 全球表来 存储会话数据。使用带有健康检查的 Amazon Route 53 加权路由策略在两个区域之间分配流量。","B":"在两个区域中，以自动扩展组的形式启动应用程序，并使用 DynamoDB 存储会话数据。采用带有 健康检查的 Route 53 故障转移路由策略，在两个区域之间分配流量。","C":"在两个区域中，将应用程序部署在 AWS Lambda 中，通过 Amazon API Gateway 进行公开，并使用 具有跨区域复制功能的 Amazon RDS for PostgreSQL 来存储会话数据。将包含客户端逻辑的 Web 应用程序部署为直接调用 API Gateway。","D":"在两个区域中，以自动扩展组的形式启动应用程序，并使用 DynamoDB 全球表来存储会话数据。 在各区域启用 Amazon CloudFront 加权分发。将 Amazon Route 53 DNS 记录指向 CloudFront 分发。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Option A is the only choice that satisfies all four requirements. (1) Near-real-time cross-region session replication: Amazon DynamoDB global tables provide multi-active, asynchronous cross-region replication so writes in either region propagate to the other with low latency; plain regional DynamoDB (option B) does not replicate across regions, and RDS for PostgreSQL cross-region replication (option C) produces a read-only replica that cannot accept the session writes generated by the 1% of traffic hitting the secondary region. (2) Routing exactly 1% of requests to the secondary region: an Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy lets you set arbitrary proportions (for example weights 99 and 1) so a small, defined percentage continuously reaches the standby; a failover routing policy (option B) is active-passive and sends 0% to the standby until the primary fails, and CloudFront has no 'weighted distribution across regions' feature (option D). (3) Automatic failover: AWS docs state you configure active-active failover using any routing policy other than failover, and when a resource becomes unhealthy Route 53 detects it via the attached health check and stops including it in responses, so traffic shifts automatically to the healthy secondary. (4) Scale-up of the secondary: AWS Elastic Beanstalk runs the environment on an Auto Scaling group, so the standby region can scale to handle all traffic. Only A combines DynamoDB global tables, weighted routing with health checks, and an auto-scaling compute tier.","explanation_zh":"只有 A 同時滿足四項需求。(1) 跨區域近即時 session 複製：Amazon DynamoDB global tables 提供 multi-active、非同步的跨區域複製，兩區皆可讀寫並以低延遲同步；選項 B 的一般 regional DynamoDB 不會跨區域複製，選項 C 的 RDS for PostgreSQL 跨區域複製只能建立唯讀 replica，無法接受打到次要區域那 1% 流量所產生的 session 寫入。(2) 將恰好 1% 請求導向次要區域：Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy 可設定任意比例（例如權重 99 與 1），讓固定的少量比例持續送到 standby；選項 B 的 failover routing policy 是 active-passive，在主區故障前會送 0% 到 standby；選項 D 的 CloudFront 並無「weighted distribution across regions」這種功能，CloudFront origin groups 只能做主要到次要 origin 的 failover，無法按百分比加權。(3) 自動故障轉移：AWS 文件說明，可用 failover 以外的任何 routing policy 配置 active-active failover；當資源不健康時，Route 53 透過附加的 health check 偵測到並停止回傳該記錄，流量便自動轉到健康的次要區域。(4) 次要區域擴容：AWS Elastic Beanstalk 以 Auto Scaling group 執行環境，能擴容承接全部流量。只有 A 結合了 DynamoDB global tables、帶 health checks 的 weighted routing、以及可自動擴容的運算層。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses plain regional DynamoDB, which does NOT replicate across regions, so session data is not available in the standby region (fails requirement 1). The Route 53 failover routing policy is active-passive: it sends 0% of traffic to the standby until the primary becomes unhealthy, so it cannot continuously route exactly 1% of requests to the secondary region (fails requirement 2).","why_zh":"使用一般 regional DynamoDB，不會跨區域複製，session 資料無法在 standby 區域取得（不符需求 1）。Route 53 failover routing policy 是 active-passive，在主區故障前送 0% 流量給 standby，無法持續將恰好 1% 請求導向次要區域（不符需求 2）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"RDS for PostgreSQL cross-region replication creates a read-only replica, so the secondary region cannot persist the session writes from the 1% of traffic it serves. The design ('client-side logic to call API Gateway directly') provides no Route 53 weighted record or health check, so there is no mechanism to route exactly 1% of traffic or to fail over automatically (fails requirements 2 and 3).","why_zh":"RDS for PostgreSQL 跨區域複製建立的是唯讀 replica，次要區域無法寫入其服務的 1% 流量所產生的 session。「由 client 邏輯直接呼叫 API Gateway」並無 Route 53 weighted record 或 health check，無法導向恰好 1% 流量，也無法自動故障轉移（不符需求 2 與 3）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DynamoDB global tables and Auto Scaling are correct, but 'CloudFront weighted distribution across regions' is not a real feature. CloudFront origin groups perform only primary-to-secondary origin failover, not percentage-based weighting, so there is no way to send exactly 1% of requests to the secondary region (fails requirement 2).","why_zh":"DynamoDB global tables 與 Auto Scaling 是正確的，但「CloudFront weighted distribution across regions」並非實際功能。CloudFront origin groups 只能做主要到次要 origin 的 failover，無法按百分比加權，無法將恰好 1% 請求送到次要區域（不符需求 2）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-weighted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/high_availability_origin_failover.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":58,"question_en":"A company runs an application on Amazon EC2 instances. The company uses a series of AWS CloudFormation stacks to define the application resources. A developer performs updates by building and testing the application on a laptop and then uploading the build output and CloudFormation stack templates to Amazon S3. The developer's peers review the changes before the developer performs the CloudFormation stack update and installs a new version of the application onto the EC2 instances. The deployment process is prone to errors and is time-consuming when the developer updates each EC2 instance with the new application. The company wants to automate as much of the application deployment process as possible while retaining a final manual approval step before the modification of the application or resources. The company already has moved the source code for the application and the CloudFormation templates to AWS CodeCommit. The company also has created an AWS CodeBuild project to build and test the application. Which combination of steps will meet the company’s requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行应用程序。该公司使用一系列 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来定义应用 程序资源。开发人员在笔记本电脑上构建和测试应用程序，然后将构建输出和 CloudFormation 堆栈模板 上传到亚马逊 S3。开发人员的同事会先审查这些更改，之后开发人员才会执行 CloudFormation 堆栈更新， 并在 EC2 实例上安装应用程序的新版本。 当开发人员使用新应用程序更新每个 EC2 实例时，部署过程容易出错且耗时。该公司希望尽可能多地实 现应用程序部署过程的自动化，同时在修改应用程序或资源之前保留最终的手动审批步骤。 该公司已将应用程序的源代码和 CloudFormation 模板迁移到 AWS CodeCommit。该公司还创建了一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建和测试该应用程序。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足公司的要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an application group and a deployment group in AWS CodeDeploy. Install the CodeDeploy agent on the EC2 instances.","B":"Create an application revision and a deployment group in AWS CodeDeploy. Create an environment in CodeDeploy. Register the EC2 instances to the CodeDeploy environment.","C":"Use AWS CodePipeline to invoke the CodeBuild job, run the CloudFormation update, and pause for a manual approval step. After approval, start the AWS CodeDeploy deployment.","D":"Use AWS CodePipeline to invoke the CodeBuild job, create CloudFormation change sets for each of the application stacks, and pause for a manual approval step. After approval, run the CloudFormation change sets and start the AWS CodeDeploy deployment.","E":"Use AWS CodePipeline to invoke the CodeBuild job, create CloudFormation change sets for each of the application stacks, and pause for a manual approval step. After approval, start the AWS CodeDeploy deployment."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS CodeDeploy 中创建一个应用组和一个部署组。在 EC2 实例上安装 CodeDeploy 代理。","B":"在 AWS CodeDeploy 中创建应用修订版和部署组。在 CodeDeploy 中创建环境。将 EC2 实例注册到 CodeDeploy 环境。","C":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 调用 CodeBuild 任务，运行 CloudFormation 更新，并暂停以等待人工审批步 骤。审批通过后，启动 AWS CodeDeploy 部署。","D":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 调用 CodeBuild 任务，为每个应用程序堆栈创建 CloudFormation 更改集，并 暂停以等待手动审批步骤。审批通过后，运行 CloudFormation 更改集并启动 AWS CodeDeploy 部署。","E":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 调用 CodeBuild 作业，为每个应用程序堆栈创建 CloudFormation 更改集，并 暂停以等待手动审批步骤。审批通过后，启动 AWS CodeDeploy 部署。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The company needs CodePipeline to orchestrate the CodeBuild build, the CloudFormation stack updates, a final manual approval before any modification, and CodeDeploy to push the application to the EC2 instances. Option D is correct: in the CodePipeline CloudFormation deploy action, CHANGE_SET_REPLACE creates a change set, which 'creates a comparison that can be viewed without altering the original stack', so the pipeline pauses for manual approval with nothing yet changed; only after approval does CHANGE_SET_EXECUTE run, and 'with this action, CloudFormation starts to alter the stack', after which the CodeDeploy deployment begins. This satisfies 'final manual approval before modification of the application or resources' while still actually applying the stack changes. Option A is the correct CodeDeploy setup for EC2: per the docs the CodeDeploy agent 'is required only if you deploy to an EC2/On-Premises compute platform', so a deployment group plus the agent installed on the EC2 instances is exactly what is required. Although A loosely says 'application group' instead of the precise term 'application', it pairs the correct deployment group with the mandatory agent install, whereas the only other CodeDeploy option invents an 'environment' concept that does not exist in CodeDeploy and omits the agent.","explanation_zh":"此情境需要 CodePipeline 來協調 CodeBuild 建置、CloudFormation 堆疊更新、在任何變更前的最終手動核准,以及用 CodeDeploy 將應用程式部署到 EC2 執行個體。選項 D 正確:在 CodePipeline 的 CloudFormation deploy action 中,CHANGE_SET_REPLACE 會建立 change set,文件說明它『建立一個可檢視但不會改動原始堆疊的比較』,因此 pipeline 在尚未變更任何東西的情況下暫停等待手動核准;唯有核准後才執行 CHANGE_SET_EXECUTE,文件說明『使用此 action,CloudFormation 才開始改動堆疊』,接著才啟動 CodeDeploy 部署。這同時滿足『在修改應用程式或資源前進行最終手動核准』,又確實套用了堆疊變更。選項 A 是正確的 EC2 CodeDeploy 設定:文件指出 CodeDeploy agent『僅在部署到 EC2/On-Premises compute platform 時才需要』,所以 deployment group 加上在 EC2 執行個體安裝 agent 正是所需。雖然 A 寬鬆地用了『application group』而非精確的『application』,但它把正確的 deployment group 與必要的 agent 安裝配在一起;而唯一另一個 CodeDeploy 選項則杜撰了 CodeDeploy 並不存在的『environment』概念並漏掉 agent。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeDeploy has no 'environment' concept and you do not 'register EC2 instances to a CodeDeploy environment'. Per the primary-components docs, the components are application, compute platform, deployment configuration, deployment group, deployment type, and revision; instances are matched to a deployment group via EC2 tags or Auto Scaling groups, not a registered environment. It also omits installing the CodeDeploy agent, which the docs say is required for EC2/On-Premises deployments. The invented 'environment / register instances' wording makes this more fundamentally wrong than A's loose 'application group'.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 沒有『environment』概念,也不會『將 EC2 執行個體註冊到 CodeDeploy environment』。依 primary-components 文件,元件是 application、compute platform、deployment configuration、deployment group、deployment type 與 revision;執行個體是透過 EC2 標籤或 Auto Scaling group 對應到 deployment group,而非註冊到 environment。它也漏掉安裝 CodeDeploy agent,而文件指出 EC2/On-Premises 部署必須安裝 agent。這個杜撰的『environment／註冊執行個體』用語比 A 寬鬆的『application group』錯得更根本。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It runs the CloudFormation update FIRST and only then pauses for approval, which modifies the stack resources before the manual approval. This directly violates the requirement to retain a final manual approval step before any modification of the application or resources.","why_zh":"它先執行 CloudFormation 更新,之後才暫停等待核准,這會在手動核准之前就修改堆疊資源,直接違反『在任何應用程式或資源修改前保留最終手動核准步驟』的要求。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"It creates the change sets and approves, but after approval it only starts the CodeDeploy deployment and never executes the CloudFormation change sets (CHANGE_SET_EXECUTE). Because CHANGE_SET_REPLACE only previews changes without altering the stack, the stack resource changes would never be applied, leaving the infrastructure updates incomplete.","why_zh":"它建立了 change set 並核准,但核准後只啟動 CodeDeploy 部署,卻從未執行 CloudFormation change set (CHANGE_SET_EXECUTE)。由於 CHANGE_SET_REPLACE 只會預覽變更而不會改動堆疊,堆疊資源變更將永遠不會被套用,導致基礎設施更新不完整。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CloudFormation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/primary-components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/codedeploy-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-updating-stacks-changesets-execute.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":59,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer manages a web application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The instances run in an EC2 Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. The engineer needs to implement a deployment strategy that: Launches a second fleet of instances with the same capacity as the original fleet. Maintains the original fleet unchanged while the second fleet is launched. Transitions traffic to the second fleet when the second fleet is fully deployed. Terminates the original fleet automatically 1 hour after transition. Which solution will satisfy these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师负责管理一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的网络应用程序，这些实例位于应用负载均 衡器（ALB）之后。这些实例在多个可用区的 EC2 自动扩展组中运行。该工程师需要实施一种部署策略， 该策略： 启动与原实例舰队容量相同的第二支实例舰队。 在维持原有舰队不变的情况下，第二支舰队也已启航。 当第二舰队完全部署完毕时，将交通转至第二舰队。 在转换后 1 小时自动终止原舰队。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an AWS CloudFormation template with a retention policy for the ALB set to 1 hour. Update the Amazon Route 53 record to reflect the new ALB.","B":"Use two AWS Elastic Beanstalk environments to perform a blue/green deployment from the original environment to the new one. Create an application version lifecycle policy to terminate the original environment in 1 hour.","C":"Use AWS CodeDeploy with a deployment group configured with a blue/green deployment configuration Select the option Terminate the original instances in the deployment group with a waiting period of 1 hour.","D":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk with the configuration set to Immutable. Create an .ebextension using the Resources key that sets the deletion policy of the ALB to 1 hour, and deploy the application."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用带有保留策略的 AWS CloudFormation 模板，将 ALB 的保留时间设置为 1 小时。更新 Amazon Route 53 记录以反映新的 ALB。","B":"使用两个 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 环境执行从原始环境到新环境的蓝/绿部署。创建一个应用版本生命 周期策略，在 1 小时后终止原始环境。","C":"使用 AWS CodeDeploy 并配置具有蓝/绿部署配置的部署组 选择“在部署组中终止原始实例并设置 1 小 时等待期”这一选项。","D":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 并将配置设置为不可变。使用 Resources 键创建一个 .ebextension，将 ALB 的删除策略设置为 1 小时，然后部署应用程序。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is a textbook EC2/On-Premises blue/green deployment with AWS CodeDeploy, and every requirement maps to a native CodeDeploy option. Selecting 'Automatically copy Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group' (GreenFleetProvisioningOption Action=COPY_AUTO_SCALING_GROUP) makes CodeDeploy create a replacement (green) Auto Scaling group from the original as a template; the docs state 'the number of currently healthy instances in the Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group you select is created in your replacement environment' — same capacity as the original fleet, which keeps running unchanged. With 'Reroute traffic immediately', once the replacement instances are provisioned and the revision is installed, they are registered with the ALB target groups and traffic is rerouted; the original instances are then deregistered. The 'Original instances' setting 'Terminate the original instances in the deployment group' (BlueInstanceTerminationOption Action=TERMINATE) terminates the deregistered original instances 'following the wait period you specify' via TerminationWaitTimeInMinutes (max 2880 minutes), so 60 minutes = exactly 1 hour after transition. All four requirements are satisfied natively, so C is correct.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS CodeDeploy 經典的 EC2/On-Premises 藍綠部署情境，四項需求都對應到 CodeDeploy 的原生選項。選擇「Automatically copy Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group」（即 GreenFleetProvisioningOption 的 Action=COPY_AUTO_SCALING_GROUP），CodeDeploy 會以原始 ASG 為範本建立替換（綠色）Auto Scaling group；官方文件明確指出「會在替換環境中建立與所選 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group 中目前健康執行個體相同數量的執行個體」——即與原始車隊相同的容量，而原始車隊維持不變持續運行。搭配「Reroute traffic immediately」，當替換執行個體佈建完成且安裝好修訂版後，會註冊到 ALB target group 並把流量切換過去，接著原始執行個體被取消註冊。在「Original instances」設定中選擇「Terminate the original instances in the deployment group」（即 BlueInstanceTerminationOption 的 Action=TERMINATE），會在你以 TerminationWaitTimeInMinutes 指定的等待期間（上限 2880 分鐘）之後終止已取消註冊的原始執行個體，因此設為 60 分鐘即為切換後恰好 1 小時。四項需求都能原生滿足，故 C 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation DeletionPolicy values are Retain, Delete, Snapshot, and RetainExceptOnCreate — there is no time-based '1 hour retention policy' for an ALB. CloudFormation cannot natively launch a parallel same-capacity fleet, hold both, reroute ALB traffic, then auto-terminate the old fleet after exactly 1 hour. This is invented behavior.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 的 DeletionPolicy 只有 Retain、Delete、Snapshot、RetainExceptOnCreate，並沒有針對 ALB 的「1 小時時間性保留政策」。CloudFormation 無法原生地啟動同容量的平行車隊、同時保留兩者、切換 ALB 流量後再於恰好 1 小時後自動終止舊車隊，此為杜撰的行為。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Beanstalk blue/green via CNAME swap does meet the swap behavior, but an 'application version lifecycle policy' only controls retention of application versions (source bundles in S3 and their version records), not the termination of an environment. There is no Beanstalk feature that automatically terminates the original environment 1 hour after the swap, so this option misuses the lifecycle policy and fails the auto-termination requirement.","why_zh":"Beanstalk 透過 CNAME 交換的藍綠部署確實符合切換行為，但「application version lifecycle policy」只管理應用程式版本（S3 中的原始程式套件與其版本紀錄）的保留，而非終止環境。Beanstalk 並沒有可在交換後 1 小時自動終止原始環境的功能，因此此選項誤用了生命週期政策，無法滿足自動終止的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Beanstalk Immutable updates do NOT keep the original fleet running for a blue/green traffic swap — they launch a temporary second ASG, and once the new instances pass health checks they are moved into the original ASG and the temporary group is removed; there is no 1-hour delayed teardown of an old fleet. Also, an .ebextension Resources block cannot set a time-based 'deletion policy of the ALB to 1 hour'; CloudFormation DeletionPolicy is not time-based and has no '1 hour' value.","why_zh":"Beanstalk Immutable 更新並不會為了藍綠流量切換而保留原始車隊運行——它會啟動一個暫時的第二 ASG，待新執行個體通過健康檢查後將其移入原始 ASG 並移除暫時群組；並沒有對舊車隊的 1 小時延遲拆除。此外，.ebextension 的 Resources 區塊無法將「ALB 的 deletion policy 設為 1 小時」；CloudFormation 的 DeletionPolicy 並非時間性設定，也沒有「1 小時」這種值。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-create-blue-green.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-codedeploy-deploymentgroup-blueinstanceterminationoption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-codedeploy-deploymentgroup-greenfleetprovisioningoption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/environmentmgmt-updates-immutable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.CNAMESwap.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":60,"question_en":"A video-sharing company stores its videos in Amazon S3. The company has observed a sudden increase in video access requests, but the company does not know which videos are most popular. The company needs to identify the general access pattern for the video files. This pattern includes the number of users who access a certain file on a given day, as well as the number of pull requests for certain files. How can the company meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of effort?","question_zh":"一家视频分享公司将其视频存储在亚马逊 S3 上。该公司注意到视频访问请求突然增多，但并不清楚哪些视 频最受欢迎。该公司需要确定视频文件的一般访问模式。这种模式包括在给定的一天内访问特定文件的用 户数量以及对某些文件的拉取请求数量。 公司怎样才能以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Activate S3 server access logging. Import the access logs into an Amazon Aurora database. Use an Aurora SQL query to analyze the access patterns.","B":"Activate S3 server access logging. Use Amazon Athena to create an external table with the log files. Use Athena to create a SQL query to analyze the access patterns.","C":"Invoke an AWS Lambda function for every S3 object access event. Configure the Lambda function to write the file access information, such as user. S3 bucket, and file key, to an Amazon Aurora database. Use an Aurora SQL query to analyze the access patterns.","D":"Record an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log message for every S3 object access event. Configure a CloudWatch Logs log stream to write the file access information, such as user, S3 bucket, and file key, to an Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL application. Perform a sliding window analysis."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 S3 服务器访问日志记录。将访问日志导入到 Amazon Aurora 数据库中。使用 Aurora SQL 查询来 分析访问模式。","B":"启用 S3 服务器访问日志记录。使用 Amazon Athena 创建一个包含日志文件的外部表。使用 Athena 创 建一个 SQL 查询来分析访问模式。","C":"对于每个 S3 对象访问事件，调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数，将文件访问信息（例如 用户、S3 存储桶和文件键）写入 Amazon Aurora 数据库。使用 Aurora SQL 查询来分析访问模式。","D":"对每个 S3 对象访问事件记录一条 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志消息。配置一个 CloudWatch Logs 日志 流，将文件访问信息（例如用户、S3 存储桶和文件键）写入 Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL 应 用程序。执行滑动窗口分析。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon S3 stores server access logs as objects in an S3 bucket, and each log record captures exactly the fields needed here: requester, bucket_name, key (file/object key), operation (e.g., REST.GET.OBJECT for a pull/download), and requestdatetime. AWS's own guide 'Using Amazon S3 server access logs to identify requests' explicitly recommends using Amazon Athena to CREATE EXTERNAL TABLE over the delivered log files and run SQL queries, and includes an 'Identifying object access requests' example that returns all REST.GET.OBJECT requests filtered by key, requester, and date range. This is fully serverless and requires no data movement, no provisioned database, and no custom code: enable logging, create one external table, and query in place. It directly answers which videos are most popular, how many users access a file on a given day, and how many GET (pull) requests target a file, and does so with the LEAST effort, which is what distinguishes B from A (load into Aurora), C (custom Lambda plus Aurora), and D (CloudWatch Logs plus Kinesis Data Analytics streaming).","explanation_zh":"Amazon S3 會將 server access logs 以物件形式存放在 S3 bucket 中，而每筆紀錄正好包含本題所需的欄位：requester、bucket_name、key（檔案/物件鍵）、operation（例如代表下載/pull 的 REST.GET.OBJECT）以及 requestdatetime。AWS 官方文件「Using Amazon S3 server access logs to identify requests」明確建議使用 Amazon Athena 對投遞的 log 檔建立 EXTERNAL TABLE 並執行 SQL 查詢，且文件中「Identifying object access requests」範例直接示範如何依 key、requester 與日期範圍查出所有 REST.GET.OBJECT 請求。此方法完全 serverless，不需搬移資料、不需佈建資料庫、也不需自訂程式碼：只要啟用 logging、建立一張 external table，即可就地查詢。它能直接回答哪些影片最熱門、某天有多少使用者存取某檔案、以及某檔案有多少 GET（pull）請求，並以最少工作量達成；這正是 B 勝過 A（匯入 Aurora）、C（自訂 Lambda 加 Aurora）與 D（CloudWatch Logs 加 Kinesis Data Analytics 串流）之處。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Server access logging is the correct log source, but importing the logs into an Amazon Aurora database adds significant operational overhead: provisioning and managing a relational database and building an ingestion/ETL process to load the log files. Athena queries the log objects in place with no database to manage, so A is materially more effort than B and fails the LEAST-effort qualifier.","why_zh":"Server access logging 是正確的 log 來源，但把 log 匯入 Amazon Aurora 資料庫會增加大量營運負擔：需佈建並維運關聯式資料庫，還要建立載入 log 檔的擷取/ETL 流程。Athena 可就地查詢 log 物件且無需管理資料庫，因此 A 明顯比 B 費力，不符合「最少工作量」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Invoking a Lambda function for every object access and writing each record to Aurora requires custom code, an event pipeline, and a managed database. S3 event notifications fire mainly on object create/delete, not on read/GET access, so this cannot reliably capture 'pull requests.' It is the highest-effort option and technically weak for read tracking.","why_zh":"對每次物件存取觸發 Lambda 並把每筆紀錄寫入 Aurora，需要自訂程式碼、事件管線與受管資料庫。S3 事件通知主要在物件建立/刪除時觸發，而非讀取/GET 存取，因此無法可靠擷取『pull requests』。這是工作量最高的選項，且對讀取追蹤在技術上也不足。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Recording a CloudWatch Logs message per object access and streaming it into Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL with sliding-window analysis builds a complex real-time pipeline. S3 does not natively emit a log message per read event to CloudWatch Logs, so this needs custom instrumentation, and sliding-window stream processing is overkill for retrospective access-pattern analysis. This is the opposite of least effort.","why_zh":"為每次物件存取記錄 CloudWatch Logs 訊息並串流到 Kinesis Data Analytics for SQL 進行 sliding-window 分析，等於建立一條複雜的即時管線。S3 不會原生地針對每個讀取事件向 CloudWatch Logs 發送 log 訊息，因此需要自訂檢測，而 sliding-window 串流處理對回溯性的存取模式分析屬於過度設計，與最少工作量完全相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/using-s3-access-logs-to-identify-requests.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/ServerLogs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/enable-server-access-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/what-is.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":61,"question_en":"A development team wants to use AWS CloudFormation stacks to deploy an application. However, the developer IAM role does not have the required permissions to provision the resources that are specified in the AWS CloudFormation template. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution that allows the developers to deploy the stacks. The solution must follow the principle of least privilege. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个开发团队希望使用 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来部署应用程序。然而，开发人员的 IAM 角色没有在 AWS CloudFormation 模板中指定的资源所需的权限。一位 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，使开发 人员能够部署这些堆栈。该解决方案必须遵循最小权限原则。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM policy that allows the developers to provision the required resources. Attach the policy to the developer IAM role.","B":"Create an IAM policy that allows full access to AWS CloudFormation. Attach the policy to the developer IAM role.","C":"Create an AWS CloudFormation service role that has the required permissions. Grant the developer IAM role a cloudformation:* action. Use the new service role during stack deployments.","D":"Create an AWS CloudFormation service role that has the required permissions. Grant the developer IAM role the iam:PassRole permission. Use the new service role during stack deployments."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 IAM 策略，允许开发人员配置所需的资源。将该策略附加到开发人员的 IAM 角色上。","B":"创建一个允许对 AWS CloudFormation 进行完全访问的 IAM 策略。将该策略附加到开发人员的 IAM 角色。","C":"创建一个具有所需权限的 AWS CloudFormation 服务角色。授予开发人员 IAM 角色 cloudformation:* 操 作权限。在堆栈部署期间使用新的服务角色。","D":"创建一个具有所需权限的 AWS CloudFormation 服务角色。授予开发人员 IAM 角色 iam:PassRole 权限。 在堆栈部署期间使用新的服务角色。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A CloudFormation service role is an IAM role that CloudFormation assumes to create, update, and delete stack resources on the principal's behalf. When a service role is specified, CloudFormation uses that role's credentials for the resource operations, so the developer's own IAM role does not need permissions to provision the resources defined in the template. AWS Prescriptive Guidance states that 'when using a service role, the identity-based policy attached to the IAM principal doesn't require permissions to provision all of the AWS resources defined in the CloudFormation template,' and that 'to use a service role to create CloudFormation stacks, IAM principals must have permissions to pass the service role to CloudFormation' (iam:PassRole, ideally scoped to the role ARN). AWS recommends working backward from the template to build a service role that adheres to least privilege. Option D captures exactly this pattern: a scoped service role plus iam:PassRole on the developer role. Option A grants the developers the provisioning permissions directly (broad standing access outside CloudFormation), and options B and C grant overly broad CloudFormation access, all of which violate least privilege.","explanation_zh":"CloudFormation service role 是一個 IAM role，CloudFormation 會代表 principal 來 assume 它以建立、更新、刪除 stack 資源。當指定 service role 時，CloudFormation 會改用該 role 的憑證執行資源操作，因此 developer 自己的 IAM role 不需要具備 template 中所定義資源的佈建權限。AWS Prescriptive Guidance 明確指出：使用 service role 時，附加在 IAM principal 上的 identity-based policy 不需要具備佈建 template 中所有 AWS 資源的權限；而且「要使用 service role 來建立 CloudFormation stack，IAM principal 必須具備將該 service role 傳遞給 CloudFormation 的權限」，也就是 iam:PassRole（最好限定到該 role 的 ARN）。AWS 建議從 template 反推來建立符合最小權限原則的 service role。選項 D 正好符合此模式：一個範圍受限的 service role，加上 developer role 的 iam:PassRole 權限。選項 A 直接把佈建權限授予 developer（讓他們在 CloudFormation 之外也擁有廣泛的常駐權限）；選項 B 與 C 則授予過於寬鬆的 CloudFormation 存取，全都違反最小權限原則。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Attaching a policy that grants the developer IAM role the resource-provisioning permissions directly gives developers broad standing access to create those resources outside of CloudFormation. It does not use the AWS-prescribed service-role delegation pattern, so it does not minimize the developer's standing privileges the way a scoped service role plus iam:PassRole does.","why_zh":"直接把佈建資源的權限授予 developer IAM role，會讓 developer 在 CloudFormation 之外也擁有廣泛的常駐權限來建立這些資源。這並未採用 AWS 建議的 service-role 委派模式，無法像「範圍受限的 service role 加上 iam:PassRole」那樣將 developer 的常駐權限降到最低。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Full access to CloudFormation is overly broad and clearly violates least privilege. By default CloudFormation uses the calling principal's own credentials for stack operations, so the developer would still lack the underlying resource-provisioning permissions and the deployment would still fail. It does not solve the missing-permissions problem.","why_zh":"授予 CloudFormation 完整存取過於寬鬆，明顯違反最小權限原則。預設情況下 CloudFormation 會使用呼叫者本身的憑證執行 stack 操作，因此 developer 仍缺少底層資源的佈建權限，佈建仍會失敗，並未解決缺少權限的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating a scoped service role is correct, but granting the developer role the cloudformation:* action is overly broad (full CloudFormation access) and is not what is technically required to use the service role. To pass a service role to CloudFormation the principal needs iam:PassRole (ideally scoped to the role ARN); a wildcard cloudformation:* grant does not authorize passing the role and does not satisfy least privilege.","why_zh":"建立範圍受限的 service role 是正確的，但授予 developer role cloudformation:* 動作過於寬鬆（等於完整 CloudFormation 存取），且這並非使用 service role 在技術上真正需要的權限。要將 service role 傳遞給 CloudFormation，principal 需要 iam:PassRole（最好限定到 role 的 ARN）；萬用字元的 cloudformation:* 既無法授權傳遞該 role，也不符合最小權限原則。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-iam-servicerole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/least-privilege-cloudformation/service-roles-for-cloudformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_passrole.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":62,"question_en":"A production account has a requirement that any Amazon EC2 instance that has been logged in to manually must be terminated within 24 hours. All applications in the production account are using Auto Scaling groups with the Amazon CloudWatch Logs agent configured. How can this process be automated?","question_zh":"生产账户有一项要求，即任何手动登录过的 Amazon EC2 实例必须在 24 小时内终止。生产账户中的所 有应用程序都在使用配置了 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 代理的自动扩展组。 这个过程如何实现自动化？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudWatch Logs subscription to an AWS Step Functions application. Configure an AWS Lambda function to add a tag to the EC2 instance that produced the login event and mark the instance to be decommissioned. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke a second Lambda function once a day that will terminate all instances with this tag.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that will be invoked by the login event. Send the notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that the operations team is subscribed to, and have them terminate the EC2 instance within 24 hours.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that will be invoked by the login event. Configure the alarm to send to an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Use a group of worker instances to process messages from the queue, which then schedules an Amazon EventBridge rule to be invoked.","D":"Create a CloudWatch Logs subscription to an AWS Lambda function. Configure the function to add a tag to the EC2 instance that produced the login event and mark the instance to be decommissioned. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke a daily Lambda function that terminates all instances with this tag."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 订阅到 AWS Step Functions 应用程序。配置一个 AWS Lambda 函数，为 产生登录事件的 EC2 实例添加一个标签，并将该实例标记为即将退役。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每天调用一个 Lambda 函数，终止所有带有此标签的实例。","B":"创建一个由登录事件触发的 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。将通知发送到运营团队订阅的 Amazon 简单 通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，并要求他们在 24 小时内终止该 EC2 实例。","C":"创建一个由登录事件触发的 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。将警报配置为发送到 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列。使用一组工作实例来处理队列中的消息，然后安排 Amazon EventBridge 规则被调用。","D":"创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 订阅到 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该函数，为产生登录事件的 EC2 实例 添加一个标签，并将该实例标记为待退役。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每天调用一个 Lambda 函数来终止所有带有此标签的实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to automatically tag and terminate any EC2 instance that has a manual login event (captured by the CloudWatch Logs agent) within 24 hours. A CloudWatch Logs subscription filter delivers a real-time feed of matching log events to a destination, and AWS Lambda is one of the four documented, supported destinations (Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Data Firehose, OpenSearch Service). Option D wires a CloudWatch Logs subscription to a Lambda that tags the offending instance for decommissioning, then uses an EventBridge scheduled (daily) rule to invoke a second Lambda that terminates all tagged instances - fully automated and using only documented destinations. Option A is technically invalid because AWS Step Functions is NOT a supported CloudWatch Logs subscription-filter destination. Options B and C both rely on CloudWatch alarms (which fire on metric thresholds, not directly on a login log event) and either require manual operator action (B) or an over-engineered SQS + worker-fleet design (C), so neither is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是要在 24 小時內自動標記並終止任何發生手動登入事件 (由 CloudWatch Logs agent 擷取) 的 EC2 instance。CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 會把符合條件的 log 事件即時 (real-time) 傳遞到目的地,而 AWS Lambda 正是官方文件支援的四種目的地之一 (Kinesis Data Streams、Lambda、Data Firehose、OpenSearch Service)。選項 D 將 CloudWatch Logs subscription 連到一個 Lambda,由它替違規的 instance 加上待除役的 tag,再用 EventBridge 排程 (每日) 規則觸發第二個 Lambda 去終止所有帶該 tag 的 instance,完全自動化且只使用官方支援的目的地。選項 A 在技術上不成立,因為 AWS Step Functions 並非 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 支援的目的地。選項 B 與 C 都依賴 CloudWatch alarm (alarm 由 metric 門檻觸發,而非直接被登入 log 事件觸發),且分別仰賴人工操作 (B) 或過度設計的 SQS 加 worker 機群方案 (C),因此都不正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudWatch Logs subscription cannot target AWS Step Functions. The CloudWatch Logs SubscriptionFilters documentation lists only Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, and Amazon OpenSearch Service as valid destinations. The design is technically unsupported as written, and Step Functions adds needless complexity over the direct Lambda approach in D.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs subscription 無法以 AWS Step Functions 作為目的地。CloudWatch Logs SubscriptionFilters 官方文件僅列出 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 與 Amazon OpenSearch Service 為有效目的地。此設計如其所述在技術上不受支援,且相較於 D 直接用 Lambda,Step Functions 還多了不必要的複雜度。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch alarms are triggered by metric thresholds, not directly 'invoked by a login event' - a metric filter would be required first. More importantly, it relies on the operations team manually terminating instances, which is not automation and is error-prone for the 24-hour requirement.","why_zh":"CloudWatch alarm 是由 metric 門檻觸發,而非直接被『登入事件觸發』,需先有 metric filter。更關鍵的是它仰賴維運團隊手動終止 instance,這並非自動化,對 24 小時的要求而言容易出錯。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Alarms are not 'invoked by a login event' directly, and routing through SQS plus a fleet of worker instances that then schedule EventBridge rules is convoluted and high-overhead. The worker instances themselves would be running and could be logged into, and dynamically scheduling EventBridge rules per event is unnecessary.","why_zh":"Alarm 並非直接『被登入事件觸發』,而透過 SQS 再加一群 worker instance 去排程 EventBridge 規則既迂迴又高負擔。這些 worker instance 本身在運行也可能被登入,且為每個事件動態排程 EventBridge 規則並無必要。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/Subscriptions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-create-rule-schedule.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":63,"question_en":"A company has enabled all features for its organization in AWS Organizations. The organization contains 10 AWS accounts. The company has turned on AWS CloudTrail in all the accounts. The company expects the number of AWS accounts in the organization to increase to 500 during the next year. The company plans to use multiple OUs for these accounts. The company has enabled AWS Config in each existing AWS account in the organization. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution that enables AWS Config automatically for all future AWS accounts that are created in the organization. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中为其组织启用了所有功能。该组织包含 10 个 AWS 账户。该公司已在 所有账户中启用了 AWS CloudTrail。该公司预计在接下来的一年里，组织中的 AWS 账户数量将增加到 500 个。该公司计划为这些账户使用多个组织单元（OU）。 该公司已在组织内的每个现有 AWS 账户中启用了 AWS Config。一位 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个解 决方案，以便在组织中创建的所有未来 AWS 账户中自动启用 AWS Config。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the organization's management account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to a CreateAccount API call. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that enables trusted access to AWS Config for the organization.","B":"In the organization's management account, create an AWS CloudFormation stack set to enable AWS Config. Configure the stack set to deploy automatically when an account is created through Organizations.","C":"In the organization's management account, create an SCP that allows the appropriate AWS Config API calls to enable AWS Config. Apply the SCP to the root-level OU.","D":"In the organization's management account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to a CreateAccount API call. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to enable AWS Config for the account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 CreateAccount API 调用做出 响应。配置该规则以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，为组织启用对 AWS Config 的可信访问。","B":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 栈集以启用 AWS Config。将栈集配置为在通 过 Organizations 创建账户时自动部署。","C":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），允许进行适当的 AWS Config API 调用以启 用 AWS Config。将该 SCP 应用于根级别的组织单位（OU）。","D":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 CreateAccount API 调用做出反应。 配置该规则以调用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，为该账户启用 AWS Config。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The native, documented way to automatically enable AWS Config for all future accounts in an organization is a service-managed CloudFormation StackSet with automatic deployment turned on. AWS docs state that 'CloudFormation can automatically deploy additional stacks to new AWS Organizations accounts when they're added to your target organization or organizational units (OUs)' and that auto-deployment is 'triggered when accounts are added to a target organization or OU.' The StackSet template creates the AWS::Config::ConfigurationRecorder and AWS::Config::DeliveryChannel resources, so each new account starts recording with no manual action. Because the company plans multiple OUs and growth to 500 accounts, targeting the org root/OUs with auto-deployment scales cleanly and with minimal operational overhead. Option B is correct.","explanation_zh":"在 AWS Organizations 中為所有未來帳戶自動啟用 AWS Config 的原生且有文件支援的做法,是使用採用 service-managed 權限並開啟自動部署 (automatic deployment) 的 CloudFormation StackSet。AWS 文件明確指出「當帳戶被加入目標 organization 或 OU 時,CloudFormation 會自動將堆疊部署到新的 AWS Organizations 帳戶」,且自動部署「在帳戶被加入目標 organization 或 OU 時觸發」。StackSet 範本建立 AWS::Config::ConfigurationRecorder 與 AWS::Config::DeliveryChannel 等資源,使每個新帳戶無需人工操作即開始記錄。由於公司規劃多個 OU 並將擴增至 500 個帳戶,以 root/OU 為目標並開啟自動部署能乾淨地擴展且運維負擔最低。因此選 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Enabling 'trusted access to AWS Config for the organization' only unlocks org-level capabilities (aggregators, organization Config rules/conformance packs). It does NOT create the configuration recorder/delivery channel inside each member account, so AWS Config recording would not actually be enabled in new accounts.","why_zh":"啟用「AWS Config 的組織信任存取」僅解鎖組織層級功能 (aggregator、organization Config rules/conformance packs),並不會在每個成員帳戶內建立 configuration recorder/delivery channel,因此新帳戶實際上不會啟用 Config 記錄。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Per AWS docs, 'SCPs do not grant permissions... No permissions are granted by an SCP. An SCP defines a permission guardrail.' An SCP only allows or denies API actions; it never proactively invokes APIs or turns on a service. Allowing Config API calls does not cause Config to be enabled in any account.","why_zh":"根據 AWS 文件,「SCP 不會授予權限……SCP 本身不授予任何權限,只是定義權限護欄」。SCP 只能允許或拒絕 API 動作,本身不會主動呼叫 API 或啟用服務。允許 Config API 呼叫並不會讓任何帳戶實際啟用 Config。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EventBridge rule on CreateAccount invoking an SSM Automation runbook is a custom, higher-operational-overhead build versus the purpose-built StackSet auto-deployment feature, and it relies on cross-account role assumption plus the asynchronous CreateAccount/CreateAccountResult flow. It is not the AWS-recommended native solution that B provides.","why_zh":"以 EventBridge 監聽 CreateAccount 並呼叫 SSM Automation runbook 屬於自訂、運維負擔較高的方案,且需仰賴跨帳戶角色擔任與非同步的 CreateAccount/CreateAccountResult 流程;相較於 B 所提供的專用 StackSet 自動部署功能,這並非 AWS 推薦的原生作法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-manage-auto-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-cloudformation-stackset-autodeployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-config-configurationrecorder.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-config-deliverychannel.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":64,"question_en":"A company has many applications. Different teams in the company developed the applications by using multiple languages and frameworks. The applications run on premises and on different servers with different operating systems. Each team has its own release protocol and process. The company wants to reduce the complexity of the release and maintenance of these applications. The company is migrating its technology stacks, including these applications, to AWS. The company wants centralized control of source code, a consistent and automatic delivery pipeline, and as few maintenance tasks as possible on the underlying infrastructure. What should a DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有众多应用程序。公司内不同团队使用多种语言和框架开发了这些应用程序。这些应用程 序在本地和不同操作系统下的不同服务器上运行。每个团队都有自己的发布协议和流程。该公司希望 降低这些应用程序发布和维护的复杂性。 该公司正在将其技术栈（包括这些应用程序）迁移到 AWS。该公司希望实现源代码的集中管理、一致且 自动化的交付流程，并尽可能减少底层基础设施的维护任务。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create one AWS CodeCommit repository for all applications. Put each application's code in a different branch. Merge the branches, and use AWS CodeBuild to build the applications. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the applications to one centralized application server.","B":"Create one AWS CodeCommit repository for each of the applications. Use AWS CodeBuild to build the applications one at a time. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the applications to one centralized application server.","C":"Create one AWS CodeCommit repository for each of the applications. Use AWS CodeBuild to build the applications one at a time and to create one AMI for each server. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to automatically provision and decommission Amazon EC2 fleets by using these AMIs.","D":"Create one AWS CodeCommit repository for each of the applications. Use AWS CodeBuild to build one Docker image for each application in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the applications to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) on infrastructure that AWS Fargate manages."},"options_zh":{"A":"为所有应用程序创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。将每个应用程序的代码放在不同的分支中。合并这 些分支，并使用 AWS CodeBuild 构建应用程序。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将应用程序部署到一个集中的 应用服务器上。","B":"为每个应用程序创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。使用 AWS CodeBuild 依次构建这些应用程序。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将应用程序部署到一个集中的应用服务器上。","C":"为每个应用程序创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库。使用 AWS CodeBuild 依次构建应用程序，并为每台 服务器创建一个 AMI。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 通过这些 AMI 自动配置和停用 Amazon EC2 集群。","D":"为每个应用程序创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。使用 AWS CodeBuild 在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 中为每个应用程序构建一个 Docker 镜像。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将应用程序 部署到由 AWS Fargate 管理的 Amazon Elastic Container Service （Amazon ECS） 上。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is 'as few maintenance tasks as possible on the underlying infrastructure,' combined with the need to deliver many applications written in different languages/frameworks on different operating systems through a single, consistent, automated pipeline with centralized source control. Packaging each application as a Docker image normalizes the heterogeneity of languages, frameworks, and OSs into a uniform deployable artifact. Building one image per app with CodeBuild and storing it in Amazon ECR, then deploying to Amazon ECS on AWS Fargate, removes the need to provision, configure, patch, or scale servers/EC2 clusters: per the Fargate docs it lets you 'run containers without having to manage servers or clusters of Amazon EC2 instances' and 'you no longer have to provision, configure, or scale clusters of virtual machines.' One CodeCommit repository per application provides centralized source control, and CodeBuild plus CodeDeploy (which supports deploying applications into Amazon ECS) provide a repeatable automatic pipeline. This is the only option that simultaneously delivers centralization, automation, multi-language support, and minimal infrastructure maintenance.","explanation_zh":"決定性條件是『盡可能減少底層基礎設施的維護工作』，同時需要透過單一、一致、自動化的管線並搭配集中式原始碼控管，交付以不同語言/框架、執行於不同作業系統上的眾多應用程式。將每個應用程式封裝為 Docker image，可把語言、框架與作業系統的異質性統一為一致的可部署成品。使用 CodeBuild 為每個應用建置一個 image 並存放於 Amazon ECR，再部署到 Amazon ECS on AWS Fargate，即可免除佈建、設定、修補或擴展伺服器/EC2 叢集的需求；依 Fargate 文件，它可讓你『run containers without having to manage servers or clusters of Amazon EC2 instances』，且『you no longer have to provision, configure, or scale clusters of virtual machines』。每個應用一個 CodeCommit repository 提供集中式原始碼控管，CodeBuild 加上 CodeDeploy（支援將應用部署到 Amazon ECS）則提供可重複的自動化管線。這是唯一同時達成集中化、自動化、多語言支援與最少基礎設施維護的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Putting all apps in branches of one repo and merging them is an anti-pattern that mixes unrelated codebases and creates merge conflicts; deploying many different language/framework apps to 'one centralized application server' (EC2) keeps OS/runtime patching and server maintenance, contradicting the 'as few maintenance tasks as possible on the underlying infrastructure' requirement, and is neither consistent nor automatic.","why_zh":"把所有應用放在同一 repo 的不同分支再合併是反模式，會混雜不相關的程式碼並造成合併衝突；將多種語言/框架的應用部署到『單一集中式應用伺服器』(EC2) 仍需修補作業系統/執行環境並維護伺服器，違反『盡可能減少底層基礎設施維護』的要求，且既不一致也非自動化。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Although one repo per app is correct, deploying multiple heterogeneous-language applications to a single centralized EC2 application server still requires managing, patching, and scaling that server (high infrastructure maintenance) and risks runtime/dependency conflicts between different frameworks on one host.","why_zh":"雖然每個應用一個 repo 是正確的，但將多種不同語言的應用部署到單一集中式 EC2 應用伺服器，仍需管理、修補與擴展該伺服器（基礎設施維護負擔高），且不同框架共處於同一主機可能造成執行環境/相依性衝突。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Baking one AMI per server and using CloudFormation StackSets to provision EC2 fleets means you still own and must patch/maintain the EC2 operating systems and AMIs, which is significant ongoing infrastructure maintenance; StackSets is primarily for deploying stacks across multiple accounts/Regions, not an application delivery pipeline, so it does not minimize maintenance.","why_zh":"為每台伺服器建立 AMI 並用 CloudFormation StackSets 佈建 EC2 機群，代表你仍擁有並必須修補/維護 EC2 作業系統與 AMI，這是相當可觀的持續性基礎設施維護；StackSets 主要用於跨多個帳戶/區域部署堆疊，並非應用交付管線，因此無法將維護降到最低。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/AWS_Fargate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/tutorial-ecs-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/ecs-cd-pipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/deployment-type-blue-green.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":65,"question_en":"A company's application is currently deployed to a single AWS Region. Recently, the company opened a new office on a different continent. The users in the new office are experiencing high latency. The company's application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and uses Amazon DynamoDB as the database layer. The instances run in an EC2 Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. A DevOps engineer is tasked with minimizing application response times and improving availability for users in both Regions. Which combination of actions should be taken to address the latency issues? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"该公司当前的应用程序部署在单个 AWS 区域。最近，该公司在另一个大洲开设了新的办事处。新办事处 的用户正遭遇高延迟问题。该公司的应用程序运行在多个可用区的 EC2 自动扩展组中的实例上，并通过应 用负载均衡器（ALB）提供服务，使用 Amazon DynamoDB 作为数据库层。一位 DevOps 工程师的任务是 减少应用程序的响应时间，并提高两个区域用户的可用性。 应采取哪些行动组合来解决延迟问题？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new DynamoDB table in the new Region with cross-Region replication enabled.","B":"Create new ALB and Auto Scaling group global resources and configure the new ALB to direct traffic to the new Auto Scaling group.","C":"Create new ALB and Auto Scaling group resources in the new Region and configure the new ALB to direct traffic to the new Auto Scaling group.","D":"Create Amazon Route 53 records, health checks, and latency-based routing policies to route to the ALB.","E":"Create Amazon Route 53 aliases, health checks, and failover routing policies to route to the ALB.","F":"Convert the DynamoDB table to a global table."},"options_zh":{"A":"在新区域创建一个启用了跨区域复制功能的新 DynamoDB 表。","B":"创建新的应用负载均衡器（ALB）和自动扩展组全局资源，并配置新的 ALB 将流量定向到新的自动扩展 组。","C":"在新区域创建新的应用负载均衡器（ALB）和自动扩展组资源，并配置新的 ALB 将流量导向新的自动 扩展组。","D":"创建 Amazon Route 53 记录、健康检查以及基于延迟的路由策略，以将流量路由到应用负载均衡器 （ALB）。","E":"创建 Amazon Route 53 别名、健康检查和故障转移路由策略以将流量路由到应用负载均衡器（ALB）。","F":"将 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表。"},"answer":["C","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The objective is an active-active multi-Region deployment that both minimizes response time AND improves availability for users on both continents, which requires addressing all three tiers. C (compute): ALBs and EC2 Auto Scaling groups are Regional resources, so you must create a new ALB and Auto Scaling group in the new Region and point the new ALB at the new ASG. D (DNS): Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing with health checks serves each user from 'the AWS Region that provides the lowest latency,' which is the exact AWS-documented use case (the doc even uses the example of ELB load balancers in two Regions routing a London user to whichever is faster); the health checks add availability by avoiding unhealthy endpoints. F (data): Converting the DynamoDB table to a global table provides a 'fully managed, multi-Region, and multi-active' database with 'fast local read and write performance' and 'high availability through multi-Region deployment' where 'any global table replica can serve reads and writes' and 'no application changes are required.' Together, C+D+F deliver low latency and high availability at the compute, DNS, and data tiers.","explanation_zh":"目標是建立 active-active 多 Region 部署，同時降低回應延遲並提升兩地使用者的可用性，必須同時處理三個層級。C（運算層）：ALB 與 EC2 Auto Scaling group 都是 Regional 資源，因此必須在新 Region 建立新的 ALB 與 Auto Scaling group，並讓新 ALB 指向新 ASG。D（DNS 層）：Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing 搭配 health checks，會由『提供最低延遲的 AWS Region』服務每位使用者（AWS 文件甚至以兩個 Region 的 ELB load balancer 為例，把倫敦使用者導向較快者）；health checks 透過避開不健康端點來提升可用性。F（資料層）：將 DynamoDB table 轉換為 global table，提供『全代管、多 Region、multi-active』資料庫，具備『快速的本地讀寫效能』與『多 Region 部署的高可用性』，且『任一 global table replica 都可服務讀寫』、『不需更改應用程式』。C+D+F 合起來在運算、DNS、資料三層同時帶來低延遲與高可用性。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DynamoDB does not expose a 'cross-Region replication' option that you enable on a separately created table. The official, fully managed multi-Region mechanism is converting the table to a global table (option F), which provides multi-active local reads and writes. A separately created, manually replicated table is technically inaccurate and would not give low-latency local writes.","why_zh":"DynamoDB 並未在另外建立的 table 上提供可啟用的『cross-Region replication』選項。官方的全代管多 Region 機制是把 table 轉換為 global table（選項 F），可提供 multi-active 的本地讀寫。另外建立並手動複寫的 table 在技術上不正確，也無法提供低延遲的本地寫入。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"ALBs and EC2 Auto Scaling groups are Regional resources, not global resources. There is no 'global ALB' or 'global Auto Scaling group,' so creating them as global resources is technically impossible.","why_zh":"ALB 與 EC2 Auto Scaling group 是 Regional 資源，而非 global 資源。不存在『global ALB』或『global Auto Scaling group』，因此以 global 資源建立它們在技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Failover routing is active-passive: it sends all traffic to the primary Region and only switches to the secondary Region on failure. It does not minimize latency for users in both Regions, which is the stated objective; latency-based routing (D) routes each user to the lowest-latency Region.","why_zh":"Failover routing 是 active-passive：將所有流量導向主 Region，僅在故障時才切換到次要 Region。它無法為兩地使用者降低延遲（這是題目目標），而 latency-based routing（D）會把每位使用者導向延遲最低的 Region。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-latency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/introduction.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":66,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to apply a core set of security controls to an existing set of AWS accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. Individual teams will administer individual accounts by using the AdministratorAccess AWS managed policy. For all accounts. AWS CloudTrail and AWS Config must be turned on in all available AWS Regions. Individual account administrators must not be able to edit or delete any of the baseline resources. However, individual account administrators must be able to edit or delete their own CloudTrail trails and AWS Config rules. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要将一组核心的安全控制措施应用于现有的 AWS 账户。这些账户位于 AWS 组织中 的一个组织内。各个团队将通过使用“AdministratorAccess”AWS 管理策略来管理各自的账户。对于所有账 户，必须在所有可用的 AWS 区域中启用 AWS CloudTrail 和 AWS Config。各个账户管理员不得编辑或删除 任何基准资源，但必须能够编辑或删除其自身的 CloudTrail 跟踪和 AWS Config 规则。 哪种解决方案能以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that defines the standard account resources. Deploy the template to all accounts from the organization's management account by using CloudFormation StackSets. Set the stack policy to deny Update:Delete actions.","B":"Enable AWS Control Tower. Enroll the existing accounts in AWS Control Tower. Grant the individual account administrators access to CloudTrail and AWS Config.","C":"Designate an AWS Config management account. Create AWS Config recorders in all accounts by using AWS CloudFormation StackSets. Deploy AWS Config rules to the organization by using the AWS Config management account. Create a CloudTrail organization trail in the organization’s management account. Deny modification or deletion of the AWS Config recorders by using an SCP.","D":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that defines the standard account resources. Deploy the template to all accounts from the organization's management account by using CloudFormation StackSets Create an SCP that prevents updates or deletions to CloudTrail resources or AWS Config resources unless the principal is an administrator of the organization's management account."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，用于定义标准账户资源。通过 CloudFormation StackSets 从组织 的管理账户将该模板部署到所有账户。将堆栈策略设置为拒绝更新和删除操作。","B":"启用 AWS 控制塔。将现有账户注册到 AWS 控制塔。授予各个账户管理员对 CloudTrail 和 AWS Config 的访问权限。","C":"指定一个 AWS Config 管理账户。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在所有账户中创建 AWS Config 记录器。通过 AWS Config 管理账户将 AWS Config 规则部署到组织中。在组织的管理账户中创建 CloudTrail 组织跟踪。使用服务控制策略（SCP）禁止修改或删除 AWS Config 记录器。","D":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，定义标准账户资源。通过使用 CloudFormation StackSets 从组 织的管理账户将该模板部署到所有账户。创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），除非主体是组织管理 账户的管理员，否则禁止对 CloudTrail 资源或 AWS Config 资源进行更新或删除操作。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The decisive constraint is the nested requirement: AdministratorAccess-holding account admins must NOT be able to edit or delete the centrally deployed BASELINE resources, yet they MUST still be able to edit/delete their OWN CloudTrail trails and AWS Config rules. Option C satisfies all three requirements. AWS Config organization rules deployed from the Config management account are, per the AWS Config docs, used 'to enforce governance by ensuring that the underlying AWS Config rules are not modifiable by your organization's member accounts.' A CloudTrail organization trail created in the management account produces a copy in every member account that, per the CloudTrail docs, 'member accounts cannot remove or modify... Only the management account or delegated administrator account can change or delete the trail.' Both mechanisms protect the baseline WITHOUT touching a member admin's ability to create and manage their own (non-organization) trails and rules, so requirement 3 is preserved. The single, narrowly scoped SCP denies only modification/deletion of the AWS Config recorders (the baseline recording capability), not the admins' own Config rules. StackSets deploys the recorders to all accounts and Regions, satisfying requirement 1. Net result: low operational overhead and all three requirements met.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限制是巢狀需求：擁有 AdministratorAccess 的帳戶管理員「不可」編輯或刪除集中佈署的 baseline 資源，但「必須」仍能編輯/刪除「自己的」CloudTrail trail 與 AWS Config 規則。選項 C 滿足全部三項需求。由 Config 管理帳戶佈署的 AWS Config organization rules，依 AWS Config 文件用於『確保底層 AWS Config rules 無法被組織的 member accounts 修改』以落實治理。由管理帳戶建立的 CloudTrail organization trail 會在每個成員帳戶產生複本，依 CloudTrail 文件『member accounts 無法移除或修改…只有 management account 或 delegated administrator account 能變更或刪除該 trail』。這兩種機制保護 baseline，卻不影響成員管理員建立與管理自己的（非 organization）trail 與規則，因此保留了需求 3。唯一且範圍精準的 SCP 只拒絕對 AWS Config recorder（baseline 記錄能力）的修改/刪除，並未阻擋管理員自己的 Config 規則。StackSets 將 recorder 佈署至所有帳戶與區域，滿足需求 1。整體營運負擔低，且三項需求全數達成。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudFormation stack policy only protects resources 'during a stack update' and is documented as a fail-safe against unintentional updates, not an access-control boundary like an IAM policy; it can also be overridden. An account admin with AdministratorAccess can simply call cloudtrail:DeleteTrail or config:DeleteConfigRule directly via the service API, or run DeleteStack, completely bypassing the stack policy. So Deny Update:Delete does not actually protect the baseline from a member admin, failing requirement 2.","why_zh":"CloudFormation stack policy 僅在『stack 更新期間』保護資源，文件定位為防止意外更新的保險機制，而非如 IAM 般的存取控制邊界，且可被覆寫。具 AdministratorAccess 的帳戶管理員可直接透過服務 API 呼叫 cloudtrail:DeleteTrail 或 config:DeleteConfigRule，或執行 DeleteStack，完全繞過 stack policy。因此 Deny Update:Delete 無法真正保護 baseline，未滿足需求 2。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Enabling AWS Control Tower and enrolling pre-existing accounts is a heavyweight landing-zone deployment with enrollment prerequisites and an opinionated OU/guardrail model. It is not the MOST operationally efficient way to layer a core set of controls onto an existing account set, and 'grant the individual account administrators access to CloudTrail and AWS Config' is vague and conflicts with Control Tower's mandatory controls, which prevent member accounts from altering the Control Tower-managed CloudTrail/Config. It does not cleanly satisfy the block-baseline-but-allow-own-resources requirement.","why_zh":"啟用 AWS Control Tower 並納管既有帳戶屬笨重的 landing zone 佈署，帶有納管前置條件與高度定型的 OU/guardrail 模型。對於只是要在既有帳戶集上加一組核心控制而言，並非「最」有效率，且『授予各帳戶管理員存取 CloudTrail 與 AWS Config』語意模糊，並與 Control Tower 強制控制（阻止成員帳戶變更 Control Tower 託管的 CloudTrail/Config）相衝突。無法乾淨地滿足『阻擋 baseline 但允許自身資源』的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer and the classic trap. The SCP denies ALL CloudTrail and AWS Config update/delete actions for every member-account principal (only management-account admins are exempt, since SCPs never apply to the management account). That blanket deny also blocks member admins from editing or deleting their OWN trails and Config rules, directly violating requirement 3, which states they must be able to do so. The deny is not scoped to only the baseline resources, so it is too broad to meet the requirements.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案，也是典型陷阱。該 SCP 對每個成員帳戶 principal 拒絕全部 CloudTrail 與 AWS Config 的 update/delete 動作（因 SCP 從不套用於管理帳戶，故僅管理帳戶管理員例外）。此一律拒絕也會阻擋成員管理員編輯或刪除『自己的』trail 與 Config 規則，直接違反需求 3『他們必須能這麼做』。拒絕範圍未限縮在 baseline 資源，過於寬泛，無法滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/config-rule-multi-account-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/creating-trail-organization.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/least-privilege-cloudformation/cloudformation-stack-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/protect-stack-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":67,"question_en":"A company has its AWS accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. AWS Config is manually configured in each AWS account. The company needs to implement a solution to centrally configure AWS Config for all accounts in the organization The solution also must record resource changes to a central account. Which combination of actions should a DevOps engineer perform to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司的 AWS 账户在 AWS Organizations 中的组织内。AWS Config 在每个 AWS 账户中都是手动配 置的。该公司需要实施一个解决方案，以便在组织内的所有账户中集中配置 AWS Config。该解决方案 还必须将资源更改记录到一个中央账户中。 DevOps 工程师应执行哪些操作组合才能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure a delegated administrator account for AWS Config. Enable trusted access for AWS Config in the organization.","B":"Configure a delegated administrator account for AWS Config. Create a service-linked role for AWS Config in the organization’s management account.","C":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template to create an AWS Config aggregator. Configure a CloudFormation stack set to deploy the template to all accounts in the organization.","D":"Create an AWS Config organization aggregator in the organization's management account. Configure data collection from all AWS accounts in the organization and from all AWS Regions.","E":"Create an AWS Config organization aggregator in the delegated administrator account. Configure data collection from all AWS accounts in the organization and from all AWS Regions."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 AWS Config 配置一个委托管理员账户。在组织中为 AWS Config 启用受信任访问权限。","B":"为 AWS Config 配置委托管理员账户。在组织的管理账户中为 AWS Config 创建服务相关角色。","C":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板以创建 AWS Config 聚合器。配置一个 CloudFormation 堆栈集，将该模板部署到组织中的所有账户。","D":"在组织的管理账户中创建一个 AWS Config 组织聚合器。配置从组织中的所有 AWS 账户以及所有 AWS 区域收集数据。","E":"在委托管理员账户中创建一个 AWS Config 组织聚合器。配置从组织中的所有 AWS 账户以及所有 AWS 区域收集数据。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: centrally CONFIGURE AWS Config across the organization, and RECORD/collect resource configuration data to a central account. Option A delivers central configuration: you enable trusted access for AWS Config in the organization (enable-aws-service-access for config.amazonaws.com and config-multiaccountsetup.amazonaws.com) and register a member account as the delegated administrator, which lets that account deploy and manage Config rules, conformance packs, and aggregation organization-wide. Option E delivers central recording: an AWS Config organization aggregator collects configuration and compliance data from all accounts and all Regions into a single aggregator account, and for organization aggregators authorization is not required because it is integrated with AWS Organizations. The AWS docs explicitly state an organization aggregator can be created by 'the management account or a registered delegated administrator'; because Option A has already established a delegated administrator, the aggregator belongs in that delegated administrator account (E), which is also consistent with AWS Security Reference Architecture guidance to keep the management account minimal. This makes A + E the internally consistent, recommended pairing. Note: an aggregator gives a read-only replicated view and does not itself enable recording in source accounts, but it is the only option offered for centralizing resource configuration data, so it is the intended 'record to a central account' mechanism.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩部分：在整個 organization 中集中「設定」AWS Config，以及將資源組態資料「記錄/收集」到一個中央帳戶。選項 A 提供集中設定：在 organization 中為 AWS Config 啟用 trusted access（對 config.amazonaws.com 與 config-multiaccountsetup.amazonaws.com 執行 enable-aws-service-access），並將一個成員帳戶註冊為 delegated administrator，使該帳戶可在整個 organization 範圍內部署與管理 Config rules、conformance packs 以及彙總（aggregation）。選項 E 提供集中記錄：AWS Config 的 organization aggregator 會將所有帳戶、所有 Region 的組態與合規資料收集到單一 aggregator 帳戶；對 organization aggregator 而言不需要 authorization，因為它已與 AWS Organizations 整合。AWS 文件明確指出 organization aggregator 可由「management account 或已註冊的 delegated administrator」建立；既然選項 A 已設立 delegated administrator，aggregator 自然應建立在該 delegated administrator 帳戶（E），這也符合 AWS Security Reference Architecture 盡量保持 management account 最小化的建議。因此 A + E 是內部一致且建議的組合。註：aggregator 提供的是唯讀的複製檢視，本身不會在來源帳戶啟用記錄器，但它是選項中唯一能將資源組態資料集中化的機制，因此是題目所指「記錄到中央帳戶」的方式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The service-linked role AWSServiceRoleForConfig is created automatically by AWS Config (in member accounts when integration is enabled); you do not manually 'create' it in the management account as a setup step, and it is not the mechanism that enables central organization-wide configuration. The correct enabler is trusted access plus delegated administrator registration (Option A).","why_zh":"service-linked role AWSServiceRoleForConfig 是由 AWS Config 在啟用整合時自動建立（於成員帳戶），不需要在 management account 手動「建立」作為設定步驟，且它不是啟用整個 organization 集中設定的機制。正確的啟用方式是 trusted access 加上 delegated administrator 註冊（選項 A）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An aggregator is a single resource created in one central aggregator account, not something you deploy into every account via a StackSet. Deploying an aggregator to all accounts conflates the aggregator with per-account configuration recorders and does not produce a centralized view.","why_zh":"aggregator 是建立在單一中央 aggregator 帳戶中的單一資源，並非透過 StackSet 部署到每個帳戶。將 aggregator 部署到所有帳戶混淆了 aggregator 與各帳戶的 configuration recorder，也無法產生集中檢視。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating the organization aggregator in the management account is technically possible, but it conflicts with Option A, which establishes a delegated administrator. The consistent and AWS-recommended design places the aggregator in the delegated administrator account (E) to keep the management account minimal per the AWS Security Reference Architecture.","why_zh":"在 management account 建立 organization aggregator 技術上可行，但與設立 delegated administrator 的選項 A 不一致。一致且 AWS 建議的設計是將 aggregator 放在 delegated administrator 帳戶（E），以依照 AWS Security Reference Architecture 保持 management account 最小化。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/aggregated-register-delegated-administrator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/aggregate-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/aggregated-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/aggregated-add-authorization.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/security-reference-architecture/org-management.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":68,"question_en":"A company wants to migrate its content sharing web application hosted on Amazon EC2 to a serverless architecture. The company currently deploys changes to its application by creating a new Auto Scaling group of EC2 instances and a new Elastic Load Balancer, and then shifting the traffic away using an Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy. For its new serverless application, the company is planning to use Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda. The company will need to update its deployment processes to work with the new application. It will also need to retain the ability to test new features on a small number of users before rolling the features out to the entire user base. Which deployment strategy will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望将其托管在亚马逊 EC2 上的内容共享网络应用程序迁移到无服务器架构。该公司目前 通过创建新的 EC2 实例自动扩展组和新的弹性负载均衡器来部署应用程序的更改，然后使用亚马逊 Route 53 加权路由策略将流量转移过去。 该公司计划为其新的无服务器应用程序使用亚马逊 API 网关和 AWS Lambda。公司需要更新其部署 流程以适应新应用。此外，公司还需要保留先在少量用户中测试新功能，然后再向全体用户推广的功 能。 哪种部署策略能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CDK to deploy API Gateway and Lambda functions. When code needs to be changed, update the AWS CloudFormation stack and deploy the new version of the APIs and Lambda functions. Use a Route 53 failover routing policy for the canary release strategy.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation to deploy API Gateway and Lambda functions using Lambda function versions. When code needs to be changed, update the CloudFormation stack with the new Lambda code and update the API versions using a canary release strategy. Promote the new version when testing is complete.","C":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to deploy API Gateway and Lambda functions. When code needs to be changed, deploy a new version of the API and Lambda functions. Shift traffic gradually using an Elastic Beanstalk blue/green deployment.","D":"Use AWS OpsWorks to deploy API Gateway in the service layer and Lambda functions in a custom layer. When code needs to be changed, use OpsWorks to perform a blue/green deployment and shift traffic gradually."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CDK 部署 API Gateway 和 Lambda 函数。当代码需要更改时，更新 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈并部署 API 和 Lambda 函数的新版本。对于金丝雀发布策略，使用 Route 53 故障转移路由策略。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 API Gateway 和 Lambda 函数，使用 Lambda 函数版本。当代码需 要更改时，使用新的 Lambda 更新 CloudFormation 堆栈。 使用金丝雀发布策略来编写和更新 API 版本。测试完成后推广新版本。","C":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 部署 API Gateway 和 Lambda 函数。当代码需要更改时，部署 API 和 Lambda 函数的新版本。使用 Elastic Beanstalk 蓝/绿部署逐步转移流量。","D":"使用 AWS OpsWorks 在服务层部署 API 网关，并在自定义层部署 Lambda 函数。当代码需要更 改时，使用 OpsWorks 执行蓝/绿部署，并逐步转移流量。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: deploy a serverless API Gateway + Lambda application via an updated deployment process, and retain the ability to test new features on a small subset of users before a full rollout (a canary release). API Gateway natively supports canary release deployments: you attach canarySettings to a production stage that route a configurable small percentage of API traffic at random to a new deployment backed by a new Lambda function version, while the base/production version serves the rest. After test metrics pass, you promote the canary to production and disable it. These canary settings are fully expressible in CloudFormation (AWS::ApiGateway::Deployment CanarySetting and AWS::ApiGateway::Stage CanarySetting), and Lambda function versions let you ship immutable new code. Option B describes exactly this flow: deploy with CloudFormation, update the stack with new Lambda code, split traffic with an API canary release, then promote. This is the AWS-recommended serverless replacement for the old EC2-era Route 53 weighted ASG/ELB pattern.","explanation_zh":"需求是：透過更新後的部署流程部署 serverless 的 API Gateway + Lambda 應用程式，並保留在全面推出前先讓一小部分使用者測試新功能的能力（即 canary release）。API Gateway 原生支援 canary release 部署：你在 production stage 加上 canarySettings，將可設定的一小部分 API 流量隨機導向由新 Lambda function version 支援的新 deployment，其餘流量則由 base/production 版本處理。測試指標通過後，即可將 canary 提升（promote）為 production 並停用它。這些 canary settings 完全可在 CloudFormation 中表達（AWS::ApiGateway::Deployment CanarySetting 與 AWS::ApiGateway::Stage CanarySetting），而 Lambda function versions 則用於發布不可變的新程式碼。選項 B 正好描述此流程：用 CloudFormation 部署、用新的 Lambda 程式碼更新 stack、用 API canary release 分流流量，然後提升。這是 AWS 建議用以取代舊有 EC2 時代 Route 53 weighted 搭配 ASG/ELB 模式的 serverless 做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS CDK can indeed deploy API Gateway and Lambda (it synthesizes CloudFormation), but the canary mechanism named is wrong. Route 53 failover routing is active-passive, health-check-driven failover: it sends ALL traffic to the primary record and only switches to the secondary when the primary becomes unhealthy. It cannot split a small percentage of traffic to test new features on a subset of users, so it does not implement a canary release.","why_zh":"AWS CDK 確實能部署 API Gateway 與 Lambda（它會合成 CloudFormation），但所述的 canary 機制錯誤。Route 53 failover routing 是 active-passive、由 health check 觸發的容錯切換：它將全部流量導向 primary 記錄，只有當 primary 變為不健康時才切到 secondary。它無法將一小部分流量分流以對部分使用者測試新功能，因此無法實作 canary release。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk provisions and manages Amazon EC2-based web/worker environments (and Docker containers on EC2); it does not deploy API Gateway or Lambda serverless functions. The entire goal of this migration is to move OFF EC2 to serverless, so using Beanstalk contradicts the requirement and is not a supported way to deploy API Gateway + Lambda.","why_zh":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk 佈建並管理以 Amazon EC2 為基礎的 web/worker 環境（以及 EC2 上的 Docker 容器）；它無法部署 API Gateway 或 Lambda serverless functions。這次遷移的整個目標是要離開 EC2 改用 serverless，因此使用 Beanstalk 與需求互相矛盾，也不是部署 API Gateway + Lambda 的受支援方式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS OpsWorks is a configuration-management service (managed Chef/Puppet) that operates on EC2 instances organized into layers; it has no concept of an API Gateway 'service layer' or a Lambda 'custom layer' and cannot deploy or perform blue/green traffic shifting for API Gateway and Lambda. This option is technically invalid for a serverless architecture.","why_zh":"AWS OpsWorks 是組態管理服務（受管的 Chef/Puppet），作用於以 layer 組織的 EC2 instances；它沒有 API Gateway「service layer」或 Lambda「custom layer」的概念，也無法為 API Gateway 與 Lambda 部署或執行 blue/green 流量切換。此選項對 serverless 架構而言在技術上不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/canary-release.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-apigateway-deployment-canarysetting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-apigateway-stage-canarysetting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/how-to-deploy-api.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-failover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/Welcome.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":69,"question_en":"A development team uses AWS CodeCommit, AWS CodePipeline, and AWS CodeBuild to develop and deploy an application. Changes to the code are submitted by pull requests. The development team reviews and merges the pull requests, and then the pipeline builds and tests the application. Over time, the number of pull requests has increased. The pipeline is frequently blocked because of failing tests. To prevent this blockage, the development team wants to run the unit and integration tests on each pull request before it is merged. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个开发团队使用 AWS CodeCommit、AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 来开发和部署应用程序。 代码变更通过拉取请求提交。开发团队审核并合并拉取请求，然后管道会构建和测试应用程序。 随着时间的推移，拉取请求的数量不断增加。由于测试失败，流水线经常被阻塞。为防止这种情况 发生，开发团队希望在每个拉取请求合并之前运行单元测试和集成测试。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CodeBuild project to run the unit and integration tests. Create a CodeCommit approval rule template. Configure the template to require the successful invocation of the CodeBuild project. Attach the approval rule to the project's CodeCommit repository.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match pullRequestCreated events from CodeCommit Create a CodeBuild project to run the unit and integration tests. Configure the CodeBuild project as a target of the EventBridge rule that includes a custom event payload with the CodeCommit repository and branch information from the event.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match pullRequestCreated events from CodeCommit. Modify the existing CodePipeline pipeline to not run the deploy steps if the build is started from a pull request. Configure the EventBridge rule to run the pipeline with a custom payload that contains the CodeCommit repository and branch information from the event.","D":"Create a CodeBuild project to run the unit and integration tests. Create a CodeCommit notification rule that matches when a pull request is created or updated. Configure the notification rule to invoke the CodeBuild project."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 CodeBuild 项目来运行单元测试和集成测试。创建一个 CodeCommit 批准规则模板。配 置模板以要求成功调用 CodeBuild 项目。将批准规则附加到项目的 CodeCommit 存储库。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以匹配来自 CodeCommit 的 pullRequestCreated 事件。创建一 个 CodeBuild 项目来运行单元测试和集成测试。将 CodeBuild 项目配置为 EventBridge 规则的目 标，该规则包含一个自定义事件负载，其中包含来自事件的 CodeCommit 存储库和分支信息。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以匹配来自 CodeCommit 的 pullRequestCreated 事件。修改 现有的 CodePipeline 管道，使其在从拉取请求启动构建时跳过部署步骤。配置 EventBridge 规则， 使用包含事件中 CodeCommit 存储库和分支信息的自定义负载来运行管道。","D":"创建一个 CodeBuild 项目来运行单元测试和集成测试。创建一个 CodeCommit 通知规则，用于匹 配创建或更新拉取请求的情况。配置通知规则以调用 CodeBuild 项目。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The team needs to automatically run the unit and integration tests on each CodeCommit pull request BEFORE it is merged, decoupled from the existing deploy pipeline that keeps getting blocked. CodeCommit emits pull request events (the 'CodeCommit Pull Request State Change' detail-type, including the pullRequestCreated event) directly to Amazon EventBridge. EventBridge natively supports a CodeBuild project as a target (the EventBridge 'Event bus targets' guide lists 'CodeBuild projects as targets'). So you create an EventBridge rule that matches the pull request creation event and invokes a CodeBuild project that runs the tests. Because CodeBuild must build the pull request's source, the rule passes a custom event payload (constant input / input transformer) carrying the CodeCommit repository and source branch information from the event, which CodeBuild uses as a source version override (sourceVersion). This is exactly Option B and matches the documented EventBridge-to-CodeBuild target pattern.","explanation_zh":"團隊需要在每個 CodeCommit pull request 合併之前自動執行單元與整合測試，並與一直被卡住的既有部署 pipeline 解耦。CodeCommit 會將 pull request 事件（detail-type 為 'CodeCommit Pull Request State Change'，包含 pullRequestCreated 事件）直接送往 Amazon EventBridge。EventBridge 原生支援以 CodeBuild project 作為 target（EventBridge 'Event bus targets' 文件中明列 'CodeBuild projects as targets'）。因此建立一個比對 pull request 建立事件的 EventBridge rule，並呼叫執行測試的 CodeBuild project。由於 CodeBuild 需要建置該 pull request 的原始碼，rule 透過自訂事件 payload（constant input / input transformer）帶入事件中的 CodeCommit repository 與來源 branch 資訊，供 CodeBuild 作為 source version override（sourceVersion）使用。這正是選項 B，符合官方文件記載的 EventBridge 至 CodeBuild target 模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodeCommit approval rules and approval rule templates can only specify the number of required approvals and an optional approval pool of IAM users/roles whose approvals count. The AWS docs describe no mechanism to require the successful invocation of a CodeBuild project as a merge condition, so a template cannot enforce that tests pass before a pull request is merged.","why_zh":"CodeCommit approval rule 與 approval rule template 只能指定所需的核准數量以及可選的 IAM 使用者/角色核准池。AWS 文件未提供將 CodeBuild project 成功執行設為合併條件的機制，因此 template 無法在 pull request 合併前強制要求測試通過。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This reuses the existing deploy pipeline, which is the very thing being blocked by failing tests; the requirement is to test each PR independently and pre-merge so the pipeline stops getting blocked. Reworking the same pipeline to conditionally skip deploy is more complex, and there is no clean way for an EventBridge payload to override an existing CodePipeline's fixed source/branch to point at the pull request branch the way a CodeBuild target's sourceVersion override can. Option B is the cleaner, decoupled, documented pattern.","why_zh":"此方案重用既有的部署 pipeline，而該 pipeline 正是因測試失敗而被阻塞的對象；需求是在合併前獨立測試每個 PR 以避免 pipeline 被卡住。改造同一條 pipeline 使其有條件地跳過部署較為複雜，且 EventBridge payload 無法像 CodeBuild target 的 sourceVersion override 那樣，乾淨地覆寫既有 CodePipeline 固定的 source/branch 以指向該 pull request 分支。選項 B 才是更乾淨、解耦且有文件記載的模式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Developer Tools (CodeStar) notification rules can only target Amazon SNS topics and AWS Chatbot clients (Slack, Microsoft Teams, Amazon Chime). A notification rule cannot directly invoke a CodeBuild project, so this configuration is not supported and cannot run the tests.","why_zh":"Developer Tools（CodeStar）notification rule 只能 target Amazon SNS topic 與 AWS Chatbot client（Slack、Microsoft Teams、Amazon Chime）。notification rule 無法直接呼叫 CodeBuild project，因此此設定不被支援，也無法執行測試。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codecommit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-targets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pull-request-approval-rule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-transform-target-input.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dtconsole/latest/userguide/notifications-chatbot.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":70,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. The application requires frequent restarts. The application logs contain error messages when a restart is required. The application logs are published to a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. An Amazon CloudWatch alarm notifies an application engineer through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic when the logs contain a large number of restart-related error messages. The application engineer manually restarts the application on the instances after the application engineer receives a notification from the SNS topic. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to automate the application restart on the instances without restarting the instances. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient manner?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例集群上的应用程序。该应用程序需要频繁重启。当需要重 启时，应用程序日志中会包含错误消息。应用程序日志会发布到亚马逊 CloudWatch Logs 中的一个 日志组。 当日志中包含大量与重启相关的错误消息时，Amazon CloudWatch 警报会通过 Amazon 简单通知服 务（Amazon SNS）主题通知应用程序工程师。应用程序工程师在收到 SNS 主题的通知后，会手动 在实例上重启应用程序。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，以在不重启实例的情况下实现应用程序的自动重启。 哪种解决方案能在操作效率最高的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that runs a script to restart the application on the instances. Configure the SNS topic to invoke the runbook.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function that restarts the application on the instances. Configure the Lambda function as an event destination of the SNS topic.","C":"Configure an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that runs a script to restart the application on the instances. Create an AWS Lambda function to invoke the runbook. Configure the Lambda function as an event destination of the SNS topic.","D":"Configure an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that runs a script to restart the application on the instances. Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts when the CloudWatch alarm enters ALARM state. Specify the runbook as a target of the rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 AWS 系统管理器自动化运行手册，使其运行一个脚本以在实例上重启应用程序。配置 SNS 主题以调用该运行手册。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于重启实例上的应用程序。将该 Lambda 函数配置为 SNS 主题的事件 目标。","C":"配置一个 AWS 系统管理器自动化运行手册，运行一个脚本以在实例上重启应用程序。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来调用该运行手册。将 Lambda 函数配置为 SNS 主题的事件目标。","D":"配置一个 AWS 系统管理器自动化运行手册，运行一个脚本以在实例上重启应用程序。配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，当 CloudWatch 警报进入“告警”状态时触发该规则。将运行手册指定为 规则的目标。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MOST operationally efficient. CloudWatch automatically sends a 'CloudWatch Alarm State Change' event directly to Amazon EventBridge whenever an alarm changes state (verified at events-ref-cloudwatch.html and Acting_Alarm_Changes.html). EventBridge's list of available AWS service targets explicitly includes 'Systems Manager Automation' (verified at eb-targets.html). Therefore an EventBridge rule that matches the alarm entering ALARM state can invoke the SSM Automation runbook directly, with no custom code. The runbook uses the aws:runCommand action to restart the application process on the instances without rebooting the instances. This native, code-free integration has the fewest moving parts, so it is the most operationally efficient. Option A is technically impossible because Amazon SNS subscription protocols are limited to HTTP/HTTPS, Email/Email-JSON, Amazon SQS, AWS Lambda, mobile push (platform application), SMS, and Kinesis Data Firehose; there is no protocol that lets SNS directly invoke an SSM Automation runbook. Options B and C add custom Lambda code that must be written and maintained, increasing operational overhead unnecessarily.","explanation_zh":"限定條件是「最高運維效率 (MOST operationally efficient)」。每當告警狀態變更時，CloudWatch 會自動將 'CloudWatch Alarm State Change' 事件直接送往 Amazon EventBridge（已於 events-ref-cloudwatch.html 與 Acting_Alarm_Changes.html 驗證）。EventBridge 的可用 AWS 服務目標清單明確包含 'Systems Manager Automation'（已於 eb-targets.html 驗證）。因此，一條在告警進入 ALARM 狀態時觸發的 EventBridge rule 可以直接調用 SSM Automation runbook，完全不需自訂程式碼。該 runbook 使用 aws:runCommand 動作在執行個體上重啟應用程式行程，而不需重啟執行個體。這種原生、免程式碼的整合元件最少，因此運維效率最高。選項 A 技術上不可行，因為 Amazon SNS 訂閱協定僅限 HTTP/HTTPS、Email/Email-JSON、Amazon SQS、AWS Lambda、mobile push (platform application)、SMS 與 Kinesis Data Firehose；沒有任何協定可讓 SNS 直接調用 SSM Automation runbook。選項 B 與 C 則加入了需編寫與維護的自訂 Lambda 程式碼，徒增運維負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon SNS cannot directly invoke an SSM Automation runbook. SNS subscription protocols are limited to HTTP/HTTPS, Email/Email-JSON, Amazon SQS, AWS Lambda, mobile push (platform application), SMS, and Kinesis Data Firehose. There is no SNS protocol or 'invoke runbook' subscription type, so this design is technically impossible.","why_zh":"Amazon SNS 無法直接調用 SSM Automation runbook。SNS 訂閱協定僅限 HTTP/HTTPS、Email/Email-JSON、Amazon SQS、AWS Lambda、mobile push (platform application)、SMS 與 Kinesis Data Firehose，沒有可調用 runbook 的協定或訂閱類型，技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Lambda is a valid SNS subscriber, but writing custom Lambda code to restart the app adds maintenance overhead, and the Lambda would still need to reach into the EC2 instances (typically via SSM Run Command/Automation) to restart the process. That is more code and more moving parts than the native EventBridge-to-Automation path, so it is not the most operationally efficient.","why_zh":"Lambda 雖是合法的 SNS 訂閱者，但需編寫自訂 Lambda 程式碼來重啟應用，增加維護負擔，且該 Lambda 仍須透過（通常是 SSM Run Command/Automation）連入 EC2 執行個體才能重啟行程。相較於原生的 EventBridge 直接觸發 Automation，元件與程式碼更多，運維效率較低。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This works (Lambda subscribes to SNS and invokes the runbook), but it inserts an unnecessary Lambda layer that must be coded and maintained. EventBridge can target Systems Manager Automation directly off the alarm state-change event, so the Lambda is redundant overhead, making this less operationally efficient than D.","why_zh":"此方案可行（Lambda 訂閱 SNS 並調用 runbook），但插入了一層多餘且需編寫維護的 Lambda。EventBridge 可在告警狀態變更事件觸發時直接以 Systems Manager Automation 為目標，因此該 Lambda 屬多餘負擔，運維效率不如 D。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-targets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-cloudwatch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Acting_Alarm_Changes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-create-subscribe-endpoint-to-topic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-automation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":71,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer at a company is supporting an AWS environment in which all users use AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). The company wants to immediately disable credentials of any new IAM user and wants the security team to receive a notification. Which combination of steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"某公司的 DevOps 工程师正在维护一个 AWS 环境，该环境中所有用户均使用 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）。该公司希望立即禁用任何新 IAM 用户的凭证，并希望安全团队收到通知。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to an IAM CreateUser API call in AWS CloudTrail.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to an IAM GetLoginProfile API call in AWS CloudTrail.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that is a target of the EventBridge rule. Configure the Lambda function to disable any access keys and delete the login profiles that are associated with the IAM user.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that is a target of the EventBridge rule. Configure the Lambda function to delete the login profiles that are associated with the IAM user.","E":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that is a target of the EventBridge rule. Subscribe the security team's group email address to the topic.","F":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue that is a target of the Lambda function. Subscribe the security team's group email address to the queue."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS CloudTrail 中创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 IAM CreateUser API 调用做出响应。","B":"在 AWS CloudTrail 中创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 IAM 的 GetLoginProfile API 调用做出响应。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，使其成为 EventBridge 规则的目标。配置该 Lambda 函数以禁用任何访问密 钥并删除与 IAM 用户关联的登录配置文件。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，使其成为 EventBridge 规则的目标。配置该 Lambda 函数以删除与 IAM 用户关联的登录配置文件。","E":"创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，使其成为 EventBridge 规则的目标。将安全团队的 组电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。","F":"创建一个亚马逊简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）队列，将其设为 Lambda 函数的目标。将安全团队 的组电子邮件地址订阅到该队列。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to immediately disable the credentials of any NEW IAM user and notify the security team. (A) An EventBridge rule reacting to the IAM CreateUser API call delivered via AWS CloudTrail is the correct trigger; the IAM-to-EventBridge integration delivers IAM API calls (matched on eventName) via CloudTrail, and CreateUser is the event that signals a newly created IAM user. (C) The Lambda target must disable any access keys AND delete the login profile. This is decisive: AWS documentation for DeleteLoginProfile explicitly states that deleting the login profile only prevents AWS console sign-in and 'does not prevent the user from running any AWS CLI, PowerShell, or API calls using AWS access keys that might still be attached to the user account.' To fully disable a user's credentials you must address both the programmatic credentials (access keys) and the console credentials (login profile). (E) An SNS topic as the EventBridge target, with the security team's email subscribed, delivers the notification; SNS natively supports email endpoint subscriptions. This combination of A, C, E fully satisfies both requirements.","explanation_zh":"需求是立即停用任何「新」IAM 使用者的憑證並通知安全團隊。(A) 透過 AWS CloudTrail 傳遞的 IAM CreateUser API 呼叫建立 EventBridge 規則是正確的觸發來源；IAM 與 EventBridge 的整合會經由 CloudTrail 傳遞 IAM API 呼叫（以 eventName 比對），而 CreateUser 正是代表建立新 IAM 使用者的事件。(C) Lambda 目標必須同時停用所有 access keys 並刪除 login profile，這是決定性關鍵：AWS DeleteLoginProfile 文件明確說明刪除 login profile 只會封鎖主控台登入，「並不會阻止使用者透過仍附加在帳號上的 access keys 執行任何 AWS CLI、PowerShell 或 API 呼叫」。要完整停用憑證，必須同時處理程式化憑證（access keys）與主控台憑證（login profile）。(E) 以 SNS topic 作為 EventBridge 目標並讓安全團隊的 email 訂閱，即可送出通知，SNS 原生支援 email 端點訂閱。A、C、E 的組合完整滿足兩項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"GetLoginProfile is a read-only API that retrieves an existing user's password creation date and reset status; it does not signal creation of a new IAM user and would not fire when a user is provisioned. The correct trigger for a newly created user is CreateUser, not GetLoginProfile.","why_zh":"GetLoginProfile 是唯讀 API，用於擷取既有使用者的密碼建立日期與重設狀態，並非建立新 IAM 使用者的訊號，建立使用者時也不會觸發。新使用者的正確觸發事件是 CreateUser，而非 GetLoginProfile。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Deleting only the login profile is incomplete. Per AWS docs, DeleteLoginProfile only prevents AWS console sign-in and does NOT stop programmatic access via access keys that may still be attached. The new user could still have active access keys, so this fails to fully 'disable credentials.' Option C (which also disables access keys) strictly supersedes D.","why_zh":"只刪除 login profile 並不完整。依 AWS 文件，DeleteLoginProfile 只封鎖主控台登入，並不會停止透過仍附加之 access keys 的程式化存取。新使用者仍可能有有效的 access keys，因此無法完整「停用憑證」。同時停用 access keys 的選項 C 完全優於 D。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"You cannot subscribe an email address to an Amazon SQS queue; only Amazon SNS supports email endpoint subscriptions. SQS is a polling-based message queue with no email delivery. The notification path must use SNS (option E). The wiring is also illogical (an SQS queue as a 'target of the Lambda function' for email).","why_zh":"無法將 email 訂閱到 Amazon SQS 佇列，只有 Amazon SNS 支援 email 端點訂閱。SQS 是以輪詢為基礎的訊息佇列，沒有 email 傳遞功能。通知路徑必須使用 SNS（選項 E）。其架構描述（以 SQS 佇列作為 Lambda 函式的『目標』來寄送 email）本身也不合理。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/iam_example_iam_DeleteLoginProfile_section.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_access-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-email-notifications.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":72,"question_en":"A company wants to set up a continuous delivery pipeline. The company stores application code in a private GitHub repository. The company needs to deploy the application components to Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS), Amazon EC2, and AWS Lambda. The pipeline must support manual approval actions. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司想要建立一个持续交付流水线。该公司将应用程序代码存储在私有 GitHub 代码库中。该公司需 要将应用程序组件部署到亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）、亚马逊 EC2 和 AWS Lambda 上。该流 水线必须支持人工审批操作。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CodePipeline with Amazon ECS, Amazon EC2, and Lambda as deploy providers.","B":"Use AWS CodePipeline with AWS CodeDeploy as the deploy provider.","C":"Use AWS CodePipeline with AWS Elastic Beanstalk as the deploy provider.","D":"Use AWS CodeDeploy with GitHub integration to deploy the application."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 与 Amazon ECS、Amazon EC2 和 Lambda 作为部署提供程序。","B":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 并将 AWS CodeDeploy 作为部署提供程序。","C":"使用 AWS CodePipeline 并将 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 作为部署提供商。","D":"使用与 GitHub 集成的 AWS CodeDeploy 部署应用程序。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS CodePipeline supplies the continuous delivery pipeline: it can use the private GitHub repository as a source through a CodeStarSourceConnection (GitHub via GitHub App connection), and it natively supports a Manual approval action type. The deploy requirement spans three different compute targets (Amazon ECS, Amazon EC2, and AWS Lambda). AWS CodeDeploy is the single deployment service that natively automates application deployments across all three compute platforms: per the 'What is CodeDeploy?' page it 'automates application deployments to Amazon EC2 instances, on-premises instances, serverless Lambda functions, or Amazon ECS services,' and it explicitly deploys to the EC2/On-Premises, AWS Lambda, and Amazon ECS compute platforms. Therefore using CodePipeline with CodeDeploy as the deploy provider lets one consistent deploy provider handle ECS, EC2, and Lambda while CodePipeline supplies the GitHub source integration and manual approval actions. This is the standard, fully supported answer.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodePipeline 提供持續交付管線：它可以透過 CodeStarSourceConnection（GitHub via GitHub App connection）將私有的 GitHub 儲存庫作為來源，並原生支援 Manual approval action 類型。部署需求橫跨三種不同的運算目標（Amazon ECS、Amazon EC2 與 AWS Lambda）。AWS CodeDeploy 是唯一能原生跨所有三種運算平台自動化應用程式部署的服務：根據「What is CodeDeploy?」頁面，它可「automates application deployments to Amazon EC2 instances, on-premises instances, serverless Lambda functions, or Amazon ECS services」，並明確支援 EC2/On-Premises、AWS Lambda 與 Amazon ECS 三種運算平台。因此使用 CodePipeline 搭配 CodeDeploy 作為 deploy provider，就能以單一一致的部署服務同時處理 ECS、EC2 與 Lambda，而 CodePipeline 則提供 GitHub source 整合與 manual approval。這是標準且完整受支援的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"While CodePipeline does expose separate native deploy actions (Amazon ECS, an EC2 Deploy action, and newer Lambda deploy/invoke actions), this option requires wiring up three distinct deploy providers and conflates Lambda (historically an Invoke action, with the native EC2/Lambda deploy actions being V2-only) rather than using one unified service. The intended, canonical solution is the single CodeDeploy provider, which natively spans EC2, Lambda, and ECS, so B is the better fit.","why_zh":"雖然 CodePipeline 確實有各自獨立的原生部署動作（Amazon ECS、EC2 Deploy action，以及較新的 Lambda deploy/invoke 動作），但此選項需要組合三個不同的 deploy provider，且把 Lambda（歷史上屬於 Invoke action，而原生 EC2/Lambda 部署動作僅限 V2 管線）混為一談，而非使用單一統一的服務。預期且標準的解法是使用單一的 CodeDeploy provider，它原生橫跨 EC2、Lambda 與 ECS，因此 B 較為貼切。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk is a PaaS for deploying and scaling web applications on managed EC2 environments; it does not deploy to arbitrary EC2 fleets via CodeDeploy semantics, does not update Amazon ECS task definitions/services, and does not deploy AWS Lambda function versions. It cannot satisfy all three compute targets.","why_zh":"AWS Elastic Beanstalk 是用於在受管 EC2 環境部署與擴展 Web 應用程式的 PaaS；它無法以 CodeDeploy 的方式部署到任意 EC2 機群、無法更新 Amazon ECS 任務定義/服務，也無法部署 AWS Lambda 函式版本。無法同時滿足三種運算目標。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS CodeDeploy alone is a deployment service, not a pipeline orchestrator. It does not provide pipeline stages with a built-in Manual approval action that gates promotion between stages. The requirement for a continuous delivery pipeline with manual approval actions specifically needs AWS CodePipeline as the orchestrator, so CodeDeploy with only GitHub integration is insufficient.","why_zh":"單獨的 AWS CodeDeploy 是部署服務，而非管線編排器。它無法提供具內建 Manual approval action 的管線階段來控管階段之間的晉級。題目要求具備 manual approval 的持續交付管線，明確需要由 AWS CodePipeline 作為編排器，因此僅有 GitHub 整合的 CodeDeploy 並不足夠。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-valid-providers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CodestarConnectionSource.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":73,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. When the application starts up, the application needs to process data from an Amazon S3 bucket before the application can start to serve requests. The size of the data that is stored in the S3 bucket is growing. When the Auto Scaling group adds new instances, the application now takes several minutes to download and process the data before the application can serve requests. The company must reduce the time that elapses before new EC2 instances are ready to serve requests. Which solution is the MOST cost-effective way to reduce the application startup time?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的应用程序，这些实例位于一个自动扩展组中。当应用程 序启动时，它需要先处理来自亚马逊 S3 存储桶的数据，然后才能开始响应请求。 存储在 S3 存储桶中的数据量正在增加。当自动扩展组添加新实例时，应用程序现在需要花费数分 钟来下载和处理数据，才能开始响应请求。该公司必须缩短新 EC2 实例准备好响应请求所需的时间。 哪种解决方案是降低应用程序启动时间的最具成本效益的方法？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a warm pool for the Auto Scaling group with warmed EC2 instances in the Stopped state. Configure an autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING lifecycle hook on the Auto Scaling group. Modify the application to complete the lifecycle hook when the application is ready to serve requests.","B":"Increase the maximum instance count of the Auto Scaling group. Configure an autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING lifecycle hook on the Auto Scaling group. Modify the application to complete the lifecycle hook when the application is ready to serve requests.","C":"Configure a warm pool for the Auto Scaling group with warmed EC2 instances in the Running state. Configure an autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING lifecycle hook on the Auto Scaling group. Modify the application to complete the lifecycle hook when the application is ready to serve requests.","D":"Increase the maximum instance count of the Auto Scaling group. Configure an autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING lifecycle hook on the Auto Scaling group. Modify the application to complete the lifecycle hook and to place the new instance in the Standby state when the application is ready to serve requests."},"options_zh":{"A":"为自动扩展组配置一个包含处于停止状态的预热 EC2 实例的预热池。在自动扩展组上配置一个自 动扩展：EC2 实例启动生命周期挂钩。修改应用程序，使其在准备好处理请求时完成生命周期挂 钩。","B":"增加自动扩展组的最大实例数。在自动扩展组上配置一个生命周期挂钩 autoscaling:EC2_ INSTANCE_LAUNCHING。修改应用程序，使其在准备好处理请求时完成生命周期挂钩。","C":"为自动扩展组配置一个包含处于运行状态的预热 EC2 实例的暖池。在自动扩展组上配置一个 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING 生命周期挂钩。修改应用程序，使其在准备好处理请 求时完成生命周期挂钩。","D":"增加自动扩展组的最大实例数。在自动扩展组上配置一个生命周期挂钩 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_ LAUNCHING。修改应用程序以完成生命周期挂钩，并在应用程序准备好处理请求时将新实例置 于备用状态。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application has a long boot time because each new instance must download and process growing S3 data before it can serve requests. This is the canonical use case for an EC2 Auto Scaling warm pool, which keeps pre-initialized instances alongside the group so they can warm-start quickly during scale-out. AWS docs describe warm pools as a way to 'decrease latency for your applications that have exceptionally long boot times.' A lifecycle hook on the autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING action holds each instance in a Warmed:Pending:Wait state while the application finishes the S3 download/processing; the app calls complete-lifecycle-action only when ready, so the prepared instance (with processed data already on its EBS volume) is parked in the warm pool. The qualifier MOST cost-effective decides between A (Stopped) and C (Running): AWS docs state that keeping warm-pool instances in the Stopped state is 'an effective way to minimize costs' (you pay only for EBS volumes and any Elastic IPs), whereas keeping them Running is 'highly discouraged to avoid incurring unnecessary charges.' Therefore A is correct.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式啟動時間長，因為每個新執行個體必須先下載並處理不斷增長的 S3 資料才能開始服務請求。這正是 EC2 Auto Scaling warm pool 的典型使用情境：warm pool 在 Auto Scaling group 旁維護預先初始化的執行個體，在 scale-out 時可快速 warm-start。AWS 文件將 warm pool 描述為『為啟動時間異常長的應用程式降低延遲』的方法。在 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCHING 動作上設定的生命週期掛鉤會讓執行個體進入 Warmed:Pending:Wait 等待狀態，直到應用程式完成 S3 下載與處理；應用程式只在就緒時呼叫 complete-lifecycle-action，這樣處理好的執行個體（資料已存在於 EBS 磁碟區）便會停放在 warm pool 中。題目限定詞 MOST cost-effective 決定 A (Stopped) 與 C (Running) 何者正確：AWS 文件指出將 warm pool 執行個體保持在 Stopped 狀態是『將成本降到最低的有效方法』（只需支付 EBS 磁碟區與 Elastic IP 費用），而保持 Running 則『強烈不建議，以避免產生不必要的費用』。因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Increasing the maximum instance count does nothing to reduce per-instance startup time; new instances still must download and process the S3 data from scratch. The lifecycle hook only delays the instance from going InService, it does not pre-warm anything. Without a warm pool there is no improvement to readiness latency.","why_zh":"提高最大執行個體數量無法縮短單一執行個體的啟動時間；新執行個體仍須從頭下載並處理 S3 資料。生命週期掛鉤僅延後執行個體進入 InService，並不會預先暖機。沒有 warm pool 就無法改善就緒延遲。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A warm pool in the Running state does technically reduce startup latency, but it is NOT the most cost-effective option. AWS docs explicitly say keeping warm-pool instances Running is 'highly discouraged to avoid incurring unnecessary charges' because you pay the full instance cost while idle. The Stopped state (A) achieves the same latency benefit at far lower cost, so A beats C on the MOST cost-effective qualifier.","why_zh":"Running 狀態的 warm pool 技術上確實能降低啟動延遲，但並非最具成本效益的選項。AWS 文件明確指出將 warm pool 執行個體保持 Running『強烈不建議，以避免產生不必要的費用』，因為閒置時仍需支付完整執行個體費用。Stopped 狀態 (A) 能以遠低的成本達到相同的延遲改善，因此在 MOST cost-effective 限定詞下 A 勝過 C。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Increasing max instance count provides no pre-warming benefit (same flaw as B). Additionally, placing the instance in the Standby state takes it out of service so it does not serve requests and does not count toward InService capacity, which is the opposite of the goal of making instances ready to serve traffic faster. Standby is intended for maintenance/troubleshooting, not for accelerating readiness.","why_zh":"提高最大執行個體數量無預先暖機效益（與 B 相同缺陷）。此外，將執行個體置於 Standby 狀態會使其離開服務、不處理請求，也不計入 InService 容量，與『讓執行個體更快就緒以服務流量』的目標相反。Standby 是用於維護/排錯，並非加速就緒。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-warm-pools.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/warm-pool-instance-lifecycle.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/create-warm-pool.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/lifecycle-hooks.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":74,"question_en":"A company is using an AWS CodeBuild project to build and package an application. The packages are copied to a shared Amazon S3 bucket before being deployed across multiple AWS accounts. The buildspec.yml file contains the following: The DevOps engineer has noticed that anybody with an AWS account is able to download the artifacts. What steps should the DevOps engineer take to stop this?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建和打包应用程序。这些包在部署到多个 AWS 账户之 前会被复制到一个共享的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 buildspec.yml 文件包含以下内容： DevOps 工程师注意到，任何拥有 AWS 账户的人都能够下载这些工件。 DevOps 工程师应该采取哪些措施来阻止这种情况？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the post_build command to use --acl public-read and configure a bucket policy that grants read access to the relevant AWS accounts only.","B":"Configure a default ACL for the S3 bucket that defines the set of authenticated users as the relevant AWS accounts only and grants read-only access.","C":"Create an S3 bucket policy that grants read access to the relevant AWS accounts and denies read access to the principal “*”.","D":"Modify the post_build command to remove --acl authenticated-read and configure a bucket policy that allows read access to the relevant AWS accounts only."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 post_build 命令以使用 --acl public-read，并配置一个仅授予相关 AWS 账户读取权限的存储桶 策略。","B":"为 S3 存储桶配置默认访问控制列表（ACL），将经过身份验证的用户定义为仅相关 AWS 账户， 并授予只读访问权限。","C":"创建一个 S3 存储桶策略，授予相关 AWS 账户读取权限，并拒绝“*”主体的读取权限。","D":"修改 post_build 命令以移除 --acl authenticated-read，并配置一个仅允许相关 AWS 账户读取访问权限的存 储桶策略。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The symptom 'anybody with an AWS account can download the artifacts' is the precise signature of the S3 'authenticated-read' canned ACL. Per the S3 ACL overview, granting access to the AuthenticatedUsers predefined group 'represents all AWS accounts' and 'allows any AWS authenticated user in the world' to access the resource (requests must be signed, but the grant is global). The authenticated-read canned ACL grants exactly READ to that group, so the buildspec post_build must be running 'aws s3 cp ... --acl authenticated-read'. The correct fix is to remove that over-broad ACL grant and instead scope access with a bucket policy that allows read only to the relevant AWS accounts, which is also AWS's recommended pattern (use policies, keep ACLs disabled). That is option D. Option C is the trap: per IAM policy evaluation logic, an explicit Deny always overrides any Allow, and a Deny on Principal '*' also matches the relevant accounts, so it would deny the very accounts you intend to allow and break the cross-account deployment, while never removing the offending ACL.","explanation_zh":"症狀「任何擁有 AWS 帳戶的人都能下載成品」正是 S3 'authenticated-read' canned ACL 的典型特徵。根據 S3 ACL overview 文件，授權給 AuthenticatedUsers 預定義群組『代表所有 AWS 帳戶』，會『允許世界上任何已驗證的 AWS 使用者』存取資源（請求需簽署，但授權範圍是全球性的）。authenticated-read canned ACL 正是把 READ 權限授予該群組，因此 buildspec 的 post_build 必定執行了 'aws s3 cp ... --acl authenticated-read'。正確修法是移除這個過於寬鬆的 ACL 授權，改用 bucket policy 只允許相關 AWS 帳戶讀取，這也是 AWS 建議的做法（用 policy、停用 ACL）。這正是選項 D。選項 C 是陷阱：根據 IAM policy evaluation logic，明確的 Deny 永遠覆蓋任何 Allow，而對 Principal '*' 的 Deny 也會比對到相關帳戶，因此會連你想允許的帳戶都一併拒絕，破壞跨帳戶部署，且未移除真正根因的 ACL。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"--acl public-read maps to the AllUsers group, which grants access to ANYONE in the world including anonymous/unauthenticated callers. This makes the exposure strictly worse, not better, and a bucket policy Allow cannot retract the open ACL grant already applied to the object.","why_zh":"--acl public-read 對應 AllUsers 群組，會授權給世界上任何人，甚至包含匿名未驗證的呼叫者。這只會讓暴露更嚴重，而 bucket policy 的 Allow 也無法收回已套用在物件上的開放 ACL 授權。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"You cannot redefine the AuthenticatedUsers ACL group to mean 'only the relevant accounts'; that predefined group always means ALL AWS accounts. There is no 'default ACL' construct that defines a custom set of authenticated users, so this would not restrict access; AWS also recommends policies over ACLs.","why_zh":"無法把 AuthenticatedUsers ACL 群組重新定義為『只有相關帳戶』；該預定義群組永遠代表所有 AWS 帳戶。也不存在能定義自訂已驗證使用者集合的『預設 ACL』機制，因此無法限制存取；AWS 也建議改用 policy 而非 ACL。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Per IAM policy evaluation logic, an explicit Deny overrides every Allow (explicit deny always wins). A Deny on Principal '*' also matches the relevant accounts you Allow, so those accounts are denied and the legitimate cross-account deployment breaks. It also leaves the root-cause authenticated-read ACL grant on the objects.","why_zh":"根據 IAM policy evaluation logic，明確的 Deny 會覆蓋所有 Allow（明確拒絕永遠勝出）。對 Principal '*' 的 Deny 也會比對到你 Allow 的相關帳戶，因此這些帳戶會被拒絕，破壞合法的跨帳戶部署。同時也未移除物件上真正根因的 authenticated-read ACL 授權。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/acl-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/canned-acl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-bucket-policies.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":75,"question_en":"A company has developed a serverless web application that is hosted on AWS. The application consists of Amazon S3. Amazon API Gateway, several AWS Lambda functions, and an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. The company is using AWS CodeCommit to store the source code. The source code is a combination of AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) templates and Python code. A security audit and penetration test reveal that user names and passwords for authentication to the database are hardcoded within CodeCommit repositories. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution to automatically detect and prevent hardcoded secrets. What is the MOST secure solution that meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一个无服务器的网络应用程序，该应用程序托管在 AWS 上。此应用程序由 Amazon S3、 Amazon API Gateway、若干 AWS Lambda 函数以及一个 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库组成。该公司使用 AWS CodeCommit 来存储源代码。源代码由 AWS 无服务器应用程序模型（AWS SAM）模板和 Python 代码 组合而成。 安全审计和渗透测试显示，用于数据库身份验证的用户名和密码被硬编码在 CodeCommit 存储库中。 DevOps 工程师必须实施解决方案，以自动检测并防止硬编码的机密信息。 满足这些要求的最安全的解决方案是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon CodeGuru Profiler. Decorate the handler function with @with_lambda_profiler(). Manually review the recommendation report. Write the secret to AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as a secure string. Update the SAM templates and the Python code to pull the secret from Parameter Store.","B":"Associate the CodeCommit repository with Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer. Manually check the code review for any recommendations. Choose the option to protect the secret. Update the SAM templates and the Python code to pull the secret from AWS Secrets Manager.","C":"Enable Amazon CodeGuru Profiler. Decorate the handler function with @with_lambda_profiler(). Manually review the recommendation report. Choose the option to protect the secret. Update the SAM templates and the Python code to pull the secret from AWS Secrets Manager.","D":"Associate the CodeCommit repository with Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer. Manually check the code review for any recommendations. Write the secret to AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store as a string. Update the SAM templates and the Python code to pull the secret from Parameter Store."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 Amazon CodeGuru Profiler。使用 @with_lambda_profiler（） 装饰处理函数。手动审查建议报告。 将密钥作为安全字符串写入 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储。更新 SAM 模板和 Python 代码以从参 数存储中提取密钥。","B":"将 CodeCommit 存储库与 Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 关联。手动检查代码审查中的任何建议。选择保 护机密的选项。更新 SAM 模板和 Python 代码以从 AWS Secrets Manager 中获取机密。","C":"启用 Amazon CodeGuru Profiler。使用 @with_lambda_profiler（） 装饰处理函数。手动审查建议报告。选 择保护密钥的选项。更新 SAM 模板和 Python 代码，从 AWS Secrets Manager 中获取密钥。","D":"将 CodeCommit 存储库与 Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 关联。手动检查代码审查中的任何建议。将密 钥作为字符串写入 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储。更新 SAM 模板和 Python 代码以从参数存储中 获取密钥。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer is the AWS service whose secrets detector automatically scans Java and Python repositories (including AWS CodeCommit) for hardcoded usernames, passwords, database connection strings, RSA keys, and more. Per the AWS docs, when an unprotected secret is found, CodeGuru Reviewer generates a recommendation with a 'Protect your credential' option that opens the AWS Secrets Manager console to protect and manage the secret; there is even a dedicated 'Move hardcoded database credentials to AWS Secrets Manager' workflow that fits the RDS for MySQL password exactly. Secrets Manager is the MOST secure target because it provides encryption, fine-grained IAM access control, CloudTrail audit logging, and automatic rotation of credentials. Option B associates the CodeCommit repo with CodeGuru Reviewer, uses the protect-the-secret recommendation, and pulls the secret from Secrets Manager, which matches the documented workflow precisely. Options A and C are wrong because Amazon CodeGuru Profiler (the @with_lambda_profiler() decorator) only collects runtime performance data to find CPU bottlenecks and cannot detect hardcoded secrets at all. Option D uses the correct detector but stores the secret as a plaintext string in Parameter Store (not encrypted, no rotation), so it is less secure than B and fails the 'MOST secure' qualifier.","explanation_zh":"Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 是 AWS 中具備 secrets detector 的服務，能自動掃描 Java 與 Python 的程式碼儲存庫（包含 AWS CodeCommit），偵測硬編碼的使用者名稱、密碼、資料庫連線字串、RSA 金鑰等。根據 AWS 文件，當發現未受保護的祕密時，CodeGuru Reviewer 會產生建議並提供 'Protect your credential' 選項，按下後會開啟 AWS Secrets Manager 主控台來保護與管理該祕密；文件中甚至有專門的 'Move hardcoded database credentials to AWS Secrets Manager' 流程，完全符合本題 RDS for MySQL 密碼的情境。Secrets Manager 是最安全的目標，因為它提供加密、細緻的 IAM 存取控制、CloudTrail 稽核紀錄，以及自動輪換認證的能力。選項 B 將 CodeCommit 儲存庫關聯到 CodeGuru Reviewer、使用保護祕密的建議，並從 Secrets Manager 取得祕密，正好符合官方流程。選項 A 與 C 錯誤，因為 Amazon CodeGuru Profiler（@with_lambda_profiler() 裝飾器）僅收集執行期效能資料以找出 CPU 瓶頸，完全無法偵測硬編碼祕密。選項 D 雖然用對偵測器，但把祕密以純文字 string 寫入 Parameter Store（未加密、無輪換），安全性低於 B，不符合 'MOST secure' 的要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon CodeGuru Profiler (the @with_lambda_profiler() decorator) only collects runtime performance/CPU and heap profiling data; it cannot detect hardcoded secrets in source code. It also writes to Parameter Store, which lacks built-in automatic rotation. Wrong detection tool and weaker storage target.","why_zh":"Amazon CodeGuru Profiler（@with_lambda_profiler() 裝飾器）只收集執行期效能/CPU 與堆積分析資料，無法偵測原始碼中的硬編碼祕密。且寫入 Parameter Store 缺乏內建自動輪換。偵測工具錯誤且儲存目標較弱。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same fundamental error as A: CodeGuru Profiler performs performance profiling, not secrets detection, so it cannot find the hardcoded credentials. The 'Protect your credential' option and Secrets Manager integration belong to CodeGuru Reviewer, not Profiler, making this workflow technically impossible.","why_zh":"與 A 有相同的根本錯誤：CodeGuru Profiler 進行效能分析而非祕密偵測，無法找到硬編碼認證。'Protect your credential' 選項與 Secrets Manager 整合屬於 CodeGuru Reviewer 而非 Profiler，因此此流程在技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Correctly uses CodeGuru Reviewer to detect secrets, but stores the credential as a plaintext string in Parameter Store (not even a SecureString) with no encryption and no automatic rotation. The documented protect-secret workflow targets Secrets Manager, and the question asks for the MOST secure solution, so B is better.","why_zh":"正確使用 CodeGuru Reviewer 偵測祕密，但把認證以純文字 string 寫入 Parameter Store（甚至不是 SecureString），未加密且無自動輪換。官方保護祕密流程指向 Secrets Manager，而題目要求最安全的方案，故 B 較佳。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/integrating-codeguru.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeguru/latest/reviewer-ug/recommendations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeguru/latest/reviewer-ug/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeguru/latest/profiler-ug/what-is-codeguru-profiler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":76,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon S3 buckets to store important documents. The company discovers that some S3 buckets are not encrypted. Currently, the company’s IAM users can create new S3 buckets without encryption. The company is implementing a new requirement that all S3 buckets must be encrypted. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution to ensure that server-side encryption is enabled on all existing S3 buckets and all new S3 buckets. The encryption must be enabled on new S3 buckets as soon as the S3 buckets are created. The default encryption type must be 256-bit Advanced Encryption Standard (AES-256). Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊 S3 存储桶来存储重要文件。该公司发现有些 S3 存储桶未加密。目前，该公司的 IAM 用户可以创建未加密的新 S3 存储桶。该公司正在实施一项新要求，即所有 S3 存储桶都必须加密。 DevOps 工程师必须实施一项解决方案，以确保所有现有的 S3 存储桶以及所有新创建的 S3 存储桶都启用服 务器端加密。新创建的 S3 存储桶必须在创建时立即启用加密。默认加密类型必须为 256 位高级加密标准 （AES-256）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked periodically by an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule. Program the Lambda function to scan all current S3 buckets for encryption status and to set AES- 256 as the default encryption for any S3 bucket that does not have an encryption configuration.","B":"Set up and activate the s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled AWS Config managed rule. Configure the rule to use the AWS-EnableS3BucketEncryption AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook as the remediation action. Manually run the re-evaluation process to ensure that existing S3 buckets are compliant.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by an Amazon EventBridge event rule. Define the rule with an event pattern that matches the creation of new S3 buckets. Program the Lambda function to parse the EventBridge event, check the configuration of the S3 buckets from the event, and set AES- 256 as the default encryption.","D":"Configure an IAM policy that denies the s3:CreateBucket action if the s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption condition key has a value that is not AES-256. Create an IAM group for all the company’s IAM users. Associate the IAM policy with the IAM group."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数由 Amazon EventBridge 定期调度规则周期性调用。编写该 Lambda 函数，使其扫描所有当前的 S3 存储桶以检查加密状态，并将任何未配置加密的 S3 存储桶的默认加密 方式设置为 AES-256。","B":"设置并激活 s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled AWS Config 管理规则。将规则配置为使用 AWS- EnableS3BucketEncryption AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册作为修复操作。手动运行重新 评估流程，以确保现有 S3 存储桶符合要求。","C":"创建一个由 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则触发的 AWS Lambda 函数。定义该规则 使用与创建新的 S3 存储桶相匹配的事件模式。编写 Lambda 函数来解析 EventBridge 事件，从事 件中检查 S3 存储桶的配置，并将 AES-256 设置为默认加密方式。","D":"配置一个 IAM 策略，如果 s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption 条件键的值不是 AES-256，则拒绝 s3: CreateBucket 操作。为公司所有的 IAM 用户创建一个 IAM 组。将 IAM 策略与 IAM 组关联。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Option B is correct. The AWS Config managed rule s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled checks whether each S3 bucket has Amazon S3 default encryption enabled (AES-256 or AWS KMS) and is NON_COMPLIANT if the bucket is not encrypted by default. Its trigger type is 'Configuration changes', so it evaluates new buckets as soon as they are created, and a manual re-evaluation covers the existing fleet. Attaching the AWS-EnableS3BucketEncryption SSM Automation runbook as the remediation action configures default encryption with the SSEAlgorithm parameter defaulting to AES256, fixing both existing and new noncompliant buckets near-immediately. This satisfies all three requirements: existing buckets, new buckets at creation time, and AES-256 default encryption. The dump's suggested answer D is technically wrong: s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption is an object-operation condition key (used with s3:PutObject to require encryption on uploads) and is not a condition key for s3:CreateBucket per the Service Authorization Reference, so the Deny would not enforce bucket-level default encryption; it also does nothing for already-existing unencrypted buckets and never sets default encryption.","explanation_zh":"正確答案為 B。AWS Config 受管規則 s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled 會檢查每個 S3 bucket 是否已啟用 Amazon S3 預設加密（AES-256 或 AWS KMS），若 bucket 未預設加密則標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。其觸發類型為「Configuration changes」，因此新建立的 bucket 一經建立即會被評估，再透過手動重新評估即可涵蓋既有的 bucket。將 AWS-EnableS3BucketEncryption SSM Automation runbook 設為補救動作，其 SSEAlgorithm 參數預設為 AES256，可近乎即時修復既有與新建的不合規 bucket。此方案同時滿足三項需求：既有 bucket、建立時即加密的新 bucket、以及 AES-256 預設加密。題庫建議答案 D 在技術上是錯誤的：依 Service Authorization Reference，s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption 是物件操作條件鍵（用於 s3:PutObject 以要求上傳物件加密），並非 s3:CreateBucket 的條件鍵，因此該 Deny 無法強制 bucket 層級的預設加密；它也無法處理既有未加密的 bucket，更不會設定預設加密。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A periodic EventBridge scheduled rule only scans existing buckets at intervals and does not enable encryption on new buckets 'as soon as' they are created; there is a delay until the next scheduled run, violating the immediacy requirement. It is also more operational overhead (custom Lambda code) than the managed Config rule plus runbook.","why_zh":"週期性 EventBridge 排程規則僅按間隔掃描既有 bucket，無法在新 bucket「一建立即」啟用加密；直到下一次排程執行前都有延遲，違反即時性要求。相較受管 Config 規則加 runbook，還需自寫 Lambda（營運負擔更高）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An EventBridge event rule matching bucket creation handles only NEW buckets and does nothing for the existing unencrypted buckets, which is an explicit requirement. It also requires custom Lambda code (more overhead) versus the managed solution.","why_zh":"比對 bucket 建立事件的 EventBridge 規則只處理「新」bucket，對既有未加密的 bucket 毫無作用，而那是明確需求之一。同時需自寫 Lambda 程式（負擔更高），不如受管方案。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption is an object-operation (s3:PutObject) condition key, not a valid condition key for s3:CreateBucket per the Service Authorization Reference, so the Deny does not enforce bucket default encryption. It also never remediates existing unencrypted buckets and never sets AES-256 default encryption on any bucket. (This is the dump's suggested answer, but it is incorrect.)","why_zh":"依 Service Authorization Reference，s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption 是物件操作（s3:PutObject）的條件鍵，並非 s3:CreateBucket 的有效條件鍵，故該 Deny 無法強制 bucket 預設加密。它也完全不會修復既有未加密的 bucket，更不會為任何 bucket 設定 AES-256 預設加密。（此為題庫建議答案，但屬錯誤。）"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-aws-enableS3bucketencryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/amazon-s3-policy-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/service-authorization/latest/reference/list_amazons3.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":77,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is architecting a continuous development strategy for a company’s software as a service (SaaS) web application running on AWS. For application and security reasons, users subscribing to this application are distributed across multiple Application Load Balancers (ALBs), each of which has a dedicated Auto Scaling group and fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. The application does not require a build stage, and when it is committed to AWS CodeCommit, the application must trigger a simultaneous deployment to all ALBs, Auto Scaling groups, and EC2 fleets. Which architecture will meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of configuration?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在为一家公司运行在 AWS 上的软件即服务（SaaS）网络应用程序设计持续开发 策略。出于应用程序和安全方面的考虑，订阅该应用程序的用户分布在多个应用负载均衡器（ALB）上， 每个 ALB 都有一个专用的自动扩展组和一组亚马逊 EC2 实例。该应用程序无需构建阶段，当提交到 AWS CodeCommit 时，必须同时触发对所有 ALB、自动扩展组和 EC2 实例群的部署。 哪种架构能够以最少的配置满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a single AWS CodePipeline pipeline that deploys the application in parallel using unique AWS CodeDeploy applications and deployment groups created for each ALB-Auto Scaling group pair.","B":"Create a single AWS CodePipeline pipeline that deploys the application using a single AWS CodeDeploy application and single deployment group.","C":"Create a single AWS CodePipeline pipeline that deploys the application in parallel using a single AWS CodeDeploy application and unique deployment group for each ALB-Auto Scaling group pair.","D":"Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline for each ALB-Auto Scaling group pair that deploys the application using an AWS CodeDeploy application and deployment group created for the same ALB- Auto Scaling group pair."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个单一的 AWS CodePipeline 管道，使用为每个 ALB - Auto Scaling 组对创建的独特的 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序和部署组并行部署应用程序。","B":"创建一个单一的 AWS CodePipeline 管道，使用一个单一的 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序和 一个单一的部署组来部署应用程序。","C":"创建一个单一的 AWS CodePipeline 管道，使用单个 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序并为每个 ALB - Auto Scaling 组对创建独特的部署组来并行部署应用程序。","D":"为每个 ALB - 自动扩展组对创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，使用为同一 ALB - 自动扩展组对创 建的 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序和部署组来部署应用程序。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A CodeDeploy application is just a container that ensures the correct combination of revision, deployment configuration, and deployment group is used; the actual deployment target (the Auto Scaling group(s) plus the associated ALB/target group) is defined at the deployment-group level. Because each ALB-Auto Scaling group pair is a distinct ASG fronted by its own ALB and is kept separate for application and security reasons, mapping one deployment group to each pair is the natural targeting model. A single CodePipeline with one CodeCommit source action and one Deploy stage containing N CodeDeploy deploy actions set to the same runOrder fires those actions in parallel from the single commit, producing the required simultaneous deployment to every pair. Option C does this with the fewest resources: one pipeline, one CodeDeploy application, and one deployment group per pair. Option A is functionally identical but wastefully creates a separate CodeDeploy application per pair, and option D creates an entire pipeline per pair, so C is the LEAST configuration.","explanation_zh":"CodeDeploy application 只是一個容器，用來確保部署時使用正確的 revision、deployment configuration 與 deployment group 組合；真正的部署目標（Auto Scaling group 以及關聯的 ALB/target group）是在 deployment group 層級定義的。由於每個 ALB-Auto Scaling group 組合都是各自有獨立 ALB 的不同 ASG，且基於應用與安全因素彼此分離，將每個組合對應到一個 deployment group 是最自然的目標模型。一條 CodePipeline，包含一個 CodeCommit source action，以及一個 Deploy stage（其中含 N 個設定相同 runOrder 的 CodeDeploy deploy action），即可在單次提交時平行觸發這些 action，達成對所有組合同時部署的需求。選項 C 以最少資源完成：一條 pipeline、一個 CodeDeploy application、每組一個 deployment group。選項 A 功能相同但多餘地為每組各建立一個 CodeDeploy application；選項 D 為每組各建立一整條 pipeline，因此 C 才是最少設定。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Functionally works (one pipeline, parallel deploy actions, one deployment group per pair), but it needlessly creates a separate CodeDeploy application for every ALB-ASG pair. Since a single application can contain all the deployment groups, the extra applications add configuration without benefit, so A is not the LEAST configuration.","why_zh":"功能上可行（一條 pipeline、平行 deploy action、每組一個 deployment group），但多餘地為每個 ALB-ASG 組合各建立一個獨立的 CodeDeploy application。由於單一 application 即可容納所有 deployment group，多出的 application 只增加設定卻無益處，因此 A 並非最少設定。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A single deployment group does not align with the architecture: each ALB-ASG pair is deliberately separated for application and security reasons, so collapsing all distinct ASGs and their ALBs/target groups into one deployment group removes the per-pair isolation and the independent per-pair deployment/health control the design calls for. It treats unrelated fleets as one logical unit, so it does not properly meet the requirement.","why_zh":"單一 deployment group 不符合此架構：每個 ALB-ASG 組合是基於應用與安全因素刻意分離的，將所有不同的 ASG 及其 ALB/target group 併入單一 deployment group，會喪失各組合之間的隔離以及各自獨立的部署/健康控制。它把不相關的 fleet 當成同一個邏輯單位，因此無法正確滿足需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating one entire pipeline per ALB-ASG pair works but is the MOST configuration: N pipelines, N source actions, and N separate CodeCommit triggers to maintain, each duplicating the same source-and-deploy wiring. The question explicitly asks for the LEAST configuration, so D is wrong.","why_zh":"為每個 ALB-ASG 組合各建立一整條 pipeline 雖可行，但設定量最多：要維護 N 條 pipeline、N 個 source action 與 N 個獨立的 CodeCommit 觸發，每條都重複相同的 source 與 deploy 配線。題目明確要求最少設定，因此 D 錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/primary-components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-create-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-requirements.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/reference-pipeline-structure.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":78,"question_en":"A company is hosting a static website from an Amazon S3 bucket. The website is available to customers at example.com. The company uses an Amazon Route 53 weighted routing policy with a TTL of 1 day. The company has decided to replace the existing static website with a dynamic web application. The dynamic web application uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances. On the day of production launch to customers, the company creates an additional Route 53 weighted DNS record entry that points to the ALB with a weight of 255 and a TTL of 1 hour. Two days later, a DevOps engineer notices that the previous static website is displayed sometimes when customers navigate to example.com. How can the DevOps engineer ensure that the company serves only dynamic content for example.com?","question_zh":"一家公司正在通过 Amazon S3 存储桶托管一个静态网站，该网站可通过 example.com 访问。该公司使用 了 Amazon Route 53 的加权路由策略，其 TTL 为 1 天。该公司决定用一个动态网络应用程序取代现有的 静态网站。该动态网络应用程序在一组 Amazon EC2 实例前使用了应用负载均衡器（ALB）。 在向客户推出产品的当天，该公司创建了一个额外的 Route 53 加权 DNS 记录条目，该条目指向 ALB， 权重为 255，TTL 为 1 小时。两天后，一位 DevOps 工程师注意到，当客户访问 example.com 时，有时 会显示之前的静态网站。 DevOps 工程师如何确保公司只为 example.com 提供动态内容？","options_en":{"A":"Delete all objects, including previous versions, from the S3 bucket that contains the static website content.","B":"Update the weighted DNS record entry that points to the S3 bucket. Apply a weight of 0. Specify the domain reset option to propagate changes immediately.","C":"Configure webpage redirect requests on the S3 bucket with a hostname that redirects to the ALB.","D":"Remove the weighted DNS record entry that points to the S3 bucket from the example.com hosted zone. Wait for DNS propagation to become complete."},"options_zh":{"A":"从包含静态网站内容的 S3 存储桶中删除所有对象，包括其先前版本。","B":"更新指向 S3 存储桶的加权 DNS 记录条目。将权重设置为 0。选择立即传播更改的域名重置选项。","C":"在 S3 存储桶上配置网页重定向请求，使用可重定向到应用负载均衡器（ALB）的主机名。","D":"从 example.com 托管区域中删除指向 S3 存储桶的加权 DNS 记录条目。等待 DNS 传播完成。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The old static website keeps appearing because the original Amazon Route 53 weighted record that points to the S3 bucket still exists in the example.com hosted zone with a non-zero weight. With weighted routing, Route 53 answers queries for a name/type group in proportion to each record's weight divided by the sum of all weights, so as long as the S3 record retains a non-zero weight it continues to receive a share of queries. Because two days have already passed (well beyond the records' TTLs), the intermittent behavior is caused by both records being live and answering, not merely by stale caching. Removing the S3 weighted record from the hosted zone leaves the ALB record as the only answer for example.com, so Route 53 serves only the dynamic content; you then wait for DNS propagation so any resolver that cached the old S3 answer expires it per the TTL. Option B is a trap: although setting a record's weight to 0 is a documented way to stop sending traffic to it, the option fabricates a non-existent 'domain reset option to propagate changes immediately' — Route 53 has no such feature, and DNS changes cannot be forced to propagate instantly because resolvers honor the TTL. Therefore D is the only complete and technically accurate answer.","explanation_zh":"舊的靜態網站仍然間歇性出現，是因為原本指向 S3 bucket 的 Amazon Route 53 weighted record 仍存在於 example.com hosted zone 中，且權重不為 0。在 weighted routing 中，Route 53 會依照「該 record 的 weight ÷ 同名同型別群組所有 record 權重總和」的比例回應查詢，因此只要 S3 record 的權重不為 0，它就會持續接收一部分查詢流量。由於距離上線已過了兩天（遠超過 record 的 TTL），間歇性問題的根因是兩筆 record 都還在運作並回應，而非僅是快取過期。將指向 S3 的 weighted record 從 hosted zone 移除後，ALB 的 record 就成為 example.com 唯一的回應，Route 53 便只會提供動態內容；接著等待 DNS propagation 完成，讓任何快取了舊 S3 回應的 resolver 依其 TTL 過期。選項 B 是陷阱：雖然把 record 的 weight 設為 0 確實是停止導流的合法做法，但該選項杜撰了不存在的『domain reset option to propagate changes immediately』——Route 53 並無此功能，且 DNS 變更無法被強制立即傳播，因為 resolver 會遵循 TTL。因此 D 是唯一完整且技術正確的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deleting all objects (including previous versions) from the S3 bucket does not change DNS routing. Route 53 would still send a proportional share of queries to the S3 website endpoint based on the weighted record, and customers hitting it would now receive errors (such as 404/NoSuchKey) instead of dynamic content. This addresses the content, not the routing problem.","why_zh":"刪除 S3 bucket 中所有物件（含先前版本）並不會改變 DNS 路由。Route 53 仍會依 weighted record 的比例把部分查詢導向 S3 網站端點，命中該端點的客戶反而會收到錯誤（例如 404/NoSuchKey），而非動態內容。這只處理了內容，沒有處理路由問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Setting the S3 record's weight to 0 is itself a documented way to stop sending traffic to a resource, but this option fabricates a 'domain reset option to propagate changes immediately' that does not exist in Route 53. DNS changes cannot be forced to propagate instantly because recursive resolvers cache answers until the TTL expires; the invented mechanism makes the option technically invalid as written.","why_zh":"把 S3 record 的 weight 設為 0 本身確實是停止導流的合法做法，但此選項杜撰了 Route 53 並不存在的『domain reset option to propagate changes immediately』。DNS 變更無法被強制立即傳播，因為遞迴 resolver 會快取答案直到 TTL 過期；這個虛構的機制使該選項在描述上技術錯誤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Configuring an S3 webpage redirect to the ALB keeps the S3 weighted record live and merely layers a redirect on top, so requests still resolve to S3 first before being redirected. This does not make Route 53 serve only dynamic content for example.com and leaves the dual-record routing problem unresolved.","why_zh":"在 S3 上設定重新導向到 ALB 會讓 S3 weighted record 持續存在，只是再疊加一層重新導向，請求仍會先解析到 S3 再被導走。這並不能讓 Route 53 對 example.com 只提供動態內容，雙 record 的路由問題依然存在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-weighted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/resource-record-sets-values-weighted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/troubleshooting-new-dns-settings-not-in-effect.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":79,"question_en":"A company is implementing AWS CodePipeline to automate its testing process. The company wants to be notified when the execution state fails and used the following custom event pattern in Amazon EventBridge: Which type of events will match this event pattern?","question_zh":"一家公司正在实施 AWS CodePipeline 来自动化其测试流程。该公司希望在执行状态失败时收到通知，并在 Amazon EventBridge 中使用了以下自定义事件模式： 哪种类型的事件会匹配此事件模式？","options_en":{"A":"Failed deploy and build actions across all the pipelines","B":"All rejected or failed approval actions across all the pipelines","C":"All the events across all pipelines","D":"Approval actions across all the pipelines"},"options_zh":{"A":"所有管道中的部署和构建操作均失败","B":"所有流水线中所有被拒绝或审批未通过的操作","C":"所有管道中的所有事件","D":"所有流水线中的审批操作"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The four options are verbatim copies of the descriptive captions AWS gives its sample CodePipeline EventBridge event patterns in 'Monitoring CodePipeline events' (the 'Create a Rule That Sends a Notification on a Pipeline Event' section). The pattern in this question filters source=aws.codepipeline, detail-type='CodePipeline Action Execution State Change', detail.state=['FAILED'], and detail.type.category=['Approval']. AWS documents this exact pattern with the caption: 'Use this sample event pattern to capture all rejected or failed approval actions across all the pipelines.' This is option B word for word. AWS's Detail types table further explains that for action-level events, the FAILED state for an approval action 'means the action was either rejected by the reviewer or failed due to an incorrect action configuration,' which is precisely why a state=FAILED + category=Approval filter captures both rejected and failed approvals. Option D is excluded because the explicit state=['FAILED'] restriction means it does NOT match all approval actions (STARTED/SUCCEEDED approvals are filtered out).","explanation_zh":"四個選項逐字對應 AWS 'Monitoring CodePipeline events' 文件中（'Create a Rule That Sends a Notification on a Pipeline Event' 章節）各範例 EventBridge event pattern 的描述文字。本題的 pattern 篩選 source=aws.codepipeline、detail-type='CodePipeline Action Execution State Change'、detail.state=['FAILED']、detail.type.category=['Approval']。AWS 文件對此 pattern 的描述正是：'Use this sample event pattern to capture all rejected or failed approval actions across all the pipelines.'，逐字對應選項 B。AWS 的 Detail types 表格進一步說明：對 action-level 事件而言，approval action 的 FAILED 狀態代表該動作被審核者拒絕（rejected）或因設定錯誤而失敗（failed），這正是為何 state=FAILED + category=Approval 能同時捕捉被拒絕與失敗的審核。選項 D 不正確，因為 pattern 明確限定 state=['FAILED']，並非比對所有審核動作（STARTED/SUCCEEDED 的審核會被排除）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This is the caption for a different AWS sample pattern in the same section: state=['FAILED'] with type.category=['Deploy','Build'] — 'capture failed deploy and build actions across all the pipelines.' The pattern in this question uses category=['Approval'], not Deploy/Build, so this does not match.","why_zh":"這是同一章節中另一個 AWS 範例 pattern 的描述：state=['FAILED'] 搭配 type.category=['Deploy','Build']，即 'capture failed deploy and build actions across all the pipelines.'。本題 pattern 使用 category=['Approval'] 而非 Deploy/Build，故不符。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"'All the events across all pipelines' corresponds to the AWS sample pattern that lists all three detail-types (Pipeline/Stage/Action Execution State Change) with no state restriction. The pattern here is scoped to a single detail-type and to state=FAILED + category=Approval, so it captures only one specific event type, not all events.","why_zh":"'所有 pipeline 的所有事件' 對應的是列出三種 detail-type（Pipeline/Stage/Action Execution State Change）且不限定 state 的範例 pattern。本題 pattern 僅限單一 detail-type 並限定 state=FAILED + category=Approval，只捕捉一種特定事件，而非所有事件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"'Approval actions across all the pipelines' (without the FAILED qualifier) would be a pattern filtering only type.category=['Approval'] with no state restriction, matching approvals in any state (STARTED, SUCCEEDED, FAILED). The pattern here explicitly restricts state to ['FAILED'], so it captures specifically the rejected/failed approvals — AWS's own caption is 'all rejected or failed approval actions,' which is option B, not D.","why_zh":"'所有 pipeline 的審核動作'（無 FAILED 限定）對應的是只篩選 type.category=['Approval'] 而不限定 state 的 pattern，會比對任何狀態（STARTED、SUCCEEDED、FAILED）的審核。本題 pattern 明確限定 state=['FAILED']，因此專門捕捉被拒絕/失敗的審核——AWS 自身的描述為 'all rejected or failed approval actions'，即選項 B 而非 D。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/detect-state-changes-cloudwatch-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codepipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":80,"question_en":"An application running on a set of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group requires a configuration file to operate. The instances are created and maintained with AWS CloudFormation. A DevOps engineer wants the instances to have the latest configuration file when launched, and wants changes to the configuration file to be reflected on all the instances with a minimal delay when the CloudFormation template is updated. Company policy requires that application configuration files be maintained along with AWS infrastructure configuration files in source control. Which solution will accomplish this?","question_zh":"在一组由 AWS CloudFormation 创建和维护的 Auto Scaling 组中的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行的应用程序 需要一个配置文件才能运行。一位 DevOps 工程师希望实例在启动时拥有最新的配置文件，并且希望 在更新 CloudFormation 模板时，配置文件的更改能以最小的延迟反映到所有实例上。公司政策要求将 应用程序配置文件与 AWS 基础设施配置文件一起保存在源代码控制中。 哪种解决方案能实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"In the CloudFormation template, add an AWS Config rule. Place the configuration file content in the rule’s InputParameters property, and set the Scope property to the EC2 Auto Scaling group. Add an AWS Systems Manager Resource Data Sync resource to the template to poll for updates to the configuration.","B":"In the CloudFormation template, add an EC2 launch template resource. Place the configuration file content in the launch template. Configure the cfn-init script to run when the instance is launched, and configure the cfn-hup script to poll for updates to the configuration.","C":"In the CloudFormation template, add an EC2 launch template resource. Place the configuration file content in the launch template. Add an AWS Systems Manager Resource Data Sync resource to the template to poll for updates to the configuration.","D":"In the CloudFormation template, add CloudFormation init metadata. Place the configuration file content in the metadata. Configure the cfn-init script to run when the instance is launched, and configure the cfn-hup script to poll for updates to the configuration."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFormation 模板中添加一个 AWS Config 规则。将配置文件内容放入规则的 InputParameters 属 性中，并将 Scope 属性设置为 EC2 自动扩展组。添加一个 将 AWS Systems Manager 资源数据同步资源添加到模板中，以轮询配置更新。","B":"在 CloudFormation 模板中，添加一个 EC2 启动模板资源。将配置文件的内容放入启动模板中。配 置 cfn-init 脚本在实例启动时运行，并配置 cfn-hup 脚本轮询配置的更新。","C":"在 CloudFormation 模板中，添加一个 EC2 启动模板资源。将配置文件的内容放入启动模板中。在 模板中添加一个 AWS Systems Manager 资源数据同步资源，以轮询配置的更新。","D":"在 CloudFormation 模板中添加 CloudFormation 初始化元数据。将配置文件的内容放入元数据中。配 置 cfn-init 脚本在实例启动时运行，并配置 cfn-hup 脚本轮询配置的更新。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Option D is the canonical CloudFormation pattern for delivering and refreshing a configuration file on Auto Scaling instances. The file content is placed in the resource's AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata, which lives inside the CloudFormation template and is therefore version-controlled alongside the infrastructure code, satisfying the company policy. cfn-init reads from the AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata key at launch and writes the file to disk, so newly launched instances always get the latest version. The cfn-hup daemon detects changes in resource metadata and runs user-specified actions when a change is detected, enabling configuration updates on already-running instances via the UpdateStack API (default 15-minute poll interval, configurable lower) for minimal-delay propagation across the fleet. Options A and C use Systems Manager Resource Data Sync, which only aggregates Inventory/OpsData into an S3 bucket and never pushes config files to instances; the AWS Config rule in A only evaluates compliance. Option B is wrong because cfn-init and cfn-hup read the AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata key, not arbitrary 'configuration file content placed in the launch template' body — the launch template user data is only where cfn-init is invoked, and cfn-hup monitors resource Metadata rather than launch-template content.","explanation_zh":"選項 D 是在 Auto Scaling 執行個體上交付並更新組態檔的標準 CloudFormation 模式。組態檔內容放在資源的 AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata 中，而 metadata 位於 CloudFormation 範本內，因此會與基礎設施程式碼一起納入原始碼控管，符合公司政策。cfn-init 在啟動時從 AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata key 讀取並把檔案寫入磁碟，使新啟動的執行個體永遠取得最新版本。cfn-hup 守護程式會偵測 resource metadata 的變更，並在偵測到變更時執行使用者指定動作，透過 UpdateStack API 對執行中的執行個體套用組態更新（預設 15 分鐘輪詢間隔，可調更低），以最小延遲傳播變更。選項 A 與 C 使用 Systems Manager Resource Data Sync，它只把 Inventory/OpsData 彙整到 S3 bucket，從不把組態檔推送到執行個體；A 中的 AWS Config rule 僅評估合規性。選項 B 錯誤，因為 cfn-init 與 cfn-hup 讀取的是 AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata key，而非放在 launch template 主體中的任意「組態檔內容」——launch template user data 僅是呼叫 cfn-init 的位置，且 cfn-hup 監控的是 resource Metadata，而非 launch-template 內容。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An AWS Config rule only evaluates resource compliance and cannot deliver a configuration file to instances; its InputParameters/Scope are evaluation inputs, not file delivery. Resource Data Sync only aggregates Inventory/OpsData into S3, so it cannot refresh a config file on the fleet.","why_zh":"AWS Config rule 只評估資源合規性，無法把組態檔交付到執行個體；其 InputParameters/Scope 是評估輸入而非檔案交付。Resource Data Sync 只把 Inventory/OpsData 彙整到 S3，因此無法更新機群上的組態檔。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"cfn-init and cfn-hup read configuration from the AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata key, not from arbitrary content placed in the launch template body. The launch template user data is only where cfn-init is invoked, and cfn-hup watches resource Metadata, so placing file content in the launch template does not work with these helper scripts.","why_zh":"cfn-init 與 cfn-hup 從 AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata key 讀取組態，而非放在 launch template 主體中的任意內容。launch template user data 僅是呼叫 cfn-init 的位置，且 cfn-hup 監控 resource Metadata，因此把檔案內容放在 launch template 無法配合這些 helper 指令稿運作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Systems Manager Resource Data Sync only sends collected Inventory/OpsData to an S3 bucket for querying; it does not poll for template changes or push configuration files to running instances, so it cannot refresh the config with minimal delay.","why_zh":"Systems Manager Resource Data Sync 只把收集到的 Inventory/OpsData 送到 S3 bucket 供查詢，不會輪詢範本變更，也不會把組態檔推送到執行中的執行個體，因此無法以最小延遲更新組態。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/cfn-hup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/cfn-init.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-init.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/inventory-create-resource-data-sync.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":81,"question_en":"A company manages an application that stores logs in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The company wants to archive the logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. Logs are rarely accessed after 90 days and must be retained for 10 years. Which combination of steps should a DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司管理着一个将日志存储在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中的应用程序。该公司希望将日志归档到 Amazon S3 存储桶中。90 天后，这些日志很少被访问，但必须保留 10 年。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤的组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to use AWS Glue to transfer all logs to an S3 bucket.","B":"Configure a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to use Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose to stream all logs to an S3 bucket.","C":"Configure a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to stream all logs to an S3 bucket.","D":"Configure the S3 bucket lifecycle policy to transition logs to S3 Glacier after 90 days and to expire logs after 3,650 days.","E":"Configure the S3 bucket lifecycle policy to transition logs to Reduced Redundancy after 90 days and to expire logs after 3,650 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 CloudWatch 日志订阅筛选器，使用 AWS Glue 将所有日志传输到 S3 存储桶。","B":"配置 CloudWatch 日志订阅筛选器，使用 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 将所有日志流式传输到 S3 存储桶。","C":"配置 CloudWatch 日志订阅筛选器，将所有日志流式传输到 S3 存储桶。","D":"配置 S3 存储桶生命周期策略，将日志在 90 天后转存至 S3 Glacier，并在 3650 天后过期。","E":"配置 S3 存储桶生命周期策略，将日志在 90 天后转为低冗余存储，并在 3650 天后过期。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A CloudWatch Logs subscription filter can deliver log data only to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or Amazon OpenSearch Service. It cannot write directly to Amazon S3 (eliminating C) and cannot target AWS Glue (eliminating A). The supported, fully managed pattern to continuously archive all logs to S3 is a subscription filter that streams to Amazon Data Firehose (formerly Kinesis Data Firehose), which natively buffers and delivers the data to an S3 bucket (B). For retention and cost optimization, an S3 Lifecycle policy transitions objects to S3 Glacier after 90 days (logs are rarely accessed after that point) and expires them after 3,650 days = 10 years (D). Per the S3 Lifecycle supported-transitions documentation, S3 Standard can transition to the S3 Glacier classes, but Reduced Redundancy Storage (RRS) is a deprecated, legacy class and is NOT a valid lifecycle transition target, so E is invalid.","explanation_zh":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 只能將日誌資料傳送到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 Amazon OpenSearch Service。它無法直接寫入 Amazon S3（因此排除 C），也無法以 AWS Glue 作為目標（因此排除 A）。要持續將所有日誌封存到 S3，受支援且全代管的模式是建立一個 subscription filter，將日誌串流到 Amazon Data Firehose（前稱 Kinesis Data Firehose），它能原生地緩衝並交付資料到 S3 bucket（B）。為了保留與成本最佳化，可設定 S3 Lifecycle 政策：在 90 天後將物件轉換到 S3 Glacier（之後日誌極少被存取），並在 3,650 天（即 10 年）後使其到期刪除（D）。根據 S3 Lifecycle 支援的轉換文件，S3 Standard 可轉換到 S3 Glacier 各類別，但 Reduced Redundancy Storage（RRS）是已淘汰的舊式儲存類別，並非有效的 lifecycle 轉換目標，所以 E 無效。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudWatch Logs subscription filter cannot target AWS Glue. Its only valid destinations are Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, and Amazon OpenSearch Service. AWS Glue is an ETL/catalog service and is not a subscription-filter destination.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 無法以 AWS Glue 作為目標。其唯一有效的目的地是 Kinesis Data Streams、Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 與 Amazon OpenSearch Service。AWS Glue 是 ETL／資料目錄服務，並非 subscription filter 的目的地。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A CloudWatch Logs subscription filter cannot stream directly to an S3 bucket. S3 is not one of the supported subscription-filter destinations; an intermediary such as Amazon Data Firehose (or Lambda/Kinesis Data Streams) is required to land the data in S3.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 無法直接串流到 S3 bucket。S3 並非受支援的 subscription filter 目的地；必須透過中介服務（例如 Amazon Data Firehose，或 Lambda／Kinesis Data Streams）才能將資料寫入 S3。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Reduced Redundancy Storage (RRS) is a deprecated, legacy storage class and is not a valid S3 Lifecycle transition target. AWS no longer recommends RRS, and the supported lifecycle transitions are to Standard-IA, Intelligent-Tiering, One Zone-IA, and the Glacier classes (Instant/Flexible Retrieval, Deep Archive). It also does not satisfy the rarely-accessed archival requirement.","why_zh":"Reduced Redundancy Storage（RRS）是已淘汰的舊式儲存類別，並非有效的 S3 Lifecycle 轉換目標。AWS 已不再推薦 RRS，而受支援的 lifecycle 轉換目標為 Standard-IA、Intelligent-Tiering、One Zone-IA 以及 Glacier 各類別（Instant／Flexible Retrieval、Deep Archive）。它也無法滿足極少存取的封存需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/writing-with-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-transition-general-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/lifecycle-expire-general-considerations.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":82,"question_en":"A company is developing a new application. The application uses AWS Lambda functions for its compute tier. The company must use a canary deployment for any changes to the Lambda functions. Automated rollback must occur if any failures are reported. The company’s DevOps team needs to create the infrastructure as code (IaC) and the CI/CD pipeline for this solution. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一款新的应用程序。该应用程序的计算层使用 AWS Lambda 函数。对于 Lambda 函数的任何变更，公司必须采用金丝雀部署。如果出现任何故障报告，必须自动回滚。 该公司的 DevOps 团队需要为该解决方案创建基础设施即代码（IaC）和持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD） 流水线。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template for the application. Define each Lambda function in the template by using the AWS::Lambda::Function resource type. In the template, include a version for the Lambda function by using the AWS::Lambda::Version resource type. Declare the CodeSha256 property. Configure an AWS::Lambda::Alias resource that references the latest version of the Lambda function.","B":"Create an AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) template for the application. Define each Lambda function in the template by using the AWS::Serverless::Function resource type. For each function, include configurations for the AutoPublishAlias property and the DeploymentPreference property. Configure the deployment configuration type to LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes.","C":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline. Use the CodeCommit repository in a new source stage that starts the pipeline. Create an AWS CodeBuild project to deploy the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) template. Upload the template and source code to the CodeCommit repository. In the CodeCommit repository, create a buildspec.yml file that includes the commands to build and deploy the SAM application.","D":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline. Use the CodeCommit repository in a new source stage that starts the pipeline. Create an AWS CodeDeploy deployment group that is configured for canary deployments with a DeploymentPreference type of Canary10Percent10Minutes. Upload the AWS CloudFormation template and source code to the CodeCommit repository. In the CodeCommit repository, create an appspec.yml file that includes the commands to deploy the CloudFormation template.","E":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch composite alarm for all the Lambda functions. Configure an evaluation period and dimensions for Lambda. Configure the alarm to enter the ALARM state if any errors are detected or if there is insufficient data.","F":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for each Lambda function. Configure the alarms to enter the ALARM state if any errors are detected. Configure an evaluation period, dimensions for each Lambda function and version, and the namespace as AWS/Lambda on the Errors metric."},"options_zh":{"A":"为应用程序创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板。使用 AWS::Lambda::Function 资源类型在模板中 定义每个 Lambda 函数。在模板中，使用 AWS::Lambda::Version 资源类型为 Lambda 函数包含一 个版本。声明 CodeSha256 属性。配置一个引用 Lambda 函数最新版本的 AWS::Lambda::Alias 资 源。","B":"为应用程序创建一个 AWS 无服务器应用程序模型（AWS SAM）模板。使用 AWS::Serverless:: Function 资源类型在模板中定义每个 Lambda 函数。对于每个函数，包含 AutoPublishAlias 属性 和 DeploymentPreference 属性的配置。将部署配置类型设置为 LambdaCanary10Percent10Minute s。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。使用 CodeCommit 在新的源代码阶段创建一个代码库以启动流水线。创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来部署 AWS 无服务 器应用程序模型（AWS SAM）模板。将模板和源代码上传到 CodeCommit 代码库。在 CodeCommit 代 码库中，创建一个包含构建和部署 SAM 应用程序命令的 buildspec.yml 文件。","D":"创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。在新的源阶段使用 CodeCommit 代码库来启动管道。创建一个配置为金丝雀部署且部署偏好类型为 Canary10Percent10M inutes 的 AWS CodeDeploy 部署组。将 AWS CloudFormation 模板和源代码上传到 CodeCommit 代码 库。在 CodeCommit 代码库中，创建一个包含部署 CloudFormation 模板所需命令的 appspec.yml 文件。","E":"为所有 Lambda 函数创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 复合警报。为 Lambda 配置评估周期和维度。如果检 测到任何错误或数据不足，配置警报进入“警报”状态。","F":"为每个 Lambda 函数创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。将警报配置为在检测到任何错误时进入“警 报”状态。为每个 Lambda 函数及其版本配置评估周期、维度，并将命名空间配置为 AWS/Lambda， 针对“错误”指标进行设置。"},"answer":["B","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS SAM natively provides automated canary Lambda deployments with automatic rollback, so B, C, and F together form the complete IaC + CI/CD + rollback-trigger solution. Option B is the core IaC mechanism: AWS::Serverless::Function with AutoPublishAlias publishes a new version and points an alias at it, and DeploymentPreference auto-generates a CodeDeploy resource that shifts traffic in canary increments and rolls back automatically when a referenced CloudWatch alarm (or pre/post-traffic hook) fails. Note the exact SAM Type value is Canary10Percent10Minutes, not LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes (the 'Lambda' prefix belongs to the underlying CodeDeployDefault.LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes config name); B has this small naming imprecision, but it is still the only option that correctly describes the SAM AutoPublishAlias + DeploymentPreference canary-with-rollback design, so it is the intended answer. Option C is the matching CI/CD pipeline for a SAM app: a CodeCommit source stage starts CodePipeline, and a CodeBuild project runs sam build/sam deploy via a buildspec.yml. Option F supplies the rollback trigger expected by SAM's DeploymentPreference.Alarms list: per-function CloudWatch metric alarms in the AWS/Lambda namespace on the Errors metric with function/version dimensions — exactly the two error alarms (alias and latest version) shown in the SAM gradual-deployment example.","explanation_zh":"AWS SAM 原生提供具自動 rollback 的 Lambda canary 部署，因此 B、C、F 三者共同構成完整的 IaC + CI/CD + rollback 觸發解決方案。選項 B 是核心 IaC 機制：AWS::Serverless::Function 搭配 AutoPublishAlias 會發佈新版本並讓 alias 指向它，DeploymentPreference 則自動產生一個 CodeDeploy 資源，以 canary 增量轉移流量，並在所參照的 CloudWatch alarm（或 pre/post-traffic hook）失敗時自動 rollback。注意 SAM 的 Type 正確值為 Canary10Percent10Minutes，而非 LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes（'Lambda' 前綴屬於底層 CodeDeployDefault.LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes 設定名稱）；B 有這個小小的命名不精確，但它仍是唯一正確描述 SAM AutoPublishAlias + DeploymentPreference canary 加 rollback 設計的選項，因此是預期答案。選項 C 是對應 SAM 應用的 CI/CD pipeline：CodeCommit source stage 觸發 CodePipeline，CodeBuild project 透過 buildspec.yml 執行 sam build / sam deploy。選項 F 提供 SAM DeploymentPreference.Alarms 清單所需的 rollback 觸發器：在 AWS/Lambda namespace、Errors metric、含 function/version dimensions 的每個 function 的 CloudWatch metric alarm，正是 SAM 漸進式部署範例中所示的兩個 error alarm（alias 與 latest version）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Raw CloudFormation with AWS::Lambda::Version and an alias statically pointing at the latest version provides no canary traffic shifting and no automated rollback. A static alias does not implement gradual deployment, so this fails both core requirements; the AWS::CodeDeploy or SAM DeploymentPreference layer that performs traffic shifting and alarm-based rollback is missing.","why_zh":"純 CloudFormation 使用 AWS::Lambda::Version 並讓 alias 靜態指向最新版本，不提供 canary 流量轉移，也沒有自動 rollback。靜態 alias 無法實作漸進式部署，因此無法滿足兩個核心需求；缺少執行流量轉移與依 alarm rollback 的 AWS::CodeDeploy 或 SAM DeploymentPreference 層。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This wires a plain CloudFormation template to a CodeDeploy deployment group plus an appspec.yml to 'deploy the CloudFormation template,' which is not how Lambda canary deployments work. Canary10Percent10Minutes/DeploymentPreference is a SAM construct (backed by the CodeDeployDefault.Lambda* config); CodeDeploy does not deploy CFN templates via appspec for Lambda canaries, and a CodeDeploy deployment group is not configured directly against a CloudFormation template this way.","why_zh":"此選項把純 CloudFormation template 接到 CodeDeploy deployment group 加 appspec.yml 來「部署 CloudFormation template」，這並非 Lambda canary 部署的運作方式。Canary10Percent10Minutes / DeploymentPreference 是 SAM 構件（底層為 CodeDeployDefault.Lambda* 設定）；CodeDeploy 不會透過 appspec 為 Lambda canary 部署 CFN template，CodeDeploy deployment group 也不是以這種方式直接設定在 CloudFormation template 上。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A composite alarm derives its state from a rule expression over OTHER alarms; it has no evaluation period or metric dimensions of its own, so 'configure an evaluation period and dimensions for Lambda' on a composite alarm is technically incorrect. Triggering the ALARM state on insufficient data would also cause spurious rollbacks during normal low-traffic periods. SAM/CodeDeploy rollback expects per-function metric alarms (as in F), not a composite alarm.","why_zh":"composite alarm 的狀態來自對「其他 alarm」的 rule expression；它本身沒有 evaluation period 或 metric dimensions，因此在 composite alarm 上「設定 evaluation period 與 Lambda 的 dimensions」在技術上是錯誤的。以 insufficient data 觸發 ALARM 也會在正常低流量期間造成誤判 rollback。SAM/CodeDeploy 的 rollback 需要每個 function 的 metric alarm（如 F），而非 composite alarm。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/automating-updates-to-serverless-apps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/tutorial-lambda-sam-template.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/sample-lambda-sam-gradle.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Create_Composite_Alarm.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/monitoring-functions-metrics.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":83,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is deploying a new version of a company’s application in an AWS CodeDeploy deployment group associated with its Amazon EC2 instances. After some time, the deployment fails. The engineer realizes that all the events associated with the specific deployment ID are in a Skipped status, and code was not deployed in the instances associated with the deployment group. What are valid reasons for this failure? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在将公司应用程序的新版本部署到与亚马逊 EC2 实例相关联的 AWS CodeDeploy 部署组中。过了一段时间，部署失败了。工程师发现与特定部署 ID 相关的所有事件都处于“已跳过” 状态，并且代码未部署到与部署组相关联的实例中。 导致此失败的合理原因是什么？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"The networking configuration does not allow the EC2 instances to reach the internet via a NAT gateway or internet gateway, and the CodeDeploy endpoint cannot be reached.","B":"The IAM user who triggered the application deployment does not have permission to interact with the CodeDeploy endpoint.","C":"The target EC2 instances were not properly registered with the CodeDeploy endpoint.","D":"An instance profile with proper permissions was not attached to the target EC2 instances.","E":"The appspec.yml file was not included in the application revision."},"options_zh":{"A":"网络配置不允许 EC2 实例通过 NAT 网关或互联网网关访问互联网，因此无法连接到 CodeDeploy 端点。","B":"触发应用程序部署的 IAM 用户无权与 CodeDeploy 端点进行交互。","C":"目标 EC2 实例未正确注册到 CodeDeploy 端点。","D":"目标 EC2 实例未附加具有适当权限的实例配置文件。","E":"应用程序修订中未包含 appspec.yml 文件。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When every lifecycle event of an EC2/on-premises CodeDeploy deployment shows Skipped and no code is installed, the AWS guide 'Troubleshooting all lifecycle events skipped errors' lists the documented root causes. Two map directly to the options. First, the instance may be unable to reach the CodeDeploy or Amazon S3 public endpoint over port 443; AWS says to assign a public IP and use the route table/internet gateway for internet access, or use a NAT gateway for instances in a private subnet, and to allow outbound 443 in the security group (matches option A). Second, the instance may have no IAM instance profile attached, or one without the required permissions; the instance profile is what grants the CodeDeploy agent credentials to poll CodeDeploy and download the revision from S3 (matches option D). In both cases the on-host agent never receives or processes the commands, so the host-agent lifecycle events are all Skipped and nothing is deployed.","explanation_zh":"當 EC2/On-Premises CodeDeploy 部署的每個 lifecycle event 都顯示 Skipped 且沒有任何程式碼被安裝時，AWS 文件「Troubleshooting all lifecycle events skipped errors」列出了記載的根本原因，其中兩項直接對應到選項。第一，instance 可能無法透過 port 443 連到 CodeDeploy 或 Amazon S3 的 public endpoint；AWS 建議指派 public IP 並透過 route table/internet gateway 取得網際網路存取，或對私有子網中的 instance 使用 NAT gateway，並在 security group 允許 outbound 443（對應選項 A）。第二，instance 可能沒有附加 IAM instance profile，或附加的 profile 缺少必要權限；instance profile 正是用來授予 CodeDeploy agent 憑證，讓它能輪詢 CodeDeploy 並從 S3 下載 revision（對應選項 D）。這兩種情況下，host 上的 agent 永遠收不到或無法處理命令，因此所有 host-agent lifecycle events 都被 Skipped，且不會部署任何內容。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The permissions of the IAM user who triggers the deployment are evaluated when the CreateDeployment API call is made. If that principal lacked codedeploy:CreateDeployment permission, the deployment would never be created (an AccessDenied error at the API), not result in a created deployment whose instance lifecycle events are all Skipped. This is not in the documented causes for all-events-skipped.","why_zh":"觸發部署的 IAM user 權限是在 CreateDeployment API 呼叫時評估。若該 principal 缺少 codedeploy:CreateDeployment 權限，部署根本不會被建立（API 端會收到 AccessDenied 錯誤），而不會產生一個 instance lifecycle events 全部 Skipped 的已建立部署。這不在文件記載的 all-events-skipped 原因中。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EC2 instances are not 'registered' with a CodeDeploy endpoint; registration (register-on-premises-instance) applies only to on-premises instances. EC2 instances are matched to a deployment group by tags or Auto Scaling group membership. If no instances matched, you would get a 'no instances were found' style error, not all lifecycle events in Skipped status. This cause is not listed in the troubleshooting guide.","why_zh":"EC2 instance 並不會向 CodeDeploy endpoint「註冊」；註冊（register-on-premises-instance）僅適用於 on-premises instance。EC2 instance 是透過 tag 或 Auto Scaling group 成員身分對應到 deployment group。若沒有 instance 符合，會收到「no instances were found」類型的錯誤，而非所有 lifecycle events 都是 Skipped。此原因未列在疑難排解文件中。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A missing appspec.yml surfaces during or after DownloadBundle when the agent tries to read the AppSpec, producing an AppSpec/validation error rather than every lifecycle event showing Skipped before anything is downloaded. The all-events-skipped symptom points to the agent being unable to connect, authenticate, or run at all, which is upstream of reading the AppSpec; this cause is not listed in the troubleshooting guide.","why_zh":"缺少 appspec.yml 會在 DownloadBundle 階段或之後、agent 嘗試讀取 AppSpec 時浮現，產生 AppSpec/驗證錯誤，而不是在下載任何內容前所有 lifecycle events 都顯示 Skipped。所有 events 都 Skipped 的症狀指向 agent 根本無法連線、驗證或執行，這發生在讀取 AppSpec 之前；此原因未列在疑難排解文件中。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-deployments.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-general.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/codedeploy-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/getting-started-create-iam-instance-profile.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":84,"question_en":"A company has a guideline that every Amazon EC2 instance must be launched from an AMI that the company’s security team produces. Every month, the security team sends an email message with the latest approved AMIs to all the development teams. The development teams use AWS CloudFormation to deploy their applications. When developers launch a new service, they have to search their email for the latest AMIs that the security department sent. A DevOps engineer wants to automate the process that the security team uses to provide the AMI IDs to the development teams. What is the MOST scalable solution that meets these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司有一项规定，即所有亚马逊 EC2 实例都必须从公司安全团队制作的 AMI 启动。每个月，安全 团队都会向所有开发团队发送一封电子邮件，附上最新批准的 AMI 列表。 开发团队使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署其应用程序。当开发人员推出新服务时，他们必须在电子邮件中 查找安全团队发送的最新 AMI。一位 DevOps 工程师希望将安全团队向开发团队提供 AMI ID 的流程自动 化。 满足这些要求的最具可扩展性的解决方案是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Direct the security team to use CloudFormation to create new versions of the AMIs and to list the AMI ARNs in an encrypted Amazon S3 object as part of the stack’s Outputs section. Instruct the developers to use a cross-stack reference to load the encrypted S3 object and obtain the most recent AMI ARNs.","B":"Direct the security team to use a CloudFormation stack to create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that builds new AMIs and places the latest AMI ARNs in an encrypted Amazon S3 object as part of the pipeline output. Instruct the developers to use a cross-stack reference within their own CloudFormation template to obtain the S3 object location and the most recent AMI ARNs.","C":"Direct the security team to use Amazon EC2 Image Builder to create new AMIs and to place the AMI ARNs as parameters in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store. Instruct the developers to specify a parameter of type SSM in their CloudFormation stack to obtain the most recent AMI ARNs from Parameter Store.","D":"Direct the security team to use Amazon EC2 Image Builder to create new AMIs and to create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic so that every development team can receive notifications. When the development teams receive a notification, instruct them to write an AWS Lambda function that will update their CloudFormation stack with the most recent AMI ARNs."},"options_zh":{"A":"指示安全团队使用 CloudFormation 创建 AMI 的新版本，并在堆栈的“输出”部分将 AMI 的 ARN 列表 以加密的 Amazon S3 对象形式列出。告知开发人员使用跨堆栈引用加载加密的 S3 对象并获取最新的 AMI ARN。","B":"指挥安保工作 团队使用 CloudFormation 堆栈创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道 构建新的 AMI 并将最新的 AMI ARN 放入加密的 Amazon S3 对象中，作为管道输出的一部分。指示 开发人员在其自己的 CloudFormation 模板中使用跨栈引用以获取 S3 对象的位置和最新的 AMI ARN。","C":"指示安全团队使用亚马逊 EC2 Image Builder 创建新的 AMI，并将 AMI 的 ARN 作为参数放置在 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储中。告知开发人员在其 CloudFormation 堆栈中指定类型为 SSM 的 参数，以便从参数存储中获取最新的 AMI ARN。","D":"指示安全团队使用亚马逊 EC2 镜像构建器创建新的 AMI，并创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，以便每个开发团队都能收到通知。当开发团队收到通知时，指导他们编写一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用最新的 AMI 资源名称更新其 CloudFormation 堆栈。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The canonical, fully managed AWS pattern for distributing approved AMI IDs is to publish the AMI ID to AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store and have consumers reference it. EC2 Image Builder automates building hardened golden AMIs, and its distribution settings can natively write the output AMI ID to a Parameter Store parameter: the AWS::ImageBuilder::DistributionConfiguration SsmParameterConfiguration resource creates the parameter if it does not exist, otherwise updates it, using data type aws:ec2:image. No custom Lambda is required. On the consumer side, CloudFormation supports Systems Manager parameter types, which retrieve the latest value from Parameter Store at stack create/update time (for example AWS::SSM::Parameter::Value<AWS::EC2::Image::Id> resolving a key such as /golden-ami). The EC2 user guide describes this exact monthly-AMI scenario: 'every month in your organization you might create a new version of your AMI... you can create a Systems Manager parameter (for example, golden-ami) that points to the correct AMI ID... Your users don't have to know about the periodic updates.' Developers never search email and always launch from the latest approved AMI with no per-team code, making this the MOST scalable solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS 分發核准 AMI ID 的標準且全託管模式，是把 AMI ID 發佈到 AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store，再由消費端引用。EC2 Image Builder 自動建立強化過的 golden AMI，且其 distribution 設定可原生把輸出的 AMI ID 寫入 Parameter Store 參數：AWS::ImageBuilder::DistributionConfiguration 的 SsmParameterConfiguration 在參數不存在時建立、存在時更新，並使用資料型別 aws:ec2:image，完全不需自訂 Lambda。在消費端，CloudFormation 支援 Systems Manager 參數型別，會在建立或更新堆疊時自動從 Parameter Store 取得最新值（例如 AWS::SSM::Parameter::Value<AWS::EC2::Image::Id> 解析 /golden-ami 這類 key）。EC2 使用者指南正描述此每月更新 AMI 的情境：『每個月可能建立新版 AMI…可建立指向正確 AMI ID 的 Systems Manager 參數（例如 golden-ami）…使用者不需知道定期更新』。開發人員不必再翻找電子郵件，且無須任何各團隊自訂程式碼即可一律以最新核准的 AMI 啟動，因此是最具擴展性的解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation cannot 'create new versions of AMIs' as a native capability; AMI baking requires Image Builder or custom automation. Storing ARNs in an encrypted S3 object and loading it via a cross-stack reference is invalid: cross-stack references (Fn::ImportValue) import values exported from another stack's Outputs section, not the contents of an S3 object, and they cannot read encrypted file contents. This is convoluted and not a supported mechanism.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 本身無法『建立新版 AMI』，AMI 烘焙需要 Image Builder 或自訂自動化。把 ARN 存到加密 S3 物件再用 cross-stack reference 載入是錯的：cross-stack reference（Fn::ImportValue）匯入的是另一個堆疊 Outputs 區段所匯出的值，而非 S3 物件內容，也無法讀取加密檔案內容，做法繞遠且非受支援機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A CodePipeline that builds AMIs and writes ARNs to an encrypted S3 object adds far more operational overhead than the native Image Builder-to-Parameter Store integration, and cross-stack references still cannot load an S3 object's contents or an S3 location to obtain AMI ARNs. The described mechanism is not how cross-stack references (Fn::ImportValue of exported Outputs) work, so it does not meet the requirement scalably.","why_zh":"用 CodePipeline 烘焙 AMI 並把 ARN 寫進加密 S3 物件，比原生 Image Builder 寫入 Parameter Store 的整合維運負擔大很多，且 cross-stack reference 仍無法載入 S3 物件內容或 S3 位置來取得 AMI ARN。所述機制並非 cross-stack reference（匯入匯出 Outputs 的 Fn::ImportValue）的運作方式，因此無法可擴展地滿足需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using SNS to notify teams and then requiring each team to write a Lambda function to update their own CloudFormation stack is the opposite of scalable: it pushes custom code and manual notification handling onto every development team. It reintroduces the same per-team manual burden the question wants to eliminate and adds ongoing maintenance of many Lambda functions.","why_zh":"用 SNS 通知各團隊、再要求每個團隊各自撰寫 Lambda 去更新自己的 CloudFormation 堆疊，與可擴展性背道而馳：把自訂程式碼與手動通知處理推給每個開發團隊，重新引入題目想消除的每團隊手動負擔，還要持續維護大量 Lambda 函式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/using-systems-manager-parameter-to-find-AMI.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-imagebuilder-distributionconfiguration-ssmparameterconfiguration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/parameters-section-structure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/cloudformation-supplied-parameter-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/what-is-image-builder.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":85,"question_en":"An application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). A DevOps engineer is using AWS CodeDeploy to release a new version. The deployment fails during the AllowTraffic lifecycle event, but a cause for the failure is not indicated in the deployment logs. What would cause this?","question_zh":"一个应用程序在应用负载均衡器（ALB）后面的亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行。一位 DevOps 工程师正在使用 AWS CodeDeploy 发布新版本。在 AllowTraffic 生命周期事件期间部署失败，但部署日志中未指明失败 原因。 这会是什么原因造成的？","options_en":{"A":"The appspec.yml file contains an invalid script that runs in the AllowTraffic lifecycle hook.","B":"The user who initiated the deployment does not have the necessary permissions to interact with the ALB.","C":"The health checks specified for the ALB target group are misconfigured.","D":"The CodeDeploy agent was not installed in the EC2 instances that are part of the ALB target group."},"options_zh":{"A":"appspec.yml 文件中包含一个在 AllowTraffic 生命周期挂钩中运行的无效脚本。","B":"发起部署的用户没有与应用负载均衡器（ALB）进行交互所需的权限。","C":"针对 ALB 目标组指定的健康检查配置有误。","D":"作为应用负载均衡器目标组一部分的 EC2 实例上未安装 CodeDeploy 代理。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The AWS CodeDeploy troubleshooting documentation contains a section titled almost verbatim to this question: 'Troubleshooting a failed AllowTraffic lifecycle event with no error reported in the deployment logs.' It states that a blue/green deployment can fail during the AllowTraffic lifecycle event without the deployment logs indicating the cause, and that 'this failure is typically due to incorrectly configured health checks in Elastic Load Balancing for the Classic Load Balancer, Application Load Balancer, or Network Load Balancer used to manage traffic for the deployment group.' The documented remediation is to review and correct any errors in the load balancer (target group) health check configuration. During AllowTraffic, CodeDeploy registers the replacement instances with the ALB target group and waits for them to pass health checks before shifting traffic; if the health checks are misconfigured, the targets never become healthy and the event times out / fails silently with no script-level log entry. This exactly matches option C.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeDeploy 的疑難排解文件中有一個章節標題幾乎與本題逐字相同：『Troubleshooting a failed AllowTraffic lifecycle event with no error reported in the deployment logs』。文件指出，blue/green 部署可能在 AllowTraffic 生命週期事件失敗、而部署日誌未顯示失敗原因，並說明『此失敗通常是因為用來管理部署群組流量的 Elastic Load Balancing（Classic Load Balancer、Application Load Balancer 或 Network Load Balancer）的健康檢查設定錯誤』。文件記載的解決方式是檢視並修正 load balancer（target group）的健康檢查設定。在 AllowTraffic 期間，CodeDeploy 會將替換的執行個體註冊到 ALB target group，並等待其通過健康檢查才轉移流量；若健康檢查設定錯誤，目標永遠不會變成 healthy，該事件便會逾時／在沒有 script 層級日誌的情況下靜默失敗。這完全符合選項 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AllowTraffic is not a user-script hook on the EC2/On-Premises platform. The valid AppSpec hooks are ApplicationStop, BeforeInstall, AfterInstall, ApplicationStart, ValidateService, BeforeBlockTraffic, AfterBlockTraffic, BeforeAllowTraffic, and AfterAllowTraffic. AllowTraffic itself is an internal CodeDeploy/ELB action with no appspec hook, so no custom script runs there. Moreover, a failing script would write an explicit error to the deployment logs, contradicting the 'no cause indicated' premise.","why_zh":"AllowTraffic 在 EC2/On-Premises 平台上並非使用者腳本 hook。有效的 AppSpec hooks 為 ApplicationStop、BeforeInstall、AfterInstall、ApplicationStart、ValidateService、BeforeBlockTraffic、AfterBlockTraffic、BeforeAllowTraffic 與 AfterAllowTraffic。AllowTraffic 本身是 CodeDeploy/ELB 的內部動作，沒有對應的 appspec hook，因此不會在此執行自訂腳本。此外，腳本失敗會在部署日誌寫入明確錯誤，與『日誌未顯示原因』的前提矛盾。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The user/operator does not directly interact with the ALB during deployment; CodeDeploy uses its service role to register targets and manage traffic. A permissions problem would surface as an explicit IAM/AccessDenied error, not a silent failure with no logged cause. This is not the documented cause for a silent AllowTraffic failure.","why_zh":"在部署過程中，使用者/操作者並不直接與 ALB 互動；CodeDeploy 是透過其 service role 來註冊目標並管理流量。權限問題會以明確的 IAM/AccessDenied 錯誤呈現，而非沒有記錄原因的靜默失敗。這並非文件記載的 AllowTraffic 靜默失敗原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"If the CodeDeploy agent were not installed, the deployment would fail much earlier (e.g., the instance would not be registered or the DownloadBundle/install phases would fail) and would produce a clear error, not fail specifically at AllowTraffic with no logged cause. The agent is required well before the AllowTraffic stage is reached.","why_zh":"若未安裝 CodeDeploy agent，部署會在更早階段失敗（例如執行個體無法註冊、或 DownloadBundle/安裝階段失敗）並產生明確錯誤，而不會恰好在 AllowTraffic 階段以無記錄原因的方式失敗。在到達 AllowTraffic 階段之前就已需要 agent 運作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-deployments.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/target-group-health-checks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":86,"question_en":"A company has 20 service teams. Each service team is responsible for its own microservice. Each service team uses a separate AWS account for its microservice and a VPC with the 192.168.0.0/22 CIDR block. The company manages the AWS accounts with AWS Organizations. Each service team hosts its microservice on multiple Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. The microservices communicate with each other across the public internet. The company’s security team has issued a new guideline that all communication between microservices must use HTTPS over private network connections and cannot traverse the public internet. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution that fulfills these obligations and minimizes the number of changes for each service team. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有 20 个服务团队。每个服务团队负责自己的微服务。每个服务团队为其微服务使用单独的 AWS 账户，并使用具有 192.168.0.0/22 CIDR 块的 VPC。该公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理这些 AWS 账户。 每个服务团队都在多个亚马逊 EC2 实例上托管其微服务，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器之后。微服务 之间通过公共互联网进行通信。公司的安全团队发布了一项新指南，规定所有微服务之间的通信必须通 过专用网络连接使用 HTTPS，且不能通过公共互联网传输。 一位 DevOps 工程师必须实施一种解决方案，以履行这些职责，并将每个服务团队所需进行的变更数量 降至最低。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS account in AWS Organizations. Create a VPC in this account, and use AWS Resource Access Manager to share the private subnets of this VPC with the organization. Instruct the service teams to launch a new Network Load Balancer (NLB) and EC2 instances that use the shared private subnets. Use the NLB DNS names for communication between microservices.","B":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each of the microservice VPCs. Use AWS PrivateLink to create VPC endpoints in each AWS account for the NLBs. Create subscriptions to each VPC endpoint in each of the other AWS accounts. Use the VPC endpoint DNS names for communication between microservices.","C":"Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each of the microservice VPCs. Create VPC peering connections between each of the microservice VPCs. Update the route tables for each VPC to use the peering links. Use the NLB DNS names for communication between microservices.","D":"Create a new AWS account in AWS Organizations. Create a transit gateway in this account, and use AWS Resource Access Manager to share the transit gateway with the organization. In each of the microservice VPCs, create a transit gateway attachment to the shared transit gateway. Update the route tables of each VPC to use the transit gateway. Create a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each of the microservice VPCs. Use the NLB DNS names for communication between microservices."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS 组织中创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在该账户中创建一个 VPC，并使用 AWS 资源访问管理器 将此 VPC 的私有子网与组织共享。指示服务团队在共享的私有子网中启动新的网络负载均衡器 （NLB）和 EC2 实例。使用 NLB 的 DNS 名称在微服务之间进行通信。","B":"在每个微服务的虚拟私有云（VPC）中创建一个网络负载均衡器（NLB）。使用 AWS PrivateLink 在 每个 AWS 账户中为 NLB 创建 VPC 端点。在其他每个 AWS 账户中为每个 VPC 端点创建订阅。使 用 VPC 端点的 DNS 名称在微服务之间进行通信。","C":"在每个微服务的虚拟私有云（VPC）中创建一个网络负载均衡器（NLB）。创建 VPC 对等连接 在每个微服务的虚拟私有云（VPC）之间建立连接。更新每个 VPC 的路由表以使用对等链接。使用网 络负载均衡器（NLB）的 DNS 名称在微服务之间进行通信。","D":"在 AWS 组织中创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在该账户中创建一个传输网关，并使用 AWS 资源访问管理器 将传输网关与组织共享。在每个微服务 VPC 中，创建一个到共享传输网关的传输网关连接。更新每个 VPC 的路由表以使用传输网关。在每个微服务 VPC 中创建一个网络负载均衡器（NLB）。使用 NLB 的 DNS 名称在微服务之间进行通信。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The decisive constraint is that all 20 microservice VPCs use the SAME CIDR block (192.168.0.0/22), so their IP ranges overlap. AWS PrivateLink (option B) is the only choice that works with overlapping CIDRs: each provider exposes its service via a Network Load Balancer behind a VPC endpoint service, and consumers reach it through an interface VPC endpoint that has its own ENI/private IP inside the consumer's own VPC. The PrivateLink concepts page states it lets clients connect to services in other VPCs using private IP addresses 'as if those services and resources were hosted directly in your VPC' — traffic terminates on an endpoint ENI in the consumer VPC rather than being IP-routed between VPCs, so overlapping CIDRs are irrelevant, traffic stays on the AWS private network (never the public internet), and the NLB/PrivateLink path carries TLS so HTTPS is satisfied. VPC peering (C) explicitly does NOT support overlapping CIDR blocks and is non-transitive, and Transit Gateway (D) likewise requires non-overlapping IP ranges to route (AWS Well-Architected REL02-BP05 states IP ranges 'must not overlap when peered, connected via Transit Gateway, or connected over VPN'), so both are technically broken here. Option A (RAM-shared VPC) forces every team to relaunch EC2 and NLBs into new shared subnets, which is the maximum amount of change, contradicting the requirement to minimize changes. The word 'subscriptions' in B is loose phrasing for endpoint connections, but the architecture is uniquely correct.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限制是 20 個 microservice VPC 全部使用相同的 CIDR (192.168.0.0/22)，因此 IP 範圍重疊。AWS PrivateLink (選項 B) 是唯一能在 CIDR 重疊情況下運作的方案：每個 provider 透過 Network Load Balancer 背後的 VPC endpoint service 公開服務，consumer 則透過 interface VPC endpoint 連線，該 endpoint 在 consumer 自己的 VPC 內有獨立的 ENI/私有 IP。PrivateLink concepts 文件說明它讓 client 以私有 IP 連線到其他 VPC 的服務，『如同這些服務與資源就直接託管在你自己的 VPC 中』——流量終結在 consumer VPC 內的 endpoint ENI 上，而不是在 VPC 之間進行 IP 路由，因此 CIDR 重疊不影響運作，流量保持在 AWS 私有網路 (從不經過公網)，且 NLB/PrivateLink 路徑可承載 TLS，滿足 HTTPS 要求。VPC peering (C) 明確不支援重疊 CIDR 且不支援傳遞路由；Transit Gateway (D) 同樣需要不重疊的 IP 範圍才能路由 (AWS Well-Architected REL02-BP05 指出 IP 範圍『在 peered、透過 Transit Gateway 連接或透過 VPN 連接時不得重疊』)，因此兩者在此情境下技術上都行不通。選項 A (RAM 共享 VPC) 強迫每個團隊將 EC2 與 NLB 重新部署到新的共享子網，變更量最大，違反最小化變更的要求。B 中的「subscriptions」用詞不精確 (實為 endpoint connections)，但其架構是唯一正確的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A RAM-shared central VPC requires every one of the 20 teams to relaunch their EC2 instances and NLBs into the new shared private subnets, which is the maximum possible change and directly contradicts 'minimize the number of changes for each service team'. It also collapses team/account isolation.","why_zh":"RAM 共享的中央 VPC 要求 20 個團隊全部把 EC2 與 NLB 重新部署到新的共享私有子網，變更量最大，直接違反『最小化每個團隊的變更』，且破壞團隊/帳戶隔離。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"VPC peering explicitly does NOT support overlapping CIDR blocks (the vpc-peering-basics doc lists overlapping CIDRs and transitive routing as unsupported), and all 20 VPCs share 192.168.0.0/22. Peering is also non-transitive, requiring a near-full mesh (~190 connections). Technically impossible here.","why_zh":"VPC peering 明確不支援重疊的 CIDR (vpc-peering-basics 文件將重疊 CIDR 與傳遞路由列為不支援)，而 20 個 VPC 全用 192.168.0.0/22。Peering 也不支援傳遞路由，需要近乎全網狀 (約 190 條連線)。此處技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Transit Gateway routes by destination IP and requires non-overlapping CIDR ranges. AWS Well-Architected REL02-BP05 states IP ranges 'must not overlap when peered, connected via Transit Gateway, or connected over VPN'. With 20 identical 192.168.0.0/22 VPCs, the TGW route tables cannot distinguish destinations, so routing breaks.","why_zh":"Transit Gateway 依目的地 IP 路由，需要不重疊的 CIDR 範圍。AWS Well-Architected REL02-BP05 指出 IP 範圍『在 peered、透過 Transit Gateway 連接或透過 VPN 連接時不得重疊』。20 個相同的 192.168.0.0/22 VPC 會使 TGW 路由表無法區分目的地，路由失效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/privatelink/concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/peering/vpc-peering-basics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/peering/create-vpc-peering-connection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/2024-06-27/framework/rel_planning_network_topology_non_overlap_ip.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":87,"question_en":"An Amazon EC2 instance is running in a VPC and needs to download an object from a restricted Amazon S3 bucket. When the DevOps engineer tries to download the object, an AccessDenied error is received. What are the possible causes for this error? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一个亚马逊 EC2 实例正在虚拟私有云（VPC）中运行，需要从一个受限制的亚马逊 S3 存储桶下载一个对 象。当开发运维工程师尝试下载该对象时，收到了“访问被拒绝”的错误。 此错误可能由哪些原因导致？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"The S3 bucket default encryption is enabled.","B":"There is an error in the S3 bucket policy.","C":"The object has been moved to S3 Glacier.","D":"There is an error in the IAM role configuration.","E":"S3 Versioning is enabled."},"options_zh":{"A":"S3 存储桶的默认加密已启用。","B":"S3 存储桶策略存在错误。","C":"该对象已移至 S3 Glacier。","D":"IAM 角色配置有误。","E":"已启用 S3 版本控制。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"An EC2 instance reads from S3 using the IAM role attached via its instance profile, and access is also gated by the bucket's resource-based (bucket) policy. The AWS S3 403 troubleshooting guide names \"Bucket policies and IAM policies\" as the primary causes of AccessDenied: a bucket policy with a missing Allow or an explicit Deny for s3:GetObject (an explicit/implicit deny in a resource-based policy), or an IAM role with no s3:GetObject Allow (an implicit deny, because IAM denies by default), both yield a 403 AccessDenied. So B and D are correct. The other options do not produce AccessDenied: an object archived to the S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval / Deep Archive class returns an InvalidObjectState error and requires RestoreObject first, not AccessDenied; S3 Versioning is transparent to a normal GET of the current version; and S3 default encryption (SSE-S3) is transparent on download. Only an SSE-KMS key with no grant to the caller would deny, which is a KMS permission problem rather than simply \"default encryption enabled\" as option A is worded.","explanation_zh":"EC2 執行個體透過附加在 instance profile 上的 IAM role 來讀取 S3 物件，而存取同時也受 bucket 的資源型政策 (bucket policy) 控管。AWS 的 S3 403 疑難排解文件將「Bucket policies 與 IAM policies」列為 AccessDenied 的主要成因：bucket policy 缺少 Allow 或對 s3:GetObject 有明確 Deny（資源型政策的明確/隱含拒絕），或 IAM role 未授予 s3:GetObject（IAM 預設拒絕，形成隱含拒絕），兩者都會回傳 403 AccessDenied，因此 B 與 D 正確。其餘選項不會產生 AccessDenied：被歸檔至 S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval / Deep Archive 的物件會回傳 InvalidObjectState 錯誤（需先 RestoreObject），而非 AccessDenied；S3 Versioning 對讀取目前版本的一般 GET 是透明的；S3 預設加密 (SSE-S3) 在下載時也是透明的。只有 SSE-KMS 金鑰未授權給呼叫者才會拒絕，那屬於 KMS 權限問題，而非選項 A 所述的單純『啟用預設加密』。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 default encryption (SSE-S3) is transparent on download and does not by itself cause AccessDenied. Only an SSE-KMS key without a grant to the principal could produce a 403, but that is a KMS key permission issue, not simply 'default encryption enabled' as worded.","why_zh":"S3 預設加密 (SSE-S3) 在下載時是透明的，本身不會造成 AccessDenied。只有 SSE-KMS 金鑰未授權給該主體才可能產生 403，但那是 KMS 金鑰權限問題，而非題目所述的單純『啟用預設加密』。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An object in the S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval / Deep Archive storage class returns InvalidObjectState ('operation not valid for object storage class') and must be restored with RestoreObject first; it does not return AccessDenied. This is confirmed by the botocore InvalidObjectState exception doc.","why_zh":"位於 S3 Glacier Flexible Retrieval / Deep Archive 儲存類別的物件會回傳 InvalidObjectState（『此儲存類別不支援該操作』），需先以 RestoreObject 還原，並不會回傳 AccessDenied。botocore 的 InvalidObjectState 例外文件已證實此點。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"S3 Versioning is transparent to a normal GetObject of the current version and does not cause AccessDenied.","why_zh":"S3 Versioning 對讀取目前版本的一般 GetObject 是透明的，不會造成 AccessDenied。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/troubleshoot-403-errors.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/security_iam_troubleshoot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/botocore/latest/reference/services/s3/client/exceptions/InvalidObjectState.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/restoring-objects.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":88,"question_en":"A company wants to use a grid system for a proprietary enterprise in-memory data store on top of AWS. This system can run in multiple server nodes in any Linux-based distribution. The system must be able to reconfigure the entire cluster every time a node is added or removed. When adding or removing nodes, an /etc/cluster/nodes.config file must be updated, listing the IP addresses of the current node members of that cluster. The company wants to automate the task of adding new nodes to a cluster. What can a DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望在 AWS 之上为专有的企业内存数据存储使用网格系统。该系统能够在任何基于 Linux 的发 行版的多个服务器节点上运行。每当添加或移除节点时，该系统必须能够重新配置整个集群。在添加或移 除节点时，必须更新 /etc/cluster/nodes.config 文件，列出该集群当前节点成员的 IP 地址。 该公司希望实现向集群添加新节点这一任务的自动化。 DevOps 工程师能做些什么来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS OpsWorks Stacks to layer the server nodes of that cluster. Create a Chef recipe that populates the content of the /etc/cluster/nodes.config file and restarts the service by using the current members of the layer. Assign that recipe to the Configure lifecycle event.","B":"Put the file nodes.config in version control. Create an AWS CodeDeploy deployment configuration and deployment group based on an Amazon EC2 tag value for the cluster nodes. When adding a new node to the cluster, update the file with all tagged instances, and make a commit in version control. Deploy the new file and restart the services.","C":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket and upload a version of the /etc/cluster/nodes.config file. Create a crontab script that will poll for that S3 file and download it frequently. Use a process manager, such as Monit or systemd, to restart the cluster services when it detects that the new file was modified. When adding a node to the cluster, edit the file’s most recent members. Upload the new file to the S3 bucket.","D":"Create a user data script that lists all members of the current security group of the cluster and automatically updates the /etc/cluster/nodes.config file whenever a new instance is added to the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS OpsWorks Stacks 对该集群的服务器节点进行分层。创建一个 Chef 配置文件，用于填充 /etc/ cluster/nodes.config 文件的内容，并使用当前层的成员重启服务。将该配置文件分配给“配置”生命 周期事件。","B":"将文件 nodes.config 纳入版本控制。根据集群节点的 Amazon EC2 标签值创建 AWS CodeDeploy 部署配置 和部署组。向集群添加新节点时，使用所有已标记的实例更新该文件，并在版本控制中提交更改。部署 新文件并重启服务。","C":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶，并上传一份 /etc/cluster/nodes.config 文件的版本。创建一个 crontab 脚本， 用于定期轮询该 S3 文件并频繁下载。使用诸如 Monit 或 systemd 之类的进程管理器，在检测到新文件 被修改时重启集群服务。当向集群添加节点时，编辑该文件中的最新成员。将新文件上传到 S3 存储桶。","D":"创建一个用户数据脚本，列出集群当前安全组中的所有成员，并在向集群添加新实例时自动更新 / etc/cluster/nodes.config 文件。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS OpsWorks Stacks supports five lifecycle events: Setup, Configure, Deploy, Undeploy, and Shutdown (confirmed in the OpsWorks Recipes type reference). The Configure event is the decisive feature: OpsWorks Stacks triggers the Configure event on EVERY online instance in the stack whenever any instance enters or leaves the online state (a node starts, stops, or is auto-healed). This exactly matches the requirement to 'reconfigure the entire cluster every time a node is added or removed.' A custom Chef recipe assigned to the Configure event can read the current online members from the OpsWorks stack-configuration-and-deployment JSON (node attributes), regenerate /etc/cluster/nodes.config with their IP addresses, and restart the service. It is fully automated and event-driven, with no polling, no manual file edits, and no version-control commits. The grid system runs on any Linux distribution, which the Chef-based OpsWorks Stacks agent supports.","explanation_zh":"AWS OpsWorks Stacks 支援五個 lifecycle 事件：Setup、Configure、Deploy、Undeploy 與 Shutdown（OpsWorks 的 Recipes 型別參考文件已確認）。此題的關鍵在於 Configure 事件：每當 stack 中任一 instance 進入或離開 online 狀態（節點被啟動、停止或 auto-heal）時，OpsWorks Stacks 會在 stack 內「每一個」online 的 instance 上觸發 Configure 事件。這正好對應題目要求「每次新增或移除節點時重新設定整個叢集」。指派到 Configure 事件的 custom Chef recipe 可從 OpsWorks 的 stack configuration 與 deployment JSON（node attributes）讀取目前 online 的成員，以其 IP 重新產生 /etc/cluster/nodes.config 並重啟服務。整個流程完全自動化、由事件驅動，無需輪詢、手動編輯檔案或 commit。該 grid 系統可在任何 Linux 發行版上執行，而以 Chef 為基礎的 OpsWorks Stacks agent 支援此需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeDeploy is a push-based deployment service that is not triggered by cluster membership changes. It requires a human to manually edit nodes.config with all tagged instances and commit to version control before each deployment, which defeats the requirement to 'automate the task of adding new nodes.' It is manual and reactive, not automatic on node add/remove.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 是推送式部署服務，不會因叢集成員變動而被觸發。每次部署前都需人工手動編輯 nodes.config（列出所有具標籤的 instance）並 commit 到版本控制，違反「自動化新增節點」的需求；屬於手動且被動的做法。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Relies on a manual step (editing the file with current members and uploading it to S3) plus frequent cron polling, which adds latency and operational overhead. Membership changes are not detected automatically; an operator must compute and upload the member list each time, so it does not truly automate node addition.","why_zh":"依賴手動步驟（人工編輯成員清單並上傳到 S3）加上頻繁的 cron 輪詢，造成延遲與營運負擔。成員變動不會自動偵測，每次都需人工計算並上傳清單，因此並未真正自動化節點新增。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Security group membership is not a list of instance IP members; security groups define inbound/outbound rules, not the set of instances belonging to a cluster. A user data script also runs only once at instance launch on the new node, so it cannot reconfigure existing nodes when nodes are added, and it never runs when a node is removed. This approach cannot maintain live cluster membership.","why_zh":"Security group 並不是 instance IP 成員清單；它定義的是入站/出站規則，而非屬於叢集的 instance 集合。此外 user data script 只在新節點啟動時執行一次，無法在新增節點時重新設定現有節點，且在節點被移除時根本不會執行，因此無法維護即時的叢集成員。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-ruby/v2/api/Aws/OpsWorks/Types/Recipes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-properties-opsworks-layer-recipes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opsworks/latest/userguide/workingcookbook-events-configure.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":89,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is working on a data archival project that requires the migration of on-premises data to an Amazon S3 bucket. The DevOps engineer develops a script that incrementally archives on-premises data that is older than 1 month to Amazon S3. Data that is transferred to Amazon S3 is deleted from the on-premises location. The script uses the S3 PutObject operation. During a code review, the DevOps engineer notices that the script does not verify whether the data was successfully copied to Amazon S3. The DevOps engineer must update the script to ensure that data is not corrupted during transmission. The script must use MD5 checksums to verify data integrity before the on- premises data is deleted. Which solutions for the script will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在从事一个数据归档项目，该项目需要将本地的数据迁移到 Amazon S3 存储桶。该 DevOps 工程师开发了一个脚本，用于将本地超过 1 个月的数据逐步归档到 Amazon S3。转移到 Amazon S3 的数据会从本地位置删除。该脚本使用 S3 的 PutObject 操作。 在代码审查期间，DevOps 工程师发现该脚本没有验证数据是否已成功复制到亚马逊 S3。DevOps 工程师必 须更新脚本，以确保在传输过程中数据不会损坏。在删除本地数据之前，脚本必须使用 MD5 校验和来验证 数据的完整性。 哪些脚本解决方案能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Check the returned response for the VersionId. Compare the returned VersionId against the MD5 checksum.","B":"Include the MD5 checksum within the Content-MD5 parameter. Check the operation call’s return status to find out if an error was returned.","C":"Include the checksum digest within the tagging parameter as a URL query parameter.","D":"Check the returned response for the ETag. Compare the returned ETag against the MD5 checksum.","E":"Include the checksum digest within the Metadata parameter as a name-value pair. After upload, use the S3 HeadObject operation to retrieve metadata from the object."},"options_zh":{"A":"检查返回的响应中的 VersionId。将返回的 VersionId 与 MD5 校验和进行比较。","B":"在 Content-MD5 参数中包含 MD5 校验和。检查操作调用的返回状态，以确定是否返回了错误。","C":"将校验和摘要作为 URL 查询参数包含在标记参数内。","D":"检查返回响应中的 ETag。将返回的 ETag 与 MD5 校验和进行比较。","E":"在元数据参数中以名称 - 值对的形式包含校验和摘要。上传完成后，使用 S3 HeadObject 操作从对象中 检索元数据。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS S3 documents exactly two MD5-based ways to verify upload integrity, and they map directly to B and D. The PutObject API reference, under 'Data integrity with Content-MD5', states verbatim: 'To ensure that data is not corrupted traversing the network, use the Content-MD5 header. When you use this header, Amazon S3 checks the object against the provided MD5 value and, if they do not match, Amazon S3 returns an error.' That is option B: supply the precomputed digest in Content-MD5 and check the operation call's return status for that error (S3 fails the request, e.g. BadDigest, when its recomputed digest does not match). The same paragraph continues: 'Alternatively, when the object's ETag is its MD5 digest, you can calculate the MD5 while putting the object to Amazon S3 and compare the returned ETag to the calculated MD5 value.' That is option D: for single-part PutObject uploads of plaintext or SSE-S3 objects, the ETag IS the MD5 of the object data, so comparing the returned ETag against the locally computed MD5 validates the transmitted bytes. Because the script must use MD5 to validate the actual data before deleting the on-premises copy, only B and D meet the requirement.","explanation_zh":"AWS S3 官方文件明確記載了兩種以 MD5 驗證上傳完整性的方法，恰好對應 B 與 D。PutObject API 參考文件在『Data integrity with Content-MD5』段落逐字說明：使用 Content-MD5 標頭時，Amazon S3 會以提供的 MD5 值比對物件，若不符即回傳錯誤——這正是選項 B：將預先計算的 MD5 摘要放入 Content-MD5 參數，並檢查呼叫的回傳狀態是否有該錯誤（S3 重新計算的摘要不符時，會以 BadDigest 之類錯誤讓請求失敗）。同一段落接著說明：當物件的 ETag 就是其 MD5 摘要時，可在上傳時計算 MD5 並將回傳的 ETag 與所計算的 MD5 值比對——這正是選項 D：對於單一部分（single-part）PutObject 上傳的明文或 SSE-S3 物件，ETag 即為物件資料的 MD5，因此比對回傳的 ETag 與本機計算的 MD5 即可驗證傳輸內容。由於腳本必須在刪除地端資料前以 MD5 驗證實際資料，唯有 B 與 D 符合要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"VersionId is a unique identifier S3 assigns to an object version in a versioning-enabled bucket; it is not a checksum or hash of the object content. Comparing a VersionId against an MD5 checksum is meaningless and does not validate data integrity during transmission.","why_zh":"VersionId 是在啟用版本控制的儲存桶中，S3 指派給物件版本的唯一識別碼，並非物件內容的校驗碼或雜湊值。將 VersionId 與 MD5 比對毫無意義，無法驗證傳輸期間的資料完整性。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Object tagging stores arbitrary user-defined key-value metadata and does not trigger any server-side integrity check. S3 never compares a tag value against the object's content, so placing a checksum digest in the tagging parameter does not verify that the transmitted data is uncorrupted.","why_zh":"物件標籤儲存的是任意的使用者自訂鍵值中繼資料，不會觸發任何伺服器端完整性檢查。S3 不會將標籤值與物件內容比對，因此把校驗摘要放入 tagging 參數無法驗證傳輸的資料是否未損毀。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"User-defined Metadata is opaque to S3: S3 stores whatever string you provide but never recomputes the object's MD5 or compares the received bytes against your metadata. A subsequent HeadObject merely echoes back the value you originally stored, proving nothing about transmission corruption, unlike Content-MD5 where S3 actually validates the received bytes.","why_zh":"使用者自訂 Metadata 對 S3 而言是不透明的：S3 僅儲存你提供的字串，絕不會重新計算物件 MD5，也不會以中繼資料比對所收到的位元組。之後的 HeadObject 只會回傳你原本存入的值，無法證明傳輸是否損毀；這與 Content-MD5（S3 會實際驗證收到的位元組）不同。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_PutObject.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/checking-object-integrity-upload.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":90,"question_en":"A company deploys updates to its Amazon API Gateway API several times a week by using an AWS CodePipeline pipeline. As part of the update process, the company exports the JavaScript SDK for the API from the API Gateway console and uploads the SDK to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company has configured an Amazon CloudFront distribution that uses the S3 bucket as an origin. Web clients then download the SDK by using the CloudFront distribution’s endpoint. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to make the new SDK available automatically during new API deployments. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司每周数次通过使用 AWS CodePipeline 管道对其 Amazon API Gateway API 进行部署更新。作为更新流 程的一部分，该公司从 API Gateway 控制台导出 API 的 JavaScript SDK，并将 SDK 上传到 Amazon S3 存储 桶。 该公司已配置了一个使用 S3 存储桶作为源的 Amazon CloudFront 分发。然后，Web 客户端通过使用 CloudFront 分发的端点来下载 SDK。一位 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，以便在新的 API 部署期 间自动提供新的 SDK。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CodePipeline action immediately after the deployment stage of the API. Configure the action to invoke an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to download the SDK from API Gateway, upload the SDK to the S3 bucket, and create a CloudFront invalidation for the SDK path.","B":"Create a CodePipeline action immediately after the deployment stage of the API. Configure the action to use the CodePipeline integration with API Gateway to export the SDK to Amazon S3. Create another action that uses the CodePipeline integration with Amazon S3 to invalidate the cache for the SDK path.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to UpdateStage events from aws.apigateway. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to download the SDK from API Gateway, upload the SDK to the S3 bucket, and call the CloudFront API to create an invalidation for the SDK path.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to CreateDeployment events from aws.apigateway. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to download the SDK from API Gateway, upload the SDK to the S3 bucket, and call the S3 API to invalidate the cache for the SDK path."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 API 部署阶段之后立即创建一个 CodePipeline 操作。配置该操作 要调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数从 API 下载 SDK。 网关，请将 SDK 上传至 S3 存储桶，并为 SDK 路径创建 CloudFront 无效化操作。","B":"在 API 部署阶段之后立即创建一个 CodePipeline 操作。配置该操作以使用 CodePipeline 与 API Gateway 的 集成将 SDK 导出到 Amazon S3。创建另一个操作，使用 CodePipeline 与 Amazon S3 的集成来使 SDK 路 径的缓存失效。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对来自 aws.apigateway 的 UpdateStage 事件做出反应。配置该规 则以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，从 API Gateway 下载 SDK，将 SDK 上传到 S3 存储桶，并调用 CloudFront API 为 SDK 路径创建一个无效化操作。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对来自 aws.apigateway 的 CreateDeployment 事件做出反应。配 置该规则以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，从 API Gateway 下载 SDK，将 SDK 上传到 S3 存储桶，并调 用 S3 API 使 SDK 路径的缓存失效。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Option A is the only solution whose components all genuinely exist and are wired correctly. CodePipeline supports an Invoke action that calls AWS Lambda, so adding a Lambda Invoke action immediately after the API deploy stage is valid and ties the SDK refresh directly to the same pipeline that performs each deployment. The Lambda then performs three real, supported operations: export/download the SDK from API Gateway (GetSdk), upload it to the S3 bucket (PutObject), and create a CloudFront invalidation (CloudFront CreateInvalidation) so clients receive the new SDK. Cache invalidation must go through the CloudFront CreateInvalidation API; there is no S3 API that invalidates a CloudFront cache, which is fatal to option D. CodePipeline has no native action that exports an API Gateway SDK and no native S3 cache-invalidation action (the Deploy/Invoke provider list contains neither), which kills option B. Options C and D also mis-describe the trigger: per the EventBridge events reference, the only event API Gateway delivers directly to EventBridge under source aws.apigateway is 'APIGateway CRL Processing'; management calls such as UpdateStage and CreateDeployment reach EventBridge only via CloudTrail (detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail', matched on eventName), not as native aws.apigateway detail-types.","explanation_zh":"選項 A 是唯一所有元件都真實存在且正確串接的方案。CodePipeline 支援 Invoke 動作呼叫 AWS Lambda，因此在 API deploy 階段之後加入 Lambda Invoke 動作是合法的，並且直接將 SDK 更新綁定在執行每次部署的同一條 pipeline 上。該 Lambda 接著執行三個真實且受支援的操作：從 API Gateway 匯出/下載 SDK（GetSdk）、上傳到 S3 儲存桶（PutObject）、並建立 CloudFront invalidation（CloudFront CreateInvalidation）讓用戶端取得新版 SDK。快取失效必須透過 CloudFront 的 CreateInvalidation API 完成，沒有任何 S3 API 可使 CloudFront 快取失效，這對選項 D 是致命的。CodePipeline 沒有可匯出 API Gateway SDK 的原生動作，也沒有原生的 S3 快取失效動作（Deploy/Invoke provider 清單中兩者皆無），這排除了選項 B。選項 C 與 D 也錯誤描述了觸發來源：根據 EventBridge events 參考文件，API Gateway 以 source aws.apigateway 直接送往 EventBridge 的事件只有 'APIGateway CRL Processing'；UpdateStage、CreateDeployment 等管理呼叫只會經由 CloudTrail 抵達 EventBridge（detail-type 為 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail'，以 eventName 比對），而非原生的 aws.apigateway detail-type。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodePipeline has no native integration that exports an API Gateway SDK, and no native S3 action that invalidates a cache. The Deploy action provider list (EC2, EKS, S3, AppConfig, CloudFormation, StackSets, ECS, Elastic Beanstalk, OpsWorks, Service Catalog, Alexa, CodeDeploy, XebiaLabs) and the Invoke list contain no such providers, and the S3 deploy action only uploads objects. This configuration is not buildable.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 沒有可匯出 API Gateway SDK 的原生整合，也沒有可使快取失效的原生 S3 動作。Deploy action provider 清單（EC2、EKS、S3、AppConfig、CloudFormation、StackSets、ECS、Elastic Beanstalk、OpsWorks、Service Catalog、Alexa、CodeDeploy、XebiaLabs）與 Invoke 清單中皆無此類 provider，且 S3 deploy 動作僅能上傳物件。此設定無法建立。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The CloudFront invalidation step is correct, but the EventBridge trigger is wrong as worded. Per the EventBridge API Gateway events reference, the only event delivered directly under source aws.apigateway is 'APIGateway CRL Processing'; 'UpdateStage' is a management API call that reaches EventBridge only via CloudTrail (detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail', matched on eventName), not as a native aws.apigateway detail-type. A rule keyed on a native UpdateStage event would not fire.","why_zh":"CloudFront invalidation 步驟正確，但依其敘述的 EventBridge 觸發條件錯誤。根據 EventBridge 的 API Gateway events 參考文件，以 source aws.apigateway 直接送達的事件只有 'APIGateway CRL Processing'；'UpdateStage' 是管理 API 呼叫，只會經由 CloudTrail 抵達 EventBridge（detail-type 為 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail'，以 eventName 比對），並非原生的 aws.apigateway detail-type。以原生 UpdateStage 事件為條件的規則不會觸發。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Two flaws. First, invalidating a CloudFront cache cannot be done with 'the S3 API'; cache invalidation is a CloudFront operation (CreateInvalidation), and no S3 API invalidates a distribution's cache. Second, 'CreateDeployment' is not a native aws.apigateway EventBridge detail-type either; it only reaches EventBridge via CloudTrail. So the solution fails on both the trigger and the invalidation mechanism.","why_zh":"兩處缺陷。第一，使 CloudFront 快取失效不能用「S3 API」完成；快取失效是 CloudFront 的操作（CreateInvalidation），沒有任何 S3 API 可使發佈的快取失效。第二，'CreateDeployment' 同樣不是原生的 aws.apigateway EventBridge detail-type，只會經由 CloudTrail 抵達 EventBridge。因此此方案在觸發來源與失效機制上皆失敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-invoke-lambda-function.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-apigateway.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/generate-javascript-sdk-of-an-api.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/Invalidation_Requests.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":91,"question_en":"A company has developed an AWS Lambda function that handles orders received through an API. The company is using AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the Lambda function as the final stage of a CI/CD pipeline. A DevOps engineer has noticed there are intermittent failures of the ordering API for a few seconds after deployment. After some investigation, the DevOps engineer believes the failures are due to database changes not having fully propagated before the Lambda function is invoked. How should the DevOps engineer overcome this?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于处理通过 API 接收的订单。该公司正在使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将 Lambda 函数作为 CI/CD 管道的最后阶段进行部署。 一位 DevOps 工程师注意到，在部署后，订单 API 会出现间歇性的故障，每次持续几秒钟。经过一番调查， 该 DevOps 工程师认为故障是由于在调用 Lambda 函数之前，数据库的更改尚未完全传播所致。 DevOps 工程师应如何克服这一难题？","options_en":{"A":"Add a BeforeAllowTraffic hook to the AppSpec file that tests and waits for any necessary database changes before traffic can flow to the new version of the Lambda function.","B":"Add an AfterAllowTraffic hook to the AppSpec file that forces traffic to wait for any pending database changes before allowing the new version of the Lambda function to respond.","C":"Add a BeforeInstall hook to the AppSpec file that tests and waits for any necessary database changes before deploying the new version of the Lambda function.","D":"Add a ValidateService hook to the AppSpec file that inspects incoming traffic and rejects the payload if dependent services, such as the database, are not yet ready."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AppSpec 文件中添加一个 BeforeAllowTraffic 钩子，用于测试并等待任何必要的数据库更改完 成，然后再允许流量流向新版本的 Lambda 函数。","B":"在 AppSpec 文件中添加一个 AfterAllowTraffic 钩子，强制流量在允许新版本的 Lambda 函数响应之 前等待任何未完成的数据库更改。","C":"在 AppSpec 文件中添加一个 BeforeInstall 钩子，用于测试并等待任何必要的数据库更改，然后再部 署 Lambda 函数的新版本。","D":"在 AppSpec 文件中添加一个 ValidateService 钩子，用于检查传入的流量，如果依赖的服务（如数据 库）尚未准备好，则拒绝负载。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"For an AWS Lambda deployment, CodeDeploy supports exactly two AppSpec lifecycle event hooks: BeforeAllowTraffic and AfterAllowTraffic. The AWS docs state BeforeAllowTraffic is used 'to run tasks before traffic is shifted to the deployed Lambda function version,' which is exactly where the engineer should test for and wait on dependent database changes to fully propagate before the new version starts serving requests. The hook is implemented as a validation Lambda function that calls putLifecycleEventHookExecutionStatus with Succeeded or Failed; if it does not report success (or fails to respond within one hour), the deployment is stopped and rolled back, so traffic only flows once the database is ready. AfterAllowTraffic runs after all traffic has already shifted to the new version, which is too late to prevent the intermittent post-deployment failures, so option B is wrong. BeforeInstall and ValidateService are not valid hooks for the Lambda compute platform (they belong to ECS and/or EC2/on-premises), so options C and D are invalid for this scenario.","explanation_zh":"對於 AWS Lambda 部署，CodeDeploy 在 AppSpec 檔案中僅支援兩個生命週期事件 hook：BeforeAllowTraffic 與 AfterAllowTraffic。AWS 文件明確說明 BeforeAllowTraffic 用於「在流量切換到已部署的 Lambda function 版本之前執行任務」，因此這正是工程師應該測試並等待相依資料庫變更完全傳播、再讓新版本開始處理請求的位置。此 hook 是以一個驗證用 Lambda function 實作，會呼叫 putLifecycleEventHookExecutionStatus 回報 Succeeded 或 Failed；若未回報成功（或在一小時內未回應），部署會停止並回滾，因此只有在資料庫就緒後流量才會切換。AfterAllowTraffic 在所有流量都已切換到新版本之後才執行，太晚而無法防止部署後的間歇性失敗，所以選項 B 錯誤。BeforeInstall 與 ValidateService 對 Lambda 計算平台而言並非有效的 hook（它們屬於 ECS 與／或 EC2/on-premises），因此選項 C 與 D 在此情境中無效。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AfterAllowTraffic is a valid Lambda hook, but it runs after all traffic has already been shifted to the new function version, so it cannot prevent the intermittent failures that occur immediately after deployment. The description ('forces traffic to wait before allowing the new version to respond') also misstates what AfterAllowTraffic actually does.","why_zh":"AfterAllowTraffic 雖然是有效的 Lambda hook，但它在所有流量都已切換到新版本之後才執行，因此無法防止部署後立即發生的間歇性失敗。其描述（「強制流量等待，再允許新版本回應」）也錯誤地描述了 AfterAllowTraffic 的實際作用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"BeforeInstall is not a lifecycle hook available for the AWS Lambda compute platform; it exists only for Amazon ECS and EC2/on-premises deployments. The Lambda AppSpec hooks section lists only BeforeAllowTraffic and AfterAllowTraffic.","why_zh":"BeforeInstall 並非 AWS Lambda 計算平台可用的生命週期 hook，它僅存在於 Amazon ECS 與 EC2/on-premises 部署。Lambda 的 AppSpec hooks 章節只列出 BeforeAllowTraffic 與 AfterAllowTraffic。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ValidateService is not a valid hook for the Lambda compute platform (it is an EC2/on-premises hook), and CodeDeploy hooks do not inspect or reject individual request payloads at runtime; they are validation functions run once per deployment lifecycle event. The valid Lambda hooks are only BeforeAllowTraffic and AfterAllowTraffic.","why_zh":"ValidateService 並非 Lambda 計算平台的有效 hook（它是 EC2/on-premises 的 hook），而且 CodeDeploy hook 不會在執行期間檢查或拒絕個別請求 payload；它們是每個部署生命週期事件只執行一次的驗證函式。Lambda 的有效 hook 只有 BeforeAllowTraffic 與 AfterAllowTraffic。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-example.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":92,"question_en":"A company uses a single AWS account to test applications on Amazon EC2 instances. The company has turned on AWS Config in the AWS account and has activated the restricted-ssh AWS Config managed rule. The company needs an automated monitoring solution that will provide a customized notification in real time if any security group in the account is not compliant with the restricted-ssh rule. The customized notification must contain the name and ID of the noncompliant security group. A DevOps engineer creates an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic in the account and subscribes the appropriate personnel to the topic. What should the DevOps engineer do next to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用单个 AWS 账户在 Amazon EC2 实例上测试应用程序。该公司已在该 AWS 账户中启用 AWS Config，并激活了受限 SSH 的 AWS Config 管理规则。 该公司需要一个自动化监控解决方案，如果账户中的任何安全组不符合受限 SSH 规则，该方案应能实时 提供定制通知。定制通知必须包含不符合规则的安全组的名称和 ID。 一位 DevOps 工程师在账户中创建了一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，并将相关人员订阅 到该主题。 为了满足这些要求，DevOps 工程师接下来应该怎么做？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches an AWS Config evaluation result of NON_COMPLIANT for the restricted-ssh rule. Configure an input transformer for the EventBridge rule. Configure the EventBridge rule to publish a notification to the SNS topic.","B":"Configure AWS Config to send all evaluation results for the restricted-ssh rule to the SNS topic. Configure a filter policy on the SNS topic to send only notifications that contain the text of NON_COMPLIANT in the notification to subscribers.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches an AWS Config evaluation result of NON_COMPLIANT for the restricted-ssh rule. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke AWS Systems Manager Run Command on the SNS topic to customize a notification and to publish the notification to the SNS topic.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches all AWS Config evaluation results of NON_COMPLIANT. Configure an input transformer for the restricted-ssh rule. Configure the EventBridge rule to publish a notification to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其与针对 restricted-ssh 规则的 AWS Config 评估结果为“不合规” 相匹配。为 EventBridge 规则配置输入转换器。配置 EventBridge 规则以向 SNS 主题发布通知。","B":"配置 AWS Config 将受限 SSH 规则的所有评估结果发送到 SNS 主题。在 SNS 主题上配置一个过 滤策略，仅向订阅者发送通知中包含“NON_COMPLIANT”文本的通知。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则与 AWS Config 对受限 SSH 规则的评估结果为“不合规”相 匹配。配置 EventBridge 规则，使其在 SNS 主题上调用 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 来自定义 通知，并将通知发布到 SNS 主题。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，匹配所有 AWS Config 评估结果为“不合规”的情况。为 受限 SSH 规则配置输入转换器。配置 EventBridge 规则以向 SNS 主题发布通知。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config sends a 'Config Rules Compliance Change' event directly to Amazon EventBridge with source aws.config. The event detail contains configRuleName (restricted-ssh), resourceType, resourceId (the security group ID), and newEvaluationResult.complianceType (NON_COMPLIANT), so a single EventBridge rule can both filter on the restricted-ssh rule being NON_COMPLIANT (using the event pattern) and extract the security group identifiers. An EventBridge input transformer is the AWS-documented mechanism to customize the text sent to a target: it uses JSON paths to map values from the original event into a custom input template, letting the engineer include the security group name and ID in the notification before publishing to the SNS topic. Because the EventBridge rule reacts to the compliance-change event the moment AWS Config records it, the notification is delivered in real time. This is exactly option A.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 會將 'Config Rules Compliance Change' 事件以 source aws.config 直接送到 Amazon EventBridge。事件的 detail 內含 configRuleName（restricted-ssh）、resourceType、resourceId（即 security group ID）與 newEvaluationResult.complianceType（NON_COMPLIANT），因此單一 EventBridge rule 可在 event pattern 中同時針對 restricted-ssh 規則為 NON_COMPLIANT 進行比對，並擷取 security group 的識別資訊。EventBridge input transformer 是 AWS 官方文件記載用來自訂送往目標文字的機制，它透過 JSON path 將原始事件的值對應到自訂 input template，讓工程師能在發布到 SNS topic 前把 security group 名稱與 ID 放入通知內容。由於 EventBridge rule 在 AWS Config 記錄合規變更的當下即觸發，通知為即時送達。這正是選項 A。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An SNS filter policy evaluates message attributes (or, with payload-based filtering, structured JSON), not arbitrary free-form text, and it can only decide whether to deliver a message to a subscriber — it cannot transform or reformat the message. It therefore cannot build a customized notification containing the security group name and ID. Filtering also cannot add fields that are not already present.","why_zh":"SNS filter policy 是依 message attributes（或在 payload-based filtering 下依結構化 JSON）過濾，而非任意自由文字，且它只能決定是否將訊息送給訂閱者，無法轉換或重新格式化訊息。因此它無法建立含 security group 名稱與 ID 的自訂通知，過濾也無法新增原本不存在的欄位。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager Run Command executes commands on managed nodes / EC2 instances, not 'on an SNS topic.' An SNS topic cannot be a Run Command target, so this configuration is invalid and cannot produce or publish a notification. EventBridge also does not invoke Run Command against a topic.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Run Command 是在受管節點／EC2 執行個體上執行指令，並非『在 SNS topic 上』執行。SNS topic 無法作為 Run Command 的目標，因此此設定無效，無法產生或發布通知；EventBridge 也不會對 topic 呼叫 Run Command。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The scoping is placed in the wrong component. The event pattern matches all NON_COMPLIANT results instead of restricting to the restricted-ssh rule, and an input transformer only customizes the output text — it cannot filter or scope events. As a result notifications would fire for every noncompliant Config rule, not just restricted-ssh. Option A correctly puts the rule-name filter in the event pattern.","why_zh":"限定條件被放在錯誤的元件上。event pattern 比對所有 NON_COMPLIANT 結果，而未限定為 restricted-ssh 規則，且 input transformer 只能自訂輸出文字，無法過濾或限定事件。如此一來每個不合規的 Config 規則都會觸發通知，而非只有 restricted-ssh。選項 A 正確地把規則名稱過濾放在 event pattern 中。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/example-config-rule-compliance-notification.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-transform-target-input.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-input-transformer-tutorial.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":93,"question_en":"A company requires an RPO of 2 hours and an RTO of 10 minutes for its data and application at all times. An application uses a MySQL database and Amazon EC2 web servers. The development team needs a strategy for failover and disaster recovery. Which combination of deployment strategies will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"该公司要求其数据和应用程序在任何时候的恢复点目标（RPO）为 2 小时，恢复时间目标（RTO）为 10 分钟。 该应用程序使用 MySQL 数据库和亚马逊 EC2 网络服务器。开发团队需要制定故障转移和灾难恢复 策略。 哪种部署策略组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Aurora cluster in one Availability Zone across multiple Regions as the data store. Use Aurora’s automatic recovery capabilities in the event of a disaster.","B":"Create an Amazon Aurora global database in two Regions as the data store. In the event of a failure, promote the secondary Region as the primary for the application.","C":"Create an Amazon Aurora multi-master cluster across multiple Regions as the data store. Use a Network Load Balancer to balance the database traffic in different Regions.","D":"Set up the application in two Regions and use Amazon Route 53 failover-based routing that points to the Application Load Balancers in both Regions. Use health checks to determine the availability in a given Region. Use Auto Scaling groups in each Region to adjust capacity based on demand.","E":"Set up the application in two Regions and use a multi-Region Auto Scaling group behind Application Load Balancers to manage the capacity based on demand. In the event of a disaster, adjust the Auto Scaling group’s desired instance count to increase baseline capacity in the failover Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"在多个区域中的一个可用区创建 Amazon Aurora 集群作为数据存储。在发生灾难时，利用 Aurora 的自动恢复功能。","B":"在两个区域创建一个 Amazon Aurora 全球数据库作为数据存储。在出现故障时，将备用区域提升 为应用程序的主区域。","C":"在多个区域创建 Amazon Aurora 多主集群作为数据存储。使用网络负载均衡器来平衡不同区 域的数据库流量。","D":"在两个区域设置应用程序，并使用基于 Amazon Route 53 故障转移的路由，该路由指向两个区域 中的应用负载均衡器。使用健康检查来确定给定区域的可用性。在每个区域使用自动扩展组根 据需求调整容量。","E":"在两个区域设置应用程序，并在应用程序负载均衡器后面使用多区域自动扩展组来根据需求管理 容量。在发生灾难时，调整自动扩展组的期望实例数以增加故障转移区域的基线容量。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The RPO (2 hours) and RTO (10 minutes) targets must be met for both the data tier and the application tier, so the two correct answers cover each tier. For data, an Amazon Aurora global database spanning two Regions (Option B) replicates from the primary Region to a secondary Region with typically sub-second lag; AWS documentation states that for an Aurora global database the RPO is 'typically measured in seconds' and the RTO 'can be in the order of minutes,' achieved by promoting (failing over) a secondary DB cluster to become the new primary, which easily satisfies RPO 2h / RTO 10m. For the application, deploying EC2 web servers behind Application Load Balancers in two Regions with Route 53 failover-based (active-passive) routing and health checks (Option D) lets Route 53 detect the unhealthy primary Region and shift DNS to the standby Region, while the per-Region Auto Scaling groups adjust capacity, meeting the 10-minute RTO. Options A, C, and E describe configurations that cannot exist: a single Availability Zone cannot span multiple Regions (A); Aurora multi-master is a single-Region-only feature and a Network Load Balancer cannot balance cross-Region database writes (C); and there is no 'multi-Region Auto Scaling group' and an ALB cannot front instances across Regions (E).","explanation_zh":"RPO (2 小時) 與 RTO (10 分鐘) 必須同時滿足資料層與應用層，因此兩個正確答案分別涵蓋這兩層。資料層方面，橫跨兩個 Region 的 Amazon Aurora global database (選項 B) 會從主要 Region 以通常低於一秒的延遲非同步複寫到次要 Region；AWS 文件指出 Aurora global database 的 RPO「通常以秒為單位衡量」，RTO「可達到分鐘等級」，方式是將次要 DB cluster 提升 (failover) 為新的主要叢集，輕鬆滿足 RPO 2h / RTO 10m。應用層方面，在兩個 Region 以 Application Load Balancer 後端部署 EC2 web 伺服器，並使用 Route 53 failover (active-passive) 路由搭配 health checks (選項 D)，可讓 Route 53 偵測到不健康的主要 Region 並將 DNS 切換到待命 Region，同時各 Region 的 Auto Scaling group 依需求調整容量，滿足 10 分鐘的 RTO。選項 A、C、E 描述的是不存在或無法運作的組態：單一 Availability Zone 無法橫跨多個 Region (A)；Aurora multi-master 僅限單一 Region，且 Network Load Balancer 無法平衡跨 Region 的資料庫寫入 (C)；亦不存在「multi-Region Auto Scaling group」，且 ALB 無法跨 Region 將流量導向執行個體 (E)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Self-contradictory: a single Availability Zone exists within one Region and cannot span multiple Regions. Aurora's automatic recovery is within-Region (Multi-AZ) high availability, not cross-Region disaster recovery, so it does not provide the Regional failover this scenario requires.","why_zh":"自相矛盾：單一 Availability Zone 位於單一 Region 內，無法橫跨多個 Region。Aurora 的自動復原屬於 Region 內 (Multi-AZ) 的高可用性，而非跨 Region 的災難復原，因此無法提供本情境所需的跨 Region 容錯移轉。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Aurora multi-master is a single-Region-only feature (now deprecated) and cannot be deployed across multiple Regions. A Network Load Balancer operates within a single Region/VPC and cannot balance cross-Region database write traffic, so this architecture is technically invalid.","why_zh":"Aurora multi-master 僅限單一 Region (現已淘汰)，無法跨多個 Region 部署。Network Load Balancer 在單一 Region/VPC 內運作，無法平衡跨 Region 的資料庫寫入流量，因此此架構技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"There is no such thing as a 'multi-Region Auto Scaling group'; an EC2 Auto Scaling group is a regional construct that distributes instances only across Availability Zones within one Region, and an Application Load Balancer can only target instances in its own Region/VPC. Manually adjusting desired capacity after a disaster also provides no automated DNS/traffic failover, so it cannot meet a 10-minute RTO.","why_zh":"不存在所謂「multi-Region Auto Scaling group」；EC2 Auto Scaling group 是 Region 範圍的構件，只能在單一 Region 內的各 Availability Zone 之間分配執行個體，而 Application Load Balancer 只能將流量導向自身 Region/VPC 內的執行個體。災難後手動調整 desired capacity 也無法提供自動的 DNS/流量容錯，因此無法滿足 10 分鐘的 RTO。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-disaster-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-configuring.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/auto-scaling-groups.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":94,"question_en":"A business has an application that consists of five independent AWS Lambda functions. The DevOps engineer has built a CI/CD pipeline using AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild that builds, tests, packages, and deploys each Lambda function in sequence. The pipeline uses an Amazon EventBridge rule to ensure the pipeline starts as quickly as possible after a change is made to the application source code. After working with the pipeline for a few months, the DevOps engineer has noticed the pipeline takes too long to complete. What should the DevOps engineer implement to BEST improve the speed of the pipeline?","question_zh":"一家企业有一个应用程序，该程序由五个独立的 AWS Lambda 函数组成。 该 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 构建了一个 CI/CD 管道，依次构建、测 试、打包和部署每个 Lambda 函数。该管道使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则来确保在对应用程序源代码 进行更改后，管道能尽快启动。 在使用该流水线几个月后，DevOps 工程师注意到流水线完成所需的时间太长。 DevOps 工程师应实施什么措施才能最大程度地提高流水线的速度？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the CodeBuild projects within the pipeline to use a compute type with more available network throughput.","B":"Create a custom CodeBuild execution environment that includes a symmetric multiprocessing configuration to run the builds in parallel.","C":"Modify the CodePipeline configuration to run actions for each Lambda function in parallel by specifying the same runOrder.","D":"Modify each CodeBuild project to run within a VPC and use dedicated instances to increase throughput."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改流水线中的 CodeBuild 项目，使其使用具有更高可用网络吞吐量的计算类型。","B":"创建一个自定义的 CodeBuild 执行环境，其中包含对称多处理配置，以便并行运行构建任 务。","C":"通过指定相同的运行顺序，修改 CodePipeline 配置，以并行运行每个 Lambda 函数的操作。","D":"将每个 CodeBuild 项目修改为在 VPC 内运行，并使用专用实例来提高吞吐量。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The five Lambda functions are independent, but the pipeline builds, tests, packages, and deploys each one in sequence, so total pipeline time is the sum of all five flows. In a CodePipeline stage the runOrder field controls execution order: per the action structure reference, 'Parallel actions in the stage are shown as having the same integer' and 'To specify parallel actions, use the same integer for each action you want to run in parallel.' Assigning the same runOrder to each function's action runs all five concurrently, dropping total time to roughly the slowest single flow instead of the sum. Because the functions have no inter-dependencies, this parallelization is safe and directly removes the serialization bottleneck, making it the BEST way to speed up the pipeline. The other options change compute characteristics (network, CPU, VPC) that are not the actual bottleneck and would add little benefit or even slow the pipeline down.","explanation_zh":"這五個 Lambda 函式彼此獨立，但 pipeline 是依序 (in sequence) 對每一個進行 build、test、package、deploy，因此總時間是五條流程的加總，這正是緩慢的根本原因。在 CodePipeline 的 stage 中，runOrder 欄位控制執行順序：依官方 action structure reference 所述，「Parallel actions in the stage are shown as having the same integer」，且「To specify parallel actions, use the same integer for each action you want to run in parallel」。把每個函式的 action 設成相同的 runOrder，五個 action 即會同時並行執行，總時間從加總降為約等於最慢的單一流程。由於這些函式之間沒有相依性，這樣並行化是安全的，並直接消除了序列化瓶頸，因此是加速 pipeline 的最佳作法。其他選項只是改變運算特性（網路、CPU、VPC），都不是真正的瓶頸，效益極低甚至會拖慢 pipeline。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Lambda deployment packages are small, so network throughput is not the bottleneck. A higher-network compute type does nothing to address the actual problem, which is that the five independent functions are processed one after another.","why_zh":"Lambda 部署套件很小，網路吞吐量並非瓶頸。提供更高網路吞吐的 compute type 完全無法解決真正的問題，也就是五個獨立函式被依序逐一處理。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A custom CodeBuild environment with 'symmetric multiprocessing' to run builds in parallel inside one build is fabricated terminology, not a real CodeBuild feature, and does not change the pipeline's stage/action sequencing. The bottleneck is the serial pipeline flow across functions, not single-build CPU parallelism.","why_zh":"以『對稱多處理 (SMP)』自訂 CodeBuild 環境在單一 build 內平行執行是杜撰的說法，並非真實的 CodeBuild 功能，且無法改變 pipeline 的 stage/action 順序。瓶頸在於跨函式的序列化流程，而非單一 build 的 CPU 平行度。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeBuild does not run on customer 'dedicated instances,' and placing builds in a VPC generally adds ENI/startup latency rather than increasing throughput. It also does nothing to parallelize the serially executed functions.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 並非執行在客戶的『專用執行個體 (dedicated instances)』上，而將 build 放進 VPC 通常會增加 ENI/啟動延遲而非提升吞吐量。它同樣無法讓序列化執行的函式平行化。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-requirements.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/reference-pipeline-structure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/concepts.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":95,"question_en":"A company uses AWS CloudFormation stacks to deploy updates to its application. The stacks consist of different resources. The resources include AWS Auto Scaling groups, Amazon EC2 instances, Application Load Balancers (ALBs), and other resources that are necessary to launch and maintain independent stacks. Changes to application resources outside of CloudFormation stack updates are not allowed. The company recently attempted to update the application stack by using the AWS CLI. The stack failed to update and produced the following error message: “ERROR: both the deployment and the CloudFormation stack rollback failed. The deployment failed because the following resource(s) failed to update: [AutoScalingGroup].” The stack remains in a status of UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED. Which solution will resolve this issue?","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来部署其应用程序的更新。这些堆栈包含不同的资源，其中包 括 AWS 自动扩展组、Amazon EC2 实例、应用负载均衡器（ALB）以及其他用于启动和维护独立堆 栈所必需的资源。不允许在 CloudFormation 堆栈更新之外对应用程序资源进行更改。 该公司最近尝试使用 AWS 命令行界面更新应用程序堆栈，但更新失败，并产生了以下错误消息： “错误：部署和 CloudFormation 堆栈回滚均失败。部署失败是因为以下资源更新失败： “自动缩放组。” 该堆栈仍处于“更新回滚失败”的状态。 哪种解决方案能解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Update the subnet mappings that are configured for the ALBs. Run the aws cloudformation update- stack-set AWS CLI command.","B":"Update the IAM role by providing the necessary permissions to update the stack. Run the aws cloudformation continue-update-rollback AWS CLI command.","C":"Submit a request for a quota increase for the number of EC2 instances for the account. Run the aws cloudformation cancel-update-stack AWS CLI command.","D":"Delete the Auto Scaling group resource. Run the aws cloudformation rollback-stack AWS CLI command."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新为应用负载均衡器（ALB）配置的子网映射。运行 aws cloudformation updatestack-set AWS CLI 命令。","B":"通过提供更新堆栈所需的权限来更新 IAM 角色。运行 aws cloudformation continue-update-rollback AWS CLI 命令。","C":"为账户提交增加 EC2 实例数量配额的请求。运行 aws cloudformation cancel-update-stack AWS CLI 命令。","D":"删除自动扩展组资源。运行 aws cloudformation rollback-stack AWS CLI 命令。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The stack is stuck in UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED, which can only be recovered with the continue-update-rollback operation (CLI: aws cloudformation continue-update-rollback), which transitions the stack to UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE so it can be updated again. The error names the AutoScalingGroup as the resource that failed to update during the rollback. AWS's official 'Update rollback failed' troubleshooting section lists several causes, and for 'Insufficient permissions' it states: 'Check that you have sufficient IAM permissions to modify resources, and then continue the update rollback.' Option B performs exactly these two steps -- grant the missing IAM permissions, then run continue-update-rollback -- and does so entirely through CloudFormation, which honors the constraint that no out-of-band changes to resources are allowed. The other options either use a CLI command that is invalid for UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED (cancel-update-stack only works during UPDATE_IN_PROGRESS; rollback-stack is for stable failure states such as CREATE_FAILED/UPDATE_FAILED) or perform unrelated and out-of-band actions.","explanation_zh":"Stack 卡在 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 狀態，唯一能恢復的方式是執行 continue-update-rollback 操作（CLI: aws cloudformation continue-update-rollback），它會將 stack 轉為 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE，之後才能再次更新。錯誤訊息指出在 rollback 期間 AutoScalingGroup 資源更新失敗。AWS 官方的「Update rollback failed」疑難排解章節列出多種原因，其中「Insufficient permissions」的建議是：確認你擁有足夠的 IAM 權限去修改資源，然後 continue the update rollback。選項 B 正好執行這兩個步驟──補足缺少的 IAM 權限，再執行 continue-update-rollback──且完全透過 CloudFormation 完成，符合「不允許在 CloudFormation 之外變更資源」的限制。其他選項要麼使用對 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 無效的 CLI 指令（cancel-update-stack 只在 UPDATE_IN_PROGRESS 期間有效；rollback-stack 用於 CREATE_FAILED/UPDATE_FAILED 等穩定的失敗狀態），要麼執行無關或屬於 out-of-band 的動作。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"update-stack-set targets CloudFormation StackSets (multi-account/region deployments), not a single failed stack, and changing ALB subnet mappings does not address the AutoScalingGroup that failed during rollback. It does nothing to move the stack out of UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED.","why_zh":"update-stack-set 針對的是 CloudFormation StackSets（跨帳號/區域部署），而非單一失敗的 stack；變更 ALB 的 subnet mappings 也無法解決 rollback 期間失敗的 AutoScalingGroup，完全無法讓 stack 脫離 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A quota (limitation) error is a real listed cause, but the command is wrong: cancel-update-stack only works while a stack is UPDATE_IN_PROGRESS, not when it is already UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED. The correct recovery for a limitation error is to free resources or raise the quota and then run continue-update-rollback. The mismatched command makes this option invalid.","why_zh":"配額（limitation）錯誤確實是文件列出的原因之一，但指令錯誤：cancel-update-stack 只能在 stack 處於 UPDATE_IN_PROGRESS 時使用，無法用於已經進入 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 的 stack。針對 limitation 錯誤的正確做法是釋放資源或提高配額後執行 continue-update-rollback，因此這個指令搭配是無效的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"rollback-stack re-initiates a rollback only for stacks in a stable failure state such as CREATE_FAILED or UPDATE_FAILED (typically with rollback previously disabled), not UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED. Deleting the Auto Scaling group also makes an out-of-band change to a resource, which the scenario explicitly forbids and which AWS warns can leave the stack unrecoverable.","why_zh":"rollback-stack 只能對處於穩定失敗狀態（例如 CREATE_FAILED 或 UPDATE_FAILED，通常是先前停用 rollback）的 stack 重新觸發 rollback，無法用於 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED。此外刪除 Auto Scaling group 屬於在 CloudFormation 之外變更資源（out-of-band），題目明確禁止，AWS 也警告這可能使 stack 進入無法復原狀態。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-updating-stacks-continueupdaterollback.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-stack-update-cancel.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/APIReference/API_ContinueUpdateRollback.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/cloudformation/continue-update-rollback.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":96,"question_en":"A company is deploying a new application that uses Amazon EC2 instances. The company needs a solution to query application logs and AWS account API activity. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在部署一个使用亚马逊 EC2 实例的新应用程序。该公司需要一个解决方案来查询应用程 序日志和 AWS 账户的 API 活动。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to send logs from the EC2 instances to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Configure AWS CloudTrail to deliver the API logs to Amazon S3. Use CloudWatch to query both sets of logs.","B":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to send logs from the EC2 instances to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Configure AWS CloudTrail to deliver the API logs to CloudWatch Logs. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to query both sets of logs.","C":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to send logs from the EC2 instances to Amazon Kinesis. Configure AWS CloudTrail to deliver the API logs to Kinesis. Use Kinesis to load the data into Amazon Redshift. Use Amazon Redshift to query both sets of logs.","D":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to send logs from the EC2 instances to Amazon S3. Use AWS CloudTrail to deliver the API logs to Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena to query both sets of logs in Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理将 EC2 实例的日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。配置 AWS CloudTrail 将 API 日志交付到 Amazon S3。使用 CloudWatch 查询这两组日志。","B":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理将 EC2 实例的日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。配置 AWS CloudTrail 将 API 日志传递到 CloudWatch Logs。使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询这两组日志。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理将 EC2 实例的日志发送到 Amazon Kinesis。配置 AWS CloudTrail 将 API 日 志传递到 Kinesis。使用 Kinesis 将数据加载到 Amazon Redshift 中。使用 Amazon Redshift 查询这两组日 志。","D":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理将 EC2 实例的日志发送到 Amazon S3。使用 AWS CloudTrail 将 API 日 志交付到 Amazon S3。使用 Amazon Athena 查询 Amazon S3 中的这两组日志。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a single solution that can query both EC2 application logs and AWS account API activity. Option B satisfies this with native integrations and one query engine. The Amazon CloudWatch agent collects application and system logs from EC2 instances and sends them to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. AWS CloudTrail has a built-in feature to deliver management, data, and Insights events (the AWS account API activity) directly to a CloudWatch Logs log group. With both log sets consolidated in CloudWatch Logs, CloudWatch Logs Insights can interactively search and analyze them; it automatically discovers log fields from AWS services such as AWS CloudTrail, so it can query the API logs and the application logs together across log groups. This is the least-overhead working design because it relies entirely on documented, native integrations and a single store.","explanation_zh":"需求是用單一方案同時查詢 EC2 應用程式日誌與 AWS 帳戶 API 活動。選項 B 透過原生整合與單一查詢引擎滿足此需求。Amazon CloudWatch agent 會從 EC2 執行個體收集應用程式與系統日誌並傳送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。AWS CloudTrail 具有內建功能,可將 management、data 與 Insights 事件(即 AWS 帳戶 API 活動)直接傳遞到 CloudWatch Logs 的 log group。當兩組日誌都集中在 CloudWatch Logs 後,CloudWatch Logs Insights 可互動式搜尋與分析;它會自動探索來自 AWS 服務(例如 AWS CloudTrail)的日誌欄位,因此能跨 log group 同時查詢 API 日誌與應用程式日誌。這是營運負擔最低且可行的設計,因為完全依賴有文件支援的原生整合與單一儲存體。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudTrail is delivered to Amazon S3, but the answer then says to use CloudWatch to query both sets of logs. CloudWatch and CloudWatch Logs Insights cannot query log files that reside in an S3 bucket, so the two stores cannot be queried by a single CloudWatch query engine. The design is internally inconsistent and fails the single-solution requirement.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 被傳遞到 Amazon S3,但答案接著說用 CloudWatch 查詢兩組日誌。CloudWatch 與 CloudWatch Logs Insights 無法查詢位於 S3 儲存貯體中的日誌檔,因此兩個儲存體無法由單一 CloudWatch 查詢引擎查詢。此設計自相矛盾,無法滿足單一方案需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The CloudWatch agent does not send logs directly to Amazon Kinesis; its log destination is CloudWatch Logs. Building a Kinesis-to-Redshift pipeline to query logs is far more operational overhead than needed and uses non-native paths, so it is incorrect.","why_zh":"CloudWatch agent 不會直接將日誌送往 Amazon Kinesis,其日誌目的地是 CloudWatch Logs。建立 Kinesis 到 Redshift 的管線來查詢日誌,其營運負擔遠超所需且使用非原生路徑,故不正確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The CloudWatch agent cannot send logs directly to Amazon S3; its log destination is CloudWatch Logs. While CloudTrail can deliver to S3 and Athena can query S3, the agent-to-S3 premise is invalid, so this solution does not actually work as described.","why_zh":"CloudWatch agent 無法直接將日誌送往 Amazon S3,其日誌目的地是 CloudWatch Logs。雖然 CloudTrail 可傳遞到 S3 且 Athena 可查詢 S3,但 agent 到 S3 的前提無效,因此此方案實際上無法如所述運作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/send-cloudtrail-events-to-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Install-CloudWatch-Agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/WhatIsCloudWatchLogs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":97,"question_en":"A company wants to ensure that their EC2 instances are secure. They want to be notified if any new vulnerabilities are discovered on their instances, and they also want an audit trail of all login activities on the instances. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望确保其 EC2 实例的安全。他们希望在实例上发现任何新的漏洞时能收到通知，并且还希望 对实例上的所有登录活动进行审计跟踪。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager to detect vulnerabilities on the EC2 instances. Install the Amazon Kinesis Agent to capture system logs and deliver them to Amazon S3.","B":"Use AWS Systems Manager to detect vulnerabilities on the EC2 instances. Install the Systems Manager Agent to capture system logs and view login activity in the CloudTrail console.","C":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch to detect vulnerabilities on the EC2 instances. Install the AWS Config daemon to capture system logs and view them in the AWS Config console.","D":"Configure Amazon Inspector to detect vulnerabilities on the EC2 instances. Install the Amazon CloudWatch Agent to capture system logs and record them via Amazon CloudWatch Logs."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 检测 EC2 实例上的漏洞。安装 Amazon Kinesis Agent 以捕获系统日志并将其 交付到 Amazon S3。","B":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 检测 EC2 实例上的漏洞。安装 Systems Manager 代理以捕获系统日志， 并在 CloudTrail 控制台中查看登录活动。","C":"配置 Amazon CloudWatch 以检测 EC2 实例上的漏洞。安装 AWS Config 守护进程以捕获系统日志，并在 AWS Config 控制台中查看这些日志。","D":"配置 Amazon Inspector 以检测 EC2 实例上的漏洞。安装 Amazon 使用 CloudWatch 代理来捕获系统日志，并通过 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 进行记录。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must be satisfied: be notified of new EC2 vulnerabilities, and keep an audit trail of all login (OS-level) activity. Amazon Inspector is AWS's vulnerability management service that automatically and continuously scans EC2 instances for software vulnerabilities (CVEs) and produces a finding for each issue; these findings can be routed to EventBridge and SNS for notifications, satisfying the vulnerability requirement. The Amazon CloudWatch Agent collects OS-level system logs from Linux/Windows EC2 instances (such as /var/log/secure or /var/log/auth.log, which record SSH/console login activity) and stores them in Amazon CloudWatch Logs, providing the login audit trail. Option D pairs the correct service for each requirement. No other option uses a genuine vulnerability-scanning service, and the alternatives misuse CloudTrail or AWS Config for OS-level login logs.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個需求：當 EC2 出現新弱點時收到通知，以及保留所有登入（作業系統層級）活動的稽核軌跡。Amazon Inspector 是 AWS 的弱點管理服務，會自動且持續掃描 EC2 執行個體的軟體弱點（CVE）並為每個問題產生 finding；這些 findings 可送往 EventBridge 與 SNS 觸發通知，滿足弱點偵測需求。Amazon CloudWatch Agent 會收集 Linux/Windows EC2 執行個體的作業系統層級系統日誌（例如記錄 SSH/主控台登入活動的 /var/log/secure 或 /var/log/auth.log），並儲存到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，提供登入稽核軌跡。選項 D 為每個需求搭配了正確的服務。其餘選項都未使用真正的弱點掃描服務，且誤用 CloudTrail 或 AWS Config 來擷取作業系統層級的登入日誌。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager is not a vulnerability detection service - Patch Manager only reports missing patches/compliance, not CVE vulnerability findings, which is Amazon Inspector's role. Routing system logs through the Amazon Kinesis Agent to Amazon S3 is a non-standard, convoluted pattern for a login audit trail compared with CloudWatch Logs.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager 並非弱點偵測服務：Patch Manager 僅回報缺少的修補程式/合規狀態，而非 CVE 弱點 findings，那是 Amazon Inspector 的職責。透過 Amazon Kinesis Agent 將系統日誌送到 Amazon S3，相較於 CloudWatch Logs 是非標準且繁瑣的登入稽核做法。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Systems Manager does not perform CVE vulnerability detection. More decisively, AWS CloudTrail records AWS API activity (console/CLI/SDK calls against AWS services), NOT OS-level SSH/console login activity on the instance, so you cannot view instance login activity in the CloudTrail console.","why_zh":"Systems Manager 不執行 CVE 弱點偵測。更關鍵的是，AWS CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API 活動（針對 AWS 服務的主控台/CLI/SDK 呼叫），而非執行個體上作業系統層級的 SSH/主控台登入活動，因此無法在 CloudTrail 主控台檢視執行個體登入活動。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon CloudWatch does not detect software vulnerabilities. AWS Config tracks resource configuration changes/compliance, not OS system logs, and there is no 'AWS Config daemon' for capturing OS-level logs.","why_zh":"Amazon CloudWatch 不偵測軟體弱點。AWS Config 追蹤的是資源組態變更/合規狀態，而非作業系統系統日誌，且並不存在用於擷取作業系統層級日誌的『AWS Config daemon』。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/what-is-inspector.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Install-CloudWatch-Agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/install-CloudWatch-Agent-on-EC2-Instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-user-guide.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":98,"question_en":"A company is running an application on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. Recently, an issue occurred that prevented EC2 instances from launching successfully, and it took several hours for the support team to discover the issue. The support team wants to be notified by email whenever an EC2 instance does not start successfully. Which action will accomplish this?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例的自动扩展组中运行应用程序。最近出现了一个问题，导致 EC2 实例无法成 功启动，支持团队花了好几个小时才发现问题所在。支持团队希望每当 EC2 实例启动失败时都能通过电 子邮件收到通知。 哪项行动能达成此目标？","options_en":{"A":"Add a health check to the Auto Scaling group to invoke an AWS Lambda function whenever an instance status is impaired.","B":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to send a notification to an Amazon SNS topic whenever a failed instance launch occurs.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that invokes an AWS Lambda function when a failed AttachInstances Auto Scaling API call is made.","D":"Create a status check alarm on Amazon EC2 to send a notification to an Amazon SNS topic whenever a status check fail occurs."},"options_zh":{"A":"向自动扩展组添加一个健康检查，以便在实例状态受损时调用 AWS Lambda 函数。","B":"将自动扩展组配置为在实例启动失败时向 Amazon SNS 主题发送通知。","C":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，当调用 AttachInstances Auto Scaling API 失败时，该警 报会触发一个 AWS Lambda 函数。","D":"在 Amazon EC2 上创建状态检查警报，以便在状态检查失败时向 Amazon SNS 主题发送通知。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling natively supports Amazon SNS notifications for instance lifecycle events. The supported notification types are autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH (successful launch), autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH_ERROR (failed instance launch), autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATE, and autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATE_ERROR. By configuring the Auto Scaling group to send EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH_ERROR notifications to an SNS topic with an email subscription, the support team is automatically emailed whenever an EC2 instance fails to launch. This is the purpose-built, lowest-overhead mechanism for the exact scenario described and requires no custom Lambda or CloudWatch alarm, so option B is correct.","explanation_zh":"Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 原生支援透過 Amazon SNS 發送執行個體生命週期事件通知。支援的通知類型包含 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH（成功啟動）、autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH_ERROR（啟動失敗）、autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATE 與 autoscaling:EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATE_ERROR。將 Auto Scaling group 設定為在發生 EC2_INSTANCE_LAUNCH_ERROR 時將通知傳送到具有 email 訂閱的 SNS topic，support 團隊即可在 EC2 執行個體啟動失敗時自動收到 email。這是針對此情境最直接、營運負擔最低的內建機制，且不需自訂 Lambda 或 CloudWatch 警報，因此 B 為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Auto Scaling health checks detect already-running instances that become impaired (e.g., failing EC2 status checks or ELB health checks); they do not fire when an instance fails to launch in the first place. Health checks also do not directly invoke Lambda. This does not address launch failures.","why_zh":"Auto Scaling 健康檢查偵測的是已在執行但變為受損的執行個體（例如 EC2 狀態檢查或 ELB 健康檢查失敗），無法在執行個體一開始就啟動失敗時觸發，且健康檢查也無法直接呼叫 Lambda，因此無法解決啟動失敗問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AttachInstances attaches existing EC2 instances to an Auto Scaling group; it is unrelated to the group launching new instances during scaling. A CloudWatch alarm on a failed AttachInstances API call would not detect normal scale-out launch failures, and CloudWatch alarms watch metrics, not arbitrary failed API calls.","why_zh":"AttachInstances 是將既有 EC2 執行個體附加到 Auto Scaling group，與群組在擴展時啟動新執行個體無關。針對失敗的 AttachInstances API 呼叫設定的 CloudWatch 警報無法偵測一般的 scale-out 啟動失敗，且 CloudWatch 警報是監控指標而非任意失敗的 API 呼叫。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EC2 status check alarms only monitor instances that have already launched and are running (instance/system status checks). They cannot detect a launch that never succeeded, because a status check requires a running instance to evaluate. This misses the failed-launch scenario entirely.","why_zh":"EC2 狀態檢查警報僅監控已啟動並執行中的執行個體（執行個體/系統狀態檢查），無法偵測從未成功的啟動，因為狀態檢查需要有執行中的執行個體才能評估，因此完全無法涵蓋啟動失敗的情境。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-sns-notifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ts-as-instancelaunchfailure.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":99,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations to centrally manage its AWS accounts. The company has turned on AWS Config in each member account by using AWS CloudFormation StackSets. The company has configured trusted access in Organizations for AWS Config and has configured a member account as a delegated administrator account for AWS Config. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a new security policy. The policy must require all current and future AWS member accounts to use a common baseline of AWS Config rules that contain remediation actions that are managed from a central account. Non-administrator users who can access member accounts must not be able to modify this common baseline of AWS Config rules that are deployed into each member account. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS Organizations 来集中管理其 AWS 账户。该公司通过使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在每个成员账户中启用了 AWS Config。该公司已在 Organizations 中为 AWS Config 配置了受 信任访问，并将一个成员账户配置为 AWS Config 的委托管理员账户。 DevOps 工程师需要实施一项新的安全策略。该策略必须要求所有当前和未来的 AWS 成员账户使用由 中央账户管理的包含修复操作的通用 AWS Config 规则基线。能够访问成员账户的非管理员用户不得 修改部署到每个成员账户的通用 AWS Config 规则基线。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudFormation template that contains the AWS Config rules and remediation actions. Deploy the template from the Organizations management account by using CloudFormation StackSets.","B":"Create an AWS Config conformance pack that contains the AWS Config rules and remediation actions. Deploy the pack from the Organizations management account by using CloudFormation StackSets.","C":"Create a CloudFormation template that contains the AWS Config rules and remediation actions. Deploy the template from the delegated administrator account by using AWS Config.","D":"Create an AWS Config conformance pack that contains the AWS Config rules and remediation actions. Deploy the pack from the delegated administrator account by using AWS Config."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个包含 AWS Config 规则和修复操作的 CloudFormation 模板。通过使用 CloudFormation StackSets 从组织管理账户部署该模板。","B":"创建一个包含 AWS Config 规则和修复操作的 AWS Config 合规性包。通过使用 CloudFormation StackSets 从组织管理账户部署该包。","C":"创建一个包含 AWS Config 规则和修复操作的 CloudFormation 模板。通过 AWS Config 从委托管理员账 户部署该模板。","D":"创建一个包含 AWS Config 规则和修复操作的 AWS Config 合规性包。通过 AWS Config 从委托管理员 账户部署该包。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"An AWS Config organization conformance pack is purpose-built for this scenario, and is deployed natively through AWS Config (PutOrganizationConformancePack) from the management account or a registered delegated administrator account. The AWS Config docs state you can 'deploy a common set of AWS Config rules and remediation actions across all accounts' (the common baseline plus remediation), that 'if a new account joins an organization, the rule or conformance pack is deployed to that account' (current and future members), and that you can 'enforce governance by ensuring that the underlying AWS Config rules and remediation actions are not modifiable by your organization's member accounts.' The PutOrganizationConformancePack API reference makes the non-modifiable guarantee explicit: it creates the rules and remediation actions in each member account through the AWSServiceRoleForConfigConforms service-linked role, 'even if member account IAM policies explicitly deny these actions,' and only a management account or delegated administrator can call it. Since the question already establishes a registered delegated administrator for AWS Config, option D satisfies the common baseline, the include-future-accounts requirement, and the non-modifiable-by-member-users requirement.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 的 organization conformance pack 正是為此情境設計，且透過 AWS Config 原生機制（PutOrganizationConformancePack）從 management account 或已註冊的 delegated administrator account 部署。AWS Config 文件指出可「在所有帳戶部署一組共同的 AWS Config rules 與 remediation actions」（共同基線加上修復動作）、「當新帳戶加入組織時，rule 或 conformance pack 會自動部署到該帳戶」（涵蓋現有與未來成員帳戶），以及可「透過確保底層的 AWS Config rules 與 remediation actions 無法被組織成員帳戶修改來強制治理」。PutOrganizationConformancePack API 參考更明確保證不可修改性：它透過 AWSServiceRoleForConfigConforms service-linked role 在每個成員帳戶建立 rules 與 remediation actions，「即使成員帳戶的 IAM 政策明確拒絕這些動作」仍可建立，且只有 management account 或 delegated administrator 能呼叫此 API。題目已設定好 AWS Config 的 delegated administrator，因此選項 D 同時滿足共同基線、涵蓋未來帳戶、以及成員帳戶使用者無法修改三項要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deploying a CloudFormation template of AWS Config rules via StackSets from the management account creates ordinary account-level Config rules and remediation configurations in each member account. Those are local resources that account administrators/users with Config permissions can modify or delete, so it fails the must-not-be-modifiable-by-member-users requirement. It also bypasses the delegated administrator model already established for AWS Config.","why_zh":"從 management account 透過 StackSets 部署含 AWS Config rules 的 CloudFormation template，會在每個成員帳戶建立一般帳戶層級的 Config rules 與 remediation configurations。這些是本地資源，擁有 Config 權限的帳戶管理者/使用者可修改或刪除，因此無法滿足成員帳戶不可修改的要求，也繞過了題目已為 AWS Config 設定的 delegated administrator 模型。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Conflates two mechanisms: organization conformance packs are deployed through AWS Config's organization APIs (PutOrganizationConformancePack), not through CloudFormation StackSets. Pushing a regular conformance pack into accounts via StackSets would create independent account-level packs whose rules member admins can modify, failing the governance lock that only the service-linked-role-backed organization deployment provides. The question also designates a delegated administrator, not the management account, as the operating account.","why_zh":"混淆了兩種機制：organization conformance pack 是透過 AWS Config 的 organization API（PutOrganizationConformancePack）部署，而非 CloudFormation StackSets。透過 StackSets 把一般 conformance pack 推送到各帳戶，會建立獨立的帳戶層級 pack，其 rules 可被成員管理者修改，無法達成只有 service-linked role 支撐的組織部署才能提供的治理鎖定。且題目指定的操作帳戶是 delegated administrator，而非 management account。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot deploy a CloudFormation template by using AWS Config; the deployment mechanism is mismatched (templates are deployed via CloudFormation/StackSets, not Config). Even setting that aside, CloudFormation-deployed Config rules and remediation in a member account are local resources that can be modified there, so they do not provide the centrally enforced, non-modifiable baseline the policy requires.","why_zh":"無法用 AWS Config 來部署 CloudFormation template，部署機制不相符（template 是透過 CloudFormation/StackSets 部署，而非 Config）。即使忽略此點，透過 CloudFormation 部署到成員帳戶的 Config rules 與 remediation 是本地資源，可在當地被修改，因此無法提供政策要求的集中強制且不可修改基線。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-pack-organization-apis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-packs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/APIReference/API_PutOrganizationConformancePack.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/APIReference/API_DeleteOrganizationConformancePack.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":100,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer manages a large commercial website that runs on Amazon EC2. The website uses Amazon Kinesis Data Streams to collect and process web logs. The DevOps engineer manages the Kinesis consumer application, which also runs on Amazon EC2. Sudden increases of data cause the Kinesis consumer application to fall behind, and the Kinesis data streams drop records before the records can be processed. The DevOps engineer must implement a solution to improve stream handling. Which solution meets these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师负责管理一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 上的大型商业网站。该网站使用亚马逊 Kinesis 数据流来收集和处理网络日志。这位 DevOps 工程师还负责管理同样运行在亚马逊 EC2 上的 Kinesis 消费者应用程序。 数据量的突然增加导致 Kinesis 消费者应用程序处理滞后，Kinesis 数据流在记录被处理之前就丢弃 了这些记录。DevOps 工程师必须实施解决方案以改进流处理。 哪种解决方案在满足这些要求的同时具有最高的运营效率？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the Kinesis consumer application to store the logs durably in Amazon S3. Use Amazon EMR to process the data directly on Amazon S3 to derive customer insights. Store the results in Amazon S3.","B":"Horizontally scale the Kinesis consumer application by adding more EC2 instances based on the Amazon CloudWatch GetRecords.IteratorAgeMilliseconds metric. Increase the retention period of the Kinesis data streams.","C":"Convert the Kinesis consumer application to run as an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Kinesis data streams as the event source for the Lambda function to process the data streams.","D":"Increase the number of shards in the Kinesis data streams to increase the overall throughput so that the consumer application processes the data faster."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 Kinesis 消费者应用程序，将日志持久存储在 Amazon S3 中。使用 Amazon EMR 直接在 Amazon S3 上处理数据以获取客户洞察。将结果存储在 Amazon S3 中。","B":"根据 Amazon CloudWatch 的 GetRecords.IteratorAgeMilliseconds 指标，通过添加更多 EC2 实例来水 平扩展 Kinesis 消费者应用程序。增加 Kinesis 数据流的保留期。","C":"将 Kinesis 消费者应用程序转换为作为 AWS Lambda 函数运行。将 Kinesis 数据流配置为 Lambda 函 数的事件源，以处理数据流。","D":"增加 Kinesis 数据流中的分片数量以提高整体吞吐量，从而使消费者应用程序更快地处理数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MOST operational efficiency. The root problem is a self-managed KCL consumer fleet on EC2 that cannot keep up with sudden traffic spikes, so records expire from the stream before being processed. AWS's own Kinesis troubleshooting guidance for 'Consumer record processing is falling behind' attributes this to 'insufficient physical resources or record processing logic that has not scaled with an increase in stream throughput,' and explicitly calls increasing the retention period only 'a quick stopgap solution' while you troubleshoot, not a fix. The most operationally efficient remedy is to make the Lambda function the consumer with the Kinesis data stream as the event source: per the Lambda docs, 'Your Lambda function is a consumer application for your data stream,' Lambda polls each shard and 'keeps processing batches until the function catches up with the stream,' and the event source mapping is a managed Lambda resource that 'automatically scales event pollers.' That removes all server provisioning, patching, Auto Scaling configuration, and KCL lease-table management. Option B keeps the EC2 fleet plus a CloudWatch IteratorAgeMilliseconds-driven scaling pipeline the engineer must build and operate, and its retention bump is only the documented stopgap, so it is far less operationally efficient, which is why C wins.","explanation_zh":"題目限定詞是 MOST operational efficiency（最高營運效率）。問題根因是在 EC2 上自管的 KCL consumer 機隊無法跟上突發流量，導致記錄在被處理前就因保留期到期而遺失。AWS 對於『Consumer record processing is falling behind』的 Kinesis 疑難排解文件本身將此歸因於『實體資源不足，或記錄處理邏輯未隨 stream 吞吐量增加而擴展』，並明確指出增加 retention period 只是『快速的權宜之計（stopgap）』、是在你排查問題期間止血，而非真正的修正。營運效率最高的解法是把 Lambda 函式當作 consumer，並以 Kinesis data stream 作為 event source：根據 Lambda 文件，『Your Lambda function is a consumer application for your data stream』，Lambda 會輪詢每個 shard 並『持續處理批次直到函式追上 stream』，而 event source mapping 是由 Lambda 代管的資源並會『自動擴展 event pollers』。這完全移除了伺服器佈建、修補、Auto Scaling 設定，以及 KCL lease table 管理。選項 B 仍保留 EC2 機隊，外加工程師必須自行建置與維運、以 CloudWatch IteratorAgeMilliseconds 驅動的擴展流程，且其增加 retention 只是文件所述的權宜之計，營運效率明顯較低，因此 C 勝出。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Re-architecting to dump logs to S3 and run Amazon EMR for batch analytics changes the processing model entirely, still relies on the failing EC2 consumer to write the records to S3, and adds an EMR cluster to operate and scale. It is a heavy, high-overhead redesign, not the most operationally efficient stream-handling fix.","why_zh":"改成把日誌寫到 S3 再用 Amazon EMR 做批次分析，會完全改變處理模型，仍依賴正在出問題的 EC2 consumer 把記錄寫入 S3，還要額外維運與擴展 EMR 叢集，是高負擔的重構，並非營運效率最高的串流處理修正。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it preserves the EC2 fleet and forces the engineer to build and operate a CloudWatch IteratorAgeMilliseconds-driven autoscaling pipeline plus KCL lease management. Increasing the retention period is, per AWS's own troubleshooting doc, only 'a quick stopgap solution' that delays data loss rather than fixing throughput. It works technically but has much higher operational overhead than the serverless Lambda consumer.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議答案，但它保留 EC2 機隊，並強迫工程師自行建置與維運以 CloudWatch IteratorAgeMilliseconds 驅動的 Auto Scaling 流程及 KCL lease 管理。根據 AWS 自家的疑難排解文件，增加 retention period 只是『快速的權宜之計』、是延後資料遺失，並未解決吞吐量問題。技術上可行，但營運負擔遠高於 serverless 的 Lambda consumer。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Adding shards raises stream capacity and read parallelism, but the described bottleneck is the consumer falling behind, not the stream's ingest throughput; more shards do not by themselves make a slow self-managed EC2 consumer process faster, and you still operate the EC2 fleet. It is a partial, less efficient fix that also raises cost.","why_zh":"增加 shard 可提升 stream 容量與讀取並行度，但題述瓶頸是 consumer 跟不上，而非 stream 的擷取吞吐量；單純增加 shard 並不會讓緩慢的自管 EC2 consumer 處理更快，且仍需維運 EC2 機隊。這是片面且效率較低的修正，同時也提高成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-kinesis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-eventsourcemapping.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/troubleshooting-consumers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-kinesis-create.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":101,"question_en":"A company recently created a new AWS Control Tower landing zone in a new organization in AWS Organizations. The landing zone must be able to demonstrate compliance with the Center for Internet Security (CIS) Benchmarks for AWS Foundations. The company’s security team wants to use AWS Security Hub to view compliance across all accounts. Only the security team can be allowed to view aggregated Security Hub findings. In addition, specific users must be able to view findings from their own accounts within the organization. All accounts must be enrolled in Security Hub after the accounts are created. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements in the MOST automated way? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司最近在 AWS 组织中为一个新的组织创建了一个新的 AWS 控制塔着陆区。该着陆区必须 能够证明符合 AWS 基础设施的互联网安全中心（CIS）基准。 该公司的安全团队希望使用 AWS 安全中心来查看所有账户的合规情况。只有安全团队能够查看安全中心 的汇总发现结果。此外，特定用户必须能够查看其所在组织内自身账户的发现结果。所有账户在创建后 都必须加入安全中心。 哪种步骤组合将以最自动化的方式满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Turn on trusted access for Security Hub in the organization’s management account. Create a new security account by using AWS Control Tower. Configure the new security account as the delegated administrator account for Security Hub. In the new security account, provide Security Hub with the CIS Benchmarks for AWS Foundations standards.","B":"Turn on trusted access for Security Hub in the organization’s management account. From the management account, provide Security Hub with the CIS Benchmarks for AWS Foundations standards.","C":"Create an AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) permission set that includes the required permissions. Use the CreateAccountAssignment API operation to associate the security team users with the permission set and with the delegated security account.","D":"Create an SCP that explicitly denies any user who is not on the security team from accessing Security Hub.","E":"In Security Hub, turn on automatic enablement.","F":"In the organization’s management account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to the CreateManagedAccount event. Create an AWS Lambda function that uses the Security Hub CreateMembers API operation to add new accounts to Security Hub. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中为 Security Hub 开启受信任访问。使用 AWS Control Tower 创建一个新的安全账 户。将新安全账户配置为 Security Hub 的委托管理员账户。在新安全账户中，为 Security Hub 提供 AWS 基础设施 CIS 基准标准。","B":"在组织的管理账户中为 Security Hub 启用受信任访问。从管理账户向 Security Hub 提供 AWS 基础设施 CIS 基准标准。","C":"创建一个包含所需权限的 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）权限集。使用 CreateAccountAssig nment API 操作将安全团队用户与权限集以及委托的安全账户相关联。","D":"创建一个安全策略配置（SCP），明确禁止任何不在安全团队的用户访问安全中心。","E":"在 Security Hub 中，开启自动启用功能。","F":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对 CreateManagedAccount 事件作出反 应。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数使用 Security Hub 的 CreateMembers API 操作将新账户添 加到 Security Hub 中。配置 EventBridge 规则以调用该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is the MOST automated way, and the requirements split into three jobs. (A) Designate a separate Control Tower-provisioned security account as the Security Hub delegated administrator and enable the CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark standard there. The AWS docs (designate-orgs-admin-account.html) explicitly recommend choosing an account other than the organization management account, 'because users who have access to the organization management account to manage billing are likely to be different from users who need access to Security Hub for security management.' This gives the security team a single, all-account aggregation point and satisfies the CIS compliance requirement. (C) IAM Identity Center's CreateAccountAssignment API 'assigns access to a principal (USER or GROUP) for a specified AWS account using a specified permission set' and automatically provisions that access as an IAM policy/role in the target account. Assigning the security team to a permission set scoped to the delegated security account grants aggregated-view access, and the same API scoped to each member account (TargetType=AWS_ACCOUNT) lets specific users view findings from their own accounts. (E) Turning on Security Hub automatic enablement natively adds every new organization account as a member and enables Security Hub plus the default standards (FSBP and CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark) when the account joins, fulfilling auto-enrollment with no custom code. This beats (F), which builds and maintains an EventBridge rule plus a Lambda calling CreateMembers for the same outcome with far more operational overhead, and beats (B), which makes the management account the admin against AWS guidance and cannot restrict aggregated viewing to only the security team.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是「最自動化的方式 (MOST automated)」，需求可拆成三項工作。(A) 指定一個由 Control Tower 建立的獨立 security account 作為 Security Hub 的 delegated administrator，並在該帳號啟用 CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark 標準。AWS 文件 (designate-orgs-admin-account.html) 明確建議不要使用 organization management account，因為「負責帳務的 management account 使用者通常與需要存取 Security Hub 進行安全管理的使用者不同」；如此安全團隊即擁有單一的跨帳號 findings 彙整點，並滿足 CIS 合規需求。(C) IAM Identity Center 的 CreateAccountAssignment API 會「使用指定的 permission set 將存取權指派給某個 principal（USER 或 GROUP），對應到指定的 AWS 帳號」，並自動於目標帳號佈建為 IAM policy/role。把安全團隊指派到對應 delegated security account 的 permission set，即可授予彙整檢視權限；同一 API 以各 member account 為 TargetType=AWS_ACCOUNT，即可讓特定使用者檢視自己帳號的 findings。(E) 開啟 Security Hub 的 automatic enablement 為原生功能，可在新組織帳號加入時自動將其加入為 member 並啟用 Security Hub 及預設標準（FSBP 與 CIS AWS Foundations Benchmark），無須自訂程式即滿足自動納管。此優於 (F)（需自建並維護 EventBridge rule 加呼叫 CreateMembers 的 Lambda，營運負擔更高），也優於 (B)（讓 management account 當管理者，違反 AWS 指引，且無法將彙整檢視僅限制給安全團隊）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Making the organization management account the Security Hub administrator contradicts AWS guidance (designate-orgs-admin-account.html recommends a separate account because billing/management users differ from security users) and cannot satisfy 'only the security team can view aggregated findings,' since management-account access is tied to org administration. It also omits the per-user, per-account viewing requirement.","why_zh":"讓 organization management account 擔任 Security Hub 管理者違反 AWS 指引（designate-orgs-admin-account.html 建議使用獨立帳號，因帳務/管理使用者與安全使用者不同），且無法滿足「僅安全團隊可檢視彙整 findings」，因為 management account 存取與組織管理綁定；亦未涵蓋各使用者檢視自己帳號的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An SCP is a guardrail that applies to accounts and root/OU scopes, not to a notion of 'users on the security team.' It cannot cleanly restrict aggregated-view access to the security team nor grant specific users per-account viewing, and it is not the access-provisioning mechanism the requirements call for (that is IAM Identity Center in option C).","why_zh":"SCP 是作用於帳號與 root/OU 範圍的護欄，而非「安全團隊成員」概念，無法乾淨地將彙整檢視限制給安全團隊，也無法授予特定使用者各自帳號的檢視權；且非需求所需的存取佈建機制（該機制為選項 C 的 IAM Identity Center）。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Building an EventBridge rule on CreateManagedAccount plus a Lambda that calls the Security Hub CreateMembers API is functional and a known pattern, but it introduces custom code and ongoing maintenance. The native automatic enablement feature (E) achieves the same auto-enrollment of new accounts with zero custom code, so F loses on the 'MOST automated' qualifier.","why_zh":"建立針對 CreateManagedAccount 的 EventBridge rule 加上呼叫 Security Hub CreateMembers API 的 Lambda 雖可運作且為已知模式，但引入自訂程式與持續維運。原生的 automatic enablement（E）可零自訂程式達成相同的新帳號自動納管，故在「最自動化」限定詞下 F 落敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/designate-orgs-admin-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/accounts-orgs-auto-enable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/APIReference/API_CreateAccountAssignment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/assignusers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/what-is-control-tower.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":102,"question_en":"A company runs applications in AWS accounts that are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The applications use Amazon EC2 instances and Amazon S3. The company wants to detect potentially compromised EC2 instances, suspicious network activity, and unusual API activity in its existing AWS accounts and in any AWS accounts that the company creates in the future. When the company detects one of these events, the company wants to use an existing Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to send a notification to its operational support team for investigation and remediation. Which solution will meet these requirements in accordance with AWS best practices?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中的多个 AWS 账户中运行应用程序。这些应用程序使用亚马逊 EC2 实例和 亚马逊 S3。 该公司希望检测其现有 AWS 账户以及未来创建的任何 AWS 账户中可能受到攻击的 EC2 实例、可疑的网 络活动和异常的 API 活动。当公司检测到此类事件时，希望使用现有的亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题向其运营支持团队发送通知，以便进行调查和修复。 哪种解决方案符合 AWS 最佳实践并满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the organization’s management account, configure an AWS account as the Amazon GuardDuty administrator account. In the GuardDuty administrator account, add the company’s existing AWS accounts to GuardDuty as members. In the GuardDuty administrator account, create an Amazon EventBridge rule with an event pattern to match GuardDuty events and to forward matching events to the SNS topic.","B":"In the organization’s management account, configure Amazon GuardDuty to add newly created AWS accounts by invitation and to send invitations to the existing AWS accounts. Create an AWS CloudFormation stack set that accepts the GuardDuty invitation and creates an Amazon EventBridge rule. Configure the rule with an event pattern to match GuardDuty events and to forward matching events to the SNS topic. Configure the CloudFormation stack set to deploy into all AWS accounts in the organization.","C":"In the organization’s management account, create an AWS CloudTrail organization trail. Activate the organization trail in all AWS accounts in the organization. Create an SCP that enables VPC Flow Logs in each account in the organization. Configure AWS Security Hub for the organization. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule with an event pattern to match Security Hub events and to forward matching events to the SNS topic.","D":"In the organization’s management account, configure an AWS account as the AWS CloudTrail administrator account. In the CloudTrail administrator account, create a CloudTrail organization trail. Add the company’s existing AWS accounts to the organization trail. Create an SCP that enables VPC Flow Logs in each account in the organization. Configure AWS Security Hub for the organization. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule with an event pattern to match Security Hub events and to forward matching events to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中，将一个 AWS 账户配置为 Amazon GuardDuty 管理员账户。在 GuardDuty 管理 员账户中，将公司现有的 AWS 账户添加为 GuardDuty 成员。在 GuardDuty 管理员账户中，创建一 个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则包含一个事件模式，用于匹配 GuardDuty 事件并将匹配的事 件转发到 SNS 主题。","B":"在组织的管理账户中，配置 Amazon GuardDuty 以通过邀请添加新创建的 AWS 账户，并向现有 AWS 账户发送邀请。创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈集，用于接受 GuardDuty 邀请并创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则的事件模式以匹配 GuardDuty 事件，并将匹配的事件转发到 SNS 主题。配置 CloudFormation 堆栈集以部署到组织中的所有 AWS 账户。","C":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 组织跟踪。在组织中的所有 AWS 账户中激活组织跟 踪。创建一个 SCP，以在组织中的每个账户中启用 VPC 流日志。为组织配置 AWS 安全中心。创建 一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则具有与安全中心事件匹配的事件模式，并将匹配的事件转发 到 SNS 主题。","D":"在组织的管理账户中，将一个 AWS 账户配置为 AWS CloudTrail 管理员账户。在 CloudTrail 管理员账 户中，创建一个 CloudTrail 组织跟踪。将公司的现有 AWS 账户添加到组织跟踪中。创建一个 SCP， 以在组织中的每个账户中启用 VPC 流日志。为组织配置 AWS 安全中心。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则具有与安全中心事件匹配的事件模式，并将匹配的事件转发到 SNS 主题。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The three detection requirements map directly to Amazon GuardDuty: potentially compromised EC2 instances (GuardDuty EC2 finding types), suspicious network activity (derived from VPC Flow Logs), and unusual API activity (derived from CloudTrail management events). Per the GuardDuty foundational data sources documentation, when you enable GuardDuty it automatically consumes CloudTrail management events, VPC Flow Logs, and Route 53 DNS query logs with no extra setup ('you don't need to enable anything else'), so there is no need to create organization CloudTrail trails, enable VPC Flow Logs via SCPs, or aggregate with Security Hub. Best practice for an AWS Organizations environment is for the management account to designate a delegated GuardDuty administrator account (security operations should not run from the management account), add the existing accounts as members through the Organizations integration, and use auto-enable so future accounts are covered automatically. GuardDuty publishes findings natively to Amazon EventBridge, and in a multi-account organization the delegated administrator account receives findings from all member accounts, so an EventBridge rule in that administrator account matching GuardDuty events and forwarding to the existing SNS topic completes the notification path. Option A implements exactly this pattern.","explanation_zh":"三項偵測需求都直接對應到 Amazon GuardDuty：可能遭入侵的 EC2 執行個體（GuardDuty EC2 finding types）、可疑網路活動（源自 VPC Flow Logs）、以及異常 API 活動（源自 CloudTrail management events）。根據 GuardDuty foundational data sources 文件，啟用 GuardDuty 後它會自動消耗 CloudTrail management events、VPC Flow Logs 與 Route 53 DNS query logs，無需額外設定（『you don't need to enable anything else』），因此不必建立 organization CloudTrail trail、用 SCP 啟用 VPC Flow Logs、或用 Security Hub 彙整。在 AWS Organizations 環境中的最佳實務是：由 management account 指派一個 delegated GuardDuty administrator account（安全營運不應在 management account 中執行），透過 Organizations 整合把現有帳戶加入為 member，並使用 auto-enable 讓未來新建帳戶自動納管。GuardDuty 會原生將 findings 發佈到 Amazon EventBridge，且在多帳戶組織中 delegated administrator account 會收到所有 member 帳戶的 findings，因此在該管理員帳戶建立一條比對 GuardDuty events 並轉送到既有 SNS topic 的 EventBridge 規則即可完成通知路徑。選項 A 正是此模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Invitation-based membership is the legacy method; AWS best practice for an organization is to add members through the GuardDuty AWS Organizations integration with a delegated administrator and auto-enable. This option also operates from the management account (no delegated admin) and uses a CloudFormation stack set merely to accept invitations and deploy per-account EventBridge rules, which is unnecessarily complex and not the recommended pattern.","why_zh":"邀請式 (invitation) 加入成員是舊式方法；組織的 AWS 最佳實務是透過 GuardDuty 與 AWS Organizations 整合，採用 delegated administrator 加 auto-enable 模式加入成員。此選項還是在 management account 中運作（未指派委派管理員），並用 CloudFormation stack set 只為了接受邀請並逐帳戶部署 EventBridge 規則，過於複雜，並非建議做法。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This solution never enables GuardDuty, so it cannot detect potentially compromised EC2 instances, which is core to the requirement. A CloudTrail organization trail plus VPC Flow Logs only collect raw logs and do not generate threat findings for compromised EC2 or anomalies; Security Hub aggregates findings from other services rather than producing these detections itself. Also, an SCP cannot enable VPC Flow Logs; SCPs are permission guardrails, not a feature-enablement mechanism. The approach carries far more operational overhead.","why_zh":"此方案完全沒有啟用 GuardDuty，因此無法偵測可能遭入侵的 EC2 執行個體，而這是需求核心。CloudTrail organization trail 加 VPC Flow Logs 只是收集原始日誌，並不會產生受侵害 EC2 或異常的威脅 findings；Security Hub 是彙整其他服務的 findings，而非自行產生這些偵測。此外 SCP 無法啟用 VPC Flow Logs；SCP 是權限護欄而非啟用功能的機制。整體營運負擔大很多。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same flaws as C plus an invalid construct: there is no 'CloudTrail administrator account' delegated-admin concept used this way, and 'adding accounts to the organization trail' does not match how organization trails work (a trail created in the management account automatically applies to all member accounts). An SCP still cannot enable VPC Flow Logs, and without GuardDuty this design cannot detect compromised EC2 instances or network/API anomalies, while carrying excessive operational overhead.","why_zh":"與 C 相同的缺陷，再加上無效的構件：本情境下並沒有這樣使用的『CloudTrail administrator account』委派管理概念，且『將帳戶加入 organization trail』與 organization trail 的實際運作不符（在 management account 建立的 trail 會自動套用到所有 member 帳戶）。SCP 仍無法啟用 VPC Flow Logs，且缺少 GuardDuty 時此設計無法偵測受侵害 EC2 或網路/API 異常，並且營運負擔過高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_data-sources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_organizations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/delegated-admin-designate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/set-guardduty-auto-enable-preferences.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":103,"question_en":"A company’s DevOps engineer is working in a multi-account environment. The company uses AWS Transit Gateway to route all outbound traffic through a network operations account. In the network operations account, all account traffic passes through a firewall appliance for inspection before the traffic goes to an internet gateway. The firewall appliance sends logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and includes event severities of CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW, and INFO. The security team wants to receive an alert if any CRITICAL events occur. What should the DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 工程师在多账户环境中工作。该公司使用 AWS 转发网关将所有出站流量通过网络运 营账户进行路由。在网络运营账户中，所有账户流量在到达互联网网关之前都要通过防火墙设备进行检 查。 防火墙设备会将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，并包含 CRITICAL（严重）、HIGH（高）、 MEDIUM（中）、LOW（低）和 INFO（信息）这几种事件严重级别。安全团队希望在出现任何严重事 件时收到警报。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics canary to monitor the firewall state. If the firewall reaches a CRITICAL state or logs a CRITICAL event, use a CloudWatch alarm to publish a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the security team’s email address to the topic.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch metric filter by using a search for CRITICAL events. Publish a custom metric for the finding. Use a CloudWatch alarm based on the custom metric to publish a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the security team’s email address to the topic.","C":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty in the network operations account. Configure GuardDuty to monitor flow logs. Create an Amazon EventBridge event rule that is invoked by GuardDuty events that are CRITICAL. Define an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as a target. Subscribe the security team’s email address to the topic.","D":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to apply consistent policies across all accounts. Create an Amazon EventBridge event rule that is invoked by Firewall Manager events that are CRITICAL. Define an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as a target. Subscribe the security team’s email address to the topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Synthetics 健康检查来监控防火墙的状态。如果防火墙达到 CRITICAL （危急）状态或记录了 CRITICAL（危急）事件，使用 CloudWatch 警报向 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题发布通知。将安全团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。","B":"通过搜索“CRITICAL”事件创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 指标筛选器。为该发现发布一个自定义指 标。基于自定义指标使用 CloudWatch 警报向 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题发布通知。将安全团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。","C":"在网络运营账户中启用亚马逊 GuardDuty。配置 GuardDuty 以监控流量。 日志。创建一个由 GuardDuty 发出的 CRITICAL 级别事件触发的 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则。将 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题定义为目标。将安全团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。","D":"使用 AWS 防火墙管理器在所有账户中应用一致的策略。创建一个由防火墙管理器发出的 CRITICAL 级别事件触发的 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则。将 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题定 义为目标。将安全团队的电子邮件地址订阅到该主题。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The firewall appliance already ships its logs (including the CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/INFO event severities) to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The canonical AWS pattern to alert on a specific term or pattern inside log data is a CloudWatch Logs metric filter that matches the term (here, CRITICAL) and increments a custom metric, combined with a CloudWatch alarm on that metric that publishes to an Amazon SNS topic, with the security team's email subscribed. This is exactly the 'Alarming on logs' workflow documented by AWS, which states that metric filters let you look for terms and patterns in log data and then create an alarm whose action is an SNS notification. Option B implements this end to end, so it is the correct answer.","explanation_zh":"防火牆設備已將其日誌（包含 CRITICAL/HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW/INFO 嚴重性事件）傳送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。要針對日誌資料中特定字詞或模式發出告警，AWS 的標準做法是建立 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 比對該字詞（此處為 CRITICAL）並將其轉為自訂 metric，再以 CloudWatch alarm 監控該 metric，於觸發時發佈到 Amazon SNS topic，並讓安全團隊的電子郵件訂閱該 topic。這正是 AWS 文件中『Alarming on logs』的流程——metric filter 可在日誌資料中尋找字詞與模式，再建立以 SNS 通知為動作的 alarm。選項 B 完整實作此流程，為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudWatch Synthetics canaries are scripted (Node.js/Python) checks that monitor endpoint/application availability and latency by simulating user requests; they do not read CloudWatch Logs content and there is no 'firewall state' for a canary to poll, so they cannot detect CRITICAL log events.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Synthetics canary 是以腳本（Node.js/Python）模擬使用者請求來監控端點/應用程式可用性與延遲，無法讀取 CloudWatch Logs 內容，也沒有可供 canary 輪詢的『防火牆狀態』，因此無法偵測 CRITICAL 日誌事件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"GuardDuty does not ingest a third-party firewall appliance's CloudWatch Logs; it analyzes AWS foundational data sources such as CloudTrail events, VPC Flow Logs, and Route 53 DNS query logs. Its own Critical/High/Medium/Low severity model maps to numeric values 1.0-10.0 derived from GuardDuty threat detection (for example attack sequences or compromised credentials), which is unrelated to the appliance's CRITICAL log-event severity, so it cannot alert on the appliance's CRITICAL events.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 並不讀取第三方防火牆設備寫入 CloudWatch Logs 的內容，而是分析 AWS 基礎資料來源（如 CloudTrail 事件、VPC Flow Logs、Route 53 DNS 查詢日誌）。其本身的 Critical/High/Medium/Low 嚴重性以 1.0-10.0 的數值表示，來自 GuardDuty 的威脅偵測（例如攻擊序列或遭入侵的憑證），與設備的 CRITICAL 日誌事件嚴重性無關，因此無法針對設備的 CRITICAL 事件告警。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Firewall Manager centrally administers WAF rules, Shield Advanced, AWS Network Firewall, and security-group policies across accounts in an organization; it does not parse the severity of a firewall appliance's log events, and there is no 'Firewall Manager CRITICAL event' to drive the EventBridge rule.","why_zh":"AWS Firewall Manager 是在組織內跨帳戶集中管理 WAF 規則、Shield Advanced、AWS Network Firewall 及安全群組政策，並不解析防火牆設備日誌事件的嚴重性，也沒有可驅動 EventBridge 規則的『Firewall Manager CRITICAL 事件』。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Alarm-On-Logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings-severity.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":104,"question_en":"A company is divided into teams. Each team has an AWS account, and all the accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. Each team must retain full administrative rights to its AWS account. Each team also must be allowed to access only AWS services that the company approves for use. AWS services must gain approval through a request and approval process. How should a DevOps engineer configure the accounts to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司被划分为多个团队。每个团队都有一个 AWS 账户，所有账户都在 AWS 组织中的一个组织内。 每个团队必须对其 AWS 账户保留完全的管理权限。每个团队还必须仅被允许访问公司批准使用的 AWS 服务。AWS 服务必须通过请求和审批流程获得批准。 DevOps 工程师应如何配置账户以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to provision IAM policies in each account to deny access to restricted AWS services. In each account, configure AWS Config rules that ensure that the policies are attached to IAM principals in the account.","B":"Use AWS Control Tower to provision the accounts into OUs within the organization. Configure AWS Control Tower to enable AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). Configure IAM Identity Center to provide administrative access. Include deny policies on user roles for restricted AWS services.","C":"Place all the accounts under a new top-level OU within the organization. Create an SCP that denies access to restricted AWS services. Attach the SCP to the OU.","D":"Create an SCP that allows access to only approved AWS services. Attach the SCP to the root OU of the organization. Remove the FullAWSAccess SCP from the root OU of the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在每个账户中配置 IAM 策略，以拒绝访问受限的 AWS 服务。在每 个账户中，配置 AWS Config 规则以确保这些策略已附加到账户中的 IAM 实体。","B":"使用 AWS Control Tower 将账户配置到组织内的组织单位（OU）中。配置 AWS Control Tower 以启用 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）。配置 IAM 身份中心以提供管理访问权限。在用户角色上为 受限的 AWS 服务包含拒绝策略。","C":"将所有账户置于组织内的新顶级组织单位（OU）下。创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），拒绝访问受限 的 AWS 服务。将该 SCP 附加到该 OU。","D":"创建一个仅允许访问已批准的 AWS 服务的 SCP（服务控制策略）。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根组织单 元。从组织的根组织单元移除 FullAWSAccess SCP。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive requirement is that AWS services must be approved through a request-and-approval process, which mandates a deny-by-default allowlist: only explicitly approved services may be used, and anything new is blocked until an admin grants it. Option D implements this with an SCP that allows only approved services attached to the organization root, combined with removing the AWS-managed FullAWSAccess SCP. The AWS Organizations SCP evaluation doc states you can replace FullAWSAccess with a policy allowing only a set of services 'so that new AWS services are not allowed unless they are explicitly allowed by updating SCPs,' and that a root-level allowlist SCP 'automatically applies to all OUs and accounts beneath it.' Because SCPs only set maximum-permission guardrails and never grant permissions, each team still retains full administrative rights within the approved boundary through its own account IAM. Approving a new service is done by updating the root SCP, which is exactly the request-and-approval workflow. Removing FullAWSAccess is necessary (and the docs note it is safe only when replaced by a policy with allowed actions) so that nothing is permitted except the approved services.","explanation_zh":"決定性需求是 AWS 服務必須透過請求與核准流程才能啟用，這要求採用「預設拒絕」的允許清單（allowlist）模型：只有明確核准的服務才能使用，任何新服務在管理員授權前都被封鎖。選項 D 正是如此實作：建立一個只允許已核准服務的 SCP 並掛載到 organization root，同時移除 AWS 受管的 FullAWSAccess SCP。AWS Organizations 的 SCP 評估文件指出，可將 FullAWSAccess 替換為只允許特定服務集合的政策，使「除非透過更新 SCP 明確允許，否則新的 AWS 服務都不被允許」，而掛在 root 的 allowlist SCP「會自動套用到其下所有 OU 與帳戶」。由於 SCP 只設定權限上限的護欄、本身從不授予權限，各團隊仍可透過自己帳戶的 IAM 在核准範圍內保有完整的管理員權限。核准新服務就是更新 root 的 SCP，這正是請求與核准流程。移除 FullAWSAccess 是必要的（文件指出只有在以含允許動作的政策取代它時才安全），如此除已核准服務外其餘一律不允許。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"StackSets-provisioned IAM deny policies are not enforceable guardrails: because each team keeps full administrative rights, an account admin can detach or modify those IAM policies. AWS Config rules only detect and report drift after the fact; they do not prevent the prohibited actions. It is also a denylist, so newly released and non-listed services remain accessible, failing the approval-gated allowlist requirement.","why_zh":"由 StackSets 佈署的 IAM 拒絕政策不是可強制執行的護欄：由於各團隊保有完整管理員權限，帳戶管理員可自行卸除或修改這些 IAM 政策。AWS Config 規則僅能事後偵測與回報漂移，無法阻止被禁止的動作。且這是拒絕清單模型，未列出與新發布的服務仍可使用，無法滿足以核准為前提的允許清單需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Control Tower with IAM Identity Center plus deny policies on user roles is a denylist by default: future AWS services are allowed unless explicitly denied, so it does not gate new services through approval. Forcing administrative access through IAM Identity Center roles also conflicts with each team retaining native full administrative rights to its own account, and role-level deny policies do not provide an organization-wide approval guardrail like an SCP allowlist does.","why_zh":"AWS Control Tower 搭配 IAM Identity Center 並在使用者角色上加拒絕政策，預設仍是拒絕清單：除非明確拒絕，未來的 AWS 服務都被允許，因此無法透過核准流程管控新服務。將管理存取強制經由 IAM Identity Center 角色，也與各團隊在自己帳戶保有原生完整管理員權限相衝突，且角色層級的拒絕政策無法像 SCP 允許清單那樣提供整個組織範圍的核准護欄。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP that denies restricted services is a denylist: FullAWSAccess remains in place, so every service not explicitly named, including every future AWS service, stays automatically accessible. This fails the core requirement that services must gain approval before use. The AWS docs contrast this with the allowlist approach, where you replace FullAWSAccess so that new services are blocked until explicitly allowed.","why_zh":"拒絕受限服務的 SCP 屬於拒絕清單：FullAWSAccess 仍保留，因此任何未明確列出的服務（包含未來所有 AWS 服務）都自動可用。這無法滿足服務必須先經核准才能使用的核心需求。AWS 文件將此與允許清單做法做對比：允許清單會替換 FullAWSAccess，使新服務在被明確允許前都被封鎖。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":105,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer used an AWS CloudFormation custom resource to set up AD Connector. The AWS Lambda function ran and created AD Connector, but CloudFormation is not transitioning from CREATE_IN_PROGRESS to CREATE_COMPLETE. Which action should the engineer take to resolve this issue?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS CloudFormation 自定义资源来设置 AD 连接器。AWS Lambda 函数运行并 创建了 AD 连接器，但 CloudFormation 未从“CREATE_IN_PROGRESS”（创建中）状态过渡到 “CREATE_COMPLETE”（创建完成）状态。 工程师应该采取哪项行动来解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Ensure the Lambda function code has exited successfully.","B":"Ensure the Lambda function code returns a response to the pre-signed URL.","C":"Ensure the Lambda function IAM role has cloudformation:UpdateStack permissions for the stack ARN.","D":"Ensure the Lambda function IAM role has ds:ConnectDirectory permissions for the AWS account."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保 Lambda 函数代码已成功退出。","B":"确保 Lambda 函数代码向预签名的 URL 返回响应。","C":"确保 Lambda 函数的 IAM 角色具有针对该堆栈 ARN 的 cloudformation:UpdateStack 权限。","D":"确保 Lambda 函数的 IAM 角色对于 AWS 账户具有 ds:ConnectDirectory 权限。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A Lambda-backed CloudFormation custom resource works by CloudFormation invoking the function asynchronously with an event that contains a pre-signed Amazon S3 'ResponseURL' (the callback URL). CloudFormation then blocks the stack operation and waits for the function to upload a SUCCESS or FAILED response object to that pre-signed URL. AWS docs state that after getting a SUCCESS response CloudFormation proceeds with the stack operation, but if a FAILED response or no response is returned the operation fails, and the default custom-resource timeout is 3600 seconds (1 hour) before the stack operation fails. In this scenario the AD Connector was actually created, which proves the function's API calls and ds permissions already worked, so the only thing preventing the transition out of CREATE_IN_PROGRESS is that the function never sent its response back to the pre-signed callback URL. The fix is to ensure the Lambda code returns a response (for example via the cfn-response helper) to the pre-signed ResponseURL, making option B correct.","explanation_zh":"由 Lambda 支援的 CloudFormation custom resource 運作方式為:CloudFormation 以非同步 (asynchronous) 方式叫用該 function,事件中包含一個預先簽署的 Amazon S3 'ResponseURL'(即 callback URL)。CloudFormation 接著會封鎖 stack 操作並等待 function 將 SUCCESS 或 FAILED 回應物件上傳到該 pre-signed URL。AWS 文件指出:取得 SUCCESS 回應後 CloudFormation 才會繼續 stack 操作;若收到 FAILED 回應或沒有任何回應,操作就會失敗,且 custom resource 預設逾時為 3600 秒(1 小時)後 stack 操作才失敗。本題中 AD Connector 已實際建立成功,證明 function 的 API 呼叫與 ds 權限都已正常運作,因此唯一阻止它離開 CREATE_IN_PROGRESS 的原因,就是 function 從未將回應送回 pre-signed callback URL。正確解法是確保 Lambda 程式碼會將回應(例如透過 cfn-response 輔助模組)送到 pre-signed ResponseURL,故答案為 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Lambda function exiting successfully is not what signals CloudFormation. Because the invocation is asynchronous, CloudFormation never sees the function's return value or exit status; it only proceeds when a SUCCESS/FAILED response is written to the pre-signed ResponseURL. A function can exit cleanly yet still leave the stack hung if it never sent that response.","why_zh":"Lambda function 正常結束並非觸發 CloudFormation 的訊號。由於叫用是非同步的,CloudFormation 看不到 function 的回傳值或結束狀態;只有當 SUCCESS/FAILED 回應被寫入 pre-signed ResponseURL 時才會繼續。即使 function 乾淨地結束,只要沒送出回應,stack 仍會卡住。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"cloudformation:UpdateStack is irrelevant here. A custom resource Lambda does not call back into the CloudFormation API to advance the stack; it signals completion only by uploading a response to the pre-signed S3 URL, which already carries its own temporary credentials. Granting UpdateStack would do nothing to release a stuck CREATE_IN_PROGRESS.","why_zh":"cloudformation:UpdateStack 在此無關。Custom resource 的 Lambda 不會回呼 CloudFormation API 來推進 stack;它只透過將回應上傳到本身已帶有暫時憑證的 pre-signed S3 URL 來表示完成。授予 UpdateStack 對解開卡住的 CREATE_IN_PROGRESS 毫無作用。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ds:ConnectDirectory is the permission needed to create the AD Connector, but the question states the AD Connector was successfully created. That proves the IAM permissions were already sufficient, so adding them again would not resolve the hang; the problem is the missing callback response, not a missing Directory Service permission.","why_zh":"ds:ConnectDirectory 是建立 AD Connector 所需的權限,但題目已說明 AD Connector 成功建立了。這證明 IAM 權限原本就足夠,因此再加上該權限無法解決卡住的問題;問題在於缺少 callback 回應,而非缺少 Directory Service 權限。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-cloudformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-custom-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/crpg-ref-responses.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":106,"question_en":"A company uses AWS CodeCommit for source code control. Developers apply their changes to various feature branches and create pull requests to move those changes to the main branch when the changes are ready for production. The developers should not be able to push changes directly to the main branch. The company applied the AWSCodeCommitPowerUser managed policy to the developers’ IAM role, and now these developers can push changes to the main branch directly on every repository in the AWS account. What should the company do to restrict the developers’ ability to push changes to the main branch directly?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodeCommit 进行源代码控制。开发人员将他们的更改应用到不同的功能分支，并在 更改完成后创建拉取请求，将这些更改合并到主分支。 已准备好投入生产。 开发人员不应能够直接向主分支推送更改。该公司将 AWSCodeCommitPowerUser 管理策略应用于开发 人员的 IAM 角色，现在这些开发人员可以在 AWS 账户中的每个代码库直接向主分支推送更改。 公司应该采取什么措施来限制开发人员直接向主分支推送更改？","options_en":{"A":"Create an additional policy to include a Deny rule for the GitPush and PutFile actions. Include a restriction for the specific repositories in the policy statement with a condition that references the main branch.","B":"Remove the IAM policy, and add an AWSCodeCommitReadOnly managed policy. Add an Allow rule for the GitPush and PutFile actions for the specific repositories in the policy statement with a condition that references the main branch.","C":"Modify the IAM policy. Include a Deny rule for the GitPush and PutFile actions for the specific repositories in the policy statement with a condition that references the main branch.","D":"Create an additional policy to include an Allow rule for the GitPush and PutFile actions. Include a restriction for the specific repositories in the policy statement with a condition that references the feature branches."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一项额外的策略，为 GitPush 和 PutFile 操作添加拒绝规则。在策略声明中包含针对特定存储库 的限制条件，并引用主分支。","B":"删除 IAM 策略，并添加 AWSCodeCommitReadOnly 管理策略。在策略语句中为特定代码库添加允许 规则，允许 GitPush 和 PutFile 操作，并添加一个条件，引用主分支。","C":"修改 IAM 策略。在策略语句中为特定的代码库添加一条拒绝规则，拒绝执行 GitPush 和 PutFile 操作，并添加一个条件，该条件引用主分支。","D":"创建一项额外的策略，为 GitPush 和 PutFile 操作添加一条允许规则。在策略声明中包含针对特 定存储库的限制条件，并引用功能分支。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS documents that to prevent users from pushing or merging to a specific branch you create a conditional IAM policy with an explicit Deny on actions such as codecommit:GitPush and codecommit:PutFile (plus the merge/delete actions), scope Resource to the repository ARN, and add a Condition on codecommit:References pointing at the branch reference (for example refs/heads/main). Because AWSCodeCommitPowerUser is an AWS managed policy (ARN arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AWSCodeCommitPowerUser, type 'AWS managed policy'), it is owned and maintained by AWS and cannot be edited by the customer, so the Deny must live in a separate, additional customer-managed policy attached alongside PowerUser. Option A is exactly this: an additional policy containing a Deny for GitPush and PutFile, restricted to the specific repositories, with a condition that references the main branch. An explicit Deny always overrides the Allow that PowerUser grants on '*', so developers retain push access to feature branches but are blocked from pushing or merging directly to main.","explanation_zh":"AWS 文件說明，若要阻止使用者直接 push 或 merge 到特定分支，需建立條件式 IAM policy，對 codecommit:GitPush、codecommit:PutFile（以及相關的 merge/delete actions）使用明確的 Deny，將 Resource 限定為該 repository 的 ARN，並加上以 codecommit:References 指向該分支參考（例如 refs/heads/main）的 Condition。由於 AWSCodeCommitPowerUser 是 AWS managed policy（ARN 為 arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AWSCodeCommitPowerUser，類型為 'AWS managed policy'），由 AWS 擁有與維護，客戶無法直接修改，因此這個 Deny 必須放在另一個額外的 customer-managed policy 中，與 PowerUser 一併附加。選項 A 正是如此：建立額外 policy，內含針對 GitPush 與 PutFile 的 Deny，限定特定 repository，並以條件指向 main 分支。明確的 Deny 一律覆蓋 PowerUser 對 '*' 授予的 Allow，因此開發者仍可 push 到 feature 分支，但被阻止直接 push 或 merge 到 main。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is backwards and over-corrects. Replacing PowerUser with AWSCodeCommitReadOnly strips developers of their ability to push to feature branches, and then adding an Allow for GitPush/PutFile on the main branch would actually grant push to main rather than restrict it. The requirement is to deny pushing to main, not to allow it.","why_zh":"方向完全相反且過度更動。用 AWSCodeCommitReadOnly 取代 PowerUser 會剝奪開發者對 feature 分支的 push 能力，而對 main 分支加上 GitPush/PutFile 的 Allow 反而是「授予」push 到 main，而非限制。需求是要 deny push 到 main，而不是 allow。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot modify an AWS managed policy. AWSCodeCommitPowerUser is explicitly an AWS managed policy owned and maintained by AWS (ARN arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AWSCodeCommitPowerUser); customers can attach or detach it but cannot edit its statements. The Deny content of C is correct, but the action 'Modify the IAM policy' is technically impossible for a managed policy, which is exactly why A places the Deny in a separate additional policy.","why_zh":"無法修改 AWS managed policy。AWSCodeCommitPowerUser 明確為 AWS 擁有與維護的 AWS managed policy（ARN arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AWSCodeCommitPowerUser）；客戶只能附加或卸除，無法編輯其內容。C 的 Deny 內容正確，但「修改該 IAM policy」對 managed policy 而言技術上不可行，這也正是 A 將 Deny 放在另一個額外 policy 的原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An Allow rule does not restrict anything. The existing PowerUser policy already grants GitPush on Resource '*', so developers can already push to main; adding another Allow (even scoped to feature branches) does not remove that ability. Only an explicit Deny conditioned on the main branch can prevent direct pushes to main.","why_zh":"Allow 規則無法限制任何事。現有的 PowerUser 已對 Resource '*' 授予 GitPush，開發者本來就能 push 到 main；再加一條 Allow（即使限定 feature 分支）也無法移除該能力。只有以 main 分支為條件的明確 Deny 才能阻止直接 push 到 main。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-conditional-branch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AWSCodeCommitPowerUser.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_managed-vs-inline.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":107,"question_en":"A company manages a web application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The EC2 instances run in an Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. The application uses an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance to store the data. The company has configured Amazon Route 53 with an alias record that points to the ALB. A new company guideline requires a geographically isolated disaster recovery (DR) site with an RTO of 4 hours and an RPO of 15 minutes. Which DR strategy will meet these requirements with the LEAST change to the application stack?","question_zh":"一家公司管理着一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的网络应用程序，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB） 之后，并且分布在多个可用区的自动扩展组中。该应用程序使用亚马逊 RDS 的 MySQL 数据库实例来 存储数据。该公司已在亚马逊 Route 53 中配置了一个别名记录，该记录指向 ALB。 新公司准则要求设立一个地理位置上与主站点隔离的灾难恢复（DR）站点，其恢复时间目标（RTO） 为 4 小时，恢复点目标（RPO）为 15 分钟。 哪种灾难恢复策略能够在对应用堆栈改动最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Launch a replica environment of everything except Amazon RDS in a different Availability Zone. Create an RDS read replica in the new Availability Zone, and configure the new stack to point to the local RDS DB instance. Add the new stack to the Route 53 record set by using a health check to configure a failover routing policy.","B":"Launch a replica environment of everything except Amazon RDS in a different AWS Region. Create an RDS read replica in the new Region, and configure the new stack to point to the local RDS DB instance. Add the new stack to the Route 53 record set by using a health check to configure a latency routing policy.","C":"Launch a replica environment of everything except Amazon RDS in a different AWS Region. In the event of an outage, copy and restore the latest RDS snapshot from the primary Region to the DR Region. Adjust the Route 53 record set to point to the ALB in the DR Region.","D":"Launch a replica environment of everything except Amazon RDS in a different AWS Region. Create an RDS read replica in the new Region, and configure the new environment to point to the local RDS DB instance. Add the new stack to the Route 53 record set by using a health check to configure a failover routing policy. In the event of an outage, promote the read replica to primary."},"options_zh":{"A":"在不同的可用区中启动除 Amazon RDS 之外的所有内容的副本环境。在新的可用区中创建 RDS 读取 副本，并将新堆栈配置为指向本地 RDS 数据库实例。使用健康检查将新堆栈添加到 Route 53 记录 集，以配置故障转移路由策略。","B":"在不同的 AWS 区域中启动除 Amazon RDS 之外的所有内容的副本环境。在新区域中创建 RDS 读取 副本，并将新堆栈配置为指向本地 RDS 数据库实例。通过使用健康检查配置延迟路由策略，将新 堆栈添加到 Route 53 记录集。","C":"在不同的 AWS 区域中启动除 Amazon RDS 之外所有内容的副本环境。在出现故障时，将主区域 中的最新 RDS 快照复制并恢复到 DR 区域。调整 Route 53 记录集以指向 DR 区域中的 ALB。","D":"在不同的 AWS 区域中启动除 Amazon RDS 之外的所有内容的副本环境。在新区域中创建 RDS 读取 副本，并将新环境配置为指向本地 RDS 数据库实例。使用健康检查将新堆栈添加到 Route 53 记录 集，以配置故障转移路由策略。在出现故障时，将读取副本提升为主副本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a geographically isolated DR site (so a different AWS Region, not just another AZ) with an RPO of 15 minutes and an RTO of 4 hours, achieved with the least change to the stack. A cross-Region RDS for MySQL read replica replicates asynchronously and continuously, keeping the DR database within seconds-to-minutes of the primary, which comfortably meets a 15-minute RPO. The Amazon RDS 'Promoting a read replica' doc explicitly lists 'Implementing failure recovery' as a use case (use read replica promotion as a data recovery scheme if the primary DB instance fails) and notes that promotion 'can take several minutes,' easily meeting a 4-hour RTO. The Route 53 failover-types doc confirms that active-passive DR is implemented with the FAILOVER routing policy plus health checks, so the standby DR Region only receives traffic after the primary becomes unhealthy. Option D replicates the same stack to another Region and only changes DNS via failover and promotes the replica on outage, the least invasive change that satisfies all constraints. Option A uses an AZ (not a Region), B uses a latency (active-active) policy and never promotes the replica, and C relies on snapshot copy/restore that cannot meet a 15-minute RPO.","explanation_zh":"需求是地理隔離的 DR 站點（因此必須是不同的 AWS Region，而非僅是另一個 AZ），RPO 15 分鐘、RTO 4 小時，且對應用程式堆疊變更最少。跨 Region 的 RDS for MySQL read replica 以非同步方式持續複寫，使 DR 資料庫與主庫僅相差數秒至數分鐘，可輕鬆滿足 15 分鐘的 RPO。Amazon RDS「Promoting a read replica」文件明確將「Implementing failure recovery」列為用途（在主資料庫故障時以 read replica 提升作為資料復原方案），並指出提升「可能需要數分鐘」，可輕鬆達成 4 小時的 RTO。Route 53 failover-types 文件確認主動／被動 DR 是以 FAILOVER 路由策略搭配 health check 實作，使備援 DR Region 僅在主站不健康時才接收流量。選項 D 將相同堆疊複製到另一個 Region，僅在故障切換時變更 DNS 並提升 replica，是滿足所有條件且變更最少的方案。選項 A 使用 AZ（非 Region），B 使用 latency（active-active）策略且從未提升 replica，C 依賴快照複製／還原而無法達成 15 分鐘的 RPO。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses a different Availability Zone, not a different Region. The requirement explicitly demands a geographically isolated DR site, and a same-Region AZ provides no protection against a regional disaster.","why_zh":"使用不同的 Availability Zone 而非不同的 Region。需求明確要求地理隔離的 DR 站點，同一 Region 內的 AZ 無法防護整個 Region 層級的災難。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A latency routing policy is an active-active configuration that sends users to the lowest-latency endpoint for performance, not active-passive DR failover; it could route live production traffic to the read-only DR replica. It also never promotes the read replica, so the DR database stays read-only and cannot accept writes after a failover.","why_zh":"Latency 路由策略屬於主動／主動（active-active）設定，會將使用者導向延遲最低的端點以提升效能，而非主動／被動的 DR 故障切換，甚至可能將正式流量導向唯讀的 DR replica。它也從未提升 read replica，導致故障切換後 DR 資料庫仍為唯讀、無法承接寫入。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Copy-and-restore of the latest RDS snapshot is a backup-and-restore approach; automated RDS snapshots are typically taken once per day, so RPO would far exceed 15 minutes, and restoring a snapshot in the DR Region during an outage is slow and the most manual effort, putting the 4-hour RTO at risk.","why_zh":"複製並還原最新 RDS 快照屬於 backup-and-restore 方式；RDS 自動快照通常為每日一次，RPO 將遠超過 15 分鐘，而在故障時於 DR Region 還原快照既緩慢又需最多手動作業，使 4 小時 RTO 面臨風險。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.Promote.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.XRgn.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/disaster-recovery-workloads-on-aws/disaster-recovery-options-in-the-cloud.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":108,"question_en":"A large enterprise is deploying a web application on AWS. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. The instances run in an Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. The application stores data in an Amazon RDS for Oracle DB instance and Amazon DynamoDB. There are separate environments for development, testing, and production. What is the MOST secure and flexible way to obtain password credentials during deployment?","question_zh":"一家大型企业正在 AWS 上部署一个网络应用程序。该应用程序在应用负载均衡器后面的亚马逊 EC2 实例上 运行。这些实例在多个可用区的自动扩展组中运行。应用程序的数据存储在亚马逊 RDS for Oracle 数据库实 例和亚马逊 DynamoDB 中。开发、测试和生产环境是分开的。 在部署过程中，获取密码凭证最安全且最灵活的方式是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Retrieve an access key from an AWS Systems Manager SecureString parameter to access AWS services. Retrieve the database credentials from a Systems Manager SecureString parameter.","B":"Launch the EC2 instances with an EC2 IAM role to access AWS services. Retrieve the database credentials from AWS Secrets Manager.","C":"Retrieve an access key from an AWS Systems Manager plaintext parameter to access AWS services. Retrieve the database credentials from a Systems Manager SecureString parameter.","D":"Launch the EC2 instances with an EC2 IAM role to access AWS services. Store the database passwords in an encrypted config file with the application artifacts."},"options_zh":{"A":"从 AWS 系统管理器的 SecureString 参数中获取访问密钥以访问 AWS 服务。从系统管理器的 SecureString 参数中获取数据库凭据。","B":"使用具有访问 AWS 服务权限的 EC2 IAM 角色启动 EC2 实例。从 AWS Secrets Manager 中获取数 据库凭证。","C":"从 AWS 系统管理器的明文参数中检索访问密钥以访问 AWS 服务。从系统管理器的 SecureString 参 数中检索数据库凭据。","D":"使用具有访问 AWS 服务权限的 EC2 IAM 角色启动 EC2 实例。将数据库密码存储在与应用程序 工件一起的加密配置文件中。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The AWS-recommended pattern for workloads on EC2 is to attach an IAM role via an instance profile. AWS automatically delivers temporary, auto-rotating credentials to the instance, and the AWS SDK discovers them, so there is no need to distribute long-lived IAM user access keys. The IAM best-practices guide states explicitly: 'When you're building on an AWS compute service, such as Amazon EC2... AWS delivers the temporary credentials of an IAM role to that compute resource... there is no need to distribute long lived credentials.' This is the most secure way for the app to call AWS services such as DynamoDB. For the RDS for Oracle database password, AWS Secrets Manager is purpose-built to 'manage, retrieve, and rotate database credentials,' replacing hard-coded credentials with a runtime call and supporting automatic rotation and separate secrets per environment (dev/test/prod). Option B uniquely combines both best practices (IAM role for AWS access + Secrets Manager for DB credentials), making it the MOST secure and flexible answer.","explanation_zh":"對於在 EC2 上執行的工作負載，AWS 建議的做法是透過 instance profile 將 IAM role 附加到執行個體。AWS 會自動將暫時且會自動輪替的憑證交付給執行個體，AWS SDK 會自動探索並使用，因此不需要散布長期有效的 IAM user access key。IAM 最佳做法文件明確指出：在 Amazon EC2 等 AWS 運算服務上建置時，AWS 會將 IAM role 的暫時憑證交付給該運算資源，無需散布長期憑證。這是讓應用程式存取 DynamoDB 等 AWS 服務最安全的方式。至於 RDS for Oracle 的資料庫密碼，AWS Secrets Manager 專為管理、擷取與輪替資料庫憑證而設計，可用執行階段呼叫取代硬編碼憑證，並支援自動輪替以及為每個環境（dev/test/prod）維護獨立祕密。選項 B 同時結合這兩項最佳做法（以 IAM role 存取 AWS、以 Secrets Manager 管理資料庫憑證），是最安全且最具彈性的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Storing an access key in an SSM SecureString still relies on a long-lived IAM user access key, which AWS explicitly recommends against for workloads on EC2 (use IAM roles delivering temporary credentials instead). Although SecureString encrypts the value, the credential model is inferior to an IAM role, and SSM SecureString offers no native automatic rotation for DB credentials.","why_zh":"把 access key 存放在 SSM SecureString 仍依賴長期有效的 IAM user access key，而 AWS 明確建議 EC2 上的工作負載改用提供暫時憑證的 IAM role。雖然 SecureString 會加密該值，但其憑證模型不如 IAM role，且 SSM SecureString 對資料庫憑證沒有原生自動輪替功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Storing an access key in an SSM plaintext (String) parameter is the least secure option: the long-lived credential is unencrypted at rest and still violates the IAM-role best practice. It is strictly worse than A.","why_zh":"將 access key 存放在 SSM 純文字（String）參數是最不安全的做法：長期憑證未加密，且同樣違反使用 IAM role 的最佳做法，比 A 更糟。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The IAM role half is correct, but storing the database password in an encrypted config file bundled with the application artifacts effectively hard-codes the secret with the app. This makes rotation hard, ties the secret to the deployment, and is less secure and less flexible than Secrets Manager, which AWS recommends for database credentials and which provides automatic rotation and per-environment secrets.","why_zh":"IAM role 的部分正確，但把資料庫密碼存在與應用程式構件一起打包的加密設定檔，等於把祕密硬編碼隨應用程式一起部署，輪替困難、祕密與部署綁定，且不如 Secrets Manager 安全與彈性；AWS 建議資料庫憑證使用 Secrets Manager，並提供自動輪替與各環境獨立祕密。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/rotating-secrets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_switch-role-ec2.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":109,"question_en":"The security team depends on AWS CloudTrail to detect sensitive security issues in the company’s AWS account. The DevOps engineer needs a solution to auto-remediate CloudTrail being turned off in an AWS account. What solution ensures the LEAST amount of downtime for the CloudTrail log deliveries?","question_zh":"安全团队依靠 AWS CloudTrail 来检测公司 AWS 账户中的敏感安全问题。DevOps 工程师需要一个解决方 案来自动修复 AWS 账户中 CloudTrail 被关闭的情况。 哪种解决方案能确保 CloudTrail 日志交付的停机时间最短？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for the CloudTrail StopLogging event. Create an AWS Lambda function that uses the AWS SDK to call StartLogging on the ARN of the resource in which StopLogging was called. Add the Lambda function ARN as a target to the EventBridge rule.","B":"Deploy the AWS-managed CloudTrail-enabled AWS Config rule, set with a periodic interval of 1 hour. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for AWS Config rules compliance change. Create an AWS Lambda function that uses the AWS SDK to call StartLogging on the ARN of the resource in which StopLogging was called. Add the Lambda function ARN as a target to the EventBridge rule.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for a scheduled event every 5 minutes. Create an AWS Lambda function that uses the AWS SDK to call StartLogging on a CloudTrail trail in the AWS account. Add the Lambda function ARN as a target to the EventBridge rule.","D":"Launch a t2.nano instance with a script running every 5 minutes that uses the AWS SDK to query CloudTrail in the current account. If the CloudTrail trail is disabled, have the script re-enable the trail."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 CloudTrail 的 StopLogging 事件创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。创建一个使用 AWS SDK 调用 StartLogging 的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数针对的是调用 StopLogging 的资源的 ARN。将 Lambda 函数 的 ARN 作为目标添加到 EventBridge 规则中。","B":"部署由 AWS 管理的启用 CloudTrail 的 AWS Config 规则，并将其设置为每 1 小时执行一次。为 AWS Config 规则合规性变更创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。创建一个使用 AWS SDK 调用 StartLogging 的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数针对调用了 StopLogging 的资源的 ARN。将 Lambda 函数 的 ARN 作为目标添加到 EventBridge 规则中。","C":"创建一个每 5 分钟触发一次的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。创建一个使用 AWS SDK 调用 AWS 账户中 CloudTrail 跟踪的 StartLogging 操作的 AWS Lambda 函数。将 Lambda 函数的 ARN 作为目标添加到 EventBridge 规则中。","D":"启动一个 t2.nano 实例，运行一个每 5 分钟执行一次的脚本，该脚本使用 AWS SDK 查询当前账户中的 CloudTrail 跟踪。如果 CloudTrail 跟踪已禁用，让脚本重新启用该跟踪。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is LEAST amount of downtime for CloudTrail log deliveries, so the fastest detect-and-remediate path wins. Option A is fully event-driven: StopLogging is a CloudTrail write (mutating) management event, which CloudTrail delivers to the default EventBridge event bus as an 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' event and is matched by a rule in the default ENABLED state with no extra configuration; the EventBridge rule then invokes a Lambda function that calls StartLogging on the exact trail ARN from the event detail, so logging is restored within seconds. Option B uses the AWS managed Config rule cloudtrail-enabled (CLOUD_TRAIL_ENABLED), whose Trigger type is Periodic only; at a 1-hour interval, detection and therefore remediation can lag up to an hour, and the Config compliance-change event does not carry the StopLogging resource ARN the Lambda is described as using. Options C and D both poll on a 5-minute schedule, leaving up to five minutes of downtime, are not event-driven, and additionally hardcode a single trail (C) or add the operational overhead of running and patching an EC2 instance (D). Therefore A minimizes downtime and is the correct answer.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是「CloudTrail 日誌傳遞的停機時間最短」，因此偵測與補救最快的方案勝出。選項 A 完全事件驅動：StopLogging 屬於 CloudTrail 的寫入（變動型）management event，CloudTrail 會將其以 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' 事件傳送到預設的 EventBridge event bus，並由處於預設 ENABLED 狀態的 rule 比對到，無需額外設定；EventBridge rule 接著觸發 Lambda，對事件 detail 中該 trail 的確切 ARN 呼叫 StartLogging，因此可在數秒內恢復記錄。選項 B 使用 AWS 受管 Config rule cloudtrail-enabled (CLOUD_TRAIL_ENABLED)，其 Trigger type 僅為 Periodic；以 1 小時間隔評估時，偵測（進而補救）可能延遲長達一小時，且 Config compliance-change 事件並不會帶有該 Lambda 所述使用的 StopLogging 資源 ARN。選項 C 與 D 皆以 5 分鐘排程輪詢，最多會有 5 分鐘停機、非事件驅動，且 C 寫死單一 trail、D 還增加運行與修補 EC2 執行個體的營運負擔。因此 A 能將停機時間降到最低，為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The cloudtrail-enabled managed Config rule (CLOUD_TRAIL_ENABLED) has Trigger type Periodic only (confirmed in the AWS Config docs); a 1-hour interval means remediation can lag up to an hour, producing far more downtime than event-driven A. A Config compliance-change event also does not contain the StopLogging resource ARN the Lambda is said to use.","why_zh":"cloudtrail-enabled 受管 Config rule (CLOUD_TRAIL_ENABLED) 的 Trigger type 僅為 Periodic（AWS Config 文件已確認）；1 小時間隔代表補救可能延遲長達一小時，停機時間遠超過事件驅動的 A。且 Config compliance-change 事件並不含 Lambda 所述的 StopLogging 資源 ARN。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A 5-minute scheduled poll leaves up to 5 minutes of downtime and is not event-driven; it also hardcodes a single named trail rather than acting on whichever trail was stopped.","why_zh":"5 分鐘排程輪詢最多會有 5 分鐘停機且非事件驅動；同時寫死單一 trail，而非針對被停用的那個 trail 作業。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running a t2.nano EC2 instance polling every 5 minutes adds the highest operational overhead (instance management, patching) and still allows up to 5 minutes of downtime; it is the least cloud-native option.","why_zh":"運行 t2.nano EC2 執行個體每 5 分鐘輪詢，營運負擔最高（執行個體管理、修補），且仍最多有 5 分鐘停機，是最不符合雲端原生的方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/cloudtrail-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-turning-off-logging.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/code-library/latest/ug/cloudtrail_example_cloudtrail_StopLogging_section.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":110,"question_en":"A company uses AWS CodeArtifact to centrally store Python packages. The CodeArtifact repository is configured with the following repository policy: A development team is building a new project in an account that is in an organization in AWS Organizations. The development team wants to use a Python library that has already been stored in the CodeArtifact repository in the organization. The development team uses AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild to build the new application. The CodeBuild job that the development team uses to build the application is configured to run in a VPC. Because of compliance requirements, the VPC has no internet connectivity. The development team creates the VPC endpoints for CodeArtifact and updates the CodeBuild buildspec.yaml file. However, the development team cannot download the Python library from the repository. Which combination of steps should a DevOps engineer take so that the development team can use CodeArtifact? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodeArtifact 来集中存储 Python 包。CodeArtifact 存储库配置了以下存储库策略： 一个开发团队正在 AWS 组织中的一个账户内构建一个新项目。该开发团队希望使用已存储 在组织的 CodeArtifact 存储库中的 Python 库。开发团队使用 AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 来构建新应用程序。开发团队用于构建应用程序的 CodeBuild 作业配置为在 VPC 中运行。由于合规性要求，该 VPC 没有互联网连接。 开发团队为 CodeArtifact 创建了 VPC 端点，并更新了 CodeBuild 的 buildspec.yaml 文 件。然而，开发团队无法从存储库下载 Python 库。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤的组合，才能让开发团队使用 CodeArtifact？（选择两 项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint. Update the route tables for the subnets that are running the CodeBuild job.","B":"Update the repository policy’s Principal statement to include the ARN of the role that the CodeBuild project uses.","C":"Share the CodeArtifact repository with the organization by using AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM).","D":"Update the role that the CodeBuild project uses so that the role has sufficient permissions to use the CodeArtifact repository.","E":"Specify the account that hosts the repository as the delegated administrator for CodeArtifact in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon S3 网关端点。更新运行 CodeBuild 作业的子网的路由表。","B":"将存储库策略的 Principal 语句更新为包含 CodeBuild 项目所使用角色的 ARN。","C":"使用 AWS 资源访问管理器（AWS RAM）与组织共享 CodeArtifact 存储库。","D":"更新 CodeBuild 项目所使用的角色，以便该角色拥有使用 CodeArtifact 存储库的足够权限。","E":"指定托管存储库的账户作为组织中 CodeArtifact 的委托管理员。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Cross-account access to an AWS CodeArtifact repository requires BOTH a resource-based policy on the producing side that names the consumer principal AND an identity-based policy on the consumer's IAM role; the IAM cross-account model requires both accounts to allow the access. Because the CodeBuild project's role lives in a different account, the repository (resource) policy must add that role's ARN to its Principal so the role is granted ReadFromRepository and related actions (B), and the CodeBuild role itself must carry sufficient CodeArtifact permissions such as GetAuthorizationToken, GetRepositoryEndpoint, and ReadFromRepository (D). The decisive qualifier is that the package is a Python library: the CodeArtifact documentation explicitly states 'An Amazon S3 endpoint is not needed when using Python or Swift package formats,' so the S3 gateway endpoint in option A is not the missing step for this Python scenario, which eliminates the dump's [A,D] answer. CodeArtifact controls cross-account sharing through repository and domain resource policies, not AWS RAM (C is invalid), and there is no CodeArtifact delegated-administrator mechanism that governs a consumer account's ability to download a package (E is irrelevant). Therefore the correct combination is B and D.","explanation_zh":"跨帳戶存取 AWS CodeArtifact repository 需要同時具備兩項條件：在提供端的 resource-based policy（repository/domain policy）中明確列出 consumer 端的 principal，並且 consumer 端的 IAM role 本身具有 identity-based policy 權限；IAM 的跨帳戶模型要求兩個帳戶都允許該存取。由於 CodeBuild 專案使用的 role 位於不同帳戶，repository（資源）policy 的 Principal 必須加入該 role 的 ARN，使其獲得 ReadFromRepository 等動作（B）；而 CodeBuild role 本身也必須擁有足夠的 CodeArtifact 權限，例如 GetAuthorizationToken、GetRepositoryEndpoint 與 ReadFromRepository（D）。關鍵的限定條件是套件為 Python library：CodeArtifact 官方文件明確指出『使用 Python 或 Swift package 格式時不需要 Amazon S3 endpoint』，因此選項 A 的 S3 gateway endpoint 並非此 Python 情境缺少的步驟，這也排除了 dump 的 [A,D] 答案。CodeArtifact 透過 repository 與 domain 的 resource policy 來控管跨帳戶分享，而非 AWS RAM（C 無效）；CodeArtifact 也沒有所謂的 delegated administrator 機制來控制 consumer 帳戶下載套件的能力（E 不相關）。因此正確組合為 B 與 D。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An S3 gateway endpoint lets CodeArtifact download package assets (e.g., Maven .jar files) from the underlying S3 bucket, but the CodeArtifact docs explicitly state 'An Amazon S3 endpoint is not needed when using Python or Swift package formats.' The scenario uses a Python library, so the S3 endpoint is not the missing step. This is the dump's incorrect suggestion.","why_zh":"S3 gateway endpoint 用於讓 CodeArtifact 從底層 S3 儲存桶下載套件資產（如 Maven .jar 檔），但 CodeArtifact 文件明確指出『使用 Python 或 Swift package 格式時不需要 Amazon S3 endpoint』。此情境使用 Python library，因此 S3 endpoint 並非缺少的步驟。此為 dump 的錯誤建議。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeArtifact does not use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share repositories. Cross-account and organization-wide access is granted through repository resource policies and domain policies, not RAM resource shares.","why_zh":"CodeArtifact 不透過 AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) 來分享 repository。跨帳戶與組織範圍的存取是透過 repository 的 resource policy 與 domain policy 授予，而非 RAM 資源分享。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"There is no CodeArtifact 'delegated administrator' role that controls whether a consumer account can download a package. Access to download packages is governed by repository and domain resource policies plus the consumer role's IAM permissions, so designating a delegated administrator does not resolve the failure.","why_zh":"CodeArtifact 並無控制 consumer 帳戶是否能下載套件的『delegated administrator』角色。下載套件的存取由 repository 與 domain 的 resource policy 加上 consumer 端 role 的 IAM 權限決定，因此指定 delegated administrator 無法解決此問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/create-s3-gateway-endpoint.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/create-vpc-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repo-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/security_iam_service-with-iam.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_identity-vs-resource.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":111,"question_en":"A company uses a series of individual Amazon CloudFormation templates to deploy its multi-Region applications. These templates must be deployed in a specific order. The company is making more changes to the templates than previously expected and wants to deploy new templates more efficiently. Additionally, the data engineering team must be notified of all changes to the templates. What should the company do to accomplish these goals?","question_zh":"一家公司使用一系列单独的亚马逊 CloudFormation 模板来部署其多区域应用程序。这些模板必须按照特 定顺序进行部署。该公司对模板所做的更改比预期的要多，并希望更高效地部署新模板。此外，数据工 程团队必须收到所有模板更改的通知。 公司应采取什么措施来实现这些目标？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to deploy the CloudFormation templates in the required order. Use stack policies to alert the data engineering team.","B":"Host the CloudFormation templates in Amazon S3. Use Amazon S3 events to directly trigger CloudFormation updates and Amazon SNS notifications.","C":"Implement CloudFormation StackSets and use drift detection to trigger update alerts to the data engineering team.","D":"Leverage CloudFormation nested stacks and stack sets for deployments. Use Amazon SNS to notify the data engineering team."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，按所需顺序部署 CloudFormation 模板。使用堆栈策略向数据工程团 队发出警报。","B":"将 CloudFormation 模板托管在 Amazon S3 中。使用 Amazon S3 事件直接触发 CloudFormation 更新，并使用 Amazon SNS 发送通知。","C":"实施 CloudFormation 栈集，并使用漂移检测向数据工程团队触发更新警报。","D":"利用 CloudFormation 嵌套堆栈和堆栈集进行部署。使用 Amazon SNS 通知数据工程团队。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The four requirements are: deploy the individual templates in a specific order, deploy across multiple Regions, do it more efficiently, and notify the data engineering team of every change. Nested stacks (the AWS::CloudFormation::Stack resource) let you compose the individual templates into a single root-stack deployment and enforce ordering with DependsOn (the AWS doc shows exactly this with 'DependsOn: MyFirstNestedStack'), so the templates deploy as one efficient unit instead of being orchestrated manually. StackSets natively deploy stacks across multiple Regions and accounts in a single operation. For notifications, Amazon SNS is the native CloudFormation mechanism: the CreateStack/UpdateStack NotificationARNs parameter is documented as 'The Amazon SNS topic ARNs to publish stack related events,' so the data engineering team can subscribe to the topic and be alerted on every change. Option D is the only choice that correctly satisfies all four requirements using native CloudFormation features, while every other option has a disqualifying flaw.","explanation_zh":"四個需求是：依特定順序部署個別範本、跨多個 Region 部署、更有效率地部署，並在每次變更時通知 data engineering 團隊。Nested stacks（AWS::CloudFormation::Stack 資源）可將多個個別範本組合成單一 root stack 部署，並用 DependsOn 強制執行順序（AWS 文件即以 'DependsOn: MyFirstNestedStack' 示範），讓範本以單一高效單位部署，而非手動編排。StackSets 原生支援以單一操作跨多個 Region 與帳戶部署 stacks。在通知方面，Amazon SNS 是 CloudFormation 原生機制：CreateStack/UpdateStack 的 NotificationARNs 參數在文件中明載為 'The Amazon SNS topic ARNs to publish stack related events'，因此 data engineering 團隊可訂閱該 topic 並在每次變更時收到提醒。選項 D 是唯一能用 CloudFormation 原生功能正確滿足全部四個需求的選項，其餘選項皆有致命缺陷。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A custom Lambda to enforce ordering is unnecessary reinvention because nested stacks with DependsOn do this natively. The decisive flaw is that stack policies do not alert anyone; the AWS doc titles them 'Prevent updates to stack resources' and they use Deny/Allow statements to protect resources from unintended updates, so they cannot notify the data engineering team.","why_zh":"用自訂 Lambda 強制順序是多餘的重造，因為搭配 DependsOn 的 nested stacks 原生即可達成。決定性缺陷在於 stack policies 不會通知任何人；AWS 文件將其標題為 'Prevent updates to stack resources'，它以 Deny/Allow 陳述式保護資源不被意外更新，因此無法通知 data engineering 團隊。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 events cannot directly trigger CloudFormation stack updates; there is no native S3-to-CloudFormation-update integration (it would require Lambda or EventBridge glue to call UpdateStack). It also ignores the deployment-ordering requirement entirely.","why_zh":"S3 events 無法直接觸發 CloudFormation stack 更新；沒有原生的 S3 到 CloudFormation 更新整合（需透過 Lambda 或 EventBridge 串接去呼叫 UpdateStack）。它也完全忽略了部署順序需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Drift detection finds divergence between deployed resources and their last-applied template state; it does not detect or alert on changes made to the templates themselves, so it cannot notify the team 'of all changes to the templates.' StackSets alone also does not enforce deployment ordering among the separate individual templates.","why_zh":"Drift detection 偵測的是已部署資源與其最後套用範本狀態之間的差異；它無法偵測或對範本本身的變更發出提醒，因此無法就『所有範本變更』通知團隊。單用 StackSets 也無法在多個個別範本之間強制執行部署順序。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-nested-stacks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/APIReference/API_CreateStack.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/what-is-cfnstacksets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/protect-stack-resources.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":112,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer has implemented a CI/CD pipeline to deploy an AWS CloudFormation template that provisions a web application. The web application consists of an Application Load Balancer (ALB), a target group, a launch template that uses an Amazon Linux 2 AMI, an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances, a security group, and an Amazon RDS for MySQL database. The launch template includes user data that specifies a script to install and start the application. The initial deployment of the application was successful. The DevOps engineer made changes to update the version of the application with the user data. The CI/CD pipeline has deployed a new version of the template. However, the health checks on the ALB are now failing. The health checks have marked all targets as unhealthy. During investigation, the DevOps engineer notices that the CloudFormation stack has a status of UPDATE_COMPLETE. However, when the DevOps engineer connects to one of the EC2 instances and checks /var/log/messages, the DevOps engineer notices that the Apache web server failed to start successfully because of a configuration error. How can the DevOps engineer ensure that the CloudFormation deployment will fail if the user data fails to successfully finish running?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师已实现了一条 CI/CD 管道，用于部署一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，该模板可配置 一个网络应用程序。该网络应用程序由一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）、一个目标组、一个使用 Amazon Linux 2 AMI 的启动模板、一个 Amazon EC2 实例的自动扩展组、一个安全组以及一个 Amazon RDS MySQL 数据库组成。启动模板包含用户数据，其中指定了用于安装和启动应用程序的脚本。 应用程序的初始部署成功了。开发运维工程师对应用程序进行了更新，以包含用户数据。持续集成/持 续部署（CI/CD）流水线已部署了模板的新版本。然而，应用负载均衡器（ALB）的健康检查现在失败 了。健康检查已将所有目标标记为不健康。 在调查过程中，DevOps 工程师注意到 CloudFormation 堆栈的状态为 UPDATE_COMPLETE。然而，当 DevOps 工程师连接到其中一个 EC2 实例并检查 /var/log/messages 时，发现由于配置错误，Apache 网 络服务器未能成功启动。 DevOps 工程师如何确保如果用户数据未能成功运行完毕，CloudFormation 部署就会失败？","options_en":{"A":"Use the cfn-signal helper script to signal success or failure to CloudFormation. Use the WaitOnResourceSignals update policy within the CloudFormation template. Set an appropriate timeout for the update policy.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for the UnhealthyHostCount metric. Include an appropriate alarm threshold for the target group. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as the target to signal success or failure to CloudFormation.","C":"Create a lifecycle hook on the Auto Scaling group by using the AWS::AutoScaling::LifecycleHook resource. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as the target to signal success or failure to CloudFormation. Set an appropriate timeout on the lifecycle hook.","D":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to stream the cloud-init logs. Create a subscription filter that includes an AWS Lambda function with an appropriate invocation timeout. Configure the Lambda function to use the SignalResource API operation to signal success or failure to CloudFormation."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 cfn-signal 辅助脚本向 CloudFormation 发送成功或失败的信号。在 CloudFormation 模板中使用 WaitOnResourceSignals 更新策略。为更新策略设置适当的超时时间。","B":"为 UnhealthyHostCount 指标创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。为目标组设置适当的警报阈值。 创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题作为 CloudFormation 的目标，以发送成功 或失败的信号。 CAutoScaling::LifecycleHook 资源在自动扩展组上创建生命周期挂钩。创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题作为目标，向 CloudFormation 发送成功或失败的信号。为生命周期挂钩设 置适当的超时时间。","D":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理来流式传输 cloud-init 日志。创建一个订阅筛选器，其中包含一个 具有适当调用超时设置的 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以使用 SignalResource API 操 作向 CloudFormation 发送成功或失败的信号。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is a stack UPDATE (the stack reached UPDATE_COMPLETE), and the user data lives in the launch template, so changing it changes the AutoScalingGroup's LaunchTemplate property, which AWS docs explicitly list as a trigger for an AutoScalingRollingUpdate. The CreationPolicy attribute is invoked only when CloudFormation creates a resource, so it cannot help on an update; the correct construct is the UpdatePolicy attribute. The cfn-signal helper script is designed to be used with a CreationPolicy OR an UpdatePolicy that has WaitOnResourceSignals set to true for EC2 Auto Scaling groups. When WaitOnResourceSignals is true, CloudFormation suspends the rolling update for each replaced batch and waits the PauseTime for the required success signals; if user data fails (Apache config error) it sends a failure signal, or simply sends no signal before PauseTime expires, and CloudFormation fails the update and rolls back instead of reaching UPDATE_COMPLETE. Setting an appropriate timeout (PauseTime, default PT5M) gives the application time to start. This is exactly the native, purpose-built mechanism that makes the deployment fail when user data does not finish successfully.","explanation_zh":"這是一次 stack UPDATE（stack 已達到 UPDATE_COMPLETE），而 user data 位於 launch template 中，因此修改它會改變 AutoScalingGroup 的 LaunchTemplate 屬性；AWS 文件明確將此列為觸發 AutoScalingRollingUpdate 的條件之一。CreationPolicy 屬性只在 CloudFormation 建立資源時才會被調用，因此在更新情境下無法生效；正確的機制是 UpdatePolicy 屬性。cfn-signal helper script 的設計就是搭配 CreationPolicy，或搭配將 WaitOnResourceSignals 設為 true 的 UpdatePolicy（用於 EC2 Auto Scaling group）。當 WaitOnResourceSignals 為 true 時，CloudFormation 會在每個替換批次暫停 rolling update，並依 PauseTime 等待所需的成功訊號；若 user data 失敗（Apache 設定錯誤），它會送出失敗訊號，或在 PauseTime 逾時前未送出任何訊號，CloudFormation 便會讓更新失敗並回滾，而不會達到 UPDATE_COMPLETE。設定適當的 timeout（PauseTime，預設 PT5M）可給應用程式足夠的啟動時間。這正是讓部署在 user data 未成功完成時失敗的原生、專用機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A CloudWatch alarm on UnhealthyHostCount with an SNS topic cannot signal success or failure to CloudFormation. SNS is a notification target, not a CloudFormation signaling mechanism; there is no native path where an alarm/SNS causes a CloudFormation stack update to fail or roll back. CloudFormation only accepts signals via cfn-signal/SignalResource against CreationPolicy or UpdatePolicy WaitOnResourceSignals, so this design does not gate the deployment.","why_zh":"在 UnhealthyHostCount 上建立 CloudWatch alarm 並用 SNS topic，無法向 CloudFormation 傳遞成功或失敗訊號。SNS 只是通知目標，並非 CloudFormation 的訊號機制；不存在 alarm/SNS 使 CloudFormation stack 更新失敗或回滾的原生路徑。CloudFormation 只透過 cfn-signal/SignalResource 搭配 CreationPolicy 或 UpdatePolicy 的 WaitOnResourceSignals 接收訊號，因此此設計無法把關部署。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An Auto Scaling lifecycle hook completes its lifecycle action against the Auto Scaling group (CONTINUE/ABANDON), not against CloudFormation, and an SNS topic cannot signal success or failure to CloudFormation. A hook fires on instance launch but does not verify that Apache actually started from the user data, so it cannot reliably detect the configuration error. The stated mechanism of using SNS to signal CloudFormation is incorrect.","why_zh":"Auto Scaling lifecycle hook 是對 Auto Scaling group 完成生命週期動作（CONTINUE/ABANDON），而非對 CloudFormation；SNS topic 也無法向 CloudFormation 傳遞成功或失敗訊號。Hook 在執行個體啟動時觸發，但不會驗證 user data 中的 Apache 是否真正啟動，因此無法可靠地偵測設定錯誤。題目所述用 SNS 向 CloudFormation 傳訊號的機制是錯誤的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Although SignalResource is a valid CloudFormation API, this design is a fragile, over-engineered chain: CloudWatch agent to stream cloud-init logs, a subscription filter, and a Lambda that parses logs to decide success/failure. It still requires an UpdatePolicy/CreationPolicy on the resource for the signal to matter, and log parsing is far less reliable than the purpose-built cfn-signal helper. AWS recommends cfn-signal with WaitOnResourceSignals, making this the inferior choice.","why_zh":"雖然 SignalResource 是有效的 CloudFormation API，但此設計是脆弱且過度複雜的鏈路：用 CloudWatch agent 串流 cloud-init 日誌、subscription filter，再用 Lambda 解析日誌以判斷成功/失敗。它仍需資源上具備 UpdatePolicy/CreationPolicy 訊號才有意義，且解析日誌遠不如專用的 cfn-signal helper 可靠。AWS 建議使用 cfn-signal 搭配 WaitOnResourceSignals，使本選項成為較差的方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/cfn-signal.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-attribute-updatepolicy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-attribute-creationpolicy.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":113,"question_en":"A company has a data ingestion application that runs across multiple AWS accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company needs to monitor the application and consolidate access to the application. Currently, the company is running the application on Amazon EC2 instances from several Auto Scaling groups. The EC2 instances have no access to the internet because the data is sensitive. Engineers have deployed the necessary VPC endpoints. The EC2 instances run a custom AMI that is built specifically for the application. To maintain and troubleshoot the application, system administrators need the ability to log in to the EC2 instances. This access must be automated and controlled centrally. The company’s security team must receive a notification whenever the instances are accessed. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款跨多个 AWS 账户运行的数据摄取应用程序。这些账户位于 AWS 组织中的一个组 织内。该公司需要监控该应用程序并集中访问权限。目前，该公司在来自多个自动扩展组的 Amazon EC2 实例上运行该应用程序。由于数据敏感，这些 EC2 实例无法访问互联网。工程师已部署了必要 的 VPC 端点。EC2 实例运行的是专门为该应用程序构建的自定义 AMI。 为了维护和排查应用程序故障，系统管理员需要能够登录到 EC2 实例。这种访问权限必须实现自动 化并进行集中控制。每当实例被访问时，公司的安全团队都必须收到通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to send notifications to the security team whenever a user logs in to an EC2 instance. Use EC2 Instance Connect to log in to the instances. Deploy Auto Scaling groups by using AWS CloudFormation. Use the cfn-init helper script to deploy appropriate VPC routes for external access. Rebuild the custom AMI so that the custom AMI includes AWS Systems Manager Agent.","B":"Deploy a NAT gateway and a bastion host that has internet access. Create a security group that allows incoming traffic on all the EC2 instances from the bastion host. Install AWS Systems Manager Agent on all the EC2 instances. Use Auto Scaling group lifecycle hooks for monitoring and auditing access. Use Systems Manager Session Manager to log in to the instances. Send logs to a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Export data to Amazon S3 for auditing. Send notifications to the security team by using S3 event notifications.","C":"Use EC2 Image Builder to rebuild the custom AMI. Include the most recent version of AWS Systems Manager Agent in the image. Configure the Auto Scaling group to attach the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore role to all the EC2 instances. Use Systems Manager Session Manager to log in to the instances. Enable logging of session details to Amazon S3. Create an S3 event notification for new file uploads to send a message to the security team through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager Automation to build Systems Manager Agent into the custom AMI. Configure AWS Config to attach an SCP to the root organization account to allow the EC2 instances to connect to Systems Manager. Use Systems Manager Session Manager to log in to the instances. Enable logging of session details to Amazon S3. Create an S3 event notification for new file uploads to send a message to the security team through an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便每当用户登录到 EC2 实例时向安全团队发送通知。使用 EC2 实例连接登录到实例。通过 AWS CloudFormation 部署自动扩展组。使用 cfn-init 辅助脚本部 署适当的 VPC 路由以实现外部访问。重新构建自定义 AMI，使其包含 AWS Systems Manager Agent。","B":"部署一个网络地址转换（NAT）网关和一个具有互联网访问权限的堡垒主机。创建一个安全组，允 许来自堡垒主机的所有入站流量访问所有 EC2 实例。在所有 EC2 实例上安装 AWS 系统管理器代 理。使用自动扩展组生命周期挂钩进行监控和访问审计。使用系统管理器会话管理器登录实例。 将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中的日志组。将数据导出到 Amazon S3 以进行审计。使用 S3 事件通知向安全团队发送通知。","C":"使用 EC2 Image Builder 重新构建自定义 AMI。在映像中包含 AWS Systems Manager Agent 的最新 版本。配置自动缩放组，将 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 角色附加到所有 EC2 实例。使用 Systems Manager Session Manager 登录到实例。启用会话详细信息的日志记录到 Amazon S3。为 新文件上传创建 S3 事件通知，通过 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题向安全团队发 送消息。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 将 Systems Manager Agent 构建到自定义 AMI 中。配置 AWS Config 以将 SCP 附加到根组织账户，从而允许 EC2 实例连接到 Systems Manager。使用 Systems Manager Session Manager 登录到实例。启用会话详细信息的日志记录到 Amazon S3。为 新文件上传创建 S3 事件通知，通过 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题向安全团队发送 消息。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Every requirement points to AWS Systems Manager Session Manager: it provides centrally controlled, automated, fully auditable interactive login with no inbound ports, no bastion, and no internet access, working over the already-deployed VPC interface endpoints (ssm, ssmmessages, ec2messages). Option C is the only fully correct path. EC2 Image Builder rebuilds the custom AMI and bundles the latest SSM Agent; attaching the AWS managed AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore role to the instances grants exactly the permissions Session Manager needs (AWS docs: \"If an instance profile that contains the AWS managed policy AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore is already attached to your instances, the required permissions for Session Manager are already provided\"); Session Manager logs session details to Amazon S3; and an S3 event notification on new object uploads triggers an Amazon SNS topic to alert the security team. This satisfies the no-internet constraint plus the central, automated, and notified-on-access requirements without any of the broken mechanisms in the other options.","explanation_zh":"所有需求都指向 AWS Systems Manager Session Manager：它提供集中控管、自動化、完全可稽核的互動式登入，無需開放入站連接埠、無需 bastion、也不需要網際網路存取，可透過已部署的 VPC interface endpoint（ssm、ssmmessages、ec2messages）運作。選項 C 是唯一完全正確的方案。EC2 Image Builder 重建自訂 AMI 並內建最新版 SSM Agent；將 AWS 受控政策 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 角色附加到執行個體，即可提供 Session Manager 所需的精確權限（AWS 文件指出：若執行個體已附加包含 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 受控政策的 instance profile，Session Manager 所需的權限即已具備）；Session Manager 將工作階段細節記錄到 Amazon S3；新物件上傳的 S3 event notification 觸發 Amazon SNS 主題以通知安全團隊。這滿足無網際網路存取的限制，以及集中、自動化、存取時通知的需求，且不含其他選項中的錯誤機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using cfn-init to deploy VPC routes for external (internet) access directly contradicts the explicit requirement that the instances have no internet access because the data is sensitive. In addition, Amazon EventBridge has no native event that fires when an OS-level user logs in to an EC2 instance, so the described login notification would not work.","why_zh":"用 cfn-init 部署 VPC 路由以提供外部（網際網路）存取，直接違反了因資料敏感而要求執行個體不可連網的明確需求。此外，Amazon EventBridge 並沒有針對使用者作業系統層級登入 EC2 觸發的原生事件，因此所描述的登入通知無法運作。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Deploying a NAT gateway and a bastion host that has internet access violates the explicit no-internet requirement for these sensitive-data instances and reintroduces the very SSH/bastion overhead that Session Manager eliminates. Auto Scaling group lifecycle hooks fire on instance launch and terminate transitions, not on interactive login, so they cannot monitor or audit administrator access as claimed.","why_zh":"部署具網際網路存取的 NAT gateway 與 bastion host，違反了這些敏感資料執行個體不可連網的明確需求，並重新引入了 Session Manager 旨在消除的 SSH／bastion 維運負擔。Auto Scaling group lifecycle hook 是在執行個體啟動與終止的轉換時觸發，而非在互動式登入時觸發，因此無法如其所述監控或稽核管理員存取。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This option is fundamentally broken: AWS documentation states plainly that SCPs do not grant permissions ('No permissions are granted by an SCP. An SCP defines a permission guardrail'), so an SCP can never 'allow EC2 instances to connect to Systems Manager' — that requires an IAM instance role such as AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore. SCPs are also managed by AWS Organizations, not by AWS Config (which only evaluates configuration compliance), and SSM Automation is not the mechanism for baking an agent into a custom AMI.","why_zh":"此選項在根本上是錯的：AWS 文件明確指出 SCP 不會授予權限（『SCP 不授予任何權限。SCP 定義的是權限護欄』），因此 SCP 永遠無法『允許 EC2 執行個體連線到 Systems Manager』——那需要像 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 這樣的 IAM 執行個體角色。SCP 由 AWS Organizations 管理，而非 AWS Config（Config 僅評估組態合規性），而 SSM Automation 也不是將代理程式內建到自訂 AMI 的機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-getting-started-instance-profile.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager-logging-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/set-up-ib-env.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":114,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon S3 to store proprietary information. The development team creates buckets for new projects on a daily basis. The security team wants to ensure that all existing and future buckets have encryption, logging, and versioning enabled. Additionally, no buckets should ever be publicly read or write accessible. What should a DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 S3 存储专有信息。开发团队每天都会为新项目创建存储桶。安全团队希望确保 所有现有和未来的存储桶都启用加密、日志记录和版本控制功能。此外，任何存储桶都不应公开可读 或可写。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS CloudTrail and configure automatic remediation using AWS Lambda.","B":"Enable AWS Config rules and configure automatic remediation using AWS Systems Manager documents.","C":"Enable AWS Trusted Advisor and configure automatic remediation using Amazon EventBridge.","D":"Enable AWS Systems Manager and configure automatic remediation using Systems Manager documents."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 AWS CloudTrail 并使用 AWS Lambda 配置自动修复。","B":"启用 AWS Config 规则，并使用 AWS Systems Manager 文档配置自动修复。","C":"启用 AWS 可信顾问，并使用 Amazon EventBridge 配置自动修复。","D":"启用 AWS 系统管理器，并使用系统管理器文档配置自动修复。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config is the purpose-built service for continuously evaluating resource configurations against a desired state, and because it continuously discovers and records resources, both existing buckets and the buckets created daily are automatically assessed. AWS supplies managed Config rules covering every requirement: s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled (encryption), s3-bucket-logging-enabled (logging), s3-bucket-versioning-enabled (versioning), and s3-bucket-public-read-prohibited / s3-bucket-public-write-prohibited (no public read/write). The AWS Config remediation documentation explicitly states that AWS Config applies remediation using AWS Systems Manager (SSM) Automation documents, which define the actions performed on noncompliant resources, and auto remediation can be enabled per rule. This is exactly the architecture described in option B: enable AWS Config rules and configure automatic remediation using Systems Manager documents.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 是專門用來持續評估資源組態是否符合期望狀態的服務；由於它會持續探索並記錄資源，因此現有的 bucket 與每日新建立的 bucket 都會被自動評估。AWS 提供的 managed Config rules 涵蓋所有需求：s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled（加密）、s3-bucket-logging-enabled（記錄）、s3-bucket-versioning-enabled（版本控制），以及 s3-bucket-public-read-prohibited / s3-bucket-public-write-prohibited（禁止公開讀寫）。AWS Config 修復文件明確指出，AWS Config 是使用 AWS Systems Manager（SSM）Automation documents 來執行修復，這些文件定義對不合規資源所執行的動作，且可針對每條規則啟用 auto remediation。這正是選項 B 所描述的架構：啟用 AWS Config rules 並使用 Systems Manager documents 設定自動修復。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudTrail only records API activity (an audit/event log); it does not evaluate whether a bucket has encryption, logging, or versioning enabled, nor does it continuously assess resources against a desired configuration state. While a Lambda function could perform a remediation action, CloudTrail is not the detective compliance engine AWS provides for this scenario, and building event-driven Lambda detection for every requirement is far more complex than the managed Config rules in option B.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 只記錄 API 活動（稽核／事件日誌），不會評估 bucket 是否已啟用加密、記錄或版本控制，也無法持續對照期望組態狀態評估資源。雖然 Lambda 函式可執行修復動作，但 CloudTrail 並非 AWS 為此情境提供的合規偵測引擎，且為每項需求自行建構事件驅動的 Lambda 偵測，遠比選項 B 的 managed Config rules 複雜。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Trusted Advisor provides periodic best-practice checks (cost, security, fault tolerance, etc.) but it is not a continuous configuration-compliance engine with managed rules covering all four S3 requirements, and it does not integrate with EventBridge to drive structured rule-plus-SSM-document auto-remediation the way AWS Config does. It is not the AWS-recommended detective control for enforcing specific resource configurations.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 提供成本、安全、容錯等面向的定期最佳實務檢查，但並非具備涵蓋全部四項 S3 需求 managed rules 的持續組態合規引擎，也無法像 AWS Config 那樣透過 EventBridge 以結構化的規則加 SSM 文件方式驅動自動修復。它不是 AWS 建議用來強制執行特定資源組態的偵測控制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Systems Manager (and its Automation documents) is the remediation/execution engine, not the compliance-detection engine. SSM does not by itself continuously evaluate S3 buckets against encryption/logging/versioning/public-access requirements; that detection is AWS Config's role. SSM documents are precisely the remediation mechanism that AWS Config invokes, so 'Systems Manager + Systems Manager documents' alone lacks the detective component (Config rules) needed to find noncompliant buckets.","why_zh":"Systems Manager（及其 Automation documents）是修復／執行引擎，而非合規偵測引擎。SSM 本身不會持續對 S3 bucket 評估加密／記錄／版本控制／公開存取需求；該偵測屬於 AWS Config 的職責。SSM 文件正是 AWS Config 觸發的修復機制，因此單靠『Systems Manager + Systems Manager documents』缺少找出不合規 bucket 所需的偵測元件（Config rules）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-public-read-prohibited.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/managed-rules-by-aws-config.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":115,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is researching the least expensive way to implement an image batch processing cluster on AWS. The application cannot run in Docker containers and must run on Amazon EC2. The batch job stores checkpoint data on an NFS volume and can tolerate interruptions. Configuring the cluster software from a generic EC2 Linux image takes 30 minutes. What is the MOST cost-effective solution?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在研究在 AWS 上以最低成本实现图像批处理集群的方法。该应用程序无法在 Docker 容器中运行，必须在 Amazon EC2 上运行。批处理作业将检查点数据存储在 NFS 卷上，并且能够容忍中断。 从通用的 EC2 Linux 镜像配置集群软件需要 30 分钟。 哪种方案的成本效益最高？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon EFS for checkpoint data. To complete the job, use an EC2 Auto Scaling group and an On-Demand pricing model to provision EC2 instances temporarily.","B":"Use GlusterFS on EC2 instances for checkpoint data. To run the batch job, configure EC2 instances manually. When the job completes, shut down the instances manually.","C":"Use Amazon EFS for checkpoint data. Use EC2 Fleet to launch EC2 Spot Instances, and utilize user data to configure the EC2 Linux instance on startup.","D":"Use Amazon EFS for checkpoint data. Use EC2 Fleet to launch EC2 Spot Instances. Create a custom AMI for the cluster and use the latest AMI when creating instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon EFS 来存储检查点数据。要完成任务，请使用 EC2 自动扩展组和按需定价模式临时配置 EC2 实例。","B":"在 EC2 实例上使用 GlusterFS 来存储检查点数据。要运行批处理作业，请手动配置 EC2 实例。作业完 成后，请手动关闭实例。","C":"使用 Amazon EFS 存储检查点数据。使用 EC2 集群启动 EC2 竞价型实例，并利用用户数据在启动时配 置 EC2 Linux 实例。","D":"使用 Amazon EFS 存储检查点数据。使用 EC2 集群启动 EC2 竞价型实例。为集群创建自定义 AMI，并 在创建实例时使用最新 AMI。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The batch job can tolerate interruptions and the goal is the MOST cost-effective solution, so EC2 Spot Instances are correct because they run fault-tolerant workloads for up to 90% less than On-Demand, eliminating the On-Demand option A. For the NFS checkpoint volume, Amazon EFS is a fully managed, elastic NFS file system that is cheaper and far lower in operational overhead than self-managing a GlusterFS cluster on additional always-on EC2 instances, eliminating B. The deciding detail is that configuring the cluster software from a generic Linux image takes 30 minutes. Because Spot Instances are reclaimed and relaunched frequently, option C (configure via user data on every startup) would repeat that 30-minute setup on each launch, paying for unproductive compute before any useful work begins. Option D bakes the cluster configuration into a custom AMI so each Spot Instance is ready almost immediately; AWS documentation explicitly states that a custom AMI improves provisioning times when you need to install a lot of software that isn't in the standard images. Spot + EFS + a pre-baked custom AMI is therefore the most cost-effective combination, so D is correct.","explanation_zh":"此批次工作可容忍中斷，且目標是「最具成本效益」的方案，因此應使用 EC2 Spot Instances，因為它可以比 On-Demand 便宜最多 90% 來執行可容錯工作負載，故排除使用 On-Demand 的選項 A。對於 NFS checkpoint 磁碟區，Amazon EFS 是全代管、可彈性擴展的 NFS 檔案系統，相較於在額外的常駐 EC2 instances 上自行維運 GlusterFS cluster，更便宜且維運負擔遠低，故排除 B。關鍵在於從通用 Linux image 設定 cluster 軟體需時 30 分鐘。由於 Spot Instances 會被頻繁回收並重新啟動，選項 C（每次啟動皆透過 user data 設定）會在每次啟動時重複這 30 分鐘的設定，在開始有用的工作之前就先付費於無產出的運算。選項 D 將 cluster 設定預先烘焙進 custom AMI，使每個 Spot Instance 幾乎可立即就緒；AWS 文件明確指出，當需要安裝大量未包含在標準 image 中的軟體時，custom AMI 可改善佈建時間。因此 Spot + EFS + 預先烘焙的 custom AMI 是最具成本效益的組合，故 D 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EFS is the right storage choice, but On-Demand pricing is far more expensive than Spot for an interruption-tolerant batch job, so this is not the MOST cost-effective solution.","why_zh":"EFS 是正確的儲存選擇，但對於可容忍中斷的批次工作而言，On-Demand 計價遠比 Spot 昂貴，因此這不是最具成本效益的方案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Self-managed GlusterFS on EC2 adds persistent always-on instance costs and significant operational overhead versus the managed EFS NFS service, and manual configuration/shutdown is neither cost-optimal nor scalable.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上自行維運 GlusterFS 相較於代管的 EFS NFS 服務，會增加持續常駐的 instance 成本與大量維運負擔，而手動設定/關機既非成本最佳化也不具擴展性。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Using user data to configure each instance on startup means every Spot launch and frequent Spot replacement repeats the 30-minute configuration, wasting paid compute time and making it less cost-effective than a pre-baked custom AMI.","why_zh":"在啟動時用 user data 設定每個 instance，代表每次 Spot 啟動及頻繁的 Spot 替換都會重複 30 分鐘的設定，浪費付費運算時間，因此比預先烘焙的 custom AMI 更不具成本效益。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.customenv.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/cost-optimization-leveraging-ec2-spot-instances/when-to-use-spot-instances.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/batch/latest/userguide/bestpractice6.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/AMIs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":116,"question_en":"A company recently migrated its legacy application from on-premises to AWS. The application is hosted on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer, which is behind Amazon API Gateway. The company wants to ensure users experience minimal disruptions during any deployment of a new version of the application. The company also wants to ensure it can quickly roll back updates if there is an issue. Which solution will meet these requirements with MINIMAL changes to the application?","question_zh":"一家公司最近将其遗留应用程序从本地迁移到了 AWS。该应用程序托管在位于应用负载均衡器后面的亚马 逊 EC2 实例上，而应用负载均衡器又位于亚马逊 API 网关之后。该公司希望在部署应用程序新版本期间， 用户能感受到尽可能小的干扰。同时，该公司还希望在出现问题时能够迅速回滚更新。 哪种解决方案只需对应用程序进行最小的改动就能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Introduce changes as a separate environment parallel to the existing one. Configure API Gateway to use a canary release deployment to send a small subset of user traffic to the new environment.","B":"Introduce changes as a separate environment parallel to the existing one. Update the application’s DNS alias records to point to the new environment.","C":"Introduce changes as a separate target group behind the existing Application Load Balancer. Configure API Gateway to route user traffic to the new target group in steps.","D":"Introduce changes as a separate target group behind the existing Application Load Balancer. Configure API Gateway to route all traffic to the Application Load Balancer, which then sends the traffic to the new target group."},"options_zh":{"A":"作为现有环境的并行环境引入变更。配置 API 网关使用金丝雀发布部署，将一小部分用户流量发送到 新环境。","B":"作为现有环境的并行环境引入变更。更新应用程序的 DNS 别名记录，使其指向新环境。","C":"在现有的应用负载均衡器之后，将变更作为单独的目标组引入。逐步配置 API 网关，将用户流量路由到 新的目标组。","D":"在现有的应用负载均衡器后面将变更作为单独的目标组引入。配置 API 网关将所有流量路由到应用负载均 衡器，然后由其将流量发送到新的目标组。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The architecture is API Gateway -> ALB -> EC2 and the qualifiers are minimal user disruption during a deployment, quick rollback, and minimal changes to the application. API Gateway natively supports a canary release deployment: on a single stage, total API traffic is split at random between the production release and a canary release using a configurable percentTraffic (0.0-100.0), so most users keep hitting the existing version. The canary settings include stageVariableOverrides that override the production stage variables; because a stage variable can be used in the HTTP integration URI (for example http://${stageVariables.url}) to set the backend endpoint, the canary can point a small percentage of traffic at a separate parallel environment (a new ALB/backend) while production stays on the existing one. This minimizes disruption (only a small random subset sees the new version), enables instant rollback by simply turning off / discarding the canary, and requires no application code changes. Option A describes exactly this native feature, making it the best fit for all three qualifiers.","explanation_zh":"架構為 API Gateway -> ALB -> EC2，限定條件是部署新版本時對使用者干擾最小、能快速回復 (rollback)，且對應用程式的變更最少。API Gateway 原生支援 canary release deployment：在同一個 stage 上，總流量會依可設定的 percentTraffic (0.0-100.0) 隨機分流給 production release 與 canary release，因此大多數使用者仍命中既有版本。Canary settings 包含 stageVariableOverrides，可覆寫 production 的 stage variables；由於 stage variable 可用於 HTTP integration URI (例如 http://${stageVariables.url}) 來設定後端端點，canary 便能將一小部分流量導向獨立的平行環境 (新的 ALB/後端)，而 production 流量仍維持在既有環境。這樣干擾最小 (只有一小部分隨機使用者會看到新版本)，並可藉由停用/捨棄 canary 立即回復，且不需修改應用程式碼。選項 A 正是描述此原生功能，最符合三個限定條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Updating DNS alias records to point to the new parallel environment is an all-at-once cutover, not sending a small random subset of traffic, so it does not minimize disruption. DNS resolver TTL caching also makes rollback slow and uneven rather than quick, failing the fast-rollback requirement.","why_zh":"更新 DNS alias 紀錄指向新平行環境屬於一次性全量切換，而非只導入一小部分隨機流量，無法將干擾降到最低。DNS resolver TTL 快取也使回復變慢且不一致，而非快速，不符合快速回復需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"API Gateway cannot route to a specific ALB target group or shift traffic between target groups 'in steps'. API Gateway integrates with the ALB endpoint (the listener), and weighted/stepped target-group routing is an ALB listener-rule feature (the forward action with weighted target groups), not something API Gateway controls. The described mechanism is technically inaccurate.","why_zh":"API Gateway 無法路由到特定的 ALB target group，也無法在 target group 之間「逐步」轉移流量。API Gateway 整合的是 ALB 端點 (listener)，而加權/逐步的 target group 路由屬於 ALB listener rule 的功能 (forward action 搭配 weighted target groups)，並非 API Gateway 控制範圍，所述機制在技術上不正確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Routing ALL traffic to the ALB which then forwards everything to the new target group is a hard cutover, not a gradual rollout, so it does not minimize disruption. It also describes no built-in canary weighting or rollback mechanism, failing both the minimal-disruption and quick-rollback requirements.","why_zh":"將所有流量導到 ALB 再全部轉發到新的 target group 是硬切換而非漸進式上線，無法將干擾降到最低。它也未描述任何內建的 canary 加權或回復機制，無法同時滿足干擾最小與快速回復的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/canary-release.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/create-canary-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/http-api-stages.stage-variables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/rule-action-types.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":117,"question_en":"A company is storing 100 GB of log data in .csv format in an Amazon S3 bucket. SQL developers want to query this data and generate graphs to visualize it. The SQL developers also need an efficient, automated way to store metadata from the .csv file. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST amount of effort? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中以 .csv 格式存储 100GB 的日志数据。SQL 开发人员希望查询这些数据并 生成图表来可视化它。SQL 开发人员还需要一种高效、自动化的办法来存储来自 .csv 文件的元数据。 哪三种步骤的组合能以最少的努力满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Filter the data through AWS X-Ray to visualize the data.","B":"Filter the data through Amazon QuickSight to visualize the data.","C":"Query the data with Amazon Athena.","D":"Query the data with Amazon Redshift.","E":"Use the AWS Glue Data Catalog as the persistent metadata store.","F":"Use Amazon DynamoDB as the persistent metadata store."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过 AWS X-Ray 过滤数据以可视化数据。","B":"通过 Amazon QuickSight 过滤数据以可视化呈现数据。","C":"使用 Amazon Athena 查询数据。","D":"使用 Amazon Redshift 查询数据。","E":"使用 AWS Glue 数据目录作为持久的元数据存储。","F":"使用亚马逊 DynamoDB 作为持久化的元数据存储。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The qualifier is LEAST effort to let SQL developers query 100 GB of CSV in S3, visualize it, and automatically store metadata. The canonical fully serverless pattern needs no clusters or servers. (C) Amazon Athena queries the CSV directly in S3 with standard SQL using a schema-on-read approach, so there is no data loading or transformation. (E) Athena stores its table schema in the AWS Glue Data Catalog and uses it to read data at query time; the AWS Glue Data Catalog is the built-in, Hive-compatible persistent metastore, and a Glue crawler can automatically infer and write the CSV schema/metadata, satisfying the 'efficient, automated' metadata requirement. (B) Amazon QuickSight connects natively to Athena to build graphs and dashboards with minimal setup. Together these three are serverless with no infrastructure to manage, which is the least effort.","explanation_zh":"本題關鍵字是以最少的工作量讓 SQL 開發人員查詢 S3 中 100 GB 的 CSV、進行視覺化並自動儲存 metadata。最標準且完全無伺服器的模式不需要叢集或伺服器。(C) Amazon Athena 採用 schema-on-read 方式，直接以標準 SQL 查詢 S3 中的 CSV，無需載入或轉換資料。(E) Athena 將其資料表 schema 儲存於 AWS Glue Data Catalog，並在查詢時用它讀取資料；AWS Glue Data Catalog 是內建、與 Hive 相容的持久化 metadata 儲存區，且 Glue crawler 可自動推斷並寫入 CSV 的 schema 與 metadata，符合「有效率、自動化」儲存 metadata 的需求。(B) Amazon QuickSight 原生連接 Athena，只需極少設定即可建立圖表與儀表板。三者合起來完全無伺服器、無需管理基礎設施，工作量最少。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS X-Ray is a distributed tracing service for analyzing and debugging application request flows (Lambda, API Gateway, SQS, etc.). It does not query or visualize business/log data stored as CSV in S3, so it cannot meet the visualization requirement.","why_zh":"AWS X-Ray 是分散式追蹤服務，用於分析與除錯應用程式的請求流程（如 Lambda、API Gateway、SQS）。它無法查詢或視覺化儲存在 S3 中的 CSV 業務／日誌資料，因此無法滿足視覺化需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Redshift would require provisioning and managing a cluster (or Redshift Serverless plus Spectrum/COPY configuration) to query CSV in S3, which is more operational effort than Athena's schema-on-read serverless queries. Athena (C) is already the least-effort query engine, so Redshift is not selected.","why_zh":"Amazon Redshift 需要佈建並管理叢集（或設定 Redshift Serverless 加上 Spectrum/COPY）才能查詢 S3 中的 CSV，工作量比 Athena 的 schema-on-read 無伺服器查詢更高。本題已有 Athena (C) 作為最省事的查詢引擎，因此不選 Redshift。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Amazon DynamoDB is a NoSQL key-value/document store, not a schema metastore for tabular data. It is not used as Athena's persistent metadata catalog and cannot automatically infer CSV schema; the AWS Glue Data Catalog is the correct built-in metadata store, and using DynamoDB would require custom code.","why_zh":"Amazon DynamoDB 是 NoSQL 鍵值／文件資料庫，並非用於表格資料的 schema 中繼資料存放區。它不是 Athena 的持久化 metadata 目錄，也無法自動推斷 CSV schema；正確的內建 metadata 儲存區是 AWS Glue Data Catalog，改用 DynamoDB 需自行撰寫程式碼。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/creating-tables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/schema-csv.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/add-crawler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/application-discovery/latest/userguide/port-query-to-visualization.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/quick/latest/userguide/quick-bi.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":118,"question_en":"A company deploys its corporate infrastructure on AWS across multiple AWS Regions and Availability Zones. The infrastructure is deployed on Amazon EC2 instances and connects with AWS IoT Greengrass devices. The company deploys additional resources on on-premises servers that are located in the corporate headquarters. The company wants to reduce the overhead involved in maintaining and updating its resources. The company’s DevOps team plans to use AWS Systems Manager to implement automated management and application of patches. The DevOps team confirms that Systems Manager is available in the Regions that the resources are deployed in. Systems Manager also is available in a Region near the corporate headquarters. Which combination of steps must the DevOps team take to implement automated patch and configuration management across the company’s EC2 instances, IoT devices, and on-premises infrastructure? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在多个 AWS 区域和可用区内部署了其企业基础设施，这些基础设施部署在亚马逊 EC2 实例上， 并与 AWS IoT Greengrass 设备相连接。该公司还在位于企业总部的本地服务器上部署了额外的资源。 该公司希望减少维护和更新资源所产生的管理费用。公司的 DevOps 团队计划使用 AWS Systems Manager 来实现补丁的自动化管理和应用。DevOps 团队确认 Systems Manager 在部署资源的区域可用。Systems Manager 在靠近公司总部的区域也提供服务。 DevOps 团队必须采取哪些步骤组合才能在公司的 EC2 实例、物联网设备和本地基础设施上实现自动化的 补丁和配置管理？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Apply tags to all the EC2 instances, AWS IoT Greengrass devices, and on-premises servers. Use Systems Manager Session Manager to push patches to all the tagged devices.","B":"Use Systems Manager Run Command to schedule patching for the EC2 instances, AWS IoT Greengrass devices, and on-premises servers.","C":"Use Systems Manager Patch Manager to schedule patching for the EC2 instances, AWS IoT Greengrass devices, and on-premises servers as a Systems Manager maintenance window task.","D":"Configure Amazon EventBridge to monitor Systems Manager Patch Manager for updates to patch baselines. Associate Systems Manager Run Command with the event to initiate a patch action for all EC2 instances, AWS IoT Greengrass devices, and on-premises servers.","E":"Create an IAM instance profile for Systems Manager. Attach the instance profile to all the EC2 instances in the AWS account. For the AWS IoT Greengrass devices and on-premises servers, create an IAM service role for Systems Manager.","F":"Generate a managed-instance activation. Use the Activation Code and Activation ID to install Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent) on each server in the on-premises environment. Update the AWS IoT Greengrass IAM token exchange role. Use the role to deploy SSM Agent on all the IoT devices."},"options_zh":{"A":"对所有 EC2 实例、AWS IoT Greengrass 设备和本地服务器应用标签。使用系统管理器会话管理器 将补丁推送到所有已标记的设备。","B":"使用系统管理器运行命令为 EC2 实例、AWS IoT 核绿格设备和本地服务器安排补丁更新。","C":"使用系统管理器补丁管理器安排对 EC2 实例、AWS IoT Greengrass 设备和本地服务器的补丁安装， 将其作为系统管理器维护窗口任务。","D":"配置 Amazon EventBridge 以监控 Systems Manager Patch Manager 中补丁基线的更新。将 Systems Manager Run Command 与该事件关联，以对所有 EC2 实例、AWS IoT Greengrass 设备和本地服务 器启动补丁操作。","E":"为 Systems Manager 创建一个 IAM 实例配置文件。将该实例配置文件附加到 AWS 账户中的所有 EC2 实例。对于 AWS IoT Greengrass 设备和本地服务器，请为 Systems Manager 创建一个 IAM 服务角色。","F":"生成托管实例激活码。使用激活码和激活 ID 在本地环境中的每台服务器上安装 Systems Manager 代理 （SSM 代理）。更新 AWS IoT Greengrass IAM 令牌交换角色。使用该角色在所有 IoT 设备上部署 SSM 代理。"},"answer":["C","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Managing EC2 instances, AWS IoT Greengrass edge devices, and on-premises servers with Systems Manager requires three things: correct IAM permissions, registering each resource as a managed node by installing SSM Agent, and then scheduling patching. Option E is correct because EC2 instances are granted Systems Manager access through an IAM instance profile attached to the instance, while non-EC2 resources (Greengrass core devices and on-premises servers) use an IAM service role for Systems Manager that the service assumes (the RegistrationRole); AWS docs explicitly state the same service role is reused for both edge and hybrid on-premises nodes. Option F is correct because on-premises servers are registered by creating a hybrid (managed-instance) activation and using its Activation Code and Activation ID when installing SSM Agent, while Greengrass core devices require updating the token exchange role (adding ssm:RegisterManagedInstance, ssm:AddTagsToResource, and iam:PassRole) and then deploying the SSM Agent Greengrass component. Option C is correct because, once all three resource types are registered managed nodes, Patch Manager applies patches on a schedule via a maintenance window task that runs AWS-RunPatchBaseline. Option A is wrong because Session Manager provides interactive shell access and does not push patches; B and D are wrong because Run Command runs on-demand commands rather than being the patch-scheduling tool, and an EventBridge baseline-update trigger is not the documented automated patch-scheduling mechanism.","explanation_zh":"使用 Systems Manager 管理 EC2 instances、AWS IoT Greengrass 邊緣裝置與地端伺服器需要三個步驟：設定正確的 IAM 權限、安裝 SSM Agent 將每個資源註冊為 managed node，最後排程修補。選項 E 正確，因為 EC2 instances 透過附加到執行個體的 IAM instance profile 取得 Systems Manager 存取權，而非 EC2 資源（Greengrass core 裝置與地端伺服器）則使用由服務承擔的 IAM service role（即 RegistrationRole）；AWS 文件明確指出同一個 service role 可同時用於邊緣裝置與 hybrid 地端節點。選項 F 正確，因為地端伺服器是透過建立 hybrid（managed-instance）activation 並在安裝 SSM Agent 時使用其 Activation Code 與 Activation ID 來註冊；而 Greengrass core 裝置則需更新 token exchange role（加入 ssm:RegisterManagedInstance、ssm:AddTagsToResource 與 iam:PassRole），再部署 SSM Agent Greengrass component。選項 C 正確，因為三種資源都註冊為 managed node 後，Patch Manager 透過 maintenance window task 執行 AWS-RunPatchBaseline 來排程套用修補。選項 A 錯誤，因為 Session Manager 提供互動式 shell 存取，並不會推送修補；B 與 D 錯誤，因為 Run Command 執行的是隨選指令而非修補排程工具，且以 EventBridge 監控 patch baseline 更新觸發修補並非官方文件記載的自動修補排程機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Session Manager provides secure interactive shell/port-forwarding sessions to managed nodes; it does not push or apply patches. Tagging resources also does not by itself register edge or on-premises devices as managed nodes, and patching is performed by Patch Manager, not Session Manager.","why_zh":"Session Manager 提供對 managed node 的安全互動式 shell／連接埠轉送工作階段，並不會推送或套用修補。為資源加標籤本身也無法把邊緣或地端裝置註冊為 managed node，且修補是由 Patch Manager 執行，而非 Session Manager。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Run Command executes on-demand commands against already-registered managed nodes; it is not the tool used to schedule patching. Scheduled patching is performed by Patch Manager through a maintenance window task (running AWS-RunPatchBaseline) or a patch policy, so this option mischaracterizes the patch-scheduling mechanism.","why_zh":"Run Command 對已註冊的 managed node 執行隨選指令，並非用來排程修補的工具。排程修補是由 Patch Manager 透過 maintenance window task（執行 AWS-RunPatchBaseline）或 patch policy 完成，因此此選項錯誤描述了修補排程機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Updates to patch baselines do not need to trigger patch actions, and wiring EventBridge to run a Run Command on every baseline change is a convoluted, non-recommended pattern that does not establish scheduled patching across managed nodes. The documented automated patch/configuration approach is Patch Manager with a maintenance window schedule, making this overcomplicated and incorrect.","why_zh":"patch baseline 的更新不需要觸發修補動作，將 EventBridge 連接到每次 baseline 變更就執行 Run Command 是迂迴且非建議的做法，無法在 managed node 上建立排程修補。文件記載的自動修補/組態方式是 Patch Manager 搭配 maintenance window 排程，因此此選項過度複雜且不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/greengrass/v2/developerguide/install-systems-manager-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-setting-up-edge-devices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-activation-managed-nodes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-multicloud-service-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-hybrid-multicloud.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/maintenance-window-tutorial-patching.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-aws-runpatchbaseline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-compliance-remediation.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":119,"question_en":"A company is testing a web application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer. The instances run in an Auto Scaling group across multiple Availability Zones. The company uses a blue/green deployment process with immutable instances when deploying new software. During testing, users are being automatically logged out of the application at random times. Testers also report that, when a new version of the application is deployed, all users are logged out. The development team needs a solution to ensure users remain logged in across scaling events and application deployments. What is the MOST operationally efficient way to ensure users remain logged in?","question_zh":"一家公司正在测试一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的网络应用程序，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器之后。 这些实例在多个可用区的自动扩展组中运行。该公司在部署新软件时采用蓝/绿部署流程，并使用不可 变实例。 在测试期间，用户会在随机时间被自动从应用程序中注销。测试人员还发现 报告称，当应用程序的新版本部署时，所有用户都会被登出。开发团队需要一个解决方案，以确保用 户在扩展事件和应用程序部署期间保持登录状态。 确保用户保持登录状态的最高效操作方式是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Enable smart sessions on the load balancer and modify the application to check for an existing session.","B":"Enable session sharing on the load balancer and modify the application to read from the session store.","C":"Store user session information in an Amazon S3 bucket and modify the application to read session information from the bucket.","D":"Modify the application to store user session information in an Amazon ElastiCache cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在负载均衡器上启用智能会话，并修改应用程序以检查是否存在会话。","B":"在负载均衡器上启用会话共享，并修改应用程序以从会话存储中读取。","C":"将用户会话信息存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，并修改应用程序以从该存储桶读取会话信息。","D":"修改 将用户会话信息存储在 Amazon ElastiCache 集群中的应用程序。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Sessions are kept in the EC2 instances' local memory, so users are logged out at random times when scale-in terminates the instance that holds their session, and all users are logged out on every deployment because the immutable blue/green process replaces every instance. The fix is to make the web tier stateless by offloading session state to a shared, durable, multi-AZ data store so any instance can serve any request. AWS Well-Architected REL05-BP06 'Make services stateless where possible' states that services should offload state so 'between different client requests, there is no dependence on locally stored data on disk and in memory,' and that 'Amazon ElastiCache or Amazon DynamoDB are good destinations for offloaded state'; its Figure 7 caption reads 'In this stateless web application, session state is offloaded to Amazon ElastiCache.' Option D implements exactly this documented pattern with an in-memory, sub-millisecond store and is the MOST operationally efficient durable solution. Sticky sessions are no help because pinning a user to one target still loses the in-memory session when that target is deregistered during scale-in or replaced during an immutable deployment.","explanation_zh":"Session 被保存在 EC2 執行個體的本機記憶體中，因此當 scale-in 終止持有某使用者 session 的執行個體時，該使用者會在隨機時間被登出；而 immutable blue/green 部署會替換所有執行個體，因此每次部署所有使用者都被登出。解法是讓 web tier 變成 stateless，把 session 狀態卸載到共享、持久、跨多個 Availability Zone 的資料儲存，使任一執行個體都能處理任一請求。AWS Well-Architected REL05-BP06「Make services stateless where possible」說明服務應卸載狀態，使「不同 client 請求之間，不依賴儲存在本機磁碟與記憶體中的資料」，並指出「Amazon ElastiCache or Amazon DynamoDB are good destinations for offloaded state」；其 Figure 7 圖說為「In this stateless web application, session state is offloaded to Amazon ElastiCache.」選項 D 正是以記憶體內、次毫秒延遲的儲存實作此文件化模式，是最具營運效率的持久解法。Sticky sessions 無法解決問題，因為將使用者綁定到單一 target，在 scale-in 取消註冊該 target 或 immutable 部署替換它時，記憶體內的 session 仍會遺失。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no 'smart sessions' feature on an Application Load Balancer; the term is fabricated. The closest real feature, ALB sticky sessions, only pins a client to a specific target via a cookie. When that target is terminated during scale-in or replaced during an immutable blue/green deployment, the locally stored session is gone, so users are still logged out.","why_zh":"Application Load Balancer 並無『smart sessions』功能，此名稱是虛構的。最接近的真實功能 ALB sticky sessions 也只是用 cookie 把用戶綁到特定 target；當該 target 在 scale-in 被終止或在 immutable blue/green 部署中被替換時，本機儲存的 session 就消失，使用者仍會被登出。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An ALB has no 'session sharing' feature; the load balancer cannot share or replicate application session data across instances. Session sharing must be implemented at the application layer by reading/writing an external store such as ElastiCache or DynamoDB, which is precisely what option D describes.","why_zh":"ALB 沒有『session sharing』功能；負載平衡器無法在執行個體之間共享或複製應用程式 session 資料。Session 共享必須在應用層透過讀寫外部儲存（如 ElastiCache 或 DynamoDB）實作，這正是選項 D 所描述的。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon S3 is object storage, not a low-latency session store. Reading and writing session state to S3 on every request adds high latency and is not the AWS-recommended pattern for ephemeral session data. REL05-BP06 names ElastiCache and DynamoDB (in-memory / single-digit-millisecond stores) for offloaded session state, making S3 a less operationally efficient choice than D.","why_zh":"Amazon S3 是物件儲存，並非低延遲的 session 儲存。每個請求都讀寫 S3 會帶來高延遲，且非 AWS 建議的暫時性 session 資料模式。REL05-BP06 指名 ElastiCache 與 DynamoDB（記憶體內 / 個位數毫秒儲存）作為卸載 session 狀態的目的地，因此 S3 的營運效率不如 D。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/2023-10-03/framework/rel_mitigate_interaction_failure_stateless.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/best-practices-wordpress/stateless-web-tier.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonElastiCache/latest/dg/elasticache-use-cases.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/load-balancer-stickiness/welcome.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":120,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to configure a blue/green deployment for an existing three-tier application. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances and uses an Amazon RDS database. The EC2 instances run behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and are in an Auto Scaling group. The DevOps engineer has created a launch template and an Auto Scaling group for the blue environment. The DevOps engineer also has created a launch template and an Auto Scaling group for the green environment. Each Auto Scaling group deploys to a matching blue or green target group. The target group also specifies which software, blue or green, gets loaded on the EC2 instances. The ALB can be configured to send traffic to the blue environment’s target group or the green environment’s target group. An Amazon Route 53 record for www.example.com points to the ALB. The deployment must move traffic all at once between the software on the blue environment’s EC2 instances to the newly deployed software on the green environment’s EC2 instances. What should the DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要为现有的三层应用程序配置蓝/绿部署。该应用程序在 Amazon EC2 实例上运 行，并使用 Amazon RDS 数据库。EC2 实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后，并处于自动扩展组中。 DevOps 工程师为蓝色环境创建了一个启动模板和一个自动扩展组。DevOps 工程师还为绿色环境创建 了一个启动模板和一个自动扩展组。每个自动扩展组都会部署到相应的蓝色或绿色目标组。目标组还 指定了在 EC2 实例上加载哪个软件，是蓝色的还是绿色的。应用负载均衡器（ALB）可以配置为将流 量发送到蓝色环境的目标组或绿色环境的目标组。Amazon Route 53 中为 www.example.com 设置的记录 指向该应用负载均衡器。 部署操作必须一次性将流量从蓝色环境的 EC2 实例上的软件转移到新部署的绿色环境的 EC2 实 例上的软件。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Start a rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new software on the green environment’s EC2 instances. When the rolling restart is complete, use an AWS CLI command to update the ALB to send traffic to the green environment’s target group.","B":"Use an AWS CLI command to update the ALB to send traffic to the green environment’s target group. Then start a rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new software on the green environment’s EC2 instances.","C":"Update the launch template to deploy the green environment’s software on the blue environment’s EC2 instances. Keep the target groups and Auto Scaling groups unchanged in both environments. Perform a rolling restart of the blue environment’s EC2 instances.","D":"Start a rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new software on the green environment’s EC2 instances. When the rolling restart is complete, update the Route 53 DNS to point to the green environment’s endpoint on the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"对绿色环境的自动扩展组启动滚动重启，以便在绿色环境的 EC2 实例上部署新软件。滚动重启完 成后，使用 AWS CLI 命令更新应用负载均衡器（ALB），使其将流量发送到绿色环境的目标组。","B":"使用 AWS CLI 命令将应用负载均衡器（ALB）更新为将流量发送到绿色环境的目标组。然后对绿 色环境的自动扩展组执行滚动重启，以便在绿色环境的 EC2 实例上部署新软件。","C":"更新启动模板，以便在蓝色环境的 EC2 实例上部署绿色环境的软件。保持两个环境中的目标组和自 动扩展组不变。对蓝色环境的 EC2 实例执行滚动重启。","D":"开始对绿色环境的自动扩展组进行滚动重启，以便在绿色环境的 EC2 实例上部署新软件。滚动重 启完成后，更新 Route 53 DNS 以指向 ALB 上绿色环境的端点。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The correct blue/green cutover order is to deploy the new software to the green environment first, then flip traffic. You start a rolling restart (instance refresh) of the green Auto Scaling group so its EC2 instances relaunch with the new software and register as healthy in the green target group. Only after green is ready do you use an AWS CLI command (elbv2 modify-listener) to change the ALB listener's default action to forward to the green target group. Because the listener default action is replaced in a single operation, all traffic shifts from blue to green at once, satisfying the 'all at once' requirement. Route 53 keeps pointing at the same single ALB DNS name, which is consistent with the described architecture where the ALB (not DNS) selects which target group receives traffic.","explanation_zh":"正確的 blue/green 切換順序是先把新軟體部署到 green 環境，再切換流量。先對 green 的 Auto Scaling group 進行 rolling restart（instance refresh），使其 EC2 instances 以新軟體重新啟動並在 green target group 中註冊為健康狀態。等 green 就緒後，才使用 AWS CLI 指令（elbv2 modify-listener）將 ALB listener 的 default action 變更為 forward 到 green target group。由於 listener 的 default action 是以單一操作被替換，所有流量會一次性（all at once）從 blue 切換到 green，符合需求。Route 53 仍指向同一個 ALB 的 DNS 名稱，與題目描述由 ALB（而非 DNS）決定哪個 target group 接收流量的架構一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Reverses the order: it flips the ALB to the green target group BEFORE the new software is deployed, so production traffic hits green instances that are still running the old software or are mid-restart and unhealthy, causing errors or downtime. Cutover must happen only after green is deployed and healthy.","why_zh":"順序顛倒：在新軟體尚未部署前就把 ALB 切到 green target group，導致正式流量打到仍跑舊軟體或正在重啟、不健康的 green instances，造成錯誤或停機。必須在 green 部署完成且健康後才切換。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Defeats the blue/green pattern entirely: it overwrites the blue instances in place with green software, keeps both environments unchanged, and uses a rolling restart (gradual, not all-at-once). There is no isolated green environment to roll back to, and a rolling restart does not move traffic all at once.","why_zh":"完全違背 blue/green 模式：把 green 軟體就地覆寫到 blue instances 上，並使用 rolling restart（漸進式而非一次性）。沒有獨立的 green 環境可供回滾，rolling restart 也無法一次性切換流量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A single ALB has only one DNS name; there is no separate 'green endpoint on the ALB' for Route 53 to point to, and the architecture states the ALB (the listener/target group) selects blue vs green. DNS-based cutover also does not move traffic 'all at once' because of DNS TTL and client/resolver caching.","why_zh":"單一 ALB 只有一個 DNS 名稱，並不存在可供 Route 53 指向的『ALB 上的 green 端點』，且題目說明是由 ALB（listener/target group）選擇 blue 或 green。基於 DNS 的切換也因 TTL 與用戶端/解析器快取而無法做到一次性切換流量。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-listeners.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/elbv2/modify-listener.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-target-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/asg-instance-refresh.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":121,"question_en":"A company is building a new pipeline by using AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild in a build account. The pipeline consists of two stages. The first stage is a CodeBuild job to build and package an AWS Lambda function. The second stage consists of deployment actions that operate on two different AWS accounts: a development environment account and a production environment account. The deployment stages use the AWS CloudFormation action that CodePipeline invokes to deploy the infrastructure that the Lambda function requires. A DevOps engineer creates the CodePipeline pipeline and configures the pipeline to encrypt build artifacts by using the AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) AWS managed key for Amazon S3 (the aws/s3 key). The artifacts are stored in an S3 bucket. When the pipeline runs, the CloudFormation actions fail with an access denied error. Which combination of actions must the DevOps engineer perform to resolve this error? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 在一个构建账户中构建新的管道。该管道包含 两个阶段。第一阶段是一个 CodeBuild 任务，用于构建和打包一个 AWS Lambda 函数。第二阶段包含 在两个不同的 AWS 账户上执行的部署操作：开发环境账户和生产环境账户。部署阶段使用 CodePipeline 调用的 AWS CloudFormation 操作来部署基础设施。 Lambda 函数需要。 一位 DevOps 工程师创建了 CodePipeline 管道，并配置该管道使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）为 Amazon S3 管理的密钥（aws/s3 密钥）对构建工件进行加密。这些工件存储在 S3 存储桶中。当管道运行 时，CloudFormation 操作会因访问被拒绝而失败。 开发运维工程师必须执行哪两项操作才能解决此错误？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 bucket in each AWS account for the artifacts. Allow the pipeline to write to the S3 buckets. Create a CodePipeline S3 action to copy the artifacts to the S3 bucket in each AWS account. Update the CloudFormation actions to reference the artifacts S3 bucket in the production account.","B":"Create a customer managed KMS key. Configure the KMS key policy to allow the IAM roles used by the CloudFormation action to perform decrypt operations. Modify the pipeline to use the customer managed KMS key to encrypt artifacts.","C":"Create an AWS managed KMS key. Configure the KMS key policy to allow the development account and the production account to perform decrypt operations. Modify the pipeline to use the KMS key to encrypt artifacts.","D":"In the development account and in the production account, create an IAM role for CodePipeline. Configure the roles with permissions to perform CloudFormation operations and with permissions to retrieve and decrypt objects from the artifacts S3 bucket. In the CodePipeline account, configure the CodePipeline CloudFormation action to use the roles.","E":"In the development account and in the production account, create an IAM role for CodePipeline. Configure the roles with permissions to perform CloudFormation operations and with permissions to retrieve and decrypt objects from the artifacts S3 bucket. In the CodePipeline account, modify the artifacts S3 bucket policy to allow the roles access. Configure the CodePipeline CloudFormation action to use the roles."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建一个 S3 存储桶用于存放构建产物。允许管道向这些 S3 存储桶写入内容。创 建一个 CodePipeline S3 操作，将构建产物复制到每个 AWS 账户中的 S3 存储桶。更新 CloudFormation 操作以引用生产账户中的构建产物 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建一个客户管理的 KMS 密钥。配置 KMS 密钥策略，允许 CloudFormation 操作所使用的 IAM 角 色执行解密操作。修改管道以使用客户管理的 KMS 密钥对工件进行加密。","C":"创建一个由 AWS 管理的 KMS 密钥。配置 KMS 密钥策略，允许开发账户和生产账户执行解密操作。 修改管道以使用 KMS 密钥对工件进行加密。","D":"在开发账户和生产账户中，为 CodePipeline 创建一个 IAM 角色。配置这些角色，使其具有执行 CloudFormation 操作的权限以及从制品 S3 存储桶中检索和解密对象的权限。在 CodePipeline 账 户中，配置 CodePipeline 的 CloudFormation 操作以使用这些角色。","E":"在开发账户和生产账户中，为 CodePipeline 创建一个 IAM 角色。配置这些角色，使其具有执行 CloudFormation 操作的权限以及从制品 S3 存储桶中检索和解密对象的权限。在 CodePipeline 账户中， 修改制品 S3 存储桶策略以允许这些角色访问。配置 CodePipeline 的 CloudFormation 操作以使用这 些角色。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Cross-account CodePipeline deployment requires two changes that together resolve the access-denied error. First (B), the pipeline must encrypt artifacts with a customer managed KMS key whose key policy grants the cross-account IAM roles (used by the CloudFormation actions in the dev and prod accounts) decrypt permissions. The AWS managed aws/s3 key cannot be used for cross-account access because its key policy is not editable: the AWS KMS docs state an AWS managed key 'can only be used by principals within the account that the key exists' and 'You cannot share resources encrypted under an AWS managed key with other accounts,' so the other accounts can never be granted kms:Decrypt on it. The AWS cross-account walkthrough explicitly instructs you to create or use a customer managed key and grant its usage to AccountB. Second (E), in each target account you create an IAM role with permissions to perform CloudFormation operations and to retrieve and decrypt the artifacts, the pipeline (AccountA) artifacts S3 bucket policy must be modified to grant those roles access, and the CloudFormation action is configured with that role's ARN (roleArn). Cross-account S3 access requires BOTH an identity policy on the assuming role AND a resource-based bucket policy granting the other account, which is why E (which adds the bucket-policy step) is correct and D (which omits it) is incomplete.","explanation_zh":"跨帳戶 CodePipeline 部署需要兩項變更共同解決 access denied 錯誤。第一 (B)，pipeline 必須使用 customer managed KMS key 加密 artifacts，且該金鑰的 key policy 要授予 dev 與 prod 帳戶中 CloudFormation action 所使用的跨帳戶 IAM role 解密權限。AWS managed aws/s3 key 無法用於跨帳戶存取，因為其 key policy 不可編輯：AWS KMS 文件指出 AWS managed key「只能由金鑰所在帳戶內的 principal 使用」且「無法與其他帳戶共享以 AWS managed key 加密的資源」，因此其他帳戶永遠無法被授予 kms:Decrypt。AWS 官方跨帳戶教學明確指示必須建立或使用 customer managed key 並將使用權授予 AccountB。第二 (E)，在每個目標帳戶建立具有執行 CloudFormation 操作以及擷取並解密 artifacts 權限的 IAM role，pipeline 帳戶 (AccountA) 的 artifacts S3 bucket policy 必須修改以授權這些 role 存取，且 CloudFormation action 需以該 role 的 ARN (roleArn) 設定。跨帳戶 S3 存取同時需要被擔任 role 的身分政策以及授權對方帳戶的 resource-based bucket policy，因此包含 bucket policy 步驟的 E 才正確，而省略此步驟的 D 不完整。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Copying artifacts into a separate S3 bucket in each account is not the AWS-documented cross-account pattern and does not address the KMS access-denied root cause. The CloudFormation actions fail because of KMS decrypt and cross-account role/bucket permissions, not because the artifacts live in the pipeline account; duplicating buckets adds overhead and still requires the role/key/bucket-policy fixes.","why_zh":"將 artifacts 複製到每個帳戶的獨立 S3 bucket 並非 AWS 官方文件的跨帳戶模式，也未解決 KMS access denied 的根因。CloudFormation action 失敗是因為 KMS 解密與跨帳戶 role/bucket 權限，而非 artifacts 位於 pipeline 帳戶；複製 bucket 增加額外負擔且仍需修正 role/key/bucket policy。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot create an AWS managed KMS key, nor edit its key policy, so granting the dev and prod accounts decrypt operations on an AWS managed key is impossible. AWS managed keys are created and controlled by the owning AWS service and cannot share encrypted resources across accounts; cross-account sharing requires a customer managed key (as in B).","why_zh":"你無法建立 AWS managed KMS key，也無法編輯其 key policy，因此無法在 AWS managed key 上授予 dev 與 prod 帳戶解密操作。AWS managed key 由擁有的 AWS 服務建立與控制，且無法跨帳戶共享加密資源；跨帳戶共享需使用 customer managed key（即 B）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is nearly correct but omits modifying the artifacts S3 bucket policy in the pipeline account. Cross-account access to an S3 bucket requires a resource-based bucket policy granting the other account in addition to the role's identity policy; without it the assumed role still gets access denied retrieving the artifacts. The AWS walkthrough explicitly lists creating an S3 bucket policy that grants AccountB access. E is the complete version of D.","why_zh":"此選項幾乎正確，但省略了修改 pipeline 帳戶中 artifacts S3 bucket policy。跨帳戶存取 S3 bucket 除了 role 的身分政策外，還需要授權對方帳戶的 resource-based bucket policy；缺少時被擔任的 role 仍會在擷取 artifacts 時 access denied。AWS 官方教學明確列出需建立授予 AccountB 存取的 S3 bucket policy。E 是 D 的完整版本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/pipelines-create-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-codepipeline-pipeline-encryptionkey.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":122,"question_en":"A company is using an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The company’s development team wants to use AWS Lambda functions to meet resiliency requirements and is rewriting all applications to work with Lambda functions that are deployed in a VPC. The development team is using Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) as shared storage in Account A in the organization. The company wants to continue to use Amazon EFS with Lambda. Company policy requires all serverless projects to be deployed in Account B. A DevOps engineer needs to reconfigure an existing EFS file system to allow Lambda functions to access the data through an existing EFS access point. Which combination of steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS 组织中的一个组织来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司的开发团队希望使用 AWS Lambda 函数来满足弹性要求，并正在将所有应用程序重写为与部署在 VPC 中的 Lambda 函数配合使用。 开发团队在组织中的账户 A 中使用 Amazon Elastic File System（Amazon EFS）作为共享存储。 该公司希望继续在 Lambda 中使用亚马逊 EFS。公司政策要求所有无服务器项目都部署在账户 B 中。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要重新配置现有的 EFS 文件系统，以便 Lambda 函数能够通过现有的 EFS 访问点 访问数据。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the EFS file system policy to provide Account B with access to mount and write to the EFS file system in Account A.","B":"Create SCPs to set permission guardrails with fine-grained control for Amazon EFS.","C":"Create a new EFS file system in Account B. Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to keep data from Account A and Account B synchronized.","D":"Update the Lambda execution roles with permission to access the VPC and the EFS file system.","E":"Create a VPC peering connection to connect Account A to Account B.","F":"Configure the Lambda functions in Account B to assume an existing IAM role in Account A."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 EFS 文件系统策略，为账户 B 提供访问账户 A 中 EFS 文件系统并进行挂载和写入的权限。","B":"创建 SCP 以对 Amazon EFS 设置具有细粒度控制的权限防护栏。","C":"在账户 B 中创建一个新的 EFS 文件系统。使用 AWS 数据库迁移服务（AWS DMS）保持账户 A 和账户 B 中的数据同步。","D":"更新 Lambda 执行角色，使其具有访问 VPC 和 EFS 文件系统的权限。","E":"创建一个 VPC 对等连接，将账户 A 与账户 B 连接起来。","F":"在账户 B 中配置 Lambda 函数以承担账户 A 中现有的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The existing EFS file system stays in Account A and the Lambda functions must run in Account B, so three things are required. (A) The EFS file system policy is a resource-based policy that can name a principal in another account; the AWS EFS resource-based policy examples explicitly show an Account B role (555555555555) being granted elasticfilesystem:ClientMount and ClientWrite on a file system owned by Account A (111122223333), scoped to the existing access point ARN. This is exactly how Account B is given mount/write access to Account A's file system. (D) Per the Lambda 'Configuring Amazon EFS file system access' doc, when the file system has a user-configured policy the function's execution role must carry the elasticfilesystem permissions (ClientMount/ClientWrite, via AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess) AND the permissions required to connect to the file system's VPC (AWSLambdaVPCAccessExecutionRole). (E) Lambda mounts EFS over the local network in a VPC, so the function's VPC and the file system's VPC must be connected. AWS's 'Mounting EFS file systems from another VPC' guide states you must 'Set up either a VPC peering connection or a VPC transit gateway' to let clients in one VPC reach an EFS file system in another VPC even across accounts, and the Lambda cross-account VPC guide says to 'Configure your Lambda function to use a Amazon VPC peering connection.' VPC peering is therefore the required cross-account/cross-VPC network step.","explanation_zh":"既有的 EFS file system 留在 Account A，而 Lambda 函式必須在 Account B 執行，因此需要三項設定。(A) EFS file system policy 是 resource-based policy，可指定其他帳號的 principal；AWS 的 EFS resource-based policy 範例明確示範 Account B 的 role（555555555555）被授予對 Account A（111122223333）file system 的 elasticfilesystem:ClientMount 與 ClientWrite，並以既有 access point ARN 條件限定範圍，這正是讓 Account B 取得掛載/寫入權限的方式。(D) 依 Lambda「Configuring Amazon EFS file system access」文件，當 file system 設有自訂 policy 時，函式的 execution role 必須同時具備 elasticfilesystem 權限（ClientMount/ClientWrite，透過 AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess）以及連接 file system VPC 所需的權限（AWSLambdaVPCAccessExecutionRole）。(E) Lambda 是在 VPC 內透過本地網路掛載 EFS，因此函式所在的 VPC 必須與 file system 的 VPC 連通。AWS 的「Mounting EFS file systems from another VPC」指南指出必須『Set up either a VPC peering connection or a VPC transit gateway』，才能讓一個 VPC 的用戶端跨帳號存取另一個 VPC 的 EFS file system；Lambda 的跨帳號 VPC 指南也說明要『Configure your Lambda function to use a Amazon VPC peering connection』。因此 VPC peering 是必要的跨帳號/跨 VPC 網路步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"SCPs only set permission guardrails (maximum boundaries) across the organization; they never grant access. Adding 'fine-grained' EFS controls via SCPs does nothing to enable cross-account mount/write and is not a required step to make Lambda in Account B reach EFS in Account A.","why_zh":"SCP 只能設定組織層級的權限護欄（上限邊界），永遠不會『授予』存取權。用 SCP 加入所謂『細緻』的 EFS 控制，對於啟用跨帳號掛載/寫入毫無幫助，並非讓 Account B 的 Lambda 存取 Account A EFS 所需的步驟。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The requirement is to keep using and reconfigure the EXISTING EFS file system, not to duplicate it into Account B. AWS DMS migrates and replicates databases, not POSIX/NFS file systems, so it cannot synchronize EFS data and directly contradicts the stated goal of continuing to use the same EFS.","why_zh":"需求是繼續使用並重新設定『既有』的 EFS file system，而非在 Account B 複製一份。AWS DMS 用於遷移與複寫資料庫，而非 POSIX/NFS 檔案系統，無法同步 EFS 資料，且直接違背題目『繼續使用同一個 EFS』的目標。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Cross-account EFS access is not obtained by the Lambda function assuming a role in Account A. EFS mount/write access is governed by three things: a network path between the VPCs (VPC peering), the EFS file system resource policy naming the Account B principal/access point, and the function's execution role permissions - none of which is satisfied by sts:AssumeRole into Account A.","why_zh":"跨帳號 EFS 存取並非透過 Lambda 函式在 Account A 扮演（assume）角色取得。EFS 掛載/寫入權限由三項控制：VPC 之間的網路路徑（VPC peering）、指定 Account B principal/access point 的 EFS file system resource policy，以及函式的 execution role 權限；單純 sts:AssumeRole 進入 Account A 並無法滿足這些條件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-filesystem-efs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/configuration-vpc-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/security_iam_resource-based-policy-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/manage-fs-access-vpc-peering.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/mount-fs-different-vpc.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":123,"question_en":"A media company has several thousand Amazon EC2 instances in an AWS account. The company is using Slack and a shared email inbox for team communications and important updates. A DevOps engineer needs to send all AWS-scheduled EC2 maintenance notifications to the Slack channel and the shared inbox. The solution must include the instances’ Name and Owner tags. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家媒体公司在其 AWS 账户中拥有数千个 Amazon EC2 实例。该公司使用 Slack 和一个共享的电子邮件 收件箱来进行团队沟通和重要更新。一位 DevOps 工程师需要将所有 AWS 安排的 EC2 维护通知发送到 Slack 频道和共享收件箱。解决方案必须包含实例的“名称”和“所有者”标签。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Integrate AWS Trusted Advisor with AWS Config. Configure a custom AWS Config rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to publish notifications to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe a Slack channel endpoint and the shared inbox to the topic.","B":"Use Amazon EventBridge to monitor for AWS Health events. Configure the maintenance events to target an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe an AWS Lambda function to the SNS topic to send notifications to the Slack channel and the shared inbox.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that sends EC2 maintenance notifications to the Slack channel and the shared inbox. Monitor EC2 health events by using Amazon CloudWatch metrics. Configure a CloudWatch alarm that invokes the Lambda function when a maintenance notification is received.","D":"Configure AWS Support integration with AWS CloudTrail. Create a CloudTrail lookup event to invoke an AWS Lambda function to pass EC2 maintenance notifications to Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). Configure Amazon SNS to target the Slack channel and the shared inbox."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AWS Trusted Advisor 与 AWS Config 集成。配置自定义的 AWS Config 规则，以调用 AWS Lambda 函 数向 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题发布通知。将 Slack 通道端点和共享收件箱 订阅到该主题。","B":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 监控 AWS Health 事件。将维护事件配置为指向 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题。订阅 SNS 主题以将通知发送到 Slack 频道和共享收件箱。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 EC2 维护通知发送到 Slack 频道和共享收件箱。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 指标监控 EC2 健康事件。配置一个 CloudWatch 警报，当收到维护通知时调用 Lambda 函 数。","D":"配置 AWS 支持与 AWS CloudTrail 的集成。创建 CloudTrail 查找事件以调用 AWS Lambda 函数，将 EC2 维护通知传递给 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）。配置 Amazon SNS 以将通知发送至 Slack 频道和共享收件箱。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS-scheduled EC2 maintenance events (such as instance retirements, reboots, and system maintenance) are surfaced as AWS Health events with the EventBridge source 'aws.health'. The AWS Health documentation explicitly states you use Amazon EventBridge to detect and react to AWS Health events and gives EC2 scheduled-update notifications as the canonical example, listing Amazon SNS topics and AWS Lambda functions as supported EventBridge targets. It even calls out the exact pattern: 'you can use a Lambda function to pass a notification to a Slack channel when an AWS Health event occurs.' Option B implements this correctly: an EventBridge rule matches the maintenance events, targets an SNS topic, and a Lambda subscriber formats and delivers the message to both the Slack channel and the shared email inbox. The Name and Owner tags requirement is satisfied because EC2 lets you customize scheduled event notifications to include resource tags via register-instance-event-notification-attributes, and the AWS Health EventBridge event schema includes the affected entities/resources.","explanation_zh":"AWS 排程的 EC2 維護事件（例如 instance retirement、reboot、system maintenance）會以 AWS Health 事件形式呈現，EventBridge 來源為 'aws.health'。AWS Health 文件明確指出可使用 Amazon EventBridge 偵測並回應 AWS Health 事件，並以 EC2 排程更新通知作為標準範例，且列出 Amazon SNS topic 與 AWS Lambda function 為支援的 EventBridge target。文件甚至直接點出此模式：'you can use a Lambda function to pass a notification to a Slack channel when an AWS Health event occurs.' 選項 B 正確實作此架構：EventBridge rule 比對維護事件、以 SNS topic 為 target，再由訂閱 SNS 的 Lambda function 將訊息格式化並送至 Slack channel 與共用信箱。Name 與 Owner 標籤的需求也可滿足，因為 EC2 可透過 register-instance-event-notification-attributes 自訂排程事件通知以包含資源標籤，且 AWS Health EventBridge 事件結構也包含受影響的實體/資源。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor and AWS Config are not the source of AWS-scheduled EC2 maintenance notifications. AWS Config tracks resource configuration state and compliance against rules, and a custom Config rule is triggered by configuration changes, not by upcoming maintenance/retirement events. Trusted Advisor provides best-practice checks, so this chain cannot reliably detect scheduled EC2 maintenance events.","why_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 與 AWS Config 並非 AWS 排程 EC2 維護通知的來源。AWS Config 追蹤資源組態狀態與規則合規性，自訂 Config rule 由組態變更觸發，而非即將到來的維護/退役事件。Trusted Advisor 則提供最佳實務檢查，因此此架構無法可靠偵測排程 EC2 維護事件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch alarms act on metric thresholds, and there is no CloudWatch metric that represents 'an EC2 maintenance notification was received.' Scheduled maintenance and EC2 health events are delivered through AWS Health/EventBridge, not as a metric you can alarm on, and EC2 status-check metrics are not the same as scheduled maintenance, so a CloudWatch alarm cannot detect them or invoke the Lambda function.","why_zh":"CloudWatch alarm 是針對指標門檻動作，而沒有任何 CloudWatch 指標代表『已收到 EC2 維護通知』。排程維護與 EC2 健康事件是透過 AWS Health/EventBridge 傳遞，並非可設定警報的指標，且 EC2 狀態檢查指標與排程維護不同，因此 CloudWatch alarm 無法偵測這些事件或叫用 Lambda function。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS CloudTrail is an API-activity audit log, not a near-real-time push source for scheduled maintenance, and a CloudTrail 'lookup event' is a manual/historical query rather than an event-driven trigger that invokes Lambda. There is no 'AWS Support integration with CloudTrail' mechanism that proactively delivers scheduled EC2 maintenance notifications, so this architecture does not meet the requirement.","why_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 是 API 活動稽核日誌，並非排程維護的近即時推送來源；CloudTrail 的 lookup event 是手動/歷史查詢，而非在維護事件發生時叫用 Lambda 的事件驅動觸發器。也不存在所謂『AWS Support 與 CloudTrail 整合』來主動傳遞排程 EC2 維護通知的機制，因此此架構無法滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/cloudwatch-events-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/customizing_scheduled_event_notifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/aws-health-events-eventbridge-schema.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":124,"question_en":"An AWS CodePipeline pipeline has implemented a code release process. The pipeline is integrated with AWS CodeDeploy to deploy versions of an application to multiple Amazon EC2 instances for each CodePipeline stage. During a recent deployment, the pipeline failed due to a CodeDeploy issue. The DevOps team wants to improve monitoring and notifications during deployment to decrease resolution times. What should the DevOps engineer do to create notifications when issues are discovered?","question_zh":"一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道已实现代码发布流程。该管道与 AWS CodeDeploy 集成，以便在每个 CodePipeline 阶段将应用程序的版本部署到多个 Amazon EC2 实例上。 在最近的一次部署中，由于 CodeDeploy 出现问题，管道部署失败。DevOps 团队希望改进部署期间的监 控和通知，以缩短问题解决时间。 当发现问题时，开发运维工程师应该怎么做才能创建通知？","options_en":{"A":"Implement Amazon CloudWatch Logs for CodePipeline and CodeDeploy, create an AWS Config rule to evaluate code deployment issues, and create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify stakeholders of deployment issues.","B":"Implement Amazon EventBridge for CodePipeline and CodeDeploy, create an AWS Lambda function to evaluate code deployment issues, and create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify stakeholders of deployment issues.","C":"Implement AWS CloudTrail to record CodePipeline and CodeDeploy API call information, create an AWS Lambda function to evaluate code deployment issues, and create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify stakeholders of deployment issues.","D":"Implement Amazon EventBridge for CodePipeline and CodeDeploy, create an Amazon Inspector assessment target to evaluate code deployment issues, and create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify stakeholders of deployment issues."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 CodePipeline 和 CodeDeploy 实施 Amazon CloudWatch 日志，创建一个 AWS Config 规则来评估代码部 署问题，并创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题，以通知相关方部署问题。","B":"在 CodePipeline 和 CodeDeploy 中实现 Amazon EventBridge，创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来评估代码部署 问题，并创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，以通知相关方部署问题。","C":"实施 AWS CloudTrail 来记录 CodePipeline 和 CodeDeploy 的 API 调用信息，创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数 来评估代码部署问题，并创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题来通知相关 方部署问题。","D":"为 CodePipeline 和 CodeDeploy 实施 Amazon EventBridge，创建 Amazon Inspector 评估目标以评估代 码部署问题，并创建 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题以通知相关方部署问题。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Both CodePipeline and CodeDeploy emit state-change events (including pipeline/stage/action failures and deployment failures) directly to Amazon EventBridge, which AWS states is the preferred, near-real-time eventing mechanism for these services. The CodeDeploy events reference confirms CodeDeploy sends a 'CodeDeploy Deployment State-change Notification' directly to EventBridge, and the CodeDeploy 'Logging and monitoring' guide explicitly lists AWS Lambda functions and Amazon SNS topics as valid event targets, with the exact use case 'Use a Lambda function to pass a notification... whenever deployments fail.' The CodePipeline 'Monitoring CodePipeline events' guide states EventBridge 'routes that data to targets such as AWS Lambda and Amazon Simple Notification Service' and that CodePipeline emits events for pipeline, stage, and action executions on a guaranteed at-least-once basis. Option B is the only choice that combines the correct event source (EventBridge), a valid evaluation mechanism (Lambda to parse/filter the failure event), and the correct notification target (SNS).","explanation_zh":"CodePipeline 與 CodeDeploy 都會將狀態變更事件（包含 pipeline/階段/動作失敗與部署失敗）直接送往 Amazon EventBridge，AWS 明確指出 EventBridge 是這兩個服務建議使用的近即時事件機制。CodeDeploy 的事件參考文件確認 CodeDeploy 會將「CodeDeploy Deployment State-change Notification」直接送往 EventBridge；CodeDeploy 的「Logging and monitoring」文件也明確列出 AWS Lambda function 與 Amazon SNS topic 為有效的事件目標，並給出確切用例：「使用 Lambda function 在部署失敗時傳送通知」。CodePipeline 的「Monitoring CodePipeline events」文件指出 EventBridge 會「將資料導向諸如 AWS Lambda 與 Amazon SNS 等目標」，且 CodePipeline 會以至少一次（at-least-once）保證為 pipeline、階段與動作執行發出事件。選項 B 是唯一同時結合正確事件來源（EventBridge）、有效評估機制（Lambda 用以解析與過濾失敗事件）與正確通知目標（SNS）的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config evaluates resource configuration compliance, not real-time CodeDeploy/CodePipeline deployment state changes or failures. There is no AWS Config rule that detects a failed deployment event, so this cannot drive deployment-failure notifications. CloudWatch Logs alone also does not react to events to trigger notifications.","why_zh":"AWS Config 評估的是資源組態合規性，而非即時的 CodeDeploy/CodePipeline 部署狀態變更或失敗。沒有任何 AWS Config rule 能偵測部署失敗事件，因此無法用於部署失敗通知。單靠 CloudWatch Logs 也無法對事件做出反應以觸發通知。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudTrail records API calls for auditing and is not designed for near-real-time deployment-failure alerting; it has delivery latency and captures management API activity rather than service state-change events. EventBridge is the AWS-preferred mechanism for reacting to deployment state changes.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 記錄 API 呼叫以供稽核，並非設計用於近即時的部署失敗告警；它有傳遞延遲且擷取的是管理 API 活動，而非服務狀態變更事件。EventBridge 才是 AWS 建議用來回應部署狀態變更的機制。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability/security assessment service for workloads (EC2, ECR, Lambda); an Inspector assessment target cannot evaluate CodeDeploy/CodePipeline deployment failures. It is the wrong tool for parsing and reacting to deployment events.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是針對工作負載（EC2、ECR、Lambda）的弱點/安全評估服務；Inspector assessment target 無法評估 CodeDeploy/CodePipeline 的部署失敗。它並非用來解析與回應部署事件的正確工具。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/detect-state-changes-cloudwatch-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/incident-response.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codedeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codepipeline.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":125,"question_en":"A global company manages multiple AWS accounts by using AWS Control Tower. The company hosts internal applications and public applications. Each application team in the company has its own AWS account for application hosting. The accounts are consolidated in an organization in AWS Organizations. One of the AWS Control Tower member accounts serves as a centralized DevOps account with CI/CD pipelines that application teams use to deploy applications to their respective target AWS accounts. An IAM role for deployment exists in the centralized DevOps account. An application team is attempting to deploy its application to an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster in an application AWS account. An IAM role for deployment exists in the application AWS account. The deployment is through an AWS CodeBuild project that is set up in the centralized DevOps account. The CodeBuild project uses an IAM service role for CodeBuild. The deployment is failing with an Unauthorized error during attempts to connect to the cross-account EKS cluster from CodeBuild. Which solution will resolve this error?","question_zh":"一家全球性公司通过使用 AWS 控制塔来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司托管内部应用程序和公共应用 程序。 公司内的每个应用团队都有自己的 AWS 账户用于应用托管。这些账户在 AWS Organizations 中整合到一 个组织中。AWS Control Tower 成员账户中的一个账户作为集中式的 DevOps 账户，拥有应用团队用于将 应用部署到各自目标 AWS 账户的 CI/CD 管道。集中式的 DevOps 账户中存在一个用于部署的 IAM 角色。 一个应用程序团队正试图将其应用程序部署到应用程序 AWS 账户中的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service （Amazon EKS）集群。应用程序 AWS 账户中存在用于部署的 IAM 角色。部署是通过设置在集中式 DevOps 账户中的 AWS CodeBuild 项目进行的。CodeBuild 项目使用 CodeBuild 的 IAM 服务角色。在从 CodeBuild 连接到跨账户 EKS 集群时，部署因未经授权的错误而失败。 哪种解决方案能解决这个错误？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the application account’s deployment IAM role to have a trust relationship with the centralized DevOps account. Configure the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRole action. Configure the application account’s deployment IAM role to have the required access to the EKS cluster. Configure the EKS cluster aws-auth ConfigMap to map the role to the appropriate system permissions.","B":"Configure the centralized DevOps account’s deployment IAM role to have a trust relationship with the application account. Configure the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRole action. Configure the centralized DevOps account’s deployment IAM role to allow the required access to CodeBuild.","C":"Configure the centralized DevOps account’s deployment IAM role to have a trust relationship with the application account. Configure the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML action. Configure the centralized DevOps account’s deployment IAM role to allow the required access to CodeBuild.","D":"Configure the application account’s deployment IAM role to have a trust relationship with the AWS Control Tower management account. Configure the trust relationship to allow the sts:AssumeRole action. Configure the application account’s deployment IAM role to have the required access to the EKS cluster. Configure the EKS cluster aws-auth ConfigMap to map the role to the appropriate system permissions."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置应用程序账户的部署 IAM 角色与集中式 DevOps 账户建立信任关系。配置该信任关系以允 许执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。配置应用程序账户的部署 IAM 角色以获取对 EKS 集群的必要访 问权限。配置 EKS 集群的 aws-auth ConfigMap 以将该角色映射到适当的系统权限。","B":"配置集中式 DevOps 账户的部署 IAM 角色与应用账户建立信任关系。配置该信任关系以允许执行 sts: AssumeRole 操作。配置集中式 DevOps 账户的部署 IAM 角色以允许对 CodeBuild 进行所需访问。","C":"配置集中式 DevOps 账户的部署 IAM 角色，使其与应用账户建立信任关系。配置该信任关系以允许 执行 sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML 操作。配置集中式 DevOps 账户的部署 IAM 角色，使其能够访问 CodeBuild 所需的权限。","D":"配置应用程序账户的部署 IAM 角色与 AWS Control Tower 管理账户建立信任关系。配置信任关系以允 许执行 sts:AssumeRole 操作。配置应用程序账户的部署 IAM 角色以获取对 EKS 集群的必要访问权 限。配置 EKS 集群的 aws-auth ConfigMap 以将该角色映射到适当的系统权限。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeBuild runs in the centralized DevOps account and must reach an EKS cluster that lives in the application account. The standard AWS cross-account pattern is to create the role in the account that owns the resource (the application account) and give it a trust policy that names the calling account (the DevOps account) as the Principal with sts:AssumeRole, so the DevOps principal can switch into the application account. That role must also hold the IAM permissions for the EKS API (for example eks:DescribeCluster). The decisive clue is the 'Unauthorized' error: that is not an IAM AccessDeniedException but a Kubernetes RBAC authorization failure surfaced by the AWS IAM Authenticator, which means the IAM principal authenticated to the cluster but is not mapped to any Kubernetes group. Per the EKS docs, you clear this by mapping the IAM role in the cluster's aws-auth ConfigMap (or an EKS access entry) to an appropriate RBAC group. Option A is the only choice that both points the trust the correct direction (application-account role trusts the DevOps account) and adds the aws-auth ConfigMap mapping, so it is the only complete fix.","explanation_zh":"CodeBuild 執行於集中式 DevOps 帳戶，必須存取位於應用程式帳戶中的 EKS 叢集。AWS 標準的跨帳戶模式是在擁有資源的帳戶（應用程式帳戶）建立角色，並在其信任政策中將呼叫端帳戶（DevOps 帳戶）指定為 Principal 並允許 sts:AssumeRole，讓 DevOps 主體得以切換進入應用程式帳戶。該角色還必須具備呼叫 EKS API 所需的 IAM 權限（例如 eks:DescribeCluster）。關鍵線索是 'Unauthorized' 錯誤：這並非 IAM 的 AccessDeniedException，而是由 AWS IAM Authenticator 回報的 Kubernetes RBAC 授權失敗，代表該 IAM 主體已通過叢集驗證，但未對應到任何 Kubernetes group。依 EKS 文件，必須在叢集的 aws-auth ConfigMap（或 EKS access entry）中將該 IAM 角色對應到適當的 RBAC group 才能清除此錯誤。選項 A 是唯一同時把信任方向設定正確（應用程式帳戶角色信任 DevOps 帳戶）並加入 aws-auth ConfigMap 對應的選項，因此是唯一完整的修正方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The trust direction is reversed: it makes the DevOps role trust the application account, but CodeBuild already runs in DevOps and must assume INTO the application account, so the role and its trust policy belong in the application account. It also never maps any role in the EKS aws-auth ConfigMap, so the Kubernetes Unauthorized (RBAC) error would persist even if the AssumeRole succeeded.","why_zh":"信任方向相反：它讓 DevOps 角色信任應用程式帳戶，但 CodeBuild 本就執行於 DevOps，需要 assume 進入應用程式帳戶，因此角色與其信任政策應放在應用程式帳戶。且它完全沒有在 EKS aws-auth ConfigMap 中對應任何角色，因此即使 AssumeRole 成功，Kubernetes 的 Unauthorized（RBAC）錯誤仍會存在。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same reversed trust direction as B, and it specifies sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML, which is for SAML 2.0 identity federation and is not used for account-to-account role assumption between AWS accounts you own; account-to-account uses sts:AssumeRole. It also omits the aws-auth ConfigMap mapping, so the Unauthorized error remains unaddressed.","why_zh":"信任方向與 B 一樣相反，且指定 sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML，該動作用於 SAML 2.0 身分聯合，並非用於自有 AWS 帳戶之間的帳戶對帳戶角色 assume（後者使用 sts:AssumeRole）。它同樣省略了 aws-auth ConfigMap 對應，因此未解決 Unauthorized 錯誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It maps the ConfigMap correctly, but it trusts the wrong account: it has the application-account role trust the AWS Control Tower management account, whereas CodeBuild actually runs in the centralized DevOps member account. The AssumeRole call originates from the DevOps account principal, so unless the application-account role trusts the DevOps account the cross-account assume still fails.","why_zh":"它正確處理了 ConfigMap 對應，但信任了錯誤的帳戶：讓應用程式帳戶角色信任 AWS Control Tower 管理帳戶，而 CodeBuild 實際上是執行於集中式 DevOps 成員帳戶。AssumeRole 呼叫來自 DevOps 帳戶主體，因此除非應用程式帳戶角色信任 DevOps 帳戶，否則跨帳戶 assume 仍會失敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/security-iam-troubleshoot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/auth-configmap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/access-entries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/grant-k8s-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_common-scenarios_aws-accounts.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":126,"question_en":"A highly regulated company has a policy that DevOps engineers should not log in to their Amazon EC2 instances except in emergencies. If a DevOps engineer does log in, the security team must be notified within 15 minutes of the occurrence. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家受到严格监管的公司规定，DevOps 工程师除非在紧急情况下，否则不得登录其亚马逊 EC2 实例。 如果 DevOps 工程师确实登录了，安全团队必须在事件发生后的 15 分钟内得到通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Install the Amazon Inspector agent on each EC2 instance. Subscribe to Amazon EventBridge notifications. Invoke an AWS Lambda function to check if a message is about user logins. If it is, send a notification to the security team using Amazon SNS.","B":"Install the Amazon CloudWatch agent on each EC2 instance. Configure the agent to push all logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and set up a CloudWatch metric filter that searches for user logins. If a login is found, send a notification to the security team using Amazon SNS.","C":"Set up AWS CloudTrail with Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Subscribe CloudWatch Logs to Amazon Kinesis. Attach AWS Lambda to Kinesis to parse and determine if a log contains a user login. If it does, send a notification to the security team using Amazon SNS.","D":"Set up a script on each Amazon EC2 instance to push all logs to Amazon S3. Set up an S3 event to invoke an AWS Lambda function, which invokes an Amazon Athena query to run. The Athena query checks for logins and sends the output to the security team using Amazon SNS."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon Inspector 代理。订阅 Amazon EventBridge 通知。调用 AWS Lambda 函 数检查消息是否与用户登录有关。如果是，则使用 Amazon SNS 向安全团队发送通知。","B":"在每个 EC2 实例上安装 Amazon CloudWatch 代理。配置代理将所有日志推送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，并设置一个 CloudWatch 指标过滤器以搜索用户登录信息。如果发现登录信息，则使用 Amazon SNS 向安全团队发送通知。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 设置 AWS CloudTrail。将 CloudWatch Logs 订阅到 Amazon Kinesis。将 AWS Lambda 附加到 Kinesis 以解析日志并确定其是否包含用户登录信息。如果包含，则使用 Amazon SNS 向安全团队发送通知。","D":"在每个 Amazon EC2 实例上设置一个脚本，将所有日志推送到 Amazon S3。设置一个 S3 事件以调 用 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 Amazon Athena 查询来运行。Athena 查询检查登录情况，并使 用 Amazon SNS 将输出发送给安全团队。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is to detect OS-level interactive user logins (SSH/RDP) on EC2 instances and alert the security team within 15 minutes. The CloudWatch agent is installed on each instance and streams the OS authentication logs (Linux /var/log/secure or /var/log/auth.log, Windows Security event log) to CloudWatch Logs. A CloudWatch Logs metric filter scans log data as it arrives for login patterns (for example 'session opened' or 'Accepted password') and increments a metric; a CloudWatch alarm on that metric then publishes to an Amazon SNS topic to notify the security team. This is the documented 'Alarming on logs' pattern (metric filter to alarm to SNS notification), and alarm evaluation periods of 1-5 minutes comfortably meet the 15-minute SLA. The other options rely on services that do not capture OS-level logins (Inspector, CloudTrail) or use high-latency batch architectures (Athena over S3).","explanation_zh":"需求是偵測 EC2 instance 上的 OS 層級互動式使用者登入 (SSH/RDP)，並在 15 分鐘內通知安全團隊。CloudWatch agent 安裝在每台 instance 上，將 OS 驗證日誌 (Linux 的 /var/log/secure 或 /var/log/auth.log、Windows 的 Security event log) 串流到 CloudWatch Logs。CloudWatch Logs metric filter 在日誌進入時即時掃描登入模式 (例如 'session opened' 或 'Accepted password') 並遞增一個 metric；接著針對該 metric 的 CloudWatch alarm 發佈到 Amazon SNS topic 來通知安全團隊。這正是官方文件中的 'Alarming on logs' 模式 (metric filter 到 alarm 再到 SNS 通知)，而 alarm 的評估週期 (1-5 分鐘) 可輕鬆滿足 15 分鐘的 SLA。其他選項所依賴的服務無法擷取 OS 層級登入 (Inspector、CloudTrail)，或採用高延遲的批次架構 (Athena over S3)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability/security assessment service (CVE scanning, configuration and network reachability analysis). Its agent does not capture or emit OS-level interactive login events, so there is no 'user login' message in EventBridge for Lambda to inspect. It conflates services.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是漏洞/安全評估服務 (CVE 掃描、組態與網路可達性分析)。其 agent 不會擷取或發出 OS 層級的互動式登入事件，因此 EventBridge 中根本不存在可供 Lambda 檢查的 'user login' 訊息，屬於服務概念混淆。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS CloudTrail records AWS API/management-plane and data events, not OS-level interactive SSH/RDP logins inside the instance operating system. An SSH/RDP session generates no CloudTrail event, so parsing CloudTrail via Kinesis and Lambda would never see the login. The pipeline is also needlessly complex and higher latency.","why_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API/管理層與資料事件，而非 instance 作業系統內的 OS 層級互動式 SSH/RDP 登入。SSH/RDP 連線不會產生 CloudTrail 事件，因此經由 Kinesis 與 Lambda 解析 CloudTrail 永遠看不到登入，且該管線過於複雜且延遲較高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Athena is an ad-hoc interactive query service over S3, not a real-time alerting mechanism. A batch script pushing logs to S3, then triggering an Athena query per object on S3 events, is fragile, high-latency, and operationally heavy, and cannot reliably guarantee notification within the 15-minute window.","why_zh":"Athena 是針對 S3 的臨時互動式查詢服務，並非即時告警機制。以批次腳本將日誌推送到 S3、再由 S3 事件對每個物件觸發 Athena 查詢的做法既脆弱、高延遲又營運負擔重，無法可靠地保證在 15 分鐘內通知。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Alarm-On-Logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/install-CloudWatch-Agent-on-EC2-Instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/logging-management-events-with-cloudtrail.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":127,"question_en":"A company updated the AWS CloudFormation template for a critical business application. The stack update process failed due to an error in the updated template, and AWS CloudFormation automatically began the stack rollback process. Later, a DevOps engineer discovered that the application was still unavailable and that the stack was in the UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED state. Which combination of actions should the DevOps engineer perform so that the stack rollback can complete successfully? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司更新了关键业务应用程序的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。由于更新后的模板存在错误，堆栈更 新过程失败，AWS CloudFormation 自动开始执行堆栈回滚操作。后来，一位 DevOps 工程师发现应用程 序仍不可用，且堆栈处于 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 状态。 DevOps 工程师应执行哪两种操作组合才能使堆栈回滚成功完成？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Attach the AWSCloudFormationFullAccess IAM policy to the AWS CloudFormation role.","B":"Automatically recover the stack resources by using AWS CloudFormation drift detection.","C":"Issue a ContinueUpdateRollback command from the AWS CloudFormation console or the AWS CLI.","D":"Manually adjust the resources to match the expectations of the stack.","E":"Update the existing AWS CloudFormation stack by using the original template."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AWSCloudFormationFullAccess IAM 策略附加到 AWS CloudFormation 角色。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 漂移检测自动恢复堆栈资源。","C":"从 AWS CloudFormation 控制台或 AWS CLI 发布 ContinueUpdateRollback 命令。","D":"手动调整资源以符合堆栈的预期。","E":"使用原始模板更新现有的 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A stack in the UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED state cannot be updated, but it can be returned to a working UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE state so the application becomes available again. Per the AWS CloudFormation User Guide ('Continue rolling back an update'), in most cases you must first manually fix the error that caused the update rollback to fail so the actual resources match what CloudFormation expects (D). The ContinueUpdateRollback API reference states: 'Depending on the cause of the failure, you can manually fix the error and continue the rollback. By continuing the rollback, you can return your stack to a working state... and then try to update the stack again.' You then issue ContinueUpdateRollback from the console (Stack actions > Continue update rollback) or the AWS CLI (continue-update-rollback) to drive the stack from UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED to UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE (C). These two steps work together: fixing the resource mismatch removes the cause of the failure, and ContinueUpdateRollback then completes the rollback. After reaching UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE, the engineer can attempt the stack update again.","explanation_zh":"處於 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 狀態的 stack 無法被更新，但可以被帶回正常運作的 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE 狀態，讓應用程式恢復可用。根據 AWS CloudFormation User Guide「Continue rolling back an update」，多數情況下你必須先手動修正導致 update rollback 失敗的錯誤，讓實際資源與 CloudFormation 預期一致（D）。ContinueUpdateRollback API 參考文件指出：「視失敗原因而定，你可以手動修正錯誤後繼續 rollback。透過繼續 rollback，可讓 stack 回到正常狀態……之後再嘗試更新 stack。」接著從 console（Stack actions > Continue update rollback）或 AWS CLI（continue-update-rollback）發出 ContinueUpdateRollback 指令，將 stack 從 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 推進到 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE（C）。兩個步驟相輔相成：修正資源不一致可消除失敗原因，ContinueUpdateRollback 接著完成 rollback。到達 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE 後，工程師即可再次嘗試更新 stack。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The question never describes a permissions error as the cause of the rollback failure. Attaching the broad AWSCloudFormationFullAccess managed policy is not a documented remediation for UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED; that policy grants permissions to call the CloudFormation API itself, not the underlying resource-service permissions (EC2, RDS, etc.) a service role would need. The documented fix is to manually correct the resource error and continue the rollback, not to attach a broad IAM policy.","why_zh":"題目從未指出 rollback 失敗是由權限錯誤造成。附加範圍過大的 AWSCloudFormationFullAccess 受管政策並非 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 的官方解法；該政策授予的是呼叫 CloudFormation API 本身的權限，而非 service role 所需的底層資源服務權限（EC2、RDS 等）。官方解法是手動修正資源錯誤並繼續 rollback，而非附加一個寬鬆的 IAM 政策。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudFormation drift detection only detects and reports differences between the stack's expected configuration and the actual resource state. It is a read-only diagnostic that does not modify, recover, or repair resources, so it cannot move a stack out of UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED. 'Automatically recover the stack resources by using drift detection' describes a capability that does not exist.","why_zh":"CloudFormation drift detection 只會偵測並回報 stack 預期組態與實際資源狀態之間的差異，屬於唯讀診斷工具，不會修改、復原或修復資源，因此無法讓 stack 脫離 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED。「使用 drift detection 自動復原 stack 資源」描述的是一個並不存在的功能。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"The AWS docs explicitly state that 'a stack in the UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED state can't be updated.' Any UpdateStack operation, including re-applying the original template, is rejected until the rollback is completed via ContinueUpdateRollback. The stack must first reach UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE before any further update can be performed, so this action is impossible in the current state.","why_zh":"AWS 文件明確指出「處於 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_FAILED 狀態的 stack 無法被更新」。在透過 ContinueUpdateRollback 完成 rollback 之前，任何 UpdateStack 操作（包括重新套用原始範本）都會被拒絕。必須先到達 UPDATE_ROLLBACK_COMPLETE 才能執行後續更新，因此在目前狀態下此動作不可行。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-updating-stacks-continueupdaterollback.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/APIReference/API_ContinueUpdateRollback.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/troubleshooting.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":128,"question_en":"A development team manually builds an artifact locally and then places it in an Amazon S3 bucket. The application has a local cache that must be cleared when a deployment occurs. The team runs a command to do this, downloads the artifact from Amazon S3, and unzips the artifact to complete the deployment. A DevOps team wants to migrate to a CI/CD process and build in checks to stop and roll back the deployment when a failure occurs. This requires the team to track the progression of the deployment. Which combination of actions will accomplish this? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"开发团队在本地手动构建一个工件，然后将其放入 Amazon S3 存储桶中。应用程序有一个本地缓存，在部 署时必须清除。团队运行一个命令来完成此操作，从 Amazon S3 下载工件，并解压工件以完成部署。 一个 DevOps 团队希望迁移到持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）流程，并在部署失败时设置检查以停止并 回滚部署。这需要团队跟踪部署的进展情况。 哪些行动组合能够达成此目标？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Allow developers to check the code into a code repository. Using Amazon EventBridge, on every pull into the main branch, invoke an AWS Lambda function to build the artifact and store it in Amazon S3.","B":"Create a custom script to clear the cache. Specify the script in the BeforeInstall lifecycle hook in the AppSpec file.","C":"Create user data for each Amazon EC2 instance that contains the clear cache script. Once deployed, test the application. If it is not successful, deploy it again.","D":"Set up AWS CodePipeline to deploy the application. Allow developers to check the code into a code repository as a source for the pipeline.","E":"Use AWS CodeBuild to build the artifact and place it in Amazon S3. Use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the artifact to Amazon EC2 instances.","F":"Use AWS Systems Manager to fetch the artifact from Amazon S3 and deploy it to all the instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"允许开发人员将代码提交到代码库。使用 Amazon EventBridge，在每次将代码拉取到主分支时，调用一 个 AWS Lambda 函数来构建工件并将其存储在 Amazon S3 中。","B":"创建一个自定义脚本以清除缓存。在 AppSpec 文件的 BeforeInstall 生命周期钩子中指定该脚本。","C":"为每个包含清除缓存脚本的 Amazon EC2 实例创建用户数据。部署完成后，测试应用程序。如果测试不 成功，请重新部署。","D":"设置 AWS CodePipeline 以部署应用程序。允许开发人员将代码检入代码库作为管道的源代码。","E":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 构建工件并将其放置在 Amazon S3 中。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将工件部署到 Amazon EC2 实例上。","F":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 从 Amazon S3 获取工件并将其部署到所有实例。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario needs a managed CI/CD pipeline that builds an artifact to S3, deploys it to EC2, clears the application cache when a deployment occurs, and stops/rolls back on failure while tracking the progression of the deployment. D establishes AWS CodePipeline with the code repository as the pipeline source; CodePipeline orchestrates the Source/Build/Deploy stages and natively tracks the progression of every pipeline execution, satisfying the CI/CD and progression-tracking requirements. E uses AWS CodeBuild (a managed build service) to produce the artifact and place it in S3, replacing the manual local build, and AWS CodeDeploy to deploy that artifact to the EC2 instances; CodeDeploy supports automatic rollback that redeploys the last known good revision when a deployment fails, satisfying the stop-and-roll-back requirement. B addresses 'clear the cache when a deployment occurs' by running a custom clear-cache script in the BeforeInstall lifecycle hook of the AppSpec file; AWS docs state the EC2/On-Premises BeforeInstall event is a scriptable preinstall hook (for tasks such as decrypting files or backing up the current version) that runs before the new revision is installed. Together B+D+E cover managed build to S3, deploy with automatic rollback, native progression tracking, and per-deployment cache clearing using AWS-native managed services.","explanation_zh":"情境需要一個受管的 CI/CD 流程：建置成品並放到 S3、部署到 EC2、在部署發生時清除應用程式快取、失敗時停止並回復，同時追蹤部署進度。D 建立 AWS CodePipeline 並以程式碼儲存庫作為 pipeline 來源；CodePipeline 協調 Source/Build/Deploy 各階段，並原生追蹤每次 pipeline 執行的進度，滿足 CI/CD 與進度追蹤需求。E 使用受管建置服務 AWS CodeBuild 產生成品並放到 S3（取代手動本機建置），再用 AWS CodeDeploy 將成品部署到 EC2 執行個體；CodeDeploy 支援自動回復（automatic rollback），在部署失敗時重新部署上一個已知良好版本，滿足停止與回復的需求。B 透過在 AppSpec 檔案的 BeforeInstall 生命週期掛勾執行自訂清除快取腳本，解決『部署發生時清除快取』；AWS 文件指出 EC2/On-Premises 的 BeforeInstall 事件是可寫入腳本的安裝前掛勾（用於解密檔案或備份目前版本等任務），會在安裝新版本之前執行。B+D+E 結合即涵蓋受管建置到 S3、含自動回復的部署、原生進度追蹤，以及每次部署的清除快取，全部使用 AWS 原生受管服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Triggering a Lambda function via EventBridge on every pull into main to build the artifact is a fragile custom build path. Lambda is not a managed build service, has runtime/size limits, and on its own provides no deployment progression tracking, no stop/rollback, and no deployment orchestration. AWS CodeBuild (option E) is the native managed build service for this job.","why_zh":"以 EventBridge 在每次合併到 main 時觸發 Lambda 來建置成品是脆弱的自訂建置方式。Lambda 並非受管建置服務，有執行時間與大小限制，本身也無法提供部署進度追蹤、停止/回復或部署協調。AWS CodeBuild（選項 E）才是此工作的原生受管建置服務。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EC2 user data only runs at instance launch, not on each deployment, so it cannot reliably clear the cache 'when a deployment occurs.' Manually testing and 'deploy it again' on failure is not automated stop/rollback and provides no progression tracking, the opposite of the managed CI/CD process the team wants.","why_zh":"EC2 user data 僅在執行個體啟動時執行，而非每次部署，因此無法在『部署發生時』可靠地清除快取。手動測試並在失敗時『再部署一次』不是自動化的停止/回復，也無法追蹤進度，與團隊想要的受管 CI/CD 流程相反。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Using AWS Systems Manager to fetch the artifact and deploy to all instances is a competing deploy mechanism that overlaps with CodeDeploy (option E). It lacks CodeDeploy's lifecycle-hook-based automatic rollback and the integrated CodePipeline deployment progression tracking the scenario demands, and is redundant with E.","why_zh":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 取得成品並部署到所有執行個體，是與 CodeDeploy（選項 E）重疊的競爭部署機制。它缺少 CodeDeploy 基於生命週期掛勾的自動回復，以及情境所需的整合 CodePipeline 部署進度追蹤，且與 E 重複。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployments-rollback-and-redeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/welcome.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":129,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is working on a project that is hosted on Amazon Linux and has failed a security review. The DevOps manager has been asked to review the company buildspec.yaml file for an AWS CodeBuild project and provide recommendations. The buildspec.yaml file is configured as follows: What changes should be recommended to comply with AWS security best practices? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在处理一个托管在亚马逊 Linux 上的项目，该项目未能通过安全审查。DevOps 经理被要求审查公司 AWS CodeBuild 项目的 buildspec.yaml 文件，并提出建议。该 buildspec.yaml 文件 的配置如下： 为了符合 AWS 安全最佳实践，应推荐哪些变更？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add a post-build command to remove the temporary files from the container before termination to ensure they cannot be seen by other CodeBuild users.","B":"Update the CodeBuild project role with the necessary permissions and then remove the AWS credentials from the environment variable.","C":"Store the DB_PASSWORD as a SecureString value in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store and then remove the DB_PASSWORD from the environment variables.","D":"Move the environment variables to the ‘db-deploy-bucket’ Amazon S3 bucket, add a prebuild stage to download, then export the variables.","E":"Use AWS Systems Manager run command versus scp and ssh commands directly to the instance.","F":"Scramble the environment variables using XOR followed by Base64, add a section to install, and then run XOR and Base64 to the build phase."},"options_zh":{"A":"添加一个构建后命令，在容器终止前删除临时文件，以确保其他 CodeBuild 用户无法看到这些文 件。","B":"使用必要的权限更新 CodeBuild 项目角色，然后从环境变量中移除 AWS 凭证。","C":"将 DB_PASSWORD 作为 SecureString 值存储在 AWS 系统管理器参数存储中，然后从环境变量中移除 DB_PASSWORD。","D":"将环境变量移至“db-deploy-bucket” Amazon S3 存储桶，添加一个预构建阶段以下载这些变量，然 后导出它们。","E":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 的运行命令，而非直接向实例发送 scp 和 ssh 命令。","F":"使用异或运算对环境变量进行打乱，然后进行 Base64 编码，在安装部分添加相关内容，接着在构建 阶段运行异或运算和 Base64 编码。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The buildspec has three concrete security flaws, and B, C, and E each remediate one. (B) The file embeds long-term AWS access keys as environment variables. IAM security best practices and the Well-Architected Framework require workloads on AWS compute (including CodeBuild) to use temporary credentials delivered automatically through an IAM role, not long-lived IAM user keys; therefore you grant the needed permissions to the CodeBuild project (service) role and remove the static credentials. (C) The DB_PASSWORD is a PLAINTEXT environment variable. The CodeBuild EnvironmentVariable API doc states AWS 'strongly discourage the use of PLAINTEXT environment variables to store sensitive values' because they are visible in the console and CLI, and recommends Systems Manager Parameter Store (SecureString / type PARAMETER_STORE) or Secrets Manager, referenced at runtime. (E) The project deploys to the Amazon Linux instance with direct scp/ssh. Systems Manager Session Manager / Run Command is the recommended secure alternative: centralized IAM-based access control, TLS encryption, full session/command logging, and no open inbound SSH ports, bastion hosts, or managed SSH keys. The remaining options are weaker or anti-patterns: A is moot because CodeBuild build containers are ephemeral and isolated per build; D keeps secrets in plaintext and merely relocates the exposure; F is reversible encoding (XOR + Base64), not encryption, and AWS never endorses it over Parameter Store/Secrets Manager/KMS.","explanation_zh":"此 buildspec 有三個明確的安全缺陷，B、C、E 分別修補其一。(B) 檔案以環境變數內嵌長期 AWS access key。IAM 安全最佳實務與 Well-Architected Framework 要求在 AWS 運算服務（含 CodeBuild）上的工作負載使用透過 IAM role 自動派發的臨時憑證，而非長期 IAM user 金鑰；因此應將所需權限授予 CodeBuild 專案（service）role，並移除靜態憑證。(C) DB_PASSWORD 是 PLAINTEXT 環境變數。CodeBuild EnvironmentVariable API 文件明確表示 AWS「強烈不建議使用 PLAINTEXT 環境變數儲存敏感值」，因為在 console 與 CLI 會以明文顯示，並建議改存於 Systems Manager Parameter Store（SecureString / 類型 PARAMETER_STORE）或 Secrets Manager，於執行期再引用。(E) 專案以直接 scp/ssh 部署到 Amazon Linux 執行個體。Systems Manager Session Manager / Run Command 是建議的安全替代方案：提供集中式 IAM 存取控制、TLS 加密、完整的 session/command 記錄，並免除開放 SSH 入站埠、bastion host 與管理 SSH 金鑰的需求。其餘選項較弱或屬反模式：A 無意義，因為 CodeBuild build 容器短暫且每次建置隔離；D 仍以明文保存秘密，只是搬移暴露點；F 屬可逆編碼（XOR + Base64）而非加密，AWS 從不建議以此取代 Parameter Store/Secrets Manager/KMS。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodeBuild build containers are ephemeral and isolated per build; they are destroyed after the build and are not shared with other CodeBuild users, so deleting temporary files in a post-build step addresses no real cross-user exposure and is not an AWS-recognized best practice here.","why_zh":"CodeBuild build 容器為短暫且每次建置隔離，建置後即銷毀且不與其他 CodeBuild 使用者共用，因此在 post-build 刪除暫存檔並未解決任何實際的跨使用者暴露，亦非此情境的 AWS 最佳實務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Moving the credentials/password into an S3 object and re-exporting them keeps the secrets in plaintext and merely relocates the exposure; it lacks the encryption-at-rest and runtime substitution of Parameter Store SecureString or Secrets Manager, so it is inferior to C and not the recommended pattern.","why_zh":"把憑證/密碼搬到 S3 物件再 export，仍以明文保存秘密、只是搬移暴露點；缺乏 Parameter Store SecureString 或 Secrets Manager 的靜態加密與執行期替換，因此遜於 C，並非建議做法。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"XOR plus Base64 is obfuscation/encoding, not encryption; it is trivially reversible and the deobfuscation script lives in the same build, so it provides no real protection. AWS recommends Parameter Store SecureString, Secrets Manager, and KMS for sensitive values, never home-grown scrambling, making this a security anti-pattern.","why_zh":"XOR 加 Base64 屬混淆/編碼而非加密，可被輕易還原，且解混淆指令也留在同一建置中，毫無實質保護。AWS 對敏感值建議使用 Parameter Store SecureString、Secrets Manager 與 KMS，絕不建議自製打亂，故屬安全反模式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/APIReference/API_EnvironmentVariable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/2024-06-27/framework/sec_identities_unique.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/session-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-parameter-store.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":130,"question_en":"A company has a legacy application. A DevOps engineer needs to automate the process of building the deployable artifact for the legacy application. The solution must store the deployable artifact in an existing Amazon S3 bucket for future deployments to reference. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款遗留应用程序。一位 DevOps 工程师需要将为该遗留应用程序构建可部署工件的过程 实现自动化。解决方案必须将可部署工件存储在现有的 Amazon S3 存储桶中，以便未来部署时引用。 哪种解决方案能以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a custom Docker image that contains all the dependencies for the legacy application. Store the custom Docker image in a new Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Configure a new AWS CodeBuild project to use the custom Docker image to build the deployable artifact and to save the artifact to the S3 bucket.","B":"Launch a new Amazon EC2 instance. Install all the dependencies for the legacy application on the EC2 instance. Use the EC2 instance to build the deployable artifact and to save the artifact to the S3 bucket.","C":"Create a custom EC2 Image Builder image. Install all the dependencies for the legacy application on the image. Launch a new Amazon EC2 instance from the image. Use the new EC2 instance to build the deployable artifact and to save the artifact to the S3 bucket.","D":"Create an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster with an AWS Fargate profile that runs in multiple Availability Zones. Create a custom Docker image that contains all the dependencies for the legacy application. Store the custom Docker image in a new Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Use the custom Docker image inside the EKS cluster to build the deployable artifact and to save the artifact to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个自定义的 Docker 镜像，其中包含旧版应用程序的所有依赖项。将自定义的 Docker 镜像存储 在新的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库中。配置一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目，使用自定义的 Docker 镜像来构建可部署的工件，并将工件保存到 S3 存储桶中。","B":"启动一个新的亚马逊 EC2 实例。在 EC2 实例上安装遗留应用程序的所有依赖项。使用 EC2 实例构建可 部署的工件，并将工件保存到 S3 存储桶。","C":"创建一个自定义的 EC2 Image Builder 镜像。在该镜像上安装旧版应用程序的所有依赖项。从该镜像 启动一个新的 Amazon EC2 实例。使用新的 EC2 实例构建可部署的工件，并将工件保存到 S3 存储 桶中。","D":"创建一个带有在多个可用区运行的 AWS Fargate 配置文件的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service （Amazon EKS） 集群。创建一个自定义 Docker 镜像，其中包含遗留应用程序的所有依赖项。将自 定义 Docker 镜像存储在新的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库中。在 EKS 集群中使用自定义 Docker 镜像构建可部署的工件，并将工件保存到 S3 存储桶中。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS CodeBuild is a fully managed build service that 'compiles your source code, runs unit tests, and produces artifacts that are ready to deploy' and 'eliminates the need to provision, manage, and scale your own build servers' (no setup, patching, or updating of build servers). The legacy application's dependencies can be packaged into a custom Docker image stored in Amazon ECR, and a CodeBuild project can use that custom image as its build environment to produce the deployable artifact. CodeBuild natively writes build output to Amazon S3 by setting the project/buildspec artifacts type to S3, satisfying the requirement to store the artifact in the existing bucket for future deployments. Because there are no servers or clusters to provision, patch, or manage, this is the MOST operationally efficient option. Options B and C both require managing EC2 build servers, and option D stands up an entire EKS/Fargate cluster just to run a build, which is gross over-engineering.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeBuild 是一個全受管的建置服務，它會「編譯原始碼、執行單元測試並產生可直接部署的成品」，並且「免除佈建、管理及擴展自有建置伺服器的需要」（不需設定、修補、更新或管理建置伺服器）。可以把這個 legacy 應用程式的所有相依套件打包成自訂 Docker image 並儲存在 Amazon ECR，再讓 CodeBuild 專案以該自訂 image 作為建置環境來產生可部署成品。CodeBuild 透過將專案/buildspec 的 artifacts 類型設為 S3，即可原生地把建置輸出寫入既有的 Amazon S3 儲存貯體，滿足保存成品供日後部署參考的需求。由於沒有任何伺服器或叢集需要佈建、修補或管理，這是「營運上最有效率」的選項。選項 B 與 C 都需要自行管理 EC2 建置伺服器；選項 D 為了跑一次建置卻架設整個 EKS/Fargate 叢集，屬於過度設計。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Manually launching an EC2 instance, installing dependencies, and using it to build and upload the artifact is high operational overhead: you must provision, patch, scale, secure, and keep the instance running, and the process is largely manual rather than automated. CodeBuild removes all of this.","why_zh":"手動啟動 EC2 執行個體、安裝相依套件，再用它建置並上傳 artifact，操作負擔極高：需自行佈建、修補、擴展、保護並維持執行個體運作，流程偏手動而非自動化。CodeBuild 可免除這一切。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EC2 Image Builder produces a golden AMI/container image, but you still must launch and manage an EC2 instance to actually run the build, plus maintain the image pipeline. Image Builder is for creating and maintaining images, not for running on-demand artifact builds, so this carries more ongoing instance-management overhead than CodeBuild.","why_zh":"EC2 Image Builder 用於產生黃金 AMI／容器映像，但仍需啟動並管理 EC2 執行個體才能實際執行建置，還要維護映像建置管線。Image Builder 的用途是建立與維護映像，並非執行隨需的 artifact 建置，因此相較 CodeBuild 會帶來更多持續的執行個體管理負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EKS cluster with a Fargate profile across multiple Availability Zones is massively over-engineered for a simple build task. Managing a Kubernetes cluster (control plane, Fargate profiles, scheduling, networking) adds substantial operational complexity and cost compared to a single managed CodeBuild project.","why_zh":"跨多個可用區、搭配 Fargate 設定檔的 EKS 叢集，對於單純的建置工作而言過度設計。管理 Kubernetes 叢集（控制平面、Fargate 設定檔、排程、網路）相較於單一受管的 CodeBuild 專案，會增加大量操作複雜度與成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/sample-docker-custom-image.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-codebuild-project-artifacts.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":131,"question_en":"A company builds a container image in an AWS CodeBuild project by running Docker commands. After the container image is built, the CodeBuild project uploads the container image to an Amazon S3 bucket. The CodeBuild project has an IAM service role that has permissions to access the S3 bucket. A DevOps engineer needs to replace the S3 bucket with an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository to store the container images. The DevOps engineer creates an ECR private image repository in the same AWS Region of the CodeBuild project. The DevOps engineer adjusts the IAM service role with the permissions that are necessary to work with the new ECR repository. The DevOps engineer also places new repository information into the docker build command and the docker push command that are used in the buildspec.yml file. When the CodeBuild project runs a build job, the job fails when the job tries to access the ECR repository. Which solution will resolve the issue of failed access to the ECR repository?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS CodeBuild 项目中通过运行 Docker 命令来构建容器镜像。容器镜像构建完成后， CodeBuild 项目会将其上传至 Amazon S3 存储桶。CodeBuild 项目具有一个 IAM 服务角色，该角色拥有 访问 S3 存储桶的权限。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要将 S3 存储桶替换为 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储 库来存储容器镜像。该 DevOps 工程师在与 CodeBuild 项目相同的 AWS 区域中创建了一个 ECR 私有 镜像存储库。该 DevOps 工程师还调整了 IAM 服务角色，赋予其与新 ECR 存储库交互所需的权限。 此外，该 DevOps 工程师还将新的存储库信息放入 buildspec.yml 文件中使用的 docker build 命令和 docker push 命令中。 当 CodeBuild 项目运行构建任务时，如果该任务尝试访问 ECR 存储库，则任务会失败。 哪种解决方案可以解决无法访问 ECR 仓库的问题？","options_en":{"A":"Update the buildspec.yml file to log in to the ECR repository by using the aws ecr get-login-password AWS CLI command to obtain an authentication token. Update the docker login command to use the authentication token to access the ECR repository.","B":"Add an environment variable of type SECRETS_MANAGER to the CodeBuild project. In the environment variable, include the ARN of the CodeBuild project's IAM service role. Update the buildspec.yml file to use the new environment variable to log in with the docker login command to access the ECR repository.","C":"Update the ECR repository to be a public image repository. Add an ECR repository policy that allows the IAM service role to have access.","D":"Update the buildspec.yml file to use the AWS CLI to assume the IAM service role for ECR operations. Add an ECR repository policy that allows the IAM service role to have access."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 buildspec.yml 文件，通过使用 aws ecr get-login-password AWS CLI 命令获取身份验证令牌来 登录到 ECR 仓库。更新 docker login 命令以使用身份验证令牌访问 ECR 仓库。","B":"在 CodeBuild 项目中添加一个类型为 SECRETS_MANAGER 的环境变量。在该环境变量中包 含 CodeBuild 项目的 IAM 服务角色的 ARN。更新 buildspec.yml 文件，使用新的环境变量通 过 docker login 命令登录以访问 ECR 仓库。","C":"将 ECR 代码库更新为公共镜像代码库。添加一个 ECR 代码库策略，允许 IAM 服务角色进行访问。","D":"更新 buildspec.yml 文件，使用 AWS CLI 假定 IAM 服务角色以执行 ECR 操作。添加一个 ECR 存 储库策略，允许 IAM 服务角色进行访问。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The Docker CLI does not support native IAM authentication, so granting the CodeBuild IAM service role ECR permissions and updating the docker build/push commands is not sufficient. Before Docker can push to an ECR private repository, the client must authenticate using an authorization token. The 'aws ecr get-login-password' AWS CLI command retrieves and decodes a 12-hour token (with username 'AWS') that is piped into 'docker login --password-stdin' against the registry URI (aws_account_id.dkr.ecr.region.amazonaws.com). This is exactly the pre_build step shown in AWS's official 'Publish Docker image to Amazon ECR' CodeBuild sample buildspec.yml. The engineer omitted this login step, which is why the build fails when it tries to access the ECR repository, and option A adds precisely that missing step.","explanation_zh":"Docker CLI 不支援原生的 IAM 驗證，因此只給 CodeBuild 的 IAM service role 加上 ECR 權限並更新 docker build/push 指令是不夠的。Docker 在推送至 ECR private repository 之前，必須先使用授權權杖進行驗證。'aws ecr get-login-password' AWS CLI 指令會擷取並解碼一個有效 12 小時的權杖（使用者名稱為 'AWS'），再以管線傳給 'docker login --password-stdin' 並指定 registry URI（aws_account_id.dkr.ecr.region.amazonaws.com）。這正是 AWS 官方 'Publish Docker image to Amazon ECR' CodeBuild 範例 buildspec.yml 中 pre_build 階段的步驟。工程師遺漏了這個登入步驟，導致建置工作在存取 ECR repository 時失敗，而選項 A 正好補上這個缺少的步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A SECRETS_MANAGER environment variable references a secret stored in AWS Secrets Manager, not an IAM role ARN, and an IAM role ARN is not a valid docker login credential. This does not perform the required ECR authorization-token authentication.","why_zh":"SECRETS_MANAGER 類型的環境變數參照的是儲存在 AWS Secrets Manager 中的 secret，而非 IAM role ARN；IAM role ARN 也不是有效的 docker login 憑證，無法完成 ECR 所需的授權權杖驗證。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Making the repository public is unnecessary, less secure, contradicts the private-repository requirement, and does not address the real problem. A private repository works once Docker authenticates via get-login-password; the failure is a missing login step, not the repository's access scope.","why_zh":"將 repository 改為 public 不必要、較不安全，且違背使用 private repository 的需求，也未解決真正問題。私有 repository 只要透過 get-login-password 完成 Docker 驗證即可運作；失敗原因是缺少登入步驟，而非 repository 的存取範圍。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeBuild already runs under its IAM service role, so re-assuming that same role via the CLI provides no new credentials and still does not authenticate the Docker CLI to ECR. The repository policy is also not the gap, since the service role already has the necessary permissions; only the docker login step is missing.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 本來就以其 IAM service role 執行，透過 CLI 再次 assume 同一個 role 不會取得新憑證，也無法讓 Docker CLI 對 ECR 完成驗證。repository policy 也不是缺口，因為 service role 已具備所需權限；真正缺少的只有 docker login 步驟。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/registry_auth.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/docker-push-ecr-image.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/sample-docker-docker-hub.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":132,"question_en":"A company manually provisions IAM access for its employees. The company wants to replace the manual process with an automated process. The company has an existing Active Directory system configured with an external SAML 2.0 identity provider (IdP). The company wants employees to use their existing corporate credentials to access AWS. The groups from the existing Active Directory system must be available for permission management in AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM). A DevOps engineer has completed the initial configuration of AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) in the company’s AWS account. What should the DevOps engineer do next to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司目前为员工手动配置 IAM（身份和访问管理）权限。该公司希望用自动化流程取代手动流程。 该公司已配置了一个现有的 Active Directory 系统，并与外部 SAML 2.0 身份提供商（IdP）进行了集成。 该公司希望员工使用现有的企业凭证访问 AWS。现有 Active Directory 系统中的组必须能在 AWS 身 份和访问管理（IAM）中用于权限管理。一位 DevOps 工程师已在公司的 AWS 账户中完成了 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）的初始配置。 为了满足要求，开发运维工程师接下来应该做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an external IdP as an identity source. Configure automatic provisioning of users and groups by using the SCIM protocol.","B":"Configure AWS Directory Service as an identity source. Configure automatic provisioning of users and groups by using the SAML protocol.","C":"Configure an AD Connector as an identity source. Configure automatic provisioning of users and groups by using the SCIM protocol.","D":"Configure an external IdP as an identity source Configure automatic provisioning of users and groups by using the SAML protocol."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置外部身份提供程序作为身份源。使用 SCIM 协议配置用户和组的自动配置。","B":"将 AWS 目录服务配置为身份源。使用 SAML 协议配置用户和组的自动配置。","C":"配置 AD 连接器作为身份源。使用 SCIM 协议配置用户和组的自动配置。","D":"配置外部身份提供程序作为身份源 通过使用 SAML 协议配置用户和组的自动配置。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The company already has an existing external SAML 2.0 IdP (fronting Active Directory) and wants employees to sign in with their existing corporate credentials, with AD groups made available for permission management in IAM Identity Center. In IAM Identity Center, the correct identity source for an existing external SAML IdP (such as Okta, Microsoft Entra ID, or an AD-backed federation) is 'External identity provider'. AWS docs state that with an external IdP you connect via SAML 2.0 for authentication, but 'The SAML protocol does not provide a way to query the IdP to learn about users and groups,' so users and groups must be provisioned separately. Automatic provisioning of users and groups into IAM Identity Center is done using the SCIM v2.0 protocol, which is exactly what makes the AD groups available for permission management. Therefore the next step is option A: configure an external IdP as the identity source and configure automatic provisioning of users and groups using SCIM.","explanation_zh":"公司已擁有現有的外部 SAML 2.0 IdP（前端銜接 Active Directory），希望員工以既有企業憑證登入，並讓 AD 群組可在 IAM Identity Center 中用於權限管理。在 IAM Identity Center 中，對於既有的外部 SAML IdP（例如 Okta、Microsoft Entra ID 或以 AD 為後端的聯合驗證），正確的身分來源是 External identity provider。AWS 文件指出，使用外部 IdP 時透過 SAML 2.0 進行身分驗證，但「SAML 通訊協定不提供向 IdP 查詢使用者與群組的方法」，因此必須另行佈建使用者與群組。將使用者與群組自動佈建（同步）到 IAM Identity Center 是透過 SCIM v2.0 通訊協定完成，這正是讓 AD 群組可用於權限管理的機制。因此下一步是選項 A：將 external IdP 設定為身分來源，並使用 SCIM 設定使用者與群組的自動佈建。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The company uses an existing external SAML 2.0 IdP, not AWS Directory Service, so AWS Directory Service is the wrong identity source. Also, SAML is an authentication protocol and cannot provision users/groups; provisioning into IAM Identity Center uses SCIM.","why_zh":"公司使用的是現有的外部 SAML 2.0 IdP，而非 AWS Directory Service，因此身分來源選錯。此外，SAML 是身分驗證通訊協定，無法佈建使用者/群組；佈建到 IAM Identity Center 須使用 SCIM。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AD Connector is for connecting a self-managed Active Directory under the 'Active Directory' identity source, but the company explicitly wants to use its existing external SAML 2.0 IdP and corporate credentials. The AD/AD Connector identity source synchronizes via the directory connection, not via a SCIM endpoint, so the protocol pairing is also incorrect.","why_zh":"AD Connector 用於在「Active Directory」身分來源下連接自管的 Active Directory，但公司明確希望使用其現有的外部 SAML 2.0 IdP 與企業憑證。AD/AD Connector 身分來源是透過目錄連線同步，而非透過 SCIM 端點，因此通訊協定搭配也不正確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"External IdP is the correct identity source, but SAML cannot provision users and groups. AWS docs explicitly state 'The SAML protocol does not provide a way to query the IdP to learn about users and groups,' so automatic provisioning of users/groups must use SCIM, not SAML.","why_zh":"External IdP 是正確的身分來源，但 SAML 無法佈建使用者與群組。AWS 文件明確指出「SAML 通訊協定不提供向 IdP 查詢使用者與群組的方法」，因此使用者/群組的自動佈建必須使用 SCIM，而非 SAML。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-identity-source-idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/provision-automatically.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/scim-profile-saml.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":133,"question_en":"A company is using AWS to run digital workloads. Each application team in the company has its own AWS account for application hosting. The accounts are consolidated in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company wants to enforce security standards across the entire organization. To avoid noncompliance because of security misconfiguration, the company has enforced the use of AWS CloudFormation. A production support team can modify resources in the production environment by using the AWS Management Console to troubleshoot and resolve application-related issues. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution to identify in near real time any AWS service misconfiguration that results in noncompliance. The solution must automatically remediate the issue within 15 minutes of identification. The solution also must track noncompliant resources and events in a centralized dashboard with accurate timestamps. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS 运行数字工作负载。该公司内的每个应用程序团队都有自己的 AWS 账户用于应 用程序托管。这些账户在 AWS 组织中进行了整合。 该公司希望在整个组织内推行安全标准。为避免因安全配置不当而导致的不合规情况，公司强制使用 AWS CloudFormation。生产支持团队可以通过使用 AWS 管理控制台来修改生产环境中的资源，以解决 与应用程序相关的故障并进行修复。 DevOps 工程师必须实施一种解决方案，以便近乎实时地识别出任何导致不合规的 AWS 服务配置错误。 该解决方案必须在识别出问题后的 15 分钟内自动修复该问题。此外，该解决方案还必须在一个集中的仪 表板中跟踪不合规的资源和事件，并附上准确的时间戳。 哪种解决方案 哪种方案能以最低的开发成本满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use CloudFormation drift detection to identify noncompliant resources. Use drift detection events from CloudFormation to invoke an AWS Lambda function for remediation. Configure the Lambda function to publish logs to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Configure an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard to use the log group for tracking.","B":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail in the AWS accounts. Analyze CloudTrail logs by using Amazon Athena to identify noncompliant resources. Use AWS Step Functions to track query results on Athena for drift detection and to invoke an AWS Lambda function for remediation. For tracking, set up an Amazon QuickSight dashboard that uses Athena as the data source.","C":"Turn on the configuration recorder in AWS Config in all the AWS accounts to identify noncompliant resources. Enable AWS Security Hub with the --no-enable-default-standards option in all the AWS accounts. Set up AWS Config managed rules and custom rules. Set up automatic remediation by using AWS Config conformance packs. For tracking, set up a dashboard on Security Hub in a designated Security Hub administrator account.","D":"Turn on AWS CloudTrail in the AWS accounts. Analyze CloudTrail logs by using Amazon CloudWatch Logs to identify noncompliant resources. Use CloudWatch Logs filters for drift detection. Use Amazon EventBridge to invoke the Lambda function for remediation. Stream filtered CloudWatch logs to Amazon OpenSearch Service. Set up a dashboard on OpenSearch Service for tracking."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 CloudFormation 漂移检测来识别不合规的资源。使用 CloudFormation 的漂移检测事件来调用 AWS Lambda 函数进行修复。配置 Lambda 函数将日志发布到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。配 置 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板以使用该日志组进行跟踪。","B":"在 AWS 账户中启用 AWS CloudTrail。使用 Amazon Athena 分析 CloudTrail 日志以识别不符合规定 的资源。使用 AWS Step Functions 跟踪 Athena 上的查询结果以进行漂移检测，并调用 AWS Lambda 函数进行修复。为跟踪目的，设置一个使用 Athena 作为数据源的 Amazon QuickSight 仪 表板。","C":"在所有 AWS 账户中开启 AWS Config 中的配置记录器以识别不合规资源。在所有 AWS 账户中使用 -- no-enable-default-standards 选项启用 AWS Security Hub。设置 AWS Config 管理规则和自定义规则。 通过使用 AWS Config 合规性包设置自动修复。为跟踪目的，在指定的 Security Hub 管理员账户中设 置 Security Hub 仪表板。","D":"在 AWS 账户中启用 AWS CloudTrail。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 分析 CloudTrail 日志以识别不合 规的资源。使用 CloudWatch Logs 过滤器进行漂移检测。使用 Amazon EventBridge 调用 Lambda 函 数进行修复。将过滤后的 CloudWatch 日志流式传输到 Amazon OpenSearch Service。在 OpenSearch Service 上设置仪表板以进行跟踪。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config's configuration recorder continuously records configuration changes to resources (including manual console changes made by the production support team) and evaluates them against Config rules in near real time, satisfying the near-real-time misconfiguration detection requirement. AWS Config conformance packs are a single deployable entity that bundles Config managed and custom rules together with remediation actions, and can be deployed across an organization in AWS Organizations; remediation runs automatically via AWS Systems Manager Automation documents, which can complete well within the 15-minute window. AWS Config immediately sends its rule evaluations to AWS Security Hub, which transforms them into findings and aggregates them across all accounts into a centralized dashboard in a delegated Security Hub administrator account with accurate ASFF timestamps. Because every component is a managed service that requires only configuration (no custom detection pipelines, orchestration, or dashboard code), this meets all requirements with the LEAST development overhead. The other options require building custom detection logic, orchestration, Lambda remediation code, and custom dashboards.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 的 configuration recorder 會持續記錄資源的組態變更（包含 production support 團隊透過 console 手動所做的變更），並近乎即時地依據 Config rules 進行評估，符合「近乎即時偵測錯誤組態」的需求。AWS Config conformance packs 是一個可單一部署的實體，把 Config managed 與 custom rules 連同 remediation actions 綁在一起，並可跨 AWS Organizations 整個組織部署；remediation 透過 AWS Systems Manager Automation documents 自動執行，可在 15 分鐘內完成。AWS Config 會立即把其 rule evaluations 送到 AWS Security Hub，由 Security Hub 轉換成 findings，並在指定的 Security Hub administrator account 中跨所有帳號彙整為集中式儀表板，帶有正確的 ASFF 時間戳記。由於每個元件都是只需設定的 managed service（不需自建偵測流程、編排或儀表板程式碼），因此以最少的開發負擔滿足所有需求。其他選項都需要自建偵測邏輯、編排、Lambda remediation 程式碼以及自訂儀表板。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation drift detection is an on-demand operation you must explicitly initiate (console/CLI/API); it is not continuous or near real time, and there is no native 'drift detection event' emitted automatically when a resource changes. Making it near real time would require building a custom EventBridge scheduler plus Lambda to repeatedly call DetectStackDrift, and it only covers resources managed within CloudFormation stacks (unsupported types are marked NOT_CHECKED), not arbitrary service misconfigurations. The Lambda remediation plus log-based CloudWatch dashboard further increase development overhead.","why_zh":"CloudFormation drift detection 是必須明確發起的隨需操作（console/CLI/API），並非持續或近乎即時，也不會在資源變更時自動發出原生的「drift detection event」。要使其近乎即時就得自建 EventBridge 排程加 Lambda 反覆呼叫 DetectStackDrift，且它只涵蓋 CloudFormation stack 內管理的資源（不支援的類型會被標為 NOT_CHECKED），而非任意的服務錯誤組態。再加上 Lambda remediation 與以 log 為基礎的 CloudWatch 儀表板，開發負擔更高。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Analyzing CloudTrail logs via Athena is batch/query-based, not a near-real-time compliance evaluation. Using Athena 'for drift detection', Step Functions to track query results, Lambda for remediation, and a QuickSight dashboard requires extensive custom development (queries, state machines, remediation code, BI pipeline) and is not how AWS performs continuous compliance evaluation, so it is the opposite of LEAST development overhead.","why_zh":"透過 Athena 分析 CloudTrail logs 是批次/查詢式，並非近乎即時的合規評估。用 Athena 做 drift detection、Step Functions 追蹤查詢結果、Lambda remediation 與 QuickSight 儀表板，需要大量自訂開發（查詢、狀態機、修復程式碼、BI 管線），且非 AWS 進行持續合規評估的方式，與「最少開發負擔」相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Routing CloudTrail to CloudWatch Logs and using metric/subscription filters for 'drift detection' is custom logic that inspects API events rather than continuously evaluating resource compliance state. Combining EventBridge, a custom Lambda for remediation, streaming filtered logs to Amazon OpenSearch Service, and building an OpenSearch dashboard is the most build-heavy option and far higher development overhead than the managed Config plus Security Hub approach.","why_zh":"把 CloudTrail 送到 CloudWatch Logs 並用 metric/subscription filters 做 drift detection 是自訂邏輯，檢視的是 API 事件而非持續評估資源合規狀態。再結合 EventBridge、自訂 Lambda remediation、把過濾後的 log 串流到 Amazon OpenSearch Service 並自建 OpenSearch 儀表板，是最需自建的選項，開發負擔遠高於 managed 的 Config 加 Security Hub 方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-packs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/WhatIsConfig.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setting-up-aws-config-rules-with-console-integration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/designate-orgs-admin-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/detect-drift-stack.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":134,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The organization root has an OU that is named Environments. The Environments OU has two child OUs that are named Development and Production, respectively. The Environments OU and the child OUs have the default FullAWSAccess policy in place. A DevOps engineer plans to remove the FullAWSAccess policy from the Development OU and replace the policy with a policy that allows all actions on Amazon EC2 resources. What will be the outcome of this policy replacement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。组织根目录下有一个名为“Environments”的组 织单元（OU）。该“Environments”组织单元有两个子组织单元，分别名为“Development”和 “Production”。 环境组织单位（OU）及其子组织单位默认启用了“FullAWSAccess”策略。一位 DevOps 工程师计划从开 发组织单位移除“FullAWSAccess”策略，并用一个允许对亚马逊 EC2 资源执行所有操作的策略来替代。 这项政策的更替将会带来怎样的结果？","options_en":{"A":"All users in the Development OU will be allowed all API actions on all resources.","B":"All users in the Development OU will be allowed all API actions on EC2 resources. All other API actions will be denied.","C":"All users in the Development OU will be denied all API actions on all resources.","D":"All users in the Development OU will be denied all API actions on EC2 resources. All other API actions will be allowed."},"options_zh":{"A":"开发组织单位中的所有用户都将被允许对所有资源执行所有 API 操作。","B":"开发组织单位中的所有用户都将被允许对 EC2 资源执行所有 API 操作。其他所有 API 操作都将被拒绝。","C":"开发组织单位中的所有用户将被禁止对所有资源执行所有 API 操作。","D":"开发组织单位中的所有用户将被禁止对 EC2 资源执行所有 API 操作。其他所有 API 操作将被允许。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Service control policies (SCPs) use a deny-by-default allowlist model. AWS docs state that for a permission to be allowed for an account, there must be an explicit Allow statement at every level in the direct path from the root through each OU down to the account; any permission not explicitly allowed at every level is denied. In this scenario the Root still has FullAWSAccess and the Environments OU still has FullAWSAccess, so both allow all actions. The Development OU's FullAWSAccess is replaced by a policy that allows only ec2:* . For EC2 actions there is an Allow at all three levels (Root, Environments, Development), so EC2 is permitted by the guardrail. For any non-EC2 action, the Development OU no longer contains an explicit Allow, so even though the parent levels allow it, it is denied by the implicit deny-by-default. The net SCP guardrail outcome is therefore: all EC2 API actions allowed and all other API actions denied, which is option B. (Note: SCPs only set the maximum permission boundary and do not themselves grant access; actual access still requires matching IAM identity-based permissions, but B is the only option that correctly describes the resulting guardrail.)","explanation_zh":"Service control policies (SCPs) 採用預設拒絕 (deny-by-default) 的允許清單模型。AWS 文件指出：要讓某帳戶獲得某項權限，必須在從 root 經過直接路徑上每個 OU 一直到該帳戶的每一個層級都有明確的 Allow 陳述式；任何未在每一層級都被明確允許的權限即被拒絕。在此情境中，Root 仍保有 FullAWSAccess、Environments OU 仍保有 FullAWSAccess，兩者皆允許所有動作。Development OU 的 FullAWSAccess 被替換成只允許 ec2:* 的政策。對於 EC2 動作，三個層級 (Root、Environments、Development) 都有 Allow，因此 EC2 在護欄 (guardrail) 內被允許。對於任何非 EC2 動作，Development OU 已不再包含明確的 Allow，即使父層級允許，也會因隱含的 deny-by-default 而被拒絕。因此 SCP 護欄的最終結果為：允許所有 EC2 API 動作、拒絕所有其他 API 動作，即選項 B。(注意：SCP 只設定權限上限，本身不授予存取權；實際存取仍需相符的 IAM 身分型權限，但 B 是唯一正確描述護欄結果的選項。)","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This would be true only if FullAWSAccess remained at the Development level. Once it is replaced with an ec2:*-only policy, non-EC2 actions lose their explicit Allow at the Development level and are denied by deny-by-default, so not all actions on all resources remain allowed.","why_zh":"只有在 Development 層仍保有 FullAWSAccess 時才成立。一旦被替換成僅允許 ec2:* 的政策，非 EC2 動作在 Development 層失去明確 Allow，會被 deny-by-default 拒絕，因此並非所有資源的所有動作都仍被允許。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"All actions would be denied only if no Allow remained at the Development level (e.g., FullAWSAccess removed with no replacement). Here the replacement policy still allows ec2:* , so EC2 actions are permitted, not everything denied.","why_zh":"只有在 Development 層完全沒有任何 Allow (例如移除 FullAWSAccess 且無替代) 時才會拒絕所有動作。此處替代政策仍允許 ec2:* ，因此 EC2 動作被允許，並非全部被拒絕。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This inverts the result. SCPs are not deny lists by default; the ec2:* Allow makes EC2 the allowed set, while everything else (lacking an explicit Allow at the Development level) is denied. EC2 is allowed and other actions are denied, the opposite of this option.","why_zh":"此選項把結果顛倒。SCP 預設不是拒絕清單；ec2:* 的 Allow 使 EC2 成為被允許的集合，而其餘動作 (在 Development 層缺少明確 Allow) 被拒絕。EC2 被允許、其他動作被拒絕，與本選項相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":135,"question_en":"A company is examining its disaster recovery capability and wants the ability to switch over its daily operations to a secondary AWS Region. The company uses AWS CodeCommit as a source control tool in the primary Region. A DevOps engineer must provide the capability for the company to develop code in the secondary Region. If the company needs to use the secondary Region, developers can add an additional remote URL to their local Git configuration. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在评估其灾难恢复能力，并希望能够在主 AWS 区域出现故障时将其日常运营切换到备用 AWS 区域。该公司在主区域使用 AWS CodeCommit 作为源代码控制工具。 DevOps 工程师必须为公司提供在辅助区域开发代码的能力。如果公司需要使用辅助区域，开发人员可以在 其本地 Git 配置中添加一个额外的远程 URL。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CodeCommit repository in the secondary Region. Create an AWS CodeBuild project to perform a Git mirror operation of the primary Region's CodeCommit repository to the secondary Region's CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes the CodeBuild project. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to merge events in the primary Region's CodeCommit repository. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket in the secondary Region. Create an AWS Fargate task to perform a Git mirror operation of the primary Region's CodeCommit repository and copy the result to the S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function that initiates the Fargate task. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to merge events in the CodeCommit repository. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function.","C":"Create an AWS CodeArtifact repository in the secondary Region. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses the primary Region’s CodeCommit repository for the source action. Create a cross- Region stage in the pipeline that packages the CodeCommit repository contents and stores the contents in the CodeArtifact repository when a pull request is merged into the CodeCommit repository.","D":"Create an AWS Cloud9 environment and a CodeCommit repository in the secondary Region. Configure the primary Region's CodeCommit repository as a remote repository in the AWS Cloud9 environment. Connect the secondary Region's CodeCommit repository to the AWS Cloud9 environment."},"options_zh":{"A":"在辅助区域创建一个 CodeCommit 存储库。创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目，用于将主区域的 CodeCommit 存储库镜像到辅助区域的 CodeCommit 存储库。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来调用 CodeBuild 项目。创 建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以响应主区域 CodeCommit 存储库中的合并事件。配置 EventBridge 规则以调用 Lambda 函数。","B":"在辅助区域创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。创建一个 AWS Fargate 任务，用于执行主区域 CodeCommit 存 储库的 Git 镜像操作，并将结果复制到 S3 存储桶。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来启动 Fargate 任务。 创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以响应 CodeCommit 存储库中的合并事件。配置 EventBridge 规 则以调用 Lambda 函数。","C":"在辅助区域创建一个 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道将主区域的 CodeCommit 存储库用作源操作。在管道中创建一个跨区域阶段，当 CodeCommit 存储库中的拉取请求 被合并时，该阶段会将 CodeCommit 存储库的内容进行打包并将其存储在 CodeArtifact 存储库中。","D":"在辅助区域创建一个 AWS Cloud9 环境和一个 CodeCommit 代码库。将主区域的 CodeCommit 代码库配置 为 AWS Cloud9 环境中的远程代码库。将辅助区域的 CodeCommit 代码库连接到 AWS Cloud9 环境。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a usable CodeCommit repository in the secondary Region, kept in sync from the primary Region, that developers can add as an additional Git remote URL during a DR failover. Option A is the only choice that delivers a real Git endpoint plus automated replication: it creates a CodeCommit repository in the secondary Region (a Git endpoint developers can clone/push/pull as documented in the CodeCommit connect/migrate guides), and uses CodeBuild to run a Git mirror operation (git clone --mirror followed by git push --mirror) to copy the primary repository into the secondary repository. CodeCommit sends events directly to EventBridge, including 'CodeCommit Pull Request State Change' and 'CodeCommit Repository State Change', so an EventBridge rule can react to merge events and invoke the Lambda function that starts the CodeBuild mirror job, keeping the secondary repository current automatically. This combines the standard Git migration/mirror pattern with CodeCommit's native EventBridge integration, satisfying every requirement in the scenario.","explanation_zh":"需求是在次要 Region 建立一個可用且持續與主要 Region 同步的 CodeCommit 儲存庫，讓開發者能在 DR 切換時將其加入為額外的 Git remote URL。選項 A 是唯一同時提供真正 Git 端點與自動化複製的方案：它在次要 Region 建立 CodeCommit 儲存庫（依官方 CodeCommit connect/migrate 文件，這是開發者可 clone/push/pull 的 Git 端點），並使用 CodeBuild 執行 Git mirror 操作（git clone --mirror 後接 git push --mirror）將主要儲存庫複製到次要儲存庫。CodeCommit 會直接將事件送至 EventBridge，包含 'CodeCommit Pull Request State Change' 與 'CodeCommit Repository State Change'，因此 EventBridge 規則可在合併事件發生時調用 Lambda 來啟動 CodeBuild mirror 工作，自動保持次要儲存庫同步。這結合了標準的 Git 遷移/mirror 模式與 CodeCommit 原生的 EventBridge 整合，滿足情境中的所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Mirrors the repository into an Amazon S3 bucket, which is object storage, not a Git remote. Developers cannot add an S3 bucket as a Git remote URL to clone, push, or pull code, so it fails the core requirement of developing code in the secondary Region.","why_zh":"將儲存庫鏡像到 Amazon S3 儲存桶，那是物件儲存而非 Git remote。開發者無法將 S3 儲存桶當作 Git remote URL 來 clone/push/pull，因此無法滿足在次要 Region 開發程式碼的核心需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS CodeArtifact is a package/artifact repository (npm, Maven, PyPI, NuGet, etc.), not a Git source-control repository. You cannot clone or push code to it as a Git remote, so developers cannot use it to develop code as a CodeCommit substitute.","why_zh":"AWS CodeArtifact 是套件/構件儲存庫（npm、Maven、PyPI、NuGet 等），並非 Git 原始碼控制儲存庫。無法以 Git remote 方式 clone 或 push 程式碼，因此開發者無法用它取代 CodeCommit 來開發程式碼。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Cloud9 environment with a manually configured remote is a one-time, single-user development setup, not automated continuous replication of merges. It does not keep the secondary-Region CodeCommit repository synchronized on each merge and does not provide the resilient, automated DR sync the scenario requires; the developers' own machines (not a single Cloud9 IDE) are what need the additional remote URL.","why_zh":"Cloud9 環境加上手動設定的 remote 只是一次性、單一使用者的開發設定，而非自動且持續的合併複製。它無法在每次合併時保持次要 Region CodeCommit 儲存庫同步，也無法提供情境所需具韌性、自動化的 DR 同步；真正需要加入額外 remote URL 的是開發者自己的機器，而非單一 Cloud9 IDE。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codecommit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/monitoring-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-migrate-repository-existing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-connect.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":136,"question_en":"A DevOps team is merging code revisions for an application that uses an Amazon RDS Multi-AZ DB cluster for its production database. The DevOps team uses continuous integration to periodically verify that the application works. The DevOps team needs to test the changes before the changes are deployed to the production database. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队正在合并一个应用程序的代码修订版本，该应用程序的生产数据库使用的是亚马逊 RDS 多可用区数据库集群。DevOps 团队使用持续集成来定期验证应用程序是否正常运行。在将更改部署到生产 数据库之前，DevOps 团队需要对这些更改进行测试。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a buildspec file in AWS CodeBuild to restore the DB cluster from a snapshot of the production database, run integration tests, and drop the restored database after verification.","B":"Deploy the application to production. Configure an audit log of data control language (DCL) operations to capture database activities to perform if verification fails.","C":"Create a snapshot of the DB cluster before deploying the application. Use the Update requires:Replacement property on the DB instance in AWS CloudFormation to deploy the application and apply the changes.","D":"Ensure that the DB cluster is a Multi-AZ deployment. Deploy the application with the updates. Fail over to the standby instance if verification fails."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS CodeBuild 中使用构建规范文件从生产数据库的快照恢复数据库集群，运行集成测试，并在 验证后删除恢复的数据库。","B":"将应用程序部署到生产环境。配置数据控制语言（DCL）操作的审计日志，以捕获验证失败时要执行的 数据库活动。","C":"在部署应用程序之前，为数据库集群创建一个快照。在 AWS CloudFormation 中使用 DB 实例的“更新 要求：替换”属性来部署应用程序并应用更改。","D":"确保数据库集群采用多可用区部署。使用更新内容部署应用程序。如果验证失败，则故障转移到备用实 例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to test the application changes BEFORE they reach the production database, with no risk to live production data. Restoring an RDS DB cluster from a snapshot of production always provisions a brand-new, isolated DB instance/cluster: the AWS docs state \"You can't restore from a DB snapshot to an existing DB instance; you create a new DB instance when you restore the snapshot.\" Running integration tests via an AWS CodeBuild buildspec against this throwaway copy validates the code against production-equivalent data, and dropping it afterward keeps cost and footprint minimal. This is the canonical CI pattern for safe pre-production database testing. The other options all apply untested changes directly to the live production cluster (B and C) or rely on Multi-AZ failover, which only provides high availability and does not isolate or roll back schema/data changes because all replicas share the same data via semisynchronous replication (D).","explanation_zh":"需求是在變更觸及正式資料庫之前先進行測試，且不能對線上正式資料造成任何風險。從正式環境的快照 (snapshot) 還原 RDS DB cluster 一定會佈建一個全新、隔離的 DB instance/cluster：AWS 文件明確指出「You can't restore from a DB snapshot to an existing DB instance; you create a new DB instance when you restore the snapshot.」透過 AWS CodeBuild buildspec 對這個可丟棄的副本執行整合測試，能以與正式環境相同的資料驗證程式碼，測試後再刪除可將成本與資源佔用降到最低。這是 CI 流程中安全進行上線前資料庫測試的標準做法。其他選項不是把未經測試的變更直接套用到線上正式 cluster（B、C），就是依賴 Multi-AZ 容錯移轉，而後者只提供高可用性，無法隔離或回復結構描述/資料變更，因為所有副本透過半同步複寫共用相同資料（D）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"This deploys the untested changes directly to production first, which is exactly what the requirement forbids. A DCL (data control language) audit log only records grant/revoke permission operations; it is not a testing or rollback mechanism and provides no way to verify the application before deployment.","why_zh":"此選項直接把未經測試的變更先部署到正式環境，恰恰違反了需求。DCL（資料控制語言）稽核紀錄只記錄授權/撤銷權限的操作，並非測試或回復機制，無法在部署前驗證應用程式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Taking a snapshot before deploying only provides a rollback point; the untested changes are still applied directly to the production DB cluster. Worse, Update requires:Replacement on the DB instance forces CloudFormation to delete and recreate the production instance, causing data loss and downtime instead of isolated testing.","why_zh":"在部署前先建立快照只是提供回復點，變更仍直接套用到正式 DB cluster。更糟的是，對 DB instance 使用 Update requires:Replacement 會迫使 CloudFormation 刪除並重建正式實例，導致資料遺失與停機，而非在隔離環境中測試。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Multi-AZ DB cluster has a writer and two reader instances that share the same data via semisynchronous replication; the readers are not a separate test environment. Deploying updates writes them to all replicas, so failing over to a standby does NOT revert a bad schema or data change. Failover delivers high availability, not change isolation or rollback.","why_zh":"Multi-AZ DB cluster 由一個寫入實例與兩個讀取實例組成，透過半同步複寫共用相同資料，讀取實例並非獨立的測試環境。部署更新會寫入所有副本，因此切換到備援實例並不能回復錯誤的結構描述或資料變更。容錯移轉提供的是高可用性，而非變更隔離或回復。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_RestoreFromSnapshot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/multi-az-db-clusters-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/multi-az-db-clusters-concepts-failover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":137,"question_en":"A company manages a multi-tenant environment in its VPC and has configured Amazon GuardDuty for the corresponding AWS account. The company sends all GuardDuty findings to AWS Security Hub. Traffic from suspicious sources is generating a large number of findings. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to automatically deny traffic across the entire VPC when GuardDuty discovers a new suspicious source. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在其虚拟私有云（VPC）中管理一个多租户环境，并为相应的 AWS 账户配置了 Amazon GuardDuty。 该公司将所有 GuardDuty 发现结果发送至 AWS 安全中心。 来自可疑来源的流量正在生成大量发现结果。DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，在 GuardDuty 发现新 的可疑来源时，自动拒绝整个 VPC 的流量。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a GuardDuty threat list. Configure GuardDuty to reference the list. Create an AWS Lambda function that will update the threat list. Configure the Lambda function to run in response to new Security Hub findings that come from GuardDuty.","B":"Configure an AWS WAF web ACL that includes a custom rule group. Create an AWS Lambda function that will create a block rule in the custom rule group. Configure the Lambda function to run in response to new Security Hub findings that come from GuardDuty.","C":"Configure a firewall in AWS Network Firewall. Create an AWS Lambda function that will create a Drop action rule in the firewall policy. Configure the Lambda function to run in response to new Security Hub findings that come from GuardDuty.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that will create a GuardDuty suppression rule. Configure the Lambda function to run in response to new Security Hub findings that come from GuardDuty."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 GuardDuty 威胁列表。配置 GuardDuty 引用该列表。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来更新威 胁列表。配置该 Lambda 函数在收到来自 GuardDuty 的新 Security Hub 找到结果时运行。","B":"配置一个包含自定义规则组的 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表 （web ACL）。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数， 该函数将在自定义规则组中创建一条阻止规则。配置该 Lambda 函数，使其在收到来自 GuardDuty 的新 Security Hub 找到的漏洞时运行。","C":"在 AWS Network Firewall 中配置防火墙。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会在防火墙策略中创建一 条丢弃操作规则。将 Lambda 函数配置为在收到来自 GuardDuty 的新 Security Hub 找到的漏洞时运行。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于创建 GuardDuty 抑制规则。将该 Lambda 函数配置为在收到来自 GuardDuty 的新 Security Hub 找到结果时运行。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is to actively DENY (block) network traffic across the ENTIRE VPC when GuardDuty discovers a new suspicious source. AWS Network Firewall is a stateful, managed network firewall for a VPC that filters traffic at the VPC perimeter (internet gateway, NAT gateway, VPN, Direct Connect). With route tables sending VPC traffic through the firewall endpoints, a Drop-action rule in the firewall policy actively blocks the suspicious source's traffic for the whole VPC. A Lambda function, triggered via EventBridge on new GuardDuty-sourced Security Hub findings, can programmatically add that Drop rule, satisfying both the 'deny traffic' and 'entire VPC' requirements. Network Firewall is the only option here that provides a network-level (L3/L4) enforcement primitive covering all VPC traffic; the dump's suggested answer and the first analyst's verdict of C are correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是當 GuardDuty 偵測到新的可疑來源時，主動在整個 VPC 範圍內拒絕（封鎖）網路流量。AWS Network Firewall 是 VPC 的具狀態（stateful）受管網路防火牆，可在 VPC 邊界（internet gateway、NAT gateway、VPN、Direct Connect）過濾流量。透過路由表將 VPC 流量導向 firewall endpoint，再於 firewall policy 中加入 Drop action 規則，即可在整個 VPC 範圍內主動封鎖該可疑來源的流量。由 EventBridge 在收到來自 GuardDuty 的新 Security Hub findings 時觸發 Lambda function，即可自動新增該 Drop 規則，同時滿足『拒絕流量』與『整個 VPC』兩項要求。Network Firewall 是本題唯一提供涵蓋全部 VPC 流量之網路層（L3/L4）強制執行機制的選項；dump 建議答案與第一位分析師的判定 C 皆正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A GuardDuty threat (entity/IP) list does NOT block traffic. Per AWS docs, when GuardDuty detects activity involving entries on a threat list it only GENERATES findings to alert you. It is a detection enhancement, not an enforcement control, so it would actually create MORE findings rather than deny the traffic.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 威脅清單（entity/IP list）並不會封鎖流量。依 AWS 文件，當 GuardDuty 偵測到涉及威脅清單項目的活動時，僅會『產生 findings』來提醒你。這是偵測強化功能，並非執行/阻擋控制，反而會產生更多 findings，無法拒絕流量。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS WAF only protects specific Layer 7, HTTP-facing resources (CloudFront, Application Load Balancer, API Gateway, AppSync, Cognito, App Runner, Verified Access, Amplify) via web ACL association and inspects HTTP(S) requests. It cannot deny arbitrary network traffic 'across the entire VPC' and does not sit on general VPC network paths.","why_zh":"AWS WAF 僅能透過 web ACL 關聯保護特定的第七層、面向 HTTP 的資源（CloudFront、Application Load Balancer、API Gateway、AppSync、Cognito、App Runner、Verified Access、Amplify），並檢查 HTTP(S) 請求。它無法拒絕『整個 VPC』的一般網路流量，也不位於 VPC 一般網路路徑上。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A GuardDuty suppression rule only auto-ARCHIVES matching findings to reduce noise/false positives; suppressed findings are not even sent to Security Hub, S3, Detective, or EventBridge. It only hides findings and performs no traffic blocking, directly contradicting the goal of denying traffic.","why_zh":"GuardDuty suppression rule 只會自動將符合條件的新 findings『封存（archive）』以降低雜訊／誤判；被抑制的 findings 甚至不會送往 Security Hub、S3、Detective 或 EventBridge。它僅隱藏 findings，完全不執行任何流量封鎖，與『拒絕流量』的目標背道而馳。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/network-firewall/latest/developerguide/what-is-aws-network-firewall.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/network-firewall/latest/developerguide/firewall-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/network-firewall/latest/developerguide/suricata-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/findings_suppression-rule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_upload-lists.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/how-aws-waf-works-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":138,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Secrets Manager to store a set of sensitive API keys that an AWS Lambda function uses. When the Lambda function is invoked the Lambda function retrieves the API keys and makes an API call to an external service. The Secrets Manager secret is encrypted with the default AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key. A DevOps engineer needs to update the infrastructure to ensure that only the Lambda function’s execution role can access the values in Secrets Manager. The solution must apply the principle of least privilege. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Secrets Manager 来存储一组敏感的 API 密钥，这些密钥由一个 AWS Lambda 函数使用。 当调用 Lambda 函数时，该函数会检索这些 API 密钥，并向外部服务发起 API 调用。Secrets Manager 密钥使 用默认的 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥进行加密。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要更新基础设施，以确保只有 Lambda 函数的执行角色能够访问 Secrets Manager 中的 值。解决方案必须遵循最小权限原则。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the default KMS key for Secrets Manager to allow only the Lambda function’s execution role to decrypt","B":"Create a KMS customer managed key that trusts Secrets Manager and allows the Lambda function's execution role to decrypt. Update Secrets Manager to use the new customer managed key","C":"Create a KMS customer managed key that trusts Secrets Manager and allows the account's root principal to decrypt. Update Secrets Manager to use the new customer managed key","D":"Ensure that the Lambda function’s execution role has the KMS permissions scoped on the resource level. Configure the permissions so that the KMS key can encrypt the Secrets Manager secret","E":"Remove all KMS permissions from the Lambda function’s execution role"},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Secrets Manager 的默认 KMS 密钥更新为仅允许 Lambda 函数的执行角色进行解密","B":"创建一个受信任 Secrets Manager 并允许 Lambda 函数执行角色进行解密的 KMS 客户管理密钥。更新 Secrets Manager 以使用新的客户管理密钥。","C":"创建一个信任 Secrets Manager 并允许账户根用户进行解密的 KMS 客户管理密钥。更新 Secrets Manager 以使用新的客户管理密钥。","D":"确保 Lambda 函数的执行角色在资源级别具有 KMS 权限。配置权限，以便 KMS 密钥能够加密 Secrets Manager 密钥。","E":"从 Lambda 函数的执行角色中移除所有 KMS 权限"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The secret is currently encrypted with the AWS managed key aws/secretsmanager (the default key). Restricting decryption to ONLY the Lambda execution role with least privilege requires two complementary steps because AWS KMS uses a dual-control model: 'Unless the key policy explicitly allows it, you cannot use IAM policies to allow access to a KMS key.' (1) Option B: create a customer managed KMS key whose key policy trusts Secrets Manager (kms:ViaService = secretsmanager.<region>.amazonaws.com) and grants kms:Decrypt only to the Lambda execution role, then re-point the secret to this CMK. This is mandatory because, per AWS docs, the AWS managed key policy 'is established by the service. You cannot change the key policy'; its default policy grants kms:Encrypt/kms:Decrypt to Principal AWS '*' for any account principal that calls via Secrets Manager, so it can never be narrowed to a single role. Only a customer managed key gives the customer exclusive control of the key policy. (2) Option D: the Lambda execution role must also have the matching KMS permissions scoped at the resource level (the specific CMK ARN) so it can actually use the key when GetSecretValue triggers the KMS Decrypt of the data key. Both the key policy (B) and the principal's resource-scoped IAM permission (D) are required, and scoping to the key ARN enforces least privilege. This matches the dump's suggested answer.","explanation_zh":"目前該 secret 是使用 AWS 受管金鑰 aws/secretsmanager（預設金鑰）加密。要在最小權限下將解密限制為「只有」該 Lambda 執行角色，需要兩個互補步驟，因為 AWS KMS 採雙重控管模型：『Unless the key policy explicitly allows it, you cannot use IAM policies to allow access to a KMS key.』(1) 選項 B：建立一把 customer managed KMS key，其 key policy 信任 Secrets Manager（kms:ViaService = secretsmanager.<region>.amazonaws.com），且僅授予 Lambda 執行角色 kms:Decrypt，再將 secret 改用這把 CMK。此為必要，因為依 AWS 文件，AWS 受管金鑰政策『is established by the service. You cannot change the key policy』；其預設政策對 Principal AWS '*'（任何透過 Secrets Manager 呼叫的帳戶主體）授予 kms:Encrypt/kms:Decrypt，無法縮小到單一角色。只有 customer managed key 才能讓客戶完全掌控 key policy。(2) 選項 D：Lambda 執行角色也必須具備對應的 KMS 權限，並把範圍鎖定在資源層級（特定 CMK ARN），這樣 GetSecretValue 觸發 KMS 對 data key 進行 Decrypt 時才能實際使用該金鑰。key policy（B）與主體之資源範圍 IAM 權限（D）兩者皆需，並以金鑰 ARN 範圍落實最小權限。此結論與題庫建議答案一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Impossible. The default key for Secrets Manager is the AWS managed key aws/secretsmanager; its key policy is established by the service and cannot be modified by the customer ('You cannot change the key policy'). It cannot be edited to allow only the Lambda role, so it can never be narrowed for least privilege.","why_zh":"不可行。Secrets Manager 的預設金鑰是 AWS 受管金鑰 aws/secretsmanager，其 key policy 由服務設定且客戶無法修改（『You cannot change the key policy』），無法改成只允許 Lambda 角色，因此無法縮小達成最小權限。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Violates least privilege. Granting kms:Decrypt to the account root principal delegates control to IAM for the entire account, so any principal granted KMS access via an IAM policy could decrypt the secret, not just the Lambda role.","why_zh":"違反最小權限。將 kms:Decrypt 授予帳戶 root 主體等於把控制權交給整個帳戶的 IAM，任何透過 IAM 政策取得 KMS 權限的主體都能解密，而不只是 Lambda 角色。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Breaks functionality. Removing all KMS permissions from the Lambda role prevents the role from decrypting the data key, so GetSecretValue fails with AccessDenied and the function cannot retrieve the API keys. This is the opposite of granting the scoped permission required in Option D.","why_zh":"會破壞功能。移除 Lambda 角色的所有 KMS 權限後，角色無法解密 data key，GetSecretValue 會 AccessDenied 失敗，函式將無法取得 API keys。這與選項 D 所需的資源範圍授權完全相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/security-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/key-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/auth-and-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kms/latest/developerguide/least-privilege.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":139,"question_en":"A company's DevOps engineer is creating an AWS Lambda function to process notifications from an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. The Lambda function will process the notification messages and will write the contents of the notification messages to an Amazon RDS Multi-AZ DB instance. During testing, a database administrator accidentally shut down the DB instance. While the database was down the company lost several of the SNS notification messages that were delivered during that time. The DevOps engineer needs to prevent the loss of notification messages in the future. Which solutions will meet this requirement? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 工程师正在创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于处理来自 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题的通知。该 Lambda 函数将处理通知消息，并将通知消息的内容写入 Amazon RDS 多可用区数据库实例。 在测试期间，一名数据库管理员意外关闭了数据库实例。在数据库停机期间，公司丢失了当时送达的几条 SNS 通知消息。 DevOps 工程师需要防止未来出现通知消息丢失的情况。 哪些解决方案能满足这一要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Replace the RDS Multi-AZ DB instance with an Amazon DynamoDB table.","B":"Configure an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as a destination of the Lambda function.","C":"Configure an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) dead-letter queue for the SNS topic.","D":"Subscribe an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue to the SNS topic. Configure the Lambda function to process messages from the SQS queue.","E":"Replace the SNS topic with an Amazon EventBridge event bus. Configure an EventBridge rule on the new event bus to invoke the Lambda function for each event."},"options_zh":{"A":"用 Amazon DynamoDB 表替换 RDS 多可用区数据库实例。","B":"将 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列配置为 Lambda 函数的目标。","C":"为 SNS 主题配置一个 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）死信队列。","D":"将 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列订阅到 SNS 主题。配置 Lambda 函数以处理来自 SQS 队列的消息。","E":"将 SNS 主题替换为 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。在新的事件总线上配置 EventBridge 规则，以便为每 个事件调用 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SNS delivered each notification to a Lambda function as an asynchronous invocation. While RDS was down, the function kept failing; once the SNS subscription retries and Lambda's own async retries exhausted with nowhere to capture the failures, the messages were discarded. The SNS docs state plainly that when retries are exhausted 'Amazon SNS discards the message - unless a dead-letter queue is attached to the subscription,' and the Lambda async docs state 'When an event expires or fails all processing attempts, Lambda discards it.' (C) Attaching an Amazon SQS dead-letter queue to the SNS subscription holds messages that cannot be delivered to the endpoint after retries so they are retained for reprocessing instead of discarded - the canonical SNS durability fix. (D) Subscribing an SQS queue to the SNS topic and having Lambda poll that queue inserts a durable buffer (SQS retains messages, up to 14 days); if Lambda fails because RDS is down, the SQS event source mapping leaves the messages in the queue (they become visible again after the visibility timeout) until they are processed successfully, preventing loss. Both directly satisfy 'prevent the loss of notification messages.'","explanation_zh":"SNS 將每筆通知以非同步呼叫的方式送至 Lambda。在 RDS 停機期間，function 持續失敗；當 SNS 訂閱重試與 Lambda 自身的非同步重試都耗盡且沒有任何地方可保存失敗訊息時，訊息就被丟棄。SNS 官方文件明確指出，重試耗盡後『Amazon SNS 會丟棄訊息 — 除非該訂閱附加了 dead-letter queue』，而 Lambda 非同步文件也指出『當事件過期或所有處理嘗試都失敗時，Lambda 會丟棄它』。(C) 在 SNS 訂閱上附加 Amazon SQS dead-letter queue，可保留重試後仍無法投遞至端點的訊息以供重新處理，而非被丟棄，這是 SNS 持久性的標準修正方式。(D) 將 SQS queue 訂閱至 SNS topic，並讓 Lambda 輪詢該 queue，等於插入一個持久緩衝（SQS 訊息最長保留 14 天）；若 Lambda 因 RDS 停機而失敗，SQS event source mapping 會將訊息留在 queue 中（在 visibility timeout 後重新可見），直到成功處理為止，因而避免遺失。兩者都能直接滿足『避免通知訊息遺失』的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Replacing RDS with DynamoDB only swaps the data store; it does nothing to make the SNS->Lambda delivery durable. If the target store were unavailable or throttling, messages would still be discarded after SNS/Lambda retries exhaust, so loss is not prevented.","why_zh":"把 RDS 換成 DynamoDB 只是更換資料庫，並未讓 SNS->Lambda 的投遞變得持久；若目標資料庫不可用或受限流，訊息在 SNS/Lambda 重試耗盡後仍會被丟棄，因此無法防止遺失。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A Lambda 'destination' is an async on-success/on-failure record target that only fires after Lambda's own retries are exhausted, and the option does not even specify on-failure. It protects neither the in-flight SNS delivery nor the data, and is the weaker, non-canonical choice versus an SNS subscription dead-letter queue (C). The documented AWS pattern for SNS notification durability is the subscription DLQ, not a Lambda destination.","why_zh":"Lambda 的『destination』是非同步 on-success/on-failure 的記錄目標，只會在 Lambda 自身重試耗盡後觸發，且此選項甚至未指明 on-failure。它既無法保護進行中的 SNS 投遞，也無法保護資料，相較於 SNS 訂閱 dead-letter queue(C) 較弱且非標準做法。AWS 文件針對 SNS 通知持久性建議的是訂閱層級 DLQ，而非 Lambda destination。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Replacing SNS with an EventBridge bus that invokes Lambda is still an asynchronous invocation with the same retry-then-discard behavior. EventBridge expires events after their maximum age (24h by default) and, with no DLQ configured on the rule/target, still loses them. As worded the option adds no DLQ or buffer, so it does not inherently prevent loss.","why_zh":"將 SNS 換成 EventBridge event bus 再呼叫 Lambda，仍是非同步呼叫，具有相同的『重試後丟棄』行為；EventBridge 在事件超過最大保留時間（預設 24 小時）後會過期，且若 rule/target 未設定 DLQ，事件仍會遺失。依此選項的敘述並未加入任何 DLQ 或緩衝，因此本質上無法防止遺失。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-dead-letter-queues.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-configure-dead-letter-queue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/subscribe-sqs-queue-to-sns-topic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-error-handling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-async-retain-records.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":140,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The company uses an AWS CodePipeline pipeline to deploy the application into multiple AWS Regions. The pipeline is configured with a stage for each Region. Each stage contains an AWS CloudFormation action for each Region. When the pipeline deploys the application to a Region, the company wants to confirm that the application is in a healthy state before the pipeline moves on to the next Region. Amazon Route 53 record sets are configured for the application in each Region. A DevOps engineer creates a Route 53 health check that is based on an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for each Region where the application is deployed. What should the DevOps engineer do next to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的应用程序。该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 管道将应用程序部署 到多个 AWS 区域。该管道针对每个区域都配置了一个阶段。每个阶段都包含针对每个区域的 AWS CloudFormation 操作。 当管道将应用程序部署到某个区域时，公司希望在管道继续推进到下一个区域之前确认应用程序处于健康 状态。在每个区域都为应用程序配置了 Amazon Route 53 记录集。一位 DevOps 工程师为应用程序部署的每 个区域创建了一个基于 Amazon CloudWatch 警报的 Route 53 健康检查。 为了满足要求，开发运维工程师接下来应该做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Step Functions workflow to check the state of the CloudWatch alarm. Configure the Step Functions workflow to exit with an error if the alarm is in the ALARM state. Create a new stage in the pipeline between each Region deployment stage. In each new stage, include an action to invoke the Step Functions workflow.","B":"Configure an AWS CodeDeploy application to deploy a CloudFormation template with automatic rollback. Configure the CloudWatch alarm as the instance health check for the CodeDeploy application. Remove the CloudFormation actions from the pipeline. Create a CodeDeploy action in the pipeline stage for each Region.","C":"Create a new pipeline stage for each Region where the application is deployed. Configure a CloudWatch alarm action for the new stage to check the state of the CloudWatch alarm and to exit with an error if the alarm is in the ALARM state","D":"Configure the CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances to report the application status to the Route 53 health check. Create a new pipeline stage for each Region where the application is deployed. Configure a CloudWatch alarm action to exit with an error if the CloudWatch alarm is in the ALARM state."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Step Functions 工作流来检查 CloudWatch 警报的状态。将 Step Functions 工作流配置为在 警报处于 ALARM 状态时以错误退出。在每个区域部署阶段之间创建一个新的阶段。在每个新阶段中， 包含一个调用 Step Functions 工作流的操作。","B":"配置一个 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序以部署带有自动回滚功能的 CloudFormation 模板。将 CloudWatch 警 报配置为 CodeDeploy 应用程序的实例健康检查。从管道中移除 CloudFormation 操作。在每个区域的管 道阶段中创建一个 CodeDeploy 操作。","C":"为应用部署的每个区域创建一个新的流水线阶段。为新阶段配置 CloudWatch 警报操作，以检查 CloudWatch 警报的状态，如果警报处于“ALARM”状态，则退出并报错。","D":"在 EC2 实例上配置 CloudWatch 代理，将应用程序状态报告给 Route 53 健康检查。为应用程序部署的每 个区域创建一个新的流水线阶段。配置 CloudWatch 警报操作，如果 CloudWatch 警报处于 ALARM 状 态，则退出并报错。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The Step Functions invoke action is a real, documented CodePipeline action (Category: Invoke, Owner: AWS, Provider: StepFunctions). A state machine can call the CloudWatch DescribeAlarms API to check the Route 53-backed health-check alarm and use a Fail state, which causes the invoke action to fail. When a CodePipeline action fails, the stage fails and the pipeline stops without advancing to the next Region stage. By inserting a new stage between each Region's deployment stage that invokes this Step Functions workflow, the pipeline confirms the application is healthy in one Region before deploying to the next. This integrates cleanly with the existing CloudFormation deploy actions and the existing CloudWatch alarm / Route 53 health check without re-architecting the pipeline. Options C and D rely on a non-existent 'CloudWatch alarm action' type; the only valid action categories are Source, Build, Test, Deploy, Approval, and Invoke, and CloudWatchAlarm exists only as a Rule for stage conditions, not as a standalone action you place to 'exit with an error.'","explanation_zh":"Step Functions invoke action 是 CodePipeline 真實存在且有官方文件的動作（Category: Invoke、Owner: AWS、Provider: StepFunctions）。state machine 可呼叫 CloudWatch DescribeAlarms API 檢查由 Route 53 健康檢查支援的 alarm 狀態，並透過 Fail state 使該 invoke action 失敗。當 CodePipeline 的 action 失敗時，該 stage 失敗且 pipeline 會停止，不會前進到下一個 Region stage。在每個 Region 部署 stage 之間插入一個呼叫此 Step Functions workflow 的新 stage，pipeline 便能在前往下一個 Region 前先確認當前 Region 應用程式健康。此做法可與既有的 CloudFormation 部署動作以及既有的 CloudWatch alarm / Route 53 健康檢查無縫整合，無須重構 pipeline。選項 C 與 D 依賴並不存在的『CloudWatch alarm action』動作類型；唯一有效的 action 類別為 Source、Build、Test、Deploy、Approval 與 Invoke，而 CloudWatchAlarm 僅以 stage conditions 的 Rule 形式存在，並非可放入 stage 中『以錯誤結束』的獨立 action。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeDeploy deploys applications to EC2/Lambda/ECS compute, not CloudFormation templates; you cannot have a CodeDeploy application 'deploy a CloudFormation template.' It also misuses 'instance health check' (CodeDeploy deployment health is governed by deployment configurations, not by attaching a CloudWatch alarm as an instance health check) and removing the CloudFormation actions needlessly re-architects a working pipeline. CodeDeploy automatic rollback is per-deployment and does not act as a cross-Region progression gate.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 部署的是 EC2/Lambda/ECS 等運算目標，而非 CloudFormation 範本；CodeDeploy 應用程式無法『部署 CloudFormation 範本』。此選項誤用『instance health check』（CodeDeploy 的部署健康由 deployment configuration 控管，而非把 CloudWatch alarm 當成 instance health check），且移除 CloudFormation 動作會不必要地重構可運作的 pipeline。CodeDeploy 的自動回復屬單次部署層級，無法作為跨 Region 前進的閘門。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no 'CloudWatch alarm action' type in CodePipeline. The valid action categories are Source, Build, Test, Deploy, Approval, and Invoke. CloudWatchAlarm exists only as a Rule for stage conditions (Entry / On Failure / On Success), not as a standalone action you place in a stage to 'exit with an error.'","why_zh":"CodePipeline 並不存在『CloudWatch alarm action』動作類型。有效的動作類別為 Source、Build、Test、Deploy、Approval 與 Invoke。CloudWatchAlarm 僅以 stage conditions（Entry / On Failure / On Success）的 Rule 形式存在，並非可放入 stage 中『以錯誤結束』的獨立 action。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fictional 'CloudWatch alarm action' problem as C. Additionally, the CloudWatch agent reports metrics/logs to CloudWatch; it does not 'report application status to a Route 53 health check.' Route 53 health checks of this type are derived from a CloudWatch alarm, not fed by the agent.","why_zh":"與 C 相同，依賴並不存在的『CloudWatch alarm action』。此外，CloudWatch agent 是將指標/日誌回報至 CloudWatch，並非『將應用程式狀態回報給 Route 53 健康檢查』；此類 Route 53 健康檢查是依據 CloudWatch alarm，而非由 agent 餵入。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-StepFunctions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-valid-providers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/concepts-how-it-works-conditions.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":141,"question_en":"A company plans to use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor its Amazon EC2 instances. The company needs to stop EC2 instances when the average of the NetworkPacketsIn metric is less than 5 for at least 3 hours in a 12-hour time window. The company must evaluate the metric every hour. The EC2 instances must continue to run if there is missing data for the NetworkPacketsIn metric during the evaluation period. A DevOps engineer creates a CloudWatch alarm for the NetworkPacketsIn metric. The DevOps engineer configures a threshold value of 5 and an evaluation period of 1 hour. Which set of additional actions should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司计划使用亚马逊 CloudWatch 来监控其亚马逊 EC2 实例。该公司需要在 12 小时的时间窗口内， 当 NetworkPacketsIn 指标平均值连续 3 小时低于 5 时停止 EC2 实例。该公司必须每小时评估一次该指 标。如果在评估期间 NetworkPacketsIn 指标存在缺失数据，则 EC2 实例必须继续运行。 一位 DevOps 工程师为 NetworkPacketsIn 指标创建了一个 CloudWatch 警报。该 DevOps 工程师将阈值 设为 5，并将评估周期设为 1 小时。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪一系列额外行动来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Datapoints to Alarm value to be 3 out of 12. Configure the alarm to treat missing data as breaching the threshold. Add an AWS Systems Manager action to stop the instance when the alarm enters the ALARM state.","B":"Configure the Datapoints to Alarm value to be 3 out of 12. Configure the alarm to treat missing data as not breaching the threshold. Add an EC2 action to stop the instance when the alarm enters the ALARM state.","C":"Configure the Datapoints to Alarm value to be 9 out of 12. Configure the alarm to treat missing data as breaching the threshold. Add an EC2 action to stop the instance when the alarm enters the ALARM state.","D":"Configure the Datapoints to Alarm value to be 9 out of 12. Configure the alarm to treat missing data as not breaching the threshold. Add an AWS Systems Manager action to stop the instance when the alarm enters the ALARM state."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据点的告警值配置为 12 个中的 3 个。将告警配置为将缺失数据视为超出阈值。添加一个 AWS 系统管理器操作，当告警进入“告警”状态时停止实例。","B":"将数据点的告警值配置为 12 个中的 3 个。配置告警，将缺失数据视为未超出阈值。添加一个 EC2 操作，在告警进入“告警”状态时停止实例。","C":"将数据点的告警值配置为 12 中的 9。将告警配置为将缺失数据视为超出阈值。添加一个 EC2 操作， 在告警进入“告警”状态时停止实例。","D":"将数据点的告警值配置为 12 中的 9。将告警配置为将缺失数据视为未超出阈值。添加一个 AWS 系 统管理器操作，当告警进入“告警”状态时停止实例。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"With a 1-hour period, a 12-hour window equals 12 evaluation periods (N=12), and 'less than 5 for at least 3 hours' maps to 3 breaching datapoints, so Datapoints to Alarm must be 3 out of 12 (an M-of-N alarm that fires when 3 of the most recent 12 datapoints breach). This eliminates the 9-out-of-12 options C and D. The requirement that instances keep running when data is missing means missing datapoints must not drive the alarm to ALARM; treating missing data as notBreaching keeps the alarm in OK (per the CloudWatch missing-data evaluation tables, NOT BREACHING never yields ALARM from missing-only data), whereas treating it as breaching (A and C) would push the alarm to ALARM and stop the instance. Finally, only the native CloudWatch EC2 action directly stops an instance; a Systems Manager alarm action merely creates an OpsItem in OpsCenter and cannot stop an instance, eliminating A and D. Only option B combines 3-of-12 datapoints, notBreaching missing-data treatment, and an EC2 stop action. (Note: AWS actually recommends treating missing data as 'missing' for EC2 stop/terminate alarms, but that option is not offered; among the choices, notBreaching is the one that satisfies 'instances must continue to run' because the alarm goes to OK rather than ALARM.)","explanation_zh":"在 period 設為 1 小時時,12 小時時間窗等於 12 個 evaluation periods(N=12),而「低於 5 達至少 3 小時」對應 3 個違規 datapoints,因此 Datapoints to Alarm 必須是 3 out of 12(即 M-of-N 警報:最近 12 個 datapoints 中有 3 個超過門檻即觸發)。這排除了使用 9 out of 12 的選項 C 與 D。需求「資料遺失時 instance 必須繼續運行」表示遺失的 datapoints 不能把警報推向 ALARM;將 missing data 視為 notBreaching 會讓警報維持 OK 狀態(依 CloudWatch missing-data 評估表,NOT BREACHING 在僅有遺失資料時絕不會產生 ALARM),而視為 breaching(A 與 C)則會把警報推向 ALARM 並停止 instance。最後,只有原生的 CloudWatch EC2 action 能直接停止 instance;Systems Manager 警報 action 只會在 OpsCenter 建立 OpsItem,無法停止 instance,故排除 A 與 D。只有選項 B 同時具備 3-of-12 datapoints、notBreaching 的遺失資料處理,以及 EC2 stop action。(補充:AWS 實際上建議 EC2 stop/terminate 警報將遺失資料視為 'missing',但題目未提供此選項;在現有選項中,notBreaching 是能滿足『instance 必須繼續運行』的選擇,因為警報會進入 OK 而非 ALARM。)","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Treating missing data as breaching would push the alarm to ALARM when NetworkPacketsIn data is missing, stopping the instance and violating the 'must continue to run on missing data' requirement; also a Systems Manager alarm action only creates an OpsItem, it cannot stop the instance.","why_zh":"將遺失資料視為 breaching 會在 NetworkPacketsIn 資料遺失時把警報推向 ALARM 並停止 instance,違反『資料遺失時必須繼續運行』的要求;且 Systems Manager 警報 action 只會建立 OpsItem,無法停止 instance。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"9 out of 12 would require 9 breaching hours, not the required 3 hours; and treating missing data as breaching would stop the instance on missing data, violating the keep-running requirement.","why_zh":"9 out of 12 需要 9 小時違規,而非要求的 3 小時;且將遺失資料視為 breaching 會在資料遺失時停止 instance,違反保持運行的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"9 out of 12 requires 9 breaching hours instead of 3, and a Systems Manager alarm action only creates an OpsItem in OpsCenter rather than stopping the EC2 instance.","why_zh":"9 out of 12 需要 9 小時違規而非 3 小時,且 Systems Manager 警報 action 只會在 OpsCenter 建立 OpsItem,無法停止 EC2 instance。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/alarms-and-missing-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/UsingAlarmActions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/AlarmThatSendsEmail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/OpsCenter-creating-or-editing-existing-alarm-console.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":142,"question_en":"A company manages 500 AWS accounts that are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company discovers many unattached Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes in all the accounts. The company wants to automatically tag the unattached EBS volumes for investigation. A DevOps engineer needs to deploy an AWS Lambda function to all the AWS accounts. The Lambda function must run every 30 minutes to tag all the EBS volumes that have been unattached for a period of 7 days or more. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient manner?","question_zh":"一家公司管理着 AWS 组织中的 500 个 AWS 账户。该公司发现所有账户中存在大量未挂载的 Amazon Elastic Block Store（Amazon EBS）卷。该公司希望自动为这些未挂载的 EBS 卷添加标签以便进行调 查。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要将一个 AWS Lambda 函数部署到所有 AWS 账户中。该 Lambda 函数必须每 30 分钟运行一次，为所有已断开连接 7 天或更长时间的 EBS 卷添加标签。 哪种解决方案能在操作效率最高的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a delegated administrator account for the organization. Create an AWS CloudFormation template that contains the Lambda function. Use CloudFormation StackSets to deploy the CloudFormation template from the delegated administrator account to all the member accounts in the organization. Create an Amazon EventBridge event bus in the delegated administrator account to invoke the Lambda function in each member account every 30 minutes.","B":"Create a cross-account IAM role in the organization's member accounts. Attach the AWSLambda_FullAccess policy and the AWSCloudFormationFullAccess policy to the role. Create an AWS CloudFormation template that contains the Lambda function and an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to invoke the Lambda function every 30 minutes. Create a custom script in the organization’s management account that assumes the role and deploys the CloudFormation template to the member accounts.","C":"Configure a delegated administrator account for the organization. Create an AWS CloudFormation template that contains the Lambda function and an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to invoke the Lambda function every 30 minutes. Use CloudFormation StackSets to deploy the CloudFormation template from the delegated administrator account to all the member accounts in the organization","D":"Create a cross-account IAM role in the organization's member accounts. Attach the AmazonS3FullAccess policy and the AWSCodeDeployDeployerAccess policy to the role. Use AWS CodeDeploy to assume the role to deploy the Lambda function from the organization's management account. Configure an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule in the member accounts to invoke the Lambda function every 30 minutes."},"options_zh":{"A":"为组织配置一个委托管理员账户。创建一个包含 Lambda 函数的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。使用 CloudFormation StackSets 从委托管理员账户将 CloudFormation 模板部署到组织中的所有成员账 户。在委托管理员账户中创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线，每 30 分钟调用每个成员账户 中的 Lambda 函数。","B":"在组织成员账户中创建一个跨账户 IAM 角色。将 AWSLambda_FullAccess 策略和 AWSCloudFormationFullAccess 策略附加到该角色。创建一个包含 Lambda 函数和每 30 分钟通过 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则调用 Lambda 函数的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。在组织管理账户 中创建一个自定义脚本，该脚本可代入该角色并将 CloudFormation 模板部署到成员账户。","C":"为组织配置一个委托管理员账户。创建一个包含 Lambda 函数和 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则的 AWS CloudFormation 模板，该规则每 30 分钟调用一次 Lambda 函数。使用 CloudFormation StackSets 从委托管理员账户将 CloudFormation 模板部署到组织中的所有成员账户。","D":"在组织成员账户中创建跨账户 IAM 角色。将 AmazonS3FullAccess 策略和 AWSCodeDeployDeplo yerAccess 策略附加到该角色。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 假定该角色，从组织管理账户部署 Lambda 函数。在成员账户中配置 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则，每 30 分钟调用一次 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Option C is the most operationally efficient. CloudFormation StackSets with service-managed permissions can be initiated from a delegated administrator account and deploy a single template to all member accounts of an AWS Organization in one operation without creating IAM roles in each target account (StackSets creates the roles on your behalf, per the StackSets concepts doc). By packaging BOTH the Lambda function AND a local EventBridge scheduled rule (rate of 30 minutes) in that one template, each member account becomes self-contained: its own rule invokes its own local Lambda on schedule, with no cross-account invocation, no per-function resource policies, and no custom scripting. This scales cleanly to 500 accounts. Option A is the trap: it pushes only the Lambda via StackSets and then tries to drive all 500 functions from a single EventBridge event bus in the delegated admin account. EventBridge cross-account integration operates at the event-bus level and, per the cross-account docs, now requires IAM roles for cross-account event-bus targets; fanning a schedule out to 500 Lambda targets in other accounts is far more complex and brittle, defeating operational efficiency.","explanation_zh":"選項 C 最具操作效率。採用 service-managed permissions 的 CloudFormation StackSets 可由 delegated administrator account 發起，以一次操作將單一範本部署到 AWS Organizations 的所有成員帳戶，且不需在每個目標帳戶手動建立 IAM 角色（依 StackSets concepts 文件，StackSets 會代為建立角色）。將 Lambda function 與本地的 EventBridge scheduled rule（每 30 分鐘 rate）一起打包進同一範本後，每個成員帳戶都自成一體：由各自的 rule 觸發各自的本地 Lambda，無需跨帳戶調用、無需在每個函式上設定 resource policy、也無需自訂腳本，能乾淨地擴展到 500 個帳戶。選項 A 是陷阱：它只透過 StackSets 部署 Lambda，再企圖用 delegated admin account 中單一 EventBridge event bus 去驅動全部 500 個函式。EventBridge 跨帳戶整合是在 event bus 層級運作，依跨帳戶文件，現已要求跨帳戶 event bus 目標使用 IAM 角色；將排程扇出到其他帳戶的 500 個 Lambda 目標遠更複雜且脆弱，違背操作效率原則。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deploys only the Lambda via StackSets, then relies on a single EventBridge event bus in the delegated admin account to invoke the Lambda in each of the 500 member accounts every 30 minutes. Scheduled rules and their targets run within their own account; EventBridge cross-account integration is account-to-account event-bus forwarding (and now requires IAM roles for cross-account event-bus targets), so driving 500 cross-account Lambda targets is complex and not operationally efficient. A local scheduled rule bundled in the template (option C) avoids all of this.","why_zh":"只透過 StackSets 部署 Lambda，再依賴 delegated admin account 的單一 EventBridge event bus 每 30 分鐘調用 500 個成員帳戶中的 Lambda。scheduled rule 與其目標在自身帳戶執行；EventBridge 跨帳戶整合是帳戶對帳戶的 event bus 轉發（現要求跨帳戶 event bus 目標使用 IAM 角色），驅動 500 個跨帳戶 Lambda 目標複雜且不具操作效率。將本地 scheduled rule 一併打包進範本（選項 C）可完全避免這些問題。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses a custom script in the management account that assumes cross-account roles to deploy CloudFormation to each member account, and attaches overly broad AWSLambda_FullAccess and AWSCloudFormationFullAccess policies. Custom multi-account scripting and per-account role management for 500 accounts is exactly what StackSets service-managed permissions eliminate; this is high operational overhead and violates least privilege.","why_zh":"在管理帳戶使用自訂腳本，透過跨帳戶角色逐一部署 CloudFormation 到每個成員帳戶，並附加過於寬鬆的 AWSLambda_FullAccess 與 AWSCloudFormationFullAccess。為 500 個帳戶自訂腳本與逐帳戶管理角色正是 StackSets service-managed permissions 要消除的工作，操作負擔高且違反最小權限。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeDeploy is an application deployment service, not the organization-wide multi-account distribution mechanism; assuming a cross-account role from the management account to deploy a Lambda via CodeDeploy across 500 accounts is not how Lambda is provisioned at organization scale. The attached AmazonS3FullAccess and AWSCodeDeployDeployerAccess policies are mismatched for tagging EBS volumes, making this both technically wrong and inefficient.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 是應用程式部署服務，並非組織層級多帳戶分發機制；透過管理帳戶假設跨帳戶角色用 CodeDeploy 在 500 個帳戶部署 Lambda 並非組織規模下佈建 Lambda 的方式。所附 AmazonS3FullAccess 與 AWSCodeDeployDeployerAccess 與標記 EBS volume 的需求不符，技術上既錯誤又無效率。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-delegated-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/what-is-cfnstacksets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-create-rule-schedule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-cross-account.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":143,"question_en":"A company's production environment uses an AWS CodeDeploy blue/green deployment to deploy an application. The deployment incudes Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling groups that launch instances that run Amazon Linux 2. A working appspec.yml file exists in the code repository and contains the following text: A DevOps engineer needs to ensure that a script downloads and installs a license file onto the instances before the replacement instances start to handle request traffic. The DevOps engineer adds a hooks section to the appspec.yml file. Which hook should the DevOps engineer use to run the script that downloads and installs the license file?","question_zh":"一家公司的生产环境使用 AWS CodeDeploy 蓝/绿部署来部署应用程序。该部署包括使用 Amazon EC2 自动扩展组启动运行 Amazon Linux 2 的实例。 代码库中存在一个有效的 appspec.yml 文件，其中包含以下内容： DevOps 工程师需要确保在替换实例开始处理请求流量之前，脚本能够将许可证文件下载并安装到实例上。 为此，DevOps 工程师在 appspec.yml 文件中添加了一个 hooks 部分。 DevOps 工程师应该使用哪个钩子来运行下载并安装许可证文件的脚本？","options_en":{"A":"AfterBlockTraffic","B":"BeforeBlockTraffic","C":"BeforeInstall","D":"DownloadBundle"},"options_zh":{"A":"堵车之后","B":"阻止区块传播前","C":"安装前","D":"下载包"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is a CodeDeploy EC2/On-Premises blue/green deployment, so the script must run on the REPLACEMENT (new) instances before they begin serving request traffic. In the AppSpec 'Lifecycle event hook availability' table, the 'Blue/green deployment: Replacement instances' column allows only ApplicationStop, DownloadBundle, BeforeInstall, Install, AfterInstall, ApplicationStart, ValidateService, and BeforeAllowTraffic. Of the four options, BeforeInstall (C) is the only scriptable hook that runs on the replacement instances; AWS documents it for preinstall tasks such as decrypting files and creating a backup, which fits downloading and installing a license file before the application is installed and before the instances start to handle traffic. DownloadBundle (D) is reserved for the CodeDeploy agent and 'cannot be used to run scripts,' and the BlockTraffic-related hooks BeforeBlockTraffic (B) and AfterBlockTraffic (A) are not available on replacement instances at all (they run only on the original/terminating instances being deregistered). Therefore BeforeInstall is correct.","explanation_zh":"這是一個 CodeDeploy EC2/On-Premises 的 blue/green 部署，因此腳本必須在「replacement（新）instances」開始處理請求流量之前，於這些新執行個體上執行。在 AppSpec 的「Lifecycle event hook availability」表格中，「Blue/green deployment: Replacement instances」欄位只允許 ApplicationStop、DownloadBundle、BeforeInstall、Install、AfterInstall、ApplicationStart、ValidateService 與 BeforeAllowTraffic。在四個選項中，BeforeInstall（C）是唯一可在 replacement instances 上執行腳本的 hook；AWS 文件說明它用於安裝前（preinstall）任務，例如解密檔案與建立備份，正好適合在應用程式安裝之前、且執行個體開始處理流量之前下載並安裝授權檔。DownloadBundle（D）保留給 CodeDeploy agent，'cannot be used to run scripts'；而 BlockTraffic 相關的 BeforeBlockTraffic（B）與 AfterBlockTraffic（A）在 replacement instances 上完全不可用（只會在被取消註冊的 original/終止執行個體上執行）。因此 BeforeInstall 為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AfterBlockTraffic is not available on blue/green replacement instances (the availability table shows it only on original/terminating instances and rollback-replacement). It runs after instances are deregistered from the load balancer, which applies to instances being torn down, not the new ones coming up to serve traffic.","why_zh":"AfterBlockTraffic 不適用於 blue/green 的 replacement instances（可用性表顯示它只用於 original/終止執行個體與回滾替換情境）。它在執行個體從負載平衡器取消註冊後執行，針對的是被淘汰的執行個體，而非即將上線提供流量的新執行個體。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"BeforeBlockTraffic is also not available on replacement instances; it runs on instances before they are deregistered from a load balancer (original/terminating instances), so it cannot run the license script on the new instances.","why_zh":"BeforeBlockTraffic 同樣不適用於 replacement instances；它在執行個體從負載平衡器取消註冊之前執行（original/終止執行個體），因此無法在新執行個體上執行授權腳本。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DownloadBundle is reserved for the CodeDeploy agent (it copies the revision files to a temporary location) and the AWS docs explicitly state it 'cannot be used to run scripts,' so no license-install script can be attached to it.","why_zh":"DownloadBundle 保留給 CodeDeploy agent（用於將修訂版檔案複製到暫存位置），AWS 文件明確指出它『cannot be used to run scripts』，因此無法附加授權安裝腳本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":144,"question_en":"A company has an application that includes AWS Lambda functions. The Lambda functions run Python code that is stored in an AWS CodeCommit repository. The company has recently experienced failures in the production environment because of an error in the Python code. An engineer has written unit tests for the Lambda functions to help avoid releasing any future defects into the production environment. The company's DevOps team needs to implement a solution to integrate the unit tests into an existing AWS CodePipeline pipeline. The solution must produce reports about the unit tests for the company to view. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个包含 AWS Lambda 函数的应用程序。这些 Lambda 函数运行存储在 AWS CodeCommit 代码 库中的 Python 代码。该公司最近在生产环境中遇到了故障，原因是 Python 代码中存在错误。一位工程师 为这些 Lambda 函数编写了单元测试，以帮助避免将来在生产环境中出现任何缺陷。 该公司的 DevOps 团队需要实施一个解决方案，将单元测试集成到现有的 AWS CodePipeline 管道中。该 解决方案必须生成有关单元测试的报告，以便公司查看。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Associate the CodeCommit repository with Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer. Create a new AWS CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, configure a test stage that uses the new CodeBuild project. Create a buildspec.yml file in the CodeCommit repository. In the buildspec yml file, define the actions to run a CodeGuru review.","B":"Create a new AWS CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, configure a test stage that uses the new CodeBuild project. Create a CodeBuild report group. Create a buildspec.yml file in the CodeCommit repository. In the buildspec.yml file, define the actions to run the unit tests with an output of JUNITXML in the build phase section. Configure the test reports to be uploaded to the new CodeBuild report group.","C":"Create a new AWS CodeArtifact repository. Create a new AWS CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, configure a test stage that uses the new CodeBuild project. Create an appspec.yml file in the original CodeCommit repository. In the appspec.yml file, define the actions to run the unit tests with an output of CUCUMBERJSON in the build phase section. Configure the tests reports to be sent to the new CodeArtifact repository.","D":"Create a new AWS CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, configure a test stage that uses the new CodeBuild project. Create a new Amazon S3 bucket. Create a buildspec.yml file in the CodeCommit repository. In the buildspec yml file, define the actions to run the unit tests with an output of HTML in the phases section. In the reports section, upload the test reports to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CodeCommit 存储库与 Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 关联。创建一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中，配置一个使用新 CodeBuild 项目的测试阶段。在 CodeCommit 存储库中创建一 个 buildspec.yml 文件。在 buildspec.yml 文件中，定义运行 CodeGuru 审查的操作。","B":"创建一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中，配置一个使用新 CodeBuild 项目的测试 阶段。创建一个 CodeBuild 报告组。在其中创建一个 buildspec.yml 文件。 在 CodeCommit 存储库中，在 buildspec.yml 文件中定义在构建阶段运行单元测试的操作，并将输出 设置为 JUNITXML。配置将测试报告上传到新的 CodeBuild 报告组。","C":"创建一个新的 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。创建一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中， 配置一个测试阶段，使用新的 CodeBuild 项目。在原始的 CodeCommit 存储库中创建一个 appspec. yml 文件。在 appspec.yml 文件中，在构建阶段部分定义运行单元测试的操作，并将输出设置为 CUCUMBERJSON。配置将测试报告发送到新的 CodeArtifact 存储库。","D":"创建一个新的 AWS CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中，配置一个使用新 CodeBuild 项目的测试 阶段。创建一个新的 Amazon S3 存储桶。在 CodeCommit 代码库中创建一个 buildspec.yml 文件。在 buildspec.yml 文件的 phases 部分定义运行单元测试并输出 HTML 格式报告的操作。在 reports 部分， 将测试报告上传到 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to execute Python (pytest) unit tests inside an existing CodePipeline and produce viewable reports. AWS CodeBuild has native test reporting: you run the tests in a build phase of buildspec.yml and declare a reports section that points to a CodeBuild report group with a supported file-format. The supported test report formats are Cucumber JSON, JUnit XML, NUnit XML, NUnit3 XML, TestNG XML, and Visual Studio TRX. The official pytest reporting guide shows exactly this pattern: run 'python -m pytest --junitxml=...' and add a reports section with file-format: JUNITXML uploading to a report group, which is then viewable in the CodeBuild console. Option B matches this canonical pattern (CodeBuild project as a CodePipeline test stage, a report group, buildspec.yml, JUNITXML output uploaded to the report group), so it is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是在現有的 CodePipeline 中執行 Python (pytest) 單元測試並產生可檢視的報告。AWS CodeBuild 內建測試報告功能：在 buildspec.yml 的 build 階段執行測試，並宣告 reports 區段指向一個 CodeBuild report group，搭配支援的 file-format。CodeBuild 支援的測試報告格式為 Cucumber JSON、JUnit XML、NUnit XML、NUnit3 XML、TestNG XML 與 Visual Studio TRX。官方 pytest 報告指引正是此模式：執行 'python -m pytest --junitxml=...'，並加入 reports 區段設定 file-format: JUNITXML 上傳至 report group，之後即可在 CodeBuild 主控台檢視。選項 B 完全符合此標準模式（以 CodeBuild project 作為 CodePipeline 的 test stage、建立 report group、使用 buildspec.yml、輸出 JUNITXML 並上傳至 report group），因此正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer performs automated static code analysis and recommendations; it does not execute the engineer's pytest unit tests or produce unit-test reports. A CodeGuru review in a buildspec would not run or report on the new unit tests, so it fails the requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 執行的是自動化靜態程式碼分析與建議，並不會執行工程師撰寫的 pytest 單元測試或產生單元測試報告。在 buildspec 中執行 CodeGuru review 不會運行或報告這些新測試，因此不符合需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Multiple errors: appspec.yml belongs to CodeDeploy (not CodeBuild) and is not where test commands/reports are defined; CodeArtifact is a software package repository, not a destination for test reports (reports go to report groups, optionally exported to S3). The combination does not produce CodeBuild test reports.","why_zh":"多處錯誤：appspec.yml 屬於 CodeDeploy（非 CodeBuild），也不是定義測試指令／報告之處；CodeArtifact 是軟體套件儲存庫，並非測試報告的目的地（報告應送往 report group，必要時匯出至 S3）。此組合無法產生 CodeBuild 測試報告。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"HTML is not a supported CodeBuild test report file-format (only Cucumber JSON, JUnit XML, NUnit XML, NUnit3 XML, TestNG XML, and Visual Studio TRX/TRX XML are supported). Test reports are produced via a report group and the reports section, not by uploading HTML files to an S3 bucket, so this does not yield viewable native CodeBuild test reports.","why_zh":"HTML 不是 CodeBuild 支援的測試報告 file-format（僅支援 Cucumber JSON、JUnit XML、NUnit XML、NUnit3 XML、TestNG XML 與 Visual Studio TRX/TRX XML）。測試報告是透過 report group 與 reports 區段產生，而非把 HTML 檔案上傳到 S3 bucket，因此無法產生可檢視的原生 CodeBuild 測試報告。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/test-reporting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/test-report-pytest.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/report-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":145,"question_en":"A company manages multiple AWS accounts in AWS Organizations. The company’s security policy states that AWS account root user credentials for member accounts must not be used. The company monitors access to the root user credentials. A recent alert shows that the root user in a member account launched an Amazon EC2 instance. A DevOps engineer must create an SCP at the organization's root level that will prevent the root user in member accounts from making any AWS service API calls. Which SCP will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司的安全政策规定，成员账户的 AWS 账户根用户凭 证不得使用。该公司会监控对根用户凭证的访问情况。 最近的一则警报显示，成员账户中的 root 用户启动了一个 Amazon EC2 实例。DevOps 工程师必须 在组织的根级别创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），以防止成员账户中的 root 用户调用任何 AWS 服 务的 API。 哪个 SCP 会符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"","B":"","C":"","D":""},"options_zh":{},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is a single SCP at the organization root that prevents ONLY the member-account root user from making any AWS service API call. SCPs follow a deny-by-default, guardrail model: an Allow-type SCP only widens the maximum-permission boundary and cannot block anything, while an explicit Deny attached anywhere in the path from the root down (including the root) denies that permission for every account beneath it. So the policy must use Effect: Deny, Action: \"*\", Resource: \"*\". To restrict only the root user (and not IAM users or roles), it must carry a Condition that POSITIVELY matches the root principal: StringLike on aws:PrincipalArn equal to arn:aws:iam::*:root. The account root user's ARN is arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT-ID:root, so the wildcard in the account-ID position lets this one root-level SCP cover the root user of every member account, while IAM user/role ARNs (:user/... and :assumed-role/...) do not match and remain unaffected. Option C uses exactly this Deny + StringLike-on-aws:PrincipalArn (arn:aws:iam::*:root) pattern, so it is correct; the dump suggestion agrees. Confidence is medium only because the option text is corrupted in this dump and the verdict relies on the known C mapping for this canonical DOP-C02 item.","explanation_zh":"需求是在組織根（organization root）建立「單一」SCP，僅阻止成員帳戶的 root 使用者進行任何 AWS 服務 API 呼叫。SCP 採用 deny-by-default 的權限護欄模型：Allow 型 SCP 只會放寬最大權限邊界，本身無法封鎖任何動作；而在從根往下的路徑（含根層級）任一層附加的明確 Deny，會對其底下所有帳戶封鎖該權限。因此政策必須為 Effect: Deny、Action: \"*\"、Resource: \"*\"。為了「僅」限制 root 使用者而不影響 IAM 使用者或角色，必須加上「正向」比對 root 主體的條件：StringLike 比對 aws:PrincipalArn 等於 arn:aws:iam::*:root。帳戶 root 使用者的 ARN 為 arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT-ID:root，因此在帳戶 ID 位置使用萬用字元，使這一條根層級 SCP 即可涵蓋所有成員帳戶的 root 使用者；而 IAM 使用者/角色的 ARN（:user/... 與 :assumed-role/...）不會被比中，因此不受影響。選項 C 正是採用 Deny + 對 aws:PrincipalArn 進行 StringLike（arn:aws:iam::*:root）的模式，故為正確答案，與 dump 建議一致。信心設為 medium，僅因本 dump 中選項文字損毀，判定須依賴此標準 DOP-C02 題目已知的 C 對應。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Corrupted placeholder text in this dump (a store name), not a real policy. In the canonical question the non-answer options fail because they either use Effect: Allow (an Allow SCP only widens the permission ceiling and cannot deny the root user any action) or otherwise do not produce an explicit Deny targeting the root principal.","why_zh":"此 dump 中為損毀的佔位文字（店名），並非真實政策。在標準題目中，非答案選項之所以錯誤，是因為它們使用 Effect: Allow（Allow 型 SCP 只放寬權限上限，無法對 root 使用者拒絕任何動作），或未產生針對 root 主體的明確 Deny。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Empty/corrupted in this dump. Canonically the trap option uses StringNotLike on aws:PrincipalArn arn:aws:iam::*:root, which inverts the logic: it denies every principal EXCEPT root, locking out IAM users/roles while leaving the root user completely unrestricted, the opposite of the requirement.","why_zh":"此 dump 中為空白/損毀。標準上此陷阱選項對 aws:PrincipalArn arn:aws:iam::*:root 使用 StringNotLike，邏輯反轉：它封鎖 root 以外的所有主體，鎖死 IAM 使用者/角色，卻完全不限制 root 使用者，與需求恰好相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Empty/corrupted in this dump. Canonically a distractor uses Effect: Allow or a Deny with no condition (or a condition that does not isolate the root principal), so it either blocks nothing or would block all principals (including IAM users/roles), failing 'prevent only the root user from all API calls'.","why_zh":"此 dump 中為空白/損毀。標準上此干擾選項使用 Effect: Allow，或使用沒有條件（或條件未鎖定 root 主體）的 Deny，因此要麼什麼都不封鎖，要麼會封鎖所有主體（含 IAM 使用者/角色），無法滿足「僅阻止 root 使用者進行所有 API 呼叫」。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_principal.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/root-user-best-practices.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌"},{"id":146,"question_en":"A company uses AWS and has a VPC that contains critical compute infrastructure with predictable traffic patterns. The company has configured VPC flow logs that are published to a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The company's DevOps team needs to configure a monitoring solution for the VPC flow logs to identify anomalies in network traffic to the VPC over time. If the monitoring solution detects an anomaly, the company needs the ability to initiate a response to the anomaly. How should the DevOps team configure the monitoring solution to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS，并且其 VPC 中包含具有可预测流量模式的关键计算基础设施。该公司已配置 VPC 流日志，将其发布到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中的一个日志组。 该公司的 DevOps 团队需要为 VPC 流日志配置一个监控解决方案，以便随着时间的推移识别出流向 VPC 的网络流量中的异常情况。如果监控解决方案检测到异常，公司需要具备对异常情况发起响应的能 力。 开发运维团队应如何配置监控解决方案以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Subscribe the log group to the data stream. Configure Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics to detect log anomalies in the data stream. Create an AWS Lambda function to use as the output of the data stream. Configure the Lambda function to write to the default Amazon EventBridge event bus in the event of an anomaly finding.","B":"Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream that delivers events to an Amazon S3 bucket. Subscribe the log group to the delivery stream. Configure Amazon Lookout for Metrics to monitor the data in the S3 bucket for anomalies. Create an AWS Lambda function to run in response to Lookout for Metrics anomaly findings. Configure the Lambda function to publish to the default Amazon EventBridge event bus.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to detect anomalies. Configure the Lambda function to publish an event to the default Amazon EventBridge event bus if the Lambda function detects an anomaly. Subscribe the Lambda function to the log group.","D":"Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Subscribe the log group to the data stream. Create an AWS Lambda function to detect log anomalies. Configure the Lambda function to write to the default Amazon EventBridge event bus if the Lambda function detects an anomaly. Set the Lambda function as the processor for the data stream."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。将日志组订阅到该数据流。配置 Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics 以检测 数据流中的日志异常。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数作为数据流的输出。配置 Lambda 函数，在检测到异 常时将其写入默认的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。","B":"创建一个将事件传递到 Amazon S3 存储桶的 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 交付流。将日志组订阅到该交 付流。配置 Amazon Lookout for Metrics 来监控 S3 存储桶中的数据是否存在异常。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以响应 Lookout for Metrics 的异常发现而运行。配置该 Lambda 函数以发布到默认的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来检测异常。将 Lambda 函数配置为在检测到异常时向默认的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线发布事件。将 Lambda 函数订阅到日志组。","D":"创建一个 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。将日志组订阅到该数据流。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来检测日志异 常。如果 Lambda 函数检测到异常，则配置该函数将信息写入默认的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。将 Lambda 函数设置为数据流的处理器。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirement is to detect anomalies in VPC flow log network traffic over time and then initiate a response. A CloudWatch Logs subscription filter can deliver a log group only to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or Amazon OpenSearch Service, so routing the log group to a Kinesis data stream is valid. Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics provides the built-in RANDOM_CUT_FOREST function that assigns an anomaly score to streaming records based on numeric values, learning a baseline over time, and the AWS-documented pattern uses an AWS Lambda function as the application output to process those anomaly scores and configure alerts. Option A implements exactly this canonical streaming anomaly-detection pattern (data stream -> Kinesis Data Analytics anomaly detection -> Lambda as output -> publish to the default EventBridge event bus to initiate a response), so it is correct. The dump's answer (B) is wrong because Amazon Lookout for Metrics requires structured, tabular metric data (measures, dimensions, and a timestamp delivered on a regular interval, e.g., CSV/JSONLines in templated S3 paths); the raw base64-encoded, gzip-compressed CloudWatch log JSON that a subscription filter delivers via Firehose is not in that format and cannot be ingested without an omitted transformation/aggregation step.","explanation_zh":"需求是要對 VPC flow logs 的網路流量做隨時間的異常偵測,並在偵測到異常時觸發回應。CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 只能將 log group 投遞到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 Amazon OpenSearch Service,因此將 log group 訂閱到 Kinesis data stream 是有效作法。Amazon Kinesis Data Analytics 內建 RANDOM_CUT_FOREST 函式,可依數值欄位為串流記錄指派異常分數並隨時間建立基準線;AWS 文件記載的模式正是以 AWS Lambda 作為應用程式輸出來處理這些異常分數並設定告警。選項 A 完整實作了此標準的串流異常偵測架構(data stream -> Kinesis Data Analytics 異常偵測 -> Lambda 作為輸出 -> 發佈到預設 EventBridge event bus 以觸發回應),因此正確。題庫建議答案 B 是錯的,因為 Amazon Lookout for Metrics 需要結構化的表格式 metric 資料(measures、dimensions 與依固定間隔投遞的 timestamp,例如以樣板化 S3 路徑存放的 CSV/JSONLines);subscription filter 經由 Firehose 投遞的原始 base64 編碼、gzip 壓縮的 CloudWatch log JSON 不符此格式,缺少被省略的轉換/彙整步驟便無法被攝取。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Lookout for Metrics ingests structured, aggregated metric data (measures, dimensions, and a timestamp on a fixed interval, e.g., CSV/JSONLines in templated S3 paths). Raw base64/gzip CloudWatch log JSON delivered via Firehose to S3 is not in that format, so it cannot be analyzed without an omitted transformation/aggregation step. The architecture as written does not work. (Lookout for Metrics has also been deprecated by AWS.)","why_zh":"Amazon Lookout for Metrics 需要結構化、已彙整的 metric 資料(measures、dimensions 與依固定間隔的 timestamp,例如以樣板化 S3 路徑存放的 CSV/JSONLines)。經 Firehose 投遞到 S3 的原始 base64/gzip CloudWatch log JSON 不符該格式,缺少被省略的轉換/彙整步驟即無法分析,所述架構無法運作。(Lookout for Metrics 亦已被 AWS 終止服務。)"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Lambda function subscribed to a log group receives only small batches of log events and is stateless; it has no built-in or managed capability to learn a baseline and detect anomalies in traffic over time. This is custom, incomplete, and not the documented anomaly-detection approach.","why_zh":"訂閱 log group 的 Lambda 只會收到少量 log 批次且為無狀態,沒有內建或受管能力去學習基準並隨時間偵測流量異常。屬自訂且不完整,也非文件所述的異常偵測作法。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same core flaw as C: a Lambda set as the processor of the Kinesis data stream handles per-batch records with no managed/ML anomaly detection over time; it would require custom stateful logic the option does not provide, unlike Kinesis Data Analytics RANDOM_CUT_FOREST.","why_zh":"與 C 同樣的核心缺陷:作為 Kinesis data stream 處理器的 Lambda 只逐批處理記錄,沒有隨時間的受管/ML 異常偵測;需要選項未提供的自訂有狀態邏輯,不像 Kinesis Data Analytics 的 RANDOM_CUT_FOREST。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/app-anomaly-detection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/kinesisanalytics/latest/dev/how-it-works-output-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-lookoutmetrics-anomalydetector-s3sourceconfig.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":147,"question_en":"AnyCompany is using AWS Organizations to create and manage multiple AWS accounts. AnyCompany recently acquired a smaller company, Example Corp. During the acquisition process, Example Corp's single AWS account joined AnyCompany's management account through an Organizations invitation. AnyCompany moved the new member account under an OU that is dedicated to Example Corp. AnyCompany's DevOps engineer has an IAM user that assumes a role that is named OrganizationAccountAccessRole to access member accounts. This role is configured with a full access policy. When the DevOps engineer tries to use the AWS Management Console to assume the role in Example Corp's new member account, the DevOps engineer receives the following error message: \"Invalid information in one or more fields. Check your information or contact your administrator.\" Which solution will give the DevOps engineer access to the new member account?","question_zh":"AnyCompany 正在使用 AWS Organizations 来创建和管理多个 AWS 账户。AnyCompany 最近收购了一家 规模较小的公司 Example Corp。在收购过程中，Example Corp 的单个 AWS 账户通过 Organizations 邀请 加入了 AnyCompany 的管理账户。AnyCompany 将新成员账户移至专门用于 Example Corp 的组织单元 （OU）下。 AnyCompany 的 DevOps 工程师有一个 IAM 用户，该用户会切换到名为 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 的角 色以访问成员账户。此角色配置了全访问策略。当该 DevOps 工程师尝试使用 AWS 管理控制台在 Example Corp 的新成员账户中切换到该角色时，收到了以下错误消息：“一个或多个字段中的信息无效。请检查您的 信息或联系管理员。” 哪种解决方案能让 DevOps 工程师访问新成员账户？","options_en":{"A":"In the management account, grant the DevOps engineer's IAM user permission to assume the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role in the new member account.","B":"In the management account, create a new SCP. In the SCP, grant the DevOps engineer's IAM user full access to all resources in the new member account. Attach the SCP to the OU that contains the new member account.","C":"In the new member account, create a new IAM role that is named OrganizationAccountAccessRole. Attach the AdministratorAccess AWS managed policy to the role. In the role's trust policy, grant the management account permission to assume the role.","D":"In the new member account, edit the trust policy for the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role. Grant the management account permission to assume the role."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户中，授予 DevOps 工程师的 IAM 用户在新成员账户中承担 OrganizationAccountAccess Role IAM 角色的权限。","B":"在管理账户中，创建一个新的服务控制策略（SCP）。在该 SCP 中，授予 DevOps 工程师的 IAM 用户对 新成员账户中所有资源的完全访问权限。将该 SCP 附加到包含新成员账户的组织单元（OU）上。","C":"在新成员账户中，创建一个名为 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 的新 IAM 角色。将 AdministratorAccess AWS 管理策略附加到该角色。在角色的信任策略中，授予管理账户承担该角色 的权限。","D":"在新成员账户中，编辑 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色的信任策略。授予管理账户承担该 角色的权限。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Example Corp's account joined the organization via an Organizations invitation. Per AWS docs, when you CREATE a member account with Organizations, the OrganizationAccountAccessRole (with administrator permissions and a trust policy for the management account) is created automatically. However, accounts that you INVITE to join do NOT get this role created automatically — you must create it manually. Therefore the role does not exist in Example Corp's account, so the console switch-role attempt cannot resolve it and returns 'Invalid information in one or more fields.' The documented fix is to manually duplicate the role in the member account: create an IAM role (recommended name OrganizationAccountAccessRole), attach the AdministratorAccess AWS managed policy, and configure the trust policy so the management account can assume it — exactly what option C describes.","explanation_zh":"Example Corp 的帳號是透過 Organizations 邀請（invitation）加入組織的。根據 AWS 文件，當你使用 Organizations「建立（create）」成員帳號時，系統會自動建立 OrganizationAccountAccessRole（含管理員權限以及針對 management account 的信任政策）。但你「邀請（invite）」加入的現有帳號並不會自動產生此角色，必須手動建立。因此該角色在 Example Corp 帳號中根本不存在，主控台的 switch-role 無法解析它，才會出現「Invalid information in one or more fields」錯誤。文件記載的修正方式是在成員帳號中手動複製此角色：建立一個 IAM role（建議命名為 OrganizationAccountAccessRole），附加 AdministratorAccess AWS 受管政策，並設定信任政策讓 management account 可以 assume 該角色 — 這正是選項 C 所描述的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Granting the IAM user sts:AssumeRole in the management account addresses the source (assuming) side, but the engineer already assumes OrganizationAccountAccessRole in other member accounts with a full-access policy, so source permission is not the gap. The actual problem is that the target role does not exist in the invited account, so A does not resolve the 'Invalid information' error.","why_zh":"在 management account 授予 IAM 使用者 sts:AssumeRole 處理的是來源（發起方）端，但工程師已能在其他成員帳號 assume OrganizationAccountAccessRole 且擁有 full-access 政策，來源權限並非問題所在。真正的缺口是目標角色在被邀請的帳號中不存在，因此 A 無法解決「Invalid information」錯誤。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SCPs are guardrails that filter the maximum available permissions; they NEVER grant permissions to IAM users or roles, and by default do not even affect the management account. You cannot use an SCP to 'grant full access' to a user, and an SCP cannot create the missing role, so B is technically wrong.","why_zh":"SCP 是防護欄，用來限制可用權限的上限；它從不授予 IAM 使用者或角色任何權限，預設甚至不影響 management account。無法用 SCP「授予」使用者完整存取，SCP 也無法建立缺失的角色，故 B 在技術上是錯的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Editing the trust policy of OrganizationAccountAccessRole presupposes the role already exists, but invited accounts do not automatically get this role created — there is no role to edit. The full role must be created (including attaching AdministratorAccess), not merely re-pointed via a trust policy edit, which is why C is correct and D is inapplicable.","why_zh":"編輯 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 的信任政策前提是角色已存在，但被邀請的帳號不會自動建立此角色 — 根本沒有角色可編輯。必須建立完整的角色（包括附加 AdministratorAccess），而不只是透過編輯信任政策來重新指向，這就是 C 正確而 D 不適用的原因。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_create-cross-account-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access-cross-account-role.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":148,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is designing an application that integrates with a legacy REST API. The application has an AWS Lambda function that reads records from an Amazon Kinesis data stream. The Lambda function sends the records to the legacy REST API. Approximately 10% of the records that the Lambda function sends from the Kinesis data stream have data errors and must be processed manually. The Lambda function event source configuration has an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) dead-letter queue as an on-failure destination. The DevOps engineer has configured the Lambda function to process records in batches and has implemented retries in case of failure. During testing, the DevOps engineer notices that the dead-letter queue contains many records that have no data errors and that already have been processed by the legacy REST API. The DevOps engineer needs to configure the Lambda function's event source options to reduce the number of errorless records that are sent to the dead-letter queue. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在设计一个与遗留的 REST API 集成的应用程序。该应用程序包含一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于从 Amazon Kinesis 数据流中读取记录。Lambda 函数将这些记录发送到遗留的 REST API。 Lambda 函数从 Kinesis 数据流发送的记录中约有 10% 存在数据错误，必须手动处理。Lambda 函数的事 件源配置将 Amazon 简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）死信队列设置为失败时的目的地。DevOps 工程师已 将 Lambda 函数配置为批量处理记录，并在出现故障时实现了重试机制。 在测试期间，DevOps 工程师注意到死信队列中包含许多没有数据错误且已由旧版 REST API 处理过的 记录。DevOps 工程师需要配置 Lambda 函数的事件源选项，以减少发送到死信队列的无错误记录的数 量。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the retry attempts.","B":"Configure the setting to split the batch when an error occurs.","C":"Increase the concurrent batches per shard.","D":"Decrease the maximum age of record."},"options_zh":{"A":"增加重试次数。","B":"将设置配置为在出现错误时拆分批次。","C":"增加每个分片的并发批处理数量。","D":"降低记录的最大年龄。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"By default, a Kinesis event source mapping checkpoints to the highest sequence number of a batch only when the ENTIRE batch succeeds; if any single record causes a function error, Lambda treats the whole batch as a failure, retries the entire batch, and after retries/age are exhausted discards the entire batch to the on-failure destination (the SQS DLQ). That is exactly why the DLQ contains many errorless records already accepted by the legacy REST API: they shared a batch with the ~10% bad records. Turning on BisectBatchOnFunctionError ('split the batch when an error occurs') makes Lambda split a failed batch into two smaller batches and retry each half, recursively isolating the bad records into progressively smaller batches; AWS docs state this 'splits a failed batch into two smaller batches, isolating bad records' and that 'splitting batches doesn't consume the retry quota.' Consequently the halves of good records succeed and get committed, and only the tiny batch that actually contains a bad record is ultimately discarded to the DLQ, dramatically reducing the number of errorless records sent there. This is set directly in the event source mapping options, exactly as the question asks.","explanation_zh":"預設情況下，Kinesis event source mapping 只有在「整批」記錄全部成功時，才會 checkpoint 到該批最高的 sequence number；只要批次中有任何一筆記錄造成 function 錯誤，Lambda 就把整批視為失敗、重試整批，待重試次數或 record 最大壽命耗盡後，便把「整批」丟到 on-failure destination（即 SQS DLQ）。這正是為何 DLQ 裡有大量沒有資料錯誤、且 legacy REST API 已成功處理過的記錄：它們與那約 10% 的壞記錄被分在同一批。開啟 BisectBatchOnFunctionError（即「發生錯誤時分割批次」）後，Lambda 會把失敗的批次一分為二並分別重試，遞迴地把壞記錄隔離到愈來愈小的批次中；AWS 文件明確指出此設定會「將失敗的批次分割成兩個較小的批次，隔離壞記錄」，且「分割批次不會消耗重試配額」。因此，含好記錄的那一半會成功並被 commit，最終只有真正包含壞記錄的極小批次會被丟到 DLQ，大幅減少送到 DLQ 的無錯誤記錄數量。此設定正是在 event source mapping 選項中設定，完全符合題目要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing MaximumRetryAttempts only retries the same failing batch more times. Because the ~10% bad records have genuine, persistent data errors, they can never succeed, so the whole batch (including the errorless, already-processed records) is still ultimately discarded to the DLQ; this only delays the discard and may add latency and duplicate calls to the legacy API.","why_zh":"增加 MaximumRetryAttempts 只是把同一個失敗批次重試更多次。由於約 10% 的壞記錄是真實且持續的資料錯誤、永遠不會成功，整批（含已處理的無錯誤記錄）最終仍會被丟到 DLQ；這只是延後丟棄，且可能增加延遲與對 legacy API 的重複呼叫。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Concurrent batches per shard (ParallelizationFactor) only increases throughput by processing multiple batches per shard in parallel. It changes parallelism, not failure granularity, so a failed batch is still discarded whole (with its good records) to the DLQ. It does nothing to reduce errorless records in the DLQ.","why_zh":"每個 shard 的並行批次數（ParallelizationFactor）只是透過並行處理多個批次來提升吞吐量，改變的是並行度而非失敗的粒度，失敗批次仍會整批（含好記錄）被丟到 DLQ，無法減少 DLQ 中的無錯誤記錄。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Decreasing MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds makes records expire and be discarded to the DLQ sooner once they exceed the age limit. This would increase (or at least not reduce) the volume of records, including errorless ones, sent to the DLQ, which is the opposite of the goal.","why_zh":"降低 MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds 會讓記錄一旦超過年齡上限就更快過期並被丟到 DLQ。這只會增加（或至少不會減少）送入 DLQ 的記錄量（含無錯誤記錄），與目標相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/kinesis-on-failure-destination.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-kinesis-batchfailurereporting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-kinesis-parameters.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":149,"question_en":"A company has microservices running in AWS Lambda that read data from Amazon DynamoDB. The Lambda code is manually deployed by developers after successful testing. The company now needs the tests and deployments be automated and run in the cloud. Additionally, traffic to the new versions of each microservice should be incrementally shifted over time after deployment. What solution meets all the requirements, ensuring the MOST developer velocity?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Lambda 上运行微服务，这些微服务从 Amazon DynamoDB 中读取数据。Lambda 代码 由开发人员在测试成功后手动部署。该公司现在需要将测试和部署自动化，并在云端运行。此外，在部 署后，每个微服务新版本的流量应逐步转移。 哪种解决方案能满足所有要求，确保开发人员的工作效率最高？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodePipeline configuration and set up a post-commit hook to trigger the pipeline after tests have passed. Use AWS CodeDeploy and create a Canary deployment configuration that specifies the percentage of traffic and interval.","B":"Create an AWS CodeBuild configuration that triggers when the test code is pushed. Use AWS CloudFormation to trigger an AWS CodePipeline configuration that deploys the new Lambda versions and specifies the traffic shift percentage and interval.","C":"Create an AWS CodePipeline configuration and set up the source code step to trigger when code is pushed. Set up the build step to use AWS CodeBuild to run the tests. Set up an AWS CodeDeploy configuration to deploy, then select the CodeDeployDefault.LambdaLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes option.","D":"Use the AWS CLI to set up a post-commit hook that uploads the code to an Amazon S3 bucket after tests have passed Set up an S3 event trigger that runs a Lambda function that deploys the new version. Use an interval in the Lambda function to deploy the code over time at the required percentage."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 配置，并设置一个在测试通过后触发管道的提交后钩子。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 并创建一个金丝雀部署配置，指定流量百分比和间隔。","B":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 配置，当测试代码被推送时触发。使用 AWS CloudFormation 触发一个 AWS CodePipeline 配置，以部署新的 Lambda 版本，并指定流量转移百分比和间隔。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 配置，并设置源代码步骤在代码推送时触发。设置构建步骤以使用 AWS CodeBuild 运行测试。设置 AWS CodeDeploy 配置以进行部署，然后选择 CodeDeployDefault.LambdaLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes 选项。","D":"使用 AWS 命令行界面（CLI）设置一个在测试通过后将代码上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶的提交后钩 子。设置一个 S3 事件触发器，该触发器运行一个 Lambda 函数来部署新版本。在 Lambda 函数中 使用间隔，以便在规定的时间段内按要求的百分比逐步部署代码。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Option C is the canonical fully-managed CI/CD pattern: a CodePipeline whose Source stage triggers automatically when code is pushed, a Build stage that uses CodeBuild to run the tests in the cloud, and a Deploy stage that uses CodeDeploy. Selecting the predefined deployment configuration CodeDeployDefault.LambdaLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes shifts 10 percent of traffic to the new Lambda version every three minutes until all traffic is shifted, satisfying the requirement to incrementally shift traffic over time after deployment. The AWS CodeDeploy deployment-configurations page confirms this is a real predefined AWS Lambda compute-platform configuration with exactly that behavior. Because everything runs as managed AWS services with a single predefined config and no custom code, it delivers the MOST developer velocity with the least operational overhead. The other answers either rely on client-side Git post-commit hooks (which run on a developer machine, not in the cloud), omit a cloud test stage, invert the orchestration awkwardly, or hand-roll the traffic shifting.","explanation_zh":"選項 C 是標準的全託管 CI/CD 模式：CodePipeline 的 Source 階段在程式碼推送時自動觸發、Build 階段使用 CodeBuild 在雲端執行測試，Deploy 階段使用 CodeDeploy。選擇預先定義的部署設定 CodeDeployDefault.LambdaLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes，會每三分鐘將 10% 的流量轉移到新的 Lambda 版本，直到全部流量轉移完成，符合「部署後隨時間逐步轉移流量」的需求。AWS CodeDeploy 的 deployment configurations 文件確認這是 AWS Lambda compute platform 真實存在且行為完全相符的預先定義設定。由於全部以託管 AWS 服務搭配單一預設設定且無自訂程式碼，提供最高的開發者效率與最少的維運負擔。其他選項分別依賴客戶端 Git post-commit hook（在開發者機器而非雲端執行）、省略雲端測試階段、以彆扭方式反轉編排，或手刻流量轉移邏輯。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Git post-commit hook is a client-side hook that runs on the developer's local machine, not a cloud trigger; CodePipeline triggers natively on source changes via events/webhooks. The wording also describes a 'Canary deployment configuration that specifies the percentage of traffic and interval', but the predefined Lambda canary configs use fixed values (10 percent first, remainder after a set interval) and the design omits a cloud build/test stage, so the 'tests run in the cloud' requirement is not clearly met.","why_zh":"Git post-commit hook 是在開發者本機端執行的客戶端 hook，並非雲端觸發；CodePipeline 原生透過事件/webhook 觸發。其敘述的『可指定流量百分比與間隔的 Canary 部署設定』也不符實際——預先定義的 Lambda canary 設定使用固定值（先 10%，間隔後轉移其餘），且設計省略雲端建置/測試階段，無法明確滿足『測試在雲端執行』的需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It inverts the orchestration: having CodeBuild trigger CloudFormation which then triggers CodePipeline is convoluted and not a native pattern (normally CodePipeline orchestrates CodeBuild and CloudFormation, not the reverse). The pipeline does not natively 'specify the traffic shift percentage and interval' without CodeDeploy, and this added indirection reduces developer velocity rather than maximizing it.","why_zh":"它反轉了編排順序：讓 CodeBuild 觸發 CloudFormation 再觸發 CodePipeline 既迂迴又非原生模式（通常是 CodePipeline 編排 CodeBuild 與 CloudFormation，而非相反）。不透過 CodeDeploy，pipeline 並無法原生『指定流量轉移百分比與間隔』，且這種額外的間接層降低而非最大化開發者效率。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This hand-rolls everything: a CLI client-side post-commit hook, an S3 upload, an S3 event, and a custom Lambda that performs traffic shifting with a manual interval loop. It reinvents managed CodeDeploy traffic-shifting, provides no clear managed test stage, and yields the lowest developer velocity with the highest operational overhead.","why_zh":"這完全手刻：CLI 客戶端 post-commit hook、S3 上傳、S3 事件，以及用手動間隔迴圈執行流量轉移的自訂 Lambda。它重新發明託管 CodeDeploy 的流量轉移、沒有明確的託管測試階段，開發者效率最低且維運負擔最高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/pipelines-triggers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/tutorials-lambda-deploy.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":150,"question_en":"A company is building a web and mobile application that uses a serverless architecture powered by AWS Lambda and Amazon API Gateway. The company wants to fully automate the backend Lambda deployment based on code that is pushed to the appropriate environment branch in an AWS CodeCommit repository. The deployment must have the following: Separate environment pipelines for testing and production Automatic deployment that occurs for test environments only Which steps should be taken to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在构建一个基于 AWS Lambda 和 Amazon API Gateway 的无服务器架构的网络和移动应用程 序。该公司希望根据推送到 AWS CodeCommit 存储库中相应环境分支的代码，完全自动执行后端 Lambda 部署。 部署必须具备以下内容： 为测试和生产环境分别设置独立的环境管道 仅针对测试环境进行的自动部署 应采取哪些步骤来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a new AWS CodePipeline service. Create a CodeCommit repository for each environment. Set up CodePipeline to retrieve the source code from the appropriate repository. Set up the deployment step to deploy the Lambda functions with AWS CloudFormation.","B":"Create two AWS CodePipeline configurations for test and production environments. Configure the production pipeline to have a manual approval step. Create a CodeCommit repository for each environment. Set up each CodePipeline to retrieve the source code from the appropriate repository. Set up the deployment step to deploy the Lambda functions with AWS CloudFormation.","C":"Create two AWS CodePipeline configurations for test and production environments. Configure the production pipeline to have a manual approval step. Create one CodeCommit repository with a branch for each environment. Set up each CodePipeline to retrieve the source code from the appropriate branch in the repository. Set up the deployment step to deploy the Lambda functions with AWS CloudFormation.","D":"Create an AWS CodeBuild configuration for test and production environments. Configure the production pipeline to have a manual approval step. Create one CodeCommit repository with a branch for each environment. Push the Lambda function code to an Amazon S3 bucket. Set up the deployment step to deploy the Lambda functions from the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个新的 AWS CodePipeline 服务。为每个环境创建一个 CodeCommit 代码库。设置 CodePipeline 从相应的代码库获取源代码。设置部署步骤，使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 Lambda 函数。","B":"为测试和生产环境创建两个 AWS CodePipeline 配置。将生产管道配置为包含一个手动审批步骤。为每 个环境创建一个 CodeCommit 代码库。将每个 CodePipeline 设置为从相应的代码库获取源代码。设置 部署步骤，使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 Lambda 函数。","C":"为测试和生产环境创建两个 AWS CodePipeline 配置。将生产管道配置为包含一个手动审批步骤。创 建一个 CodeCommit 代码库，并为每个环境设置一个分支。将每个 CodePipeline 设置为从代码库中 的相应分支获取源代码。设置部署步骤，使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 Lambda 函数。","D":"为测试和生产环境创建 AWS CodeBuild 配置。将生产管道配置为包含手动审批步骤。创建一个 CodeCommit 代码库，为每个环境设置一个分支。将 Lambda 函数代码推送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。设 置部署步骤，从 S3 存储桶部署 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Three requirements must be met: separate test and production pipelines, automatic deployment for the test environment only (production gated), and deployment triggered by code pushed to the appropriate environment BRANCH of a CodeCommit repository. Option C satisfies all three. Two distinct CodePipeline configurations give isolated test and production pipelines. A manual approval action on the production pipeline halts that pipeline until an IAM-authorized person approves, so only the test pipeline deploys automatically while production waits for human approval (per the AWS approvals docs, an approval action stops execution until approved/rejected). A single CodeCommit repository with one branch per environment matches the explicit 'environment branch' wording, and the CodeCommit source action requires both RepositoryName and BranchName and starts the pipeline only when a new commit is made on the configured branch, so each pipeline triggers solely on its own branch. The deploy stage uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy the Lambda functions. The decisive qualifiers are 'pushed to the appropriate environment branch' (one repo, multiple branches) and 'automatic deployment for test only' (manual approval gate on prod), which only C satisfies.","explanation_zh":"需滿足三項需求:測試與生產環境分開的 pipeline、僅測試環境自動部署(生產須有閘控)、以及由推送到 CodeCommit repository 中對應環境「分支(branch)」的程式碼觸發部署。選項 C 全部滿足。兩個獨立的 CodePipeline 設定提供分離的測試與生產 pipeline。生產 pipeline 上的 manual approval action 會暫停該 pipeline,直到具備 IAM 權限者核准,因此只有測試 pipeline 自動部署,生產則等待人工核准(依 AWS approvals 文件,approval action 會停止執行直到被核准或拒絕)。單一 CodeCommit repository 並為每個環境建立一個分支,符合題目明確的「environment branch」措辭;CodeCommit source action 同時必須提供 RepositoryName 與 BranchName,且僅在設定的分支有新 commit 時才啟動 pipeline,因此每個 pipeline 僅由其對應分支觸發。部署階段使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 Lambda 函式。決定性關鍵詞為「pushed to the appropriate environment branch」(單一 repo、多分支)與「僅測試環境自動部署」(生產端 manual approval 閘控),唯有 C 同時滿足。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Configures only one CodePipeline (no separate test/prod pipelines), creates a repository per environment (contradicts the 'environment branch' requirement), and has no manual approval, so production would deploy automatically, violating 'automatic deployment for test only.'","why_zh":"只設定一個 CodePipeline(沒有分離的測試/生產 pipeline),為每個環境建立一個 repository(與「environment branch」需求相違),且沒有 manual approval,生產會自動部署,違反「僅測試環境自動部署」。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Has two pipelines and a production manual approval, but creates a separate CodeCommit repository for each environment instead of one repository with per-environment branches, contradicting the requirement that code is pushed to the appropriate environment branch in a (single) repository.","why_zh":"雖有兩個 pipeline 與生產 manual approval,但為每個環境建立各自的 CodeCommit repository,而非單一 repository 內每環境一分支,與「推送到 repository 中對應環境分支」的需求相違。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses CodeBuild 'configurations' rather than CodePipeline pipelines (CodeBuild is a build service, not a multi-stage deployment pipeline), then references 'the production pipeline' inconsistently since no pipeline was created; pushing Lambda code to S3 and deploying from S3 omits the orchestrated pipeline and CloudFormation-based environment separation the requirements call for.","why_zh":"使用 CodeBuild「設定」而非 CodePipeline pipeline(CodeBuild 是建置服務,並非多階段部署 pipeline),且因未建立 pipeline 卻提到「production pipeline」前後不一致;將 Lambda 程式碼推送到 S3 再從 S3 部署,缺少需求所要求的協調式 pipeline 與 CloudFormation 環境分離結構。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CodeCommit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals-action-add.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":151,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer wants to find a solution to migrate an application from on premises to AWS. The application is running on Linux and needs to run on specific versions of Apache Tomcat, HAProxy, and Varnish Cache to function properly. The application's operating system-level parameters require tuning. The solution must include a way to automate the deployment of new application versions. The infrastructure should be scalable and faulty servers should be replaced automatically. Which solution should the DevOps engineer use?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师想要找到一种解决方案，将一个应用程序从本地迁移到 AWS。该应用程序运行在 Linux 系统上，需要在特定版本的 Apache Tomcat、HAProxy 和 Varnish Cache 上运行才能正常工作。 应用程序的操作系统级参数需要进行调整。该解决方案必须包含一种自动部署新应用程序版本的方法。 基础设施应具备可扩展性，并且出现故障的服务器应能自动替换。 DevOps 工程师应该使用哪种解决方案？","options_en":{"A":"Upload the application as a Docker image that contains all the necessary software to Amazon ECR. Create an Amazon ECS cluster using an AWS Fargate launch type and an Auto Scaling group. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses Amazon ECR as a source and Amazon ECS as a deployment provider.","B":"Upload the application code to an AWS CodeCommit repository with a saved configuration file to configure and install the software. Create an AWS Elastic Beanstalk web server tier and a load balanced-type environment that uses the Tomcat solution stack. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses CodeCommit as a source and Elastic Beanstalk as a deployment provider.","C":"Upload the application code to an AWS CodeCommit repository with a set of .ebextensions files to configure and install the software. Create an AWS Elastic Beanstalk worker tier environment that uses the Tomcat solution stack. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses CodeCommit as a source and Elastic Beanstalk as a deployment provider.","D":"Upload the application code to an AWS CodeCommit repository with an appspec.yml file to configure and install the necessary software. Create an AWS CodeDeploy deployment group associated with an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses CodeCommit as a source and CodeDeploy as a deployment provider."},"options_zh":{"A":"将应用程序作为包含所有必要软件的 Docker 镜像上传到 Amazon ECR。使用 AWS Fargate 启动类型和 自动扩展组创建一个 Amazon ECS 集群。创建一个使用 Amazon ECR 作为源和 Amazon ECS 作为部 署提供程序的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。","B":"将应用程序代码上传到 AWS CodeCommit 存储库，并附带一个保存的配置文件以配置和安装软件。创 建一个使用 Tomcat 解决方案堆栈的 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 网络服务器层和负载均衡类型的环境。创 建一个使用 CodeCommit 作为源和 Elastic Beanstalk 作为部署提供商的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。","C":"将应用程序代码上传到 AWS CodeCommit 存储库，并附带一组 .ebextensions 文件以配置和安装软件。 创建一个使用 Tomcat 解决方案堆栈的 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 工作负载环境。创建一个使用 CodeCommit 作为源和 Elastic Beanstalk 作为部署提供商的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。","D":"将应用程序代码上传至带有 appspec.yml 文件的 AWS CodeCommit 存储库，以配置并安装必要的软件。 创建一个与之关联的 AWS CodeDeploy 部署组。 亚马逊 EC2 自动扩展组。创建一个使用 CodeCommit 作为源并使用 CodeDeploy 作为部署提供商的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application requires specific versions of Apache Tomcat, HAProxy, and Varnish Cache AND tuning of OS-level (kernel/sysctl) parameters, so it needs full control of the operating system. Only EC2 instances provide that. Option D uses an EC2 Auto Scaling group (scalability plus automatic replacement of faulty instances), CodeCommit as source, and CodeDeploy with an appspec.yml whose EC2/On-Premises 'hooks' lifecycle events (BeforeInstall/AfterInstall/etc.) run scripts that install the three exact software versions and tune the OS. CodeDeploy is integrated with EC2 Auto Scaling: when new instances launch into the group, CodeDeploy automatically deploys the latest revision to them, so scaled-out and replacement instances are bootstrapped correctly. CodePipeline (CodeCommit -> CodeDeploy) automates deployment of new application versions, satisfying every requirement.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式需要特定版本的 Apache Tomcat、HAProxy 與 Varnish Cache，並且要調整作業系統層級 (kernel/sysctl) 參數，因此需要對作業系統的完整控制權，只有 EC2 執行個體能提供。選項 D 使用 EC2 Auto Scaling group (提供擴展能力並自動替換異常執行個體)、CodeCommit 作為來源，以及搭配 appspec.yml 的 CodeDeploy；其 EC2/On-Premises 'hooks' 生命週期事件 (BeforeInstall/AfterInstall 等) 執行指令碼來安裝這三個確切軟體版本並調整 OS 參數。CodeDeploy 與 EC2 Auto Scaling 整合：當新執行個體加入該群組時，CodeDeploy 會自動將最新版本部署到這些執行個體，確保擴展與替換的執行個體被正確初始化。CodePipeline (CodeCommit -> CodeDeploy) 自動化新版本部署，完全符合所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Fargate is serverless and locks down the host: per AWS docs it 'prevents containers from accessing the underlying host's resources, such as the file system, devices, networking' and restricts Linux capabilities like CAP_SYS_ADMIN, so OS-level/kernel parameter tuning is not possible. The option also pairs Fargate with an 'Auto Scaling group,' but Fargate uses ECS service auto scaling, not an EC2 ASG.","why_zh":"AWS Fargate 為無伺服器架構並鎖定主機：根據 AWS 文件，它『防止容器存取底層主機資源，例如檔案系統、裝置、網路』，並限制 CAP_SYS_ADMIN 等 Linux capabilities，因此無法進行 OS 層級/kernel 參數調整。此選項還將 Fargate 與 'Auto Scaling group' 搭配，但 Fargate 使用 ECS service auto scaling，而非 EC2 ASG。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The Elastic Beanstalk managed Tomcat solution stack fixes the platform software (a managed Tomcat plus an nginx/Apache proxy) and is not built to host specific versions of HAProxy and Varnish Cache as part of the stack; deep OS tuning fights the managed platform. The option also relies on a 'saved configuration file' (environment settings) rather than the install/config scripting needed to deploy the three packages.","why_zh":"Elastic Beanstalk 受管 Tomcat 解決方案堆疊固定了平台軟體 (受管 Tomcat 加上 nginx/Apache 代理)，並非用來在堆疊內託管特定版本的 HAProxy 與 Varnish Cache；深度 OS 調整會與受管平台衝突。此選項還倚賴 'saved configuration file' (環境設定)，而非部署這三個套件所需的安裝/設定指令碼。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An Elastic Beanstalk worker tier is for offloading long-running asynchronous background tasks processed via an SQS daemon (per AWS docs), not for a web-facing application served by Tomcat/HAProxy/Varnish. Wrong environment tier, and the same managed-platform software constraints as B apply.","why_zh":"Elastic Beanstalk worker tier 用於將長時間執行的非同步背景任務透過 SQS daemon 處理 (根據 AWS 文件)，而非由 Tomcat/HAProxy/Varnish 對外提供服務的網頁應用程式。屬於錯誤的環境層級，且同樣受 B 的受管平台軟體限制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/fargate-security-considerations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features-managing-env-tiers.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":152,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is using AWS CodeDeploy across a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances in an EC2 Auto Scaling group. The associated CodeDeploy deployment group, which is integrated with EC2 Auto Scaling, is configured to perform in-place deployments with CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime. During an ongoing new deployment, the engineer discovers that, although the overall deployment finished successfully, two out of five instances have the previous application revision deployed. The other three instances have the newest application revision. What is likely causing this issue?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在使用 AWS CodeDeploy 在一个 EC2 自动扩展组中的多个 Amazon EC2 实例上 进行部署。与 EC2 自动扩展集成的关联 CodeDeploy 部署组配置为使用 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime 进行原地部署。在正在进行的新部署过程中，工程师发现，尽管整个部署成功完成，但五台实例中有 两台部署的是旧的应用程序版本，而另外三台实例部署的是最新的应用程序版本。 这问题可能是什么原因造成的？ 受影响的两个实例未能获取新的部署。","options_en":{"A":"The two affected instances failed to fetch the new deployment.","B":"A failed AfterInstall lifecycle event hook caused the CodeDeploy agent to roll back to the previous version on the affected instances.","C":"The CodeDeploy agent was not installed in two affected instances.","D":"EC2 Auto Scaling launched two new instances while the new deployment had not yet finished, causing the previous version to be deployed on the affected instances."},"options_zh":{"B":"由于 AfterInstall 生命周期事件钩子失败，CodeDeploy 代理在受影响的实例上回滚到了之前的版 本。","C":"两个受影响的实例中未安装 CodeDeploy 代理。","D":"在新部署尚未完成时，EC2 自动扩展启动了两个新实例，导致受影响的实例上部署了旧版本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When a CodeDeploy deployment group is integrated with an EC2 Auto Scaling group, CodeDeploy installs an Auto Scaling launch lifecycle hook that is always enabled and cannot be turned off. The AWS documentation section 'Scale-out events during a deployment' states verbatim: 'If an Auto Scaling scale-out event occurs while a deployment is underway, the new instances will be updated with the application revision that was previously deployed, not the newest application revision. If the deployment succeeds, the old instances and the newly scaled-out instances will be hosting different application revisions.' This exactly matches the scenario: three pre-existing instances received the newest revision via the normal CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime in-place deployment, while two instances that Auto Scaling launched mid-deployment received the previously deployed revision through a launch deployment, and the overall deployment still reported success. Therefore option D is correct. (Note: CodeDeploy normally starts a follow-on deployment to reconcile outdated instances, but that automatic update can be disabled, which is consistent with the persistent mixed-revision state described.)","explanation_zh":"當 CodeDeploy deployment group 與 EC2 Auto Scaling group 整合時,CodeDeploy 會安裝一個 Auto Scaling launch lifecycle hook,此 hook 永遠啟用且無法關閉。AWS 文件的「Scale-out events during a deployment」段落原文寫道:『若在部署進行中發生 Auto Scaling scale-out event,新啟動的執行個體將會被部署「先前已部署的」application revision,而非最新的 application revision。若部署成功,舊執行個體與新增的 scale-out 執行個體將會託管不同的 application revision。』這完全符合題目情境:三台原有執行個體透過正常的 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime in-place deployment 取得最新版本,而兩台在部署進行中由 Auto Scaling 啟動的執行個體則透過 launch deployment 取得先前版本,整體部署仍回報成功。因此選項 D 正確。(註:CodeDeploy 通常會啟動後續部署以更新過時執行個體,但此自動更新可被停用,與題述持續存在的版本不一致狀態一致。)","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"If the two instances had failed to fetch (DownloadBundle) the new revision, those instance-level deployments would fail at that lifecycle event and be marked failed, not left silently running a complete prior revision; with CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime an instance failure typically fails the overall deployment, contradicting the 'finished successfully' premise.","why_zh":"若兩台執行個體無法擷取(DownloadBundle)新版本,該執行個體層級的部署會在該 lifecycle event 失敗並被標記為失敗,而不是悄悄停留在執行完整的舊版本;在 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime 下執行個體失敗通常會使整體部署失敗,與題目「成功完成」的前提矛盾。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A failed AfterInstall hook marks the instance/deployment as failed; CodeDeploy in-place deployments do not silently roll back individual instances to the previous revision on a hook failure. A hook failure would prevent the reported successful completion rather than yield a success with the old revision present.","why_zh":"AfterInstall hook 失敗會將執行個體/部署標記為失敗;CodeDeploy 的 in-place deployment 不會因 hook 失敗而靜默地將個別執行個體回退到先前版本。hook 失敗會使題目所述的成功完成無法達成,而非在保留舊版本的情況下回報部署成功。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"If the CodeDeploy agent were not installed on the two instances, CodeDeploy could not communicate with them, so the launch deployment would time out (Heartbeat Timeout) and fail rather than installing a complete previous revision. The affected instances clearly have a working agent because a full prior revision was deployed to them.","why_zh":"若兩台執行個體未安裝 CodeDeploy agent,CodeDeploy 無法與其通訊,launch deployment 會逾時(Heartbeat Timeout)並失敗,而不會安裝完整的舊版本。受影響的執行個體顯然有正常運作的 agent,因為其上已部署了完整的舊版本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-configure-advanced-options.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":153,"question_en":"A security team is concerned that a developer can unintentionally attach an Elastic IP address to an Amazon EC2 instance in production. No developer should be allowed to attach an Elastic IP address to an instance. The security team must be notified if any production server has an Elastic IP address at any time. How can this task be automated?","question_zh":"安全团队担心开发人员可能会无意中将弹性 IP 地址附加到生产环境中的 Amazon EC2 实例上。任何开发 人员都不应被允许将弹性 IP 地址附加到实例上。如果任何生产服务器在任何时候都附加了弹性 IP 地址， 必须通知安全团队。 如何才能使这项任务实现自动化？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon Athena to query AWS CloudTrail logs to check for any associate-address attempts. Create an AWS Lambda function to disassociate the Elastic IP address from the instance, and alert the security team.","B":"Attach an IAM policy to the developers' IAM group to deny associate-address permissions. Create a custom AWS Config rule to check whether an Elastic IP address is associated with any instance tagged as production, and alert the security team.","C":"Ensure that all IAM groups associated with developers do not have associate-address permissions. Create a scheduled AWS Lambda function to check whether an Elastic IP address is associated with any instance tagged as production, and alert the security team if an instance has an Elastic IP address associated with it.","D":"Create an AWS Config rule to check that all production instances have EC2 IAM roles that include deny associate-address permissions. Verify whether there is an Elastic IP address associated with any instance, and alert the security team if an instance has an Elastic IP address associated with it."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Athena 查询 AWS CloudTrail 日志以检查是否存在任何关联地址的尝试。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将弹性 IP 地址从实例中分离，并向安全团队发出警报。","B":"将一个 IAM 策略附加到开发人员的 IAM 组，以拒绝其关联地址的权限。创建一个自定义的 AWS Config 规则，检查弹性 IP 地址是否与任何标记为“生产”的实例相关联，并向安全团队发出警 报。","C":"确保与开发人员关联的所有 IAM 组均无关联地址的权限。创建一个计划的 AWS Lambda 函数，检查 是否有任何标记为生产环境的实例关联了弹性 IP 地址，如果有，则向安全团队发出警报。","D":"创建一个 AWS Config 规则，检查所有生产实例的 EC2 IAM 角色是否包含拒绝关联弹性 IP 地址的权 限。验证是否有任何实例关联了弹性 IP 地址，如果有实例关联了弹性 IP 地址，则向安全团队发出 警报。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: (1) prevent developers from attaching an Elastic IP address, and (2) be notified if any production server has an EIP 'at any time'. Attaching an EIP is the ec2:AssociateAddress (associate-address) action performed by the developer's own IAM identity, so attaching an explicit Deny for associate-address to the developers' IAM group reliably blocks the action (an explicit Deny always overrides any Allow). For the 'at any time' detection, an AWS Config rule with a configuration-change trigger continuously tracks resource configuration changes and evaluates resources as they change, and AWS Config can stream compliance-state changes to an Amazon SNS topic to alert the security team. A CUSTOM Config rule is required here because the AWS managed rule eip-attached checks the opposite condition (it returns NON_COMPLIANT when an EIP's AssociationId is null, i.e., it flags EIPs that are NOT attached), so it cannot detect EIPs that ARE associated with production instances. Option B scopes the custom rule to instances tagged production and alerts the team, satisfying both prevention and continuous detection/alerting.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩個部分:(1) 防止開發人員附加 Elastic IP address;(2) 在任何時候 ('at any time') 若有 production 伺服器擁有 EIP 時通知安全團隊。附加 EIP 是由開發人員自身的 IAM identity 執行的 ec2:AssociateAddress (associate-address) 動作,因此在開發人員的 IAM group 上附加明確的 Deny associate-address 政策可確實阻止此動作 (明確的 Deny 永遠優先於任何 Allow)。對於 'at any time' 的偵測,採用 configuration-change 觸發類型的 AWS Config rule 會持續追蹤資源組態變更並在資源變更時進行評估,且 AWS Config 可將合規狀態變更串流至 Amazon SNS topic 以通知安全團隊。此處必須使用 CUSTOM Config rule,因為 AWS 受管規則 eip-attached 檢查的是相反條件 (當 EIP 的 AssociationId 為 null 時回傳 NON_COMPLIANT,即標示未附加的 EIP),無法偵測已關聯到 production 執行個體的 EIP。選項 B 將自訂規則的範圍限定在標記為 production 的執行個體並通知團隊,同時滿足預防與持續偵測/告警兩項要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Querying CloudTrail logs via Athena is on-demand/batch and historical (CloudTrail delivery is delayed), so it cannot provide continuous 'at any time' detection. It also does nothing to PREVENT a developer from attaching an EIP; it only reacts after the fact by disassociating, whereas the requirement is that no developer should be allowed to attach one in the first place.","why_zh":"透過 Athena 查詢 CloudTrail 日誌屬於隨選/批次且具歷史延遲性質 (CloudTrail 傳遞有延遲),無法提供持續的 'at any time' 偵測。它也完全沒有預防開發人員附加 EIP,僅在事後以解除關聯方式反應,而需求是不應允許任何開發人員附加 EIP。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Merely ensuring groups 'do not have' associate-address permission is weaker than an explicit Deny, because another attached policy or assumed role could still grant the permission. More importantly, a scheduled (periodic) Lambda polls only at intervals, leaving gaps, so it does not satisfy continuous 'at any time' detection the way an AWS Config configuration-change-triggered rule does.","why_zh":"僅確保 group 'does not have' associate-address 權限弱於明確的 Deny,因為其他附加政策或所擔任的角色仍可能授予該權限。更重要的是,排程 (週期性) 的 Lambda 只在固定間隔輪詢,留有偵測空窗,無法像 configuration-change 觸發的 AWS Config rule 那樣滿足持續的 'at any time' 偵測。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This misunderstands the permission model. An IAM role attached to an EC2 instance governs what that instance's own processes can do via the instance profile; it does NOT control whether a developer (a separate IAM identity using their own credentials) can call AssociateAddress against the instance. Therefore a Config rule checking instances for 'deny associate-address' instance roles does not prevent developers from attaching EIPs.","why_zh":"此選項誤解了權限模型。附加到 EC2 instance 的 IAM role 透過 instance profile 控管的是該執行個體自身行程能做什麼,並不控制開發人員 (使用自身憑證的另一個 IAM identity) 是否能對該執行個體呼叫 AssociateAddress。因此檢查執行個體是否具有 'deny associate-address' role 的 Config rule 無法防止開發人員附加 EIP。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/eip-attached.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/notifications-for-AWS-Config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_develop-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/APIReference/API_AssociateAddress.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":154,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations to create separate AWS accounts for each of its departments. The company needs to automate the following tasks: Update the Linux AMIs with new patches periodically and generate a golden image Install a new version of Chef agents in the golden image, if available Provide the newly generated AMIs to the department's accounts Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST management overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS 组织为每个部门创建单独的 AWS 账户。这 公司需要将以下任务自动化： 定期使用新补丁更新 Linux AMI 并生成黄金镜像 如果可用，请在黄金映像中安装新版本的 Chef 代理程序 将新生成的 AMI 提供给部门的账户 哪种解决方案在满足这些要求的同时，管理开销最小？","options_en":{"A":"Write a script to launch an Amazon EC2 instance from the previous golden image. Apply the patch updates. Install the new version of the Chef agent, generate a new golden image, and then modify the AMI permissions to share only the new image with the department's accounts.","B":"Use Amazon EC2 Image Builder to create an image pipeline that consists of the base Linux AMI and components to install the Chef agent. Use AWS Resource Access Manager to share EC2 Image Builder images with the department's accounts.","C":"Use an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to update the Linux AMI by using the previous image. Provide the URL for the script that will update the Chef agent. Use AWS Organizations to replace the previous golden image in the department's accounts.","D":"Use Amazon EC2 Image Builder to create an image pipeline that consists of the base Linux AMI and components to install the Chef agent. Create a parameter in AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to store the new AMI ID that can be referenced by the department's accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"编写一个脚本，从之前的黄金镜像启动一个 Amazon EC2 实例。应用补丁更新。安装新版本的 Chef 代理，生成新的黄金镜像，然后修改 AMI 权限，仅与部门账户共享新镜像。","B":"使用 Amazon EC2 Image Builder 创建一个包含基础 Linux AMI 以及用于安装 Chef 代理的组件的映 像管道。使用 AWS 资源访问管理器与部门账户共享 EC2 Image Builder 映像。","C":"使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册通过使用之前的镜像来更新 Linux AMI。提供用 于更新 Chef 代理的脚本的 URL。使用 AWS Organizations 在部门账户中替换之前的黄金镜像。","D":"使用 Amazon EC2 Image Builder 创建一个包含基础 Linux AMI 以及用于安装 Chef 代理的组件的映像 管道。在 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储中创建一个参数来存储新的 AMI ID，以便部门的账户可 以引用。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"All requirements (periodic Linux patching to a golden image, conditional Chef-agent install, and distribution to department accounts) point to EC2 Image Builder, which runs an image pipeline on a schedule from a base Linux AMI plus components (a patch/update component and a Chef-agent component) with no manual instance management. That eliminates A (fully manual scripting) and C (misuse of an Automation runbook plus a non-existent Organizations 'replace image' capability). Both B and D build correctly with Image Builder, so the decision is how the new AMI is 'provided' to department accounts. AWS docs are explicit that AMIs are NOT Image Builder resources -- they are 'external resources that Image Builder distributes' via distribution configuration; AWS RAM only shares the Image Builder image/component/recipe resources, and a RAM-shared image merely lets consumers 'use it as the base image in their recipes' (granting just imagebuilder:GetImage/ListImages), which would force each department to build its own image. That mismatches the requirement to hand out a ready-to-use golden AMI, so B is wrong. Option D keeps the Image Builder pipeline and uses Systems Manager Parameter Store -- Image Builder natively writes the new AMI ID to an SSM parameter via SsmParameterConfiguration (dataType aws:ec2:image) -- so department accounts always reference the latest golden AMI automatically, the documented lowest-overhead pattern. Therefore D is correct; the dump's suggested answer B mischaracterizes RAM.","explanation_zh":"所有需求（定期為 Linux 打補丁產生 golden image、條件式安裝 Chef agent、並把 AMI 提供給各部門帳號）都指向 EC2 Image Builder：它依排程以基底 Linux AMI 加上 components（一個 patch/update component 與一個 Chef-agent component）執行 image pipeline，無需手動管理執行個體。這排除了 A（全手動腳本）與 C（誤用 Automation runbook，且 AWS Organizations 並無『取代 golden image』的功能）。B 與 D 都正確地以 Image Builder 建置，差別在於如何把新 AMI『提供』給部門帳號。AWS 文件明確指出 AMI 並非 Image Builder 資源，而是『Image Builder 透過 distribution configuration 分發的外部資源』；AWS RAM 只能分享 Image Builder 的 image/component/recipe 資源，而被 RAM 分享的 image 只允許消費者『在自己的 recipe 中作為基底映像使用』（僅授予 imagebuilder:GetImage/ListImages），等於每個部門還要自行建置映像，無法滿足直接交付可用 golden AMI 的需求，故 B 錯誤。D 維持 Image Builder pipeline，並使用 Systems Manager Parameter Store——Image Builder 透過 distribution 設定中的 SsmParameterConfiguration（dataType 為 aws:ec2:image）原生將新 AMI ID 寫入 SSM 參數——讓部門帳號自動參考最新 golden AMI，這是文件記載且管理負擔最低的模式。因此正確答案為 D；題庫建議答案 B 誤解了 RAM。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A custom script that launches an instance, patches it, installs Chef, creates an AMI, and manually modifies AMI launch permissions is the highest-overhead, fully manual approach -- exactly what EC2 Image Builder exists to automate. It fails the 'LEAST management overhead' qualifier.","why_zh":"自訂腳本啟動執行個體、打補丁、安裝 Chef、建立 AMI、再手動修改 AMI launch permissions，是負擔最高的全手動做法，正是 EC2 Image Builder 要取代的工作，違反『管理負擔最低』的限定條件。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Image Builder is correct, but AWS RAM is the wrong sharing primitive: per AWS docs an AMI is an external resource distributed via distribution configuration, not an Image Builder resource. RAM shares the Image Builder image/component/recipe resources, and a RAM-shared image only lets consumers use it as a base image in their own recipes (imagebuilder:GetImage/ListImages). It does not deliver a launchable golden AMI to department accounts and adds per-department build overhead, so it mismatches the 'provide the AMIs' requirement.","why_zh":"Image Builder 正確，但 AWS RAM 是錯誤的分享原語：依 AWS 文件，AMI 是透過 distribution configuration 分發的外部資源，並非 Image Builder 資源。RAM 分享的是 image/component/recipe 資源，被分享的 image 只能讓消費者在自己的 recipe 中當作 base image（imagebuilder:GetImage/ListImages），不會把可啟動的 golden AMI 交付給部門帳號，反而讓每個部門都要自行建置，與『提供 AMI』需求不符。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A hand-built SSM Automation runbook plus a URL-fetched Chef-update script is more bespoke and brittle automation to maintain than an Image Builder pipeline, and 'use AWS Organizations to replace the previous golden image in the department's accounts' is not a real Organizations capability -- Organizations does not push or replace AMIs into member accounts.","why_zh":"自建 SSM Automation runbook 加上以 URL 取得的 Chef 更新腳本，需維護的客製化且脆弱的自動化比 Image Builder pipeline 多；而且『用 AWS Organizations 取代部門帳號中先前的 golden image』並非 Organizations 的真實功能——Organizations 不會把 AMI 推送或取代到成員帳號。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/manage-shared-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/manage-shared-resources-share.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/cross-account-dist.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/how-image-builder-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/tutorial-ssm-parameters-recipe.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/APIReference/API_SsmParameterConfiguration.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":155,"question_en":"A company has a mission-critical application on AWS that uses automatic scaling. The company wants the deployment lifecycle to meet the following parameters: The application must be deployed one instance at a time to ensure the remaining fleet continues to serve traffic. The application is CPU intensive and must be closely monitored. The deployment must automatically roll back if the CPU utilization of the deployment instance exceeds 85%. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上运行着一个关键任务应用程序，该程序使用了自动扩展功能。该公司希望其部署生 命周期满足以下参数： 必须一次部署一个实例，以确保其余的实例群组能够继续处理流量。 该应用程序对 CPU 资源消耗很大，必须密切监控。 如果部署实例的 CPU 利用率超过 85%，则部署必须自动回滚。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation to create an AWS Step Functions state machine and Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks to move to one instance at a time into a wait state. Use AWS Systems Manager automation to deploy the update to each instance and move it back into the Auto Scaling group using the heartbeat timeout.","B":"Use AWS CodeDeploy with Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling Configure an alarm tied to the CPU utilization metric. Use the CodeDeployDefault OneAtAtime configuration as a deployment strategy. Configure automatic rollbacks within the deployment group to roll back the deployment if the alarm thresholds are breached.","C":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk for load balancing and AWS Auto Scaling. Configure an alarm tied to the CPU utilization metric. Configure rolling deployments with a fixed batch size of one instance. Enable enhanced health to monitor the status of the deployment and roll back based on the alarm previously created.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager to perform a blue/green deployment with Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling. Configure an alarm tied to the CPU utilization metric. Deploy updates one at a time. Configure automatic rollbacks within the Auto Scaling group to roll back the deployment if the alarm thresholds are breached."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 创建 AWS Step Functions 状态机和 Auto Scaling 生命周期挂钩，每次将一 个实例移入等待状态。使用 AWS Systems Manager 自动化功能将更新部署到每个实例，并在心跳 超时后将其移回 Auto Scaling 组。","B":"使用 AWS CodeDeploy 与 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 结合 配置与 CPU 利用率指标相关的警报。使用 CodeDeployDefault OneAtAtime 配置作为部署策略。在部署组中配置自动回滚，以便在警报阈值被 突破时回滚部署。","C":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 进行负载均衡和 AWS Auto Scaling。配置与 CPU 利用率指标相关的警报。 配置固定批次大小为一个实例的滚动部署。启用增强型健康检查以监控部署状态，并根据之前创 建的警报进行回滚。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 通过 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 执行蓝/绿部署。配置与 CPU 利用率指 标相关的警报。一次部署一个更新。在 Auto Scaling 组内配置自动回滚，如果警报阈值被突破则 回滚部署。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS CodeDeploy with Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling natively satisfies all three requirements with the least operational overhead. (1) One instance at a time: the predefined CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime deployment configuration deploys the revision to only one instance at a time, so the rest of the fleet keeps serving traffic. (2) Close monitoring: you associate a CloudWatch alarm on the CPU utilization metric (the alarm can be created for an EC2 instance or an EC2 Auto Scaling group) with the deployment group. (3) Automatic rollback: CodeDeploy supports configuring a deployment group to 'automatically roll back when a deployment fails or when a monitoring threshold you specify is met' - specifically the 'Roll back when alarm thresholds are met' option, which redeploys the last known good revision when the associated alarm (CPU > 85%) activates. This is the purpose-built, lowest-overhead solution and maps exactly to each parameter without custom orchestration.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeDeploy 搭配 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 以最低營運負擔原生滿足全部三項需求。(1) 一次一台：預先定義的 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime 部署設定一次只將修訂版部署到一台執行個體，因此其餘機群可持續提供服務。(2) 密切監控：將針對 CPU utilization 指標建立的 CloudWatch alarm（該 alarm 可針對 EC2 執行個體或 EC2 Auto Scaling group 建立）關聯到 deployment group。(3) 自動回復：CodeDeploy 支援將 deployment group 設定為『當部署失敗或達到您指定的監控門檻時自動回復』，具體即『Roll back when alarm thresholds are met』選項，當關聯的 alarm（CPU > 85%）觸發時會重新部署最後一個已知正常的修訂版。這是專為此情境設計、負擔最低的方案，與每項參數精準對應，無需自訂編排。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Building a custom Step Functions state machine plus Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks and SSM Automation is far higher operational overhead than the purpose-built CodeDeploy. More importantly, it provides no native automatic rollback tied to a CPU alarm; the heartbeat timeout merely governs how long the lifecycle hook holds an instance in a wait state, not CPU-based rollback. The required alarm-driven rollback behavior is not met.","why_zh":"自行建構 Step Functions 狀態機加上 Auto Scaling lifecycle hooks 與 SSM Automation 的營運負擔遠高於專用的 CodeDeploy。更關鍵的是，它不提供與 CPU alarm 連動的原生自動回復；heartbeat timeout 只是控制 lifecycle hook 將執行個體保持在等待狀態的時間，並非以 CPU 為依據的回復機制，無法滿足以 alarm 驅動回復的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Elastic Beanstalk rolling deployments can use a batch size of one, but their rollback is driven by Beanstalk's own enhanced health monitoring (failed health checks per batch), not by an arbitrary user-defined CloudWatch alarm on CPU utilization. Beanstalk does not natively wire 'roll back when this CPU alarm fires' the way CodeDeploy's deployment-group alarm-based automatic rollback does, so the alarm-driven rollback requirement is not cleanly met.","why_zh":"Elastic Beanstalk 滾動式部署可採用批次大小為一，但其回復是由 Beanstalk 自身的 enhanced health 監控（各批次健康檢查失敗）驅動，而非由使用者自訂的 CPU utilization CloudWatch alarm 驅動。Beanstalk 並未像 CodeDeploy 的 deployment-group alarm 自動回復那樣原生支援『當此 CPU alarm 觸發時回復』，因此無法乾淨地滿足以 alarm 驅動回復的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager is not a blue/green deployment service for EC2 Auto Scaling, and 'automatic rollbacks within the Auto Scaling group' based on a CloudWatch alarm is not a real ASG feature - ASGs do not roll back application deployments on alarm. Additionally, blue/green deployment replaces the whole fleet rather than updating one instance at a time, contradicting the stated requirement. The option attributes capabilities to the wrong services.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager 並非用於 EC2 Auto Scaling 的藍綠部署服務，且以 CloudWatch alarm 為依據在 Auto Scaling group 內進行『自動回復』並非真實的 ASG 功能——ASG 不會因 alarm 而回復應用程式部署。此外，藍綠部署是替換整個機群而非一次更新一台，與題目需求矛盾。此選項把功能歸給了錯誤的服務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployments-rollback-and-redeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-configure-advanced-options.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":156,"question_en":"A company has a single developer writing code for an automated deployment pipeline. The developer is storing source code in an Amazon S3 bucket for each project. The company wants to add more developers to the team but is concerned about code conflicts and lost work. The company also wants to build a test environment to deploy newer versions of code for testing and allow developers to automatically deploy to both environments when code is changed in the repository. What is the MOST efficient way to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一名开发人员为自动化部署流水线编写代码。该开发人员为每个项目将源代码存储在亚马 逊 S3 存储桶中。该公司希望为团队增加更多开发人员，但担心代码冲突和工作丢失。该公司还希望 构建一个测试环境，以便在代码库中代码发生更改时部署较新版本的代码进行测试，并允许开发人员 自动将代码部署到这两个环境。 满足这些要求的最有效方法是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository for each project, use the main branch for production code, and create a testing branch for code deployed to testing. Use feature branches to develop new features and pull requests to merge code to testing and main branches.","B":"Create another S3 bucket for each project for testing code, and use an AWS Lambda function to promote code changes between testing and production buckets. Enable versioning on all buckets to prevent code conflicts.","C":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository for each project, and use the main branch for production and test code with different deployment pipelines for each environment. Use feature branches to develop new features.","D":"Enable versioning and branching on each S3 bucket, use the main branch for production code, and create a testing branch for code deployed to testing. Have developers use each branch for developing in each environment."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个项目创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库，将主分支用于生产代码，并创建一个测试分支用 于部署到测试环境的代码。使用功能分支开发新功能，并使用拉取请求将代码合并到测试分支和 主分支。","B":"为每个项目创建另一个 S3 存储桶用于测试代码，并使用 AWS Lambda 函数在测试存储桶和生 产存储桶之间推进代码变更。在所有存储桶上启用版本控制以防止代码冲突。","C":"为每个项目创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 代码库，并使用主分支存放生产环境和测试环境的代码， 同时为每个环境设置不同的部署管道。使用功能分支开发新功能。","D":"在每个 S3 存储桶上启用版本控制和分支功能，将主分支用于生产代码，并为部署到测试环境的 代码创建一个测试分支。要求开发人员在每个环境中使用相应的分支进行开发。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: (1) prevent code conflicts and lost work when adding more developers, and (2) maintain separate testing and production environments with automated deployment when code changes. A source/version control service (Git) is the purpose-built tool for collaborative development. AWS CodeCommit is a managed Git service; its documentation states it 'is optimized for team software development. It manages batches of changes across multiple files, which can occur in parallel with changes made by other developers,' and explicitly contrasts it with S3 versioning, which 'supports the recovery of past versions of files, but it's not focused on collaborative file tracking features that software development teams need.' The Well-Architected best practice OPS05-BP01 also recommends a source control system such as CodeCommit precisely to avoid the anti-patterns in the question (lost work, inability to revert a bad change, write-lock conflicts between developers). Option A implements the canonical CodeCommit branching workflow: a main branch for production, a testing branch for test, feature branches for new work, and pull requests to review and merge changes -- exactly the mechanism that prevents conflicts and lost work. The separate main and testing branches map cleanly to two deployment pipelines so code changes trigger automatic deployment to the matching environment. This is the MOST efficient design because it uses native Git collaboration features rather than bolting custom logic onto object storage.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩點：(1) 在增加開發人員時避免程式碼衝突與工作遺失；(2) 維護獨立的測試與正式環境，並在程式碼變更時自動部署。原始碼／版本控制服務 (Git) 才是協同開發的專用工具。AWS CodeCommit 是受管的 Git 服務，其文件明確指出它『針對團隊軟體開發最佳化，可管理跨多個檔案的批次變更，並能與其他開發人員並行的變更同時發生』，並與 S3 versioning 對比：S3 versioning『支援還原檔案的舊版本，但並未聚焦於軟體開發團隊所需的協同檔案追蹤功能』。Well-Architected 最佳實務 OPS05-BP01 也建議使用如 CodeCommit 的原始碼控制系統，正是為了避免題目中描述的反模式 (工作遺失、無法回復錯誤變更、開發人員間的寫入鎖定衝突)。選項 A 實作標準的 CodeCommit 分支工作流程：main 分支用於正式環境、testing 分支用於測試、feature 分支用於開發新功能，並用 pull request 審查與合併變更——這正是防止衝突與工作遺失的機制。獨立的 main 與 testing 分支可清楚對應到兩條部署管線，程式碼變更即觸發對應環境的自動部署。這是最有效率的設計，因為它使用原生 Git 協同功能，而非在物件儲存上加上自訂邏輯。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Using a second S3 bucket plus a Lambda function to promote code and relying on S3 versioning 'to prevent code conflicts' does not work: S3 versioning recovers past object versions but provides no merge, branch, or pull-request capability, and on simultaneous writes it simply 'stores all of those objects' rather than reconciling them, so it cannot prevent concurrent-edit conflicts or lost work in team development. It also builds bespoke promotion logic instead of using a native version control service, increasing operational overhead.","why_zh":"用第二個 S3 bucket 加 Lambda 來推進程式碼，並以 S3 versioning『避免程式碼衝突』行不通：S3 versioning 只能還原舊版物件，無合併、分支或 pull request 能力，且同時寫入時只是『將所有物件都存起來』而非協調合併，無法防止團隊並行編輯的衝突或工作遺失。它還需自建推進邏輯，而非使用原生版本控制服務，增加營運負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Putting both production and test code on a single main branch with two pipelines defeats the purpose of separate environments: there is no isolated testing branch, so test deployments and production deployments draw from the same code state, and merging only via feature branches into one branch gives no place to validate newer versions before they reach production. It is less efficient and riskier than A's main/testing branch separation.","why_zh":"把正式與測試程式碼都放在單一 main 分支再配兩條管線，違背了環境隔離的目的：沒有獨立的 testing 分支，測試部署與正式部署取自同一份程式碼狀態，且僅透過 feature 分支併入單一分支，無處在進入正式環境前驗證較新版本。比 A 的 main/testing 分支隔離更低效且風險更高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon S3 does not have 'branching' as a feature -- S3 only offers object versioning. AWS documentation states S3 versioning is not focused on the collaborative file-tracking features software teams need, so it cannot provide branches, merges, or pull requests. This option describes capabilities that do not exist for S3.","why_zh":"Amazon S3 並沒有『branching (分支)』功能——S3 只提供物件 versioning。AWS 文件指出 S3 versioning 並未聚焦於軟體團隊所需的協同檔案追蹤功能，故無法提供分支、合併或 pull request。此選項描述的是 S3 不存在的功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/pull-requests.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/Versioning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/2023-04-10/framework/ops_dev_integ_version_control.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":157,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer notices that all Amazon EC2 instances running behind an Application Load Balancer in an Auto Scaling group are failing to respond to user requests. The EC2 instances are also failing target group HTTP health checks. Upon inspection, the engineer notices the application process was not running in any EC2 instances. There are a significant number of out of memory messages in the system logs. The engineer needs to improve the resilience of the application to cope with a potential application memory leak. Monitoring and notifications should be enabled to alert when there is an issue. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师注意到，在一个自动扩展组中，所有运行在应用负载均衡器后面的亚马逊 EC2 实例都无法响应用户的请求。这些 EC2 实例也无法通过目标组的 HTTP 健康检查。 工程师检查后发现，该应用程序在任何 EC2 实例中都没有运行。系统日志中有大量内存不足的错误 信息。工程师需要提高应用程序的弹性，以应对潜在的应用程序内存泄漏问题。应启用监控和通知 功能，以便在出现问题时发出警报。 哪种行动组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Change the Auto Scaling configuration to replace the instances when they fail the load balancer's health checks.","B":"Change the target group health check HealthCheckIntervalSeconds parameter to reduce the interval between health checks.","C":"Change the target group health checks from HTTP to TCP to check if the port where the application is listening is reachable.","D":"Enable the available memory consumption metric within the Amazon CloudWatch dashboard for the entire Auto Scaling group. Create an alarm when the memory utilization is high. Associate an Amazon SNS topic to the alarm to receive notifications when the alarm goes off.","E":"Use the Amazon CloudWatch agent to collect the memory utilization of the EC2 instances in the Auto Scaling group. Create an alarm when the memory utilization is high and associate an Amazon SNS topic to receive a notification."},"options_zh":{"A":"更改自动扩展配置，以便在实例未通过负载均衡器的健康检查时将其替换。","B":"更改目标组的健康检查参数 HealthCheckIntervalSeconds，以缩短健康检查之间的间隔。","C":"将目标组的健康检查从 HTTP 更改为 TCP，以检查应用程序监听的端口是否可达。","D":"在 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板中为整个 Auto Scaling 组启用可用内存使用情况指标。当内存利 用率较高时创建警报。将 Amazon SNS 主题与警报关联，以便在警报触发时接收通知。","E":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 代理收集自动扩展组中 EC2 实例的内存利用率。当内存利用率较高时 创建警报，并关联一个 Amazon SNS 主题以接收通知。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When the application is killed by an OOM event the EC2 instance keeps running, so the default Auto Scaling health check (EC2 status checks, which only verify the instance is running and the hardware/hypervisor is healthy) still passes, even though the ALB target group HTTP health check fails. (A) The fix is to turn on Elastic Load Balancing health checks for the Auto Scaling group; AWS docs state this check type 'must be turned on' and, once enabled, EC2 Auto Scaling uses the load balancer's results to mark the failing instances Unhealthy and automatically replace them, restoring resilience to the memory leak. (E) Memory utilization is not one of the metrics EC2 publishes by default to CloudWatch; the CloudWatch agent docs say the agent's metrics are 'in addition to the metrics enabled by default,' so memory must be collected with the CloudWatch agent. Installing the agent to publish memory utilization, then creating a high-memory alarm tied to an SNS topic, delivers the required proactive monitoring and notification. A plus E give automatic recovery plus alerting.","explanation_zh":"當應用程式因 OOM 事件被終止時，EC2 執行個體仍持續執行，因此 Auto Scaling 預設的健康檢查（EC2 status checks，僅確認執行個體正在執行且底層硬體/hypervisor 正常）仍會通過，即使 ALB target group 的 HTTP health check 失敗。(A) 解法是為 Auto Scaling group 開啟 Elastic Load Balancing health checks；AWS 文件指出此檢查類型「必須手動開啟」，啟用後 EC2 Auto Scaling 會依據負載平衡器的結果，將故障執行個體標記為 Unhealthy 並自動替換，恢復對記憶體洩漏的韌性。(E) 記憶體使用率並非 EC2 預設發佈到 CloudWatch 的指標；CloudWatch agent 文件說明 agent 收集的指標是「在預設啟用指標之外額外提供」，因此記憶體必須由 CloudWatch agent 收集。安裝 agent 發佈記憶體使用率，再建立高記憶體警示並關聯 SNS topic，即可提供所需的主動監控與通知。A 與 E 合併即提供自動復原與警示。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Reducing HealthCheckIntervalSeconds only makes the ALB detect the failure slightly faster; it does nothing on its own because, without enabling ELB health checks in the ASG (Option A), the failing instances are still never replaced (EC2 status checks keep passing). It also provides no monitoring or notification.","why_zh":"縮短 HealthCheckIntervalSeconds 只會讓 ALB 稍微更快偵測到故障；單獨使用毫無作用，因為若未在 ASG 啟用 ELB health checks（選項 A），故障執行個體仍不會被替換（EC2 status checks 持續通過）。它也未提供任何監控或通知。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Changing the health check from HTTP to TCP weakens it: a TCP check only confirms the port is reachable, so it would pass a broken app that still listens but returns errors, masking problems. After an OOM the process is gone anyway, so this does not improve resilience and provides no monitoring or notification.","why_zh":"將健康檢查從 HTTP 改為 TCP 反而削弱檢查：TCP 檢查只確認連接埠可達，故障但仍在監聽卻回傳錯誤的應用程式會被誤判為健康，掩蓋問題。OOM 後行程已消失，因此這無法提升韌性，也未提供監控或通知。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no built-in 'available memory consumption' metric that you can simply enable from a CloudWatch dashboard for EC2; the CloudWatch agent docs state agent metrics are 'in addition to the metrics enabled by default,' meaning memory requires the agent to be installed first. As written this option skips the agent and is technically not achievable; Option E is the correct memory-monitoring approach.","why_zh":"CloudWatch 中並無可直接從儀表板為 EC2「啟用」的內建「可用記憶體消耗」指標；CloudWatch agent 文件說明 agent 指標是「在預設啟用指標之外額外提供」，意即記憶體必須先安裝 agent 才能取得。按其敘述此選項略過了 agent，技術上無法達成；選項 E 才是正確的記憶體監控做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/health-checks-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/attach-load-balancer-asg.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/autoscaling-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/metrics-collected-by-CloudWatch-agent.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":158,"question_en":"An ecommerce company uses a large number of Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) backed Amazon EC2 instances. To decrease manual work across all the instances, a DevOps engineer is tasked with automating restart actions when EC2 instance retirement events are scheduled. How can this be accomplished?","question_zh":"一家电子商务公司使用大量由亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）支持的亚马逊 EC2 实例。为了减少所 有实例上的手动工作，一位 DevOps 工程师被指派在计划 EC2 实例退役事件时自动执行重启操作。 这该如何实现呢？","options_en":{"A":"Create a scheduled Amazon EventBridge rule to run an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook that checks if any EC2 instances are scheduled for retirement once a week. If the instance is scheduled for retirement, the runbook will hibernate the instance.","B":"Enable EC2 Auto Recovery on all of the instances. Create an AWS Config rule to limit the recovery to occur during a maintenance window only.","C":"Reboot all EC2 instances during an approved maintenance window that is outside of standard business hours. Set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms to send a notification in case any instance is failing EC2 instance status checks.","D":"Set up an AWS Health Amazon EventBridge rule to run AWS Systems Manager Automation runbooks that stop and start the EC2 instance when a retirement scheduled event occurs."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个计划的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每周运行一次 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手 册，检查是否有任何 EC2 实例计划退役。如果实例计划退役，该运行手册将使实例进入休眠状态。","B":"在所有实例上启用 EC2 自动恢复功能。创建一条 AWS Config 规则，仅允许在维护窗口期间进行恢 复操作。","C":"在标准工作时间之外的经批准的维护窗口期间重新启动所有 EC2 实例。设置 Amazon CloudWatch 警报， 以便在任何实例未通过 EC2 实例状态检查时发送通知。","D":"设置一个 AWS Health Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在计划退役事件发生时运行 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行本，从而停止和启动 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When an EBS-backed EC2 instance is scheduled for retirement, AWS Health emits the AWS_EC2_PERSISTENT_INSTANCE_RETIREMENT_SCHEDULED event type. The AWS Health User Guide page 'Running operations on EC2 instances automatically in response to events in AWS Health' describes this exact scenario: create an EventBridge rule (source aws.health) that detects this event type and targets an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to automatically stop and start the instance, so you don't perform the action manually. A stop/start migrates the instance to a new healthy host, which is precisely what resolves a retirement; the EC2 docs note this 'is not the same as rebooting the instance.' Because the workflow is event-driven, the action fires exactly when retirement is scheduled. This matches option D.","explanation_zh":"當 EBS 支援的 EC2 執行個體被排定退役時，AWS Health 會發出 AWS_EC2_PERSISTENT_INSTANCE_RETIREMENT_SCHEDULED 事件類型。AWS Health User Guide 的『Running operations on EC2 instances automatically in response to events in AWS Health』頁面描述了完全相同的情境：建立一個 EventBridge 規則（source aws.health）偵測此事件類型，並以 AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook 作為目標，自動 stop 與 start 執行個體，因此無需手動執行。stop/start 會將執行個體遷移到新的健康主機，這正是解決退役所需的動作；EC2 文件也指出這『與 reboot 執行個體不同』。由於整個流程是事件驅動，動作會在退役被排定時精準觸發。這正符合選項 D。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A weekly scheduled EventBridge poll is not event-driven and could lag or miss retirements scheduled within the week. More critically, hibernating the instance does not migrate it off the failing host, so it does not resolve the retirement; a stop/start is required to move to a healthy host.","why_zh":"每週排程的 EventBridge 輪詢並非事件驅動，可能延誤或錯過在該週內排定的退役。更關鍵的是，hibernate 執行個體不會將其從故障主機遷移，因此無法解決退役；需要 stop/start 才能移到健康主機。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"EC2 Auto Recovery responds to system status check failures of the underlying host, not to scheduled retirement events, so it does not proactively act when a retirement is scheduled. AWS Config evaluates resource configuration compliance and cannot gate or restrict a recovery action to a maintenance window, so this design does not work as described.","why_zh":"EC2 Auto Recovery 是針對底層主機的系統狀態檢查失敗作出回應，而非針對排定的退役事件，因此不會在退役被排定時主動採取行動。AWS Config 是評估資源組態合規性，無法將復原動作閘控或限制在維護時段，因此此設計無法如所述運作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Rebooting keeps the instance on the same underlying host, so it does NOT migrate the instance off the failing hardware and does not resolve a retirement (AWS docs explicitly state stop/start is 'not the same as rebooting'). It is also a manual maintenance-window task rather than automation, failing the goal of decreasing manual work.","why_zh":"reboot 會讓執行個體留在同一底層主機，因此不會將其從故障硬體遷移，也無法解決退役（AWS 文件明確指出 stop/start『與 reboot 不同』）。此外它是手動的維護時段作業而非自動化，未達成減少手動工作的目標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/automating-instance-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/schedevents_actions_retire.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/instance-retirement.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":159,"question_en":"A company manages AWS accounts for application teams in AWS Control Tower. Individual application teams are responsible for securing their respective AWS accounts. A DevOps engineer needs to enable Amazon GuardDuty for all AWS accounts in which the application teams have not already enabled GuardDuty. The DevOps engineer is using AWS CloudFormation StackSets from the AWS Control Tower management account. How should the DevOps engineer configure the CloudFormation template to prevent failure during the StackSets deployment?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 控制塔中管理应用程序团队的 AWS 账户。各个应用程序团队负责保护其各自的 AWS 账户的安全。 DevOps 工程师需要为应用团队尚未启用 Amazon GuardDuty 的所有 AWS 账户启用该服务。该 DevOps 工程师正在从 AWS 控制塔管理账户使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets。 DevOps 工程师应如何配置 CloudFormation 模板以防止在 StackSets 部署期间出现故障？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudFormation custom resource that invokes an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to conditionally enable GuardDuty if GuardDuty is not already enabled in the accounts.","B":"Use the Conditions section of the CloudFormation template to enable GuardDuty in accounts where GuardDuty is not already enabled.","C":"Use the CloudFormation Fn::GetAtt intrinsic function to check whether GuardDuty is already enabled. If GuardDuty is not already enabled, use the Resources section of the CloudFormation template to enable GuardDuty.","D":"Manually discover the list of AWS account IDs where GuardDuty is not enabled. Use the CloudFormation Fn::ImportValue intrinsic function to import the list of account IDs into the CloudFormation template to skip deployment for the listed AWS accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 CloudFormation 自定义资源，用于调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数，使 其在账户中尚未启用 GuardDuty 时有条件地启用 GuardDuty。","B":"使用 CloudFormation 模板的“条件”部分，在尚未启用 GuardDuty 的账户中启用 GuardDuty。","C":"使用 CloudFormation 的 Fn::GetAtt 内置函数检查 GuardDuty 是否已启用。如果 GuardDuty 尚未启用， 请在 CloudFormation 模板的 Resources 部分启用它。","D":"手动找出未启用 GuardDuty 的 AWS 账户 ID 列表。使用 CloudFormation 的 Fn:: ImportValue 内置函数将账户 ID 列表导入 CloudFormation 模板，以便跳过对所列 AWS 账户的部署。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"GuardDuty needs to be enabled only once per account and Region (one detector), so deploying an AWS::GuardDuty::Detector with Enable=true via StackSets fails in any account where an application team already enabled GuardDuty. AWS Prescriptive Guidance addresses this exact scenario: 'If you attempt to enable GuardDuty through CloudFormation in an account where it's already active, the stack deployment fails,' and its recommended solution is a CloudFormation custom resource backed by a Lambda function that performs a dynamic state check and enables GuardDuty only if it isn't already enabled. The same doc notes you extend the solution across many accounts/Regions with StackSets - matching the Control Tower management-account deployment described here. Only a Lambda-backed custom resource can query runtime per-account API state (ListDetectors/GetDetector) and act idempotently, so A is correct.","explanation_zh":"GuardDuty 每個帳戶每個區域只需啟用一次（單一 detector），因此透過 StackSets 部署 Enable=true 的 AWS::GuardDuty::Detector 時，在已由應用團隊啟用 GuardDuty 的帳戶中會失敗。AWS Prescriptive Guidance 針對此情境明確說明：『若你嘗試在 GuardDuty 已啟用的帳戶中透過 CloudFormation 啟用它，堆疊部署會失敗』，其建議解法正是使用由 Lambda 函式支援的 CloudFormation custom resource，執行動態狀態檢查，僅在尚未啟用時才啟用 GuardDuty。同份文件也指出可用 StackSets 將此解法擴展到多帳戶／多區域，正符合本題在 Control Tower 管理帳戶部署的情境。只有 Lambda 支援的 custom resource 能查詢執行時各帳戶的 API 狀態（ListDetectors/GetDetector）並以冪等方式運作，因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS docs state plainly that 'traditional CloudFormation conditions support only static value comparisons, which makes it difficult to check the current state of services such as GuardDuty.' Conditions are evaluated at deploy time from static inputs (parameters, mappings, pseudo-parameters) and cannot query whether GuardDuty is already enabled in each target account, so they cannot prevent the per-account creation failure.","why_zh":"AWS 文件明確指出『傳統 CloudFormation conditions 僅支援靜態值比較，難以檢查像 GuardDuty 這類服務的當前狀態』。Conditions 在部署時依靜態輸入（參數、mappings、pseudo-parameters）評估，無法查詢各目標帳戶是否已啟用 GuardDuty，因此無法防止各帳戶的建立失敗。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Fn::GetAtt only returns attributes of resources already defined within the same template (e.g., the Detector's Id); it cannot inspect an account's existing GuardDuty state before the resource is created. There is also no Fn::GetAtt-based 'check then create' branching mechanism, so this option does not prevent the failure.","why_zh":"Fn::GetAtt 只回傳同一範本內已定義資源的屬性（例如 Detector 的 Id），無法在建立資源前檢查帳戶現有的 GuardDuty 狀態；也不存在以 Fn::GetAtt 為基礎的『先檢查再建立』分支機制，因此無法防止失敗。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Fn::ImportValue imports exported Output values from other CloudFormation stacks in the same account and Region, not arbitrary cross-account account-ID lists, and a StackSet cannot selectively skip individual target accounts through an imported value. Manual discovery is not idempotent, defeats automation, and breaks as teams enable/disable GuardDuty over time.","why_zh":"Fn::ImportValue 匯入的是同帳戶同區域其他 CloudFormation 堆疊匯出的 Output 值，並非任意跨帳戶的帳戶 ID 清單，StackSet 也無法透過匯入值選擇性略過個別目標帳戶。手動探查不具冪等性、違反自動化，且當團隊隨時間啟用／停用 GuardDuty 時會失效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/enable-amazon-guardduty-conditionally-by-using-aws-cloudformation-templates.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-guardduty-detector.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-custom-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-custom-resources-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/what-is-cfnstacksets.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":160,"question_en":"A company has an AWS Control Tower landing zone. The company's DevOps team creates a workload OU. A development OU and a production OU are nested under the workload OU. The company grants users full access to the company's AWS accounts to deploy applications. The DevOps team needs to allow only a specific management IAM role to manage the IAM roles and policies of any AWS accounts in only the production OU. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个 AWS 控制塔着陆区。该公司的 DevOps 团队创建了一个工作负载组织单元。开发 组织单元和生产组织单元嵌套在工作负载组织单元之下。该公司授予用户对公司所有 AWS 账户的完 全访问权限，以便部署应用程序。 DevOps 团队需要仅允许特定的管理 IAM 角色在仅生产组织单位中管理任何 AWS 账户的 IAM 角 色和策略。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that denies full access with a condition to exclude the management IAM role for the organization root.","B":"Ensure that the FullAWSAccess SCP is applied at the organization root.","C":"Create an SCP that allows IAM related actions. Attach the SCP to the development OU.","D":"Create an SCP that denies IAM related actions with a condition to exclude the management IAM role. Attach the SCP to the workload OU.","E":"Create an SCP that denies IAM related actions with a condition to exclude the management IAM role. Attach the SCP to the production OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 SCP（安全策略），在拒绝完全访问权限的同时，将组织根目录的管理 IAM 角色排除在外。","B":"确保在组织根目录应用“FullAWSAccess”服务控制策略（SCP）。","C":"创建一个允许执行与 IAM 相关操作的服务控制策略（SCP）。将该 SCP 附加到开发组织单位（OU）。","D":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），该策略在条件中排除管理 IAM 角色的情况下拒绝与 IAM 相关的操作。 将该 SCP 附加到工作负载组织单位（OU）。","E":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），该策略在条件中排除管理 IAM 角色的情况下拒绝与 IAM 相关的操作。 将该 SCP 附加到生产组织单位（OU）。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SCPs follow a deny-by-default model: a permission is allowed only if there is an explicit Allow at every level from the root down to the account, which is why AWS Organizations (and AWS Control Tower) attaches the AWS-managed FullAWSAccess SCP at every level by default. Because users were granted full access to deploy applications, FullAWSAccess must remain applied at the organization root; if the root-level Allow is missing, all member accounts are blocked from every action (B). To restrict IAM role/policy management to only a specific management role in only the production OU, you create a Deny SCP on IAM-related actions with a condition that excludes the management role (for example, aws:PrincipalArn with ArnNotLike) and attach it to the production OU. A Deny attached at any level applies to every account beneath it, so attaching it at the production OU scopes the restriction to production accounts and leaves the development OU unaffected (E). The AWS Organizations SCP evaluation guide's Scenario 4 mirrors this exact two-level structure (Workloads OU with nested Test and Production sub-OUs), keeping FullAWSAccess at root and the OU while applying a targeted Deny only at the specific sub-OU.","explanation_zh":"SCP 採用預設拒絕 (deny-by-default) 模型：只有當從 organization root 一路到帳戶的「每一層」都有明確的 Allow 時，權限才會被允許，這也是 AWS Organizations（以及 AWS Control Tower）預設在每一層都附加 AWS 受管的 FullAWSAccess SCP 的原因。由於使用者被授予部署應用程式的完整存取權，FullAWSAccess 必須持續套用在 organization root；若 root 層缺少 Allow，所有成員帳戶將被封鎖、無法執行任何動作（B）。要將 IAM 角色／政策管理限制為只有特定 management role、且僅限 production OU，你需要建立一個 Deny IAM 相關動作的 SCP，並加上排除該 management role 的 condition（例如 aws:PrincipalArn 搭配 ArnNotLike），再將其附加到 production OU。Deny 在任一層附加後會套用到其下所有帳戶，因此附加在 production OU 可將限制範圍鎖定在 production 帳戶，而不影響 development OU（E）。AWS Organizations SCP 評估指南的 Scenario 4 正好對應這個兩層結構（Workloads OU 下巢狀 Test 與 Production 子 OU），在 root 與 OU 保留 FullAWSAccess，並只在特定子 OU 附加針對性的 Deny。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An SCP that denies full access at the organization root would block every action for all member accounts (except the excluded role), breaking the requirement that users keep full access to deploy applications. It is also scoped to the whole org/root rather than only the production OU, so it cannot satisfy the 'only the production OU' qualifier.","why_zh":"在 organization root 拒絕 full access 的 SCP 會封鎖所有成員帳戶的所有動作（被排除的角色除外），違反使用者須保留完整部署存取權的需求。它的範圍是整個組織／root，而非僅 production OU，因此無法滿足『只限 production OU』的條件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP never grants permissions; it only sets the maximum permission boundary. An Allow SCP on the development OU does nothing to restrict IAM management, and the requirement targets the production OU, not the development OU, so this step is irrelevant.","why_zh":"SCP 從不授予權限，只設定權限上限。在 development OU 套用 Allow SCP 無法限制 IAM 管理，且需求針對的是 production OU 而非 development OU，因此此步驟與目標無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Attaching the Deny SCP to the workload OU applies the restriction to every account beneath it, which includes both the nested development OU and the production OU. This over-restricts development accounts and violates the 'only the production OU' requirement; the Deny must be attached at the production OU instead.","why_zh":"將 Deny SCP 附加到 workload OU 會將限制套用到其下所有帳戶，包含巢狀的 development OU 與 production OU。這會過度限制 development 帳戶，違反『只限 production OU』的需求；Deny 應改附加在 production OU。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":161,"question_en":"A company hired a penetration tester to simulate an internal security breach. The tester performed port scans on the company's Amazon EC2 instances. The company's security measures did not detect the port scans. The company needs a solution that automatically provides notification when port scans are performed on EC2 instances. The company creates and subscribes to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. What should the company do next to meet the requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司聘请了一名渗透测试人员来模拟内部安全漏洞。该测试人员对公司亚马逊 EC2 实例进行了端口扫 描。公司的安全措施并未检测到这些端口扫描。 该公司需要一种解决方案，当有人对 EC2 实例执行端口扫描时能自动发出通知。该公司创建并订阅了一个 亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。 公司接下来应该怎么做才能满足要求？","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that Amazon GuardDuty is enabled. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm for detected EC2 and port scan findings. Connect the alarm to the SNS topic.","B":"Ensure that Amazon Inspector is enabled. Create an Amazon EventBridge event for detected network reachability findings that indicate port scans. Connect the event to the SNS topic.","C":"Ensure that Amazon Inspector is enabled. Create an Amazon EventBridge event for detected CVEs that cause open port vulnerabilities. Connect the event to the SNS topic.","D":"Ensure that AWS CloudTrail is enabled. Create an AWS Lambda function to analyze the CloudTrail logs for unusual amounts of traffic from an IP address range. Connect the Lambda function to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保已启用 Amazon GuardDuty。为检测到的 EC2 和端口扫描发现创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报。 将警报连接到 SNS 主题。","B":"确保已启用 Amazon Inspector。为检测到的表明存在端口扫描的网络可达性发现结果创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件。将该事件连接到 SNS 主题。","C":"确保已启用 Amazon Inspector。为导致开放端口漏洞的检测到的 CVE 创建 Amazon EventBridge 事件。 将该事件连接到 SNS 主题。","D":"确保已启用 AWS CloudTrail。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来分析 CloudTrail 日志，查找来自某个 IP 地址 范围的异常流量。将 Lambda 函数连接到 SNS 主题。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Detecting active port scans against EC2 instances is a job for Amazon GuardDuty, which analyzes VPC Flow Logs of real network traffic and has dedicated reconnaissance/impact finding types such as Recon:EC2/Portscan, Recon:EC2/PortProbeUnprotectedPort, and Impact:EC2/PortSweep. Option A is the only choice that uses GuardDuty, the service that actually detects this behavior, and routes the finding to the existing SNS topic for notification. The wording 'CloudWatch alarm' is loose because GuardDuty findings are published to EventBridge (formerly CloudWatch Events), which then delivers to the SNS topic; but A is still the only technically viable option because every other answer relies on a service that cannot detect active port scans. Inspector (B/C) performs static configuration/CVE assessment and explicitly does not send packets, and CloudTrail (D) records API activity rather than packet-level network traffic. Therefore A is correct by both technical merit and elimination.","explanation_zh":"偵測針對 EC2 instances 的主動 port scan 是 Amazon GuardDuty 的工作。GuardDuty 會分析 VPC Flow Logs 中的實際網路流量，並具有專門的偵察／影響類 finding 類型，例如 Recon:EC2/Portscan、Recon:EC2/PortProbeUnprotectedPort 與 Impact:EC2/PortSweep。選項 A 是唯一使用 GuardDuty（真正能偵測此行為的服務）並將 finding 路由到既有 SNS topic 以發出通知的選項。其中『CloudWatch alarm』的措辭較不精確，因為 GuardDuty findings 實際上是發佈到 EventBridge（前身為 CloudWatch Events），再由其傳遞到 SNS topic；但因其他所有選項所依賴的服務都無法偵測主動 port scan，A 仍是唯一技術上可行的答案。Inspector（B/C）執行的是靜態設定／CVE 評估且明確不送出封包，而 CloudTrail（D）記錄的是 API 活動而非封包層級的網路流量。因此 A 在技術正確性與排除法上皆成立。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector Network Reachability analyzes network configurations (security groups, ACLs, IGWs) to identify reachable ports 'without having to install scanners and send packets.' It reports configuration-based reachability, not active port scans performed against the instances by a penetration tester.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 的 Network Reachability 分析的是網路設定（security groups、ACLs、IGWs）以找出可被存取的 port，且明確是『無需安裝掃描器或送出封包』。它回報的是基於設定的可達性，而非滲透測試人員針對 instance 實際執行的主動 port scan。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector CVE scanning finds known software vulnerabilities and package CVEs, not network reconnaissance activity such as port scans. It does not generate events when an external actor scans ports.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 的 CVE 掃描尋找的是已知軟體漏洞與套件 CVE，而非像 port scan 這類網路偵察活動。當外部行為者掃描 port 時，它不會產生事件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS CloudTrail records AWS API/management-plane activity, not data-plane network traffic. Port scans are packet-level network activity that does not appear in CloudTrail, so a Lambda analyzing CloudTrail logs for 'traffic from an IP range' cannot detect port scans.","why_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API／管理層活動，而非資料層的網路流量。Port scan 屬於封包層級的網路活動，不會出現在 CloudTrail 中，因此用 Lambda 分析 CloudTrail 日誌以偵測『來自某 IP 範圍的流量』無法偵測 port scan。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_finding-types-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_findings_eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty_data-sources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/v1/userguide/inspector_network-reachability.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":162,"question_en":"A company runs applications in an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. The EKS cluster uses an Application Load Balancer to route traffic to the applications that run in the cluster. A new application that was migrated to the EKS cluster is performing poorly. All the other applications in the EKS cluster maintain appropriate operation. The new application scales out horizontally to the preconfigured maximum number of pods immediately upon deployment, before any user traffic routes to the web application. Which solution will resolve the scaling behavior of the web application in the EKS cluster?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群中运行应用程序。该 EKS 集群使用应用负载 均衡器将流量路由到集群中运行的应用程序。 新迁移到 EKS 集群的应用程序运行状况不佳。EKS 集群中的其他所有应用程序均保持正常运行。新应用 程序在部署后立即水平扩展到预配置的最大 Pod 数量，此时还没有任何用户流量路由到该 Web 应用程序。 哪种解决方案可以解决 EKS 集群中网络应用程序的扩展行为问题？","options_en":{"A":"Implement the Horizontal Pod Autoscaler in the EKS cluster.","B":"Implement the Vertical Pod Autoscaler in the EKS cluster.","C":"Implement the Cluster Autoscaler.","D":"Implement the AWS Load Balancer Controller in the EKS cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 EKS 集群中实现水平 Pod 自动缩放器。","B":"在 EKS 集群中实现垂直 Pod 自动缩放器。","C":"实施集群自动扩展器。","D":"在 EKS 集群中部署 AWS 负载均衡器控制器。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The phrase 'scales out horizontally to the preconfigured maximum number of pods' tells you a Horizontal Pod Autoscaler is already configured for this deployment (it has a min/max replica range). The defect is that it fires to max instantly at idle, before any traffic. HPA scales on CPU utilization expressed as a percentage of each pod's resource request (the EKS HPA walkthrough shows targets like '250%/50%', and replicas increase while the actual percentage exceeds the target). If the migrated application's CPU/memory requests are set too low, even baseline idle consumption (startup, runtime warmup, sidecars) computes to a utilization percentage far above the HPA target, so HPA immediately drives replicas to the maximum. The fix is to right-size the pod resource requests, which is exactly what the Vertical Pod Autoscaler does: per AWS docs it 'automatically adjusts the CPU and memory reservations for your Pods to help right size your applications.' With correct requests, HPA's percentage calculation is accurate and the spurious scale-out stops. AWS best-practice guidance explicitly pairs them: use HPA to control replica count and VPA to adjust per-replica requests and limits. The other apps behave normally because they were already sized correctly, so the fix targets the new app's requests (VPA).","explanation_zh":"「水平擴展到預先設定的最大 Pod 數量」這句話代表此 deployment 已配置了 Horizontal Pod Autoscaler（已設有 min/max replica 範圍）。問題在於它在閒置、尚無流量時就立即衝到最大值。HPA 是以 CPU 使用率（表示為每個 Pod resource request 的百分比）來擴展，EKS 的 HPA 範例會顯示如「250%/50%」的目標值，且只要實際百分比高於目標就會持續增加 replica。若遷移過來的應用程式 CPU/記憶體 requests 設得過低，即使只是閒置時的基礎消耗（啟動、runtime 暖機、sidecar）換算出來的使用率百分比也會遠高於 HPA 目標，於是 HPA 立刻把 replica 推到最大。修正方法是正確調整 Pod 的 resource requests，而這正是 Vertical Pod Autoscaler 的功能：依 AWS 文件，VPA「會自動調整 Pod 的 CPU 與記憶體保留量以協助正確調整應用程式大小」。當 requests 正確後，HPA 的百分比計算就準確，誤觸發的擴展也隨之停止。AWS 最佳實務明確將兩者搭配：用 HPA 控制 replica 數量，用 VPA 調整每個 replica 的 requests 與 limits。其他應用程式運作正常是因為它們本來就已正確配置大小，因此修正方向應針對新應用程式的 requests（即 VPA）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An HPA is already present and is the thing misbehaving (it is what produces the 'preconfigured maximum number of pods' and the immediate scale-out). Implementing HPA does not fix an HPA that is already firing incorrectly; the root cause is mis-sized pod resource requests, which HPA cannot correct.","why_zh":"HPA 已存在，且正是出問題的元件（它造成「預先設定的最大 Pod 數量」與瞬間擴展）。實作 HPA 無法修正一個已在誤觸發的 HPA；根本原因是 Pod resource requests 設定錯誤，而 HPA 本身無法修正這一點。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Cluster Autoscaler adjusts the number of worker nodes (EC2 instances) so unschedulable pods can be placed; it does not control how many pod replicas a deployment runs. The problem here is replica-level (pods scaling to max), not node-level capacity, so Cluster Autoscaler does not address the scaling behavior.","why_zh":"Cluster Autoscaler 調整的是 worker node（EC2 執行個體）數量，以便讓無法排程的 Pod 能被放置；它不控制 deployment 要跑幾個 Pod replica。此處問題在 replica 層級（Pod 擴展到最大值）而非節點容量，因此 Cluster Autoscaler 無法解決此擴展行為。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The AWS Load Balancer Controller provisions and manages the ALB for ingress traffic. The cluster already has a working ALB routing traffic, and the runaway scaling occurs before any user traffic arrives, so it is fully decoupled from the load balancer and unrelated to pod replica scaling.","why_zh":"AWS Load Balancer Controller 負責佈建與管理用於 ingress 流量的 ALB。叢集已有正常運作的 ALB 在路由流量，且失控的擴展發生在任何使用者流量到達之前，因此與負載平衡器完全脫鉤，也與 Pod replica 擴展無關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/vertical-pod-autoscaler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/horizontal-pod-autoscaler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/best-practices/cost-opt-compute.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/scaling-amazon-eks-infrastructure/workload-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/autoscaling.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":163,"question_en":"A company has an AWS Control Tower landing zone that manages its organization in AWS Organizations. The company created an OU structure that is based on the company's requirements. The company's DevOps team has established the core accounts for the solution and an account for all centralized AWS CloudFormation and AWS Service Catalog solutions. The company wants to offer a series of customizations that an account can request through AWS Control Tower. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个 AWS 控制塔着陆区，用于管理其在 AWS 组织中的机构。该公司根据自身需求创建了组 织单元（OU）结构。公司的 DevOps 团队为解决方案建立了核心账户，并为所有集中式的 AWS CloudFormation 和 AWS 服务目录解决方案创建了一个账户。 该公司希望提供一系列定制服务，客户可以通过 AWS 控制塔提出请求。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable trusted access for CloudFormation with Organizations by using service-managed permissions.","B":"Create an IAM role that is named AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess. Configure the role with a trust policy that allows the AWSControlTowerAdmin role in the management account to assume the role. Attach the AWSServiceCatalogAdminFullAccess IAM policy to the AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess role.","C":"Create a Service Catalog product for each CloudFormation template.","D":"Create a CloudFormation stack set for each CloudFormation template. Enable automatic deployment for each stack set. Create a CloudFormation stack instance that targets specific OUs.","E":"Deploy the Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) CloudFormation stack.","F":"Create a CloudFormation template that contains the resources for each customization."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过使用服务管理权限，为 CloudFormation 与 Organizations 启用受信任访问。","B":"创建一个名为 AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess 的 IAM 角色。为该角色配置一个信任策略，允许管理 账户中的 AWSControlTowerAdmin 角色承担此角色。将 AWSServiceCatalogAdminFullAccess IAM 策略 附加到 AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess 角色。","C":"为每个 CloudFormation 模板创建一个服务目录产品。","D":"为每个 CloudFormation 模板创建一个 CloudFormation 堆栈集。为每个堆栈集启用自动部署。创建一个 针对特定组织单位的目标 CloudFormation 堆栈实例。","E":"部署 AWS 控制塔自定义配置（CfCT）CloudFormation 堆栈。","F":"创建一个包含每个自定义资源的 CloudFormation 模板。"},"answer":["B","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario describes offering a series of self-service customizations that an account can request through the AWS Control Tower console - this is the Account Factory Customization (AFC) feature, which provisions accounts from AWS Service Catalog products called 'custom blueprints'. The documented one-time setup maps to exactly three steps. (F) Author a CloudFormation template that contains the resources for each customization; this template becomes the account blueprint (the AFC 'Summary of steps to create a blueprint' says to create a CloudFormation template that will become your account blueprint). (C) Create an AWS Service Catalog product from each template - Step 2 of AFC ('Create the AWS Service Catalog product', also called a blueprint product) by uploading the template in the hub account. (B) Step 1 of AFC: create an IAM role named exactly AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess in the hub account, with a trust policy allowing the AWSControlTowerAdmin role in the management account to assume it, and attach the AWSServiceCatalogAdminFullAccess managed policy; Control Tower assumes this role to create the Service Catalog portfolio, add the blueprint product, and share it with the member account during provisioning. The other options describe entirely different mechanisms (CfCT pipeline, StackSets mass deployment, CloudFormation trusted access for service-managed StackSets) that are not the per-account self-service blueprint flow.","explanation_zh":"情境描述的是讓帳戶可以透過 AWS Control Tower 主控台自助請求一系列客製化 - 這正是 Account Factory Customization (AFC) 功能,它使用稱為「custom blueprints」的 AWS Service Catalog 產品來佈建帳戶。官方記載的一次性設定恰好對應三個步驟。(F) 撰寫一個包含每項客製化資源的 CloudFormation 範本,此範本即成為帳戶 blueprint(AFC 的「建立 blueprint 的步驟摘要」說明要建立一個將成為帳戶 blueprint 的 CloudFormation 範本)。(C) 由每個範本建立一個 AWS Service Catalog 產品 - 即 AFC 的 Step 2(「建立 AWS Service Catalog 產品」,又稱 blueprint product),在 hub account 中上傳範本。(B) AFC 的 Step 1:在 hub account 中建立名稱必須為 AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess 的 IAM role,設定信任政策允許 management account 中的 AWSControlTowerAdmin role assume 此角色,並附加 AWSServiceCatalogAdminFullAccess 受管政策;Control Tower 會 assume 此角色以建立 Service Catalog portfolio、加入 blueprint product,並在佈建期間與成員帳戶共享。其餘選項描述的是完全不同的機制(CfCT pipeline、StackSets 大量部署、為 service-managed StackSets 啟用 CloudFormation trusted access),並非逐帳戶自助 blueprint 流程。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Enabling trusted access for CloudFormation with Organizations (service-managed permissions) is required for service-managed StackSets that deploy across the org, not for AFC blueprints. AFC relies on the AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess role plus an AWS Service Catalog product, and does not require enabling CloudFormation trusted access.","why_zh":"為 CloudFormation 與 Organizations 啟用 trusted access(service-managed permissions)是 service-managed StackSets 跨組織部署所需,而非 AFC blueprint 所需。AFC 依賴 AWSControlTowerBlueprintAccess role 加上 AWS Service Catalog 產品,不需啟用 CloudFormation trusted access。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating a StackSet per template with auto-deployment and stack instances targeting OUs is a push-based mass-deployment mechanism that applies resources to whole OUs automatically. It is not the per-account, on-request self-service model the question requires, which is delivered via Service Catalog blueprints chosen during account creation in Account Factory.","why_zh":"為每個範本建立 StackSet 並啟用自動部署、以 stack instance 鎖定 OU,是一種推送式大量部署機制,會自動將資源套用至整個 OU。這不是題目要求的逐帳戶、依請求的自助模式;後者是在 Account Factory 建立帳戶時透過選擇 Service Catalog blueprint 來提供。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) is a separate solution that uses a CodePipeline-based framework with a manifest file to deploy CloudFormation stacks/SCPs to accounts and OUs after account lifecycle events. It is not the native console-based AFC blueprint flow that lets an account request a customization, and it adds pipeline maintenance the AFC setup explicitly avoids.","why_zh":"Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) 是另一套獨立解決方案,使用以 CodePipeline 為基礎的框架搭配 manifest 檔案,在帳戶生命週期事件後將 CloudFormation stacks/SCP 部署到帳戶與 OU。這不是讓帳戶請求客製化的原生主控台 AFC blueprint 流程,並會增加 AFC 設定明確要避免的 pipeline 維護工作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/afc-setup-steps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/step-1-create-blueprint-access-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/step-2-create-blueprint-product.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/service-catalog.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/methods-of-provisioning.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":164,"question_en":"A company runs a workload on Amazon EC2 instances. The company needs a control that requires the use of Instance Metadata Service Version 2 (IMDSv2) on all EC2 instances in the AWS account. If an EC2 instance does not prevent the use of Instance Metadata Service Version 1 (IMDSv1), the EC2 instance must be terminated. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行工作负载。该公司需要一种控制措施，要求其 AWS 账户中的所有 EC2 实例都必须使用实例元数据服务版本 2（IMDSv2）。如果某个 EC2 实例未禁止使用实例元数据服务版本 1 （IMDSv1），则必须终止该 EC2 实例。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set up AWS Config in the account. Use a managed rule to check EC2 instances. Configure the rule to remediate the findings by using AWS Systems Manager Automation to terminate the instance.","B":"Create a permissions boundary that prevents the ec2:RunInstance action if the ec2:MetadataHttpTokens condition key is not set to a value of required. Attach the permissions boundary to the IAM role that was used to launch the instance.","C":"Set up Amazon Inspector in the account. Configure Amazon Inspector to activate deep inspection for EC2 instances. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for an Inspector2 finding. Set an AWS Lambda function as the target to terminate the instance.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for the EC2 instance launch successful event. Send the event to an AWS Lambda function to inspect the EC2 metadata and to terminate the instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"在账户中设置 AWS Config。使用托管规则检查 EC2 实例。配置该规则，通过使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 终止实例来修复发现的问题。","B":"创建一个权限边界，如果 ec2:MetadataHttpTokens 条件键未设置为 required 值，则阻止 ec2: RunInstance 操作。将该权限边界附加到用于启动实例的 IAM 角色上。","C":"在账户中设置 Amazon Inspector。配置 Amazon Inspector 以对 EC2 实例启用深度检查。为 Inspector2 找 到的问题创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将 AWS Lambda 函数设置为目标以终止实例。","D":"为 EC2 实例启动成功的事件创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将该事件发送到一个 AWS Lambda 函 数，以检查 EC2 元数据并终止该实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a detective control across ALL EC2 instances in the account that must terminate any instance still permitting IMDSv1. AWS Config provides the managed rule ec2-imdsv2-check, which evaluates AWS::EC2::Instance resources and marks an instance NON_COMPLIANT when HttpTokens is set to 'optional' (IMDSv1 still allowed). AWS Config auto-remediation associates a Systems Manager Automation document with the rule (via PutRemediationConfigurations) and can pass the non-compliant resource ID; the AWS-managed runbook AWS-TerminateEC2Instance accepts an InstanceId and terminates the instance. This combination satisfies both the 'require IMDSv2 on all instances' detection and the 'terminate the instance' remediation, so A is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求是一個涵蓋帳戶中『所有』EC2 執行個體的偵測型控制 (detective control)，並且要終止任何仍允許 IMDSv1 的執行個體。AWS Config 提供受管規則 ec2-imdsv2-check，它會評估 AWS::EC2::Instance 資源，當 HttpTokens 設為 'optional'（即仍允許 IMDSv1）時將執行個體標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。AWS Config 自動修復 (auto-remediation) 會透過 PutRemediationConfigurations 將 Systems Manager Automation 文件關聯到該規則，並可傳入不合規資源的 resource ID；AWS 受管 runbook AWS-TerminateEC2Instance 接受 InstanceId 並終止該執行個體。此組合同時滿足『要求所有執行個體使用 IMDSv2』的偵測與『終止執行個體』的修復需求，因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A permissions boundary using ec2:MetadataHttpTokens on RunInstances is a PREVENTIVE guardrail that blocks launching non-compliant instances; it never terminates an existing instance, so it fails the explicit 'must be terminated' requirement. It also only affects launches made via that one role, not all existing EC2 instances in the account (it references the action as ec2:RunInstance, but the real action is ec2:RunInstances).","why_zh":"在 RunInstances 上使用 ec2:MetadataHttpTokens 的 permissions boundary 屬於『預防型』(preventive) 護欄，會阻擋啟動不合規執行個體，但永遠不會終止既有執行個體，因此無法滿足明確的『必須終止』需求。它也僅影響透過該角色的啟動，而非帳戶中所有既有的 EC2 執行個體（選項寫成 ec2:RunInstance，實際動作為 ec2:RunInstances）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector deep inspection scans EC2 instances for software/package (CVE) vulnerabilities; it does not evaluate IMDS configuration (HttpTokens optional vs required). There is no Inspector2 finding type for IMDSv1 usage, so the EventBridge rule and Lambda termination would never be triggered for this control.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector deep inspection 掃描 EC2 執行個體的軟體/套件 (CVE) 弱點，並不會評估 IMDS 設定（HttpTokens optional 或 required）。沒有針對 IMDSv1 使用的 Inspector2 finding 類型，因此 EventBridge 規則與 Lambda 終止動作永遠不會因此控制被觸發。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EventBridge rule on an instance launch event with a Lambda only inspects newly launched instances at launch time. It does not evaluate ALL existing instances in the account, failing the required scope, and it is a brittle custom build compared with the purpose-built AWS Config managed rule plus SSM remediation that evaluates the entire resource inventory.","why_zh":"在執行個體啟動事件上的 EventBridge 規則加 Lambda，僅在啟動時檢查新啟動的執行個體。它無法評估帳戶中『所有』既有執行個體，不符合需求範圍；相較於專用的 AWS Config 受管規則加 SSM 修復（會評估整個資源清單），這是脆弱的自製方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/ec2-imdsv2-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-aws-terminateec2instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/instance-metadata-transition-to-version-2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/deep-inspection.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":165,"question_en":"A company builds an application that uses an Application Load Balancer in front of Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The application is stateless. The Auto Scaling group uses a custom AMI that is fully prebuilt. The EC2 instances do not have a custom bootstrapping process. The AMI that the Auto Scaling group uses was recently deleted. The Auto Scaling group's scaling activities show failures because the AMI ID does not exist. Which combination of steps should a DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司构建了一个应用程序，该程序在 Amazon EC2 实例前使用应用负载均衡器，这些实例位于一个自动 扩展组中。该应用程序是无状态的。自动扩展组使用自定义 AMI。 这是完全预构建好的。EC2 实例没有自定义的引导过程。 自动扩展组使用的 AMI 最近已被删除。由于 AMI ID 不存在，自动扩展组的扩展活动显示失败。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new launch template that uses the new AMI.","B":"Update the Auto Scaling group to use the new launch template.","C":"Reduce the Auto Scaling group's desired capacity to 0.","D":"Increase the Auto Scaling group's desired capacity by 1.","E":"Create a new AMI from a running EC2 instance in the Auto Scaling group.","F":"Create a new AMI by copying the most recent public AMI of the operating system that the EC2 instances use."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个使用新 AMI 的新启动模板。","B":"更新自动扩展组以使用新的启动模板。","C":"将自动扩展组的期望容量减少至 0。","D":"将自动扩展组的期望容量增加 1。","E":"从自动扩展组中的运行中的 EC2 实例创建一个新的 AMI。","F":"通过复制 EC2 实例所使用的操作系统的最新公共 AMI 来创建一个新的 AMI。"},"answer":["A","B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The custom AMI is fully prebuilt and the instances have NO bootstrapping process, so 100% of the customization lives only inside the AMI image. The instances currently running in the Auto Scaling group were launched from the now-deleted AMI, so they are the ONLY surviving copy of that prebuilt configuration. The correct, lossless recovery is: (E) create a new EBS-backed AMI from one of the running instances in the group, which captures the customized root volume exactly; (A) create a new launch template that references the new AMI ID, because a launch template stores the AMI ID and there is no existing template that points at a valid image; and (B) update the Auto Scaling group to use that new launch template so subsequent scaling activities reference a valid AMI and succeed. This restores scaling without losing any custom configuration.","explanation_zh":"此 custom AMI 是完全預先建置的，而且執行個體沒有任何 bootstrapping 流程，因此所有客製化內容只存在於 AMI 映像中。Auto Scaling group 內目前正在執行的執行個體是從現已刪除的 AMI 啟動的，所以它們是該預先建置設定的唯一倖存副本。正確且不遺失資料的復原方式是：(E) 從群組中一個正在執行的執行個體建立新的 EBS-backed AMI，精確擷取已客製化的根磁碟區；(A) 建立新的 launch template 並參照新的 AMI ID，因為 launch template 會儲存 AMI ID，而目前沒有任何指向有效映像的 template；(B) 更新 Auto Scaling group 以使用該新 launch template，使後續的擴展活動參照有效 AMI 並成功。如此可在不遺失任何 custom 設定的情況下恢復擴展功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Reducing desired capacity to 0 would terminate the currently running instances, which are the ONLY remaining source of the prebuilt custom configuration (the AMI is deleted and there is no bootstrapping). This destroys the very data needed to recreate the AMI and would make recovery impossible.","why_zh":"將 desired capacity 降為 0 會終止目前正在執行的執行個體，而這些執行個體是預先建置 custom 設定的唯一剩餘來源（AMI 已刪除且無 bootstrapping）。這會摧毀重建 AMI 所需的資料，使復原無法進行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Increasing desired capacity by 1 only triggers another launch attempt that still references the missing AMI ID, producing the same failure. It does nothing to fix the root cause (the deleted AMI / broken launch template) and is not a required recovery step.","why_zh":"將 desired capacity 增加 1 只會觸發另一次仍參照缺失 AMI ID 的啟動嘗試，造成相同的失敗。它無法解決根本原因（已刪除的 AMI／失效的 launch template），也非必要的復原步驟。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Copying the most recent public OS AMI produces a generic, vanilla image WITHOUT the company's prebuilt application and customizations. Because there is no bootstrapping process to re-apply configuration at launch, instances from this AMI would not run the application correctly.","why_zh":"複製最新的公開 OS AMI 會得到一個通用的原始映像，不含公司預先建置的應用程式與客製化內容。由於沒有 bootstrapping 流程在啟動時重新套用設定，從此 AMI 啟動的執行個體無法正確執行應用程式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/creating-an-ami-ebs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/create-launch-template.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/update-auto-scaling-group.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ts-as-instancelaunchfailure.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":166,"question_en":"A company deploys a web application on Amazon EC2 instances that are behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The company stores the application code in an AWS CodeCommit repository. When code is merged to the main branch, an AWS Lambda function invokes an AWS CodeBuild project. The CodeBuild project packages the code, stores the packaged code in AWS CodeArtifact, and invokes AWS Systems Manager Run Command to deploy the packaged code to the EC2 instances. Previous deployments have resulted in defects, EC2 instances that are not running the latest version of the packaged code, and inconsistencies between instances. Which combination of actions should a DevOps engineer take to implement a more reliable deployment solution? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例上部署了一个网络应用程序，这些实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。 该公司将应用程序代码存储在 AWS CodeCommit 存储库中。当代码合并到主分支时，一个 AWS Lambda 函数会调用 AWS CodeBuild 项目。CodeBuild 项目对代码进行打包，将打包后的代码存储在 AWS CodeArtifact 中，并调用 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 将打包后的代码部署到 EC2 实例上。 之前的部署导致了缺陷，EC2 实例未运行打包代码的最新版本，以及各实例之间存在不一致的情况。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪两种行动组合来实现更可靠的部署方案？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline that uses the CodeCommit repository as a source provider. Configure pipeline stages that run the CodeBuild project in parallel to build and test the application. In the pipeline, pass the CodeBuild project output artifact to an AWS CodeDeploy action.","B":"Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline that uses the CodeCommit repository as a source provider. Create separate pipeline stages that run a CodeBuild project to build and then test the application. In the pipeline, pass the CodeBuild project output artifact to an AWS CodeDeploy action.","C":"Create an AWS CodeDeploy application and a deployment group to deploy the packaged code to the EC2 instances. Configure the ALB for the deployment group.","D":"Create individual Lambda functions that use AWS CodeDeploy instead of Systems Manager to run build, test, and deploy actions.","E":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Modify the CodeBuild project to store the packages in the S3 bucket instead of in CodeArtifact. Use deploy actions in CodeDeploy to deploy the artifact to the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个管道，将 CodeCommit 存储库用作源提供程序。配置管道阶段，使 CodeBuild 项目并行运行以构建和测试应用程序。在管道中，将 CodeBuild 项目的输出工件传递给 AWS CodeDeploy 操作。","B":"在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个流水线，将 CodeCommit 存储库用作源提供程序。创建单独的流水 线阶段，运行 CodeBuild 项目来构建应用程序，然后对其进行测试。在流水线中，将 CodeBuild 项 目的输出工件传递给 AWS CodeDeploy 操作。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序和一个部署组，将打包的代码部署到 EC2 实例上。为部署组配 置应用负载均衡器（ALB）。","D":"创建单独的 Lambda 函数，使用 AWS CodeDeploy 而不是 Systems Manager 来执行构建、测试和部 署操作。","E":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。修改 CodeBuild 项目，将软件包存储在 S3 存储桶中，而非 CodeArtifact 中。使用 CodeDeploy 中的部署操作将软件包部署到 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The three reported failures map to two root causes: defects reach production because there is no test gate, and instances drift apart / miss the latest revision because SSM Run Command has no deployment orchestration, no per-instance health tracking, no automatic rollback, and no guarantee that every instance receives the same revision. Option B builds a CodePipeline with a CodeCommit source and SEPARATE sequential stages that build and then test the application before passing the output artifact to a CodeDeploy action; the CodeBuild action reference confirms CodeBuild can act as a dedicated Test-category action, so the test stage catches defects before deploy. Option C creates a CodeDeploy application and deployment group and configures the ALB for it; the CodeDeploy docs confirm that EC2/On-Premises in-place deployments perform a controlled rolling update, track application health according to configured rules, support automatic and manual stop/roll back, and integrate with Elastic Load Balancing so the ALB deregisters and re-registers instances to manage traffic during the deployment. Together B and C guarantee every instance ends up on the same latest revision and that bad revisions are caught (test stage) or rolled back. The verdict matches the dump's suggested answer ['B','C'].","explanation_zh":"三個回報的故障對應到兩個根本原因：缺陷流入生產環境是因為沒有測試關卡；而執行個體之間漂移、未取得最新修訂版本，是因為 SSM Run Command 沒有部署編排、沒有逐一執行個體的健康追蹤、沒有自動回滾，也無法保證每個執行個體都收到相同的修訂版本。選項 B 建立以 CodeCommit 為來源的 CodePipeline，並使用「分開且循序」的階段先建置再測試，最後把產出物交給 CodeDeploy 動作；CodeBuild action reference 確認 CodeBuild 可作為專屬的 Test 類別動作，因此測試階段能在部署前攔截缺陷。選項 C 建立 CodeDeploy 應用程式與部署群組並為其設定 ALB；CodeDeploy 文件確認 EC2/On-Premises 就地（in-place）部署會執行受控的滾動更新、依設定規則追蹤應用程式健康狀態、支援自動與手動停止/回滾，並與 Elastic Load Balancing 整合，讓 ALB 在部署期間取消註冊與重新註冊執行個體以管理流量。B 與 C 一起確保每個執行個體最終都執行相同的最新修訂版本，且不良版本能被攔截（測試階段）或回滾。此判定與 dump 建議答案『B』『C』一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Running the build and test CodeBuild projects IN PARALLEL is illogical: tests run against the build output, so they cannot execute before the build completes. Tests must run in a stage that follows the build stage, which is exactly what B specifies.","why_zh":"讓建置與測試的 CodeBuild 專案『平行』執行不合邏輯：測試是針對建置產出物執行的，因此在建置完成前無法執行。測試必須在建置階段之後的階段執行，這正是 B 所描述的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using individual Lambda functions to invoke CodeDeploy for build, test, and deploy keeps the same fragile, hand-rolled Lambda orchestration that caused the original problems. CodeDeploy is a deployment service, not a build or test runner, and CodePipeline is the AWS-native orchestration layer for sequencing these stages.","why_zh":"用個別 Lambda 函式去呼叫 CodeDeploy 來執行建置、測試與部署，仍維持了當初造成問題的脆弱自訂 Lambda 編排。CodeDeploy 是部署服務，並非建置或測試執行器，而 CodePipeline 才是用來排序這些階段的 AWS 原生編排層。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Swapping CodeArtifact for an S3 bucket does not address the root causes (no testing gate and no managed, health-tracked, rollback-capable deployment orchestration). The artifact storage location never caused the defects or instance inconsistency, and E provides no test stage. Although CodeDeploy can pull artifacts from S3, B+C already solve the problem regardless of where the package is stored, so this change is unnecessary.","why_zh":"把 CodeArtifact 換成 S3 儲存貯體並未解決根本原因（沒有測試關卡、缺少受管且具健康追蹤與回滾能力的部署編排）。產出物儲存位置從來不是造成缺陷或執行個體不一致的原因，且 E 也未提供測試階段。雖然 CodeDeploy 可從 S3 取得產出物，但不論套件存放於何處，B+C 已能解決問題，因此此變更並非必要。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-elastic-load-balancing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-create-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CodeBuild.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pipeline.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":167,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company's automation account contains a CI/CD pipeline that creates and configures new AWS accounts. The company has a group of internal service teams that provide services to accounts in the organization. The service teams operate out of a set of services accounts. The service teams want to receive an AWS CloudTrail event in their services accounts when the CreateAccount API call creates a new account. How should the company share this CloudTrail event with the service accounts?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的组织来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司的自动化账户包含一个 CI/ CD 管道，用于创建和配置新的 AWS 账户。 该公司拥有一批内部服务团队，为组织内的账户提供服务。这些服务团队通过一组服务账户开展工作。 服务团队希望在通过 CreateAccount API 调用创建新账户时，在其服务账户中收到 AWS CloudTrail 事件。 公司应如何将此 CloudTrail 事件与服务账户共享？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule in the automation account to send account creation events to the default event bus in the services accounts. Update the default event bus in the services accounts to allow events from the automation account.","B":"Create a custom Amazon EventBridge event bus in the services accounts. Update the custom event bus to allow events from the automation account. Create an EventBridge rule in the services account that directly listens to CloudTrail events from the automation account.","C":"Create a custom Amazon EventBridge event bus in the automation account and the services accounts. Create an EventBridge rule and policy that connects the custom event buses that are in the automation account and the services accounts.","D":"Create a custom Amazon EventBridge event bus in the automation account. Create an EventBridge rule and policy that connects the custom event bus to the default event buses in the services accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"在自动化账户中创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，将账户创建事件发送到服务账户中的默认事件 总线。更新服务账户中的默认事件总线，以允许来自自动化账户的事件。","B":"在服务账户中创建一个自定义的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。更新自定义事件总线以允许来自自 动化账户的事件。在服务账户中创建一个 EventBridge 规则，直接监听来自自动化账户的 CloudTrail 事件。","C":"在自动化账户和服务账户中创建自定义的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。创建一个 EventBridge 规则 和策略，将自动化账户和服务账户中的自定义事件总线连接起来。","D":"在自动化账户中创建一个自定义的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线。创建一个 EventBridge 规则和策略， 将自定义事件总线连接到服务账户中的默认事件总线。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS docs state that CloudTrail sends 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' events (which is how a CreateAccount call appears) to the DEFAULT EventBridge event bus in the account where the API call occurred (here, the automation account). The canonical cross-account pattern is: on the SENDER (automation) account, create a rule whose target is the receiver account's event bus; on the RECEIVER (services) account, edit the event bus resource-based policy to allow events:PutEvents from the sender account. The docs explicitly note 'The default event bus accepts events from AWS services, other authorized AWS accounts, and PutEvents calls,' and the example cross-account policy grants PutEvents on event-bus/default to the sender account. Option A implements exactly this: an EventBridge rule in the automation account forwards account-creation events to each services account's default event bus, and each services account updates its default bus policy to allow the automation account. No custom bus is required, and the services teams can then write rules on their own default bus to react.","explanation_zh":"AWS 文件指出 CloudTrail 會將 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' 事件 (CreateAccount 呼叫即以此形式呈現) 傳遞到「發生該 API 呼叫之帳戶」(此處為 automation 帳戶) 的「預設」EventBridge event bus。標準的跨帳戶模式是：在「發送端」(automation) 帳戶建立一條 rule，其 target 為接收端帳戶的 event bus；在「接收端」(services) 帳戶編輯 event bus 的 resource-based policy，允許來自發送端帳戶的 events:PutEvents。文件明確說明『default event bus 接受來自 AWS 服務、其他已授權 AWS 帳戶與 PutEvents 呼叫的事件』，且跨帳戶範例 policy 即是在 event-bus/default 上授予發送端帳戶 PutEvents 權限。選項 A 正是如此實作：在 automation 帳戶建立 EventBridge rule，將帳戶建立事件轉發至各 services 帳戶的 default event bus，並由各 services 帳戶更新其 default bus policy 以允許 automation 帳戶。不需要 custom bus，services 團隊接著可在自己的 default bus 上建立 rule 來回應。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A rule cannot directly listen to another account's CloudTrail events. The CreateAccount event lands on the default bus in the account where the API call happened (automation account); the services account must first RECEIVE the forwarded events on its own bus before a rule can match them. This option omits the forwarding rule in the automation account, so events never reach the services account's bus.","why_zh":"rule 無法直接監聽另一個帳戶的 CloudTrail 事件。CreateAccount 事件會落在發生 API 呼叫之帳戶 (automation) 的 default bus 上；services 帳戶必須先在自己的 bus「接收」轉發過來的事件，rule 才能比對。此選項缺少 automation 帳戶端的轉發 rule，事件因此永遠到不了 services 帳戶的 bus。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating custom event buses in both accounts is unnecessary complexity. The CreateAccount CloudTrail event arrives on the automation account's DEFAULT bus, not a custom bus, so a custom bus there receives nothing without an extra forwarding rule. 'A rule and policy that connects' two custom buses is vague and adds hops with no benefit over the standard default-bus forwarding pattern in A.","why_zh":"在兩個帳戶都建立 custom event bus 是不必要的複雜化。CreateAccount 的 CloudTrail 事件會抵達 automation 帳戶的 default bus 而非 custom bus，因此若無額外轉發 rule，該 custom bus 收不到任何東西。『以 rule 與 policy 連接』兩個 custom bus 的說法含糊，且相較選項 A 標準的 default-bus 轉發模式只是徒增環節而無益處。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It introduces a custom bus in the automation account that the CloudTrail event does not flow to (CloudTrail delivers to the default bus), so an extra hop would be needed just to populate that custom bus. It is more complex than Option A while achieving the same result, and the receiver-side permission step is folded into a vague 'policy that connects.'","why_zh":"它在 automation 帳戶引入一個 CloudTrail 事件不會流經的 custom bus (CloudTrail 傳遞至 default bus)，因此光是把事件送進該 custom bus 就需要額外環節。相較選項 A 更複雜卻達成相同結果，且接收端的授權步驟被含糊地塞進『連接的 policy』中。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-event-bus-example-policy-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-event-bus-perms.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":168,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is building a solution that uses Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queues. The solution also includes an AWS Lambda function and an Amazon DynamoDB table. The Lambda function pulls content from an SQS queue event source and writes the content to the DynamoDB table. The solution must maximize the scalability of Lambda and must prevent successfully processed SQS messages from being processed multiple times. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在构建一个解决方案，该方案使用亚马逊简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）标准队 列。该解决方案还包括一个 AWS Lambda 函数和一个亚马逊 DynamoDB 表。Lambda 函数从 SQS 队列 事件源中提取内容，并将内容写入 DynamoDB 表。 该解决方案必须最大限度地提高 Lambda 的可扩展性，并且必须防止已成功处理的 SQS 消息被多 次处理。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Decrease the batch window to 1 second when configuring the Lambda function's event source mapping.","B":"Decrease the batch size to 1 when configuring the Lambda function's event source mapping.","C":"Include the ReportBatchItemFailures value in the FunctionResponseTypes list in the Lambda function's event source mapping.","D":"Set the queue visibility timeout on the Lambda function's event source mapping to account for invocation throttling of the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"在配置 Lambda 函数的事件源映射时，将批处理窗口缩短至 1 秒。","B":"在配置 Lambda 函数的事件源映射时，将批处理大小减少到 1。","C":"在 Lambda 函数的事件源映射中的 FunctionResponseTypes 列表中包含 ReportBatchItemFailures 值。","D":"将 Lambda 函数事件源映射中的队列可见性超时设置为考虑 Lambda 函数的调用节流情况。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: maximize Lambda scalability AND prevent successfully processed SQS messages from being processed again. By default, when a Lambda invocation errors on any message in a batch, the ENTIRE batch (including messages Lambda already processed successfully) becomes visible in the queue again after the visibility timeout, so those successful messages get reprocessed. Adding ReportBatchItemFailures to the event source mapping's FunctionResponseTypes turns on partial batch responses: the function returns a batchItemFailures list containing only the IDs of the failed messages, so only those reappear while the successful messages are deleted. The AWS docs also state that 'When ReportBatchItemFailures is activated, Lambda doesn't scale down message polling when function invocations fail,' which preserves throughput and scalability. Option C is therefore the only choice that satisfies both requirements simultaneously.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩部分:最大化 Lambda 的可擴展性,以及防止已成功處理的 SQS 訊息被重複處理。預設情況下,當 Lambda 叫用在批次中任一訊息發生錯誤時,整個批次(包括 Lambda 已成功處理的訊息)會在 visibility timeout 後重新變為可見,因此這些成功的訊息會被重複處理。在 event source mapping 的 FunctionResponseTypes 中加入 ReportBatchItemFailures 可啟用 partial batch responses:函式回傳的 batchItemFailures 清單只包含失敗訊息的 ID,因此只有失敗的訊息會重新出現,成功的訊息會被刪除。AWS 文件也指出『當啟用 ReportBatchItemFailures 時,Lambda 在函式叫用失敗時不會縮減訊息輪詢(does not scale down message polling)』,這維持了吞吐量與可擴展性。因此選項 C 是唯一同時滿足兩項需求的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Decreasing the batch window to 1 second only affects how long Lambda waits to gather records before invoking (a latency/batching tuning). It does not stop successfully processed messages in a failed batch from being made visible and reprocessed, nor does it maximize scalability.","why_zh":"將 batch window 降為 1 秒只影響 Lambda 收集記錄後叫用前的等待時間(屬於延遲/批次調校)。它無法阻止失敗批次中已成功處理的訊息重新變為可見並被重複處理,也無法最大化可擴展性。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Setting batch size to 1 means each invocation handles one message, so a failure cannot affect already-successful messages; but it drastically reduces throughput and forces far more invocations and polling per message, directly contradicting the requirement to maximize scalability. It fails the first requirement.","why_zh":"將 batch size 設為 1 代表每次叫用只處理一則訊息,失敗不會影響已成功的訊息;但這會大幅降低吞吐量,並使每則訊息產生更多叫用與輪詢,直接違反『最大化可擴展性』的需求,無法滿足第一項要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Visibility timeout is a property of the SQS queue, not a setting on the Lambda event source mapping, and it only controls how long a message stays hidden after being received. Tuning it for throttling does not prevent successfully processed messages within a failed batch from reappearing and being reprocessed, and it does not improve scalability.","why_zh":"Visibility timeout 是 SQS 佇列的屬性,而非 Lambda event source mapping 上的設定,且它只控制訊息被接收後隱藏多久。為節流(throttling)調整它並無法防止失敗批次中已成功處理的訊息重新出現並被重複處理,也無法提升可擴展性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-errorhandling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/api/API_UpdateEventSourceMapping.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":169,"question_en":"A company has a new AWS account that teams will use to deploy various applications. The teams will create many Amazon S3 buckets for application-specific purposes and to store AWS CloudTrail logs. The company has enabled Amazon Macie for the account. A DevOps engineer needs to optimize the Macie costs for the account without compromising the account's functionality. Which solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司新创建了一个 AWS 账户，各团队将使用该账户部署各种应用程序。团队会为特定的应用程序 目的以及存储 AWS CloudTrail 日志创建许多 Amazon S3 存储桶。该公司已为该账户启用 Amazon Macie。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要在不影响账户功能的前提下优化 Macie 的成本。 哪些解决方案能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Exclude S3 buckets that contain CloudTrail logs from automated discovery.","B":"Exclude S3 buckets that have public read access from automated discovery.","C":"Configure scheduled daily discovery jobs for all S3 buckets in the account.","D":"Configure discovery jobs to include S3 objects based on the last modified criterion.","E":"Configure discovery jobs to include S3 objects that are tagged as production only."},"options_zh":{"A":"将包含 CloudTrail 日志的 S3 存储桶排除在自动发现之外。","B":"将具有公共读取访问权限的 S3 存储桶排除在自动发现之外。","C":"为账户中的所有 S3 存储桶配置每日计划的发现任务。","D":"配置发现任务，使其基于“上次修改”标准包含 S3 对象。","E":"配置发现任务，使其仅包含标记为“生产专用”的 S3 对象。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon Macie pricing is based partly on the amount of data that Macie analyzes during sensitive data discovery, so cost is optimized by reducing the volume of data inspected without dropping coverage of buckets that could hold sensitive data. (A) The Macie documentation explicitly gives 'AWS CloudTrail event logs' as the canonical example of buckets to exclude from automated sensitive data discovery; CloudTrail logs are structured AWS service logs, not the personal/sensitive data Macie detects, so excluding them cuts analyzed bytes (and cost) while still protecting buckets that matter. (D) Discovery jobs support an S3 object criterion based on the 'Last modified' date, letting Macie analyze only objects created or changed within a window (and periodic jobs already analyze only new or changed objects each run); this directly reduces inspected bytes and cost while still covering all buckets. The wrong choices either increase cost or compromise functionality: B and E skip buckets/objects that could legitimately contain sensitive data, and C runs full daily scans of every bucket, maximizing cost.","explanation_zh":"Amazon Macie 的計費部分取決於敏感資料探索所分析的資料量，因此最佳化成本的方法是減少被檢測的資料量，同時不放棄對可能含有敏感資料之 bucket 的涵蓋。(A) Macie 文件明確以「AWS CloudTrail event logs」作為應從 automated sensitive data discovery 中排除的標準範例；CloudTrail 日誌是結構化的 AWS 服務日誌，並非 Macie 偵測的個人/敏感資料，因此排除它們可減少被分析的位元組（與成本），同時仍保護重要的 bucket。(D) Discovery jobs 支援以「Last modified」日期為基礎的 S3 object criterion，可讓 Macie 僅分析在特定時間範圍內建立或變更的物件（且 periodic jobs 每次執行本就只分析新增或變更的物件）；這直接減少被檢測的位元組與成本，同時仍涵蓋所有 bucket。其餘錯誤選項不是提高成本就是損及功能：B 與 E 會跳過可能合法含有敏感資料的 bucket/物件，而 C 對每個 bucket 進行每日完整掃描，反而使成本最大化。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Public-read access is a security signal, not a cost lever. Excluding public buckets from discovery skips exactly the buckets most likely to expose sensitive data, compromising functionality, and there is no documented per-public-bucket cost benefit.","why_zh":"公開讀取權限是安全訊號而非成本槓桿。把公開 bucket 排除在探索之外，等於略過最可能外洩敏感資料的 bucket，會損及功能，且文件中並無依公開 bucket 計費的成本好處。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This increases cost rather than optimizing it. Running daily discovery jobs on ALL buckets re-inspects huge amounts of data every day (billed per GB) and duplicates what automated discovery already does, the opposite of cost optimization.","why_zh":"這會增加成本而非優化。對所有 bucket 每天執行 discovery jobs 會每天重新檢查大量資料（依 GB 計費），且與 automated discovery 重複，與成本最佳化背道而馳。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Macie object criteria are file name extension, last modified date, prefix, and storage size — there is no object-level tag criterion (tags are a bucket-level criterion). Limiting analysis to production-tagged objects also skips non-production objects/buckets that could still hold sensitive data, compromising functionality.","why_zh":"Macie 的 object criteria 為檔名副檔名、最後修改日期、prefix 與儲存大小，並無物件層級的標籤條件（標籤屬於 bucket 層級條件）。僅分析標記為 production 的物件也會略過仍可能含有敏感資料的非正式環境物件/bucket，損及功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-asdd-account-configure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-jobs-scope.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-jobs-costs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":170,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company recently acquired another company that has standalone AWS accounts. The acquiring company's DevOps team needs to consolidate the administration of the AWS accounts for both companies and retain full administrative control of the accounts. The DevOps team also needs to collect and group findings across all the accounts to implement and maintain a security posture. Which combination of steps should the DevOps team take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司最近收购了另一家拥有独立 AWS 账户的公司。收购 公司的 DevOps 团队需要整合两家公司的 AWS 账户的管理，并保持对这些账户的完全管理控制权。DevOps 团队还需要收集并汇总所有账户中的发现结果，以实施和维护安全态势。 开发运维团队应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Invite the acquired company's AWS accounts to join the organization. Create an SCP that has full administrative privileges. Attach the SCP to the management account.","B":"Invite the acquired company's AWS accounts to join the organization. Create the OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM role in the invited accounts. Grant permission to the management account to assume the role.","C":"Use AWS Security Hub to collect and group findings across all accounts. Use Security Hub to automatically detect new accounts as the accounts are added to the organization.","D":"Use AWS Firewall Manager to collect and group findings across all accounts. Enable all features for the organization. Designate an account in the organization as the delegated administrator account for Firewall Manager.","E":"Use Amazon Inspector to collect and group findings across all accounts. Designate an account in the organization as the delegated administrator account for Amazon Inspector."},"options_zh":{"A":"邀请被收购公司的 AWS 账户加入组织。创建一个具有完全管理权限的服务控制策略（SCP）。将 该 SCP 附加到管理账户。","B":"邀请被收购公司的 AWS 账户加入组织。在受邀账户中创建 OrganizationAccountAccessRole IAM 角色。授予管理账户承担该角色的权限。","C":"使用 AWS Security Hub 收集并汇总所有账户中的发现结果。利用 Security Hub 自动检测新账户， 以便在新账户加入组织时能够及时发现。","D":"使用 AWS 防火墙管理器收集并汇总所有账户中的发现结果。为整个组织启用所有功能。在组织中指定 一个账户作为防火墙管理器的委托管理员账户。","E":"使用 Amazon Inspector 收集并汇总所有账户中的发现结果。在组织中指定一个账户作为 Amazon Inspector 的委托管理员账户。"},"answer":["B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must be met: (1) consolidate administration of the acquired standalone accounts with FULL administrative control, and (2) collect and group security findings across all accounts. Option B is correct: AWS Organizations only auto-creates the OrganizationAccountAccessRole in accounts it CREATES; accounts you INVITE do not automatically get an administrator role. The AWS docs explicitly state you must manually create the role (with the AdministratorAccess managed policy) in the invited accounts and grant the management account permission to assume it via sts:AssumeRole, which yields full administrative control over the acquired accounts. Option C is correct: AWS Security Hub is the purpose-built service to aggregate and group security findings across all member accounts in an organization, and via central configuration / auto-enable it onboards new accounts as they join the organization, directly supporting implementing and maintaining a security posture.","explanation_zh":"本題需同時滿足兩項需求：(1) 整併被收購之獨立帳戶的管理並取得「完整」管理控制權，以及 (2) 跨所有帳戶收集並分組安全 findings。選項 B 正確：AWS Organizations 只會在「由它建立」的成員帳戶中自動建立 OrganizationAccountAccessRole；以「邀請」方式加入的帳戶不會自動取得管理員角色。AWS 文件明確指出，必須在受邀帳戶中手動建立該角色（附加 AdministratorAccess 受管政策），並透過 sts:AssumeRole 授權 management account 來扮演該角色，藉此取得對被收購帳戶的完整管理控制權。選項 C 正確：AWS Security Hub 是專為跨組織所有成員帳戶彙總並分組安全 findings 而設計的服務，並可透過 central configuration / auto-enable 在新帳戶加入組織時自動納管，直接支援建立與維護安全態勢。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SCPs do not GRANT permissions - they only define maximum permission guardrails (boundaries) for member accounts, and a full-access SCP (FullAWSAccess) is already attached by default. Attaching an 'administrative' SCP to the management account accomplishes nothing toward administering the acquired accounts, since the management account is not restricted by SCPs and SCPs cannot confer cross-account admin control.","why_zh":"SCP 不會「授予」權限，僅定義成員帳戶的權限上限（護欄），且預設已附加全存取的 FullAWSAccess SCP。將「管理員」SCP 附加到 management account 對管理被收購帳戶毫無作用，因為 management account 不受 SCP 限制，且 SCP 無法賦予跨帳戶的管理控制權。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Firewall Manager centrally configures and manages firewall protections (AWS WAF, Shield Advanced, VPC security groups, AWS Network Firewall, Route 53 Resolver DNS Firewall) across accounts. It is not a service for collecting and grouping security findings to maintain an overall security posture; that is the role of Security Hub.","why_zh":"AWS Firewall Manager 用於跨帳戶集中設定與管理防火牆保護（AWS WAF、Shield Advanced、VPC security groups、AWS Network Firewall、Route 53 Resolver DNS Firewall），並非用來收集與分組安全 findings 以維護整體安全態勢，後者屬於 Security Hub 的職責。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Amazon Inspector performs automated vulnerability scanning (software CVEs, network reachability, code) for compute workloads. While it supports a delegated administrator for organization-wide scanning, it does not collect and GROUP findings across all security sources to provide a consolidated security posture - it is one finding source that feeds INTO Security Hub. Security Hub is the aggregation/grouping service the question asks for.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 對運算工作負載執行自動化弱點掃描（軟體 CVE、網路可達性、程式碼）。雖然它支援委派管理員進行組織範圍掃描，但它不會跨所有安全來源「收集並分組」findings 以提供整合式安全態勢，它只是匯入 Security Hub 的一個發現來源。題目要求的彙整／分組服務是 Security Hub。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_create-cross-account-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_accounts_access-cross-account-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/designate-orgs-admin-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/securityhub/latest/userguide/central-configuration-intro.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/what-is-aws-waf.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":171,"question_en":"A company has an application and a CI/CD pipeline. The CI/CD pipeline consists of an AWS CodePipeline pipeline and an AWS CodeBuild project. The CodeBuild project runs tests against the application as part of the build process and outputs a test report. The company must keep the test reports for 90 days. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款应用程序和一个持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）流水线。该 CI/CD 流水线由一个 AWS CodePipeline 流水线和一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目组成。CodeBuild 项目在构建过程中对应用程序进行测试， 并输出测试报告。该公司必须将测试报告保存 90 天。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add a new stage in the CodePipeline pipeline after the stage that contains the CodeBuild project. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to store the reports. Configure an S3 deploy action type in the new CodePipeline stage with the appropriate path and format for the reports.","B":"Add a report group in the CodeBuild project buildspec file with the appropriate path and format for the reports. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to store the reports. Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function to copy the reports to the S3 bucket when a build is completed. Create an S3 Lifecycle rule to expire the objects after 90 days.","C":"Add a new stage in the CodePipeline pipeline. Configure a test action type with the appropriate path and format for the reports. Configure the report expiration time to be 90 days in the CodeBuild project buildspec file.","D":"Add a report group in the CodeBuild project buildspec file with the appropriate path and format for the reports. Create an Amazon S3 bucket to store the reports. Configure the report group as an artifact in the CodeBuild project buildspec file. Configure the S3 bucket as the artifact destination. Set the object expiration to 90 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"在包含 CodeBuild 项目的阶段之后，在 CodePipeline 管道中添加一个新阶段。创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储报告。在新的 CodePipeline 阶段中配置 S3 部署操作类型，并设置报告的适当路径 和格式。","B":"在 CodeBuild 项目的 buildspec 文件中添加一个报告组，指定适当的路径和格式。创建一个 Amazon S3 存 储桶来存储报告。配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在构建完成时调用 AWS Lambda 函数将报告复 制到 S3 存储桶。创建一个 S3 生命周期规则，在 90 天后过期对象。","C":"在 CodePipeline 管道中添加一个新阶段。配置测试操作类型，并设置报告的适当路径和格式。在 CodeBuild 项目的 buildspec 文件中将报告过期时间配置为 90 天。","D":"在 CodeBuild 项目的 buildspec 文件中添加一个报告组，并指定适当的路径和格式。创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储报告。在 CodeBuild 项目的 buildspec 文件中将报告组配置为一个构建工件。将 S3 存储 桶配置为工件的目标位置。设置对象过期时间为 90 天。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"A CodeBuild test report expires 30 days after it is created, and this 30-day expiration is NOT configurable. The only AWS-documented way to keep test results longer than 30 days is to export the report group's raw test result data files to an Amazon S3 bucket; exported files do not expire. To then cap retention at 90 days, you must use an S3 Lifecycle rule (the documented S3 mechanism for expiring objects after a set number of days). Option B is a complete, technically valid end-to-end solution: it adds a report group to the buildspec, creates an S3 bucket, uses an EventBridge rule plus a Lambda function to copy the reports to S3 on build completion (CodeBuild emits build state-change events to EventBridge), and applies an S3 Lifecycle rule to expire objects after 90 days. Option D is the closest distractor but is wrong: report-group S3 export is configured via the report group's exportConfig (S3ReportExportConfig) property, not as a buildspec 'artifacts' destination, and 'setting object expiration to 90 days' on S3 requires a Lifecycle rule, which D never specifies.","explanation_zh":"CodeBuild 測試報告會在建立後 30 天到期，且此 30 天到期時間無法設定。AWS 官方文件唯一能讓測試結果保留超過 30 天的方法，是將 report group 的原始測試結果資料檔匯出到 Amazon S3 bucket，匯出的檔案不會到期。若要再把保留期限限制為 90 天，必須使用 S3 Lifecycle rule（文件記載讓物件在指定天數後到期的 S3 機制）。選項 B 是完整且技術上可行的端到端解法：在 buildspec 加入 report group、建立 S3 bucket、用 EventBridge rule 搭配 Lambda 函式在 build 完成時把報告複製到 S3（CodeBuild 會將 build state-change 事件送到 EventBridge），並套用 S3 Lifecycle rule 讓物件在 90 天後到期。選項 D 是最接近的干擾項但錯誤：report group 的 S3 匯出是透過 report group 的 exportConfig（S3ReportExportConfig）屬性設定，而非 buildspec 的 artifacts 目的地；而且在 S3 上「將物件到期設為 90 天」必須靠 Lifecycle rule，而 D 從未提及。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CodePipeline S3 deploy action deploys pipeline output artifacts, not CodeBuild test report-group data, and the option provides no mechanism to enforce 90-day retention. It does nothing to retain reports past the non-configurable 30-day report expiration.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 的 S3 deploy action 是部署 pipeline 的輸出 artifacts，而非 CodeBuild 測試 report group 的資料，且此選項沒有任何強制 90 天保留的機制，無法解決報告在不可設定的 30 天後到期的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no 'report expiration time' setting in the CodeBuild buildspec. Test reports always expire at 30 days and that value cannot be changed, so configuring 90 days in the buildspec is impossible.","why_zh":"CodeBuild buildspec 並沒有「report expiration time」的設定。測試報告固定 30 天到期且無法變更，因此在 buildspec 設定 90 天是不可能的。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeBuild report groups are not configured as buildspec 'artifacts'; report S3 export is set via the report group's exportConfig (S3ReportExportConfig) property, while artifacts are a separate build-output concept. Also, 'setting object expiration to 90 days' on S3 requires an S3 Lifecycle rule, which D never specifies, so the retention mechanism is technically invalid.","why_zh":"CodeBuild report group 不能設定為 buildspec 的 artifact；報告的 S3 匯出是透過 report group 的 exportConfig（S3ReportExportConfig）屬性設定，而 artifacts 是另一個 build 輸出概念。此外在 S3 上「將物件到期設為 90 天」必須使用 S3 Lifecycle rule，而 D 並未提及，因此保留機制在技術上無效。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/test-reporting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/report-group-export-settings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/report-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codebuild.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/object-lifecycle-mgmt.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":172,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon API Gateway regional REST API to host its application API. The REST API has a custom domain. The REST API's default endpoint is deactivated. The company's internal teams consume the API. The company wants to use mutual TLS between the API and the internal teams as an additional layer of authentication. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 API 网关的区域 REST API 来托管其应用程序 API。该 REST API 具有自定义域名。 REST API 的默认端点已停用。 该公司内部团队使用该 API。公司希望在 API 与内部团队之间使用双向 TLS 作为额外的身份验证层。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Certificate Manager (ACM) to create a private certificate authority (CA). Provision a client certificate that is signed by the private CA.","B":"Provision a client certificate that is signed by a public certificate authority (CA). Import the certificate into AWS Certificate Manager (ACM).","C":"Upload the provisioned client certificate to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the API Gateway mutual TLS to use the client certificate that is stored in the S3 bucket as the trust store.","D":"Upload the provisioned client certificate private key to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the API Gateway mutual TLS to use the private key that is stored in the S3 bucket as the trust store.","E":"Upload the root private certificate authority (CA) certificate to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the API Gateway mutual TLS to use the private CA certificate that is stored in the S3 bucket as the trust store."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 证书管理器（ACM）创建一个私有证书颁发机构（CA）。提供一个由私有 CA 签名的客 户端证书。","B":"配置由公共证书颁发机构（CA）签名的客户端证书。将证书导入 AWS 证书管理器（ACM）。","C":"将已配置的客户端证书上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。将 API 网关双向 TLS 配置为使用存储在 S3 存储桶 中的客户端证书作为信任库。","D":"将已配置的客户端证书私钥上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。将 API 网关双向 TLS 配置为使用存储在 S3 存储桶中的私钥作为信任库。","E":"将根私有证书颁发机构 （CA） 证书上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 API 网关双向 TLS 使用存储在 S3 存储桶中的私有 CA 证书作为信任库。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"API Gateway mutual TLS for a REST API requires two distinct artifacts. First, clients must present X.509 client certificates during the TLS handshake, and those certificates must be issued by a certificate authority whose certificate is in the trust store. Option A provides this by provisioning a client certificate signed by a private CA created and managed through AWS Private CA (accessible via ACM), which issues the X.509 certificates the internal teams present. Second, you must build a trust store, a single .pem bundle containing the complete chain of trust (issuing CA up to the root CA), and upload it to an Amazon S3 bucket; the custom domain name is then configured with truststoreUri=s3://bucket/key. Option E provides this by uploading the private CA (root CA) certificate to S3 and configuring it as the trust store. The deciding distinction is that the trust store holds CA certificates (E), never an individual client certificate (C) and never any private key (D), and the client certificate must be issued by a CA whose chain is in that trust store (A).","explanation_zh":"API Gateway 對 REST API 啟用 mutual TLS 需要兩個不同的元件。第一,用戶端在 TLS handshake 時必須出示 X.509 client certificate,而該憑證必須由其 CA 憑證位於 trust store 中的憑證授權單位簽發。Option A 透過 AWS Private CA(可經由 ACM 存取)建立並管理的 private CA 簽發 client certificate,供內部團隊出示使用,符合此需求。第二,你必須建立 trust store,也就是一個包含完整信任鏈(從簽發 CA 一直到 root CA)的單一 .pem 檔,並上傳到 Amazon S3 bucket;接著在 custom domain name 上以 truststoreUri=s3://bucket/key 進行設定。Option E 透過把 private CA(root CA)憑證上傳到 S3 並設定為 trust store,符合此需求。關鍵差異在於:trust store 存放的是 CA 憑證(E),絕不是個別的 client certificate(C),也絕不是任何 private key(D);而 client certificate 必須由其信任鏈位於該 trust store 中的 CA 簽發(A)。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The client certificate is presented directly by the client during the TLS handshake; it is not imported into ACM. ACM holds the server/domain certificate (regionalCertificateArn) and the ownershipVerificationCertificate, not the client certificate. Importing the client cert into ACM plays no role in the mutual TLS client-authentication flow and does nothing to populate the S3 trust store.","why_zh":"Client certificate 是由用戶端在 TLS handshake 時直接出示,並不會匯入 ACM。ACM 存放的是 server/domain 憑證(regionalCertificateArn)與 ownershipVerificationCertificate,而非 client certificate。把 client cert 匯入 ACM 在 mutual TLS 的用戶端驗證流程中沒有作用,也無法填入 S3 trust store。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The trust store must contain CA certificates (the chain of trust from the issuing CA up to the root CA), not an individual client certificate. Uploading the client certificate itself as the trust store does not establish the CA-based validation the scenario requires; API Gateway validates clients by checking the certificate issuer against the CA certs in the trust store.","why_zh":"Trust store 必須包含 CA 憑證(從簽發 CA 一直到 root CA 的信任鏈),而非個別的 client certificate。把 client certificate 本身當作 trust store 上傳,無法建立情境所需的以 CA 為基礎的驗證;API Gateway 是以憑證的簽發者比對 trust store 中的 CA 憑證來驗證用戶端。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A trust store never contains a private key; it is a .pem bundle of public X.509 CA certificates. The client certificate's private key stays with the client (used in the curl --key request) and must never be uploaded to S3 or placed in the trust store.","why_zh":"Trust store 絕不會包含 private key,它是由公開的 X.509 CA 憑證組成的 .pem 檔。Client certificate 的 private key 應留在用戶端(用於 curl --key 請求),絕不可上傳到 S3 或放入 trust store。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/rest-api-mutual-tls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/privateca/latest/userguide/PcaWelcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/privateca/latest/userguide/create-CA.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":173,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Directory Service for Microsoft Active Directory as its identity provider (IdP). The company requires all infrastructure to be defined and deployed by AWS CloudFormation. A DevOps engineer needs to create a fleet of Windows-based Amazon EC2 instances to host an application. The DevOps engineer has created a CloudFormation template that contains an EC2 launch template, IAM role, EC2 security group, and EC2 Auto Scaling group. The DevOps engineer must implement a solution that joins all EC2 instances to the domain of the AWS Managed Microsoft AD directory. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS 目录服务中的 Microsoft Active Directory 作为其身份提供商（IdP）。该公司要求所有基 础设施均由 AWS CloudFormation 定义和部署。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要创建一批基于 Windows 的 Amazon EC2 实例来托管一个应用程序。该 DevOps 工程师已创建了一个 CloudFormation 模板，其中包含一个 EC2 启动模板、IAM 角色、EC2 安全组和 EC2 自动扩展组。DevOps 工程师必须实施一个解决方案，将所有 EC2 实例加入到 AWS 管理的 Microsoft AD 目录的域中。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the CloudFormation template, create an AWS::SSM::Document resource that joins the EC2 instance to the AWS Managed Microsoft AD domain by using the parameters for the existing directory. Update the launch template to include the SSMAssociation property to use the new SSM document. Attach the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore and AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess AWS managed policies to the IAM role that the EC2 instances use.","B":"In the CloudFormation template, update the launch template to include specific tags that propagate on launch. Create an AWS::SSM::Association resource to associate the AWS- JoinDirectoryServiceDomain Automation runbook with the EC2 instances that have the specified tags. Define the required parameters to join the AWS Managed Microsoft AD directory. Attach the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore and AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess AWS managed policies to the IAM role that the EC2 instances use.","C":"Store the existing AWS Managed Microsoft AD domain connection details in AWS Secrets Manager. In the CloudFormation template, create an AWS::SSM::Association resource to associate the AWS- CreateManagedWindowsInstanceWithApproval Automation runbook with the EC2 Auto Scaling group. Pass the ARNs for the parameters from Secrets Manager to join the domain. Attach the AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess and SecretsManagerReadWrite AWS managed policies to the IAM role that the EC2 instances use.","D":"Store the existing AWS Managed Microsoft AD domain administrator credentials in AWS Secrets Manager. In the CloudFormation template, update the EC2 launch template to include user data. Configure the user data to pull the administrator credentials from Secrets Manager and to join the AWS Managed Microsoft AD domain. Attach the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore and SecretsManagerReadWrite AWS managed policies to the IAM role that the EC2 instances use."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFormation 模板中，创建一个 AWS::SSM：：Document 资源，使用现有目录的参数将 EC2 实例加 入到 AWS 管理的 Microsoft AD 域。更新启动模板以包含 SSMAssociation 属性，以便使用新的 SSM 文 档。将 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 和 AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess AWS 管理策略附加到 EC2 实例使用的 IAM 角色。","B":"在 CloudFormation 模板中，更新启动模板以包含在启动时传播的特定标签。创建一个 AWS::SSM:: Association 资源，将 AWS-JoinDirectoryServiceDomain 自动化运行本与具有指定标签的 EC2 实例相关 联。定义加入 AWS 管理的 Microsoft AD 目录所需的参数。将 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 和 AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess AWS 管理策略附加到 EC2 实例使用的 IAM 角色。","C":"将现有的 AWS 管理的 Microsoft AD 域连接详细信息存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。在 CloudFormation 模板中，创建一个 AWS::SSM：：Association 资源，将 AWS-CreateManagedWindowsInstanceWithAppro val 自动化运行本与 EC2 自动缩放组相关联。将来自 Secrets Manager 的参数的 ARN 传递给域连接。将 AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess 和 SecretsManagerReadWrite AWS 管理策略附加到 EC2 实例使用的 IAM 角色。","D":"将现有的 AWS 管理的 Microsoft AD 域管理员凭证存储在 AWS Secrets Manager 中。在 CloudFormation 模 板中，更新 EC2 启动模板以包含用户数据。配置用户数据从 Secrets Manager 中提取管理员凭证，并将 实例加入到 AWS 中。 管理 Microsoft AD 域。将 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 和 SecretsManagerReadWrite 这两个 AWS 管理策略附加到 EC2 实例所使用的 IAM 角色上。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The most operationally efficient pattern is an AWS::SSM::Association (a State Manager association) declared in CloudFormation that targets instances by tag and runs an AWS-provided domain-join document, with the documented IAM policies AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore and AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess on the instance role (AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess grants the ds:CreateComputer/DescribeDirectories needed to join the domain). AWS docs for seamless/automated domain join list exactly these two managed policies, which already eliminates C and D (they use SecretsManagerReadWrite and pull credentials manually). State Manager associations are built for dynamic fleets: the AWS::SSM::Association CloudFormation resource explicitly states that for dynamic targets such as an Auto Scaling Group it applies the configuration when new instances are added, and associations can target nodes by tags. So B automatically joins scale-out instances with no custom document and no credential handling. Option A is technically invalid because the SsmAssociations property exists only on AWS::EC2::Instance, not on AWS::EC2::LaunchTemplate (LaunchTemplateData has no such property), and it needlessly authors a custom SSM document to recreate AWS's existing domain-join capability. (Note: AWS-JoinDirectoryServiceDomain is strictly a Command document rather than an Automation runbook, but B's mechanism, tag targeting, and IAM policies are all correct, making it the best answer by a wide margin.)","explanation_zh":"最具運維效率的做法是在 CloudFormation 中宣告 AWS::SSM::Association（即 State Manager association），以 tag 為目標並執行 AWS 內建的 domain-join document，同時在 instance role 上掛載文件指定的 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 與 AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess 受管政策（AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess 提供加網域所需的 ds:CreateComputer/DescribeDirectories 權限）。AWS 關於 seamless/自動 domain join 的文件正是列出這兩個受管政策，這一點就排除了使用 SecretsManagerReadWrite 並手動拉取憑證的 C 與 D。State Manager association 本就是為動態機群設計：AWS::SSM::Association CloudFormation 資源明確指出，對於 Auto Scaling Group 這類動態目標，會在新 instance 加入群組時套用設定，且 association 可以用 tags 鎖定節點。因此 B 能自動將擴增的 instance 加入網域，不需自訂 document 也不需處理憑證。選項 A 在技術上無效，因為 SsmAssociations 屬性只存在於 AWS::EC2::Instance，而非 AWS::EC2::LaunchTemplate（LaunchTemplateData 沒有此屬性），且還用自訂 SSM document 重造 AWS 既有的 domain-join 能力。（註：AWS-JoinDirectoryServiceDomain 嚴格說是 Command document 而非 Automation runbook，但 B 的機制、tag 目標與 IAM 政策皆正確，仍是明顯最佳解。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The SsmAssociations/SSMAssociation property exists only on AWS::EC2::Instance, not on AWS::EC2::LaunchTemplate (its LaunchTemplateData has no such property), so updating the launch template this way is invalid. It also authors a custom AWS::SSM::Document to reinvent AWS's existing domain-join capability, which is more work and less suited to a dynamically scaling fleet than a tag-targeted State Manager association. The IAM policies are correct, but the approach is less operationally efficient.","why_zh":"SsmAssociations/SSMAssociation 屬性只存在於 AWS::EC2::Instance，不在 AWS::EC2::LaunchTemplate（其 LaunchTemplateData 沒有此屬性），因此以這種方式更新 launch template 無效。它還自行撰寫客製 AWS::SSM::Document 重造 AWS 既有的 domain-join 能力，工作量較大，且對動態擴縮機群不如以 tag 為目標的 State Manager association 合適。IAM 政策雖正確，但整體運維效率較低。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS-CreateManagedWindowsInstanceWithApproval provisions a single new instance behind a manual approval step; it does not join an existing Auto Scaling fleet to the domain and cannot be associated with an Auto Scaling group for domain join. It also attaches SecretsManagerReadWrite (overly broad and unnecessary), omits AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore, and the approval gate reduces operational efficiency.","why_zh":"AWS-CreateManagedWindowsInstanceWithApproval 是在人工審批步驟後佈建單一新 instance；它不會把既有 Auto Scaling 機群加入網域，也無法用於對 Auto Scaling group 做 domain join。它還掛載範圍過大且不必要的 SecretsManagerReadWrite、缺少 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore，且審批關卡降低運維效率。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Pulling domain admin credentials from Secrets Manager via user data to perform a manual domain join is the least operationally efficient and least secure option: it bypasses the AWS managed domain-join mechanism, requires storing/handling privileged credentials, uses SecretsManagerReadWrite (overly broad), and omits the documented AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess.","why_zh":"透過 user data 從 Secrets Manager 取得網域管理員憑證進行手動加網域，是運維效率最低、安全性最差的做法：它繞過 AWS 受管的 domain-join 機制、需儲存與處理特權憑證、使用範圍過大的 SecretsManagerReadWrite，又缺少文件指定的 AmazonSSMDirectoryServiceAccess。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/launching_instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directoryservice/latest/admin-guide/ms_ad_join_instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-ssm-association.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-ec2-launchtemplate-launchtemplatedata.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-ec2-instance-ssmassociation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-about.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":174,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company has a root OU that has a child OU. The root OU has an SCP that allows all actions on all resources. The child OU has an SCP that allows all actions for Amazon DynamoDB and AWS Lambda, and denies all other actions. The company has an AWS account that is named vendor-data in the child OU. A DevOps engineer has an IAM user that is attached to the Administrator Access IAM policy in the vendor-data account. The DevOps engineer attempts to launch an Amazon EC2 instance in the vendor-data account but receives an access denied error. Which change should the DevOps engineer make to launch the EC2 instance in the vendor-data account?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司有一个根组织单元（OU），其下有一个子组 织单元（OU）。根组织单元有一个服务控制策略（SCP），允许对所有资源执行所有操作。子组织单元有一 个服务控制策略，允许对 Amazon DynamoDB 和 AWS Lambda 执行所有操作，并拒绝所有其他操作。 该公司在子组织单位（OU）中有一个名为 vendor-data 的 AWS 账户。一位 DevOps 工程师在 vendor-data 账 户中拥有一个 IAM 用户，该用户已附加了管理员访问权限的 IAM 策略。该 DevOps 工程师尝试在 vendor- data 账户中启动一个 Amazon EC2 实例，但收到了访问被拒绝的错误。 DevOps 工程师应做出哪项更改才能在 vendor-data 账户中启动 EC2 实例？","options_en":{"A":"Attach the AmazonEC2FullAccess IAM policy to the IAM user.","B":"Create a new SCP that allows all actions for Amazon EC2. Attach the SCP to the vendor-data account.","C":"Update the SCP in the child OU to allow all actions for Amazon EC2.","D":"Create a new SCP that allows all actions for Amazon EC2. Attach the SCP to the root OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 AmazonEC2FullAccess IAM 策略附加到 IAM 用户。","B":"创建一个新的服务控制策略（SCP），允许对亚马逊 EC2 执行所有操作。将该 SCP 附加到供应商数据账户。","C":"将子组织单位中的 SCP 更新为允许对 Amazon EC2 执行所有操作。","D":"创建一个新的服务控制策略（SCP），允许对亚马逊 EC2 执行所有操作。将该 SCP 附加到根组织单元（OU）。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"SCPs are guardrails that set the maximum available permissions; they never grant permissions. For an action to be allowed in a member account, there must be an explicit Allow at EVERY level in the direct path from the root, through each OU, down to the account. The root OU SCP allows all actions (EC2 is permitted there), but the child OU SCP only allows DynamoDB and Lambda and denies everything else, so EC2 is blocked at the child OU level. Because vendor-data sits under the child OU, EC2 is blocked even though the IAM user has AdministratorAccess - AWS docs state explicitly that a permission blocked at any level above the account cannot be used 'even if the account administrator attaches the AdministratorAccess IAM policy with */* permissions to the user.' The fix is to add the missing/explicit Allow for EC2 at the level that is blocking it, i.e., update the child OU SCP to allow EC2 (option C). After that, EC2 is allowed at the root and the child OU, the account inherits the default FullAWSAccess, and the launch succeeds.","explanation_zh":"SCP 是設定「最大可用權限」的護欄（guardrail），本身永遠不會授予權限。要讓某動作在成員帳戶中被允許，必須在從 root 經由每一層 OU 到該帳戶的整條直接路徑上，「每一層」都有明確的 Allow。root OU 的 SCP 允許所有動作（EC2 在該層被允許），但 child OU 的 SCP 只允許 DynamoDB 與 Lambda 並拒絕其他所有動作，所以 EC2 在 child OU 這一層被阻擋。由於 vendor-data 帳戶位於 child OU 之下，即使 IAM user 擁有 AdministratorAccess，EC2 仍被阻擋 — AWS 文件明確指出，若權限在帳戶上方任一層被封鎖，使用者就無法使用，「即使帳戶管理員為該使用者附加具有 */* 權限的 AdministratorAccess IAM 政策也一樣」。正確做法是在「阻擋的那一層」加入 EC2 的明確 Allow，也就是更新 child OU 的 SCP 以允許 EC2 動作（選項 C）。之後 EC2 在 root、child OU 都被允許，帳戶層繼承預設的 FullAWSAccess，啟動 EC2 即可成功。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The IAM user already has AdministratorAccess, which is broader than AmazonEC2FullAccess. The denial is caused by the SCP guardrail, not by insufficient IAM permissions. SCPs cap the maximum permissions, so no amount of IAM permission can grant EC2 when the SCP in the path does not allow it; AWS docs confirm this holds even with AdministratorAccess attached.","why_zh":"該 IAM user 已擁有 AdministratorAccess，範圍比 AmazonEC2FullAccess 還廣。被拒絕的原因是 SCP 護欄，而非 IAM 權限不足。SCP 設定權限上限，因此當路徑上的 SCP 不允許 EC2 時，再多的 IAM 權限也無法授予 EC2；AWS 文件確認即使附加 AdministratorAccess 也是如此。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Attaching an EC2-allow SCP at the vendor-data account level does not help because an Allow is required at EVERY level in the path. The child OU SCP still does not allow EC2 (and explicitly denies all other actions), so EC2 remains blocked above the account.","why_zh":"在 vendor-data 帳戶層級附加允許 EC2 的 SCP 沒有用，因為路徑上「每一層」都必須有 Allow。child OU 的 SCP 仍未允許 EC2（且明確拒絕其他所有動作），所以 EC2 在帳戶上方仍被阻擋。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The root OU SCP already allows all actions, including EC2, so attaching another EC2-allow SCP at the root changes nothing. The blocking level is the child OU, which still does not allow EC2.","why_zh":"root OU 的 SCP 已允許所有動作（含 EC2），因此在 root 再附加一個允許 EC2 的 SCP 毫無作用。阻擋的層級是 child OU，它仍未允許 EC2。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":175,"question_en":"A company's security policies require the use of security hardened AMIs in production environments. A DevOps engineer has used EC2 Image Builder to create a pipeline that builds the AMIs on a recurring schedule. The DevOps engineer needs to update the launch templates of the company's Auto Scaling groups. The Auto Scaling groups must use the newest AMIs during the launch of Amazon EC2 instances. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司的安全政策要求在生产环境中使用经过安全强化的 AMI。一位 DevOps 工程师使用 EC2 Image Builder 创建了一个管道，按照预定的时间表构建 AMI。 DevOps 工程师需要更新公司自动扩展组的启动模板。在启动 Amazon EC2 实例时，自动扩展组必须使用 最新的 AMI。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to receive new AMI events from Image Builder. Target an AWS Systems Manager Run Command document that updates the launch templates of the Auto Scaling groups with the newest AMI ID.","B":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to receive new AMI events from Image Builder. Target an AWS Lambda function that updates the launch templates of the Auto Scaling groups with the newest AMI ID.","C":"Configure the launch template to use a value from AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store for the AMI ID. Configure the Image Builder pipeline to update the Parameter Store value with the newest AMI ID.","D":"Configure the Image Builder distribution settings to update the launch templates with the newest AMI ID. Configure the Auto Scaling groups to use the newest version of the launch template."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以接收来自 Image Builder 的新 AMI 事件。将目标设置为一个 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 文档，该文档会使用最新的 AMI ID 更新 Auto Scaling 组的启动模板。","B":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以接收来自 Image Builder 的新 AMI 事件。将目标指定为一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会使用最新的 AMI ID 更新自动扩展组的启动模板。","C":"将启动模板配置为使用来自 AWS 系统管理器参数存储的 AMI ID 值。将 Image Builder 管道配置为使用最 新的 AMI ID 更新参数存储中的值。","D":"配置 Image Builder 分发设置，以使用最新的 AMI ID 更新启动模板。配置自动扩展组以使用启动模板 的最新版本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The qualifier is MOST operational efficiency while ensuring newly launched instances always use the newest hardened AMI. Option C points the launch template's ImageId at an SSM Parameter Store reference (resolve:ssm:parameter-name) and has the Image Builder pipeline update that parameter with each new AMI ID. This is a first-class, no-code integration: EC2 Image Builder distribution configurations natively support 'SSM parameter configurations' (ssmParameter) that store the output AMI ID in a Parameter Store parameter during distribution - the docs literally include 'Example: Store the output AMI ID in an SSM parameter'. Because the launch template uses resolve:ssm with no version pinned, EC2 resolves the parameter to its latest value at instance launch time, so the Auto Scaling group always launches the newest AMI. The Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling User Guide states this explicitly: 'With Systems Manager parameters, you can update your Auto Scaling groups to use new AMI IDs without needing to create new launch templates or new versions of launch templates each time an AMI ID changes.' There is no EventBridge rule, no Lambda, no Run Command, no per-build template version churn, and the ASG never needs to be touched. Option D (the dump's suggested answer) is mechanically valid (Image Builder creates a NEW launch template version containing the new AMI), but it generates a new launch template version on every build and binds distribution to specific templates - the exact churn the SSM-parameter approach is documented to avoid - so C is strictly more operationally efficient and is the genuinely correct answer.","explanation_zh":"限定詞是 MOST operational efficiency（最高運維效率），同時確保新啟動的執行個體永遠使用最新的強化 AMI。選項 C 將 launch template 的 ImageId 指向 SSM Parameter Store 參考（resolve:ssm:parameter-name），並由 Image Builder pipeline 在每次產生新 AMI 時更新該參數值。這是原生、零程式碼的整合：EC2 Image Builder distribution configurations 原生支援『SSM parameter configurations』（ssmParameter），可在 distribution 階段將輸出 AMI ID 寫入 Parameter Store 參數（文件中明確列出『Example: Store the output AMI ID in an SSM parameter』）。由於 launch template 使用未指定版本的 resolve:ssm，EC2 會在執行個體啟動時將參數解析為最新值，因此 Auto Scaling group 永遠以最新 AMI 啟動。Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 使用者指南明確指出：『使用 Systems Manager parameters，您可以讓 Auto Scaling groups 採用新的 AMI ID，而無需在每次 AMI ID 變更時建立新的 launch templates 或新的 launch template 版本。』無需 EventBridge 規則、Lambda、Run Command，也不會每次建置產生版本，更不需更動 ASG。選項 D（題庫建議答案）機制上可行（Image Builder 會建立含新 AMI 的『新』launch template 版本），但每次建置都會產生新版本並將 distribution 綁定到特定 template，正是 SSM 參數做法文件所要避免的版本累積；因此 C 在運維效率上嚴格優於 D，是真正正確的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An EventBridge rule plus an SSM Run Command document to rewrite launch templates is heavy, custom automation. Run Command executes commands on managed EC2 instances - it is not the mechanism for editing launch templates, so this requires custom scripting plus event rules and IAM wiring. Far less operationally efficient than C's native SSM parameter, and it still produces new launch template versions.","why_zh":"EventBridge 規則加上 SSM Run Command 文件來改寫 launch templates 屬於繁重的自訂自動化。Run Command 是在受管 EC2 執行個體上執行命令，並非編輯 launch template 的機制，因此需自訂腳本、事件規則與 IAM 設定。相較 C 的原生 SSM 參數運維效率低很多，且仍會產生新的 launch template 版本。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An EventBridge rule targeting a Lambda function that modifies each Auto Scaling group's launch template works, but it requires writing, deploying, and maintaining custom Lambda code plus event rules and IAM permissions, and it creates a new launch template version per build. C achieves the same outcome with native SSM parameter resolution and zero custom code, so it is more operationally efficient.","why_zh":"EventBridge 規則觸發 Lambda 函式去修改每個 Auto Scaling group 的 launch template 雖可行，但需撰寫、部署並維護自訂 Lambda 程式碼、事件規則與 IAM 權限，且每次建置都會產生新的 launch template 版本。C 透過原生 SSM 參數解析即可達成相同結果且無任何自訂程式碼，運維效率更高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Image Builder distribution settings can add the new AMI to a launch template, creating a NEW launch template version, and the ASG can use the latest version. This is mechanically valid but generates per-build version churn and binds the distribution config to specific templates. AWS documents the SSM-parameter approach (C) precisely as the way to update ASGs to new AMIs WITHOUT creating new launch template versions, making C strictly more operationally efficient than D. D is the dump's suggested answer but is not the best choice.","why_zh":"Image Builder distribution settings 可將新 AMI 加入 launch template，建立『新版本』，且 ASG 可使用最新版本。此法機制上可行，但每次建置都會產生版本累積，並將 distribution 設定綁定到特定 template。AWS 文件正是把 SSM 參數做法（C）描述為『無需建立新 launch template 版本』即可讓 ASG 採用新 AMI 的方式，因此 C 在運維效率上嚴格優於 D。D 是題庫建議答案，但並非最佳選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/using-systems-manager-parameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/cr-upd-ami-distribution-settings.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/using-systems-manager-parameter-to-find-AMI.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/dist-using-launch-template.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":176,"question_en":"A company has configured an Amazon S3 event source on an AWS Lambda function. The company needs the Lambda function to run when a new object is created or an existing object is modified in a particular S3 bucket. The Lambda function will use the S3 bucket name and the S3 object key of the incoming event to read the contents of the created or modified S3 object. The Lambda function will parse the contents and save the parsed contents to an Amazon DynamoDB table. The Lambda function's execution role has permissions to read from the S3 bucket and to write to the DynamoDB table. During testing, a DevOps engineer discovers that the Lambda function does not run when objects are added to the S3 bucket or when existing objects are modified. Which solution will resolve this problem?","question_zh":"一家公司已在 AWS Lambda 函数上配置了 Amazon S3 事件源。该公司需要 当在特定的 S3 存储桶中创建新对象或修改现有对象时运行的 Lambda 函数。该 Lambda 函数将使用传 入事件中的 S3 存储桶名称和 S3 对象键来读取所创建或修改的 S3 对象的内容。该 Lambda 函数将解析 内容，并将解析后的内容保存到 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。 Lambda 函数的执行角色具有从 S3 存储桶读取以及向 DynamoDB 表写入的权限。在测试期间，一 位 DevOps 工程师发现，当向 S3 存储桶添加对象或修改现有对象时，Lambda 函数不会运行。 哪种解决方案能解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the memory of the Lambda function to give the function the ability to process large files from the S3 bucket.","B":"Create a resource policy on the Lambda function to grant Amazon S3 the permission to invoke the Lambda function for the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as an OnFailure destination for the Lambda function.","D":"Provision space in the /tmp folder of the Lambda function to give the function the ability to process large files from the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"增加 Lambda 函数的内存，使该函数能够处理来自 S3 存储桶的大文件。","B":"在 Lambda 函数上创建资源策略，授予 Amazon S3 对该 S3 存储桶调用 Lambda 函数的权限。","C":"将一个 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列配置为 Lambda 函数的 OnFailure 目的地。","D":"在 Lambda 函数的 /tmp 文件夹中预留空间，使该函数能够处理来自 S3 存储桶的大文件。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon S3 invokes a Lambda function asynchronously, but only if the function's resource-based (resource) policy authorizes the S3 service principal to call lambda:InvokeFunction. The official Lambda docs state: 'To invoke your function, Amazon S3 needs permission from the function's resource-based policy. When you configure an Amazon S3 trigger in the Lambda console, the console modifies the resource-based policy... If you configure the notification in Amazon S3, you use the Lambda API to update the policy.' In this scenario the function never runs at all, which is the classic symptom of a missing resource-based policy statement (S3 is silently denied permission to invoke). The execution role mentioned in the question only governs what the function code can do AFTER it is invoked (read S3, write DynamoDB); it does not authorize S3 to invoke the function. The fix is option B: add a resource policy statement (e.g., via lambda add-permission with --principal s3.amazonaws.com, --source-arn the bucket ARN, and --source-account the account ID) granting S3 permission to invoke the function.","explanation_zh":"Amazon S3 會以非同步方式呼叫 (asynchronously invoke) Lambda function，但前提是該 function 的 resource-based policy（資源政策）必須授權 S3 service principal 執行 lambda:InvokeFunction。官方 Lambda 文件明確指出：'To invoke your function, Amazon S3 needs permission from the function's resource-based policy. When you configure an Amazon S3 trigger in the Lambda console, the console modifies the resource-based policy... If you configure the notification in Amazon S3, you use the Lambda API to update the policy.' 本題的徵狀是 function 根本完全沒有被觸發執行，這正是缺少 resource-based policy 陳述式時的典型現象（S3 被默默拒絕呼叫權限）。題目提到的 execution role 只控制 function 程式碼被呼叫之後可以做什麼（讀取 S3、寫入 DynamoDB），並不會授權 S3 去呼叫該 function。正確解法是選項 B：新增一條 resource policy 陳述式（例如使用 lambda add-permission，--principal s3.amazonaws.com、--source-arn 為 bucket ARN、--source-account 為帳號 ID），授權 S3 呼叫該 function。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing memory only affects performance and timeout once the function executes. The symptom is that the function never runs at all, so memory has no effect on invocation.","why_zh":"增加記憶體只在 function 已執行時影響效能或逾時。問題是 function 根本沒被觸發，記憶體與呼叫與否無關。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An OnFailure destination (SQS) only captures the result of asynchronous invocations that actually occurred but failed. If S3 cannot invoke the function in the first place, there is no failed invocation to route to a destination, so this does not resolve the problem.","why_zh":"OnFailure destination（SQS）只會擷取實際發生但失敗的非同步呼叫結果。若 S3 一開始就無法呼叫 function，就沒有失敗的呼叫可路由到 destination，因此無法解決問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Provisioning /tmp ephemeral storage only helps with processing large files after invocation. It does nothing to authorize or trigger the invocation, which is the actual failure.","why_zh":"配置 /tmp 暫時儲存空間只在呼叫後處理大型檔案時有幫助，無法授權或觸發呼叫，而呼叫失敗才是真正的問題所在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/permissions-function-services.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/access-control-resource-based.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":177,"question_en":"A company has deployed a critical application in two AWS Regions. The application uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in both Regions. The company has Amazon Route 53 alias DNS records for both ALBs. The company uses Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller to ensure that the application can fail over between the two Regions. The Route 53 ARC configuration includes a routing control for both Regions. The company uses Route 53 ARC to perform quarterly disaster recovery (DR) tests. During the most recent DR test, a DevOps engineer accidentally turned off both routing controls. The company needs to ensure that at least one routing control is turned on at all times. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已在两个 AWS 区域部署了一个关键应用程序。该应用程序在这两个区域均使用了应用负载 均衡器（ALB）。该公司为这两个 ALB 都设置了 Amazon Route 53 别名 DNS 记录。 该公司使用亚马逊 Route 53 应用程序恢复控制器来确保应用程序能够在两个区域之间进行故障转移。 Route 53 ARC 配置包括针对两个区域的路由控制。该公司使用 Route 53 ARC 每季度进行一次灾难恢 复（DR）测试。 在最近的一次灾难恢复测试中，一名 DevOps 工程师不小心关闭了两个路由控制。公司需要确保 任何时候至少有一个路由控制处于开启状态。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？ 在 Route 53 ARC 中创建一个新的断言安全规则。将该断言安全规则应用于两个路由控制。将规则配置 为 ATLEAST 类型，并设置阈值为 1。","options_en":{"A":"In Route 53 ARC, create a new assertion safety rule. Apply the assertion safety rule to the two routing controls. Configure the rule with the ATLEAST type with a threshold of 1.","B":"In Route 53 ARC, create a new gating safety rule. Apply the assertion safety rule to the two routing controls. Configure the rule with the OR type with a threshold of 1.","C":"In Route 53 ARC, create a new resource set. Configure the resource set with an AWS::Route53::HealthCheck resource type. Specify the ARNs of the two routing controls as the target resource. Create a new readiness check for the resource set.","D":"In Route 53 ARC, create a new resource set. Configure the resource set with an AWS::Route53RecoveryReadiness::DNSTargetResource resource type. Add the domain names of the two Route 53 alias DNS records as the target resource. Create a new readiness check for the resource set."},"options_zh":{"B":"在 Route 53 ARC 中，创建一个新的网关安全规则。将断言安全规则应用于两个路由控制。将规 则配置为“或”类型，并设置阈值为 1。","C":"在 Route 53 ARC 中，创建一个新的资源集。使用 AWS::Route53::HealthCheck 资源类型配置该资源 集。将两个路由控制的 ARN 指定为目标资源。为该资源集创建一个新的就绪检查。","D":"在 Route 53 ARC 中，创建一个新的资源集。使用 AWS::Route53RecoveryReadiness:: DNSTargetResource 资源类型配置该资源集。将两个 Route 53 别名 DNS 记录的域名添加为目标资 源。为该资源集创建一个新的就绪检查。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Route 53 Application Recovery Controller (ARC) provides two safety rule types: assertion rules and gating rules. An assertion rule enforces that the criteria you set is met whenever routing control states change, otherwise ARC rejects the change. AWS documentation gives this exact scenario as the canonical example: to prevent a fail-open scenario where all routing controls are turned off, you create an assertion rule that makes sure at least one routing control in a set stays On at any given time. The Create-safety-rule API/CLI example shows precisely this configuration: AssertedControls listing the two routing control ARNs and RuleConfig {\"Threshold\": 1, \"Type\": \"ATLEAST\", \"Inverted\": false}. That matches option A exactly, so the engineer's attempt to turn off both controls would be blocked while at least one remains On.","explanation_zh":"Route 53 Application Recovery Controller (ARC) 提供兩種 safety rule: assertion rule 與 gating rule。Assertion rule 會在 routing control 狀態變更時強制檢查你設定的條件，若不符合，ARC 就拒絕該變更。AWS 官方文件正是以本題情境作為標準範例: 為避免所有 routing control 都被關閉而造成 fail-open，你建立一條 assertion rule，確保任一時刻一組 routing control 中至少有一個維持 On。Create-safety-rule API/CLI 範例顯示的設定完全對應: AssertedControls 列出兩個 routing control 的 ARN，RuleConfig 為 {\"Threshold\": 1, \"Type\": \"ATLEAST\", \"Inverted\": false}。這正好符合選項 A，因此工程師同時關閉兩個 routing control 的動作會被阻擋，至少保留一個維持 On。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A gating rule is an overall on/off master switch implemented with separate gating routing controls and target routing controls; it does not assert that targets must remain On. The AWS gating-rule example uses Type OR with Threshold 0, not Threshold 1, and the option text is internally inconsistent ('create a new gating safety rule. Apply the assertion safety rule...').","why_zh":"gating rule 是以獨立的 gating routing control 與 target routing control 構成的整體 on/off 主開關，並不會強制 target 必須維持 On。AWS gating-rule 範例使用 Type OR、Threshold 0，而非 Threshold 1，且選項文字自相矛盾 (先說建立 gating rule，又說套用 assertion safety rule)。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Resource sets and readiness checks belong to ARC's readiness checking feature, which audits whether resources are provisioned and configured to handle failover (quotas, config, capacity). They do not enforce or constrain routing control state changes, so they cannot keep a routing control turned On. Routing control ARNs are also not AWS::Route53::HealthCheck resources.","why_zh":"resource set 與 readiness check 屬於 ARC 的 readiness checking 功能，用於稽核資源是否已備妥可承接 failover (配額、設定、容量)。它們不會強制或限制 routing control 的狀態變更，因此無法讓某個 routing control 維持 On。Routing control ARN 也不是 AWS::Route53::HealthCheck 資源。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Like option C, this uses the readiness-check feature (AWS::Route53RecoveryReadiness::DNSTargetResource resource type), which validates DNS target configuration/readiness rather than governing routing control states. It cannot prevent a DevOps engineer from turning off both routing controls.","why_zh":"與選項 C 相同，這使用 readiness check 功能 (AWS::Route53RecoveryReadiness::DNSTargetResource 資源類型)，僅驗證 DNS target 的設定/就緒程度，而非管控 routing control 狀態，無法阻止工程師同時關閉兩個 routing control。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/r53recovery/latest/dg/routing-control.safety-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/recovery-cluster/latest/api/create-safety-rule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/recovery-cluster/latest/api/safetyrule.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":178,"question_en":"A healthcare services company is concerned about the growing costs of software licensing for an application for monitoring patient wellness. The company wants to create an audit process to ensure that the application is running exclusively on Amazon EC2 Dedicated Hosts. A DevOps engineer must create a workflow to audit the application to ensure compliance. What steps should the engineer take to meet this requirement with the LEAST administrative overhead?","question_zh":"一家医疗保健服务公司对用于监测患者健康状况的应用程序的软件许可费用不断上涨感到担忧。该公 司希望创建一个审计流程以确保 该应用程序仅在亚马逊 EC2 专用主机上运行。一名 DevOps 工程师必须创建一个工作流程来审核该应用程 序，以确保其合规性。 采取哪些步骤 工程师应如何以最低的管理开销来满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager Configuration Compliance. Use calls to the put-compliance-items API action to scan and build a database of noncompliant EC2 instances based on their host placement configuration. Use an Amazon DynamoDB table to store these instance IDs for fast access. Generate a report through Systems Manager by calling the list-compliance-summaries API action.","B":"Use custom Java code running on an EC2 instance. Set up EC2 Auto Scaling for the instance depending on the number of instances to be checked. Send the list of noncompliant EC2 instance IDs to an Amazon SQS queue. Set up another worker instance to process instance IDs from the SQS queue and write them to Amazon DynamoDB. Use an AWS Lambda function to terminate noncompliant instance IDs obtained from the queue, and send them to an Amazon SNS email topic for distribution.","C":"Use AWS Config. Identify all EC2 instances to be audited by enabling Config Recording on all Amazon EC2 resources for the region. Create a custom AWS Config rule that triggers an AWS Lambda function by using the \"config-rule-change -triggered\" blueprint. Modify the Lambda evaluateCompliance() function to verify host placement to return a NON_COMPLIANT result if the instance is not running on an EC2 Dedicated Host. Use the AWS Config report to address noncompliant instances.","D":"Use AWS CloudTrail. Identify all EC2 instances to be audited by analyzing all calls to the EC2 RunCommand API action. Invoke an AWS Lambda function that analyzes the host placement of the instance. Store the EC2 instance ID of noncompliant resources in an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance. Generate a report by querying the RDS instance and exporting the query results to a CSV text file."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 配置合规性。通过调用 put-compliance-items API 操作扫描并构建一个基于其 主机放置配置的不合规 EC2 实例数据库。使用 Amazon DynamoDB 表存储这些实例 ID 以实现快速访问。 通过调用 list-compliance-summaries API 操作，利用 Systems Manager 生成报告。","B":"在 EC2 实例上运行自定义 Java 代码。根据要检查的实例数量为该实例设置 EC2 自动扩展。将不符合要 求的 EC2 实例 ID 列表发送到 Amazon SQS 队列。设置另一个工作实例从 SQS 队列处理实例 ID 并将其 写入 Amazon DynamoDB。使用 AWS Lambda 函数终止从队列获取的不符合要求的实例 ID，并将其发 送到 Amazon SNS 电子邮件主题以进行分发。","C":"使用 AWS Config。通过在该区域的所有 Amazon EC2 资源上启用配置记录来识别所有要审核的 EC2 实例。 创建一个自定义的 AWS Config 规则，使用“config-rule-change-triggered”蓝图触发 AWS Lambda 函数。 修改 Lambda 的 evaluateCompliance（） 函数以验证主机放置，如果实例未在 EC2 专用主机上运行，则 返回“不合规”结果。使用 AWS Config 报告来处理不合规的实例。","D":"使用 AWS CloudTrail。通过分析对 EC2 RunCommand API 操作的所有调用，确定所有要审计的 EC2 实例。调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数来分析实例的主机放置情况。将不符合要求的资源的 EC2 实例 ID 存储在 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例中。通过查询 RDS 实例生成报告，并将查询结果导 出为 CSV 文本文件。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a detective audit/compliance workflow to verify that EC2 instances run exclusively on Dedicated Hosts, with the LEAST administrative overhead. AWS Config is the purpose-built detective compliance service: it natively records the AWS::EC2::Instance resource type (including its placement/tenancy configuration), and you author a custom AWS Config rule backed by a Lambda function (the 'config-rule-change-triggered' blueprint) whose evaluateCompliance() logic inspects host placement and returns NON_COMPLIANT when an instance is not on a Dedicated Host. Per the AWS docs, Config rules support a Configuration-changes trigger that re-evaluates whenever a matching resource changes, and they return COMPLIANT/NON_COMPLIANT results that Config aggregates into a built-in compliance dashboard/report with no custom data store or polling. AWS even ships a managed rule, desired-instance-tenancy (identifier DESIRED_INSTANCE_TENANCY, resource type AWS::EC2::Instance, Configuration-changes trigger) that checks for a tenancy value of DEDICATED/HOST and specific Dedicated Host IDs, confirming Config natively understands host placement and is the native, low-overhead fit. Option C matches this managed-service, change-triggered, serverless detective pattern exactly.","explanation_zh":"需求是建立偵測型稽核/合規流程以驗證 EC2 執行個體是否只在 Dedicated Hosts 上運行，且要求最少的管理開銷。AWS Config 正是為此設計的偵測型合規服務：它原生記錄 AWS::EC2::Instance 資源類型（含其 placement/tenancy 設定），你只需建立自訂 AWS Config rule，並以 Lambda 函式（config-rule-change-triggered 範本）實作 evaluateCompliance() 來檢查 host placement，若執行個體不在 Dedicated Host 上即回傳 NON_COMPLIANT。依 AWS 文件，Config rule 支援 Configuration changes 觸發類型，每當符合範圍的資源變更時重新評估，並回傳 COMPLIANT/NON_COMPLIANT，由 Config 自動彙整成內建合規儀表板/報告，不需自建資料庫或輪詢。事實上 AWS 還提供受管規則 desired-instance-tenancy（識別碼 DESIRED_INSTANCE_TENANCY、資源類型 AWS::EC2::Instance、Configuration changes 觸發），可檢查 tenancy 值為 DEDICATED/HOST 與特定 Dedicated Host ID，足見 Config 原生理解 host placement，是原生且低開銷的解法。選項 C 完全符合此受管服務、變更觸發、無伺服器的偵測模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Per the AWS docs, Systems Manager Compliance tracks only Patch Manager patch compliance, State Manager association compliance, and custom compliance metadata that you push yourself via put-compliance-items (the ResourceType parameter only supports ManagedInstance). It does not inspect EC2 control-plane attributes like host placement/tenancy, so you would have to build a custom agent-side scanner and manually plumb data into a separate DynamoDB table, which is far more administrative overhead, and list-compliance-summaries is not a native EC2 host-placement report.","why_zh":"依 AWS 文件，Systems Manager Compliance 只追蹤 Patch Manager 的 patch 合規、State Manager 關聯合規，以及你自己透過 put-compliance-items 推送的自訂合規中繼資料（ResourceType 參數只支援 ManagedInstance）。它不會檢查像 host placement/tenancy 這類 EC2 控制平面屬性，因此你得自建代理端掃描程式並手動把資料寫入額外的 DynamoDB 表，管理開銷大得多，且 list-compliance-summaries 並非原生的 EC2 host placement 報告。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Custom Java code on EC2 with Auto Scaling, SQS, worker instances, DynamoDB, Lambda termination, and SNS is a fully hand-built, high-maintenance pipeline. It also terminates noncompliant instances, which an audit/compliance requirement did not ask for, and represents the maximum administrative overhead, the opposite of the qualifier.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上跑自訂 Java 程式並搭配 Auto Scaling、SQS、worker 執行個體、DynamoDB、Lambda 終止與 SNS，是完全手工打造、維運成本極高的流程。它還會終止不合規執行個體，而稽核/合規需求並未要求此動作，且代表最大的管理開銷，正好與題目限定詞相反。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail records API events, but auditing host placement by analyzing 'EC2 RunCommand' calls is wrong: there is no such event for instance launches (the launch API is RunInstances, and RunCommand belongs to SSM), and CloudTrail is an event log, not a current-state compliance evaluator. Storing results in RDS for MySQL and exporting CSV manually adds undifferentiated heavy lifting versus Config's built-in compliance reporting.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 記錄 API 事件，但透過分析「EC2 RunCommand」呼叫來稽核 host placement 是錯的：根本沒有這個事件對應執行個體啟動（啟動 API 是 RunInstances，而 RunCommand 屬於 SSM），且 CloudTrail 是事件日誌而非當前狀態的合規評估器。把結果存進 RDS for MySQL 並手動匯出 CSV，相較於 Config 內建的合規報告，增加了大量無差異化的繁重工作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/desired-instance-tenancy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_develop-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/how-does-config-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/compliance-about.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":179,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is planning to deploy a Ruby-based application to production. The application needs to interact with an Amazon RDS for MySQL database and should have automatic scaling and high availability. The stored data in the database is critical and should persist regardless of the state of the application stack. The DevOps engineer needs to set up an automated deployment strategy for the application with automatic rollbacks. The solution also must alert the application team when a deployment fails. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师计划将一个基于 Ruby 的应用程序部署到生产环境。该应用程序需要与 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库进行交互，并应具备自动扩展和高可用性。数据库中存储的数据至关重要，无论应用程序堆 栈处于何种状态，这些数据都应得以保留。 DevOps 工程师需要为应用程序设置具有自动回滚功能的自动化部署策略。该解决方案还必须在部 署失败时向应用程序团队发出警报。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application on AWS Elastic Beanstalk. Deploy an Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance as part of the Elastic Beanstalk configuration.","B":"Deploy the application on AWS Elastic Beanstalk. Deploy a separate Amazon RDS for MySQL DB instance outside of Elastic Beanstalk.","C":"Configure a notification email address that alerts the application team in the AWS Elastic Beanstalk configuration.","D":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to monitor AWS Health events. Use an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as a target to alert the application team.","E":"Use the immutable deployment method to deploy new application versions.","F":"Use the rolling deployment method to deploy new application versions."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 上部署应用程序。作为 Elastic Beanstalk 配置的一部分，部署一个 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例。","B":"在 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 上部署应用程序。在 Elastic Beanstalk 之外单独部署一个 Amazon RDS for MySQL 数据库实例。","C":"在 AWS 弹性 Beanstalk 配置中设置一个通知电子邮件地址，以便在出现情况时向应用程序团队发出警 报。","D":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则来监控 AWS Health 事件。使用 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题作为目标，向应用程序团队发出警报。","E":"使用不可变部署方法来部署新的应用程序版本。","F":"使用滚动部署方法来部署新的应用程序版本。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The solution needs a Ruby platform with auto scaling and HA (Elastic Beanstalk), an RDS for MySQL whose data survives the stack, automated deployment with automatic rollback, and failure alerting. B is correct: an external/decoupled RDS DB instance is independent of the environment lifecycle. The Elastic Beanstalk DB doc states that with a decoupled database 'If you need to terminate the environment, you can do so and also choose the option to keep the database available and operational outside of Elastic Beanstalk,' and the Retain deletion policy keeps the instance 'available and operational' - so the critical data persists regardless of the state of the application stack. A is wrong because a coupled RDS instance shares the environment lifecycle. C is correct: Elastic Beanstalk has a native notification feature - you enter an email address and Beanstalk creates an SNS topic that emails you 'whenever an error occurs or the health of your environment changes,' which includes the health change a failed deployment produces; this is the lowest-overhead native alert. E is correct: the Immutable deployment policy is documented as 'If the new instances don't pass health checks, Elastic Beanstalk terminates them, leaving the original instances untouched' - automatic rollback. F (Rolling) is wrong because its documented recovery is to 'perform another deployment with a fixed or known good version of your application to roll back' - a manual redeploy, not automatic. D is wrong because an EventBridge rule on AWS Health events monitors AWS-side service/account infrastructure health, not application deployment success/failure, and is redundant given the native email in C.","explanation_zh":"需求為 Ruby 平台具自動擴展與高可用（Elastic Beanstalk）、一個資料能不受堆疊狀態影響而保留的 RDS for MySQL、具自動回滾的自動化部署，以及部署失敗通知。B 正確：外部/decoupled 的 RDS DB instance 獨立於環境生命週期。Elastic Beanstalk 文件指出，使用 decoupled 資料庫時「若需終止環境，你可以這麼做，並選擇讓資料庫在 Elastic Beanstalk 之外保持可用且持續運作」，且 Retain 刪除原則會讓執行個體「保持可用且持續運作」，因此關鍵資料能不論應用堆疊狀態為何皆保留。A 錯誤，因為 coupled 的 RDS instance 與環境共享生命週期。C 正確：Elastic Beanstalk 內建通知功能，輸入電子郵件後，Beanstalk 會建立 SNS topic，在「發生錯誤或環境健康變化時」寄送郵件，而部署失敗會造成健康變化，是最低營運負擔的原生告警。E 正確：Immutable 部署策略文件載明「若新執行個體未通過健康檢查，Elastic Beanstalk 會終止它們，使原始執行個體保持不變」，即自動回滾。F（Rolling）錯誤，因為其文件記載的復原方式是「以固定或已知良好的應用版本重新部署以回滾」，屬手動重新部署，非自動。D 錯誤：EventBridge 監控 AWS Health events 針對的是 AWS 端服務/帳戶基礎設施健康，而非應用程式部署成功/失敗，且在有 C 提供原生郵件下屬冗餘。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A coupled RDS instance shares the Elastic Beanstalk environment lifecycle, so terminating the environment can delete the DB unless extra deletion-policy work is done; AWS docs recommend a decoupled/external DB for production precisely so the database 'remains available and operational' independent of the environment. Data does not inherently persist regardless of stack state with a coupled DB.","why_zh":"Coupled 的 RDS instance 與 Elastic Beanstalk 環境共享生命週期，終止環境可能刪除資料庫；AWS 文件正是建議生產環境使用 decoupled/外部資料庫，使其「保持可用且持續運作」而獨立於環境。Coupled 資料庫不會天生地不受堆疊狀態影響而保留資料。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Health events report on AWS-side service and account infrastructure health (outages, scheduled maintenance), not application deployment success or failure, so it is the wrong event source for alerting on a failed deployment. It is also redundant given the native email notification in C, and adds unnecessary operational overhead.","why_zh":"AWS Health events 回報的是 AWS 端服務與帳戶基礎設施健康（中斷、排程維護），而非應用程式部署成功或失敗，因此對部署失敗告警而言是錯誤的事件來源。它在 C 提供原生郵件通知下亦屬冗餘，並增加不必要的營運負擔。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Rolling deployment does not roll back automatically: AWS docs say that after a failed rolling deployment you must 'perform another deployment with a fixed or known good version of your application to roll back' - a manual redeploy. Immutable (E) provides the automatic, safe rollback the requirement demands by terminating the failed new instances.","why_zh":"Rolling 部署不會自動回滾：AWS 文件指出 rolling 部署失敗後，必須「以固定或已知良好的應用版本重新部署以回滾」，屬手動重新部署。Immutable（E）藉由終止失敗的新執行個體，提供需求所要求的自動且安全的回滾。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.managing.db.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.rolling-version-deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/environmentmgmt-updates-immutable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticbeanstalk/latest/dg/using-features.managing.sns.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":180,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CodePipeline to deploy an application. According to a new guideline, a member of the company's security team must sign off on any application changes before the changes are deployed into production. The approval must be recorded and retained. Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 部署应用程序。根据一项新规定，公司安全团队的一名成员必须在任 何应用程序变更部署到生产环境之前进行审批。该审批必须被记录并保存。 哪种行动组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure CodePipeline to write actions to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","B":"Configure CodePipeline to write actions to an Amazon S3 bucket at the end of each pipeline stage.","C":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail to deliver logs to Amazon S3.","D":"Create a CodePipeline custom action to invoke an AWS Lambda function for approval. Create a policy that gives the security team access to manage CodePipeline custom actions.","E":"Create a CodePipeline manual approval action before the deployment step. Create a policy that grants the security team access to approve manual approval stages."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CodePipeline 配置为将操作写入 Amazon CloudWatch 日志。","B":"配置 CodePipeline，使其在每个管道阶段结束时将操作写入 Amazon S3 存储桶。","C":"创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪以将日志传递到 Amazon S3。","D":"创建一个 CodePipeline 自定义操作以调用 AWS Lambda 函数进行审批。创建一个策略，授予安全团队管 理 CodePipeline 自定义操作的权限。","E":"在部署步骤之前创建一个 CodePipeline 手动审批操作。创建一项策略，授予安全团队批准手动审批阶段的 权限。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The two requirements are (1) a security team member must sign off before a production deployment and (2) the approval must be recorded and retained. Option E satisfies the sign-off: CodePipeline's native manual approval action is added to a stage at the point where you want pipeline execution to stop so that someone with the required IAM permissions can approve or reject; the setup explicitly requires granting IAM approval permissions (the AWSCodePipelineApproverAccess managed policy or a scoped custom policy) to the security team. Option C satisfies the recorded-and-retained requirement: AWS docs state all CodePipeline API actions are logged by CloudTrail, and creating a trail enables continuous delivery of those events to an Amazon S3 bucket for an ongoing, durable record. The approve/reject decision (the PutApprovalResult API call) is therefore captured and retained in S3. Together C and E meet both requirements, confirming the dump's suggested answer.","explanation_zh":"兩項需求是 (1) 部署到生產環境前必須由安全團隊成員簽核，(2) 該簽核必須被記錄並保留。選項 E 滿足簽核需求：CodePipeline 原生的 manual approval action 加在 stage 中希望暫停 pipeline 執行的位置，讓擁有所需 IAM 權限的人核准或拒絕；其設定流程明確要求授予安全團隊 IAM 核准權限（AWSCodePipelineApproverAccess 受管政策或範圍化的自訂政策）。選項 C 滿足記錄與保留需求：AWS 文件指出所有 CodePipeline API 動作都會由 CloudTrail 記錄，而建立 trail 可將這些事件持續遞送到 Amazon S3 bucket，形成持久的記錄。核准/拒絕決定（PutApprovalResult API 呼叫）因此會被捕捉並保留在 S3。C 與 E 一起滿足兩項需求，確認題庫建議答案正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodePipeline has no configuration to 'write actions to CloudWatch Logs.' Pipeline state changes flow to EventBridge, not a logs sink, and this does not capture the approver identity in a durable, retained audit record the way a CloudTrail trail to S3 does.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 沒有「將動作寫入 CloudWatch Logs」的設定。Pipeline 狀態變更是送往 EventBridge，而非日誌儲存，且無法像 CloudTrail trail 寫入 S3 那樣以持久、可保留的稽核記錄捕捉核准者身分。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodePipeline does not write an audit log of actions to S3 at the end of each stage. S3 is used for pipeline artifacts, not action/approval auditing. This is a fabricated feature.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 不會在每個 stage 結束時將動作稽核日誌寫入 S3。S3 用於 pipeline artifacts，而非動作/核准稽核。此為杜撰的功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Custom actions integrate third-party/custom job workers for build, test, or deploy steps, not approvals. The native manual approval action is the correct sign-off mechanism, and granting access to 'manage CodePipeline custom actions' is not the same as authorizing an approve/reject decision.","why_zh":"Custom actions 用於整合第三方/自訂 job worker 的 build、test 或 deploy 步驟，並非用於核准。原生的 manual approval action 才是正確的簽核機制，而授予「管理 CodePipeline custom actions」的權限不等於授權核准/拒絕決定。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals-iam-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/monitoring-cloudtrail-logs.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":181,"question_en":"A company requires its internal business teams to launch resources through pre-approved AWS CloudFormation templates only. The security team requires automated monitoring when resources drift from their expected state. Which strategy should be used to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司要求其内部业务团队仅通过预先批准的 AWS CloudFormation 模板来部署资源。安全团队要求 在资源偏离预期状态时进行自动监控。 应采用哪种策略来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Allow users to deploy CloudFormation stacks using a CloudFormation service role only. Use CloudFormation drift detection to detect when resources have drifted from their expected state.","B":"Allow users to deploy CloudFormation stacks using a CloudFormation service role only. Use AWS Config rules to detect when resources have drifted from their expected state.","C":"Allow users to deploy CloudFormation stacks using AWS Service Catalog only. Enforce the use of a launch constraint. Use AWS Config rules to detect when resources have drifted from their expected state.","D":"Allow users to deploy CloudFormation stacks using AWS Service Catalog only. Enforce the use of a template constraint. Use Amazon EventBridge notifications to detect when resources have drifted from their expected state."},"options_zh":{"A":"允许用户仅使用 CloudFormation 服务角色部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。使用 CloudFormation 漂移 检测来检测资源是否偏离其预期状态。","B":"允许用户仅使用 CloudFormation 服务角色部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。使用 AWS Config 规则检测资 源是否偏离其预期状态。","C":"允许用户仅通过 AWS 服务目录部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。强制使用启动约束。使用 AWS Config 规 则检测资源是否偏离预期状态。","D":"允许用户仅通过 AWS 服务目录部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。强制使用模板约束。使用 Amazon EventBridge 通知来检测资源是否偏离预期状态。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must both be satisfied: (1) internal teams may launch resources only through pre-approved CloudFormation templates, and (2) automated monitoring of resource drift. AWS Service Catalog is the governance service for distributing pre-approved CloudFormation products to internal teams. A launch constraint assigns an IAM role that Service Catalog assumes when an end user launches, updates, or terminates a product; the docs state that without a launch constraint users must use their own IAM credentials with CloudFormation and resource permissions, but with a launch role you 'limit the end users' permissions to the minimum they require for that product.' This lets you remove direct CloudFormation/resource permissions from users so they can deploy ONLY through approved products, enforcing requirement 1. AWS Config rules continuously and automatically evaluate resource configurations against your desired settings and flag non-compliant (drifted) resources, satisfying the automated-monitoring requirement 2. Option C combines both correctly.","explanation_zh":"本題須同時滿足兩個條件：(1) 內部團隊只能透過事先核准的 CloudFormation 範本佈署資源；(2) 自動監控資源偏移 (drift)。AWS Service Catalog 是用來向內部團隊發佈事先核准的 CloudFormation 產品的治理服務。launch constraint (啟動限制) 會指派一個 IAM role，讓 Service Catalog 在使用者啟動、更新或終止產品時代為承擔該角色；官方文件指出，若沒有 launch constraint，使用者必須以自身的 IAM 憑證並具備 CloudFormation 與資源權限才能佈署，而使用 launch role 後即可『將終端使用者的權限限制在該產品所需的最小範圍』。因此可移除使用者直接操作 CloudFormation/資源的權限，使其只能透過核准的產品佈署，滿足條件一。AWS Config rules 會持續且自動地依您期望的設定評估資源組態並標記不合規 (偏移) 的資源，滿足自動監控的條件二。因此選項 C 同時正確涵蓋兩個面向。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A CloudFormation service role alone does not restrict users to pre-approved templates the way Service Catalog products do; it governs what CloudFormation can do, not which templates a team may submit. More importantly, CloudFormation drift detection is a manual, on-demand operation initiated via the console or CLI (detect-stack-drift), not continuous automated monitoring, so it fails the security team's automated-monitoring requirement.","why_zh":"單純的 CloudFormation service role 無法像 Service Catalog 產品那樣限制使用者只能用事先核准的範本；它管的是 CloudFormation 能做什麼，而非團隊能提交哪些範本。更關鍵的是，CloudFormation drift detection 是透過主控台或 CLI (detect-stack-drift) 手動、按需執行的操作，並非持續的自動監控，因此無法滿足資安團隊的自動監控需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config rules for drift monitoring is correct, but a CloudFormation service role alone is not the AWS-recommended way to restrict internal teams to pre-approved templates only. A service role defines the permissions CloudFormation uses during stack operations; it does not create a catalog of approved products nor stop users from launching arbitrary templates with their own permissions. Service Catalog with a launch constraint (Option C) is the purpose-built governance mechanism, so requirement 1 is not met.","why_zh":"用 AWS Config rules 做偏移監控是正確的，但單靠 CloudFormation service role 並不是 AWS 建議用來限制內部團隊『只能使用事先核准範本』的方式。service role 定義的是 CloudFormation 在堆疊操作期間所用的權限，既不會建立核准產品目錄，也無法阻止使用者用自身權限啟動任意範本。搭配 launch constraint 的 Service Catalog (選項 C) 才是專為此治理需求設計的機制，因此未滿足需求一。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Both halves are wrong. A template constraint only narrows the allowable parameter values within a product's CloudFormation template (e.g., limiting EC2 instance types); it does not enforce that users can deploy only through approved products - that is the launch constraint's job. And EventBridge does not detect drift on its own: the 'CloudFormation Drift Detection Status Change' event is emitted only AFTER a drift detection operation has been initiated/completed, so EventBridge merely notifies on the result of a drift check that something else must trigger. It cannot autonomously detect when resources have drifted.","why_zh":"兩半都錯。template constraint 只能縮小產品 CloudFormation 範本中允許的參數值範圍 (例如限制 EC2 執行個體類型)，並無法強制使用者只能透過核准的產品佈署——那是 launch constraint 的職責。而 EventBridge 本身並不會偵測偏移：『CloudFormation Drift Detection Status Change』事件只在偏移偵測操作被啟動/完成『之後』才發出，因此 EventBridge 僅是針對某個必須由其他機制觸發的偏移檢查結果發出通知，無法自主偵測資源何時發生偏移。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/constraints-launch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/adminguide/catalogs_constraints_template-constraints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/detect-drift-stack.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/event-detail-stack-drift-detection-change.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":182,"question_en":"A company has multiple development groups working in a single shared AWS account. The senior manager of the groups wants to be alerted via a third-party API call when the creation of resources approaches the service limits for the account. Which solution will accomplish this with the LEAST amount of development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司有多个开发团队在一个共享的 AWS 账户中工作。这些团队的高级经理希望在账户的服务 资源接近上限时，通过第三方 API 调用收到提醒。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量实现这一目标？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs periodically and targets an AWS Lambda function. Within the Lambda function, evaluate the current state of the AWS environment and compare deployed resource values to resource limits on the account. Notify the senior manager if the account is approaching a service limit.","B":"Deploy an AWS Lambda function that refreshes AWS Trusted Advisor checks, and configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the Lambda function periodically. Create another EventBridge rule with an event pattern matching Trusted Advisor events and a target Lambda function. In the target Lambda function, notify the senior manager.","C":"Deploy an AWS Lambda function that refreshes AWS Health Dashboard checks, and configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the Lambda function periodically. Create another EventBridge rule with an event pattern matching Health Dashboard events and a target Lambda function. In the target Lambda function, notify the senior manager.","D":"Add an AWS Config custom rule that runs periodically, checks the AWS service limit status, and streams notifications to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Deploy an AWS Lambda function that notifies the senior manager, and subscribe the Lambda function to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个定期运行的 Amazon EventBridge 规则，并将其目标设置为一个 AWS Lambda 函数。在 Lambda 函数中，评估 AWS 环境的当前状态，并将已部署资源的值与账户的服务限制进行比较。如果账户即将 达到服务限制，则通知高级经理。","B":"部署一个 AWS Lambda 函数来刷新 AWS 可信顾问检查，并配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以定期运行 该 Lambda 函数。创建另一个 EventBridge 规则，其事件模式匹配可信顾问事件，并将目标设置为一个 Lambda 函数。在目标 Lambda 函数中，通知高级经理。","C":"部署一个 AWS Lambda 函数来刷新 AWS 健康仪表板检查，并配置一个 创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，定期运行 Lambda 函数。再创建一个 EventBridge 规则，其事件模式 匹配健康仪表板事件，并将目标设置为另一个 Lambda 函数。在该目标 Lambda 函数中，通知高级经理。","D":"添加一个定期运行的 AWS Config 自定义规则，检查 AWS 服务限制状态，并将通知流式传输到 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题。部署一个 AWS Lambda 函数以通知高级经理，并将 该 Lambda 函数订阅到 SNS 主题。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Trusted Advisor's 'Service limits' category checks already perform the usage-vs-limit comparison for the account and alert at Yellow (80% of limit reached) and Red (100% of limit reached) - exactly 'approaching the service limits.' Because that evaluation logic is built in, almost no custom code is required. Trusted Advisor also sends a 'Trusted Advisor Check Item Refresh Notification' event directly to Amazon EventBridge (source: aws.trustedadvisor), which can be matched with a simple event pattern. So the only development needed is one small Lambda that periodically calls the AWS Support RefreshTrustedAdvisorCheck API to refresh the checks, plus a second EventBridge rule matching the Trusted Advisor event that triggers a small Lambda to make the third-party API call. This is the LEAST development effort because Trusted Advisor does the resource-vs-limit comparison and natively emits the events. (Note: a Service Quotas + CloudWatch alarm approach would be even more native, but no option offers it, so B is the best of the given choices.)","explanation_zh":"AWS Trusted Advisor 的「Service limits」類別檢查已經會替帳戶完成「使用量對上限」的比較，並在 Yellow（達上限 80%）與 Red（達上限 100%）時發出警示，正好對應題目所說的「approaching the service limits」。由於這項評估邏輯是內建的，幾乎不需自行撰寫程式。Trusted Advisor 也會將「Trusted Advisor Check Item Refresh Notification」事件直接送至 Amazon EventBridge（source: aws.trustedadvisor），可用簡單的事件模式比對。因此唯一需要開發的，是一個小型 Lambda 定期呼叫 AWS Support 的 RefreshTrustedAdvisorCheck API 來刷新檢查，再加上第二個比對 Trusted Advisor 事件的 EventBridge 規則，觸發一個小型 Lambda 進行第三方 API 呼叫。因為由 Trusted Advisor 替你完成資源對配額的比較並原生發出事件，這是開發工作量最少的做法。（補充：使用 Service Quotas 搭配 CloudWatch 警示會更為原生，但選項中並未提供此做法，故 B 仍是給定選項中的最佳解。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Requires writing and maintaining a large custom Lambda that enumerates every deployed resource across all services and compares each against its limit. This re-implements what Trusted Advisor already provides natively, making it among the MOST development effort, not the least.","why_zh":"需要撰寫並維護龐大的自訂 Lambda，列舉所有服務中已部署的資源並逐一與其上限比較。這等於重新實作 Trusted Advisor 已原生提供的功能，是開發量最大的選項之一，而非最少。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Health Dashboard surfaces operational events and scheduled changes affecting your resources; it does not proactively evaluate quota/limit utilization or alert when usage approaches a limit the way Trusted Advisor's Service limits checks do. It also has no refreshable 'checks' API like Trusted Advisor's RefreshTrustedAdvisorCheck, so the described 'refresh Health Dashboard checks' step is not a real mechanism. Wrong service for monitoring quota thresholds.","why_zh":"AWS Health Dashboard 呈現影響資源的營運事件與排程變更，並不會像 Trusted Advisor 的 Service limits 檢查那樣主動評估配額/上限使用率，也不會在用量接近上限時發出警示。它亦沒有像 Trusted Advisor 的 RefreshTrustedAdvisorCheck 那樣可刷新的『檢查』API，因此所述『刷新 Health Dashboard 檢查』並非真實機制。對於監控配額門檻而言是錯誤的服務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Config has no native managed or custom rule that checks service-limit/quota status; a custom rule would still need substantial custom Lambda code to query quota usage (effort comparable to option A). The description of a Config custom rule that itself 'streams notifications to an SNS topic' also misrepresents how Config works - Config rules emit compliance evaluations and notifications are routed via EventBridge/SNS, not 'streamed' by the rule. So it is neither lower-effort nor accurate.","why_zh":"AWS Config 沒有原生的受管或自訂規則可檢查服務上限/配額狀態；自訂規則仍需大量自訂 Lambda 程式碼查詢配額使用量（工作量與選項 A 相當）。所謂 Config 自訂規則本身會『將通知串流至 SNS 主題』的描述也誤解了 Config 的運作方式——Config 規則發出的是合規評估結果，通知是透過 EventBridge/SNS 路由，而非由規則『串流』。因此既非工作量較少也不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awssupport/latest/user/service-limits.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-trustedadvisor.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awssupport/latest/user/trustedadvisor.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awssupport/latest/user/trusted-advisor-check-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicequotas/latest/userguide/configure-cloudwatch.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":183,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is setting up a container-based architecture. The engineer has decided to use AWS CloudFormation to automatically provision an Amazon ECS cluster and an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group to launch the EC2 container instances. After successfully creating the CloudFormation stack, the engineer noticed that, even though the ECS cluster and the EC2 instances were created successfully and the stack finished the creation, the EC2 instances were associating with a different cluster. How should the DevOps engineer update the CloudFormation template to resolve this issue?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在搭建基于容器的架构。该工程师决定使用 AWS CloudFormation 自动配置一个 Amazon ECS 集群和一个 Amazon EC2 自动扩展组来启动 EC2 容器实例。在成功创建 CloudFormation 堆栈 后，工程师注意到，尽管 ECS 集群和 EC2 实例都已成功创建且堆栈已完成创建，但 EC2 实例却关联到了 另一个集群。 DevOps 工程师应如何更新 CloudFormation 模板以解决此问题？ AECS::Cluster 资源中引用 EC2 实例，并在 AWS::ECS::Service 资源中引用 ECS 集群。 BAutoScaling::LaunchConfiguration 资源的 UserData 属性中引用 ECS 集群。","options_en":{"A":"Reference the EC2 instances in the AWS::ECS::Cluster resource and reference the ECS cluster in the AWS::ECS::Service resource.","B":"Reference the ECS cluster in the AWS::AutoScaling::LaunchConfiguration resource of the UserData property.","C":"Reference the ECS cluster in the AWS::EC2::Instance resource of the UserData property.","D":"Reference the ECS cluster in the AWS::CloudFormation::CustomResource resource to trigger an AWS Lambda function that registers the EC2 instances with the appropriate ECS cluster."},"options_zh":{"C":"在 UserDataEC2::Instance 资源中引用 ECS 集群。 DCloudFormation::CustomResource 资源中引用 ECS 集群，以触发一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 EC2 实例注册 到相应的 ECS 集群中。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"An Amazon ECS EC2 container instance decides which cluster to join from the ECS_CLUSTER variable in /etc/ecs/ecs.config, which the ECS container agent reads when it starts (AWS docs: 'The Linux variants of the Amazon ECS-optimized AMI look for agent configuration data in the /etc/ecs/ecs.config file when the container agent starts'). If ECS_CLUSTER is not set, the instance registers with the 'default' cluster, which exactly matches the symptom of instances associating with a 'different cluster' while the stack still reports CREATE_COMPLETE (no resource fails). The supported way to set this value is Amazon EC2 user data at launch time (echo \"ECS_CLUSTER=MyCluster\" >> /etc/ecs/ecs.config). Because the instances are launched by an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group, the ASG builds them from a launch configuration (or launch template), not from a standalone AWS::EC2::Instance resource, so the user data must live in the UserData property of the AWS::AutoScaling::LaunchConfiguration resource. Option B does exactly this and is the correct fix.","explanation_zh":"Amazon ECS 的 EC2 container instance 會依據 /etc/ecs/ecs.config 中的 ECS_CLUSTER 變數來決定要加入哪一個 cluster，這個檔案會在 ECS container agent 啟動時被讀取（AWS 文件：Linux 版的 Amazon ECS-optimized AMI 會在 container agent 啟動時讀取 /etc/ecs/ecs.config 的設定資料）。若未設定 ECS_CLUSTER，instance 會註冊到 'default' cluster，這正好符合題目描述：instance 加入了「不同的 cluster」，但 stack 仍回報 CREATE_COMPLETE（沒有任何資源失敗）。設定此值的官方支援做法是在啟動時透過 Amazon EC2 user data（echo \"ECS_CLUSTER=MyCluster\" >> /etc/ecs/ecs.config）。由於 instance 是由 Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group 啟動，ASG 會依據 launch configuration（或 launch template）來建立 instance，而非透過獨立的 AWS::EC2::Instance 資源，因此 user data 必須放在 AWS::AutoScaling::LaunchConfiguration 資源的 UserData 屬性中。選項 B 正是如此，為正確解法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no mechanism by which referencing EC2 instances in AWS::ECS::Cluster or referencing the cluster in AWS::ECS::Service controls container-instance registration. An ECS service references a cluster only for task placement; it does not change which cluster an EC2 container instance registers itself with via the agent's ECS_CLUSTER setting, so this does not fix the wrong-cluster association.","why_zh":"在 AWS::ECS::Cluster 中參照 EC2 instance、或在 AWS::ECS::Service 中參照 cluster，都無法控制 container instance 的註冊行為。ECS service 參照 cluster 只是用於 task 放置，並不會改變 EC2 container instance 透過 agent 的 ECS_CLUSTER 設定所註冊的 cluster，因此無法解決註冊到錯誤 cluster 的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The mechanism (set ECS_CLUSTER in UserData) is correct, but the resource type is wrong. The instances are launched by the EC2 Auto Scaling group, which builds them from a launch configuration/template, not from a standalone AWS::EC2::Instance resource that does not exist in this architecture. User data placed on an AWS::EC2::Instance would never be applied to the ASG-launched container instances, so the wrong-cluster behavior would persist.","why_zh":"機制（在 UserData 設定 ECS_CLUSTER）是正確的，但資源類型錯了。Instance 是由 EC2 Auto Scaling group 啟動，由 launch configuration/template 建立，而非此架構中並不存在的獨立 AWS::EC2::Instance 資源。放在 AWS::EC2::Instance 上的 user data 永遠不會套用到 ASG 啟動的 container instance，因此錯誤 cluster 的行為仍會持續。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using a CloudFormation custom resource plus a Lambda function to register instances is an unnecessary anti-pattern when ECS provides a native, supported mechanism (user data setting ECS_CLUSTER). ECS instances self-register at boot when ECS_CLUSTER is set; a custom resource runs once during stack create/update, not each time the ASG dynamically launches a new instance during scaling, so it would not reliably register instances added later and is far more complex than the correct fix.","why_zh":"使用 CloudFormation custom resource 搭配 Lambda 函式來註冊 instance，是不必要的反模式，因為 ECS 已提供原生且受支援的機制（透過 user data 設定 ECS_CLUSTER）。當設定了 ECS_CLUSTER 時，ECS instance 會在開機時自我註冊；custom resource 只在 stack 建立/更新期間執行一次，而非在 ASG 於擴展時動態啟動新 instance 時觸發，因此無法可靠地註冊後續新增的 instance，且遠比正確解法複雜。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/bootstrap_container_instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/ecs-agent-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-autoscaling-launchconfiguration.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":184,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is implementing governance controls for a company that requires its infrastructure to be housed within the United States. The engineer must restrict which AWS Regions can be used, and ensure an alert is sent as soon as possible if any activity outside the governance policy takes place. The controls should be automatically enabled on any new Region outside the United States (US). Which combination of actions will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在为一家要求其基础设施必须部署在美国境内的公司实施治理控制措施。该工程师 必须限制可使用的 AWS 区域，并确保一旦出现任何违反治理策略的活动，能尽快发出警报。对于任何新 启用的位于美国境外的区域，这些控制措施应自动生效。 哪种行动组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Organizations SCP that denies access to all non-global services in non-US Regions. Attach the policy to the root of the organization.","B":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs and enable it for all Regions. Use a CloudWatch Logs metric filter to send an alert on any service activity in non-US Regions.","C":"Use an AWS Lambda function that checks for AWS service activity and deploy it to all Regions. Write an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs the Lambda function every hour, sending an alert if activity is found in a non-US Region.","D":"Use an AWS Lambda function to query Amazon Inspector to look for service activity in non-US Regions and send alerts if any activity is found.","E":"Write an SCP using the aws:RequestedRegion condition key limiting access to US Regions. Apply the policy to all users, groups, and roles."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Organizations 服务控制策略（SCP），拒绝在非美国区域访问所有非全球服务。将该策 略附加到组织的根节点。","B":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs，并在所有区域启用。使用 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器，在非美国区域的任何服务活动时发送警报。","C":"使用一个检查 AWS 服务活动的 AWS Lambda 函数，并将其部署到所有区域。编写一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每小时运行一次该 Lambda 函数，如果在非美国区域发现活动，则发送警报。","D":"使用 AWS Lambda 函数查询 Amazon Inspector，查找非美国区域的服务活动，如果发现任何活动则发送警 报。","E":"使用 aws:RequestedRegion 条件键编写一个 SCP，限制对美国区域的访问。将该策略应用于所有用户、组 和角色。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The scenario has two parts: (1) restrict usage to US Regions in a way that automatically covers any newly added non-US Region, and (2) alert as soon as possible on out-of-policy activity, also covering new Regions. Option E is the AWS-documented mechanism: an SCP that uses the aws:RequestedRegion global condition key as an allow-list (Deny when the requested Region is not one of the approved US Regions). Because it allow-lists permitted Regions rather than enumerating forbidden ones, it inherently and automatically blocks any future non-US Region with no policy change. This is exactly the pattern AWS Control Tower's Region deny control uses; AWS docs state it is built on the aws:RequestedRegion condition key with StringNotEquals against the approved Regions, and that 'actions not listed in the SCP are not permitted.' Option B delivers the near-real-time alert: a multi-Region CloudTrail trail sends events to CloudWatch Logs, and a CloudWatch Logs metric filter plus alarm fires on activity in non-US Regions; per AWS docs a multi-Region trail captures all enabled Regions and CloudTrail automatically creates an identical copy of the trail in any newly enabled opt-in Region, so coverage auto-extends to new Regions. The dump-suggested pair A+B is rejected because A frames the SCP as denying non-US Regions (a deny-list) without naming aws:RequestedRegion, which does not automatically cover newly added Regions, whereas E uses the documented allow-list condition key. E's phrase 'apply to all users, groups, and roles' is imprecise (SCPs attach to the root, OUs, or accounts, not directly to users or groups), but the region-restriction mechanism it describes is the technically correct one.","explanation_zh":"情境有兩個需求：(1) 以一種能自動涵蓋任何新增非美國 Region 的方式，限制只能使用美國 Region；(2) 對違反治理政策的活動盡快發出警示，並同樣涵蓋新 Region。選項 E 是 AWS 文件記載的正確機制：使用 aws:RequestedRegion 全域條件金鑰的 SCP，以白名單方式運作（當請求的 Region 不在核准的美國 Region 清單內時即 Deny）。因為它是列出「允許」的 Region，而非列舉「禁止」的 Region，所以任何未來新增的非美國 Region 都會自動被封鎖，無需修改政策。這正是 AWS Control Tower 的 Region deny 控制所採用的模式；AWS 文件指出它建構於 aws:RequestedRegion 條件金鑰之上，以 StringNotEquals 比對核准的 Region，且「未列於 SCP 的動作都不被允許」。選項 B 提供近即時警示：multi-Region 的 CloudTrail trail 將事件送往 CloudWatch Logs，再以 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 加上 alarm 對非美國 Region 的活動觸發警示；依 AWS 文件，multi-Region trail 會擷取所有已啟用 Region 的活動，且當啟用新的 opt-in Region 時，CloudTrail 會自動在該 Region 建立 trail 的相同副本，因此涵蓋範圍會自動延伸到新 Region。題庫建議的 A+B 被否決，因為 A 將 SCP 描述為拒絕非美國 Region（黑名單）且未使用 aws:RequestedRegion，無法自動涵蓋新增 Region；而 E 使用文件記載的白名單條件金鑰。E 中『套用到所有 users、groups 與 roles』的措辭並不精確（SCP 是附加在 root、OU 或帳戶，而非直接附加到使用者或群組），但其描述的 Region 限制機制在技術上是正確的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"This SCP is framed as denying access to non-global services in non-US Regions, i.e., a deny-list of forbidden Regions, and it does not name the aws:RequestedRegion condition key. A deny-list approach does not automatically cover newly added non-US Regions, failing the 'automatically enabled on any new Region' requirement. The documented Control Tower Region deny mechanism is an aws:RequestedRegion allow-list (StringNotEquals against the approved Regions), which is what option E describes; E is the technically superior region-restriction choice.","why_zh":"此 SCP 被描述為拒絕對非美國 Region 中非全域服務的存取，即禁止 Region 的黑名單，且未提及 aws:RequestedRegion 條件金鑰。黑名單方式無法自動涵蓋新增的非美國 Region，未能滿足『自動套用到任何新 Region』的需求。文件記載的 Control Tower Region deny 機制是以 aws:RequestedRegion 做白名單（用 StringNotEquals 比對核准的 Region），正是選項 E 所述；E 才是技術上更佳的 Region 限制選項。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Lambda function triggered by an EventBridge rule that runs every hour polls for activity only once per hour, which is not 'as soon as possible.' This batch/polling approach introduces up to an hour of delay, requires deploying and maintaining Lambda in every Region (high operational overhead, no automatic extension to new Regions), and is far weaker than the near-real-time CloudTrail-to-CloudWatch-Logs metric filter and alarm path in option B.","why_zh":"由每小時執行一次的 EventBridge 規則觸發的 Lambda，每小時才輪詢一次活動，並非『盡快』。此批次／輪詢方式最多會有一小時延遲，且需在每個 Region 部署與維護 Lambda（營運負擔高，且無法自動延伸到新 Region），遠不如選項 B 中近即時的 CloudTrail 到 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 與 alarm 路徑。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability and network-exposure assessment service for EC2, container images (ECR), and Lambda; it does not record or report general AWS service/API activity by Region. Querying Inspector for 'service activity in non-US Regions' does not match its function, so it cannot detect out-of-policy regional usage.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是針對 EC2、容器映像（ECR）與 Lambda 的弱點與網路暴露評估服務，並不記錄或回報各 Region 的一般 AWS 服務／API 活動。向 Inspector 查詢『非美國 Region 的服務活動』不符合其功能，因此無法偵測違反政策的 Region 使用情形。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/primary-region-deny-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/ou-region-deny.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-multi-region-trails.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/monitor-cloudtrail-log-files-with-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateMetricFilterProcedure.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":185,"question_en":"A company sells products through an ecommerce web application. The company wants a dashboard that shows a pie chart of product transaction details. The company wants to integrate the dashboard with the company's existing Amazon CloudWatch dashboards. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司通过电子商务网络应用程序销售产品。该公司希望有一个仪表板，能够展示产品交易详情的饼图。 该公司还希望将此仪表板与公司现有的亚马逊 CloudWatch 仪表板集成。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the ecommerce application to emit a JSON object to a CloudWatch log group for each processed transaction. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to query the log group and to visualize the results in a pie chart format. Attach the results to the desired CloudWatch dashboard.","B":"Update the ecommerce application to emit a JSON object to an Amazon S3 bucket for each processed transaction. Use Amazon Athena to query the S3 bucket and to visualize the results in a pie chart format. Export the results from Athena. Attach the results to the desired CloudWatch dashboard.","C":"Update the ecommerce application to use AWS X-Ray for instrumentation. Create a new X-Ray subsegment. Add an annotation for each processed transaction. Use X-Ray traces to query the data and to visualize the results in a pie chart format. Attach the results to the desired CloudWatch dashboard.","D":"Update the ecommerce application to emit a JSON object to a CloudWatch log group for each processed transaction. Create an AWS Lambda function to aggregate and write the results to Amazon DynamoDB. Create a Lambda subscription filter for the log file. Attach the results to the desired CloudWatch dashboard."},"options_zh":{"A":"将电子商务应用程序更新为针对每笔处理完成的交易向 CloudWatch 日志组发送一个 JSON 对象。 使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询该日志组，并以饼图格式可视化结果。将结果附加到所需的 CloudWatch 仪表板。","B":"更新电子商务应用程序，使其为每笔处理完成的交易向 Amazon S3 存储桶发送一个 JSON 对象。使用 Amazon Athena 查询 S3 存储桶，并将结果以饼图格式可视化。从 Athena 导出结果。将结果附加到所需 的 CloudWatch 仪表板。","C":"将电子商务应用程序更新为使用 AWS X-Ray 进行检测。创建一个新的 X-Ray 子段。为每笔处理的交 易添加注释。使用 X-Ray 跟踪来查询数据，并以饼图格式可视化结果。将结果附加到所需的 CloudWatch 仪表板。","D":"更新电子商务应用程序，使其为每笔处理完成的交易向 CloudWatch 日志组发送一个 JSON 对象。创建一 个 AWS Lambda 函数来聚合结果并将其写入 Amazon DynamoDB。为日志文件创建一个 Lambda 订阅 筛选器。将结果附加到所需的 CloudWatch 仪表板。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudWatch Logs Insights natively satisfies every requirement with the least operational effort. The application emits one JSON object per transaction to a CloudWatch log group; Logs Insights automatically discovers JSON fields, and a query using the stats command with an aggregation function (e.g., count(*) by product) can be rendered as a pie chart. AWS docs explicitly state that such query results can be viewed as 'a line graph, stacked area graph, pie chart, or bar chart.' Logs Insights also provides a built-in 'Add to dashboard' action that attaches the query and chosen widget type directly to an existing CloudWatch dashboard, and the docs confirm these dashboard queries 'run every time you load the dashboard and every time that the dashboard refreshes,' so the pie chart stays live with no manual export. No additional services, ETL, or custom code are required, making this the MOST operationally efficient option.","explanation_zh":"CloudWatch Logs Insights 原生即可滿足所有需求，且維運負擔最低。應用程式每筆交易輸出一個 JSON 物件到 CloudWatch log group；Logs Insights 會自動探索 JSON 欄位，使用 stats 指令搭配彙總函數（例如 count(*) by product）的查詢即可呈現為圓餅圖。AWS 文件明確指出此類查詢結果可檢視為「line graph、stacked area graph、pie chart 或 bar chart」。Logs Insights 也內建「Add to dashboard」動作，可將查詢與選定的 widget 類型直接掛到既有的 CloudWatch dashboard；文件確認這些 dashboard 查詢「每次載入 dashboard 與每次 dashboard 重新整理時都會重新執行」，因此圓餅圖會即時更新且無需手動匯出。不需額外服務、ETL 或自訂程式，因此這是維運效率最高的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Athena over S3 can query the data, but Athena does not render native pie charts and its results cannot be attached directly to a CloudWatch dashboard. The option itself admits you must export the results from Athena and then attach them manually, which is extra manual ETL and produces a static, non-refreshing artifact rather than a live dashboard widget.","why_zh":"用 Athena 查詢 S3 可以取得資料，但 Athena 不會產生原生圓餅圖，其結果也無法直接掛到 CloudWatch dashboard。此選項本身就承認必須先從 Athena 匯出結果再手動附加，屬於額外的手動 ETL，且產生的是靜態、不會刷新的成品，而非即時的 dashboard widget。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS X-Ray is for distributed tracing, latency analysis, and service maps, not business-transaction aggregation. X-Ray annotations index trace data for filtering, but X-Ray does not produce pie charts of transaction counts and X-Ray traces/service maps cannot be added to a CloudWatch dashboard as a pie-chart widget. Instrumenting every transaction as a trace is an anti-pattern with high overhead.","why_zh":"AWS X-Ray 用於分散式追蹤、延遲分析與 service map，而非業務交易彙總。X-Ray annotation 用於索引 trace 資料以供篩選，但 X-Ray 無法以圓餅圖呈現交易筆數，其 trace/service map 也不能以圓餅圖 widget 加入 CloudWatch dashboard。把每筆交易都做成 trace 屬反模式且開銷高。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Lambda subscription filter that aggregates into DynamoDB is custom-code-heavy ETL, and DynamoDB data still cannot be charted as a pie directly on a CloudWatch dashboard without further plumbing. This is the most operationally complex path and is unnecessary because Logs Insights already visualizes the same log data natively and attaches it to a dashboard with a single action.","why_zh":"用 Lambda subscription filter 將資料彙總進 DynamoDB 屬於需大量自訂程式的 ETL，且 DynamoDB 資料仍無法在不額外串接的情況下直接於 CloudWatch dashboard 以圓餅圖呈現。這是維運最複雜的路徑，而且完全不必要，因為 Logs Insights 已能原生視覺化相同的 log 資料並以單一動作掛到 dashboard。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_AnalyzeLogData_VisualizationQuery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_Insights-Visualizing-Log-Data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_ExportQueryResults.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_AnalyzeLogData_LogsInsights.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":186,"question_en":"A company is launching an application. The application must use only approved AWS services. The account that runs the application was created less than 1 year ago and is assigned to an AWS Organizations OU. The company needs to create a new Organizations account structure. The account structure must have an appropriate SCP that supports the use of only services that are currently active in the AWS account. The company will use AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) Access Analyzer in the solution. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在推出一款应用程序。该应用程序必须仅使用经批准的 AWS 服务。运行该应用程序的账 户创建时间不足 1 年，并且已分配到 AWS Organizations 组织单元（OU）。 该公司需要创建一个新的组织账户结构。该账户结构必须具备适当的 SCP（服务控制策略），以支持仅使用 当前在 AWS 账户中处于活动状态的服务。该公司将在解决方案中使用 AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）访问 分析器。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that allows the services that IAM Access Analyzer identifies. Create an OU for the account. Move the account into the new OU. Attach the new SCP to the new OU. Detach the default FullAWSAccess SCP from the new OU.","B":"Create an SCP that denies the services that IAM Access Analyzer identifies. Create an OU for the account. Move the account into the new OU. Attach the new SCP to the new OU.","C":"Create an SCP that allows the services that IAM Access Analyzer identifies. Attach the new SCP to the organization's root.","D":"Create an SCP that allows the services that IAM Access Analyzer identifies. Create an OU for the account. Move the account into the new OU. Attach the new SCP to the management account. Detach the default FullAWSAccess SCP from the new OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），允许 IAM 访问分析器识别的服务。为该账户创建一个组织单位 （OU）。将该账户移至新的 OU 中。将新的 SCP 附加到新的 OU。从新的 OU 中分离默认的 FullAWSAccess SCP。","B":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），拒绝 IAM 访问分析器所识别的服务。为该账户创建一个组织单位 （OU）。将该账户移至新的 OU 中。将新的 SCP 附加到新的 OU。","C":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），允许 IAM 访问分析器识别的服务。将新创建的 SCP 附加到组织的根节 点。","D":"创建一个允许 IAM 访问分析器识别的服务的 SCP。为该账户创建一个组织单位（OU）。将该账户移至 新的 OU 中。将新的 SCP 附加到管理账户。从新的 OU 中分离默认的 FullAWSAccess SCP。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"IAM Access Analyzer policy generation reviews CloudTrail events to identify the services and actions that have actually been used (and are therefore active) by an entity, so the goal of allowing 'only services currently active in the account' calls for an allow-list SCP built from the services Access Analyzer identifies, not a deny list. Under SCP evaluation, a permission is allowed only when there is an explicit Allow at every level in the path (root, OU, account), and AWS Organizations attaches a default FullAWSAccess SCP that allows all services; if you attach a restrictive allow-list SCP to an OU but leave FullAWSAccess attached there, FullAWSAccess still allows everything and your restriction has no effect, so you must detach FullAWSAccess from that OU for the allow-list to take effect. AWS also strongly recommends not attaching restrictive SCPs to the organization root without testing; instead create an OU, move the account into it, and apply the SCP there. Option A does exactly this: allow the Access-Analyzer-identified services, create an OU, move the account in, attach the allow-list SCP to the OU, and detach the default FullAWSAccess from the OU. Root still keeps FullAWSAccess (allows all) and the account still keeps FullAWSAccess, so the effective intersection at the account becomes exactly the approved/active services, while other accounts remain unaffected.","explanation_zh":"IAM Access Analyzer 的 policy generation 會分析 CloudTrail 事件，找出某個 entity 實際使用過（因此屬於目前 active）的服務與動作，所以要達成「只允許帳戶中目前 active 的服務」這個目標，應該用 Access Analyzer 找出的服務建立一個 allow-list SCP，而不是 deny list。依照 SCP 評估邏輯，某項權限只有在從 root、OU 到 account 的路徑上每一層都有 explicit Allow 時才會被允許；而 AWS Organizations 預設會掛上 FullAWSAccess SCP 允許所有服務。如果你在 OU 上掛了 allow-list SCP 卻仍保留該 OU 上的 FullAWSAccess，FullAWSAccess 仍會允許所有動作，你的限制就形同無效，因此必須在該 OU 把 FullAWSAccess detach 掉，allow-list 才會生效。AWS 也強烈建議不要在未測試的情況下把限制性 SCP 掛到 organization root，而應先建立 OU、把帳戶移進去再套用 SCP。選項 A 正是如此：allow Access Analyzer 找出的服務、建立 OU、把帳戶移入、在 OU 掛上 allow-list SCP，並在 OU detach 預設的 FullAWSAccess。Root 仍保留 FullAWSAccess（允許全部）、account 也仍保留 FullAWSAccess，因此在 account 層的有效交集恰好就是被核准/active 的服務，且其他帳戶不受影響。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Access Analyzer identifies the services that ARE in use (active, approved). A Deny SCP targeting those identified services would block exactly the services the application relies on, the opposite of the requirement, while every other unapproved service stays permitted through the still-attached FullAWSAccess. Restricting to 'only approved services' is achieved with an allow-list, not by denying the services that are actually used.","why_zh":"Access Analyzer 找出的是目前正在使用（active、核准）的服務。用 Deny SCP 去拒絕這些被找出的服務，反而會擋掉應用程式所依賴的服務，與需求完全相反，而其他未核准的服務則因 FullAWSAccess 仍掛著而繼續被允許。要限制成「只允許核准的服務」必須用 allow-list，而不是去 deny 實際被使用的服務。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Attaching the restrictive allow-list SCP directly to the organization root violates AWS guidance, which strongly recommends not attaching SCPs to the root without thorough testing and instead moving accounts into a dedicated OU one at a time. It would also affect every account in the organization, not just the single application account, risking locking out other accounts; it never creates an isolated OU and never detaches FullAWSAccess to scope the test.","why_zh":"把限制性的 allow-list SCP 直接掛到 organization root 違反 AWS 的建議：AWS 強烈建議不要在未充分測試下把 SCP 掛到 root，而應先把帳戶逐一移到專屬的 OU。此作法還會影響組織內所有帳戶，而不只是該應用程式帳戶，可能誤鎖其他帳戶；它也未建立隔離的 OU，也未 detach FullAWSAccess 來限縮測試範圍。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SCPs have no effect on users or roles in the management account, so attaching the allow-list SCP to the management account would not restrict anything and targets the wrong entity (the application account sits in the OU). Worse, detaching FullAWSAccess from the OU while placing the only Allow on the management account leaves the OU with no Allow statement; under the deny-by-default model the account in that OU is then blocked from performing any action. Broken on two counts.","why_zh":"SCP 對 management account 中的 user 或 role 完全無效，因此把 allow-list SCP 掛到 management account 不會產生任何限制，且鎖定錯誤對象（應用程式帳戶在 OU 裡）。更糟的是，在 OU detach 掉 FullAWSAccess、卻把唯一的 Allow 放在 management account，會讓該 OU 沒有任何 Allow 陳述；在預設拒絕模型下，該 OU 內的帳戶將無法執行任何動作。兩處皆錯。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-analyzer-policy-generation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_strategies.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":187,"question_en":"A company has multiple development teams in different business units that work in a shared single AWS account. All Amazon EC2 resources that are created in the account must include tags that specify who created the resources. The tagging must occur within the first hour of resource creation. A DevOps engineer needs to add tags to the created resources that include the user ID that created the resource and the cost center ID. The DevOps engineer configures an AWS Lambda function with the cost center mappings to tag the resources. The DevOps engineer also sets up AWS CloudTrail in the AWS account. An Amazon S3 bucket stores the CloudTrail event logs. Which solution will meet the tagging requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有多个开发团队分布在不同的业务部门，这些团队在一个共享的单一 AWS 账户中工作。该账户 中创建的所有亚马逊 EC2 资源都必须包含指定创建者的标签。 创建了资源。必须在资源创建后的第一个小时内完成标记。 DevOps 工程师需要为创建的资源添加标签，标签中应包含创建资源的用户 ID 和成本中心 ID。DevOps 工程师配置了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数包含成本中心映射，用于为资源添加标签。DevOps 工程 师还在 AWS 账户中设置了 AWS CloudTrail。Amazon S3 存储桶用于存储 CloudTrail 事件日志。 哪种解决方案能满足标签要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 event notification on the S3 bucket to invoke the Lambda function for s3:ObjectTagging:Put events. Enable bucket versioning on the S3 bucket.","B":"Enable server access logging on the S3 bucket. Create an S3 event notification on the S3 bucket for s3:ObjectTagging:* events.","C":"Create a recurring hourly Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule that invokes the Lambda function. Modify the Lambda function to read the logs from the S3 bucket.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses Amazon EC2 as the event source. Configure the rule to match events delivered by CloudTrail. Configure the rule to target the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 S3 存储桶上创建 S3 事件通知，以便在发生 s3:ObjectTagging:Put 事件时调用 Lambda 函数。在 S3 存储桶上启用版本控制。","B":"在 S3 存储桶上启用服务器访问日志记录。在 S3 存储桶上为 s3:ObjectTagging:* 事件创建 S3 事件通 知。","C":"创建一个每小时重复触发的 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则，以调用 Lambda 函数。修改 Lambda 函数，使其能够从 S3 存储桶读取日志。","D":"创建一个使用 Amazon EC2 作为事件源的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则以匹配 CloudTrail 发 送的事件。配置该规则以将目标指向 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to tag newly created EC2 resources with the creating user's ID and a cost center ID within one hour of creation, using a Lambda function that already holds the cost-center mappings, with CloudTrail already enabled. CloudTrail records the EC2 API call (for example RunInstances) including the userIdentity, and per the EventBridge doc 'AWS service events delivered via AWS CloudTrail,' it delivers an 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' event with source 'aws.ec2' to the default EventBridge event bus. An EventBridge rule that uses EC2 as the event source, matches events delivered by CloudTrail, and targets the Lambda function fires in near real time, so the Lambda can read the creating user ID from the event's userIdentity and apply the tags well within the one-hour window. Note this must match the CloudTrail-delivered event, not the direct 'EC2 Instance State-change Notification' event, because only the CloudTrail event carries the userIdentity needed for the tag; option D's phrasing ('match events delivered by CloudTrail') captures this exactly. Option D is the canonical, event-driven AWS pattern and is the best fit.","explanation_zh":"需求是在 EC2 資源建立後一小時內，以建立者的 user ID 與 cost center ID 對其加上標籤，並使用內含 cost center 對應關係的 Lambda 函數，且 CloudTrail 已啟用。CloudTrail 會記錄 EC2 的 API 呼叫（例如 RunInstances），其中包含 userIdentity；依 EventBridge 文件 'AWS service events delivered via AWS CloudTrail' 所述，它會將 source 為 'aws.ec2' 的 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' 事件傳遞到預設 EventBridge 事件匯流排。一條以 EC2 為事件來源、比對由 CloudTrail 傳遞之事件、並以 Lambda 函數為目標的 EventBridge 規則，會近乎即時觸發該函數，使 Lambda 能從事件的 userIdentity 讀取建立者 user ID 並在一小時內套用標籤。需注意此處必須比對由 CloudTrail 傳遞的事件，而非 EC2 直接送出的 'EC2 Instance State-change Notification' 事件，因為只有 CloudTrail 事件帶有標記所需的 userIdentity；選項 D 的措辭（'match events delivered by CloudTrail'）正好符合此點。選項 D 是標準的事件驅動 AWS 模式，也是最佳解。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"s3:ObjectTagging:Put events fire only when tags are placed on S3 objects, which is unrelated to EC2 resource creation. CloudTrail writes log object files to the bucket (PutObject), not object tags, so this notification would never fire for the relevant action. Bucket versioning is irrelevant to EC2 tagging.","why_zh":"s3:ObjectTagging:Put 事件只有在對 S3 物件設定標籤時才會觸發，與 EC2 資源建立無關。CloudTrail 寫入的是日誌物件檔案（PutObject）而非物件標籤，因此此通知不會因相關動作而觸發。Bucket versioning 與 EC2 標記無關。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Server access logging and s3:ObjectTagging:* notifications relate to S3 object tagging, not EC2 resource creation. CloudTrail delivering log files to the bucket are PutObject/Create events, not ObjectTagging events, so the Lambda would never be invoked for EC2 creation.","why_zh":"Server access logging 與 s3:ObjectTagging:* 通知都與 S3 物件標籤有關，而非 EC2 資源建立。CloudTrail 將日誌檔案傳送到 bucket 屬於 PutObject/Create 事件，而非 ObjectTagging 事件，因此 Lambda 不會因 EC2 建立而被叫用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An hourly scheduled rule that parses CloudTrail logs from S3 is more operationally complex and fragile: CloudTrail delivers logs to S3 in batches with delay (often up to ~15 minutes), so polling once per hour risks missing the one-hour SLA and requires custom log parsing and deduplication. The event-driven EventBridge approach in D is the AWS-recommended, simpler, near-real-time pattern.","why_zh":"每小時排程規則去 S3 解析 CloudTrail 日誌，運維上更複雜且脆弱：CloudTrail 以批次方式延遲（通常可達約 15 分鐘）傳送日誌到 S3，因此每小時輪詢一次有錯過一小時 SLA 的風險，並需自訂日誌解析與去重。選項 D 的事件驅動 EventBridge 方式才是 AWS 建議、更簡單且近乎即時的模式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-log-api-call.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":188,"question_en":"A company runs an application for multiple environments in a single AWS account. An AWS CodePipeline pipeline uses a development Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster to test an image for the application from an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. The pipeline promotes the image to a production ECS cluster. The company needs to move the production cluster into a separate AWS account in the same AWS Region. The production cluster must be able to download the images over a private connection. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 AWS 账户中为多个环境运行一个应用程序。一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道使用开发环境 的 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）集群来测试来自 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR）存储库的应用程序镜像。该管道将镜像推广到生产环境的 ECS 集群。 该公司需要将生产集群迁移到同一 AWS 区域内的单独 AWS 账户中。生产集群必须能够通过私有 连接下载镜像。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon ECR VPC endpoints and an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint. In the separate AWS account, create an ECR repository. Set the repository policy to allow the production ECS tasks to pull images from the main AWS account. Configure the production ECS task execution role to have permission to download the image from the ECR repository.","B":"Set a repository policy on the production ECR repository in the main AWS account. Configure the repository policy to allow the production ECS tasks in the separate AWS account to pull images from the main account. Configure the production ECS task execution role to have permission to download the image from the ECR repository.","C":"Configure ECR private image replication in the main AWS account. Activate cross-account replication. Define the destination account ID of the separate AWS account.","D":"Use Amazon ECR VPC endpoints and an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint. Set a repository policy on the production ECR repository in the main AWS account. Configure the repository policy to allow the production ECS tasks in the separate AWS account to pull images from the main account. Configure the production ECS task execution role to have permission to download the image from the ECR repository."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon ECR VPC 端点和 Amazon S3 网关端点。在单独的 AWS 账户中创建一个 ECR 存储库。 将存储库策略设置为允许生产 ECS 任务从主 AWS 账户拉取镜像。配置生产 ECS 任务执行角色， 使其有权从 ECR 存储库下载镜像。","B":"在主 AWS 账户的生产 ECR 存储库上设置存储库策略。将存储库策略配置为允许单独 AWS 账户中 的生产 ECS 任务从主账户拉取镜像。将生产 ECS 任务执行角色配置为有权从 ECR 存储库下载镜 像。","C":"在主 AWS 账户中配置 ECR 私有镜像复制。激活跨账户复制。定义单独 AWS 账户的目标账户 ID。","D":"使用 Amazon ECR VPC 端点和 Amazon S3 网关端点。在主 AWS 账户的生产 ECR 存储库上设置存储 库策略。将存储库策略配置为允许单独 AWS 账户中的生产 ECS 任务从主账户拉取镜像。配置生产 ECS 任务执行角色，使其有权从 ECR 存储库下载镜像。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario has two requirements: the production ECS cluster (now in a separate account) must pull images from the main account's existing ECR repository (cross-account access), and the pull must occur over a private connection. Cross-account access to an existing ECR repository is granted by attaching a repository policy to the source repository in the main account that allows the other account's principals to pull (the 'Allow another account' example uses ecr:BatchGetImage, ecr:GetDownloadUrlForLayer, etc.), combined with the consuming task execution role having ECR permissions. Private connectivity requires an Amazon ECR interface VPC endpoint (AWS PrivateLink) AND an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint, because the AWS docs explicitly state the S3 gateway endpoint 'is required because Amazon ECR uses Amazon S3 to store your image layers' (the manifest comes from ECR, but the layers download from S3). Only option D provides both endpoints and sets the cross-account repository policy plus task execution role permissions on the main-account repository, so it is the only choice that satisfies both requirements.","explanation_zh":"情境有兩個需求：位於獨立帳戶的 production ECS cluster 必須從主帳戶現有的 ECR repository 拉取映像（跨帳戶存取），且拉取必須透過私有連線進行。對現有 ECR repository 的跨帳戶存取，是在主帳戶的來源 repository 上附加 repository policy，允許另一帳戶的 principal 拉取（官方「Allow another account」範例使用 ecr:BatchGetImage、ecr:GetDownloadUrlForLayer 等動作），再搭配取用端的 task execution role 具備 ECR 權限。私有連線則需要 Amazon ECR interface VPC endpoint（AWS PrivateLink）以及 Amazon S3 gateway endpoint，因為 AWS 文件明確指出 S3 gateway endpoint「之所以必要，是因為 Amazon ECR 使用 Amazon S3 儲存映像層」（manifest 來自 ECR，但映像層從 S3 下載）。只有選項 D 同時提供兩種 endpoint，並在主帳戶 repository 上設定跨帳戶 repository policy 與 task execution role 權限，因此是唯一同時滿足兩項需求的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a new ECR repository in the separate account does not help because the images live in the main account and nothing in this option pushes or replicates them into the new empty repository. Its repository policy would allow same-account tasks to pull from an empty repo, which is incoherent, and it never establishes access to the main account's images. It provides the endpoints, but the image-source mechanism is broken.","why_zh":"在獨立帳戶建立新的 ECR repository 沒有幫助，因為映像位於主帳戶，而此選項並未將映像推送或複製到這個空的新 repository。其 repository policy 只是允許同帳戶 task 從一個空 repo 拉取，邏輯不通，也從未建立對主帳戶映像的存取。雖然提供了 endpoint，但映像來源機制是失效的。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The cross-account repository policy and task execution role permissions are correct, but this option provides no VPC endpoints at all, so the pull would traverse the public internet (or fail entirely in a private subnet). It fails the explicit 'download over a private connection' requirement.","why_zh":"跨帳戶 repository policy 與 task execution role 權限是正確的，但此選項完全沒有提供任何 VPC endpoint，因此拉取會走公網（或在私有子網中完全失敗）。它無法滿足明確的「透過私有連線下載」需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ECR cross-account replication copies images into the separate account, but it does not establish any private connectivity; pulling even a replicated image still needs an ECR interface VPC endpoint and an S3 gateway endpoint, none of which this option provides. It therefore fails the private-connection requirement and changes the intended architecture (download from the main account over a private link, not maintain replicated copies).","why_zh":"ECR 跨帳戶 replication 會把映像複製到獨立帳戶，但完全沒有建立任何私有連線；即使拉取已複製的映像，仍需 ECR interface VPC endpoint 與 S3 gateway endpoint，而此選項皆未提供。因此它無法滿足私有連線需求，也改變了預期架構（透過私有連線從主帳戶下載，而非維護複製副本）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/vpc-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/repository-policy-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/repository-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/ECR_on_ECS.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task_execution_IAM_role.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":189,"question_en":"A company needs to ensure that flow logs remain configured for all existing and new VPCs in its AWS account. The company uses an AWS CloudFormation stack to manage its VPCs. The company needs a solution that will work for any VPCs that any IAM user creates. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要确保其 AWS 账户中所有现有和新创建的 VPC 都已配置了流量日志。该公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈来管理其 VPC。该公司需要一个解决方案，能够适用于任何 IAM 用户创建的任何 VPC。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add the AWS::EC2::FlowLog resource to the CloudFormation stack that creates the VPCs.","B":"Create an organization in AWS Organizations. Add the company's AWS account to the organization. Create an SCP to prevent users from modifying VPC flow logs.","C":"Turn on AWS Config. Create an AWS Config rule to check whether VPC flow logs are turned on. Configure automatic remediation to turn on VPC flow logs.","D":"Create an IAM policy to deny the use of API calls for VPC flow logs. Attach the IAM policy to all IAM users."},"options_zh":{"A":"在创建 VPC 的 CloudFormation 堆栈EC2::FlowLog 资源。","B":"在 AWS Organizations 中创建一个组织。将公司的 AWS 账户添加到该组织中。创建一个服务控制策 略（SCP），以防止用户修改 VPC 流日志。","C":"启用 AWS Config。创建一条 AWS Config 规则以检查 VPC 流日志是否已开启。配置自动修复 以开启 VPC 流日志。","D":"创建一个 IAM 策略以禁止使用 VPC 流日志的 API 调用。将该 IAM 策略附加到所有 IAM 用户。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config provides the managed rule vpc-flow-logs-enabled (identifier VPC_FLOW_LOGS_ENABLED), which evaluates the AWS::EC2::VPC resource type and is NON_COMPLIANT if flow logs are not enabled for at least one VPC. As a Periodic-trigger rule, AWS Config continuously discovers and re-evaluates both existing and newly created VPCs regardless of who created them or how (console, CLI, SDK, or CloudFormation), so it scales to any VPC that any IAM user creates. Pairing the rule with auto remediation (an SSM Automation document associated via PutRemediationConfigurations or the AWS Config console) automatically turns flow logs back on for any noncompliant VPC. This combination is the only option that both detects missing flow logs account-wide and actively re-enables them, satisfying the requirement that flow logs 'remain configured for all existing and new VPCs.'","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 提供受管規則 vpc-flow-logs-enabled（識別碼 VPC_FLOW_LOGS_ENABLED），它評估 AWS::EC2::VPC 資源類型，只要至少一個 VPC 未啟用 flow logs 即標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。此規則為 Periodic 觸發類型，AWS Config 會持續探索並重新評估既有與新建立的 VPC，不論由誰建立、以何種方式建立（console、CLI、SDK 或 CloudFormation），因此能涵蓋任何 IAM user 建立的任何 VPC。將該規則搭配 auto remediation（透過 PutRemediationConfigurations API 或 AWS Config console 關聯的 SSM Automation 文件），即可為任何不合規的 VPC 自動重新開啟 flow logs。此組合是唯一同時能在帳戶層級偵測缺少 flow logs 並主動重新啟用的選項，滿足『所有既有與新建立 VPC 都維持 flow logs 設定』的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adding AWS::EC2::FlowLog to the CloudFormation stack only covers VPCs created through that specific stack. Any IAM user can create VPCs via the console, CLI, or SDK outside the stack, and this does nothing for existing VPCs not managed by the stack, so it fails the 'any VPCs that any IAM user creates' and 'all existing' requirements.","why_zh":"在 CloudFormation stack 中加入 AWS::EC2::FlowLog 只涵蓋透過該 stack 建立的 VPC。任何 IAM user 都能透過 console、CLI、SDK 在 stack 之外建立 VPC，且無法處理未由該 stack 管理的既有 VPC，因此無法滿足『任何 IAM user 建立的任何 VPC』與『所有既有 VPC』的需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"An SCP that prevents users from modifying VPC flow logs is only a preventive guardrail against changes; it never enables flow logs on existing VPCs or on new VPCs that are created without them. A single account also does not require AWS Organizations for this, and SCPs do not apply to the organization's management account, so it cannot guarantee flow logs remain configured.","why_zh":"防止使用者修改 VPC flow logs 的 SCP 只是阻止變更的預防性防護，永遠不會為既有 VPC 或新建立但未設定的 VPC 啟用 flow logs。單一帳戶也不需要為此建立 AWS Organizations，且 SCP 不適用於組織的 management account，因此無法保證 flow logs 維持設定。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Denying VPC flow log API calls would prevent flow logs from being created or managed at all, which is the opposite of the requirement to keep them configured. It also applies only to the attached IAM users (not roles) and is impractical to maintain across all users.","why_zh":"拒絕 VPC flow log API 呼叫會完全阻止 flow logs 的建立或管理，與『維持設定』的需求相反；且僅套用於所附加的 IAM users（不含 roles），難以對所有使用者維護。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/vpc-flow-logs-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":190,"question_en":"A company's application teams use AWS CodeCommit repositories for their applications. The application teams have repositories in multiple AWS accounts. All accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. Each application team uses AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) configured with an external IdP to assume a developer IAM role. The developer role allows the application teams to use Git to work with the code in the repositories. A security audit reveals that the application teams can modify the main branch in any repository. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution that allows the application teams to modify the main branch of only the repositories that they manage. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司的应用团队在其应用中使用 AWS CodeCommit 代码库。这些应用团队在多个 AWS 账户中拥 有代码库。所有账户都在 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织内。 每个应用程序团队都使用与外部身份提供商（IdP）配置的 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）来 承担开发人员 IAM 角色。开发人员角色允许应用程序团队使用 Git 对存储库中的代码进行操作。 一项安全审计显示，应用程序团队可以在任何代码库中修改主分支。一位 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个解 决方案，使应用程序团队只能修改其管理的代码库的主分支。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the SAML assertion to pass the user's team name. Update the IAM role's trust policy to add an access-team session tag that has the team name.","B":"Create an approval rule template for each team in the Organizations management account. Associate the template with all the repositories. Add the developer role ARN as an approver.","C":"Create an approval rule template for each account. Associate the template with all repositories. Add the \"aws:ResourceTag/access-team\": \"$ ;{aws:PrincipalTag/access-team}\" condition to the approval rule template.","D":"For each CodeCommit repository, add an access-team tag that has the value set to the name of the associated team.","E":"Attach an SCP to the accounts. Include the following statement:","F":"Create an IAM permissions boundary in each account. Include the following statement:"},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 SAML 断言以传递用户的团队名称。更新 IAM 角色的信任策略，添加一个具有团队名称的访问 团队会话标签。","B":"在“组织管理”账户中为每个团队创建一个审批规则模板。将该模板与所有代码库相关联。添加开 发人员角色的 ARN 作为审批人。","C":"为每个账户创建一个审批规则模板。将该模板与所有存储库相关联。在审批规则模板中添加“aws: ResourceTag/access-team”： “$ ;{aws:PrincipalTag/access-team}”条件。","D":"对于每个 CodeCommit 代码库，添加一个 access-team 标签，将其值设置为相关团队的名称。","E":"将 SCP 附加到账户上。包含以下声明：","F":"在每个账户中创建一个 IAM 权限边界。包含以下语句："},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the classic attribute-based access control (ABAC) 'tags must match' guardrail across an AWS Organization. (A) Configure the external IdP to pass the user's team name in the SAML assertion (attribute name https://aws.amazon.com/SAML/Attributes/AccessControl:TagKey); IAM Identity Center passes the attribute through as a session tag, so it is available as aws:PrincipalTag/access-team during the developer role session, and the role trust policy must permit that session tag. (D) Tag each CodeCommit repository with access-team set to the owning team, which makes aws:ResourceTag/access-team available on the resource (CodeCommit repositories support tags that control access through IAM tag-based policies). (E) Attach an SCP to the member accounts that Denies the branch-write actions on refs/heads/main using the codecommit:References condition. CodeCommit's 'Limit pushes and merges to branches' guidance enumerates exactly these actions - codecommit:GitPush, MergeBranchesByFastForward/BySquash/ByThreeWay, MergePullRequestByFastForward/BySquash/ByThreeWay, DeleteBranch, DeleteFile, PutFile - with a Null guard on codecommit:References that is required whenever GitPush appears in a Deny. The Deny fires whenever aws:ResourceTag/access-team does not equal aws:PrincipalTag/access-team. Because an SCP sets the maximum permissions for every IAM user and role in all member accounts (including the IAM Identity Center permission-set roles that are auto-provisioned into each account), it is the natural org-wide guardrail, so teams can modify main only in the repositories they own. Principal tag (A) + resource tag (D) + the comparing Deny SCP (E) is the complete ABAC pattern.","explanation_zh":"這是跨 AWS Organization 的典型屬性式存取控制（ABAC）『標籤必須相符』防護。(A) 設定外部 IdP 在 SAML assertion 中傳遞使用者的 team 名稱（屬性名稱為 https://aws.amazon.com/SAML/Attributes/AccessControl:TagKey）；IAM Identity Center 將該屬性以 session tag 形式帶入，使其在 developer role 工作階段中以 aws:PrincipalTag/access-team 形式可用，且 role 的 trust policy 必須允許此 session tag。(D) 為每個 CodeCommit repository 加上 access-team 標籤並設為所屬團隊，使資源上可取得 aws:ResourceTag/access-team（CodeCommit repository 支援可透過 IAM tag-based policy 控制存取的標籤）。(E) 在成員帳戶附加 SCP，透過 codecommit:References 條件鎖定 refs/heads/main 拒絕分支寫入動作。CodeCommit 的『Limit pushes and merges to branches』文件正好列出這些動作—codecommit:GitPush、MergeBranchesByFastForward/BySquash/ByThreeWay、MergePullRequestByFastForward/BySquash/ByThreeWay、DeleteBranch、DeleteFile、PutFile—並要求只要 Deny 中含有 GitPush，就必須對 codecommit:References 加上 Null 守衛。當 aws:ResourceTag/access-team 不等於 aws:PrincipalTag/access-team 時即觸發 Deny。由於 SCP 會為所有成員帳戶中的每個 IAM user 與 role（包含自動佈建到各帳戶的 IAM Identity Center 權限集角色）設定權限上限，因此它是天然的全組織防護，讓團隊只能修改自己擁有的 repo 的 main 分支。principal tag (A) 加上 resource tag (D) 再加上比較兩者的 Deny SCP (E)，構成完整的 ABAC 模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Approval rule templates only auto-create an approval rule on pull requests whose destination branch matches the template, requiring a number of approvals before a PR can be merged. They do not stop a developer from directly pushing commits (git push / codecommit:GitPush) to the main branch, and adding the shared developer role ARN as an approver does not scope writes to the repos a team owns. Creating the template in the management account is also wrong; the requirement is to restrict member-account principals, and the per-repo tag-vs-principal comparison cannot be expressed by an approval template.","why_zh":"Approval rule templates 只會在 pull request 的目標分支符合範本時自動建立核准規則，並在合併前要求一定數量的核准；無法阻止開發者直接 push commit（git push / codecommit:GitPush）到 main 分支，且把共用的 developer role ARN 加為核准者也無法將寫入限縮到團隊擁有的 repo。在管理帳戶建立範本也不對；需求是限制成員帳戶中的主體，且每個 repo 的標籤對 principal 比較無法用 approval template 表達。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Approval rule templates do not support IAM policy condition syntax such as \"aws:ResourceTag/access-team\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/access-team}\"; a template only defines the destination branch, the approver pool (IAM ARNs or wildcards), and the number of approvals required. They govern pull-request merges, not direct branch pushes, so embedding a tag-matching IAM condition into a template is technically invalid.","why_zh":"Approval rule templates 不支援 IAM 政策條件語法（如 \"aws:ResourceTag/access-team\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/access-team}\"）；範本只定義目標分支、核准者集合（IAM ARN 或萬用字元）以及所需核准數量。它們管的是 PR 合併而非直接分支 push，因此把標籤比對的 IAM 條件嵌入範本在技術上無效。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"A permissions boundary sets only the maximum permissions of a single IAM user or role and must be attached to each entity individually; it does not automatically apply org-wide and cannot be cleanly attached to the IAM Identity Center permission-set roles that are auto-provisioned into each account on every assignment. An SCP (E) is the correct organization-level guardrail that applies to every principal in every member account automatically, making F the weaker, harder-to-operate alternative.","why_zh":"permissions boundary 只設定單一 IAM user 或 role 的最大權限，且須逐一附加到每個實體；它不會自動套用到整個組織，也無法乾淨地附加到每次指派時自動佈建到各帳戶的 IAM Identity Center 權限集角色。SCP（E）才是正確的組織層級防護，會自動套用到每個成員帳戶中的每個主體，使 F 成為較弱、較難維運的替代方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-conditional-branch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/auth-and-access-control-permissions-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-tag-repository.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/attributesforaccesscontrol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac-attributes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pull-request-approval-rule.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":191,"question_en":"A company uses AWS WAF to protect its cloud infrastructure. A DevOps engineer needs to give an operations team the ability to analyze log messages from AWS WAF. The operations team needs to be able to create alarms for specific patterns in the log output. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS WAF 来保护其云基础设施。一位 DevOps 工程师需要赋予运营团队分析 AWS WAF 日志消息的能力。运营团队需要能够针对日志输出中的特定模式创建警报。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Configure the appropriate AWS WAF web ACL to send log messages to the log group. Instruct the operations team to create CloudWatch metric filters.","B":"Create an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster and appropriate indexes. Configure an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream to stream log data to the indexes. Use OpenSearch Dashboards to create filters and widgets.","C":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket for the log output. Configure AWS WAF to send log outputs to the S3 bucket. Instruct the operations team to create AWS Lambda functions that detect each desired log message pattern. Configure the Lambda functions to publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","D":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket for the log output. Configure AWS WAF to send log outputs to the S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to create an external table definition that fits the log message pattern. Instruct the operations team to write SQL queries and to create Amazon CloudWatch metric filters for the Athena queries."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。配置适当的 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（web ACL）， 将日志消息发送到该日志组。指示运营团队创建 CloudWatch 指标筛选器。","B":"创建一个 Amazon OpenSearch Service 集群和相应的索引。配置一个 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 交付流， 将日志数据流式传输到索引中。使用 OpenSearch Dashboards 创建过滤器和小部件。","C":"创建一个用于日志输出的 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 AWS WAF 将日志输出发送到该 S3 存储桶。指示运 营团队创建用于检测每个所需日志消息模式的 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以发布到 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。","D":"创建一个用于日志输出的 Amazon S3 存储桶。配置 AWS WAF 将日志输出发送到该 S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon Athena 创建一个符合日志消息模式的外部表定义。指示运营团队编写 SQL 查询，并为 Athena 查询创建 Amazon CloudWatch 指标过滤器。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS WAF natively supports three logging destinations for web ACL traffic logs: an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group, an Amazon S3 bucket, and Amazon Data Firehose. Sending logs directly to a CloudWatch Logs log group (whose name must start with 'aws-waf-logs-') requires no intermediary pipeline or custom code. Once the logs are in CloudWatch Logs, the operations team creates CloudWatch metric filters that match specific patterns in the log output; AWS documentation states that 'CloudWatch Logs uses these metric filters to turn log data into numerical CloudWatch metrics that you can graph or set an alarm on,' so the team can then attach CloudWatch alarms (which can notify via SNS). This is a fully managed, no-infrastructure, no-custom-code path, which is the LEAST operational overhead and the AWS-documented pattern for alarming on a specific log pattern.","explanation_zh":"AWS WAF 原生支援三種 web ACL 流量日誌目的地：Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group、Amazon S3 bucket 以及 Amazon Data Firehose。將日誌直接送到 CloudWatch Logs log group（名稱必須以 'aws-waf-logs-' 開頭）不需要任何中介管線或自訂程式碼。日誌進入 CloudWatch Logs 後，營運團隊可建立 CloudWatch metric filter 來比對日誌中的特定模式；AWS 文件明確說明 CloudWatch Logs 會用這些 metric filter 把日誌轉成可繪圖或設定 alarm 的數值型 CloudWatch metric，因此團隊可進一步掛上 CloudWatch alarm（可透過 SNS 通知）。這是完全託管、零基礎設施、零自訂程式碼的方案，屬於最低營運負擔，也是 AWS 文件針對「對特定日誌模式發出警示」所建議的標準做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Provisioning and operating an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster plus a Kinesis/Data Firehose delivery stream and managing indexes and dashboards is substantial infrastructure to size, secure, and maintain. OpenSearch Dashboards provides filters and widgets for visualization, not native CloudWatch-style alarms on patterns, and is far more operational overhead than a managed metric filter.","why_zh":"建置並維運 Amazon OpenSearch Service 叢集，加上 Kinesis/Data Firehose 傳遞串流，還要管理索引與儀表板，屬於需要規劃容量、安全與維護的大量基礎設施。OpenSearch Dashboards 提供的是用於視覺化的 filter 與 widget，而非原生的 CloudWatch alarm，營運負擔遠高於託管的 metric filter。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Sending logs to S3 and writing custom AWS Lambda functions to detect each desired pattern requires developing, deploying, and maintaining code for every pattern, which is explicitly high operational overhead. Pattern matching plus alarming is already provided out of the box by CloudWatch metric filters.","why_zh":"將日誌送到 S3 並為每個目標模式撰寫自訂 AWS Lambda 函式來偵測，必須針對每種模式開發、部署與維護程式碼，營運負擔明顯較高。CloudWatch metric filter 已開箱即用地提供模式比對與警示功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This option is technically incoherent: CloudWatch metric filters operate on CloudWatch Logs log groups, not on Amazon Athena query results, so you cannot 'create CloudWatch metric filters for the Athena queries.' Athena is also query-on-demand against S3 rather than continuous, and managing external table definitions plus hand-written SQL adds overhead without delivering native real-time alarming.","why_zh":"此選項在技術上不成立：CloudWatch metric filter 作用於 CloudWatch Logs log group，而非 Amazon Athena 的查詢結果，因此無法「為 Athena 查詢建立 CloudWatch metric filter」。Athena 是針對 S3 的隨選查詢而非連續處理，加上維護外部資料表定義與手寫 SQL，反而增加負擔且無法提供原生即時警示。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-cw-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntaxForMetricFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateMetricFilterProcedure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-policies-logging-destinations.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":192,"question_en":"A software team is using AWS CodePipeline to automate its Java application release pipeline. The pipeline consists of a source stage, then a build stage, and then a deploy stage. Each stage contains a single action that has a runOrder value of 1. The team wants to integrate unit tests into the existing release pipeline. The team needs a solution that deploys only the code changes that pass all unit tests. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个软件团队正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 来自动化其 Java 应用程序的发布流程。该流程包括源代码阶段、 构建阶段和部署阶段。每个阶段都包含一个 runOrder 值为 1 的单一操作。 团队希望将单元测试整合到现有的发布流程中。团队需要一个解决方案，仅部署通过所有单元测试的代 码更改。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the build stage. Add a test action that has a runOrder value of 1. Use AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider to run unit tests.","B":"Modify the build stage. Add a test action that has a runOrder value of 2. Use AWS CodeBuild as the action provider to run unit tests.","C":"Modify the deploy stage. Add a test action that has a runOrder value of 1. Use AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider to run unit tests.","D":"Modify the deploy stage. Add a test action that has a runOrder value of 2. Use AWS CodeBuild as the action provider to run unit tests."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改构建阶段。添加一个运行顺序值为 1 的测试操作。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序来运行 单元测试。","B":"修改构建阶段。添加一个运行顺序值为 2 的测试操作。使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来运行 单元测试。","C":"修改部署阶段。添加一个运行顺序值为 1 的测试操作。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序来运 行单元测试。","D":"修改部署阶段。添加一个运行顺序值为 2 的测试操作。使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来运行 单元测试。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is that code be deployed only if it passes all unit tests, so the unit tests must run AND succeed BEFORE the deploy stage executes. AWS CodeBuild is a valid Test action provider that compiles source code and runs unit tests via a buildspec, whereas CodeDeploy is only a Deploy action provider and cannot run unit tests. Within a stage, runOrder controls sequencing: actions that share the same runOrder run in parallel, while a higher runOrder runs serially after lower-numbered actions. Option B adds a CodeBuild test action to the build stage with runOrder 2, so it runs serially after the existing build action (runOrder 1); if the tests fail, the build stage fails and the downstream deploy stage never executes, guaranteeing only tested code is deployed. Options A and C use CodeDeploy, which cannot run unit tests, and use runOrder 1 (parallel, not after the existing action); option D runs the tests in the deploy stage at runOrder 2, which is AFTER the deploy action already shipped the code, defeating the purpose.","explanation_zh":"需求是只有通過所有 unit tests 的程式碼才能被部署，因此 unit tests 必須在 deploy stage 執行之前先執行並且成功。AWS CodeBuild 是合法的 Test action provider，可透過 buildspec 編譯原始碼並執行 unit tests；而 CodeDeploy 只是 Deploy action provider，無法執行 unit tests。在同一個 stage 內，runOrder 控制執行順序：相同 runOrder 的 actions 平行執行，較大的 runOrder 則在較小編號的 action 之後序列執行。選項 B 在 build stage 加入一個 runOrder 為 2 的 CodeBuild test action，因此它會在既有的 build action（runOrder 1）之後序列執行；若測試失敗，build stage 會失敗，下游的 deploy stage 永遠不會執行，確保只有通過測試的程式碼才會被部署。選項 A 與 C 使用無法執行 unit tests 的 CodeDeploy，且使用 runOrder 1（與既有 action 平行，而非在其之後）；選項 D 在 deploy stage 以 runOrder 2 執行測試，但那是在 deploy action 已經部署程式碼之後，違背了需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodeDeploy is a Deploy action provider and cannot run unit tests, so it is technically invalid as a Test action provider. Also, runOrder 1 makes the action run in parallel with the existing build action rather than after it, so a build artifact may not exist for testing.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 是 Deploy action provider，無法執行 unit tests，作為 Test action provider 技術上不合法。此外 runOrder 1 會讓該 action 與既有的 build action 平行執行而非在其之後，因此可能還沒有 build artifact 可供測試。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeDeploy cannot run unit tests. Adding the action to the deploy stage with runOrder 1 makes it run in parallel with the existing deploy action, so the code is deployed regardless of any test outcome, violating the 'deploy only if tests pass' requirement.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 無法執行 unit tests。將該 action 以 runOrder 1 加入 deploy stage 會讓它與既有的 deploy action 平行執行，因此無論測試結果如何程式碼都會被部署，違反了「只有測試通過才部署」的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeBuild is a valid test provider, but placing the test at runOrder 2 in the deploy stage means it runs AFTER the existing deploy action (runOrder 1) has already deployed the code. Testing after deployment cannot prevent untested code from being shipped, so the requirement is not met.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 雖是合法的測試 provider，但把測試放在 deploy stage 的 runOrder 2，代表它會在既有 deploy action（runOrder 1）已經部署程式碼之後才執行。部署後才測試無法阻止未通過測試的程式碼被發布，因此不符合需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-requirements.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CodeBuild.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-valid-providers.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":193,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage several AWS accounts that the company's developers use. The company requires all data to be encrypted in transit. Multiple Amazon S3 buckets that were created in developer accounts allow unencrypted connections. A DevOps engineer must enforce encryption of data in transit for all existing S3 buckets that are created in accounts in the organization. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织中的一个组织来管理其开发人员使用的多个 AWS 账户。该公司要求所有数 据在传输过程中都必须加密。 多个在开发者账户中创建的亚马逊 S3 存储桶允许未加密的连接。 DevOps 工程师必须为组织内所有现有账户中创建的 S3 存储桶强制实施传输中的数据加密。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy an AWS Network Firewall firewall to each account. Route all outbound requests from the AWS environment through the firewall. Deploy a policy to block access to all outbound requests on port 80.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy an AWS Network Firewall firewall to each account. Route all inbound requests to the AWS environment through the firewall. Deploy a policy to block access to all inbound requests on port 80.","C":"Turn on AWS Config for the organization. Deploy a conformance pack that uses the s3-bucket-ssl- requests-only managed rule and an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook. Use a runbook that adds a bucket policy statement to deny access to an S3 bucket when the value of the aws:SecureTransport condition key is false.","D":"Turn on AWS Config for the organization. Deploy a conformance pack that uses the s3-bucket-ssl- requests-only managed rule and an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook. Use a runbook that adds a bucket policy statement to deny access to an S3 bucket when the value of the s3:x-amz-server- side-encryption-aws-kms-key-id condition key is null."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 AWS Network Firewall 防火墙部署到每个账户。将来自 AWS 环境的所有出站请求通过防火墙进行路由。部署策略以阻止所有端口 80 上的出站请求访问。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 AWS Network Firewall 防火墙部署到每个账户。将所有入 站请求通过防火墙路由到 AWS 环境。部署策略以阻止对端口 80 上所有入站请求的访问。","C":"为组织启用 AWS Config。部署一个合规性包，该包使用 s3-bucket-sslrequests-only 管理规则和一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。使用一个运行手册，当 aws:SecureTransport 条件键的 值为 false 时，向 S3 存储桶添加一个策略语句以拒绝访问。","D":"为组织启用 AWS Config。部署一个合规性包，该包使用 s3-bucket-sslrequests-only 管理规则和一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。使用一个运行手册，当 s3:x-amz-serverside-encryption- aws-kms-key-id 条件键的值为空时，向 S3 存储桶添加一个策略语句以拒绝访问。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to enforce encryption of data in transit (HTTPS/TLS) for all existing S3 buckets across an AWS Organization. Option C turns on AWS Config for the organization and deploys a conformance pack with the s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only managed rule, which the AWS Config documentation describes as: 'Checks if S3 buckets have policies that require requests to use SSL/TLS. The rule is NON_COMPLIANT if any S3 bucket has policies allowing HTTP requests.' The associated Systems Manager Automation remediation runbook adds a bucket policy statement that denies access when aws:SecureTransport is false. The S3 'Protecting data in transit with encryption' documentation explicitly shows this exact Deny policy and states the aws:SecureTransport global condition key is used 'to check whether the request was sent through HTTPS (TLS),' which is precisely how AWS enforces encryption in transit. Conformance packs can be deployed organization-wide and Config rules support SSM Automation remediation, so the solution scales to all existing buckets. Options A and B (AWS Network Firewall blocking port 80) operate at the network layer and never modify the bucket policies, and Option D uses the wrong condition key (server-side encryption at rest, not in transit).","explanation_zh":"需求是針對 AWS Organization 中所有現有 S3 buckets 強制執行傳輸中資料加密（HTTPS/TLS）。選項 C 為組織啟用 AWS Config，並部署包含 s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only 受管規則的 conformance pack。AWS Config 文件對該規則的描述為：「檢查 S3 buckets 的政策是否要求請求使用 SSL/TLS。若任何 S3 bucket 的政策允許 HTTP 請求，則規則為 NON_COMPLIANT。」搭配的 Systems Manager Automation 修復 runbook 會新增一段 bucket policy，在 aws:SecureTransport 為 false 時拒絕存取。S3「Protecting data in transit with encryption」文件明確展示了這段完全相同的 Deny 政策，並說明 aws:SecureTransport 全域條件鍵用於「檢查請求是否透過 HTTPS（TLS）傳送」，這正是 AWS 強制傳輸中加密的方式。Conformance packs 可在組織範圍部署，且 Config 規則支援 SSM Automation 修復，因此可套用至所有現有 buckets。選項 A 與 B（用 AWS Network Firewall 封鎖 port 80）作用於網路層且從未修改 bucket 政策；選項 D 使用了錯誤的條件鍵（靜態的伺服器端加密，而非傳輸中加密）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Network Firewall filtering outbound port 80 operates at the network layer and does not enforce TLS on the S3 buckets themselves. It does not remediate the existing buckets that 'allow unencrypted connections,' and S3 access generally uses HTTPS on port 443 through public/regional endpoints, so blocking port 80 does not guarantee the buckets reject unencrypted requests. It addresses network egress, not S3 resource-policy enforcement.","why_zh":"AWS Network Firewall 過濾對外 port 80 是在網路層運作，無法在 S3 buckets 本身強制 TLS。它無法修復「允許未加密連線」的現有 buckets，且 S3 存取通常透過公開/區域端點以 HTTPS（port 443）進行，因此封鎖 port 80 無法保證 buckets 拒絕未加密的請求。它處理的是網路出站，而非 S3 資源政策的強制執行。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Blocking inbound port 80 via Network Firewall is even less relevant to S3 than A. Client-to-S3 traffic is outbound from the accounts and reaches S3 over AWS public/regional endpoints, not through a customer-managed inbound firewall. It does not modify bucket policies or enforce aws:SecureTransport.","why_zh":"透過 Network Firewall 封鎖入站 port 80 比 A 更不適用。用戶端到 S3 的流量是從帳戶向外（outbound）的，並透過 AWS 公用/區域端點抵達 S3，而非經由客戶管理的入站防火牆。它不會修改 bucket 政策，也不會強制 aws:SecureTransport。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The overall structure (org-wide AWS Config + s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only + SSM Automation runbook) is right, but the condition key is wrong. s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption-aws-kms-key-id controls server-side encryption AT REST (which KMS key is used), not encryption IN TRANSIT. Denying access when that key is null forces SSE-KMS at rest, which does not satisfy the stated requirement to encrypt data in transit (HTTPS/TLS).","why_zh":"整體結構（組織範圍 AWS Config + s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only + SSM Automation runbook）正確，但條件鍵錯誤。s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption-aws-kms-key-id 控制的是靜態（at rest）的伺服器端加密（使用哪個 KMS 金鑰），而非傳輸中（in transit）加密。當該鍵為 null 時拒絕存取是強制靜態 SSE-KMS，並不符合題目要求的傳輸中（HTTPS/TLS）資料加密。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/s3-bucket-ssl-requests-only.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/UsingEncryptionInTransit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-bucket-policies.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":194,"question_en":"A company is reviewing its IAM policies. One policy written by the DevOps engineer has been flagged as too permissive. The policy is used by an AWS Lambda function that issues a stop command to Amazon EC2 instances tagged with Environment: NonProduction over the weekend. The current policy is: What changes should the engineer make to achieve a policy of least permission? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在审查其身份和访问管理（IAM）策略。由 DevOps 工程师编写的一项策略被标记为过于宽 松。该策略被一个 AWS Lambda 函数使用，该函数会在周末向标记为“环境：非生产”的 Amazon EC2 实例发出停止命令。当前的策略是： 工程师应做出哪些更改才能实现最小权限策略？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add the following conditional expression:","B":"Change \"Resource\": \"*\"to \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:ec2:*:*:instance/*\"","C":"Add the following conditional expression:","D":"Add the following conditional expression:","E":"Change \"Action\": \"ec2:*\"to \"Action\": \"ec2:StopInstances\"","F":"Add the following conditional expression:"},"options_zh":{"A":"添加以下条件表达式：","C":"添加以下条件表达式：","D":"添加以下条件表达式："},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"This is a genuine 'Choose three' question, but the source rendered the marked answer as a single letter ['B'] and the actual condition JSON for four options was embedded as an image that did not OCR, so options A, C, D, and F all appear as the identical literal text 'Add the following conditional expression:' and cannot be told apart from text. The current policy is over-permissive in three independent ways, and AWS least privilege requires narrowing each one: (1) scope the Action from the wildcard ec2:* down to the single ec2:StopInstances (option E); (2) scope the Resource from '*' down to the instance ARN pattern arn:aws:ec2:*:*:instance/* (option B); and (3) add a Condition restricting to the tag, i.e. StringEquals on aws:ResourceTag/Environment = NonProduction (whichever of A/C/D/F literally encodes that condition). The canonical AWS IAM example 'Amazon EC2: Allows starting or stopping EC2 instances a user has tagged' shows this exact three-part structure: Action limited to ec2:StartInstances/ec2:StopInstances, Resource set to arn:aws:ec2:*:*:instance/*, and a Condition of StringEquals on aws:ResourceTag/<key>. Both B and E are readable and verifiably correct, so the defensible verdict for the identifiable changes is B + E; the dump's single ['B'] is incomplete because E is equally required, and the third required change is the unidentifiable tag-condition option.","explanation_zh":"這是真正的「選三項」題目，但來源只把標記答案渲染成單一字母 ['B']，且四個選項實際的條件 JSON 以圖片嵌入而未能 OCR，因此 A、C、D、F 在文字上都呈現為完全相同的「Add the following conditional expression:」，無法彼此區分。目前的策略在三個獨立面向上過於寬鬆，AWS 最小權限要求逐一收斂：(1) 將 Action 由萬用字元 ec2:* 收斂為單一 ec2:StopInstances（選項 E）；(2) 將 Resource 由 '*' 收斂為實例 ARN 樣式 arn:aws:ec2:*:*:instance/*（選項 B）；(3) 加入限制標籤的 Condition，即對 aws:ResourceTag/Environment 做 StringEquals 等於 NonProduction（即 A/C/D/F 中真正寫出該條件的那一個）。AWS IAM 官方範例『Amazon EC2: Allows starting or stopping EC2 instances a user has tagged』正是此三段式結構：Action 限定 ec2:StartInstances/ec2:StopInstances、Resource 設為 arn:aws:ec2:*:*:instance/*、並對 aws:ResourceTag/<key> 加 StringEquals Condition。B 與 E 皆可閱讀且可驗證為正確，故可辨識變更的 verdict 應為 B + E；題庫單一的 ['B'] 並不完整，因為 E 同屬必要，而第三個必要變更則是那個無法辨識的標籤條件選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Renders as the identical garbled/image text 'Add the following conditional expression:'. It is plausibly the correct third answer (the aws:ResourceTag/Environment = NonProduction condition), but it cannot be distinguished from C/D/F by text, so it cannot be confirmed as the specific correct option. Only the option literally encoding StringEquals on ResourceTag/Environment NonProduction belongs.","why_zh":"渲染為相同的亂碼/圖片文字「Add the following conditional expression:」。它有可能是正確的第三個答案（aws:ResourceTag/Environment = NonProduction 條件），但文字上無法與 C/D/F 區分，故無法確認為特定的正確選項；只有真正寫出對 ResourceTag/Environment NonProduction 做 StringEquals 的那一個才正確。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Identical garbled/image text and in this dataset often carries injected vendor watermark OCR noise, confirming it is corrupted image content rather than a cleanly identifiable distinct condition. Indistinguishable from A/D/F.","why_zh":"相同的亂碼/圖片文字，且在此資料集中常夾帶注入的販售浮水印 OCR 雜訊，確認為損毀的圖片內容而非可清楚辨識的條件；與 A/D/F 無法區分。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Identical garbled/image text 'Add the following conditional expression:'; cannot be reliably identified or distinguished from A/C/F. Only the conditional expression matching aws:ResourceTag/Environment = NonProduction would be a correct narrowing.","why_zh":"相同的亂碼/圖片文字「Add the following conditional expression:」，無法可靠辨識，亦無法與 A/C/F 區分；只有符合 aws:ResourceTag/Environment = NonProduction 的條件式才是正確的收斂。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Identical garbled/image text; cannot be reliably identified or distinguished from A/C/D. The single correct tag condition belongs to whichever option literally encodes ResourceTag/Environment = NonProduction.","why_zh":"相同的亂碼/圖片文字，無法可靠辨識，亦無法與 A/C/D 區分；正確的標籤條件屬於真正寫出 ResourceTag/Environment = NonProduction 的那一個選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_ec2_tag-owner.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/service-authorization/latest/reference/list_amazonec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_condition.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_action.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":195,"question_en":"A company is developing an application that will generate log events. The log events consist of five distinct metrics every one tenth of a second and produce a large amount of data. The company needs to configure the application to write the logs to Amazon Timestream. The company will configure a daily query against the Timestream table. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the FASTEST query performance? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一款应用程序，该程序每十分之一秒会生成包含五项不同指标的日志事件，从而产生大量 数据。 该公司需要将应用程序配置为将日志写入亚马逊 Timestream。该公司将针对 Timestream 表配置每日查询。 哪种步骤组合能以最快的速度满足这些查询性能要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use batch writes to write multiple log events in a single write operation.","B":"Write each log event as a single write operation.","C":"Treat each log as a single-measure record.","D":"Treat each log as a multi-measure record.","E":"Configure the memory store retention period to be longer than the magnetic store retention period.","F":"Configure the memory store retention period to be shorter than the magnetic store retention period."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用批量写入在单次写入操作中写入多个日志事件。","B":"将每个日志事件作为一次单独的写入操作来写入。","C":"将每个日志条目视为单个度量记录。","D":"将每个日志条目视为多度量记录。","E":"将内存存储保留期设置为长于磁盘存储保留期。","F":"将内存存储保留期设置为短于磁盘存储保留期。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The qualifier is FASTEST QUERY PERFORMANCE for a DAILY analytical query over a large volume of data, where the application emits 5 distinct metrics at the same timestamp every 1/10 second. (A) AWS Timestream's 'Batching writes with WriteRecords API' page states that 'Batching multiple data points in a single write operation is beneficial from a performance and cost perspective,' and you can batch points from a single series or many series in one request -- the correct ingestion design for a high-frequency producer (50 points/sec). (D) The Data modeling guide says that 'when your application is emitting multiple measures/events at the same time instant, then modeling the data as multi-measure records is usually recommended for performant data access,' that 'Multi-measure records results in lower query latency for most query types,' and that 'For queries referencing three or more measures, multi-measure records result in lower bytes metered' -- the query here references 5 measures, so multi-measure is fastest. (F) The Configuring Timestream guide gives this exact scenario: when 'applications send many queries that process a day's-worth, week's-worth, or month's-worth of data... you may want to configure a smaller retention period for the memory store (2-3 hours) and allow more data to flow to the magnetic store given the magnetic store is optimized for fast analytical queries.' The memory store is optimized for fast point-in-time queries on small recent data; the magnetic store is optimized for fast analytical queries on medium-to-large data. So for a daily analytical query, memory store retention should be SHORTER than magnetic store retention. Thus A, D, F.","explanation_zh":"此題限定詞為「最快查詢效能 (FASTEST QUERY PERFORMANCE)」，情境是針對大量資料、每 0.1 秒於同一時間戳記產生 5 個不同 metrics、且每日執行一次的分析型查詢。(A) Timestream『Batching writes with WriteRecords API』頁面指出『在單一寫入操作中批次寫入多個 data points 對效能與成本皆有利』，並可在單一請求中批次同一或多個 series 的資料點，對於每秒 50 個資料點的高頻產生者是正確的寫入設計。(D) Data modeling 文件說明『當應用程式於同一時間瞬間發出多個 measures/events 時，建議以 multi-measure records 建模以獲得高效能資料存取』，且『multi-measure records 在大多數查詢類型下可帶來更低的查詢延遲 (lower query latency)』，並指出『查詢參考三個以上 measures 時，multi-measure records 計量的位元組更少』；本題查詢涉及 5 個 measures，故 multi-measure 最快。(F) Configuring Timestream 文件給出與本題完全相符的情境：當『應用程式送出許多處理一天、一週或一個月份量資料的查詢時……應為 memory store 設定較短的保留期 (2-3 小時)，讓更多資料流入 magnetic store，因為 magnetic store 針對快速分析型查詢進行最佳化』。memory store 適合針對少量近期資料的 fast point-in-time 查詢，magnetic store 適合中大量資料的 fast analytical 查詢。因此每日分析型查詢時，memory store 保留期應「短於」magnetic store 保留期。故選 A、D、F。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Writing each log event as a single write operation contradicts the Timestream 'Batching writes with WriteRecords API' guidance that batching multiple data points in one write is beneficial for performance and cost; per-event writes add overhead and are the opposite of the recommended ingestion design for a high-frequency producer.","why_zh":"將每筆 log event 以單獨寫入操作送出，違反 Timestream『Batching writes with WriteRecords API』所述『在單一寫入中批次多個資料點有利於效能與成本』；逐筆寫入會增加負擔，與高頻產生者的建議寫入設計相反。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Single-measure records are intended for devices that emit different metrics at different time periods. Here 5 metrics share the same timestamp, so single-measure modeling raises storage (about 8X higher), and for queries referencing three or more measures it scans more bytes and yields higher query latency than multi-measure.","why_zh":"single-measure records 適用於裝置在不同時間發出不同 metrics 的情況。本題 5 個 metrics 共用同一時間戳記，採 single-measure 會提高儲存（約 8 倍），且在查詢參考三個以上 measures 時掃描更多位元組並產生較高查詢延遲，劣於 multi-measure。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Setting memory store retention longer than magnetic store keeps large historical data in the memory store, which is optimized only for fast point-in-time queries on small recent data; the AWS configuration guidance for daily/weekly/monthly queries is to use a smaller memory store retention and let more data flow to the magnetic store, which is optimized for fast analytical queries. This option is the reverse and hurts query performance.","why_zh":"將 memory store 保留期設得比 magnetic store 長，會把大量歷史資料留在僅針對少量近期資料 fast point-in-time 查詢最佳化的 memory store；AWS 針對每日/每週/每月查詢的建議是設定較短的 memory store 保留期，讓更多資料流入針對 fast analytical 查詢最佳化的 magnetic store。此選項恰好相反，損害查詢效能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/timestream/latest/developerguide/data-modeling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/timestream/latest/developerguide/configuration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/timestream/latest/developerguide/writes.batching-writes.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":196,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer has created an AWS CloudFormation template that deploys an application on Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances run Amazon Linux. The application is deployed to the EC2 instances by using shell scripts that contain user data. The EC2 instances have an IAM instance profile that has an IAM role with the AmazonSSMManagedinstanceCore managed policy attached. The DevOps engineer has modified the user data in the CloudFormation template to install a new version of the application. The engineer has also applied the stack update. However, the application was not updated on the running EC2 instances. The engineer needs to ensure that the changes to the application are installed on the running EC2 instances. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师创建了一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，用于在亚马逊上部署应用程序。 EC2 实例。这些 EC2 实例运行的是 Amazon Linux 操作系统。应用程序通过包含用户数据的 shell 脚本部 署到 EC2 实例上。EC2 实例具有一个 IAM 实例配置文件，该配置文件包含一个附加了 AmazonSSMManagedinstanceCore 管理策略的 IAM 角色。 DevOps 工程师已在 CloudFormation 模板中修改了用户数据以安装应用程序的新版本，并已应用了堆栈 更新。然而，运行中的 EC2 实例上的应用程序并未更新。工程师需要确保将应用程序的更改安装到运 行中的 EC2 实例上。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure the user data content to use the Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) multipart format. Set the scripts-user parameter to always in the text/cloud-config section.","B":"Refactor the user data commands to use the cfn-init helper script. Update the user data to install and configure the cfn-hup and cfn-init helper scripts to monitor and apply the metadata changes.","C":"Configure an EC2 launch template for the EC2 instances. Create a new EC2 Auto Scaling group. Associate the Auto Scaling group with the EC2 launch template. Use the AutoScalingScheduledAction update policy for the Auto Scaling group.","D":"Refactor the user data commands to use an AWS Systems Manager document (SSM document). Add an AWS CLI command in the user data to use Systems Manager Run Command to apply the SSM document to the EC2 instances.","E":"Refactor the user data command to use an AWS Systems Manager document (SSM document). Use Systems Manager State Manager to create an association between the SSM document and the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"将用户数据内容配置为使用多用途互联网邮件扩展（MIME）多部分格式。在 text/cloud-config 部 分将 scripts-user 参数设置为 always 。","B":"重构用户数据命令以使用 cfn-init 辅助脚本。更新用户数据以安装和配置 cfn-hup 和 cfn-init 辅助脚本， 以监控并应用元数据更改。","C":"为 EC2 实例配置一个 EC2 启动模板。创建一个新的 EC2 自动缩放组。将自动缩放组与 EC2 启动模 板相关联。为自动缩放组使用 AutoScalingScheduledAction 更新策略。","D":"重构用户数据命令以使用 AWS 系统管理器文档（SSM 文档）。在用户数据中添加一个 AWS CLI 命 令，使用系统管理器运行命令将 SSM 文档应用于 EC2 实例。","E":"将用户数据命令重构为使用 AWS 系统管理器文档（SSM 文档）。使用系统管理器状态管理器在 SSM 文档和 EC2 实例之间创建关联。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"EC2 user data is processed by cloud-init only once at first launch by default. When the engineer changes the user data property in the CloudFormation template and calls UpdateStack, CloudFormation updates the property, but a user-data-only change does not trigger instance replacement and does not re-run user data on already-running instances, so the new application version is never installed. Two distinct, complete, AWS-recommended patterns fix this on the existing running instances. Option B refactors the bootstrap into cfn-init, which reads AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata, and installs the cfn-hup daemon. The cfn-hup doc states it 'detects changes in resource metadata and runs user-specified actions when a change is detected. This allows you to make configuration updates on your running Amazon EC2 instances through the UpdateStack API action.' so when UpdateStack changes the metadata, cfn-hup invokes cfn-init to apply the new version. Option E moves the install logic into an SSM document and uses Systems Manager State Manager to create an association that applies and enforces the desired state on the running instances on a schedule; the instances already run the SSM Agent (Amazon Linux) and carry the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore policy, so the association can run immediately and on each cycle. Options A, C, and D either only run at boot, leave the existing instances untouched, or are self-defeating.","explanation_zh":"EC2 user data 預設只由 cloud-init 在首次啟動時處理一次。當工程師變更 CloudFormation 範本中的 user data 屬性並呼叫 UpdateStack 時，CloudFormation 雖更新了該屬性，但僅變更 user data 不會觸發執行個體替換，也不會在已執行中的執行個體上重新執行 user data，因此新版本的應用程式從未被安裝。兩個各自完整且為 AWS 建議的做法可在現有執行中的執行個體上解決此問題。選項 B 將啟動程序重構為 cfn-init（讀取 AWS::CloudFormation::Init metadata），並安裝 cfn-hup 常駐程式。cfn-hup 文件指出它『偵測資源 metadata 的變更，並在偵測到變更時執行使用者指定的動作。這可讓你透過 UpdateStack API 動作對執行中的 EC2 執行個體進行設定更新。』因此當 UpdateStack 改變 metadata 時，cfn-hup 會呼叫 cfn-init 套用新版本。選項 E 將安裝邏輯移入 SSM document，並使用 Systems Manager State Manager 建立 association，依排程在執行中的執行個體上套用並強制維持所需狀態；這些執行個體已執行 SSM Agent（Amazon Linux）並具備 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 政策，association 可立即且週期性地執行。選項 A、C、D 分別只在開機時執行、未觸及現有執行個體，或本身自相矛盾。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Setting cloud-init's scripts-user to 'always' via MIME multipart makes user data run on every boot/reboot, not on a stack update. The instances are already running and a user-data property change does not reboot them, so the new version is still not applied to the running instances.","why_zh":"透過 MIME multipart 將 cloud-init 的 scripts-user 設為 'always' 只會讓 user data 在每次開機/重啟時執行，而非在堆疊更新時。執行個體已在執行中，且變更 user data 屬性不會重啟它們，因此新版本仍不會套用到執行中的執行個體。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating a brand-new launch template and a new Auto Scaling group does not touch the existing running instances. The AutoScalingScheduledAction update policy only governs how CloudFormation handles scheduled scaling actions during a stack update (it prevents CloudFormation from overriding min/max/desired capacity); per the UpdatePolicy docs, replacing or rolling instances to pick up new user data is done by AutoScalingReplacingUpdate or AutoScalingRollingUpdate, and the instances aren't even in an ASG. It is a large refactor that still fails the requirement.","why_zh":"建立全新的 launch template 與新的 Auto Scaling group 並不會影響現有執行中的執行個體。AutoScalingScheduledAction 更新政策僅控管 CloudFormation 在堆疊更新期間如何處理排程擴縮動作（避免 CloudFormation 覆寫 min/max/desired capacity）；依 UpdatePolicy 文件，替換或輪替執行個體以套用新 user data 是由 AutoScalingReplacingUpdate 或 AutoScalingRollingUpdate 完成，而這些執行個體甚至不在 ASG 中。這是大幅重構卻仍無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Placing the AWS CLI Run Command call inside user data is self-defeating: user data only executes at launch, so on a stack update it will not run on the already-running instances. The Run Command would only fire on a fresh launch, leaving running instances un-updated.","why_zh":"把呼叫 Run Command 的 AWS CLI 放進 user data 是自相矛盾的：user data 只在啟動時執行，因此堆疊更新時不會在已執行中的執行個體上執行。Run Command 只會在全新啟動時觸發，執行中的執行個體仍不會被更新。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/cfn-hup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/cfn-init.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-init.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-attribute-updatepolicy.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":197,"question_en":"A company is refactoring applications to use AWS. The company identifies an internal web application that needs to make Amazon S3 API calls in a specific AWS account. The company wants to use its existing identity provider (IdP) auth.company.com for authentication. The IdP supports only OpenID Connect (OIDC). A DevOps engineer needs to secure the web application's access to the AWS account. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在重构应用程序以使用 AWS。该公司确定了一个内部网络应用程序，需要在特定的 AWS 账 户中调用 Amazon S3 API。 该公司希望使用其现有的身份提供商 auth.company.com 进行身份验证。该身份提供商仅支持 OpenID Connect（OIDC）。一位 DevOps 工程师需要确保网络应用程序能够安全访问 AWS 账户。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). Configure an IdP. Upload the IdP metadata from the existing IdP.","B":"Create an IAM IdP by using the provider URL, audience, and signature from the existing IP.","C":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows the necessary S3 actions. Configure the role's trust policy to allow the OIDC IP to assume the role if the sts.amazon.com:aud context key is appid_from_idp.","D":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows the necessary S3 actions. Configure the role's trust policy to allow the OIDC IP to assume the role if the auth.company.com:aud context key is appid_from_idp.","E":"Configure the web application to use the AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity API operation to retrieve temporary credentials. Use the temporary credentials to make the S3 API calls.","F":"Configure the web application to use the GetFederationToken API operation to retrieve temporary credentials. Use the temporary credentials to make the S3 API calls."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）。配置身份提供方。上传现有身份提供方的元数据。","B":"使用现有 IP 的提供程序 URL、受众和签名创建一个 IAM 身份提供商。","C":"创建一个具有允许执行必要 S3 操作策略的 IAM 角色。配置该角色的信任策略，以便在 sts.amazon. com:aud 上下文键为 appid_from_idp 时允许 OIDC IP 假冒该角色。","D":"创建一个具有允许执行必要 S3 操作策略的 IAM 角色。配置该角色的信任策略，以便在 auth. company.com:aud 上下文键为 appid_from_idp 时，允许 OIDC IP 假冒该角色。","E":"配置网络应用程序使用 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity API 操作来获取临时凭证。使用临时凭证 来调用 S3 API。","F":"配置网络应用程序使用 GetFederationToken API 操作来获取临时凭证。使用临时凭证来调用 S3 API。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario requires an internal web application to make programmatic Amazon S3 API calls authenticated by an existing OIDC-only IdP (auth.company.com). This is textbook OIDC web identity federation, which has three documented steps. (B) First register the external IdP in IAM as an OpenID Connect identity provider. AWS creates this entity from the provider URL (issuer), the audience (the client/app ID issued by the IdP), and the IdP server certificate thumbprint (the 'signature') - exactly the values in the IAM 'Create an OIDC identity provider' procedure. (D) Then create an IAM role whose permissions policy allows the needed S3 actions and whose trust policy allows sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity, restricted with the aud context key. The IAM docs state explicitly: 'For OIDC providers, use the fully qualified URL of the OIDC IdP with the aud context key, such as server.example.com:aud: appid_from_oidc_idp.' Here the fully qualified URL is auth.company.com, so the condition is auth.company.com:aud = appid_from_idp. (E) The web application calls AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity, passing the OIDC token, to obtain temporary credentials and uses them for the S3 calls; per the AWS STS API reference this operation does not require any long-term AWS credentials and validates the caller via the web identity token. B, D, and E together form the complete documented OIDC federation flow.","explanation_zh":"情境要求一個內部 web application 透過既有且僅支援 OIDC 的 IdP (auth.company.com) 進行驗證後，對 Amazon S3 發出程式化 API 呼叫。這正是標準的 OIDC web identity federation，文件記載為三個步驟。(B) 首先在 IAM 中將外部 IdP 註冊為 OpenID Connect identity provider，AWS 依據 provider URL (issuer)、audience (IdP 發給應用程式的 client/app ID) 以及 IdP 伺服器憑證的 thumbprint (即「signature」) 建立此實體，這正是 IAM 建立 OIDC identity provider 程序所需的值。(D) 接著建立一個 IAM role，其 permissions policy 允許所需的 S3 動作，trust policy 允許 sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity 並以 aud context key 限制。IAM 文件明確指出：對於 OIDC providers，要使用 OIDC IdP 的完整 URL 搭配 aud context key，例如 server.example.com:aud: appid_from_oidc_idp。此處完整 URL 為 auth.company.com，因此條件為 auth.company.com:aud = appid_from_idp。(E) web application 呼叫 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity 並傳入 OIDC token 以取得臨時憑證，再用這些憑證呼叫 S3；依 AWS STS API 參考，此操作不需任何長期 AWS 憑證，並透過 web identity token 驗證呼叫者。B、D、E 共同構成完整且有文件依據的 OIDC federation 流程。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS IAM Identity Center's external IdP integration is built on SAML 2.0 (you upload SAML metadata XML), not OIDC, and it targets human single sign-on into the console/CLI rather than a web application making programmatic S3 API calls. The scenario's IdP supports only OIDC and the app needs STS-style temporary credentials, so Identity Center with uploaded IdP metadata does not produce the role-assumption flow the application needs.","why_zh":"AWS IAM Identity Center 的外部 IdP 整合是以 SAML 2.0 為基礎 (上傳 SAML metadata XML)，並非 OIDC，且其目標是人類使用者 SSO 登入 console/CLI，而非 web application 進行程式化的 S3 API 呼叫。情境中的 IdP 僅支援 OIDC，應用程式需要 STS 風格的臨時憑證，因此 Identity Center 搭配上傳的 IdP metadata 無法產生應用程式所需的 role-assumption 流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The trust-policy condition key prefix is wrong. AWS docs require the aud context key to be prefixed by the OIDC IdP's fully qualified URL (here auth.company.com:aud), as in option D. 'sts.amazon.com:aud' is not a valid web-identity condition key (and is misspelled versus sts.amazonaws.com), so this restriction would not match the IdP's token and role assumption would fail.","why_zh":"trust policy 的條件 key 前綴錯誤。AWS 文件要求以 OIDC IdP 的完整 URL 作為 aud context key 的前綴 (此處應為 auth.company.com:aud)，如選項 D。sts.amazon.com:aud 並非有效的 web identity 條件 key (且拼字與 sts.amazonaws.com 不符)，因此此限制無法與 IdP token 相符，role 的承接會失敗。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"GetFederationToken is for a server-based custom identity broker and must be called using the long-term security credentials of an IAM user; it does not consume an OIDC web identity token. The AWS STS docs explicitly recommend AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity (or Amazon Cognito) for web/mobile apps authenticated by an OIDC IdP, so this option is technically invalid for the scenario and would require embedding long-term AWS credentials.","why_zh":"GetFederationToken 用於以伺服器為基礎的自訂 identity broker，且必須使用某個 IAM user 的長期安全憑證來呼叫；它不接受 OIDC web identity token。AWS STS 文件明確建議由 OIDC IdP 驗證的 web/mobile 應用程式應使用 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity (或 Amazon Cognito)，因此此選項在此情境中技術上不成立，且會需要嵌入長期 AWS 憑證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_create_oidc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create_for-idp_oidc.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/API_AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/STS/latest/APIReference/API_GetFederationToken.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_oidc.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":198,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon RDS for all databases in its AWS accounts. The company uses AWS Control Tower to build a landing zone that has an audit and logging account. All databases must be encrypted at rest for compliance reasons. The company's security engineer needs to receive notification about any noncompliant databases that are in the company’s accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"该公司在其所有 AWS 账户中使用 Amazon RDS 来管理数据库。该公司使用 AWS Control Tower 构建了一 个包含审计和日志记录账户的着陆区。出于合规性原因，所有数据库在静止状态下都必须进行加密。该公 司的安全工程师需要收到有关其账户中任何不符合规定的数据库的通知。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Control Tower to activate the optional detective control (guardrail) to determine whether the RDS storage is encrypted. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic in the company's audit account. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to filter noncompliant events from the AWS Control Tower control (guardrail) to notify the SNS topic. Subscribe the security engineer's email address to the SNS topic.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy AWS Lambda functions to every account. Write the Lambda function code to determine whether the RDS storage is encrypted in the account the function is deployed to. Send the findings as an Amazon CloudWatch metric to the management account. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Create a CloudWatch alarm that notifies the SNS topic when metric thresholds are met. Subscribe the security engineer's email address to the SNS topic.","C":"Create a custom AWS Config rule in every account to determine whether the RDS storage is encrypted. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic in the audit account. Create an Amazon EventBidge rule to filter noncompliant events from the AWS Control Tower control (guardrail) to notify the SNS topic. Subscribe the security engineer's email address to the SNS topic.","D":"Launch an Amazon C2 instance. Run an hourly cron job by using the AWS CLI to determine whether the RDS storage is encrypted in each AWS account. Store the results in an RDS database. Notify the security engineer by sending email messages from the EC2 instance when noncompliance is detected"},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 控制塔激活可选的检测控制（防护栏），以确定 RDS 存储是否已加密。在公司的审计账户中 创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，从 AWS 控制塔控制（防护栏）中筛选出不符合规定的事件，并通知 SNS 主题。将安全工程师的电子邮件地址 订阅到 SNS 主题。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 AWS Lambda 函数部署到每个账户。编写 Lambda 函数代码以确定 函数部署到的账户中的 RDS 存储是否已加密。将发现结果作为 Amazon CloudWatch 指标发送到管理账 户。创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，当 指标阈值达到时通知 SNS 主题。将安全工程师的电子邮件地址订阅到 SNS 主题。","C":"在每个账户中创建自定义的 AWS Config 规则，以确定 RDS 存储是否已加密。在审计账户中创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，从 AWS 控制塔控 制（防护栏）中筛选出不符合要求的事件，并通知 SNS 主题。将安全工程师的电子邮件地址订阅到 SNS 主题。","D":"启动一个 Amazon C2 实例。使用 AWS CLI 每小时运行一次 cron 任务，以确定每个 AWS 账户中的 RDS 存储是否已加密。将结果存储在 RDS 数据库中。当检测到不符合规定的情况时，从 EC2 实例发送电子 邮件通知安全工程师。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Control Tower ships a managed, AWS-owned detective control named 'Detect Whether Storage Encryption is Enabled for Amazon RDS Database Instances', listed under the Strongly recommended controls. Per the docs it is implemented behind the scenes with an AWS Config rule (SourceIdentifier RDS_STORAGE_ENCRYPTED) and is NOT enabled by default, which is exactly the 'optional detective control' option A activates. Once enabled, it evaluates every enrolled account automatically with zero custom code. AWS Control Tower already aggregates all AWS Config compliance and noncompliance notifications into SNS topics in the AUDIT account (for example aws-controltower-AggregateSecurityNotifications), and the AWS documentation explicitly states administrators can 'set up an EventBridge rule to filter notifications' to be alerted on noncompliant resources. So creating an SNS topic in the audit account, adding an EventBridge rule that filters the noncompliant findings, and subscribing the security engineer's email is the documented, lowest-effort pattern, making A the MOST operationally efficient solution. (Minor wording nuance: the noncompliance event is technically emitted by AWS Config's 'Config Rules Compliance Change', not directly by aws.controltower, but Control Tower is what deploys that managed Config rule, so A's description is accurate in substance.) Option C reinvents the same check as a custom Config rule in every account yet then claims to filter events 'from the AWS Control Tower control (guardrail)' it never created, so it is both higher overhead and self-contradictory. Option B (StackSets + custom Lambda in every account + cross-account CloudWatch metrics to the management account) and Option D (an EC2 hourly cron job using the CLI, storing results in RDS, emailing from the instance) are far more code to build, secure, and operate.","explanation_zh":"AWS Control Tower 內建一個由 AWS 擁有的託管偵測型控制 (detective control)，名為 'Detect Whether Storage Encryption is Enabled for Amazon RDS Database Instances'，列在 Strongly recommended controls 之下。依官方文件，它背後以 AWS Config rule (SourceIdentifier RDS_STORAGE_ENCRYPTED) 實作，且預設未啟用，這正是選項 A 所啟用的「optional 偵測型控制」。啟用後會自動評估每個已納管帳戶，完全不需自訂程式碼。AWS Control Tower 本來就會把所有 AWS Config 的合規/不合規通知彙整到 audit 帳戶的 SNS topic (例如 aws-controltower-AggregateSecurityNotifications)，且官方文件明確指出管理員可以「set up an EventBridge rule to filter notifications」以針對不合規資源收到告警。因此在 audit 帳戶建立 SNS topic、加上一條 EventBridge rule 過濾不合規結果、再讓安全工程師訂閱 email，正是文件記載且工作量最低的做法，故 A 營運效率最高。(措辭上的小細節：不合規事件嚴格說是由 AWS Config 的 'Config Rules Compliance Change' 發出，而非直接由 aws.controltower 發出；但部署該託管 Config rule 的正是 Control Tower，所以 A 的描述在實質上是正確的。) 選項 C 在每個帳戶用自訂 Config rule 重造同一檢查，卻又宣稱要過濾它從未建立的「AWS Control Tower control (guardrail)」事件，因此既負擔更高又自相矛盾。選項 B (StackSets + 在每個帳戶部署自訂 Lambda + 跨帳戶把 CloudWatch metric 送到 management 帳戶) 與選項 D (用 EC2 每小時跑 cron 與 CLI、把結果存到 RDS、再由 EC2 寄信) 都需要建置、保護與維運大量程式碼，效率遠低於 A。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Deploying custom Lambda to every account via CloudFormation StackSets, writing custom RDS-encryption-check code, and piping cross-account CloudWatch metrics to the management account is high operational overhead and reinvents the managed RDS storage-encryption detective control that Control Tower already provides. It also targets the management account, whereas Control Tower aggregates security and compliance notifications in the audit account.","why_zh":"用 CloudFormation StackSets 在每個帳戶部署自訂 Lambda、撰寫 RDS 加密檢查程式碼、再跨帳戶把 CloudWatch metric 送到 management 帳戶，營運負擔極高，且重造 Control Tower 已提供的 RDS 儲存加密託管偵測型控制。它還把通知導向 management 帳戶，但 Control Tower 是把安全與合規通知彙整在 audit 帳戶。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Authoring and deploying a custom AWS Config rule in every account is unnecessary because a native AWS-managed detective control already checks RDS storage encryption. The option is also self-contradictory: it builds a custom Config rule but then says the EventBridge rule filters noncompliant events 'from the AWS Control Tower control (guardrail)' that it never enabled. Net result is more build/maintain effort than simply activating the built-in control.","why_zh":"在每個帳戶撰寫並部署自訂 AWS Config rule 並無必要，因為原生 AWS 託管偵測型控制已能檢查 RDS 儲存加密。此選項亦自相矛盾：它建立自訂 Config rule，卻又說 EventBridge rule 要過濾「來自它從未啟用的 AWS Control Tower control (guardrail)」的不合規事件。結果就是比直接啟用內建控制需要更多建置與維運工作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EC2 instance running an hourly cron job with the AWS CLI, storing results in an RDS database, and sending email directly from the instance is the least efficient and most fragile approach. It requires building, securing, patching, and operating compute plus cross-account access, lacks any native managed compliance detection, and does not scale across many accounts.","why_zh":"用 EC2 每小時跑 cron 與 AWS CLI、把結果存到 RDS、再直接由 EC2 寄信，是效率最低且最脆弱的做法。需自行建置、保護、修補與維運運算資源與跨帳戶存取，完全沒有原生託管的合規偵測，且難以橫跨眾多帳戶擴展。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/strongly-recommended-detective-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/detective-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/receive-notifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-controltower.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":199,"question_en":"A company is migrating from its on-premises data center to AWS. The company currently uses a custom on-premises CI/CD pipeline solution to build and package software. The company wants its software packages and dependent public repositories to be available in AWS CodeArtifact to facilitate the creation of application-specific pipelines. Which combination of steps should the company take to update the CI/CD pipeline solution and to configure CodeArtifact with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在从其本地数据中心迁移到 AWS。该公司目前使用自定义的本地 CI/CD 管道解决方案来构建 和打包软件。 该公司希望其软件包及相关的公共存储库能在 AWS CodeArtifact 中获取，以方便创建特定于应用程序 的流水线。 公司应采取哪两种步骤的组合来更新 CI/CD 管道解决方案，并以最低的操作开销配置 CodeArtifact？ （选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the CI/CD pipeline to create a VM image that contains newly packaged software. Use AWS Import/Export to make the VM image available as an Amazon EC2 AMI. Launch the AMI with an attached IAM instance profile that allows CodeArtifact actions. Use AWS CLI commands to publish the packages to a CodeArtifact repository.","B":"Create an AWS Identity and Access Management Roles Anywhere trust anchor. Create an IAM role that allows CodeArtifact actions and that has a trust relationship on the trust anchor. Update the on- premises CI/CD pipeline to assume the new IAM role and to publish the packages to CodeArtifact.","C":"Create a new Amazon S3 bucket. Generate a presigned URL that allows the PutObject request. Update the on-premises CI/CD pipeline to use the presigned URL to publish the packages from the on- premises location to the S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function that runs when packages are created in the bucket through a put command. Configure the Lambda function to publish the packages to CodeArtifact.","D":"For each public repository, create a CodeArutact repository that is configured with an external connection. Configure the dependent repositories as upstream public repositories.","E":"Create a Codeartitact repository that is configured with a set of external connections to the public repositories. Configure the external connections to be downstream of the repository."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 CI/CD 管道以创建包含新打包软件的虚拟机映像。使用 AWS 导入/导出服务将虚拟机映像作为 Amazon EC2 AMI 提供。使用允许执行 CodeArtifact 操作的 IAM 实例配置文件启动 AMI。使用 AWS CLI 命令将软件包发布到 CodeArtifact 存储库。","B":"创建一个 AWS 身份和访问管理（IAM）Roles Anywhere 信任锚。创建一个允许执行 CodeArtifact 操作 且与信任锚建立信任关系的 IAM 角色。更新本地 CI/CD 管道以承担新 IAM 角色，并将软件包发布 到 CodeArtifact。","C":"创建一个新的 Amazon S3 存储桶。生成一个预签名 URL，允许执行 PutObject 请求。更新本地的 CI/CD 管道，使其使用预签名 URL 将本地位置的软件包发布到 S3 存储桶。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，当 通过 put 命令在存储桶中创建软件包时运行。配置 Lambda 函数将软件包发布到 CodeArtifact。","D":"对于每个公共代码库，创建一个配置了外部连接的 CodeArutact 代码库。将依赖的代码库配置为 上游公共代码库。","E":"创建一个 Codeartitact 代码库，并将其配置为与公共代码库建立一组外部连接。将这些外部连接配置 为该代码库的下游。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The CI/CD pipeline keeps running in the on-premises data center (outside AWS), so the lowest-overhead way to give it AWS credentials to publish to CodeArtifact is IAM Roles Anywhere (B). The IAM Roles Anywhere docs state it lets 'workloads such as servers, containers, and applications that run outside of AWS' obtain temporary IAM credentials so 'you don't need to manage long-term AWS credentials.' You create a trust anchor that references your CA, create an IAM role that grants CodeArtifact actions and trusts the IAM Roles Anywhere service via the trust anchor, then have the on-prem pipeline present its X.509 certificate to assume the role and publish packages directly. No extra AWS infrastructure is needed. For the dependent public repositories (D), the CodeArtifact docs explicitly state 'Each CodeArtifact repository can only have one external connection' and 'the intended way to use external connections is to have one repository per domain with an external connection to a given public repository... configure all the other repositories with an upstream to it.' That is exactly D, and it disqualifies E.","explanation_zh":"CI/CD pipeline 仍執行在地端資料中心（AWS 之外），因此以最少維運負擔提供 AWS 憑證以發佈到 CodeArtifact 的方式是 IAM Roles Anywhere（B）。IAM Roles Anywhere 文件指出，它可讓『執行在 AWS 之外的伺服器、容器與應用程式等工作負載』取得臨時 IAM 憑證，因此『不需管理長期 AWS 憑證』。做法是建立指向 CA 的 trust anchor，建立一個授予 CodeArtifact 動作且透過 trust anchor 信任 IAM Roles Anywhere 服務的 IAM role，地端 pipeline 再以其 X.509 憑證取得臨時憑證並直接發佈套件，無需任何額外 AWS 基礎設施。對於相依的公開儲存庫（D），CodeArtifact 文件明確指出『每個 CodeArtifact repository 只能有一個 external connection』，且『使用 external connection 的預期方式是每個 domain 對單一公開儲存庫配置一個帶 external connection 的 repository……其餘 repository 以 upstream 連到它』。這正好對應 D，並否定 E。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Building a VM image, importing it as an EC2 AMI, and launching instances to run AWS CLI publish commands is enormous, unnecessary operational overhead. AWS Import/Export is a deprecated physical-disk shipping service, not a VM-to-AMI conversion tool. This badly violates the LEAST operational overhead requirement.","why_zh":"建立 VM 映像、匯入為 EC2 AMI 並啟動執行個體來跑 CLI 發佈指令，維運負擔極高且毫無必要。AWS Import/Export 是已淘汰的實體磁碟運送服務，並非 VM 轉 AMI 的轉換工具。嚴重違反最少維運負擔要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Routing packages through an S3 bucket via a presigned URL and then a Lambda function to relay them into CodeArtifact adds multiple moving parts (bucket, URL generation, event trigger, Lambda code) when the pipeline could publish directly to CodeArtifact once it has credentials. Far more operational overhead than IAM Roles Anywhere.","why_zh":"透過 presigned URL 將套件送到 S3，再以 Lambda 轉發到 CodeArtifact，增加多個元件（bucket、URL 產生、事件觸發、Lambda 程式碼），而 pipeline 取得憑證後其實可直接發佈到 CodeArtifact。維運負擔遠高於 IAM Roles Anywhere。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A single CodeArtifact repository cannot hold 'a set of external connections' — the docs state each repository can have only one external connection. The phrase 'configure the external connections to be downstream of the repository' is also wrong: a repo with an external connection serves its downstream repositories, and you connect others via upstream. The documented pattern is one repo per public repo plus upstreams (D).","why_zh":"單一 CodeArtifact repository 無法擁有『一組 external connections』——文件指出每個 repository 只能有一個 external connection。『將 external connection 設為 repository 的下游』也是錯的：帶有 external connection 的 repo 是供其下游 repo 使用，其他 repo 透過 upstream 連入。文件記載的模式是每個公開 repo 一個 repository 加上 upstream（D）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/external-connection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/APIReference/Welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_credentials_temp.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":200,"question_en":"A DevOps team uses AWS CodePipeline, AWS CodeBuild, and AWS CodeDeploy to deploy an application. The application is a REST API that uses AWS Lambda functions and Amazon API Gateway. Recent deployments have introduced errors that have affected many customers. The DevOps team needs a solution that reverts to the most recent stable version of the application when an error is detected. The solution must affect the fewest customers possible. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队使用 AWS CodePipeline、AWS CodeBuild 和 AWS CodeDeploy 来部署应用程序。该应用 程序是一个使用 AWS Lambda 函数和 Amazon API Gateway 的 REST API。最近的部署引入了错误，影响 了许多客户。 当检测到错误时，DevOps 团队需要一个解决方案，能够回退到应用程序的最新稳定版本。该解决方案对 客户的干扰应尽可能小。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Set the deployment configuration in CodeDeploy to LambdaAllAtOnce. Configure automatic rollbacks on the deployment group. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that detects HTTP Bad Gateway errors on API Gateway. Configure the deployment group to roll back when the number of alarms meets the alarm threshold.","B":"Set the deployment configuration in CodeDeploy to LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes. Configure automatic rollbacks on the deployment group. Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm that detects HTTP Bad Gateway errors on API Gateway. Configure the deployment group to roll back when the number of alarms meets the alarm threshold.","C":"Set the deployment configuration in CodeDeploy to LambdaAllAtOnce. Configure manual rollbacks on the deployment group. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to send notifications every time a deployment fails. Configure the SNS topic to invoke a new Lambda function that stops the current deployment and starts the most recent successful deployment.","D":"Set the deployment configuration in CodeDeploy to LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes. Configure manual rollbacks on the deployment group. Create a metric filter on an Amazon CloudWatch log group for API Gateway to monitor HTTP Bad Gateway errors. Configure the metric filter to invoke a new Lambda function that stops the current deployment and starts the most recent successful deployment."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CodeDeploy 中将部署配置设置为 LambdaAllAtOnce。在部署组上配置自动回滚。创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，用于检测 API Gateway 上的 HTTP 错误网关错误。配置部署组，使其在警报数量达 到警报阈值时回滚。","B":"在 CodeDeploy 中将部署配置设置为 LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes。在部署组中配置自动回滚。创建 一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报，用于检测 API Gateway 上的 HTTP 网关错误。配置部署组，使其在警报 数量达到警报阈值时回滚。","C":"在 CodeDeploy 中将部署配置设置为 LambdaAllAtOnce。在部署组上配置手动回滚。创建一个 Amazon 简 单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，以便每次部署失败时发送通知。配置 SNS 主题以调用一个新的 Lambda 函数，该函数会停止当前部署并启动最近一次成功的部署。","D":"在 CodeDeploy 中将部署配置设置为 LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes。在部署组上配置手动回滚。在 API Gateway 的 Amazon CloudWatch 日志组上创建一个指标过滤器，以监控 HTTP 网关错误。配置指标 过滤器以调用一个新的 Lambda 函数，该函数会停止当前部署并启动最近一次成功的部署。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are three-fold: automatically revert to the most recent stable version when an error is detected, affect the fewest customers possible, and do so with the MOST operational efficiency (favoring built-in features over custom code). Per the AWS CodeDeploy docs, CodeDeployDefault.LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes 'Shifts 10 percent of traffic in the first increment. The remaining 90 percent is deployed 10 minutes later,' so at most 10 percent of customers are exposed to a faulty release during the 10-minute validation window, satisfying the 'fewest customers' requirement. CodeDeploy natively supports automatic rollback: 'You can configure a deployment group or deployment to automatically roll back when a deployment fails or when a monitoring threshold you specify is met. In this case, the last known good version of an application revision is deployed.' That monitoring threshold is a CloudWatch alarm, and for AWS Lambda/Amazon ECS deployments CodeDeploy can stop and roll back the deployment when the alarm fires. Option B wires these built-in capabilities together (canary + automatic rollback on a CloudWatch alarm for API Gateway errors) with no custom Lambda, SNS-to-Lambda glue, or metric-filter orchestration, making it the most operationally efficient choice. Options A and C use LambdaAllAtOnce, which shifts 100 percent of traffic at once and exposes every customer, while C and D add custom code for rollback, increasing operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"此題有三個需求:偵測到錯誤時自動回復到最近的穩定版本、影響最少的客戶,並且以最高的運維效率達成(優先使用內建功能而非自訂程式碼)。依 AWS CodeDeploy 文件,CodeDeployDefault.LambdaCanary10Percent10Minutes『在第一個增量切換 10% 流量,剩餘 90% 在 10 分鐘後部署』,因此在 10 分鐘的驗證視窗內最多只有 10% 客戶接觸到有問題的版本,符合『影響最少客戶』需求。CodeDeploy 原生支援自動 rollback:『你可以設定 deployment group 或 deployment 在部署失敗或達到你指定的監控門檻時自動 rollback,屆時會部署上一個已知良好版本。』該監控門檻即為 CloudWatch alarm,對於 AWS Lambda / Amazon ECS 部署,CodeDeploy 可在 alarm 觸發時停止並 rollback 部署。選項 B 將這些內建能力串接在一起(canary + 以 API Gateway 錯誤的 CloudWatch alarm 觸發自動 rollback),不需自訂 Lambda、SNS-to-Lambda 接線或 metric filter 編排,因此運維效率最高。選項 A 與 C 使用 LambdaAllAtOnce,一次切換 100% 流量、所有客戶都受影響;而 C 與 D 額外加入自訂程式碼來執行 rollback,增加運維負擔。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The automatic-rollback-on-CloudWatch-alarm mechanism is correct and native, but LambdaAllAtOnce 'Shifts all traffic to the updated Lambda functions at once,' so 100 percent of customers hit the faulty version before any rollback can fire. This violates the 'affect the fewest customers possible' requirement.","why_zh":"其『以 CloudWatch alarm 觸發自動 rollback』的機制正確且為原生功能,但 LambdaAllAtOnce『一次將所有流量切到更新後的 Lambda 函式』,因此在任何 rollback 觸發前,100% 客戶都會命中有問題的版本,違反『影響最少客戶』的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Doubly wrong: LambdaAllAtOnce exposes all customers at once, and it relies on manual rollbacks driven by a custom SNS topic invoking a custom Lambda that stops the current deployment and starts the prior successful one. CodeDeploy already provides native automatic rollback to the last known good version, so this custom orchestration is unnecessary overhead, failing both the 'fewest customers' and 'most operational efficiency' requirements.","why_zh":"雙重錯誤:LambdaAllAtOnce 一次曝露所有客戶,且依賴自訂 SNS topic 觸發自訂 Lambda 停止當前部署並啟動前一個成功版本的手動 rollback。CodeDeploy 本身就提供回到上一個已知良好版本的原生自動 rollback,因此這套自訂編排是多餘的負擔,同時違反『最少客戶』與『最高運維效率』需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The canary configuration correctly limits customer impact to 10 percent, but it uses manual rollbacks plus a custom CloudWatch Logs metric filter that invokes a custom Lambda to stop and restart deployments. Building and maintaining that custom orchestration is far more operational overhead than CodeDeploy's built-in automatic rollback triggered by a CloudWatch alarm, so it loses on the MOST operational efficiency qualifier.","why_zh":"Canary 設定正確地將客戶影響限制在 10%,但採用手動 rollback 加上自訂的 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 觸發自訂 Lambda 來停止並重啟部署。建置與維護這套自訂編排的運維負擔遠高於 CodeDeploy 內建的『以 CloudWatch alarm 觸發自動 rollback』,因此在『最高運維效率』這個限定條件上落敗。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployments-rollback-and-redeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-configure-advanced-options.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":201,"question_en":"A company recently deployed its web application on AWS. The company is preparing for a large-scale sales event and must ensure that the web application can scale to meet the demand. The application's frontend infrastructure includes an Amazon CloudFront distribution that has an Amazon S3 bucket as an origin. The backend infrastructure includes an Amazon API Gateway API, several AWS Lambda functions, and an Amazon Aurora DB cluster. The company's DevOps engineer conducts a load test and identifies that the Lambda functions can fulfil the peak number of requests. However, the DevOps engineer notices request latency during the initial burst of requests. Most of the requests to the Lambda functions produce queries to the database. A large portion of the invocation time is used to establish database connections. Which combination of steps will provide the application with the required scalability? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司最近将其网络应用程序部署在了亚马逊网络服务（AWS）上。该公司正在为一场大规模的促 销活动做准备，必须确保网络应用程序能够扩展以满足需求。 该应用程序的前端基础设施包括一个以 Amazon S3 存储桶作为源的 Amazon CloudFront 分发。后端基础设 施包括一个 Amazon API Gateway API、若干个 AWS Lambda 函数以及一个 Amazon Aurora 数据库集群。 该公司的 DevOps 工程师进行了负载测试，发现 Lambda 函数能够满足峰值请求数量。然而，DevOps 工程 师注意到在请求初始激增时存在请求延迟。大多数对 Lambda 函数的请求都会生成对数据库的查询。调用 时间的很大一部分用于建立数据库连接。 哪些步骤组合能为应用程序提供所需的可扩展性？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure a higher reserved concurrency for the Lambda functions.","B":"Configure a higher provisioned concurrency for the Lambda functions.","C":"Convert the DB cluster to an Aurora global database. Add additional Aurora Replicas in AWS Regions based on the locations of the company's customers.","D":"Refactor the Lambda functions. Move the code blocks that initialize database connections into the function handlers.","E":"Use Amazon RDS Proxy to create a proxy for the Aurora database. Update the Lambda functions to use the proxy endpoints for database connections."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 Lambda 函数配置更高的预留并发量。","B":"为 Lambda 函数配置更高的预置并发量。","C":"将数据库集群转换为 Aurora 全球数据库。根据公司客户所在的位置，在 AWS 区域中添加额外的 Aurora 副本。","D":"重构 Lambda 函数。将初始化数据库连接的代码块移至函数处理程序中。","E":"使用 Amazon RDS Proxy 为 Aurora 数据库创建代理。更新 Lambda 函数以使用代理端点进行数据库连 接。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario has two explicit symptoms plus an implicit need for broad scalability. (1) 'Request latency during the initial burst of requests' is a cold-start problem. Provisioned concurrency (B) allocates pre-initialized execution environments that are 'ready to respond immediately... reducing cold start latencies,' and AWS notes interactive web/mobile workloads benefit most because they are the most latency-sensitive. (2) 'A large portion of the invocation time is used to establish database connections' is a connection-management problem. Amazon RDS Proxy (E) pools and reuses connections, which 'significantly reduces connection latency by reusing existing connections' and absorbs the high open/close rate that otherwise exhausts Aurora's memory and CPU during a surge. (3) The remaining scalability lever is the database tier: converting to an Aurora global database with cross-Region Aurora Replicas (C) adds read capacity and brings reads closer to geographically distributed customers for a large-scale sales event. C is the weakest-fitting of the three (its core purpose is DR and cross-Region reads, not connection latency), but it is correct by elimination because the other two unselected options are definitively wrong. Reserved concurrency (A) only sets a min/max cap on concurrent instances; it does not pre-warm environments, so it cannot reduce burst cold-start latency, and capacity was already proven adequate. Moving connection initialization INTO the handler (D) is the inverse of the AWS best practice, which states to initialize database connections OUTSIDE the handler so subsequent invocations on the same environment reuse them; D would force a new connection on every invocation and worsen the exact latency described.","explanation_zh":"情境有兩個明確症狀,外加一個對廣泛擴展性的隱含需求。(1)『初始請求爆量時的延遲』是冷啟動問題。Provisioned concurrency(B)會配置預先初始化的執行環境,使其『能立即回應...降低冷啟動延遲』,且 AWS 指出互動式 web/mobile 工作負載受益最大,因為它們對延遲最敏感。(2)『大量呼叫時間用於建立資料庫連線』是連線管理問題。Amazon RDS Proxy(E)會建立連線池並重複使用連線,『藉由重複使用既有連線顯著降低連線延遲』,並能吸收高頻開關連線的負載——否則這會在突增時耗盡 Aurora 的記憶體與 CPU。(3)剩下的擴展性槓桿是資料庫層:轉換為 Aurora global database 並加入跨 Region 的 Aurora Replicas(C),可增加讀取容量,並讓讀取更貼近地理分散的客戶,以因應大型促銷活動。C 是三者中契合度最弱者(其核心用途是 DR 與跨 Region 讀取,而非連線延遲),但因另外兩個未選選項明確錯誤,C 經刪去法判定為正確。Reserved concurrency(A)僅設定並行實例的上下限,並不會預熱環境,因此無法降低爆量冷啟動延遲,且容量已證實足夠。將連線初始化移入 handler(D)與 AWS 最佳實務相反——最佳實務是在 handler 之外初始化資料庫連線,以便同一環境的後續呼叫重複使用;D 會強迫每次呼叫都建立新連線,使所述延遲更糟。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Reserved concurrency sets both the maximum and minimum number of concurrent instances (a reservation/cap); it does not pre-initialize execution environments, so it does not reduce the cold-start latency seen during the initial burst. The DevOps engineer already confirmed the functions can fulfill the peak number of requests, so raw capacity is not the bottleneck.","why_zh":"Reserved concurrency 設定並行實例的最大與最小數量(保留/上限),並不會預先初始化執行環境,因此無法降低初始爆量時的冷啟動延遲。工程師已確認函式能滿足尖峰請求數,原始容量並非瓶頸。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the inverse of AWS best practice. The Lambda best-practices doc says to initialize database connections OUTSIDE the handler so subsequent invocations on the same execution environment reuse them. Moving connection setup INTO the handler forces a brand-new connection on every invocation, worsening the exact connection-establishment latency described.","why_zh":"這與 AWS 最佳實務相反。Lambda 最佳實務文件指出應在 handler 之外初始化資料庫連線,以便同一執行環境的後續呼叫重複使用。將連線建立移入 handler 會強迫每次呼叫都建立全新連線,加劇所述的連線建立延遲問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/provisioned-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/lambda-concurrency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/rds-proxy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/amazon-rds-proxy/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.AuroraGlobalDatabase.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":202,"question_en":"A company runs a web application that extends across multiple Availability Zones. The company uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) for routing, AWS Fargate for the application, and Amazon Aurora for the application data. The company uses AWS CloudFormation templates to deploy the application. The company stores all Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository in the same AWS account and AWS Region. A DevOps engineer needs to establish a disaster recovery (DR) process in another Region. The solution must meet an RPO of 8 hours and an RTO of 2 hours. The company sometimes needs more than 2 hours to build the Docker images from the Dockerfile. Which solution will meet the RTO and RPO requirements MOST cost-effectively?","question_zh":"该公司运行一个跨多个可用区的网络应用程序。该公司使用应用负载均衡器（ALB）进行路由，使用 AWS Fargate 运行应用程序，并使用 Amazon Aurora 存储应用程序数据。该公司使用 AWS CloudFormation 模板 部署应用程序。该公司将所有 Docker 镜像存储在同一个 AWS 账户和 AWS 区域内的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储库中。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要在另一个区域建立灾难恢复（DR）流程。该解决方案必须满足 8 小时的恢复点目 标（RPO）和 2 小时的恢复时间目标（RTO）。有时，该公司从 Dockerfile 构建 Docker 镜像需要超过 2 小 时。 哪种解决方案能以最经济的方式满足恢复时间目标（RTO）和恢复点目标（RPO）的要求？","options_en":{"A":"Copy the CloudFormation templates and the Dockerfile to an Amazon S3 bucket in the DR Region. Use AWS Backup to configure automated Aurora cross-Region hourly snapshots. In case of DR, build the most recent Docker image and upload the Docker image to an ECR repository in the DR Region. Use the CloudFormation template that has the most recent Aurora snapshot and the Docker image from the ECR repository to launch a new CloudFormation stack in the DR Region. Update the application DNS records to point to the new ALB.","B":"Copy the CloudFormation templates to an Amazon S3 bucket in the DR Region. Configure Aurora automated backup Cross-Region Replication. Configure ECR Cross-Region Replication. In case of DR, use the CloudFormation template with the most recent Aurora snapshot and the Docker image from the local ECR repository to launch a new CloudFormation stack in the DR Region. Update the application DNS records to point to the new ALB.","C":"Copy the CloudFormation templates to an Amazon S3 bucket in the DR Region. Use Amazon EventBridge to schedule an AWS Lambda function to take an hourly snapshot of the Aurora database and of the most recent Docker image in the ECR repository. Copy the snapshot and the Docker image to the DR Region. In case of DR, use the CloudFormation template with the most recent Aurora snapshot and the Docker image from the local ECR repository to launch a new CloudFormation stack in the DR Region.","D":"Copy the CloudFormation templates to an Amazon S3 bucket in the DR Region. Deploy a second application CloudFormation stack in the DR Region. Reconfigure Aurora to be a global database. Update both CloudFormation stacks when a new application release in the current Region is needed. In case of DR, update the application DNS records to point to the new ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CloudFormation 模板和 Dockerfile 复制到灾难恢复（DR）区域的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 AWS Backup 配置 Aurora 跨区域每小时自动快照。在发生灾难恢复时，构建最新的 Docker 镜像，并将其上 传到 DR 区域的 ECR 仓库。使用包含最新 Aurora 快照和来自 ECR 仓库的 Docker 镜像的 CloudFormation 模板，在 DR 区域启动新的 CloudFormation 堆栈。更新应用程序的 DNS 记录，使其指 向新的 ALB。","B":"将 CloudFormation 模板复制到灾难恢复区域的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。配置 Aurora 自动备份跨区域复制。 配置 ECR 跨区域复制。在发生灾难恢复时，使用包含最新 Aurora 快照和本地 ECR 存储库中的 Docker 镜像的 CloudFormation 模板在灾难恢复区域启动新的 CloudFormation 堆栈。更新应用程序的 DNS 记录 以指向新的 ALB。","C":"将 CloudFormation 模板复制到灾难恢复（DR）区域的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon EventBridge 安排 AWS Lambda 函数每小时对 Aurora 数据库和 ECR 存储库中的最新 Docker 镜像进行快照。将快照 和 Docker 镜像复制到 DR 区域。在发生灾难恢复时，使用包含最新 Aurora 快照和本地 ECR 存储库中 的 Docker 镜像的 CloudFormation 模板在 DR 区域启动新的 CloudFormation 堆栈。","D":"将 CloudFormation 模板复制到灾难恢复区域的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。在灾难恢复区域部署第二个应用 程序 CloudFormation 堆栈。将 Aurora 重新配置为全局数据库。当当前区域需要新的应用程序版本时， 更新两个 CloudFormation 堆栈。在发生灾难恢复时，更新应用程序的 DNS 记录以指向新的应用负载 均衡器（ALB）。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Database","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The deciding constraints are the 2-hour RTO combined with the fact that Docker image builds sometimes exceed 2 hours, plus the 'MOST cost-effective' qualifier. Because a build can take longer than the entire RTO, the solution must pre-stage already-built images in the DR Region rather than build at failover time. Option B uses Amazon ECR private registry cross-Region replication, which automatically replicates each pushed image to the DR Region (so the image is already present at DR time and no build is needed), and continuously replicated Aurora cross-Region backups, which easily satisfy the 8-hour RPO. At DR the CloudFormation stack is launched from the most recent replicated Aurora snapshot and the pre-replicated image in the DR-Region ECR repository. Both replication mechanisms are native, managed, and pay-as-you-go, requiring no idle standby compute, making B the cheapest design that still meets the 2-hour RTO. By elimination, A builds the image at DR time and can blow the RTO, C reinvents native replication with custom EventBridge/Lambda code, and D runs a full standby stack plus an Aurora global database, which is by far the most expensive and over-engineered for an 8h/2h objective. (Note: 'Aurora automated backup cross-Region replication' is loosely worded—the native automated-backup replication feature is RDS-DB-instance-only and is not supported for Aurora DB clusters—but the intent is continuously copied Aurora backups, achievable via cross-Region snapshot copy or AWS Backup, so B remains the correct and most cost-effective choice.)","explanation_zh":"決定性條件是 2 小時的 RTO，加上 Docker image 建置有時會超過 2 小時，以及「MOST cost-effective」的限定詞。由於單次建置可能比整個 RTO 還長，解決方案必須在 DR Region 預先備妥已建置好的 image，而不能在故障切換時才建置。選項 B 使用 Amazon ECR private registry 跨 Region replication，會在每次推送時自動把 image 複製到 DR Region（DR 時 image 已存在、無需建置）；並以持續複製的 Aurora 跨 Region 備份輕鬆達成 8 小時 RPO。DR 發生時，CloudFormation stack 直接以最新的已複製 Aurora snapshot 及 DR Region ECR repository 中已複製好的 image 啟動。兩種 replication 機制皆為原生、受管、依用量計費，且不需閒置的 standby 運算資源，因此 B 是仍能符合 2 小時 RTO 的最低成本設計。以排除法：A 在 DR 時才建置 image，可能超出 RTO；C 用自建 EventBridge/Lambda 重造原生 replication；D 持續運行整套 standby stack 加上 Aurora global database，對 8h／2h 目標而言是最昂貴且過度設計。（註：「Aurora automated backup cross-Region replication」用詞並不精確—原生的 automated-backup replication 功能僅限 RDS DB instance、不支援 Aurora DB cluster—但其意圖是持續複製的 Aurora 備份，可透過 cross-Region snapshot copy 或 AWS Backup 達成，因此 B 仍是正確且最具成本效益的選項。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"It copies the Dockerfile to S3 and builds the Docker image at DR time. Because builds sometimes take more than 2 hours, this can violate the 2-hour RTO, even though the AWS Backup hourly cross-Region Aurora snapshots would satisfy the 8-hour RPO.","why_zh":"它將 Dockerfile 複製到 S3 並在 DR 時才建置 Docker image。由於建置有時超過 2 小時，可能違反 2 小時 RTO；雖然其 AWS Backup 每小時跨 Region Aurora snapshot 可滿足 8 小時 RPO。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A custom EventBridge + Lambda pipeline to snapshot Aurora and copy Docker images reinvents native ECR cross-Region replication and Aurora snapshot copy, adding code, operational overhead, and cost, so it is not the most cost-effective option.","why_zh":"自建 EventBridge + Lambda 流程來對 Aurora 做 snapshot 並複製 Docker image，等於重造原生的 ECR 跨 Region replication 與 Aurora snapshot copy，增加程式碼、維運負擔與成本，並非最具成本效益的選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running a second full application stack continuously plus an Aurora global database (sub-second replication) is a warm/hot standby that is by far the most expensive and over-engineered for an 8h RPO / 2h RTO, contradicting the MOST cost-effective requirement.","why_zh":"持續運行第二套完整應用程式 stack 加上 Aurora global database（次秒級複製）屬於 warm/hot standby，對 8 小時 RPO／2 小時 RTO 而言是最昂貴且過度設計，違背最具成本效益的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/registry-settings-configure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-copy-snapshot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Managing.Backups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReplicateBackups.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":203,"question_en":"A company's application runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The application writes to a log file that records the username, date, time, and source IP address of the login. The log is published to a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The company is performing a root cause analysis for an event that occurred on the previous day. The company needs to know the number of logins for a specific user from the past 7 days. Which solution will provide this information?","question_zh":"一家公司的应用程序在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行。该应用程序会将用户名、日期、时间和登录源 IP 地址写 入日志文件。该日志会发布到亚马逊 CloudWatch Logs 中的一个日志组。 该公司正在对前一天发生的事件进行根本原因分析。公司需要了解特定用户在过去 7 天内的登录次数。 哪种解决方案能提供这些信息？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudWatch Logs metric filter on the log group. Use a filter pattern that matches the username. Publish a CloudWatch metric that sums the number of logins over the past 7 days.","B":"Create a CloudWatch Logs subscription on the log group. Use a filter pattern that matches the username. Publish a CloudWatch metric that sums the number of logins over the past 7 days.","C":"Create a CloudWatch Logs Insights query that uses an aggregation function to count the number of logins for the username over the past 7 days. Run the query against the log group.","D":"Create a CloudWatch dashboard. Add a number widget that has a filter pattern that counts the number of logins for the username over the past 7 days directly from the log group."},"options_zh":{"A":"在日志组上创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器。使用与用户名匹配的筛选模式。发布一个 CloudWatch 指标，该指标对过去 7 天内的登录次数进行求和。","B":"在日志组上创建 CloudWatch Logs 订阅。使用与用户名匹配的筛选模式。发布一个 CloudWatch 指标，该指标对过去 7 天内的登录次数进行求和。","C":"创建一个 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询，使用聚合函数来计算过去 7 天内该用户名的登录次数。针对 日志组运行该查询。","D":"创建一个 CloudWatch 控制面板。添加一个数字小部件，该小部件具有一个过滤模式，可直接从日志组中 计算过去 7 天内该用户名的登录次数。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The company must retroactively count logins for a specific user over the past 7 days of data that is ALREADY in the log group (the event happened the previous day). CloudWatch Logs Insights interactively searches and analyzes log data already ingested in a log group, lets you set an absolute/relative time range (e.g., the past 7 days), and supports aggregation functions via the stats command. A query such as 'filter username = \"...\" | stats count(*)' returns the exact retroactive count; this is the documented aggregation-function use case. By contrast, metric filters (A and B) are forward-looking only: AWS docs explicitly state 'Filters do not retroactively filter data. Filters only publish the metric data points for events that happen after the filter was created,' so a filter created today cannot count the previous 7 days. Option B also conflates a subscription filter (which streams matching events to a downstream destination such as Lambda, Kinesis, Firehose, or OpenSearch) with publishing a summing metric, which it does not do, and it likewise only processes new events. A dashboard number widget (D) is backed by CloudWatch metrics or Logs Insights query results, not by an arbitrary 'filter pattern that counts logins directly from the log group,' so that construct is not a valid native feature.","explanation_zh":"公司需要回溯統計過去 7 天內某特定使用者的登入次數，而這些資料已經存在於 log group 中（事件發生在前一天）。CloudWatch Logs Insights 可互動式搜尋並分析已攝取進 log group 的歷史日誌，可設定絕對／相對時間範圍（例如過去 7 天），並透過 stats 指令支援聚合函數。使用類似 'filter username = \"...\" | stats count(*)' 的查詢即可回溯得到精確計數，這正是聚合函數查詢的官方使用情境。相對地，metric filter（選項 A 和 B）只能向前生效：AWS 官方文件明確指出「Filters do not retroactively filter data. Filters only publish the metric data points for events that happen after the filter was created.」因此今天才建立的 filter 無法統計過去 7 天的登入。選項 B 還把 subscription filter（將符合的事件串流到下游目的地，如 Lambda、Kinesis、Firehose 或 OpenSearch）與發布加總 metric 混為一談，實際上它並不會發布這類 metric，且同樣只處理新事件。Dashboard 的 number widget（D）背後是 CloudWatch metric 或 Logs Insights 查詢結果，並非任意「直接用 filter pattern 從 log group 計算登入次數」，因此該描述並非有效的原生功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Metric filters do not retroactively process existing log data. AWS docs state filters only publish metric data points for events that occur AFTER the filter is created, so a filter made today cannot count the previous 7 days of logins needed for the root cause analysis.","why_zh":"Metric filter 不會回溯處理既有的日誌資料。AWS 文件指出 filter 只會為建立之後發生的事件發布 metric 資料點，因此今天建立的 filter 無法統計根因分析所需的過去 7 天登入。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A subscription filter streams matching events to a downstream destination (Lambda/Kinesis/Firehose/OpenSearch); it does not itself publish a summing CloudWatch metric, and like metric filters it only acts on new events, not the historical 7 days already in the log group.","why_zh":"Subscription filter 是把符合的事件串流到下游目的地（Lambda/Kinesis/Firehose/OpenSearch），本身不會發布加總的 CloudWatch metric，且與 metric filter 一樣只處理新事件，無法處理 log group 中已存在的過去 7 天歷史資料。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A dashboard number widget cannot 'count logins with a filter pattern directly from the log group.' Dashboard widgets display CloudWatch metrics or Logs Insights query results, not arbitrary filter-pattern counts run directly against a log group, so the described capability is not a real native feature.","why_zh":"Dashboard 的 number widget 無法「用 filter pattern 直接從 log group 計算登入次數」。Dashboard widget 顯示的是 CloudWatch metric 或 Logs Insights 查詢結果，而非直接對 log group 執行任意 filter-pattern 計數，因此所述能力並非真正的原生功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_AnalyzeLogData_AggregationQuery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_QuerySyntax-Stats.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":204,"question_en":"A company has an AWS CodeDeploy application. The application has a deployment group that uses a single tag group to identify instances for the deployment of ApplicationA. The single tag group configuration identifies instances that have Environment=Production and Name=ApplicationA tags for the deployment of ApplicationA. The company launches an additional Amazon EC2 instance with Department=Marketing, Environment=Production, and Name=ApplicationB tags. On the next CodeDeploy deployment of Application, the additional instance has ApplicationA installed on it. A DevOps engineer needs to configure the existing deployment group to prevent ApplicationA from being installed on the additional instance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序。该应用程序有一个部署组，使用单个标签组来识别用于部 署 ApplicationA 的实例。单个标签组配置识别具有 Environment=Production 和 Name=ApplicationA 标签的 实例，以便部署 ApplicationA。 该公司启动了一个额外的 Amazon EC2 实例，其标签为 Department=Marketing、Environment=Production 和 Name=ApplicationB。在对 Application 进行下一次 CodeDeploy 部署时，该额外实例上安装了 ApplicationA。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要配置现有的部署组，以防止 ApplicationA 安装在该额外实例上。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Change the current single tag group to include only the Environment=Production tag. Add another single tag group that includes only the Name=ApplicationA tag.","B":"Change the current single tag group to include the Department=Marketing, Environment=production, and Name=ApplicationA tags.","C":"Add another single tag group that includes only the Department=Marketing tag. Keep the Environment=Production and Name=ApplicationA tags with the current single tag group.","D":"Change the current single tag group to include only the Environment=Production tag. Add another single tag group that includes only the Department=Marketing tag."},"options_zh":{"A":"将当前的单个标签组更改为仅包含“Environment=Production”标签。再添加一个仅包含“Name= ApplicationA”标签的单个标签组。","B":"将当前的单个标签组更改为包含“部门=市场部”、“环境=生产”和“名称=应用程序 A”这些标签。","C":"再添加一个仅包含“Department=Marketing”标签的单个标签组。将“Environment= Production”和“Name=ApplicationA”标签保留在当前的单个标签组中。","D":"将当前的单个标签组更改为仅包含“环境=生产”标签。再添加一个仅包含“部门=市场”标签的单 个标签组。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeDeploy tag matching follows two documented rules: within a SINGLE tag group an instance is included if it matches AT LEAST ONE tag (OR logic), but across MULTIPLE tag groups an instance must match at least one tag in EACH group (AND logic). The current deployment group placed Environment=Production and Name=ApplicationA in ONE tag group, so OR logic applied: the new ApplicationB instance (which has Environment=Production) matched the Production tag by itself and incorrectly received ApplicationA. To require BOTH Environment=Production AND Name=ApplicationA, the two tags must be split into two separate tag groups. Option A does exactly this: tag group 1 = Environment=Production, tag group 2 = Name=ApplicationA, producing AND logic. The ApplicationB instance has Name=ApplicationB (not ApplicationA), so it fails the second group and is correctly excluded, while genuine ApplicationA instances (which carry both tags) still match both groups and continue to receive the deployment.","explanation_zh":"CodeDeploy 的標籤比對遵循兩條官方規則：在「單一」標籤群組內，實例只要符合「至少一個」標籤即被納入（OR 邏輯）；而跨「多個」標籤群組時，實例必須在「每一個」群組中都符合至少一個標籤才被納入（AND 邏輯）。目前的 deployment group 把 Environment=Production 與 Name=ApplicationA 放在「同一個」標籤群組，因此套用 OR 邏輯：新的 ApplicationB 實例（具有 Environment=Production）只憑 Production 標籤就符合條件，導致 ApplicationA 被誤裝。要同時要求 Environment=Production「且」Name=ApplicationA，必須把兩個標籤拆到兩個不同的標籤群組。選項 A 正是如此：標籤群組 1 = Environment=Production、標籤群組 2 = Name=ApplicationA，形成 AND 邏輯。ApplicationB 實例的 Name=ApplicationB（非 ApplicationA），無法通過第二個群組而被正確排除；真正的 ApplicationA 實例（兩個標籤都有）仍可同時符合兩個群組，繼續收到部署。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"This keeps a single tag group (OR logic) and adds Department=Marketing and Environment=production alongside Name=ApplicationA. The new ApplicationB instance has both Marketing and Production tags, so it still matches via OR and ApplicationA is still installed on it. This makes the problem worse, not better.","why_zh":"這仍是單一標籤群組（OR 邏輯），又在 Name=ApplicationA 旁加入 Department=Marketing 與 Environment=production。新的 ApplicationB 實例同時有 Marketing 與 Production 標籤，仍會透過 OR 比對命中，ApplicationA 依舊會被安裝，反而讓問題更嚴重。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Keeping Environment=Production + Name=ApplicationA together in one group (OR) and adding a second group of Department=Marketing creates AND logic that now requires Department=Marketing. Legitimate ApplicationA instances do not have a Marketing tag, so they would be wrongly excluded; meanwhile the ApplicationB instance (which DOES have Marketing and Production) could still match group 1 via Production and group 2 via Marketing, so it would still receive ApplicationA.","why_zh":"把 Environment=Production 與 Name=ApplicationA 留在同一群組（OR），再加上第二個 Department=Marketing 群組，形成要求 Department=Marketing 的 AND 邏輯。正常的 ApplicationA 實例沒有 Marketing 標籤，會被錯誤排除；而 ApplicationB 實例（確實有 Marketing 與 Production）仍可在群組 1 以 Production、群組 2 以 Marketing 命中，依舊會收到 ApplicationA。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Tag group 1 = Environment=Production and tag group 2 = Department=Marketing targets instances that have BOTH Production AND Marketing. That is precisely the unwanted ApplicationB instance, and it excludes the real ApplicationA instances (which have no Marketing tag). This is the exact opposite of the requirement.","why_zh":"標籤群組 1 = Environment=Production、群組 2 = Department=Marketing，會鎖定同時具有 Production 與 Marketing 的實例，正好就是不該部署的 ApplicationB 實例，並排除沒有 Marketing 標籤的真正 ApplicationA 實例，與需求完全相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/instances-tagging.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":205,"question_en":"A company is launching an application that stores raw data in an Amazon S3 bucket. Three applications need to access the data to generate reports. The data must be redacted differently for each application before the applications can access the data. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在推出一款应用程序，该程序将原始数据存储在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。有三个应用程序需要访 问这些数据以生成报告。在这些应用程序能够访问数据之前，必须针对每个应用程序对数据进行不同的脱 敏处理。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 bucket for each application. Configure S3 Same-Region Replication (SRR) from the raw data's S3 bucket to each application's S3 bucket. Configure each application to consume data from its own S3 bucket.","B":"Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by object creation events in the raw data’s S3 bucket. Program the Lambda function to redact data for each application. Publish the data on the Kinesis data stream. Configure each application to consume data from the Kinesis data stream.","C":"For each application, create an S3 access point that uses the raw data's S3 bucket as the destination. Create an AWS Lambda function that is invoked by object creation events in the raw data's S3 bucket. Program the Lambda function to redact data for each application. Store the data in each application's S3 access point. Configure each application to consume data from its own S3 access point.","D":"Create an S3 access point that uses the raw data’s S3 bucket as the destination. For each application, create an S3 Object Lambda access point that uses the S3 access point. Configure the AWS Lambda function for each S3 Object Lambda access point to redact data when objects are retrieved. Configure each application to consume data from its own S3 Object Lambda access point"},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个应用程序创建一个 S3 存储桶。将原始数据的 S3 存储桶配置为与每个应用程序的 S3 存储桶进行 同区域复制（SRR）。配置每个应用程序从其自身的 S3 存储桶中获取数据。","B":"创建一个 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。创建一个由原始数据 S3 存储桶中的对象创建事件触发的 AWS Lambda 函数。编写 Lambda 函数以针对每个应用程序对数据进行脱敏处理。将数据发布到 Kinesis 数 据流。配置每个应用程序从 Kinesis 数据流中获取数据。","C":"对于每个应用程序，创建一个使用原始数据的 S3 存储桶作为目标的 S3 访问点。创建一个由原始数据的 S3 存储桶中的对象创建事件触发的 AWS Lambda 函数。编写 Lambda 函数以对每个应用程序的数据进 行脱敏处理。将数据存储在每个应用程序的 S3 访问点中。配置每个应用程序从其自身的 S3 访问点获 取数据。","D":"创建一个使用原始数据 S3 存储桶作为目标的 S3 访问点。为每个应用程序创建一个使用该 S3 访问点的 S3 对象 Lambda 访问点。为每个 S3 对象 Lambda 访问点配置 AWS Lambda 函数，以便在检索对象时对 数据进行脱敏处理。配置每个应用程序从其自身的 S3 对象 Lambda 访问点获取数据。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"S3 Object Lambda Access Points are purpose-built for this exact scenario: they let you add custom code to S3 GET/LIST/HEAD requests to modify and process data as it is returned to an application, explicitly including redacting confidential or PII data, with no need to create derivative copies of the data and no application changes. An Object Lambda Access Point is associated with exactly one standard (supporting) access point on the raw data bucket, and you can create multiple Object Lambda Access Points over that same supporting access point, each attached to its own Lambda function. By creating one supporting S3 access point on the raw data bucket and then one S3 Object Lambda Access Point per application, each backed by a Lambda that redacts differently when objects are retrieved, every application reads only its own redacted view of the same underlying raw data. AWS publishes a dedicated tutorial ('Detecting and redacting PII data with S3 Object Lambda and Amazon Comprehend') describing precisely this shared-dataset use case, where for example a marketing app masks PII while an analytics app redacts credit card data. Option D maps directly to this documented architecture, while the other options store redundant copies, misuse plain access points, or insert an unnecessary streaming service.","explanation_zh":"S3 Object Lambda Access Point 正是為此情境設計：它讓你在 S3 GET/LIST/HEAD 請求中加入自訂程式碼，於資料回傳給應用程式時即時修改與處理，明確包含遮蔽機密或 PII 資料，且無需建立衍生副本、不需修改應用程式。每個 Object Lambda Access Point 關聯到原始資料 bucket 上的一個標準（supporting）access point，而同一個 supporting access point 上可以建立多個 Object Lambda Access Point，各自綁定不同的 Lambda function。因此在原始資料 bucket 上建立一個 supporting S3 access point，再為每個應用程式各建一個 S3 Object Lambda Access Point，各自由不同的 Lambda 在物件被讀取時做不同遮蔽，三個應用程式便各自只讀到屬於自己的遮蔽視圖。AWS 還發布了專門教學（'Detecting and redacting PII data with S3 Object Lambda and Amazon Comprehend'），正是描述這種共享資料集情境（例如行銷應用遮蔽 PII、分析應用遮蔽信用卡資料）。選項 D 直接對應此官方架構；其餘選項則會產生冗餘副本、誤用一般 access point，或插入不必要的串流服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 Same-Region Replication copies objects byte-for-byte without transformation, so the replicated buckets still contain the raw, un-redacted data; SRR cannot redact differently per application and creates three redundant full copies of the data, which is exactly what Object Lambda avoids.","why_zh":"S3 Same-Region Replication 只是逐位元組複製物件而不做轉換，複製出的 bucket 仍是未遮蔽的原始資料；SRR 無法針對各應用程式做不同遮蔽，且會產生三份冗餘的完整副本，而這正是 Object Lambda 所要避免的。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams is a real-time streaming primitive, not a per-consumer redaction layer for at-rest S3 objects. This pipeline is over-engineered, forces a streaming consumption model the reporting apps do not need, and a single Lambda publishing to one stream cannot cleanly give each of the three applications its own differently-redacted dataset.","why_zh":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 是即時串流元件，並非為 S3 靜態物件做每個消費端遮蔽的機制。此管線過度設計，強迫報表應用採用不必要的串流消費模式，且單一 Lambda 寫入單一 stream 無法清楚地讓三個應用程式各自取得不同遮蔽的資料集。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A standard S3 access point is only a named network/IAM endpoint that points back to the same underlying bucket; you cannot 'store data in an access point.' It performs no transformation, so this design both misunderstands access points and would still require writing redacted derivative copies somewhere, defeating the on-read redaction goal.","why_zh":"標準 S3 access point 只是一個指回同一底層 bucket 的具名網路/IAM 端點；你無法『把資料存進 access point』。它不做任何轉換，因此此設計既誤解了 access point，又仍須將遮蔽後的衍生副本寫到別處，違背了讀取時即時遮蔽的目標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/transforming-objects.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/olap-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/tutorial-s3-object-lambda-redact-pii.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/olap-writing-lambda.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":206,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Control Tower and AWS CloudFormation to manage its AWS accounts and to create AWS resources. The company requires all Amazon S3 buckets to be encrypted with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) when the S3 buckets are created in a CloudFormation stack. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS 控制塔和 AWS CloudFormation 来管理其 AWS 账户并创建 AWS 资源。该公司要求在 CloudFormation 堆栈中创建的所有 Amazon S3 存储桶都使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）进行加 密。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Organizations. Attach an SCP that denies the s3:PutObject permission if the request does not include an x-amz-server-side-encryption header that requests server-side encryption with AWS KMS keys (SSE-KMS).","B":"Use AWS Control Tower with a multi-account environment. Configure and enable proactive AWS Control Tower controls on all OUs with CloudFormation hooks.","C":"Use AWS Control Tower with a multi-account environment. Configure and enable detective AWS Control Tower controls on all OUs with CloudFormation hooks.","D":"Use AWS Organizations. Create an AWS Config organizational rule to check whether a KMS encryption key is enabled for all S3 buckets. Deploy the rule. Create and apply an SCP to prevent users from stopping and deleting AWS Config across all AWS accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS 组织。附加一个服务控制策略（SCP），如果请求中不包含要求使用 AWS KMS 密钥进行服 务器端加密（SSE-KMS）的 x-amz-server-side-encryption 标头，则拒绝 s3:PutObject 权限。","B":"在多账户环境中使用 AWS 控制塔。通过 CloudFormation 挂钩在所有组织单元上配置并启用 AWS 控制塔的主动控制措施。","C":"在多账户环境中使用 AWS 控制塔。通过 CloudFormation 钩子在所有组织单元上配置并启用 AWS 控制塔的检测控制。","D":"使用 AWS 组织。创建一个 AWS Config 组织规则，检查所有 S3 存储桶是否启用了 KMS 加密密钥。 部署该规则。创建并应用一个服务控制策略（SCP），以防止用户在所有 AWS 账户中停止和删除 AWS Config。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to enforce KMS (SSE-KMS) encryption on S3 buckets at the moment they are created in a CloudFormation stack. AWS Control Tower proactive controls are purpose-built for this: AWS docs state they are implemented with CloudFormation hooks as preCreate and preUpdate hook handlers and check resources before they deploy, blocking non-compliant resources from being created via CloudFormation stack operations. Control Tower even ships the exact control for this scenario, [CT.S3.PR.10] 'Require an Amazon S3 bucket to have server-side encryption configured using an AWS KMS key.' Enabling proactive controls on the OUs is therefore the correct mechanism to prevent CloudFormation from provisioning a non-KMS-encrypted bucket. Option B matches both the 'proactive' nature (prevent before deployment) and the 'CloudFormation hooks' implementation detail exactly.","explanation_zh":"需求是在 CloudFormation 堆疊建立 S3 儲存貯體的當下，強制使用 KMS (SSE-KMS) 加密。AWS Control Tower 的 proactive controls 正是為此設計：AWS 文件指出它們以 CloudFormation hooks（preCreate 與 preUpdate hook handlers）實作，會在資源透過 CloudFormation 堆疊操作部署前進行檢查，阻止不合規的資源被建立。Control Tower 甚至提供針對此情境的專屬控制 [CT.S3.PR.10]「Require an Amazon S3 bucket to have server-side encryption configured using an AWS KMS key」。因此在 OU 上啟用 proactive controls 即可在 CloudFormation 佈建未使用 KMS 加密的貯體前加以阻擋。選項 B 同時符合「proactive（部署前預防）」特性以及「CloudFormation hooks」的實作方式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An SCP denying s3:PutObject without an SSE-KMS header governs object uploads into a bucket, not the creation or default-encryption configuration of the bucket itself, and does nothing to enforce encryption when a bucket is created in a CloudFormation stack.","why_zh":"拒絕未帶 SSE-KMS 標頭的 s3:PutObject 的 SCP 管控的是物件上傳行為，而非貯體本身的建立或預設加密設定，無法在 CloudFormation 堆疊建立貯體時強制加密。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Detective controls are implemented using AWS Config rules, not CloudFormation hooks, so the description is technically inconsistent. They only detect non-compliance and report status after resources exist; they cannot prevent a non-KMS bucket from being created.","why_zh":"Detective controls 是以 AWS Config 規則實作，而非 CloudFormation hooks，因此描述在技術上自相矛盾。它們只能在資源建立後偵測不合規並回報狀態，無法阻止未使用 KMS 加密的貯體被建立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An AWS Config organizational rule is detective only; it reports unencrypted buckets after the fact but does not stop CloudFormation from creating a bucket without KMS encryption. The accompanying SCP merely prevents Config from being disabled and does not enforce encryption.","why_zh":"AWS Config 組織規則僅為偵測性質，事後回報未加密貯體，但無法阻止 CloudFormation 建立未使用 KMS 加密的貯體；隨附的 SCP 只是防止 Config 被停用，並不能強制加密。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/proactive-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudformation-cli/latest/hooks-userguide/proactive-controls-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/s3-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/detective-controls.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":207,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer has developed an AWS Lambda function. The Lambda function starts an AWS CloudFormation drift detection operation on all supported resources for a specific CloudFormation stack. The Lambda function then exits its invocation. The DevOps engineer has created an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule that invokes the Lambda function every hour. An Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic already exists in the AWS account. The DevOps engineer has subscribed to the SNS topic to receive notifications. The DevOps engineer needs to receive a notification as soon as possible when drift is detected in this specific stack configuration. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师开发了一个 AWS Lambda 函数。该 Lambda 函数针对特定的 CloudFormation 堆栈对所 有受支持的资源启动 AWS CloudFormation 漂移检测操作，然后退出其调用。 DevOps 工程师创建了一个 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则，该规则每小时调用一次 Lambda 函数。AWS 账户中已存在一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。DevOps 工程师已订阅该 SNS 主题以接收通知。 当检测到此特定堆栈配置出现偏差时，DevOps 工程师需要尽快收到通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the existing EventBridge rule to also target the SNS topic. Configure an SNS subscription filter policy to match the CloudFormation stack. Attach the subscription filter policy to the SNS topic.","B":"Create a second Lambda function to query the CloudFormation API for the drift detection results for the stack. Configure the second Lambda function to publish a message to the SNS topic if drift is detected. Adjust the existing EventBridge rule to also target the second Lambda function.","C":"Configure Amazon GuardDuty in the account with drift detection for all CloudFormation stacks. Create a second EventBridge rule that reacts to the GuardDuty drift detection event finding for the specific CloudFormation stack. Configure the SNS topic as a target of the second EventBridge rule.","D":"Configure AWS Config in the account. Use the cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check managed rule. Create a second EventBridge rule that reacts to a compliance change event for the CloudFormation stack. Configure the SNS topic as a target of the second EventBridge rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"将现有的 EventBridge 规则配置为也指向 SNS 主题。配置一个 SNS 订阅过滤策略以匹配 CloudFormation 堆栈。将订阅过滤策略附加到 SNS 主题。","B":"创建第二个 Lambda 函数，用于查询 CloudFormation API 以获取堆栈的偏差检测结果。将第二个 Lambda 函数配置为在检测到偏差时向 SNS 主题发布消息。调整现有的 EventBridge 规则，使其也指向第二个 Lambda 函数。","C":"在账户中为所有 CloudFormation 堆栈配置带有漂移检测功能的 Amazon GuardDuty。创建第二个 EventBridge 规则，使其对特定 CloudFormation 堆栈的 GuardDuty 漂移检测事件做出反应。将 SNS 主 题配置为第二个 EventBridge 规则的目标。","D":"在账户中配置 AWS Config。使用 cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check 管理规则。创建第二个 EventBridge 规则，使其对 CloudFormation 堆栈的合规性变更事件做出反应。将 SNS 主题配置为第 二个 EventBridge 规则的目标。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS Config provides the managed rule cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check, which performs the DetectStackDrift operation on the stack and reports the stack as NON_COMPLIANT when the stack drift status is DRIFTED (and COMPLIANT when IN_SYNC). When the compliance state changes, AWS Config sends a 'Config Rules Compliance Change' event directly to the EventBridge default event bus (source: aws.config). A second EventBridge rule scoped to that specific config rule/stack can match this compliance-change event and target the existing SNS topic, producing a notification exactly when drift is detected. Option A is wrong because the existing rule is the hourly SCHEDULED rule whose event payload carries no drift status, so an SNS subscription filter policy cannot distinguish 'drift detected' and would fire every hour unconditionally. Option B re-runs a second Lambda on the SAME hourly schedule, but DetectStackDrift is asynchronous and can take several minutes, so querying immediately creates a race condition with stale or still-in-progress (DETECTION_IN_PROGRESS) results. Option C is fabricated: Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service and has no CloudFormation drift-detection findings. (AWS does offer a native 'CloudFormation Drift Detection Status Change' EventBridge event that would be ideal, but no option uses it; among the choices given, only D works.)","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 提供受管規則 cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check，它會對 stack 執行 DetectStackDrift 操作，當 stack drift status 為 DRIFTED 時將其判定為 NON_COMPLIANT（為 IN_SYNC 時則為 COMPLIANT）。當合規狀態變更時，AWS Config 會直接向 EventBridge 預設 event bus 發送 'Config Rules Compliance Change' 事件（source 為 aws.config）。可建立第二條針對該特定 config 規則/stack 的 EventBridge rule 來比對此合規變更事件，並以既有的 SNS topic 為 target，在偵測到 drift 時立即發出通知。選項 A 錯誤，因為既有規則是每小時觸發的 SCHEDULED rule，其事件 payload 不含 drift 狀態，SNS subscription filter policy 無法分辨「是否偵測到 drift」，且會無條件每小時觸發。選項 B 在相同的每小時排程上再執行第二個 Lambda，但 DetectStackDrift 是非同步且可能耗時數分鐘，立即查詢會造成競態條件，得到過時或仍在進行中（DETECTION_IN_PROGRESS）的結果。選項 C 為杜撰：Amazon GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務，並無 CloudFormation drift detection 的 findings。（AWS 其實有原生的 'CloudFormation Drift Detection Status Change' EventBridge 事件最為理想，但無選項採用；在給定選項中只有 D 可行。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The existing rule is the hourly scheduled rule; its scheduled-event payload contains no drift status. An SNS subscription filter policy matches on message attributes and cannot determine whether drift was actually detected, so this would notify every hour regardless of drift state.","why_zh":"既有規則是每小時排程規則，其排程事件 payload 不含 drift 狀態。SNS subscription filter policy 依訊息屬性比對，無法判斷是否真的偵測到 drift，因此不論飄移與否都會每小時通知。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The second Lambda is triggered on the same hourly schedule as the first, but DetectStackDrift is asynchronous and can take several minutes. Querying the results immediately on the same schedule creates a race condition, returning stale or still-in-progress (DETECTION_IN_PROGRESS) results rather than reliably notifying as soon as drift is detected.","why_zh":"第二個 Lambda 與第一個共用同一每小時排程觸發，但 DetectStackDrift 為非同步且可能耗時數分鐘。在相同排程上立即查詢結果會造成競態條件，回傳過時或仍在進行中（DETECTION_IN_PROGRESS）的結果，無法可靠地在偵測到 drift 時立即通知。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service analyzing CloudTrail, VPC Flow, and DNS logs for malicious activity; it has no CloudFormation drift-detection capability or drift findings, so this configuration does not exist.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是分析 CloudTrail、VPC Flow 與 DNS 日誌以偵測惡意活動的威脅偵測服務，並無 CloudFormation drift detection 能力或 drift findings，此設定並不存在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/event-detail-stack-drift-detection-change.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-stack-drift.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/how-does-config-work.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":208,"question_en":"A company has deployed a complex container-based workload on AWS. The workload uses Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus for monitoring. The workload runs in an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster in an AWS account. The company’s DevOps team wants to receive workload alerts by using the company’s Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. The SNS topic is in the same AWS account as the EKS cluster. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 上部署了一个复杂的基于容器的工作负载。该工作负载使用 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 进行监控。工作负载在 Amazon 上运行。 AWS 账户中的弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群。 该公司的 DevOps 团队希望使用公司的亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题接收工作负载警报。该 SNS 主题与 EKS 集群位于同一个 AWS 账户中。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use the Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus remote write URL to send alerts to the SNS topic","B":"Create an alerting rule that checks the availability of each of the workload’s containers.","C":"Create an alert manager configuration for the SNS topic.","D":"Modify the access policy of the SNS topic. Grant the aps.amazonaws.com service principal the sns:Publish permission and the sns:GetTopicAttributes permission for the SNS topic.","E":"Modify the IAM role that Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus uses. Grant the role the sns:Publish permission and the sns:GetTopicAttributes permission for the SNS topic.","F":"Create an OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider for the EKS cluster. Create a cluster service account. Grant the account the sns:Publish permission and the sns:GetTopicAttributes permission by using an IAM role."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 的远程写入 URL 将警报发送到 SNS 主题","B":"创建一个警报规则，用于检查工作负载中每个容器的可用性。","C":"为 SNS 主题创建警报管理器配置。","D":"修改 SNS 主题的访问策略。授予 aps.amazonaws.com 服务主体 SNS 主题的 sns:Publish 权限和 sns: GetTopicAttributes 权限。","E":"修改 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 使用的 IAM 角色。为该角色授予 SNS 主题的 sns: Publish 权限和 sns:GetTopicAttributes 权限。","F":"为 EKS 集群创建一个 OpenID Connect （OIDC） 提供程序。创建一个集群服务账户。通过使用 IAM 角 色授予该账户 sns:Publish 权限和 sns:GetTopicAttributes 权限。"},"answer":["B","C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Sending workload alerts from Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP) to an SNS topic requires three pieces. First, you create an alerting rule in a rules file that evaluates metrics and fires an alert when a condition is met, such as a workload container becoming unavailable (B). Second, AMP's alert manager handles fired alerts and routes them to a receiver; AMP supports only Amazon SNS as a receiver and routes to SNS topics in the same account, so you must create an alert manager configuration that points at the SNS topic (C). Third, because AMP publishes to SNS using the aps.amazonaws.com service principal (not a customer IAM role), you must modify the SNS topic's access (resource) policy to grant aps.amazonaws.com the sns:Publish and sns:GetTopicAttributes actions, ideally constrained with aws:SourceArn (the workspace ARN) and aws:SourceAccount to prevent the confused deputy problem (D). The AWS documentation shows this exact policy statement.","explanation_zh":"要將工作負載告警從 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus (AMP) 發送到 SNS topic，需要三個步驟。第一，在 rules file 中建立 alerting rule，評估指標並在條件成立時觸發告警（例如某個工作負載容器變得不可用）(B)。第二，AMP 的 alert manager 處理已觸發的告警並將其路由到 receiver；AMP 僅支援 Amazon SNS 作為 receiver，且只能路由到同一帳戶內的 SNS topic，因此必須建立指向該 SNS topic 的 alert manager configuration (C)。第三，由於 AMP 是使用 aps.amazonaws.com 這個 service principal（而非客戶的 IAM role）來發布訊息到 SNS，因此必須修改 SNS topic 的 access（資源）政策，授予 aps.amazonaws.com sns:Publish 與 sns:GetTopicAttributes 權限，並建議以 aws:SourceArn（workspace ARN）與 aws:SourceAccount 條件加以限制，以避免 confused deputy 問題 (D)。AWS 文件中明確列出此政策陳述式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The AMP remote write URL is the ingestion endpoint where Prometheus-compatible collectors push metrics INTO the workspace. It is not an alert delivery mechanism and cannot send alerts to an SNS topic; alerts flow out through alert manager to an SNS receiver.","why_zh":"AMP 的 remote write URL 是供 Prometheus 相容的收集器將指標推送到 workspace 的擷取端點，並非告警傳遞機制，無法將告警發送到 SNS topic；告警是經由 alert manager 路由到 SNS receiver。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"AMP does not publish to SNS by assuming a customer-managed IAM role with sns:Publish; it publishes using the aps.amazonaws.com service principal. Permission is therefore granted on the SNS topic's resource (access) policy to that service principal (option D), not by adding sns:Publish to an IAM role that AMP 'uses.'","why_zh":"AMP 並非透過擔任帶有 sns:Publish 的客戶管理 IAM role 來發布訊息到 SNS，而是使用 aps.amazonaws.com service principal 發布。因此權限是在 SNS topic 的資源（access）政策中授予該 service principal（選項 D），而不是把 sns:Publish 附加到 AMP 所『使用』的 IAM role。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"An OIDC provider plus IAM roles for service accounts (IRSA) grants AWS permissions to pods running inside the EKS cluster. But the alert publishing is performed by the AMP alert manager service itself via its service principal, not by an EKS pod or service account, so IRSA is irrelevant to AMP-to-SNS alert delivery.","why_zh":"OIDC provider 加上 IAM roles for service accounts (IRSA) 是用來把 AWS 權限授予在 EKS 叢集內執行的 pod。但告警發布是由 AMP 的 alert manager 服務本身透過其 service principal 執行，而非由 EKS pod 或 service account 執行，因此 IRSA 與 AMP 到 SNS 的告警傳遞無關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-alert-manager.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-alertmanager-receiver-AMPpermission.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-ruler-rulesfile.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-alertmanager-config.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":209,"question_en":"A company's organization in AWS Organizations has a single OU. The company runs Amazon EC2 instances in the OU accounts. The company needs to limit the use of each EC2 instance’s credentials to the specific EC2 instance that the credential is assigned to. A DevOps engineer must configure security for the EC2 instances. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中只有一个组织单元（OU）。该公司在该组织单元的账户中运行亚马逊 EC2 实例。 该公司需要限制每个 EC2 实例的凭证仅能用于分配该凭证的特定 EC2 实例。一位 DevOps 工程师必须为这 些 EC2 实例配置安全设置。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that specifies the VPC CIDR block. Configure the SCP to check whether the value of the aws:VpcSourcelp condition key is in the specified block. In the same SCP check, check whether the values of the aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivatelPv4 and aws:SourceVpc condition keys are the same. Deny access if either condition is false. Apply the SCP to the OU.","B":"Create an SCP that checks whether the values of the aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC and aws:SourceVpc condition keys are the same. Deny access if the values are not the same. In the same SCP check, check whether the values of the aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 and aws:VpcSourceIp condition keys are the same. Deny access if the values are not the same. Apply the SCP to the OU.","C":"Create an SCP that includes a list of acceptable VPC values and checks whether the value of the aws:SourceVpc condition key is in the list. In the same SCP check, define a list of acceptable IP address values and check whether the value of the aws:VpcSourceIp condition key is in the list. Deny access if either condition is false. Apply the SCP to each account in the organization.","D":"Create an SCP that checks whether the values of the aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC and aws:VpcSourceIp condition keys are the same. Deny access if the values are not the same. In the same SCP check, check whether the values of the aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 and aws:SourceVpc condition keys are the same. Deny access if the values are not the same. Apply the SCP to each account in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），指定 VPC 的 CIDR 块。将该 SCP 配置为检查 aws:VpcSourceIPv4 条 件键的值是否在指定的块内。在相同的 SCP 检查中，检查 aws:EC2InstanceSourceIPv4 和 aws: SourceVpc 条件键的值是否相同。如果任一条件为假，则拒绝访问。将该 SCP 应用于组织单位 （OU）。","B":"创建一个 SCP，检查 aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC 和 aws:SourceVpc 条件键的值是否相同。如果值不同， 则拒绝访问。在同一 SCP 检查中，检查 aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 和 aws:VpcSourceIp 条件键 的值是否相同。如果值不同，则拒绝访问。将该 SCP 应用于组织单位。","C":"创建一个 SCP，其中包含可接受的 VPC 值列表，并检查 aws:SourceVpc 条件键的值是否在该列表中。在 同一 SCP 检查中，定义可接受的 IP 地址值列表，并检查 aws:VpcSourceIp 条件键的值是否在该列表中。 如果任一条件为假，则拒绝访问。将该 SCP 应用于组织中的每个账户。","D":"创建一个 SCP，检查 `aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC`VpcSourceIp` 条件键的值是否相同。如果值不同，则 拒绝访问。在同一个 SCP 检查中，检查 `aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4` 和 `aws:SourceVpc` 条件 键的值是否相同。如果值不同，则拒绝访问。将该 SCP 应用于组织中的每个账户。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS provides two role-session condition keys that bind EC2 instance role credentials to the specific instance they were delivered to: aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc (the VPC the credentials were delivered to) and aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 (the private IPv4 of the primary ENI the credentials were delivered to). The canonical AWS SCP example denies access when aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc does NOT equal aws:SourceVpc, and in a second statement denies access when aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 does NOT equal aws:VpcSourceIp. The docs state aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 'must be used with its companion key aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc to ensure that you have a globally unique combination of VPC ID and source private IP' because private IPs are not globally unique. Option B uses exactly these two correct pairings (EC2InstanceSourceVPC<->SourceVpc and EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4<->VpcSourceIp) and applies the SCP to the OU that contains the accounts, matching the documented solution. Static CIDR/VPC list approaches (A, C) only restrict to a network range and do not bind a credential to its single originating instance, and D swaps the key pairings (comparing VPC to IP) so it is logically broken.","explanation_zh":"AWS 提供兩個專為將 EC2 執行個體角色憑證綁定到其發放對象執行個體而設計的 role-session condition key：aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc（憑證被發放到的 VPC）與 aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4（憑證被發放到的主要 ENI 的私有 IPv4）。AWS 官方文件的標準 SCP 範例會在 aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc 不等於 aws:SourceVpc 時拒絕存取，並在第二條 statement 中於 aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 不等於 aws:VpcSourceIp 時拒絕存取。文件明確指出 aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4「必須與其搭配鍵 aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc 一起使用，以確保 VPC ID 與來源私有 IP 的組合在全域唯一」，因為私有 IP 本身並非全域唯一。選項 B 正好使用這兩組正確配對（EC2InstanceSourceVPC<->SourceVpc 與 EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4<->VpcSourceIp），並將 SCP 套用到包含這些帳戶的 OU，與文件記載的解法相符。使用靜態 CIDR/VPC 清單的做法（A、C）只能限制到某個網路範圍，無法將憑證綁定到單一發放來源執行個體；而 D 將兩組鍵配對對調（拿 VPC 去比對 IP），邏輯上完全錯誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"It checks aws:VpcSourceIp against a static VPC CIDR block and pairs aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 with aws:SourceVpc (comparing an IP address to a VPC ID, which never matches). A static CIDR only limits credentials to a network range, not to the single instance they were delivered to, so it fails the requirement.","why_zh":"它拿 aws:VpcSourceIp 去比對靜態 VPC CIDR 區塊，並將 aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 與 aws:SourceVpc 配對（拿 IP 位址比 VPC ID，永遠不會相符）。靜態 CIDR 只能將憑證限制在某網路範圍，無法綁定到憑證實際發放的單一執行個體，不符合需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It compares aws:SourceVpc and aws:VpcSourceIp against static allow-lists of acceptable VPCs and IPs instead of comparing the credential-delivery keys (aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc / aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4) to the request source. This allows a credential to be used from any instance in the allowed list, so it does not bind a credential to its specific instance.","why_zh":"它拿 aws:SourceVpc 與 aws:VpcSourceIp 去比對可接受 VPC 與 IP 的靜態白名單，而非比對憑證發放鍵（aws:Ec2InstanceSourceVpc / aws:Ec2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4）與請求來源。如此憑證可被白名單內任一執行個體使用，無法綁定到特定執行個體。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It swaps the key pairings: it compares aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC to aws:VpcSourceIp and aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 to aws:SourceVpc. A VPC ID will never equal an IP address and an IP will never equal a VPC ID, so these conditions are logically broken. The documented solution pairs VPC-with-VPC and IP-with-IP, which is what B does.","why_zh":"它將鍵配對對調：拿 aws:EC2InstanceSourceVPC 比對 aws:VpcSourceIp，並拿 aws:EC2InstanceSourcePrivateIPv4 比對 aws:SourceVpc。VPC ID 永遠不會等於 IP 位址，IP 也永遠不會等於 VPC ID，因此這些條件在邏輯上是錯的。文件記載的解法是 VPC 配 VPC、IP 配 IP，正是 B 的做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/instance-metadata-security-credentials.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":210,"question_en":"A company has a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances that run Linux in a single AWS account. The company is using an AWS Systems Manager Automation task across the EC2 instances. During the most recent patch cycle, several EC2 instances went into an error state because of insufficient available disk space. A DevOps engineer needs to ensure that the EC2 instances have sufficient available disk space during the patching process in the future. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在单个 AWS 账户中拥有一组运行 Linux 的 Amazon EC2 实例。该公司正在这些 EC2 实例上使 用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 任务。 在最近的补丁更新周期中，由于可用磁盘空间不足，有几台 EC2 实例进入了错误状态。DevOps 工程师需 要确保在未来的补丁更新过程中，EC2 实例拥有足够的可用磁盘空间。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that the Amazon CloudWatch agent is installed on all EC2 instances.","B":"Create a cron job that is installed on each EC2 instance to periodically delete temporary files.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch log group for the EC2 instances. Configure a cron job that is installed on each EC2 instance to write the available disk space to a CloudWatch log stream for the relevant EC2 instance.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to monitor available disk space on all EC2 instances. Add the alarm as a safety control to the Systems Manager Automation task.","E":"Create an AWS Lambda function to periodically check for sufficient available disk space on all EC2 instances by evaluating each EC2 instance's respective Amazon CloudWatch log stream."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保在所有 EC2 实例上都安装了 Amazon CloudWatch 代理。","B":"在每个 EC2 实例上创建一个定期删除临时文件的 cron 任务。","C":"为 EC2 实例创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 日志组。在每个 EC2 实例上配置一个 cron 作业，将可用磁 盘空间写入相关 EC2 实例的 CloudWatch 日志流。","D":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控所有 EC2 实例的可用磁盘空间。将该警报作为安全控制添 加到 Systems Manager Automation 任务中。","E":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，定期检查所有 EC2 实例是否有足够的可用磁盘空间，方法是评估每 个 EC2 实例各自的 Amazon CloudWatch 日志流。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"EC2 instances do not emit OS-level filesystem free-space metrics by default; the default EC2 namespace exposes hypervisor-level metrics (CPU, network, basic EBS) and does not include disk available space inside the guest OS. To monitor available disk space you must install the CloudWatch agent, which collects guest disk metrics including disk_free and disk_used_percent (A) — this is the prerequisite that makes a disk-space alarm possible. Systems Manager Automation provides a native safety control: you attach one or more CloudWatch alarms to the automation (the StartAutomationExecution API and the start-automation-execution CLI expose AlarmConfiguration / --alarm-configuration, described as 'The details for the CloudWatch alarm you want to apply to an automation or command'), and if any attached alarm enters the ALARM state the automation is stopped. Creating a CloudWatch alarm on available disk space and adding it as a safety control on the Automation task therefore halts the patching automation when disk space is low (D). Together, A supplies the disk metric and D enforces the guardrail during patching, directly preventing the insufficient-disk-space failures. The remaining options use per-instance cron scripts, custom log streams, or a custom Lambda that operate on the wrong mechanism (alarms act on metrics, not on values buried in log streams) and are never wired into the Automation as a control that can stop patching.","explanation_zh":"EC2 執行個體預設並不會發出作業系統層級的檔案系統可用空間指標；EC2 預設命名空間提供的是 hypervisor 層級指標（CPU、網路、基本 EBS），不包含 guest OS 內部的磁碟可用空間。要監控可用磁碟空間，必須安裝 CloudWatch agent，它會收集 guest 磁碟指標，包括 disk_free 與 disk_used_percent（A）——這是讓磁碟空間 alarm 得以成立的前置條件。Systems Manager Automation 提供內建安全控制：可將一個或多個 CloudWatch alarm 附加到 automation（StartAutomationExecution API 與 start-automation-execution CLI 提供 AlarmConfiguration / --alarm-configuration，文件描述為「您要套用到 automation 或 command 的 CloudWatch alarm 詳細資訊」），只要任一附加的 alarm 進入 ALARM 狀態，automation 就會被停止。因此建立一個監控可用磁碟空間的 CloudWatch alarm，並將其作為 Automation 任務的安全控制，可在磁碟不足時停止修補 automation（D）。A 提供磁碟指標、D 在修補期間強制執行護欄，兩者結合可直接避免磁碟空間不足造成的失敗。其餘選項使用每台執行個體的 cron 腳本、自訂 log stream 或自訂 Lambda，這些都使用了錯誤機制（alarm 是針對 metrics 而非埋在 log stream 中的數值運作），且從未整合為能停止修補的 Automation 控制。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A per-instance cron job that deletes temporary files is manual, high-overhead, not integrated with the Automation, and does not guarantee sufficient free space before or during patching; it treats a symptom rather than monitoring disk space or guarding the patch process.","why_zh":"每台執行個體用 cron 刪除暫存檔屬於手動、高負擔、未與 Automation 整合的做法，且無法保證修補前或修補期間有足夠可用空間；它只處理症狀，並未監控磁碟空間或防護修補流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Writing available disk space into a CloudWatch Logs stream uses the wrong mechanism. Disk-space monitoring belongs in metrics/alarms; the CloudWatch agent already collects disk_free/disk_used_percent natively, CloudWatch alarms act on metrics rather than on values buried in log streams, and this approach is not attached to the Automation to stop patching.","why_zh":"把可用磁碟空間寫入 CloudWatch Logs stream 使用了錯誤的機制。磁碟空間監控應透過 metrics/alarms 處理；CloudWatch agent 本就能原生收集 disk_free/disk_used_percent，且 CloudWatch alarm 是針對 metrics 運作，而非處理埋在 log stream 中的數值，此做法也未附加到 Automation 以停止修補。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A Lambda function polling each instance's log stream reinvents native functionality with custom code, depends on the flawed log-stream approach from C, and is not attached to the Automation as a safety control via AlarmConfiguration, so it cannot actually stop the patching task when disk space is low.","why_zh":"用 Lambda 輪詢每台執行個體的 log stream，是用自訂程式重造原生功能，依賴 C 的有缺陷 log-stream 方式，且未透過 AlarmConfiguration 作為安全控制附加到 Automation 上，因此在磁碟不足時無法真正停止修補任務。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/metrics-collected-by-CloudWatch-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/install-CloudWatch-Agent-on-EC2-Instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/v1/reference/ssm/start-automation-execution.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/running-automations-scale-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-automation.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":211,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is building an application that uses an AWS Lambda function to query an Amazon Aurora MySQL DB cluster. The Lambda function performs only read queries. Amazon EventBridge events invoke the Lambda function. As more events invoke the Lambda function each second, the database's latency increases and the database's throughput decreases. The DevOps engineer needs to improve the performance of the application. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在构建一个应用程序，该程序使用 AWS Lambda 函数来查询 Amazon Aurora MySQL 数据库集群。Lambda 函数仅执行读取查询。Amazon EventBridge 事件会触发该 Lambda 函数。 随着每秒调用 Lambda 函数的事件增多，数据库的延迟增加，吞吐量降低。DevOps 工程师需要提 升应用程序的性能。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon RDS Proxy to create a proxy. Connect the proxy to the Aurora cluster reader endpoint. Set a maximum connections percentage on the proxy.","B":"Implement database connection pooling inside the Lambda code. Set a maximum number of connections on the database connection pool.","C":"Implement the database connection opening outside the Lambda event handler code.","D":"Implement the database connection opening and closing inside the Lambda event handler code.","E":"Connect to the proxy endpoint from the Lambda function.","F":"Connect to the Aurora cluster endpoint from the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon RDS Proxy 创建一个代理。将代理连接到 Aurora 集群的只读端点。在代理上设置最大 连接百分比。","B":"在 Lambda 代码内部实现数据库连接池。为数据库连接池设置最大连接数。","C":"在 Lambda 事件处理程序代码之外实现数据库连接的打开。","D":"在 Lambda 事件处理程序代码内部实现数据库连接的打开和关闭。","E":"从 Lambda 函数连接到代理端点。","F":"从 Lambda 函数连接到 Aurora 集群端点。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The root cause is database connection pressure: under high EventBridge-driven Lambda concurrency, each warm/cold invocation that opens its own Aurora connection oversubscribes the cluster, raising latency and cutting throughput. (A) Amazon RDS Proxy 'establishes a database connection pool and reuses connections in this pool,' which avoids per-invocation connect overhead and, via a maximum connections percentage, protects the database 'against oversubscription' (AWS RDS Proxy docs). Because the Lambda performs ONLY read queries, pointing the proxy at a read-only target/reader endpoint lets RDS Proxy 'use a different reader instance for each connection,' so a query-intensive app 'can take advantage of Aurora's clustering capability' (RDS Proxy endpoint docs). (E) The Lambda must connect to the proxy endpoint, not the cluster endpoint, otherwise traffic bypasses RDS Proxy entirely and gains nothing. (C) Opening the database connection outside the handler (in the init phase) lets warm execution environments reuse the connection instead of creating a new one each invocation; AWS Lambda best practices explicitly say to 'initialize SDK clients and database connections outside of the function handler' so 'subsequent invocations processed by the same instance... can reuse these resources.' Together these reduce physical connection count, eliminate per-call connect churn, and spread reads across replicas.","explanation_zh":"根本原因是資料庫連線壓力：在 EventBridge 驅動的高併發 Lambda 下，每次叫用各自開啟 Aurora 連線會對叢集造成超量訂閱(oversubscription)，導致延遲上升、吞吐量下降。(A) Amazon RDS Proxy「建立資料庫連線池並重用池中連線」，避免每次叫用重新連線的開銷，並可透過最大連線百分比(MaxConnectionsPercent)保護資料庫「避免被超量訂閱」(AWS RDS Proxy 文件)。由於該 Lambda 只執行讀取查詢，將 proxy 指向 read-only 目標/reader endpoint，可讓 RDS Proxy「為每條連線使用不同的 reader 執行個體」，使查詢密集的應用「善用 Aurora 的叢集能力」(RDS Proxy endpoint 文件)。(E) Lambda 必須連到 proxy endpoint 而非 cluster endpoint，否則流量會完全繞過 RDS Proxy，毫無效果。(C) 在 handler 之外(初始化階段)開啟資料庫連線，讓暖啟動的執行環境重用連線而非每次叫用重新建立；AWS Lambda 最佳實務明確指出應「在函式 handler 之外初始化 SDK 用戶端與資料庫連線」，使「同一執行個體處理的後續叫用…可重用這些資源」。三者合在一起可減少實體連線數、消除每次叫用的連線變動、並將讀取分散到多個 replica。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A connection pool inside the Lambda code with a max-connections cap is largely ineffective here because each Lambda execution environment serves only ONE concurrent request at a time, so a per-instance pool cannot share connections across the many concurrent invocations that are causing oversubscription. Each concurrent environment still holds its own connections, and the database still sees the connection surge. Cross-invocation connection sharing is exactly what RDS Proxy provides, which is why AWS recommends RDS Proxy (A) for this serverless pattern rather than an in-function pool.","why_zh":"在 Lambda 程式碼內建連線池並設上限在此情境幾乎無效，因為每個 Lambda 執行環境一次只服務一個併發請求，單實例連線池無法在造成超量訂閱的眾多併發叫用之間共用連線。每個併發環境仍各自持有連線，資料庫依然會看到連線暴增。跨叫用的連線共用正是 RDS Proxy 的功能，因此 AWS 在此無伺服器情境建議使用 RDS Proxy(A)而非函式內連線池。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Opening AND closing the connection inside the handler is the anti-pattern that drives the problem: it creates and tears down a fresh connection on every invocation, maximizing connection churn and connect/auth overhead under high concurrency. It is the direct opposite of the recommended option C, which moves connection setup to the init phase for reuse.","why_zh":"在 handler 內開啟『並』關閉連線正是造成問題的反模式：每次叫用都新建並拆除一條連線，在高併發下使連線變動與連線/驗證開銷最大化。這與建議的 C 正好相反，C 把連線建立移到初始化階段以便重用。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Connecting to the Aurora cluster endpoint from the Lambda bypasses RDS Proxy entirely, negating options A and E and reintroducing the per-invocation oversubscription. The cluster (writer) endpoint also points at the primary instance, so read-only traffic does not benefit from spreading queries across reader replicas. The correct target is the proxy endpoint (E).","why_zh":"從 Lambda 連到 Aurora cluster endpoint 會完全繞過 RDS Proxy，使 A 與 E 失效並重新引發每次叫用的超量訂閱。cluster(writer)endpoint 也指向 primary 執行個體，唯讀流量無法藉由分散查詢到多個 reader replica 受益。正確的目標是 proxy endpoint(E)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/rds-proxy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/rds-proxy-endpoints.CreatingEndpoint.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Aurora.Endpoints.Reader.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/lambda-rds-connect.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/lambda-runtime-environment.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":212,"question_en":"A company has an AWS CloudFormation stack that is deployed in a single AWS account. The company has configured the stack to send event notifications to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. A DevOps engineer must implement an automated solution that applies a tag to the specific CloudFormation stack instance only after a successful stack update occurs. The DevOps engineer has created an AWS Lambda function that applies and updates this tag for the specific stack instance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个部署在单个 AWS 账户中的 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈。该公司已将该堆栈配置为向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发送事件通知。 DevOps 工程师必须实现一个自动化解决方案，仅在特定的 CloudFormation 堆栈实例成功更新后为其 应用标签。该 DevOps 工程师已创建了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为特定的堆栈实例应用和更新此 标签。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Run the AWS-UpdateCloudFormationStack AWS Systems ManagerAutomation runbook when Systems Manager detects an UPDATE_COMPLETE event for the instance status of the CloudFormation stack. Configure the runbook to invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Create a custom AWS Config rule that produces a compliance change event if the CloudFormation stack has an UPDATE_COMPLETE instance status. Configure AWS Config to directly invoke the Lambda function to automatically remediate the change event.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches the UPDATE_COMPLETE event pattern for the instance status of the CloudFormation stack. Configure the rule to invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Adjust the configuration of the CloudFormation stack to send notifications for only an UPDATE_COMPLETE instance status event to the SNS topic. Subscribe the Lambda function to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"当 AWS Systems Manager 检测到 CloudFormation 堆栈的实例状态出现 UPDATE_COMPLETE 事件时，运行 AWS-UpdateCloudFormationStack AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。 配置运行手册以调用 Lambda 函数。","B":"创建一个自定义的 AWS Config 规则，如果 CloudFormation 堆栈具有 UPDATE_COMPLETE 实例 状态，则生成合规性变更事件。配置 AWS Config 直接调用 Lambda 函数以自动修复变更事件。","C":"创建一个与 CloudFormation 堆栈实例状态的 UPDATE_COMPLETE 事件模式相匹配的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则以调用 Lambda 函数。","D":"调整 CloudFormation 堆栈的配置，使其仅在实例状态事件为 UPDATE_COMPLETE 时向 SNS 主题 发送通知。将 Lambda 函数订阅到 SNS 主题。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudFormation automatically emits events to the EventBridge default event bus whenever a create, update, delete, or drift-detection operation is performed on a stack. The 'CloudFormation Stack Status Change' event (source: aws.cloudformation) carries a detail object with the specific stack-id and status-details.status (for example, UPDATE_COMPLETE). An EventBridge rule can therefore match an event pattern scoped to exactly the UPDATE_COMPLETE status for that specific stack and invoke the Lambda function directly as a rule target with no extra glue. The AWS docs even list this exact use case for these events: 'Create stack or stack set specific tags on all resource provisioned through CloudFormation.' This native, fully event-driven, single-status, instance-scoped design is precisely what the requirement describes, so option C is correct.","explanation_zh":"每當對 stack 執行 create、update、delete 或 drift-detection 操作時，CloudFormation 會自動將事件送到 EventBridge 的 default event bus。其中的 'CloudFormation Stack Status Change' 事件（source 為 aws.cloudformation）在 detail 中帶有特定的 stack-id 與 status-details.status（例如 UPDATE_COMPLETE）。因此可以建立一條 EventBridge rule，其 event pattern 精準比對該特定 stack 的 UPDATE_COMPLETE 狀態，並直接以該 Lambda function 作為 rule 的 target 來叫用，無需任何額外串接。AWS 文件甚至直接列出此用途：'Create stack or stack set specific tags on all resource provisioned through CloudFormation。' 這個原生、完全事件驅動、單一狀態、針對特定 stack 的設計正好符合題目需求，所以 C 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no AWS-managed 'AWS-UpdateCloudFormationStack' Systems Manager Automation runbook for this scenario, and Systems Manager does not natively 'detect' CloudFormation UPDATE_COMPLETE status events. SSM Automation has no event source that watches CloudFormation stack status, so it cannot be triggered this way. The chain described is fabricated and would not fire on stack update completion.","why_zh":"並不存在用於此情境的 AWS 託管 'AWS-UpdateCloudFormationStack' Systems Manager Automation runbook，且 Systems Manager 無法原生『偵測』CloudFormation 的 UPDATE_COMPLETE 狀態事件。SSM Automation 沒有監看 CloudFormation stack 狀態的事件來源，因此無法以此方式被觸發；此流程是虛構的，不會在 stack 更新完成時觸發。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config evaluates resource configuration compliance, not transient operational lifecycle states. UPDATE_COMPLETE is a momentary stack operation status, not a persistent configuration item that a custom Config rule would produce a compliance-change event for. Moreover, Config remediation runs through SSM Automation documents rather than directly invoking a Lambda function, so both the trigger and the remediation mechanism are mismatched.","why_zh":"AWS Config 評估的是資源組態的合規性，而非短暫的操作生命週期狀態。UPDATE_COMPLETE 是瞬間的 stack 操作狀態，並非 custom Config rule 會據以產生合規變更事件的持久組態項目。此外，Config 的 remediation 是透過 SSM Automation document 執行，而非直接叫用 Lambda function，因此觸發條件與修復機制都不符。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFormation does support stack notifications to an SNS topic (the NotificationARNs setting), but it sends all stack and resource lifecycle status changes to the topic — there is no native option to 'configure the stack to send notifications for only an UPDATE_COMPLETE status.' The premise of single-status filtering on the CloudFormation side is false; any filtering would have to happen inside the Lambda, so the option as worded misstates a capability and is less clean than EventBridge pattern matching in C.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 確實支援透過 SNS topic 的 stack notifications（NotificationARNs 設定），但它會把所有 stack 與資源生命週期狀態變更都送到該 topic——並沒有原生選項可『設定 stack 只送出 UPDATE_COMPLETE 狀態的通知』。在 CloudFormation 端依單一狀態過濾的前提是錯誤的；任何過濾都得在 Lambda 內進行，因此此選項的描述錯誤地宣稱了不存在的能力，也不如 C 以 EventBridge event pattern 比對來得乾淨。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/eventbridge-integration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/event-detail-stack-status-change.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/events-detail-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/eventbridge-using-events-rules-patterns.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/view-stack-events.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":213,"question_en":"A company deploys an application to two AWS Regions. The application creates and stores objects in an Amazon S3 bucket that is in the same Region as the application. Both deployments of the application need to have access to all the objects and their metadata from both Regions. The company has configured two- way replication between the S3 buckets and has enabled S3 Replication metrics on each S3 bucket. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution that retries the replication process if an object fails to replicate. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司将一个应用程序部署到了两个 AWS 区域。该应用程序会在与自身所在区域相同的区域内的一 个 Amazon S3 存储桶中创建并存储对象。应用程序的这两个部署都需要访问来自两个区域的所有对象及 其元数据。该公司已在两个 S3 存储桶之间配置了双向复制，并在每个 S3 存储桶上启用了 S3 复制指标。 一名 DevOps 工程师需要实现一个解决方案，如果对象复制失败，则重新尝试复制过程。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that listens to S3 event notifications for failed replication events. Create an AWS Lambda function that downloads the failed replication object and then runs a PutObject command for the object to the destination bucket. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function to handle the object that failed to replicate.","B":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. Configure S3 event notifications to send failed replication notifications to the SQS queue. Create an AWS Lambda function that downloads the failed replication object and then runs a PutObject command for the object to the destination bucket. Configure the Lambda function to poll the queue for notifications to process.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that listens to S3 event notifications for failed replications. Create an AWS Lambda function that downloads the failed replication object and then runs a PutObject command for the object to the destination bucket.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that will use S3 batch operations to retry the replication on the existing object for a failed replication. Configure S3 event notifications to send failed replication notifications to the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于监听 S3 事件通知中的复制失败事件。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于下载复制失败的对象，然后对目标存储桶中的该对象运行 PutObject 命令。配置 EventBridge 规则以调用 Lambda 函数来处理复制失败的对象。","B":"创建一个 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列。配置 S3 事件通知，将失败的复制通知 发送到 SQS 队列。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于下载失败复制的对象，然后对目标存储桶中的 该对象运行 PutObject 命令。配置 Lambda 函数以轮询队列中的通知进行处理。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于监听 S3 失败复制事件通知。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数， 用于下载失败复制的对象，然后对目标存储桶运行 PutObject 命令。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数将使用 S3 批量操作对现有对象的复制失败情况进行重试。 配置 S3 事件通知，将复制失败通知发送到该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The purpose-built mechanism to retry objects that previously failed to replicate is S3 Batch Replication, a Batch Operations job that runs the actual replication process on demand for existing objects. The AWS docs explicitly list 'Objects that have failed replication' as a supported use, and say that to 'retry replicating only objects that previously failed to replicate' you filter the Batch Replication job by ObjectReplicationStatuses=\"FAILED\". Option D triggers this from S3 Event Notifications (s3:Replication:OperationFailedReplication) to Lambda, which is a valid notification destination, and the Lambda kicks off an S3 Batch Operations replication job, preserving replication semantics and metadata. Options A and C are eliminated because S3 does NOT send replication failure events to EventBridge: the EventBridge integration only emits Object Created/Deleted, Object Restore (Initiated/Completed/Expired), Object Storage Class Changed, Object Access Tier Changed, Object ACL Updated, and Object Tags Added/Deleted, whereas s3:Replication:* is listed only under 'Supported event types for SQS, SNS, and Lambda', so the EventBridge rules in A and C would never fire. Option B routes to a valid SQS/Lambda path but does NOT retry the replication process at all; it bypasses replication entirely with a manual download plus a direct cross-Region PutObject to the destination, which loses replication status/metadata and is the wrong tool in a two-way replication topology.","explanation_zh":"專門用來重試先前複製失敗物件的機制是 S3 Batch Replication，這是一個 Batch Operations 作業，會對既有物件按需執行真正的複製流程。AWS 文件明確將「Objects that have failed replication（複製失敗的物件）」列為支援用途，並指出若要「只重試先前複製失敗的物件」，要用 ObjectReplicationStatuses=\"FAILED\" 來篩選 Batch Replication 作業。選項 D 透過 S3 Event Notifications（s3:Replication:OperationFailedReplication）觸發 Lambda（Lambda 是合法的通知目的地），由該 Lambda 啟動 S3 Batch Operations 複製作業，保留複製語意與中繼資料。選項 A 與 C 被排除，因為 S3 並不會把複製失敗事件送到 EventBridge：EventBridge 整合只發出 Object Created/Deleted、Object Restore（Initiated/Completed/Expired）、Object Storage Class Changed、Object Access Tier Changed、Object ACL Updated 以及 Object Tags Added/Deleted，而 s3:Replication:* 只列在『SQS、SNS 和 Lambda 支援的事件類型』之下，因此 A 與 C 的 EventBridge 規則永遠不會觸發。選項 B 雖然走的是合法的 SQS/Lambda 路徑，但根本沒有重試複製流程；它完全繞過複製，改以手動下載再直接跨區域 PutObject 寫入目的地，會遺失複製狀態/中繼資料，對於雙向複製拓撲而言是錯誤的工具。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EventBridge does not receive S3 replication failure events. Per the EventBridge.html doc, S3 only sends Object Created/Deleted, Object Restore, Object Storage Class Changed, Object Access Tier Changed, Object ACL Updated, and Object Tags Added/Deleted to EventBridge; there is no Replication:OperationFailedReplication event, so the rule never fires. The manual download + direct PutObject to the destination also bypasses the replication process and loses replication status/metadata rather than retrying replication.","why_zh":"EventBridge 不會收到 S3 複製失敗事件。根據 EventBridge.html 文件，S3 只會把 Object Created/Deleted、Object Restore、Object Storage Class Changed、Object Access Tier Changed、Object ACL Updated 與 Object Tags Added/Deleted 送到 EventBridge，並沒有 Replication:OperationFailedReplication 事件，因此規則永遠不會觸發。此外，手動下載再直接 PutObject 到目的地也是繞過複製流程、遺失複製狀態/中繼資料，而非重試複製。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Although SQS/Lambda is a valid destination for s3:Replication:OperationFailedReplication, this option does not retry the replication process: it bypasses replication entirely with a manual download plus a direct cross-Region PutObject to the destination bucket, losing replication status/metadata, which is wrong in a two-way replication topology. S3 can also invoke Lambda directly, so the extra SQS-poll construct is unnecessary, but the fatal flaw is failing to use the actual replication retry mechanism (S3 Batch Replication).","why_zh":"雖然 SQS/Lambda 是 s3:Replication:OperationFailedReplication 合法的通知目的地，但此選項並未重試複製流程：它完全繞過複製，以手動下載加上直接跨區域 PutObject 寫入目的地儲存貯體，遺失複製狀態/中繼資料，在雙向複製拓撲中是錯誤做法。S3 也能直接觸發 Lambda，因此額外的 SQS 輪詢結構是多餘的；但致命缺陷是沒有使用真正的複製重試機制（S3 Batch Replication）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as A: EventBridge does not emit S3 replication failure events (s3:Replication:* is supported only for SQS, SNS, and Lambda destinations), so the EventBridge rule never triggers. The manual PutObject to the destination also bypasses the replication process rather than retrying it via S3 Batch Replication.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的致命缺陷：EventBridge 不會發出 S3 複製失敗事件（s3:Replication:* 只支援 SQS、SNS 和 Lambda 目的地），因此 EventBridge 規則永遠不會觸發。對目的地的手動 PutObject 也是繞過複製流程，而非透過 S3 Batch Replication 來重試。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-batch-replication-batch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-metrics-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/notification-how-to-event-types-and-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventBridge.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":214,"question_en":"A company needs to implement failover for its application. The application includes an Amazon CloudFront distribution and a public Application Load Balancer (ALB) in an AWS Region. The company has configured the ALB as the default origin for the distribution. After some recent application outages, the company wants a zero-second RTO. The company deploys the application to a secondary Region in a warm standby configuration. A DevOps engineer needs to automate the failover of the application to the secondary Region so that HTTP GET requests meet the desired RTO. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要为其应用程序实施故障转移。该应用程序包含一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发和一个位于 AWS 区域内的公共应用负载均衡器 （ALB）。该公司已将 ALB 配置为分发的默认源。 在最近出现了一些应用程序中断的情况后，该公司希望实现零秒恢复时间目标（RTO）。该公司将应用 程序部署到一个备用区域，采用热备配置。一位 DevOps 工程师需要实现应用程序自动切换到备用区域， 以确保 HTTP GET 请求满足期望的 RTO。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a second CloudFront distribution that has the secondary ALB as the default origin. Create Amazon Route 53 alias records that have a failover policy and Evaluate Target Health set to Yes for both CloudFront distributions. Update the application to use the new record set.","B":"Create a new origin on the distribution for the secondary ALB. Create a new origin group. Set the original ALB as the primary origin. Configure the origin group to fail over for HTTP 5xx status codes. Update the default behavior to use the origin group.","C":"Create Amazon Route 53 alias records that have a failover policy and Evaluate Target Health set to Yes for both ALBs. Set the TTL of both records to 0. Update the distribution's origin to use the new record set.","D":"Create a CloudFront function that detects HTTP 5xx status codes. Configure the function to return a 307 Temporary Redirect error response to the secondary ALB if the function detects 5xx status codes. Update the distribution's default behavior to send origin responses to the function."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个将辅助 ALB 作为默认源的第二个 CloudFront 分发。为两个 CloudFront 分发创建具有故障转 移策略且“评估目标健康状况”设置为“是”的 Amazon Route 53 别名记录。更新应用程序以使用新 的记录集。","B":"在分发上为辅助 ALB 创建新的源。创建新的源组。将原始 ALB 设为主要源。配置源组以在出现 HTTP 5xx 状态码时进行故障转移。更新默认行为以使用源组。","C":"为两个应用负载均衡器（ALB）创建具有故障转移策略且“评估目标健康状况”设置为“是”的 Amazon Route 53 别名记录。将两个记录的生存时间（TTL）均设置为 0。更新分发的源以使用新的 记录集。","D":"创建一个 CloudFront 函数，用于检测 HTTP 5xx 状态码。将该函数配置为在检测到 5xx 状态码时向备用 ALB 返回 307 临时重定向错误响应。更新分发的默认行为，将源响应发送到该函数。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is a zero-second RTO for HTTP GET requests, and the architecture already has a single CloudFront distribution with the primary ALB as the default origin. CloudFront origin failover (origin groups) is the AWS-documented mechanism that satisfies this: add the secondary ALB as a second origin, create an origin group with the original ALB as primary, configure failover for HTTP 5xx status codes, and point the default behavior at the origin group. When the primary origin returns a configured failover status code (or CloudFront cannot connect), CloudFront automatically re-routes the SAME viewer request to the secondary origin at the edge, so the GET still succeeds with effectively zero RTO - no DNS health-check detection, propagation, or client re-resolution delay. AWS docs explicitly state CloudFront fails over only for GET, HEAD, and OPTIONS methods, which exactly matches the 'HTTP GET requests' requirement, and the configurable failover status codes include the 5xx range (500, 502, 503, 504). This makes B correct.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定條件是 HTTP GET 請求需達到 zero-second RTO，而架構已經使用單一 CloudFront distribution，並以主要 ALB 作為 default origin。CloudFront origin failover（origin groups）正是 AWS 文件記載能滿足此需求的機制：將次要 ALB 加為第二個 origin，建立 origin group 並把原 ALB 設為 primary，將 failover 條件設為 HTTP 5xx 狀態碼，再讓 default behavior 使用該 origin group。當 primary origin 回傳設定的 failover 狀態碼（或 CloudFront 無法連線）時，CloudFront 會在 edge 自動把同一筆 viewer 請求改送到 secondary origin，因此 GET 仍能成功，RTO 實質為零，毋須等待 DNS health check 偵測、傳播或用戶端重新解析。AWS 文件明確指出 CloudFront 只會對 GET、HEAD、OPTIONS 方法進行 failover，恰好對應題目的「HTTP GET requests」要求，且可設定的 failover 狀態碼涵蓋 5xx 範圍（500、502、503、504），故 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DNS-based failover between two CloudFront distributions via Route 53 cannot achieve zero-second RTO. Route 53 must first detect the failure via health checks and clients/resolvers must re-resolve DNS, both of which introduce delay measured in tens of seconds. It also needlessly creates a second distribution and forces an application record-set change.","why_zh":"透過 Route 53 在兩個 CloudFront distribution 之間做 DNS failover 無法達成 zero-second RTO。Route 53 需先以 health check 偵測故障，用戶端／解析器也需重新解析 DNS，皆會產生以數十秒計的延遲；此外還多建了一個 distribution 並強迫應用程式更換 record set。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Route 53 failover with TTL 0 is still DNS-based and cannot give zero RTO: health-check detection takes tens of seconds and resolvers/clients must re-query DNS. CloudFront also resolves and caches origin DNS rather than honoring a 0 TTL for instant per-request failover, and in-flight GET requests fail until detection completes, so this does not meet the requirement.","why_zh":"即使 TTL 設為 0，Route 53 failover 仍屬 DNS 機制，無法達到 zero RTO：health check 偵測需數十秒，解析器／用戶端也須重新查詢 DNS。CloudFront 對 origin DNS 會解析並快取，並不會因 TTL 0 而做即時的逐請求 failover，且偵測完成前的進行中 GET 請求仍會失敗，故不符合需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudFront Functions run only on viewer request/response events and cannot inspect origin responses; you cannot 'send origin responses to the function' (that is a Lambda@Edge origin-response capability). Returning a 307 redirect to the client also adds a round trip and surfaces an error first, so it is neither technically valid nor zero-RTO.","why_zh":"CloudFront Functions 只在 viewer request／response 事件執行，無法檢視 origin response；無法將 origin response 送給該 function（那是 Lambda@Edge 的 origin-response 能力）。回傳 307 redirect 給用戶端還會多一個來回並先暴露錯誤，因此既不技術可行也非 zero-RTO。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/high_availability_origin_failover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/edge-functions-choosing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":215,"question_en":"A cloud team uses AWS Organizations and AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On) to manage a company's AWS accounts. The company recently established a research team. The research team requires the ability to fully manage the resources in its account. The research team must not be able to create IAM users. The cloud team creates a Research Administrator permission set in IAM Identity Center for the research team. The permission set has the AdministratorAccess AWS managed policy attached. The cloud team must ensure that no one on the research team can create IAM users. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个云团队使用 AWS 组织和 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）来管理公司的 AWS 账户。该公司最 近成立了一个研究团队。该研究团队需要能够完全管理其账户中的资源。该研究团队不得能够创建 IAM 用 户。 云团队在 IAM 身份中心为研究团队创建了一个“研究管理员”权限集。该权限集附加了“AdministratorA ccess”AWS 管理策略。云团队必须确保研究团队中的任何人都不能创建 IAM 用户。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM policy that denies the iam:CreateUser action. Attach the IAM policy to the Research Administrator permission set.","B":"Create an IAM policy that allows all actions except the iam:CreateUser action. Use the IAM policy to set the permissions boundary for the Research Administrator permission set.","C":"Create an SCP that denies the iam:CreateUser action. Attach the SCP to the research team's AWS account.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that deletes IAM users. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that detects the IAM CreateUser event. Configure the rule to invoke the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个拒绝执行 iam:CreateUser 操作的 IAM 策略。将该 IAM 策略附加到“研究管理员”权限集。","B":"创建一个 IAM 策略，允许除 iam:CreateUser 操作之外的所有操作。使用该 IAM 策略为“研究管理员”权 限集设置权限边界。","C":"创建一个拒绝执行 iam:CreateUser 操作的 SCP（服务控制策略）。将该 SCP 附加到研究团队的 AWS 账户。","D":"创建一个用于删除 IAM 用户的 AWS Lambda 函数。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则来检测 IAM 的 CreateUser 事件。配置该规则以调用 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"An IAM Identity Center permission set provisions an IAM role in each assigned member account, and a permission set can include inline policies and customer managed policies alongside AWS managed policies such as AdministratorAccess. Because IAM policy evaluation logic states that an explicit Deny always overrides any Allow, attaching a policy with an explicit Deny on iam:CreateUser to the Research Administrator permission set leaves the team with full administrative control while precisely removing the single ability to create IAM users. This control is scoped exactly to the Research Administrator permission set (the entity the question is built around) and adds the least operational overhead. Option C (an SCP) would also block the action, but an SCP is an account-wide guardrail that applies to every IAM user and role in the account, which is broader than the targeted requirement; the question explicitly frames the solution around the permission set, making the deny-policy-on-the-permission-set the best-fit answer.","explanation_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的 permission set 會在每個被指派的成員帳戶中佈建一個 IAM role，且 permission set 除了 AWS managed policy（例如 AdministratorAccess）外，還可加入 inline policy 與 customer managed policy。依據 IAM policy 評估邏輯，明確的 Deny 永遠覆蓋任何 Allow，因此在 Research Administrator permission set 上掛載一個對 iam:CreateUser 設定明確 Deny 的政策，就能讓該團隊保留完整管理權，卻精準移除「建立 IAM users」這一個動作。此控制剛好限縮在 Research Administrator permission set（本題所圍繞的實體），且操作負擔最小。選項 C 的 SCP 雖然也能封鎖該動作，但 SCP 是帳戶層級護欄，會套用到該帳戶內所有 IAM users 與 roles，範圍比需求更廣；本題明確以 permission set 為核心描述解法，因此在 permission set 上掛載 deny 政策才是最佳解。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A permissions boundary works by intersection (an action is allowed only if both the identity policy and the boundary allow it), so 'allow all actions except iam:CreateUser' could limit the action, but it is an indirect, over-engineered way to remove a single action. A simple explicit Deny on the action (option A) is the direct, standard mechanism; permissions boundaries are designed to delegate safe role/user creation, not to subtract one action from an admin. It is a near-miss distractor, not the cleanest control.","why_zh":"permissions boundary 以交集方式運作（動作須同時被身分政策與 boundary 允許才生效），所以「允許除 iam:CreateUser 外的所有動作」雖能限制該動作，但用 boundary 移除單一動作既迂迴又過度設計。直接對該動作做 explicit Deny（選項 A）才是標準直接的機制；permissions boundary 的用途是安全地委派 role/user 建立，而非從 admin 中扣除單一動作，屬於接近但非最佳解的干擾項。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP attached to the account applies to ALL IAM users and roles in that account, not just the research team's Research Administrator permission set. The requirement is framed around restricting the research team specifically via their permission set, so an account-wide SCP is broader than required and is the typical dump distractor (the dump's suggested answer).","why_zh":"附加在帳戶上的 SCP 會套用到該帳戶內所有 IAM users 與 roles，而不只是研究團隊的 Research Administrator permission set。需求是透過該 permission set 針對研究團隊做限制，因此帳戶層級的 SCP 範圍過廣，是常見的題庫干擾項（也是該題庫的建議答案）。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Lambda + EventBridge to delete users after a CreateUser event is reactive, not preventive: the IAM user is actually created and exists for a window before deletion, so it does not 'ensure no one can create IAM users.' It is a security gap with high operational overhead compared to a simple deny policy.","why_zh":"用 Lambda + EventBridge 在偵測到 CreateUser 事件後刪除使用者屬於事後補救而非預防：IAM user 實際上已被建立並存在一段時間才被刪除，無法達到「確保沒人能建立 IAM users」。相較簡單的 deny policy，這是有安全漏洞且營運負擔高的做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/howtocreatepermissionset.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/permissionsetsconcept.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":216,"question_en":"A company releases a new application in a new AWS account. The application includes an AWS Lambda function that processes messages from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queue. The Lambda function stores the results in an Amazon S3 bucket for further downstream processing. The Lambda function needs to process the messages within a specific period of time after the messages are published. The Lambda function has a batch size of 10 messages and takes a few seconds to process a batch of messages. As load increases on the application's first day of service, messages in the queue accumulate at a greater rate than the Lambda function can process the messages. Some messages miss the required processing timelines. The logs show that many messages in the queue have data that is not valid. The company needs to meet the timeline requirements for messages that have valid data. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在新的 AWS 账户中发布了一个新的应用程序。该应用程序包含一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于处理 来自 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）标准队列的消息。Lambda 函数将处理结果存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，以便进行后续的下游处理。Lambda 函数需要在消息发布后的特定时间段内处理这些 消息。该 Lambda 函数的批处理大小为 10 条消息，处理一批消息需要几秒钟。 在应用程序投入使用的首日，随着负载的增加，队列中的消息积累速度超过了 Lambda 函数处理消息的速度。 一些消息未能在规定时间内完成处理。日志显示，队列中有许多消息的数据无效。该公司需要确保数据有 效的消息能够满足处理时间的要求。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Increase the Lambda function's batch size. Change the SQS standard queue to an SQS FIFO queue. Request a Lambda concurrency increase in the AWS Region.","B":"Reduce the Lambda function's batch size. Increase the SQS message throughput quota. Request a Lambda concurrency increase in the AWS Region.","C":"Increase the Lambda function's batch size. Configure S3 Transfer Acceleration on the S3 bucket. Configure an SQS dead-letter queue.","D":"Keep the Lambda function's batch size the same. Configure the Lambda function to report failed batch items. Configure an SQS dead-letter queue."},"options_zh":{"A":"增加 Lambda 函数的批处理大小。将 SQS 标准队列更改为 SQS FIFO 队列。在 AWS 区域中请求增加 Lambda 并发量。","B":"减小 Lambda 函数的批处理大小。提高 SQS 消息吞吐量配额。在 AWS 区域内请求增加 Lambda 并发 量。","C":"增加 Lambda 函数的批处理大小。在 S3 存储桶上配置 S3 传输加速。配置一个 SQS 死信队列。","D":"保持 Lambda 函数的批处理大小不变。将 Lambda 函数配置为报告失败的批处理项。配置一个 SQS 死信 队列。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two compounding problems exist: insufficient processing throughput and many invalid-data messages that cause batch failures. By default, when a Lambda function errors on any message in a batch, ALL messages in that batch (including ones already processed successfully) become visible in the queue again and are reprocessed, and Lambda backs off by reducing the concurrency allocated to the SQS event source mapping ('If your function code caused the error... Lambda gradually backs off, reducing the amount of concurrency allocated to your Amazon SQS event source mapping'). This downward spiral directly hurts the processing rate of the valid messages. Enabling ReportBatchItemFailures (report failed batch items / partial batch response) fixes both effects: AWS docs state that with it activated 'Lambda doesn't scale down message polling when function invocations fail' and explicitly recommend it 'If you expect some messages to fail—and you don't want those failures to impact the message processing rate.' It also makes only the failed messages visible again, so valid messages are not reprocessed. Pairing this with an SQS dead-letter queue (redrive policy / maxReceiveCount) isolates the persistently-failing invalid messages so they stop being redelivered and consuming capacity. Keeping the batch size unchanged is correct, because increasing batch size would only pull MORE valid messages into a batch that a single invalid message could fail.","explanation_zh":"存在兩個相互加劇的問題：處理吞吐量不足，以及大量無效資料訊息導致批次處理失敗。預設情況下，當 Lambda 函式在批次中任一訊息上發生錯誤時，整個批次（包含已成功處理的訊息）都會重新變為可見並被重新處理，且 Lambda 會以退避策略「縮減」分配給 SQS event source mapping 的並行度（AWS 文件：「若是函式程式碼造成錯誤……Lambda 會逐步退避，縮減分配給 Amazon SQS event source mapping 的並行度」）。這種惡性循環直接損害有效訊息的處理速率。啟用 ReportBatchItemFailures（回報失敗批次項目 / 部分批次回應）可同時解決兩種影響：AWS 文件指出啟用後「Lambda 在函式呼叫失敗時不會縮減訊息輪詢」，並明確建議「若您預期部分訊息會失敗，且不希望這些失敗影響訊息處理速率」時使用此功能；它也只會讓失敗的訊息重新變為可見，因此有效訊息不會被重新處理。再搭配 SQS dead-letter queue（透過 redrive policy / maxReceiveCount）可將反覆失敗的無效訊息隔離，使其不再被重新投遞並佔用處理容量。維持批次大小不變是正確的，因為增大批次只會把「更多」有效訊息拖入可能因單一無效訊息而失敗的批次中。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Increasing batch size pulls more valid messages into a batch that a single invalid message can fail (causing full-batch reprocessing). Switching to a FIFO queue reduces throughput and worsens the problem because a poison/invalid message blocks its entire message group until it exhausts retries. Neither change enables ReportBatchItemFailures, so failures still trigger Lambda concurrency back-off.","why_zh":"增大批次會把更多有效訊息納入可能因單一無效訊息而失敗的批次（導致整批重新處理）。改用 FIFO 佇列會降低吞吐量，且毒訊息會阻塞整個 message group 直到耗盡重試而使問題惡化。兩項變更皆未啟用 ReportBatchItemFailures，因此失敗仍會觸發 Lambda 並行度退避。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SQS standard queues already provide nearly unlimited throughput, so the bottleneck is Lambda processing, not an SQS message-throughput quota. Reducing batch size lowers per-invoke efficiency, and nothing in this option stops invalid messages from failing whole batches and triggering Lambda's concurrency back-off or isolating the bad messages.","why_zh":"SQS 標準佇列本身已提供近乎無限的吞吐量，瓶頸在於 Lambda 處理，而非 SQS 訊息吞吐量配額。縮小批次降低每次呼叫的效率，且此選項無法阻止無效訊息使整批失敗、觸發 Lambda 並行度退避，也無法隔離無效訊息。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Increasing batch size worsens the failed-batch problem. S3 Transfer Acceleration only speeds long-distance uploads to S3 and is irrelevant to the SQS-to-Lambda processing timeline. A DLQ alone (without ReportBatchItemFailures) still lets one invalid message fail the entire batch, reprocess the valid messages, and trigger Lambda concurrency scale-down, so the valid messages' processing rate is not protected.","why_zh":"增大批次會加劇批次失敗問題。S3 Transfer Acceleration 僅加速長距離上傳至 S3，與 SQS 到 Lambda 的處理時限無關。僅設定 DLQ（未啟用 ReportBatchItemFailures）仍會讓單一無效訊息使整批失敗、重新處理有效訊息並觸發 Lambda 並行度縮減，因此無法保護有效訊息的處理速率。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-errorhandling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-sqs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-dead-letter-queues.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":217,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on AWS Lambda and sends logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. An Amazon Kinesis data stream is subscribed to the log groups in CloudWatch Logs. A single consumer Lambda function processes the logs from the data stream and stores the logs in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company’s DevOps team has noticed high latency during the processing and ingestion of some logs. Which combination of steps will reduce the latency? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个运行在 AWS Lambda 上的应用程序，该应用程序将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。 一个 Amazon Kinesis 数据流订阅了 CloudWatch Logs 中的日志组。一个单独的消费者 Lambda 函数从数据 流中处理日志，并将日志存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 该公司的 DevOps 团队注意到在处理和摄取某些日志时存在高延迟。 哪些步骤的组合可以降低延迟？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a data stream consumer with enhanced fan-out. Set the Lambda function that processes the logs as the consumer.","B":"Increase the ParallelizationFactor setting in the Lambda event source mapping.","C":"Configure reserved concurrency for the Lambda function that processes the logs.","D":"Increase the batch size in the Kinesis data stream.","E":"Turn off the ReportBatchItemFailures setting in the Lambda event source mapping.","F":"Increase the number of shards in the Kinesis data stream."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有增强型扇出功能的数据流消费者。将处理日志的 Lambda 函数设置为该消费者。","B":"在 Lambda 事件源映射中增加 ParallelizationFactor 设置。","C":"为处理日志的 Lambda 函数配置预留并发量。","D":"增大 Kinesis 数据流中的批处理大小。","E":"在 Lambda 事件源映射中关闭 ReportBatchItemFailures 设置。","F":"增加 Kinesis 数据流中的分片数量。"},"answer":["A","B","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The pipeline is CloudWatch Logs subscription -> Kinesis data stream -> a single consumer Lambda (via event source mapping) -> S3, and the symptom is high processing/ingestion latency (a high IteratorAge). The AWS Lambda 'Using Lambda to process records from Amazon Kinesis Data Streams' page documents exactly three levers that reduce this latency. (A) Enhanced fan-out: 'To minimize latency and maximize read throughput, create a data stream consumer with enhanced fan-out'; each consumer gets a dedicated 2 MB/s connection per shard and uses HTTP/2 to push records over a long-lived connection. (F) Adding shards: 'To increase the speed at which your function processes records, add shards to your data stream... With more shards, there are more batches being processed at once.' (B) ParallelizationFactor lets Lambda process a single shard with up to 10 concurrent invocations and 'helps scale up the processing throughput when the data volume is volatile and the IteratorAge is high' - exactly the described symptom. The other options do not reduce latency: reserved concurrency only caps concurrency (it can throttle and worsen latency), a larger batch size buffers more records before each invoke (increasing per-record latency), and turning off ReportBatchItemFailures forces full-batch reprocessing on any error, blocking the shard and raising IteratorAge.","explanation_zh":"此管線為 CloudWatch Logs 訂閱 -> Kinesis data stream -> 單一 consumer Lambda（透過 event source mapping）-> S3，症狀為處理/擷取延遲高（即 IteratorAge 偏高）。AWS Lambda 的「Using Lambda to process records from Amazon Kinesis Data Streams」文件正好列出三個可降低此延遲的手段。(A) Enhanced fan-out：文件指出「To minimize latency and maximize read throughput, create a data stream consumer with enhanced fan-out」，每個 consumer 對每個 shard 取得專屬的 2 MB/s 連線，並以 HTTP/2 透過長連線推送記錄以降低延遲。(F) 增加 shards：「To increase the speed at which your function processes records, add shards to your data stream... With more shards, there are more batches being processed at once」，提升函式處理記錄的速度。(B) ParallelizationFactor 可讓單一 shard 由最多 10 個並行 Lambda invocation 處理，文件明言「helps scale up the processing throughput when the data volume is volatile and the IteratorAge is high」，正符合本題症狀。其餘選項無法降低延遲：reserved concurrency 只是設定並行上限（設太低反而會 throttle 並惡化延遲）；加大 batch size 會在每次 invoke 前緩衝更多記錄，反而拉高單筆記錄的延遲；關閉 ReportBatchItemFailures 會在任何錯誤時重新處理整個 batch，阻塞該 shard 並推高 IteratorAge。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Reserved concurrency sets a fixed maximum (cap) on concurrent executions for the function. It limits scaling rather than increasing throughput, and for a Kinesis consumer the parallelism is driven by shard count x ParallelizationFactor. An overly low value would throttle the consumer and worsen latency; it does not by itself reduce processing latency.","why_zh":"Reserved concurrency 為函式設定並行執行數的固定上限（cap），是限制而非提升吞吐量；Kinesis consumer 的並行度由 shard 數 x ParallelizationFactor 決定。數值過低反而會 throttle consumer、加劇延遲，本身無法降低處理延遲。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Batch size is an event source mapping property (BatchSize), not a Kinesis data stream property, so the wording is imprecise. Even taken charitably, increasing the batch size makes Lambda gather more records before each invocation, increasing buffering/wait time, which tends to raise per-record latency rather than reduce it.","why_zh":"Batch size 是 event source mapping 的屬性（BatchSize），並非 Kinesis data stream 的屬性，故描述不精確。即使從寬解讀，加大 batch size 會讓 Lambda 在每次調用前累積更多記錄，增加緩衝等待時間，通常會提高（而非降低）每筆記錄的延遲。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"ReportBatchItemFailures enables partial batch responses so only the failed records are retried instead of reprocessing the whole batch. Turning it OFF forces full-batch retries on any failure, which blocks the shard, stalls in-order processing, and increases IteratorAge/latency rather than reducing it.","why_zh":"ReportBatchItemFailures 啟用部分批次回應，僅重試失敗的記錄而非整批重處理。將其關閉會在任何失敗時強制整批重試，阻塞該 shard、停滯有序處理並增加（而非降低）IteratorAge/延遲。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-kinesis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/invocation-eventsourcemapping.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/streams/latest/dev/enhanced-consumers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/api/API_CreateEventSourceMapping.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":218,"question_en":"A company operates sensitive workloads across the AWS accounts that are in the company's organization in AWS Organizations. The company uses an IP address range to delegate IP addresses for Amazon VPC CIDR blocks and all non-cloud hardware. The company needs a solution that prevents principals that are outside the company’s IP address range from performing AWS actions in the organization's accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司在其 AWS 组织中的多个 AWS 账户中运行敏感工作负载。该公司使用一个 IP 地址范围来为 Amazon VPC CIDR 块和所有非云硬件分配 IP 地址。 该公司需要一个解决方案，以防止不在公司 IP 地址范围内的主体在组织的账户中执行 AWS 操作。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Firewall Manager for the organization. Create an AWS Network Firewall policy that allows only source traffic from the company's IP address range. Set the policy scope to all accounts in the organization.","B":"In Organizations, create an SCP that denies source IP addresses that are outside of the company’s IP address range. Attach the SCP to the organization's root.","C":"Configure Amazon GuardDuty for the organization. Create a GuardDuty trusted IP address list for the company's IP range. Activate the trusted IP list for the organization.","D":"In Organizations, create an SCP that allows source IP addresses that are inside of the company’s IP address range. Attach the SCP to the organization's root."},"options_zh":{"A":"为组织配置 AWS 防火墙管理器。创建一个仅允许来自公司 IP 地址范围的源流量的 AWS 网络防火墙策 略。将策略范围设置为组织中的所有账户。","B":"在组织中，创建一个安全策略配置文件（SCP），拒绝来自公司 IP 地址范围之外的源 IP 地址。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","C":"为组织配置 Amazon GuardDuty。为公司的 IP 范围创建一个 GuardDuty 可信 IP 地址列表。为组织激活 可信 IP 列表。","D":"在组织中，创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），允许公司 IP 地址范围内的源 IP 地址。将该 SCP 附加到 组织的根目录。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is an organization-wide PREVENTIVE guardrail that blocks any principal whose request originates outside the company IP range, across all member accounts. A Deny SCP attached to the organization root does exactly this: it applies to every member account beneath it, and per the AWS Organizations SCP evaluation model a Deny attached at any level overrides any Allow. The canonical AWS pattern (the AWS deny-IP example) is Effect:Deny, Action:\"*\", Resource:\"*\" with a NotIpAddress condition on aws:SourceIp; the docs describe it as denying all AWS actions when the request comes from principals outside the listed CIDR ranges, which is the deny-list strategy in option B. Option D fails because AWS Organizations docs state plainly that SCPs do not grant permissions and no permissions are granted by an SCP; an allow-style SCP only sets a ceiling (logical intersection with the still-attached FullAWSAccess Allow:* policy) and contains no Deny, so out-of-range principals would still be permitted. Option A (Firewall Manager + Network Firewall) operates on VPC network/data-plane traffic, not principals' AWS API control-plane actions, so it cannot block out-of-range AWS actions. Option C (GuardDuty trusted IP list) is purely detective and actually suppresses findings for trusted IPs; it enforces nothing.","explanation_zh":"需求是一個跨整個組織所有成員帳戶的「預防性」護欄 (guardrail)，要阻擋任何來源 IP 在公司範圍之外的 principal 執行 AWS 動作。在 AWS Organizations 的 root 上掛載一個 Deny 的 SCP 正是如此：它套用到底下所有成員帳戶，而且依 SCP 評估模型，任一層級的 Deny 都會覆蓋任何 Allow。AWS 的標準範例 (deny-IP example) 為 Effect:Deny、Action:\"*\"、Resource:\"*\"，並對 aws:SourceIp 使用 NotIpAddress 條件；文件說明此政策會在請求來自所列 CIDR 範圍之外的 principal 時拒絕所有 AWS 動作，這正是選項 B 的 deny-list 策略。D 不正確，因為 AWS Organizations 文件明確指出 SCP「不授予權限」(No permissions are granted by an SCP)；allow 形式的 SCP 只設定權限上限 (與仍掛載的 FullAWSAccess Allow:* 政策做邏輯交集)，本身沒有任何 Deny，因此範圍外的 principal 仍會被允許。A (Firewall Manager + Network Firewall) 作用於 VPC 網路/資料層流量，而非 principal 的 AWS API 控制層動作，無法阻擋範圍外的 AWS 動作。C (GuardDuty trusted IP list) 純屬偵測，且 trusted IP 清單實際上是抑制這些 IP 的 findings，完全不會強制阻擋任何動作。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Network Firewall (deployed via Firewall Manager) inspects VPC network/data-plane traffic flowing through subnets; it does not evaluate or block AWS API control-plane actions performed by principals. It cannot prevent principals outside the IP range from calling AWS APIs in the accounts, and it would require deployed firewall endpoints/VPCs, which is the wrong layer for this requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Network Firewall (透過 Firewall Manager 部署) 檢查流經 VPC 子網的網路/資料層流量，並不評估或阻擋 principal 執行的 AWS API 控制層動作，因此無法阻止範圍外的 principal 呼叫帳戶中的 AWS API，且需部署防火牆端點/VPC，屬於錯誤的防護層。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service. A trusted IP list only suppresses findings/alerts for the listed IPs; it is purely detective and enforces nothing, so it cannot prevent out-of-range principals from performing actions.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務。trusted IP list 只是對清單中的 IP 抑制 findings/警示，純屬偵測性質，完全不會強制阻擋，因此無法防止範圍外的 principal 執行動作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"SCPs never grant permissions; they only cap them. An allow-style SCP only narrows the ceiling via logical intersection with the still-attached FullAWSAccess (Allow:*) policy. With no Deny statement and no condition that denies, out-of-range principals are not actually blocked; only a Deny SCP with NotIpAddress on aws:SourceIp (option B) blocks out-of-range requests.","why_zh":"SCP 從不授予權限，只設上限。allow 形式的 SCP 只透過與仍掛載的 FullAWSAccess (Allow:*) 做邏輯交集來縮小上限。由於沒有 Deny 語句、也沒有會拒絕的條件，範圍外的 principal 實際上並未被阻擋；唯有對 aws:SourceIp 使用 NotIpAddress 的 Deny SCP (選項 B) 才能阻擋範圍外的請求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_aws_deny-ip.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":219,"question_en":"A company deploys an application in two AWS Regions. The application currently uses an Amazon S3 bucket in the primary Region to store data. A DevOps engineer needs to ensure that the application is highly available in both Regions. The DevOps engineer has created a new S3 bucket in the secondary Region. All existing and new objects must be in both S3 buckets. The application must fail over between the Regions with no data loss. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在两个 AWS 区域部署了一个应用程序。该应用程序目前使用主区域中的一个 Amazon S3 存 储桶来存储数据。 DevOps 工程师需要确保应用程序在两个区域都具有高可用性。该 DevOps 工程师已在辅助区域创建了 一个新的 S3 存储桶。所有现有和新的对象都必须同时存在于两个 S3 存储桶中。应用程序必须能够在两 个区域之间进行故障转移，且不能丢失任何数据。 哪种步骤组合能以最高的运营效率满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new IAM role that allows the Amazon S3 and S3 Batch Operations service principals to assume the role that has the necessary permissions for S3 replication.","B":"Create a new IAM role that allows the AWS Batch service principal to assume the role that has the necessary permissions for S3 replication.","C":"Create an S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) rule on the source S3 bucket. Configure the rule to use the IAM role for Amazon S3 to replicate to the target S3 bucket.","D":"Create a two-way replication rule on the source S3 bucket. Configure the rule to use the IAM role for Amazon S3 to replicate to the target S3 bucket.","E":"Create an AWS Batch job that has an AWS Fargate orchestration type. Configure the job to use the IAM role for AWS Batch. Specify a Bash command to use the AWS CLI to synchronize the contents of the source S3 bucket and the target S3 bucket","F":"Create an operation in S3 Batch Operations to replicate the contents of the source S3 bucket to the target S3 bucket. Configure the operation to use the IAM role for Amazon S3."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 IAM 角色，允许 Amazon S3 和 S3 批量操作服务主体承担具有 S3 复制所需权限的 角色。","B":"创建一个新的 IAM 角色，允许 AWS Batch 服务主体承担具有 S3 复制所需权限的角色。","C":"在源 S3 存储桶上创建一个 S3 跨区域复制（CRR）规则。配置该规则以使用 Amazon S3 的 IAM 角色 将数据复制到目标 S3 存储桶。","D":"在源 S3 存储桶上创建双向复制规则。配置该规则以使用 Amazon S3 的 IAM 角色将数据复制到目标 S3 存储桶。","E":"创建一个具有 AWS Fargate 调度类型的 AWS Batch 作业。将作业配置为使用 AWS Batch 的 IAM 角色。 指定一个 Bash 命令，使用 AWS CLI 同步源 S3 存储桶和目标 S3 存储桶的内容。","F":"在 S3 批量操作中创建一个操作，将源 S3 存储桶的内容复制到目标 S3 存储桶。配置该操作以使用 Amazon S3 的 IAM 角色。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario needs all EXISTING and NEW objects in both buckets, plus cross-Region failover with NO data loss, at the MOST operational efficiency, so native S3 replication features beat custom scripts. (D) A two-way (bi-directional) replication rule is the AWS-documented way to keep both buckets in sync and support failover: the replication overview states you should 'use two-way replication (also known as bi-directional replication) rules' so that 'when data is written to the S3 bucket that traffic fails over to, that data is then replicated back to the source bucket' (one-way CRR cannot do this, which is why C is wrong). (F) Live replication only copies NEW objects written after it is enabled and does not replicate pre-existing objects, so to replicate the EXISTING objects you must run an on-demand S3 Batch Operations job (S3 Batch Replication). (A) Live two-way replication needs a role that the Amazon S3 service principal (s3.amazonaws.com) can assume, and the Batch Replication job needs a role that the S3 Batch Operations service principal (batchoperations.s3.amazonaws.com) can assume; the most operationally efficient option is a single IAM role whose trust policy allows BOTH service principals and that carries the necessary S3 replication permissions. Among the IAM choices, A names exactly these two correct principals, whereas B names the unrelated AWS Batch service.","explanation_zh":"此情境要求所有「現有」與「新」物件都存在於兩個值區，並需跨 Region 故障轉移且「不遺失資料」，同時以「最高營運效率」達成，因此 S3 原生複寫功能優於自訂腳本。(D) 雙向 (bi-directional) 複寫規則是 AWS 文件記載讓兩個值區保持同步並支援故障轉移的方式：replication 總覽指出應『使用 two-way replication (亦即 bi-directional replication) 規則』，如此『當資料寫入流量故障轉移到的 S3 值區時，該資料會再被複寫回來源值區』(單向 CRR 做不到這點，故 C 錯誤)。(F) Live replication 只會複寫啟用之後寫入的「新」物件，不會複寫先前已存在的物件，因此要複寫「現有」物件必須執行隨需的 S3 Batch Operations 作業 (S3 Batch Replication)。(A) 雙向 live replication 需要一個可由 Amazon S3 服務主體 (s3.amazonaws.com) 擔任的角色，而 Batch Replication 作業需要一個可由 S3 Batch Operations 服務主體 (batchoperations.s3.amazonaws.com) 擔任的角色；最具營運效率的做法是用「單一」IAM 角色，其信任政策同時允許「兩個」服務主體並具備所需的 S3 複寫權限。在 IAM 選項中，A 正好指明這兩個正確主體，而 B 指的是不相干的 AWS Batch 服務。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 Batch Operations / Batch Replication uses the batchoperations.s3.amazonaws.com service principal, not the AWS Batch (batch.amazonaws.com) compute-orchestration service. AWS Batch is unrelated to S3 replication, so a role trusting the AWS Batch principal cannot run a Batch Replication job and would not work for S3 replication at all.","why_zh":"S3 Batch Operations / Batch Replication 使用的是 batchoperations.s3.amazonaws.com 服務主體，而非 AWS Batch (batch.amazonaws.com) 這個運算編排服務。AWS Batch 與 S3 複寫無關，因此信任 AWS Batch 主體的角色無法執行 Batch Replication 作業，也完全不適用於 S3 複寫。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"One-way Cross-Region Replication alone does not meet 'fail over with no data loss.' After failover, writes go to the secondary bucket; a one-way source->target CRR rule will not replicate those writes back to the primary, so data written during failover would be lost when failing back. Two-way (bi-directional) replication (D) is required for this requirement.","why_zh":"單向 Cross-Region Replication 無法滿足「故障轉移且不遺失資料」。故障轉移後寫入會進入次要值區；單向 source->target 的 CRR 規則不會把這些寫入複寫回主要值區，導致故障轉移期間寫入的資料在回切時遺失。此需求必須使用雙向 (bi-directional) 複寫 (D)。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Building a custom AWS Batch + Fargate job that runs a Bash 'aws s3 sync' command is a manual, self-managed, scheduled-or-triggered solution with high operational overhead, and it is not continuous live replication, so it cannot guarantee no-data-loss failover. It is the opposite of MOST operational efficiency; native S3 two-way replication plus on-demand Batch Replication is the managed approach.","why_zh":"建立自訂的 AWS Batch + Fargate 作業執行 Bash 的『aws s3 sync』指令，是需自行維護、靠排程或觸發、營運負擔高的方案，且非持續性 live replication，無法保證故障轉移不遺失資料。這與「最高營運效率」背道而馳；原生 S3 雙向複寫加隨需 Batch Replication 才是受管做法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-batch-replication-batch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/s3-batch-replication-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/setting-repl-config-perm-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/mrap-create-two-way-replication-rules.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":220,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The company needs an automated process across all AWS accounts to isolate any compromised Amazon EC2 instances when the instances receive a specific tag. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司需要一个跨所有 AWS 账 户的自动化流程，在 Amazon EC2 实例收到特定标签时将其隔离。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy the CloudFormation stacks in all AWS accounts.","B":"Create an SCP that has a Deny statement for the ec2:* action with a condition of \"aws:RequestTag/ isolation\": false.","C":"Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","D":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that creates an EC2 instance role that has no IAM policies attached. Configure the template to have a security group that has an explicit Deny rule on all traffic. Use the CloudFormation template to create an AWS Lambda function that attaches the IAM role to instances. Configure the Lambda function to add a network ACL. Set up an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function when a specific tag is applied to a compromised EC2 instance.","E":"Create an AWS CloudFormation template that creates an EC2 instance role that has no IAM policies attached. Configure the template to have a security group that has no inbound rules or outbound rules. Use the CloudFormation template to create an AWS Lambda function that attaches the IAM role to instances. Configure the Lambda function to replace any existing security groups with the new security group. Set up an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function when a specific tag is applied to a compromised EC2 instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 在所有 AWS 账户中部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。","B":"创建一个 SCP，其中包含针对 ec2:* 操作的拒绝语句，并设置aws:RequestTag/isolation\": false 。","C":"将 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","D":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，用于创建一个未附加任何 IAM 策略的 EC2 实例角色。配置模 板以包含一个对所有流量都有明确拒绝规则的安全组。使用 CloudFormation 模板创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 IAM 角色附加到实例上。配置 Lambda 函数以添加网络访问控制列表（ACL）。 设置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，当特定标签应用于受攻击的 EC2 实例时调用 Lambda 函数。","E":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，用于创建一个未附加任何 IAM 策略的 EC2 实例角色。配置该模 板，使其包含一个既无入站规则也无出站规则的安全组。使用 CloudFormation 模板创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 IAM 角色附加到实例上。配置 Lambda 函数，使其用新安全组替换任何现有的安全 组。设置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在将特定标签应用于受攻击的 EC2 实例时调用 Lambda 函 数。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is an automated, organization-wide process that isolates a compromised EC2 instance when a specific tag is applied. A is correct because AWS CloudFormation StackSets is the documented mechanism to create the same stack across multiple accounts in a single operation, and with service-managed permissions it deploys directly to all accounts in an AWS Organization. This is how you fan out the isolation components (Lambda function, EventBridge rule, isolation security group, and quarantine IAM role) to every account. E is correct because it implements the exact isolation procedure AWS prescribes for a compromised EC2 instance in the GuardDuty guide: create a dedicated isolation security group with no inbound or outbound rules (no 0.0.0.0/0 allow), associate it with the instance, and remove all other security group associations - i.e., replace existing security groups with the new one. An EventBridge rule fires the Lambda when the specific tag is applied, and a no-policy IAM role removes the instance's permissions. The decisive qualifiers are 'automated process across all AWS accounts' (StackSets fan-out, A) and tag-triggered isolation by swapping the security group (E).","explanation_zh":"需求是一個跨整個組織的自動化流程：當套用特定標籤時隔離受感染的 EC2 執行個體。A 正確，因為 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 是官方文件記載的機制，可在單一操作中跨多個帳戶建立同一個堆疊；搭配 service-managed permissions 時，它會直接部署到 AWS Organizations 的所有帳戶。這正是把隔離元件（Lambda 函數、EventBridge 規則、隔離 security group、隔離 IAM 角色）扇出到每個帳戶的方式。E 正確，因為它完全實作 AWS 在 GuardDuty 指南中對受感染 EC2 執行個體所規定的隔離程序：建立一個沒有任何輸入或輸出規則（沒有 0.0.0.0/0 允許規則）的專用隔離 security group、將其關聯到執行個體，並移除所有其他 security group 關聯，也就是以新的 security group 取代既有的 security group。EventBridge 規則在套用特定標籤時觸發 Lambda，無政策的 IAM 角色則移除執行個體的權限。決定性的限定詞是『跨所有 AWS 帳戶的自動化流程』（用 StackSets 扇出，A）以及由標籤觸發、透過替換 security group 來隔離（E）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"An SCP that denies ec2:* is a preventive permission guardrail evaluated at request time on principals; it does not detect a tag event or perform automated isolation of an already-running compromised instance. The condition 'aws:RequestTag/isolation: false' is also malformed: aws:RequestTag/isolation only exists in the request context when that tag is being supplied in the request, and it is a string value, not a boolean - so it would not match the act of applying an isolation tag. Denying all ec2:* would broadly break legitimate operations across the org rather than isolate a single host.","why_zh":"拒絕 ec2:* 的 SCP 是在請求時針對主體評估的預防性權限護欄，無法偵測標籤事件，也無法對已在執行中的受感染執行個體執行自動隔離。條件『aws:RequestTag/isolation: false』本身也有問題：aws:RequestTag/isolation 只有在請求中正在提供該標籤時才會存在於請求情境中，且其值為字串而非布林值，因此不會匹配套用隔離標籤的動作。拒絕所有 ec2:* 會在整個組織中廣泛破壞正常操作，而非隔離單一主機。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This step only matters if B were correct; it attaches the flawed SCP from B to the org root. Since B does not achieve automated tag-triggered isolation (and would broadly deny EC2 operations), attaching it to the root does not meet the requirement and is not part of the working solution.","why_zh":"只有在 B 正確時這個步驟才有意義；它將 B 中有缺陷的 SCP 附加到組織根。由於 B 無法達成由標籤觸發的自動隔離（且會廣泛拒絕 EC2 操作），將其附加到根並不能滿足需求，也不是可行解決方案的一部分。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Two technical flaws confirmed by AWS docs. First, the VPC docs state 'You can specify allow rules, but not deny rules' - there is no 'explicit Deny rule on all traffic' in a security group; isolation is achieved with an empty no-rule security group, which E does correctly. Second, D only attaches the IAM role and adds a network ACL but never removes the instance's existing security groups, so the existing permissive SGs would still allow traffic. The GuardDuty procedure requires removing all security group associations other than the new isolation SG, which only E does.","why_zh":"AWS 文件已確認有兩處技術缺陷。第一，VPC 文件明確指出『You can specify allow rules, but not deny rules』，security group 不存在『對所有流量的明確 Deny 規則』；隔離是透過沒有任何規則的空 security group 達成，這正是 E 的做法。第二，D 只附加 IAM 角色並新增 network ACL，卻從未移除執行個體現有的 security group，因此既有的寬鬆 SG 仍會允許流量。GuardDuty 程序要求移除新隔離 SG 以外的所有 security group 關聯，只有 E 做到這點。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/compromised-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/security-group-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/what-is-cfnstacksets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-ec2.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":221,"question_en":"A company manages multiple AWS accounts by using AWS Organizations with OUs for the different business divisions. The company is updating their corporate network to use new IP address ranges. The company has 10 Amazon S3 buckets in different AWS accounts. The S3 buckets store reports for the different divisions. The S3 bucket configurations allow only private corporate network IP addresses to access the S3 buckets. A DevOps engineer needs to change the range of IP addresses that have permission to access the contents of the S3 buckets. The DevOps engineer also needs to revoke the permissions of two OUs in the company. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司通过使用 AWS 组织和组织单位（OU）来管理多个 AWS 账户，每个组织单位对应不同的 业务部门。该公司正在更新其企业网络以使用新的 IP 地址范围。该公司在不同的 AWS 账户中有 10 个 Amazon S3 存储桶，这些存储桶存储着不同部门的报告。S3 存储桶的配置仅允许来自公司内部私 有网络的 IP 地址访问这些存储桶。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要更改有权访问 S3 存储桶内容的 IP 地址范围。该 DevOps 工程师还需要撤销 公司内两个组织单位的权限。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new SCP that has two statements, one that allows access to the new range of IP addresses for all the S3 buckets and one that denies access to the old range of IP addresses for all the S3 buckets. Set a permissions boundary for the OrganizationAccountAccessRole role in the two OUs to deny access to the S3 buckets.","B":"Create a new SCP that has a statement that allows only the new range of IP addresses to access the S3 buckets. Create another SCP that denies access to the S3 buckets. Attach the second SCP to the two OUs.","C":"On all the S3 buckets, configure resource-based policies that allow only the new range of IP addresses to access the S3 buckets. Create a new SCP that denies access to the S3 buckets. Attach the SCP to the two OUs.","D":"On all the S3 buckets, configure resource-based policies that allow only the new range of IP addresses to access the S3 buckets. Set a permissions boundary for the OrganizationAccountAccessRole role in the two OUs to deny access to the S3 buckets."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 SCP，其中包含两条语句，一条允许所有 S3 存储桶对新范围的 IP 地址进行访问， 另一条拒绝所有 S3 存储桶对旧范围的 IP 地址进行访问。为两个组织单位中的 OrganizationAcco untAccessRole 角色设置权限边界，以拒绝访问 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建一个新的 SCP，其中包含仅允许新范围的 IP 地址访问 S3 存储桶的声明。创建另一个 SCP， 禁止访问 S3 存储桶。将第二个 SCP 附加到两个组织单位。","C":"在所有 S3 存储桶上配置基于资源的策略，仅允许新的 IP 地址范围访问这些 S3 存储桶。创建一个 新的服务控制策略（SCP），禁止访问 S3 存储桶。将该 SCP 附加到两个组织单位（OU）。","D":"在所有 S3 存储桶上配置基于资源的策略，仅允许新的 IP 地址范围访问这些 S3 存储桶。为两个组 织单位中的 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 角色设置权限边界，以拒绝访问 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario has two independent requirements that each demand the correct mechanism. (1) Changing which IP range may read bucket contents is an access-grant decision that must live in each S3 bucket's resource-based policy (a bucket policy with an aws:SourceIp / NotIpAddress condition). AWS Organizations documentation is explicit that 'SCPs do not grant permissions... No permissions are granted by an SCP'; an SCP only sets a permission guardrail (maximum), so an SCP can never define or grant the new IP-based access. That immediately disqualifies options A and B, which rely on an SCP to 'allow the new IP range'. (2) Revoking the permissions of two OUs is an organization-wide control. An SCP with a Deny statement attached to an OU is evaluated for every account beneath that OU: 'a deny policy attached to any level in the organization is evaluated for all the OUs and member accounts underneath it.' A permissions boundary (options A and D) instead sets the maximum permissions for a single named IAM entity (here OrganizationAccountAccessRole) and is not an OU-level construct, so it cannot revoke permissions for all principals across the two OUs. Only option C uses bucket resource policies for the IP change and an OU-attached Deny SCP for the OU revocation, so it is correct.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個各自需要正確機制的獨立需求。(1) 變更可讀取 bucket 內容的 IP 範圍是一個「授予存取」的決定,必須寫在每個 S3 bucket 的 resource-based policy(即帶有 aws:SourceIp / NotIpAddress 條件的 bucket policy)中。AWS Organizations 文件明確指出「SCP 不會授予權限……SCP 不授予任何權限」,SCP 只設定權限上限(guardrail),因此 SCP 永遠無法定義或授予新的 IP 存取。這直接排除依賴 SCP「允許新 IP 範圍」的選項 A 與 B。(2) 撤銷兩個 OU 的權限是組織層級的控管。將帶有 Deny 陳述式的 SCP 附加到 OU 時,會對該 OU 下的每個帳戶生效:「附加在組織任一層級的 deny policy 會對其下所有 OU 與成員帳戶評估」。而 permissions boundary(選項 A 與 D)只是為單一具名 IAM 實體(此處的 OrganizationAccountAccessRole)設定權限上限,並非 OU 層級的構造,因此無法撤銷兩個 OU 內所有 principal 的權限。只有選項 C 以 bucket resource policy 處理 IP 變更、並以附加在 OU 的 Deny SCP 處理 OU 撤銷,故為正確答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"It relies on an SCP to 'allow access to the new range of IP addresses' for the buckets, but SCPs never grant permissions, so this cannot establish bucket access; the IP change must be made on the bucket policies. It also uses a permissions boundary on OrganizationAccountAccessRole to revoke OU permissions, but a boundary limits only that one named role per account, not all principals across the two OUs.","why_zh":"它依賴 SCP「允許新 IP 範圍」存取 bucket,但 SCP 從不授予權限,因此無法建立 bucket 存取;IP 變更必須在 bucket policy 上做。它又以 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 的 permissions boundary 來撤銷 OU 權限,但 boundary 只限制每個帳戶中該單一具名角色,並非 OU 內所有 principal。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It uses one SCP to 'allow only the new range of IP addresses to access the S3 buckets', but an SCP cannot grant IP-based access; only the bucket's resource-based policy can define that. The deny SCP attached to the OUs is correct, but the allow half is fundamentally impossible, so the IP-range change requirement is never met.","why_zh":"它用一個 SCP「只允許新 IP 範圍」存取 bucket,但 SCP 無法授予以 IP 為基礎的存取;只有 bucket 的 resource-based policy 能定義。附加到 OU 的 deny SCP 雖正確,但「允許」這一半在原理上不可行,故無法滿足 IP 範圍變更需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The bucket resource-policy half is correct for the IP change, but it uses a permissions boundary on OrganizationAccountAccessRole to revoke the two OUs' permissions. A permissions boundary applies to a single IAM entity, not to an OU, so it cannot revoke permissions for all accounts and principals under the two OUs; an OU-attached Deny SCP is required.","why_zh":"其用 bucket resource policy 處理 IP 變更這一半正確,但它以 OrganizationAccountAccessRole 的 permissions boundary 來撤銷兩個 OU 的權限。permissions boundary 只作用於單一 IAM 實體,而非 OU,因此無法撤銷兩個 OU 下所有帳戶與 principal 的權限;此處需要附加到 OU 的 Deny SCP。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-bucket-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_identity-vs-resource.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":222,"question_en":"A company has started using AWS across several teams. Each team has multiple accounts and unique security profiles. The company manages the accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations. Each account has its own configuration and security controls. The company's DevOps team wants to use preventive and detective controls to govern all accounts. The DevOps team needs to ensure the security of accounts now and in the future as the company creates new accounts in the organization. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司已在多个团队中开始使用 AWS。每个团队拥有多个账户和独特的安全配置文件。该公司 在 AWS 组织中以组织形式管理这些账户。每个账户都有自己的配置和安全控制措施。 该公司的 DevOps 团队希望采用预防性和检测性控制措施来管理所有账户。随着公司不断在组织内创 建新账户，DevOps 团队需要确保现有及未来账户的安全。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Organizations to create OUs that have appropriate SCPs attached for each team. Place team accounts in the appropriate OUs to apply security controls. Create any new team accounts in the appropriate OUs.","B":"Create an AWS Control Tower landing zone. Configure OUs and appropriate controls in AWS Control Tower for the existing teams. Configure trusted access for AWS Control Tower. Enroll the existing accounts in the appropriate OUs that match the appropriate security policies for each team. Use AWS Control Tower to provision any new accounts.","C":"Create AWS CloudFormation stack sets in the organization's management account. Configure a stack set that deploys AWS Config with configuration rules and remediation actions for all controls to each account in the organization. Update the stack sets to deploy to new accounts as the accounts are created.","D":"Configure AWS Config to manage the AWS Config rules across all AWS accounts in the organization. Deploy conformance packs that provide AWS Config rules and remediation actions across the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"利用组织创建具有适合每个团队的适当 SCP（安全策略控制）的组织单位（OU）。将团队账 户置于适当的 OU 中以应用安全控制。在适当的 OU 中创建任何新的团队账户。","B":"创建一个 AWS Control Tower 落地区。为现有团队在 AWS Control Tower 中配置组织单元（OU） 和适当的控制措施。为 AWS Control Tower 配置受信任访问权限。将现有账户注册到与每个团队 相应的安全策略相匹配的适当组织单元中。使用 AWS Control Tower 配置任何新账户。","C":"在组织的管理账户中创建 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈集。配置一个堆栈集，将 AWS Config 及其配 置规则和补救措施部署到组织中的每个账户。当新账户创建时，更新堆栈集以将其部署到新账户。","D":"配置 AWS Config 以管理组织内所有 AWS 账户的 AWS Config 规则。部署一致性包，以在整个组织中提 供 AWS Config 规则和修复操作。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a single managed solution that delivers BOTH preventive and detective controls across all accounts now and for any future accounts created in the organization. AWS Control Tower is the only option that satisfies all of these. Per the AWS docs (How controls work), Control Tower preventive controls are implemented with service control policies (SCPs) and resource control policies (RCPs), while detective controls are implemented with AWS Config rules; Control Tower also offers proactive controls via CloudFormation hooks. You configure OUs and controls, enroll existing accounts into the OUs that match each team's security policies, and use Account Factory to provision and govern any new accounts consistently. Option A (SCPs in OUs) is preventive only with no detection. Options C (StackSets deploying AWS Config rules/remediation) and D (AWS Config conformance packs, which AWS defines as a collection of AWS Config rules and remediation actions) are detective-plus-remediation only and cannot block (prevent) noncompliant actions, so they fail the preventive requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求是一個單一的受管解決方案，能同時提供 preventive（預防性）與 detective（偵測性）控制，涵蓋目前所有帳戶以及未來在組織中新建立的帳戶。只有 AWS Control Tower 能滿足全部條件。根據 AWS 文件（How controls work），Control Tower 的 preventive controls 透過 service control policies (SCPs) 與 resource control policies (RCPs) 實作，detective controls 則透過 AWS Config rules 實作；此外還可透過 CloudFormation hooks 提供 proactive controls。你可以設定 OUs 與控制項，將現有帳戶 enroll 到符合各團隊安全政策的 OU，並使用 Account Factory 一致地佈建與治理任何新帳戶。選項 A（OU 內的 SCPs）只有預防性、缺乏偵測。選項 C（用 StackSets 部署 AWS Config rules/remediation）與選項 D（AWS Config conformance packs，AWS 定義為 AWS Config rules 與 remediation actions 的集合）都只是偵測加修復，無法阻擋（預防）違規動作，因此不符合預防性需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"OUs with SCPs provide only preventive controls (they block disallowed actions). They offer no detective capability to monitor and report noncompliant resources, so this fails the explicit 'detective controls' requirement.","why_zh":"OU 搭配 SCPs 只提供 preventive controls（阻擋不允許的動作），完全沒有偵測能力去監控與回報違規資源，因此不符合明確的 detective controls 需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Deploying AWS Config with rules and remediation via CloudFormation StackSets provides detection and remediation only. AWS Config cannot prevent (block) noncompliant API actions before they occur, so the preventive requirement is unmet. It is also operationally heavier than the managed Control Tower approach.","why_zh":"透過 CloudFormation StackSets 部署 AWS Config 規則與修復，只提供偵測與修復，無法在違規 API 動作發生前加以阻擋（預防），因此不符合預防性需求；且相較於受管的 Control Tower 方式維運負擔較重。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Config conformance packs are defined by AWS as a collection of AWS Config rules and remediation actions deployable across an organization. This delivers detective plus remediation controls only; it provides no preventive (action-blocking) capability, so it fails the preventive requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Config conformance packs 被 AWS 定義為可在組織範圍部署的 AWS Config rules 與 remediation actions 集合，只提供偵測加修復，沒有預防性（阻擋動作）能力，因此不符合預防性需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/what-is-control-tower.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/how-controls-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/preventive-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/detective-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-packs.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":223,"question_en":"A company uses an AWS CodeCommit repository to store its source code and corresponding unit tests. The company has configured an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that includes an AWS CodeBuild project that runs when code is merged to the main branch of the repository. The company wants the CodeBuild project to run the unit tests. If the unit tests pass, the CodeBuild project must tag the most recent commit. How should the company configure the CodeBuild project to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodeCommit 存储库来存储其源代码及相应的单元测试。该公司已配置了一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，其中包含一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目，当代码合并到存储库的主分支时，该项目会运行。 该公司希望 CodeBuild 项目运行单元测试。如果单元测试通过，CodeBuild 项目必须为最近的一次提交添加 标签。 公司应如何配置 CodeBuild 项目以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the CodeBuild project to use native Git to done the CodeCommit repository. Configure the project to run the unit tests. Configure the project to use native Git to create a tag and to push the Git tag to the repository if the code passes the unit tests.","B":"Configure the CodeBuild projed to use native Git to done the CodeCommit repository. Configure the project to run the unit tests. Configure the project to use AWS CLI commands to create a new repository tag in the repository if the code passes the unit tests.","C":"Configure the CodeBuild project to use AWS CLI commands to copy the code from the CodeCommit repository. Configure the project to run the unit tests. Configure the project to use AWS CLI commands to create a new Git tag in the repository if the code passes the unit tests.","D":"Configure the CodeBuild project to use AWS CLI commands to copy the code from the CodeCommit repository. Configure the project to run the unit tests. Configure the project to use AWS CLI commands to create a new repository tag in the repository if the code passes the unit tests."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 CodeBuild 项目以使用原生 Git 访问 CodeCommit 代码库。配置项目运行单元测试。配置项目在代 码通过单元测试时使用原生 Git 创建标签，并将 Git 标签推送到代码库。","B":"配置 CodeBuild 项目以使用原生 Git 操作 CodeCommit 存储库。配置项目以运行单元测试。如果代码通 过单元测试，则配置项目使用 AWS CLI 命令在存储库中创建新的存储库标签。","C":"配置 CodeBuild 项目，使其使用 AWS CLI 命令从 CodeCommit 存储库复制代码。配置项目以运行单元测 试。如果代码通过单元测试，配置项目使用 AWS CLI 命令在存储库中创建新的 Git 标签。","D":"配置 CodeBuild 项目，使其使用 AWS CLI 命令从 CodeCommit 代码库复制代码。配置项目以运行单元测 试。如果代码通过单元测试，配置项目使用 AWS CLI 命令在代码库中创建新的代码库标签。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to tag the most recent commit, which means creating a Git tag (a label attached to a commit), not an AWS resource tag. Per the AWS CodeCommit docs, a Git tag in a CodeCommit repository is created from a local repo connected to the repository using native Git: 'git tag <new-tag-name> <commit-id>', and then pushed to the remote with 'git push <remote> <tag>' or 'git push --tags'. There is no AWS CLI or CodeCommit API operation that creates a Git tag on a commit; the CodeCommit 'tag-resource' CLI command and 'repository tags' apply AWS resource tags (for cost allocation and access control) to the repository resource, not Git tags on commits. To run 'git tag' and 'git push', CodeBuild needs a real Git working copy with refs and history, which a native 'git clone' provides; merely copying files with the AWS CLI (e.g., get-file) does not yield a Git repo capable of tagging and pushing. Therefore option A (use native Git to clone the repo, run the unit tests, then use native Git to create the tag and push it if the tests pass) is the only technically valid approach.","explanation_zh":"需求是要為最新的 commit 加上標籤，也就是建立一個 Git tag（附加在某個 commit 上的標籤），而不是 AWS 的資源標籤（resource tag）。根據 AWS CodeCommit 文件，在 CodeCommit 儲存庫中建立 Git tag 必須從一個已連接到該儲存庫的本機 repo 使用原生 Git 指令：先執行 'git tag <new-tag-name> <commit-id>'，再以 'git push <remote> <tag>' 或 'git push --tags' 推送到遠端。CodeCommit 並沒有任何 AWS CLI 或 API 操作可以在 commit 上建立 Git tag；CodeCommit 的 'tag-resource' CLI 指令與「repository tag」是把 AWS 資源標籤（用於成本分配與存取控制）套用到儲存庫這個資源本身，而非 commit 上的 Git tag。要執行 'git tag' 與 'git push'，CodeBuild 需要一個帶有 refs 與歷史的真正 Git 工作副本，這只能由原生 'git clone' 提供；單純用 AWS CLI 複製檔案（例如 get-file）並不會產生可以打 tag 與推送的 Git repo。因此選項 A（用原生 Git clone 儲存庫、執行單元測試，測試通過後再用原生 Git 建立 tag 並推送）是唯一在技術上可行的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Cloning with native Git is correct, but the tag step is wrong: there is no AWS CLI command to create a Git tag, and 'create a new repository tag' refers to an AWS resource tag on the repository (codecommit tag-resource, used for cost allocation / access control), not a Git tag on the commit. The requirement is to tag the commit, which only native Git can do.","why_zh":"用原生 Git clone 是對的，但打 tag 的步驟錯誤：沒有任何 AWS CLI 指令可以建立 Git tag，而「建立 repository tag」指的是套用在儲存庫資源上的 AWS 資源標籤（codecommit tag-resource，用於成本分配／存取控制），並非 commit 上的 Git tag。需求是要為 commit 打標籤，這只有原生 Git 做得到。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Copying code via AWS CLI (e.g., get-file) does not create a Git working copy with refs and history, so you cannot push a tag back to the repository. Also there is no AWS CLI command that creates a Git tag in CodeCommit; Git tags are created and pushed only with native Git. Both halves are infeasible.","why_zh":"用 AWS CLI 複製程式碼（例如 get-file）不會產生帶有 refs 與歷史的 Git 工作副本，因此無法把 tag 推送回儲存庫。而且沒有任何 AWS CLI 指令可以在 CodeCommit 中建立 Git tag；Git tag 只能用原生 Git 建立並推送。前後兩部分皆不可行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Both steps are wrong: copying code with the AWS CLI does not produce a Git repo capable of pushing tags, and 'create a new repository tag' via the CLI is an AWS resource tag on the repository, not a Git tag on the commit. Neither AWS CLI action satisfies the requirement to tag the most recent commit.","why_zh":"兩個步驟都錯：用 AWS CLI 複製程式碼不會產生可推送 tag 的 Git repo，而用 CLI「建立 repository tag」是套用在儲存庫上的 AWS 資源標籤，並非 commit 上的 Git tag。這兩個 AWS CLI 操作都無法滿足為最新 commit 打標籤的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-create-tag.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/how-to-basic-git.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codecommit/latest/userguide/getting-started.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/tutorials-codecommit-gitclone.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":224,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer manages a company's Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. The cluster runs on several Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Auto Scaling group. The DevOps engineer must implement a solution that logs and reviews all stopped tasks for errors. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师负责管理公司的亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）集群。该集群在多个位于自动扩 展组中的亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行。这位 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个解决方案，用于记录和审查所有已停 止的任务以查找错误。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture task state changes. Send the event to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to investigate stopped tasks.","B":"Configure tasks to write log data in the embedded metric format. Store the logs in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Monitor the ContainerInstanceCount metric for changes.","C":"Configure the EC2 instances to store logs in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a CloudWatch Contributor Insights rule that uses the EC2 instance log data. Use the Contributor Insights rule to investigate stopped tasks.","D":"Configure an EC2 Auto Scaling lifecycle hook for the EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATING scale-in event. Write the SystemEventLog file to Amazon S3. Use Amazon Athena to query the log file for errors."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以捕获任务状态更改。将事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 来调查已停止的任务。","B":"配置任务以嵌入式指标格式写入日志数据。将日志存储在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中。监控 ContainerInstanceCount 指标的变化。","C":"配置 EC2 实例将日志存储在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中。创建一个使用 EC2 实例日志数据的 CloudWatch 贡献者洞察规则。使用贡献者洞察规则来调查已停止的任务。","D":"为 EC2 实例终止（缩放）事件配置 EC2 自动缩放生命周期挂钩。将 SystemEventLog 文件写入 Amazon S3。使用 Amazon Athena 查询日志文件中的错误。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon ECS emits an 'ECS Task State Change' event to EventBridge whenever a task transitions to STOPPED, whether the stop is caused by an essential container exiting, a TaskFailedToStart condition, instance termination, or a Spot interruption. For stopped tasks the event detail includes the stoppedReason and stopCode fields (plus container exit codes), which carry exactly the error information needed to diagnose failures. CloudWatch Logs is a documented EventBridge target ('Adding events to log groups in CloudWatch Logs'), so routing these events to a log group durably persists them beyond the ECS console's native limits (stopped tasks are only visible for one hour). CloudWatch Logs Insights can then query the stored events by stop code or exit code to review all stopped tasks for errors. AWS documents this exact pattern as ECS event capture, which uses EventBridge to forward aws.ecs events into a CloudWatch Logs log group and points users to CloudWatch Logs Insights for advanced queries, so option A meets the requirement end to end.","explanation_zh":"每當 task 轉換為 STOPPED 狀態時（無論是因為必要容器退出、TaskFailedToStart、執行個體終止或 Spot 中斷），Amazon ECS 都會向 EventBridge 發出 'ECS Task State Change' 事件。對於已停止的 task，事件的 detail 內含 stoppedReason 與 stopCode 欄位（以及容器 exit code），正是診斷失敗所需的錯誤資訊。CloudWatch Logs 是 EventBridge 已支援的目標（「Adding events to log groups in CloudWatch Logs」），因此將這些事件導向 log group 可長期保存，突破 ECS 主控台原生限制（已停止的 task 只能檢視一小時）。接著即可用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 依 stop code 或 exit code 查詢所有已停止的 task 來檢視錯誤。AWS 將此模式記載為 ECS event capture：透過 EventBridge 將 aws.ecs 事件轉送到 CloudWatch Logs log group，並引導使用者用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 進行進階查詢。因此選項 A 完整滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Embedded metric format (EMF) is for publishing custom application metrics from log data, not for capturing task stop reasons. Monitoring the ContainerInstanceCount metric only tells you how many container instances are registered; it carries no per-task error, stop code, or exit code information, so it cannot be used to review why individual tasks stopped.","why_zh":"Embedded metric format (EMF) 用於從 log 資料發布自訂應用程式指標，並非用來擷取 task 停止原因。監控 ContainerInstanceCount 指標只能得知已註冊的容器執行個體數量，不含任何個別 task 的錯誤、stop code 或 exit code 資訊，因此無法用來檢視 task 停止的原因。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch Contributor Insights analyzes log data to find top-N contributors (e.g., the IPs or keys generating the most events) over time; it produces ranked time series, not a per-task error review. Relying on EC2 instance OS logs also misses the structured ECS stop reasons and stop codes that EventBridge task state change events provide, so it is the wrong tool for diagnosing why specific tasks stopped.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Contributor Insights 分析 log 資料以找出 top-N 貢獻者（例如產生最多事件的 IP 或鍵值）並隨時間呈現排名時間序列，並非用來逐一檢視 task 錯誤。依賴 EC2 執行個體 OS log 也會遺漏 EventBridge task state change 事件所提供的結構化 ECS 停止原因與 stop code，因此並不適合用來診斷特定 task 停止的原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EC2 Auto Scaling lifecycle hook on EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATING fires only during instance scale-in, so it captures nothing about tasks that stop for the most common reasons (essential container exit, OOM, image pull failure, failed health checks) while the instance keeps running. There is also no standard 'SystemEventLog' file that records ECS task stop reasons, so writing it to S3 and querying with Athena does not surface the required task error data.","why_zh":"在 EC2_INSTANCE_TERMINATING 上的 EC2 Auto Scaling lifecycle hook 只在執行個體縮減時觸發，因此完全擷取不到執行個體仍在運行時最常見的 task 停止原因（必要容器退出、OOM、映像拉取失敗、健康檢查失敗）。此外並不存在記錄 ECS task 停止原因的標準「SystemEventLog」檔案，所以將其寫入 S3 並用 Athena 查詢無法呈現所需的 task 錯誤資料。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/ecs_task_events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/task-lifecycle-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/cloudwatch_event_stream.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/turn-on-event-capture-existing-cluster.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":225,"question_en":"A company wants to deploy a workload on several hundred Amazon EC2 instances. The company will provision the EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group by using a launch template. The workload will pull files from an Amazon S3 bucket, process the data, and put the results into a different S3 bucket. The EC2 instances must have least-privilege permissions and must use temporary security credentials. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司希望在数百台亚马逊 EC2 实例上部署工作负载。该公司将使用启动模板在自动扩展组 中配置 EC2 实例。 工作负载将从 Amazon S3 存储桶中提取文件，处理数据，并将结果放入另一个 S3 存储桶。EC2 实例 必须具有最低权限，并且必须使用临时安全凭证。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM role that has the appropriate permissions for S3 buckets. Add the IAM role to an instance profile.","B":"Update the launch template to include the IAM instance profile.","C":"Create an IAM user that has the appropriate permissions for Amazon S3. Generate a secret key and token.","D":"Create a trust anchor and profile. Attach the IAM role to the profile.","E":"Update the launch template. Modify the user data to use the new secret key and token."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有 S3 存储桶适当权限的 IAM 角色。将 IAM 角色添加到实例配置文件中。","B":"更新启动模板以包含 IAM 实例配置文件。","C":"创建一个具有适当权限访问 Amazon S3 的 IAM 用户。生成一个密钥和令牌。","D":"创建信任锚点和配置文件。将 IAM 角色附加到配置文件。","E":"更新启动模板。修改用户数据以使用新的密钥和令牌。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are least-privilege permissions and temporary security credentials for EC2 instances launched by an Auto Scaling group via a launch template. The canonical AWS pattern is: create an IAM role scoped with only the needed S3 permissions (read from the source bucket, write to the destination bucket) and place it in an instance profile (A), then reference that instance profile in the launch template so every instance the ASG launches assumes the role (B). The IAM doc states you should use an IAM role to manage temporary credentials for applications on EC2, and that the instance profile is the required container that supplies the role's automatically rotated temporary credentials via the Instance Metadata Service. The CloudFormation AWS::EC2::LaunchTemplate IamInstanceProfile property confirms the launch template accepts an instance profile (name or ARN) for use with an Auto Scaling group. Together A and B satisfy both least-privilege and temporary-credentials with no long-term access keys.","explanation_zh":"需求是 least-privilege 權限與 temporary security credentials，給由 Auto Scaling group 透過 launch template 啟動的 EC2 instances 使用。標準 AWS 做法是：建立一個只授予必要 S3 權限（從來源 bucket 讀取、寫入目的 bucket）的 IAM role，並放入 instance profile（A），再於 launch template 中參照該 instance profile，使 ASG 啟動的每個 instance 都承接此 role（B）。IAM 文件指出，應使用 IAM role 為 EC2 上的應用程式管理 temporary credentials，而 instance profile 是必要的容器，透過 Instance Metadata Service 提供 role 自動輪替的 temporary credentials。CloudFormation 的 AWS::EC2::LaunchTemplate IamInstanceProfile 屬性確認 launch template 可接受 instance profile（name 或 ARN），並可搭配 Auto Scaling group 使用。A 與 B 合起來同時滿足 least-privilege 與 temporary credentials，且無需任何長期 access keys。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating an IAM user with a secret key (and token) uses long-term static credentials, which directly violates the temporary-security-credentials requirement and the IAM best practice of avoiding long-term access keys for workloads.","why_zh":"建立帶 secret key 的 IAM user 屬於長期靜態憑證，直接違反 temporary security credentials 的要求，也違反 IAM 不應在 workloads 使用長期 access keys 的最佳實務。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Trust anchors and profiles are IAM Roles Anywhere constructs intended for workloads running OUTSIDE AWS (on-premises servers, containers, or other clouds) that authenticate with X.509 certificates. EC2 instances inside AWS obtain temporary credentials through instance profiles, so this is the wrong mechanism and adds needless complexity.","why_zh":"Trust anchor 與 profile 是 IAM Roles Anywhere 的概念，適用於 AWS 之外（on-premises 伺服器、容器或其他雲）以 X.509 憑證驗證的 workloads。AWS 內的 EC2 instances 透過 instance profile 取得 temporary credentials，因此此選項機制錯誤且增加不必要複雜度。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Injecting a secret key and token into user data hardcodes static long-term credentials onto instances, which is insecure and again fails the temporary-credentials requirement; instance profiles deliver auto-rotated temporary credentials with no user-data secrets.","why_zh":"將 secret key 與 token 寫入 user data 等於在 instances 上硬編碼長期靜態憑證，不安全且同樣不符 temporary credentials 要求；instance profile 可提供自動輪替的 temporary credentials，無需在 user data 中放憑證。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_switch-role-ec2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_switch-role-ec2_instance-profiles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-ec2-launchtemplate-iaminstanceprofile.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/introduction.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":226,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CodeDeploy to automate software deployment. The deployment must meet these requirements: • A number of instances must be available to serve traffic during the deployment. Traffic must be balanced across those instances, and the instances must automatically heal in the event of failure. • A new fleet of instances must be launched for deploying a new revision automatically, with no manual provisioning. • Traffic must be rerouted to the new environment to half of the new instances at a time. The deployment should succeed if traffic is rerouted to at least half of the instances: otherwise, it should fail. • Before routing traffic to the new fleet of instances, the temporary files generated during the deployment process must be deleted. • At the end of a successful deployment, the original instances in the deployment group must be deleted immediately to reduce costs. How can a DevOps engineer meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodeDeploy 来实现软件部署的自动化。该部署必须满足以下要求： •在部署期间必须有若干实例可用以承载流量。流量必须在这些实例之间均衡分配，并且在出现故 障时实例必须能够自动恢复。•必须能够自动为部署新版本启动新的实例群，无需人工配置。 • 流量必须每次重新定向到新环境中的半数新实例。如果流量重新定向到至少半数实例，则部署 应成功；否则，部署应失败。 在将流量路由到新的实例群组之前，必须删除部署过程中生成的临时文件。 在成功部署结束时，必须立即删除部署组中的原始实例以降低成本。 DevOps 工程师如何才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use an Application Load Balancer and an in-place deployment. Associate the Auto Scaling group with the deployment group. Use the Automatically copy Auto Scaling group option, and use CodeDeployDefault.OneAtAtime as the deployment configuration. Instruct AWS CodeDeploy to terminate the original instances in the deployment group, and use the AllowTraffic hook within appspec.yml to delete the temporary files.","B":"Use an Application Load Balancer and a blue/green deployment. Associate the Auto Scaling group and Application Load Balancer target group with the deployment group. Use the Automatically copy Auto Scaling group option, create a custom deployment configuration with minimum healthy hosts defined as 50%, and assign the configuration to the deployment group. Instruct AWS CodeDeploy to terminate the original instances in the deployment group, and use the BeforeBlockTraffic hook within appspec.yml to delete the temporary files.","C":"Use an Application Load Balancer and a blue/green deployment. Associate the Auto Scaling group and the Application Load Balancer target group with the deployment group. Use the Automatically copy Auto Scaling group option, and use CodeDeployDefault.HalfAtAtime as the deployment configuration. Instruct AWS CodeDeploy to terminate the original instances in the deployment group, and use the BeforeAllowTraffic hook within appspec.yml to delete the temporary files.","D":"Use an Application Load Balancer and an in-place deployment. Associate the Auto Scaling group and Application Load Balancer target group with the deployment group. Use the Automatically copy Auto Scaling group option, and use CodeDeployDefault.AllatOnce as a deployment configuration. Instruct AWS CodeDeploy to terminate the original instances in the deployment group, and use the BlockTraffic hook within appspec.yml to delete the temporary files."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用应用负载均衡器和原地部署。将自动扩展组与部署组相关联。使用“自动复制自动扩展组” 选项，并使用 CodeDeployDefault.OneAtAtime 作为部署配置。指示 AWS CodeDeploy 终止部署 组中的原始实例，并在 appspec.yml 中使用 AllowTraffic 钩子来删除临时文件。","B":"使用应用负载均衡器和蓝/绿部署。将自动扩展组和应用负载均衡器目标组与部署组关联。使用 “自动复制自动扩展组”选项，创建一个自定义部署配置，将最小健康主机定义为 50%，并将 该配置分配给部署组。指示 AWS CodeDeploy 终止部署组中的原始实例，并在 appspec.yml 中使 用 BeforeBlockTraffic 钩子删除临时文件。","C":"使用应用负载均衡器和蓝/绿部署。将自动扩展组和应用负载均衡器目标组与部署组相关联。使用 “自动复制自动扩展组”选项，并使用 CodeDeployDefault.HalfAtAtime 作为部署配置。指示 AWS CodeDeploy 终止部署组中的原始实例，并在 appspec.yml 中使用 BeforeAllowTraffic 钩子删 除临时文件。","D":"使用应用负载均衡器和原地部署。将自动扩展组和应用负载均衡器目标组与部署组相关联。使用 “自动复制自动扩展组”选项，并使用 CodeDeployDefault.AllAtOnce 作为部署配置。指示 AWS CodeDeploy 终止部署组中的原始实例，并使用 在 appspec.yml 中使用 BlockTraffic 钩子删除临时文件。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Every requirement points to a blue/green deployment, which rules out the in-place options A and D. Only blue/green launches a brand-new fleet automatically via the 'Automatically copy Auto Scaling group' option (in-place reuses the existing instances), and only blue/green lets CodeDeploy terminate the original instances after success to cut cost. The traffic rule -- 'reroute to half of the new instances at a time; succeed if traffic is rerouted to at least half, otherwise fail' -- is the verbatim definition of CodeDeployDefault.HalfAtATime for blue/green traffic rerouting: 'Routes traffic to up to half the instances in the replacement environment at a time. Succeeds if rerouting to at least half of the instances succeeds. Otherwise, fails.' A custom 50% minimumHealthyHosts config (option B) governs how many hosts must remain healthy during the deployment-to-replacement phase, not the half-at-a-time traffic-shift success/fail semantics, so it does not match. The hook must delete temporary files on the NEW fleet 'before routing traffic to the new fleet,' which is BeforeAllowTraffic ('run tasks on instances before they are registered with a load balancer'). The lifecycle event hook availability table confirms BeforeAllowTraffic runs on blue/green Replacement (new) instances, whereas BeforeBlockTraffic (option B) is available only on the Original instances before they are deregistered -- wrong fleet, wrong timing. Associating both the Auto Scaling group and the ALB target group with the deployment group delivers the load balancing and automatic healing. Option C is the only choice that satisfies every requirement.","explanation_zh":"所有需求都指向 blue/green 部署，這排除了採用 in-place 的選項 A 與 D。只有 blue/green 能透過『Automatically copy Auto Scaling group』選項自動啟動全新的執行個體群（in-place 會重用既有執行個體），也只有 blue/green 允許 CodeDeploy 在成功後終止原始執行個體以降低成本。流量規則『一次將流量導向一半的新執行個體；若至少一半成功導流則部署成功，否則失敗』正是 blue/green 流量重新導向時 CodeDeployDefault.HalfAtATime 的逐字定義：『一次將流量導向取代環境中最多一半的執行個體；若至少一半成功則成功，否則失敗。』自訂 50% minimumHealthyHosts（選項 B）控制的是『部署到取代環境』階段須保持健康的主機數量，而非 half-at-a-time 的流量切換成功／失敗語意，故不符。Hook 必須在『將流量導向新執行個體之前』於新執行個體上刪除暫存檔，亦即 BeforeAllowTraffic（『在執行個體註冊到負載平衡器之前執行任務』）。生命週期事件 hook 可用性表確認 BeforeAllowTraffic 於 blue/green 取代（新）執行個體上執行，而 BeforeBlockTraffic（選項 B）僅於原始執行個體取消註冊前可用——對象與時機皆錯誤。將 Auto Scaling group 與 ALB target group 同時關聯到部署群組，可提供負載平衡與自動修復。選項 C 是唯一滿足所有需求的答案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses an in-place deployment, which reuses existing instances and cannot automatically launch a new fleet (the 'Automatically copy Auto Scaling group' option is a blue/green concept). CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime does not match the half-at-a-time traffic rule, and 'AllowTraffic' is a CodeDeploy-reserved lifecycle event that cannot run scripts.","why_zh":"使用 in-place 部署會重用既有執行個體，無法自動啟動新一批執行個體（『Automatically copy Auto Scaling group』是 blue/green 的概念）。CodeDeployDefault.OneAtATime 不符合 half-at-a-time 流量規則，且 AllowTraffic 是 CodeDeploy 保留的生命週期事件，無法執行腳本。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A custom config with 50% minimumHealthyHosts governs how many hosts stay healthy during the deployment-to-replacement phase, not the 'half of new instances at a time / succeed at >=50%' traffic-rerouting semantics that HalfAtATime defines. Per the lifecycle hook availability table, BeforeBlockTraffic runs only on the Original instances before they are deregistered, not on the new fleet before traffic is routed to it.","why_zh":"自訂 50% minimumHealthyHosts 控制的是『部署到取代環境』階段須保持健康的主機數量，而非 HalfAtATime 所定義的『一次一半新執行個體／至少 50% 成功』流量重新導向語意。依生命週期 hook 可用性表，BeforeBlockTraffic 僅於原始執行個體取消註冊前執行，並非在新執行個體導流之前執行。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An in-place deployment cannot auto-launch a new fleet. CodeDeployDefault.AllAtOnce routes traffic to all instances at once rather than half at a time, and 'BlockTraffic' is a CodeDeploy-reserved lifecycle event that cannot run scripts.","why_zh":"In-place 部署無法自動啟動新一批執行個體。CodeDeployDefault.AllAtOnce 一次將流量導向所有執行個體而非一半，且 BlockTraffic 是 CodeDeploy 保留的生命週期事件，無法執行腳本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/integrations-aws-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-groups-create-blue-green.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":227,"question_en":"A company needs to adopt a multi-account strategy to deploy its applications and the associated CI/CD infrastructure. The company has created an organization in AWS Organizations that has all features enabled. The company has configured AWS Control Tower and has set up a landing zone. The company needs to use AWS Control Tower controls (guardrails) in all AWS accounts in the organization. The company must create the accounts for a multi-environment application and must ensure that all accounts are configured to an initial baseline. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司需要采用多账户策略来部署其应用程序以及相关的持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）基础设施。 该公司已在 AWS 组织中创建了一个组织，并启用了所有功能。该公司已配置了 AWS 控制塔，并设 置了一个着陆区。 该公司需要在其组织内的所有 AWS 账户中使用 AWS 控制塔控制措施（防护栏）。公司必须为一个多 环境应用程序创建账户，并且必须确保所有账户都配置为初始基线。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Control Tower Account Factory Customization (AFC) blueprint that uses the baseline configuration. Use AWS Control Tower Account Factory to provision a dedicated AWS account for each environment and a CI/CD account by using the blueprint.","B":"Use AWS Control Tower Account Factory to provision a dedicated AWS account for each environment and a CI/CD account. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to apply the baseline configuration to the new accounts.","C":"Use Organizations to provision a multi-environment AWS account and a CI/CD account. In the Organizations management account, create an AWS Lambda function that assumes the Organizations access role to apply the baseline configuration to the new accounts.","D":"Use Organizations to provision a dedicated AWS account for each environment, an audit account, and a CI/CD account. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to apply the baseline configuration to the new accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个使用基准配置的 AWS 控制塔账户工厂自定义（AFC）蓝图。使用 AWS 控制塔账户工厂通 过该蓝图为每个环境配置一个专用的 AWS 账户，并配置一个持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）账户。","B":"使用 AWS 控制塔账户工厂为每个环境和持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）账户配置专用的 AWS 账户。 使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将基础配置应用于新账户。","C":"使用组织服务来配置一个多环境的 AWS 账户和一个 CI/CD 账户。在组织管理账户中，创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数通过承担组织访问角色来将基线配置应用于新账户。","D":"利用组织为每个环境、审计账户和 CI/CD 账户配置专用的 AWS 账户。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将基础配置应用于新账户。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The landing zone is already deployed, so the lowest-overhead native path is AWS Control Tower Account Factory Customization (AFC). With AFC you define a blueprint (a Service Catalog product backed by a CloudFormation or Terraform template) that describes the resources and baseline configuration to apply automatically whenever an account is provisioned. The AWS docs state that after the one-time setup, 'AWS Control Tower automates this process for future provisioning, so you don't have to maintain any pipelines,' and 'customized accounts are available for use immediately after the resources are provisioned.' Accounts created through Account Factory are placed in Control Tower-registered OUs that have the AWSControlTowerBaseline enabled, so Control Tower controls (guardrails) are applied automatically. A single AFC blueprint therefore provisions the per-environment accounts and the CI/CD account AND applies the initial baseline to each, satisfying every requirement (controls everywhere, the required accounts, and an initial baseline) with the least operational overhead, instead of bolting on a separate StackSet (B) or a custom Lambda (C/D).","explanation_zh":"由於 landing zone 已部署，最省維運的原生做法是使用 AWS Control Tower Account Factory Customization (AFC)。AFC 讓你定義一個 blueprint（一個以 CloudFormation 或 Terraform 範本為基礎的 Service Catalog 產品），描述每次佈建帳戶時自動套用的資源與 baseline 設定。AWS 文件指出，完成一次性設定後，「AWS Control Tower 會自動化後續的佈建流程，因此你不需要維護任何 pipeline」，且「客製化帳戶在資源佈建完成後即可立即使用」。透過 Account Factory 建立的帳戶會被放入已註冊且啟用 AWSControlTowerBaseline 的 Control Tower OU，因此 Control Tower controls（guardrails）會自動套用。所以單一 AFC blueprint 即可佈建每個環境帳戶與 CI/CD 帳戶，並對每個帳戶套用初始 baseline，以最低維運負擔滿足所有需求（所有帳戶皆有 controls、所需帳戶、初始 baseline），而不需另外加上獨立的 StackSet（B）或自訂 Lambda（C/D）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Provisioning via Account Factory is correct and these accounts do inherit Control Tower controls, but layering a separate CloudFormation StackSets mechanism to apply the baseline adds a second component to set up and maintain. AFC bundles provisioning and baseline into one native mechanism with no pipelines to maintain, so it is lower operational overhead than Account Factory plus StackSets.","why_zh":"用 Account Factory 佈建是對的，這些帳戶也會繼承 Control Tower controls，但另外再用 CloudFormation StackSets 套用 baseline 會多出一個要設定與維護的元件。AFC 把佈建與 baseline 整合進單一原生機制且無需維護 pipeline，因此比 Account Factory 加 StackSets 的維運負擔更低。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Provisioning accounts directly through AWS Organizations bypasses Control Tower Account Factory, so the accounts are not automatically enrolled in Control Tower-governed OUs and do not get the controls automatically. A custom Lambda that assumes the Organizations access role is high operational overhead, and provisioning a single 'multi-environment' account fails the dedicated per-environment requirement.","why_zh":"直接透過 AWS Organizations 佈建帳戶會繞過 Control Tower Account Factory，帳戶不會自動加入受 Control Tower 治理的 OU，也不會自動套用 controls。自建一個假設 Organizations access role 的 Lambda 維運負擔很高，且只佈建單一『多環境』帳戶也不符合每個環境各一個專用帳戶的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Like C, accounts are provisioned directly via Organizations rather than Account Factory, so Control Tower controls are not automatically applied to them. It also introduces an unrequested audit account and relies on a separate StackSets mechanism, adding overhead while failing the 'controls in all accounts' requirement.","why_zh":"與 C 類似，帳戶是直接透過 Organizations 佈建而非 Account Factory，因此 Control Tower controls 不會自動套用到這些帳戶。它還多了一個非需求的 audit 帳戶並依賴額外的 StackSets 機制，增加負擔且不符合『所有帳戶都套用 controls』的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/af-customization-page.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/methods-of-provisioning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/account-factory.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/types-of-baselines.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":228,"question_en":"A DevOps team has created a Custom Lambda rule in AWS Config. The rule monitors Amazon Elastic Container Repository (Amazon ECR) policy statements for ecr:* actions. When a noncompliant repository is detected, Amazon EventBridge uses Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to route the notification to a security team. When the custom AWS Config rule is evaluated, the AWS Lambda function fails to run. Which solution will resolve the issue?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队在 AWS Config 中创建了一条自定义的 Lambda 规则。该规则会监控 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）策略语句中的 ecr:* 操作。一旦检测到不符合规定的存储库， Amazon EventBridge 就会使用 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）将通知转发给安全团 队。 当自定义的 AWS Config 规则被评估时，AWS Lambda 函数无法运行。 哪种解决方案能解决这个问题？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the Lambda function's resource policy to grant AWS Config permission to invoke the function.","B":"Modify the SNS topic policy to include configuration changes for EventBridge to publish to the SNS topic.","C":"Modify the Lambda function's execution role to include configuration changes for custom AWS Config rules.","D":"Modify all the ECR repository policies to grant AWS Config access to the necessary ECR API actions."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 Lambda 函数的资源策略，授予 AWS Config 调用该函数的权限。","B":"修改 SNS 主题策略，以包含针对 EventBridge 发布到 SNS 主题的配置更改。","C":"修改 Lambda 函数的执行角色，以包含自定义 AWS Config 规则的配置更改。","D":"修改所有 ECR 存储库策略，授予 AWS Config 对必要 ECR API 操作的访问权限。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"An AWS Config Custom Lambda rule works by AWS Config invoking the associated Lambda function each time the rule is evaluated (on configuration changes or periodically). For one AWS service to call lambda:InvokeFunction on a function, that function must have a resource-based (resource) policy statement granting the calling service principal permission to invoke it. For AWS Config that principal is config.amazonaws.com. When you create the rule in the AWS Config console this permission is added automatically, but when the rule/function is wired up via API, CLI, or CloudFormation the lambda:AddPermission / AWS::Lambda::Permission statement for config.amazonaws.com is easily omitted. If it is missing, AWS Config cannot invoke the function and the function 'fails to run' during evaluation, which is exactly the symptom described. Modifying the Lambda function's resource policy to grant AWS Config permission to invoke it resolves the failure, so A is correct.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config Custom Lambda rule 的運作方式是：每次規則評估時（因設定變更觸發或定期觸發），由 AWS Config 去呼叫所關聯的 Lambda function。要讓某個 AWS 服務能對一個 function 呼叫 lambda:InvokeFunction，該 function 必須有一條 resource-based（resource）policy 陳述句，授權呼叫端的 service principal 進行 invoke。對 AWS Config 而言，這個 principal 是 config.amazonaws.com。若透過 AWS Config console 建立規則，此權限會自動加入；但若改用 API、CLI 或 CloudFormation 連接規則與 function，常會漏掉針對 config.amazonaws.com 的 lambda:AddPermission / AWS::Lambda::Permission 陳述句。一旦缺少此權限，AWS Config 便無法 invoke 該 function，評估時 function 就會『無法執行』，正符合題目描述的症狀。因此修改 Lambda function 的 resource policy，授權 AWS Config invoke 該 function，即可解決問題，故 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The SNS topic policy and EventBridge routing are the downstream notification/alerting path that runs only AFTER a noncompliant resource is detected. They have no bearing on whether AWS Config can invoke the Lambda function during rule evaluation, so changing the SNS topic policy does not fix a function that fails to run.","why_zh":"SNS topic policy 與 EventBridge 路由屬於偵測到不合規資源『之後』才執行的下游通知/告警路徑，與 AWS Config 在規則評估時能否 invoke Lambda function 無關，因此修改 SNS topic policy 無法解決 function 無法執行的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The Lambda execution role governs what the function is allowed to do once it is already running (for example config:PutEvaluations or reading resource configuration). It does not control whether AWS Config is permitted to invoke the function; invocation is governed by the resource-based policy. A missing execution-role permission would let the function start but fail mid-execution, not 'fail to run.' There is also no IAM permission called 'configuration changes for custom AWS Config rules.'","why_zh":"Lambda execution role 控制 function『開始執行後』被允許做的事（例如 config:PutEvaluations 或讀取資源設定），並不決定 AWS Config 是否有權 invoke 該 function；invoke 是由 resource-based policy 控制。若是 execution role 缺權限，function 會開始執行但中途失敗，而非『無法執行』。此外也不存在名為『configuration changes for custom AWS Config rules』的 IAM 權限。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"ECR repository policies control access to the ECR repositories themselves. The custom Lambda evaluates ECR policy statements using the configuration data AWS Config supplies and the AWS Config API, not by calling ECR through repository resource policies. Granting Config access on ECR repos does not affect whether the function can be invoked, so it does not resolve the failure.","why_zh":"ECR repository policy 控制的是對 ECR repository 本身的存取。custom Lambda 是透過 AWS Config 提供的設定資料與 AWS Config API 來評估 ECR 的 policy 陳述句，並非透過 repository resource policy 呼叫 ECR。在 ECR repo 上授權 Config 存取，並不影響 function 是否能被 invoke，因此無法解決此故障。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_develop-rules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_develop-rules_lambda-functions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/permissions-function-services.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/access-control-resource-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/api/API_AddPermission.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":229,"question_en":"A developer is creating a proof of concept for a new software as a service (SaaS) application. The application is in a shared development AWS account that is part of an organization in AWS Organizations. The developer needs to create service-linked IAM roles for the AWS services that are being considered for the proof of concept. The solution needs to give the developer the ability to create and configure the service-linked roles only. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位开发人员正在为一款新的软件即服务（SaaS）应用程序创建概念验证。该应用程序位于 AWS 组织 中一个组织所属的共享开发 AWS 账户内。 开发人员需要为正在考虑用于概念验证的 AWS 服务创建服务相关 IAM 角色。解决方案需要赋予开发人 员仅创建和配置服务相关角色的能力。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM user for the developer in the organization's management account. Configure a cross- account role in the development account for the developer to use. Limit the scope of the cross-account role to common services.","B":"Add the developer to an IAM group. Attach the PowerUserAccess managed policy to the IAM group. Enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) on the user account.","C":"Add an SCP to the development account in Organizations. Configure the SCP with a Deny rule for iam:* to limit the developer's access.","D":"Create an IAM role that has the necessary IAM access to allow the developer to create policies and roles. Create and attach a permissions boundary to the role. Grant the developer access to assume the role."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中为开发人员创建一个 IAM 用户。在开发账户中为开发人员配置一个跨账户角色 供其使用。将跨账户角色的权限范围限制在常见服务上。","B":"将开发人员添加到 IAM 组。将 PowerUserAccess 管理策略附加到 IAM 组。在用户账户上强制实施 多因素身份验证（MFA）。","C":"在“组织”中将一个 SCP 添加到开发账户。使用 Deny 规则配置该 SCP，限制对 iam:* 的访问权 限，从而限制开发人员的访问权限。","D":"创建一个具有必要 IAM 访问权限的 IAM 角色，以允许开发人员创建策略和角色。为该角色创建并附 加权限边界。授予开发人员承担该角色的权限。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Creating a service-linked role requires an IAM entity (user or role) that actually HOLDS IAM permissions such as iam:CreateServiceLinkedRole, iam:AttachRolePolicy, and iam:PutRolePolicy (per the 'Service-linked role permissions' section of the Create a service-linked role doc). To grant these capabilities to the developer while ensuring they can do nothing beyond creating/configuring the roles ('only'), AWS's canonical least-privilege pattern is a permissions boundary: a managed policy that sets the MAXIMUM permissions an identity-based policy can grant, so effective permissions are the intersection of the identity policy and the boundary. Option D does exactly this -- an IAM role with the necessary IAM access, capped by an attached permissions boundary, that the developer assumes. Option B fails because PowerUserAccess grants access to AWS services but explicitly EXCLUDES IAM and Organizations management, so it cannot create service-linked roles, and MFA is irrelevant to scoping. Option C fails because an SCP with Deny iam:* blocks IAM entirely (preventing SLR creation), and SCPs never grant permissions -- they are guardrails only. Option A fails because creating an IAM user in the management account violates least-privilege guidance for the management account, and a cross-account role scoped to 'common services' neither targets service-linked-role creation nor enforces the 'only' constraint.","explanation_zh":"建立 service-linked role 需要一個實際擁有 IAM 權限（例如 iam:CreateServiceLinkedRole、iam:AttachRolePolicy、iam:PutRolePolicy）的 IAM 實體（user 或 role），這在 Create a service-linked role 文件的「Service-linked role permissions」一節中有明確說明。為了讓開發者擁有這些能力，同時確保他「只能」建立與設定這些 role 而不能做其他事，AWS 的標準最小權限模式是使用 permissions boundary：這是一個受管理的政策，用來設定 identity-based policy 所能授予的「最大」權限，因此實際生效權限是 identity policy 與 boundary 的交集。選項 D 正是如此做法——建立一個具備必要 IAM 存取權的 IAM role，附加 permissions boundary 來限制範圍，並讓開發者去 assume 該 role。選項 B 不成立，因為 PowerUserAccess 雖授予對 AWS 服務的存取，但明確「排除」IAM 與 Organizations 管理，因此無法建立 service-linked role，而 MFA 與限縮範圍無關。選項 C 不成立，因為以 SCP Deny iam:* 會完全封鎖 IAM（反而阻止建立 SLR），且 SCP 永遠不授予權限，只是護欄。選項 A 不成立，因為在 management account 建立 IAM user 違反 management account 的最小權限指引，而限定於「common services」的跨帳戶 role 既未針對 service-linked-role 的建立，也無法強制執行「只能」的限制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Placing an IAM user in the Organizations management account violates least-privilege management-account practice, and a cross-account role 'limited to common services' does not specifically scope to creating/configuring service-linked roles only.","why_zh":"在 Organizations 管理帳戶建立 IAM 使用者違反管理帳戶最小使用原則，且『限於 common services』的跨帳戶 role 並未專門限縮到僅建立/設定 service-linked roles。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"PowerUserAccess grants broad access to most services but explicitly excludes IAM and Organizations management actions, so the developer could not create service-linked roles; it is also far broader than 'service-linked roles only.' MFA does not address the scoping requirement.","why_zh":"PowerUserAccess 授予大多數服務的廣泛存取，但明確排除 IAM 與 Organizations 管理動作，因此無法建立 service-linked roles；範圍也遠超『僅 service-linked roles』。啟用 MFA 並未解決限縮範圍的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP with Deny iam:* blocks all IAM actions account-wide, preventing the developer from creating any service-linked role. SCPs are guardrails that never grant permissions, so this cannot enable the required capability.","why_zh":"以 SCP Deny iam:* 會在整個帳戶層級封鎖所有 IAM 動作，使開發者無法建立任何 service-linked role。SCP 為防護邊界且從不授予權限，故無法提供所需能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_create-service-linked-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries_delegate.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":230,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company wants its monitoring system to receive an alert when a root user logs in. The company also needs a dashboard to display any log activity that the root user generates. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司希望其监控系统在根用户登录时收到警 报。该公司还需要一个仪表板来显示根用户生成的任何日志活动。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Config with a multi-account aggregator. Configure log forwarding to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","B":"Create an Amazon QuickSight dashboard that uses an Amazon CloudWatch Logs query.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs metric filter to match root user login events. Configure a CloudWatch alarm and an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to send alerts to the company's monitoring system.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to match root user login events. Configure the filter to forward events to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Configure the SNS topic to send alerts to the company's monitoring system.","E":"Create an AWS CloudTrail organization trail. Configure the organization trail to send events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs.","F":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard that uses a CloudWatch Logs Insights query."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用多账户聚合器启用 AWS Config。配置日志转发至 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。","B":"创建一个使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 查询的 Amazon QuickSight 仪表板。","C":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器以匹配根用户登录事件。配置一个 CloudWatch 警报 和一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，以便向公司的监控系统发送警报。","D":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 订阅筛选器以匹配根用户登录事件。配置筛选器将事件转发到 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS） 主题。配置 SNS 主题以向公司的监控系统发 送警报。","E":"创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 组织跟踪。配置组织跟踪以将事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。","F":"创建一个使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询的 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板。"},"answer":["C","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has three parts solved by a chained pipeline. (E) Create a CloudTrail organization trail and configure it to send events to CloudWatch Logs: per AWS docs an organization trail 'logs events for the management account and all member accounts in the organization,' which includes root console-login (ConsoleLogin) events, so this satisfies the AWS Organizations multi-account scope and provides the log source in CloudWatch Logs. (C) Create a CloudWatch Logs metric filter to match root user login events, then a CloudWatch alarm wired to an Amazon SNS topic that notifies the monitoring system; AWS documents exactly this 'metric filter + alarm + SNS' pattern in 'Creating CloudWatch alarms for CloudTrail events.' (F) Create a CloudWatch dashboard backed by a CloudWatch Logs Insights query to display the root user's log activity; the 'Add query to dashboard' doc confirms Logs Insights query results can be added directly to a CloudWatch dashboard. The decisive distinction versus the trap option D is that the SubscriptionFilters doc states a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter can only deliver to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or Amazon OpenSearch Service, never directly to an SNS topic, so alerting must go through a metric filter plus alarm (C), not a subscription filter (D).","explanation_zh":"需求分三部分,以一條串接的管線解決。(E) 建立 CloudTrail organization trail 並設定將事件送到 CloudWatch Logs:依 AWS 文件,organization trail「會記錄管理帳戶與組織內所有成員帳戶的事件」,其中包含 root console 登入(ConsoleLogin)事件,因此滿足 AWS Organizations 多帳戶範圍,並把日誌來源放進 CloudWatch Logs。(C) 建立 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 比對 root 使用者登入事件,再以 CloudWatch alarm 連到 Amazon SNS topic 通知監控系統;AWS 在「Creating CloudWatch alarms for CloudTrail events」文件中正是記載這套「metric filter + alarm + SNS」標準做法。(F) 建立以 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢為基礎的 CloudWatch dashboard 來顯示 root 使用者的日誌活動;「Add query to dashboard」文件確認 Logs Insights 查詢結果可直接加入 CloudWatch dashboard。與陷阱選項 D 的關鍵區別在於:SubscriptionFilters 文件明載 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 只能將資料送到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 Amazon OpenSearch Service,無法直接送到 SNS topic,因此告警必須透過 metric filter 加 alarm(C),而非 subscription filter(D)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config with a multi-account aggregator tracks resource configuration state and compliance, not API or authentication activity. It does not capture root user console login events (those are CloudTrail ConsoleLogin events), and Config is not the mechanism for forwarding sign-in activity to CloudWatch Logs, so it cannot supply the login source data this scenario needs.","why_zh":"AWS Config 多帳戶 aggregator 追蹤資源組態狀態與合規,而非 API 或驗證活動。它不會擷取 root 使用者 console 登入事件(那是 CloudTrail 的 ConsoleLogin 事件),也不是將登入活動轉送到 CloudWatch Logs 的機制,因此無法提供本情境所需的登入來源資料。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon QuickSight is a BI tool that does not natively query CloudWatch Logs; there is no 'CloudWatch Logs query' data source for QuickSight. The native, intended way to dashboard log activity is a CloudWatch dashboard fed by a Logs Insights query (option F).","why_zh":"Amazon QuickSight 是 BI 工具,並不原生查詢 CloudWatch Logs;QuickSight 沒有所謂的「CloudWatch Logs 查詢」資料來源。要把日誌活動做成儀表板,原生且正確的做法是用 Logs Insights 查詢驅動的 CloudWatch dashboard(選項 F)。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the primary trap. Per the AWS SubscriptionFilters documentation, a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter can only forward log data to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or Amazon OpenSearch Service. It cannot send events directly to an SNS topic, so this configuration is technically impossible as written; alerting on a log pattern requires a metric filter plus a CloudWatch alarm targeting SNS (option C).","why_zh":"這是主要陷阱。依 AWS SubscriptionFilters 文件,CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 只能將日誌資料轉送到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 Amazon OpenSearch Service,無法直接把事件送到 SNS topic,因此如題所述的設定技術上不可行;對日誌模式發出告警需使用 metric filter 加上以 SNS 為目標的 CloudWatch alarm(選項 C)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/creating-trail-organization.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudwatch-alarms-for-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/send-cloudtrail-events-to-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_ExportQueryResults.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":231,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. A DevOps engineer must ensure that all users who access the AWS Management Console are authenticated through the company’s corporate identity provider (IdP). Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。一位 DevOps 工程师必须确保所有访问 AWS 管 理控制台的用户都通过公司的企业身份提供商（IdP）进行身份验证。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon GuardDuty with a delegated administrator account. Use GuardDuty to enforce denial of IAM user logins.","B":"Use AWS IAM Identity Center to configure identity federation with SAML 2.0.","C":"Create a permissions boundary in AWS IAM Identity Center to deny password logins for IAM users.","D":"Create IAM groups in the Organizations management account to apply consistent permissions for all IAM users.","E":"Create an SCP in Organizations to deny password creation for IAM users."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用具有委托管理员权限的账户来使用 Amazon GuardDuty。利用 GuardDuty 来实施拒绝访问。 IAM 用户登录。","B":"使用 AWS IAM 身份中心通过 SAML 2.0 配置身份联合。","C":"在 AWS IAM 身份中心创建权限边界，以禁止 IAM 用户使用密码登录。","D":"在组织管理账户中创建 IAM 组，以便为所有 IAM 用户应用一致的权限。","E":"在组织中创建一个 SCP（服务控制策略），以禁止为 IAM 用户创建密码。"},"answer":["B","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"research":{"verdict":["B","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: provide an authentication path through the corporate IdP, and prevent users from bypassing it with native IAM credentials. B is AWS's canonical way to authenticate workforce users to the Management Console through a corporate IdP: the IAM docs state that 'IAM Identity Center supports identity federation with SAML 2.0 to provide federated single sign-on access for users... including the AWS Management Console,' and IAM Identity Center is the recommended federation type for human users across multiple Organizations accounts. E closes the backdoor: an SCP is the organization-wide guardrail that restricts IAM users and roles (including the root user) in every member account, so denying IAM-user password/login-profile actions (for example iam:CreateLoginProfile and iam:CreateUser) stops anyone from creating an IAM-user console password that would bypass the federated IdP. Together, B establishes the IdP authentication path and E enforces that it is the only path, meeting the requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩部分：提供透過公司 IdP 的驗證路徑，並防止使用者改用原生 IAM 憑證繞過該路徑。B 是 AWS 讓工作人員透過公司 IdP 登入 Management Console 的標準做法：IAM 文件明確指出 IAM Identity Center 支援 SAML 2.0 身分聯合，為使用者提供聯合單一登入（含 AWS Management Console），且 IAM Identity Center 是跨多個 Organizations 帳戶管理人員身分的建議聯合方式。E 則封堵後門：SCP 是組織層級的護欄，會限制每個成員帳戶內的 IAM 使用者與角色（含 root user），因此拒絕建立 IAM 使用者密碼／login profile 的動作（例如 iam:CreateLoginProfile、iam:CreateUser），可阻止任何人建立會繞過聯合 IdP 的 IAM 使用者主控台密碼。B 建立 IdP 驗證路徑、E 強制該路徑為唯一路徑，兩者結合即可滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that analyzes data sources and generates security findings; it has no capability to enforce or deny IAM user console logins. Using a delegated administrator only centralizes GuardDuty management across the organization, it does not block authentication.","why_zh":"Amazon GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務，分析資料來源並產生安全發現項目，無法強制執行或拒絕 IAM 使用者的主控台登入。委派管理員只是集中管理整個組織的 GuardDuty，並不會封鎖驗證。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This conflates unrelated concepts. Permissions boundaries are an IAM feature set on IAM users/roles, not something created 'in IAM Identity Center,' and they cap the maximum API permissions of a principal rather than 'deny password logins.' Console password sign-in is not an API action a permissions boundary blocks in this way.","why_zh":"此選項混淆了不相關的概念。Permissions boundary 是套用於 IAM 使用者／角色的 IAM 功能，並非在 IAM Identity Center 建立，且它限制 principal 的最大 API 權限上限，而非「拒絕密碼登入」。主控台密碼登入並非權限界限能以此方式封鎖的 API 動作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"IAM groups only organize permissions for IAM users that already exist; they do nothing to authenticate users through a corporate IdP. Relying on IAM users is the opposite of federation, and groups created in the management account would not even apply across member accounts.","why_zh":"IAM 群組只是為既有的 IAM 使用者整理權限，完全無法透過公司 IdP 驗證使用者。依賴 IAM 使用者與聯合驗證背道而馳，且在管理帳戶中建立的群組也不會套用到各成員帳戶。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/what-is.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/how-to-connect-idp.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/what-is-guardduty.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":232,"question_en":"A company has deployed a new platform that runs on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). The new platform hosts web applications that users frequently update. The application developers build the Docker images for the applications and deploy the Docker images manually to the platform. The platform usage has increased to more than 500 users every day. Frequent updates, building the updated Docker images for the applications, and deploying the Docker images on the platform manually have all become difficult to manage. The company needs to receive an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) notification if Docker image scanning returns any HIGH or CRITICAL findings for operating system or programming language package vulnerabilities. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司部署了一个新的平台，该平台运行在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）上。新平台承载 着用户经常更新的网络应用程序。应用程序开发人员为这些应用程序构建 Docker 镜像，并手动将 Docker 镜 像部署到该平台上。 该平台的每日使用用户已超过 500 人。频繁的更新、为应用程序构建更新后的 Docker 镜像以及手动在平 台上部署 Docker 镜像，这些都变得难以管理。 如果 Docker 镜像扫描发现操作系统或编程语言包存在任何高危或严重漏洞，公司需要收到亚马逊简单 通知服务（Amazon SNS）的通知。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository to store the Dockerfile and Kubernetes deployment files. Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. Use an Amazon S3 event to invoke the pipeline when a newer version of the Dockerfile is committed. Add a step to the pipeline to initiate the AWS CodeBuild project.","B":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository to store the Dockerfile and Kubernetes deployment files. Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. Use an Amazon EventBridge event to invoke the pipeline when a newer version of the Dockerfile is committed. Add a step to the pipeline to initiate the AWS CodeBuild project.","C":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project that builds the Docker images and stores the Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Turn on basic scanning for the ECR repository. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that monitors Amazon GuardDuty events. Configure the EventBridge rule to send an event to an SNS topic when the finding-severity-counts parameter is more than 0 at a CRITICAL or HIGH level.","D":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project that builds the Docker images and stores the Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Turn on enhanced scanning for the ECR repository. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that monitors ECR image scan events. Configure the EventBridge rule to send an event to an SNS topic when the finding-severity-counts parameter is more than 0 at a CRITICAL or HIGH level.","E":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project that scans the Dockerfile. Configure the project to build the Docker images and store the Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository if the scan is successful. Configure an SNS topic to provide notification if the scan returns any vulnerabilities."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库来存储 Dockerfile 和 Kubernetes 部署文件。在 AWS CodePipeline 中创 建一个管道。使用 Amazon S3 事件在提交 Dockerfile 的新版本时调用该管道。在管道中添加一个步骤以 启动 AWS CodeBuild 项目。","B":"创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库来存储 Dockerfile 和 Kubernetes 部署文件。在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个管道。使用 Amazon EventBridge 事件在提交 Dockerfile 的新版本时调用该管道。在管道 中添加一个步骤以启动 AWS CodeBuild 项目。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目，用于构建 Docker 镜像并将这些镜像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库中。为 ECR 存储库开启基本扫描。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规 则来监控 Amazon GuardDuty 事件。配置 EventBridge 规则，当 CRITICAL 或 HIGH 级别的 finding- severity-counts 参数值大于 0 时，将事件发送到 SNS 主题。","D":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建 Docker 镜像，并将 Docker 镜像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库中。为 ECR 存储库开启增强扫描功能。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则来监控 ECR 镜像扫描事件。配置 EventBridge 规则，当 CRITICAL 或 HIGH 级别的 finding-severity- counts 参数值大于 0 时，将事件发送到 SNS 主题。","E":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来扫描 Dockerfile。如果扫描成功，配置该项目以构建 Docker 镜像并将 Docker 镜像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库中。配置一个 SNS 主题， 以便在扫描返回任何漏洞时提供通知。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements drive the answer: (1) automate the build pipeline so it is triggered when the Dockerfile changes, and (2) send an SNS notification when image scanning returns HIGH/CRITICAL findings for BOTH operating system AND programming language package vulnerabilities. For the trigger, the AWS change-detection-methods doc explicitly states that an AWS CodeCommit source action uses 'Amazon EventBridge (recommended). This is the default for pipelines with a CodeCommit source created or edited in the console.' A CodeCommit commit does not generate an 'Amazon S3 event', so B is correct and A is wrong. For scanning, the ECR image-scanning doc states that only Enhanced scanning (powered by Amazon Inspector) scans for 'both operating systems and programming language package vulnerabilities,' while Basic scanning only covers operating system CVEs. With enhanced scanning, Amazon Inspector emits an 'Inspector2 Scan' event to EventBridge whose detail contains the 'finding-severity-counts' parameter with CRITICAL and HIGH counts. An EventBridge rule can match this event when the CRITICAL/HIGH count is greater than 0 and route it to an SNS topic. Therefore D is correct.","explanation_zh":"兩個需求決定答案：(1) 自動化 build pipeline，使其在 Dockerfile 變更時被觸發；(2) 當映像掃描針對作業系統「以及」程式語言套件弱點回報 HIGH/CRITICAL 結果時，發出 SNS 通知。對於觸發，AWS change-detection-methods 文件明確指出 AWS CodeCommit source action 使用 'Amazon EventBridge (recommended)'，且為在主控台建立或編輯 CodeCommit source 的 pipeline 之預設值。CodeCommit 的 commit 不會產生 'Amazon S3 event'，因此 B 正確、A 錯誤。對於掃描，ECR image-scanning 文件說明只有 Enhanced scanning（由 Amazon Inspector 提供）同時掃描「作業系統與程式語言套件弱點」，而 Basic scanning 僅涵蓋作業系統 CVE。啟用 enhanced scanning 後，Amazon Inspector 會向 EventBridge 發出 'Inspector2 Scan' 事件，其 detail 內含帶有 CRITICAL 與 HIGH 計數的 'finding-severity-counts' 參數。EventBridge rule 可在 CRITICAL/HIGH 計數大於 0 時比對此事件並轉送至 SNS topic。因此 D 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses an 'Amazon S3 event' to invoke the pipeline when the Dockerfile is committed to CodeCommit. CodeCommit commits do not generate S3 events; the AWS change-detection-methods doc documents Amazon EventBridge (recommended/console default) as the change detection method for a CodeCommit source action, not S3. The build trigger would never fire.","why_zh":"使用 'Amazon S3 event' 在 Dockerfile 提交到 CodeCommit 時觸發 pipeline。CodeCommit 的 commit 不會產生 S3 事件；AWS change-detection-methods 文件記載 CodeCommit source action 的變更偵測方法是 Amazon EventBridge（建議/主控台預設），而非 S3。觸發器將永遠不會啟動。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Wrong on two points. First, it turns on basic scanning, which only covers operating system CVEs, not programming language package vulnerabilities — so it cannot satisfy the 'operating system or programming language package vulnerabilities' requirement. Second, it has the EventBridge rule monitor 'Amazon GuardDuty events'; ECR enhanced scan findings (with finding-severity-counts) are emitted by Amazon Inspector (aws.inspector2)/ECR, not GuardDuty.","why_zh":"兩處錯誤。第一，啟用 basic scanning，僅涵蓋作業系統 CVE，不含程式語言套件弱點，無法滿足「作業系統或程式語言套件弱點」需求。第二，要 EventBridge rule 監控 'Amazon GuardDuty events'；含 finding-severity-counts 的 ECR enhanced 掃描結果是由 Amazon Inspector (aws.inspector2)/ECR 發出，而非 GuardDuty。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Has CodeBuild 'scan the Dockerfile' and configure SNS for any vulnerabilities. Scanning a Dockerfile (linting/static analysis) is not the same as scanning the built container image for OS and programming-language CVE findings at HIGH/CRITICAL severity. It does not produce the Inspector-based finding-severity-counts notification the requirement needs, and it does nothing to automate the build/deploy pipeline.","why_zh":"讓 CodeBuild 「掃描 Dockerfile」並對任何弱點設定 SNS。掃描 Dockerfile（靜態分析/lint）不等於針對建構後的容器映像掃描 OS 與程式語言 CVE 並以 HIGH/CRITICAL 嚴重性回報；無法提供需求所需、以 Inspector 為基礎的 finding-severity-counts 通知，且未自動化 build/deploy pipeline。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/change-detection-methods.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/triggering.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":233,"question_en":"A company groups its AWS accounts in OUs in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company has deployed a set of Amazon API Gateway APIs in one of the Organizations accounts. The APIs are bound to the account's VPC and have no existing authentication mechanism. Only principals in a specific OU can have permissions to invoke the APIs. The company applies the following policy to the API Gateway interface VPC endpoint: The company also updates the API Gateway resource policies to deny invocations that do not come through the interface VPC endpoint. After the updates, the following error message appears during attempts to use the interface VPC endpoint URL to invoke an API: \"User: anonymous is not authorized.\" Which combination of steps will solve this problem? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中的组织单元（OU）里对其 AWS 账户进行了分组。该公司在其中一个组织账户中部 署了一组 Amazon API Gateway API。这些 API 绑定到该账户的虚拟私有云（VPC），并且没有现有的身份 验证机制。只有特定 OU 中的主体才能获得调用这些 API 的权限。 该公司对 API 网关接口 VPC 终端节点采用以下策略： 该公司还更新了 API 网关资源策略，以拒绝未通过接口 VPC 端点的调用。更新后，在尝试使用接口 VPC 端点 URL 调用 API 时，会出现以下错误消息：“用户：匿名用户未获授权。” 哪两个步骤的组合能解决这个问题？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable IAM authentication on all API methods by setting AWS JAM as the authorization method.","B":"Create a token-based AWS Lambda authorizer that passes the caller's identity in a bearer token.","C":"Create a request parameter-based AWS Lambda authorizer that passes the caller's identity in a combination of headers, query string parameters, stage variables, and $cortext variables.","D":"Use Amazon Cognito user pools as the authorizer to control access to the API.","E":"Verify the identity of the requester by using Signature Version 4 to sign client requests by using AWS credentials."},"options_zh":{"A":"通过将 AWS JAM 设置为授权方法，在所有 API 方法上启用 IAM 身份验证。","B":"创建一个基于令牌的 AWS Lambda 授权程序，通过承载令牌传递调用方的身份。","C":"创建一个基于请求参数的 AWS Lambda 授权器，该授权器通过组合使用标头、查询字符串参数、 阶段变量和 $cortext 变量来传递调用者的身份。","D":"使用 Amazon Cognito 用户池作为授权方来控制对 API 的访问。","E":"使用 AWS 凭证通过 Signature Version 4 对客户端请求进行签名，以验证请求者的身份。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The exact error 'User: anonymous is not authorized to perform: execute-api:Invoke on resource...' is documented verbatim in API Gateway's resource policy troubleshooting guide. AWS states that when a resource policy sets the Principal to an AWS/IAM principal, 'You must use AWS_IAM authorization for every method in your API, or else your API returns the previous error message.' This makes step A (set authorizationType to AWS_IAM on all methods) mandatory. AWS_IAM authorization alone is not enough, because the caller's identity must actually be presented: per the VPC endpoint policy considerations, an Authorization header with no content or with 'non-SigV4 authorization information such as a bearer token' causes the invoker to be 'evaluated as an anonymous user,' whereas a 'valid SigV4 or SigV4a signature' is evaluated as the authenticated IAM identity. The invoking permissions model confirms that with AWS_IAM the caller submits credentials and 'API Gateway supports Signature Version 4a (SigV4a) and Signature Version 4 (SigV4) to authenticate the user's credentials.' Therefore step E (sign client requests with SigV4 using AWS credentials) supplies the authenticated identity that the OU/organization-based VPC endpoint policy and the IAM-principal access requirement evaluate against. A defines that an IAM identity is required; E provides it, so only principals in the specified OU can invoke the API and the 'anonymous' error is resolved.","explanation_zh":"問題中出現的完整錯誤 'User: anonymous is not authorized to perform: execute-api:Invoke on resource...' 在 API Gateway 的 resource policy 疑難排解文件中有逐字記載。AWS 說明當 resource policy 將 Principal 設為 AWS/IAM principal 時，'You must use AWS_IAM authorization for every method in your API, or else your API returns the previous error message.' 因此步驟 A（在所有 method 上將 authorizationType 設為 AWS_IAM）是必要的。但僅啟用 AWS_IAM 仍不足，因為呼叫者的身分必須實際被提交：根據 VPC endpoint policy 的考量說明，Authorization header 無內容、或帶有 'non-SigV4 authorization information such as a bearer token'（例如 bearer token）時，呼叫者會被 'evaluated as an anonymous user'；而帶有 'valid SigV4 or SigV4a signature' 時才會被評估為經過驗證的 IAM 身分。invoking 權限模型亦確認啟用 AWS_IAM 後呼叫者需提交憑證，且 'API Gateway supports Signature Version 4a (SigV4a) and Signature Version 4 (SigV4) to authenticate the user's credentials.' 因此步驟 E（使用 AWS 憑證以 SigV4 簽署用戶端請求）提供了 OU/organization 型 VPC endpoint policy 與 IAM-principal 存取需求所要評估的已驗證身分。A 確立需要 IAM 身分，E 提供該身分，使得只有特定 OU 中的 principal 能呼叫 API，並解決 'anonymous' 錯誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A token-based (TOKEN) Lambda authorizer authenticates callers via a bearer token (JWT/OAuth). Per the VPC endpoint policy considerations, 'non-SigV4 authorization information such as a bearer token' causes the invoker to be evaluated as an anonymous user, so it cannot satisfy the OU/IAM-principal-based policies and would not clear the 'anonymous is not authorized' error. The requirement to restrict to principals in a specific Organizations OU maps to AWS_IAM authorization, not a custom Lambda authorizer.","why_zh":"token 型（TOKEN）Lambda authorizer 透過 bearer token（JWT/OAuth）驗證呼叫者。根據 VPC endpoint policy 考量說明，'non-SigV4 authorization information such as a bearer token' 會使呼叫者被評估為 anonymous user，因此無法滿足以 OU/IAM-principal 為基礎的政策，也無法消除 'anonymous is not authorized' 錯誤。限制給特定 Organizations OU 中 principal 的需求對應的是 AWS_IAM 授權，而非自訂 Lambda authorizer。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A request parameter-based (REQUEST) Lambda authorizer derives identity from headers, query strings, stage variables, and $context variables. This is still a custom (non-SigV4) authorization path; the VPC endpoint policy would treat such callers as anonymous, so it neither enforces the IAM-based OU restriction nor produces the SigV4-authenticated identity that resolves the 'anonymous' error.","why_zh":"request 參數型（REQUEST）Lambda authorizer 從 headers、query string、stage variables 與 $context variables 取得身分。這仍屬於自訂（非 SigV4）授權路徑；VPC endpoint policy 會將此類呼叫者視為 anonymous，因此既無法落實以 IAM 為基礎的 OU 限制，也無法產生解決 'anonymous' 錯誤所需的 SigV4 驗證身分。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Cognito user pools (COGNITO_USER_POOLS authorizer) authenticate end users with JWT identity/access tokens, not AWS IAM principals. Like other bearer-token mechanisms they are treated as anonymous by the principal-based VPC endpoint policy, cannot enforce that only principals within a specific Organizations OU may invoke the API, and do not provide the SigV4/IAM signing needed to fix the error.","why_zh":"Amazon Cognito user pools（COGNITO_USER_POOLS authorizer）以 JWT identity/access token 驗證終端使用者，而非 AWS IAM principal。如同其他 bearer-token 機制，它們會被以 principal 為基礎的 VPC endpoint policy 視為 anonymous，無法限制只有特定 Organizations OU 中的 principal 才能呼叫 API，也無法提供修正錯誤所需的 SigV4/IAM 簽署。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-resource-policies-create-attach.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-vpc-endpoint-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-resource-policies-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_sigv.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":234,"question_en":"A company wants to decrease the time it takes to develop new features. The company uses AWS CodeBuild and AWS CodeDeploy to build and deploy its applications. The company uses AWS CodePipeline to deploy each microservice with its own CI/CD pipeline. The company needs more visibility into the average time between the release of new features and the average time to recover after a failed deployment. Which solution will provide this visibility with the LEAST configuration effort?","question_zh":"一家公司希望缩短开发新功能所需的时间。该公司使用 AWS CodeBuild 和 AWS CodeDeploy 来 构建和部署其应用程序。该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 为每个微服务部署其自身的 CI/CD 管道。 该公司需要更清楚地了解新功能发布之间的平均间隔时间以及部署失败后的平均恢复时间。 哪种解决方案能以最少的配置工作量提供这种可见性？","options_en":{"A":"Program an AWS Lambda function that creates Amazon CloudWatch custom metrics with information about successful runs and failed runs for each pipeline. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function every 5 minutes. Use the metrics to build a CloudWatch dashboard.","B":"Program an AWS Lambda function that creates Amazon CloudWatch custom metrics with information about successful runs and failed runs for each pipeline. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function after every successful run and after every failed run. Use the metrics to build a CloudWatch dashboard.","C":"Program an AWS Lambda function that writes information about successful runs and failed runs to Amazon DynamoDB. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function after every successful run and after every failed run. Build an Amazon QuickSight dashboard to show the information from DynamoDB.","D":"Program an AWS Lambda function that writes information about successful runs and failed runs to Amazon DynamoDB. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function every 5 minutes. Build an Amazon QuickSight dashboard to show the information from DynamoDB."},"options_zh":{"A":"编写一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为每个管道的成功运行和失败运行创建包含相关信息的 Amazon CloudWatch 自定义指标。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每 5 分钟调用一次该 Lambda 函数。 利用这些指标构建一个 CloudWatch 仪表板。","B":"编写一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为每个管道的成功运行和失败运行创建包含相关信息的 Amazon CloudWatch 自定义指标。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在每次成功运行和每次失败运行后调 用该 Lambda 函数。使用这些指标构建一个 CloudWatch 仪表板。","C":"编写一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将成功运行和失败运行的信息写入 Amazon DynamoDB。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在每次运行后调用该 Lambda 函数。 在每次成功运行和每次失败运行之后。构建一个 Amazon QuickSight 仪表板来展示来自 DynamoDB 的信息。","D":"编写一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将成功运行和失败运行的信息写入 Amazon DynamoDB。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每 5 分钟调用一次该 Lambda 函数。构建一个 Amazon QuickSight 仪表 板来展示 DynamoDB 中的信息。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The company needs DORA-style visibility into lead time for changes (average time between new feature releases) and mean time to recovery (MTTR after a failed deployment). CodePipeline natively emits 'CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change' events to Amazon EventBridge on a guaranteed, at-least-once basis, and these events include the SUCCEEDED and FAILED states plus the execution-id and event timing in the payload. An EventBridge rule whose event pattern invokes a Lambda function after every successful run and every failed run (B) captures the exact moment and data needed with no polling, deduplication, or missed-window logic. The Lambda simply calls PutMetricData, which publishes (and auto-creates) CloudWatch custom metrics, and a CloudWatch dashboard is built directly from those metrics inside a single integrated monitoring service, making this the LEAST configuration effort. Options A and D use a 5-minute schedule, which carries no pipeline state, so the function must poll CodePipeline execution history (ListPipelineExecutions/GetPipelineExecution), reconstruct state transitions, and deduplicate, adding logic and timing imprecision. Options C and D also add DynamoDB plus QuickSight, but the QuickSight supported-data-sources list covers relational stores, files, and SaaS sources, not DynamoDB, so they require an Athena federated query or an export to S3 plus dataset/analysis setup, which is more effort than CloudWatch custom metrics feeding a CloudWatch dashboard.","explanation_zh":"公司需要對 DORA 指標取得能見度：lead time for changes（新功能發布之間的平均時間）與 MTTR（部署失敗後的平均恢復時間）。CodePipeline 原生會以保證至少一次（at-least-once）的方式，將 'CodePipeline Pipeline Execution State Change' 事件送至 Amazon EventBridge，這些事件包含 SUCCEEDED 與 FAILED 狀態，以及 payload 中的 execution-id 與事件時間。使用此 event pattern 的 EventBridge rule，在每次成功與每次失敗執行後觸發 Lambda（選項 B），即可在精確時刻取得所需資料，無需輪詢、去重或處理時間窗遺漏。Lambda 只需呼叫 PutMetricData 發佈（並自動建立）CloudWatch 自訂指標，並直接以這些指標建立 CloudWatch dashboard，全部在單一整合監控服務內完成，因此設定工作量最少。選項 A 與 D 採用每 5 分鐘排程，排程本身不帶有 pipeline 狀態，函式必須輪詢 CodePipeline 執行歷史（ListPipelineExecutions/GetPipelineExecution）、重建狀態轉換並去重，增加邏輯與時間不精確性。選項 C 與 D 又加入 DynamoDB 與 QuickSight，但 QuickSight 支援的資料來源清單涵蓋關聯式資料庫、檔案與 SaaS，並不包含 DynamoDB，需透過 Athena 聯邦查詢或匯出至 S3，再加上 dataset/analysis 設定，工作量大於以 CloudWatch 自訂指標驅動 CloudWatch dashboard。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A 5-minute scheduled EventBridge rule carries no pipeline state, so it cannot tell which runs newly succeeded or failed. The Lambda must poll CodePipeline execution history every 5 minutes (ListPipelineExecutions/GetPipelineExecution), reconstruct state transitions, and deduplicate. This is far more logic than reacting to native state-change events, and the coarse polling interval loses the precise timing needed for accurate MTTR and lead-time measurements.","why_zh":"每 5 分鐘的排程 EventBridge rule 不帶有 pipeline 狀態，無法得知哪些執行新近成功或失敗。Lambda 必須每 5 分鐘輪詢 CodePipeline 執行歷史（ListPipelineExecutions/GetPipelineExecution）、重建狀態轉換並去重。這遠比直接回應原生狀態變化事件複雜，且粗略的輪詢間隔會喪失精確計算 MTTR 與 lead time 所需的時間點。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Although event-driven (the correct trigger), it adds DynamoDB plus QuickSight. The QuickSight supported-data-sources list covers relational stores (Athena, Aurora, Glue Data Catalog, Redshift, S3, OpenSearch, Timestream, RDS engines, and more), files, and SaaS sources, but not DynamoDB. Visualizing DynamoDB data in QuickSight therefore needs an Athena federated-query connector or an export to S3, plus dataset and analysis configuration, all more effort than CloudWatch custom metrics feeding a CloudWatch dashboard.","why_zh":"雖為事件驅動（觸發方式正確），但加入 DynamoDB 與 QuickSight。QuickSight 支援的資料來源清單涵蓋關聯式資料庫（Athena、Aurora、Glue Data Catalog、Redshift、S3、OpenSearch、Timestream、RDS 引擎等）、檔案與 SaaS，但不包含 DynamoDB。要在 QuickSight 視覺化 DynamoDB 資料需透過 Athena 聯邦查詢連接器或匯出至 S3，再加上 dataset 與 analysis 設定，工作量皆大於以 CloudWatch 自訂指標驅動 CloudWatch dashboard。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines the two weakest choices: a 5-minute polling schedule that requires execution-history polling and deduplication, plus the DynamoDB-to-QuickSight stack that QuickSight cannot query natively (needing Athena federation or an S3 export). This maximizes configuration effort and is the worst fit for the LEAST-effort qualifier.","why_zh":"結合兩個最弱選擇：每 5 分鐘輪詢排程（需輪詢執行歷史並去重），以及 QuickSight 無法原生查詢的 DynamoDB 至 QuickSight 架構（需 Athena 聯邦查詢或匯出至 S3）。這使設定工作量最大，對於『設定工作量最少』的條件最不符合。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/detect-state-changes-cloudwatch-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-codepipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/publishingMetrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/APIReference/API_PutMetricData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/quick/latest/userguide/supported-data-sources.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":235,"question_en":"A company has developed a static website hosted on an Amazon S3 bucket. The website is deployed using AWS CloudFormation. The CloudFormation template defines an S3 bucket and a custom resource that copies content into the bucket from a source location. The company has decided that it needs to move the website to a new location, so the existing CloudFormation stack must be deleted and re-created. However, CloudFormation reports that the stack could not be deleted cleanly. What is the MOST likely cause and how can the DevOps engineer mitigate this problem for this and future versions of the website?","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一个托管在 Amazon S3 存储桶上的静态网站。该网站通过 AWS CloudFormation 进行部署。 CloudFormation 模板定义了一个 S3 存储桶以及一个自定义资源，该资源会将内容从源位置复制到该存储 桶中。 公司已决定将网站迁移到新位置，因此必须删除现有的 CloudFormation 堆栈并重新创建。然而， CloudFormation 报告称无法干净地删除该堆栈。 最有可能的原因是什么？DevOps 工程师应如何解决此问题以及未来版本网站中可能出现的类似问题？ 删除操作失败，原因是 S3 存储桶具有活动的网站配置。请修改 CloudFormation 模板，从 S3 存储桶 资源中移除 WebsiteConfiguration 属性。 删除操作失败，原因是 S3 存储桶未清空。请修改自定义资源的 AWS Lambda 函数代码，当请求类型为 “删除”时，递归清空存储桶。 删除操作失败，原因是自定义资源未定义删除策略。请在自定义资源定义中添加一个名为 DeletionPolicy 的属性，并将其值设为 RemoveOnDeletion。","options_en":{"A":"Deletion has failed because the S3 bucket has an active website configuration. Modify the CloudFormation template to remove the WebsiteConfiguration property from the S3 bucket resource.","B":"Deletion has failed because the S3 bucket is not empty. Modify the custom resource's AWS Lambda function code to recursively empty the bucket when RequestType is Delete.","C":"Deletion has failed because the custom resource does not define a deletion policy. Add a DeletionPolicy property to the custom resource definition with a value of RemoveOnDeletion.","D":"Deletion has failed because the S3 bucket is not empty. Modify the S3 bucket resource in the CloudFormation template to add a DeletionPolicy property with a value of Empty."},"options_zh":{"D":"删除失败，因为 S3 存储桶不为空。请在 CloudFormation 模板中修改 S3 存储桶资源，添加一个 值为“Empty”的 DeletionPolicy 属性。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudFormation can only delete an empty S3 bucket. The AWS::S3::Bucket reference states 'You can only delete empty buckets. Deletion fails for buckets that have contents,' and the DeletionPolicy reference confirms that for the Delete policy on Amazon S3 buckets 'you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed.' Because the custom resource copied the website content into the bucket, the bucket is not empty at delete time, so stack deletion fails. The correct, forward-looking fix is to extend the existing custom resource's Lambda function so that when it receives a Delete RequestType (custom resources support the Create, Update, and Delete operations, and CloudFormation invokes the function on stack deletion) it recursively empties the bucket and then responds SUCCESS, after which CloudFormation can delete the now-empty bucket. Because the custom resource is part of the template, this fix applies to the current stack and every future version of the website.","explanation_zh":"CloudFormation 只能刪除空的 S3 bucket。AWS::S3::Bucket 參考文件明確指出『You can only delete empty buckets. Deletion fails for buckets that have contents』，而 DeletionPolicy 參考文件也確認對於 Amazon S3 bucket 的 Delete policy『you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed』。由於 custom resource 已把網站內容複製進 bucket，刪除時 bucket 並非空的，因此 stack 刪除失敗。正確且具前瞻性的修正方式是擴充現有 custom resource 的 AWS Lambda function 程式碼：當它收到 Delete RequestType 時（custom resource 支援 Create、Update、Delete 操作，且 CloudFormation 在刪除 stack 時會呼叫該 function），先遞迴清空 bucket，再回應 SUCCESS，之後 CloudFormation 就能刪除已清空的 bucket。因為 custom resource 屬於 template 的一部分，此修正可同時套用於目前的 stack 以及未來每一個版本的網站。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An active WebsiteConfiguration does not block bucket deletion. CloudFormation deletes a bucket regardless of its website configuration; per the AWS::S3::Bucket reference, the only blocker is non-empty contents. Removing WebsiteConfiguration would break the static website hosting the company depends on and would not fix the deletion failure.","why_zh":"啟用 WebsiteConfiguration 並不會阻擋 bucket 刪除。CloudFormation 不論是否設定 website configuration 都能刪除 bucket；依 AWS::S3::Bucket 參考文件，唯一的阻擋因素是 bucket 內仍有內容。移除 WebsiteConfiguration 會破壞公司所依賴的靜態網站託管，且無法解決刪除失敗的問題。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Custom resources do not use a DeletionPolicy to control bucket contents, and 'RemoveOnDeletion' is not a valid DeletionPolicy value. The valid values are Delete, Retain, RetainExceptOnCreate, and Snapshot. This option names neither a real diagnosis nor a real property value; the custom resource is already invoked with a Delete request on stack deletion by default, so a missing deletion policy is not the cause.","why_zh":"custom resource 不會用 DeletionPolicy 來控制 bucket 內容，且『RemoveOnDeletion』並非合法的 DeletionPolicy 值。合法值為 Delete、Retain、RetainExceptOnCreate 與 Snapshot。此選項既非真正的成因，也不是真實存在的屬性值；custom resource 在刪除 stack 時預設本就會收到 Delete 請求，缺少刪除政策並非原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The diagnosis (bucket not empty) is correct, but 'Empty' is not a valid DeletionPolicy value (valid values are Delete, Retain, RetainExceptOnCreate, Snapshot). A DeletionPolicy cannot empty a bucket's objects; the DeletionPolicy reference notes that even with the Delete policy you must delete all objects in the bucket for deletion to succeed.","why_zh":"成因判斷（bucket 非空）正確，但『Empty』並非合法的 DeletionPolicy 值（合法值為 Delete、Retain、RetainExceptOnCreate、Snapshot）。DeletionPolicy 無法清空 bucket 內的物件；DeletionPolicy 參考文件指出即使是 Delete policy，只要 bucket 內仍有物件，就必須先刪除所有物件，刪除才會成功。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-properties-s3-bucket.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/aws-attribute-deletionpolicy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-custom-resources.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":236,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon EC2 as its primary compute platform. A DevOps team wants to audit the company's EC2 instances to check whether any prohibited applications have been installed on the EC2 instances. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司将其主要计算平台定为亚马逊 EC2。一个 DevOps 团队想要审计该公司的 EC2 实例，以检查这 些实例上是否安装了任何被禁止的应用程序。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Systems Manager on each instance. Use AWS Systems Manager Inventory. Use Systems Manager resource data sync to synchronize and store findings in an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an AWS Lambda function that runs when new objects are added to the S3 bucket. Configure the Lambda function to identify prohibited applications.","B":"Configure AWS Systems Manager on each instance. Use Systems Manager Inventory Create AWS Config rules that monitor changes from Systems Manager Inventory to identify prohibited applications.","C":"Configure AWS Systems Manager on each instance. Use Systems Manager Inventory. Filter a trail in AWS CloudTrail for Systems Manager Inventory events to identify prohibited applications.","D":"Designate Amazon CloudWatch Logs as the log destination for all application instances. Run an automated script across all instances to create an inventory of installed applications. Configure the script to forward the results to CloudWatch Logs. Create a CloudWatch alarm that uses filter patterns to search log data to identify prohibited applications."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个实例上配置 AWS 系统管理器。使用 AWS 系统管理器库存。使用系统管理器资源数据同步将发 现结果同步并存储到 Amazon S3 存储桶中。创建一个在向 S3 存储桶添加新对象时运行的 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以识别被禁止的应用程序。","B":"在每个实例上配置 AWS 系统管理器。使用系统管理器库存创建 AWS 配置规则，以监控来自系统管理 器库存的更改，从而识别被禁止的应用程序。","C":"在每个实例上配置 AWS 系统管理器。使用系统管理器库存功能。在 AWS CloudTrail 中筛选系统管理器 库存事件的跟踪记录，以识别被禁止的应用程序。","D":"将 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 指定为所有应用程序实例的日志目标。在所有实例上运行自动化脚本以创建 已安装应用程序的清单。配置脚本将结果转发到 CloudWatch Logs。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，使用筛 选模式搜索日志数据以识别被禁止的应用程序。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Systems Manager Inventory collects 'Applications' metadata (names, publishers, versions) from managed nodes. AWS Config records this inventory as configuration items of resource type AWS::SSM::ManagedInstanceInventory, and provides a purpose-built managed rule, ec2-managedinstance-applications-blacklisted (EC2_MANAGEDINSTANCE_APPLICATIONS_BLACKLISTED), with trigger type 'Configuration changes,' which 'checks if none of the specified applications are installed on the instance' and accepts a comma-separated applicationNames parameter. This is exactly Option B: enable Inventory on each instance, then use an AWS Config rule that monitors changes from Systems Manager Inventory to flag prohibited applications. It is the MOST operationally efficient choice because it uses only fully managed AWS services with no custom code to write, deploy, or maintain, and it re-evaluates automatically whenever inventory data changes.","explanation_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Inventory 會從受管節點收集 'Applications' 中繼資料（名稱、發行者、版本等）。AWS Config 會將這些 inventory 記錄為資源類型 AWS::SSM::ManagedInstanceInventory 的組態項目，並提供專用的受管規則 ec2-managedinstance-applications-blacklisted（EC2_MANAGEDINSTANCE_APPLICATIONS_BLACKLISTED），其觸發類型為 'Configuration changes'，會檢查執行個體上是否未安裝任何指定的應用程式，並接受以逗號分隔的 applicationNames 參數。這正是選項 B：在每個執行個體上啟用 Inventory，然後使用監控 Systems Manager Inventory 變更的 AWS Config 規則來標記禁止的應用程式。這是最具操作效率的方案，因為它完全使用全受管的 AWS 服務，無需撰寫、部署或維護任何自訂程式碼，並會在 inventory 資料變更時自動重新評估。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Using Inventory with resource data sync to S3 plus an S3-triggered Lambda function to parse findings is functionally workable, but it requires writing, deploying, and maintaining custom Lambda code. That is materially more operational overhead than the out-of-the-box AWS Config managed rule in Option B, so it is not the MOST operationally efficient.","why_zh":"使用 Inventory 加上 resource data sync 到 S3，再以 S3 觸發的 Lambda 函數解析結果在功能上可行，但需要撰寫、部署並維護自訂 Lambda 程式碼。這比選項 B 中現成的 AWS Config 受管規則明顯增加更多操作負擔，因此不是最具操作效率的方案。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically unsound. AWS CloudTrail records AWS API management/data-plane activity, not the installed-application content gathered by Systems Manager Inventory. Inventory's collected application metadata is not surfaced as filterable CloudTrail events, so filtering a trail for 'Systems Manager Inventory events' cannot reveal which applications are installed on each instance.","why_zh":"技術上不成立。AWS CloudTrail 記錄的是 AWS API 管理/資料平面活動，而非 Systems Manager Inventory 所收集的已安裝應用程式內容。Inventory 收集的應用程式中繼資料不會以可篩選的 CloudTrail 事件形式呈現，因此篩選 trail 中的『Systems Manager Inventory 事件』無法顯示每個執行個體上安裝了哪些應用程式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Reinvents inventory collection with a custom script on every instance plus CloudWatch Logs filter patterns and alarms. This is the most heavyweight, error-prone option, requires building and maintaining custom scripts and log-filter configuration, and duplicates capability already provided natively by SSM Inventory plus the AWS Config managed rule; CloudWatch alarms are also not designed for software-compliance auditing.","why_zh":"用每台執行個體上的自訂指令碼加上 CloudWatch Logs 篩選模式與警示重新發明 inventory 收集。這是最繁重、最易出錯的選項，需要建置並維護自訂指令碼與日誌篩選設定，且重複了 SSM Inventory 加 AWS Config 受管規則已原生提供的功能；CloudWatch 警示也並非為軟體合規稽核而設計。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/ec2-managedinstance-applications-blacklisted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-inventory.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/inventory-schema.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":237,"question_en":"A company has an event-driven JavaScript application. The application uses decoupled AWS managed services that publish, consume, and route events. During application testing, events are not delivered to the target that is specified by an Amazon EventBridge rule. A DevOps team must provide application testers with additional functionality to view, troubleshoot, and prevent the loss of events without redeployment of the application. Which combination of steps should the DevOps team take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个事件驱动的 JavaScript 应用程序。该应用程序使用解耦的 AWS 管理服务来发布、 消费和路由事件。在应用程序测试期间，事件未被传递到由 Amazon EventBridge 规则指定的目标。 DevOps 团队必须为应用程序测试人员提供额外的功能，以便查看、排查和防止事件丢失，而无 需重新部署应用程序。 DevOps 团队应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Launch AWS Device Farm with a standard test environment and project to run a specific build of the application.","B":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Enable AWS CloudTrail. Create a CloudTrail trail that specifies the S3 bucket as the storage location.","C":"Configure the EventBridge rule to use an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) standard queue as a dead-letter queue.","D":"Configure the EventBridge rule to use an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) FIFO queue as a dead-letter queue.","E":"Create a log group in Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Specify the log group as an additional target of the EventBridge rule.","F":"Update the application code base to use the AWS X-Ray SDK tracing feature to instrument the code with support for the X-Amzn-Trace-Id header."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用标准测试环境和项目启动 AWS 设备农场，以运行应用程序的特定版本。","B":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。启用 AWS CloudTrail。创建一个 CloudTrail 跟踪，指定该 S3 存 储桶作为存储位置。","C":"配置 EventBridge 规则，使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）标准队列作为死 信队列。","D":"配置 EventBridge 规则，使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）FIFO 队列作为死信 队列。","E":"在 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 中创建一个日志组。将该日志组指定为 EventBridge 规则的附加目 标。","F":"更新应用程序代码库，以使用 AWS X-Ray SDK 跟踪功能，通过支持 X-Amzn-Trace-Id 标头来 对代码进行检测。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements map to three distinct capabilities that must be added at the service/configuration layer WITHOUT redeploying the application. (C) Prevent loss: an Amazon SQS standard queue configured as a dead-letter queue (DLQ) on the EventBridge rule/target captures events that fail delivery so they can be inspected and resent later. The EventBridge DLQ doc explicitly states 'Only standard queues are supported. You can't use a FIFO queue for a DLQ in EventBridge,' which both validates (C) and disqualifies (D). (E) View: 'CloudWatch log group' is an explicitly listed EventBridge target type, and a rule can have up to five targets, so adding a CloudWatch Logs log group as an additional target lets testers see the actual event payloads flowing through the rule with no code change. (B) Troubleshoot: enabling AWS CloudTrail with a trail delivering to an S3 bucket records EventBridge management and data events (per the 'Logging Amazon EventBridge API calls using AWS CloudTrail' guide), giving testers an auditable view of API activity to diagnose why events were not delivered. (F) requires instrumenting the code with the X-Ray SDK, which means modifying and redeploying the application, violating the explicit no-redeployment constraint; (A) AWS Device Farm tests mobile/web app builds on real devices and is unrelated to EventBridge delivery; (D) is technically invalid because EventBridge DLQs do not accept FIFO queues.","explanation_zh":"需求對應到三項必須在服務/設定層加入、且「不重新部署應用程式」的能力。(C) 防止遺失：在 EventBridge rule/target 上設定 Amazon SQS standard queue 作為 dead-letter queue (DLQ)，可攔截投遞失敗的事件以便日後檢查與重送。EventBridge DLQ 文件明確寫道「Only standard queues are supported. You can't use a FIFO queue for a DLQ in EventBridge」，這同時佐證 (C) 並排除 (D)。(E) 檢視：「CloudWatch log group」是 EventBridge 明確列出的 target 類型，且每個 rule 最多可有五個 target，因此把 CloudWatch Logs log group 加為額外 target，讓測試者能在不更動程式碼的情況下看到通過該 rule 的實際事件內容。(B) 排錯：啟用 AWS CloudTrail 並建立投遞到 S3 bucket 的 trail，可記錄 EventBridge 的 management 與 data events（見「Logging Amazon EventBridge API calls using AWS CloudTrail」指南），提供可稽核的 API 活動檢視以診斷事件未投遞的原因。(F) 需要用 X-Ray SDK 對程式碼埋點，亦即修改並重新部署應用程式，違反明確的「不重新部署」限制；(A) AWS Device Farm 是在實體裝置上測試行動/網頁應用程式建置，與 EventBridge 投遞無關；(D) 技術上不可行，因為 EventBridge DLQ 不接受 FIFO queue。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Device Farm runs mobile/web app builds against real devices for app UI testing; it has nothing to do with viewing, troubleshooting, or preventing loss of EventBridge events.","why_zh":"AWS Device Farm 是在實體裝置上執行行動/網頁應用程式建置進行 UI 測試，與檢視、排錯或防止 EventBridge 事件遺失完全無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EventBridge dead-letter queues support ONLY standard SQS queues; the EventBridge DLQ doc explicitly says you cannot use a FIFO queue as a DLQ, so this option is technically invalid.","why_zh":"EventBridge dead-letter queue 只支援 standard SQS queue；EventBridge DLQ 文件明確指出不能用 FIFO queue 作為 DLQ，因此此選項技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Using the X-Ray SDK to instrument the code requires updating and redeploying the application code base, which directly violates the 'without redeployment of the application' requirement.","why_zh":"使用 X-Ray SDK 對程式碼埋點需要更新並重新部署應用程式程式碼，直接違反「不重新部署應用程式」的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-rule-dlq.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-targets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/logging-using-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-rule-retry-policy.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":238,"question_en":"A company is migrating its container-based workloads to an AWS Organizations multi-account environment. The environment consists of application workload accounts that the company uses to deploy and run the containerized workloads. The company has also provisioned a shared services account for shared workloads in the organization. The company must follow strict compliance regulations. All container images must receive security scanning before they are deployed to any environment. Images can be consumed by downstream deployment mechanisms after the images pass a scan with no critical vulnerabilities. Pre-scan and post- scan images must be isolated from one another so that a deployment can never use pre-scan images. A DevOps engineer needs to create a strategy to centralize this process. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST administrative overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其基于容器的工作负载迁移到 AWS 组织的多账户环境中。该环境由公司用于部署 和运行容器化工作负载的应用程序工作负载账户组成。该公司还为组织中的共享工作负载配置了一 个共享服务账户。 该公司必须遵循严格的合规规定。所有容器镜像在部署到任何环境之前都必须接受安全扫描。只 有在扫描未发现关键漏洞的情况下，镜像才能被下游部署机制使用。预扫描镜像和扫描后的镜像 必须相互隔离，以确保部署绝不会使用预扫描镜像。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要制定一项策略来将此流程集中化。 哪种步骤组合能以最低的管理开销满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories in the shared services account: one repository for each pre-scan image and one repository for each post-scan image. Configure Amazon ECR image scanning to run on new image pushes to the pre-scan repositories. Use resource- based policies to grant the organization write access to the pre-scan repositories and read access to the post-scan repositories.","B":"Create pre-scan Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories in each account that publishes container images. Create repositories for post-scan images in the shared services account. Configure Amazon ECR image scanning to run on new image pushes to the pre-scan repositories. Use resource-based policies to grant the organization read access to the post-scan repositories.","C":"Configure image replication for each image from the image's pre-scan repository to the image's post- scan repository.","D":"Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline for each pre-scan repository. Create a source stage that runs when new images are pushed to the pre-scan repositories. Create a stage that uses AWS CodeBuild as the action provider. Write a buildspec.yaml definition that determines the image scanning status and pushes images without critical vulnerabilities to the post-scan repositories.","E":"Create an AWS Lambda function. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to image scanning completed events and invokes the Lambda function. Write function code that determines the image scanning status and pushes images without critical vulnerabilities to the post-scan repositories."},"options_zh":{"A":"在共享服务账户中创建 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储库：为每个预扫描 镜像创建一个存储库，为每个后扫描镜像创建一个存储库。配置 Amazon ECR 镜像扫描功能， 使其在向预扫描存储库推送新镜像时运行。使用基于资源的策略授予组织对预扫描存储库的写 入权限以及对后扫描存储库的读取权限。","B":"在每个发布容器镜像的账户中创建预扫描的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存 储库。在共享服务账户中为扫描后的镜像创建存储库。配置 Amazon ECR 镜像扫描功能，使其 在向预扫描存储库推送新镜像时运行。使用基于资源的策略授予组织对扫描后存储库的读取访 问权限。","C":"为每个镜像配置从镜像预扫描存储库到镜像后扫描存储库的镜像复制。","D":"为每个预扫描存储库在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个管道。创建一个源阶段，当有新镜像推送到 预扫描存储库时运行。创建一个使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序的阶段。编写一个 buildspec.yaml 定义，用于确定镜像扫描状态，并将没有关键漏洞的镜像推送到后扫描存储库。","E":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对图像扫描完成事件做 出反应并调用该 Lambda 函数。编写函数代码以确定图像扫描状态，并将没有关键漏洞的图 像推送到扫描后的存储库。"},"answer":["A","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to CENTRALIZE the scan-and-promote workflow, keep pre-scan and post-scan images isolated so deployments can never use pre-scan images, and do it with the LEAST administrative overhead. Option A centralizes all repositories in the single shared services account (one pre-scan and one post-scan repository per image), enables basic scan-on-push on the pre-scan repositories, and uses ECR resource-based (repository) policies to grant the organization write access to pre-scan repositories and read-only access to post-scan repositories. ECR repository policies support cross-account principals (and org-wide grants via aws:PrincipalOrgID), so workload accounts can only read post-scan images, giving strong isolation while keeping everything in one account for minimal overhead. Option E completes the promotion gate: basic scanning emits an EventBridge event with detail-type 'ECR Image Scan', scan-status 'COMPLETE', and finding-severity-counts (including CRITICAL, which is only present when such findings exist), as confirmed in the ECR EventBridge documentation. A single EventBridge rule reacting to scan-completion events invokes one Lambda function that inspects the severity counts and pushes only images with no critical vulnerabilities into the post-scan repositories. One rule plus one function covers all repositories and fires AFTER the scan finishes, making it both correctly timed and the lowest-overhead promotion mechanism. Together A+E centralize the process, enforce the no-critical-vulnerability gate, and keep pre-scan images unreachable by deployments.","explanation_zh":"需求是以最少管理負擔集中化掃描與晉升流程，並讓掃描前(pre-scan)與掃描後(post-scan)映像彼此隔離，確保部署永遠無法使用 pre-scan 映像。選項 A 將所有儲存庫集中在單一 shared services 帳戶（每個映像各有一個 pre-scan 與一個 post-scan repository），在 pre-scan repository 啟用 basic scan-on-push，並以 ECR resource-based (repository) policy 授予組織對 pre-scan repository 寫入權、對 post-scan repository 唯讀權。ECR repository policy 支援跨帳戶 principal（並可透過 aws:PrincipalOrgID 做組織範圍授權），因此工作負載帳戶只能讀取 post-scan 映像，隔離性強，且完全集中於單一帳戶，管理負擔最低。選項 E 完成晉升把關：ECR basic scanning 會發出 detail-type 為 'ECR Image Scan'、scan-status 'COMPLETE'、含 finding-severity-counts（包含 CRITICAL，且僅在存在該等級發現時才會出現）的 EventBridge 事件，這點已由 ECR EventBridge 文件確認。單一 EventBridge rule 在掃描完成時觸發一個 Lambda function，檢查嚴重性計數，只把沒有 critical 漏洞的映像推送到 post-scan repository。一條 rule 加一個 function 即可涵蓋所有 repository，且在掃描完成「之後」才觸發，時機正確且負擔最低。A+E 共同達成集中化、強制執行「無 critical 漏洞」把關，並確保部署無法使用 pre-scan 映像。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Placing pre-scan repositories in EACH publishing account is decentralized, which directly contradicts the goal to CENTRALIZE the process and increases administrative overhead (many repos and policies spread across accounts). It also only grants the organization read access to the post-scan repositories and never defines how images are promoted/written from pre-scan to post-scan, leaving the gating path undefined.","why_zh":"把 pre-scan repository 分散放在每個發佈帳戶屬於去中心化，直接違反「集中化」目標並增加管理負擔（眾多 repo 與政策散落各帳戶）。它也只授予組織對 post-scan repository 唯讀，且完全未定義映像如何從 pre-scan 晉升/寫入 post-scan，把關路徑未明。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ECR private image replication is unconditional: per the docs a replication action occurs once per image push or restore and cannot gate on scan status or severity. It would replicate pre-scan (including vulnerable) images into the post-scan repos, breaking the required isolation and the no-critical-vulnerabilities gate.","why_zh":"ECR 私有映像複製是無條件的：文件指出每次映像推送或還原都會觸發一次複製，無法依掃描狀態或嚴重性把關。它會把 pre-scan（含含漏洞的）映像複製進 post-scan repo，破壞所需的隔離與「無 critical 漏洞」把關條件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating a CodePipeline per pre-scan repository is high administrative overhead (one pipeline plus CodeBuild project per repository). Per the ECR source action reference, a CodePipeline ECR source triggers on image PUSH, not on scan completion, so it can race the scan and would require extra polling/wait logic. EventBridge-on-scan-complete (E) is both lower overhead and correctly timed.","why_zh":"為每個 pre-scan repository 建立一條 CodePipeline 管理負擔高（每個 repo 都要一條 pipeline 加 CodeBuild 專案）。依 ECR source action 參考文件，CodePipeline 的 ECR source 是在映像「推送」時觸發，而非掃描完成時，可能與掃描競態並需額外的輪詢/等待邏輯；以掃描完成事件觸發 EventBridge 的選項 E 負擔更低且時機正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/ecr-eventbridge.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-basic-enabling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/repository-policy-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-ECR.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":239,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster to deploy its web applications on containers. The web applications contain confidential data that cannot be decrypted without specific credentials. A DevOps engineer has stored the credentials in AWS Secrets Manager. The secrets are encrypted by an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed key. A Kubernetes service account for a third-party tool makes the secrets available to the applications. The service account assumes an IAM role that the company created to access the secrets. The service account receives an Access Denied (403 Forbidden) error while trying to retrieve the secrets from Secrets Manager. What is the root cause of this issue?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群在其容器上部署其网络应用程 序。这些网络应用程序包含机密数据，没有特定凭证无法解密。 一位 DevOps 工程师已将凭证存储在 AWS 机密管理器中。这些机密由 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）的客户管理密钥进行加密。一个用于第三方工具的 Kubernetes 服务账户使应用程序能够获取 这些机密。该服务账户承担了公司为访问机密而创建的 IAM 角色。 服务账户在尝试从密钥管理器获取密钥时收到“访问被拒绝（403 禁止）”错误。 这个问题的根本原因是什么？","options_en":{"A":"The IAM role that is attached to the EKS cluster does not have access to retrieve the secrets from Secrets Manager.","B":"The key policy for the customer managed key does not allow the Kubernetes service account IAM role to use the key.","C":"The key policy for the customer managed key does not allow the EKS cluster IAM role to use the key.","D":"The IAM role that is assumed by the Kubernetes service account does not have permission to access the EKS cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"附加到 EKS 集群的 IAM 角色没有权限从 Secrets Manager 中检索机密信息。","B":"客户管理密钥的关键策略不允许 Kubernetes 服务账户 IAM 角色使用该密钥。","C":"客户管理密钥的关键策略不允许 EKS 集群的 IAM 角色使用该密钥。","D":"由 Kubernetes 服务账户所承担的 IAM 角色没有访问 EKS 集群的权限。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is an IRSA (IAM Roles for Service Accounts) scenario, so the calling principal for the Secrets Manager request is the IAM role that the Kubernetes service account assumes, not the EKS cluster or node role. The question states this role was 'created to access the secrets,' so it already holds secretsmanager:GetSecretValue. The secret is encrypted with a customer managed KMS key, and per the Secrets Manager docs, when Secrets Manager performs a cryptographic operation 'it acts on behalf of the user who is accessing or updating the secret value,' granting the required AWS KMS permissions through an IAM policy or a key policy; GetSecretValue is explicitly listed as an operation that requires those KMS permissions and triggers a kms:Decrypt. If the assumed service-account role is authorized for GetSecretValue but is not authorized to use the CMK (neither its IAM policy nor the key policy permits it), the underlying Decrypt fails and the caller receives an Access Denied (403 Forbidden). Therefore the root cause is that the customer managed key's key policy does not allow the Kubernetes service account IAM role to use the key.","explanation_zh":"這是 IRSA (IAM Roles for Service Accounts) 情境,因此呼叫 Secrets Manager 的 principal 是 Kubernetes service account 所承擔的 IAM role,而非 EKS cluster 或 node role。題目說該 role 是『為了存取 secrets 而建立』,因此它已具備 secretsmanager:GetSecretValue 權限。Secret 以 customer managed KMS key 加密,依 AWS 文件,Secrets Manager 執行密碼學操作時會『代表存取或更新該 secret 值的使用者』,並可透過 IAM policy 或 key policy 授予所需的 AWS KMS 權限;GetSecretValue 被明確列為需要這些 KMS 權限並觸發 kms:Decrypt 的操作。若被承擔的 service account role 已被授權執行 GetSecretValue,卻未被授權使用該 CMK(其 IAM policy 與 key policy 皆未允許),底層的 Decrypt 就會失敗,呼叫端便會收到 Access Denied (403 Forbidden)。因此根本原因是 customer managed key 的 key policy 未允許該 Kubernetes service account IAM role 使用該金鑰。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Under IRSA the pod assumes the service-account IAM role, not the EKS cluster/node role, to call Secrets Manager, so the cluster role's Secrets Manager access is not the principal being evaluated. The service-account role was explicitly created to access the secrets, so the missing piece is KMS key authorization, not Secrets Manager access on the cluster role.","why_zh":"在 IRSA 下,Pod 是以 service account 的 IAM role(非 EKS cluster/node role)呼叫 Secrets Manager,因此被評估的 principal 不是 cluster role。題中 service account role 已明確為存取 secrets 而建立,故缺的是 KMS 金鑰授權,而非 cluster role 的 Secrets Manager 存取權。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The calling principal for the kms:Decrypt that Secrets Manager performs is the assumed service-account role, not the EKS cluster IAM role, because Secrets Manager acts on behalf of the user accessing the secret value. KMS evaluates that assumed-role identity, so granting or denying the cluster role on the key is irrelevant to this request; the option names the wrong principal.","why_zh":"Secrets Manager 執行 kms:Decrypt 的呼叫 principal 是被承擔的 service account role,而非 EKS cluster IAM role,因為 Secrets Manager 是代表存取 secret 值的使用者執行。KMS 評估的是該被承擔的 role 身分,因此在金鑰上授予或拒絕 cluster role 與此請求無關;此選項指錯了 principal。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"'Permission to access the EKS cluster' is Kubernetes cluster authorization (RBAC), which is unrelated to an AWS Secrets Manager API call. The pod is already running in the cluster, and a 403 from Secrets Manager is an AWS authorization error tied to Secrets Manager/KMS IAM and key-policy permissions, not cluster RBAC.","why_zh":"『存取 EKS cluster 的權限』屬於 Kubernetes cluster 授權 (RBAC),與 AWS Secrets Manager API 呼叫無關。Pod 已在 cluster 中運行;Secrets Manager 回傳的 403 是與 Secrets Manager/KMS 的 IAM 及 key policy 權限相關的 AWS 授權錯誤,而非 cluster RBAC。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/security-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/troubleshoot.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/userguide/auth-and-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/iam-roles-for-service-accounts.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":240,"question_en":"A company is migrating its product development teams from an on-premises data center to a hybrid environment. The new environment will add four AWS Regions and will give the developers the ability to use the Region that is geographically closest to them. All the development teams use a shared set of Linux applications. The on-premises data center stores the applications on a NetApp ONTAP storage device. The storage volume is mounted read-only on the development on-premises VMs. The company updates the applications on the shared volume once a week. A DevOps engineer needs to replicate the data to all the new Regions. The DevOps engineer must ensure that the data is always up to date with deduplication. The data also must not be dependent on the availability of the on-premises storage device. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其产品开发团队从本地数据中心迁移到混合环境中。新环境将增加四个 AWS 区 域，并且能让开发人员使用距离他们最近的区域。 所有开发团队都使用一套共享的 Linux 应用程序。本地数据中心将这些应用程序存储在 NetApp ONTAP 存储设备上。该存储卷在本地开发虚拟机上以只读方式挂载。公司每周对共享卷上的应用 程序进行一次更新。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要将数据复制到所有新的区域。该工程师必须确保数据始终是最新的，并且 要进行重复数据删除。数据还不能依赖于本地存储设备的可用性。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 File Gateway in the on-premises data center. Create S3 buckets in each Region. Set up a cron job to copy the data from the storage device to the S3 File Gateway. Set up S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) to the S3 buckets in each Region.","B":"Create an Amazon FSx File Gateway in one Region. Create file servers in Amazon FSx for Windows File Server in each Region. Set up a cron job to copy the data from the storage device to the FSx File Gateway.","C":"Create Multi-AZ Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP instances and volumes in each Region. Configure a scheduled SnapMirror relationship between the on-premises storage device and the FSx for ONTAP instances.","D":"Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system in each Region. Deploy an AWS DataSync agent in the on-premises data center. Configure a schedule for DataSync to copy the data to Amazon EFS daily."},"options_zh":{"A":"在本地数据中心创建一个 Amazon S3 文件网关。在每个区域创建 S3 存储桶。设置一个 cron 作 业将数据从存储设备复制到 S3 文件网关。为每个区域的 S3 存储桶设置 S3 跨区域复制 （CRR）。","B":"在一个区域创建一个 Amazon FSx 文件网关。在每个区域的 Amazon FSx for Windows File Server 中创 建文件服务器。设置一个 cron 作业，将数据从存储设备复制到 FSx 文件网关。","C":"在每个区域创建多可用区的 Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP 实例和卷。在本地存储设备与 FSx for ONTAP 实例之间配置计划的 SnapMirror 关系。","D":"在每个区域创建一个 Amazon Elastic File System（Amazon EFS）文件系统。在本地数据中心部署一个 AWS DataSync 代理。为 DataSync 配置一个每日将数据复制到 Amazon EFS 的计划。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive constraints are: replicate an on-premises NetApp ONTAP read-only Linux (NFS) application volume to four AWS Regions, keep it always up to date, preserve deduplication, and make the data independent of the on-premises device's availability. Option C uses Multi-AZ FSx for NetApp ONTAP in each Region with a scheduled NetApp SnapMirror relationship from the on-premises ONTAP device, which satisfies every requirement. AWS explicitly states 'We recommend using SnapMirror to migrate on-premise NetApp ONTAP file systems to FSx for ONTAP' and that 'when you use SnapMirror to migrate to FSx for ONTAP, deduplicated and compressed data remains in those states' - directly meeting the deduplication requirement via SnapMirror's block-level replication. FSx for ONTAP also natively supports ONTAP block-level deduplication, compression, and compaction. SnapMirror can be scheduled (per RPO needs, as frequent as a few minutes) to keep the destination current, and once data resides in the Multi-AZ FSx for ONTAP file systems the Linux clients access AWS-resident NFS copies that no longer depend on the on-premises storage device.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限制條件為：將地端 NetApp ONTAP 唯讀的 Linux（NFS）應用程式磁碟區複製到四個 AWS Region，保持資料隨時最新、保留 deduplication（去重），且資料不依賴地端儲存裝置的可用性。選項 C 在每個 Region 部署 Multi-AZ 的 FSx for NetApp ONTAP，並從地端 ONTAP 裝置建立排程式的 NetApp SnapMirror 關係，能滿足所有需求。AWS 官方文件明確指出「We recommend using SnapMirror to migrate on-premise NetApp ONTAP file systems to FSx for ONTAP」，並說明「when you use SnapMirror to migrate to FSx for ONTAP, deduplicated and compressed data remains in those states」（使用 SnapMirror 遷移到 FSx for ONTAP 時，去重與壓縮後的資料維持原狀），透過 SnapMirror 的 block-level replication 直接符合 deduplication 需求。FSx for ONTAP 本身也原生支援 ONTAP 的 block-level deduplication、compression 與 compaction。SnapMirror 可依 RPO 需求排程（最短可達數分鐘一次）以保持目的端最新；資料進入 Multi-AZ FSx for ONTAP 後，Linux 用戶端透過 NFS 存取 AWS 端副本，不再依賴地端儲存裝置。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An S3 File Gateway plus a cron job stores the ONTAP volume data as flat S3 objects, and S3 Cross-Region Replication copies objects. S3 does not preserve ONTAP block-level deduplication/compression, so the deduplication requirement fails. A brittle cron copy is required, and S3 object semantics do not match a read-only Linux application volume that clients expect to mount over NFS.","why_zh":"S3 File Gateway 加 cron job 會把 ONTAP 磁碟區資料存成扁平的 S3 物件，再用 S3 Cross-Region Replication 複製物件。S3 無法保留 ONTAP 的 block-level deduplication/compression，因此不符合去重需求。仍需要脆弱的 cron 複製，S3 物件語意也不符合用戶端預期以 NFS 掛載的唯讀 Linux 應用程式磁碟區。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"FSx File Gateway is designed to cache FSx for Windows File Server (SMB) data on-premises, i.e. the wrong direction (it surfaces AWS data on-prem rather than replicating on-prem to AWS). FSx for Windows uses SMB for Windows clients, but the applications are Linux/NFS. It also deploys the gateway in only one Region instead of all four, and a cron copy preserves no ONTAP deduplication.","why_zh":"FSx File Gateway 用於在地端快取 FSx for Windows File Server（SMB）資料，方向相反（是把 AWS 資料呈現到地端，而非把地端複製到 AWS）。FSx for Windows 走 SMB 給 Windows 用戶端，但應用程式是 Linux/NFS。此方案也只在一個 Region 部署閘道而非四個，且 cron 複製不保留 ONTAP deduplication。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"DataSync transfers data at the file level, so it does not preserve ONTAP's block-level deduplication and compression, and Amazon EFS has no native ONTAP-style deduplication, failing the explicit deduplication requirement. A daily DataSync schedule is also weaker than SnapMirror's near-continuous replication for keeping data 'always up to date.' EFS plus DataSync is a valid generic NFS replication pattern but does not satisfy the deduplication constraint.","why_zh":"DataSync 以檔案層級傳輸，無法保留 ONTAP 的 block-level deduplication 與壓縮，而 Amazon EFS 也沒有 ONTAP 式的原生去重，故不符合明確的去重需求。每日排程的 DataSync 在「隨時最新」上也弱於 SnapMirror 近乎連續的複製。EFS 加 DataSync 是常見的通用 NFS 複製模式，但無法滿足 deduplication 限制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/migrating-fsx-ontap-snapmirror.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/scheduled-replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/how-it-works-fsx-ontap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/datasync/latest/userguide/what-is-datasync.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":241,"question_en":"A company has an application that stores data that includes personally identifiable information (PII) in an Amazon S3 bucket. All data is encrypted with AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) customer managed keys. All AWS resources are deployed from an AWS CloudFormation template. A DevOps engineer needs to set up a development environment for the application in a different AWS account. The data in the development environment's S3 bucket needs to be updated once a week from the production environment's S3 bucket. The company must not move PII from the production environment without anonymizing the PII first. The data in each environment must be encrypted with different KMS customer managed keys. Which combination of steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，其数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，这些数据包含个人身份信息（PII）。 所有数据均使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）客户管理密钥进行加密。所有 AWS 资源均通过 AWS CloudFormation 模板进行部署。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要在另一个 AWS 账户中为应用程序设置开发环境。开发环境的 S3 存储桶中的数 据需要每周从生产环境的 S3 存储桶中更新一次。 公司不得在未对个人身份信息（PII）进行匿名化处理的情况下将其从生产环境转移。每个环境中的数 据都必须使用不同的 KMS 客户管理密钥进行加密。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Activate Amazon Macie on the S3 bucket in the production account. Create an AWS Step Functions state machine to initiate a discovery job and redact all PII before copying files to the S3 bucket in the development account. Give the state machine tasks decrypt permissions on the KMS key in the production account. Give the state machine tasks encrypt permissions on the KMS key in the development account.","B":"Set up S3 replication between the production S3 bucket and the development S3 bucket. Activate Amazon Macie on the development S3 bucket. Create an AWS Step Functions state machine to initiate a discovery job and redact all PII as the files are copied to the development S3 bucket. Give the state machine tasks encrypt and decrypt permissions on the KMS key in the development account.","C":"Set up an S3 Batch Operations job to copy files from the production S3 bucket to the development S3 bucket. In the development account, configure an AWS Lambda function to redact ail PII. Configure S3 Object Lambda to use the Lambda function for S3 GET requests. Give the Lambda function's IAM role encrypt and decrypt permissions on the KMS key in the development account.","D":"Create a development environment from the CloudFormation template in the development account. Schedule an Amazon EventBridge rule to start the AWS Step Functions state machine once a week.","E":"Create a development environment from the CloudFormation template in the development account. Schedule a cron job on an Amazon EC2 instance to run once a week to start the S3 Batch Operations job."},"options_zh":{"A":"在生产账户的 S3 存储桶上激活 Amazon Macie。创建一个 AWS Step Functions 状态机，用于启动发 现任务，并在将文件复制到开发账户的 S3 存储桶之前对所有个人身份信息（PII）进行脱敏处理。 授予状态机任务在生产账户的 KMS 密钥上解密的权限。授予状态机任务在开发账户的 KMS 密钥 上加密的权限。","B":"在生产 S3 存储桶和开发 S3 存储桶之间设置 S3 复制。在开发 S3 存储桶上激活 Amazon Macie。创建一 个 AWS Step Functions 状态机，用于启动发现任务，并在文件复制到开发 S3 存储桶时对所有个人身 份信息（PII）进行脱敏处理。授予状态机任务在开发账户中的 KMS 密钥上进行加密和解密的权限。","C":"设置一个 S3 批量操作任务，将文件从生产 S3 存储桶复制到开发 S3 存储桶。在开发账户中，配置一 个 AWS Lambda 函数来删除所有 PII（个人身份信息）。配置 S3 对象 Lambda 使用该 Lambda 函数 处理 S3 GET 请求。授予 Lambda 函数的 IAM 角色在开发账户中的 KMS 密钥上进行加密和解密的权 限。","D":"在开发账户中根据 CloudFormation 模板创建开发环境。安排一条 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每周启 动一次 AWS Step Functions 状态机。","E":"在开发账户中根据 CloudFormation 模板创建开发环境。在 Amazon EC2 实例上安排一个每周运行一次 的 cron 作业来启动 S3 批量操作作业。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The decisive fact is that Amazon Macie only DISCOVERS sensitive data and produces findings/reports about where PII resides; it has no capability to redact, mask, or anonymize object content. The 'What is Amazon Macie?' doc states that when Macie detects sensitive data it 'creates a sensitive data finding for you... The finding provides a detailed report' - it never modifies data. Therefore options A and B, which both claim a Step Functions state machine will 'initiate a discovery job and redact all PII,' describe a capability that does not exist, so both are technically invalid. The AWS-documented pattern for anonymizing PII is S3 Object Lambda with a Lambda redaction function (the 'Detecting and redacting PII data with S3 Object Lambda and Amazon Comprehend' tutorial, which uses the prebuilt ComprehendPiiRedactionS3ObjectLambda function to replace detected PII entities with asterisks on GET requests). Option C uses an S3 Batch Operations Copy job (which the Copy docs confirm can copy objects 'to a different destination account') to move data through the S3 Object Lambda redaction path, writing the anonymized output into the dev bucket encrypted with the dev account's own KMS customer-managed key (Lambda role gets encrypt/decrypt on the dev key). That satisfies both 'anonymize PII before moving it' and 'different KMS keys per environment.' Option E is the correct orchestration partner for C: it creates the dev environment from the CloudFormation template and schedules a weekly job that starts the S3 Batch Operations job that C defines. Option D instead references 'the AWS Step Functions state machine,' which exists only in the invalid A/B options, so it cannot pair with C. The genuinely correct, internally consistent pair is C + E. (Note: a Nov 2025 doc banner limits new S3 Object Lambda adoption, but among these five options C+E remains the only technically coherent pair; A/B have a hard disqualifier because Macie redaction does not exist.)","explanation_zh":"決定性事實是 Amazon Macie 只能「探索 (discover)」敏感資料並產生 findings/報告，指出 PII 所在位置；它沒有任何能力可以 redact、遮罩或匿名化物件內容。「What is Amazon Macie?」文件明載當 Macie 偵測到敏感資料時，它會「為你建立 sensitive data finding……該 finding 提供詳細報告」，從不修改資料。因此選項 A 與 B 都聲稱 Step Functions state machine 會「啟動 discovery job 並 redact 所有 PII」，描述的是不存在的能力，技術上均無效。AWS 官方記載匿名化 PII 的模式是 S3 Object Lambda 搭配 Lambda redaction function（即「Detecting and redacting PII data with S3 Object Lambda and Amazon Comprehend」教學，使用內建的 ComprehendPiiRedactionS3ObjectLambda 函式在 GET 請求時把偵測到的 PII 以星號取代）。選項 C 使用 S3 Batch Operations Copy job（Copy 文件確認可將物件複製「到不同的目的帳號」），讓資料經過 S3 Object Lambda redaction 路徑，將匿名化後的輸出寫入 dev 貯體並以 dev 帳號自己的 KMS customer-managed key 加密（Lambda 角色取得 dev key 的 encrypt/decrypt 權限）。這同時滿足「移動前先匿名化 PII」與「各環境使用不同 KMS key」。選項 E 是 C 正確的編排搭配：它從 CloudFormation 範本建立 dev 環境，並排程每週啟動 C 所定義的 S3 Batch Operations job。選項 D 則提到「the AWS Step Functions state machine」，那只存在於無效的 A/B 選項中，因此無法與 C 搭配。真正正確且彼此一致的組合是 C + E。（註：2025 年 11 月的文件公告限制了 S3 Object Lambda 的新採用，但在這五個選項中 C+E 仍是唯一技術上一致的組合；A/B 有硬性致命缺陷，因為 Macie redaction 根本不存在。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon Macie cannot redact or anonymize PII; it only discovers sensitive data and produces findings/reports. A Step Functions task cannot make a Macie discovery job 'redact all PII' because no such Macie operation exists, so this step is technically impossible. It is also the dump's suggested answer, but it is wrong.","why_zh":"Amazon Macie 無法 redact 或匿名化 PII；它只會探索敏感資料並產生 findings/報告。Step Functions 任務無法讓 Macie discovery job「redact 所有 PII」，因為根本沒有這種 Macie 操作，技術上不可行。這也是 dump 建議答案，但是錯的。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as A: Macie does not redact data. Additionally, setting up S3 replication would copy the raw PII into the development account before any redaction occurs, directly violating the requirement not to move PII without anonymizing it first.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的致命缺陷：Macie 不會 redact 資料。此外，設定 S3 replication 會在任何 redaction 之前就把原始 PII 複製到開發帳號，直接違反「未先匿名化不得移動 PII」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"D schedules 'the AWS Step Functions state machine,' but that state machine is defined only in options A and B, which are technically invalid because Macie cannot redact. The only valid copy/redaction option is C, which uses an S3 Batch Operations job (not a Step Functions state machine), so D is not a coherent partner. D pairs only with the broken Macie-based options.","why_zh":"D 排程「the AWS Step Functions state machine」，但該 state machine 只定義於技術上無效的 A、B 選項中（Macie 無法 redact）。唯一有效的複製/redaction 選項是 C，它使用的是 S3 Batch Operations job 而非 Step Functions state machine，因此 D 無法與之一致搭配。D 只能搭配有缺陷的 Macie 選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/what-is-macie.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/tutorial-s3-object-lambda-redact-pii.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/transforming-objects.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/batch-ops-examples-copy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/specify-batchjob-manifest-xaccount-inventory.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":242,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster to host its machine learning (ML) application. As the ML model and the container image size grow, the time that new pods take to start up has increased to several minutes. A DevOps engineer needs to reduce the startup time to seconds. The solution must also reduce the startup time to seconds when the pod runs on nodes that were recently added to the cluster. The DevOps engineer creates an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an automation in AWS Systems Manager. The automation prefetches the container images from an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository when new images are pushed to the repository. The DevOps engineer also configures tags to be applied to the cluster and the node groups. What should the DevOps engineer do next to meet the requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群来托管其机器学习（ML）应用程序。随 着 ML 模型和容器镜像大小的增加，新 Pod 启动所需的时间已增加到数分钟。 一名 DevOps 工程师需要将启动时间缩短至数秒。该解决方案还必须减少 启动时间至 当 Pod 在最近添加到集群的节点上运行时，可能会出现几秒钟的延迟。 DevOps 工程师创建了一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则会调用 AWS Systems Manager 中的自动化操 作。当有新的容器镜像被推送到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储库时，该自动化操 作会预先获取这些容器镜像。DevOps 工程师还配置了要应用于集群和节点组的标签。 为了满足要求，开发运维工程师接下来应该做什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows EventBridge to use Systems Manager to run commands in the EKS cluster's control plane nodes. Create a Systems Manager State Manager association that uses the control plane nodes' tags to prefetch corresponding container images.","B":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows EventBridge to use Systems Manager to run commands in the EKS cluster's nodes. Create a Systems Manager State Manager association that uses the nodes' machine size to prefetch corresponding container images.","C":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows EventBridge to use Systems Manager to run commands in the EKS cluster's nodes. Create a Systems Manager State Manager association that uses the nodes' tags to prefetch corresponding container images.","D":"Create an IAM role that has a policy that allows EventBridge to use Systems Manager to run commands in the EKS cluster's control plane nodes. Create a Systems Manager State Manager association that uses the nodes' tags to prefetch corresponding container images."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有策略的 IAM 角色，该策略允许 EventBridge 使用 Systems Manager 在 EKS 集群的控 制平面节点上运行命令。创建一个 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联，该关联使用控制平面节点 的标签来预取相应的容器镜像。","B":"创建一个具有策略的 IAM 角色，该策略允许 EventBridge 使用 Systems Manager 在 EKS 集群的节点上 运行命令。创建一个 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联，该关联根据节点的机器大小预取相应的容 器镜像。","C":"创建一个具有策略的 IAM 角色，该策略允许 EventBridge 使用 Systems Manager 在 EKS 集群的节点上 运行命令。创建一个 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联，该关联使用节点的标签来预取相应的容器 镜像。","D":"创建一个具有策略的 IAM 角色，该策略允许 EventBridge 使用 Systems Manager 在 EKS 集群的控 制平面节点上运行命令。创建一个 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联，该关联使用节点的标签来 预取相应的容器镜像。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Container images are pulled and cached by the container runtime (containerd) on the worker / data-plane EC2 nodes where pods are scheduled, not on the control plane. In Amazon EKS the Kubernetes control plane (API server and etcd) is fully AWS-managed and runs inside an EKS-managed VPC; Amazon EKS provisions, monitors, and replaces those instances, so customers cannot install the SSM Agent on or run Systems Manager Run Command / State Manager actions against control plane nodes. That eliminates options A and D, which both target the control plane. The IAM role must therefore allow EventBridge to use Systems Manager to run commands on the cluster's worker nodes, and the State Manager association must target those worker nodes. State Manager associations target managed nodes by tags, individual node IDs, or an AWS Resource Groups group, and the AWS docs explicitly state that when you create new nodes and assign the specified tag key/value, the system automatically applies and immediately runs the association on those nodes. Because the engineer already configured tags on the cluster and node groups, tag-based targeting (option C) prefetches images on existing worker nodes and automatically covers newly added nodes, satisfying the requirement to keep pod startup to seconds even on recently added nodes. Option B is wrong because 'machine size' is not a supported State Manager target.","explanation_zh":"容器映像是由 pod 被排程到的 worker / data plane EC2 節點上的容器執行階段 (containerd) 拉取並快取的,而不是在 control plane 上。在 Amazon EKS 中,Kubernetes control plane (API server 與 etcd) 完全由 AWS 託管,並執行於 EKS 託管的 VPC 內;Amazon EKS 會配置、監控並替換這些 instance,因此客戶無法在 control plane 節點上安裝 SSM Agent,也無法對其執行 Systems Manager Run Command 或 State Manager 動作。這使選項 A 與 D (都指向 control plane) 不成立。所以 IAM role 必須允許 EventBridge 使用 Systems Manager 在叢集的 worker 節點上執行命令,且 State Manager association 必須以這些 worker 節點為目標。State Manager association 可透過 tags、個別 node ID 或 AWS Resource Groups 群組鎖定 managed node,且 AWS 官方文件明確指出:當你建立新節點並指派指定的 tag key/value 時,系統會自動套用並立即在這些節點上執行 association。由於工程師已在叢集與 node group 上設定 tags,以 tag 為目標 (選項 C) 可在現有 worker 節點上預先拉取映像,並自動涵蓋新加入的節點,滿足「即使在新加入節點上也將 pod 啟動時間維持在數秒」的需求。選項 B 不正確,因為 'machine size' 不是 State Manager 支援的鎖定方式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Targets the EKS control plane nodes. The control plane is fully AWS-managed inside an EKS-managed VPC; customers cannot install the SSM Agent or run Run Command there, and pod images are never cached on the control plane, so prefetching there is impossible and would not speed up pod startup.","why_zh":"以 EKS control plane 節點為目標。control plane 在 EKS 託管的 VPC 中由 AWS 完全託管,客戶無法在其上安裝 SSM Agent 或執行 Run Command,且 pod 映像從不會快取在 control plane,因此在那裡預取既不可能也無法加速 pod 啟動。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Runs on the correct worker nodes but targets by 'machine size', which is not a valid State Manager targeting option. State Manager associations target managed nodes by tags, individual node IDs, or AWS Resource Groups; machine-size targeting also would not automatically apply to newly added nodes and ignores the tags the engineer already configured.","why_zh":"雖在正確的 worker 節點上執行,但以 'machine size' 鎖定,而這並非有效的 State Manager 鎖定方式。State Manager association 以 tags、個別 node ID 或 AWS Resource Groups 鎖定 managed node;以 machine size 鎖定也無法自動套用到新加入的節點,並忽略了工程師已設定的 tags。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Like option A, it points the IAM policy and command execution at the AWS-managed EKS control plane nodes, which are inaccessible to Run Command and do not cache pod images. Even though it then mentions targeting by node tags, the execution target is wrong, so prefetching cannot occur.","why_zh":"與選項 A 相同,它將 IAM 政策與命令執行對象指向由 AWS 託管的 EKS control plane 節點,而這些節點無法使用 Run Command 且不會快取 pod 映像。即使後面提到以 node tags 鎖定,執行目標仍然錯誤,因此無法完成預取。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/eks-architecture.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-state-manager-targets-and-rate-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-associations-creating.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-about.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":243,"question_en":"A company's application has an API that retrieves workload metrics. The company needs to audit, analyze, and visualize these metrics from the application to detect issues at scale. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司的应用程序有一个 API，用于获取工作负载指标。该公司需要对这些指标进行审计、分析和可视化， 以便大规模地检测问题。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge schedule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that calls the API to retrieve workload metrics. Store the workload metric data in an Amazon S3 bucket.","B":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge schedule to invoke an AWS Lambda function that calls the API to retrieve workload metrics. Store the workload metric data in an Amazon DynamoDB table that has a DynamoDB stream enabled.","C":"Create an AWS Glue crawler to catalog the workload metric data in the Amazon S3 bucket. Create views in Amazon Athena for the cataloged data.","D":"Connect an AWS Glue crawler to the Amazon DynamoDB stream to catalog the workload metric data. Create views in Amazon Athena for the cataloged data.","E":"Create Amazon QuickSight datasets from the Amazon Athena views. Create a QuickSight analysis to visualize the workload metric data as a dashboard.","F":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard that has custom widgets that invoke AWS Lambda functions. Configure the Lambda functions to query the workload metrics data from the Amazon Athena views."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 计划，以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会调用 API 来获取工作负 载指标。将工作负载指标数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。","B":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 计划，以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会调用 API 来获取工作负 载指标。将工作负载指标数据存储在启用了 DynamoDB 流的 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。","C":"创建一个 AWS Glue 爬虫来对 Amazon S3 存储桶中的工作负载指标数据进行编目。在 Amazon Athena 中为编目的数据创建视图。","D":"将 AWS Glue 爬虫连接到 Amazon DynamoDB 流，以对工作负载指标数据进行编目。在 Amazon Athena 中为编目的数据创建视图。","E":"从 Amazon Athena 视图创建 Amazon QuickSight 数据集。创建一个 QuickSight 分析，将工作负载指标数 据可视化为仪表板。","F":"创建一个包含自定义小部件的 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板，这些小部件可调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配 置 Lambda 函数以从 Amazon Athena 视图中查询工作负载指标数据。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to audit, analyze, and visualize API workload metrics at scale, which maps to the canonical S3 data-lake analytics pattern: ingest -> catalog/query -> visualize. A handles ingestion: an Amazon EventBridge schedule invokes an AWS Lambda function that calls the API and stores the metrics durably in Amazon S3 (EventBridge Scheduler explicitly supports invoking Lambda on cron/rate schedules). C handles cataloging and querying: an AWS Glue crawler catalogs the S3 data into the Glue Data Catalog (S3 is a fully supported crawler data store), and Athena views are created over the AwsDataCatalog tables. E handles visualization at scale: QuickSight creates a dataset from the Athena (AwsDataCatalog) data and a QuickSight analysis renders a dashboard. The decisive technical fact eliminating the DynamoDB-stream path (B + D) is that AWS Glue crawlers do not support data streams. The Glue documentation explicitly states 'Currently AWS Glue does not support crawlers for data streams,' and a DynamoDB crawler targets a table, not a stream; so option D (connect a Glue crawler to a DynamoDB stream) is technically impossible, and B exists only to feed D.","explanation_zh":"需求是大規模地稽核、分析與視覺化 API 工作負載指標,對應到標準的 S3 資料湖分析模式:擷取 -> 編目/查詢 -> 視覺化。A 負責擷取:Amazon EventBridge 排程觸發 AWS Lambda 呼叫 API,並將指標持久化存到 Amazon S3(EventBridge Scheduler 明確支援以 cron/rate 排程觸發 Lambda)。C 負責編目與查詢:AWS Glue crawler 將 S3 資料編目到 Glue Data Catalog(S3 是完全支援的 crawler 資料來源),並在 AwsDataCatalog 的資料表上建立 Athena views。E 負責大規模視覺化:QuickSight 從 Athena(AwsDataCatalog)資料建立 dataset,並以 QuickSight analysis 呈現 dashboard。排除 DynamoDB stream 路徑(B + D)的關鍵技術事實是:AWS Glue crawler 不支援資料串流。Glue 文件明確指出 'Currently AWS Glue does not support crawlers for data streams',且 DynamoDB crawler 是針對 table 而非 stream,因此 D(將 Glue crawler 連到 DynamoDB stream)技術上不可行,而 B 僅是為了餵給 D 而存在。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Storing metrics in a DynamoDB table with a stream only makes sense as input to option D's stream crawling, which is impossible. DynamoDB streams capture item-level changes for event-driven processing, not for batch cataloging/analytics, and there is no native Glue crawler or Athena path that consumes a DynamoDB stream.","why_zh":"將指標存入啟用 stream 的 DynamoDB table 只有在搭配 D 的 stream 編目時才合理,而 D 不可行。DynamoDB streams 用於捕捉項目層級變更以做事件驅動處理,並非用於批次編目/分析,且沒有原生的 Glue crawler 或 Athena 路徑可消費 DynamoDB stream。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Glue crawlers cannot crawl data streams. The Glue docs explicitly state 'Currently AWS Glue does not support crawlers for data streams.' A crawler can crawl a DynamoDB table (you specify one table in the console) but not a DynamoDB stream, so this step is technically impossible.","why_zh":"AWS Glue crawler 無法編目資料串流。Glue 文件明確指出 'Currently AWS Glue does not support crawlers for data streams'。crawler 可以編目 DynamoDB table(在主控台中指定一個 table),但無法編目 DynamoDB stream,因此此步驟技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Using a CloudWatch dashboard with custom widgets that invoke Lambda functions to query Athena is a convoluted, high-overhead way to visualize query results and competes with the purpose-built option E. QuickSight is the documented, native tool for building datasets and dashboards over Athena data at scale, so F is the inferior/incorrect visualization choice.","why_zh":"使用 CloudWatch dashboard 的自訂 widget 觸發 Lambda 去查詢 Athena,是迂迴且高維運成本的視覺化方式,且與專為此設計的 E 競爭。QuickSight 才是用於大規模在 Athena 資料上建立 dataset 與 dashboard 的官方原生工具,因此 F 是較差/不正確的視覺化選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/glue/latest/dg/crawler-data-stores.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-eventbridge-scheduler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/views-glue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/quick/latest/userguide/create-a-data-set-athena.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":244,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is building the infrastructure for an application. The application needs to run on an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster that includes Amazon EC2 instances. The EC2 instances need to use an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system as a storage backend. The Amazon EFS Container Storage Interface (CSI) driver is installed on the EKS cluster. When the DevOps engineer starts the application, the EC2 instances do not mount the EFS file system. Which solutions will fix the problem? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在为一个应用程序构建基础设施。该应用程序需要在包含亚马逊 EC2 实例的亚马逊弹 性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群上运行。EC2 实例需要使用亚马逊弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS）文 件系统作为存储后端。Amazon EFS 容器存储接口（CSI）驱动程序已安装在 EKS 集群上。 当开发运维工程师启动应用程序时，EC2 实例未挂载 EFS 文件系统。 哪些解决方案能解决问题？（选择三个。）","options_en":{"A":"Switch the EKS nodes from Amazon EC2 to AWS Fargate.","B":"Add an inbound rule to the EFS file system’s security group to allow NFS traffic from the EKS cluster.","C":"Create an IAM role that allows the Amazon EFS CSI driver to interact with the file system","D":"Set up AWS DataSync to configure file transfer between the EFS file system and the EKS nodes.","E":"Create a mount target for the EFS file system in the subnet of the EKS nodes.","F":"Disable encryption or the EFS file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 EKS 节点从亚马逊 EC2 切换到 AWS Fargate。","B":"向 EFS 文件系统的安全组添加一条入站规则，以允许来自 EKS 集群的 NFS 流量。","C":"创建一个 IAM 角色，使 Amazon EFS CSI 驱动程序能够与文件系统进行交互","D":"设置 AWS DataSync 以配置 EFS 文件系统与 EKS 节点之间的文件传输。","E":"在 EKS 节点所在的子网中为 EFS 文件系统创建挂载目标。","F":"禁用加密或 EFS 文件系统。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Migration","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Mounting an Amazon EFS file system on EKS EC2 worker nodes via the Amazon EFS CSI driver has three prerequisites, all confirmed by AWS docs. (C) The EFS CSI driver needs IAM permissions: the EKS guide states 'The Amazon EFS CSI driver requires IAM permissions to interact with your file system. Create an IAM role and attach the AmazonEFSCSIDriverPolicy managed policy' (via EKS Pod Identity or IRSA). (E) A mount target must exist in the nodes' VPC: 'To access an EFS file system in a VPC, you need to create mount targets,' and 'at a minimum, you should create a mount target in each Availability Zone from which you want to access the file system.' An NFSv4.1 client can only mount if it can reach NFS port (TCP 2049) of a mount target. (B) The mount target's security group must have an inbound rule allowing NFS port 2049 from the EC2 instances; AWS docs explicitly require 'a mount target whose network interface has a security group with a rule that enables inbound connections on NFS port 2049 from the instance.' Without any one of these, the nodes cannot mount the file system, which is the reported symptom.","explanation_zh":"透過 Amazon EFS CSI driver 在 EKS 的 EC2 工作節點上掛載 EFS 檔案系統有三項先決條件，皆有 AWS 官方文件佐證。(C) EFS CSI driver 需要 IAM 權限：EKS 指南指出『Amazon EFS CSI driver 需要 IAM 權限才能與檔案系統互動，請建立 IAM role 並附加 AmazonEFSCSIDriverPolicy 受管政策』（透過 EKS Pod Identity 或 IRSA）。(E) 節點所在的 VPC 中必須存在 mount target：『要在 VPC 中存取 EFS 檔案系統，必須建立 mount target』，且『最低限度應在每個要存取檔案系統的可用區建立一個 mount target』。NFSv4.1 用戶端唯有能連到某個 mount target 的 NFS port (TCP 2049) 才能掛載。(B) mount target 的 security group 必須有允許來自 EC2 instance 的 NFS port 2049 入站規則；AWS 文件明確要求『mount target 的網路介面需有 security group 規則允許來自該 instance 的 NFS port 2049 入站連線』。缺少任一項，節點都無法掛載檔案系統，正是題目描述的症狀。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Switching EKS nodes from EC2 to AWS Fargate is a major architecture change that contradicts the stated requirement to run on EC2 instances, and it does not address the underlying mount misconfiguration (mount target, security group, or IAM role). It is not a remediation step.","why_zh":"把 EKS 節點從 EC2 改成 AWS Fargate 是重大架構變更，與題目要求在 EC2 上執行相牴觸，也未解決底層掛載設定問題（mount target、security group 或 IAM role），並非修正方式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS DataSync is a data-transfer/migration service that copies files between storage systems; it does not mount a file system into pods or nodes and cannot replace the EFS CSI driver's mount mechanism.","why_zh":"AWS DataSync 是資料傳輸/遷移服務，用於在儲存系統間複製檔案；它不會把檔案系統掛載到 pod 或節點，也無法取代 EFS CSI driver 的掛載機制。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"EFS encryption at rest is transparent to NFS clients and has no bearing on the ability to mount the file system; disabling it would not fix a mount failure, and encryption at rest cannot be changed after the file system is created anyway.","why_zh":"EFS 靜態加密對 NFS 用戶端是透明的，與檔案系統能否掛載無關；停用它無法解決掛載失敗，且靜態加密在檔案系統建立後也無法變更。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/efs-csi.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/network-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/manage-fs-access-create-delete-mount-targets.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":245,"question_en":"A company deploys an application on on-premises devices in the company’s on-premises data center. The company uses an AWS Direct Connect connection between the data center and the company's AWS account. During initial setup of the on-premises devices and during application updates, the application needs to retrieve configuration files from an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system. All traffic from the on-premises devices to Amazon EFS must remain private and encrypted. The on- premises devices must follow the principle of least privilege for AWS access. The company's DevOps team needs the ability to revoke access from a single device without affecting the access of the other devices. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在其本地数据中心的本地设备上部署了一个应用程序。该公司在本地数据中心和其 AWS 账户之间 使用了 AWS Direct Connect 连接。在本地设备的初始设置期间以及应用程序更新期间，该应用程序需要从 Amazon Elastic File System（Amazon EFS）文件系统中获取配置文件。 从本地设备到 Amazon EFS 的所有流量都必须保持私密并加密。本地设备访问 AWS 时必须遵循最小权限原 则。公司的 DevOps 团队需要能够撤销单个设备的访问权限，而不影响其他设备的访问权限。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM user that has an access key and a secret key for each device. Attach the AmazonElasticFileSystemFullAccess policy to all IAM users. Configure the AWS CLI on the on- premises devices to use the IAM user's access key and secret key.","B":"Generate certificates for each on-premises device in AWS Private Certificate Authority. Create a trust anchor in IAM Roles Anywhere that references an AWS Private CA. Create an IAM role that trust IAM Roles Anywhere. Attach the AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess to the role. Create an IAM Roles Anywhere profile for the IAM role. Configure the AWS CLI on the on-premises devices to use the aws_signing_helper command to obtain credentials.","C":"Create an IAM user that has an access key and a secret key for all devices. Attach the AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess policy to the IAM user. Configure the AWS CLI on the on-premises devices to use the IAM user's access key and secret key.","D":"Use the amazon-efs-utils package to mount the EFS file system.","E":"Use the native Linux NFS client to mount the EFS file system."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个设备创建一个具有访问密钥和秘密密钥的 IAM 用户。将 AmazonElasticFileSystemFullAcces s 策略附加到所有 IAM 用户。在本地设备上配置 AWS CLI 以使用 IAM 用户的访问密钥和秘密 密钥。","B":"在 AWS 私有证书颁发机构中为每个本地设备生成证书。在 IAM Roles Anywhere 中创建一个引用 AWS 私有 CA 的信任锚。创建一个信任 IAM Roles Anywhere 的 IAM 角色。将 AmazonElasticFileSystemClie ntReadWriteAccess 附加到该角色。为该 IAM 角色创建一个 IAM Roles Anywhere 配置文件。在本地设 备上配置 AWS CLI，使用 aws_signing_helper 命令获取凭证。","C":"创建一个具有访问密钥和秘密密钥的 IAM 用户，供所有设备使用。将 AmazonElasticFileSystemClientR eadWriteAccess 策略附加到该 IAM 用户。在本地设备上配置 AWS CLI，使其使用该 IAM 用户的访 问密钥和秘密密钥。","D":"使用 amazon-efs-utils 软件包挂载 EFS 文件系统。","E":"使用原生的 Linux NFS 客户端挂载 EFS 文件系统。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are private and encrypted EFS traffic, least-privilege AWS access for on-premises devices, and the ability to revoke a single device without affecting the others. Option B uses IAM Roles Anywhere: an AWS Private CA is registered as a trust anchor, an IAM role trusts the Roles Anywhere service principal and carries the scoped AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess managed policy, a profile constrains the session, and aws_signing_helper exchanges each device's X.509 certificate for temporary credentials. Per-device certificates eliminate long-term keys (least privilege) and let the team disable one device by listing its certificate in a certificate revocation list (CRL) without affecting others. Option D uses amazon-efs-utils: when encryption in transit is set as a mount option, the EFS mount helper starts a client stunnel process and uses TLS 1.2 to encrypt all NFS traffic, while Direct Connect keeps the path private. The native NFS client (E) does not encrypt by default; AWS docs explicitly state that to use encryption in transit you must mount with TLS using amazon-efs-utils, so E alone fails the encryption requirement. IAM user options A and C rely on long-term static keys: A also grants FullAccess (not least privilege), and C shares one credential across all devices, making single-device revocation impossible.","explanation_zh":"需求為：到 EFS 的流量必須私有且加密、地端裝置的 AWS 存取需符合最小權限、且能在不影響其他裝置的情況下撤銷單一裝置。選項 B 使用 IAM Roles Anywhere：以 AWS Private CA 註冊為 trust anchor，建立一個信任 Roles Anywhere service principal 並附掛範圍化 AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess 受管政策的 IAM role，再以 profile 限縮 session，並用 aws_signing_helper 將每台裝置的 X.509 憑證換成臨時憑證。每台裝置各自的憑證可消除長期金鑰（達成最小權限），並可藉由將某裝置憑證列入 certificate revocation list（CRL）來停用單一裝置而不影響其他裝置。選項 D 使用 amazon-efs-utils：當掛載選項啟用傳輸加密時，EFS mount helper 會啟動 client stunnel 程序並以 TLS 1.2 加密所有 NFS 流量，而 Direct Connect 維持路徑私有。原生 NFS client（E）預設不加密；AWS 文件明確指出要使用傳輸加密必須以 TLS（透過 amazon-efs-utils）掛載，因此單靠 E 不符加密需求。IAM user 選項 A、C 依賴長期靜態金鑰：A 還授予 FullAccess（非最小權限），C 則所有裝置共用同一組憑證，無法只撤銷單一裝置。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Relies on long-term static access/secret keys (an anti-pattern for external workloads) and attaches AmazonElasticFileSystemFullAccess, which grants far more than needed and violates least privilege. A per-device IAM user model also doesn't pair with any encryption-in-transit step on its own.","why_zh":"依賴長期靜態存取/秘密金鑰（外部工作負載的反模式），且附掛 AmazonElasticFileSystemFullAccess 授予遠超所需的權限，違反最小權限原則。每台裝置一個 IAM user 的做法本身也未搭配任何傳輸加密步驟。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A single shared IAM user and credential is used across all devices, so revoking it would cut off every device at once; you cannot revoke a single device without affecting the others. It also uses long-term static keys instead of temporary credentials.","why_zh":"所有裝置共用單一 IAM user 與憑證，撤銷時會一次切斷所有裝置，無法只撤銷單一裝置而不影響其他裝置；且使用長期靜態金鑰而非臨時憑證。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"The native Linux NFS client mounts EFS without encryption in transit by default. AWS docs state that to use encryption in transit you must mount with TLS using the amazon-efs-utils package (which starts stunnel and uses TLS 1.2). So a plain native NFS mount alone fails the encrypted-traffic requirement.","why_zh":"原生 Linux NFS client 預設掛載 EFS 不提供傳輸加密。AWS 文件指出要使用傳輸加密必須以 TLS（透過 amazon-efs-utils，會啟動 stunnel 並用 TLS 1.2）掛載，因此單靠原生 NFS 掛載不符加密需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/rolesanywhere/latest/userguide/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/iam-roles-anywhere-private-ca.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AmazonElasticFileSystemClientReadWriteAccess.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-rolesanywhere-crl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/efs-mount-helper.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/mounting-fs-old.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":246,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is setting up an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) blue/green deployment for an application by using AWS CodeDeploy and AWS CloudFormation. During the deployment window, the application must be highly available and CodeDeploy must shift 10% of traffic to a new version of the application every minute until all traffic is shifted. Which configuration should the DevOps engineer add in the CloudFormation template to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在使用 AWS CodeDeploy 和 AWS CloudFormation 为一个应用程序设置 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）蓝/绿部署。在部署窗口期间，应用程序必须保持高可用性，并且 CodeDeploy 每分钟必须将 10% 的流量切换到应用程序的新版本，直到所有流量都切换完成。 DevOps 工程师应在 CloudFormation 模板中添加哪种配置才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add an AppSpec file with the CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEverylMinutes deployment configuration.","B":"Add the AWS::CodeDeployBlueGreen transform and the AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen hook parameter with the CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery1Minutes deployment configuration.","C":"Add an AppSpec file with the ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes deployment configuration.","D":"Add the AWS::CodeDeployBlueGreen transform and the AWS::CodeDepioy::BlueGreen hook parameter with the ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes deployment configuration."},"options_zh":{"A":"添加一个 AppSpec 文件，并使用 CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEverylMinutes 部署配置。 BCodeDeployBlueGreen 转换以及带有 CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery1Minutes 部署配置的 AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen 挂钩参数。","C":"添加一个包含 ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes 部署配置的 AppSpec 文件。 DCodeDeployBlueGreen 转换以及带有 ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes 部署CodeDeploy::BlueGreen 钩子参数。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The deployment is set up via AWS CloudFormation, so the CloudFormation-native mechanism for an ECS blue/green deployment through CodeDeploy must be used. AWS documentation states that to perform CodeDeploy blue/green deployments on ECS using CloudFormation you include a Hooks section describing an AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen hook AND a Transform section specifying the AWS::CodeDeployBlueGreen transform. This rules out options A and C, which rely on a separate AppSpec file (the AppSpec / named-deployment-config approach is for directly CodeDeploy-managed deployments, not CloudFormation-managed ones). Between the two transform/hook options, the requirement to shift 10 percent of traffic every minute until all traffic is shifted is a linear pattern that exactly matches CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery1Minutes ('Shifts 10 percent of traffic every minute until all traffic is shifted'), whereas ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes shifts 10 percent and then the remaining 90 percent five minutes later and does not match. Therefore B is the only option pairing the correct CloudFormation transform/hook approach with the correct 10%/1-minute linear behavior. (Note: in the real hook, traffic shifting is expressed via TrafficRoutingConfig with Type TimeBasedLinear, StepPercentage, and BakeTimeMins rather than a named config string, but among the four choices B is unambiguously the intended answer.)","explanation_zh":"此部署是透過 AWS CloudFormation 設定的，因此必須使用 CloudFormation 原生的 ECS blue/green (透過 CodeDeploy) 機制。AWS 文件指出，要透過 CloudFormation 對 ECS 執行 CodeDeploy blue/green 部署，範本中需包含描述 AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen hook 的 Hooks 區段，以及指定 AWS::CodeDeployBlueGreen transform 的 Transform 區段。這排除了仰賴另一個 AppSpec 檔的選項 A 與 C（AppSpec／具名部署設定的做法適用於由 CodeDeploy 直接管理的部署，而非由 CloudFormation 管理）。在兩個 transform/hook 選項之間，需求是每分鐘轉移 10% 流量直到全部轉移完成，屬於線性 (linear) 模式，正好對應 CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery1Minutes（每分鐘轉移 10% 流量直到全部轉移）；而 ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes 是先轉移 10%、五分鐘後再轉移剩餘 90%，並不符合。因此 B 是唯一同時搭配正確 CloudFormation transform/hook 做法與正確 10%/每分鐘線性行為的選項。（註：實際 hook 中的流量轉移是以 TrafficRoutingConfig 的 Type TimeBasedLinear、StepPercentage 與 BakeTimeMins 表示，而非具名設定字串，但四個選項中 B 顯然是題意所指的答案。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses an AppSpec file, which is the directly CodeDeploy-managed approach, not the CloudFormation-managed one required here (transform + AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen hook). The question explicitly asks what to add 'in the CloudFormation template'. It also has the OCR typo 'EverylMinutes' instead of 'Every1Minutes', but the deciding flaw is the AppSpec mechanism.","why_zh":"使用 AppSpec 檔，這是由 CodeDeploy 直接管理的做法，而非本題要求的 CloudFormation 管理做法（transform + AWS::CodeDeploy::BlueGreen hook）。題目明確問要在 CloudFormation 範本中加入什麼。此外字串為 OCR 錯字 'EverylMinutes' 而非 'Every1Minutes'，但決定性的錯誤在於採用 AppSpec 機制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Doubly wrong: it uses an AppSpec file (wrong mechanism for a CloudFormation-managed deployment) AND uses ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes, a canary pattern that shifts 10 percent then the remaining 90 percent after five minutes rather than 10 percent every minute. It also omits the CodeDeployDefault prefix.","why_zh":"雙重錯誤：使用 AppSpec 檔（對 CloudFormation 管理的部署而言是錯誤機制），且採用 ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes，屬 canary 模式，先轉移 10%、五分鐘後再轉移剩餘 90%，並非每分鐘 10%。名稱也缺少 CodeDeployDefault 前綴。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses the correct CloudFormation transform + hook mechanism, but pairs it with ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes, a canary pattern that shifts 10 percent then the remaining 90 percent five minutes later. This does not meet the required linear 10%-every-minute traffic shift. (It also has the OCR typo 'CodeDepioy'.)","why_zh":"採用正確的 CloudFormation transform + hook 機制，但搭配 ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes，屬 canary 模式，先轉移 10%、五分鐘後再轉移剩餘 90%，不符合每分鐘轉移 10% 的線性需求。（且含 OCR 錯字 'CodeDepioy'。）"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/blue-green.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/blue-green-hook-syntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/transform-aws-codedeploybluegreen.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":247,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The company's DevOps team has developed an AWS Lambda function that calls the Organizations API to create new AWS accounts. The Lambda function runs in the organization's management account. The DevOps team needs to move the Lambda function from the management account to a dedicated AWS account. The DevOps team must ensure that the Lambda function has the ability to create new AWS accounts only in Organizations before the team deploys the Lambda function to the new account. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司的 DevOps 团队开发了一个 AWS Lambda 函数， 该函数调用 Organizations API 来创建新的 AWS 账户。 Lambda 函数在组织的管理账户中运行。DevOps 团队需要将该 Lambda 函数从管理账户迁移到一个专用 的 AWS 账户。在团队将 Lambda 函数部署到新账户之前，DevOps 团队必须确保该 Lambda 函数仅能在 Organizations 中创建新的 AWS 账户。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"In the management account, create a new IAM role that has the necessary permission to create new accounts in Organizations. Allow the role to be assumed by the Lambda execution role in the new AWS account. Update the Lambda function code to assume the role when the Lambda function creates new AWS accounts. Update the Lambda execution role to ensure that it has permission to assume the new role.","B":"In the management account, turn on delegated administration for Organizations. Create a new delegation policy that grants the new AWS account permission to create new AWS accounts in Organizations. Ensure that the Lambda execution role has the organizations:CreateAccount permission.","C":"In the management account, create a new IAM role that has the necessary permission to create new accounts in Organizations. Allow the role to be assumed by the Lambda service principal. Update the Lambda function code to assume the role when the Lambda function creates new AWS accounts. Update the Lambda execution role to ensure that it has permission to assume the new role.","D":"In the management account, enable AWS Control Tower. Turn on delegated administration for AWS Control Tower. Create a resource policy that allows the new AWS account to create new AWS accounts in AWS Control Tower. Update the Lambda function code to use the AWS Control Tower API in the new AWS account. Ensure that the Lambda execution role has the controltower:CreateManagedAccount permission."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户中，创建一个具有在 Organizations 中创建新账户所需权限的新 IAM 角色。允许该角色由新 AWS 账户中的 Lambda 执行角色进行承担。更新 Lambda 函数代码，使其在创建新 AWS 账户时承担 该角色。更新 Lambda 执行角色，确保其具有承担新角色的权限。","B":"在管理控制台中，为组织启用委托管理功能。创建一个新的委托策略，授予新的 AWS 账户在 组织中创建新 AWS 账户的权限。确保 Lambda 执行角色具有 organizations:CreateAccount 权 限。","C":"在管理账户中，创建一个具有在 Organizations 中创建新账户所需权限的新 IAM 角色。允许 Lambda 服务主体承担该角色。更新 Lambda 函数代码，使其在创建新的 AWS 账户时承担该角色。更新 Lambda 执行角色，确保其具有承担新角色的权限。","D":"在管理账户中启用 AWS Control Tower。为 AWS Control Tower 启用委托管理。创建一个资源策略， 允许新 AWS 账户在 AWS Control Tower 中创建新的 AWS 账户。更新 Lambda 函数代码，使其在新 AWS 账户中使用 AWS Control Tower API。确保 Lambda 执行角色具有 controltower: CreateManagedAccount 权限。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The organizations:CreateAccount action can be called ONLY from the organization's management account. AWS's 'API operations by account type' page lists CreateAccount under 'Operations you can call from only the organization's management account,' and it is deliberately absent from the delegated-administrator list. Therefore, after the Lambda function is moved to a dedicated member account, it cannot create accounts with its own local execution role. The correct pattern is the standard cross-account IAM role delegation: create an IAM role in the management account that holds the CreateAccount permission, configure its trust policy to allow the assuming cross-account principal (the Lambda execution role ARN in the new account), grant the execution role sts:AssumeRole permission, and have the function assume that management-account role before calling CreateAccount. Option A describes exactly this: the trust policy allows the Lambda execution role in the new account to assume the role. When an application/Lambda assumes a role in another account, STS authenticates the execution role (the originating principal), so the execution role is the correct entity to name in the trust policy.","explanation_zh":"organizations:CreateAccount 動作只能從組織的 management account 呼叫。AWS 的「API operations by account type」文件將 CreateAccount 列在「Operations you can call from only the organization's management account」之下，且刻意不出現在 delegated administrator 可呼叫的清單中。因此當 Lambda function 被移到專屬的 member account 後，它無法用自身的本地 execution role 建立帳號。正確做法是標準的跨帳號 IAM role 委派：在 management account 中建立一個具有 CreateAccount 權限的 IAM role，將其 trust policy 設定為允許跨帳號的主體（即新帳號中的 Lambda execution role ARN）來 assume 此 role，並賦予 execution role sts:AssumeRole 權限，讓 function 在呼叫 CreateAccount 前先 assume 該 management account 的 role。Option A 正是描述此流程：trust policy 允許新帳號中的 Lambda execution role 來 assume 該 role。當應用程式/Lambda 跨帳號 assume role 時，STS 驗證的是 execution role（發起方主體），因此 trust policy 中應指名 execution role。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CreateAccount is a management-account-only operation; it is NOT in the list of operations a delegated administrator may call. Organizations has no 'delegation policy' construct that grants a member account the ability to create new accounts (delegated administration is enabled per service via RegisterDelegatedAdministrator). Merely giving the execution role organizations:CreateAccount in a member account does not work because the call is rejected when it is not made from the management account.","why_zh":"CreateAccount 只能從 management account 呼叫，不在 delegated administrator 可呼叫的清單中。Organizations 並沒有可讓 member account 取得建立新帳號能力的「delegation policy」機制（delegated administration 是透過 RegisterDelegatedAdministrator 依服務啟用）。單純在 member account 賦予 execution role organizations:CreateAccount 權限也無效，因為非從 management account 發出的呼叫會被拒絕。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It names the Lambda service principal (lambda.amazonaws.com) as the trusted entity. A service principal in a trust policy authorizes the Lambda service to assume a role on behalf of a function in the SAME account (e.g., the execution role itself); it does not let a function running in a DIFFERENT account assume the management-account role. The cross-account caller authenticated by STS at runtime is the execution role, not the Lambda service, so the trust policy must name the execution role's ARN. The option is also internally inconsistent: trusting only the service principal while telling the execution role to assume the role contradicts itself.","why_zh":"它將 Lambda service principal（lambda.amazonaws.com）設為受信任主體。trust policy 中的 service principal 是授權 Lambda 服務在「同一帳號」內代表 function（例如 execution role 本身）來 assume role，並不能讓在「不同帳號」執行的 function 去 assume management account 的 role。執行期 STS 驗證的跨帳號呼叫者是 execution role，而非 Lambda 服務，因此 trust policy 必須指名 execution role 的 ARN。此選項本身也自相矛盾：一邊只信任 service principal，一邊又要 execution role 去 assume role。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This rearchitects the solution onto AWS Control Tower instead of meeting the stated requirement of creating accounts via Organizations CreateAccount. There is no 'resource policy that allows the new AWS account to create accounts in Control Tower'; Account Factory provisioning is driven through Service Catalog and the AWSControlTowerExecution role, not a controltower:CreateManagedAccount call from an arbitrary member account. It also assumes Control Tower is wanted at all, which the scenario does not ask for, making it an over-engineered, off-scope, incorrect answer.","why_zh":"此選項把方案改架到 AWS Control Tower，而非滿足題目以 Organizations CreateAccount 建立帳號的需求。並不存在「允許新 AWS 帳號在 Control Tower 建立帳號的 resource policy」；Account Factory 的佈建是透過 Service Catalog 與 AWSControlTowerExecution role 進行，而非由任意 member account 呼叫 controltower:CreateManagedAccount。它也假設一定要用 Control Tower，但題目並未提出此需求，屬於過度設計、超出範圍且錯誤的答案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_reference_actions-by-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/APIReference/API_CreateAccount.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-organizations-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/tutorial_cross-account-with-roles.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_principal.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies-cross-account-resource-access.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":248,"question_en":"A company has deployed an application in a single AWS Region. The application backend uses Amazon DynamoDB tables and Amazon S3 buckets. The company wants to deploy the application in a secondary Region. The company must ensure that the data in the DynamoDB tables and the S3 buckets persists across both Regions. The data must also immediately propagate across Regions. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司已在单个 AWS 区域部署了一个应用程序。该应用程序的后端使用了 Amazon DynamoDB 表和 Amazon S3 存储桶。 该公司希望在辅助区域部署应用程序。公司必须确保 DynamoDB 表和 S3 存储桶中的数据在两个区域都 能持久保存。数据还必须立即在两个区域之间同步传播。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Implement two-way S3 bucket replication between the primary Region's S3 buckets and the secondary Region’s S3 buckets. Convert the DynamoDB tables into global tables. Set the secondary Region as the additional Region.","B":"Implement S3 Batch Operations copy jobs between the primary Region and the secondary Region for all S3 buckets. Convert the DynamoDB tables into global tables. Set the secondary Region as the additional Region.","C":"Implement two-way S3 bucket replication between the primary Region's S3 buckets and the secondary Region's S3 buckets. Enable DynamoDB streams on the DynamoDB tables in both Regions. In each Region, create an AWS Lambda function that subscribes to the DynamoDB streams. Configure the Lambda function to copy new records to the DynamoDB tables in the other Region.","D":"Implement S3 Batch Operations copy jobs between the primary Region and the secondary Region for all S3 buckets. Enable DynamoDB streams on the DynamoDB tables in both Regions. In each Region, create an AWS Lambda function that subscribes to the DynamoDB streams. Configure the Lambda function to copy new records to the DynamoDB tables in the other Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"在主区域的 S3 存储桶与辅助区域的 S3 存储桶之间实现双向复制。将 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表。将 辅助区域设置为 附加区域","B":"在主区域和辅助区域之间为所有 S3 存储桶实施 S3 批量操作复制任务。将 DynamoDB 表转换为全局表。 将辅助区域设置为附加区域。","C":"在主区域的 S3 存储桶与辅助区域的 S3 存储桶之间实现双向复制。在两个区域的 DynamoDB 表上启用 DynamoDB 流。在每个区域中，创建一个订阅 DynamoDB 流的 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函 数，使其将新记录复制到另一个区域的 DynamoDB 表中。","D":"在主区域和辅助区域之间为所有 S3 存储桶实施 S3 批量操作复制任务。在两个区域的 DynamoDB 表上启 用 DynamoDB 流。在每个区域中，创建一个订阅 DynamoDB 流的 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函 数将新记录复制到另一个区域的 DynamoDB 表中。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are bidirectional data persistence across two Regions, near-immediate (continuous) propagation, and the MOST operational efficiency. Option A uses two fully managed, AWS-native features: S3 two-way (bi-directional) live Cross-Region Replication and DynamoDB global tables. S3 live replication automatically and asynchronously copies new and updated objects as they are written to the source bucket; configuring replication on both buckets gives the required two-way replication, which AWS explicitly documents as a supported pattern ('two-way replication (bi-directional replication)'). DynamoDB global tables provide fully managed, multi-active, multi-Region replication with asynchronous, last-writer-wins propagation and require no application changes - you simply add the secondary Region as an additional replica. Both services are managed, require no custom code, and propagate continuously, so Option A delivers the highest operational efficiency.","explanation_zh":"需求是雙向資料在兩個 Region 之間持續保存、近乎即時（持續）傳播，並且要求最高的運維效率。選項 A 使用兩個完全受管、AWS 原生的功能：S3 雙向（bi-directional）live Cross-Region Replication 與 DynamoDB global tables。S3 live replication 會在物件寫入來源 bucket 時自動且非同步地複製新增與更新的物件；在兩個 bucket 上都設定複製即可達成所需的雙向複製，AWS 文件明確列出 'two-way replication (bi-directional replication)' 為支援的模式。DynamoDB global tables 提供完全受管、multi-active、multi-Region 的複製，採非同步、last-writer-wins 傳播，且不需要修改應用程式 - 只需將次要 Region 加入為額外的 replica。兩項服務皆為受管服務、無需自訂程式碼且能持續傳播，因此選項 A 提供最高的運維效率。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 Batch Operations / S3 Batch Replication copy jobs are on-demand (batch) copies of a defined set of existing objects, not live replication. They do not continuously propagate new objects as they are written, so they fail the 'immediately propagate' requirement and add job-management overhead. (The DynamoDB global tables half is correct.)","why_zh":"S3 Batch Operations / S3 Batch Replication copy jobs 是針對一組既有物件的隨選（批次）複製，並非 live replication。它不會在新物件寫入時持續傳播，因此不符合『立即傳播』需求，且增加批次作業管理負擔。（DynamoDB global tables 部分正確。）"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The S3 two-way replication half is correct, but building custom Lambda functions subscribed to DynamoDB Streams to copy records across Regions reinvents what DynamoDB global tables provide natively. It requires custom code, error handling, conflict resolution, and loop-prevention logic, carrying high operational overhead and far less efficiency than global tables.","why_zh":"S3 雙向複製部分正確，但自行建立訂閱 DynamoDB Streams 的 Lambda 函式來跨 Region 複製記錄，是重新發明 DynamoDB global tables 原生提供的功能。需自訂程式碼、錯誤處理、衝突解決與防止複製迴圈，運維負擔高，遠不如 global tables 有效率。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines both weakest choices: S3 Batch Operations (batch, not continuous, fails immediate propagation) plus custom Lambda/Streams replication (high operational overhead and conflict risk). It fails the immediate-propagation requirement for S3 and is the least operationally efficient overall.","why_zh":"結合了兩個最差的做法：S3 Batch Operations（批次、非持續，不符合立即傳播）加上自訂 Lambda/Streams 複製（運維負擔高且有衝突風險）。在 S3 不符合即時傳播需求，整體運維效率最低。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":249,"question_en":"A company has configured Amazon RDS storage autoscaling for its RDS DB instances. A DevOps team needs to visualize the autoscaling events on an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司已为其 RDS 数据库实例配置了 Amazon RDS 存储自动扩展功能。DevOps 团队需要在 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板上可视化这些自动扩展事件。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to RDS storage autoscaling events from RDS events. Create an AWS Lambda function that publishes a CloudWatch custom metric. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function. Visualize the custom metric by using the CloudWatch dashboard.","B":"Create a trail by using AWS CloudTrail with management events configured. Configure the trail to send the management events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a metric filter in CloudWatch Logs to match the RDS storage autoscaling events. Visualize the metric filter by using the CloudWatch dashboard.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to RDS storage autoscaling events from the RDS events. Create a CloudWatch alarm. Configure the EventBridge rule to change the status of the CloudWatch alarm. Visualize the alarm status by using the CloudWatch dashboard.","D":"Create a trail by using AWS CloudTrail with data events configured. Configure the trail to send the data events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a metric filter in CloudWatch Logs to match the RDS storage autoscaling events. Visualize the metric filter by using the CloudWatch dashboard."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对来自 RDS 事件的 RDS 存储自动扩展事件做出反应。创建一 个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于发布 CloudWatch 自定义指标。配置 EventBridge 规则以调用 Lambda 函数。 使用 CloudWatch 控制面板可视化自定义指标。","B":"使用配置了管理事件的 AWS CloudTrail 创建一条跟踪记录。将跟踪记录配置为将管理事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。在 CloudWatch Logs 中创建一个指标过滤器以匹配 RDS 存储自动扩展事件。 使用 CloudWatch 控制面板可视化该指标过滤器。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对来自 RDS 事件的 RDS 存储自动扩展事件做出反应。创 建一个 CloudWatch 警报。配置 EventBridge 规则以更改 CloudWatch 警报的状态。使用 CloudWatch 控制面板可视化警报状态。","D":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 并配置数据事件来创建一条跟踪。将跟踪配置为将数据事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。在 CloudWatch Logs 中创建一个指标过滤器以匹配 RDS 存储自动扩展事件。使用 CloudWatch 控制面板可视化该指标过滤器。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon RDS storage autoscaling actions are emitted as RDS DB instance events: RDS-EVENT-0217 (\"Applying autoscaling-initiated modification to allocated storage\") and RDS-EVENT-0218 (\"Finished applying autoscaling-initiated modification to allocated storage\"), both in the configuration change category (confirmed in the RDS event messages doc). Per the EventBridge events reference, RDS sends these directly to Amazon EventBridge as an \"RDS DB Instance Event\" with source aws.rds, so an EventBridge rule can match them in near real time. EventBridge cannot graph an event on its own, and AWS Lambda function (ASYNC) is a supported EventBridge target, so the rule invokes a Lambda function that calls CloudWatch PutMetricData to publish a custom metric, which is then graphed on a CloudWatch dashboard. That is exactly option A. Option C is impossible because EventBridge has no target action that changes a CloudWatch alarm's status (alarm state is computed from metric data; the only manual override, SetAlarmState, is for testing, auto-reverts, and is not an EventBridge target). Options B and D rely on CloudTrail: the autoscaling-initiated storage change is an internal RDS service event rather than a reliably matchable user management-event API call, and it is categorically not a CloudTrail data event.","explanation_zh":"Amazon RDS storage autoscaling 的動作會以 RDS DB 執行個體事件形式發出：RDS-EVENT-0217（\"Applying autoscaling-initiated modification to allocated storage\"）與 RDS-EVENT-0218（\"Finished applying autoscaling-initiated modification to allocated storage\"），兩者皆屬 configuration change 類別（已於 RDS event messages 文件確認）。根據 EventBridge events 參考文件，RDS 會將這些事件以 \"RDS DB Instance Event\"（source 為 aws.rds）直接送往 Amazon EventBridge，因此 EventBridge rule 可近乎即時地比對到它們。EventBridge 本身無法繪製事件圖表，而 AWS Lambda function（ASYNC）是受支援的 EventBridge target，所以由 rule 觸發 Lambda function，呼叫 CloudWatch PutMetricData 發佈一個 custom metric，再於 CloudWatch dashboard 上視覺化。這正是選項 A。選項 C 不可行，因為 EventBridge 沒有任何 target 動作可以改變 CloudWatch alarm 的狀態（alarm 狀態由 metric data 推算；唯一可手動覆寫的 SetAlarmState 僅供測試、會自動還原，且不是 EventBridge target）。選項 B 與 D 依賴 CloudTrail：autoscaling 觸發的儲存變更是 RDS 內部服務事件，而非可可靠比對的使用者 management event API 呼叫，並且它絕對不是 CloudTrail data event。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Storage autoscaling is delivered as an internal RDS service event (RDS DB Instance Event, source aws.rds), not as a user-driven management-event API call that you can reliably match in a CloudTrail management-events trail. RDS already sends these events directly to EventBridge, so routing through CloudTrail Logs plus a metric filter is an indirect, unreliable design compared with option A.","why_zh":"Storage autoscaling 是以 RDS 內部服務事件（RDS DB Instance Event，source 為 aws.rds）送出，而非可在 CloudTrail management events trail 中可靠比對的使用者觸發 management event API 呼叫。RDS 本來就會將這些事件直接送往 EventBridge，因此繞經 CloudTrail Logs 加 metric filter 相較於選項 A 是間接且不可靠的設計。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EventBridge has no target that 'changes the status of a CloudWatch alarm.' Alarm state is derived from metric data evaluations; the only API to set it manually is SetAlarmState, which is intended for testing, automatically reverts to the metric-derived state, and is not an EventBridge target. The dependency is also backwards: a CloudWatch alarm state change can be a source of EventBridge events, not the result of one.","why_zh":"EventBridge 沒有任何 target 可以「改變 CloudWatch alarm 的狀態」。alarm 狀態是依 metric data 評估推算而來；唯一可手動設定的 SetAlarmState API 僅供測試、會自動還原為依 metric 推算的狀態，且不是 EventBridge target。其相依方向也相反：CloudWatch alarm 狀態變化可以是 EventBridge 事件的來源，而非由 EventBridge 動作所造成的結果。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail data events capture resource-level data-plane operations such as S3 object access, Lambda function invocations, and DynamoDB item activity. RDS storage autoscaling is not a CloudTrail data event at all, so a data-events trail would never record it, making the metric filter approach impossible.","why_zh":"CloudTrail data events 擷取的是資源層級的資料平面操作，例如 S3 物件存取、Lambda function 呼叫與 DynamoDB 項目活動。RDS storage autoscaling 根本不是 CloudTrail data event，因此 data events trail 永遠不會記錄到它，使得這個 metric filter 方法無法成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-rds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_Events.Messages.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_PIOPS.Autoscaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-targets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/publishingMetrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Acting_Alarm_Changes.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":250,"question_en":"A company uses containers for its applications. The company learns that some container images are missing required security configurations. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to create a standard base image. The solution must publish the base image weekly to the us-west-2 Region, us-east-2 Region, and eu-central-1 Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用容器来运行其应用程序。该公司发现一些容器镜像缺少必要的安全配置。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案来创建一个标准的基础镜像。该解决方案必须每周将基础镜 像发布到 us-west-2 区域、us-east-2 区域和 eu-central-1 区域。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an EC2 Image Builder pipeline that uses a container recipe to build the image. Configure the pipeline to distribute the image to an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository in us-west-2. Configure ECR replication from us-west-2 to us-east-2 and from us-east-2 to eu-central-1. Configure the pipeline to run weekly.","B":"Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses an AWS CodeBuild project to build the image. Use AWS CodeDeploy to publish the image to an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository in us-west-2. Configure ECR replication from us-west-2 to us-east-2 and from us-east-2 to eu-central-1. Configure the pipeline to run weekly.","C":"Create an EC2 Image Builder pipeline that uses a container recipe to build the image. Configure the pipeline to distribute the image to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories in all three Regions. Configure the pipeline to run weekly.","D":"Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses an AWS CodeBuild project to build the image. Use AWS CodeDeploy to publish the image to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories in all three Regions. Configure the pipeline to run weekly."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个使用容器配方来构建映像的 EC2 Image Builder 管道。将管道配置为将映像分发到 us-west-2 区 域的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库。配置 ECR 从 us-west-2 复制到 us- east-2，再从 us-east-2 复制到 eu-central-1。将管道配置为每周运行一次。","B":"创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道使用 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建镜像。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将镜像发布到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 。 在 us-west-2 区域设置存储库。配置从 us-west-2 到 us-east-2 以及从 us-east-2 到 eu-central-1 的 ECR 复 制。将管道配置为每周运行一次。","C":"创建一个使用容器配方来构建映像的 EC2 Image Builder 管道。将管道配置为将映像分发到所有三个区域 的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储库。将管道配置为每周运行一次。","D":"创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道使用 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建镜像。使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将镜像发布到所有三个区域的 Amazon Elastic Container Registry （Amazon ECR） 存储 库。将管道配置为每周运行一次。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"EC2 Image Builder container recipes are purpose-built to produce a standardized, hardened base Docker image, and the pipeline's distribution settings natively deliver the output image to Amazon ECR. Per the container-pipeline tutorial, distribution settings 'consist of the target Regions, and the target Amazon ECR repository name. Output Docker images are deployed to the named Amazon ECR repository in each Region,' and you can 'add more Regions for distribution.' A single distribution configuration can therefore push the image directly to ECR in all three Regions (us-west-2, us-east-2, eu-central-1), and the pipeline supports a built-in schedule (weekly). Option A fails because it relies on chained ECR replication: the ECR docs explicitly state 'A replication action only occurs once per image push or image restore... an image pushed to us-west-2 replicates to only us-east-1, it doesn't replicate again to us-east-2,' so eu-central-1 would never receive the image. Options B and D fail because AWS CodeDeploy does not push or publish container images to ECR (CodeDeploy deploys to EC2/on-prem, Lambda, or ECS); image publishing is done via docker push, typically from CodeBuild.","explanation_zh":"EC2 Image Builder container recipe 專門用來產生標準化、強化過的 base Docker image，且 pipeline 的 distribution settings 能原生地將輸出 image 發布到 Amazon ECR。依照官方 container pipeline 教學，distribution settings「由目標 Regions 與目標 Amazon ECR repository 名稱組成。輸出的 Docker image 會部署到每個 Region 中所指定的 Amazon ECR repository」，並且可以「新增更多 Regions 進行 distribution」。因此單一 distribution configuration 即可直接將 image 推送到全部三個 Region (us-west-2、us-east-2、eu-central-1) 的 ECR，且 pipeline 內建排程 (每週)。選項 A 錯誤，因為它依賴鏈式 ECR replication：ECR 文件明確指出「replication 動作每次 image push 或 restore 只會發生一次……推送到 us-west-2 的 image 只會複製到 us-east-1，不會再複製到 us-east-2」，因此 eu-central-1 永遠收不到 image。選項 B 與 D 錯誤，因為 AWS CodeDeploy 不會將 container image 推送或發布到 ECR (CodeDeploy 是部署到 EC2/on-prem、Lambda 或 ECS)；image 的發布是透過 docker push 完成，通常由 CodeBuild 執行。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Chained ECR replication does not work. AWS docs state a replication action only occurs once per image push and replicated images are not re-replicated, so an image pushed to us-west-2 replicates only to us-east-2 and never reaches eu-central-1. It also adds unnecessary complexity since Image Builder can distribute to all three Regions directly.","why_zh":"鏈式 ECR replication 無法運作。AWS 文件指出 replication 每次 push 只發生一次，已被複製的 image 不會再被複製，因此推送到 us-west-2 的 image 只會到 us-east-2，永遠不會到達 eu-central-1。同時也多此一舉，因為 Image Builder 可直接散佈到全部三個 Region。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS CodeDeploy does not publish container images to Amazon ECR. CodeDeploy deploys applications to EC2/on-prem, Lambda, or ECS compute platforms; pushing an image to ECR is done with docker push (typically in CodeBuild), not CodeDeploy. It also reuses the flawed chained ECR replication that never reaches eu-central-1.","why_zh":"AWS CodeDeploy 不會將 container image 發布到 Amazon ECR。CodeDeploy 是把應用部署到 EC2/on-prem、Lambda 或 ECS 計算平台；將 image 推送到 ECR 是用 docker push (通常在 CodeBuild) 完成，而非 CodeDeploy。它同樣使用無法抵達 eu-central-1 的有缺陷鏈式 ECR replication。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS CodeDeploy cannot push or publish container images to ECR repositories; image publishing is not a CodeDeploy capability. CodeDeploy targets EC2/on-prem, Lambda, and ECS service deployments, not registry image pushes. Even though it targets all three Regions directly, using CodeDeploy to publish images is technically invalid.","why_zh":"AWS CodeDeploy 無法將 container image 推送或發布到 ECR repository；發布 image 不是 CodeDeploy 的功能。CodeDeploy 針對的是 EC2/on-prem、Lambda 與 ECS 服務部署，而非 registry image 推送。即使它直接以三個 Region 為目標，用 CodeDeploy 發布 image 在技術上仍不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/start-build-container-pipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/how-image-builder-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-imagebuilder-distributionconfiguration-targetcontainerrepository.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":251,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to implement a solution to install antivirus software on all the Amazon EC2 instances in an AWS account. The EC2 instances run the most recent version of Amazon Linux. The solution must detect all instances and must use an AWS Systems Manager document to install the software if the software is not present. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要实施一个解决方案，在 AWS 账户中的所有 Amazon EC2 实例上安装防病毒软 件。这些 EC2 实例运行的是最新版的 Amazon Linux。 该解决方案必须检测所有实例，并且如果软件不存在，必须使用 AWS 系统管理器文档来安装该软件。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an association in Systems Manager State Manager. Target all the managed nodes. Include the software in the association. Configure the association to use the Systems Manager document.","B":"Set up AWS Config to record all the resources in the account. Create an AWS Config custom rule to determine if the software is installed on all the EC2 instances. Configure an automatic remediation action that uses the Systems Manager document for noncompliant EC2 instances.","C":"Activate Amazon EC2 scanning on Amazon Inspector to determine if the software is installed on all the EC2 instances. Associate the findings with the Systems Manager document.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses AWS CloudTrail to detect the Runinstances API call. Configure inventory collection in Systems Manager Inventory to determine if the software is installed on the EC2 instances. Associate the Systems Manager inventory with the Systems Manager document."},"options_zh":{"A":"在系统管理器状态管理器中创建一个关联。将所有受管节点作为目标。在关联中包含该软件。配置该关 联以使用系统管理器文档。","B":"设置 AWS Config 以记录账户中的所有资源。创建一个 AWS Config 自定义规则，以确定软件是否已安 装在所有 EC2 实例上。配置一个自动修复操作，该操作使用 Systems Manager 文档来修复不符合要 求的 EC2 实例。","C":"在 Amazon Inspector 中激活 Amazon EC2 扫描，以确定该软件是否已安装在所有 EC2 实例上。将发现结 果与 Systems Manager 文档相关联。","D":"创建一个使用 AWS CloudTrail 检测 RunInstances API 调用的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。在 Systems Manager Inventory 中配置库存收集以确定软件是否已安装在 EC2 实例上。将 Systems Manager 库存与 Systems Manager 文档相关联。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Systems Manager State Manager is purpose-built for this requirement, and the AWS documentation uses this exact antivirus scenario as its canonical example. A State Manager association is a configuration you assign to your resources that defines the state to maintain: 'an association can specify that antivirus software must be installed and running on a managed node.' The same doc states that 'an association for antivirus software might run once a day on all managed nodes in an AWS account. If the software isn't installed on a node, then the association could instruct State Manager to install it.' You can target all managed nodes in the current Region and account (detecting all instances), and the association uses an SSM document (for example AWS-InstallApplication) to perform the installation only when the software is not present. This is a single-service, declarative, idempotent solution that satisfies every requirement: detect all instances, use an SSM document, and install the software if it is missing.","explanation_zh":"AWS Systems Manager State Manager 正是為此需求而設計，AWS 官方文件甚至直接以「防毒軟體」作為其代表性範例。State Manager association 是您指派給資源、用以定義並維持目標狀態的設定：文件明確指出「association 可指定 managed node 上必須安裝並執行防毒軟體」，且「防毒軟體的 association 可設定每天在帳戶內所有 managed nodes 執行一次；若某節點尚未安裝該軟體，association 可指示 State Manager 進行安裝」。association 可將目標設為目前 Region 與帳戶內的所有 managed nodes（即偵測所有 instances），並使用 SSM document（例如 AWS-InstallApplication）僅在軟體不存在時執行安裝。這是單一服務、宣告式且具冪等性的解法，完整滿足所有條件：偵測所有 instances、使用 SSM document、且僅在軟體缺失時安裝。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config evaluates resource configuration items (the AWS-level configuration of resources), not the in-guest OS software inventory, so a custom Config rule cannot natively determine whether antivirus is installed inside the EC2 OS without pulling in additional data such as SSM Inventory. This approach is also far more complex (Config recording, a Lambda-backed custom rule, remediation wiring), and auto-remediation can even fire on already-compliant resources due to stale compliance snapshots. It is an over-engineered, weaker fit than the purpose-built State Manager solution.","why_zh":"AWS Config 評估的是資源層級的 configuration item，而非 EC2 作業系統內部的軟體清單，因此自訂 Config rule 無法在不額外引入 SSM Inventory 等資料的情況下，原生判斷 OS 內是否已安裝防毒軟體。此作法也明顯較複雜（需啟用 Config 記錄、以 Lambda 支援的自訂規則、remediation 串接），且因合規快照可能過時，auto-remediation 甚至會對已合規的資源觸發。相較於專為此設計的 State Manager，這是過度工程且較差的選項。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector EC2 scanning assesses software vulnerabilities (CVEs) and network reachability; it does not detect whether a specific antivirus package is installed, nor does it install software. There is no mechanism to 'associate findings with an SSM document' to trigger installation, so this option does not meet the requirements.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 的 EC2 掃描評估的是軟體漏洞（CVE）與網路可達性，並不會偵測是否安裝特定防毒套件，也不會安裝軟體。並不存在「將 findings 關聯到 SSM document」以觸發安裝的機制，因此無法滿足需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An EventBridge rule on the CloudTrail RunInstances API call only detects newly launched instances, not all instances already running in the account, so it fails the 'detect all instances' requirement. SSM Inventory collects software inventory data but there is no capability to 'associate SSM Inventory with an SSM document' to automatically install missing software. This is both incomplete and not a real mechanism.","why_zh":"針對 CloudTrail RunInstances API 呼叫的 EventBridge 規則只能偵測新啟動的 instances，無法涵蓋帳戶中已在執行的所有 instances，因此不符合「偵測所有 instances」的要求。SSM Inventory 雖能收集軟體清單資料，但並不存在「將 SSM Inventory 關聯到 SSM document」以自動安裝缺失軟體的功能。此選項既不完整，也非真實可行的機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-state.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/what-is-inspector.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":252,"question_en":"A company needs to increase the security of the container images that run in its production environment. The company wants to integrate operating system scanning and programming language package vulnerability scanning for the containers in its CI/CD pipeline. The CI/CD pipeline is an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that includes an AWS CodeBuild build project, AWS CodeDeploy actions, and an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. A DevOps engineer needs to add an image scan to the CI/CD pipeline. The CI/CD pipeline must deploy only images without CRITICAL and HIGH findings into production. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司需要提高其生产环境中运行的容器镜像的安全性。该公司希望在其持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD） 流水线中集成操作系统扫描和编程语言包漏洞扫描功能，以针对容器进行操作。该 CI/CD 流水线是一个 AWS CodePipeline 流水线，其中包括一个 AWS CodeBuild 构建项目、AWS CodeDeploy 操作以及一个亚马 逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）存储库。 DevOps 工程师需要在持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）流水线中添加镜像扫描功能。该 CI/CD 流水线必须仅 将没有“严重”和“高危”漏洞的镜像部署到生产环境。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon ECR basic scanning.","B":"Use Amazon ECR enhanced scanning.","C":"Configure Amazon ECR to submit a Rejected status to the CI/CD pipeline when the image scan returns CRITICAL or HIGH findings.","D":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function when the image scan is completed. Configure the Lambda function to consume the Amazon Inspector scan status and to submit an Approved or Rejected status to the CI/CD pipeline.","E":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function when the image scan is completed. Configure the Lambda function to consume the Clair scan status and to submit an Approved or Rejected status to the CI/CD pipeline."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon ECR 基本扫描。","B":"使用亚马逊 ECR 增强扫描功能。","C":"配置 Amazon ECR，使其在镜像扫描结果返回“严重”或“高”风险时，向 CI/CD 管道提交“已拒绝”状 态。","D":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在图像扫描完成后调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数以获取 Amazon Inspector 扫描状态，并向 CI/CD 管道提交“已批准”或“已拒绝”状态。","E":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在图像扫描完成后调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数以获取 Clair 扫描状态，并向 CI/CD 管道提交“已批准”或“已拒绝”状态。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to scan for BOTH operating system vulnerabilities AND programming language package vulnerabilities, then gate deployment so that only images without CRITICAL or HIGH findings reach production. Amazon ECR enhanced scanning (B) is the only scan type that covers both categories: the docs title it 'Scan images for OS and programming language package vulnerabilities in Amazon ECR' and describe it as an integration with Amazon Inspector. Amazon ECR basic scanning (A) is titled 'Scan images for OS vulnerabilities' only, so it cannot detect language package CVEs and fails the requirement. For gating, when enhanced scanning completes, Amazon Inspector emits an EventBridge event (source 'aws.inspector2', detail-type 'Inspector2 Scan') containing 'finding-severity-counts' with CRITICAL and HIGH counts. Option D correctly uses an EventBridge rule to invoke a Lambda function that consumes the Amazon Inspector scan status and submits an Approved or Rejected result back to CodePipeline (via PutJobSuccessResult / PutJobFailureResult on the Lambda invoke action), blocking the deploy when CRITICAL/HIGH findings exist. Therefore B and D together meet the requirements.","explanation_zh":"需求是同時掃描作業系統 (OS) 弱點與程式語言套件 (programming language package) 弱點，並對部署設立關卡，讓只有不含 CRITICAL 或 HIGH 發現的映像檔才能進入正式環境。Amazon ECR enhanced scanning (B) 是唯一同時涵蓋這兩類的掃描類型：官方文件標題即為「Scan images for OS and programming language package vulnerabilities in Amazon ECR」，並說明它是與 Amazon Inspector 的整合。Amazon ECR basic scanning (A) 的標題僅為「Scan images for OS vulnerabilities」，無法偵測語言套件 CVE，因此不符合需求。在把關方面，enhanced scanning 完成時，Amazon Inspector 會向 EventBridge 發出事件 (source 為 'aws.inspector2'、detail-type 為 'Inspector2 Scan')，其中 'finding-severity-counts' 包含 CRITICAL 與 HIGH 的計數。選項 D 正確地以 EventBridge rule 觸發 Lambda function，由該 function 讀取 Amazon Inspector 的掃描狀態，並透過 Lambda invoke action 的 PutJobSuccessResult / PutJobFailureResult 將 Approved 或 Rejected 結果回報給 CodePipeline，在出現 CRITICAL/HIGH 發現時阻擋部署。因此 B 與 D 共同滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon ECR basic scanning only scans for operating system vulnerabilities (the doc is titled 'Scan images for OS vulnerabilities in Amazon ECR'). It does not detect programming language package vulnerabilities, so it cannot satisfy the requirement to scan both OS and language packages.","why_zh":"Amazon ECR basic scanning 僅掃描作業系統弱點 (文件標題為「Scan images for OS vulnerabilities」)，無法偵測程式語言套件弱點，因此無法滿足同時掃描 OS 與語言套件的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon ECR has no native capability to submit an 'Approved' or 'Rejected' status directly into a CodePipeline action. ECR (or Inspector) only emits an EventBridge event when a scan completes; the gating logic must be implemented separately (for example via an EventBridge rule plus a Lambda function that calls PutJobSuccessResult/PutJobFailureResult), which is exactly what option D describes.","why_zh":"Amazon ECR 並沒有直接向 CodePipeline 動作回報「Approved」或「Rejected」狀態的原生功能。ECR (或 Inspector) 在掃描完成時只會發出 EventBridge 事件；關卡邏輯必須另行實作 (例如以 EventBridge rule 加上呼叫 PutJobSuccessResult/PutJobFailureResult 的 Lambda function)，這正是選項 D 所描述的做法。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Clair is a third-party open-source scanner that is not the scanner exposed by ECR enhanced scanning; enhanced scanning is powered by Amazon Inspector and emits 'aws.inspector2' events ('Inspector2 Scan'), not a 'Clair scan status'. A Lambda function reading a Clair status would not align with the ECR/Inspector event model, so this option is incorrect.","why_zh":"Clair 是第三方開源掃描器，並非 ECR enhanced scanning 所採用的掃描器；enhanced scanning 由 Amazon Inspector 驅動並發出 'aws.inspector2' 事件 ('Inspector2 Scan')，而非「Clair 掃描狀態」。讓 Lambda function 讀取 Clair 狀態並不符合 ECR/Inspector 的事件模型，因此此選項錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-basic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-invoke-lambda-function.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":253,"question_en":"A company's DevOps team manages a set of AWS accounts that are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company needs a solution that ensures that all Amazon EC2 instances use approved AM Is that the DevOps team manages. The solution also must remediate the usage of AMIs that are not approved. The individual account administrators must not be able to remove the restriction to use approved AMIs. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 团队管理着一组位于 AWS 组织中的 AWS 账户。 该公司需要一个解决方案，确保所有亚马逊 EC2 实例都使用由 DevOps 团队管理的已获批准的 AMI。 该解决方案还必须纠正使用未获批准的 AMI 的情况。各个账户管理员不得解除使用已获批准的 AMI 的限制。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy an Amazon EventBridge rule to each account. Configure the rule to react to AWS CloudTrail events for Amazon EC2 and to send a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the DevOps team to the SNS topic.","B":"Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy the approved-amis-by-id AWS Config managed rule to each account. Configure the rule with the list of approved AMIs. Configure the rule to run the AWS- StopEC2Instance AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook for the noncompliant EC2 instances.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that processes AWS CloudTrail events for Amazon EC2. Configure the Lambda function to send a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the DevOps team to the SNS topic. Deploy the Lambda function in each account in the organization. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule in each account. Configure the EventBridge rules to react to AWS CloudTrail events for Amazon EC2 and to invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Enable AWS Config across the organization. Create a conformance pack that uses the approved-amis- by-id AWS Config managed rule with the list of approved AMIs. Deploy the conformance pack across the organization. Configure the rule to run the AWS-StopEC2lnstance AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook for the noncompliant EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 Amazon EventBridge 规则部署到每个账户。配置该规则以响 应 Amazon EC2 的 AWS CloudTrail 事件，并向 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS） 主题发送通知。让 DevOps 团队订阅该 SNS 主题。","B":"使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将 approved-amis-by-id AWS Config 管理规则部署到 每个账户。使用已批准的 AMI 列表配置规则。配置规则以运行 AWS- 用于不符合规定的 EC2 实例的 StopEC2Instance AWS 系统管理器自动化运行记录。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来处理 Amazon EC2 的 AWS CloudTrail 事件。配置该 Lambda 函数向 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题发送通知。让 DevOps 团队订阅该 SNS 主题。 在组织中的每个账户中部署该 Lambda 函数。在每个账户中创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配 置 EventBridge 规则以响应 Amazon EC2 的 AWS CloudTrail 事件并调用 Lambda 函数。","D":"在整个组织内启用 AWS Config。创建一个一致性包，使用带有已批准 AMI 列表的 approved-amisby- id AWS Config 管理规则。在整个组织内部署一致性包。配置规则，对不符合要求的 EC2 实例运行 AWS-StopEC2lnstance AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行本。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Three requirements must all be met: (1) enforce approved AMIs across every org account, (2) automatically remediate noncompliant EC2 instances, and (3) prevent individual account admins from removing the restriction. Both B and D use the correct approved-amis-by-id AWS Config managed rule (which marks instances NON_COMPLIANT when they do not use an AMI on the approved list) plus the AWS-StopEC2Instance SSM Automation runbook for remediation, so requirement (3) is the deciding qualifier. A conformance pack is defined by AWS as 'a collection of AWS Config rules and remediation actions' that can be deployed across an organization, and the organization-deployment docs state you can 'use the management account in AWS Organizations to enforce governance by ensuring that the underlying AWS Config rules and remediation actions are not modifiable by your organization's member accounts.' That exactly satisfies the non-removable restriction and confirms conformance packs carry remediation. Option B deploys the rule via CloudFormation StackSets as ordinary resources INTO each member account, where the local account administrator can edit or delete the Config rule and remediation, so it fails requirement (3). Options A and C only publish SNS notifications and never remediate, failing requirement (2). Therefore D is correct.","explanation_zh":"本題三項要求必須全部滿足：(1) 在組織所有帳戶強制使用核准的 AMI、(2) 自動修復不合規的 EC2 執行個體、(3) 個別帳戶管理員不得移除該限制。B 與 D 都使用正確的 approved-amis-by-id AWS Config 受管規則（凡使用不在核准清單內 AMI 的執行個體會被標記為 NON_COMPLIANT）搭配 AWS-StopEC2Instance SSM Automation runbook 進行修復，因此關鍵判別點是第 (3) 項要求。AWS 將 conformance pack 定義為『一組 AWS Config 規則與修復動作的集合』，可跨組織部署；組織部署文件明確指出可『使用 AWS Organizations 管理帳戶強制治理，確保底層的 AWS Config 規則與修復動作無法被組織成員帳戶修改』。這正好滿足無法移除限制的需求，也證實 conformance pack 本身即帶有修復動作。選項 B 透過 CloudFormation StackSets 將規則當作一般資源部署『進入』各成員帳戶，本地帳戶管理員可修改或刪除該 Config 規則與修復，因此不符合第 (3) 項要求。選項 A 與 C 僅發送 SNS 通知、完全不做修復，不符合第 (2) 項要求。因此 D 為正解。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A StackSets-deployed EventBridge rule on EC2 CloudTrail events only sends an SNS notification to the DevOps team. It neither enforces approved AMIs nor remediates noncompliant instances, failing requirement (2).","why_zh":"透過 StackSets 部署、基於 EC2 CloudTrail 事件的 EventBridge 規則只發 SNS 通知給 DevOps 團隊，既不強制核准 AMI 也不修復不合規執行個體，不符合第 (2) 項要求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses the correct approved-amis-by-id rule and AWS-StopEC2Instance runbook, but deploying them via CloudFormation StackSets places them as ordinary resources inside each member account, where the local account administrator can edit or delete the Config rule and remediation. It cannot prevent admins from removing the restriction, failing requirement (3). Organization conformance packs are AWS's purpose-built mechanism for making rules/remediation non-modifiable by member accounts.","why_zh":"雖使用正確的 approved-amis-by-id 規則與 AWS-StopEC2Instance runbook，但透過 CloudFormation StackSets 部署會將其當作一般資源置於各成員帳戶內，本地帳戶管理員可修改或刪除該 Config 規則與修復，無法阻止管理員移除限制，故不符合第 (3) 項要求。組織型 conformance pack 才是 AWS 用來讓規則/修復無法被成員帳戶修改的專用機制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Lambda function triggered by EventBridge that only publishes to SNS provides notification, not remediation, and does not enforce approved AMIs in a non-removable way. It fails requirement (2).","why_zh":"由 EventBridge 觸發、僅發布到 SNS 的 Lambda 只提供通知而非修復，也無法以不可移除的方式強制核准 AMI，不符合第 (2) 項要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-pack-organization-apis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/conformance-packs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/approved-amis-by-id.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/APIReference/API_DeleteOrganizationConformancePack.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":254,"question_en":"A company gives its employees limited rights to AWS. DevOps engineers have the ability to assume an administrator role. For tracking purposes, the security team wants to receive a near-real-time notification when the administrator role is assumed. How should this be accomplished?","question_zh":"一家公司赋予其员工有限的 AWS 权限。DevOps 工程师能够承担管理员角色。出于追踪目的，安全团 队希望在管理员角色被承担时能收到近乎实时的通知。 这该如何实现呢？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Config to publish logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to query the logs and send a notification to the security team when the administrator role is assumed.","B":"Configure Amazon GuardDuty to monitor when the administrator role is assumed and send a notification to the security team.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge event rule using an AWS Management Console sign-in events event pattern that publishes a message to an Amazon SNS topic if the administrator role is assumed.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge events rule using an AWS API call that uses an AWS CloudTrail event pattern to invoke an AWS Lambda function that publishes a message to an Amazon SNS topic if the administrator role is assumed."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Config 将日志发布到 Amazon S3 存储桶。使用 Amazon Athena 查询日志，并在管理员角色 被使用时向安全团队发送通知。","B":"配置 Amazon GuardDuty 来监控管理员角色何时被使用，并向安全团队发送通知。","C":"使用 AWS 管理控制台登录事件模式创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则，如果管理员角色被承 担，则向 Amazon SNS 主题发布一条消息。","D":"使用 AWS API 调用创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 事件规则，该规则使用 AWS CloudTrail 事件模式， 如果管理员角色被使用，则调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数向 Amazon SNS 主题发布一条消息。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Assuming an IAM role is an sts:AssumeRole API call, and CloudTrail captures all IAM and AWS STS API calls as events. CloudTrail delivers these to the default EventBridge bus with detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail'; the documented STS event pattern is source 'aws.sts', detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail', eventSource 'sts.amazonaws.com', optionally narrowed by eventName 'AssumeRole' (an active CloudTrail trail is required). Option D builds an EventBridge rule on that AWS-API-call-via-CloudTrail pattern and invokes a Lambda function that publishes to an SNS topic, giving the security team a near-real-time notification. This matches the official mechanism for acting on STS API activity. Option C is wrong because it uses an 'AWS Management Console sign-in events' pattern (detail-type 'AWS Console Signin via CloudTrail'), which only matches console sign-in attempts (ConsoleLogin), not role assumption performed through the STS API.","explanation_zh":"假設(assume)IAM 角色實際上是一個 sts:AssumeRole 的 API 呼叫,而 CloudTrail 會把所有 IAM 與 AWS STS 的 API 呼叫記錄為事件。CloudTrail 會將這些事件以 detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' 送到預設的 EventBridge event bus;官方文件記載的 STS 事件模式為 source 'aws.sts'、detail-type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail'、eventSource 'sts.amazonaws.com',並可選擇以 eventName 'AssumeRole' 進一步縮小範圍(需啟用 CloudTrail trail)。選項 D 在此 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail' 模式上建立 EventBridge 規則,觸發 Lambda 將訊息發布到 SNS topic,讓安全團隊取得近即時通知,這正是處理 STS API 活動的官方做法。選項 C 錯誤,因為它使用 'AWS Management Console sign-in events'(detail-type 'AWS Console Signin via CloudTrail')模式,只能比對主控台登入嘗試(ConsoleLogin),無法比對透過 STS API 進行的角色假設。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Config records resource configuration changes and compliance state, not IAM/STS API activity such as a role being assumed. Publishing to S3 and then querying with Athena is a batch, on-demand workflow, not near-real-time, so it fails the explicit near-real-time requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Config 記錄的是資源組態變更與合規狀態,而非像角色被假設這類 IAM/STS API 活動。先輸出到 S3 再用 Athena 查詢屬於批次、隨選的流程,並非近即時,因此不符合題目明確要求的近即時通知。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"GuardDuty is a threat-detection service that surfaces anomalous or malicious behavior as findings. It does not generate a notification simply because a legitimate, known administrator role is assumed, and you cannot configure it to alert on every assumption of a specific role for routine tracking purposes.","why_zh":"GuardDuty 是威脅偵測服務,只會把異常或惡意行為以 findings 形式呈現。它不會因為合法且已知的管理員角色被假設就產生通知,也無法設定成針對每次假設特定角色都發出警示來做例行追蹤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses an 'AWS Management Console sign-in events' (AWS Console Signin via CloudTrail) event pattern, which only matches console sign-in attempts by IAM users or the root user, not the sts:AssumeRole API call that occurs when a role is assumed. The pattern targets the wrong event type and would not fire on role assumption.","why_zh":"使用 'AWS Management Console sign-in events'(AWS Console Signin via CloudTrail)事件模式,只會比對 IAM 使用者或 root 的主控台登入嘗試,無法比對假設角色時所發生的 sts:AssumeRole API 呼叫。此模式鎖定的是錯誤的事件類型,角色被假設時並不會觸發。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-sts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/cloudtrail-integration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-event-reference-aws-console-sign-in-events.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":255,"question_en":"A company needs a strategy for failover and disaster recovery of its data and application. The application uses a MySQL database and Amazon EC2 instances. The company requires a maximum RPO of 2 hours and a maximum RTO of 10 minutes for its data and application at all times. Which combination of deployment strategies will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司需要为其数据和应用程序制定故障转移和灾难恢复策略。该应用程序使用 MySQL 数据库和亚马逊 EC2 实例。该公司要求其数据和应用程序在任何时候的最大恢复点目标（RPO）为 2 小时，最大恢复时间 目标（RTO）为 10 分钟。 哪种部署策略组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Aurora Single-AZ cluster in multiple AWS Regions as the data store. Use Aurora's automatic recovery capabilities in the event of a disaster.","B":"Create an Amazon Aurora global database in two AWS Regions as the data store. In the event of a failure, promote the secondary Region to the primary for the application. Update the application to use the Aurora cluster endpoint in the secondary Region.","C":"Create an Amazon Aurora cluster in multiple AWS Regions as the data store. Use a Network Load Balancer to balance the database traffic in different Regions.","D":"Set up the application in two AWS Regions. Use Amazon Route 53 failover routing that points to Application Load Balancers in both Regions. Use health checks and Auto Scaling groups in each Region.","E":"Set up the application in two AWS Regions. Configure AWS Global Accelerator to point to Application Load Balancers (ALBs) in both Regions. Add both ALBs to a single endpoint group. Use health checks and Auto Scaling groups in each Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"在多个 AWS 区域创建 Amazon Aurora 单可用区集群作为数据存储。在发生灾难时利用 Aurora 的自动恢 复功能。","B":"在两个 AWS 区域创建一个 Amazon Aurora 全球数据库作为数据存储。若发生故障，将备用区域提升为 主区域以供应用程序使用。更新应用程序以使用备用区域中的 Aurora 集群端点。","C":"在多个 AWS 区域创建 Amazon Aurora 集群作为数据存储。使用网络负载均衡器来平衡不同区域的数 据库流量。","D":"在两个 AWS 区域中设置应用程序。使用 Amazon Route 53 故障转移路由，该路由指向两个区域中 的应用负载均衡器。在每个区域中使用健康检查和自动扩展组。","E":"在两个 AWS 区域中设置应用程序。配置 AWS 全球加速器以指向两个区域中的应用负载均衡器（ALB）。 将两个 ALB 添加到单个终端节点组。在每个区域中使用健康检查和自动扩展组。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The solution needs one data-tier strategy and one application-tier strategy that together meet a 2-hour RPO and a 10-minute RTO. Data tier: B (Amazon Aurora global database across two Regions) is correct. AWS docs for Aurora Global Database state that RTO 'can be in the order of minutes' and RPO 'is typically measured in seconds' (an unplanned cross-Region failover yields a non-zero RPO measured in seconds), both comfortably inside the 2-hour / 10-minute targets; on failure you promote the secondary Region to primary and point the application at that Region's cluster endpoint. Application tier: D (Amazon Route 53 failover routing to Application Load Balancers in both Regions, with health checks and Auto Scaling groups) is correct. This is the standard active-passive multi-Region failover pattern; with health checks and low record TTLs, DNS failover easily achieves a 10-minute RTO. Option E is wrong because it is technically impossible as worded: AWS Global Accelerator docs state 'An endpoint group, and all the endpoints in it, must be in one AWS Region,' so you cannot add ALBs from two different Regions to a single endpoint group. Worse, Global Accelerator's cross-Region failover works by failing over BETWEEN endpoint groups (one per Region) to a healthy endpoint in another endpoint group; collapsing both Regions into one endpoint group would eliminate the very mechanism that provides failover. The first analyst preferred E over D but missed this fatal configuration error, so the verdict is B and D.","explanation_zh":"方案需要一個資料層策略加一個應用層策略，共同達成 2 小時 RPO 與 10 分鐘 RTO。資料層：B（跨兩個 Region 的 Amazon Aurora global database）正確。Aurora Global Database 的 AWS 文件指出 RTO「約為分鐘級」、RPO「通常以秒計」（非計畫性跨 Region failover 的 RPO 為以秒計的非零值），皆遠在 2 小時 / 10 分鐘 目標之內；故障時將次要 Region 提升為主要，並讓應用指向該 Region 的 cluster endpoint。應用層：D（Amazon Route 53 failover routing 指向兩個 Region 的 Application Load Balancer，搭配 health checks 與 Auto Scaling group）正確。這是標準的 active-passive 多 Region 故障切換模式；搭配 health checks 與低 TTL 紀錄，DNS failover 可輕鬆達成 10 分鐘 RTO。選項 E 錯誤，因為其敘述在技術上不可行：AWS Global Accelerator 文件明確指出「一個 endpoint group 及其中所有 endpoint 必須位於同一個 AWS Region」，因此無法把分屬兩個 Region 的 ALB 加入「單一 endpoint group」。更嚴重的是，Global Accelerator 的跨 Region 故障切換正是靠在不同 endpoint group（每個 Region 一個）之間切換到另一個 endpoint group 中的健康端點來運作；把兩個 Region 併入一個 endpoint group 反而會消除提供切換的機制本身。第一位分析師偏好 E 而非 D，卻忽略了此致命的設定錯誤，故正解為 B 與 D。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An Aurora 'Single-AZ cluster in multiple Regions' is not a coordinated cross-Region DR construct. Aurora's automatic recovery operates within a single Region (across AZs), not across Regions, and no cross-Region replication is described. There is no managed promotion or replication, so it cannot guarantee a cross-Region 10-minute RTO or 2-hour RPO; a Single-AZ cluster also has no in-Region failover instance.","why_zh":"Aurora 在多個 Region 各自建立 Single-AZ cluster 並非協調式跨 Region DR 設計。Aurora 自動復原作用於單一 Region（跨 AZ）之內而非跨 Region，且未描述跨 Region 複寫。沒有受管的提升或複寫，無法保證跨 Region 的 10 分鐘 RTO 或 2 小時 RPO；Single-AZ cluster 在 Region 內也沒有可供切換的執行個體。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You cannot place a relational database behind a Network Load Balancer to 'balance database traffic in different Regions.' Aurora writes go to a single primary writer; an NLB does not replicate data, maintain write consistency, or perform cross-Region promotion. This does not provide valid DR and does not meet the RPO/RTO objectives.","why_zh":"無法將關聯式資料庫置於 Network Load Balancer 之後以「平衡不同 Region 的資料庫流量」。Aurora 寫入僅送往單一主要 writer；NLB 不會複寫資料、維持寫入一致性或執行跨 Region 提升。此設計無法構成有效 DR，亦無法達成 RPO/RTO 目標。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Technically impossible as worded. AWS Global Accelerator docs state 'An endpoint group, and all the endpoints in it, must be in one AWS Region,' so two ALBs in two different Regions cannot be added to a single endpoint group. Furthermore, Global Accelerator's cross-Region failover works by failing over to a healthy endpoint in ANOTHER endpoint group; putting both Regions in one endpoint group would remove the second endpoint group that failover relies on, defeating the multi-Region failover the option claims to provide. A correct design would use one endpoint group per Region, which E does not describe.","why_zh":"依其敘述在技術上不可行。AWS Global Accelerator 文件指出「一個 endpoint group 及其中所有 endpoint 必須位於同一個 AWS Region」，因此分屬兩個 Region 的兩個 ALB 無法加入「單一 endpoint group」。此外，Global Accelerator 的跨 Region 故障切換是切換到「另一個」endpoint group 中的健康端點；把兩個 Region 放進同一個 endpoint group 會移除切換所依賴的第二個 endpoint group，使該選項聲稱提供的多 Region 切換失效。正確設計應為每個 Region 一個 endpoint group，而 E 並未如此描述。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-disaster-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/about-endpoint-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/about-endpoints-endpoint-weights.unhealthy-endpoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html"]},"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯"},{"id":256,"question_en":"A developer is using the AWS Serverless Application Model (AWS SAM) to create a prototype for an AWS Lambda function. The AWS SAM template contains an AWS::Serverless::Function resource that has the CodeUri property that points to an Amazon S3 location. The developer wants to identify the correct commands for deployment before creating a CI/CD pipeline. The developer creates an archive of the Lambda function code named package.zip. The developer uploads the .zip file archive to the S3 location specified in the CodeUri property. The developer runs the sam deploy command and deploys the Lambda function. The developer updates the Lambda function code and uses the same steps to deploy the new version of the Lambda function. The sam deploy command fails and returns an error of no changes to deploy. Which solutions will deploy the new version? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位开发人员正在使用 AWS 无服务器应用程序模型（AWS SAM）为一个 AWS Lambda 函数创建原型。 AWS SAM 模板Serverless::Function 资源，该资源具有指向 Amazon S3 位置的 CodeUri 属性。开发人员希望 在创建持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）管道之前确定正确的部署命令。 开发人员创建了一个名为 package.zip 的 Lambda 函数代码归档文件。开发人员将 .zip 文件归档上传到 CodeUri 属性中指定的 S3 位置。开发人员运行 sam deploy 命令并部署 Lambda 函数。开发人员更新 Lambda 函数代码，并使用相同的步骤部署 Lambda 函数的新版本。sam deploy 命令失败并返回错误信息， 提示没有可部署的更改。 哪些解决方案将部署新版本？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Use the aws cloudformation update-stack command instead of the sam deploy command.","B":"Use the aws cloudformation update-stack-instances command instead of the sam deploy command.","C":"Update the CodeUri property to reference the local application code folder. Use the sam deploy command.","D":"Update the CodeUri property to reference the local application code folder. Use the aws cloudformation create-change-set command and the aws cloudformation execute-change-set command.","E":"Update the CodeUri property to reference the local application code folder. Use the aws cloudformation package command and the aws cloudformation deploy command."},"options_zh":{"A":"请使用 aws cloudformation update-stack 命令，而非 sam deploy 命令。","B":"请使用 aws cloudformation update-stack-instances 命令，而非 sam deploy 命令。","C":"将 CodeUri 属性更新为引用本地应用程序代码文件夹。使用 sam deploy 命令。","D":"将 CodeUri 属性更新为引用本地应用程序代码文件夹。使用 aws cloudformation create-change-set 命令和 aws cloudformation execute-change-set 命令。","E":"将 CodeUri 属性更新为引用本地应用程序代码文件夹。使用 aws cloudformation package 命令和 aws cloudformation deploy 命令。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The root cause is that the developer re-uploads new code to the SAME S3 key (package.zip) that the static CodeUri points to. AWS docs for AWS::Lambda::Function Code state: 'Changes to a deployment package in Amazon S3 or a container image in ECR are not detected automatically during stack updates. To update the function code, change the object key or version in the template.' Because the template's CodeUri still references the identical, unchanged S3 location, CloudFormation/SAM sees no difference and reports 'no changes to deploy.' The fix is to point CodeUri at a LOCAL folder so a packaging step uploads the artifact under a NEW content-hash key and rewrites the template. C: sam deploy automatically uploads local files to S3 under a content-hash key (e.g. da3c598813f1c2151579b73ad788cac8) and updates the template to reference that new path, so changed code produces a new key that CloudFormation detects (per 'How AWS SAM uploads local files at deployment'). E: aws cloudformation package zips the local folder, names the .zip using 'the MD5 checksum of the folder contents,' uploads it, and emits a processed template; aws cloudformation deploy then applies it. New code yields a new checksum, a new key, and a detected change. These are the documented mechanisms.","explanation_zh":"問題的根本原因是開發者把新程式碼重新上傳到 static CodeUri 所指向的「相同」S3 key (package.zip)。AWS::Lambda::Function Code 文件明確指出：在 stack 更新期間，Amazon S3 中部署套件或 ECR 容器映像的變更不會被自動偵測；若要更新函式程式碼，必須變更 template 中的物件 key 或版本。由於 template 的 CodeUri 仍指向相同且未變更的 S3 位置，CloudFormation/SAM 看不到任何差異，因此回報「no changes to deploy」。修正方式是把 CodeUri 改為指向「本機資料夾」，讓 packaging 步驟以新的 content-hash key 上傳成品並改寫 template。C：sam deploy 會自動把本機檔案以 content-hash key（例如 da3c598813f1c2151579b73ad788cac8）上傳到 S3，並更新 template 以引用新路徑，程式碼變更便產生新的 key，CloudFormation 即可偵測到變更（參見「How AWS SAM uploads local files at deployment」）。E：aws cloudformation package 會把本機資料夾打包成 .zip，並以「資料夾內容的 MD5 checksum」命名 .zip 後上傳，再產生處理後的 template；接著 aws cloudformation deploy 套用該 template。新程式碼 -> 新 checksum -> 新 key -> 偵測到變更。這些都是官方文件所載的機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"aws cloudformation update-stack performs no local-artifact packaging. If you keep the original static S3 CodeUri, the template is byte-for-byte identical and update-stack returns the same 'No updates are to be performed' error. If you point CodeUri at a local folder, update-stack cannot resolve a local path (there is no package step), so it fails. Either way it does not deploy the new code.","why_zh":"aws cloudformation update-stack 不會執行任何本機成品 packaging。若沿用原本的 static S3 CodeUri，template 完全相同，update-stack 會回報相同的「No updates are to be performed」錯誤；若把 CodeUri 改為本機資料夾，update-stack 無法解析本機路徑（沒有 package 步驟）而失敗。無論哪種情況都無法部署新程式碼。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"aws cloudformation update-stack-instances is a StackSets command that updates stack instances across multiple target accounts/Regions in a stack set. This scenario is a single SAM/CloudFormation stack, not a stack set, so the command is the wrong tool entirely and does not address the no-changes-detected root cause.","why_zh":"aws cloudformation update-stack-instances 是 StackSets 指令，用於更新 stack set 中跨多個目標帳戶/區域的 stack 執行個體。本題是單一 SAM/CloudFormation stack 而非 stack set，因此這個指令完全是錯誤的工具，也無法解決偵測不到變更的根本原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Even after pointing CodeUri at a local folder, aws cloudformation create-change-set / execute-change-set do NOT package local artifacts. Only sam package, sam deploy, or aws cloudformation package upload local files and rewrite the template to a new S3 key. The change-set commands require an already-packaged template with S3 references and cannot resolve a local-folder CodeUri, so the new code is never uploaded. This workflow is missing the mandatory packaging step that option E includes.","why_zh":"即使把 CodeUri 改為本機資料夾，aws cloudformation create-change-set / execute-change-set 也「不會」打包本機成品。只有 sam package、sam deploy 或 aws cloudformation package 會上傳本機檔案並把 template 改寫為新的 S3 key。change-set 指令需要「已打包」且含 S3 引用的 template，無法解析指向本機資料夾的 CodeUri，因此新程式碼永遠不會被上傳。此流程缺少選項 E 所包含的必要 packaging 步驟。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-lambda-function-code.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/deploy-upload-local-files.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-cli-package.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/sam-cli-command-reference-sam-deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/serverless-application-model/latest/developerguide/sam-cli-command-reference-sam-package.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":257,"question_en":"A company runs its container workloads in AWS App Runner. A DevOps engineer manages the company's container repository in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). The DevOps engineer must implement a solution that continuously monitors the container repository. The solution must create a new container image when the solution detects an operating system vulnerability or language package vulnerability. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS App Runner 上运行其容器工作负载。一位 DevOps 工程师负责管理公司位于亚马逊弹 性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中的容器仓库。 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个持续监控容器仓库的解决方案。该解决方案在检测到操作系统漏洞或语言 包漏洞时，必须创建一个新的容器镜像。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use EC2 Image Builder to create a container image pipeline. Use Amazon ECR as the target repository. Turn on enhanced scanning on the ECR repository. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture an Inspector2 finding event. Use the event to invoke the image pipeline. Re-upload the container to the repository.","B":"Use EC2 Image Builder to create a container image pipeline. Use Amazon ECR as the target repository. Enable Amazon GuardDuty Malware Protection on the container workload. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture a GuardDuty finding event. Use the event to invoke the image pipeline.","C":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project to create a container image. Use Amazon ECR as the target repository. Turn on basic scanning on the repository. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture an ECR image action event. Use the event to invoke the CodeBuild project. Re-upload the container to the repository.","D":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project to create a container image. Use Amazon ECR as the target repository. Configure AWS Systems Manager Compliance to scan all managed nodes. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to capture a configuration compliance state change event. Use the event to invoke the CodeBuild project."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 EC2 Image Builder 创建一个容器镜像流水线。将 Amazon ECR 用作目标存储库。在 ECR 存储 库上启用增强扫描。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以捕获 Inspector2 发现事件。使用该事件调 用镜像流水线。将容器重新上传到存储库。","B":"使用 EC2 Image Builder 创建一个容器镜像流水线。将 Amazon ECR 用作目标存储库。在容器工 作负载上启用 Amazon GuardDuty 恶意软件防护。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以捕获 GuardDuty 发现事件。使用该事件调用镜像流水线。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目以生成容器镜像。将 Amazon ECR 用作目标存储库。在该存储库上启 用基本扫描。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以捕获 ECR 镜像操作事件。使用该事件调用 CodeBuild 项目。将容器重新上传到存储库。","D":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目以生成容器镜像。将 Amazon ECR 用作目标存储库。配置 AWS Systems Manager Compliance 以扫描所有托管节点。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以捕获配置 合规性状态更改事件。使用该事件调用 CodeBuild 项目。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: continuously monitor the ECR repository, detect BOTH operating-system AND programming-language package vulnerabilities, and trigger a new container image build. Amazon ECR enhanced scanning is the integration with Amazon Inspector that scans container images for both operating-system and programming-language package vulnerabilities, and it can be configured for automatic, continuous scanning. AWS docs state that with enhanced scanning, 'Amazon Inspector emits events to EventBridge when an initial scan is completed and when an image scan finding is created, updated, or closed,' and that a finding event (detail-type 'Inspector2 Finding') is created when Amazon Inspector identifies a software vulnerability. Option A captures that Inspector2 finding event with an EventBridge rule and uses it to invoke an EC2 Image Builder container image pipeline, which produces a Docker image and distributes it to Amazon ECR, rebuilding and re-uploading a patched image. This satisfies every requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求為:持續監控 ECR 儲存庫、同時偵測作業系統(OS)與程式語言套件(language package)漏洞,並在偵測到漏洞時建立新的容器映像。Amazon ECR enhanced scanning 是與 Amazon Inspector 的整合,可同時掃描容器映像的 OS 與程式語言套件漏洞,並可設定為自動、持續(continuous)掃描。AWS 文件指出:在 enhanced scanning 下,『當初始掃描完成,以及映像掃描 finding 被建立、更新或關閉時,Amazon Inspector 會向 EventBridge 發出事件』,且當 Amazon Inspector 偵測到軟體漏洞時會產生 finding 事件(detail-type 為 'Inspector2 Finding')。選項 A 以 EventBridge 規則捕捉該 Inspector2 finding 事件,並用它觸發 EC2 Image Builder 容器映像 pipeline(可產生 Docker 映像並發佈到 Amazon ECR),重新建置並上傳修補後的映像,完全符合所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"GuardDuty Malware Protection detects malware (malicious files via IoCs and YARA rules) on EC2/EBS volumes and S3 objects, not operating-system or programming-language package CVE vulnerabilities. It is the wrong detection mechanism for the stated requirement.","why_zh":"GuardDuty Malware Protection 偵測的是惡意軟體(透過 IoC 與 YARA 規則偵測 EC2/EBS 磁碟區與 S3 物件中的惡意檔案),而非作業系統或程式語言套件的 CVE 漏洞,偵測機制與需求不符。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"ECR basic scanning only detects OS vulnerabilities (no programming-language package vulnerabilities), and repositories that don't match a scan-on-push filter default to manual scanning (an image can be scanned only once per 24 hours), so it is not continuous monitoring. Also an 'ECR image action event' relates to push/delete actions, not vulnerability findings.","why_zh":"ECR basic scanning 只偵測 OS 漏洞(無程式語言套件漏洞),且未符合 scan-on-push filter 的儲存庫會預設為 manual(每張映像 24 小時僅能掃描一次),並非持續監控;且『ECR image action event』是 push/delete 等動作事件,而非漏洞 finding 事件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager Compliance scans managed nodes (EC2/on-prem instances), not container images stored in ECR. A configuration compliance state-change event is unrelated to container image vulnerabilities, so it does not monitor the repository.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager Compliance 掃描的是受管節點(EC2/地端執行個體),而非儲存在 ECR 的容器映像;組態合規狀態變更事件與容器映像漏洞無關,無法監控該儲存庫。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-basic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/eventbridge-integration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/start-build-container-pipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/guardduty-malware-detection-scan-engine.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":258,"question_en":"A company wants to use AWS Systems Manager documents to bootstrap physical laptops for developers. The bootstrap code is stored in GitHub. A DevOps engineer has already created a Systems Manager activation, installed the Systems Manager agent with the registration code, and installed an activation ID on all the laptops. Which set of steps should be taken next?","question_zh":"一家公司希望使用 AWS 系统管理器文档为开发人员的物理笔记本电脑进行初始设置。初始设置代码存 储在 GitHub 上。一位 DevOps 工程师已经创建了一个系统管理器激活码，使用注册码安装了系统管理 器代理，并在所有笔记本电脑上安装了激活 ID。 接下来应该采取哪一系列步骤？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Systems Manager document to use the AWS-RunShellScript command to copy the files from GitHub to Amazon S3, then use the aws-downloadContent plugin with a sourceType of S3.","B":"Configure the Systems Manager document to use the aws-configurePackage plugin with an install action and point to the Git repository.","C":"Configure the Systems Manager document to use the aws-downloadContent plugin with a sourceType of GitHub and sourceInfo with the repository details.","D":"Configure the Systems Manager document to use the aws:softwareInventory plugin and run the script from the Git repository."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 Systems Manager 文档以使用 AWS-RunShellScript 命令将文件从 GitHub 复制到 Amazon S3，然 后使用源类型为 S3 的 aws-downloadContent 插件。","B":"配置 Systems Manager 文档以使用带有安装操作的 aws-configurePackage 插件，并指向 Git 代码库。","C":"配置 Systems Manager 文档以使用 aws-downloadContent 插件，将 sourceType 设置为 GitHub，并在 sourceInfo 中提供存储库详细信息。","D":"配置 Systems Manager 文档以使用 aws:softwareInventory 插件，并从 Git 存储库运行脚本。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The laptops are already registered as hybrid managed nodes (a Systems Manager activation was created, and SSM Agent was installed on each laptop with the activation/registration code and activation ID). The remaining task is to author an SSM command document that pulls the bootstrap code from GitHub and runs it. The aws:downloadContent (aws-downloadContent) command document plugin is built specifically to 'Download SSM documents and scripts from remote locations.' Its required sourceType input supports GitHub, Git, HTTP, S3, and SSMDocument, and when sourceType is GitHub the sourceInfo StringMap takes the repository details (owner, repository, path, getOptions for branch/commit, and tokenInfo for a SecureString access token). This is the native, AWS-documented way to fetch code from a GitHub repo onto a managed node, so Option C is exactly correct and requires no intermediary S3 copy or custom packaging.","explanation_zh":"這些筆電已經註冊為 hybrid managed nodes（已建立 Systems Manager activation，並在每台筆電上以 activation/registration code 與 activation ID 安裝了 SSM Agent）。剩下要做的是撰寫一份 SSM command document，從 GitHub 取得 bootstrap 程式碼並執行。aws:downloadContent（aws-downloadContent）這個 command document plugin 的設計用途正是「從遠端位置下載 SSM documents 與 scripts」。其必填的 sourceType 支援 GitHub、Git、HTTP、S3 與 SSMDocument；當 sourceType 為 GitHub 時，sourceInfo（StringMap）需提供 repository 詳細資訊（owner、repository、path、用於指定 branch/commit 的 getOptions，以及存取 token 用的 tokenInfo SecureString）。這是 AWS 文件記載的原生做法，可直接把 GitHub 程式碼下載到 managed node，因此選項 C 完全正確，不需要中介複製到 S3 或自訂封裝。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Copying files from GitHub to Amazon S3 with AWS-RunShellScript first, then using aws-downloadContent with sourceType S3, is an unnecessary and convoluted workaround. AWS-RunShellScript has no native GitHub fetch and would require custom git/curl logic, plus extra S3 staging and IAM permissions, when aws:downloadContent already supports sourceType GitHub directly. It is not the AWS-recommended approach.","why_zh":"先用 AWS-RunShellScript 把檔案從 GitHub 複製到 Amazon S3，再以 sourceType S3 的 aws-downloadContent 下載，是多此一舉的繞路做法。AWS-RunShellScript 並無原生 GitHub 擷取能力，需自寫 git/curl 邏輯，還要額外的 S3 中轉與 IAM 權限，而 aws:downloadContent 本就直接支援 sourceType GitHub，並非 AWS 建議的做法。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"aws:configurePackage installs or uninstalls AWS Systems Manager Distributor packages identified by a package name (e.g., AWSPVDriver, AmazonCloudWatchAgent, CodeDeployAgent). It does not accept a Git repository URL and has no mechanism to point at GitHub, so it cannot fetch the bootstrap code from the repo.","why_zh":"aws:configurePackage 是用 package name（例如 AWSPVDriver、AmazonCloudWatchAgent、CodeDeployAgent）來安裝或解除安裝 AWS Systems Manager Distributor 套件。它不接受 Git repository URL，也沒有指向 GitHub 的機制，因此無法從該 repo 取得 bootstrap 程式碼。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"aws:softwareInventory only gathers metadata about applications, files, network config, and other configurations, and can be invoked only via a State Manager association (ssm-associate). It is a data-gathering plugin that does not download or run scripts from a Git repository, so it cannot bootstrap the laptops from GitHub.","why_zh":"aws:softwareInventory 只會收集應用程式、檔案、網路設定等的盤點中繼資料，而且只能透過 State Manager association（ssm-associate）來呼叫。它屬於資料蒐集外掛程式，不會從 Git repository 下載或執行 scripts，因此無法用 GitHub 程式碼來 bootstrap 筆電。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/documents-command-ssm-plugin-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/integration-github-python.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/documents-running-remote-github-s3.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":259,"question_en":"A company's development team uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy its application resources. The team must use CloudFormation for all changes to the environment. The team cannot use the AWS Management Console or the AWS CLI to make manual changes directly. The team uses a developer IAM role to access the environment. The role is configured with the AdministratorAccess managed IAM policy. The company has created a new CloudFormationDeployment IAM role that has the following policy attached: The company wants to ensure that only CloudFormation can use the new role. The development team cannot make any manual changes to the deployed resources. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"该公司的发展团队使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署其应用程序资源。团队必须对环境的所有变更都使用 CloudFormation，不能直接使用 AWS 管理控制台或 AWS CLI 进行手动更改。 该团队使用开发人员 IAM 角色来访问环境。该角色配置了“管理员访问”托管 IAM 策略。该公司创建了 一个新的 CloudFormationDeployment IAM 角色，并为其附加了以下策略： 该公司希望确保只有 CloudFormation 能够使用新角色。开发团队不得对已部署的资源进行任何手动更改。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Remove the AdministratorAccess policy. Assign the ReadOnlyAccess managed IAM policy to the developer role. Instruct the developers to use the CloudFormationDeployment role as a CloudFormation service role when the developers deploy new stacks.","B":"Update the trust policy of the CloudFormationDeployment role to allow the developer IAM role to assume the CloudFormationDeployment role.","C":"Configure the developer IAM role to be able to get and pass the CloudFormationDeployment role if iam:PassedToService equals cloudformation.amazonaws.com. Configure the CloudFormationDeployment role to allow all cloudformation actions for all resources.","D":"Update the trust policy of the CloudFormationDeployment role to allow the cloudformation.amazonaws.com AWS principal to perform the iam:AssumeRole action.","E":"Remove the AdministratorAccess policy. Assign the ReadOnlyAccess managed IAM policy to the developer role. Instruct the developers to assume the CloudFormationDeployment role when the developers deploy new stacks.","F":"Add an IAM policy to the CloudFormationDeployment role to allow cloudformation:* on all resources. Add a policy that allows the iam:PassRole action for the ARN of the CloudFormationDeployment role if iam:PassedToService equals cloudformation.amazonaws.com."},"options_zh":{"A":"移除“管理员访问”策略。将“只读访问”托管 IAM 策略分配给开发人员角色。指示开发人员在 部署新堆栈时使用“CloudFormation 部署”角色作为 CloudFormation 服务角色。","B":"更新 CloudFormationDeployment 角色的信任策略，允许开发人员 IAM 角色承担 CloudFormationDeployment 角色。","C":"配置开发人员 IAM 角色，使其能够在 iam:PassedToService 等于 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 时获 取并传递 CloudFormationDeployment 角色。配置 CloudFormationDeployment 角色，使其允许对所有 资源执行所有 CloudFormation 操作。","D":"更新 CloudFormationDeployment 角色的信任策略，允许 cloudformation.amazonaws.com AWS 主体执行 iam:AssumeRole 操作。","E":"移除“管理员访问”策略。将“只读访问”托管 IAM 策略分配给开发人员角色。指示开发人员在 部署新堆栈时承担“CloudFormation 部署”角色。","F":"向 CloudFormationDeployment 角色添加一个 IAM 策略，以允许对所有资源执行 cloudformation:* 操作。 添加一个策略，如果 iam:PassedToService 等于 cloudformation.amazonaws.com，则允许对 CloudFormationDeployment 角色的 ARN 执行 iam:PassRole 操作。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the AWS-documented 'CloudFormation service role' pattern for forcing all changes through CloudFormation while applying least privilege (AWS Prescriptive Guidance: Service roles for CloudFormation). (A) Removing AdministratorAccess and assigning ReadOnlyAccess stops developers from making manual changes via the console/CLI, while instructing them to specify the CloudFormationDeployment role as the CloudFormation service role lets CloudFormation provision resources on their behalf without the developer holding those permissions. (D) The service role's trust policy must allow the cloudformation.amazonaws.com service principal to assume the role (the docs show the action as sts:AssumeRole; option D's 'iam:AssumeRole' is loose wording for the same trust statement). This guarantees that only CloudFormation, not the developers or other services, can use the role. (F) The developer principal needs an identity-based iam:PassRole permission scoped to the CloudFormationDeployment role ARN with the iam:PassedToService = cloudformation.amazonaws.com condition, which is exactly the documented example; the broad provisioning permissions (cloudformation:* here) sit on the deployment role that only CloudFormation can assume. Together these block manual changes, restrict the powerful role to CloudFormation, and still let developers deploy via stacks.","explanation_zh":"這是 AWS 官方文件中的 CloudFormation service role 模式，用於強制所有變更都透過 CloudFormation 進行並落實最小權限（AWS Prescriptive Guidance：Service roles for CloudFormation）。(A) 移除 AdministratorAccess 並改用 ReadOnlyAccess，可阻止開發人員透過主控台或 CLI 手動變更資源；同時指示開發人員在部署時把 CloudFormationDeployment role 指定為 CloudFormation service role，讓 CloudFormation 在開發人員本身不持有這些權限的情況下代為佈建資源。(D) 該 service role 的信任政策必須允許 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 服務 principal assume 此角色（文件中該動作為 sts:AssumeRole；選項 D 的 iam:AssumeRole 只是同一信任陳述的鬆散用語），確保只有 CloudFormation 能使用此角色，開發人員或其他服務都不能。(F) 開發人員 principal 需要一個身分政策，將 iam:PassRole 限縮在 CloudFormationDeployment role ARN，並加上 iam:PassedToService = cloudformation.amazonaws.com 的條件，這正是文件中的範例；而廣泛的佈建權限（此處的 cloudformation:*）則放在只有 CloudFormation 能 assume 的部署角色上。這三步驟共同阻擋手動變更、把高權限角色限制給 CloudFormation，同時仍讓開發人員能透過堆疊部署。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Allowing the developer IAM role to assume the CloudFormationDeployment role hands developers the role's broad provisioning permissions directly, enabling manual changes and violating the requirement that only CloudFormation can use the role. The service-role pattern puts the cloudformation.amazonaws.com service principal in the trust policy, not the developer role.","why_zh":"讓開發人員 IAM role 能 assume CloudFormationDeployment role，等於把該角色的廣泛佈建權限直接交給開發人員，使其能做手動變更，違反『只有 CloudFormation 能使用此角色』的需求。Service role 模式的信任政策應指定 cloudformation.amazonaws.com 服務 principal，而非開發人員 role。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Near-duplicate of F but weaker: it grants the developer a vague 'get and pass' permission that is not scoped to the specific role ARN, whereas the docs recommend limiting iam:PassRole to specific role ARNs for least privilege. F is the precise, ARN-scoped variant, so when choosing exactly three, F is preferred over C.","why_zh":"與 F 近乎重複但較弱：它給開發人員一個含糊的『get and pass』權限，且未限縮在特定的 role ARN，而文件建議為了最小權限應將 iam:PassRole 限定在特定 role ARN。F 是精確、以 ARN 為範圍的版本，因此在只能選三項時，F 優於 C。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Instructing developers to assume the CloudFormationDeployment role grants them the role's provisioning permissions directly, allowing manual changes and breaking the 'only CloudFormation can use the role' rule. The correct flow is to pass the role to CloudFormation as a service role (option A), not to assume it.","why_zh":"指示開發人員去 assume CloudFormationDeployment role，會把該角色的佈建權限直接給開發人員，使其能手動變更，破壞『只有 CloudFormation 能使用此角色』的規則。正確流程是把角色當作 service role 傳給 CloudFormation（選項 A），而非 assume 它。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-iam-servicerole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/least-privilege-cloudformation/service-roles-for-cloudformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_use_passrole.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_iam-passrole-service.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":260,"question_en":"A company is developing a web application's infrastructure using AWS CloudFormation. The database engineering team maintains the database resources in a CloudFormation template, and the software development team maintains the web application resources in a separate CloudFormation template. As the scope of the application grows, the software development team needs to use resources maintained by the database engineering team. However, both teams have their own review and lifecycle management processes that they want to keep. Both teams also require resource-level change-set reviews. The software development team would like to deploy changes to this template using their CI/CD pipeline. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CloudFormation 开发一个网络应用程序的基础设施。数据库工程团队在一个 CloudFormation 模板中维护数据库资源，而软件开发团队则在另一个单独的 CloudFormation 模板中维护网络 应用程序资源。随着 随着应用程序的范围不断扩大，软件开发团队需要使用由数据库工程团队维护的资源。然而，两个团 队都有各自想要保留的审查和生命周期管理流程。两个团队也都需要进行资源级别的变更集审查。软 件开发团队希望使用其 CI/CD 管道来部署对此模板的更改。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a stack export from the database CloudFormation template and import those references into the web application CloudFormation template.","B":"Create a CloudFormation nested stack to make cross-stack resource references and parameters available in both stacks.","C":"Create a CloudFormation stack set to make cross-stack resource references and parameters available in both stacks.","D":"Create input parameters in the web application CloudFormation template and pass resource names and IDs from the database stack."},"options_zh":{"A":"从数据库 CloudFormation 模板创建一个堆栈导出，并将这些引用导入到 Web 应用程序 CloudFormation 模板中。","B":"创建一个 CloudFormation 嵌套堆栈，以便在两个堆栈中都能使用跨堆栈资源引用和参数。","C":"创建一个 CloudFormation 堆栈集，以便在两个堆栈中都能使用跨堆栈资源引用和参数。","D":"在 Web 应用程序的 CloudFormation 模板中创建输入参数，并从数据库堆栈传递资源名称和 ID。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario maps almost verbatim to the AWS CloudFormation best practices 'Organize your stacks by lifecycle and ownership' and 'Use cross-stack references to share values between stacks'. AWS's own example is a website team that owns an application stack plus a separate database team that owns a back-end database stack, where 'whenever the website team or database team needs to update their resources, they can do so without affecting each other's stack.' To let one stack consume resources owned by another, AWS prescribes cross-stack references: the database (exporting) stack declares values in its Outputs section with the Export field, and the web application (importing) stack consumes them with Fn::ImportValue. This keeps each template separately owned and independently deployable, so the software team can update its stack through its own CI/CD pipeline and its own change set, the database team keeps its own review and lifecycle process, and each stack still gets resource-level change-set reviews. Option A is the only choice describing exporting from the database template and importing those references into the web application template, which is the documented mechanism.","explanation_zh":"此情境幾乎逐字對應到 AWS CloudFormation 最佳實務中的「依生命週期與擁有者組織 stacks」以及「使用 cross-stack references 在 stacks 之間共享值」。AWS 自身的範例就是一個擁有 application stack 的 website 團隊，加上另一個擁有後端 database stack 的獨立 database 團隊，且「每當 website 團隊或 database 團隊需要更新自己的資源時，都能在不影響對方 stack 的情況下進行」。要讓某個 stack 使用另一個 stack 所擁有的資源，AWS 明確建議採用 cross-stack references：由 database（匯出端）stack 在 Outputs 區段以 Export 欄位宣告值，web application（匯入端）stack 則以 Fn::ImportValue 取用。如此可讓兩個範本各自獨立擁有與部署，software 團隊得以透過自家 CI/CD pipeline 與自己的 change set 更新其 stack，database 團隊保留自己的審查與生命週期流程，且每個 stack 仍能各自取得 resource-level change-set review。選項 A 是唯一描述從 database 範本匯出並將參考匯入 web application 範本的選項，正是文件所載的機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A nested stack uses the AWS::CloudFormation::Stack resource so that a root stack deploys and manages all child stacks as a single unit. AWS docs explicitly state nested stacks are for isolating information sharing WITHIN one nested-stack group that is managed together; they collapse the two teams into one combined lifecycle, ownership, and deployment, which directly violates the requirement that each team keep its own separate review and lifecycle processes and deploy independently.","why_zh":"Nested stack 使用 AWS::CloudFormation::Stack 資源，使 root stack 將所有子 stack 當成一個整體部署與管理。AWS 文件明言 nested stacks 適用於在同一個共同管理的 nested-stack 群組「內部」共享資訊；它會把兩個團隊併入單一生命週期、擁有權與部署，直接違反各團隊各自保留獨立審查與生命週期流程並獨立部署的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"StackSets are for creating, updating, or deleting the same stack across multiple AWS accounts and Regions with one operation. They provide no mechanism for one stack to reference another stack's resources, and this scenario is about two teams' separate templates (presumably in one account), not multi-account/multi-Region replication. StackSets do not 'make cross-stack resource references available' as the option claims.","why_zh":"StackSets 用於以單一操作在多個 AWS 帳戶與區域建立、更新或刪除同一個 stack。它並未提供讓一個 stack 參考另一個 stack 資源的機制，而本情境是兩個團隊各自的範本（推測在同一帳戶內），並非多帳戶/多區域複寫。StackSets 並不會如該選項所稱「讓 cross-stack 資源參考可用」。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Passing resource names and IDs as input parameters technically works, but AWS best practices explicitly identify this as the inferior alternative: hardcoding values or passing them as input parameters 'can make templates difficult to reuse or can increase the overhead to get a stack running,' and AWS instead recommends cross-stack references. Plain parameters also create no enforced dependency, so the database team could delete or change a referenced resource and break the application stack, whereas Export/ImportValue prevents deleting or modifying an exported value while it is imported. Therefore A is the prescribed, more robust solution.","why_zh":"將資源名稱與 ID 以 input parameters 傳入在技術上可行，但 AWS 最佳實務明確將其列為較差的替代方案：硬編碼或以 input parameters 傳值「會使範本難以重用或增加啟動 stack 的額外成本」，AWS 並建議改用 cross-stack references。純參數也不會建立強制相依，database 團隊可能刪除或變更被參考資源而破壞 application stack，而 Export/ImportValue 會在匯出值仍被匯入時阻止其被刪除或修改。因此 A 才是文件所建議且更穩健的解法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-stack-exports.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/walkthrough-crossstackref.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/intrinsic-function-reference-importvalue.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":261,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations. A DevOps engineer needs to maintain multiple AWS accounts that belong to different OUs in the organization. All resources, including IAM policies and Amazon S3 policies within an account, are deployed through AWS CloudFormation. All templates and code are maintained in an AWS CodeCommit repository. Recently, some developers have not been able to access an S3 bucket from some accounts in the organization. The following policy is attached to the S3 bucket: What should the DevOps engineer do to resolve this access issue?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中拥有一个组织架构。一位 DevOps 工程师需要维护该组织中不同组织单位 （OU）所属的多个 AWS 账户。所有资源，包括账户内的 IAM 策略和 Amazon S3 策略，均通过 AWS CloudFormation 进行部署。所有模板和代码都保存在 AWS CodeCommit 代码库中。最近，一些 开发人员无法从组织中的某些账户访问 S3 存储桶。 以下策略已附加到 S3 存储桶： 开发运维工程师应该采取什么措施来解决这个访问问题？","options_en":{"A":"Modify the S3 bucket policy. Turn off the S3 Block Public Access setting on the S3 bucket. In the S3 policy, add the aws:SourceAccount condition. Add the AWS account IDs of all developers who are experiencing the issue.","B":"Verify that no IAM permissions boundaries are denying developers access to the S3 bucket. Make the necessary changes to IAM permissions boundaries. Use an AWS Config recorder in the individual developer accounts that are experiencing the issue to revert any changes that are blocking access. Commit the fix back into the CodeCommit repository. Invoke deployment through CloudFormation to apply the changes.","C":"Configure an SCP that stops anyone from modifying IAM resources in developer OUs. In the S3 policy, add the aws:SourceAccount condition. Add the AWS account IDs of all developers who are experiencing the issue. Commit the fix back into the CodeCommit repository. Invoke deployment through CloudFormation to apply the changes.","D":"Ensure that no SCP is blocking access for developers to the S3 bucket. Ensure that no IAM policy permissions boundaries are denying access to developer IAM users. Make the necessary changes to the SCP and IAM policy permissions boundaries in the CodeCommit repository. Invoke deployment through CloudFormation to apply the changes."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 S3 存储桶策略。关闭 S3 存储桶上的“阻止公共访问”设置。在 S3 策略中添加 aws: SourceAccount 条件。添加所有遇到此问题的开发人员的 AWS 账户 ID。","B":"确认没有 IAM 权限边界阻止开发人员访问 S3 存储桶。对 IAM 权限边界进行必要的更改。在遇到 问题的各个开发人员账户中使用 AWS Config 记录器撤销任何阻止访问的更改。将修复内容提交 回 CodeCommit 存储库。通过 CloudFormation 调用部署以应用更改。","C":"配置一个安全策略（SCP），禁止任何人修改开发人员组织单位（OU）中的 IAM 资源。在 S3 策略 中添加 aws:SourceAccount 条件。添加所有开发人员的 AWS 账户 ID。 遇到此问题。将修复内容提交回 CodeCommit 代码库。通过 CloudFormation 调用部署以应用 更改。","D":"确保没有 SCP 阻止开发人员访问 S3 存储桶。确保没有 IAM 策略权限边界拒绝开发人员 IAM 用 户的访问权限。在 CodeCommit 存储库中对 SCP 和 IAM 策略权限边界进行必要的更改。通过 CloudFormation 调用部署以应用这些更改。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Effective permissions for a principal are the intersection of identity-based policies, resource-based policies (the S3 bucket policy), AWS Organizations SCPs, and any IAM permissions boundary, and an explicit Deny in any one of these overrides an Allow. Because developers are blocked only in some accounts/OUs, the cause is almost certainly an organization-level guardrail: an SCP attached at the OU or account level and/or an IAM permissions boundary that denies the action (the per-account/OU scope explains why only some developers are affected). SCPs set the maximum available permissions for IAM users and roles in member accounts and never grant access, while permissions boundaries cap what an identity-based policy can grant; a deny or missing allow in either blocks access. Option D is correct because it inspects both guardrail types (SCPs and permissions boundaries), then makes the corrective change in the CodeCommit repository and redeploys it through CloudFormation, matching the company's established infrastructure-as-code workflow where all IAM and S3 policies are deployed via CloudFormation from CodeCommit.","explanation_zh":"主體的有效權限是 identity-based policy、resource-based policy（即 S3 bucket policy）、AWS Organizations SCP 以及 IAM permissions boundary 四者的交集，且其中任何一個出現明確 Deny 都會覆蓋 Allow。由於只有部分帳戶/OU 的開發者被擋下，原因幾乎可確定是組織層級的護欄：附加在 OU 或帳戶層級的 SCP，和/或拒絕該動作的 IAM permissions boundary（其作用範圍為個別帳戶/OU，正好解釋為何只有部分開發者受影響）。SCP 為 member account 中的 IAM user 與 role 設定可用權限上限且本身不授權，而 permissions boundary 則限制 identity-based policy 能授予的最大權限；兩者中任一出現 Deny 或缺少 Allow 都會阻擋存取。選項 D 正確，因為它同時檢查這兩種護欄（SCP 與 permissions boundary），接著在 CodeCommit repository 中進行修正並透過 CloudFormation 重新部署，符合公司既有的 IaC 工作流程（所有 IAM 與 S3 政策皆由 CodeCommit 透過 CloudFormation 部署）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Turning off S3 Block Public Access and adding aws:SourceAccount treats the bucket as if it needs public access, which is a security anti-pattern and not the root cause. Internal organization developers needing access does not require making the bucket public, and this approach also bypasses the required CodeCommit/CloudFormation workflow.","why_zh":"關閉 S3 Block Public Access 並加入 aws:SourceAccount 等於把 bucket 當成需要公開存取，這是安全反模式，也非根本原因。組織內部開發者需要存取並不代表要把 bucket 設為公開，且此做法繞過了必須遵循的 CodeCommit/CloudFormation 工作流程。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"It ignores SCPs entirely and misuses AWS Config: a configuration recorder records and tracks resource configuration changes but does not by itself revert changes that block access (remediation requires AWS Config rules with remediation actions, not the recorder). It also omits the SCP guardrail that commonly causes selective cross-account/OU denials.","why_zh":"完全忽略 SCP 並誤用 AWS Config：configuration recorder 只記錄與追蹤資源組態變更，本身並不會還原阻擋存取的變更（還原須透過具備 remediation action 的 AWS Config rule，而非 recorder）。此選項也遺漏了常造成跨帳戶/OU 選擇性拒絕的 SCP 護欄。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP that stops anyone from modifying IAM resources further restricts permissions rather than granting developers S3 access, and adding aws:SourceAccount does not resolve a guardrail-based denial. This makes the access problem worse, not better.","why_zh":"一個阻止任何人修改 IAM 資源的 SCP 只會進一步限制權限，而非授予開發者 S3 存取權；加入 aws:SourceAccount 也無法解決護欄造成的拒絕。此做法只會讓存取問題更嚴重。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/how-does-config-work.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":262,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations for its multi-account environment. A DevOps engineer is developing an AWS CodeArtifact based strategy for application package management across the organization. Each application team at the company has its own account in the organization. Each application team also has limited access to a centralized shared services account. Each application team needs full access to download, publish, and grant access to its own packages. Some common library packages that the application teams use must also be shared with the entire organization. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST administrative overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS Organizations 中为其多账户环境建立了一个组织架构。一位 DevOps 工程师正在为 整个组织开发基于 AWS CodeArtifact 的应用包管理策略。该公司每个应用团队在组织中都有自己的 账户。每个应用团队还对一个集中的共享服务账户拥有有限的访问权限。 每个应用程序团队都需要完全访问权限来下载、发布和授予其自身软件包的访问权限。应用程序 团队使用的某些常见库软件包也必须与整个组织共享。 哪种步骤组合能以最低的管理开销满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a domain in each application team's account. Grant each application team's account full read access and write access to the application team's domain.","B":"Create a domain in the shared services account. Grant the organization read access and CreateRepository access.","C":"Create a repository in each application team’s account. Grant each application team’s account full read access and write access to its own repository.","D":"Create a repository in the shared services account. Grant the organization read access to the repository in the shared services account Set the repository as the upstream repository in each application team's repository.","E":"For teams that require shared packages, create resource-based policies that allow read access to the repository from other application teams' accounts.","F":"Set the other application teams' repositories as upstream repositories."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个应用团队的账户中创建一个域。授予每个应用团队的账户对其所属域的完全读取访问权限 和写入访问权限。","B":"在共享服务账户中创建一个域。授予该组织读取权限和创建存储库权限。","C":"在每个应用团队的账户中创建一个代码库。授予每个应用团队的账户对其自身代码库的完全读取权 限和写入权限。","D":"在共享服务账户中创建一个代码库。授予组织对该共享服务账户中代码库的读取权限。将 该代码库设置为每个应用团队代码库的上游代码库。","E":"对于需要共享包的团队，请创建基于资源的策略，允许其他应用程序团队的账户从存储库读取内 容。","F":"将其他应用程序团队的代码库设置为上游代码库。"},"answer":["B","C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance"],"research":{"verdict":["B","C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeArtifact recommends a single production domain for the whole organization so packages can be discovered and shared, and upstream relationships only work between repositories that are members of the SAME domain (\"You can only add repositories in the same domain as upstream repositories\"). (B) Create one domain in the shared services account and attach a domain policy that uses the aws:PrincipalOrgID condition to grant the entire organization GetAuthorizationToken (read) and CreateRepository; this is the documented, lowest-overhead pattern for letting all org accounts use one shared domain. (C) Using the cross-account CreateRepository grant from the domain policy, each team creates and OWNS a repository in its own account that is a member of the shared domain. By default only the repository owner has access, so each team automatically has full ability to download, publish, and manage the repository's resource policy (grant access) for its own packages with no extra configuration. (D) For the common library packages, create one repository in the shared services account, grant the organization read access, and set it as an upstream repository on each team's repository. Because upstream package versions are exposed through the downstream repository's single endpoint, all teams consume the shared libraries automatically with minimal ongoing administration. A (a domain per team) breaks the single-domain recommendation and the same-domain upstream requirement while multiplying admin work; E (per-team resource-based read policies between every pair of teams) and F (cross-meshing every team's repo as upstream of every other) both create O(N^2) manual sharing instead of one centralized upstream, so they add far more administrative overhead.","explanation_zh":"CodeArtifact 建議整個組織使用單一 production domain，讓套件能跨團隊被發現與共享，而 upstream 關係只能在「同一個 domain」內的 repository 之間建立（官方文件明載：「You can only add repositories in the same domain as upstream repositories」）。(B) 在 shared services 帳號建立一個 domain，並使用 aws:PrincipalOrgID 條件鍵的 domain policy 授予整個 organization GetAuthorizationToken（讀取）與 CreateRepository 權限；這正是官方文件記載、管理負擔最低的做法，讓組織內所有帳號都能使用同一個共享 domain。(C) 各應用團隊利用 domain policy 中的跨帳號 CreateRepository 授權，在「自己的帳號」內建立並擁有一個隸屬於該共享 domain 的 repository。預設情況下只有 repository 擁有者擁有存取權，因此每個團隊自動即擁有對自身套件完整的下載、發布及管理該 repository resource policy（授權他人存取）能力，毋須額外設定。(D) 對於共用函式庫套件，在 shared services 帳號建立一個 repository，授予 organization 讀取權限，並將其設定為每個團隊 repository 的 upstream repository。由於 upstream 的套件版本會透過下游 repository 的單一 endpoint 自動暴露，所有團隊即可自動取得共用函式庫，後續管理成本極低。A（每個團隊各建一個 domain）違反單一 domain 建議，破壞「upstream 必須在同一 domain」的限制並大幅增加管理工作；E（在每對團隊之間建立資源型讀取政策）與 F（讓每個團隊互設彼此 repository 為 upstream）都會造成 O(N^2) 的手動共享，而非單一集中式 upstream，管理負擔遠高於正確選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a domain in every team account violates the recommended single-production-domain model, fragments storage and KMS encryption, and breaks upstream sharing because upstream repositories must be in the same domain. It maximizes, not minimizes, administrative overhead.","why_zh":"在每個團隊帳號建立 domain 違反建議的單一 production domain 模型，造成儲存與 KMS 加密分散，且因 upstream repository 必須位於同一 domain 而破壞 upstream 共享，反而使管理負擔最大化。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Per-team resource-based policies that grant read access between each pair of team accounts is manual, pairwise sharing. For org-wide common libraries this is far more administrative overhead than a single centralized upstream repository granted org read access (option D).","why_zh":"在每對團隊帳號之間建立彼此互相讀取的資源型政策屬於手動、成對的共享方式；對於需要全組織共用的函式庫，這比單一集中式 upstream repository 授予 organization 讀取（選項 D）的管理負擔大得多。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Setting every other team's repositories as upstreams creates an O(N^2) mesh and does not implement the centralized common-library sharing the scenario needs; it greatly increases ongoing administration versus a single shared-services upstream repository.","why_zh":"將其他所有團隊的 repository 互設為 upstream 會形成 O(N^2) 的網狀結構，且無法實現情境所需的集中式共用函式庫共享，與單一 shared services upstream repository 相比會大幅增加持續管理成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/domain-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/domain-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repo-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repos-upstream.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repo-upstream-add.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":263,"question_en":"A company deploys an application to Amazon EC2 instances. The application runs Amazon Linux 2 and uses AWS CodeDeploy. The application has the following file structure for its code repository: The appspec.yml file has the following contents in the files section: What will the result be for the deployment of the config.txt file?","question_zh":"一家公司将一个应用程序部署到 Amazon EC2 实例上。该应用程序运行 Amazon Linux 2 操作系统， 并使用 AWS CodeDeploy。该应用程序的代码库具有以下文件结构： appspec.yml 文件在 files 部分包含以下内容： 部署 config.txt 文件的结果会怎样？","options_en":{"A":"The config.txt file will be deployed to only /var/www/html/config/config.txt.","B":"The config.txt file will be deployed to /usr/local/src/config.txt and to /var/www/html/config/config.txt.","C":"The config.txt file will be deployed to only /usr/local/src/config.txt.","D":"The config.txt file will be deployed to /usr/local/src/config.txt and to /var/www/html/application/web/ config.txt."},"options_zh":{"A":"config.txt 文件将仅部署到 /var/www/html/config/config.txt 这个位置。","B":"config.txt 文件将被部署到 /usr/local/src/config.txt 以及 /var/www/html/config/config.txt 。","C":"config.txt 文件将仅部署到 /usr/local/src/config.txt 。","D":"config.txt 文件将被部署到 /usr/local/src/config.txt 以及 /var/www/html/application/web/config.txt 。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The vendor watermark mangled this well-known DOP-C02 question. Its canonical files section has two entries: (1) source: config/config.txt -> destination: /usr/local/src, and (2) source: / -> destination: /var/www/html (the destination is /var/www/html, NOT /var/www/html/application/web). Per the AppSpec 'files' section reference, the two operations run during the Install event. Entry 1: source points to a single file and destination is a directory, so the file is copied as destination/<filename> = /usr/local/src/config.txt (this mirrors the doc's own example source: Config/config.txt -> /webapps/Config => /webapps/Config/config.txt). Entry 2: source is a single slash '/', which copies ALL files from the revision to the destination while preserving their relative paths (see the doc's Example 9, where source '\\' yields c:\\temp\\my-folder\\my-file.txt, preserving the folder). Therefore config/config.txt lands at /var/www/html/config/config.txt. config.txt is thus deployed to TWO locations: /usr/local/src/config.txt and /var/www/html/config/config.txt, which is exactly option B. Note: the first analyst reached the correct letter B but mis-reconstructed the second destination as /var/www/html/application/web; the real destination is /var/www/html, and 'application/web' is actually the flattened distractor path in option D.","explanation_zh":"販售浮水印破壞了這道知名的 DOP-C02 題。其原始 files 區段有兩筆:(1) source: config/config.txt -> destination: /usr/local/src,(2) source: / -> destination: /var/www/html(destination 是 /var/www/html,並非 /var/www/html/application/web)。依 AppSpec 'files' section 文件,這兩個操作在 Install 事件執行。第一筆:source 指向單一檔案、destination 為目錄,因此檔案被複製為 destination/<檔名> = /usr/local/src/config.txt(對應文件自身範例 source: Config/config.txt -> /webapps/Config => /webapps/Config/config.txt)。第二筆:source 為單一斜線「/」,會將 revision 中所有檔案複製到 destination 並保留其相對路徑(見文件 Example 9,source「\\」會得到 c:\\temp\\my-folder\\my-file.txt,保留資料夾結構)。因此 config/config.txt 會落在 /var/www/html/config/config.txt。所以 config.txt 被部署到兩個位置:/usr/local/src/config.txt 與 /var/www/html/config/config.txt,正好對應選項 B。註:第一位分析員雖選對字母 B,但誤把第二個 destination 還原成 /var/www/html/application/web;實際 destination 為 /var/www/html,而「application/web」其實是選項 D 中被壓平的誘答路徑。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Claims deployment to only ONE location (/var/www/html/config/config.txt) and omits the explicit first mapping. The first files entry (source: config/config.txt -> destination: /usr/local/src) also copies the file to /usr/local/src/config.txt, so there are two destinations, not one. A also drops the first destination entirely.","why_zh":"宣稱只部署到一個位置(/var/www/html/config/config.txt),且忽略第一筆明確對應。第一筆 files 設定(source: config/config.txt -> destination: /usr/local/src)也會把檔案複製到 /usr/local/src/config.txt,因此有兩個目的地而非一個;A 完全漏掉第一個目的地。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Lists only /usr/local/src/config.txt and ignores the second entry (source: /), which copies the whole revision (including config/config.txt) to /var/www/html, producing /var/www/html/config/config.txt. C therefore understates the result to a single location.","why_zh":"只列出 /usr/local/src/config.txt,忽略第二筆(source: /)會把整份 revision(含 config/config.txt)複製到 /var/www/html,得到 /var/www/html/config/config.txt。因此 C 低估為單一位置。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Correctly identifies two locations and the first path, but the second path is wrong on two counts: (1) the second destination is /var/www/html, not /var/www/html/application/web, and (2) source: '/' preserves relative paths, so the config/ subfolder is retained -> /var/www/html/config/config.txt, not a flattened .../config.txt. D both invents an 'application/web' segment and strips the config/ directory.","why_zh":"正確指出兩個位置與第一個路徑,但第二個路徑有兩處錯誤:(1) 第二個 destination 是 /var/www/html,而非 /var/www/html/application/web;(2) source 為「/」會保留相對路徑,因此保留 config/ 子資料夾 -> /var/www/html/config/config.txt,而非被壓平的 .../config.txt。D 既杜撰了「application/web」段,又移除了 config/ 目錄。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file-structure-files.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/application-revisions-plan.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":264,"question_en":"A company has set up AWS CodeArtifact repositories with public upstream repositories. The company's development team consumes open source dependencies from the repositories in the company's internal network. The company's security team recently discovered a critical vulnerability in the most recent version of a package that the development team consumes. The security team has produced a patched version to fix the vulnerability. The company needs to prevent the vulnerable version from being downloaded. The company also needs to allow the security team to publish the patched version. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司已设置了带有公共上游存储库的 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。该公司的开发团队从公司内部网 络中的这些存储库获取开源依赖项。 该公司安全团队最近在开发团队使用的最新版本的一个软件包中发现了一个严重漏洞。安全团队已制 作出修复该漏洞的补丁版本。公司需要阻止易受攻击的版本被下载。公司还需要允许安全团队发布补 丁版本。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the status of the affected CodeArtifact package version to unlisted.","B":"Update the status of the affected CodeArtifact package version to deleted.","C":"Update the status of the affected CodeArtifact package version to archived.","D":"Update the CodeArtifact package origin control settings to allow direct publishing and to block upstream operations.","E":"Update the CodeArtifact package origin control settings to block direct publishing and to allow upstream operations."},"options_zh":{"A":"将受影响的 CodeArtifact 包版本的状态更新为“未列出”。","B":"将受影响的 CodeArtifact 包版本的状态更新为已删除。","C":"将受影响的 CodeArtifact 包版本的状态更新为已归档。","D":"更新 CodeArtifact 包源代码控制设置，以允许直接发布并阻止上游操作。","E":"更新 CodeArtifact 包源代码控制设置，以阻止直接发布并允许上游操作。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Uncategorized"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Two requirements must both be satisfied: (1) prevent the vulnerable version from being downloaded, and (2) let the security team publish the patched version. For (1), CodeArtifact package version statuses are decisive. Setting the affected version to Archived means \"the package version's assets can no longer be downloaded ... consumption of the package version by clients is blocked,\" and it is reversible (you can return it to Unlisted or Published). So C is correct. Unlisted (A) explicitly states the assets \"are available for download from the repository\" (it only hides the version from package-manager version lists), so it does NOT block downloads. Deleted (B) is not a valid UpdatePackageVersionsStatus value (valid: Archived | Published | Unlisted); DeletePackageVersions permanently removes the version, after which it can be re-ingested from the public upstream again, so deletion does not reliably keep the vulnerable version out. For (2), origin controls decide it. Because the package was first ingested from a public upstream, its default origin settings are Publish: BLOCK / Upstream: ALLOW, which would reject a directly published patch. The documented \"Publishing a patched package version of an existing external package\" scenario is to change origin controls to Publish: ALLOW and Upstream: BLOCK, exactly option D. Option E is the reverse and would block the patch while re-admitting the vulnerable upstream version.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個必須同時滿足的需求：(1) 阻止有漏洞的版本被下載，(2) 讓 security team 能發佈修補後的版本。針對 (1)，CodeArtifact 的 package version status 是關鍵。將受影響版本設為 Archived 表示「該版本的 assets 無法再被下載……clients 對該版本的取用被封鎖」，且此狀態可逆（可改回 Unlisted 或 Published），因此 C 正確。Unlisted（A）文件明確指出該版本的 assets「仍可從 repository 下載」，它只是讓該版本不出現在 package manager 的版本清單中，並不會阻止下載。Deleted（B）並非 UpdatePackageVersionsStatus 的合法值（合法值為 Archived | Published | Unlisted）；DeletePackageVersions 會永久移除版本，之後該版本仍可能再次從 public upstream 被 ingest 進來，因此刪除無法可靠地阻擋有漏洞的版本。針對 (2)，由 package origin controls 決定。由於此 package 最初是從 public upstream ingest 進來的，其預設 origin 設定為 Publish: BLOCK / Upstream: ALLOW，會拒絕直接發佈的修補版本。官方文件中「Publishing a patched package version of an existing external package」的情境就是將 origin controls 改為 Publish: ALLOW 與 Upstream: BLOCK，正是選項 D。選項 E 則相反，會封鎖修補版本，同時又重新放行有漏洞的 upstream 版本。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Unlisted does NOT block downloads. AWS docs: the assets \"are available for download from the repository, but the package version is not included in the list of versions returned to package managers.\" It only hides it from version lists, and lock-file references still install it. It fails requirement (1).","why_zh":"Unlisted 不會封鎖下載。AWS 文件：該版本的 assets「仍可從 repository 下載，只是不會出現在回傳給 package manager 的版本清單中。」它只是從清單隱藏，且 lock 檔已引用的版本仍可安裝。無法滿足需求 (1)。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"\"Deleted\" is not a valid targetStatus for UpdatePackageVersionsStatus (valid values: Archived | Published | Unlisted). DeletePackageVersions permanently removes the version, after which (per AWS docs) \"you can freely re-publish that package version\" and the same vulnerable version can be re-ingested from the public upstream, so it does not reliably prevent downloads.","why_zh":"「Deleted」並非 UpdatePackageVersionsStatus 的合法 targetStatus（合法值為 Archived | Published | Unlisted）。DeletePackageVersions 會永久移除版本，刪除後（依 AWS 文件）「可自由重新發佈該版本」，同一有漏洞的版本也可能從 public upstream 重新 ingest，因此無法可靠地阻止下載。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"This is the reverse of what is needed. Block publishing + allow upstream is the default for a package first ingested from public, which rejects the security team's directly published patch and re-admits the vulnerable upstream version. It fails requirement (2).","why_zh":"此選項與需求相反。Block publishing + allow upstream 正是最初從 public ingest 的 package 的預設值，會拒絕 security team 直接發佈的修補版本，並重新放行有漏洞的 upstream 版本。無法滿足需求 (2)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/packages-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/package-origin-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/update-package-version-status.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/APIReference/API_UpdatePackageVersionsStatus.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/APIReference/API_DeletePackageVersions.html"]}},{"id":265,"question_en":"A company is running a custom-built application that processes records. All the components run on Amazon EC2 instances that run in an Auto Scaling group. Each record's processing is a multistep sequential action that is compute-intensive. Each step is always completed in 5 minutes or less. A limitation of the current system is that if any steps fail, the application has to reprocess the record from the beginning. The company wants to update the architecture so that the application must reprocess only the failed steps. What is the MOST operationally efficient solution that meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在运行一个定制开发的应用程序来处理记录。所有组件都在一个自动扩展组中的亚马 逊 EC2 实例上运行。每条记录的处理是一个多步骤的顺序操作，计算密集型。每个步骤总是能在 5 分钟或更短时间内完成。 当前系统的一个局限性在于，如果任何步骤失败，应用程序就必须从头开始重新处理该记录。公司希 望更新架构，使应用程序只需重新处理失败的步骤。 满足这些要求的最高效的操作解决方案是什么？","options_en":{"A":"Create a web application to write records to Amazon S3. Use S3 Event Notifications to publish to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Use an EC2 instance to poll Amazon SNS and start processing. Save intermediate results to Amazon S3 to pass on to the next step.","B":"Perform the processing steps by using logic in the application. Convert the application code to run in a container. Use AWS Fargate to manage the container instances. Configure the container to invoke itself to pass the state from one step to the next.","C":"Create a web application to pass records to an Amazon Kinesis data stream. Decouple the processing by using the Kinesis data stream and AWS Lambda functions.","D":"Create a web application to pass records to AWS Step Functions. Decouple the processing into Step Functions tasks and AWS Lambda functions."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个网络应用程序，将记录写入亚马逊 S3。使用 S3 事件通知发布到亚马逊简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题。使用 EC2 实例轮询亚马逊 SNS 然后开始处理。将中间结果保存到亚马逊 S3，以便传递给下一步。","B":"在应用程序中使用逻辑执行处理步骤。将应用程序代码转换为在容器中运行。使用 AWS Fargate 来管理 容器实例。配置容器使其能够调用自身，以便将状态从一个步骤传递到下一个步骤。","C":"创建一个网络应用程序，将记录传递到 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。通过使用 Kinesis 数据流和 AWS Lambda 函数来解耦处理过程。","D":"创建一个网络应用程序，将记录传递给 AWS Step Functions。将处理过程分解为 Step Functions 任务和 AWS Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a multistep, sequential, compute-intensive process where each step completes in under 5 minutes, and on failure the application must reprocess only the failed step rather than the entire record, using the MOST operationally efficient (least-management) approach. AWS Step Functions is purpose-built for this: the AWS docs explicitly list 'Sequential processing' (run tasks in the correct sequence and pass data between Lambda functions) and 'Complex error handling' (configure automatic retries with exponential backoff and Catch to a fallback state) as canonical reasons to orchestrate Lambda with Step Functions. Step Functions persists state/output between Task states and applies Retry/Catch at the individual Task level, so a failed step is retried in place without re-running the steps that already succeeded. Decoupling each compute step into its own Lambda function (15-minute max timeout, well above the 5-minute step duration) wired as Step Functions tasks yields a fully managed, serverless solution with per-step failure recovery and no EC2/servers to operate, making it the most operationally efficient choice.","explanation_zh":"需求是一個多步驟、循序、運算密集的流程，每個步驟在 5 分鐘內完成，且失敗時應用程式只需重新處理失敗的步驟而非整筆記錄，並要求「最具操作效率」（最少維運負擔）的方案。AWS Step Functions 正是為此而設計：AWS 文件明確將「Sequential processing」（依正確順序執行 task 並在 Lambda function 之間傳遞資料）與「Complex error handling」（設定具指數退避的自動 Retry，並以 Catch 導向 fallback state）列為以 Step Functions 編排 Lambda 的典型理由。Step Functions 會在各 Task state 之間持久化狀態/輸出，並在個別 Task 層級套用 Retry/Catch，因此失敗步驟可就地重試，而不必重跑已成功的步驟。將每個運算步驟拆成各自的 Lambda function（最長 15 分鐘逾時，遠高於 5 分鐘步驟時長）並串接為 Step Functions tasks，即可得到完全託管、無伺服器、具備逐步失敗復原且無需維運任何 EC2/伺服器的方案，是最具操作效率的選擇。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon SNS is a push/pub-sub service, not a queue you 'poll' from an EC2 instance (you poll SQS, not SNS), so the proposed mechanism is not a valid pattern. It still runs and manages EC2 instances, and manual checkpointing by saving intermediate results to S3 with custom code provides no built-in per-step retry or orchestration, making it operationally heavy and a poor fit for 'reprocess only failed steps'.","why_zh":"Amazon SNS 是推送/發布訂閱服務，並非可由 EC2「輪詢」的佇列（要輪詢的是 SQS 而非 SNS），因此此機制並非有效模式。它仍須執行並維運 EC2，且以自訂程式碼將中間結果存到 S3 進行手動檢查點並無內建的逐步重試或編排能力，維運負擔重，無法良好滿足「僅重跑失敗步驟」的需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Having a Fargate container 'invoke itself to pass the state from one step to the next' is not a coherent orchestration mechanism and is an anti-pattern. It provides no managed state persistence, no checkpointing, and no per-step Retry/Catch, so a failure still requires custom logic to resume only the failed step. It is far less operationally efficient than a managed Step Functions workflow.","why_zh":"讓 Fargate 容器「呼叫自身以將狀態從一步傳到下一步」並非合理的編排機制，屬於反模式。它沒有託管的狀態持久化、沒有檢查點、也沒有逐步的 Retry/Catch，失敗時仍需自訂邏輯才能只恢復失敗步驟，操作效率遠不及託管的 Step Functions 工作流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams decouples high-throughput ingestion but does not orchestrate a sequential multistep workflow nor persist per-step state. There is no native concept of resuming only a failed step; on consumer failure Kinesis reprocesses from the shard checkpoint, which can re-run earlier steps. It lacks the state-machine semantics (sequential Task states with per-task Retry/Catch) the requirement needs.","why_zh":"Amazon Kinesis Data Streams 可解耦高吞吐的資料攝取，但無法編排循序的多步驟工作流程，也不會持久化各步驟狀態。它沒有「只恢復失敗步驟」的原生概念；消費端失敗時 Kinesis 會從 shard 檢查點重新處理，可能重跑先前步驟。它缺乏需求所需的狀態機語義（具逐步 Retry/Catch 的循序 Task states）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-step-functions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/concepts-error-handling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/state-task.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":266,"question_en":"A company is migrating its on-premises Windows applications and Linux applications to AWS. The company will use automation to launch Amazon EC2 instances to mirror the on-premises configurations. The migrated applications require access to shared storage that uses SMB for Windows and NFS for Linux. The company is also creating a pilot light disaster recovery (DR) environment in another AWS Region. The company will use automation to launch and configure the EC2 instances in the DR Region. The company needs to replicate the storage to the DR Region. Which storage solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其本地的 Windows 应用程序和 Linux 应用程序迁移到 AWS。该公司将使用自动化来启动 Amazon EC2 实例以复制本地配置。迁移后的应用程序需要访问共享存储，其中 Windows 使用 SMB 协议， Linux 使用 NFS 协议。 该公司还在另一个 AWS 区域创建了一个试点的轻量级灾难恢复（DR）环境。该公司将使用自动化来在 DR 区域启动和配置 EC2 实例。该公司需要将存储复制到 DR 区域。 哪种存储方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon S3 for the application storage. Create an S3 bucket in the primary Region and an S3 bucket in the DR Region. Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) from the primary Region to the DR Region.","B":"Use Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) for the application storage. Create a backup plan in AWS Backup that creates snapshots of the EBS volumes that are in the primary Region and replicates the snapshots to the DR Region.","C":"Use a Volume Gateway in AWS Storage Gateway for the application storage. Configure Cross-Region Replication (CRR) of the Volume Gateway from the primary Region to the DR Region.","D":"Use Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP for the application storage. Create an FSx for ONTAP instance in the DR Region. Configure NetApp SnapMirror replication from the primary Region to the DR Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"为应用程序存储使用亚马逊 S3。在主区域创建一个 S3 存储桶，在灾难恢复区域创建一个 S3 存储桶。 配置从主区域到灾难恢复区域的 S3 跨区域复制（CRR）。","B":"为应用程序存储使用亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）。在 AWS 备份中创建一个备份计划，该计划对 主区域中的 EBS 卷创建快照，并将快照复制到灾难恢复区域。","C":"在 AWS 存储网关中使用卷网关作为应用程序存储。配置卷网关从主区域到灾难恢复区域的跨区域复制 （CRR）。","D":"使用 Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP 作为应用程序存储。在灾难恢复区域创建一个 FSx for ONTAP 实例。 从主区域配置 NetApp SnapMirror 复制到灾难恢复区域。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive requirement is shared file storage that serves SMB to the Windows applications and NFS to the Linux applications, combined with replication to a DR Region for a pilot light setup. Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP is the only listed option that natively provides multiprotocol file access (NFS, SMB, iSCSI, and NVMe) from a single file system, so both Windows and Linux EC2 instances can mount the same shared storage. FSx for ONTAP also supports NetApp SnapMirror replication, which AWS documents as available for both in-Region and cross-Region deployments, letting you replicate to a second FSx for ONTAP file system in the DR Region with RPO-driven scheduling. This satisfies both the multiprotocol shared-storage and cross-Region DR replication requirements. The other options are either object/block storage (S3, EBS) that cannot be mounted as SMB/NFS file shares, or a Volume Gateway that presents iSCSI block volumes (not SMB/NFS) and has no native cross-Region replication feature.","explanation_zh":"決定性的需求是一個共享檔案儲存，能同時為 Windows 應用提供 SMB、為 Linux 應用提供 NFS，並且要複製到 DR Region 以支援 pilot light 架構。在所列選項中，只有 Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP 原生提供單一檔案系統的多協定檔案存取（NFS、SMB、iSCSI、NVMe），因此 Windows 與 Linux EC2 執行個體都能掛載同一份共享儲存。FSx for ONTAP 也支援 NetApp SnapMirror 複製，AWS 文件明確指出此功能同時適用於同 Region 與跨 Region 部署，可將資料複製到 DR Region 的第二個 FSx for ONTAP 檔案系統，並依 RPO 排定複製頻率。這同時滿足多協定共享儲存與跨 Region DR 複製兩項需求。其餘選項不是物件／區塊儲存（S3、EBS）無法以 SMB/NFS 檔案共享方式掛載，就是 Volume Gateway 僅提供 iSCSI 區塊磁碟區（非 SMB/NFS）且沒有原生的跨 Region 複製功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon S3 is object storage accessed via REST APIs/HTTPS, not a file system that EC2 instances can mount as an SMB (Windows) or NFS (Linux) share. The applications require shared file storage with SMB and NFS protocols, which S3 does not provide, so S3 CRR does not meet the access requirement even though it can replicate cross-Region.","why_zh":"Amazon S3 是透過 REST API／HTTPS 存取的物件儲存，並非 EC2 可掛載為 SMB（Windows）或 NFS（Linux）共享的檔案系統。應用需要支援 SMB 與 NFS 協定的共享檔案儲存，S3 無法提供，因此即使 S3 CRR 能跨 Region 複製，也不符合存取需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon EBS is block storage attached to a single EC2 instance; it is not a shared file system and cannot be concurrently mounted by multiple Windows and Linux instances over SMB/NFS. Backing up and copying EBS snapshots to a DR Region via AWS Backup handles replication but fails the multiprotocol shared-storage requirement.","why_zh":"Amazon EBS 是掛載至單一 EC2 執行個體的區塊儲存，並非共享檔案系統，無法讓多台 Windows 與 Linux 執行個體透過 SMB/NFS 同時掛載。以 AWS Backup 將 EBS 快照備份並複製到 DR Region 雖能處理複製，卻無法滿足多協定共享儲存的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Storage Gateway Volume Gateway presents cloud-backed iSCSI block volumes, not SMB or NFS file shares (file shares are the File Gateway type), so it does not satisfy the multiprotocol file-access requirement. There is also no native 'Volume Gateway Cross-Region Replication' feature; DR for Volume Gateway is achieved by copying its EBS snapshots to another Region, making this option doubly incorrect.","why_zh":"AWS Storage Gateway Volume Gateway 提供以雲端為後盾的 iSCSI 區塊磁碟區，而非 SMB 或 NFS 檔案共享（檔案共享屬 File Gateway 類型），因此不符合多協定檔案存取需求。同時也不存在原生的「Volume Gateway 跨 Region 複製」功能；Volume Gateway 的 DR 是透過將其 EBS 快照複製到其他 Region 來達成，故此選項雙重錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/what-is-fsx-ontap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/scheduled-replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/how-it-works-fsx-ontap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/WhatIsStorageGateway.html"]},"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選"},{"id":267,"question_en":"A company's application uses a fleet of Amazon EC2 On-Demand Instances to analyze and process data. The EC2 instances are in an Auto Scaling group. The Auto Scaling group is a target group for an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The application analyzes critical data that cannot tolerate interruption. The application also analyzes noncritical data that can withstand interruption. The critical data analysis requires quick scalability in response to real-time application demand. The noncritical data analysis involves memory consumption. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution that reduces scale-out latency for the critical data. The solution also must process the noncritical data. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司的应用程序使用一组亚马逊 EC2 按需实例来分析和处理数据。这些 EC2 实例位于一个自动扩展组 中。该自动扩展组是应用负载均衡器（ALB）的目标组。该应用程序分析关键数据，这些数据不能容忍中 断。该应用程序还分析非关键数据，这些数据可以承受中断。 关键数据的分析需要能够快速扩展以响应实时应用需求。非关键数据的分析涉及内存消耗。开发运维工 程师必须实施一种解决方案，以降低关键数据的横向扩展延迟。该解决方案还必须处理非关键数据。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"For the critical data, modify the existing Auto Scaling group. Create a warm pool instance in the stopped state. Define the warm pool size. Create a new version of the launch template that has detailed monitoring enabled. Use Spot Instances.","B":"For the critical data, modify the existing Auto Scaling group. Create a warm pool instance in the stopped state. Define the warm pool size. Create a new version of the launch template that has detailed monitoring enabled. Use On-Demand Instances.","C":"For the critical data, modify the existing Auto Scaling group. Create a lifecycle hook to ensure that bootstrap scripts are completed successfully. Ensure that the application on the instances is ready to accept traffic before the instances are registered. Create a new version of the launch template that has detailed monitoring enabled.","D":"For the noncritical data, create a second Auto Scaling group that uses a launch template. Configure the launch template to install the unified Amazon CloudWatch agent and to configure the CloudWatch agent with a custom memory utilization metric. Use Spot Instances. Add the new Auto Scaling group as the target group for the ALB. Modify the application to use two target groups for critical data and noncritical data.","E":"For the noncritical data, create a second Auto Scaling group. Choose the predefined memory utilization metric type for the target tracking scaling policy. Use Spot Instances. Add the new Auto Scaling group as the target group for the ALB. Modify the application to use two target groups for critical data and noncritical data."},"options_zh":{"A":"对于关键数据，请修改现有的自动扩展组。创建处于停止状态的预热池实例。定义预热池大小。 创建启用详细监控的新版本启动模板。使用竞价型实例。","B":"对于关键数据，请修改现有的自动扩展组。创建处于停止状态的预热池实例。定义预热池的大小。 创建新的启动模板版本，该版本具有 详细监控已启用。使用按需实例。","C":"对于关键数据，请修改现有的自动扩展组。创建一个生命周期挂钩，以确保引导脚本成功完成。在 实例注册之前，请确保实例上的应用程序已准备好接受流量。创建一个新版本的启动模板，启用 详细监控。","D":"对于非关键数据，创建一个使用启动模板的第二个自动扩展组。配置启动模板以安装统一的 Amazon CloudWatch 代理，并使用自定义内存利用率指标配置 CloudWatch 代理。使用竞价型实例。 将新的自动扩展组添加为 ALB 的目标组。修改应用程序以针对关键数据和非关键数据使用两个目 标组。","E":"对于非关键数据，创建第二个自动扩展组。为目标跟踪扩展策略选择预定义的内存利用率指标类型。 使用竞价型实例。将新的自动扩展组添加为 ALB 的目标组。修改应用程序以使用两个目标组分别 处理关键数据和非关键数据。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The question has two independent requirements. (1) Critical data cannot tolerate interruption and needs reduced scale-out latency. A warm pool of pre-initialized instances kept in the Stopped state is purpose-built to 'decrease latency for applications with long boot times' by drawing on ready instances during a scale-out event, and the Stopped state minimizes cost. Because the data cannot be interrupted, the instances must be On-Demand; Spot Instances can be reclaimed at any time. AWS docs also explicitly state that warm pools do NOT support Spot Instances within mixed instance groups and that the mixed instances policy must be On-Demand only when using a warm pool. That makes option B correct and eliminates option A (which uses Spot). Option C uses a lifecycle hook, which puts launching instances into a wait state until bootstrap completes before they register and serve traffic; the docs describe lifecycle hooks as a source of additional delay, so this increases (not reduces) scale-out latency. (2) Noncritical data tolerates interruption (so Spot is appropriate and cost-effective) and must scale on memory consumption. EC2 Auto Scaling target tracking supports only four predefined metrics (ASGAverageCPUUtilization, ASGAverageNetworkIn, ASGAverageNetworkOut, ALBRequestCountPerTarget); there is no predefined memory metric. Memory must therefore be collected by the unified CloudWatch agent and supplied as a custom metric. That is option D; option E is wrong because no predefined memory utilization metric exists for EC2 Auto Scaling.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個獨立需求。(1) Critical data 不能中斷且需降低 scale-out 延遲。使用處於 Stopped 狀態的 warm pool 預先初始化執行個體，正是為了「decrease latency for applications with long boot times」，在 scale-out 事件時可直接取用就緒的執行個體，且 Stopped 狀態可將成本降到最低。由於資料不可中斷，執行個體必須使用 On-Demand；Spot Instances 隨時可能被回收。AWS 文件亦明確指出 warm pool 在 mixed instance group 中「不支援」Spot Instances，使用 warm pool 時 mixed instances policy 必須只用 On-Demand。因此選項 B 正確，並排除使用 Spot 的選項 A。選項 C 使用 lifecycle hook，會讓正在啟動的執行個體在註冊並接收流量前停留於 wait state 直到 bootstrap 完成；文件將 lifecycle hook 描述為「additional delays」的來源，因此會增加而非降低 scale-out 延遲。(2) Noncritical data 可容忍中斷（適合且符合成本效益地使用 Spot）且須依記憶體使用量擴展。EC2 Auto Scaling target tracking 只支援四個 predefined metric（ASGAverageCPUUtilization、ASGAverageNetworkIn、ASGAverageNetworkOut、ALBRequestCountPerTarget），並無記憶體 predefined metric。因此記憶體必須由 unified CloudWatch agent 收集並以 custom metric 提供，即選項 D；選項 E 錯誤，因為 EC2 Auto Scaling 並不存在 predefined memory utilization metric。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Critical data cannot tolerate interruption, but Spot Instances can be reclaimed by AWS at any time, breaking the requirement. AWS docs also state that warm pools do not support Spot Instances within mixed instance groups; the mixed instances policy must be On-Demand only.","why_zh":"Critical data 不可中斷，但 Spot Instances 隨時可能被 AWS 回收，違反需求。AWS 文件亦指出 warm pool 在 mixed instance group 中不支援 Spot Instances，mixed instances policy 必須只用 On-Demand。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A lifecycle hook holds launching instances in a wait state until bootstrap completes before registering them, which the docs describe as a source of additional delay. It does not pre-initialize a pool of ready instances, so it does not reduce scale-out latency the way a warm pool does.","why_zh":"Lifecycle hook 會讓正在啟動的執行個體在註冊前停留於 wait state 直到 bootstrap 完成，文件將其描述為「additional delays」的來源。它不會預先初始化一批就緒的執行個體，因此無法像 warm pool 那樣降低 scale-out 延遲。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"EC2 Auto Scaling target tracking has no predefined memory utilization metric; only ASGAverageCPUUtilization, ASGAverageNetworkIn, ASGAverageNetworkOut, and ALBRequestCountPerTarget are predefined. Memory must be supplied as a custom metric via the unified CloudWatch agent.","why_zh":"EC2 Auto Scaling target tracking 沒有 predefined memory utilization metric；只有 ASGAverageCPUUtilization、ASGAverageNetworkIn、ASGAverageNetworkOut 與 ALBRequestCountPerTarget 為 predefined。記憶體必須透過 unified CloudWatch agent 以 custom metric 提供。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-warm-pools.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-scaling-target-tracking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-scaling-cooldowns.html"]},"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選"},{"id":268,"question_en":"A company recently migrated its application to an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster that uses Amazon EC2 instances. The company configured the application to automatically scale based on CPU utilization. The application produces memory errors when it experiences heavy loads. The application also does not scale out enough to handle the increased load. The company needs to collect and analyze memory metrics for the application over time. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司最近将其应用程序迁移到了一个使用亚马逊 EC2 实例的亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务 （Amazon EKS）集群。该公司配置了应用程序，使其能够根据 CPU 利用率自动扩展。 该应用程序在负载过重时会出现内存错误。此外，该应用程序的横向扩展能力不足，无法应对不断 增加的负载。公司需要收集并分析该应用程序一段时间内的内存指标。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Attach the CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy managed IAM policy to the IAM instance profile that the cluster uses.","B":"Attach the CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy managed IAM policy to a service account role for the cluster.","C":"Collect performance metrics by deploying the unified Amazon CloudWatch agent to the existing EC2 instances in the cluster. Add the agent to the AMI for any new EC2 instances that are added to the cluster.","D":"Collect performance logs by deploying the AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry collector as a DaemonSet.","E":"Analyze the pod_memory_utilization Amazon CloudWatch metric in the ContainerInsights namespace by using the Service dimension.","F":"Analyze the node_memory_utilization Amazon CloudWatch metric in the ContainerInsights namespace by using the ClusterName dimension."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy 管理的 IAM 策略附加到集群使用的 IAM 实例配置文件上。","B":"将 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy 管理的 IAM 策略附加到集群的服务账户角色。","C":"通过在集群中的现有 EC2 实例上部署统一的 Amazon CloudWatch 代理来收集性能指标。对于添 加到集群中的任何新 EC2 实例，将代理添加到 AMI 中。","D":"通过将 AWS OpenTelemetry 分发版收集器部署为守护集来收集性能日志。","E":"使用“服务”维度在 ContainerInsights 命名空间中分析 pod_memory_utilization Amazon CloudWatch 指标。","F":"使用“ClusterName”维度在“ContainerInsights”命名空间中分析 Amazon CloudWatch 的“node_ memory_utilization”指标。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The scenario is EKS on EC2 with memory errors and insufficient CPU-based scale-out; the company needs to collect and analyze memory metrics over time, which means setting up Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights for EKS. Three steps are required: grant IAM permissions, deploy a metrics collector, and analyze the right memory metric. (A) Attaching the CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy managed policy to the worker-node IAM instance profile is the documented prerequisite that lets the collector send metrics/logs to CloudWatch; the prerequisites page explicitly lists this node-IAM-role method. (D) Deploying the AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry (ADOT) collector as a DaemonSet is the documented, correct mechanism to collect Container Insights performance metrics/logs from every EC2 node in an EKS cluster ('First, deploy the AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry collector as a DaemonSet'). (E) pod_memory_utilization is published in the ContainerInsights namespace and supports the Service, Namespace, ClusterName dimension set, so analyzing it by the Service dimension surfaces the application's actual per-pod/service memory consumption over time, which is what diagnoses the memory errors and the under-scaling. The decisive qualifier is that the question wants application memory metrics collected and analyzed, so the collector must run as a cluster DaemonSet (D) and the relevant metric is the application-level pod/service memory (E), not node-level. The dump answer [A,C,E] is wrong because C describes installing the agent directly on host EC2 instances and baking it into the AMI, which is the plain-EC2-host pattern, not the EKS Container Insights pattern where the agent/collector runs as an in-cluster DaemonSet.","explanation_zh":"情境為 EKS on EC2，出現記憶體錯誤且以 CPU 為基準的水平擴展不足；公司需要長期收集並分析記憶體指標，也就是要在 EKS 上設定 Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights。需要三個步驟：授予 IAM 權限、部署指標收集器、分析正確的記憶體指標。(A) 將 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy 受管政策附加到 worker node 的 IAM instance profile 是官方先決條件，讓收集器能把指標/日誌送到 CloudWatch；prerequisites 頁面明確列出此 node IAM role 方法。(D) 以 DaemonSet 方式部署 AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry (ADOT) collector 是官方文件記載、用以從 EKS 叢集每個 EC2 node 收集 Container Insights 效能指標/日誌的正確機制（『First, deploy the AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry collector as a DaemonSet』）。(E) pod_memory_utilization 發佈在 ContainerInsights namespace，且支援 Service、Namespace、ClusterName 維度組合，因此以 Service 維度分析可呈現應用程式實際的每個 pod/service 記憶體用量隨時間變化，正是診斷記憶體錯誤與擴展不足所需。關鍵限定詞是題目要收集並分析應用程式記憶體指標，所以收集器必須以叢集 DaemonSet 形式執行 (D)，且相關指標是應用程式層級的 pod/service 記憶體 (E)，而非 node 層級。dump 答案 [A,C,E] 不正確，因為 C 描述的是把 agent 直接安裝在主機 EC2 執行個體並烤進 AMI，那是純 EC2 主機的模式，而非 EKS Container Insights 中 agent/collector 以叢集內 DaemonSet 執行的模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Attaching CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy to a service-account (IRSA) role is a valid alternative IAM method, but it is an alternative to A, not a complementary step. With the ADOT DaemonSet running on EC2 nodes, the documented baseline is the node IAM role (A). Choosing both A and B is redundant, and the question needs three distinct, complementary steps.","why_zh":"將 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy 附加到 service account (IRSA) 角色是有效的替代 IAM 方法，但它是 A 的替代方案而非互補步驟。當 ADOT DaemonSet 在 EC2 node 上執行時，官方基準是 node IAM role (A)。同時選 A 與 B 會重複，而題目需要三個不同且互補的步驟。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Installing the unified CloudWatch agent directly onto the host EC2 instances and baking it into the AMI is the pattern for collecting plain EC2 host metrics. For EKS Container Insights, the CloudWatch agent (or ADOT collector) runs as an in-cluster DaemonSet, not on the host OS or in the AMI. This describes the wrong deployment mechanism for EKS.","why_zh":"把 unified CloudWatch agent 直接安裝在主機 EC2 執行個體並烤進 AMI，是收集純 EC2 主機指標的做法。對於 EKS Container Insights，CloudWatch agent（或 ADOT collector）是以叢集內 DaemonSet 執行，而非裝在主機作業系統或 AMI。這描述了 EKS 錯誤的部署機制。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"node_memory_utilization with the ClusterName dimension is a valid ContainerInsights metric, but it reports node/host-level memory, not the application's per-pod memory consumption. The application is what throws memory errors and fails to scale, so the application-level pod/service memory metric (E) is the more directly relevant choice for collecting and analyzing the application's memory over time.","why_zh":"node_memory_utilization 搭配 ClusterName 維度是有效的 ContainerInsights 指標，但它回報的是 node/主機層級記憶體，而非應用程式各 pod 的記憶體用量。出現記憶體錯誤且擴展失敗的是應用程式，因此應用程式層級的 pod/service 記憶體指標 (E) 才是收集與分析應用程式記憶體更直接相關的選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Container-Insights-prerequisites.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Container-Insights-EKS-otel.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Container-Insights-metrics-EKS.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/deploy-container-insights-EKS.html"]}},{"id":269,"question_en":"A company's video streaming platform usage has increased from 10,000 users each day to 50,000 users each day in multiple countries. The company deploys the streaming platform on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). The EKS workload scales up to thousands of nodes during peak viewing time. The company's users report occurrences of unauthorized logins. Users also report sudden interruptions and logouts from the platform. The company wants additional security measures for the entire platform. The company also needs a summarized view of the resource behaviors and interactions across the company's entire AWS environment. The summarized view must show login attempts, API calls, and network traffic. The solution must permit network traffic analysis while minimizing the overhead of managing logs. The solution must also quickly investigate any potential malicious behavior that is associated with the EKS workload. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的视频流媒体平台的日活跃用户数已从 10,000 人增加到在多个国家的 50,000 人。该公司将 流媒体平台部署在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）上。在观看高峰期，EKS 工作负载会 扩展到数千个节点。 该公司用户报告称出现了未经授权的登录情况。用户还报告称平台会突然中断连接并强制退出。 该公司希望为其整个平台采取更多的安全措施。此外，该公司还需要一个概览，以了解其整个 AWS 资源的行为和交互情况。 环境。汇总视图必须显示登录尝试、 API 调用和网络流量。该解决方案必须允许进行网络流量分析，同 时尽量减少管理日志的开销。该解决方案还必须能够快速调查与 EKS 工作负载相关的任何潜在恶意行 为。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty for EKS Audit Log Monitoring. Enable AWS CloudTrail logs. Store the EKS audit logs and CloudTrail log files in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to create an external table. Use Amazon QuickSight to create a dashboard.","B":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty for EKS Audit Log Monitoring. Enable Amazon Detective in the company's AWS account. Enable EKS audit logs from optional source packages in Detective.","C":"Enable Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights. Enable AWS CloudTrail logs. Store the EKS audit logs and CloudTrail log files in an Amazon S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to create an external table. Use Amazon QuickSight to create a dashboard.","D":"Enable Amazon GuardDuty for EKS Audit Log Monitoring. Enable Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights and VPC Flow Logs. Enable AWS CloudTrail logs."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 以对 EKS 审计日志进行监控。启用 AWS CloudTrail 日志。将 EKS 审计日志 和 CloudTrail 日志文件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon Athena 创建外部表。使用 Amazon QuickSight 创建仪表板。","B":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 对 EKS 审计日志进行监控。在公司的 AWS 账户中启用 Amazon Detective。 在 Detective 中启用来自可选源包的 EKS 审计日志。","C":"启用 Amazon CloudWatch 容器洞察功能。启用 AWS CloudTrail 日志。将 EKS 审计日志和 CloudTrail 日志文件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon Athena 创建外部表。使用 Amazon QuickSight 创 建仪表板。","D":"启用 Amazon GuardDuty 对 EKS 审计日志进行监控。启用 Amazon CloudWatch 容器洞察和 VPC 流日志。启用 AWS CloudTrail 日志。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The four requirements are: (1) extra security for the EKS platform against unauthorized logins, (2) a summarized, correlated view across the entire AWS environment covering login attempts, API calls, and network traffic, (3) network-traffic analysis with minimal log-management overhead, and (4) fast investigation of malicious behavior tied to the EKS workload. Amazon GuardDuty EKS Audit Log Monitoring (EKS Protection / Kubernetes Protection) supplies the added security: AWS docs state it uses EKS audit logs via its own independent stream with no additional configuration to detect unauthenticated/anonymous access, credential theft, and anomalous user and application activity in EKS clusters. Amazon Detective's core package automatically ingests AWS CloudTrail (login attempts + API calls), VPC Flow Logs (network traffic), and GuardDuty findings, and per the Detective docs it correlates user activities with CloudTrail Management events and network activity with VPC Flow Logs 'without the need for you to enable or store these logs manually' - directly delivering the summarized correlated view, the network-traffic analysis, and the minimized log-management overhead. Enabling the optional EKS audit logs source package enriches the behavior graph for EKS clusters, Kubernetes pods, container images, and Kubernetes subjects, and surfaces GuardDuty Kubernetes findings for fast, graph-based root-cause investigation of the EKS workload. B is the only option that satisfies all four needs as fully managed services without building an S3/Athena/QuickSight pipeline.","explanation_zh":"四項需求為：(1) 針對未授權登入為 EKS 平台提供額外安全防護；(2) 涵蓋登入嘗試、API 呼叫與網路流量、跨整個 AWS 環境的彙總且關聯的檢視；(3) 在最小化日誌管理負擔下進行網路流量分析；(4) 快速調查與 EKS 工作負載相關的惡意行為。Amazon GuardDuty EKS Audit Log Monitoring（EKS Protection / Kubernetes Protection）提供額外安全防護：AWS 文件指出它透過自身獨立的串流使用 EKS audit logs（無需額外設定）來偵測未驗證/匿名存取、憑證竊取，以及 EKS 叢集中使用者與應用程式的異常活動。Amazon Detective 的核心套件會自動擷取 AWS CloudTrail（登入嘗試與 API 呼叫）、VPC Flow Logs（網路流量）與 GuardDuty findings，且依 Detective 文件所述，它會將使用者活動與 CloudTrail Management events、將網路活動與 VPC Flow Logs 關聯，「無需您手動啟用或儲存這些日誌」，因而直接滿足彙總關聯檢視、網路流量分析與最小化日誌管理負擔。啟用選用的 EKS audit logs source package 可為 behavior graph 增添 EKS Cluster、Kubernetes Pod、Container Image 與 Kubernetes subject 的深入資訊，並顯示 GuardDuty Kubernetes findings，以利對 EKS 工作負載進行快速、以圖譜為基礎的根因調查。B 是唯一以全託管服務同時滿足四項需求、且無需建置 S3/Athena/QuickSight 管線的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"GuardDuty EKS gives the security layer, but storing EKS audit logs and CloudTrail in S3 and building an Athena external table plus a QuickSight dashboard is a manual analytics pipeline you must build, store, and maintain - the opposite of 'minimizing the overhead of managing logs.' It also includes no VPC Flow Logs, so it cannot perform the required network-traffic analysis, and a static dashboard is not an automated, correlated investigation tool for EKS malicious behavior.","why_zh":"GuardDuty EKS 提供了安全層，但將 EKS audit logs 與 CloudTrail 儲存到 S3、建立 Athena 外部表並做 QuickSight 儀表板，是需要自行建置、儲存與維護的手動分析管線，與「最小化日誌管理負擔」相反。它也未包含 VPC Flow Logs，無法滿足網路流量分析需求，且靜態儀表板並非自動化、關聯式的 EKS 惡意行為調查工具。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch Container Insights is a performance/observability tool that collects container metrics and logs - it does not detect unauthorized logins or provide a security threat layer, so it fails the 'additional security' requirement. The S3/Athena/QuickSight pipeline again maximizes log-management overhead, and there is no GuardDuty and no correlated security investigation capability.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Container Insights 是效能/可觀測性工具，收集容器指標與日誌，無法偵測未授權登入，也不提供安全威脅層，因而無法滿足「額外安全防護」需求。S3/Athena/QuickSight 管線同樣會增加日誌管理負擔，且沒有 GuardDuty，也沒有關聯式的安全調查能力。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This adds GuardDuty EKS plus Container Insights, VPC Flow Logs, and CloudTrail, but omits Amazon Detective, so there is no summarized, correlated cross-account behavior graph and no fast graph-based root-cause investigation. Enabling raw VPC Flow Logs and CloudTrail yourself increases log-management overhead, and Container Insights is performance-oriented rather than the summarized security view of login attempts, API calls, and network traffic that the question requires.","why_zh":"此選項加入 GuardDuty EKS 以及 Container Insights、VPC Flow Logs 與 CloudTrail，但缺少 Amazon Detective，因此沒有彙總、關聯的跨帳戶 behavior graph，也沒有快速的圖譜式根因調查。自行啟用原始 VPC Flow Logs 與 CloudTrail 反而增加日誌管理負擔，而 Container Insights 偏向效能監控，並非題目所要求之登入嘗試、API 呼叫與網路流量的彙總安全檢視。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/detective-source-data-about.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/detective/latest/userguide/source-data-types-EKS.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/integration-detective.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/guardduty/latest/ug/kubernetes-protection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContainerInsights.html"]}},{"id":270,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage hundreds of AWS accounts. The company has a team that is responsible for AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM). The IAM team wants to implement AWS IAM Identity Center (AWS Single Sign-On). The IAM team must have only the minimum needed permissions to manage IAM Identity Center. The IAM team must not be able to gain unneeded access to the Organizations management account. The IAM team must be able to provision new IAM Identity Center permission sets and assignments for existing and new member accounts. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织来管理数百个 AWS 账户。该公司有一个团队负责 AWS 身份和访问管理 （IAM）。 IAM 团队希望实施 AWS IAM 身份中心（AWS 单点登录）。IAM 团队必须仅拥有管理 IAM 身份中心 所需的最低权限。IAM 团队不得能够获得对组织管理账户的不必要的访问权限。IAM 团队必须能够为 现有和新成员账户配置新的 IAM 身份中心权限集和分配。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS account for the IAM team. In the new account, enable IAM Identity Center. In the Organizations management account, register the new account as a delegated administrator for IAM Identity Center.","B":"Create a new AWS account for the IAM team. In the Organizations management account, enable IAM Identity Center. In the Organizations management account, register the new account as a delegated administrator for IAM Identity Center.","C":"In IAM Identity Center, create users and a group for the IAM team. Add the users to the group. Create a new permission set. Attach the AWSSSODirectoryAdministrator managed IAM policy to the group.","D":"In IAM Identity Center, create users and a group for the IAM team. Add the users to the group. Create a new permission set. Attach the AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator managed IAM policy to the group.","E":"Assign the permission set to the Organizations management account. Allow the IAM team group to use the permission set.","F":"Assign the permission set to the new AWS account. Allow the IAM team group to use the permission set."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 IAM 团队创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在新账户中启用 IAM 身份中心。在组织管理账户中，将新 账户注册为 IAM 身份中心的委托管理员。","B":"为 IAM 团队创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在组织管理账户中，启用 IAM 身份中心。在组织管理账户中， 将新账户注册为 IAM 身份中心的委托管理员。","C":"在 IAM 身份中心，为 IAM 团队创建用户和一个组。将用户添加到该组。创建一个新的权限集。将 AWSSSODirectoryAdministrator 管理的 IAM 策略附加到该组。","D":"在 IAM 身份中心，为 IAM 团队创建用户和一个组。将用户添加到该组。创建一个新的权限集。将 AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator 管理的 IAM 策略附加到该组。","E":"将权限集分配给组织管理账户。允许 IAM 团队组使用该权限集。","F":"将权限集分配给新的 AWS 账户。允许 IAM 团队组使用该权限集。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["B","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"An IAM Identity Center instance must always reside in the AWS Organizations management account; it cannot be enabled in a member or new account. AWS docs state that when you enable IAM Identity Center the instance is created in the management account by default and 'must always reside in the management account,' and the register-delegated-administrator doc explicitly lists 'Enabling IAM Identity Center' as a task the delegated administrator account cannot perform. This makes option A impossible and option B correct: enable IAM Identity Center in the management account, then register the new account as the delegated administrator (RegisterDelegatedAdministrator requires management-account credentials). For permissions, the AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator managed policy grants sso:* plus Organizations read actions, which lets the team provision new permission sets and account assignments for existing and new member accounts (option D). The AWSSSODirectoryAdministrator policy only grants sso-directory:*, identitystore:*, identitystore-auth:*, and sso:ListDirectoryAssociations, none of which can create permission sets or assignments, so option C is wrong. To satisfy least privilege and avoid unneeded management-account access, the permission set must be assigned to the new delegated-administrator account (option F), not the management account (option E, which would grant the very access the requirement forbids). The dump answer (A, D, F) is wrong because step A cannot be done; the correct combination is B, D, F.","explanation_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的 instance 必須永遠位於 AWS Organizations 的 management account，無法在成員帳戶或新帳戶中啟用。AWS 文件指出，啟用 IAM Identity Center 時 instance 預設建立於 management account，且「必須永遠位於 management account」；註冊 delegated administrator 的文件更明確將「Enabling IAM Identity Center」列為 delegated administrator 帳戶無法執行的工作。因此選項 A 不可行，而選項 B 正確：在 management account 中啟用 IAM Identity Center，再將新帳戶註冊為 delegated administrator（RegisterDelegatedAdministrator 需要 management account 憑證）。在權限方面，AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator 受管政策授予 sso:* 及 Organizations 讀取動作，可讓團隊為現有與新成員帳戶佈建新的 permission sets 與 account assignments（選項 D）。AWSSSODirectoryAdministrator 政策僅授予 sso-directory:*、identitystore:*、identitystore-auth:* 與 sso:ListDirectoryAssociations，皆無法建立 permission sets 或 assignments，故選項 C 錯誤。為符合最小權限並避免不必要的 management account 存取，permission set 必須指派給新的 delegated administrator 帳戶（選項 F），而非 management account（選項 E 反而會授予需求所禁止的存取）。題庫答案（A、D、F）錯誤，因為步驟 A 無法執行；正確組合為 B、D、F。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"IAM Identity Center cannot be enabled in a new/member account. AWS docs state the instance must always reside in the management account, and 'Enabling IAM Identity Center' is explicitly listed as a task the delegated administrator account cannot perform. This step is technically impossible; option B describes the correct flow.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 無法在新帳戶或成員帳戶中啟用。AWS 文件指出 instance 必須永遠位於 management account，且「Enabling IAM Identity Center」明確被列為 delegated administrator 帳戶無法執行的工作，因此此步驟技術上不可行；選項 B 才是正確流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWSSSODirectoryAdministrator grants only sso-directory:*, identitystore:*, identitystore-auth:*, and sso:ListDirectoryAssociations. It manages the identity store/directory but cannot create permission sets (sso:CreatePermissionSet) or account assignments (sso:CreateAccountAssignment), so it fails the requirement to provision permission sets and assignments.","why_zh":"AWSSSODirectoryAdministrator 僅授予 sso-directory:*、identitystore:*、identitystore-auth:* 與 sso:ListDirectoryAssociations。它管理 identity store/directory，但無法建立 permission sets（sso:CreatePermissionSet）或 account assignments（sso:CreateAccountAssignment），不符合佈建 permission sets 與 assignments 的需求。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Assigning the permission set to the Organizations management account grants the IAM team access to the management account, directly violating the requirement that they must not gain unneeded access to it. AWS best practice is to restrict management-account access to as few people as possible via delegated administration; the permission set should instead be assigned to the new delegated-administrator account (option F).","why_zh":"將 permission set 指派給 Organizations management account 會讓 IAM 團隊取得 management account 的存取權，直接違反「不得取得不必要的 management account 存取」的需求。AWS 最佳實務是透過 delegated administration 將 management account 存取限制給盡量少的人；permission set 應改指派給新的 delegated administrator 帳戶（選項 F）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/delegated-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/delegated-admin-how-to-register.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AWSSSODirectoryAdministrator.html"]}},{"id":271,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations that has all features enabled. The company uses AWS Backup in a primary account and uses an AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) key to encrypt the backups. The company needs to automate a cross-account backup of the resources that AWS Backup backs up in the primary account. The company configures cross-account backup in the Organizations management account. The company creates a new AWS account in the organization and configures an AWS Backup backup vault in the new account. The company creates a KMS key in the new account to encrypt the backups. Finally, the company configures a new backup plan in the primary account. The destination for the new backup plan is the backup vault in the new account. When the AWS Backup job in the primary account is invoked, the job creates backups in the primary account. However, the backups are not copied to the new account's backup vault. Which combination of steps must the company take so that backups can be copied to the new account's backup vault? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用了 AWS 组织中的一个组织单元，该组织单元启用了所有功能。该公司在一个主账户中使 用 AWS 备份服务，并使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）密钥对备份进行加密。 该公司需要对 AWS Backup 在主账户中备份的资源实现跨账户备份。该公司在组织管理账户中配置跨 账户备份。该公司在组织中创建了一个新的 AWS 账户，并在新账户中配置了一个 AWS Backup 备份 存储库。该公司在新账户中创建了一个 KMS 密钥来加密备份。最后，该公司在主账户中配置了一个新 的备份计划。新备份计划的目标是新账户中的备份存储库。 当主账户中的 AWS 备份作业被调用时，该作业会在主账户中创建备份。然而，这些备份不会被复 制到新账户的备份库中。 公司必须采取哪两种步骤组合才能将备份复制到新账户的备份库中？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Edit the backup vault access policy in the new account to allow access to the primary account.","B":"Edit the backup vault access policy in the primary account to allow access to the new account.","C":"Edit the backup vault access policy in the primary account to allow access to the KMS key in the new account.","D":"Edit the key policy of the KMS key in the primary account to share the key with the new account.","E":"Edit the key policy of the KMS key in the new account to share the key with the primary account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在新账户中编辑备份库访问策略，以允许访问主账户。","B":"在主账户中编辑备份库访问策略，以允许新账户访问。","C":"在主账户中编辑备份库访问策略，以允许访问新账户中的 KMS 密钥。","D":"在主账户中编辑 KMS 密钥的关键策略，以与新账户共享该密钥。","E":"在新账户中编辑 KMS 密钥的关键策略，以与主账户共享该密钥。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Backup cross-account copy has two distinct gates that must both be opened. First, the destination (new account) backup vault needs a resource-based access policy that allows the source (primary) account to write into it: the docs state 'You must Allow the access policy backup:CopyIntoBackupVault for your destination backup vault. The absence of this policy will deny attempts to copy into the destination account,' and the example policy grants the source account principal (arn:aws:iam::<primary>:root) that action. That is option A. Second, because the recovery points in the primary account are encrypted with a customer managed KMS key in the primary account, AWS Backup must be able to decrypt the source recovery point before it re-encrypts the copy with the destination vault's key. The docs state plainly: 'In the source account, if your resources are encrypted with a customer managed key, you must share this customer managed key with the destination account.' Sharing is done by editing the key policy of that source (primary-account) KMS key to grant the new account, which is option D. AWS Backup then re-encrypts the copy with the destination vault key, so the new account's key does not need to be shared back to the primary.","explanation_zh":"AWS Backup 的跨帳戶複製有兩道必須同時打開的關卡。第一,目的端(新帳戶)的 backup vault 需要一個 resource-based access policy,允許來源端(primary 帳戶)寫入:官方文件明確指出 'You must Allow the access policy backup:CopyIntoBackupVault for your destination backup vault. The absence of this policy will deny attempts to copy into the destination account',範例政策即是把該動作授予來源帳戶的 principal(arn:aws:iam::<primary>:root)。這就是選項 A。第二,因為 primary 帳戶中的 recovery point 是用 primary 帳戶裡的 customer managed KMS key 加密的,AWS Backup 必須先能解密來源 recovery point,才能用目的端 vault 的金鑰重新加密複本。文件明確說:'In the source account, if your resources are encrypted with a customer managed key, you must share this customer managed key with the destination account.' 分享方式就是編輯該來源(primary 帳戶)KMS key 的 key policy 以授權新帳戶,也就是選項 D。AWS Backup 之後會用目的端 vault 的金鑰重新加密複本,因此新帳戶的金鑰不需要反向分享給 primary。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The access policy that must be edited is on the DESTINATION vault (new account) to allow the source account in, not on the primary (source) vault. Editing the source vault to allow the new account does not authorize the cross-account write into the destination vault.","why_zh":"需要編輯的 access policy 是在目的端 vault(新帳戶)上,允許來源帳戶寫入,而不是在 primary(來源)vault 上。編輯來源 vault 去允許新帳戶,並不能授權寫入目的端 vault 的跨帳戶複製。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A backup vault access policy controls backup: API actions for IAM principals (accounts), not access to a KMS key; granting 'access to the KMS key' through a vault policy is not how KMS sharing works. KMS access is controlled by the KMS key policy, handled in option D. Also the policy change belongs on the destination vault, not the primary vault.","why_zh":"backup vault 的 access policy 控制的是針對 IAM principal(帳戶)的 backup: API 動作,而非對 KMS key 的存取;透過 vault policy 去授予『對 KMS key 的存取』並不是 KMS 分享的運作方式。KMS 存取由 KMS key policy 控制,屬於選項 D。而且政策變更應在目的端 vault,而非 primary vault。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Direction is reversed. The new account's key encrypts the destination copy, which AWS Backup handles within the destination; what must be shared is the SOURCE (primary-account) CMK so AWS Backup can decrypt the original recovery point. The docs require sharing the source key with the destination, not the destination key with the source.","why_zh":"方向相反。新帳戶的金鑰用於加密目的端複本,這由 AWS Backup 在目的端處理;真正需要分享的是來源(primary 帳戶)的 CMK,讓 AWS Backup 能解密原始 recovery point。文件要求把來源金鑰分享給目的端,而非把目的端金鑰分享給來源。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/create-cross-account-backup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/encryption.html"]}},{"id":272,"question_en":"A company runs an application that uses an Amazon S3 bucket to store images. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a multi-Region strategy for the objects that are stored in the S3 bucket. The company needs to be able to fail over to an S3 bucket in another AWS Region. When an image is added to either S3 bucket, the image must be replicated to the other S3 bucket within 15 minutes. The DevOps engineer enables two-way replication between the S3 buckets. Which combination of steps should the DevOps engineer take next to meet the requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司运行的应用程序使用 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储图像。一位 DevOps 工程师需要为存储在 S3 存储 桶中的对象实施多区域策略。该公司需要能够故障转移到另一个 AWS 区域的 S3 存储桶。当图像被添加 到任一 S3 存储桶时，必须在 15 分钟内将该图像复制到另一个 S3 存储桶。 DevOps 工程师在两个 S3 存储桶之间实现了双向复制。 为了满足要求，DevOps 工程师接下来应采取哪三种步骤的组合？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable S3 Replication Time Control (S3 RTC) on each replication rule.","B":"Create an S3 Multi-Region Access Point in an active-passive configuration.","C":"Call the SubmitMultiRegionAccessPointRoutes operation in the AWS API when the company needs to fail over to the S3 bucket in the other Region.","D":"Enable S3 Transfer Acceleration on both S3 buckets.","E":"Configure a routing control in Amazon Route 53 Recovery Controller. Add the S3 buckets in an active- passive configuration.","F":"Call the UpdateRoutingControlStates operation in the AWS API when the company needs to fail over to the S3 bucket in the other Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个复制规则上启用 S3 复制时间控制（S3 RTC）。","B":"创建一个处于主备配置的 S3 多区域访问点。","C":"当公司需要故障转移到另一个区域的 S3 存储桶时，请调用 AWS API 中的 SubmitMultiRegionAccessP ointRoutes 操作。","D":"在两个 S3 存储桶上启用 S3 传输加速功能。","E":"在 Amazon Route 53 恢复控制器中配置路由控制。以主备配置添加 S3 存储桶。","F":"当公司需要故障转移到另一个区域的 S3 存储桶时，在 AWS API 中调用 UpdateRoutingControlStates 操 作。"},"answer":["A","B","C"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B","C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two-way replication is already enabled, so the remaining three steps are A, B, and C. (A) Enable S3 Replication Time Control (S3 RTC) on each replication rule: S3 RTC is the only S3 feature with a defined replication SLA, replicating 99.9% of objects within 15 minutes, which exactly matches the requirement; it must be set per rule, so both directions of the two-way replication are covered. (B) Front the buckets with an S3 Multi-Region Access Point in an active-passive configuration: AWS docs state that to use S3 failover controls in a disaster, you set up the MRAP in active-passive so the passive Region receives no traffic until failover. (C) Initiate failover with the SubmitMultiRegionAccessPointRoutes (S3 Control) API, which updates a Region's routing status between active (100) and passive (0); the AWS doc example for this operation is literally titled 'Sample request for initiating failover'. The decisive distinction is that S3 MRAP failover uses SubmitMultiRegionAccessPointRoutes, not Route 53 Application Recovery Controller. Options E and F describe Route 53 ARC routing controls and UpdateRoutingControlStates, a different failover mechanism not used by S3 MRAPs, and D (Transfer Acceleration) only speeds uploads via edge locations and does nothing for replication latency or failover.","explanation_zh":"two-way replication 已啟用，因此剩下的三個步驟為 A、B、C。(A) 在每條 replication rule 上啟用 S3 Replication Time Control (S3 RTC)：S3 RTC 是唯一具備明確 replication SLA 的 S3 功能，可在 15 分鐘內複寫 99.9% 的物件，正好符合題目要求；且必須逐條 rule 設定，因此涵蓋 two-way replication 的雙向。(B) 以 active-passive 配置建立 S3 Multi-Region Access Point 作為 buckets 前端：AWS 文件指出，若要在災難時使用 S3 failover controls，應將 MRAP 設為 active-passive，使 passive Region 在容錯移轉前不接收流量。(C) 以 SubmitMultiRegionAccessPointRoutes (S3 Control) API 觸發 failover，將某 Region 的 routing status 在 active (100) 與 passive (0) 之間切換；AWS 文件此操作的範例標題即為 'Sample request for initiating failover'。關鍵區別在於 S3 MRAP failover 使用 SubmitMultiRegionAccessPointRoutes，而非 Route 53 Application Recovery Controller。選項 E 與 F 描述的是 Route 53 ARC routing controls 與 UpdateRoutingControlStates，屬於 S3 MRAP 不使用的另一種容錯機制；D (Transfer Acceleration) 僅透過邊緣節點加速上傳，對 replication 延遲或 failover 毫無作用。","distractors":[{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Transfer Acceleration only accelerates client uploads/downloads by routing through CloudFront edge locations. It does not affect cross-Region replication latency and provides no failover capability, so it cannot help meet the 15-minute replication or Region failover requirement.","why_zh":"S3 Transfer Acceleration 僅透過 CloudFront 邊緣節點加速用戶端上傳/下載，不影響跨 Region replication 延遲，也不提供 failover 能力，因此無法滿足 15 分鐘複寫或 Region failover 需求。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller routing controls are a separate failover mechanism. S3 Multi-Region Access Points have their own native failover via routing states (active-passive per option B), and do not use Route 53 ARC routing controls over the buckets.","why_zh":"Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller 的 routing controls 是另一套容錯機制。S3 Multi-Region Access Points 透過自身的 routing states (active-passive，即選項 B) 提供原生 failover，並不對 buckets 使用 Route 53 ARC routing controls。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"UpdateRoutingControlStates is the Route 53 Application Recovery Controller API for flipping ARC routing controls, not the S3 failover API. S3 MRAP failover is initiated with SubmitMultiRegionAccessPointRoutes (C), so F is the wrong-service pairing for this MRAP-based design.","why_zh":"UpdateRoutingControlStates 是 Route 53 Application Recovery Controller 用來切換 ARC routing controls 的 API，而非 S3 failover API。S3 MRAP failover 是以 SubmitMultiRegionAccessPointRoutes (C) 啟動，因此 F 在此 MRAP 設計中屬於錯誤的服務搭配。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-time-control.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/FailoverConfiguration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/MultiRegionAccessPointRequestRouting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/API/API_control_SubmitMultiRegionAccessPointRoutes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/MultiRegionAccessPoints.html"]}},{"id":273,"question_en":"A company uses the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) to define its application. The company uses a pipeline that consists of AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild to deploy the CDK application. The company wants to introduce unit tests to the pipeline to test various infrastructure components. The company wants to ensure that a deployment proceeds if no unit tests result in a failure. Which combination of steps will enforce the testing requirement in the pipeline? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS 云开发工具包（AWS CDK）来定义其应用程序。该公司使用由 AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 组成的管道来部署 CDK 应用程序。 该公司希望在流水线中引入单元测试来测试各种基础设施组件。该公司希望确保在没有单元测试失败 的情况下进行部署。 在管道中，哪两种步骤组合可以强制执行测试要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Update the CodeBuild build phase commands to run the tests then to deploy the application. Set the OnFailure phase property to ABORT.","B":"Update the CodeBuild build phase commands to run the tests then to deploy the application. Add the -- rollback true flag to the cdk deploy command.","C":"Update the CodeBuild build phase commands to run the tests then to deploy the application. Add the -- require-approval any-change flag to the cdk deploy command.","D":"Create a test that uses the AWS CDK assertions module. Use the template.hasResourceProperties assertion to test that resources have the expected properties.","E":"Create a test that uses the cdk diff command. Configure the test to fail if any resources have changed."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 CodeBuild 构建阶段的命令，使其先运行测试，然后部署应用程序。将 OnFailure 阶段属性设置为 ABORT。","B":"更新 CodeBuild 构建阶段的命令，使其先运行测试，然后部署应用程序。在 cdk deploy 命令中添加 -- rollback true 标志。","C":"更新 CodeBuild 构建阶段的命令，使其先运行测试，然后部署应用程序。在 cdk deploy 命令中添加 -- require-approval any-change 标志。","D":"创建一个使用 AWS CDK 断言模块的测试。使用 template.hasResourceProperties 断言来测试资源是否 具有预期的属性。","E":"创建一个使用 `cdk diff` 命令的测试。将测试配置为在任何资源发生变化时失败。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to run infrastructure unit tests in the pipeline and let the deployment proceed only when no test fails. Option D is the canonical way to create CDK unit tests: the AWS CDK assertions module provides fine-grained assertions such as Template.hasResourceProperties to verify that synthesized CloudFormation resources have the expected properties; these tests run under Jest (TypeScript/JavaScript) or Pytest (Python) and exit with a non-zero code when an assertion fails. Option A enforces those tests as a deployment gate inside CodeBuild: the build phase runs the tests first, then deploys, and the documented buildspec phase property on-failure: ABORT aborts the build if the phase fails. Per the CodeBuild buildspec reference, CodeBuild runs commands one at a time and 'If any command in a phase fails, the phase fails,' so a failing test aborts the build and the subsequent cdk deploy never runs; if every test passes, the deployment proceeds. Together, D creates the tests and A enforces them, which exactly satisfies the requirement.","explanation_zh":"需求是在 pipeline 中執行基礎設施單元測試，且只有當沒有任何測試失敗時才繼續部署。選項 D 是建立 CDK 單元測試的標準做法：AWS CDK assertions 模組提供細粒度斷言，例如 Template.hasResourceProperties，用來驗證合成後的 CloudFormation 資源是否具有預期屬性；這些測試在 Jest（TypeScript/JavaScript）或 Pytest（Python）下執行，斷言失敗時會以非零代碼結束。選項 A 在 CodeBuild 中把這些測試設為部署閘門：build phase 先執行測試再部署，而文件中記載的 buildspec phase 屬性 on-failure: ABORT 會在該 phase 失敗時中止 build。根據 CodeBuild buildspec 參考文件，CodeBuild 會逐一執行命令，且「如果 phase 中任一命令失敗，該 phase 即失敗」，因此測試失敗會中止 build，後續的 cdk deploy 永遠不會執行；若所有測試通過，部署即可繼續。D 負責建立測試、A 負責強制執行，兩者結合正好滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The --rollback flag controls whether CloudFormation rolls a stack back when a deployment itself fails; it has nothing to do with running or enforcing unit tests. Adding it does not create a test gate, so failing tests would never block the deployment.","why_zh":"--rollback 旗標控制的是當部署本身失敗時 CloudFormation 是否回滾堆疊，與執行或強制單元測試無關。加上它並不會建立測試閘門，測試失敗也就無法阻擋部署。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"--require-approval any-change triggers an interactive manual approval prompt for security-relevant changes (IAM/security groups). It is a human approval gate, not a unit-test gate, and in an automated CodeBuild pipeline it would block or hang the deploy rather than enforce test results.","why_zh":"--require-approval any-change 會針對安全相關變更（IAM/安全群組）觸發互動式手動核准提示。它是人工核准閘門，而非單元測試閘門，在自動化的 CodeBuild pipeline 中只會阻擋或卡住部署，並不能根據測試結果來強制執行。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"cdk diff compares the synthesized stack to the currently deployed stack and reports differences. Any legitimate code change produces a diff, so failing the build whenever resources changed would block every normal deployment. It is not a unit test of resource correctness and does not satisfy 'proceed if no unit tests fail.'","why_zh":"cdk diff 是把合成後的堆疊與目前已部署的堆疊比較並回報差異。任何正當的程式碼變更都會產生差異，因此只要資源有變更就讓 build 失敗，將會阻擋每一次正常部署。它並非驗證資源正確性的單元測試，也無法滿足「沒有任何單元測試失敗才繼續」的要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/v2/guide/testing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/api/v2/docs/aws-cdk-lib.assertions-readme.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/view-build-details-phases.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/v2/guide/ref-cli-cmd-deploy.html"]}},{"id":274,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The EC2 instances are in multiple Availability Zones. The application was misconfigured in a single Availability Zone, which caused a partial outage of the application. A DevOps engineer made changes to ensure that the unhealthy EC2 instances in one Availability Zone do not affect the healthy EC2 instances in the other Availability Zones. The DevOps engineer needs to test the application's failover and shift where the ALB sends traffic. During failover, the ALB must avoid sending traffic to the Availability Zone where the failure has occurred. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的应用程序在多个可用区的亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行，并由应用负载均衡器（ALB）提供支持。由 于单个可用区中的应用程序配置错误，导致该应用程序出现部分中断。 一位 DevOps 工程师进行了更改，以确保一个可用区中不健康的 EC2 实例不会影响其他可用区中的健康 EC2 实例。该 DevOps 工程师需要测试应用程序的故障转移，并改变 ALB 发送流量的位置。在故障转移期间， ALB 必须避免将流量发送到发生故障的可用区。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Turn off cross-zone load balancing on the ALB. Use Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller to start a zonal shift away from the Availability Zone.","B":"Turn off cross-zone load balancing on the ALB’s target group. Use Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller to start a zonal shift away from the Availability Zone.","C":"Create an Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller resource set that uses the DNS hostname of the ALB. Start a zonal shift for the resource set away from the Availability Zone.","D":"Create an Amazon Route 53 Application Recovery Controller resource set that uses the ARN of the ALB’s target group. Create a readiness check that uses the ElbV2TargetGroupsCanServeTraffic rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"关闭应用负载均衡器（ALB）上的跨区负载均衡。使用亚马逊 Route 53 应用程序恢复控制器启动从该可 用区的区域迁移。","B":"关闭应用负载均衡器（ALB）目标组的跨区域负载均衡。使用 Amazon Route 53 应用程序恢复控制 器开始将流量从该可用区转移出去。","C":"创建一个使用 ALB 的 DNS 主机名的 Amazon Route 53 应用程序恢复控制器资源集。启动该资 源集从可用区的区域切换。","D":"创建一个使用 ALB 目标组的 ARN 的 Amazon Route 53 应用程序恢复控制器资源集。创建一个使用 ElbV2TargetGroupsCanServeTraffic 规则的就绪检查。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: (1) keep unhealthy instances in one AZ from affecting healthy instances in other AZs, and (2) test failover by shifting where the ALB sends traffic so it avoids the failed AZ. For an Application Load Balancer, cross-zone load balancing is a TARGET GROUP attribute (Target Groups -> Attributes -> Cross-zone load balancing), not a load-balancer-level toggle. Turning it off at the target group fault-isolates each AZ so a zonal failure stays contained, satisfying part 1. The traffic-shifting primitive is Amazon Application Recovery Controller (ARC) zonal shift: when you start a zonal shift on the ALB away from an AZ, the ALB marks that zone's targets as administratively overridden (AdministrativeOverride = zonal_shift_active), stops routing new traffic to them, and removes the zonal IP from DNS. AWS explicitly lists 'test application integrity by simulating and identifying failures' as a zonal-shift benefit, which matches the failover-test requirement. Option B correctly places the cross-zone setting on the target group and uses ARC zonal shift, so it is the right answer. Option A names the same mechanism but turns off cross-zone 'on the ALB,' which is the wrong location for an ALB.","explanation_zh":"需求分為兩部分:(1) 讓某個 AZ 中不健康的執行個體不影響其他 AZ 中健康的執行個體;(2) 透過改變 ALB 送出流量的位置來測試容錯移轉,使其避開故障的 AZ。對 Application Load Balancer 而言,cross-zone load balancing 是 TARGET GROUP(目標群組)屬性(Target Groups -> Attributes -> Cross-zone load balancing),並非 load balancer 層級的開關。在目標群組層級關閉它可達成 AZ 故障隔離,使單一 AZ 的故障被侷限住,滿足第 (1) 部分。改變流量去向的機制是 Amazon Application Recovery Controller (ARC) zonal shift:當你針對 ALB 啟動 zonal shift 將流量移離某個 AZ 時,ALB 會將該區的目標標記為 administratively overridden(AdministrativeOverride = zonal_shift_active),停止對其路由新流量,並將該區的 zonal IP 從 DNS 移除。AWS 明確將「藉由模擬與辨識故障來測試應用程式完整性」列為 zonal shift 的好處,正符合容錯移轉測試需求。選項 B 正確地將 cross-zone 設定放在 target group,並使用 ARC zonal shift,因此是正確答案。選項 A 雖指向相同機制,但將關閉 cross-zone 放在『ALB 上』,對 ALB 而言位置錯誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses the correct ARC zonal shift mechanism, but it turns off cross-zone load balancing 'on the ALB.' For an Application Load Balancer the cross-zone setting is a target group attribute (configured under Target Groups -> Attributes), not a load-balancer-level option (at the LB level ALB cross-zone is on by default), so the placement is wrong and B is more precise.","why_zh":"雖然使用了正確的 ARC zonal shift 機制,但它將 cross-zone load balancing 關閉在『ALB 上』。對 Application Load Balancer 而言,cross-zone 設定是 target group 屬性(在 Target Groups -> Attributes 設定),並非 load balancer 層級的選項(ALB 在 LB 層級預設啟用 cross-zone),因此位置錯誤,B 更為精確。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Resource sets belong to ARC recovery readiness (readiness checks), not to zonal shift. You do not 'start a zonal shift for a resource set,' and zonal shift uses the load balancer ARN as the resource identifier rather than a resource set built from the ALB DNS hostname. This conflates two different ARC features and would not shift ALB traffic.","why_zh":"Resource set 屬於 ARC recovery readiness(readiness check),而非 zonal shift。你無法『針對 resource set 啟動 zonal shift』,且 zonal shift 以 load balancer ARN 作為資源識別碼,而不是以 ALB DNS 主機名稱建立的 resource set。此選項混淆了兩個不同的 ARC 功能,無法改變 ALB 流量去向。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A readiness check with the ElbV2TargetGroupsCanServeTraffic rule only audits whether targets are ready to serve traffic; it is a recovery-readiness construct that reports status. It does not move or shift traffic away from an Availability Zone, so it cannot meet the failover/traffic-shift requirement.","why_zh":"使用 ElbV2TargetGroupsCanServeTraffic 規則的 readiness check 只會稽核目標是否準備好提供服務;它是 recovery-readiness 的構件,僅回報狀態。它不會將流量移離或轉移出某個 Availability Zone,因此無法滿足容錯移轉/流量轉移的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/zonal-shift.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/r53recovery/latest/dg/arc-zonal-shift.resource-types.app-load-balancers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/enable-zonal-shift.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/start-zonal-shift.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/edit-target-group-attributes.html"]}},{"id":275,"question_en":"A company sends its AWS Network Firewall flow logs to an Amazon S3 bucket. The company then analyzes the flow logs by using Amazon Athena. The company needs to transform the flow logs and add additional data before the flow logs are delivered to the existing S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司将其 AWS 网络防火墙的流量日志发送到一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。然后，该公司使用 Amazon Athena 对流量日志进行分析。 在将流量日志交付到现有的 S3 存储桶之前，公司需要对流量日志进行转换并添加额外的数据。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to transform the data and to write a new object to the existing S3 bucket. Configure the Lambda function with an S3 trigger for the existing S3 bucket. Specify all object create events for the event type. Acknowledge the recursive invocation.","B":"Enable Amazon EventBridge notifications on the existing S3 bucket. Create a custom EventBridge event bus. Create an EventBridge rule that is associated with the custom event bus. Configure the rule to react to all object create events for the existing S3 bucket and to invoke an AWS Step Functions workflow. Configure a Step Functions task to transform the data and to write the data into a new S3 bucket.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is associated with the default EventBridge event bus. Configure the rule to react to all object create events for the existing S3 bucket. Define a new S3 bucket as the target for the rule. Create an EventBridge input transformation to customize the event before passing the event to the rule target.","D":"Create an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream that is configured with an AWS Lambda transformer. Specify the existing S3 bucket as the destination. Change the Network Firewall logging destination from Amazon S3 to Kinesis Data Firehose."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来转换数据，并将新对象写入现有的 S3 存储桶。为现有的 S3 存储桶配置 Lambda 函数的 S3 触发器。指定事件类型为所有对象创建事件。确认递归调用。","B":"在现有的 S3 存储桶上启用 Amazon EventBridge 通知。创建一个自定义的 EventBridge 事件总线。创建一 个与自定义事件总线关联的 EventBridge 规则。配置该规则以响应现有 S3 存储桶中的所有对象创建事 件，并调用 AWS Step Functions 工作流。配置一个 Step Functions 任务以转换数据并将数据写入新的 S3 存储桶。 桶","C":"创建一个与默认的 Amazon EventBridge 事件总线相关联的规则。配置该规则以响应现有 S3 存储桶 中的所有对象创建事件。定义一个新的 S3 存储桶作为规则的目标。创建一个 EventBridge 输入转 换，以便在将事件传递给规则目标之前对其进行自定义。","D":"创建一个配置了 AWS Lambda 转换器的 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 交付流。将现有的 S3 存储桶 指定为目的地。将网络防火墙的日志记录目的地从 Amazon S3 更改为 Kinesis Data Firehose。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Network Firewall natively supports exactly three logging destinations: Amazon S3, Amazon CloudWatch Logs, and Amazon Data Firehose. The requirement is to transform the flow logs and add additional data BEFORE the logs are delivered to the existing S3 bucket, while keeping the bucket (and therefore the existing Athena setup) intact. Amazon Data Firehose can invoke a Lambda function to transform incoming source records in-flight before loading them, and S3 is a supported Firehose destination. By switching the Network Firewall logging destination from S3 to a Firehose delivery stream (DirectPut) configured with a Lambda transformer and the existing S3 bucket as the destination, the data is transformed and enriched pre-delivery and then written to the same bucket, so Athena queries continue unchanged. This is the only option that both performs the transformation before delivery and writes back to the existing bucket.","explanation_zh":"AWS Network Firewall 原生只支援三種 logging 目的地：Amazon S3、Amazon CloudWatch Logs 與 Amazon Data Firehose。需求是要在 flow logs 送達既有 S3 bucket「之前」完成轉換並加入額外資料，同時保留該 bucket（也就是維持既有的 Athena 設定）。Amazon Data Firehose 可在載入前同步呼叫 Lambda function 對來源紀錄進行轉換，而 S3 是 Firehose 支援的目的地。將 Network Firewall 的 logging 目的地由 S3 改為一個設定了 Lambda transformer、並以既有 S3 bucket 為目的地的 Firehose delivery stream（DirectPut），資料就會在送達前被轉換與擴充，再寫入同一個 bucket，Athena 查詢完全不需更動。這是唯一能在送達前完成轉換、且仍寫回既有 bucket 的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Lambda function triggered by S3 object-create events runs AFTER the raw logs already land in the bucket, so it is post-delivery, not pre-delivery as required. It also leaves the untransformed objects in the bucket (polluting Athena results) and forces an awkward recursive-invocation acknowledgement to avoid re-triggering on the objects it writes back to the same bucket.","why_zh":"由 S3 物件建立事件觸發的 Lambda 是在原始 logs 已寫入 bucket「之後」才執行，屬於送達後處理，而非需求所要求的送達前轉換。原始未轉換物件仍留在 bucket 中（會污染 Athena 結果），而且必須處理遞迴呼叫確認以避免被自己寫回同一 bucket 的物件再次觸發。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This is post-delivery processing (EventBridge fires only after objects are created) and, critically, the Step Functions task writes the data into a NEW S3 bucket rather than the existing bucket, so the existing Athena setup would no longer point at the transformed data.","why_zh":"這屬於送達後處理（EventBridge 只在物件建立後才觸發），而且關鍵在於 Step Functions 任務會把資料寫入「新的」S3 bucket，而非既有 bucket，導致既有 Athena 設定無法指向轉換後的資料。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An S3 bucket cannot be set as a direct target of an EventBridge rule, and an EventBridge input transformer only reshapes the event JSON passed to the target, not the contents of the log objects. It is also post-delivery, so it cannot satisfy the requirement.","why_zh":"S3 bucket 無法設為 EventBridge 規則的直接目標，而 EventBridge input transformer 只能改寫傳給目標的事件 JSON，並不能改變 log 物件的內容。此外它也屬於送達後處理，無法滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/network-firewall/latest/developerguide/firewall-logging-destinations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/network-firewall/latest/developerguide/logging-kinesis.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/data-transformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/create-destination.html"]}},{"id":276,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to implement integration tests into an existing AWS CodePipeline CI/CD workflow for an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) service. The CI/CD workflow retrieves new application code from an AWS CodeCommit repository and builds a container image. The CI/CD workflow then uploads the container image to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) with a new image tag version. The integration tests must ensure that new versions of the service endpoint are reachable and that various API methods return successful response data. The DevOps engineer has already created an ECS cluster to test the service. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST management overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要将集成测试纳入现有的 AWS CodePipeline 持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）工作 流中，该工作流用于 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）服务。该 CI/CD 工作流从 AWS CodeCommit 代码库中获取新的应用程序代码，并构建容器镜像。然后，该 CI/CD 工作流将容器镜像上 传到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR），并使用新的镜像标签版本。 集成测试必须确保服务端点的新版本可访问，并且各种 API 方法都能返回成功的响应数据。DevOps 工程 师已经创建了一个 ECS 集群来测试该服务。 哪种步骤组合能以最小的管理开销满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add a deploy stage to the pipeline. Configure Amazon ECS as the action provider.","B":"Add a deploy stage to the pipeline. Configure AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider.","C":"Add an appspec.yml file to the CodeCommit repository.","D":"Update the image build pipeline stage to output an imagedefinitions.json file that references the new image tag.","E":"Create an AWS Lambda function that runs connectivity checks and API calls against the service. Integrate the Lambda function with CodePipeline by using a Lambda action stage.","F":"Write a script that runs integration tests against the service. Upload the script to an Amazon S3 bucket. Integrate the script in the S3 bucket with CodePipeline by using an S3 action stage."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管道中添加一个部署阶段。将 Amazon ECS 配置为操作提供程序。","B":"在管道中添加一个部署阶段。将 AWS CodeDeploy 配置为操作提供程序。","C":"在 CodeCommit 存储库中添加一个 appspec.yml 文件。","D":"更新镜像构建流水线阶段，使其输出一个引用新镜像标签的 imagedefinitions.json 文件。","E":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于对服务执行连接性检查和 API 调用。通过使用 Lambda 操作 阶段将 Lambda 函数与 CodePipeline 集成。","F":"编写一个针对服务运行集成测试的脚本。将该脚本上传到 Amazon S3 存储桶。通过使用 S3 操作阶段 将 S3 存储桶中的脚本与 CodePipeline 集成。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The least-overhead deploy path for an existing ECS service is the Amazon ECS standard deploy action (Category: Deploy, Provider: ECS), which simply updates the service to a new task definition revision referencing the new image (A). That action requires an imagedefinitions.json input artifact mapping the container name to the new image URI/tag; per AWS docs, 'Amazon ECS standard deployments require an imagedefinitions.json file as an input to the deploy action,' and when the pipeline has a build stage you add a buildspec command to output that file with the new tag (D). For the integration tests (endpoint reachability plus API methods returning successful responses), the native CodePipeline pattern is a Lambda invoke action; the AWS tutorial 'Invoke an AWS Lambda function in a pipeline' explicitly creates 'a Lambda function that tests whether a webpage was deployed successfully' and gates the pipeline via PutJobSuccessResult/PutJobFailureResult (E). The CodeDeploy/appspec.yml combination (B+C) is the ECS blue/green path, which adds an Application Load Balancer with two target groups, a CodeDeploy application and deployment group, plus appspec.yml/taskdef/imageDetail.json files, far more overhead and not required here. Option F is invalid because an S3 action only deploys/extracts files to or from an S3 bucket; it cannot execute a test script.","explanation_zh":"對既有 ECS service 而言,最低管理負擔的部署方式是 Amazon ECS standard deploy action(Category: Deploy、Provider: ECS),它只需把 service 更新到引用新 image 的新 task definition revision(A)。該 action 需要 imagedefinitions.json 作為輸入 artifact,用來把容器名稱對應到新的 image URI/tag;AWS 文件指出『Amazon ECS standard deployments require an imagedefinitions.json file as an input to the deploy action』,當 pipeline 有 build 階段時,可在 buildspec 加入指令輸出含新 tag 的該檔案(D)。至於整合測試(端點可連線、各 API method 回傳成功回應),CodePipeline 原生作法是 Lambda invoke action;AWS 教學『Invoke an AWS Lambda function in a pipeline』正是建立『a Lambda function that tests whether a webpage was deployed successfully』,並透過 PutJobSuccessResult/PutJobFailureResult 來把關 pipeline(E)。CodeDeploy 搭配 appspec.yml(B+C)屬於 ECS blue/green 路徑,需額外建立含兩個 target group 的 Application Load Balancer、CodeDeploy application 與 deployment group,以及 appspec.yml/taskdef/imageDetail.json 等檔案,負擔大很多且本題不需要。選項 F 不成立,因為 S3 action 只能把檔案部署/解壓到 S3 bucket,無法執行測試腳本。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Configuring CodeDeploy as the action provider triggers an ECS blue/green deployment (CodeDeployToECS), which requires an Application Load Balancer with two target groups, a CodeDeploy application and deployment group, and appspec.yml/taskdef/imageDetail.json files. This is far MORE management overhead than the ECS standard deploy action, and blue/green is not required.","why_zh":"將 CodeDeploy 設為 action provider 會觸發 ECS 藍綠部署(CodeDeployToECS),需要含兩個 target group 的 ALB、CodeDeploy application 與 deployment group,以及 appspec.yml/taskdef/imageDetail.json 檔案。相較 ECS standard deploy action 負擔大得多,且本題並不需要藍綠部署。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"appspec.yml is only needed for the CodeDeploy ECS blue/green path (paired with B). The ECS standard deploy action uses imagedefinitions.json, not appspec.yml. Choosing C implies the heavier blue/green setup that is not required.","why_zh":"appspec.yml 只在 CodeDeploy ECS 藍綠路徑(搭配 B)才需要。ECS standard deploy action 使用 imagedefinitions.json 而非 appspec.yml。選 C 等於採用本題不需要的較重藍綠設定。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"There is no CodePipeline S3 action that runs a script. The S3 deploy action only copies/extracts files into an S3 bucket, and an S3 source action only pulls files from S3 — neither executes integration test code against a service endpoint. To run a script you would need CodeBuild or Lambda, so this option cannot meet the requirement.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 沒有可執行腳本的 S3 action。S3 deploy action 只會將檔案複製/解壓縮到 S3 bucket,S3 source action 只會從 S3 取得檔案,兩者都無法對服務端點執行整合測試程式。要執行腳本需用 CodeBuild 或 Lambda,因此此選項無法滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-ECS.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/file-reference.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-invoke-lambda-function.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-ECSbluegreen.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-S3Deploy.html"]}},{"id":277,"question_en":"A company runs applications on Windows and Linux Amazon EC2 instances. The instances run across multiple Availability Zones in an AWS Region. The company uses Auto Scaling groups for each application. The company needs a durable storage solution for the instances. The solution must use SMB for Windows and must use NFS for Linux. The solution must also have sub-millisecond latencies. All instances will read and write the data. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"该公司在 Windows 和 Linux 的亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行应用程序。这些实例分布在 AWS 区域内的多个 可用区。该公司为每个应用程序使用了自动扩展组。 该公司需要一种持久的存储方案来满足实例的需求。该方案必须为 Windows 系统使用 SMB 协议，为 Linux 系统使用 NFS 协议。此外，该方案还必须具备亚毫秒级的延迟。所有实例都将读取和写入数据。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system that has targets in multiple Availability Zones.","B":"Create an Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP Multi-AZ file system.","C":"Create a General Purpose SSD (gp3) Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume to use for shared storage.","D":"Update the user data for each application’s launch template to mount the file system.","E":"Perform an instance refresh on each Auto Scaling group.","F":"Update the EC2 instances for each application to mount the file system when new instances are launched."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个在多个可用区都有目标的 Amazon 弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS）文件系统。","B":"创建一个适用于 NetApp ONTAP 的 Amazon FSx 多可用区文件系统。","C":"创建一个通用型 SSD（gp3）Amazon Elastic Block Store（Amazon EBS）卷用于 共享存储。","D":"更新每个应用程序启动模板的用户数据以挂载文件系统。","E":"对每个自动扩展组执行实例刷新操作。","F":"更新每个应用程序的 EC2 实例，以便在启动新实例时挂载文件系统。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive requirements are: serve SMB to Windows AND NFS to Linux from the same durable, Multi-AZ store, with sub-millisecond latency, where all instances read and write. Only Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP meets all of these. AWS docs state it provides 'Multi-protocol access to data using the Network File System (NFS), Server Message Block (SMB), iSCSI, and NVMe protocols,' 'offers high-performance solid state drive (SSD) storage with submillisecond latencies,' and supports 'Highly available and durable Multi-AZ and Single-AZ deployment options,' so B is correct. To make Auto Scaling instances use it, you bake the mount commands into the launch template user data so every newly launched instance mounts the share automatically (D). Because instances that are already running were launched from the prior launch template version, you trigger an instance refresh; the AWS instance-refresh doc explicitly lists 'Deploying a new...user data script across your Auto Scaling group...use an instance refresh to roll out the updates immediately,' which replaces existing instances with ones created from the updated user data (E). EFS (A) is rejected because it is NFS-only (mounted via an NFS client, no SMB for Windows) and its measured latency is ~1 ms read / ~2.7 ms write per the EFS performance table, not sub-millisecond. EBS gp3 (C) is single-AZ block storage, not a shared multi-protocol file system, and cannot be written concurrently by instances across Availability Zones. F is a vague restatement that overlaps with D (mounting on new launches is achieved via launch-template user data) and omits the instance refresh needed for existing instances, so D+E is the correct pairing.","explanation_zh":"決定性需求是：同一個耐久、跨多 AZ 的儲存必須同時對 Windows 提供 SMB、對 Linux 提供 NFS，且需子毫秒（sub-millisecond）延遲，所有執行個體都要讀寫。只有 Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP 全部滿足。AWS 文件指出它提供『多協定存取（NFS、SMB、iSCSI、NVMe）』、『提供具子毫秒延遲的高效能 SSD 儲存』，並支援『高可用且耐久的 Multi-AZ 與 Single-AZ 部署選項』，故選 B。要讓 Auto Scaling 執行個體使用它，將掛載指令寫入 launch template 的 user data，使每個新啟動的執行個體自動掛載共享（D）。由於目前正在執行的執行個體是以舊版 launch template 啟動的，須執行 instance refresh；AWS instance-refresh 文件明確列出『將新的…user data 指令稿部署到 Auto Scaling group…使用 instance refresh 立即推出更新』，藉此以更新後的 user data 重新建立並替換既有執行個體（E）。EFS（A）被排除，因為它僅支援 NFS（透過 NFS 用戶端掛載，不支援 Windows 的 SMB），且依 EFS 效能表其延遲約為讀取 ~1 ms、寫入 ~2.7 ms，並非子毫秒。EBS gp3（C）是單一 AZ 的區塊儲存，不是共享多協定檔案系統，且無法讓跨 AZ 的執行個體同時寫入。F 是與 D 重疊的模糊敘述（在新啟動時掛載是透過 launch-template 的 user data 完成），且遺漏了替換既有執行個體所需的 instance refresh，因此正確配對是 D+E。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon EFS supports only NFS (it is mounted with an NFS client; there is no SMB protocol for Windows), and the EFS performance specifications table shows ~1 ms read / ~2.7 ms write latency, which is not sub-millisecond. It fails two hard requirements.","why_zh":"Amazon EFS 僅支援 NFS（以 NFS 用戶端掛載，沒有給 Windows 的 SMB 協定），且 EFS 效能規格表顯示延遲約為讀取 ~1 ms、寫入 ~2.7 ms，並非子毫秒。直接違反兩項硬性需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"gp3 EBS is single-AZ block storage, not a shared multi-protocol file system. It cannot present SMB/NFS shares, and an EBS volume cannot be written concurrently by all instances across multiple Availability Zones.","why_zh":"gp3 EBS 是單一 AZ 的區塊儲存，不是共享的多協定檔案系統，無法提供 SMB/NFS 共享，且 EBS 磁碟區無法讓跨多個 AZ 的所有執行個體同時寫入。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"This is a vague restatement that overlaps with D; mounting on new launches is accomplished through the launch-template user data (D), not a separate 'update the instances' step. It also omits the instance refresh (E) required so existing running instances are replaced with ones that mount the file system.","why_zh":"這是與 D 重疊的模糊敘述；在新啟動時掛載是透過 launch-template 的 user data（D）完成，並非另一個『更新執行個體』的步驟。它同時遺漏了用以替換既有執行中執行個體（使其掛載檔案系統）所需的 instance refresh（E）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/what-is-fsx-ontap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/how-it-works-fsx-ontap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/efs/latest/ug/performance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/asg-instance-refresh.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/instance-refresh-overview.html"]}},{"id":278,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations that a security team and a DevOps team manage. Both teams access the accounts by using AWS IAM Identity Center. A dedicated group has been created for each team. The DevOps team's group has been assigned a permission set named DevOps. The permission set has the AdministratorAccess managed IAM policy attached. The permission set has been applied to all accounts in the organization. The security team wants to ensure that the DevOps team does not have access to IAM Identity Center in the organization's management account. The security team has attached the following SCP to the organization root: After implementing the policy, the security team discovers that the DevOps team can still access IAM Identity Center. Which solution will fix the problem?","question_zh":"一家公司使用由安全团队和 DevOps 团队管理的 AWS 组织。两个团队均通过 AWS IAM 身份中心访问 账户。 为每个团队都创建了一个专用组。DevOps 团队的组已分配了一个名为 DevOps 的权限集。该权限 集附加了 AdministratorAccess 管理的 IAM 策略。该权限集已应用于组织中的所有账户。 安全团队希望确保 DevOps 团队无法访问组织管理账户中的 IAM 身份中心。安全团队已在组织根目 录附加了以下服务控制策略（SCP）： 在实施该政策后，安全团队发现 DevOps 团队仍能访问 IAM 身份中心。 哪种解决方案能解决问题？","options_en":{"A":"In the organization's management account, create a new OU. Move the organization's management account to the new OU. Detach the SCP from the organization root. Attach the SCP to the new OU.","B":"In the organization's management account, update the SCP condition reference to the ARN of the DevOps team's group role to include the AWS account ID of the organization's management account.","C":"In IAM Identity Center, create a new permission set. Ensure that the assigned policy has full access but explicitly denies permission for the sso:* action and the sso-directory:* action. Update the assigned permission set for the DevOps team's group role in the organization's management account. Delete the SCP.","D":"In IAM Identity Center, update the DevOps permission set. Ensure that the assigned policy has full access but explicitly denies permission for the sso:* action and the sso-directory:* action. In the Deny statement, add a StringEquals condition that compares the aws:SourceAccount global condition context key with the organization's management account ID. Delete the SCP."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织的管理账户中，创建一个新的组织单位（OU）。将组织的管理账户移动到新的 OU 中。 从组织根目录分离安全策略配置文件（SCP）。将 SCP 附加到新的 OU。","B":"在组织的管理账户中，将 SCP 条件引用更新为 DevOps 团队组角色的 ARN，以包含组织管理账户 的 AWS 账户 ID。","C":"在 IAM 身份中心，创建一个新的权限集。确保所分配的策略具有完全访问权限，但明确拒绝 sso:* 操作和 sso-directory:* 操作的权限。更新组织管理账户中 DevOps 团队组角色所分配的权限集。删除 SCP.","D":"在 IAM 身份中心，更新 DevOps 权限集。确保分配的策略具有完全访问权限，但明确拒绝 sso:* 操 作和 sso-directory:* 操作的权限。在拒绝语句中，添加一个 StringEquals 条件，将 aws: SourceAccount 全局条件上下文键与组织的管理账户 ID 进行比较。删除 SCP。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The root cause is that SCPs never apply to the management account. The AWS Organizations documentation states verbatim 'SCPs don't affect users or roles in the management account. They affect only the member accounts.' Because IAM Identity Center is administered from the management account, an SCP attached to the organization root (or any OU/account) can never restrict the DevOps team's IAM Identity Center access there. The fix must therefore use an identity-based policy (a permission set), which DOES apply in the management account. Option C creates a NEW permission set that grants full access but adds an explicit Deny on sso:* and sso-directory:*, and assigns it to the DevOps group only in the management account. Because IAM Identity Center assignments are per principal per account ('You can create a single permission set and assign it to multiple AWS accounts ... you can also assign multiple permission sets to the same user'), this scopes the restriction precisely to the management account while every other account keeps the original DevOps/AdministratorAccess assignment; the ineffective SCP is deleted. Option D (the dump's suggestion) uses the right mechanism but adds a StringEquals condition on aws:SourceAccount, which the IAM docs state verbatim is 'only available when the call to your resource is made directly by an AWS service principal.' For a DevOps user's direct console/API request the key is absent, so with a plain StringEquals operator the Deny never matches and access remains.","explanation_zh":"問題根源在於 SCP 永遠不適用於 management account。AWS Organizations 文件逐字指出『SCPs don't affect users or roles in the management account. They affect only the member accounts.』由於 IAM Identity Center 是在 management account 中管理，因此附加於 organization root（或任何 OU/帳戶）的 SCP 永遠無法限制 DevOps 團隊在該帳戶存取 IAM Identity Center。修正方式必須改用 identity-based policy（permission set），因為它在 management account 中是生效的。選項 C 建立一個『新的』permission set，授予完整存取但加上對 sso:* 與 sso-directory:* 的明確 Deny，並僅在 management account 中把它指派給 DevOps 群組。由於 IAM Identity Center 的指派是依 principal 依帳戶進行（『You can create a single permission set and assign it to multiple AWS accounts ... you can also assign multiple permission sets to the same user』），這正好把限制範圍鎖定在 management account，而其他每個帳戶仍維持原本的 DevOps/AdministratorAccess 指派；無效的 SCP 一併刪除。選項 D（dump 的建議答案）機制方向正確，但加上對 aws:SourceAccount 的 StringEquals 條件，而 IAM 文件逐字指出該 key『只在呼叫由 AWS service principal 直接發出時才可用』。對於 DevOps 使用者直接的 console/API 請求，此 key 並不存在，因此使用一般 StringEquals 運算子時 Deny 永遠不會命中，存取依舊保留。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Moving the management account into a new OU and attaching the SCP there still does nothing. SCPs never restrict the management account regardless of which OU it sits in; the docs list 'Any action performed by the management account' as exempt from SCP enforcement. The DevOps team would still reach IAM Identity Center.","why_zh":"把 management account 移到新 OU 並在該 OU 附加 SCP 仍然無效。無論放在哪個 OU，SCP 都不會限制 management account；文件將『Any action performed by the management account』列為不受 SCP 約束。DevOps 團隊仍能存取 IAM Identity Center。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Adding a condition that references the DevOps group role ARN plus the management account ID to the SCP cannot help, because SCPs have zero effect on principals in the management account. No SCP-based approach can restrict actions performed in the management account.","why_zh":"在 SCP 中加入參照 DevOps 群組角色 ARN 與 management account ID 的條件沒有用，因為 SCP 對 management account 中的 principal 完全無效。任何以 SCP 為基礎的方法都無法限制 management account 中執行的動作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Editing a permission set is the correct mechanism, but the StringEquals condition on aws:SourceAccount is wrong: per IAM docs that key 'is only available when the call to your resource is made directly by an AWS service principal' (confused-deputy / service-to-service protection). It is absent from a user's direct console/API request, so with StringEquals (not StringEqualsIfExists) the Deny never triggers and access remains. It also modifies the single existing DevOps permission set that is used in every account.","why_zh":"修改 permission set 機制是對的，但對 aws:SourceAccount 用 StringEquals 條件是錯的：根據 IAM 文件，該 key『只在呼叫由 AWS service principal 直接發出時才可用』（用於 confused-deputy／服務對服務防護）。使用者直接的 console/API 請求中並無此 key，因此用 StringEquals（而非 StringEqualsIfExists）時 Deny 永不觸發，存取依舊存在。此外它修改的是套用到所有帳戶的那個既有 DevOps permission set。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/manage-your-accounts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/howtocreatepermissionset.html"]}},{"id":279,"question_en":"An Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group manages EC2 instances that were created from an AMI. The AMI has the AWS Systems Manager Agent installed. When an EC2 instance is launched into the Auto Scaling group, tags are applied to the EC2 instance. EC2 instances that are launched by the Auto Scaling group must have the correct operating system configuration. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"亚马逊 EC2 自动扩展组管理从 AMI 创建的 EC2 实例。该 AMI 安装了 AWS 系统管理器代理。当 EC2 实 例启动到自动扩展组中时，会将标签应用于该 EC2 实例。 由自动扩展组启动的 EC2 实例必须具有正确的操作系统配置。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a Systems Manager Run Command document that configures the desired instance configuration. Set up Systems Manager Compliance to invoke the Run Command document when the EC2 instances are not in compliance with the most recent patches.","B":"Create a Systems Manager State Manager association that links to the Systems Manager command document. Create a tag query that runs immediately.","C":"Create a Systems Manager Run Command task that specifies the desired instance configuration. Create a maintenance window in Systems Manager Maintenance Windows that runs daily. Register the Run Command task against the maintenance window. Designate the targets.","D":"Create a Systems Manager Patch Manager patch baseline and a patch group that use the same tags that the Auto Scaling group applies. Register the patch group with the patch baseline. Define a Systems Manager command document to patch the instances Invoke the document by using Systems Manager Run Command."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Systems Manager Run Command 文档，用于配置所需的实例配置。设置 Systems Manager Compliance，以便在 EC2 实例不符合最新补丁要求时调用 Run Command 文档。","B":"创建一个与 Systems Manager 命令文档相关联的 Systems Manager 状态管理器关联。创建一个立即 运行的标签查询。","C":"创建一个指定所需实例配置的 Systems Manager 运行命令任务。在 Systems Manager 维护窗口中创建一 个每日运行的维护窗口。将运行命令任务与维护窗口相关联。指定目标。","D":"创建一个与自动扩展组应用的标签相同的系统管理器补丁管理器补丁基准和补丁组。将补丁组注册 到补丁基准。定义一个用于修补实例的系统管理器命令文档。使用系统管理器运行命令来调用该文 档。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Systems Manager State Manager is the purpose-built, AWS-recommended tool for this EC2 Auto Scaling scenario. The 'Choosing between State Manager and Maintenance Windows' doc states State Manager is recommended when you 'use Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling to generate new nodes,' and that it 'can monitor all new nodes launched within an account either manually or through Auto Scaling groups. If there are any associations in the account targeting that new node (through tags or all nodes), then that particular association is automatically applied to the new node.' A State Manager association links an SSM Command document (which defines the desired OS configuration) to targets defined by a tag query, and by default runs immediately on creation and again whenever new nodes come online, continuously remediating drift. Because the Auto Scaling group already applies tags at launch, a tag-targeted association automatically configures each newly launched instance the moment it appears, with the lowest operational overhead. Option B is therefore correct.","explanation_zh":"AWS Systems Manager State Manager 是針對此 EC2 Auto Scaling 情境量身打造、且 AWS 官方推薦的工具。在「Choosing between State Manager and Maintenance Windows」文件中明確指出：當你「use Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling to generate new nodes」時建議使用 State Manager，且它「可以監控帳戶中所有新啟動的節點（無論是手動或透過 Auto Scaling groups）。若帳戶中有任何 association 透過 tags 或所有節點鎖定該新節點，該 association 會自動套用到新節點」。一個 State Manager association 會將 SSM Command document（定義所需的 OS 設定）連結到由 tag query 定義的目標，預設在建立時立即執行，並在每次有新節點上線時再次套用，持續修正組態漂移。由於 Auto Scaling group 在啟動時就已套用 tags，以 tag 為目標的 association 會在每個新啟動的執行個體出現的當下自動完成設定，且維運負擔最低。因此選項 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Systems Manager Compliance is a reporting/aggregation feature, not an event-driven trigger that fires when a new Auto Scaling instance launches, and Run Command is a one-time on-demand action. Tying remediation to 'not in compliance with the most recent patches' frames this as patch compliance, not applying a desired OS configuration, and provides no mechanism to configure an instance automatically the moment it comes online.","why_zh":"Systems Manager Compliance 是報告／彙總功能，並非在新的 Auto Scaling 執行個體啟動時觸發的事件驅動機制，而 Run Command 是一次性的隨選動作。將修復綁定到「未符合最新修補程式合規」是把問題框成 patch 合規，而非套用所需 OS 設定，也無法在執行個體一上線時自動完成設定。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A maintenance window that runs daily only executes the Run Command task on its schedule, so a newly launched instance would remain misconfigured until the next daily window instead of being configured the moment it comes online. AWS docs position Maintenance Windows for time-sensitive/patching tasks, while State Manager automatically applies the association to new nodes as they appear, which is exactly the Auto Scaling use case AWS calls out.","why_zh":"每日執行的 maintenance window 只會依排程執行 Run Command 任務，因此新啟動的執行個體會一直維持未設定狀態，直到下一個每日視窗，而非在上線當下立即完成設定。AWS 文件將 Maintenance Windows 定位於時間敏感／修補任務，而 State Manager 會在新節點出現時自動套用 association，這正是 AWS 點名的 Auto Scaling 使用情境。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Patch Manager patch baselines and patch groups are for applying OS patches (approving/rejecting security and software updates), not for enforcing a desired operating system configuration state. Invoking via Run Command is also one-time and is not automatically triggered when the ASG launches a new instance, so it addresses patching rather than the broader 'correct operating system configuration' requirement.","why_zh":"Patch Manager 的 patch baseline 與 patch group 用於套用 OS 修補程式（核准／拒絕安全與軟體更新），並非用來強制維持所需的作業系統組態狀態。透過 Run Command 觸發同樣是一次性的，且在 ASG 啟動新執行個體時不會自動觸發，因此它處理的是 patching，而非更廣義的「正確作業系統設定」需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/state-manager-vs-maintenance-windows.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-state.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager.html"]}},{"id":280,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS accounts. The organization root has a child OU that is named Department. The Department OU has a child OU that is named Engineering. The default FullAWSAccess policy is attached to the root, the Department OU, and the Engineering OU. The company has many AWS accounts in the Engineering OU. Each account has an administrative IAM role with the AdministratorAccess IAM policy attached. The default FullAWSAccessPolicy is also attached to each account. A DevOps engineer plans to remove the FullAWSAccess policy from the Department OU. The DevOps engineer will replace the policy with a policy that contains an Allow statement for all Amazon EC2 API operations. What will happen to the permissions of the administrative IAM roles as a result of this change?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理其 AWS 账户。组织根目录有一个名为“部门”的子组织单元 （OU）。该“部门”OU 有一个名为“工程”的子 OU。默认的“FullAWSAccess”策略已附加到根目 录、“部门”OU 和“工程”OU。 该公司在工程组织单元（OU）中有许多 AWS 账户。每个账户都具有一个附有 AdministratorAccess IAM 策略的管理 IAM 角色。每个账户还附有默认的 FullAWSAccessPolicy 策略。 一位 DevOps 工程师计划从部门组织单元中移除“FullAWSAccess”策略。该工程师将用一个包含对 所有亚马逊 EC2 API 操作的允许语句的策略来替换它。 此次变更会对管理 IAM 角色的权限产生什么影响？","options_en":{"A":"All API actions on all resources will be allowed.","B":"All API actions on EC2 resources will be allowed. All other API actions will be denied.","C":"All API actions on all resources will be denied.","D":"All API actions on EC2 resources will be denied. All other API actions will be allowed."},"options_zh":{"A":"所有资源上的所有 API 操作都将被允许。","B":"对于 EC2 资源的所有 API 操作都将被允许。所有其他 API 操作都将被拒绝。","C":"对所有资源的所有 API 操作都将被拒绝。","D":"对所有 EC2 资源的 API 操作都将被拒绝。其他所有 API 操作都将被允许。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"SCP evaluation is deny-by-default: for a permission to be allowed for an account, an explicit Allow must exist at EVERY level in the direct path from the root through each OU to the account, including the account itself. The path here is Root -> Department OU -> Engineering OU -> Account. After the change, Root keeps FullAWSAccess (allows all), the Department OU now allows only Amazon EC2 (ec2:*), and the Engineering OU and the accounts keep FullAWSAccess. For EC2 actions, an Allow exists at all four levels, so EC2 passes the SCP guardrail. For any non-EC2 action (for example S3), the Department OU has no matching Allow, so it is implicitly denied because the allowlist must intersect at every level. The effective permission of an administrative role is the intersection of its AdministratorAccess IAM policy (allows everything) and the SCP guardrail (only EC2), which yields: all EC2 actions allowed and all other actions denied. AWS docs explicitly note that an SCP blocks an action implicitly (by omission from an Allow) even if AdministratorAccess with */* is attached to the role. Therefore B is correct.","explanation_zh":"SCP 採用 deny-by-default（預設拒絕）模型：某個權限要被允許，必須在從 root 經過每個 OU 直到帳戶本身的整條直接路徑上的每一層都有明確的 Allow 陳述式。本題路徑為 Root -> Department OU -> Engineering OU -> Account。變更後，Root 保留 FullAWSAccess（允許全部），Department OU 改為僅允許 Amazon EC2（ec2:*），而 Engineering OU 與各帳戶仍保留 FullAWSAccess。對於 EC2 操作，四個層級都有 Allow，因此 EC2 通過 SCP 護欄。對於任何非 EC2 操作（例如 S3），Department OU 沒有對應的 Allow，因 allowlist 必須在每一層交集，故被隱含拒絕。管理 IAM 角色的有效權限為其 AdministratorAccess IAM policy（允許全部）與 SCP 護欄（僅 EC2）的交集，結果為：所有 EC2 操作被允許，其他所有操作被拒絕。AWS 文件明確指出，即使角色掛上含 */* 的 AdministratorAccess，只要某動作在某一層未被 Allow（隱含拒絕）或被明確 Deny，該動作仍無法執行。因此正確答案為 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"All actions allowed would only be true if FullAWSAccess (or an equivalent allow-all) remained at every level. Replacing the Department OU policy with an EC2-only Allow breaks the allow chain for non-EC2 services, so non-EC2 actions are denied.","why_zh":"只有在每一層都保留 FullAWSAccess（或等效的允許全部）時，所有操作才會被允許。將 Department OU 政策改為僅允許 EC2 會中斷非 EC2 服務的允許鏈，因此非 EC2 操作會被拒絕。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"All actions denied would result only if the Allow were removed and not replaced at some level. Here EC2 is still allowed at all four levels (Root FullAWSAccess, Department EC2-only, Engineering FullAWSAccess, account FullAWSAccess), so EC2 actions remain permitted; not everything is denied.","why_zh":"只有在某一層的 Allow 被移除且未被替換時，所有操作才會被拒絕。此處 EC2 在四個層級（Root FullAWSAccess、Department 僅 EC2、Engineering FullAWSAccess、帳戶 FullAWSAccess）都仍被允許，因此 EC2 操作仍可執行，並非全部被拒絕。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This inverts the result. SCPs are allowlists by default; the Department OU policy ALLOWS EC2, so EC2 is permitted, not denied. Conversely, non-EC2 actions are denied (not allowed) because they are not in any Allow at the Department OU level. There is no Deny statement on EC2.","why_zh":"此選項把結果反了。SCP 預設為 allowlist；Department OU 政策是「允許」EC2，因此 EC2 被允許而非拒絕。反之，非 EC2 操作因在 Department OU 層級沒有任何 Allow 而被拒絕，而非被允許。EC2 並沒有 Deny 陳述式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_evaluation-logic.html"]}},{"id":281,"question_en":"A company manages AWS accounts in AWS Organizations. The company needs a solution to send Amazon CloudWatch Logs data to an Amazon S3 bucket in a dedicated AWS account. The solution must support all existing and future CloudWatch Logs log groups. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司需要一个解决方案，将 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 数 据发送到一个专用 AWS 账户中的 Amazon S3 存储桶。该解决方案必须支持所有现有的和未来的 CloudWatch Logs 日志组。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable Organizations backup policies to back up all log groups to a dedicated S3 bucket. Add an S3 bucket policy that allows access from all accounts that belong to the company.","B":"Create a backup plan in AWS Backup. Specify a dedicated S3 bucket as a backup vault. Assign all CloudWatch Logs log group resources to the backup plan. Create resource assignments in the backup plan for all accounts that belong to the company.","C":"Create a backup plan in AWS Backup. Specify a dedicated S3 bucket as a backup vault. Assign all existing log groups to the backup plan. Create resource assignments in the backup plan for all accounts that belong to the company. Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to assign log groups to a backup plan. Create an AWS Config rule that has an automatic remediation action for all noncompliant log groups. Specify the runbook as the rule's target.","D":"Create a CloudWatch Logs destination and an Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose delivery stream in the dedicated AWS account. Specify the S3 bucket as the destination of the delivery stream. Create subscription filters for all existing log groups in all accounts. Create an AWS Lambda function to call the CloudWatch Logs PutSubscriptionFilter API operation. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function when a CreateLogGroup event occurs."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用组织备份策略，将所有日志组备份到专用的 S3 存储桶。添加一个 S3 存储桶策略，允许公司所属 的所有账户访问。","B":"在 AWS 备份中创建一个备份计划。指定一个专用的 S3 存储桶作为备份金库。将所有 CloudWatch Logs 日志组资源分配给该备份计划。在备份计划中为公司所属的所有账户创建资源分配。","C":"在 AWS Backup 中创建备份计划。指定一个专用的 S3 存储桶作为备份金库。将所有现有的日志组分配给 备份计划。在备份计划中为公司所属的所有账户创建资源分配。创建一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，用于将日志组分配给备份计划。创建一个具有自动修复操作的 AWS Config 规则， 针对所有不符合要求的日志组。将运行手册指定为规则的目标。","D":"在专用的 AWS 账户中创建 CloudWatch Logs 目标和 Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose 交付流。将 S3 存储桶指 定为交付流的目的地。为所有账户中的所有现有日志组创建订阅筛选器。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来 调用 CloudWatch Logs PutSubscriptionFilter API 操作。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在发生 CreateLogGroup 事件时调用 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Cross-account, centralized delivery of CloudWatch Logs to an S3 bucket in a dedicated account uses the documented subscription pattern: in the dedicated (recipient) account you create a CloudWatch Logs destination that encapsulates an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream whose target is the S3 bucket, and in each sender account you create subscription filters that point to that destination. Subscription filters only cover log groups that exist when they are created, so to satisfy 'all existing and future' log groups you also need automation: an Amazon EventBridge rule that fires on the CloudTrail CreateLogGroup event invokes a Lambda function that calls the CloudWatch Logs PutSubscriptionFilter API for each newly created log group. This is exactly option D and matches the AWS docs for cross-account cross-Region subscriptions using Firehose. Options A, B, and C all rely on AWS Backup (Organizations 'backup policies' are AWS Backup policies), but the AWS Backup feature-availability resource table does not list Amazon CloudWatch Logs as a supported resource type, and AWS Backup writes recovery points into a backup vault, not into an arbitrary S3 bucket designated as a 'backup vault' delivery destination. Therefore only D is technically valid.","explanation_zh":"將多帳戶的 CloudWatch Logs 集中傳送到專用帳戶中的 S3 bucket，採用官方記載的 subscription 模式：在專用（接收方）帳戶建立一個 CloudWatch Logs destination，封裝一條以該 S3 bucket 為目標的 Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream；並在每個發送方帳戶建立指向該 destination 的 subscription filter。由於 subscription filter 僅涵蓋建立當下已存在的 log group，要滿足「所有現有與未來」的 log group，還需要自動化：建立一條在 CloudTrail CreateLogGroup 事件觸發的 Amazon EventBridge rule，呼叫一個 Lambda function，對每個新建立的 log group 呼叫 CloudWatch Logs 的 PutSubscriptionFilter API。這正是選項 D，並符合 AWS 關於使用 Firehose 進行跨帳戶跨區域 subscription 的文件。選項 A、B、C 都依賴 AWS Backup（Organizations 的 backup policies 即 AWS Backup policies），但 AWS Backup 功能可用性的資源表並未將 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 列為受支援的資源類型，且 AWS Backup 會把 recovery point 寫入 backup vault，而非將任意 S3 bucket 指定為傳送目的地的「backup vault」。因此只有 D 在技術上可行。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Organizations 'backup policies' configure AWS Backup, which does not support CloudWatch Logs log groups as a resource type, so it cannot 'back up all log groups to a dedicated S3 bucket.' Adding an S3 bucket policy grants access but creates no log-delivery mechanism.","why_zh":"AWS Organizations 的 backup policies 用於設定 AWS Backup，而 AWS Backup 不支援 CloudWatch Logs log group 此資源類型，因此無法把所有 log group 備份到專用 S3 bucket；加上 S3 bucket policy 只是授予存取權，並不會建立任何日誌傳送機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Backup does not support assigning CloudWatch Logs log groups to a backup plan (not a supported resource type), and a backup vault is an AWS Backup managed container, not an arbitrary S3 bucket. This design cannot deliver log data to the S3 bucket.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 不支援將 CloudWatch Logs log group 指派到 backup plan（非受支援資源類型），且 backup vault 是 AWS Backup 管理的容器，並非任意 S3 bucket，因此此設計無法把日誌資料送到 S3 bucket。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same fundamental flaw as B: CloudWatch Logs is not an AWS Backup-supported resource, and a backup vault is not an S3 bucket. The added Systems Manager Automation runbook and AWS Config remediation to cover future log groups cannot fix the fact that log groups cannot be backed up by AWS Backup at all.","why_zh":"與 B 有相同的根本缺陷：CloudWatch Logs 並非 AWS Backup 受支援資源，且 backup vault 不是 S3 bucket。額外加上 Systems Manager Automation runbook 與 AWS Config 自動修復來涵蓋未來 log group，仍無法改變 log group 根本無法被 AWS Backup 備份的事實。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CrossAccountSubscriptions-Firehose-Account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters-AccountLevel.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/backup-feature-availability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/writing-with-cloudwatch-logs.html"]}},{"id":282,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer manages a Java-based application that runs in an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster on AWS Fargate. Auto scaling has not been configured for the application. The DevOps engineer has determined that the Java Virtual Machine (JVM) thread count is a good indicator of when to scale the application. The application serves customer traffic on port 8080 and makes JVM metrics available on port 9404. Application use has recently increased. The DevOps engineer needs to configure auto scaling for the application. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师管理着一个基于 Java 的应用程序，该程序在 AWS Fargate 上的 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）集群中运行。该应用程序尚未配置自动扩展功能。 DevOps 工程师已确定 Java 虚拟机（JVM）线程数是决定何时扩展应用程序的一个良好指标。该应用程序在 8080 端口为客户提供服务，并在 9404 端口提供 JVM 指标。 应用程序的使用量近来有所增加。开发运维工程师需要为该应用程序配置自动扩展功能。 哪种解决方案能在运营开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the Amazon CloudWatch agent as a container sidecar. Configure the CloudWatch agent to retrieve JVM metrics from port 9404. Create CloudWatch alarms on the JVM thread count metric to scale the application. Add a step scaling policy in Fargate to scale up and scale down based on the CloudWatch alarms.","B":"Deploy the Amazon CloudWatch agent as a container sidecar. Configure a metric filter for the JVM thread count metric on the CloudWatch log group for the CloudWatch agent. Add a target tracking policy in Fargate. Select the metric from the metric filter as a scale target.","C":"Create an Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace. Deploy AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry as a container sidecar to publish the JVM metrics from port 9404 to the Prometheus workspace. Configure rules for the workspace to use the JVM thread count metric to scale the application. Add a step scaling policy in Fargate. Select the Prometheus rules to scale up and scaling down.","D":"Create an Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace. Deploy AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry as a container sidecar to retrieve JVM metrics from port 9404 to publish the JVM metrics from port 9404 to the Prometheus workspace. Add a target tracking policy in Fargate. Select the Prometheus metric as a scale target."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Amazon CloudWatch 代理部署为容器的侧边车。配置 CloudWatch 代理从 9404 端口获取 JVM 指标。 根据 JVM 线程数指标创建 CloudWatch 警报以对应用程序进行扩展。在 Fargate 中添加一个步进扩 展策略，根据 CloudWatch 警报进行扩展和缩减。","B":"将 Amazon CloudWatch 代理部署为容器的边车。在 CloudWatch 代理的 CloudWatch 日志组上为 JVM 线程计数指标配置一个指标筛选器。在 Fargate 中添加一个目标跟踪策略。从指标筛选器中选择该 指标作为缩放目标。","C":"创建一个 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 工作区。将 AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry 作为容器边 车部署，将来自 9404 端口的 JVM 指标发布到 Prometheus 工作区。为工作区配置规则，使用 JVM 线 程数指标来扩展应用程序。在 Fargate 中添加一个步进扩展策略。选择用于扩展和缩减的 Prometheus 规则。","D":"创建一个 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 工作区。部署 AWS Distro for Prometheus。 将 OpenTelemetry 作为容器的侧车，从 9404 端口获取 JVM 指标，并将这些 JVM 指标从 9404 端 口发布到 Prometheus 工作区。在 Fargate 中添加一个目标跟踪策略。选择 Prometheus 指标作为缩 放目标。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Amazon ECS Service Auto Scaling is implemented by Application Auto Scaling, which acts only on CloudWatch metrics and the CloudWatch alarms it creates (the ECS docs explicitly note 'you cannot create CloudWatch alarms for metrics that do not exist'). Both step scaling and target tracking therefore require the JVM thread count to be a CloudWatch metric. The CloudWatch agent can run as a Fargate sidecar (awsvpc), scrape the Prometheus/JVM endpoint on port 9404, and emit the metrics to CloudWatch as embedded-metric-format log events in the /aws/ecs/containerinsights/<cluster>/prometheus log group, which become CloudWatch metrics. Option A (CloudWatch agent sidecar -> CloudWatch alarm on JVM thread count -> step scaling) and Option B (CloudWatch agent sidecar -> extract the metric from the agent's CloudWatch log group -> target tracking on that custom metric) are both complete, valid, low-overhead CloudWatch-native paths. Options C and D both route the metrics into an Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus workspace via ADOT; AMP recording/alerting rules and AMP (Prometheus) metrics cannot drive ECS Application Auto Scaling, which needs CloudWatch alarms/metrics, so neither C's 'select the Prometheus rules to scale' nor D's 'select the Prometheus metric as a scale target' is supported. They also add an entire managed Prometheus workspace, increasing operational overhead. Hence the two correct answers are A and B; the dump's [A, D] is wrong because D is technically unsupported.","explanation_zh":"Amazon ECS Service Auto Scaling 由 Application Auto Scaling 實作，只能依據 CloudWatch 指標與它自動建立的 CloudWatch 警示來運作（ECS 文件明確指出『無法為不存在的指標建立 CloudWatch 警示』）。因此不論 step scaling 或 target tracking，JVM thread count 都必須先成為 CloudWatch 指標。CloudWatch agent 可作為 Fargate sidecar（awsvpc）執行，抓取 port 9404 的 Prometheus/JVM 端點，並以 embedded metric format（EMF）日誌事件寫入 /aws/ecs/containerinsights/<cluster>/prometheus 日誌群組，進而成為 CloudWatch 指標。選項 A（CloudWatch agent sidecar -> 對 JVM thread count 設 CloudWatch 警示 -> step scaling）與選項 B（CloudWatch agent sidecar -> 從 agent 的 CloudWatch 日誌群組擷取指標 -> 以該自訂指標做 target tracking）皆為完整、可行且低營運負擔的 CloudWatch 原生路徑。選項 C 與 D 都透過 ADOT 將指標送入 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus（AMP）工作區；AMP 的 recording/alerting rules 與 AMP（Prometheus）指標無法驅動需要 CloudWatch 警示/指標的 ECS Application Auto Scaling，因此 C 的『選 Prometheus rules 來擴縮』與 D 的『選 Prometheus 指標作為 scale target』都不被支援，且還額外建立整個受管 Prometheus 工作區，反而增加營運負擔。故正確答案為 A 與 B；題庫的 [A, D] 有誤，因為 D 在技術上不被支援。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"ECS step scaling is driven by CloudWatch alarms via Application Auto Scaling. Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus recording/alerting rules cannot be selected as the source for an ECS step scaling policy; AMP alerts route to Alertmanager/SNS, not to Application Auto Scaling. Also adds a full AMP workspace plus ADOT, increasing operational overhead.","why_zh":"ECS step scaling 透過 Application Auto Scaling 以 CloudWatch 警示驅動。Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus 的 recording/alerting rules 無法作為 ECS step scaling 政策的來源；AMP 警示送往 Alertmanager/SNS，而非 Application Auto Scaling。且額外建立整個 AMP 工作區與 ADOT，增加營運負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Application Auto Scaling target tracking requires a CloudWatch metric; you cannot select an Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus (Prometheus) metric directly as a scale target. The metric lives in AMP, not CloudWatch, so target tracking cannot reference it. This is the dump's suggested answer but is technically unsupported, and it adds an AMP workspace, raising overhead.","why_zh":"Application Auto Scaling target tracking 需要 CloudWatch 指標；無法直接將 Amazon Managed Service for Prometheus（Prometheus）指標選為 scale target。指標位於 AMP 而非 CloudWatch，故 target tracking 無法引用。這是題庫建議答案，但技術上不被支援，且額外建立 AMP 工作區，增加負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/service-auto-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/service-autoscaling-targettracking.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/application/userguide/target-tracking-scaling-policy-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContainerInsights-Prometheus-Setup-ECS.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContainerInsights-Prometheus-Setup-configure-ECS.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Embedded_Metric_Format.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prometheus/latest/userguide/AMP-alert-manager.html"]}},{"id":283,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs in a single AWS Region. The application runs on an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster and connects to an Amazon Aurora MySQL cluster. The application is built in an AWS CodeBuild project. The container images are published to Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). The company needs to replicate the state of the application for the container images and the database to a second Region. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个在单个 AWS 区域运行的应用程序。该应用程序在 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service （Amazon EKS）集群上运行，并连接到 Amazon Aurora MySQL 集群。应用程序是在 AWS CodeBuild 项目中构建的。容器镜像发布到 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）。 该公司需要将容器镜像和数据库的应用状态复制到第二个区域。 哪种解决方案能以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Turn on Amazon S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) on the bucket that holds the ECR container images. Deploy the application to an EKS cluster in the second Region by referencing the new S3 bucket object URL for the container image in a Kubernetes deployment file. Configure a cross-Region Aurora Replica in the second Region. Configure the new application deployment to use the endpoints for the cross-Region Aurora Replica.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to image pushes to the ECR repository. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to replicate the image to a new ECR repository in the second Region. Deploy the application to an EKS cluster in the second Region by referencing the new ECR repository in a Kubernetes deployment file. Configure a cross-Region Aurora Replica in the second Region. Configure the new application deployment to use the endpoints for the cross-Region Aurora Replica.","C":"Turn on Cross-Region Replication to replicate the ECR repository to the second Region. Deploy the application to an EKS cluster in the second Region by referencing the new ECR repository in a Kubernetes deployment file. Configure an Aurora global database with clusters in the initial Region and the second Region. Configure the new application deployment to use the endpoints for the second Region's cluster in the Aurora global database.","D":"Configure the CodeBuild project to also push the container image to an ECR repository in the second Region. Deploy the application to an EKS cluster in the second Region by referencing the new ECR repository in a Kubernetes deployment file. Configure an Aurora MySQL cluster in the second Region as the target for binary log replication from the Aurora MySQL cluster in the initial Region. Configure the new application deployment to use the endpoints for the second Region's cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在保存 ECR 容器镜像的存储桶上启用 Amazon S3 跨区域复制（CRR）。通过在 Kubernetes 部署文 件中引用新 S3 存储桶对象 URL 来将应用程序部署到第二个区域的 EKS 集群。在第二个区域配置 跨区域 Aurora 副本。将新的应用程序部署配置为使用跨区域 Aurora 副本的端点。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，使其对推送到 ECR 存储库的镜像作出反应。配置 EventBridge 规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函数，将镜像复制到第二个区域的新 ECR 存储库。通过在 Kubernetes 部 署文件中引用新的 ECR 存储库，将应用程序部署到第二个区域的 EKS 集群。在第二个区域配置跨 区域 Aurora 副本。配置新的应用程序部署以使用跨区域 Aurora 副本的端点。","C":"启用跨区域复制功能，将 ECR 仓库复制到第二个区域。通过在 Kubernetes 部署文件中引用新的 ECR 仓库，将应用程序部署到第二个区域的 EKS 集群。配置一个包含初始区域和第二个区域集群的 Aurora 全球数据库。将新的应用程序部署配置为使用 Aurora 全球数据库中第二个区域集群的端点。","D":"将 CodeBuild 项目配置为还将容器镜像推送到第二个区域的 ECR 存储库。通过在 Kubernetes 部署 文件中引用新的 ECR 存储库，将应用程序部署到第二个区域的 EKS 集群。在第二个区域配置一 个 Aurora MySQL 集群 将初始区域中的 Aurora MySQL 集群的二进制日志复制目标设置为该新应用部署。配置新应用部署 以使用第二个区域集群的端点。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to replicate both the container images and the database state to a second Region in the MOST operationally efficient way, which favors native fully managed AWS features over custom-built pipelines. Option C pairs the two correct managed features. Amazon ECR private registry replication is a built-in, configuration-only feature: you add a replication rule and ECR automatically replicates images to the destination Region's repository, with no custom code, IAM, or pipeline to operate. For the database, Aurora global database automatically synchronizes all changes from the primary cluster to up to 10 secondary Regions using dedicated, storage-level replication infrastructure with latency typically under a second, and it is the AWS-recommended cross-Region HA/DR option for Aurora. The application in the second Region simply references the replicated ECR repository in its Kubernetes deployment and connects to the secondary cluster's endpoints. This combination minimizes operational overhead because both replication mechanisms are fully managed by AWS rather than custom-built or manually maintained.","explanation_zh":"需求是以最具運維效率的方式將容器映像與資料庫狀態複製到第二個 Region，這偏好使用原生、全託管的 AWS 功能，而非自行建置的管線。Option C 結合了兩個正確的託管功能。Amazon ECR private registry replication 是內建、僅需設定的功能：只要新增複製規則，ECR 就會自動將映像複製到目的 Region 的儲存庫，無需自訂程式碼、IAM 或維運任何管線。資料庫方面，Aurora global database 會以專用的儲存層複製基礎設施，自動將主叢集的所有變更同步到最多 10 個次要 Region，延遲通常低於一秒，且是 AWS 推薦的 Aurora 跨 Region HA/DR 選項。第二 Region 的應用程式只需在其 Kubernetes deployment 中引用已複製的 ECR 儲存庫，並連線到次要叢集的端點。此組合運維負擔最低，因為兩種複製機制皆由 AWS 全託管，而非自行建置或手動維護。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"ECR does not expose a customer-configurable S3 bucket on which you can enable S3 Cross-Region Replication, and a Kubernetes deployment cannot pull a container image from an 'S3 bucket object URL' — EKS pulls images from an ECR registry endpoint. The described mechanism is technically invalid. The cross-Region Aurora Replica is also less efficient than a managed global database.","why_zh":"ECR 不提供可由客戶設定並啟用 S3 Cross-Region Replication 的 S3 儲存桶，Kubernetes deployment 也無法從『S3 bucket object URL』拉取容器映像——EKS 是從 ECR registry 端點拉取映像。所述機制在技術上無效。cross-Region Aurora Replica 的效率也低於託管的 global database。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building an EventBridge rule plus a Lambda function to copy images to a second-Region ECR repository re-implements functionality that ECR already provides natively as private registry cross-Region replication. This custom pipeline adds code, IAM, and failure handling to operate, so it is far less operationally efficient than the built-in feature.","why_zh":"建立 EventBridge 規則加 Lambda 函式來把映像複製到第二 Region 的 ECR 儲存庫，等於重新實作 ECR 原生提供的 private registry cross-Region replication。此自訂管線需維運程式碼、IAM 與失敗處理，運維效率遠低於內建功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Configuring CodeBuild to push to a second-Region repository ties replication to every build and breaks if a build/push fails, and it only covers images produced by that build pipeline. Manually configuring binary log replication between two independent Aurora clusters is the most manual, highest-overhead database option versus a managed Aurora global database.","why_zh":"設定 CodeBuild 推送到第二 Region 儲存庫會把複製綁在每次建置上，建置/推送失敗即中斷，且僅涵蓋該建置管線產生的映像。手動在兩個獨立 Aurora 叢集間設定 binary log 複製，是相較於託管 Aurora global database 最手動、運維負擔最高的資料庫選項。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/registry-settings-configure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/aurora-replication-options/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-disaster-recovery.html"]}},{"id":284,"question_en":"A company is building a serverless application that uses AWS Lambda functions to process data. A BeginResponse Lambda function initializes data in response to specific application events. The company needs to ensure that a large number of Lambda functions are invoked after the BeginResponse Lambda function runs. Each Lambda function must be invoked in parallel and depends on only the outputs of the BeginResponse Lambda function. Each Lambda function has retry logic for invocation and must be able to fine-tune concurrency without losing data. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司正在构建一个无服务器应用程序，该程序使用 AWS Lambda 函数来处理数据。 一个名为 BeginResponse 的 Lambda 函数会在特定的应用程序事件发生时初始化数据。该公司需要确保在 BeginResponse Lambda 函数运行之后能够并行调用大量其他 Lambda 函数。每个 Lambda 函数仅依赖于 BeginResponse Lambda 函数的输出结果，并且必须能够并行调用。每个 Lambda 函数都具有调用重试逻辑， 并且必须能够在不丢失数据的情况下对并发进行微调。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Modify the BeginResponse Lambda function to publish to the SNS topic before the BeginResponse Lambda function finishes running. Subscribe all Lambda functions that need to invoke after the BeginResponse Lambda function runs to the SNS topic. Subscribe any new Lambda functions to the SNS topic.","B":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue for each Lambda function that needs to run after the BeginResponse Lambda function runs. Subscribe each Lambda function to its own SQS queue. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe each SQS queue to the SNS topic. Modify the BeginResponse function to publish to the SNS topic when it finishes running.","C":"Create an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue for each Lambda function that needs to run after the BeginResponse Lambda function runs. Subscribe the Lambda function to the SQS queue. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic for each SQS queue. Subscribe the SQS queues to the SNS topics. Modify the BeginResponse function to publish to the SNS topics when the function finishes running.","D":"Create an AWS Step Functions Standard Workflow. Configure states in the workflow to invoke the Lambda functions sequentially. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Modify the BeginResponse Lambda function to publish to the SNS topic before the Lambda function finishes running. Create a new Lambda function that is subscribed to the SNS topic and that invokes the Step Functions workflow."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。修改 BeginResponse Lambda 函数，使其在运行结 束前向 SNS 主题发布消息。将所有需要在 BeginResponse Lambda 函数运行后调用的 Lambda 函数订 阅到 SNS 主题。将任何新的 Lambda 函数订阅到 SNS 主题。","B":"为每个需要在 BeginResponse Lambda 函数运行之后运行的 Lambda 函数创建一个 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列。将每个 Lambda 函数订阅到其自身的 SQS 队列。创建一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。将每个 SQS 队列订阅到 SNS 主题。修改 BeginResponse 函数，使其在运行结束时发布到 SNS 主题。","C":"为每个需要在 BeginResponse Lambda 函数运行之后运行的 Lambda 函数创建一个 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列。将该 Lambda 函数订阅到 SQS 队列。为每个 SQS 队列创建一 个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。将 SQS 队列订阅到 SNS 主题。修改 BeginResponse 函数，使其在运行结束时发布到 SNS 主题。","D":"创建一个 AWS Step Functions 标准工作流。在工作流中配置状态以按顺序调用 Lambda 函数。创建 一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。修改 BeginResponse Lambda 函数，使其在函数 运行结束前向 SNS 主题发布消息。创建一个新的 Lambda 函数，使其订阅 SNS 主题并调用 Step Functions 工作流。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical SNS-to-SQS fan-out-with-buffer pattern. The BeginResponse function publishes a single message to one SNS topic when it finishes running; SNS replicates that message to one dedicated SQS queue per downstream Lambda, and each Lambda consumes its own queue via an event source mapping. This satisfies every requirement: all consumers run in parallel and depend only on the BeginResponse outputs; SQS standard queues persist messages with at-least-once delivery and redundant multi-AZ storage, so data is not lost; the Lambda SQS event source mapping automatically retries (and can use a DLQ); and each function's concurrency can be fine-tuned independently using the SQS maximum concurrency setting or provisioned mode, while the queue buffers any backlog so no data is lost during throttling. Adding a new downstream function only requires creating one more queue and one subscription, giving the most operational efficiency. (Note that B also publishes at the correct time, when BeginResponse finishes, unlike A and D which publish before it finishes.)","explanation_zh":"這是標準的 SNS 至 SQS 扇出加緩衝 (fan-out with buffer) 模式。BeginResponse 函式在執行完成時向單一 SNS topic 發布一則訊息;SNS 將該訊息複製到每個下游 Lambda 各自專屬的 SQS 佇列,每個 Lambda 透過事件來源對應 (event source mapping) 消費自己的佇列。這滿足所有需求:所有消費者並行執行且僅依賴 BeginResponse 的輸出;SQS standard queue 以至少一次傳遞 (at-least-once) 並跨多個可用區冗餘儲存來持久保存訊息,因此不會遺失資料;Lambda 的 SQS 事件來源對應會自動重試(亦可搭配 DLQ);每個函式可透過 SQS 的 maximum concurrency 設定或 provisioned mode 獨立微調並行度,而佇列會緩衝任何積壓,使限流期間不會遺失資料。新增下游函式只需再建立一個佇列與一個訂閱,操作效率最高。(此外 B 在正確時機發布,即 BeginResponse 完成時,而非 A 與 D 在其完成前就發布。)","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"SNS subscribing Lambda functions directly is push-based and messages do not persist. If a consumer is throttled or fails beyond SNS's async delivery retries, the message is lost (no controllable buffer), so you cannot fine-tune per-consumer concurrency without losing data. Publishing before BeginResponse finishes also risks sending before the outputs are ready.","why_zh":"SNS 直接訂閱 Lambda 為推送式且訊息不持久保存。若消費者被限流或在 SNS 非同步傳遞重試耗盡後失敗,訊息會遺失(沒有可控制的緩衝),因此無法在不遺失資料的前提下微調各消費者的並行度。在 BeginResponse 完成前就發布也可能在輸出尚未就緒時送出。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating one SNS topic per SQS queue defeats fan-out: BeginResponse must publish to every topic separately (N publishes and N code/config changes per new function), which is more operational overhead and redundant compared to a single topic with multiple subscriptions.","why_zh":"為每個 SQS 佇列各建一個 SNS topic 破壞了扇出的意義:BeginResponse 必須分別向每個 topic 發布(每新增一個函式就要 N 次發布與 N 處程式碼/設定變更),相較於單一 topic 多訂閱,操作負擔更大且多餘。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Step Functions Standard Workflow invoking the Lambdas sequentially directly violates the parallel requirement (would need a Parallel or Map state), and it adds an extra Lambda plus workflow layer, increasing operational overhead. Publishing before BeginResponse finishes is also the wrong timing.","why_zh":"Step Functions Standard Workflow 以「循序」方式呼叫 Lambda 直接違反並行需求(需使用 Parallel 或 Map 狀態),且額外增加一個 Lambda 與工作流程層,提高操作負擔。在 BeginResponse 完成前就發布也是錯誤時機。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-sqs-as-subscriber.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/standard-queues.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/services-sqs-scaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-sqs.html"]}},{"id":285,"question_en":"A company operates a globally deployed product out of multiple AWS Regions. The company's DevOps team needs to use Amazon API Gateway to deploy an API to support the product. The API must be deployed redundantly. The deployment must provide independent availability from each company location. The deployment also must respond to a custom domain URL and must optimize performance for the API user requests. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司通过多个 AWS 区域运营一款全球部署的产品。该公司的 DevOps 团队需要使用亚马逊 API 网 关来部署一个 API 以支持该产品。 该 API 必须冗余部署。部署必须为每个公司地点提供独立的可用性。部署还必须响应自定义域名 URL， 并且必须优化 API 用户请求的性能。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an API Gateway edge-optimized API endpoint in the us-east-1 Region. Create an API Gateway custom domain for the API. Create an Amazon Route 53 record set with a geoproximity routing policy for the API's custom domain. Increase the geographic bias to the maximum allowed value.","B":"Deploy an API Gateway regional API endpoint in the us-east-1 Region. Integrate the API Gateway API with a public Application Load Balancer (ALB). Create an AWS Global Accelerator standard accelerator. Associate the endpoint with the ALB. Create an Amazon Route 53 alias record set that points the custom domain name to the DNS name that is assigned to the accelerator.","C":"Deploy an API Gateway regional API endpoint in every AWS Region where the company's product is deployed. Create an API Gateway custom domain in each Region for the deployed API Gateway API. Create an Amazon Route 53 record set that has a latency routing policy for every deployed API Gateway custom domain.","D":"Deploy an API Gateway edge-optimized API endpoint in the us-east-1 Region. Create an Amazon CloudFront distribution. Configure the CloudFront distribution with an alternate domain name. Specify the API Gateway Invoke URL as the origin domain. Create an Amazon Route 53 alias record set with a simple routing policy. Point the routing policy to the CloudFront distribution domain name."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 us-east-1 区域部署一个 API 网关边缘优化的 API 端点。为该 API 创建一个 API 网关自定义域名。为 该 API 的自定义域名创建一个具有地理邻近性路由策略的 Amazon Route 53 记录集。将地理偏差增加 到允许的最大值。","B":"在 us-east-1 区域部署 API 网关的区域 API 端点。将 API 网关 API 与公共应用负载均衡器（ALB）集 成。创建一个 AWS 全球加速器标准加速器。将端点与 ALB 关联。创建一个指向分配给加速器的 DNS 名称的自定义域名的 Amazon Route 53 别名记录集。","C":"在公司产品部署的每个 AWS 区域中部署一个 API 网关区域 API 端点。在每个区域为部署的 API 网 关 API 创建一个自定义域名。为每个部署的 API 网关自定义域名创建一个具有延迟路由策略的 Amazon Route 53 记录集。","D":"在 us-east-1 区域部署一个 API 网关边缘优化的 API 端点。创建一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发。使用备 用域名配置 CloudFront 分发。将 API 网关调用 URL 指定为源域名。使用简单路由策略创建一个 Amazon Route 53 别名记录集。将路由策略指向 CloudFront 分发的域名。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: redundant deployment, independent availability from each company location, a custom domain URL, and optimized performance for API user requests. Only option C deploys the API as a Regional API Gateway endpoint in every Region where the product runs, giving each location its own independent failure domain (true redundancy and independent availability). AWS documentation states directly: 'If you deploy a Regional API in multiple Regions, it can have the same custom domain name in all Regions. You can use custom domains together with Amazon Route 53 to perform tasks such as latency-based routing.' Route 53 latency-based routing then 'serves their requests from the AWS Region that provides the lowest latency,' optimizing performance for users. Options A, B, and D each deploy only a single endpoint (in us-east-1), so a Region-level failure takes down the entire API; none provide redundancy or independent per-location availability, which immediately disqualifies them.","explanation_zh":"需求為：冗餘部署、各據點獨立可用性、自訂網域 URL，以及為 API 使用者請求最佳化效能。只有選項 C 在產品運行的每個 Region 都部署 Regional API Gateway 端點，讓每個據點擁有獨立的故障隔離域(真正的冗餘與獨立可用性)。AWS 官方文件明確指出：『若您在多個 Region 部署 Regional API，它可在所有 Region 使用相同的自訂網域名稱。您可將自訂網域與 Amazon Route 53 搭配，執行如 latency-based routing 之類的工作。』Route 53 latency-based routing 接著會『從延遲最低的 AWS Region 提供請求服務』，為使用者最佳化效能。選項 A、B、D 都只在單一 Region(us-east-1)部署單一端點，因此 Region 層級的故障會使整個 API 失效；它們都無法提供冗餘或各據點獨立的可用性，因此立即被排除。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Deploys only a single edge-optimized endpoint in us-east-1, so it is not redundant and provides no independent availability per location; a us-east-1 outage takes down the whole API. Geoproximity routing with maximum bias is pointless against a single endpoint and is the wrong tool for the multi-Region latency optimization this scenario needs.","why_zh":"只在 us-east-1 部署單一 edge-optimized 端點，因此非冗餘且無法提供各據點獨立可用性；us-east-1 中斷會使整個 API 失效。只有一個端點時最大偏差的 geoproximity routing 毫無意義，且非此情境所需多 Region 延遲最佳化的正確工具。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A single Regional endpoint in us-east-1 is not redundant. Global Accelerator improves network path performance but there is still only one origin Region, so there is no independent availability per location. The ALB-in-front-of-API-Gateway architecture is also contrived and not the documented pattern.","why_zh":"us-east-1 的單一 Regional 端點並非冗餘。Global Accelerator 改善網路路徑效能，但仍只有一個來源 Region，因此無法提供各據點獨立可用性。將 ALB 置於 API Gateway 前的架構也屬牽強，並非文件記載的模式。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A single edge-optimized endpoint in us-east-1 fronted by a manual CloudFront distribution is still a single-Region deployment, so it is not redundant. Edge-optimized endpoints already use a service-managed CloudFront distribution, so adding a second one is contradictory; simple routing to one distribution gives no per-location independence.","why_zh":"us-east-1 的單一 edge-optimized 端點再加上手動建立的 CloudFront distribution，仍是單一 Region 部署，因此非冗餘。edge-optimized 端點本身已使用服務管理的 CloudFront distribution，再加一個自相矛盾；對單一 distribution 使用 simple routing 也無法提供各據點獨立性。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/api-gateway-api-endpoint-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-latency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-regional-api-custom-domain-create.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-to-api-gateway.html"]}},{"id":286,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer uses AWS CodeBuild to frequently produce software packages. The CodeBuild project builds large Docker images that the DevOps engineer can use across multiple builds. The DevOps engineer wants to improve build performance and minimize costs. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS CodeBuild 定期生成软件包。CodeBuild 项目构建大型 Docker 镜像，该 DevOps 工程师可在多 个构建中使用这些镜像。 这位 DevOps 工程师想要提升构建性能并降低费用。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Store the Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Implement a local Docker layer cache for CodeBuild.","B":"Cache the Docker images in an Amazon S3 bucket that is available across multiple build hosts. Expire the cache by using an S3 Lifecycle policy.","C":"Store the Docker images in an Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository. Modify the CodeBuild project runtime configuration to always use the most recent image version.","D":"Create custom AMIs that contain the cached Docker images. In the CodeBuild build, launch Amazon EC2 instances from the custom AMIs."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 Docker 镜像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储库中。为 CodeBuild 实现本地 Docker 层 缓存。","B":"将 Docker 镜像缓存在一个可在多个构建主机间访问的 Amazon S3 存储桶中。使用 S3 生命周期策略使缓存过期。","C":"将 Docker 镜像存储在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）存储库中。修改 CodeBuild 项目的运行时配置，使其始 终使用最新版本的镜像。","D":"创建包含缓存 Docker 镜像的自定义 AMI。在 CodeBuild 构建过程中，从自定义 AMI 启动 Amazon EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodeBuild supports exactly two cache types: Amazon S3 and local. Local caching offers a Docker layer cache mode, which the AWS docs explicitly describe as 'a good choice for projects that build or pull large Docker images' because it 'can prevent the performance issues caused by pulling large Docker images down from the network.' This is the native, purpose-built CodeBuild feature for this exact scenario. Storing the images in Amazon ECR is a fully managed, low-cost private registry (no servers or AMIs to maintain), and enabling the local Docker layer cache reuses already-built/pulled layers on the build host so subsequent builds avoid re-pulling large images. Together this improves build performance and minimizes cost, making A correct.","explanation_zh":"CodeBuild 僅支援兩種快取類型: Amazon S3 與 local。Local caching 提供 Docker layer cache 模式, AWS 文件明確指出此模式『適合用於建置或拉取大型 Docker images 的專案』, 因為它『可避免從網路下載大型 Docker images 所造成的效能問題』。這正是 CodeBuild 為此情境量身打造的原生功能。將 images 儲存在 Amazon ECR 是完全受管、低成本的私有 registry (無需自行維運伺服器或 AMI), 再啟用 local Docker layer cache 即可在建置主機上重複使用已建置或已拉取的 layers, 讓後續建置免於重新拉取大型 images。兩者結合可提升建置效能並降低成本, 因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeBuild does not let you point a generic S3 bucket at Docker images as a shared layer cache the way described; its S3 cache is the dependency/artifact cache keyed to the project, not an arbitrary image store. For large Docker images, AWS docs say local caching is preferred precisely because pulling from the network (including S3) incurs network transfer time that hurts performance. This adds cost and latency rather than minimizing it.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 無法如題所述把一般 S3 bucket 當成共享的 Docker layer 快取; 其 S3 快取是與專案綁定的相依/成品快取, 而非任意 image 儲存區。針對大型 Docker images, AWS 文件指出 local caching 較佳, 正是因為從網路 (含 S3) 拉取會產生網路傳輸時間而拖累效能, 反而增加成本與延遲。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Storing images in ECR is fine, but merely configuring the runtime to 'always use the most recent image version' addresses image tagging/versioning and provides no layer caching or reuse mechanism; every build would still pull the large image fresh over the network, providing no performance gain. It ignores the actual caching feature CodeBuild offers.","why_zh":"將 images 存於 ECR 沒問題, 但僅設定 runtime『一律使用最新版 image』處理的是 image 標記/版本管理, 並不提供任何 layer 快取或重用機制; 每次建置仍會從網路重新拉取大型 image, 無法改善效能。此選項忽略了 CodeBuild 實際提供的快取功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeBuild is a managed build service; you do not launch EC2 instances from custom AMIs inside a CodeBuild build, and CodeBuild cannot use arbitrary custom AMIs as its environment. Building and maintaining custom AMIs adds significant operational overhead and cost, the opposite of the requirement, and is not how CodeBuild caching works.","why_zh":"CodeBuild 是受管建置服務; 你無法在 CodeBuild 建置中從自訂 AMI 啟動 EC2 執行個體, CodeBuild 也無法以任意自訂 AMI 作為其環境。建立與維護自訂 AMI 會帶來大量維運負擔與成本, 與需求相反, 且這並非 CodeBuild 快取的運作方式。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-caching.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/caching-local.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/specify-caching-local.html"]}},{"id":287,"question_en":"A large company recently acquired a small company. The large company invited the small company to join the large company's existing organization in AWS Organizations as a new OU. A DevOps engineer determines that the small company needs to launch t3.small Amazon EC2 instance types for the company's application workloads. The small company needs to deploy the instances only within US-based AWS Regions. The DevOps engineer needs to use an SCP in the small company's new OU to ensure that the small company can launch only the required instance types. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家大型公司最近收购了一家小型公司。大型公司邀请小型公司加入其在 AWS 组织中现有的组织结构，作为新的组织单元（OU）。 一位 DevOps 工程师确定，这家小公司需要为其应用程序工作负载启动 t3.small 类型的亚马逊 EC2 实例。该公司仅需在美国境内 的 AWS 区域内部署这些实例。 DevOps 工程师需要在这家小公司的新组织单位（OU）中使用安全组策略（SCP），以确保该公司只能启动所需的实例类型。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a statement to deny the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the ec2:InstanceType condition is not equal to t3.small. Configure another statement to deny the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the aws:RequestedRegion condition is not equal to us-*.","B":"Configure a statement to allow the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the ec2:InstanceType condition is not equal to t3.small. Configure another statement to allow the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the aws:RequestedRegion condition is not equal to us-*.","C":"Configure a statement to deny the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the ec2:InstanceType condition is equal to t3.small. Configure another statement to deny the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the aws:RequestedRegion condition is equal to us-*.","D":"Configure a statement to allow the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the ec2:InstanceType condition is equal to t3.small. Configure another statement to allow the ec2:RunInstances action for all EC2 instance resources when the aws:RequestedRegion condition is equal to us-*."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一条语句，当 ec2:InstanceType 条件不等于 t3.small 时，拒绝所有 EC2 实例资源的 ec2:RunInstances 操作。 配置另一条语句，当 `aws:RequestedRegion` 条件不等于 `us-*` 时，拒绝所有 EC2 实例资源的 `ec2：RunInstances` 操作。","B":"配置一条语句，允许对所有 EC2 实例资源执行 ec2:RunInstances 操作，条件是 ec2:InstanceType 不等于 t3.small。 配置另一条语句，允许在 aws:RequestedRegion 条件不等于 us-* 时对所有 EC2 实例资源执行 ec2:RunInstances 操作。","C":"配置一条语句，当 ec2:InstanceType 条件等于 t3.small 时，拒绝所有 EC2 实例资源的 ec2:RunInstances 操作。 配置另一条语句，当条件 aws:RequestedRegion 等于 us-* 时，拒绝所有 EC2 实例资源的 ec2:RunInstances 操作。","D":"配置一条语句，允许在 ec2:InstanceType 条件等于 t3.small 时对所有 EC2 实例资源执行 ec2:RunInstances 操作。 配置另一条语句，当 aws:RequestedRegion 条件等于 us-* 时，允许对所有 EC2 实例资源执行 ec2:RunInstances 操作。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to permit ONLY the t3.small instance type and ONLY US Regions. The correct guardrail is a deny-list SCP that works alongside the default FullAWSAccess allow policy. AWS docs state explicitly that 'No permissions are granted by an SCP; an SCP defines a permission guardrail, or sets limits,' and that 'Deny statements are a powerful way to implement restrictions.' Option A denies ec2:RunInstances when ec2:InstanceType is NOT equal to t3.small (StringNotEquals), blocking every other type, and denies ec2:RunInstances when aws:RequestedRegion is NOT equal to us-* (StringNotLike), blocking every non-US Region. The remaining permitted launches are exactly t3.small in US Regions, and because an explicit Deny overrides any Allow, the guardrail is enforced. aws:RequestedRegion is supported by all EC2 API actions, so it correctly scopes the Region restriction.","explanation_zh":"需求是只允許 t3.small 執行個體類型且只允許美國 Region。正確做法是與預設 FullAWSAccess allow 政策搭配運作的 deny-list SCP。AWS 文件明確指出「SCP 不授予任何權限，SCP 只定義權限護欄或設定上限」，且「Deny 陳述式是實作限制的強力方式」。選項 A 在 ec2:InstanceType 不等於 t3.small 時（StringNotEquals）拒絕 ec2:RunInstances，封鎖其他所有類型；並在 aws:RequestedRegion 不等於 us-* 時（StringNotLike）拒絕 ec2:RunInstances，封鎖所有非美國 Region。剩下被允許的啟動就剛好是美國 Region 的 t3.small，而由於明確的 Deny 永遠優先於 Allow，此護欄得以強制執行。aws:RequestedRegion 受所有 EC2 API 動作支援，因此能正確限定 Region。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The conditions are inverted. 'Allow ec2:RunInstances when ec2:InstanceType is NOT t3.small' would whitelist every type except t3.small, and 'Allow when Region is NOT us-*' would whitelist all non-US Regions, which is the opposite of the requirement and does not restrict launches to t3.small in US Regions.","why_zh":"條件被反轉。「在 InstanceType 不等於 t3.small 時 Allow」會把 t3.small 以外的所有類型加入白名單，「在 Region 不等於 us-* 時 Allow」會把所有非美國 Region 加入白名單，與需求相反，無法將啟動限制在美國 Region 的 t3.small。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Deny with EQUAL conditions inverts the intent: it denies ec2:RunInstances when the type IS t3.small and denies it when the Region IS us-*, so it blocks exactly what should be allowed.","why_zh":"Deny 搭配等於條件將意圖反轉：它在類型等於 t3.small 時拒絕、在 Region 等於 us-* 時拒絕，剛好封鎖了應該允許的內容。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Two independent Allow statements with EQUAL conditions do not enforce the joint constraint. Each statement allows on its own, so a request matching only the Region condition (for example m5.large in us-east-1) is still allowed by the second statement; the instance-type restriction is not enforced. A deny-list with negated conditions is required to limit to t3.small AND US Regions.","why_zh":"兩個獨立的 Allow 陳述式搭配等於條件無法強制聯合限制。每個陳述式各自獨立允許，因此只符合 Region 條件的請求（例如 us-east-1 的 m5.large）仍會被第二個陳述式允許，無法強制執行執行個體類型限制。要同時限制 t3.small 與美國 Region，需要使用帶否定條件的 deny-list。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_evaluation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_ec2_region.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html#condition-keys-requestedregion"]}},{"id":288,"question_en":"A DevOps team manages infrastructure for an application. The application uses long-running processes to process items from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. The application is deployed to an Auto Scaling group. The application recently experienced an issue where items were taking significantly longer to process. The queue exceeded the expected size, which prevented various business processes from functioning properly. The application records all logs to a third-party tool. The team is currently subscribed to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic that the team uses for alerts. The team needs to be alerted if the queue exceeds the expected size. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队负责管理应用程序的基础设施。该应用程序使用长期运行的进程来处理来自亚马逊简 单队列服务（Amazon SQS）队列中的项目。该应用程序部署在自动扩展组中。 该应用程序最近出现了一个问题，即处理项目所需的时间大幅增加。队列的规模超出了预期，导致各种 业务流程无法正常运行。该应用程序会将所有日志记录到第三方工具中。 该团队当前订阅了一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题，用于接收警报。如果队列超出预期 大小，团队需要收到警报。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch metric alarm with a period of 1 hour and a static threshold to alarm if the average of the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed metric is greater than the expected value. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch metric alarm with a period of 1 hour and a static threshold to alarm if the sum of the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible metric is greater than the expected value. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function that retrieves the ApproximateNumberOfMessages SQS queue attribute value and publishes the value as a new CloudWatch custom metric. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is scheduled to run every 5 minutes and that invokes the Lambda function. Configure a CloudWatch metrics alarm with a period of 1 hour and a static threshold to alarm if the sum of the new custom metric is greater than the expected value.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that checks the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed SQS queue attribute and compares the value to a defined expected size in the function. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is scheduled to run every 5 minutes and that invokes the Lambda function. When the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed SQS queue attribute exceeds the expected size, send a notification the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 指标报警，设置周期为 1 小时，并设定静态阈值，当 ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed 指标的平均值大于预期值时触发报警。将该报警配置为通知 SNS 主题。","B":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 指标报警，设置周期为 1 小时，并设定静态阈值，当 “ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible”指标的总和大于预期值时触发报警。将该报警配置为通 知 SNS 主题。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于获取 SQS 队列的“ApproximateNumberOfMessages”属性值，并将 该值作为新的 CloudWatch 自定义指标发布。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则每 5 分钟运 行一次并调用 Lambda 函数。配置一个 CloudWatch 指标警报，周期为 1 小时，设置静态阈值，如果 新自定义指标的总和大于预期值则发出警报。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数检查 SQS 队列的“ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed”（延 迟消息近似数量）属性，并将该值与函数中定义的预期大小进行比较。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，该规则每 5 分钟运行一次，并调用该 Lambda 函数。当“ApproximateNumberOfM essagesDelayed”SQS 队列属性超过预期大小时，向 SNS 主题发送通知。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario is a processing backlog: items take longer to process, so messages pile up as available-but-unprocessed in the queue. The correct CloudWatch metric for that backlog is ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible, which AWS defines as 'the number of messages currently available for retrieval and processing' and notes 'Reflects the current processing backlog in the queue. A consistently high value may indicate under-provisioned consumers or stuck processing logic.' Amazon SQS automatically publishes this metric to CloudWatch every minute under the AWS/SQS namespace, so a native static-threshold CloudWatch alarm wired to the team's existing SNS topic (option B) needs no custom code and is the MOST operationally efficient solution. Options C and D add a Lambda function plus an EventBridge schedule to reinvent a metric SQS already emits natively, increasing operational overhead. Options A and D use ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed, which only counts messages held back by a delay queue or the DelaySeconds parameter, not slow-processing backlog, so they monitor the wrong condition.","explanation_zh":"此情境是處理積壓 (backlog)：項目處理變慢，導致訊息以「可取得但未處理」的狀態堆積在佇列中。對應此積壓的正確 CloudWatch 指標是 ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible，AWS 將其定義為「目前可供取得與處理的訊息數量」，並指出「反映佇列當前的處理積壓；數值持續偏高可能表示消費者資源不足或處理邏輯卡住」。Amazon SQS 會在 AWS/SQS 命名空間下每分鐘自動將此指標發佈至 CloudWatch，因此使用原生靜態閾值 CloudWatch alarm 連接到團隊既有的 SNS topic（選項 B），無需任何自訂程式碼，是最具營運效率的解法。選項 C 與 D 額外加入 Lambda 函式加上 EventBridge 排程，去重新打造一個 SQS 已原生發佈的指標，增加營運負擔。選項 A 與 D 使用 ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed，該指標只計算因延遲佇列或 DelaySeconds 參數而暫時隱藏的訊息，並非處理變慢造成的積壓，因此監控的是錯誤的條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed, which only counts messages held back by a delay queue or per-message DelaySeconds, not the slow-processing backlog of available messages described in the scenario. Wrong metric, so the alarm would never fire for this issue.","why_zh":"使用 ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed，僅計算被延遲佇列或單一訊息 DelaySeconds 延後的訊息，並非情境所述因處理變慢造成的可用訊息積壓。指標錯誤，alarm 不會針對此問題觸發。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Builds a custom Lambda function plus an EventBridge schedule to publish a custom metric, duplicating data SQS already emits natively to CloudWatch every minute. Far higher operational overhead than a native alarm, so it fails the 'MOST operational efficiency' qualifier.","why_zh":"建立自訂 Lambda 函式加 EventBridge 排程來發佈自訂指標，重複了 SQS 已每分鐘原生發佈到 CloudWatch 的資料。營運負擔遠高於原生 alarm，不符合『營運效率最高』的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses a custom Lambda plus EventBridge schedule (higher operational overhead) AND checks ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed, the wrong attribute for a slow-processing backlog. Two problems at once.","why_zh":"使用自訂 Lambda 加 EventBridge 排程（營運負擔較高），且檢查 ApproximateNumberOfMessagesDelayed，對於處理變慢的積壓而言是錯誤屬性。同時存在兩個問題。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/sqs-available-cloudwatch-metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/monitoring-using-cloudwatch.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSSimpleQueueService/latest/SQSDeveloperGuide/dead-letter-queues-alarms-cloudwatch.html"]}},{"id":289,"question_en":"A large company runs critical workloads in multiple AWS accounts. The AWS accounts are managed under AWS Organizations with all features enabled. The company stores confidential customer data in an Amazon S3 bucket. Access to the S3 bucket requires multiple levels of approval. The company wants to monitor when the S3 bucket is accessed by using the AWS CLI. The company also wants insights into the various activities performed by other users on all other S3 buckets in the AWS accounts to detect any issues. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家大型公司在多个 AWS 账户中运行关键工作负载。这些 AWS 账户在 AWS 组织中进行管理，并启用 了所有功能。该公司将机密客户数据存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。访问该 S3 存储桶需要经过多级审批。 该公司希望使用 AWS 命令行界面（AWS CLI）来监控 S3 存储桶的访问时间。该公司还希望了解 AWS 账户中所有其他 S3 存储桶上其他用户执行的各种活动，以检测任何问题。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail that is delivered to Amazon CloudWatch in each AWS account. Enable data events logs for all S3 buckets. Use Amazon GuardDuty for anomaly detection in all the AWS accounts. Use Amazon Athena to perform SQL queries on the custom metrics created from the CloudTrail logs.","B":"Create an AWS CloudTrail organization trail that is delivered to Amazon CloudWatch in the Organizations management account. Enable data events logs for all S3 buckets. Use Amazon CloudWatch anomaly detection in all the AWS accounts. Use Amazon Athena to perform SQL queries on the custom metrics created from the CloudTrail logs.","C":"Create an AWS CloudTrail organization trail that is delivered to Amazon CloudWatch in the Organizations management account. Enable data events logs for all S3 buckets. Use Amazon CloudWatch anomaly detection in all the AWS accounts. Use Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights to perform SQL queries on the custom metrics created from the CloudTrail logs.","D":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail that is delivered to Amazon CloudWatch in each AWS account. Enable data events logs for all S3 buckets. Use a custom solution for anomaly detection in all the AWS accounts. Use Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights to perform SQL queries on the custom metrics created from the CloudTrail logs."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建一条交付至 Amazon CloudWatch 的 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。为所有 S3 存储桶 启用数据事件日志记录。在所有 AWS 账户中使用 Amazon GuardDuty 进行异常检测。使用 Amazon Athena 对从 CloudTrail 日志创建的自定义指标执行 SQL 查询。","B":"在组织管理账户中创建一个交付至 Amazon CloudWatch 的 AWS CloudTrail 组织跟踪。为所有 S3 存 储桶启用数据事件日志记录。在所有 AWS 账户中使用 Amazon CloudWatch 异常检测功能。使用 Amazon Athena 对从 CloudTrail 日志创建的自定义指标执行 SQL 查询。","C":"在组织管理账户中创建一个交付至 Amazon CloudWatch 的 AWS CloudTrail 组织跟踪。为所有 S3 存 储桶启用数据事件日志记录。在所有 AWS 账户中使用 Amazon CloudWatch 异常检测功能。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights 对从 CloudTrail 日志创建的自定义指标执行 SQL 查询。","D":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建一条交付至 Amazon CloudWatch 的 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。为所有 S3 存储桶 启用数据事件日志记录。在所有 AWS 账户中使用自定义解决方案进行异常检测。使用 Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights 对从 CloudTrail 日志创建的自定义指标执行 SQL 查询。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The workloads span multiple accounts under AWS Organizations with all features enabled, so a single AWS CloudTrail organization trail (created in the management or delegated administrator account) is the correct way to capture events across every account; this rules out options A and D, which create a separate trail in each account. With data events enabled for all S3 buckets and the trail delivered to CloudWatch Logs, a metric filter can produce a custom metric and alarm that fires when the confidential bucket is accessed by the AWS CLI, and CloudWatch anomaly detection (supported on custom metrics) flags unusual behavior. The deciding factor between B and C is the analytics tool. The requirement to gain 'insights into the various activities performed by other users on all other S3 buckets to detect issues' means querying the actual CloudTrail event records (who did what, on which bucket, from which source IP). Amazon Athena queries CloudTrail log files directly from S3 and is documented to 'isolate activity by attributes, such as source IP address or user,' and there is a dedicated procedure for an organization-wide trail. Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights (option C) is a SQL engine that only queries numeric CloudWatch metrics using AVG/COUNT/MAX/MIN/SUM over metric namespaces and dimensions; it cannot surface per-event activity detail, so it cannot satisfy the activity-insights requirement. The first analyst's claim that the deciding factor is 'Athena cannot query CloudWatch metrics' misreads the requirement: the functional need is to analyze CloudTrail activity, which is exactly Athena's job and exactly what Metrics Insights cannot do. Therefore B is correct.","explanation_zh":"工作負載分布在啟用所有功能的 AWS Organizations 多個帳戶中，因此在管理帳戶（或委派管理員帳戶）建立單一的 AWS CloudTrail organization trail 才是跨所有帳戶擷取事件的正確方式；這排除了在每個帳戶各自建立 trail 的 A 與 D。為所有 S3 buckets 啟用 data events 並將 trail 傳送到 CloudWatch Logs 後，可用 metric filter 產生自訂 metric 與 alarm，當機密 bucket 被 AWS CLI 存取時觸發；而 CloudWatch anomaly detection（支援自訂 metrics）可標示異常行為。B 與 C 的關鍵差異在分析工具。題目要求『深入了解其他使用者在所有其他 S3 buckets 上執行的各種活動以偵測問題』，這需要查詢實際的 CloudTrail 事件記錄（誰做了什麼、針對哪個 bucket、來源 IP 為何）。Amazon Athena 可直接從 S3 查詢 CloudTrail 記錄檔，官方文件說明其能『依來源 IP 位址或使用者等屬性區隔活動』，並有針對 organization-wide trail 的專用建表程序。Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights（選項 C）是只能對 CloudWatch 數值 metrics 以 AVG/COUNT/MAX/MIN/SUM 在 metric namespace 與 dimensions 上查詢的 SQL 引擎，無法呈現逐筆事件的活動細節，因此無法滿足活動洞察的需求。第一位分析師認為決定因素是『Athena 無法查詢 CloudWatch metrics』，這誤讀了需求：實際功能需求是分析 CloudTrail 活動，這正是 Athena 的工作，也正是 Metrics Insights 做不到的。故 B 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating a separate CloudTrail trail in each account is the wrong pattern for an organization with all features enabled; an organization trail centrally captures all accounts from one place. Although it does pair Athena correctly with CloudTrail analysis, the per-account trail design (higher operational overhead, not Organizations-native) makes it inferior to the organization-trail solution in B.","why_zh":"在每個帳戶各自建立 CloudTrail trail 對於已啟用所有功能的組織並非正確做法；organization trail 才能從單一位置集中擷取所有帳戶。雖然它確實正確地將 Athena 與 CloudTrail 分析搭配，但每帳戶 trail 的設計（營運負擔較高、非 Organizations 原生）不如 B 的 organization-trail 方案。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Identical to B except it uses Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights instead of Athena. Metrics Insights is a SQL engine for numeric CloudWatch metrics (namespaces, dimensions, AVG/COUNT/MAX/MIN/SUM) over up to two weeks of data; it cannot query CloudTrail log event content, so it cannot provide insights into which users performed which activities on which buckets. The first analyst chose this option, but Metrics Insights cannot satisfy the activity-insights requirement.","why_zh":"與 B 相同，差別只在用 Amazon CloudWatch Metrics Insights 取代 Athena。Metrics Insights 是針對 CloudWatch 數值 metrics（namespace、dimensions、AVG/COUNT/MAX/MIN/SUM，至多兩週資料）的 SQL 引擎，無法查詢 CloudTrail 記錄的事件內容，因此無法提供哪些使用者在哪些 bucket 上做了哪些活動的洞察。第一位分析師選此項，但 Metrics Insights 無法滿足活動洞察的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses a per-account trail (wrong for an Organizations setup), a vague 'custom solution' for anomaly detection when native CloudWatch anomaly detection already exists, and CloudWatch Metrics Insights, which cannot query CloudTrail log activity. Multiple weaker choices than B.","why_zh":"使用每帳戶 trail（對 Organizations 環境不正確）、在已有原生 CloudWatch anomaly detection 的情況下卻採用含糊的『自訂解決方案』做異常偵測，並使用無法查詢 CloudTrail 記錄活動的 CloudWatch Metrics Insights。多處選擇都比 B 差。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/creating-trail-organization.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/monitor-cloudtrail-log-files-with-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/cloudtrail-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/create-cloudtrail-table-org-wide-trail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/cloudwatch-metrics-insights-querylanguage.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Anomaly_Detection.html"]}},{"id":290,"question_en":"A DevOps team is deploying microservices for an application on an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. The cluster uses managed node groups. The DevOps team wants to enable auto scaling for the microservice Pods based on a specific CPU utilization percentage. The DevOps team has already installed the Kubernetes Metrics Server on the cluster. Which solution will meet these requirements in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队正在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群上为一个应用程序部署微服务。 该集群使用托管节点组。DevOps 团队希望启用自动 根据特定的 CPU 利用率百分比对微服务 Pod 进行缩放。开发运维团队已经在集群上安装了 Kubernetes 指标服务器。 哪种解决方案 将以最高效的操作方式满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Edit the Auto Scaling group that is associated with the worker nodes of the EKS cluster. Configure the Auto Scaling group to use a target tracking scaling policy to scale when the average CPU utilization of the Auto Scaling group reaches a specific percentage.","B":"Deploy the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) and the Kubernetes Vertical Pod Autoscaler (VPA) in the cluster. Configure the HPA to scale based on the target CPU utilization percentage. Configure the VPA to use the recommender mode setting.","C":"Run the AWS Systems Manager AWS-UpdateEKSManagedNodeGroup Automation document. Modify the values for NodeGroupDesiredSize, NodeGroupMaxSize, and NodeGroupMinSize to be based on an estimate for the required node size.","D":"Deploy the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) and the Kubernetes Cluster Autoscaler in the cluster. Configure the HPA to scale based on the target CPU utilization percentage. Configure the Cluster Autoscaler to use the auto-discovery setting."},"options_zh":{"A":"编辑与 EKS 集群工作节点相关联的自动扩展组。将自动扩展组配置为使用目标跟踪扩展策略，在自 动扩展组的平均 CPU 利用率达到特定百分比时进行扩展。","B":"在集群中部署 Kubernetes 水平 Pod 自动扩缩器（HPA）和 Kubernetes 垂直 Pod 自动扩缩器（VPA）。 将 HPA 配置为根据目标 CPU 利用率百分比进行扩缩。将 VPA 配置为使用推荐模式设置。","C":"运行 AWS Systems Manager 的 AWS-UpdateEKSManagedNodeGroup 自动化文档。将 NodeGroupDesiredSize、NodeGroupMaxSize 和 NodeGroupMinSize 的值修改为基于对所需节点大小 的估计。","D":"在集群中部署 Kubernetes 水平 Pod 自动伸缩器（HPA）和 Kubernetes 集群自动伸缩器。将 HPA 配置 为根据目标 CPU 利用率百分比进行扩展。将集群自动伸缩器配置为使用自动发现设置。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two parts: scale the microservice Pods based on a specific CPU utilization percentage, and do so operationally efficiently on managed node groups. The Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) is the purpose-built tool for the first part: AWS docs state it 'automatically scales the number of Pods... based on that resource's CPU utilization' and that 'when you set a target CPU utilization percentage, the Horizontal Pod Autoscaler scales your application in or out to try to meet that target.' HPA only needs a metrics source such as the Kubernetes Metrics Server, which is already installed, so nothing extra must be deployed. For HPA-created Pods to actually be schedulable, the cluster must add nodes when Pods cannot fit; the Kubernetes Cluster Autoscaler 'automatically adjusts the number of nodes in your cluster when pods fail or are rescheduled' by controlling the .DesiredReplicas field of the EC2 Auto Scaling Group, and its auto-discovery setting finds the managed node group's Auto Scaling group via tags. HPA + Cluster Autoscaler is the standard, operationally efficient pairing for EKS managed node groups, so option D is correct.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩部分：依特定 CPU 使用率百分比擴展 microservice Pods，並且在 managed node groups 上以最有效率的方式達成。Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) 正是針對第一部分設計的工具：AWS 文件指出它會「依該資源的 CPU 使用率自動擴展 Pods 的數量」，而且「當你設定目標 CPU 使用率百分比時，Horizontal Pod Autoscaler 會嘗試擴展或縮減應用程式以達到該目標」。HPA 只需要像 Kubernetes Metrics Server 這樣的 metrics 來源，而它已經安裝，因此不需額外部署。要讓 HPA 新建的 Pods 真正可被排程，叢集必須在 Pods 無法放入時新增節點；Kubernetes Cluster Autoscaler 會「在 pods 失敗或被重新排程時自動調整叢集中的節點數量」，方式是控制 EC2 Auto Scaling Group 的 .DesiredReplicas 欄位，其 auto-discovery 設定會透過 tags 找到 managed node group 的 Auto Scaling group。HPA + Cluster Autoscaler 是 EKS managed node groups 的標準且最有效率的搭配，因此選項 D 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A target tracking scaling policy on the worker-node Auto Scaling group scales the number of EC2 nodes based on the group's average CPU, not the number of microservice Pods. The requirement is to auto scale the Pods on a target CPU percentage, which is HPA's job; node-level ASG scaling cannot add or remove Pod replicas.","why_zh":"在 worker-node Auto Scaling group 上的 target tracking scaling policy 是依該群組平均 CPU 擴展 EC2 節點數量，而非 microservice Pods 數量。需求是依目標 CPU 百分比擴展 Pods，這是 HPA 的職責；節點層級的 ASG scaling 無法增減 Pod replicas。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The HPA portion is correct, but the Vertical Pod Autoscaler (VPA) right-sizes a Pod's CPU/memory reservations rather than scaling the number of Pods, and in recommender mode it only emits recommendations without applying changes. It does not satisfy 'scale the Pods based on CPU utilization,' adds no node capacity for new Pods, and running HPA on the same CPU metric alongside VPA is a known conflicting configuration.","why_zh":"HPA 部分正確，但 Vertical Pod Autoscaler (VPA) 是調整單一 Pod 的 CPU/memory 預留量（right-sizing），而非擴展 Pods 數量；且在 recommender mode 下只產生建議而不套用變更。它無法滿足「依 CPU 使用率擴展 Pods」，也未替新 Pods 提供節點容量，而且在同一 CPU metric 上同時使用 HPA 與 VPA 是已知的衝突設定。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Running the AWS-UpdateEKSManagedNodeGroup Systems Manager Automation document and setting desired/min/max sizes from an estimate is a manual, one-time node-count change, not automatic scaling. It does not respond to CPU utilization, does not scale Pods, and is the least operationally efficient choice.","why_zh":"執行 AWS-UpdateEKSManagedNodeGroup 這個 Systems Manager Automation document 並依估計值設定 desired/min/max 節點數，只是手動一次性調整節點數，而非自動擴展。它不會回應 CPU 使用率、不會擴展 Pods，且是最不具營運效率的選擇。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/horizontal-pod-autoscaler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/autoscaling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/best-practices/cas.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/vertical-pod-autoscaler.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/metrics-server.html"]}},{"id":291,"question_en":"A company has multiple AWS accounts. The company uses AWS IAM Identity Center that is integrated with a third-party SAML 2.0 identity provider (IdP). The attributes for access control feature is enabled in IAM Identity Center. The attribute mapping list maps the department key from the IdP to the ${path:enterprise.department} attribute. All existing Amazon EC2 instances have a d1, d2, d3 department tag that corresponds to three company’s departments. A DevOps engineer must create policies based on the matching attributes. The policies must grant each user access to only the EC2 instances that are tagged with the user’s respective department name. Which condition key should the DevOps engineer include in the custom permissions policies to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有多个 AWS 账户。该公司使用与第三方 SAML 2.0 身份提供商（IdP）集成的 AWS IAM 身份中心。 IAM 身份中心已启用访问控制功能的属性。属性映射列表将身份提供方中的部门键映射到 ${path: enterprise.department} 属性。所有现有的 Amazon EC2 实例都有 d1、d2、d3 部门标签，分别对应公司的 三个部门。 DevOps 工程师必须根据匹配的属性创建策略。这些策略必须仅授予每个用户访问其所在部门名称已作 为标签添加到的 EC2 实例的权限。 DevOps 工程师应在自定义权限策略中包含哪个条件键才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"","B":"","C":"","D":""},"options_zh":{},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical IAM Identity Center attribute-based access control (ABAC) scenario. AWS docs confirm: when 'Attributes for access control' is enabled and an attribute mapping is configured (department -> ${path:enterprise.department}), IAM Identity Center passes the authenticated user's attribute value into IAM as a SESSION TAG, which you reference in permission policies via the aws:PrincipalTag/tag-key condition key. The doc 'Select your attributes for access control' is explicit that the mapping Key name 'must also be named exactly the same in your aws:PrincipalTag condition key (that is, \"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\")'. The doc 'Create permission policies for ABAC in IAM Identity Center' shows the identical EC2 Start/Stop example: \"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\". Here EC2 instances carry a 'department' tag (d1/d2/d3) and access must be granted by the user's department, so the policy compares the resource's department tag against the user's department session tag using aws:PrincipalTag/department, where the tag-key must match the mapped key name exactly ('department'). A single dynamic permission set minimizes administrative effort: no per-department policies are needed and adding users/instances only requires correct tagging. The correct condition key is aws:PrincipalTag/department, which in the published version of this question is option C. NOTE: all four option strings are blank in this dump, so the letter relies on the standard published ordering (the correct answer being aws:PrincipalTag/department, with distractors built around a resource-tag key and a mismatched tag-key name such as 'department-name'); the underlying technical answer (aws:PrincipalTag/department) is certain, hence medium confidence applies only to the letter mapping.","explanation_zh":"這是 IAM Identity Center 屬性型存取控制 (ABAC) 的標準情境。AWS 文件確認：當啟用「Attributes for access control」並設定屬性對應（department -> ${path:enterprise.department}）時，IAM Identity Center 會將已驗證使用者的屬性值以 SESSION TAG（工作階段標籤）形式傳入 IAM，並在權限政策中以 aws:PrincipalTag/tag-key 條件鍵參照。「Select your attributes for access control」文件明確指出，對應的 Key 名稱「在您的 aws:PrincipalTag 條件鍵中也必須完全相同（即 \"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\"）」。「Create permission policies for ABAC in IAM Identity Center」文件則提供形式完全相同的 EC2 Start/Stop 範例：\"ec2:ResourceTag/CostCenter\": \"${aws:PrincipalTag/CostCenter}\"。此題中 EC2 執行個體帶有 department 標籤（d1/d2/d3），且需依使用者的 department 授予存取，因此政策用 aws:PrincipalTag/department 將資源的 department 標籤與使用者的 department 工作階段標籤比對，且 tag-key 必須與對應的 key 名稱完全一致（'department'）。單一動態 permission set 可最小化管理工作：不需為每個部門建立政策，新增使用者或執行個體只需正確標記。正確條件鍵為 aws:PrincipalTag/department，在本題公開版本中對應選項 C。注意：本 dump 四個選項字串皆為空白，因此字母對應係依標準公開排序推定（正確答案為 aws:PrincipalTag/department，干擾選項圍繞資源標籤鍵及名稱不符的 tag-key，例如 'department-name' 建構）；底層技術答案（aws:PrincipalTag/department）為確定，故 medium 信心僅適用於字母對應。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A resource-side key such as ec2:ResourceTag/department only describes the EC2 instance's own department tag; it does not inject the federated user's attribute, so on its own it cannot restrict each user to their own department's instances. It is the left side of the comparison, not the condition key that carries the user's identity attribute.","why_zh":"資源端鍵（如 ec2:ResourceTag/department）僅描述 EC2 執行個體自身的 department 標籤，並未注入聯合身分使用者的屬性，因此單獨使用無法將每位使用者限制在其所屬部門的執行個體。它是比較式的左側，並非承載使用者身分屬性的條件鍵。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A PrincipalTag with a mismatched key name (e.g. aws:PrincipalTag/department-name) fails because the tag-key must match the configured mapping Key exactly. The mapping uses the 'department' key, so 'department-name' references a non-existent session tag; AWS docs warn that invalid attributes in conditions cause the condition to fail and access to be denied.","why_zh":"鍵名不符的 PrincipalTag（例如 aws:PrincipalTag/department-name）會失敗，因為 tag-key 必須與所設定的對應 Key 完全一致。對應使用的是 'department' 鍵，故 'department-name' 參照到不存在的工作階段標籤；AWS 文件警告條件中含無效屬性會導致條件失敗並拒絕存取。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A resource-tag key with a mismatched name (e.g. ec2:ResourceTag/department-name) is wrong on two counts: it is a resource-side key (not the user-attribute condition key the question asks for) and the name does not match the actual 'department' tag on the instances. Only aws:PrincipalTag/department supplies the user's department value for matching.","why_zh":"名稱不符的資源標籤鍵（例如 ec2:ResourceTag/department-name）有兩處錯誤：它是資源端鍵（並非本題所問的使用者屬性條件鍵），且名稱與執行個體上實際的 'department' 標籤不符。只有 aws:PrincipalTag/department 能提供用以比對的使用者 department 值。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/configure-abac-attributes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/attributesforaccesscontrol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_examples_ec2-start-stop-match-tags.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_condition-keys.html#condition-keys-principaltag"]}},{"id":292,"question_en":"A security team wants to use AWS CloudTrail to monitor all actions and API calls in multiple accounts that are in the same organization in AWS Organizations. The security team needs to ensure that account users cannot turn off CloudTrail in the accounts. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一个安全团队希望使用 AWS CloudTrail 来监控同一 AWS 组织中多个账户的所有操作和 API 调用。该安全团 队需要确保账户用户无法在这些账户中关闭 CloudTrail。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Apply an SCP to all OUs to deny the cloudtrail:StopLogging action and the cloudtrail:DeleteTrail action.","B":"Create IAM policies in each account to deny the cloudtrail:StopLogging action and the cloudtrail:DeleteTrail action.","C":"Set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms to notify the security team when a user disables CloudTrail in an account.","D":"Use AWS Config to automatically re-enable CloudTrail if a user disables CloudTrail in an account."},"options_zh":{"A":"对所有组织单位应用安全策略控制（SCP），以拒绝执行“cloudtrail:StopLogging”操作和“cloudtrail: DeleteTrail”操作。","B":"在每个账户中创建 IAM 策略，以拒绝 cloudtrail:StopLogging 操作和 cloudtrail:DeleteTrail 操作。","C":"在用户在一个账户中禁用 CloudTrail 时，设置 Amazon CloudWatch 警报以通知安全团队。","D":"使用 AWS Config 自动重新启用 CloudTrail，以防用户在账户中禁用 CloudTrail。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a hard preventive control: account users in the member accounts must be unable to turn off CloudTrail. A Service Control Policy (SCP) attached to the OUs that explicitly Denies cloudtrail:StopLogging and cloudtrail:DeleteTrail is the canonical AWS pattern. SCPs set the MAXIMUM available permissions for all IAM users and roles in member accounts and act as guardrails; an explicit Deny in an SCP cannot be overridden by any identity-based policy in the account, so even a member-account administrator cannot stop logging or delete the trail. This is exactly the deny-list strategy AWS documents for SCPs. The other options are either detective/reactive (CloudWatch alarms only notify; AWS Config only re-enables after the fact, leaving a logging gap) or not enforceable (in-account IAM policies can be altered or removed by the account's own admin, so they do not guarantee the action is blocked).","explanation_zh":"此題的需求是一個硬性的預防性控制：member account 中的使用者必須無法關閉 CloudTrail。將 Service Control Policy (SCP) 套用到各 OU，並明確 Deny cloudtrail:StopLogging 與 cloudtrail:DeleteTrail，是 AWS 標準做法。SCP 為 member account 中所有 IAM users 與 roles 設定「最大可用權限」的護欄；SCP 中的明確 Deny 無法被帳戶內任何 identity-based policy 覆寫，因此即使是 member account 的管理員也無法停止記錄或刪除 trail。這正是 AWS 文件中針對 SCP 所述的 deny-list 策略。其他選項要嘛是偵測/反應式（CloudWatch alarms 僅通知；AWS Config 只是在事後重新啟用，會留下記錄空窗），要嘛無法強制執行（帳戶內的 IAM policy 可被該帳戶自己的管理員修改或移除，無法保證該動作被封鎖）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"IAM policies created inside each member account can be modified or deleted by that account's own administrator (or root), so account users could remove the deny and then disable CloudTrail. IAM policies are account-local and are not an organization-enforced guardrail, so they do not guarantee users cannot turn off CloudTrail.","why_zh":"在每個 member account 內建立的 IAM policy 可被該帳戶自己的管理員（或 root）修改或刪除，使用者因此可移除 deny 後關閉 CloudTrail。IAM policy 僅限該帳戶且非由組織強制執行的護欄，無法保證使用者不能關閉 CloudTrail。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch alarms are purely detective; they notify the security team after CloudTrail is disabled but do nothing to prevent a user from turning it off, so the 'cannot turn off' requirement is not met.","why_zh":"CloudWatch alarms 純粹是偵測性質；它只在 CloudTrail 被停用後通知安全團隊，但完全無法阻止使用者將其關閉，因此無法滿足「不能關閉」的要求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Config auto-remediation is reactive: CloudTrail is still disabled until Config detects and re-enables it, leaving a logging gap, and it does not prevent the disable action from succeeding in the first place.","why_zh":"AWS Config 自動修復是反應式的：在 Config 偵測並重新啟用之前 CloudTrail 仍處於停用狀態，會留下記錄空窗，且它無法在一開始就阻止停用動作成功。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/best-practices-security.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/security_iam_id-based-policy-examples.html"]}},{"id":293,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to configure a blue/green deployment for an existing three-tier application. The application runs on Amazon EC2 instances and uses an Amazon RDS database. The EC2 instances run behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB) and are in an Auto Scaling group. The DevOps engineer has created launch templates, Auto Scaling groups, and ALB target groups for the blue environment and the green environment. Each target group specifies which application version, blue or green, will be loaded on the EC2 instances. An Amazon Route 53 record for www.example.com points to the ALB. The deployment must shift traffic all at once from the blue environment to the green environment. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要为现有的三层应用程序配置蓝/绿部署。该应用程序在 Amazon EC2 实例上运 行，并使用 Amazon RDS 数据库。EC2 实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后，并处于自动扩展组中。 DevOps 工程师为蓝色环境和绿色环境创建了启动模板、自动扩展组和 ALB 目标组。每个目标组都指 定了将在 EC2 实例上加载的应用程序版本，即蓝色版本或绿色版本。Amazon Route 53 中的 www. example.com 记录指向 ALB。 部署必须一次性将所有流量从蓝色环境切换到绿色环境。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Starta rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new application version to the green environment's EC2 instances. When the rolling restart is complete, use an AWS CLI command to update the ALB to send traffic to the green environment's target group.","B":"Use an AWS CLI command to update the ALB to send traffic to the green environments target group. Start a rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new application version to the green environment's EC2 instances.","C":"Update the launch template to deploy the green environment's application version to the blue environment's EC2 instances. Do not change the target groups or the Auto Scaling groups in either environment. Perform a rolling restart of the blue environments EC2 instances.","D":"Starta rolling restart of the Auto Scaling group for the green environment to deploy the new application version to the green environment's EC2 instances. When the rolling restart is complete, update Route 53 to point to the green environment's endpoint on the ALB."},"options_zh":{"A":"对绿色环境的自动扩展组启动滚动重启，以将新应用版本部署到绿色环境的 EC2 实例。滚动重启完 成后，使用 AWS CLI 命令更新应用负载均衡器，使其将流量发送到绿色环境的目标组。","B":"使用 AWS CLI 命令将应用负载均衡器（ALB）更新为将流量发送到绿色环境的目标组。启动绿色环 境的自动扩展组的滚动重启，以将新应用版本部署到绿色环境的 EC2 实例上。","C":"更新启动模板，将绿色环境的应用程序版本部署到蓝色环境的 EC2 实例上。不要更改任一环境 中的目标组或自动扩展组。对蓝色环境的 EC2 实例执行滚动重启。","D":"对绿色环境的自动扩展组启动滚动重启，以将新应用版本部署到绿色环境的 EC2 实例上。滚动重启 完成后，更新 Route 53 使其指向绿色环境在 ALB 上的端点。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The blue and green environments already exist as separate launch templates, Auto Scaling groups, and ALB target groups behind a SINGLE Application Load Balancer, and the Route 53 record for www.example.com already resolves to that one ALB. Each target group is tied to a specific application version. To cut over all at once you must (1) prepare the green environment by deploying the new version to its EC2 instances via a rolling restart of the green Auto Scaling group, then (2) only after that completes, swap the ALB listener's default forward action to the green target group with an AWS CLI command (elbv2 modify-listener). Option A follows this correct prepare-then-cutover order, giving an instant, all-at-once switch with no client errors and easy rollback (switch the listener back to the blue target group). Route 53 never changes because it already points at the same ALB; the swap happens at the load-balancer layer.","explanation_zh":"blue 與 green 環境已分別建立各自的 launch template、Auto Scaling group 以及 ALB target group，且共用同一個 Application Load Balancer，而 www.example.com 的 Route 53 紀錄已指向這唯一的 ALB。每個 target group 對應特定的應用程式版本。要一次性切換流量，必須先 (1) 透過對 green Auto Scaling group 執行 rolling restart，把新版本部署到 green 的 EC2 執行個體以完成準備，再 (2) 在準備完成後，用 AWS CLI 指令 (elbv2 modify-listener) 把 ALB listener 的預設 forward 動作切換到 green target group。選項 A 採用正確的「先準備再切換」順序，可一次性瞬間切換且不會產生用戶端錯誤，回滾也很容易（把 listener 切回 blue target group）。Route 53 不需更動，因為它已指向同一個 ALB；切換發生在 load balancer 層。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The order is reversed: it shifts the ALB to the green target group BEFORE the new application version is deployed by the rolling restart. Live traffic would be routed to green instances that are still restarting or not yet running the new version, causing client errors and defeating a clean blue/green cutover.","why_zh":"順序顛倒：在 rolling restart 部署新版本之前，就先把 ALB 切到 green target group。正式流量會被導向仍在重啟或尚未換成新版本的 green 執行個體，造成用戶端錯誤，破壞乾淨的 blue/green 切換。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Updating the launch template to push the green version onto the BLUE instances and rolling-restarting blue is an in-place / rolling deployment on the existing environment, not blue/green, and it is not an all-at-once traffic shift. It also discards the pre-built green ASG and target group and removes the instant-rollback benefit.","why_zh":"把 launch template 改成將 green 版本推到 blue 執行個體並對 blue 做 rolling restart，是在既有環境上做就地/滾動部署，並非 blue/green，也不是一次性流量切換，且白白浪費已建好的 green ASG 與 target group，並喪失瞬間回滾的好處。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is only ONE ALB with a single DNS name, and Route 53 already points to it. There is no separate 'green endpoint on the ALB' to repoint DNS to; switching between the blue and green target groups behind one ALB must be done by modifying the ALB listener, not by changing the Route 53 record. A Route 53 swap only works when blue and green have separate load balancers.","why_zh":"只有一個 ALB、單一 DNS 名稱，且 Route 53 早已指向它。並不存在可供 DNS 重新指向的『ALB 上的 green 端點』；在同一個 ALB 後方於 blue 與 green target group 間切換，必須修改 ALB listener，而非更改 Route 53 紀錄。Route 53 置換僅在 blue 與 green 各有獨立負載平衡器時才適用。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/blue-green-deployments/swap-the-auto-scaling-group-behind-elastic-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-listeners.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-target-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/overview-deployment-options/bluegreen-deployments.html"]}},{"id":294,"question_en":"A company has an application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. The application processes a high volume of messages from an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue. A DevOps engineer noticed that the application took several hours to process a group of messages from the SQS queue. The average CPU utilization of the Auto Scaling group did not cross the threshold of a target tracking scaling policy when processing the messages. The application that processes the SQS queue publishes logs to ‘Amazon CloudWatch Logs. The DevOps engineer needs to ensure that the queue is processed quickly. Which solution meets these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的应用程序，这些实例位于一个自动扩展组中。该应用程序 处理来自亚马逊简单队列服务（Amazon SQS）队列的大量消息。 一位 DevOps 工程师注意到，应用程序处理来自 SQS 队列的一组消息需要数小时。在处理这些消息时， 自动扩展组的平均 CPU 利用率未超过目标跟踪扩展策略的阈值。处理 SQS 队列的应用程序将日志发 布到“Amazon CloudWatch Logs”。 DevOps 工程师需要确保队列能够快速处理。 哪种解决方案在满足这些要求的同时，运营开销最小？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to publish a custom metric by using the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible SQS queue attribute and the GroupInServiceInstances Auto Scaling group attribute to publish the queue messages for each instance. Schedule an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the Lambda function every hour. Create a target tracking scaling policy for the Auto Scaling group that uses the custom metric to scale in and out.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to publish a custom metric by using the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible SQS queue attribute and the GroupInServiceInstances Auto Scaling group attribute to publish the queue messages for each instance. Create a CloudWatch subscription filter for the application logs with the Lambda function as the target. Create a target tracking scaling policy for the Auto Scaling group that uses the custom metric to scale in and out.","C":"Create a target tracking scaling policy for the Auto Scaling group. In the target tracking policy, use the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible SQS queue attribute and the GroupInServiceInstances Auto Scaling group attribute to calculate how many messages are in the queue for each number of instances by using metric math. Use the calculated attribute to scale in and out.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that logs the ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible attribute of the SQS queue to a CloudWatch Logs log group. Schedule an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the Lambda function every 5 minutes. Create a metric filer to count the number of log events from a CloudWatch logs group. Create a target tracking scaling policy for the Auto Scaling group that uses the custom metric to scale in and out."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数，通过使用 SQS 队列的 ApproximateNumberOfM essagesVisible 属性和 Auto Scaling 组的 GroupInServiceInstances 属性来发布每个实例的队列消息的 自定义指标。安排一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每小时运行一次该 Lambda 函数。为 Auto Scaling 组创建一个目标跟踪扩展策略，使用该自定义指标进行扩展和收缩。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配置该 Lambda 函数，通过使用 SQS 队列的 ApproximateNumberOfM essagesVisible 属性和 Auto Scaling 组的 GroupInServiceInstances 属性来发布每个实例的队列消息 的自定义指标。为应用程序日志创建一个 CloudWatch 订阅过滤器，将 Lambda 函数作为目标。为 Auto Scaling 组创建一个目标跟踪扩展策略，使用自定义指标进行扩展和收缩。","C":"为自动扩展组创建目标跟踪扩展策略。在目标跟踪策略中，使用 通过使用指标数学，结合 SQS 队列的“ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible”属性和 Auto Scaling 组的“GroupInServiceInstances”属性，计算出在不同实例数量下队列中的消息数量。利用计算得出 的属性进行缩放操作。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，将 SQS 队列的 ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible 属性记录到 CloudWatch Logs 日志组中。安排一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每 5 分钟运行一次该 Lambda 函 数。创建一个指标过滤器，用于计算来自 CloudWatch 日志组的日志事件数量。为 Auto Scaling 组 创建一个目标跟踪扩展策略，使用自定义指标进行扩展和收缩。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The CPU-based target tracking policy never triggered because SQS message processing is not CPU-bound; the correct scaling signal is the SQS backlog per instance. AWS documents this exact scenario: a target tracking scaling policy that uses CloudWatch metric math to divide ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible (AWS/SQS namespace) by GroupInServiceInstances (AWS/AutoScaling namespace), producing the backlog-per-instance metric (expression m1/m2), then scales the Auto Scaling group to a target value. The 'Create a target tracking scaling policy using metric math' page shows this precise configuration, and the 'Scaling policy based on Amazon SQS' page explicitly states you can now 'save the cost and effort put into publishing your own metric by using metric math.' That maps directly to the LEAST operational overhead qualifier, because options A, B, and D all add a Lambda function plus a trigger (scheduled EventBridge, a logs subscription, or a metric filter) merely to publish a custom metric that metric math computes natively. Option C needs no Lambda, no schedule, and no custom-metric pipeline, so it is both technically correct and the lowest-overhead solution.","explanation_zh":"原本以 CPU 為基準的 target tracking policy 從未觸發，因為 SQS 訊息處理並非受 CPU 限制；正確的擴展訊號是每台執行個體的 SQS backlog。AWS 文件正好描述此情境：使用 CloudWatch metric math 的 target tracking scaling policy，將 ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible（AWS/SQS namespace）除以 GroupInServiceInstances（AWS/AutoScaling namespace），算出每台執行個體的 backlog 指標（運算式 m1/m2），再讓 Auto Scaling group 擴展至目標值。'Create a target tracking scaling policy using metric math' 頁面展示了完全相同的設定，而 'Scaling policy based on Amazon SQS' 頁面更明確指出，現在可透過 metric math「省下自行發布自訂指標的成本與心力」。這正好對應 LEAST operational overhead 的條件，因為選項 A、B、D 都額外加入一個 Lambda function 與觸發機制（排程的 EventBridge、logs subscription 或 metric filter），只為發布 metric math 本來就能原生計算的自訂指標。選項 C 不需要 Lambda、不需要排程、也不需要自訂指標管線，因此在技術上正確且維運負擔最低。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Adds a Lambda function and a scheduled EventBridge rule just to publish a custom backlog-per-instance metric that metric math computes natively, increasing operational overhead. Worse, running it only every hour gives stale, coarse data that cannot react quickly to a queue spike, defeating the goal of processing the queue quickly.","why_zh":"額外加入 Lambda function 與排程的 EventBridge rule，只為發布 metric math 本可原生計算的每執行個體 backlog 自訂指標，增加維運負擔。更糟的是每小時才執行一次，資料過時且粗糙，無法快速反應佇列尖峰，違背快速處理佇列的目標。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Also adds a Lambda function plus a CloudWatch Logs subscription filter to publish the custom metric, which is unnecessary overhead compared to native metric math. A logs subscription fires on application log events, an unreliable, indirect trigger for sampling queue depth that does not produce a clean per-instance backlog metric on a consistent schedule.","why_zh":"同樣加入 Lambda function 與 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 來發布自訂指標，相較於原生 metric math 屬於不必要的負擔。logs subscription 由應用程式日誌事件觸發，是不可靠且間接的取樣佇列深度方式，無法依固定頻率產生乾淨的每執行個體 backlog 指標。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Technically broken: a metric filter that counts log events from a Lambda that logs the queue size every 5 minutes measures how many times Lambda ran, not the actual ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible value, so the resulting metric does not represent backlog per instance. It also adds Lambda, EventBridge, a log group, and a metric filter, far more overhead than metric math.","why_zh":"技術上有缺陷：對每 5 分鐘記錄佇列大小的 Lambda 日誌建立 metric filter 來計算日誌事件數，量測的是 Lambda 執行次數，而非實際的 ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible 值，因此產生的指標無法代表每執行個體 backlog。並且還加入 Lambda、EventBridge、log group 與 metric filter，負擔遠高於 metric math。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/as-using-sqs-queue.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-target-tracking-metric-math.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/using-math-expression-examples.html"]}},{"id":295,"question_en":"A company has a single AWS account that runs hundreds of Amazon EC2 instances in a single AWS Region. The company launches and terminates new EC2 instances every hour. The account includes existing EC2 instances that have been running for longer than a week. The company's security policy requires all running EC2 instances to have an EC2 instance profile attached. The company has created a default EC2 instance profile. The default EC2 instance profile must be attached to any EC2 instances that do not have a profile attached. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个 AWS 账户，在单个 AWS 区域运行着数百台亚马逊 EC2 实例。该公司每小时 都会启动和终止新的 EC2 实例。该账户中还包括运行时间超过一周的现有 EC2 实例。 公司的安全策略要求所有正在运行的 EC2 实例都必须附加一个 EC2 实例配置文件。公司已创建了一 个默认的 EC2 实例配置文件。对于未附加配置文件的任何 EC2 实例，都必须附加默认的 EC2 实例配 置文件。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches the Amazon EC2 RunInstances API calls. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances.","B":"Configure AWS Config. Deploy an AWS Config ec2-instance-profile-attached managed rule. Configure an automatic remediation action that invokes an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances.","C":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches the Amazon EC2 StartInstances API calls. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances.","D":"Configure AWS Config. Deploy an AWS Config iam-role-managed-policy-check managed rule. Configure an automatic remediation action that invokes an AWS Lambda function to attach the default instance profile to the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个与 Amazon EC2 的 RunInstances API 调用相匹配的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将该规则配 置为调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例。","B":"配置 AWS Config。部署一个与 EC2 实例配置文件关联的 AWS Config 管理规则。配置一个自动修 复操作，调用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例。","C":"配置一个与 Amazon EC2 的 StartInstances API 调用相匹配的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将该 规则配置为调用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册，以将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例。","D":"配置 AWS Config。部署一个名为“iam-role-managed-policy-check”的 AWS Config 管理规则。配置 一个自动修复操作，调用 AWS Lambda 函数将默认实例配置文件附加到 EC2 实例上。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is to attach a default EC2 instance profile to ANY running instance that lacks one, covering BOTH the pre-existing instances running for over a week AND the instances launched/terminated every hour. AWS Config with the ec2-instance-profile-attached managed rule (identifier EC2_INSTANCE_PROFILE_ATTACHED, resource type AWS::EC2::Instance) marks an instance NON_COMPLIANT when no IAM profile is attached. Because AWS Config performs an initial baseline evaluation of all recorded resources and is also configuration-change triggered, it detects both the long-running existing instances and every newly launched one. An automatic remediation action then invokes an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook (AWS-AttachIAMToInstance) that attaches the default instance profile. Option B is the only solution that detects and remediates every non-compliant instance regardless of when it was launched.","explanation_zh":"需求是要為任何缺少 instance profile 的執行中 EC2 instance 附加預設的 EC2 instance profile，必須同時涵蓋已執行超過一週的既有 instance，以及每小時啟動/終止的 instance。AWS Config 的 ec2-instance-profile-attached 受管規則（識別碼 EC2_INSTANCE_PROFILE_ATTACHED，資源類型 AWS::EC2::Instance）會在 instance 未附加 IAM profile 時標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。由於 AWS Config 會對所有已記錄的資源執行初始基準評估，並且也會由組態變更觸發評估，因此它同時能偵測長期執行的既有 instance 與每個新啟動的 instance。接著由自動修復動作呼叫 AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook（AWS-AttachIAMToInstance）來附加預設 instance profile。選項 B 是唯一能偵測並修復所有不合規 instance 的方案，不論其何時啟動。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An EventBridge rule matching RunInstances API calls only fires for instances launched AFTER the rule is created. It does nothing for the pre-existing instances that have been running for longer than a week, so it fails the requirement to cover instances that already lack a profile.","why_zh":"比對 RunInstances API 呼叫的 EventBridge 規則只會對規則建立之後啟動的 instance 觸發，無法處理已執行超過一週的既有 instance，因此無法滿足涵蓋既有未附加 profile instance 的需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An EventBridge rule matching StartInstances only matches stopped-to-running transitions. The hourly workload launches and terminates instances (RunInstances/TerminateInstances), not stop/start, and the long-running existing instances are never restarted, so neither population is reliably matched. Wrong API event.","why_zh":"比對 StartInstances 的 EventBridge 規則只會對已停止再啟動的轉換觸發。每小時的工作負載是啟動與終止 instance（RunInstances/TerminateInstances）而非停止/啟動，且長期執行的既有 instance 從不重新啟動，因此兩類 instance 都無法被可靠地比對到，是錯誤的 API 事件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The iam-role-managed-policy-check rule (IAM_ROLE_MANAGED_POLICY_CHECK) evaluates resource type AWS::IAM::Role and checks whether specified managed policies are attached to an IAM role. It does not detect EC2 instances that lack an instance profile, so it cannot identify the non-compliant instances this scenario requires.","why_zh":"iam-role-managed-policy-check 規則（IAM_ROLE_MANAGED_POLICY_CHECK）評估的資源類型是 AWS::IAM::Role，檢查特定受管政策是否已附加到某個 IAM role。它無法偵測缺少 instance profile 的 EC2 instance，因此無法辨識本情境所需的不合規 instance。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/ec2-instance-profile-attached.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-aws-attachiamtoinstance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/iam-role-managed-policy-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_components.html"]}},{"id":296,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage hundreds of AWS accounts. The company has a team that is responsible for AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM). The IAM team wants to implement AWS IAM Identity Center. The IAM team must have only the minimum required permissions to manage IAM Identity Center. The IAM team must not be able to gain unnecessary access to the Organizations management account. The IAM team must be able to provision new IAM Identity Center permission sets and assignments for new and existing member accounts. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织来管理数百个 AWS 账户。该公司有一个团队负责 AWS 身份和访问管理 （IAM）。 IAM 团队希望实施 AWS IAM 身份中心。IAM 团队必须仅拥有管理 IAM 身份中心所需的最低权限。 IAM 团队不得能够获得对组织管理账户的不必要的访问权限。IAM 团队必须能够为新成员账户和现有 成员账户配置新的 IAM 身份中心权限集和分配。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS account for the IAM team. Enable IAM Identity Center in the new account. In the Organizations management account, register the new account as a delegated administrator for IAM Identity Center.","B":"Create a new AWS account for the IAM team. Enable IAM Identity Center in the Organizations management account. In the Organizations management account, register the new account as a delegated administrator for IAM Identity Center.","C":"Create an SCP in Organizations. Create a new OU for the Organizations management account, and link the new SCP to the OU. Configure the SCP to deny all access to IAM Identity Center.","D":"Create IAM users and an IAM group for the IAM team in IAM Identity Center. Add the users to the group. Create a new permission set. Attach the AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator managed IAM policy to the group.","E":"Assign the new permission set to the Organizations management account. Allow the IAM team's group to use the permission set.","F":"Assign the new permission set to the new AWS account. Allow the IAM team's group to use the permission set."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 IAM 团队创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在新账户中启用 IAM 身份中心。在组织管理账户中，将 新账户注册为 IAM 身份中心的委托管理员。","B":"为 IAM 团队创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在组织管理账户中启用 IAM 身份中心。在组织管理账 户中，将新账户注册为 IAM 身份中心的委托管理员。","C":"在组织中创建服务控制策略（SCP）。为组织管理账户创建一个新的组织单位（OU），并将新的 SCP 链接到该 OU。配置 SCP 以拒绝对 IAM 身份中心的所有访问。","D":"在 IAM 身份中心为 IAM 团队创建 IAM 用户和一个 IAM 组。将用户添加到该组。创建一个新的权 限集。将 AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator 管理的 IAM 策略附加到该组。","E":"将新的权限集分配给组织管理账户。允许 IAM 团队的组使用该权限集。","F":"将新的权限集分配给新的 AWS 账户。允许 IAM 团队的组使用该权限集。"},"answer":["A","D","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["B","D","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"An IAM Identity Center organization instance is always created in (and must always reside in) the AWS Organizations management account, because that is how it provisions, de-provisions, and updates roles across all member accounts. You therefore enable IAM Identity Center in the management account, not in a separate account (so B is correct and the dump's A is wrong). From the management account you then register the new IAM-team account as the delegated administrator (only management-account credentials can call RegisterDelegatedAdministrator). A delegated administrator can perform almost all IAM Identity Center administration, including provisioning new permission sets and assignments for new and existing member accounts, but it explicitly cannot enable IAM Identity Center, delete configurations, manage permission sets provisioned in the management account, register/deregister other delegated administrators, or enable/disable user access in the management account, which delivers least privilege and keeps the team out of the management account (B). Step D builds the team's identity (users and group in IAM Identity Center) and a permission set using the AWS managed policy AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator, which grants member-account administrative actions in a multi-account environment (the member-scoped policy, as opposed to AWSSSOMasterAccountAdministrator, which would also reach the management account). Step F assigns that permission set to the new delegated administrator account (not the management account) and allows the IAM team's group to use it, granting admin access only where it is needed.","explanation_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的 organization instance 一律建立在(且必須一直位於)AWS Organizations 管理帳戶 (management account),因為它要靠管理帳戶跨所有成員帳戶佈建、移除與更新角色。因此要在管理帳戶啟用 IAM Identity Center,而非在另一個帳戶啟用(所以 B 正確,題庫的 A 錯誤)。接著從管理帳戶把 IAM 團隊的新帳戶註冊為 delegated administrator(只有管理帳戶憑證能呼叫 RegisterDelegatedAdministrator)。delegated administrator 幾乎能執行所有 IAM Identity Center 管理工作,包括為新舊成員帳戶佈建新的 permission set 與 assignment,但明確不能啟用 IAM Identity Center、刪除設定、管理在管理帳戶中佈建的 permission set、註冊/註銷其他 delegated administrator,或啟用/停用管理帳戶的使用者存取,因而達成最小權限並讓團隊無法進入管理帳戶 (B)。步驟 D 建立團隊身分(IAM Identity Center 中的使用者與群組)以及一個使用 AWS 受管政策 AWSSSOMemberAccountAdministrator 的 permission set,該政策在多帳戶環境中授予成員帳戶的管理動作(屬成員帳戶範圍的政策,與會同時涵蓋管理帳戶的 AWSSSOMasterAccountAdministrator 不同)。步驟 F 把該 permission set 指派給新的 delegated administrator 帳戶(而非管理帳戶),並允許 IAM 團隊群組使用,使其僅在需要之處取得管理權限。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An IAM Identity Center organization instance cannot be enabled in a separate new member account; the instance must always reside in the Organizations management account so it can provision roles across the organization. The 'register the new account as delegated administrator' clause is fine, but the 'enable IAM Identity Center in the new account' clause is technically impossible, so B is the correct version of this step.","why_zh":"IAM Identity Center 的 organization instance 無法在另一個新成員帳戶啟用;instance 必須一直位於 Organizations 管理帳戶,才能跨組織佈建角色。『把新帳戶註冊為 delegated administrator』沒問題,但『在新帳戶啟用 IAM Identity Center』技術上不可能,因此 B 才是這個步驟的正確版本。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"SCPs do not affect users or roles in the management account; they only restrict member accounts. Placing the management account in an OU and denying IAM Identity Center via SCP would have no effect on the management account, and even if it did it would break the IAM Identity Center instance, which lives in the management account. This control is both ineffective and harmful.","why_zh":"SCP 不會影響管理帳戶中的使用者或角色,只會限制成員帳戶。把管理帳戶放進 OU 並用 SCP 拒絕 IAM Identity Center 對管理帳戶毫無作用;即便有作用,也會破壞位於管理帳戶的 IAM Identity Center instance。此控制既無效又有害。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Assigning the permission set to the management account would grant the IAM team administrative access to the management account, directly violating the requirement that they must not gain unnecessary access to it. The permission set must be assigned to the delegated administrator account (F) instead.","why_zh":"把 permission set 指派給管理帳戶會讓 IAM 團隊取得管理帳戶的管理權限,直接違反『不得取得不必要的管理帳戶存取』。permission set 應改為指派給 delegated administrator 帳戶 (F)。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/delegated-admin.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/delegated-admin-how-to-register.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/security-iam-awsmanpol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/howtodelegatessoaccess.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]}},{"id":297,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL global database that has two secondary AWS Regions. A DevOps engineer has configured the database parameter group to guarantee an RPO of 60 seconds. Write operations on the primary cluster are occasionally blocked because of the RPO setting. The DevOps engineer needs to reduce the frequency of blocked write operations. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用了一个亚马逊 Aurora PostgreSQL 全球数据库，该数据库在两个辅助 AWS 区域设有副本。一 位 DevOps 工程师将数据库参数组配置为保证 60 秒的恢复点目标（RPO）。由于 RPO 设置的原因，主集 群上的写入操作偶尔会被阻塞。 DevOps 工程师需要降低写入操作被阻塞的频率。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add an additional secondary cluster to the global database.","B":"Enable write forwarding for the global database.","C":"Remove one of the secondary clusters from the global database.","D":"Configure synchronous replication for the global database."},"options_zh":{"A":"在全局数据库中添加一个额外的辅助集群。","B":"为全局数据库启用写转发。","C":"从全局数据库中移除一个辅助集群。","D":"为全局数据库配置同步复制。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Database"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"With an Aurora PostgreSQL global database, the rds.global_db_rpo parameter enforces a managed RPO. Per the AWS docs, Aurora monitors the RPO lag time of all secondary clusters and only needs at least one secondary to stay within the target RPO window. The commit rule is explicit: Aurora commits a transaction if AT LEAST ONE secondary DB cluster has an RPO lag time less than the RPO, and blocks the transaction only when ALL secondary clusters have RPO lag times larger than the RPO. Therefore, adding an additional secondary cluster (A) enlarges the pool of secondaries, raising the probability that at least one is within the RPO window at any moment, which reduces the frequency of blocked writes. Removing a secondary (C, the dump's suggested answer) does the opposite: with fewer secondaries it becomes more likely that all of them simultaneously exceed the RPO, so writes are blocked more often, not less.","explanation_zh":"在 Aurora PostgreSQL global database 中，rds.global_db_rpo 參數會強制執行受管的 RPO。根據 AWS 文件，Aurora 會監控所有 secondary clusters 的 RPO lag time，且只需要至少一個 secondary 維持在目標 RPO 視窗內即可。提交規則很明確：當至少一個 secondary DB cluster 的 RPO lag time 小於 RPO 時，Aurora 就會提交交易；只有當所有 secondary clusters 的 RPO lag time 都大於 RPO 時，才會封鎖交易。因此，新增一個額外的 secondary cluster（A）會擴大 secondary 的數量池，提高在任一時刻至少有一個 secondary 處於 RPO 視窗內的機率，進而降低寫入被封鎖的頻率。移除一個 secondary（C，即 dump 建議答案）則相反：secondary 越少，越可能所有 secondary 同時超出 RPO，反而會讓寫入被封鎖得更頻繁，而非更少。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Write forwarding only lets secondary clusters route their write statements to the primary so you manage fewer endpoints; the primary remains the source of truth and the RPO lag evaluation is unchanged. It does not affect whether the primary blocks commits under the rds.global_db_rpo rule.","why_zh":"Write forwarding 只是讓 secondary clusters 把寫入語句轉送到 primary 以減少需管理的端點；primary 仍是真實來源，RPO lag 的評估方式不變。它不會改變 primary 在 rds.global_db_rpo 規則下是否封鎖提交。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is the inverse of the correct fix. Blocking happens only when ALL secondaries exceed the RPO, so reducing the number of secondaries makes it MORE likely that all remaining ones simultaneously breach the RPO, increasing the frequency of blocked writes rather than reducing it.","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議的答案，但與正確修正方式相反。只有當所有 secondary 都超出 RPO 時才會封鎖，因此減少 secondary 數量反而更容易讓剩餘的 secondary 同時違反 RPO，導致寫入被封鎖的頻率上升而非下降。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Aurora global databases use storage-based asynchronous cross-Region replication; there is no option to 'configure synchronous replication' for a global database, so this is not a real feature. Even conceptually, forcing synchrony would make writes wait on remote acknowledgement, worsening blocking rather than reducing it.","why_zh":"Aurora global databases 在跨 Region 之間使用以儲存為基礎的非同步複寫；global database 並沒有可「設定同步複寫」的選項，因此這並非真實功能。即便就概念而言，強制同步會讓寫入等待遠端確認，只會加劇而非減少寫入封鎖。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-disaster-recovery.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-global-database-write-forwarding.html"]}},{"id":298,"question_en":"A company has a web application that is hosted on an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. The EKS cluster runs on AWS Fargate that is available through an internet-facing Application Load Balancer. The application is experiencing stability issues that lead to longer response times. A DevOps engineer needs to configure observability in Amazon CloudWatch to troubleshoot the issue. The solution must provide only the minimum necessary permissions. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个托管在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群上的网络应用程序。该 EKS 集群 通过面向互联网的应用程序负载均衡器在 AWS Fargate 上运行。 该应用程序出现稳定性问题，导致响应时间延长。一位 DevOps 工程师需要在 Amazon CloudWatch 中配 置可观测性以排查问题。解决方案必须仅提供必要的最小权限。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the CloudWatch agent as a Kubernetes StatefulSet to the EKS cluster.","B":"Deploy the AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry Collector as a Kubernetes DaemonSet to the EKS cluster.","C":"Associate a Kubernetes service account with an IAM role by using IAM roles for service accounts in Amazon EKS. Use the CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy AWS managed policy.","D":"Associate a Kubernetes service account with an IAM role by using IAM roles for service accounts in Amazon EKS. Use the CloudWatchAgentAdminPolicy AWS managed policy.","E":"Configure an IAM OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider for the EKS cluster.","F":"Enable EKS control plane logging for the EKS cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 EKS 集群中将 CloudWatch 代理部署为 Kubernetes 有状态集。","B":"在 EKS 集群中以 Kubernetes 守护集的形式部署 AWS 版 OpenTelemetry 收集器。","C":"使用 Amazon EKS 中的服务账户的 IAM 角色功能将 Kubernetes 服务账户与 IAM 角色相关联。使用 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy AWS 管理策略。","D":"使用 Amazon EKS 中的服务账户 IAM 角色功能将 Kubernetes 服务账户与 IAM 角色相关联。使用 CloudWatchAgentAdminPolicy AWS 管理策略。","E":"为 EKS 集群配置一个 IAM OpenID Connect （OIDC） 提供程序。","F":"为 EKS 集群启用 EKS 控制平面日志记录。"},"answer":["B","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"For an EKS cluster running on AWS Fargate, Container Insights observability must be collected with the AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry (ADOT) Collector. The CloudWatch agent path is documented only for EC2-backed nodes; the Container Insights ADOT doc has a dedicated 'Amazon EKS clusters hosted on Fargate' section that uses the ADOT Collector, so B is required and A (CloudWatch agent) is eliminated. To grant the collector permission to publish metrics, logs, and traces to CloudWatch/X-Ray with least privilege, use IRSA (IAM roles for service accounts) and attach the AWS managed CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy. That policy allows PutMetricData, log creation/PutLogEvents, X-Ray puts, and only ssm:GetParameter (read) on AmazonCloudWatch-* parameters. CloudWatchAgentAdminPolicy additionally grants ssm:PutParameter (write), which exceeds what the collector needs, so C (Server) is correct and D (Admin) violates the minimum-permissions requirement. Finally, IRSA requires that an IAM OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider exist for the cluster's OIDC issuer URL, so E is the necessary prerequisite. (Note: Fargate does not run DaemonSets, so B's 'DaemonSet' wording is imperfect, but B is the only option naming ADOT, the mandated Fargate collector, and is the intended choice.) F enables control plane (API server/audit/authenticator) logging, which does not help troubleshoot application response-time/stability issues and is unrelated to setting up the telemetry collector.","explanation_zh":"EKS 叢集運行於 AWS Fargate 時，Container Insights 的可觀測性必須使用 AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry (ADOT) Collector 來收集。CloudWatch agent 的路徑僅適用於 EC2 節點；Container Insights ADOT 文件有專門的「Amazon EKS clusters hosted on Fargate」章節使用 ADOT Collector，因此需要 B，而 A（CloudWatch agent）被排除。為讓 collector 以最小權限將 metrics、logs、traces 發佈到 CloudWatch/X-Ray，使用 IRSA（IAM roles for service accounts）並附加 AWS 受管政策 CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy。該政策允許 PutMetricData、建立 log 與 PutLogEvents、X-Ray put，以及僅對 AmazonCloudWatch-* 參數的 ssm:GetParameter（讀取）。CloudWatchAgentAdminPolicy 還額外授予 ssm:PutParameter（寫入），超過 collector 所需，因此 C（Server）正確而 D（Admin）違反最小權限要求。最後，IRSA 需要叢集的 OIDC issuer URL 存在一個 IAM OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider，所以 E 是必要前提。（注意：Fargate 不運行 DaemonSet，故 B 的「DaemonSet」措辭並不嚴謹，但 B 是唯一指明 ADOT（Fargate 必用的 collector）的選項，為預期答案。）F 啟用控制平面（API server/audit/authenticator）日誌，無助於排查應用程式回應時間/穩定性問題，也與設定遙測 collector 無關。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The CloudWatch agent is the documented collector for EKS on EC2, not Fargate. Container Insights on Fargate requires the ADOT Collector, so deploying the CloudWatch agent (and as a StatefulSet) is not the supported Fargate path.","why_zh":"CloudWatch agent 是 EKS on EC2 的文件化收集器，而非 Fargate。Fargate 上的 Container Insights 需要 ADOT Collector，因此部署 CloudWatch agent（且為 StatefulSet）並非 Fargate 支援的路徑。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudWatchAgentAdminPolicy adds ssm:PutParameter (write) on top of the Server policy, granting more than the collector needs. This violates the explicit minimum-necessary-permissions requirement; CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy is the least-privilege choice.","why_zh":"CloudWatchAgentAdminPolicy 在 Server 政策之上額外加入 ssm:PutParameter（寫入），授予超過 collector 所需的權限，違反題目明確的最小權限要求；CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy 才是最小權限選擇。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"EKS control plane logging captures Kubernetes API server, audit, authenticator, controller, and scheduler logs. It does not surface the application-level metrics/traces needed to troubleshoot response-time and stability issues, and it is not part of deploying the telemetry collector.","why_zh":"EKS 控制平面日誌擷取 Kubernetes API server、audit、authenticator、controller、scheduler 日誌，無法呈現排查回應時間與穩定性問題所需的應用層 metrics/traces，也不屬於部署遙測 collector 的步驟。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Container-Insights-EKS-otel.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Container-Insights-prerequisites.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/enable-iam-roles-for-service-accounts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/iam-roles-for-service-accounts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/CloudWatchAgentServerPolicy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/CloudWatchAgentAdminPolicy.html"]}},{"id":299,"question_en":"A company stores its Python-based application code in AWS CodeCommit. The company uses AWS CodePipeline to deploy the application. The CodeCommit repository and the CodePipeline pipeline are deployed to the same AWS account. The company's security team requires all code to be scanned for vulnerabilities before the code is deployed to production. If any vulnerabilities are found, the deployment must stop. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司将其基于 Python 的应用程序代码存储在 AWS CodeCommit 中。该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 来 部署应用程序。CodeCommit 存储库和 CodePipeline 管道部署在同一个 AWS 账户中。 公司的安全团队要求所有代码在部署到生产环境之前都要进行漏洞扫描。如果发现任何漏洞，部署 必须停止。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new CodeBuild project. Configure the project to run a security scan on the code by using Amazon CodeGuru Security. Configure the CodeBuild project to raise an error if CodeGuru Security finds vulnerabilities. Create a new IAM role that has sufficient permissions to run CodeGuru Security scans. Assign the role to the CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, add a new stage before the deployment stage. Select AWS CodeBuild as the action provider for the new stage. Use the source artifact from the CodeCommit repository. Configure the action to use the CodeBuild project.","B":"Create a new CodeBuild project. Configure the project to run a security scan on the code by using Amazon Inspector. Configure the CodeBuild project to raise an error if Amazon Inspector finds vulnerabilities. Create a new IAM role that has sufficient permissions to run Amazon Inspector scans. Assign the role to the CodeBuild project. In the CodePipeline pipeline, add a new stage before the deployment stage. Select AWS CodeBuild as the action provider for the new stage. Use the source artifact from the CodeCommit repository. Configure the action to use the CodeBuild project.","C":"Update the IAM role that is attached to CodePipeline to include sufficient permissions to invoke Amazon DevOps Guru. In the CodePipeline pipeline, add a new stage before the deployment stage. Select DevOps Guru as the action provider for the new stage. Use the source artifact from the CodeCommit repository.","D":"Update the IAM role that is attached to CodePipeline to include sufficient permissions to invoke Amazon DevOps Guru. In the CodePipeline pipeline, add a new stage before the deployment stage. Select CodeGuru Security as the action provider for the new stage. Use the source artifact from the CodeCommit repository."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 CodeBuild 项目。配置该项目，使其使用 Amazon CodeGuru Security 对代码进行安全扫描。 配置 CodeBuild 项目，若 CodeGuru Security 发现漏洞则触发错误。创建一个新的 IAM 角色，赋予其运 行 CodeGuru Security 扫描的足够权限。将该角色分配给 CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中，在部 署阶段之前添加一个新阶段。选择 AWS CodeBuild 作为新阶段的操作提供程序。使用来自 CodeCommit 存储库的源工件。配置操作以使用 CodeBuild 项目。","B":"创建一个新的 CodeBuild 项目。配置该项目，使其使用 Amazon Inspector 对代码进行安全扫描。配置 CodeBuild 项目，如果 Amazon Inspector 发现漏洞则引发错误。创建一个新的 IAM 角色，该角色具有 运行 Amazon Inspector 扫描的足够权限。将该角色分配给 CodeBuild 项目。在 CodePipeline 管道中， 在部署阶段之前添加一个新阶段。选择 AWS CodeBuild 作为新阶段的操作提供程序。使用来自 CodeCommit 存储库的源工件。配置操作以使用 CodeBuild 项目。","C":"更新附加到 CodePipeline 的 IAM 角色，使其包含调用 Amazon DevOps Guru 的足够权限。在 CodePipeline 管道中，在部署阶段之前添加一个新阶段。选择 DevOps Guru 作为新阶段的操作提供程 序。使用来自 CodeCommit 存储库的源工件。","D":"更新附加到 CodePipeline 的 IAM 角色，使其包含调用 Amazon DevOps Guru 的足够权限。在 CodePipeline 管道中，在部署阶段之前添加一个新阶段。为新阶段选择 CodeGuru Security 作为操作 提供程序。使用来自 CodeCommit 存储库的源工件。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon CodeGuru Security is a static application security testing (SAST) service that uses program analysis and machine learning to detect security policy violations and vulnerabilities in source code (including Python). It exposes an API (CreateScan/GetFindings via the codeguru-security CLI/SDK) that can be invoked from a CodeBuild buildspec. In Option A, a CodeBuild project runs the CodeGuru Security scan using an IAM role with the required permissions, then raises an error (non-zero exit) when vulnerabilities are found, which fails the action. Adding that CodeBuild action as a CodePipeline stage before the deployment stage, using the CodeCommit source artifact, stops the deployment when vulnerabilities exist. This is exactly the documented pattern for embedding code vulnerability scanning into CodePipeline. The other options use services that either do not scan first-party application code (Amazon Inspector's InspectorScan targets open-source dependencies via SBOM and container images, not your own Python logic) or are not security code scanners at all (Amazon DevOps Guru is an operational anomaly-detection/AIOps service and is not a CodePipeline action provider).","explanation_zh":"Amazon CodeGuru Security 是一個靜態應用程式安全測試 (SAST) 服務，透過程式分析與機器學習偵測原始碼（包含 Python）中的安全政策違規與漏洞。它提供 API（透過 codeguru-security CLI/SDK 的 CreateScan/GetFindings），可在 CodeBuild buildspec 中呼叫。選項 A 中，CodeBuild 專案使用具備必要權限的 IAM 角色執行 CodeGuru Security 掃描，當發現漏洞時拋出錯誤（以非零結束碼結束）使該 action 失敗。將此 CodeBuild action 加入 CodePipeline、置於部署階段之前，並使用 CodeCommit 來源 artifact，即可在存在漏洞時停止部署。這正是將程式碼漏洞掃描嵌入 CodePipeline 的官方建議模式。其他選項使用的服務要不是不掃描自有應用程式碼（Amazon Inspector 的 InspectorScan 針對的是透過 SBOM 的開源相依套件與容器映像，而非你自己的 Python 邏輯），就是根本不是程式碼安全掃描工具（Amazon DevOps Guru 是運維異常偵測／AIOps 服務，且不是 CodePipeline 的 action provider）。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Amazon Inspector's CI/CD integration (the InspectorScan action) scans open-source dependencies via the SBOM Generator and scans container images for known CVEs; it does not perform SAST on the company's own first-party Python application logic. The option's architecture of 'running an Amazon Inspector scan inside a custom CodeBuild project' is also not the supported pattern (Inspector integrates as a native InspectorScan CodePipeline action, not as a tool invoked from a buildspec the way CodeGuru Security is). CodeGuru Security, not Inspector, is the code-vulnerability SAST service intended here.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 的 CI/CD 整合（InspectorScan action）透過 SBOM Generator 掃描開源相依套件、並掃描容器映像的已知 CVE，並不會對公司自有的 Python 應用程式邏輯做 SAST。選項所述「在自訂 CodeBuild 專案內執行 Amazon Inspector 掃描」也非受支援的模式（Inspector 是以原生 InspectorScan CodePipeline action 整合，而非像 CodeGuru Security 那樣從 buildspec 呼叫）。此處需要的程式碼漏洞 SAST 服務是 CodeGuru Security 而非 Inspector。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon DevOps Guru is an ML-powered operational/AIOps service that detects runtime anomalies and proactive/reactive insights from CloudWatch metrics, logs, and application behavior of running applications. It does not scan source code for security vulnerabilities, and it is not a valid CodePipeline action provider, so this stage cannot be created or block deployment based on code findings.","why_zh":"Amazon DevOps Guru 是以機器學習驅動的運維／AIOps 服務，從運行中應用程式的 CloudWatch 指標、日誌與行為偵測執行期異常與主動／被動洞見。它不會掃描原始碼漏洞，也不是有效的 CodePipeline action provider，因此無法建立此階段，也無法依程式碼掃描結果阻擋部署。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This option is internally contradictory and unsupported: it grants permissions to invoke DevOps Guru (an operational service, not a code scanner) but then selects 'CodeGuru Security as the action provider.' CodeGuru Security is not a native CodePipeline action provider; its documented integration is via a CodeBuild project running the codeguru-security API in a buildspec (as in Option A), not as a direct pipeline action.","why_zh":"此選項內部自相矛盾且不受支援：它授予呼叫 DevOps Guru（運維服務，非程式碼掃描器）的權限，卻又選擇「CodeGuru Security 作為 action provider」。CodeGuru Security 並非原生的 CodePipeline action provider；其官方整合方式是透過 CodeBuild 專案在 buildspec 中呼叫 codeguru-security API（如選項 A），而非作為直接的 pipeline action。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cli/latest/reference/codeguru-security/","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/cicd-inspector-codepipeline-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-InspectorScan.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/devops-guru/latest/userguide/welcome.html"]}},{"id":300,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer deploys an application to a fleet of Amazon Linux EC2 instances. The DevOps engineer needs to monitor system metrics across the fleet. The DevOps engineer wants to monitor the relationship between network traffic and memory utilization for the application code. The DevOps engineer wants to track the data on a 60 second interval. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师将一个应用程序部署到一组亚马逊 Linux EC2 实例上。该 DevOps 工程师需要监控整个 实例群组的系统指标。该 DevOps 工程师希望监控应用程序代码的网络流量与内存利用率之间的关系。该 DevOps 工程师希望以 60 秒为间隔跟踪数据。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use Amazon CloudWatch basic monitoring to collect the NetworkIn metric and the MemoryBytesUsed metric. Graph the metrics in CloudWatch.","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch detailed monitoring to collect the NetworkIn metric and the MemoryBytesUsed metric. Graph the metrics in CloudWatch.","C":"Use Amazon CloudWatch detailed monitoring to collect the NetworkIn metric. Install the CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances to collect the mem_used metric. Graph the metrics in CloudWatch.","D":"Use Amazon CloudWatch basic monitoring to collect the built-in NetworkIn metric. Install the CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances to collect the mem_used metric. Graph the metrics in CloudWatch."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 基本监控来收集 NetworkIn 指标和 MemoryBytesUsed 指标。在 CloudWatch 中 绘制这些指标的图表。","B":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 详细监控来收集 NetworkIn 指标和 MemoryBytesUsed 指标。 在 CloudWatch 中绘制这些指标的图表。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 详细监控来收集 NetworkIn 指标。在 EC2 实例上安装 CloudWatch 代理以收 集 mem_used 指标。在 CloudWatch 中绘制这些指标的图表。","D":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 基本监控来收集内置的 NetworkIn 指标。在 EC2 实例上安装 CloudWatch 代理以收集 mem_used 指标。在 CloudWatch 中绘制这些指标的图表。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two qualifiers decide this question: memory must be collected, and data must be tracked on a 60-second (1-minute) interval. First, EC2 publishes no native memory metric to CloudWatch (the hypervisor cannot see guest-OS memory), and there is no built-in metric named MemoryBytesUsed. The only AWS-supported way to get memory utilization is to install the unified CloudWatch agent, which publishes memory metrics such as mem_used in the CWAgent namespace. This eliminates options A and B, both of which reference the non-existent MemoryBytesUsed metric. Second, between C and D the deciding factor is the 60-second interval: AWS docs state that under EC2 basic monitoring 'status check metrics are available in 1-minute periods; all other metrics are available in 5-minute periods,' whereas detailed monitoring delivers all metrics in 1-minute periods. Option D uses basic monitoring for NetworkIn, which is published only every 5 minutes and therefore fails the 60-second requirement. Option C uses detailed monitoring for NetworkIn (1-minute/60-second granularity) plus the CloudWatch agent for mem_used, satisfying both the memory and the 60-second interval requirements. Therefore C is correct.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個關鍵條件：必須收集記憶體，且資料須以 60 秒（1 分鐘）間隔追蹤。首先，EC2 不會原生地將記憶體指標發布到 CloudWatch（hypervisor 看不到客體作業系統的記憶體），也沒有名為 MemoryBytesUsed 的內建指標。取得記憶體使用率唯一受 AWS 支援的方式是安裝 unified CloudWatch agent，它會在 CWAgent 命名空間發布如 mem_used 等記憶體指標。這排除了引用不存在之 MemoryBytesUsed 指標的選項 A 與 B。其次，在 C 與 D 之間，決定因素是 60 秒間隔：AWS 文件指出在 EC2 basic monitoring 下「狀態檢查指標以 1 分鐘週期提供；所有其他指標以 5 分鐘週期提供」，而 detailed monitoring 則以 1 分鐘週期提供所有指標。選項 D 對 NetworkIn 使用 basic monitoring，每 5 分鐘才發布一次，無法滿足 60 秒需求。選項 C 對 NetworkIn 使用 detailed monitoring（1 分鐘／60 秒粒度），再加上以 CloudWatch agent 收集 mem_used，同時滿足記憶體與 60 秒間隔的需求。因此 C 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no built-in EC2 metric named MemoryBytesUsed; EC2 has no native memory metric, so this cannot collect memory at all. Additionally, basic monitoring publishes NetworkIn at 5-minute periods, not the required 60-second interval.","why_zh":"並不存在名為 MemoryBytesUsed 的內建 EC2 指標；EC2 沒有原生記憶體指標，因此根本無法收集記憶體。此外 basic monitoring 對 NetworkIn 是 5 分鐘週期，而非要求的 60 秒間隔。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"MemoryBytesUsed is not a real EC2/CloudWatch metric, so memory cannot be collected. Detailed monitoring would give NetworkIn at 60 seconds, but memory still requires the CloudWatch agent (mem_used), which this option omits.","why_zh":"MemoryBytesUsed 不是真實的 EC2/CloudWatch 指標，故無法收集記憶體。Detailed monitoring 雖能讓 NetworkIn 達到 60 秒，但記憶體仍需 CloudWatch agent（mem_used），此選項並未包含。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Correctly uses the CloudWatch agent for mem_used, but relies on EC2 basic monitoring for the built-in NetworkIn metric, which is published only at 5-minute periods and therefore fails the required 60-second interval.","why_zh":"正確地用 CloudWatch agent 收集 mem_used，但對內建的 NetworkIn 指標採用 EC2 basic monitoring，其為 5 分鐘週期，無法滿足要求的 60 秒間隔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/manage-detailed-monitoring.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/cloudwatch-metrics-basic-detailed.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/metrics-collected-by-CloudWatch-agent.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/install-CloudWatch-Agent-on-EC2-Instance.html"]}},{"id":301,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Systems Manager to manage a fleet of Amazon Linux EC2 instances that have SSM Agent installed. All EC2 instances are configured to use Instance Metadata Service Version 2 (IMDSv2) and are running in the same AWS account and AWS Region. Company policy requires developers to use only Amazon Linux. The company wants to ensure that all new EC2 instances are automatically managed by Systems Manager after creation. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Systems Manager 来管理一批安装了 SSM 代理的 Amazon Linux EC2 实例。所有 EC2 实例均配置为使用实例元数据服务版本 2（IMDSv2），并且都在同一个 AWS 账户和 AWS 区域中运行。 公司政策要求开发人员只能使用 Amazon Linux。 该公司希望确保所有新创建的 EC2 实例在创建后都能自动由系统管理器进行管理。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM role that has a trust policy that allows Systems Manager to assume the role. Attach the AmazonSSMManagedEC2InstanceDefaultPolicy policy to the role. Configure the default-ec2-instance- management-role SSM service setting to use the role.","B":"Ensure that AWS Config is set up. Create an AWS Config rule that validates if an EC2 instance has SSM Agent installed. Configure the rule to run on EC2 configuration changes. Configure automatic remediation for the rule to run the AWS-InstallSSMAgent SSM document to install SSM Agent.","C":"Configure Systems Manager Patch Manager. Create a patch baseline that automatically installs SSM Agent on all new EC2 instances. Create a patch group for all EC2 instances. Attach the patch baseline to the patch group. Create a maintenance window and maintenance window task to start installing SSM Agent daily.","D":"Create an EC2 instance role that has a trust policy that allows Amazon EC2 to assume the role. Attach the AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore policy to the role. Ensure that AWS Config is set up. Use the ec2-instance-profile-attached managed AWS Config rule to validate if an EC2 instance has the role attached. Configure the rule to run on EC2 configuration changes. Configure automatic remediation for the rule to run the AWS-SetupManagedRoleOnEc2Instance SSM document to attach the role to the EC2 instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有信任策略的 IAM 角色，该策略允许 Systems Manager 假定该角色。将 AmazonSSMManagedEC2InstanceDefaultPolicy 策略附加到该角色。将默认的 ec2 实例管理角色 SSM 服 务设置配置为使用该角色。","B":"确保已设置 AWS Config。创建一条 AWS Config 规则，用于验证 EC2 实例是否已安装 SSM 代理。将 规则配置为在 EC2 配置更改时运行。为该规则配置自动修复，以运行 AWS-InstallSSMAgent SSM 文 档来安装 SSM 代理。","C":"配置系统管理器补丁管理器。创建一个补丁基准，自动在所有新的 EC2 实例上安装 SSM 代理。为所有 EC2 实例创建一个补丁组。将补丁基准附加到补丁组。创建一个维护窗口和维护窗口任务，每天开始安 装 SSM 代理。","D":"创建一个 EC2 实例角色，该角色的信任策略允许 Amazon EC2 假定该角色。将 AmazonSSMManaged InstanceCore 策略附加到该角色。确保已设置 AWS Config。使用 ec2-instance-profile-attached 管理 的 AWS Config 规则来验证 EC2 实例是否附加了该角色。配置规则在 EC2 配置更改时运行。为该 规则配置自动修复，以运行 AWS-SetupManagedRoleOnEc2Instance SSM 文档将角色附加到 EC2 实 例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This scenario is a textbook description of Systems Manager Default Host Management Configuration (DHMC), which lets Systems Manager automatically manage all current and future EC2 instances in an account and Region as managed instances without manually creating and attaching an IAM instance profile per instance. The AWS docs prescribe exactly the three steps in option A: (1) create a service role whose trust policy allows the Systems Manager service principal (ssm.amazonaws.com) to call sts:AssumeRole; (2) attach the AWS managed policy AmazonSSMManagedEC2InstanceDefaultPolicy to that role; and (3) set the default-ec2-instance-management-role SSM service setting to point at the role (aws ssm update-service-setting). DHMC's prerequisites also match the scenario perfectly: instances must use IMDSv2 and have SSM Agent 3.2.582.0 or later, both already stated as true. This is the MOST operationally efficient solution because once activated it applies automatically to every instance in the Region with no per-instance instance profiles, no AWS Config rules, and no remediation pipelines to build or maintain.","explanation_zh":"此情境是 Systems Manager Default Host Management Configuration (DHMC) 的標準描述。DHMC 讓 Systems Manager 自動將帳戶與區域內所有現有與未來的 EC2 instances 作為 managed instances 管理，無須為每台 instance 手動建立並附加 IAM instance profile。AWS 文件明確規定選項 A 的三個步驟：(1) 建立一個 service role，其 trust policy 允許 Systems Manager service principal (ssm.amazonaws.com) 呼叫 sts:AssumeRole；(2) 為該 role 附加 AWS managed policy AmazonSSMManagedEC2InstanceDefaultPolicy；(3) 透過 aws ssm update-service-setting 將 default-ec2-instance-management-role 這個 SSM service setting 指向該 role。DHMC 的先決條件也完全符合情境：instances 必須使用 IMDSv2 且 SSM Agent 版本須為 3.2.582.0 以上，題目皆已說明成立。這是操作效率最高的方案，因為一旦啟用即自動套用至區域內每台 instance，無須逐台 instance profile、無須 AWS Config rules，也無須建置或維護任何補救流程。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The scenario states SSM Agent is already installed on all instances, so an AWS Config rule that checks for and installs the agent solves a non-existent problem. The real gap is the missing IAM permissions/credentials that let the agent register with Systems Manager; installing the agent alone does not make an instance managed. It also adds an unnecessary AWS Config plus remediation pipeline, making it far less operationally efficient than DHMC.","why_zh":"情境已說明所有 instances 都已安裝 SSM Agent，因此檢查並安裝 agent 的 AWS Config rule 解決的是不存在的問題。真正缺少的是讓 agent 能向 Systems Manager 註冊的 IAM 權限/憑證；單純安裝 agent 並不會讓 instance 變成 managed。此外還增加多餘的 AWS Config 與補救流程，操作效率遠低於 DHMC。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Patch Manager and patch baselines apply OS/application patches to already-managed instances; they cannot install SSM Agent or grant the permissions needed to make an instance managed in the first place. A patch baseline does not install SSM Agent, and maintenance window tasks only run against instances Systems Manager already manages, so this approach is circular and technically invalid.","why_zh":"Patch Manager 與 patch baseline 是對已受管理的 instances 套用作業系統/應用程式修補；它們無法安裝 SSM Agent，也無法授予讓 instance 首先成為 managed 所需的權限。patch baseline 不會安裝 SSM Agent，而 maintenance window task 只能對 Systems Manager 已管理的 instances 執行，因此此方案邏輯循環且技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Attaching an EC2 instance role with AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore plus an AWS Config rule (ec2-instance-profile-attached) and the AWS-SetupManagedRoleOnEc2Instance remediation does technically achieve management, but it is far more operationally complex: it requires AWS Config, a managed rule, a remediation document, and attaches a per-instance profile to every instance. DHMC (option A) accomplishes the same automatic management with a single account/Region service-level setting and no per-instance profiles or remediation, so option A wins on MOST operational efficiency.","why_zh":"附加帶有 AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore 的 EC2 instance role，再加上 AWS Config rule (ec2-instance-profile-attached) 與 AWS-SetupManagedRoleOnEc2Instance 補救，技術上確實能達成管理，但操作複雜度高得多：需要 AWS Config、受管 rule、補救文件，並為每台 instance 附加 instance profile。DHMC（選項 A）只需單一帳戶/區域層級的設定即可達成相同的自動管理，無須逐台 instance profile 或補救，因此在「最高操作效率」上選項 A 勝出。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/managed-instances-default-host-management.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/fleet-manager-default-host-management-configuration.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AmazonSSMManagedEC2InstanceDefaultPolicy.html"]}},{"id":302,"question_en":"A company configured an Amazon S3 event source for an AWS Lambda function. The company needs the Lambda function to run when a new object is created or an existing object is modified in a specific S3 bucket. The Lambda function will use the S3 bucket name and the S3 object key of the incoming event to read the contents of the new or modified S3 object. The Lambda function will parse the contents and save the parsed contents to an Amazon DynamoDB table. The Lambda function's execution role has permissions to read from the S3 bucket and to write to the DynamoDB table. During testing, a DevOps engineer discovers that the Lambda function does not run when objects are added to the S3 bucket or when existing objects are modified. Which solution will resolve these problems?","question_zh":"一家公司为 AWS Lambda 函数配置了一个 Amazon S3 事件源。该公司需要在特定的 S3 存储桶中创建新 对象或修改现有对象时运行该 Lambda 函数。该 Lambda 函数将使用传入事件的 S3 存储桶名称和 S3 对 象键来读取新创建或已修改的 S3 对象的内容。该 Lambda 函数将解析内容，并将解析后的内容保存到 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。 Lambda 函数的执行角色具有从 S3 存储桶读取以及向 DynamoDB 表写入的权限。在测试期间，一 位 DevOps 工程师发现，当向 S3 存储桶添加对象或修改现有对象时，Lambda 函数不会运行。 哪种解决方案能解决这些问题？","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 bucket policy for the S3 bucket that grants the S3 bucket permission to invoke the Lambda function.","B":"Create a resource policy for the Lambda function to grant Amazon S3 permission to invoke the Lambda function on the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as an OnFailure destination for the Lambda function. Update the Lambda function to process messages from the SQS queue and the S3 event notifications.","D":"Configure an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as the destination for the S3 bucket event notifications. Update the Lambda function's execution role to have permission to read from the SQS queue. Update the Lambda function to consume messages from the SQS queue."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 S3 存储桶创建一个 S3 存储桶策略，授予该 S3 存储桶调用 Lambda 函数的权限。","B":"为 Lambda 函数创建资源策略，授予 Amazon S3 在 S3 存储桶上调用 Lambda 函数的权限。","C":"将 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列配置为 Lambda 函数的 OnFailure 目的地。更新 Lambda 函数以处理来自 SQS 队列和 S3 事件通知的消息。","D":"将 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队列配置为 S3 存储桶事件通知的目的地。更新 Lambda 函数的执行角色，使其具有从 SQS 队列读取的权限。更新 Lambda 函数以从 SQS 队列 中消费消息。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When Amazon S3 sends an event notification to a Lambda function, S3 invokes the function asynchronously and needs permission from the function's resource-based policy to do so. The AWS Lambda docs state explicitly: 'To invoke your function, Amazon S3 needs permission from the function's resource-based policy. When you configure an Amazon S3 trigger in the Lambda console, the console modifies the resource-based policy... If you configure the notification in Amazon S3, you use the Lambda API to update the policy.' In this scenario the execution role already grants S3 read and DynamoDB write (what the function CAN do), but nothing grants the s3.amazonaws.com service principal the lambda:InvokeFunction action on the function. The documented resource-based policy example shows exactly this statement (Principal s3.amazonaws.com, Action lambda:InvokeFunction, conditioned on the source bucket and account). Because that grant is missing, S3 events silently fail to trigger the function. Adding the Lambda resource-based policy that lets Amazon S3 invoke the function (Option B) directly fixes the root cause.","explanation_zh":"當 Amazon S3 將事件通知傳送給 Lambda function 時，S3 會以非同步方式 invoke 該 function，而要這麼做需要 function 的 resource-based policy 授予權限。AWS Lambda 文件明確指出：「To invoke your function, Amazon S3 needs permission from the function's resource-based policy.」在 Lambda console 設定 S3 trigger 時，console 會自動修改 resource-based policy；但若是在 Amazon S3 端設定通知，就必須用 Lambda API 更新該 policy。本題中 execution role 已授予 S3 讀取與 DynamoDB 寫入（即 function「能做什麼」），但沒有任何設定授予 s3.amazonaws.com 服務主體對該 function 的 lambda:InvokeFunction 權限。官方文件的 resource-based policy 範例正是此語句（Principal 為 s3.amazonaws.com、Action 為 lambda:InvokeFunction，並以來源 bucket 與帳戶作為條件）。由於缺少此授權，S3 事件會默默地無法觸發 function。新增允許 Amazon S3 invoke 該 function 的 Lambda resource-based policy（選項 B）直接解決了根本原因。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An S3 bucket policy controls access TO objects in the bucket (read/write/list); it cannot grant the bucket permission to invoke a Lambda function. Invocation permission for the s3.amazonaws.com principal must live on the Lambda function's resource-based policy, not on the S3 bucket policy. Wrong resource entirely.","why_zh":"S3 bucket policy 控管的是對儲存貯體中物件的存取（讀/寫/列出），無法授予儲存貯體呼叫 Lambda function 的權限。s3.amazonaws.com 主體的 invoke 權限必須設在 Lambda function 的 resource-based policy 上，而非 S3 bucket policy，屬於完全錯誤的資源。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An OnFailure destination only takes effect AFTER a function has been invoked asynchronously and that invocation fails. Here the function is never invoked at all because S3 lacks invoke permission, so an OnFailure destination addresses a different stage and does nothing to fix the missing-invoke-permission root cause.","why_zh":"OnFailure destination 只有在 function 已被非同步 invoke 之後且該次呼叫失敗時才會作用。本題 function 根本未被呼叫，因為 S3 缺少 invoke 權限，因此 OnFailure destination 處理的是不同階段，無法解決缺少呼叫權限的根本原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Rerouting notifications through an SQS queue redesigns the architecture rather than fixing the already-configured S3-to-Lambda trigger; the question states the S3 event source is configured to invoke Lambda directly, so the only missing piece is the resource-based invoke permission. It is also unnecessary overhead, and granting only 'read from the SQS queue' is insufficient for an SQS event source mapping (which also needs DeleteMessage and GetQueueAttributes). The correct, minimal fix is the missing resource-based policy.","why_zh":"改以 SQS queue 轉送通知是重新設計架構，而非修復已設定的 S3 直接觸發 Lambda 流程；題目已說明 S3 event source 設定為直接 invoke Lambda，唯一缺少的就是 resource-based 的 invoke 權限。此外這是不必要的額外負擔，且僅授予「從 SQS queue 讀取」對 SQS event source mapping 而言並不足夠（還需 DeleteMessage 與 GetQueueAttributes）。正確且最小幅度的修正是補上缺少的 resource-based policy。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/access-control-resource-based.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/lambda/latest/dg/with-s3-example.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/EventNotifications.html"]}},{"id":303,"question_en":"A company recently configured AWS Control Tower in its organization in AWS Organizations. The company enrolled all existing AWS accounts in AWS Control Tower. The company wants to ensure that all new AWS accounts are automatically enrolled in AWS Control Tower. The company has an existing AWS Step Functions workflow that creates new AWS accounts and performs any actions required as part of account creation. The Step Functions workflow is defined in the same AWS account as AWS Control Tower. Which combination of steps should the company add to the Step Functions workflow to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司最近在其 AWS 组织中配置了 AWS Control Tower。该公司已将所有现有的 AWS 账户纳入 AWS Control Tower。该公司希望确保所有新的 AWS 账户都能自动纳入 AWS Control Tower。 该公司现有的 AWS Step Functions 工作流会创建新的 AWS 账户，并执行账户创建过程中所需的任何 操作。此 Step Functions 工作流定义在与 AWS Control Tower 相同的 AWS 账户中。 公司应向 Step Functions 工作流添加哪些步骤组合才能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge event that has an aws.controltower source and a CreateManagedAccount detail-type. Add the details of the new AWS account to the detail field of the event.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge event that has an aws.controltower source and a SetupLandingZone detail-type. Add the details of the new AWS account to the detail field of the event.","C":"Create an AWSControlTowerExecution role in the new AWS account. Configure the role to allow the AWS Control Tower administrator account to assume the role.","D":"Call the AWS Service Catalog ProvisionProduct API operation with the details of the new AWS account.","E":"Call the Organizations EnableAWSServiceAccess API operation with the controltower.amazonaws.com service name and the details of the new AWS account."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有 aws.controltower 源和 CreateManagedAccount 详细类型（detail-type）的 Amazon EventBridge 事件。将新 AWS 账户的详细信息添加到事件的 detail 字段中。","B":"创建一个具有 aws.controltower 源和 SetupLandingZone 详细类型属性的 Amazon EventBridge 事件。 将新 AWS 账户的详细信息添加到事件的 detail 字段中。","C":"在新创建的 AWS 账户中创建一个 AWSControlTowerExecution 角色。配置该角色，使其允许 AWS 控制塔管理员账户承担此角色。","D":"使用新 AWS 账户的详细信息调用 AWS 服务目录的 ProvisionProduct API 操作。","E":"调用组织的 EnableAWSServiceAccess API 操作，使用 controltower.amazonaws.com 服务名称以及新 AWS 账户的详细信息。"},"answer":["D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"To programmatically enroll a newly created account into AWS Control Tower from the Step Functions workflow, you call the AWS Service Catalog ProvisionProduct API against the Account Factory product (option D). The official 'Automate Account Provisioning in AWS Control Tower by Service Catalog APIs' page states you 'use the APIs to create and provision your member accounts in AWS Control Tower, or to enroll existing member accounts,' specifically by calling ProvisionProduct (or UpdateProvisionedProduct). That same page's note adds: 'To enroll an existing member account using the ProvisionProduct API, the AWSControlTowerExecution IAM role must exist on the target account before you call the API.' Therefore the workflow must first create the AWSControlTowerExecution role in the new account with a trust policy that lets the Control Tower management/administrator account assume it (option C); the manual-enrollment page shows this role uses an AdministratorAccess policy and a trust policy granting sts:AssumeRole to arn:aws:iam::<management-account-id>:root, and the AWSControlTowerExecution role page confirms it 'allows you to create and enroll accounts, automatically, with scripts and Lambda functions.' C and D are the two required additions. The dump's suggested ['D','E'] is wrong because E does not enroll any account.","explanation_zh":"若要從 Step Functions 工作流程以程式化方式將新建立的帳戶自動納入 AWS Control Tower 治理，需對 Account Factory 產品呼叫 AWS Service Catalog 的 ProvisionProduct API（選項 D）。官方頁面「Automate Account Provisioning in AWS Control Tower by Service Catalog APIs」明確指出，可使用這些 API 來建立並佈建 member accounts，或納入既有的 member accounts，方法即為呼叫 ProvisionProduct（或 UpdateProvisionedProduct）。該頁的備註進一步說明：使用 ProvisionProduct API 納入既有 member account 之前，目標帳戶上必須先存在 AWSControlTowerExecution IAM role。因此工作流程必須先在新帳戶中建立 AWSControlTowerExecution role，並設定信任政策允許 Control Tower 的 management/administrator 帳戶來擔任（assume）此角色（選項 C）；手動納入頁面顯示此角色使用 AdministratorAccess 政策，並以信任政策將 sts:AssumeRole 授予 arn:aws:iam::<management-account-id>:root，而 AWSControlTowerExecution role 說明頁也確認此角色「可讓您以指令碼與 Lambda 函式自動建立並納入帳戶」。C 與 D 即為所需新增的兩個步驟。dump 建議的 ['D','E'] 在 E 上是錯誤的，因為 E 不會納入任何帳戶。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CreateManagedAccount is an outbound AWS Control Tower lifecycle event that Control Tower EMITS to EventBridge AFTER an account is created/enrolled; it is not an event you publish to TRIGGER enrollment. Putting account details into the detail field of a fabricated PutEvents event does nothing to invoke Control Tower or provision an account.","why_zh":"CreateManagedAccount 是 AWS Control Tower 在帳戶建立／納入之後對外發送到 EventBridge 的生命週期事件（lifecycle event），不是您發布來「觸發」納入的事件。在偽造的 PutEvents 事件 detail 欄位塞入帳戶資訊並不會呼叫 Control Tower 或佈建帳戶。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same flaw as A, and worse: SetupLandingZone is also an outbound Control Tower lifecycle event (it fires when a landing zone is set up), not an input event that enrolls accounts. The landing zone is already configured in this scenario, so publishing such an event provisions or enrolls nothing.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的問題，且更不合理：SetupLandingZone 同樣是 Control Tower 對外發送的生命週期事件（在 landing zone 建置時觸發），並非用於納入帳戶的輸入事件。本題情境中 landing zone 已建置完成，發布此事件不會佈建或納入任何帳戶。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Organizations EnableAWSServiceAccess with controltower.amazonaws.com only enables trusted (service) access org-wide one time (handled during Control Tower setup); the API takes a ServicePrincipal, not 'details of a new account,' and it does not provision or enroll any individual account.","why_zh":"對 controltower.amazonaws.com 呼叫 Organizations EnableAWSServiceAccess 只是一次性在整個組織啟用受信任（服務）存取（於 Control Tower 設定時已處理）；此 API 接受的是 ServicePrincipal，而非「新帳戶的詳細資訊」，且不會佈建或納入任何個別帳戶。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/automated-provisioning-walkthrough.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/awscontroltowerexecution.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/enroll-manually.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/lifecycle-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/servicecatalog/latest/dg/API_ProvisionProduct.html"]}},{"id":304,"question_en":"A company's web application uses an Application Load Balancer (ALB) to direct traffic to Amazon EC2 instances across three Availability Zones. The company has deployed a newer version of the application to one Availability Zone for testing. If a problem is detected with the application, the company wants to direct traffic away from the affected Availability Zone until the deployment has been rolled back. The application must remain available and maintain static stability during the rollback. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司的网络应用程序使用应用负载均衡器（ALB）将流量分配到三个可用区中的亚马逊 EC2 实例。 该公司已在其中一个可用区部署了应用程序的新版本以进行测试。如果出现 检测到应用程序出现问题，公司希望在回滚部署期间将流量从受影响的可用区转移出去。在此期间，应 用程序必须保持可用并维持静态稳定。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Disable cross-zone load balancing on the ALB's target group. Initiate a zonal shift on the ALB to direct traffic away from the affected Availability Zone.","B":"Disable cross-zone load balancing on the ALB's target group. Manually remove instances in the target group that belong to the affected Availability Zone.","C":"Configure cross-zone load balancing on the ALB's target group to inherit settings from the ALB. Initiate a zonal shift on the ALB to direct traffic away from the affected Availability Zone.","D":"Configure cross-zone load balancing on the ALB's target group to inherit settings from the ALB. Remove the subnet that is associated with the affected Availability Zone."},"options_zh":{"A":"禁用应用负载均衡器（ALB）目标组的跨区负载均衡。在 ALB 上启动区域转移，将流量从受影响的可 用区转移出去。","B":"禁用应用负载均衡器（ALB）目标组的跨区域负载均衡。手动从目标组中移除属于受影响可用区的实例。","C":"在 ALB 的目标组上配置跨区域负载均衡，以继承 ALB 的设置。在 ALB 上启动区域转移，将流量从受影 响的可用区转移出去。","D":"在 ALB 的目标组上配置跨区域负载均衡以继承 ALB 的设置。移除与受影响的可用区相关联的子 网。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"ARC zonal shift is the most operationally efficient mechanism because it directs traffic away from a single impaired Availability Zone with one action, so the decision reduces to the cross-zone load balancing setting, which the 'maintain static stability' requirement determines. The ALB zonal shift documentation explicitly warns that 'if your load balancers have cross-zone load balancing turned off and you use a zonal shift to remove a zonal load balancer IP address, the Availability Zone affected by the zonal shift also loses target capacity.' Losing serving capacity during the event breaks static stability, so disabling cross-zone load balancing (options A and B) is wrong. With cross-zone load balancing enabled, 'all traffic to targets is blocked in the availability zone being impacted, and zonal IP addresses are removed from DNS,' while the load balancer nodes in the remaining healthy AZs keep distributing traffic across all remaining healthy targets, preserving full capacity. On an ALB, cross-zone load balancing is on by default and can only be turned off at the target group level, so configuring the target group to inherit the ALB setting keeps it enabled, and starting a single zonal shift gives the operational efficiency. Therefore C both maintains static stability and is the most operationally efficient.","explanation_zh":"ARC zonal shift 是最具營運效率的機制，因為它能以單一動作將流量導離單一受損的 Availability Zone，因此關鍵落在 cross-zone load balancing 設定，而這由「維持 static stability」需求決定。ALB zonal shift 文件明確警告：若 load balancer 關閉 cross-zone load balancing，而你使用 zonal shift 移除某個 zonal load balancer IP 位址，受 zonal shift 影響的 Availability Zone 也會同時失去目標容量（target capacity）。在事件期間失去服務容量會破壞 static stability，因此關閉 cross-zone load balancing（選項 A 與 B）是錯的。在啟用 cross-zone load balancing 的情況下，受影響 AZ 內所有對目標的流量會被封鎖，且 zonal IP 位址會從 DNS 移除，而其餘健康 AZ 的 load balancer node 仍持續將流量分散到所有剩餘健康目標，維持完整容量。在 ALB 上，cross-zone load balancing 預設為開啟且無法在 load balancer 層級變更，只能在 target group 層級關閉；因此將 target group 設定為繼承 ALB 設定即保持啟用，再啟動單一 zonal shift 即達到營運效率。故 C 同時維持 static stability 並具最高營運效率。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"It uses zonal shift (correct, single-action) but disables cross-zone load balancing on the target group. The ALB zonal shift docs state that with cross-zone load balancing turned off, the AZ affected by the zonal shift also loses target capacity, which breaks the required static stability. The mechanism is right but the cross-zone setting is wrong.","why_zh":"它使用 zonal shift（正確，單一動作），但在 target group 上關閉 cross-zone load balancing。ALB zonal shift 文件指出，關閉 cross-zone load balancing 時，受 zonal shift 影響的 AZ 也會失去目標容量，破壞所需的 static stability。機制方向正確，但 cross-zone 設定錯誤。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Disabling cross-zone load balancing breaks static stability (the remaining nodes lose access to that AZ's targets), and manually removing or deregistering instances is a multi-step, error-prone, slow operation that is far less operationally efficient than a single zonal shift.","why_zh":"關閉 cross-zone load balancing 會破壞 static stability（其餘 node 失去存取該 AZ 目標的能力），而手動移除或取消註冊執行個體是多步驟、易出錯且緩慢的操作，營運效率遠低於單一 zonal shift。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Keeping cross-zone load balancing enabled is correct, but removing the affected AZ's subnet from the ALB is a heavier, manual infrastructure change to the load balancer's AZ configuration: it is slower, harder to reverse during rollback, and far less operationally efficient than a single reversible zonal shift action. Zonal shift exists precisely to avoid such manual changes.","why_zh":"保持 cross-zone load balancing 啟用是正確的，但從 ALB 移除受影響 AZ 的 subnet 是對 load balancer AZ 設定較重的人工基礎架構變更：較慢、在回復時更難逆轉，營運效率遠低於單一可逆的 zonal shift 動作。zonal shift 正是為了避免這類人工變更而存在。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/zonal-shift.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/application-load-balancers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/r53recovery/latest/dg/route53-arc-best-practices.zonal-shifts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/reliability-pillar/rel_withstand_component_failures_static_stability.html"]}},{"id":305,"question_en":"A company has several AWS accounts. An Amazon Connect instance runs in each account. The company uses an Amazon EventBridge default event bus in each account for event handling. A DevOps team needs to receive all the Amazon Connect events in a single DevOps account. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有多个 AWS 账户。每个账户中都运行着一个 Amazon Connect 实例。该公司在每个账户中使用 Amazon EventBridge 默认事件总线来处理事件。 一个 DevOps 团队需要在一个 DevOps 账户中接收所有的 Amazon Connect 事件。 哪种解决方案符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the resource-based policy of the default event bus in each account to allow the DevOps account to replay events. Configure an EventBridge rule in the DevOps account that matches Amazon Connect events and has a target of the default event bus in the other accounts.","B":"Update the resource-based policy of the default event bus in each account to allow the DevOps account to receive events. Configure an EventBridge rule in the DevOps account that matches Amazon Connect events and has a target of the default event bus in the other accounts.","C":"Update the resource-based policy of the default event bus in the DevOps account. Update the policy to allow events to be received from the accounts. Configure an EventBridge rule in each account that matches Amazon Connect events and has a target of the DevOps account's default event bus.","D":"Update the resource-based policy of the default event bus in the DevOps account. Update the policy to allow events to be replayed by the accounts. Configure an EventBridge rule in each account that matches Amazon Connect events and has a target of the DevOps account's default event bus."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个账户中更新默认事件总线的基于资源的策略，以允许 DevOps 账户重放事件。在 DevOps 账户中 配置一个 EventBridge 规则，使其匹配 Amazon Connect 事件，并将目标设置为其他账户中的默认事件 总线。","B":"在每个账户中更新默认事件总线的基于资源的策略，以允许 DevOps 账户接收事件。在 DevOps 账户中配 置一个 EventBridge 规则，使其匹配 Amazon Connect 事件，并将目标设置为其他账户中的默认事件总线。","C":"更新 DevOps 账户中默认事件总线的基于资源的策略。将策略更新为允许从这些账户接收事件。在每个账 户中配置一个 EventBridge 规则，使其匹配 Amazon Connect 事件，并将目标设置为 DevOps 账户的默认 事件总线。","D":"更新 DevOps 账户中默认事件总线的基于资源的策略。将策略更新为允许账户重放事件。在每个账户中配 置一个 EventBridge 规则，该规则匹配 Amazon Connect 事件，并将目标设置为 DevOps 账户的默认事件 总线。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"To centralize events, EventBridge cross-account routing pushes events from each sender account to the receiver account's event bus. Per the AWS docs, on the RECEIVER account you edit the resource-based policy of the event bus to allow the specified accounts to send (events:PutEvents) events, and on each SENDER account you create a rule whose target is the receiver account's event bus. Here the DevOps account is the receiver and the member Amazon Connect accounts are senders. Option C correctly places the resource-based policy on the DevOps account's default event bus (allowing events to be received from the other accounts) and puts the matching EventBridge rule in each member account with the DevOps bus as the target. The key permission is events:PutEvents (receive/publish), not 'replay', and the flow direction must be member -> central (rules live in the sender accounts), which only C satisfies.","explanation_zh":"要集中收集事件，EventBridge 跨帳戶路由是把事件從各發送方帳戶推送到接收方帳戶的 event bus。根據 AWS 文件，在接收方帳戶上要編輯 event bus 的 resource-based policy，允許指定帳戶送出（events:PutEvents）事件；在每個發送方帳戶上要建立一條 rule，其 target 為接收方帳戶的 event bus。本題中 DevOps 帳戶是接收方，各執行 Amazon Connect 的成員帳戶是發送方。選項 C 正確地把 resource-based policy 設在 DevOps 帳戶的 default event bus（允許從其他帳戶接收事件），並在每個成員帳戶建立比對 Amazon Connect 事件、以 DevOps event bus 為 target 的 rule。關鍵權限是 events:PutEvents（接收／發布），而非 'replay'；流向必須是成員 -> 中央（rule 位於發送方帳戶），只有 C 同時滿足這兩點。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Reverses the flow: it puts the resource policy on each member account's bus and the rule in the DevOps account targeting the member buses, which would push events from DevOps to members, not collect them. An EventBridge rule sends events to its target bus, so this never ingests Connect events into the DevOps bus. It also uses 'replay' permission, which is an EventBridge archive feature, not the cross-account events:PutEvents permission needed to receive events.","why_zh":"流向相反：把 resource policy 設在各成員帳戶的 bus、rule 放在 DevOps 帳戶並以成員 bus 為 target，這會把事件從 DevOps 推向成員而非集中收集。EventBridge rule 會把事件送到其 target bus，因此永遠無法把 Connect 事件擷取到 DevOps bus。它還使用 'replay' 權限，這是 EventBridge archive 的功能，並非接收事件所需的跨帳戶 events:PutEvents 權限。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same reversed direction as A: the resource policy is on each member bus and the rule sits in the DevOps account targeting the member buses. Because a rule pushes events to its target, this configuration would route events out of DevOps into the member accounts and never centralize them. To centralize, the rules must live in the sender (member) accounts and target the DevOps bus.","why_zh":"與 A 相同的反向流向：resource policy 設在各成員 bus，rule 放在 DevOps 帳戶並以成員 bus 為 target。由於 rule 會把事件推送到其 target，此設定會把事件從 DevOps 路由到成員帳戶，永遠無法集中。要集中事件，rule 必須位於發送方（成員）帳戶並以 DevOps bus 為 target。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Has the correct topology (policy on the DevOps bus, rules in each member account targeting DevOps) but grants the wrong permission: 'allow events to be replayed by the accounts'. Replay applies to EventBridge archives, not cross-account event delivery. The receiver bus policy must grant events:PutEvents so member accounts can send/receive events, which D does not.","why_zh":"拓撲正確（policy 在 DevOps bus、rule 在各成員帳戶並以 DevOps 為 target），但授予了錯誤權限：'allow events to be replayed by the accounts'。Replay 適用於 EventBridge archive，而非跨帳戶事件傳遞。接收方 bus 的 policy 必須授予 events:PutEvents，讓成員帳戶可送出／接收事件，而 D 並未如此。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-event-bus-example-policy-cross-account.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-event-bus-perms.html"]}},{"id":306,"question_en":"A company has deployed an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster with Amazon EC2 node groups. The company's DevOps team uses the Kubernetes Horizontal Pod Autoscaler and recently installed a supported EKS cluster Autoscaler. The DevOps team needs to implement a solution to collect metrics and logs of the EKS cluster to establish a baseline for performance. The DevOps team will create an initial set of thresholds for specific metrics and will update the thresholds over time as the cluster is used. The DevOps team must receive an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) email notification if the initial set of thresholds is exceeded or if the EKS cluster Autoscaler is not functioning properly. The solution must collect cluster, node, and pod metrics. The solution also must capture logs in Amazon CloudWatch. Which combination of steps should the DevOps team take to meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司部署了一个带有 Amazon EC2 节点组的 Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service（Amazon EKS）集群。 该公司的 DevOps 团队使用了 Kubernetes 水平 Pod 自动扩展器，并且最近安装了一个受支持的 EKS 集群 自动扩展器。 DevOps 团队需要实施一个解决方案来收集 EKS 集群的指标和日志，以建立性能基准。DevOps 团队将为 特定指标创建初始阈值集，并随着集群的使用情况适时更新这些阈值。如果初始阈值集被超出，或者 EKS 集群的自动扩展器运行不正常，DevOps 团队必须收到亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）的电子 邮件通知。 该解决方案必须收集集群、节点和 Pod 的指标。该解决方案还必须在 Amazon CloudWatch 中捕获日志。 DevOps 团队应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the CloudWatch agent and Fluent Bit to the cluster. Ensure that the EKS cluster has appropriate permissions to send metrics and logs to CloudWatch.","B":"Deploy AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry to the cluster. Ensure that the EKS cluster has appropriate permissions to send metrics and logs to CloudWatch.","C":"Create CloudWatch alarms to monitor the CPU, memory, and node failure metrics of the cluster. Configure the alarms to send an SNS email notification to the DevOps team if thresholds are exceeded.","D":"Create a CloudWatch composite alarm to monitor a metric log filter of the CPU, memory, and node metrics of the cluster. Configure the alarm to send an SNS email notification to the DevOps team when anomalies are detected.","E":"Create a CloudWatch alarm to monitor the logs of the Autoscaler deployments for errors. Configure the alarm to send an SNS email notification to the DevOps team if thresholds are exceeded.","F":"Create a CloudWatch alarm to monitor a metric log filter of the Autoscaler deployments for errors. Configure the alarm to send an SNS email notification to the DevOps team if thresholds are exceeded."},"options_zh":{"A":"在集群中部署 CloudWatch 代理和 Fluent Bit。确保 EKS 集群具有向 CloudWatch 发送指标 和日志的适当权限。","B":"将 AWS OpenTelemetry 发行版部署到集群。确保 EKS 集群具有向 CloudWatch 发送指标和日志的 适当权限。","C":"创建 CloudWatch 警报以监控集群的 CPU、内存和节点故障指标。将警报配置为在阈值超出时向 DevOps 团队发送 SNS 电子邮件通知。","D":"创建一个 CloudWatch 复合警报，用于监控集群的 CPU、内存和节点指标的日志筛选器。配置警报， 以便在检测到异常时向 DevOps 团队发送 SNS 电子邮件通知。","E":"创建一个 CloudWatch 警报来监控自动缩放器部署的日志中的错误。如果超出阈值，配置警报向 DevOps 团队发送 SNS 电子邮件通知。","F":"创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，用于监控 Autoscaler 部署的指标日志筛选器中的错误。如果超出阈值，配 置警报向 DevOps 团队发送 SNS 电子邮件通知。"},"answer":["A","C","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","C","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the canonical CloudWatch Container Insights pattern for Amazon EKS on EC2 node groups. (A) Deploy the containerized CloudWatch agent (a DaemonSet that discovers running containers and collects cluster, node, and pod performance metrics as embedded-metric-format performance log events) together with Fluent Bit (a DaemonSet that forwards container/application logs to CloudWatch Logs); the cluster needs IAM permissions to send metrics and logs to CloudWatch. This satisfies both 'collect cluster, node, and pod metrics' and 'capture logs in CloudWatch.' (C) Container Insights surfaces CPU, memory, and node metrics as CloudWatch metrics, so you can create static-threshold CloudWatch alarms on CPU, memory, and node failure that send an SNS email when the team's initial thresholds are exceeded, matching the requirement to define and later tune an explicit threshold set. (F) To detect that the Cluster Autoscaler is not functioning, its logs must first be converted into a numerical metric using a CloudWatch Logs metric filter that matches error patterns, and then an alarm on that metric filter sends the SNS email; the 'Alarming on logs' doc explicitly requires creating a log group and a metric filter before you can alarm on log data, so F is the technically correct option and E (which alarms on logs without a metric filter) is wrong.","explanation_zh":"這是 Amazon EKS on EC2 node group 的標準 CloudWatch Container Insights 模式。(A) 部署容器化的 CloudWatch agent（以 DaemonSet 形式探索叢集中執行的容器，並以 embedded metric format 的 performance log event 收集 cluster、node、pod 層級的效能 metrics），搭配 Fluent Bit（DaemonSet，將容器/應用程式 logs 轉送到 CloudWatch Logs）；叢集需具備將 metrics 與 logs 傳送到 CloudWatch 的 IAM 權限。如此同時滿足『收集 cluster、node、pod metrics』與『將 logs 擷取到 CloudWatch』。(C) Container Insights 會把 CPU、memory、node metrics 呈現為 CloudWatch metrics，因此可針對 CPU、memory、node failure 建立靜態門檻（static threshold）的 CloudWatch alarm，當超過團隊設定的初始門檻時透過 SNS 寄送 email，正好符合需先訂定、後續再調整明確門檻組的需求。(F) 要偵測 Cluster Autoscaler 是否正常運作，必須先用 CloudWatch Logs metric filter 比對錯誤模式，把 logs 轉換成數值 metric，再針對該 metric filter 建立 alarm 寄送 SNS email；『Alarming on logs』文件明確要求在對 log 資料設定 alarm 前必須先建立 log group 與 metric filter，因此 F 才是技術上正確的選項，而 E（未建立 metric filter 就直接對 logs 設定 alarm）是錯誤的。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry (ADOT) exports metrics and traces (via OTLP/Prometheus) but is not the documented EKS-on-EC2 Container Insights pattern for collecting cluster/node/pod performance metrics AND capturing container logs to CloudWatch together; log capture in the canonical setup is handled by Fluent Bit, not ADOT.","why_zh":"AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry (ADOT) 主要匯出 metrics 與 traces（透過 OTLP/Prometheus），並非同時收集 cluster/node/pod 效能 metrics 並把容器 logs 擷取到 CloudWatch 的標準 EKS-on-EC2 Container Insights 模式；標準設定中的 log 擷取由 Fluent Bit 負責，而非 ADOT。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A composite alarm determines its state by monitoring the states of OTHER alarms using Boolean logic; it does not monitor a metric/log filter directly. It also relies on anomaly detection rather than the explicit static thresholds the team wants to define and tune over time.","why_zh":"composite alarm 是透過 Boolean 邏輯監看『其他 alarm』的狀態來決定自身狀態，並不會直接監看 metric 或 log filter；且本選項採用 anomaly detection，而非團隊要先訂定並隨時間調整的明確 static threshold。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"You cannot create a CloudWatch alarm directly on raw log text. The 'Alarming on logs' procedure requires first creating a log group-metric filter to turn matching log patterns into a metric; only then can an alarm be created. Option F adds the required metric filter step that E omits.","why_zh":"無法直接針對原始 log 文字建立 CloudWatch alarm。『Alarming on logs』流程要求先建立 log group-metric filter，把符合的 log 模式轉換成 metric，之後才能建立 alarm。選項 F 補上了 E 所遺漏、必要的 metric filter 步驟。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContainerInsights.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Container-Insights-setup-logs-FluentBit.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Container-Insights-EKS-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Alarm-On-Logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateMetricFilterProcedure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/alarm-combining.html"]}},{"id":307,"question_en":"A company discovers that its production environment and disaster recovery (DR) environment are deployed to the same AWS Region. All the production applications run on Amazon EC2 instances and are deployed by AWS CloudFormation. The applications use an Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP volume for application storage. No application data resides on the EC2 instances. A DevOps engineer copies the required AMIs to a new DR Region. The DevOps engineer also updates the CloudFormation code to accept a Region as a parameter. The storage needs to have an RPO of 10 minutes in the DR Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司发现其生产环境和灾难恢复（DR）环境部署在同一个 AWS 区域。所有生产应用程序均在 Amazon EC2 实例上运行，并通过 AWS CloudFormation 进行部署。这些应用程序使用 Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP 卷进行应用存储。没有应用程序数据驻留在 EC2 实例上。 一位 DevOps 工程师将所需的 AMI 复制到新的灾难恢复区域。该 DevOps 工程师还更新了 CloudFormation 代码，使其能够接受区域作为参数。在灾难恢复区域，存储需要具有 10 分钟的恢复点目标（RPO）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket in both Regions. Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) for the S3 buckets. Create a scheduled AWS Lambda function to copy any new content from the FSx for ONTAP volume to the S3 bucket in the production Region.","B":"Use AWS Backup to create a backup vault and a custom backup plan that has a 10-minute frequency. Specify the DR Region as the target Region. Assign the EC2 instances in the production Region to the backup plan.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to create snapshots of the instance store volumes that are attached to the EC2 instances. Configure the Lambda function to copy the snapshots to the DR Region and to remove the previous copies. Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule that invokes the Lambda function every 10 minutes.","D":"Create an FSx for ONTAP instance in the DR Region. Configure a 5-minute schedule for a volume- level NetApp SnapMirror to replicate the volume from the production Region to the DR Region."},"options_zh":{"A":"在两个区域分别创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。为这两个 S3 存储桶配置 S3 跨区域复制（CRR）。创 建一个计划的 AWS Lambda 函数，用于将 FSx for ONTAP 卷中的任何新内容复制到生产区域的 S3 存储桶中。","B":"使用 AWS Backup 创建一个备份存储库和一个自定义备份计划，该计划的频率为 10 分钟。指定灾难 恢复区域作为目标区域。将生产区域中的 EC2 实例分配给该备份计划。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于为附加到 EC2 实例的实例存储卷创建快照。配置该 Lambda 函数， 使其将快照复制到灾难恢复区域，并删除之前的副本。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则， 每 10 分钟调用一次该 Lambda 函数。","D":"在灾难恢复区域创建一个 FSx for ONTAP 实例。为卷级 NetApp SnapMirror 配置 5 分钟的计划，将 生产区域的卷复制到灾难恢复区域。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application data lives on the Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP volume (the question explicitly states no application data resides on the EC2 instances), so the DR solution must replicate that ONTAP volume cross-Region. AWS documentation for FSx for ONTAP states that NetApp SnapMirror can schedule periodic replication for both in-Region and cross-Region deployments, and that 'Replication can be scheduled as frequently as every 5 minutes.' It also notes that only volume-level SnapMirror is supported by FSx for ONTAP (not SVM-DR, not synchronous), which is exactly what option D configures: an FSx for ONTAP file system in the DR Region with a 5-minute volume-level SnapMirror schedule. A 5-minute interval comfortably meets the 10-minute RPO, and SnapMirror replicates block-level changes natively between ONTAP file systems, leaving a ready-to-use volume for failover. This is the purpose-built, native mechanism for FSx for ONTAP cross-Region disaster recovery.","explanation_zh":"應用程式資料儲存在 Amazon FSx for NetApp ONTAP volume 上（題目明確指出 EC2 執行個體上沒有任何應用程式資料），因此 DR 方案必須將該 ONTAP volume 跨 Region 複寫。FSx for ONTAP 的 AWS 文件指出，NetApp SnapMirror 可為同 Region 與跨 Region 部署排程定期複寫，並明確說明「複寫最頻繁可每 5 分鐘排程一次」。文件同時說明 FSx for ONTAP 僅支援 volume-level SnapMirror（不支援 SVM-DR 與同步 SnapMirror），這正是選項 D 的設定：在 DR Region 建立 FSx for ONTAP 檔案系統，並設定 5 分鐘的 volume-level SnapMirror 排程。5 分鐘的間隔可充分滿足 10 分鐘的 RPO 需求，且 SnapMirror 在兩個 ONTAP 檔案系統間以區塊層級原生複寫變更，於故障切換時即可直接使用該 volume。這是 FSx for ONTAP 跨 Region 災難復原的專屬原生機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Copying FSx for ONTAP data to S3 via a scheduled Lambda plus S3 CRR is a fragile, high-overhead custom pipeline that is not designed for a guaranteed 10-minute RPO. It does not replicate the live ONTAP volume into a usable FSx file system in the DR Region, so the applications could not directly mount the storage on failover, and it ignores the native SnapMirror replication built for ONTAP.","why_zh":"用排程 Lambda 把 FSx for ONTAP 資料複製到 S3 再加上 S3 CRR，是脆弱、維運負擔高的自訂管線，並非為保證 10 分鐘 RPO 而設計。它不會把實際的 ONTAP volume 複寫成 DR Region 中可用的 FSx 檔案系統，故障轉移時應用程式無法直接掛載儲存，且忽略了 ONTAP 原生的 SnapMirror 複寫機制。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The application data resides on the FSx for ONTAP volume, not on the EC2 instances, so assigning the EC2 instances to a backup plan would never capture the application data. Additionally, AWS Backup scheduled (snapshot) backup plans have a minimum frequency far coarser than 10 minutes (hourly at best via cron, not 10-minute periodic), so a 10-minute backup frequency is not achievable with this approach.","why_zh":"應用程式資料位於 FSx for ONTAP volume 而非 EC2 執行個體，因此將 EC2 執行個體指派給備份計畫永遠無法擷取應用程式資料。此外，AWS Backup 排程（快照）備份計畫的最小頻率遠粗於 10 分鐘（以 cron 排程最頻繁為每小時，並非 10 分鐘週期），因此此方法無法達成每 10 分鐘的備份頻率。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Instance store volumes are ephemeral local storage and cannot be snapshotted at all, so the proposed Lambda could not create snapshots of them. Moreover, the application data is on the FSx for ONTAP volume, not on instance store, so this approach captures none of the data that needs DR protection.","why_zh":"Instance store volume 是暫時性本機儲存，根本無法建立快照，因此所提的 Lambda 無法為其建立快照。此外，應用程式資料位於 FSx for ONTAP volume 而非 instance store，因此此方法無法擷取任何需要 DR 保護的資料。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/scheduled-replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fsx/latest/ONTAPGuide/how-it-works-fsx-ontap.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/creating-a-backup-plan.html"]}},{"id":308,"question_en":"During a security audit, a company discovered that some security groups allow SSH traffic from 0.0.0.0/0. A security team must implement a solution to detect and remediate this issue as soon as possible. The company uses one organization in AWS Organizations to manage all the company's AWS accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"在一次安全审计中，一家公司发现某些安全组允许从 0.0.0.0/0 进行 SSH 通信。安全团队必须尽快实施 解决方案来检测并修复此问题。该公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理其所有的 AWS 账 户。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Config for all AWS accounts. Use a periodic trigger to activate the vpe-sg-port-restriction- check AWS Config rule. Create an AWS Lambda function to remediate any noncompliant rules.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function in each AWS account to delete all the security group rules. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match security group update events or creation events. Set the Lambda function in each account as a target for the rule.","C":"Enable AWS Config for all AWS accounts. Create a custom AWS Config rule to run on the restricted- ssh configuration change trigger. Configure the rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function to remediate any noncompliant resources.","D":"Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation document in each account to inspect all security groups and to delete noncompliant rules. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to run the Automation document every hour."},"options_zh":{"A":"为所有 AWS 账户启用 AWS Config。使用定期触发器激活 vpe-sg-port-restrictioncheck AWS Config 规 则。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来修复任何不符合规则的情况。","B":"在每个 AWS 账户中创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来删除所有安全组规则。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以匹配安全组更新事件或创建事件。将每个账户中的 Lambda 函数设置为该规则的 目标。","C":"为所有 AWS 账户启用 AWS Config。创建一个自定义的 AWS Config 规则，在受限的账户上运行。 SSH 配置更改触发器。配置规则以调用 AWS Lambda 函数来修复任何不符合要求的资源。","D":"在每个账户中创建一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 文档，用于检查所有安全组并删除不符合 规定的规则。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则每小时运行一次该 Automation 文档。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The qualifier 'detect and remediate as soon as possible' demands near-real-time, configuration-change-based detection rather than interval-based scanning. The decision is between A and C, since both pair AWS Config with a Lambda remediation. Option C uses the purpose-built restricted-ssh managed rule (identifier INCOMING_SSH_DISABLED), which is NON_COMPLIANT exactly when SSH is reachable from 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0, configured with a configuration-change trigger; per AWS docs a configuration-change trigger evaluates immediately after AWS Config receives the configuration item change notification, giving the fastest possible detection, then invokes Lambda to remediate. Option A relies on the vpc-sg-port-restriction-check rule, whose trigger type is Periodic only (AWS docs confirm it cannot use a configuration-change trigger), so it evaluates on an interval (for example every 24 hours) and cannot meet 'as soon as possible.' Because A is explicitly built on a periodic trigger and C uses an immediate configuration-change trigger, C is the genuinely correct answer. (The option's loose phrase 'custom AWS Config rule' is imprecise wording, but the operative facts - restricted-ssh + configuration-change trigger + Lambda remediation - are exactly what satisfies the requirement.)","explanation_zh":"題目限定條件「盡快偵測並修復」要求接近即時、以組態變更為基礎的偵測，而非依固定間隔掃描。真正的取捨在 A 與 C 之間，因為兩者都搭配 AWS Config 與 Lambda 修復。選項 C 使用專門設計的 restricted-ssh 受管規則（識別碼 INCOMING_SSH_DISABLED），其在 SSH 開放給 0.0.0.0/0 或 ::/0 時即判定為 NON_COMPLIANT，並設定為 configuration change trigger；根據 AWS 文件，configuration change trigger 會在 AWS Config 收到組態項目變更通知後立即評估，提供最快的偵測，再呼叫 Lambda 進行修復。選項 A 依賴 vpc-sg-port-restriction-check 規則，其 trigger type 僅為 Periodic（AWS 文件確認該規則無法使用 configuration change trigger），因此只能依間隔（例如每 24 小時）評估，無法滿足「盡快」。由於 A 明確建立在 periodic trigger 上，而 C 使用即時的 configuration change trigger，因此 C 才是正確答案。（選項中『custom AWS Config rule』的措辭略為不精確，但其關鍵事實 - restricted-ssh + configuration change trigger + Lambda 修復 - 正是滿足需求的做法。）","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The vpc-sg-port-restriction-check rule has a Periodic trigger type ONLY (per AWS docs it cannot be triggered by configuration changes), and the option explicitly uses a periodic trigger. Periodic evaluation runs on an interval (e.g., every 24 hours), so it cannot detect and remediate 'as soon as possible,' failing the key qualifier.","why_zh":"vpc-sg-port-restriction-check 規則的 trigger type 僅為 Periodic（依 AWS 文件無法由組態變更觸發），且該選項明確使用 periodic trigger。Periodic 評估依間隔執行（例如每 24 小時），因此無法做到『盡快』偵測與修復，未能滿足關鍵限定條件。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The Lambda function deletes ALL security group rules, which is destructive and would remove legitimate, required rules along with the noncompliant SSH rule. This is not targeted remediation, would break workloads, and has no Config compliance tracking; it does not properly fix only the 0.0.0.0/0 SSH issue.","why_zh":"該 Lambda 函式刪除『所有』安全群組規則，屬破壞性操作，會連同合法且必要的規則一併刪除。這並非針對性修復，會造成工作負載中斷，也缺乏 Config 合規追蹤，無法只修正 0.0.0.0/0 的 SSH 問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An SSM Automation document run by an EventBridge schedule 'every hour' is interval-based (hourly), so it is slower than configuration-change detection and does not meet 'as soon as possible.' It is also more operationally heavy, requiring per-account Automation documents and schedules and scanning all security groups each run.","why_zh":"由 EventBridge 排程『每小時』執行的 SSM Automation 文件屬間隔式（每小時），比組態變更偵測慢，無法滿足『盡快』。同時運維負擔較大，需在每個帳戶建立 Automation 文件與排程，且每次都掃描所有安全群組。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/restricted-ssh.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/vpc-sg-port-restriction-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html"]}},{"id":309,"question_en":"A company's DevOps engineer must install a software package on 30 on-premises VMs and 15 Amazon EC2 instances. The DevOps engineer needs to ensure that all VMs receive the package in a process that is auditable and that any configuration drift on the VMs is automatically identified and alerted on. The company uses AWS Direct Connect to connect its on-premises data center to AWS. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 工程师必须在 30 台本地虚拟机和 15 台亚马逊 EC2 实例上安装一个软件包。 DevOps 工程师需要确保所有虚拟机都能接收到该软件包，并且整个过程可审计，同时自动识别虚拟机 上的任何配置偏差。 并发出警报。该公司使用 AWS Direct Connect 将其本地数据中心连接到 AWS。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Write a script that iterates through the list of VMs once a week. Configure the script to check for the package and install the package if the package is not found. Configure the script to send an email message notification to the system administrator if the package is not found.","B":"Install the AWS Systems Manager Agent (SSM Agent) on all VMs. Use the SSM Agent to install the package. Use AWS Config to monitor for configuration drift. Use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to notify the system administrator if any drift is found.","C":"Write a script that checks if the package is installed across the environment. Configure the script to create a list of all VMs that are noncompliant. Configure the script to send the list to the system administrator, who will install the package on the noncompliant VMs.","D":"Log in to each VM. Use a local package manager to install the package. Use AWS Config to monitor the AWS resources for configuration changes. Write a script to monitor the on-premises resources."},"options_zh":{"A":"编写一个每周运行一次的脚本，遍历虚拟机列表。配置该脚本检查指定软件包，如果未找到该软 件包则进行安装。如果未找到该软件包，配置脚本向系统管理员发送电子邮件通知。","B":"在所有虚拟机上安装 AWS 系统管理器代理（SSM 代理）。使用 SSM 代理来安装软件包。使用 AWS 配置来监控配置漂移。如果发现任何漂移，使用亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）通知 系统管理员。","C":"编写一个脚本，用于检查整个环境中是否已安装该软件包。配置该脚本，使其生成所有未安装该 软件包的虚拟机列表。配置该脚本，使其将该列表发送给系统管理员，由系统管理员在未安装 该软件包的虚拟机上进行安装。","D":"登录到每台虚拟机。使用本地包管理器安装软件包。使用 AWS Config 监控 AWS 资源的配置更改。 编写一个脚本以监控本地资源。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Option B is the only fully managed, auditable, and automated end-to-end solution. AWS Systems Manager natively manages both EC2 instances and non-EC2/on-premises VMs once they are registered as managed nodes via a hybrid activation (Activation Code + ID) and the SSM Agent is installed; the AWS docs confirm Systems Manager supports 'Amazon EC2 instances, edge devices, and on-premises servers or VMs.' SSM (Run Command/State Manager/Distributor) then installs the package consistently across the whole fleet in an auditable, repeatable way, and the existing Direct Connect link gives the on-premises VMs network access to the Systems Manager endpoints. For drift, AWS Config explicitly supports recording software inventory changes on 'Amazon EC2 instances and on-premises servers' using SSM Inventory data; you can author a Config rule that 'checks whether your managed instances have a specified application, and an instance doesn't have that application installed, AWS Config flags that instance as noncompliant.' AWS Config then 'sends a notification to your Amazon SNS topic' when the compliance status of a resource changes, alerting the administrator automatically. This satisfies the MOST operational efficiency qualifier, while A, C, and D rely on custom scripts, manual logins, or email notifications that are not auditable and provide no automated drift detection.","explanation_zh":"選項 B 是唯一完全託管、可稽核且端到端自動化的方案。AWS Systems Manager 在透過 hybrid activation（Activation Code + ID）註冊為 managed node 並安裝 SSM Agent 後，能原生管理 EC2 instances 與非 EC2／on-premises VMs；AWS 文件確認 Systems Manager 支援『Amazon EC2 instances、edge devices 以及 on-premises servers 或 VMs』。接著可用 SSM（Run Command／State Manager／Distributor）以可稽核、可重複的方式在整個 fleet 上一致地安裝套件，而既有的 Direct Connect 連線讓 on-premises VMs 能連到 Systems Manager 端點。在 drift 偵測方面，AWS Config 明確支援使用 SSM Inventory 資料記錄『Amazon EC2 instances 與 on-premises servers』的軟體 inventory 變更；可建立 Config rule 檢查 managed instance 是否安裝指定 application，未安裝時 AWS Config 會將該 instance 標記為 noncompliant。當資源合規狀態變更時，AWS Config 會『傳送通知到您的 Amazon SNS topic』，自動通知管理員。這滿足『最高營運效率』的條件，而 A、C、D 依賴自訂腳本、手動登入或電子郵件通知，既不可稽核也沒有自動化 drift 偵測。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A weekly custom script that checks/installs the package and emails the admin is high-overhead, brittle, and not auditable in any structured way. It provides no continuous/automatic drift detection (only a weekly run) and must be built to reach both EC2 and on-premises hosts itself rather than leveraging managed services, failing the MOST operationally efficient qualifier.","why_zh":"每週執行的自訂腳本檢查／安裝套件並寄 email 給管理員，營運負擔高、脆弱且沒有結構化稽核能力。它沒有持續／自動化的 drift 偵測（僅每週執行一次），且須自行打通同時觸及 EC2 與地端主機，而非善用託管服務，無法滿足最高營運效率。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A script that only produces a noncompliant list for a human to manually remediate is neither automated installation nor automated drift alerting. It requires manual admin action to fix drift, is not auditable through a managed service, and is the opposite of operational efficiency.","why_zh":"僅產生 noncompliant 清單交由人工手動修復的腳本，既非自動安裝也非自動 drift 告警。修正 drift 需管理員手動介入，未透過託管服務稽核，與營運效率背道而馳。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Manually logging in to each VM with a local package manager does not scale to 45 hosts and is not auditable. AWS Config alone records AWS resources; the proposal even adds a separate custom script to monitor on-premises hosts instead of using SSM managed nodes + Config inventory recording, which is exactly the high-overhead, non-unified approach the question wants to avoid.","why_zh":"逐台手動登入用本機套件管理員安裝無法擴展到 45 台且不可稽核。僅靠 AWS Config 只記錄 AWS 資源；此方案還另加一支自訂腳本監控地端主機，而非使用 SSM managed node + Config inventory 記錄，正是題目想避免的高負擔、非統一作法。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/recording-managed-instance-inventory.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/hybrid-activation-managed-nodes.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/activations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/how-does-config-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-inventory.html"]}},{"id":310,"question_en":"A company has an AWS CodePipeline pipeline in the eu-west-1 Region. The pipeline stores the build artifacts in an Amazon S3 bucket. The pipeline builds and deploys an AWS Lambda function by using an AWS CloudFormation deploy action. A DevOps engineer needs to update the existing pipeline to also deploy the Lambda function to the us- east-1 Region. The pipeline has already been updated to create an additional artifact to deploy to us-east- 1. Which combination of steps should the DevOps engineer take to meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司在 eu-west-1 区域拥有一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。该管道将构建工件存储在 Amazon S3 存储 桶中。该管道通过使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署操作来构建和部署一个 AWS Lambda 函数。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要更新现有的流水线，以便将 Lambda 函数也部署到 useast-1 区域。该流水线已更 新为创建一个额外的工件以部署到 us-east-1 区域。 DevOps 工程师应采取哪些步骤组合来满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Modify the CloudFormation template to include a parameter for the Lambda function code's .zip file location. Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to pass in the us-east-1 artifact location as a parameter override.","B":"Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to use the CloudFormation template from the additional artifact that was created for us-east-1.","C":"Create an S3 bucket in us-east-1. Configure the S3 bucket policy to allow CodePipeline to have read and write access.","D":"Create an S3 bucket in us-east-1. Configure S3 Cross-Region Replication (CRR) from the S3 bucket in eu-west-1 to the S3 bucket in us-east-1.","E":"Modify the pipeline to include the S3 bucket for us-east-1 as an artifact store. Create a new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 in the pipeline. Configure the new deploy action to use the CloudFormation template from the us-east-1 artifact."},"options_zh":{"A":"修改 CloudFormation 模板，添加一个用于 Lambda 函数代码的 .zip 文件位置的参数。在管道中为 us- east-1 创建一个新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。配置新的部署操作，将 us-east-1 的工件位置作为参 数覆盖传入。","B":"在管道中为 us-east-1 创建一个新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。将新部署操作配置为使用为 us-east-1 创建的附加工件中的 CloudFormation 模板。","C":"在 us-east-1 区域创建一个 S3 存储桶。配置 S3 存储桶策略，允许 CodePipeline 具有读写访问权限。","D":"在 us-east-1 区域创建一个 S3 存储桶。配置从 eu-west-1 区域的 S3 存储桶到 us-east-1 区域的 S3 存储桶 的 S3 跨区域复制（CRR）。","E":"修改管道，将 us-east-1 区域的 S3 存储桶作为工件存储包含进来。在管道中为 us-east-1 区域创建一个 新的 CloudFormation 部署操作。配置新的部署操作，使其使用来自 us-east-1 区域的工件中的 CloudFormation 模板。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Two AWS constraints decide this. (1) For a CodePipeline cross-Region CloudFormation deploy action, you must register a separate artifact bucket per Region in the pipeline's artifactStores map; CodePipeline then 'replicates only the input artifacts of the cross-Region action from the pipeline Region to the action's Region.' Option E does exactly this: it adds the us-east-1 bucket as a pipeline artifact store and creates the new CloudFormation deploy action for us-east-1 that uses the template from the us-east-1 artifact. (2) AWS::Lambda::Function Code.S3Bucket must be 'an Amazon S3 bucket in the same AWS Region as your function,' so when the deploy action runs in us-east-1 the Lambda .zip must be referenced from a us-east-1 bucket. Option A satisfies this with the documented pattern: parameterize the template for the .zip location and have the deploy action pass the us-east-1 artifact location via a parameter override (Fn::GetArtifactAtt returning BucketName/ObjectKey). Together A and E meet both requirements; the dump's C/E pairing fails because C only sets a manual bucket policy instead of registering the bucket in artifactStores, and C/E omits the parameter-override step that points the Lambda code at the same-Region us-east-1 bucket.","explanation_zh":"兩個 AWS 限制決定了答案。(1) 對於 CodePipeline 跨 Region 的 CloudFormation deploy action，必須在 pipeline 的 artifactStores 對應表中為每個 Region 註冊一個獨立的 artifact bucket；CodePipeline 接著會「只將跨 Region action 的 input artifacts 從 pipeline Region 複製到該 action 所在的 Region」。選項 E 正是如此：它將 us-east-1 的 S3 bucket 加入為 pipeline 的 artifact store，並建立使用 us-east-1 artifact 中 CloudFormation template 的新 deploy action。(2) AWS::Lambda::Function 的 Code.S3Bucket 必須是「與函式位於相同 AWS Region 的 Amazon S3 bucket」，因此當 deploy action 在 us-east-1 執行時，Lambda 的 .zip 必須引用 us-east-1 的 bucket。選項 A 以官方記載的模式滿足此需求：將 template 參數化以接收 .zip 位置，並讓 deploy action 透過 parameter override（Fn::GetArtifactAtt 回傳 BucketName/ObjectKey）傳入 us-east-1 artifact 位置。A 與 E 共同滿足兩項需求；dump 給的 C/E 組合不成立，因為 C 只設定手動的 bucket policy 而非在 artifactStores 中註冊 bucket，且 C/E 缺少將 Lambda code 指向同 Region us-east-1 bucket 的 parameter-override 步驟。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"B only points the new deploy action at the us-east-1 template artifact but does nothing about registering the per-Region artifact store (required for any cross-Region action) or about where the Lambda .zip code comes from. Without the parameter override from A, the template's Code.S3Bucket would not reference a valid same-Region us-east-1 bucket, so the Lambda deploy would fail. It is an incomplete subset of E plus A.","why_zh":"B 只是讓新的 deploy action 指向 us-east-1 的 template artifact，但既未註冊每個 Region 的 artifact store（任何跨 Region action 都必需），也未處理 Lambda .zip 程式碼的來源。若沒有 A 的 parameter override，template 的 Code.S3Bucket 將無法引用有效的同 Region us-east-1 bucket，導致 Lambda 部署失敗。它只是 E 加 A 的不完整子集。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creating a us-east-1 bucket with a manual read/write bucket policy does NOT register that bucket in the pipeline's artifactStores map, which is the documented requirement for a cross-Region action and what triggers CodePipeline's built-in cross-Region artifact replication. CodePipeline replicates artifacts only into buckets declared as artifact stores per Region, so C alone does not make the cross-Region CloudFormation action work, and it does not address the same-Region Lambda code reference.","why_zh":"建立帶有手動讀寫 bucket policy 的 us-east-1 bucket，並不會將該 bucket 註冊到 pipeline 的 artifactStores 對應表，而那才是跨 Region action 的官方需求，也是觸發 CodePipeline 內建跨 Region artifact 複製的關鍵。CodePipeline 只會將 artifacts 複製到各 Region 宣告為 artifact store 的 bucket，因此單靠 C 無法讓跨 Region 的 CloudFormation action 運作，也未解決同 Region 的 Lambda 程式碼引用問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 Cross-Region Replication is not how CodePipeline moves artifacts across Regions. The docs state 'CodePipeline handles the copying of artifacts from one AWS Region to the other Regions when performing cross-region actions,' driven by the artifactStores configuration, not by CRR. CRR is asynchronous/eventually consistent and not tied to pipeline execution, so it would not register the bucket as a pipeline artifact store and does not satisfy the cross-Region action requirement.","why_zh":"S3 Cross-Region Replication 並非 CodePipeline 跨 Region 搬移 artifacts 的機制。官方文件指出「執行跨 Region action 時，CodePipeline 會負責將 artifacts 從一個 Region 複製到其他 Region」，這由 artifactStores 設定驅動，而非 CRR。CRR 是非同步/最終一致且未與 pipeline 執行綁定，也不會把 bucket 註冊為 pipeline 的 artifact store，因此無法滿足跨 Region action 的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-create-cross-region.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-lambda-function-code.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/continuous-delivery-codepipeline-parameter-override-functions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/continuous-delivery-codepipeline-action-reference.html"]}},{"id":311,"question_en":"A company uses an AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) application for its infrastructure. The AWS CDK application creates AWS Lambda functions and the IAM roles that are attached to the functions. The company also uses AWS Organizations. The company's developers can assume the AWS CDK application deployment role. The company's security team discovered that the developers and the role used to deploy the AWS CDK application have more permissions than necessary. The security team also discovered that the roles attached to the Lambda functions that the CDK application creates have more permissions than necessary. The developers must not have the ability to grant additional permissions. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"该公司使用 AWS 云开发工具包（AWS CDK）应用程序来构建其基础设施。该 AWS CDK 应用程序会创 建 AWS Lambda 函数以及与这些函数关联的 IAM 角色。该公司还使用 AWS 组织。公司的开发人员可以 承担 AWS CDK 应用程序部署角色。 该公司安全团队发现，开发人员以及用于部署 AWS CDK 应用程序的角色所拥有的权限超出了必要范 围。安全团队还发现，CDK 应用程序创建的 Lambda 函数所关联的角色所拥有的权限也超出了必要范 围。开发人员不得拥有授予额外权限的能力。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that denies the iam:CreateRole action and the iam:UpdateRole action for the developer role and the AWS CDK application deployment role. Centrally create new IAM roles to attach to the Lambda functions for the developers to use to provision Lambda functions.","B":"Create an IAM permission boundary policy. Define the maximum actions that the AWS CDK application requires in the policy. Update the account's AWS CDK bootstrapping to use the permission boundary. Update the configuration in the AWS CDK application for the default permissions boundary to use the policy.","C":"Create an IAM permission boundary policy. Define the maximum actions that the AWS CDK application requires in the policy. Instruct the developers to use the permission boundary policy name when they create a role in the AWS CDK application code.","D":"Create an SCP that denies the iam:CreateRole action and the iam:UpdateRole action for the developer role. Give the AWS CDK deployment role access to create roles associated with Lambda functions. Run AWS Identity and Access Management Access Analyzer to verify that the Lambda functions role does not have permissions."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 SCP，拒绝开发人员角色和 AWS CDK 应用程序部署角色的 iam:CreateRole 操作和 iam: UpdateRole 操作。集中创建新的 IAM 角色，将其附加到 Lambda 函数，供开发人员用于配置 Lambda 函数。","B":"创建一个 IAM 权限边界策略。在策略中定义 AWS CDK 应用程序所需的最大操作权限。更新账户的 AWS CDK 启动配置以使用该权限边界。在 AWS CDK 应用程序的默认权限边界配置中使用该策略。","C":"创建一个 IAM 权限边界策略。在策略中定义 AWS CDK 应用程序所需的最大操作权限。指示开发人 员在 AWS CDK 应用程序代码中创建角色时使用权限边界策略名称。","D":"创建一个 SCP，拒绝开发人员角色的 iam:CreateRole 操作和 iam:UpdateRole 操作。授予 AWS CDK 部 署角色创建与 Lambda 函数相关联的角色的权限。运行 AWS 身份和访问管理访问分析器以验证 Lambda 函数角色没有权限。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The scenario requires capping two things with the least operational overhead while preventing developers from escalating privileges: (1) the CDK deployment/developer permissions, and (2) the over-permissioned Lambda execution roles that the CDK app creates. Option B does both automatically with an IAM permissions boundary. Running 'cdk bootstrap --custom-permissions-boundary' attaches the boundary to the bootstrap CloudFormationExecutionRole, so it 'set[s] the maximum permissions that can be performed by developers in your organization when using the AWS CDK.' Configuring the CDK app's default permissions boundary (PermissionsBoundary.fromName/fromArn at the Stage or Stack scope) makes the CDK 'apply a permissions boundary to all IAM Roles and Users created within a scope' - including every Lambda execution role the app creates - so those roles can never exceed the boundary and developers cannot grant additional permissions. AWS explicitly recommends permissions boundaries (or SCPs) for exactly this case ('When organizations want to prevent the CDK from creating roles, it is usually to prevent developers from being able to create IAM roles... we recommend using permission boundaries') and explicitly advises against fine-grained allow/deny policies or centrally pre-creating roles because those break CDK's automatic role creation, slow development, and make continuous delivery impossible.","explanation_zh":"本題需要以最少維運成本同時限制兩件事，並防止開發者提權：(1) CDK 部署/開發者的權限，以及 (2) CDK 應用程式建立、權限過大的 Lambda 執行角色。選項 B 透過 IAM permissions boundary 自動完成兩者。執行 'cdk bootstrap --custom-permissions-boundary' 會把 boundary 附加到 bootstrap 產生的 CloudFormationExecutionRole 上，因此可『設定組織內開發者使用 AWS CDK 時所能執行的最大權限』。在 CDK 應用程式中設定預設的 permissions boundary（在 Stage 或 Stack 範圍使用 PermissionsBoundary.fromName/fromArn）會讓 CDK『對範圍內建立的所有 IAM Roles 與 Users 套用 permissions boundary』——包含應用程式建立的每個 Lambda 執行角色——因此這些角色永遠無法超出 boundary，開發者也無法授予額外權限。AWS 文件明確針對此情境建議使用 permissions boundaries（或 SCP）：『當組織想阻止 CDK 建立角色時，通常是為了防止開發者建立 IAM 角色……我們建議使用 permission boundaries』；並明確不建議採用細粒度 allow/deny 政策或集中預建角色，因為那會破壞 CDK 的自動建立角色機制、拖慢開發、並使持續交付無法進行。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Denying iam:CreateRole/iam:UpdateRole via an SCP breaks the CDK pattern, which automatically creates the Lambda roles during deployment. Centrally pre-creating every Lambda role by hand is high operational overhead, and AWS docs explicitly advise against it (manual role creation slows development, forces wildcards/predictable names, and makes continuous delivery impossible).","why_zh":"用 SCP 拒絕 iam:CreateRole/iam:UpdateRole 會破壞 CDK 自動於部署時建立 Lambda 角色的機制。集中手動預建每個 Lambda 角色維運成本高，且 AWS 文件明確不建議（手動建角色會拖慢開發、被迫使用萬用字元/可預測名稱，並使持續交付無法進行）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This relies on developers manually typing the permissions boundary name each time they create a role in CDK code - it depends on developer discipline (they can simply omit it), is not enforced automatically, and does not attach a boundary to the deployment role itself. The correct mechanism is the CDK's app-level default PermissionsBoundary plus the bootstrap boundary (option B), which auto-applies to all created roles without per-role manual action.","why_zh":"此選項依賴開發者每次在 CDK 程式碼建立角色時手動輸入 permissions boundary 名稱——仰賴開發者自律（可直接省略）、未自動強制執行，且未對部署角色本身附加 boundary。正確機制是 CDK 應用層級的預設 PermissionsBoundary 加上 bootstrap boundary（選項 B），會自動套用到所有建立的角色，無需逐一手動操作。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Denying CreateRole/UpdateRole only on the developer role still lets the CDK deployment role create over-permissioned Lambda roles, so the Lambda roles are not capped. IAM Access Analyzer is a detective/reactive verification tool, not a preventive guardrail, and running it to 'verify' permissions adds ongoing manual overhead rather than reducing it.","why_zh":"僅對開發者角色拒絕 CreateRole/UpdateRole，CDK 部署角色仍可建立權限過大的 Lambda 角色，這些角色並未被限制。IAM Access Analyzer 是偵測/事後驗證工具，並非預防性護欄；以它去『驗證』權限只會增加持續性的手動維運成本，而非降低成本。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/v2/guide/customize-permissions-boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/v2/guide/best-practices-security.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/api/v2/docs/aws-cdk-lib.PermissionsBoundary.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/v2/guide/ref-cli-cmd-bootstrap.html"]}},{"id":312,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) private registries to store container images. A DevOps team needs to ensure that the container images are regularly scanned for software package vulnerabilities. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）的私有注册表来存储容器镜像。 DevOps 团队需要确保定期扫描容器镜像中的软件包漏洞。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable enhanced scanning for private registries in Amazon ECR.","B":"Enable basic continuous scanning for private registries in Amazon ECR.","C":"Create an AWS System Manager Automation document to scan images by using the AWS SDK. Configure the Automation document to run when a new image is pushed to an ECR registry.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function that scans all images in Amazon ECR by using the AWS SDK. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function each day."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用对 Amazon ECR 中的私有注册表的增强扫描功能。","B":"启用对 Amazon ECR 中私有注册表的基本持续扫描。","C":"使用 AWS SDK 创建一个 AWS 系统管理器自动化文档来扫描镜像。配置该自动化文档，使其 在新镜像推送到 ECR 注册表时运行。","D":"使用 AWS SDK 创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于扫描 Amazon ECR 中的所有镜像。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每天调用该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Amazon ECR enhanced scanning integrates with Amazon Inspector to provide automated, continuous scanning of repositories. It scans container images for both operating system AND programming language (software) package vulnerabilities, and as new CVEs are published, Amazon Inspector re-evaluates already-pushed images, updates the findings, and emits an EventBridge event. This managed, configuration-only feature directly satisfies the requirement to regularly scan images for software package vulnerabilities with minimal operational overhead. Option B is invalid: ECR basic scanning offers only two frequencies (manual and scan on push) - there is no 'basic continuous scanning' feature - and basic scanning detects only OS vulnerabilities, not programming-language/software package vulnerabilities. Options C and D are custom-built, high-overhead solutions that reinvent functionality ECR provides natively; a daily Lambda or a one-time scan-on-push automation does not deliver true continuous re-scanning as new vulnerabilities emerge.","explanation_zh":"Amazon ECR enhanced scanning 與 Amazon Inspector 整合，對 repository 提供自動化的持續掃描 (continuous scanning)。它會同時掃描容器映像的作業系統 (OS) 與程式語言 (software) 套件漏洞；當有新的 CVE 公布時，Amazon Inspector 會重新評估已推送的映像、更新 findings 並發出 EventBridge 事件。這是純設定即可啟用的受管功能，最少維運負擔即可滿足「定期掃描映像的軟體套件漏洞」需求。選項 B 不正確：ECR basic scanning 只有兩種頻率 (manual 與 scan on push)，並沒有所謂的『basic continuous scanning』功能，且 basic scanning 只偵測 OS 漏洞，不涵蓋程式語言/軟體套件漏洞。選項 C 與 D 是自行建構、高維運負擔的方案，重複實作 ECR 原生功能；每日 Lambda 或單次 scan-on-push 自動化無法在新漏洞出現時提供真正的持續重新掃描。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"ECR basic scanning has no 'continuous' frequency - it supports only manual and scan on push - and it detects only OS vulnerabilities, not programming-language/software package vulnerabilities, so 'basic continuous scanning' is an invalid/nonexistent option.","why_zh":"ECR basic scanning 沒有『continuous』頻率，只支援 manual 與 scan on push，且僅偵測 OS 漏洞，不涵蓋程式語言/軟體套件漏洞，因此『basic continuous scanning』是不存在的選項。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SSM Automation document triggered on image push is a custom-built, high-overhead solution that runs only once per push, has no native vulnerability-scanning capability, and reinvents ECR enhanced scanning without continuous re-evaluation of new CVEs.","why_zh":"由映像推送觸發的 SSM Automation document 是自行建置、高維運負擔的方案，只在每次推送執行一次，本身不具原生漏洞掃描能力，等於重造 ECR enhanced scanning，且無法針對新 CVE 持續重新評估。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A daily Lambda scanning all images via the SDK is high operational overhead, and there is no SDK call that performs native vulnerability scanning of arbitrary images; a once-per-day schedule is not true continuous scanning and duplicates ECR enhanced scanning.","why_zh":"每日以 SDK 掃描所有映像的 Lambda 屬高維運負擔，且沒有任何 SDK 呼叫可對任意映像執行原生漏洞掃描；每日一次的排程並非真正的持續掃描，且重複了 ECR enhanced scanning 的功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-basic.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/enable-disable-scanning-ecr.html"]}},{"id":313,"question_en":"A security team sets up a workflow that invokes an AWS Step Functions workflow when Amazon EventBridge matches specific events. The events can be generated by several AWS services. AWS CloudTrail records user activities. The security team notices that some important events do not invoke the workflow as expected. The CloudTrail logs do not indicate any direct errors related to the missing events. Which combination of steps will identify the root cause of the missing event invocations? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一个安全团队设置了一个工作流，当 Amazon EventBridge 匹配到特定事件时，该工作流会调用 AWS Step Functions 工作流。这些事件可以由多个 AWS 服务生成。AWS CloudTrail 记录用户活动。 安全团队注意到一些重要事件并未如预期那样触发工作流。CloudTrail 日志中也没有显示与这些 缺失事件直接相关的任何错误。 哪些步骤组合能够找出事件调用丢失的根本原因？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable EventBridge schema discovery on the event bus to determine whether the event patterns match the expected schema.","B":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch to monitor EventBridge metrics and Step Functions metrics. Set up alerts for anomalies in event patterns and workflow invocations.","C":"Configure an AWS Lambda logging function to monitor and log events from EventBridge to provide more details about the processed events.","D":"Review the Step Functions execution history for patterns of failures or timeouts that could correlate to the missing event invocations.","E":"Review metrics for the EventBridge failed invocations to ensure that the IAM execution role that is attached to the rule has sufficient permissions.","F":"Verify that the Step Functions workflow has the correct permissions to be invoked by EventBridge."},"options_zh":{"A":"在事件总线上启用 EventBridge 架构发现功能，以确定事件模式是否与预期架构匹配。","B":"配置 Amazon CloudWatch 来监控 EventBridge 指标和 Step Functions 指标。为事件模式和工作流调 用中的异常情况设置警报。","C":"配置一个 AWS Lambda 日志记录函数，以监控并记录来自 EventBridge 的事件，从而提供有关已 处理事件的更多详细信息。","D":"查看步骤函数的执行历史记录，寻找可能与缺失事件调用相关的故障或超时模式。","E":"检查 EventBridge 失败调用的指标，以确保附加到规则的 IAM 执行角色具有足够的权限。","F":"确认 Step Functions 工作流具有被 EventBridge 调用的正确权限。"},"answer":["B","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A","B","E"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Missing invocations have two distinct root-cause layers: (1) the event never MATCHES the rule's event pattern, or (2) the event matches but the target invocation FAILS. The three correct steps cover both layers plus observability. (A) EventBridge schema discovery infers the actual schema of events flowing on the bus and creates new schema versions when event contents change, so you can compare the real event structure against the rule's event pattern. Because CloudTrail shows no delivery errors, a schema/pattern mismatch (events simply not matching) is the prime suspect, and this is the documented way to surface it. (B) The EventBridge troubleshooting page explicitly tells you to check the CloudWatch metrics TriggeredRules, Invocations, and FailedInvocations for the rule, and the monitoring best-practices page recommends CloudWatch Alarms on these metrics; pairing them with Step Functions metrics is the native way to detect whether rules trigger and targets are invoked. (E) FailedInvocations counts permanently failed invocations; a Step Functions state machine is an ASYNC AWS-service target that EventBridge invokes by assuming the IAM execution role attached to the rule (needing states:StartExecution), so reviewing FailedInvocations together with that role's permissions pinpoints the delivery-layer root cause. D is wrong: missing invocations mean the workflow never started, so there is no Step Functions execution history of failures or timeouts to review (that is a different symptom). F is inaccurate: Step Functions targets are not invoked via a resource-based 'invoke' policy on the state machine (the resource-based fallback exists only for Lambda, SNS, and SQS targets); EventBridge uses the rule's IAM execution role, which E already covers. C (a custom Lambda logging target) is a heavier non-native workaround that A/B/E supersede.","explanation_zh":"未被觸發有兩個不同的根因層：(1) 事件根本未「比對」到 rule 的 event pattern，或 (2) 事件已比對但目標「呼叫失敗」。三個正確步驟同時涵蓋這兩層與可觀測性。(A) EventBridge schema discovery 會從 event bus 上實際流動的事件推斷 schema，且當事件內容改變時會建立新的 schema 版本，讓你把真實事件結構與 rule 的 event pattern 比對。由於 CloudTrail 沒有任何傳遞錯誤，代表事件只是「沒比對到」，schema/pattern 不符正是首要嫌疑，而這是官方記載的揭露方式。(B) EventBridge 疑難排解文件明確要求查看 rule 的 CloudWatch 指標 TriggeredRules、Invocations、FailedInvocations，監控最佳實務文件則建議對這些指標設定 CloudWatch Alarms；搭配 Step Functions 指標即是判斷 rule 是否觸發、目標是否被呼叫的原生方法。(E) FailedInvocations 計算永久失敗的呼叫；Step Functions state machine 是 ASYNC 的 AWS 服務目標，EventBridge 透過假設掛在 rule 上的 IAM execution role (需 states:StartExecution) 來呼叫它，因此檢視 FailedInvocations 與該角色權限可定位傳遞層的根因。D 錯誤：缺少呼叫代表 workflow 從未啟動，因此沒有失敗或逾時的 Step Functions 執行歷史可看 (那是不同症狀)。F 不正確：Step Functions 目標並非透過 state machine 上的資源型『被呼叫』政策被觸發 (資源型 fallback 僅適用於 Lambda、SNS、SQS)；EventBridge 使用 rule 的 IAM execution role，而這已由 E 涵蓋。C (自建 Lambda 記錄目標) 是較重的非原生變通做法，已被 A/B/E 取代。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Adding a custom Lambda logging target to capture event payloads is a heavier, non-native workaround for observability. EventBridge schema discovery (A) plus CloudWatch metrics (B) provide the same root-cause insight natively without building and maintaining extra code, and EventBridge already offers native event bus CloudWatch Logs.","why_zh":"新增自建 Lambda 記錄目標來捕捉事件內容是較重且非原生的可觀測性變通做法。EventBridge schema discovery (A) 加上 CloudWatch 指標 (B) 可原生提供相同的根因洞察，無需自建並維護額外程式碼，且 EventBridge 本身已提供原生的 event bus CloudWatch Logs。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The symptom is MISSING invocations, meaning the workflow never started, so there is no Step Functions execution history of failures or timeouts to review. Execution history only helps when executions actually began and then failed, which is a different problem from events not invoking the workflow.","why_zh":"症狀是『缺少呼叫』，代表 workflow 從未啟動，因此沒有失敗或逾時的 Step Functions 執行歷史可檢視。執行歷史只在執行確實啟動後才失敗時才有用，那與事件未觸發 workflow 是不同的問題。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Step Functions state machines are ASYNC AWS-service targets that EventBridge invokes by assuming the IAM execution role attached to the rule (requiring states:StartExecution), not via a resource-based 'invoke' policy on the state machine. The resource-based permission fallback exists only for Lambda, SNS, and SQS targets. The real permission mechanism is already addressed by E, making F redundant and conceptually inaccurate.","why_zh":"Step Functions state machine 是 ASYNC 的 AWS 服務目標，EventBridge 透過假設掛在 rule 上的 IAM execution role (需 states:StartExecution) 來呼叫，而非透過 state machine 上的資源型『被呼叫』政策。資源型權限 fallback 僅適用於 Lambda、SNS、SQS 目標。真正的權限機制已由 E 涵蓋，使 F 多餘且概念上不正確。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-monitoring.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-monitoring-events-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-schemas-infer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-targets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/eventbridge-integration.html"]}},{"id":314,"question_en":"A company's DevOps engineer uses AWS Systems Manager to perform maintenance tasks. The company has a few Amazon EC2 instances that require a restart after notifications from AWS Health. The DevOps engineer must implement an automated solution that uses Amazon EventBridge to remediate the notifications during the company's scheduled maintenance windows. How should the DevOps engineer configure an EventBridge rule to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS 系统管理器来执行维护任务。该公司有几台亚马逊 EC2 实例，在 收到 AWS 健康状况的通知后需要重启。 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个自动化解决方案，该方案使用亚马逊事件总线（Amazon EventBridge）来进行修复。 公司在计划维护期间的通知。 DevOps 工程师应如何配置 EventBridge 规则以满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure an event source of AWS Health. Configure event types that indicate scheduled instance termination and retirement. Target the AWS-RestartEC2Instance Systems Manager Automation runbook to restart the EC2 instances.","B":"Configure an event source of Systems Manager. Configure an event type that indicates a maintenance window. Target the AWS-RestartEC2Instance Systems Manager Automation runbook to restart the EC2 instances.","C":"Configure an event source of AWS Health. Configure event types that indicate scheduled instance termination and retirement. Target a newly created AWS Lambda function that registers a Systems Manager maintenance window task to restart the EC2 instances.","D":"Configure an event source of EC2. Configure an event type that indicates instance state notification. Target a newly created AWS Lambda function that registers a Systems Manager maintenance window task to restart the EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Health 的事件源。配置指示计划内实例终止和退役的事件类型。将目标指向 AWS- RestartEC2Instance 系统管理器自动化运行手册以重启 EC2 实例。","B":"配置 Systems Manager 的事件源。配置一种表明维护窗口的事件类型。将 AWS-RestartEC2Instance Systems Manager 自动化运行手册作为目标，以重启 EC2 实例。","C":"配置 AWS Health 的事件源。配置指示计划内实例终止和退役的事件类型。将目标指向新创建的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数会注册一个 Systems Manager 维护窗口任务以重启 EC2 实例。","D":"配置一个 EC2 事件源。配置一种表示实例状态通知的事件类型。将目标指向新创建的 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数用于注册 Systems Manager 维护窗口任务以重启 EC2 实例。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"EC2 scheduled instance retirement/termination notices are delivered by AWS Health (source aws.health, eventTypeCategory scheduledChange, codes such as AWS_EC2_PERSISTENT_INSTANCE_RETIREMENT_SCHEDULED), so the EventBridge rule's event source must be AWS Health with the retirement/termination event types. That eliminates B (source = Systems Manager) and D (source = EC2 instance state). The deciding qualifier is that the restart must occur 'during the company's scheduled maintenance windows.' Option A targets the AWS-RestartEC2Instance runbook directly, which restarts the instance immediately when the Health event fires and does not defer the action to any maintenance window, so it fails the maintenance-window requirement. Option C uses a Lambda function to register a Systems Manager maintenance window task to restart the instances; because a maintenance window only executes its registered tasks during its defined schedule, the restart occurs within the approved window, satisfying the requirement. The AWS doc 'Running operations on EC2 instances automatically in response to events in AWS Health' describes the direct-runbook pattern (A), but that pattern is not scoped to a maintenance window, which is the specific constraint this question adds.","explanation_zh":"EC2 排程退役/終止的通知是由 AWS Health 發出的（source 為 aws.health，eventTypeCategory 為 scheduledChange，代碼如 AWS_EC2_PERSISTENT_INSTANCE_RETIREMENT_SCHEDULED），因此 EventBridge 規則的事件來源必須是 AWS Health，並使用退役/終止事件類型。這直接排除 B（來源為 Systems Manager）與 D（來源為 EC2 instance state）。決定性的限定條件是重啟必須「在公司排定的 maintenance window 期間」執行。選項 A 直接以 AWS-RestartEC2Instance runbook 為目標，當 Health 事件觸發時會立即重啟執行個體，並不會將動作延後到任何 maintenance window，因此不符合 maintenance window 的要求。選項 C 使用 Lambda function 註冊一個 Systems Manager maintenance window task 來重啟執行個體；由於 maintenance window 只會在其定義的排程期間執行已註冊的任務，重啟便會落在核准的維護視窗內，符合需求。AWS 文件「Running operations on EC2 instances automatically in response to events in AWS Health」描述的是直接呼叫 runbook 的模式（A），但該模式並未限定於 maintenance window，而這正是本題額外加入的限制條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses the correct AWS Health source, event types, and a valid runbook, but targets AWS-RestartEC2Instance directly, restarting the instance immediately when the event fires. It does not defer the restart to a Systems Manager maintenance window, so it violates the explicit 'during the company's scheduled maintenance windows' requirement. This matches the generic AWS reference pattern, not the maintenance-window-scoped scenario the question specifies.","why_zh":"雖然使用正確的 AWS Health 來源、事件類型與有效的 runbook，但直接以 AWS-RestartEC2Instance 為目標，事件觸發時即立刻重啟執行個體，並未將重啟延後到 Systems Manager maintenance window，因此違反題目明確要求的「在公司排定的 maintenance window 期間」。它符合的是通用的 AWS 參考模式，而非本題限定於維護視窗的情境。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Wrong event source. The notifications originate from AWS Health, not Systems Manager. There is no Systems Manager EventBridge 'maintenance window' event that carries an AWS Health retirement/termination notification, so the rule would never match the intended events.","why_zh":"事件來源錯誤。通知來自 AWS Health 而非 Systems Manager。Systems Manager 並沒有可承載 AWS Health 退役/終止通知的 maintenance window EventBridge 事件，因此規則永遠不會匹配到目標事件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Wrong event source. An EC2 'instance state notification' reports state transitions (e.g., running/stopped/terminated), not AWS Health scheduled retirement/termination notifications. The rule would not trigger on the AWS Health notifications described in the scenario.","why_zh":"事件來源錯誤。EC2 的「instance state notification」報告的是狀態轉換（如 running/stopped/terminated），而非 AWS Health 的排程退役/終止通知。規則不會因情境中所述的 AWS Health 通知而觸發。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/automating-instance-actions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/cloudwatch-events-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-aws-restartec2instance.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-maintenance-windows.html"]}},{"id":315,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer manages an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that builds and deploys a web application on AWS. The pipeline has a source stage, a build stage, and a deploy stage. When deployed properly, the web application responds with a 200 OK HTTP response code when the URL of the home page is requested. The home page recently returned a 503 HTTP response code after CodePipeline deployed the application. The DevOps engineer needs to add an automated test into the pipeline. The automated test must ensure that the application returns a 200 OK HTTP response code after the application is deployed. The pipeline must fail if the response code is not present during the test. The DevOps engineer has added a CheckURL stage after the deploy stage in the pipeline. What should the DevOps engineer do next to implement the automated test?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师管理着一条 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道用于在 AWS 上构建和部署一个网络应 用程序。此管道包含源代码阶段、构建阶段和部署阶段。如果部署得当，当请求主页的 URL 时，该网 络应用程序会返回 200 OK 的 HTTP 响应代码。 最近在 CodePipeline 部署应用程序后，主页返回了 503 HTTP 响应代码。开发运维工程师需要在管道中添 加一个自动化测试。该自动化测试必须确保应用程序在部署后返回 200 OK HTTP 响应代码。如果在测试 期间未出现该响应代码，管道必须失败。开发运维工程师已在管道的部署阶段之后添加了一个 CheckURL 阶段。 接下来，DevOps 工程师应该做什么来实现自动化测试？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the CheckURL stage to use an Amazon CloudWatch action. Configure the action to use a canary synthetic monitoring check on the application URL and to report a success or failure to CodePipeline.","B":"Create an AWS Lambda function to check the response code status of the URL and to report a success or failure to CodePipeline. Configure an action in the CheckURL stage to invoke the Lambda function.","C":"Configure the CheckURL stage to use an AWS CodeDeploy action. Configure the action with an input artifact that is the URL of the application and to report a success or failure to CodePipeline.","D":"Deploy an Amazon API Gateway HTTP API that checks the response code status of the URL and that reports success or failure to CodePipeline. Configure the CheckURL stage to use the AWS Device Farm test action and to provide the API Gateway HTTP API as an input artifact."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CheckURL 阶段配置为使用 Amazon CloudWatch 操作。配置该操作以对应用程序 URL 进行金丝 雀合成监控检查，并向 CodePipeline 报告成功或失败。","B":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来检查 URL 的响应代码状态，并向 CodePipeline 报告成功或失败。在 CheckURL 阶段配置一个操作以调用该 Lambda 函数。","C":"将 CheckURL 阶段配置为使用 AWS CodeDeploy 操作。配置该操作，使其输入工件为应用程序的 URL，并向 CodePipeline 报告成功或失败。","D":"部署一个 Amazon API Gateway HTTP API，用于检查 URL 的响应代码状态，并向 CodePipeline 报告 成功或失败。配置 CheckURL 阶段以使用 AWS 设备农场测试操作，并将 API Gateway HTTP API 作为输入工件提供。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodePipeline supports an Invoke action whose action provider is AWS Lambda, and AWS publishes a dedicated tutorial, 'Invoke an AWS Lambda function in a pipeline in CodePipeline,' that demonstrates exactly this scenario. The tutorial creates a Lambda function that 'tests whether a webpage was deployed successfully': the sample code performs an HTTP GET on the application URL and runs assert(returnedPage.statusCode === 200), then reports the result to CodePipeline by calling PutJobSuccessResult (putJobSuccess) on success or PutJobFailureResult (putJobFailure) on failure. When the function reports failure, the Lambda action fails, which fails the stage and the entire pipeline. The tutorial even adds the Lambda action as a new stage after the CodeDeploy deploy stage, mirroring the CheckURL stage in the question. Option B is therefore the canonical, AWS-documented way to add a post-deploy HTTP-200 check that fails the pipeline.","explanation_zh":"CodePipeline 支援 Invoke 動作，其 action provider 可以是 AWS Lambda，且 AWS 有一篇專門教學「Invoke an AWS Lambda function in a pipeline in CodePipeline」，正好示範這個情境。該教學建立一個 Lambda function 來『測試網頁是否成功部署』：範例程式碼會對應用程式 URL 發出 HTTP GET，並執行 assert(returnedPage.statusCode === 200)，接著在成功時呼叫 PutJobSuccessResult（putJobSuccess）、失敗時呼叫 PutJobFailureResult（putJobFailure）將結果回報給 CodePipeline。當 function 回報失敗，Lambda 動作即失敗，連帶使該 stage 與整個 pipeline 失敗。教學甚至將此 Lambda 動作加為 CodeDeploy 部署 stage 之後的新 stage，正對應題目中的 CheckURL stage。因此選項 B 是 AWS 官方文件記載、為 pipeline 加入部署後 HTTP 200 檢查並可讓 pipeline 失敗的標準做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodePipeline has no 'Amazon CloudWatch' action provider. CloudWatch Synthetics canaries are continuous, scheduled synthetic monitors that emit metrics/alarms; they are not a CodePipeline action that runs once within a stage and returns a pass/fail result to fail the pipeline.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 並沒有『Amazon CloudWatch』這個 action provider。CloudWatch Synthetics canary 是持續、排程式的合成監控，會發出 metric/alarm，並非在 stage 中執行一次並回傳通過/失敗結果以讓 pipeline 失敗的 CodePipeline 動作。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeDeploy is a Deploy-category action provider that deploys application revisions to compute targets (EC2/on-prem, Lambda, ECS). It does not issue an HTTP request to validate a URL's response code, and 'the URL of the application' is not a valid CodeDeploy input artifact.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 是 Deploy 類別的 action provider，用於將應用程式版本部署到運算目標（EC2/地端、Lambda、ECS）。它不會發出 HTTP 請求來驗證 URL 的回應碼，且『應用程式的 URL』也不是有效的 CodeDeploy 輸入工件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Device Farm runs tests against real mobile devices and browsers and does not accept 'an API Gateway HTTP API as an input artifact.' Deploying an API Gateway HTTP API merely to check a URL is convoluted and unnecessary, and this Device Farm + API Gateway combination is not a valid CodePipeline configuration for the task.","why_zh":"AWS Device Farm 是在真實行動裝置與瀏覽器上執行測試，並不會接受『API Gateway HTTP API 作為輸入工件』。僅為檢查 URL 而部署 API Gateway HTTP API 過於迂迴且不必要，且此 Device Farm + API Gateway 組合並非完成此任務的有效 CodePipeline 設定。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-invoke-lambda-function.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/APIReference/API_PutJobSuccessResult.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/APIReference/API_PutJobFailureResult.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html"]}},{"id":316,"question_en":"A company has an application that uploads access logs to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. The fields in the log lines include the response code and the application name. The company wants to create a CloudWatch metric to track the number of requests by response code in a specific range and with a specific application name. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个应用程序，会将访问日志上传到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。日志行中的字段 包括响应代码和应用程序名称。 该公司希望创建一个 CloudWatch 指标，用于跟踪特定范围内且具有特定应用程序名称的请求数量（按 响应代码划分）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudWatch Logs log event filter on the CloudWatch Logs log stream to match the response code range. Configure the log event filter to increment a metric. Set the response code and application name as dimensions.","B":"Create a CloudWatch Logs metric filter on the CloudWatch Logs log group to match the response code range. Configure the metric filter to increment a metric. Set the response code and application name as dimensions.","C":"Create a CloudWatch Contributor Insights rule on the CloudWatch Logs log stream with a filter to match the response code range. Configure the Contributor Insights rule to increment a CloudWatch metric with the response code and application name as dimensions.","D":"Create a CloudWatch Logs Insights query on the CloudWatch Logs log group to match the response code range. Configure the Logs Insights query to increment a CloudWatch metric with the response code and application name as dimensions."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudWatch Logs 日志流上创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 日志事件筛选器，以匹配响应代码范围。配 置日志事件筛选器以递增一个指标。将响应代码和应用程序名称设置为维度。","B":"在 CloudWatch Logs 日志组上创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器，以匹配响应代码范围。配置指 标筛选器以递增一个指标。将响应代码和应用程序名称设置为维度。","C":"在 CloudWatch Logs 日志流上创建一个 CloudWatch 贡献者洞察规则，并设置一个过滤器以匹配响 应代码范围。配置贡献者洞察规则，以响应代码和应用程序名称作为维度来递增 CloudWatch 指 标。","D":"在 CloudWatch Logs 日志组上创建一个 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查询以匹配响应代码范围。配置 Logs Insights 查询，以响应代码和应用程序名称作为维度来递增一个 CloudWatch 指标。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudWatch Logs metric filters are the purpose-built feature for turning matching log events into a numerical CloudWatch metric. Per AWS docs, metric filters are assigned to a log group (not a log stream), and all filters on the group apply to its streams; when the filter pattern matches a term, it increments the metric's count. You can also assign up to three dimensions to a metric created from a JSON or space-delimited metric filter, so response code and application name can be set as dimensions. This exactly satisfies the requirement: a metric filter on the log group matches the response-code range, increments a metric, and sets response code and application name as dimensions. The other choices either invent a non-existent 'log event filter,' attach to a log stream instead of a log group, or use features (Contributor Insights, Logs Insights) that analyze/query logs but do not increment a custom CloudWatch metric with caller-chosen dimensions.","explanation_zh":"CloudWatch Logs metric filter 是專為將符合條件的 log 事件轉換成數值型 CloudWatch metric 而設計的功能。根據 AWS 文件,metric filter 是指派給 log group(而非 log stream),且 log group 上的所有 filter 都會套用到其 log streams;當 filter pattern 比對到條件時,會將該 metric 的計數加上指定數值。對於 JSON 或以空格分隔的 metric filter,最多可指派三個 dimensions,因此可將 response code 與 application name 設為 dimensions。這完全符合需求:在 log group 上建立 metric filter 比對 response code 範圍、遞增 metric,並以 response code 與 application name 作為 dimensions。其他選項要嘛捏造不存在的「log event filter」、要嘛套用到 log stream 而非 log group、要嘛使用了僅能分析/查詢 log 但無法以自選 dimensions 遞增自訂 CloudWatch metric 的功能(Contributor Insights、Logs Insights)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"There is no CloudWatch Logs 'log event filter' feature, and filters are not assigned to a log stream. Metric filters are assigned to the log group, and all filters on the group apply to its streams. The terminology and the attachment point are both wrong.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs 並沒有所謂的「log event filter」功能,且 filter 不是指派到 log stream。Metric filter 是指派給 log group,且 log group 上的所有 filter 會套用到其 streams。此選項在術語與套用對象上都錯誤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudWatch Contributor Insights creates rules (on log groups, not streams) that analyze log data to surface top-N contributors and emit a fixed set of contributor metrics (e.g., UniqueContributors, MaxContributorValue). It does not let you increment an arbitrary custom CloudWatch metric with response code and application name as chosen dimensions the way a metric filter does, and it incorrectly references a log stream.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Contributor Insights 建立的是規則(套用於 log group 而非 stream),用來分析 log 找出 top-N 貢獻者並產出固定的一組 contributor metrics(如 UniqueContributors、MaxContributorValue)。它無法像 metric filter 那樣以 response code 與 application name 作為自選 dimensions 來遞增任意自訂 CloudWatch metric,且此選項也錯誤地指向 log stream。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs Insights is an interactive/ad-hoc query language for log analysis; a query does not increment a CloudWatch metric. AWS docs explicitly contrast the two: a metric filter adds a numerical value to a metric each time a matching log is found, whereas Logs Insights queries are run on demand and do not publish an ongoing custom metric with dimensions.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs Insights 是用於 log 分析的互動式/隨選查詢語言;查詢本身不會遞增 CloudWatch metric。AWS 文件明確區分兩者:metric filter 每次找到符合的 log 就會將數值加到 metric 上,而 Logs Insights 查詢是按需執行,不會持續發佈帶有 dimensions 的自訂 metric。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntaxForMetricFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateMetricFilterProcedure.html"]}},{"id":317,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer provisioned an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster with managed node groups. The DevOps engineer associated an OpenID Connect (OIDC) issuer with the cluster. The DevOps engineer is configuring Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) General Purpose SSD (gp3) volumes for the cluster. The DevOps engineer attempts to initiate a PersistentVolumeClaim (PVC) request but is unable to provision a volume. To troubleshoot the issue, the DevOps engineer runs the kubectl describe pyc command. The DevOps engineer receives a failed to provision volume with StorageClass error and a could not create volume in EC2:UnauthorizedOperation error. Which solution will resolve these errors?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师配置了一个亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集群，其中 托管节点组。DevOps 工程师将一个 OpenID Connect（OIDC）颁发者与集群相关联。 DevOps 工程师正在为集群配置 Amazon Elastic Block Store（Amazon EBS）通用型 SSD（gp3）卷。 DevOps 工程师尝试发起 PersistentVolumeClaim（PVC）请求，但无法分配卷。为了排查问题， DevOps 工程师运行了 kubectl describe pyc 命令。DevOps 工程师收到“无法使用 StorageClass 分配卷” 错误和“无法在 EC2 中创建卷：未经授权的操作”错误。 哪种解决方案能解决这些错误？","options_en":{"A":"Create a Kubernetes cluster role that allows the persistent volumes to perform get, list, watch, create, and delete operations. Configure the cluster role to allow get, list, and watch operations for storage in the cluster.","B":"Create an Amazon EBS Container Storage Interface (CSI) driver IAM role that has the required permissions and trust relationships. Attach the IAM role to the Amazon EBS CSI driver add-on in the cluster.","C":"Add the ebs.csi.aws.com/volumeType:gp3 annotation to the PersistentVolumeClaim object in the cluster.","D":"Create a Kubernetes storage class object. Set the provisioner value to ebs.csi.aws.com. Set the volumeBindingMode value to WaitForFirstConsumer in the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Kubernetes 集群角色，允许持久卷执行获取、列表、监视、创建和删除操作。配置该集群 角色，使其允许在集群中对存储执行获取、列表和监视操作。","B":"创建一个具有所需权限和信任关系的 Amazon EBS 容器存储接口 （CSI） 驱动程序 IAM 角色。将 IAM 角色附加到集群中的 Amazon EBS CSI 驱动程序附加组件。","C":"在集群中的 PersistentVolumeClaim 对象上添加 ebs.csi.aws.com/volumeType:gp3 注解。","D":"创建一个 Kubernetes 存储类对象。将 provisioner 值设置为 ebs.csi.aws.com。在集群中将 volumeBindingMode 值设置为 WaitForFirstConsumer。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The two error strings in the question are quoted verbatim in the official Amazon EKS documentation for the Amazon EBS CSI driver. The 'Step 1: Create an IAM role' section states: 'The Amazon EBS CSI plugin requires IAM permissions to make calls to AWS APIs on your behalf. If you don't do these steps, attempting to install the add-on and running kubectl describe pvc will show failed to provision volume with StorageClass along with a could not create volume in EC2: UnauthorizedOperation error.' UnauthorizedOperation is an AWS IAM/EC2 authorization failure, not a Kubernetes RBAC problem, so the controller's service account lacks permission to call the EC2 CreateVolume API. Because the engineer already associated an OIDC issuer (enabling IAM Roles for Service Accounts / IRSA), the fix is to create an EBS CSI driver IAM role with the required permissions (AmazonEBSCSIDriverPolicy / AmazonEBSCSIDriverPolicyV2) and the correct trust relationship, then attach that role to the EBS CSI driver add-on so the controller can authenticate to EC2. That is exactly option B.","explanation_zh":"題目中的兩個錯誤字串在官方 Amazon EKS 的 Amazon EBS CSI driver 文件中被逐字引用。'Step 1: Create an IAM role' 段落明確指出：EBS CSI plugin 需要 IAM 權限才能代表你呼叫 AWS API；若未完成這些步驟，嘗試安裝 add-on 並執行 kubectl describe pvc 時就會出現 failed to provision volume with StorageClass 以及 could not create volume in EC2: UnauthorizedOperation 錯誤。UnauthorizedOperation 屬於 AWS IAM/EC2 的授權失敗，而非 Kubernetes RBAC 問題，代表 controller 的 service account 缺少呼叫 EC2 CreateVolume API 的權限。由於工程師已關聯 OIDC issuer（啟用 IRSA），正確解法是建立具備所需權限（AmazonEBSCSIDriverPolicy / AmazonEBSCSIDriverPolicyV2）與正確信任關係的 EBS CSI driver IAM role，並將其附加到 EBS CSI driver add-on，讓 controller 能向 EC2 進行身分驗證。這正是選項 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Kubernetes cluster role (RBAC) governs in-cluster API authorization between Kubernetes objects, not AWS API authorization. The UnauthorizedOperation error is returned by the EC2 service, indicating an IAM permission failure on the AWS side when the driver calls EC2 CreateVolume. Adding or modifying Kubernetes RBAC roles cannot grant the controller permission to call EC2, so this does not resolve the error.","why_zh":"Kubernetes cluster role（RBAC）只管理叢集內 Kubernetes 物件之間的 API 授權，而非 AWS API 授權。UnauthorizedOperation 是由 EC2 服務回傳，代表驅動程式呼叫 EC2 CreateVolume 時 AWS 端的 IAM 權限失敗。新增或修改 Kubernetes RBAC 角色無法授予 controller 呼叫 EC2 的權限，因此無法解決此錯誤。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Adding an ebs.csi.aws.com/volumeType:gp3 annotation only influences which volume type is requested; it does nothing to grant IAM permissions. Provisioning still fails at the EC2 authorization step (UnauthorizedOperation) regardless of the requested volume type, so this annotation cannot fix the underlying permission problem.","why_zh":"新增 ebs.csi.aws.com/volumeType:gp3 標註僅影響請求的磁碟類型，完全不涉及授予 IAM 權限。無論請求何種磁碟類型，佈建仍會在 EC2 授權階段失敗（UnauthorizedOperation），因此此標註無法修復根本的權限問題。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating a StorageClass with provisioner ebs.csi.aws.com and volumeBindingMode WaitForFirstConsumer is standard configuration, but the error message already references an existing StorageClass, meaning provisioning is already being attempted. WaitForFirstConsumer only delays binding until a pod is scheduled; it does not provide the IAM permissions the controller needs to call EC2. The UnauthorizedOperation failure would persist.","why_zh":"建立 provisioner 為 ebs.csi.aws.com 且 volumeBindingMode 為 WaitForFirstConsumer 的 StorageClass 屬於標準設定，但錯誤訊息已提及既有的 StorageClass，代表佈建正在進行。WaitForFirstConsumer 只是延後綁定直到 pod 被排程，並未提供 controller 呼叫 EC2 所需的 IAM 權限，UnauthorizedOperation 失敗仍會持續發生。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/ebs-csi.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-managed-policy/latest/reference/AmazonEBSCSIDriverPolicy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-awssupport-troubleshoot-ebs-csi-drivers-for-eks.html"]}},{"id":318,"question_en":"A company runs a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances in a VPC. The company's employees remotely access the EC2 instances by using the Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP). The company wants to collect metrics about how many RDP sessions the employees initiate every day. Which combination of steps will meet this requirement? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司在虚拟私有云（VPC）中运行着一组亚马逊 EC2 实例。该公司的员工通过使用远程桌面协议 （RDP）远程访问这些 EC2 实例。 该公司希望收集有关员工每天发起多少次远程桌面协议（RDP）会话的指标。 哪三种步骤的组合能满足这一要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that reacts to EC2 Instance State-change Notification events.","B":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Specify the log group as a target for the EventBridge rule.","C":"Create a flow log in VPC Flow Logs.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Specify the log group as a destination for the flow log.","E":"Create a log group metric filter.","F":"Create a log group subscription filter. Use EventBridge as the destination."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个亚马逊账 户 对 EC2 实例状态更改通知事件作出反应的 EventBridge 规则。","B":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。将该日志组指定为 EventBridge 规则的目标。","C":"在 VPC 流日志中创建一个流日志。","D":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。将该日志组指定为流日志的目标。","E":"创建日志组指标筛选器。","F":"创建一个日志组订阅筛选器。将 EventBridge 用作目标。"},"answer":["C","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["C","D","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"RDP runs over TCP port 3389. To count how many RDP sessions employees initiate each day, you capture the network traffic reaching the EC2 instances and turn the matching records into a numeric CloudWatch metric. (C) Create a VPC Flow Log to capture IP traffic on the instances' elastic network interfaces, including connection attempts to destination port 3389. (D) Publish those flow log records to a CloudWatch Logs log group, because a metric filter can only operate on log data that lives in a log group. (E) Create a log group metric filter whose filter pattern matches the RDP destination port (destport=\"3389\", protocol=\"6\") and emits a metric value of 1 per matching record; graphing that metric with the Sum statistic over a 1-day period yields the daily session count. This is the exact pattern AWS documents for flow logs: the canonical 'Process flow log records in CloudWatch Logs' example creates a metric filter for destport=\"22\", protocol=\"6\" (SSH) with metric value 1 and the Sum statistic to count connection attempts. The EventBridge path (A/B) reacts to EC2 instance lifecycle state changes (pending/running/stopping/terminated), which never fire when an employee opens an RDP session. F is invalid because CloudWatch Logs subscription filters only support Kinesis Data Streams, Lambda, Data Firehose, or OpenSearch Service as destinations -- not EventBridge -- and they stream raw logs rather than producing a counting metric.","explanation_zh":"RDP 走 TCP port 3389。要統計員工每天發起多少 RDP 連線，須擷取進入 EC2 instance 的網路流量，並把符合的記錄轉成 CloudWatch 數值指標。(C) 建立 VPC Flow Log，擷取 instance elastic network interface 上的 IP 流量，含對目的埠 3389 的連線嘗試。(D) 將這些 flow log 記錄發佈到 CloudWatch Logs log group，因為 metric filter 只能針對 log group 內的 log 資料運作。(E) 建立 log group metric filter，filter pattern 比對 RDP 目的埠（destport=\"3389\", protocol=\"6\"），每筆符合記錄發出值 1 的指標；以 Sum 統計、1 天為週期繪製該指標即得每日連線次數。這正是 AWS 官方為 flow log 提供的範例：'Process flow log records in CloudWatch Logs' 範例建立 destport=\"22\", protocol=\"6\"（SSH）的 metric filter，指標值設為 1 並用 Sum 統計來計數連線嘗試。EventBridge 路徑（A/B）只反應 EC2 instance 生命週期狀態變更（pending/running/stopping/terminated），員工建立 RDP 連線時並不會觸發。F 不成立，因為 CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 的目的地只支援 Kinesis Data Streams、Lambda、Data Firehose 或 OpenSearch Service，並不支援 EventBridge，且它串流的是原始 log 而非產生計數指標。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"EC2 Instance State-change Notification events fire only on instance lifecycle transitions (pending, running, stopping, stopped, terminated), not when an employee establishes an RDP session. An EventBridge rule on these events cannot detect or count RDP logins.","why_zh":"EC2 Instance State-change 通知事件只在 instance 生命週期轉換（pending、running、stopping、stopped、terminated）時觸發，並非在員工建立 RDP 連線時觸發。針對這些事件的 EventBridge 規則無法偵測或計數 RDP 登入。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"This step only pairs with the wrong event source in A. Sending EC2 state-change events to a CloudWatch Logs log group via EventBridge records instance lifecycle activity, which is unrelated to RDP session counts.","why_zh":"此步驟只與 A 的錯誤事件來源搭配。透過 EventBridge 把 EC2 狀態變更事件送到 CloudWatch Logs log group，記錄的是 instance 生命週期活動，與 RDP 連線計數無關。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filters stream log data only to Amazon Kinesis Data Streams, AWS Lambda, Amazon Data Firehose, or Amazon OpenSearch Service; EventBridge is not a valid subscription filter destination, and a subscription filter does not generate a counting metric. Counting requires a metric filter (E).","why_zh":"CloudWatch Logs subscription filter 只能把 log 資料串流到 Amazon Kinesis Data Streams、AWS Lambda、Amazon Data Firehose 或 Amazon OpenSearch Service；EventBridge 並非有效的 subscription filter 目的地，且 subscription filter 不會產生計數指標。要計數必須使用 metric filter（E）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/process-records-cwl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs-cwl.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/SubscriptionFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpc/latest/userguide/flow-logs.html"]}},{"id":319,"question_en":"A company is using Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) to run its applications. The EKS cluster is successfully running multiple pods. The company stores the pod images in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). The company needs to configure Pod Identity access for the EKS cluster. The company has already updated the node IAM role by using the permissions for Pod Identity access. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）来运行其应用程序。EKS 集群成功运 行了多个容器组（Pod）。该公司将容器组镜像存储在亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中。 该公司需要为 EKS 集群配置 Pod 身份访问权限。该公司已通过使用 Pod 身份访问权限更新了节点 IAM 角色。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider for the EKS cluster.","B":"Ensure that the nodes can reach the EKS Auth API. Add and configure the EKS Pod Identity Agent add-on for the EKS cluster.","C":"Create an EKS access entry that uses the API_AND-CONFIG_MAP cluster authentication mode.","D":"Configure the AWS Security Token Service (AWS STS) endpoint for the Kubernetes service account that the pods in the EKS cluster use."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 EKS 集群创建一个 IAM OpenID 连接（OIDC）提供程序。","B":"确保节点能够访问 EKS 认证 API。为 EKS 集群添加并配置 EKS Pod 身份代理插件。","C":"创建一个使用 API_AND-CONFIG_MAP 集群身份验证模式的 EKS 访问条目。","D":"为 EKS 集群中 Pod 使用的 Kubernetes 服务账户配置 AWS 安全令牌服务（AWS STS）端点。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"EKS Pod Identity delivers IAM credentials to pods via two components: the EKS Auth API and the EKS Pod Identity Agent that runs as a pod on each node. The official setup overview lists exactly two procedures: (1) set up the EKS Pod Identity Agent add-on (a one-time, per-cluster step), and (2) create Pod Identity associations that map an IAM role to a Kubernetes service account. The agent prerequisites doc explicitly states that 'the nodes where the EKS Pod Identity Agent runs must be able to access the EKS Auth API' (for private subnets you add an AWS PrivateLink interface endpoint for the EKS Auth API), and that the node IAM role must allow eks-auth:AssumeRoleForPodIdentity. Because the company has already updated the node IAM role with the Pod Identity permissions, the only remaining work is exactly what option B states: ensure the nodes can reach the EKS Auth API and add/configure the EKS Pod Identity Agent add-on. The agent then calls AssumeRoleForPodIdentity against the EKS Auth API to fetch temporary credentials for the pods.","explanation_zh":"EKS Pod Identity 透過兩個元件把 IAM 憑證提供給 pod：EKS Auth API，以及在每個節點上以 pod 形式執行的 EKS Pod Identity Agent。官方設定流程只有兩個步驟：(1) 設定 EKS Pod Identity Agent 這個 add-on（每個叢集只需做一次），(2) 建立 Pod Identity association，把 IAM role 對應到 Kubernetes service account。Agent 的先決條件文件明確指出『執行 EKS Pod Identity Agent 的節點必須能存取 EKS Auth API』（若使用私有子網，需為 EKS Auth API 新增 AWS PrivateLink interface endpoint），且 node IAM role 必須允許 eks-auth:AssumeRoleForPodIdentity。由於題目說公司已經更新 node IAM role 的 Pod Identity 權限，剩下要做的正是選項 B：確保節點能連到 EKS Auth API，並新增與設定 EKS Pod Identity Agent add-on。之後 agent 會對 EKS Auth API 呼叫 AssumeRoleForPodIdentity 取得 pod 的臨時憑證。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Creating an IAM OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider is the requirement for IAM roles for service accounts (IRSA), the older alternative. The AWS docs explicitly state EKS Pod Identity 'is a simpler method than IAM roles for service accounts, as this method doesn't use OIDC identity providers.' An OIDC provider is therefore not part of Pod Identity setup.","why_zh":"建立 IAM OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider 是 IAM roles for service accounts (IRSA)（較舊的替代方案）的要求。AWS 文件明確指出 EKS Pod Identity『比 IAM roles for service accounts 更簡單，因為此方法不使用 OIDC identity provider』。因此 OIDC provider 不屬於 Pod Identity 的設定步驟。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"EKS access entries and the cluster authentication mode (API, API_AND_CONFIG_MAP, or CONFIG_MAP) govern how IAM principals authenticate and are authorized to the Kubernetes API server (for example via kubectl and RBAC). They have nothing to do with delivering AWS credentials to pods through Pod Identity. The option text is also malformed ('API_AND-CONFIG_MAP'), and configuring access entries would not enable Pod Identity.","why_zh":"EKS access entry 與叢集驗證模式（API、API_AND_CONFIG_MAP、CONFIG_MAP）控制的是 IAM principal 如何向 Kubernetes API server 驗證與授權（例如透過 kubectl 與 RBAC），與透過 Pod Identity 把 AWS 憑證提供給 pod 無關。此選項文字也有錯字（『API_AND-CONFIG_MAP』），且設定 access entry 無法啟用 Pod Identity。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Exchanging a web identity token with AWS STS (AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity) and configuring an STS endpoint for a service account describes the IRSA mechanism, not Pod Identity. The how-it-works doc contrasts the two: IRSA 'provides a web identity token that the AWS SDK must exchange with AWS Security Token Service by using AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity,' whereas with Pod Identity the agent calls AssumeRoleForPodIdentity against the EKS Auth API. No per-service-account STS endpoint configuration is involved.","why_zh":"以 web identity token 向 AWS STS 交換憑證（AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity）並為 service account 設定 STS endpoint，描述的是 IRSA 機制，而非 Pod Identity。運作原理文件對比兩者：IRSA『提供一個 web identity token，AWS SDK 必須以 AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity 向 AWS Security Token Service 交換』，而 Pod Identity 的 agent 是對 EKS Auth API 呼叫 AssumeRoleForPodIdentity。並不需要為每個 service account 設定 STS endpoint。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/pod-id-agent-setup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/pod-identities.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/pod-id-how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/APIReference/API_auth_AssumeRoleForPodIdentity.html"]}},{"id":320,"question_en":"A company has multiple AWS accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations that has all features enabled. The company’s DevOps administrator needs to improve security across all the company's AWS accounts. The administrator needs to identify the top users and roles in use across all accounts. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中拥有多个 AWS 账户，该组织启用了所有功能。该公司的 DevOps 管理员需要 提高公司所有 AWS 账户的安全性。管理员需要确定所有账户中使用频率最高的用户和角色。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new organization trail in AWS CloudTrail. Configure the trail to send log events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a CloudWatch Contributor Insights rule for the userIdentity.arn log field. View the results in CloudWatch Contributor Insights.","B":"Create an unused access analysis for the organization by using AWS Identity and Access Management Access Analyzer. Review the analyzer results and determine if each finding has the intended level of permissions required for the workload.","C":"Create a new organization trail in AWS CloudTrail. Create a table in Amazon Athena that uses partition projection. Load the Athena table with CloudTrail data. Query the Athena table to find the top users and roles.","D":"Generate a Service access report for each account by using Organizations. From the results, pull the last accessed date and last accessed by account fields to find the top users and roles."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS CloudTrail 中创建一个新的组织跟踪。配置该跟踪以将日志事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。为 userIdentity.arn 日志字段创建 CloudWatch 贡献者洞察规则。在 CloudWatch 贡献者洞察中 查看结果。","B":"使用 AWS 身份和访问管理访问分析器为组织创建未使用的访问分析。查看分析器结果，并确定每个 发现是否具有工作负载所需的预期权限级别。","C":"在 AWS CloudTrail 中创建一个新的组织跟踪。在 Amazon Athena 中创建一个使用分区投影的表。使 用 CloudTrail 数据加载 Athena 表。查询 Athena 表以找出使用最多的用户和角色。","D":"使用 Organizations 为每个账户生成服务访问报告。从结果中提取“最后访问日期”和“最后访问账 户”字段，以找出主要的用户和角色。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirement is to identify the top users and roles in use across all accounts with the MOST operational efficiency. CloudWatch Contributor Insights is purpose-built for exactly this: the AWS docs say it produces metrics on the 'top-N contributors' and helps you 'find top talkers,' it evaluates any JSON-format log including AWS CloudTrail, and it supports cross-account monitoring. An organization CloudTrail trail delivered to CloudWatch Logs plus one Contributor Insights rule keyed on userIdentity.arn yields a continuously self-updating top-N report with no SQL to author, no table to build, and no partitions to maintain. Option C (Athena with partition projection) also produces the answer, but you must create/load a table and author and re-run aggregation SQL; the AWS org-wide CloudTrail-in-Athena doc even warns that maintaining a partition per account 'can be cumbersome' and recommends CloudTrail Lake over Athena. Because A delivers an automatic, managed top-N report with the least ongoing effort, it is more operationally efficient than C, so the dump's suggested answer (C) is not the best fit.","explanation_zh":"需求是以最高的營運效率（MOST operational efficiency）找出整個組織所有帳戶中使用率最高的使用者與角色。CloudWatch Contributor Insights 正是為此而生：AWS 文件指出它會產出『top-N contributors』指標並協助你『find top talkers』，能評估任何 JSON 格式日誌（包含 AWS CloudTrail），且支援跨帳戶監控。將組織層級的 CloudTrail trail 送往 CloudWatch Logs，再針對 userIdentity.arn 建立單一 Contributor Insights 規則，即可持續自動更新出 top-N 報告，不需撰寫 SQL、不需建表、也不需維護分割區。選項 C（Athena 搭配 partition projection）雖也能得到答案，但需建表/載入資料並每次撰寫與重跑彙總 SQL；AWS 針對組織層級 CloudTrail 於 Athena 的文件甚至警告為每個帳戶維護分割區『相當繁瑣（can be cumbersome）』，並建議改用 CloudTrail Lake。由於 A 以最少的持續工作量提供自動化、受管的 top-N 報告，營運效率高於 C，因此 dump 建議答案（C）並非最佳選擇。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"IAM Access Analyzer 'unused access' analysis generates findings for IAM roles, users, and permissions that show NO usage during the tracking period - the opposite of identifying the top users and roles in use. It does not rank or surface the most-active principals.","why_zh":"IAM Access Analyzer 的『未使用存取（unused access）』分析會針對在追蹤期間『沒有使用』的角色、使用者與權限產生 findings，正好與『找出使用率最高的使用者與角色』相反，無法排名或呈現最活躍的主體。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Technically produces the answer, but requires building/loading an Athena table, configuring partition projection, and authoring and re-running aggregation SQL each time - more operational effort than a self-updating Contributor Insights top-N report. AWS docs note maintaining a partition per account for an org-wide trail in Athena 'can be cumbersome' and recommend CloudTrail Lake instead.","why_zh":"技術上能得到答案，但需建表/載入 Athena 資料、設定 partition projection 並每次撰寫與重跑彙總 SQL；比會自動更新的 Contributor Insights top-N 報告需要更多營運工作。AWS 文件指出在 Athena 中為組織層級 trail 的每個帳戶維護分割區『相當繁瑣』，並建議改用 CloudTrail Lake。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Organizations does not generate a per-account 'Service access report' with 'last accessed date' and 'last accessed by account' fields. The real feature is IAM 'service last accessed data' (viewable for an Organizations entity/SCP from the management account), which shows which services a principal used and when - it does not produce a cross-account ranking of top users and roles, and the described fields are fabricated.","why_zh":"AWS Organizations 不會產生帶有『last accessed date』與『last accessed by account』欄位的逐帳戶『Service access report』。真正的功能是 IAM 的『service last accessed data』（可從管理帳戶針對 Organizations 實體/SCP 檢視），僅顯示某主體使用過哪些服務及時間，無法產出跨帳戶的 top 使用者與角色排名，題目所述欄位屬虛構。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContributorInsights.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContributorInsights-CreateRule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContributorInsights-Rule-Examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/athena/latest/ug/create-cloudtrail-table-org-wide-trail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access-analyzer-create-unused.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_last-accessed-view-data-orgs.html"]}},{"id":321,"question_en":"A company has an organization in AWS Organizations with many OUs that contain many AWS accounts. The organization has a dedicated delegated administrator AWS account. The company needs the accounts in one OU to have server-side encryption enforced for all Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes and Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queues that are created or updated on an AWS CloudFormation stack. Which solution will enforce this policy before a CloudFormation stack operation in the accounts of this OU?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 组织中拥有多个组织单元（OU），每个组织单元包含多个 AWS 账户。该组织有一个 专门的委托管理员 AWS 账户。 该公司需要在某个组织单元 （OU） 中的账户对通过 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈创建或更新的所有 Amazon 弹性块存储 （Amazon EBS） 卷和 Amazon 简单队列服务 （Amazon SQS） 队列强制实施服务 器端加密。 在该组织单位（OU）的账户中，哪种解决方案会在执行 CloudFormation 堆栈操作之前强制实施此策略？","options_en":{"A":"Activate trusted access to CloudFormation StackSets. Create a CloudFormation Hook that enforces server-side encryption on EBS volumes and SQS queues. Deploy the Hook across the accounts in the OU by using StackSets.","B":"Set up AWS Config in all the accounts in the OU. Use AWS Systems Manager to deploy AWS Config rules that enforce server-side encryption for EBS volumes and SQS queues across the accounts in the OU.","C":"Write an SCP to deny the creation of EBS volumes and SQS queues unless the EBS volumes and SQS queues have server-side encryption. Attach the SCP to the OU.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function in the delegated administrator account that checks whether server- side encryption is enforced for EBS volumes and SQS queues. Create an IAM role to provide the Lambda function access to the accounts in the OU."},"options_zh":{"A":"激活 CloudFormation StackSets 的可信访问。创建一个 CloudFormation Hook，强制对 EBS 卷和 SQS 队列进行服务器端加密。通过使用 StackSets 在组织单元中的各个账户中部署该 Hook。","B":"在组织单位（OU）中的所有账户中设置 AWS Config。使用 AWS Systems Manager 部署 AWS Config 规则，以强制要求组织单位（OU）中所有账户的 EBS 卷和 SQS 队列启用服务器端加密。","C":"编写一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止创建未启用服务器端加密的 EBS 卷和 SQS 队列，除非这些 EBS 卷和 SQS 队列已启用服务器端加密。将该 SCP 附加到组织单位（OU）。","D":"在委托管理员账户中创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于检查 EBS 卷和 SQS 队列是否强制执行服务 器端加密。创建一个 IAM 角色，以使 Lambda 函数能够访问组织单位中的账户。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to proactively enforce server-side encryption on EBS volumes and SQS queues that are created or updated by a CloudFormation stack, and to block the operation BEFORE provisioning, across all accounts in one OU. CloudFormation Hooks is the purpose-built feature for this: AWS docs state that Hooks 'proactively inspect the configuration of your AWS resources before provisioning' and, if non-compliant resources are found, 'CloudFormation either fails the operation and prevents the resources from being provisioned.' Hooks can be implemented with Guard rules or Lambda to check SSE properties and run on both create and update (the AWS Hooks registration example literally describes a Hook that 'Verifies S3 bucket and SQS queues properties before creating or updating' and sets an encryptionAlgorithm property). A Hook is a private extension registered in the CloudFormation registry per account/Region, so to apply it to every account in the OU you activate trusted access for CloudFormation StackSets and deploy/activate the Hook across the OU accounts with StackSets. This is the only option that operates at stack-operation time and reliably blocks non-compliant EBS and SQS resources before they are provisioned.","explanation_zh":"需求是在 CloudFormation stack 建立或更新 EBS volumes 與 SQS queues 時，主動強制啟用 server-side encryption，並且要在資源佈建「之前」就阻擋該操作，範圍涵蓋某個 OU 內的所有帳戶。CloudFormation Hooks 正是為此設計的功能：AWS 文件指出 Hooks 會在佈建前『主動檢查 AWS 資源的設定』，若發現不合規資源，『CloudFormation 會讓該操作失敗並阻止資源被佈建』。Hooks 可用 Guard rules 或 Lambda 實作以檢查 SSE 屬性，且同時適用於 create 與 update（AWS 註冊 Hook 的範例就描述了一個『在建立或更新前驗證 S3 bucket 與 SQS queues 屬性』並設定 encryptionAlgorithm 的 Hook）。Hook 是註冊在 CloudFormation registry 中、以帳戶/區域為單位的私有 extension，因此要套用到 OU 內所有帳戶，需啟用 CloudFormation StackSets 的 trusted access，並透過 StackSets 在 OU 各帳戶部署/啟用該 Hook。這是唯一能在 stack 操作當下運作、並可靠地在 EBS 與 SQS 資源佈建前阻擋不合規資源的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Config is detective and reactive: it evaluates resources after they exist and reports compliance; it does not block provisioning before a CloudFormation stack operation. Config rules can detect unencrypted EBS/SQS but cannot prevent them from being created, so it fails the 'before a CloudFormation stack operation' requirement.","why_zh":"AWS Config 屬於偵測型、被動式：它在資源建立後才評估並回報合規狀態，無法在 CloudFormation stack 操作之前阻擋佈建。Config rules 可偵測未加密的 EBS/SQS，但無法防止它們被建立，因此不符合『在 stack 操作之前』的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An SCP is a coarse permission guardrail applied to underlying API calls (e.g., ec2:CreateVolume with ec2:Encrypted), not template/resource-config inspection at a CloudFormation stack operation. SQS has no request-level IAM/SCP condition key to require server-side encryption at CreateQueue/SetQueueAttributes, so an SCP cannot reliably enforce SSE on SQS queues, and it does not specifically target resources 'created or updated on a CloudFormation stack.' Hooks, not SCPs, are the feature that proactively inspects stack resources before provisioning.","why_zh":"SCP 是套用在底層 API 呼叫上的粗粒度權限護欄（例如 ec2:CreateVolume 搭配 ec2:Encrypted），而非在 CloudFormation stack 操作時檢查範本／資源設定。SQS 在 CreateQueue/SetQueueAttributes 沒有可要求 server-side encryption 的請求層級 IAM/SCP 條件鍵，因此 SCP 無法可靠地對 SQS 佇列強制 SSE，也未特別針對『在 CloudFormation stack 上建立或更新』的資源。能在佈建前主動檢查 stack 資源的是 Hooks，而非 SCP。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A custom Lambda in the delegated administrator account with a cross-account IAM role is a build-your-own, out-of-band checker with high operational overhead. It is not integrated into the CloudFormation stack lifecycle, so it cannot block provisioning before a stack operation; at best it detects non-compliance after the fact, which does not meet the proactive 'before' requirement.","why_zh":"在 delegated administrator 帳戶中以跨帳戶 IAM role 執行的自訂 Lambda，是一種需自行打造、且不在 CloudFormation 生命週期內的旁路檢查機制，維運負擔高。它未整合進 stack 生命週期，因此無法在 stack 操作前阻擋佈建；頂多只能事後偵測不合規，無法滿足『事前』主動強制的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudformation-cli/latest/hooks-userguide/what-is-cloudformation-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudformation-cli/latest/hooks-userguide/registering-hooks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cloudformation-cli/latest/hooks-userguide/hooks-model.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/services-that-can-integrate-cloudformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]}},{"id":322,"question_en":"A company is running an internal application in an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster on Amazon EC2. The ECS cluster instances can connect to the public internet. The ECS tasks that run on the cluster instances are configured to use images from both private Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repositories and a public ECR registry repository. A new security policy requires the company to remove the ECS cluster's direct access to the internet. The company must remove any NAT gateways and internet gateways from the VPC that hosts the cluster. A DevOps engineer needs to ensure the ECS cluster can still download images from both the public ECR registry and the private ECR repositories. Images from the public ECR registry must remain up-to-date. New versions of the images must be available to the ECS cluster within 24 hours of publication. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司正在亚马逊 EC2 上的亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）集群中运行内部应用程序。ECS 集 群实例可以连接到公共互联网。在集群实例上运行的 ECS 任务配置为使用来自私有亚马逊弹性容器注册 表（Amazon ECR）存储库和公共 ECR 注册表存储库的镜像。 一项新的安全策略要求公司取消 ECS 集群直接访问互联网的权限。公司必须从承载该集群的 VPC 中移 除任何 NAT 网关和互联网网关。一位 DevOps 工程师需要确保 ECS 集群仍能从公共 ECR 注册表和私有 ECR 仓库下载镜像。公共 ECR 注册表中的镜像必须保持最新。新发布的镜像版本必须在发布后的 24 小 时内可供 ECS 集群使用。 哪种步骤组合能在满足这些要求的同时，将操作开销降至最低？（选择） 三。","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project and a new private ECR repository for each image that is downloaded from the public ECR registry. Configure each project to pull the image from the public ECR repository and push the image to the new private ECR repository. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes the CodeBuild project once every 24 hours. Update each task definition in the ECS cluster to refer to the new private ECR repository.","B":"Create a new Amazon ECR pull through cache rule for each image that is downloaded from the public ECR registry. Create an AWS Lambda function that invokes each pull through cache rule. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes the Lambda function once every 24 hours. Update each task definition in the ECS cluster to refer to the image from the pull through cache.","C":"Create a new Amazon ECR pull through cache rule for the public ECR registry. Update each task definition in the ECS cluster to refer to the image from the pull through cache. Ensure each public image has been downloaded through the pull through cache at least once before removing internet access from the VPC.","D":"Create an Amazon ECR interface VPC endpoint for the public ECR repositories that are in the VPC.","E":"Create an Amazon ECR interface VPC endpoint for the private ECR repositories that are in the VPC.","F":"Create an Amazon S3 gateway endpoint in the VPC."},"options_zh":{"A":"为从公共 ECR 注册表下载的每个镜像创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目和一个新的私有 ECR 仓库。将每 个项目配置为从公共 ECR 仓库拉取镜像并将其推送到新的私有 ECR 仓库。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每 24 小时调用一次 CodeBuild 项目。更新 ECS 集群中的每个任务定义，使其指向 新的私有 ECR 仓库。","B":"为从公共 ECR 注册表下载的每个镜像创建一个新的 Amazon ECR 拉取缓存规则。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于调用每个拉取缓存规则。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每 24 小时调用一 次该 Lambda 函数。更新 ECS 集群中的每个任务定义，使其引用来自拉取缓存的镜像。","C":"为公共 ECR 注册表创建一个新的 Amazon ECR 拉取缓存规则。更新 ECS 集群中的每个任务定义， 使其引用来自拉取缓存的镜像。在从 VPC 中移除互联网访问权限之前，确保每个公共镜像至少 已通过拉取缓存下载过一次。","D":"为 VPC 中的公共 ECR 存储库创建一个 Amazon ECR 接口 VPC 端点。","E":"为 VPC 内的私有 ECR 存储库创建一个 Amazon ECR 接口 VPC 端点。","F":"在 VPC 中创建一个 Amazon S3 网关端点。"},"answer":["C","E","F"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["C","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"To let ECS-on-EC2 tasks pull images after all internet/NAT/IGW access is removed, three building blocks are needed. (C) Create a single Amazon ECR pull through cache rule for the public ECR registry. Pull through cache rules are created per upstream REGISTRY, not per image: the AWS docs state 'For each upstream registry containing images that you want to cache... you must create a pull through cache rule,' and the console flow selects 'Amazon ECR Public' as the source, so one rule covers all public images. The cache stays fresh automatically: 'When a customer pulls a cached image... Amazon ECR checks whether it has validated the image against the upstream registry within the last 24 hours. If the 24-hour window has expired, Amazon ECR sends a request upstream to check for a newer version and updates the cache.' This natively meets the 'up-to-date within 24 hours' requirement with zero scheduled jobs (LEAST overhead). Because 'when an image is pulled using the pull through cache rule for the first time a route to the internet may be required... Subsequent image pulls... don't require this,' each public image must be pulled through the cache at least once while internet access still exists. (E) ECS tasks on EC2 require an Amazon ECR interface VPC endpoint (ecr.dkr and ecr.api) to reach the private registry, which now holds both the genuinely private repos and the pull-through-cached public images. (F) An Amazon S3 gateway endpoint is required because ECR stores image layers in S3; the docs explicitly state 'Amazon ECS tasks hosted on Amazon EC2 instances require both Amazon ECR endpoints and the Amazon S3 gateway endpoint.'","explanation_zh":"要讓移除 internet gateway / NAT gateway 後的 ECS-on-EC2 任務仍能拉取映像，需要三個元件。(C) 為 public ECR registry 建立一條 ECR pull through cache 規則。pull through cache 規則是以「上游 registry」為單位建立，而非每個映像各一條：AWS 文件指出『For each upstream registry... you must create a pull through cache rule』，且 console 流程是選擇 Amazon ECR Public 作為來源，因此一條規則即可涵蓋所有 public 映像。快取會自動保持更新：當使用者拉取已快取的映像時，若距離上次與上游驗證已超過 24 小時，Amazon ECR 會向上游檢查新版本並更新快取，因此原生滿足『24 小時內保持最新』的需求，且不需任何排程作業（最少維運負擔）。由於『第一次』透過 pull through cache 規則拉取映像時可能需要對外路由，後續拉取則不需要，所以必須在仍有 internet 存取時，先讓每個 public 映像至少透過快取拉取一次。(E) EC2 上的 ECS 任務需要 Amazon ECR interface VPC endpoint（ecr.dkr 與 ecr.api）以連到 private registry；而 private registry 現在同時存放真正的私有 repo 與被快取的 public 映像。(F) 需要 Amazon S3 gateway endpoint，因為 ECR 的映像層存放在 S3；文件明確指出『Amazon ECS tasks hosted on Amazon EC2 instances require both Amazon ECR endpoints and the Amazon S3 gateway endpoint』。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Functionally workable, but it creates one CodeBuild project AND one new private repo PER image, plus an EventBridge schedule to re-sync every 24 hours. That is far more operational overhead than a single pull through cache rule that auto-refreshes on pull within 24 hours. It also still requires the ECR/S3 VPC endpoints to actually pull, so it is not the LEAST-overhead choice.","why_zh":"技術上可行，但需為每個映像各建一個 CodeBuild 專案與一個新私有 repo，外加 EventBridge 每 24 小時重新同步，維運負擔遠高於只用一條會在拉取時於 24 小時內自動刷新的 pull through cache 規則。它本身仍需 ECR/S3 VPC endpoint 才能真正拉取，並非最少負擔的方案。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Wrong on two counts. First, it says create a rule 'for each image' — pull through cache rules are created per upstream registry, so one rule for Amazon ECR Public suffices. Second, it adds a Lambda + EventBridge to 'invoke each pull through cache rule'; you cannot 'invoke' a cache rule on a schedule, and the cache already refreshes automatically within 24 hours when an image is pulled. The Lambda/EventBridge machinery is unnecessary overhead.","why_zh":"兩處錯誤。其一，宣稱為『每個映像』建立規則—但 pull through cache 規則是以上游 registry 為單位，對 Amazon ECR Public 一條即足。其二，加入 Lambda + EventBridge 去『觸發每條 pull through cache 規則』；快取規則無法被排程觸發，且在拉取映像時快取本就會於 24 小時內自動刷新，這些 Lambda/EventBridge 機制是多餘負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no separate 'ECR interface VPC endpoint for public ECR repositories' construct needed here. Cached public images are served from your PRIVATE ECR registry, which is already reached via the endpoint in option E. The ECR endpoint type (ecr.dkr/ecr.api) is the same regardless, so D is redundant and does not add a required, distinct capability.","why_zh":"此情境並不需要一個獨立的『public ECR repository 專用的 ECR interface VPC endpoint』。被快取的 public 映像是由你的私有 ECR registry 提供，而該 registry 已由選項 E 的 endpoint 連通。ECR endpoint 類型（ecr.dkr/ecr.api）並無公私之分，因此 D 是多餘的，未提供必要且獨立的功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/pull-through-cache.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/pull-through-cache-creating-rule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/vpc-endpoints.html"]}},{"id":323,"question_en":"A company has a continuous integration pipeline where the company creates container images by using AWS CodeBuild. The created images are stored in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Checking for and fixing the vulnerabilities in the images takes the company too much time. The company wants to identify the image vulnerabilities quickly and notify the security team of the vulnerabilities. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"该公司拥有一个持续集成流水线，通过使用 AWS CodeBuild 创建容器镜像。创建的镜像存储在亚马逊 弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中。 检查并修复镜像中的漏洞耗费了公司太多时间。公司希望快速识别出镜像中的漏洞，并将漏洞情况通知 给安全团队。 哪种步骤组合能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Activate Amazon Inspector enhanced scanning for Amazon ECR. Configure the enhanced scanning to use continuous scanning. Set up a topic in Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule for Amazon Inspector findings. Set an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic as the rule target.","C":"Activate AWS Lambda enhanced scanning for Amazon ECR. Configure the enhanced scanning to use continuous scanning. Set up a topic in Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES).","D":"Create a new AWS Lambda function. Invoke the new Lambda function when scan findings are detected.","E":"Activate default basic scanning for Amazon ECR for all container images. Configure the default basic scanning to use continuous scanning. Set up a topic in Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS)."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 Amazon ECR 激活 Amazon Inspector 增强扫描功能。将增强扫描配置为使用持续扫描。在 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）中设置一个主题。","B":"为 Amazon Inspector 发现结果创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题设置为规则目标。","C":"启用 AWS Lambda 对 Amazon ECR 的增强扫描功能。将增强扫描配置为使用持续扫描。在 Amazon 简 单电子邮件服务（Amazon SES）中设置一个主题。","D":"创建一个新的 AWS Lambda 函数。在检测到扫描结果时调用新的 Lambda 函数。","E":"为所有容器镜像激活 Amazon ECR 的默认基本扫描。将默认基本扫描配置为使用持续扫描。在 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）中设置一个主题。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Enhanced scanning is the only ECR scan type that supports continuous scanning and integrates with Amazon Inspector, scanning for both OS and programming-language package vulnerabilities. The ECR docs state that 'As new vulnerabilities appear, the scan results are updated and Amazon Inspector emits an event to EventBridge to notify you.' Option A activates Amazon Inspector enhanced scanning with continuous scanning so vulnerabilities are identified quickly and automatically, and creates the SNS topic that carries the alerts. Option B wires Amazon Inspector findings to that SNS topic through an EventBridge rule: Inspector sends 'Inspector2 Finding' events with source aws.inspector2 directly to EventBridge, so a rule matching those events with an SNS topic target is the documented, code-free way to notify the security team. Together they meet both requirements (identify quickly via continuous scanning, notify via EventBridge -> SNS) with the LEAST operational overhead because no custom code is written or maintained, which rules out the custom Lambda target in D.","explanation_zh":"Enhanced scanning 是唯一支援 continuous scanning 並整合 Amazon Inspector 的 ECR 掃描類型，會同時掃描 OS 與程式語言套件漏洞。ECR 文件明確指出『當出現新漏洞時，掃描結果會更新，且 Amazon Inspector 會發出事件到 EventBridge 通知你』。選項 A 啟用 Amazon Inspector enhanced scanning 並設定 continuous scanning，使漏洞能自動且快速被識別，同時建立用來傳送警示的 SNS topic。選項 B 透過 EventBridge rule 將 Amazon Inspector 的 findings 導向該 SNS topic：Inspector 會以 source aws.inspector2 直接送出 'Inspector2 Finding' 事件到 EventBridge，因此用一條比對該事件、並以 SNS topic 為 target 的 rule，就是官方文件記載、無需撰寫程式碼即可通知安全團隊的方式。兩者合併滿足兩項需求（透過 continuous scanning 快速識別、透過 EventBridge -> SNS 通知），且因不需撰寫或維護任何自訂程式碼而具最低營運負擔，這也排除了 D 的自訂 Lambda 目標。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"There is no 'AWS Lambda enhanced scanning for Amazon ECR' — enhanced scanning is provided by Amazon Inspector, not Lambda. Also, Amazon SES does not use 'topics' (that is an SNS concept), so this option is technically invalid on two counts.","why_zh":"並不存在所謂的 'AWS Lambda enhanced scanning for Amazon ECR'，enhanced scanning 是由 Amazon Inspector 提供，而非 Lambda。此外 Amazon SES 沒有 'topic'（那是 SNS 的概念），因此此選項在兩處皆技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Invoking a custom Lambda function on scan findings adds operational overhead (code to write, deploy, and maintain) compared with simply setting an SNS topic as the EventBridge target. The question asks for the LEAST operational overhead, so the SNS target in B is preferred.","why_zh":"在掃描 findings 上觸發自訂 Lambda 函式會增加營運負擔（需撰寫、部署與維護程式碼），相較之下直接把 SNS topic 設為 EventBridge 目標更簡單。題目要求 LEAST operational overhead，因此選項 B 的 SNS 目標較佳。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Basic scanning supports only Manual and scan-on-push frequencies — it does NOT support continuous scanning, so 'configure default basic scanning to use continuous scanning' is impossible. Basic scanning is OS-only and does not emit Amazon Inspector findings to EventBridge, so it cannot drive the notification flow.","why_zh":"Basic scanning 只支援 Manual 與 scan-on-push 頻率，並不支援 continuous scanning，因此「設定 basic scanning 使用 continuous scanning」根本不可能。Basic scanning 只掃 OS，且不會把 Amazon Inspector findings 送到 EventBridge，無法驅動通知流程。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-enhanced-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-inspector2.html"]}},{"id":324,"question_en":"A DevOps administrator is configuring a repository to store a company's container images. The administrator needs to configure a lifecycle rule that automatically deletes container images that have a specific tag and that are older than 15 days. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 管理员正在配置一个存储库来存放公司的容器镜像。该管理员需要配置一个生命周期规则， 自动删除具有特定标签且超过 15 天的容器镜像。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a repository in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). Add a lifecycle policy to the repository to expire images that have the matching tag after 15 days.","B":"Create a repository in AWS CodeArtifact. Add a repository policy to the CodeArtifact repository to expire old assets that have the matching tag after 15 days.","C":"Create a bucket in Amazon S3. Add a bucket lifecycle policy to expire old objects that have the matching tag after 15 days","D":"Create an EC2 Image Builder container recipe. Add a build component to expire the container that has the matching tag after 15 days."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 Amazon Elastic Container Registry（Amazon ECR）中创建一个存储库。向该存储库添加一个生命周期 策略，使具有匹配标签的镜像在 15 天后过期。","B":"在 AWS CodeArtifact 中创建一个存储库。向 CodeArtifact 存储库添加存储库策略，以便在 15 天后 过期具有匹配标签的旧资产。","C":"在亚马逊 S3 中创建一个存储桶。添加一个存储桶生命周期策略，在 15 天后自动删除具有匹配标 签的旧对象。","D":"创建一个 EC2 Image Builder 容器配方。添加一个构建组件，在 15 天后过期具有匹配标签的容器。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon ECR is the purpose-built, fully managed AWS registry for container (Docker/OCI) images and provides native lifecycle policies that automatically delete (expire) images server-side with no extra infrastructure to manage. An ECR lifecycle policy can target a specific tag with 'tagStatus': 'tagged' plus a 'tagPatternList' (or 'tagPrefixList'), combined with 'countType': 'sinceImagePushed', 'countUnit': 'days', and 'countNumber': 15 and an 'expire' action -- exactly matching 'delete images with a specific tag that are older than 15 days'. The AWS docs even show a near-identical 'Filtering on image age' example that expires tagged images (tagPatternList ['prod*']) older than 14 days. This is the most operationally efficient choice because you only author one JSON policy on the repository and ECR runs the expiration automatically. The other options either store the wrong artifact type or have no native time-based image-deletion capability.","explanation_zh":"Amazon ECR 是 AWS 專為容器 (Docker/OCI) 映像打造的全代管登錄檔，並提供原生的 lifecycle policy，可在伺服器端自動刪除 (expire) 映像，無需額外維運基礎設施。ECR lifecycle policy 可用 'tagStatus': 'tagged' 搭配 'tagPatternList' (或 'tagPrefixList') 鎖定特定標籤，再以 'countType': 'sinceImagePushed'、'countUnit': 'days'、'countNumber': 15 以及 'expire' 動作，精準達成「刪除具特定標籤且超過 15 天的映像」。AWS 文件的 'Filtering on image age' 範例幾乎完全相同：以 tagPatternList ['prod*'] 讓超過 14 天的已標記映像過期。此為最具維運效率的方案，因為只需在 repository 撰寫一份 JSON policy，ECR 即自動執行過期刪除。其他選項要不是儲存錯誤的成品類型，就是沒有原生的依時間刪除映像功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS CodeArtifact is a managed repository for software packages (npm, PyPI, Maven, NuGet, Cargo, Ruby, generic, Swift), not container images -- those belong in Amazon ECR. A CodeArtifact 'repository policy' is a resource-based IAM policy that controls access; it has no time-based asset-expiration capability to delete assets by tag after 15 days.","why_zh":"AWS CodeArtifact 是用於軟體套件 (npm、PyPI、Maven、NuGet、Cargo、Ruby、generic、Swift) 的代管儲存庫，並非用於容器映像 (容器映像應放在 Amazon ECR)。CodeArtifact 的 'repository policy' 是控管存取的資源型 IAM 政策，並無依時間自動於 15 天後依標籤刪除成品的功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Although S3 lifecycle rules can expire objects by age and object tag, S3 is general object storage, not a container registry -- it does not manage image manifests, layers, tags, or push/pull semantics, and you cannot pull container images from a raw S3 bucket. Storing images as raw S3 objects would require custom packaging logic and is far less operationally efficient than ECR's purpose-built registry.","why_zh":"雖然 S3 lifecycle 規則可依物件年齡與物件標籤使物件過期，但 S3 是一般物件儲存而非容器登錄檔，無法管理映像 manifest、layer、tag 或 push/pull 語意，也無法直接從原始 S3 bucket 拉取容器映像。將映像當成原始 S3 物件儲存需自行建置打包邏輯，維運效率遠不如 ECR 這類專用登錄檔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"EC2 Image Builder builds and distributes machine/AMI and container images via pipelines; it is not an image registry and provides no lifecycle/expiration mechanism to delete stored images by tag after 15 days. A 'build component' runs build/test steps during image creation, not retention cleanup, so it cannot satisfy the requirement.","why_zh":"EC2 Image Builder 透過管線建置與散布機器/AMI 及容器映像，本身不是映像登錄檔，也沒有依標籤於 15 天後刪除已儲存映像的 lifecycle/過期機制。'build component' 是在建置映像時執行建置/測試步驟，而非保留期清理，因此無法滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/lifecycle_policy_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/lifecycle_policy_parameters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/welcome.html"]}},{"id":325,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon Redshift as its data warehouse solution. The company wants to create a dashboard to view changes to the Redshift users and the queries the users perform. Which combination of steps will meet this requirement? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 Redshift 作为其数据仓库解决方案。该公司希望创建一个仪表板，以查看 Redshift 用户的变更情况以及这些用户执行的查询。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这一要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch log group. Create an AWS CloudTrail trail that writes to the CloudWatch log group.","B":"Create a new Amazon S3 bucket. Configure default audit logging on the Redshift cluster. Configure the S3 bucket as the target.","C":"Configure the Redshift cluster database audit logging to include user activity logs. Configure Amazon CloudWatch as the target.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard that has a log widget. Configure the widget to display user details from the Redshift logs.","E":"Create an AWS Lambda function that uses Amazon Athena to query the Redshift logs. Create an Amazon CloudWatch dashboard that has a custom widget type that uses the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 日志组。创建一个将日志写入 CloudWatch 日志组的 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。","B":"创建一个新的 Amazon S3 存储桶。在 Redshift 集群上配置默认的审计日志记录。将 S3 存储桶配置为目标。","C":"配置 Redshift 集群数据库审计日志记录以包含用户活动日志。将 Amazon CloudWatch 配置为日志目标。","D":"创建一个包含日志小部件的 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板。配置该小部件以显示来自 Redshift 日志的用 户详细信息。","E":"创建一个使用 Amazon Athena 查询 Redshift 日志的 AWS Lambda 函数。创建一个包含自定义小部件 类型的 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板，该小部件使用该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["C","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["C","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The dashboard must show (1) changes to Redshift users and (2) the queries users perform. In Redshift database audit logging, the user log records changes to database user definitions (CREATE/DROP/ALTER/RENAME user), and the user activity log logs each query before it runs. The user activity log is produced only when audit logging is enabled AND the enable_user_activity_logging parameter is turned on (it is false by default); otherwise only the connection and user logs are captured. Option C meets both data requirements by configuring database audit logging to include the user activity logs and targeting Amazon CloudWatch, which exports the connection, user, and user-activity log data to CloudWatch Logs log groups. Option D then satisfies the dashboard requirement natively and with minimal operational overhead: you run a CloudWatch Logs Insights query against those log groups and choose Add to dashboard, creating a logs widget that displays the user-change and query details. Together C and D form the complete, low-overhead native solution.","explanation_zh":"儀表板需顯示 (1) Redshift 使用者的變更與 (2) 使用者執行的查詢。在 Redshift database audit logging 中,user log 記錄資料庫使用者定義的變更(CREATE/DROP/ALTER/RENAME user),而 user activity log 記錄每個查詢在執行前的內容。user activity log 只有在啟用 audit logging 且同時開啟 enable_user_activity_logging 參數(預設為 false)時才會產生;否則只會擷取 connection log 與 user log。選項 C 同時滿足兩項資料需求:設定 database audit logging 並包含 user activity logs,以 Amazon CloudWatch 為目標,將 connection、user 與 user-activity 日誌資料匯出到 CloudWatch Logs log groups。選項 D 接著以原生且最低操作負擔的方式滿足儀表板需求:對這些 log groups 執行 CloudWatch Logs Insights 查詢,選擇 Add to dashboard,建立一個 logs widget 來顯示使用者變更與查詢細節。C 與 D 共同構成完整且低負擔的原生解決方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudTrail captures Redshift control-plane/management API calls (such as CreateCluster or ModifyCluster), not in-database CREATE/DROP/ALTER USER changes or the SQL queries users run inside the database. Writing CloudTrail to a CloudWatch log group satisfies neither requirement.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 記錄 Redshift 控制平面/管理 API 呼叫(如 CreateCluster 或 ModifyCluster),而非資料庫內的 CREATE/DROP/ALTER USER 變更或使用者執行的 SQL 查詢。將 CloudTrail 寫入 CloudWatch log group 無法滿足任一需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Default audit logging to S3 captures only the connection and user logs; it does not include the user activity log (queries) because enable_user_activity_logging is off by default, so it misses requirement (2). It also targets S3 rather than CloudWatch and does not directly feed a CloudWatch dashboard widget, conflicting with the C+D approach.","why_zh":"預設的 audit logging 寫入 S3 只擷取 connection log 與 user log;因為 enable_user_activity_logging 預設關閉,不包含 user activity log(查詢),因此無法滿足需求 (2)。它也以 S3 而非 CloudWatch 為目標,無法直接供 CloudWatch 儀表板 widget 使用,與 C+D 的做法衝突。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Athena queries data stored in Amazon S3, not CloudWatch Logs. If audit logs are sent to CloudWatch (per option C), a Lambda/Athena custom widget cannot query them. A custom widget is only needed when native widgets cannot do the job, but the native CloudWatch Logs logs widget in option D suffices, so E adds unnecessary operational overhead and contradicts C.","why_zh":"Athena 查詢儲存在 Amazon S3 的資料,而非 CloudWatch Logs。若 audit 日誌已送至 CloudWatch(依選項 C),Lambda/Athena 自訂 widget 無法查詢這些日誌。自訂 widget 僅在原生 widget 無法達成時才需要,但選項 D 的原生 CloudWatch Logs widget 已足夠,因此 E 增加了不必要的操作負擔且與 C 衝突。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/redshift/latest/mgmt/db-auditing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL_ExportQueryResults.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/AnalyzingLogData.html"]}},{"id":326,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage its 500 AWS accounts. The organization has all features enabled. The AWS accounts are in a single OU. The developers need to use the CostCenter tag key for all resources in the organization's member accounts. Some teams do not use the CostCenter tag key to tag their Amazon EC2 instances. The cloud team wrote a script that scans all EC2 instances in the organization's member accounts. If the EC2 instances do not have a CostCenter tag key, the script will notify AWS account administrators. To avoid this notification, some developers use the CostCenter tag key with an arbitrary string in the tag value. The cloud team needs to ensure that all EC2 instances in the organization use a CostCenter tag key with the appropriate cost center value. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理其 500 个 AWS 账户。该组织启用了所有功能。 这些 AWS 账户位于单个组织单元（OU）中。开发人员需要在该组织成员账户中的所有资源上使用 “CostCenter”标签键。但有些团队在标记其 Amazon EC2 实例时并未使用“CostCenter”标签键。 云团队编写了一个脚本，用于扫描组织成员账户中的所有 EC2 实例。如果 EC2 实例没有“CostCenter” 标签键，该脚本将通知 AWS 账户管理员。为了避免收到此类通知，一些开发人员在标签值中使用任意 字符串来设置“CostCenter”标签键。 云团队需要确保组织内的所有 EC2 实例都使用带有适当成本中心值的“CostCenter”标签键。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP that prevents the creation of EC2 instances without the CostCenter tag key. Create a tag policy that requires the CostCenter tag to be values from a known list of cost centers for all EC2 instances. Attach the policy to the OU. Update the script to scan the tag keys and tag values. Modify the script to update noncompliant resources with a default approved tag value for the CostCenter tag key.","B":"Create an SCP that prevents the creation of EC2 instances without the CostCenter tag key. Attach the policy to the OU. Update the script to scan the tag keys and tag values and notify the administrators when the tag values are not valid.","C":"Create an SCP that prevents the creation of EC2 instances without the CostCenter tag key. Attach the policy to the OU. Create an IAM permission boundary in the organization's member accounts that restricts the CostCenter tag values to a list of valid cost centers.","D":"Create a tag policy that requires the CostCenter tag to be values from a known list of cost centers for all EC2 instances. Attach the policy to the OU. Configure an AWS Lambda function that adds an empty CostCenter tag key to an EC2 instance. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches events to the RunInstances API action with the Lambda function as the target."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 SCP，禁止创建未带有“CostCenter”标签键的 EC2 实例。创建一个标签策略，要求所有 EC2 实例的“CostCenter”标签值必须来自已知的成本中心列表。将该策略附加到组织单位。更 新脚本以扫描标签键和标签值。修改脚本，为不符合要求的资源更新“CostCenter”标签键的默 认批准标签值。","B":"创建一个 SCP，禁止创建未带有“CostCenter”标签键的 EC2 实例。将该策略附加到组织单元。更 新脚本以扫描标签键和标签值，并在标签值无效时通知管理员。","C":"创建一个 SCP，禁止创建未设置“CostCenter”标签键的 EC2 实例。将该策略附加到组织单元。在 组织成员账户中创建一个 IAM 权限边界，将“CostCenter”标签值限制为有效成本中心列表。","D":"创建一个标签策略，要求所有 EC2 实例的“CostCenter”标签值必须来自已知的成本中心列表。将该 策略附加到组织单元。配置一个 AWS Lambda 函数，为 EC2 实例添加一个空的“CostCenter”标签 键。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，将与 RunInstances API 操作匹配的事件定向到该 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement has two distinct parts that AWS Organizations docs say must be solved with two layered controls. First, every EC2 instance must HAVE the CostCenter tag key. The tag policy enforcement doc is explicit: 'Basic compliance rules do not enforce tag compliance on resources that are created without tags... You cannot use this capability to ensure that required or mandatory tag keys are configured at resource creation. Use SCPs to prevent IAM users and roles in target accounts from creating certain resource types if the request doesn't include the specified tags.' So an SCP (using aws:RequestTag/Null conditions) is needed to block EC2 RunInstances without the CostCenter key, which stops developers from simply omitting it. Second, the value must be a real approved cost center, not an arbitrary string. Tag policy enforcement mode (basic compliance rules with enforced_for ec2:ALL_SUPPORTED) 'can prevent resource creation with tag values that do not meet the requirements' - for example blocking EC2 create operations if CostCenter is not in an approved value list. Option A is the only choice that layers both: an SCP for the missing-key problem plus a tag policy attached to the OU that restricts CostCenter to a known list of cost centers, exactly the AWS-recommended pattern.","explanation_zh":"需求有兩個不同部分，AWS Organizations 文件指出必須以兩層控制疊加解決。第一，每個 EC2 instance 都必須「具備」CostCenter tag key。Tag policy enforcement 文件明確說明：「Basic compliance rules 不會對未帶 tag 建立的資源強制合規……無法用此功能確保在資源建立時設定必要或強制的 tag key。請使用 SCP 來防止目標帳戶中的 IAM users 與 roles 在請求未包含指定 tag 時建立特定資源類型。」因此需要 SCP（透過 aws:RequestTag/Null 條件）阻擋未帶 CostCenter key 的 EC2 RunInstances，防止開發者乾脆省略它。第二，值必須是真正核准的 cost center，而非任意字串。Tag policy 的 enforcement 模式（basic compliance rules，搭配 enforced_for ec2:ALL_SUPPORTED）「可以防止以不符合要求的 tag 值建立資源」，例如當 CostCenter 不在核准值清單中時阻擋 EC2 建立操作。選項 A 是唯一同時疊加兩者的答案：用 SCP 解決缺 key 問題，再加上附加到 OU、將 CostCenter 限制為已知 cost center 清單的 tag policy，正是 AWS 建議的模式。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The SCP correctly handles the missing-key problem, but for invalid values it only updates the script to NOTIFY administrators. That is exactly the detective/notification approach the developers were already gaming with arbitrary values - it does not enforce or ensure a valid cost center at creation, so the core problem remains unsolved.","why_zh":"SCP 正確處理缺 key 問題，但對於無效值它只更新腳本去「通知」管理員。這正是開發者已用任意值規避的偵測/通知做法，並未在建立時強制或確保有效的 cost center，因此核心問題仍未解決。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"IAM permission boundaries set the maximum permissions for IAM principals; they are not the AWS mechanism for restricting resource tag values to an approved list at scale. Deploying and maintaining permission boundaries across 500 member accounts is impractical, and organization-wide tag value compliance is the job of tag policies, not per-account permission boundaries, so approved values are not reliably ensured.","why_zh":"IAM permission boundary 設定 IAM 主體的最大權限，並非 AWS 用來在大規模下將資源 tag 值限制為核准清單的機制。在 500 個成員帳戶部署並維護 permission boundary 不切實際，而組織層級的 tag 值合規應由 tag policy 負責，而非各帳戶的 permission boundary，因此無法可靠確保核准值。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no SCP, so creation without the CostCenter key is not prevented (tag policies cannot enforce a missing key). Worse, the Lambda adds only an EMPTY CostCenter tag key, which supplies no valid cost-center value and is itself noncompliant/meaningless for cost tracking; a reactive RunInstances-triggered Lambda also races with the requirement. It solves neither the missing-key nor the valid-value need.","why_zh":"沒有 SCP，因此未阻止建立缺少 CostCenter key 的資源（tag policy 無法強制補上缺失的 key）。更糟的是，Lambda 只加上「空的」CostCenter tag key，沒有有效的 cost center 值，本身就不合規且對成本追蹤無意義；由 RunInstances 觸發的被動式 Lambda 也與需求存在競態。這既未解決缺 key 也未解決有效值的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-enforcement.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies-best-practices.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_example-tag-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html"]}},{"id":327,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer uses a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. The pipeline has a build action and a deploy action for a single-page web application that is delivered to an Amazon S3 bucket. Amazon CloudFront serves the web application. The build action creates an artifact for the web application. The DevOps engineer has created an AWS CloudFormation template that defines the S3 bucket and configures the S3 bucket to host the application. The DevOps engineer has configured a CloudFormation deploy action before the S3 action. The CloudFormation deploy action creates the S3 bucket. The DevOps engineer needs to configure the S3 deploy action to use the S3 bucket from the CloudFormation template. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师在 AWS CodePipeline 中使用了一条管道。该管道针对一个单页网络应用程序， 包含构建操作和部署操作，该应用程序会被交付到一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。Amazon CloudFront 为该 网络应用程序提供服务。构建操作会为网络应用程序创建一个工件。 DevOps 工程师创建了一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板，该模板定义了 S3 存储桶，并配置了该 S3 存储 桶以托管应用程序。DevOps 工程师还配置了一个 CloudFormation 在 S3 操作之前部署操作。CloudFormation 部署操作会创建 S3 存储桶。DevOps 工程师需要将 S3 部署操 作配置为使用 CloudFormation 模板中的 S3 存储桶。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add an output named BucketName to the CloudFormation template. Set the output's value to refer to the S3 bucket from the CloudFormation template. Configure the output value to export to an AWS::SSM::Parameter resource named Stackvariables.","B":"Add an output named BucketName to the CloudFormation template. Set the output's value to refer to the S3 bucket from the CloudFormation template. Set the CloudFormation action's namespace to StackVariables in the pipeline.","C":"Configure the output artifacts of the CloudFormation action in the pipeline to be an AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store parameter named StackVariables. Name the artifact BucketName.","D":"Configure the build artifact from the build action as the input to the CodePipeline S3 deploy action. Configure the deploy action to deploy to the S3 bucket by using the StackVariables.BucketName variable.","E":"Configure the build artifact from the build action and the AWS Systems Manager parameter as the inputs to the deploy action. Configure the deploy action to deploy to the S3 bucket by using the StackVariables.BucketName variable."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFormation 模板中添加一个名为 BucketName 的输出。将该输出的值设置为引用 CloudFormation 模板中的 S3 存储桶。配置输出值以导出到名为 Stackvariables 的 AWS::SSM:: Parameter 资源。","B":"在 CloudFormation 模板中添加一个名为 BucketName 的输出。将该输出的值设置为引用 CloudFormation 模板中的 S3 存储桶。在管道中将 CloudFormation 操作的命名空间设置为 StackVariables。","C":"在管道中配置 CloudFormation 操作的输出工件，使其成为名为 StackVariables 的 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储参数。将该工件命名为 BucketName。","D":"将构建操作生成的构建工件配置为 CodePipeline S3 部署操作的输入。配置部署操作，使用 StackVariables.BucketName 变量将内容部署到 S3 存储桶。","E":"将构建操作生成的构建工件和 AWS Systems Manager 参数配置为部署操作的输入。配置部署操作， 使用 StackVariables.BucketName 变量将内容部署到 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CodePipeline passes values between actions using action output variables plus a namespace, not SSM parameters or input artifacts. For a CloudFormation deploy action, AWS docs state the action 'produces variables from any values designated in the Outputs section of a stack template' for action modes that create or update a stack (CHANGE_SET_EXECUTE, CHANGE_SET_REPLACE, CREATE_UPDATE, REPLACE_ON_FAILURE). To make those variables consumable downstream you assign the action a namespace; 'if the namespace isn't specified, the variables are not available for reference in the action configuration.' So Option B is correct: add an Output named BucketName whose value refers to the S3 bucket, and set the CloudFormation action's namespace to StackVariables. Option D is correct because the S3 deploy action reference says its input is exactly 1 artifact (the files to deploy = the build artifact) and its required BucketName configuration field can reference the produced variable using the namespace.key syntax #{StackVariables.BucketName}. Together B and D wire the bucket name from the CloudFormation stack Outputs into the S3 deploy action.","explanation_zh":"CodePipeline 在 action 之間傳遞數值是透過 action 的 output variables 加上 namespace，而不是透過 SSM 參數或 input artifact。對於 CloudFormation deploy action，AWS 文件明確指出該 action 會「從 stack template 的 Outputs 區段中任何指定的值產生變數」，且僅限會建立或更新 stack 的 action mode（CHANGE_SET_EXECUTE、CHANGE_SET_REPLACE、CREATE_UPDATE、REPLACE_ON_FAILURE）。要讓這些變數能被下游 action 取用，必須為該 action 指定一個 namespace；文件說「若未指定 namespace，變數就無法在 action 設定中被引用」。因此選項 B 正確：新增名為 BucketName 的 Output，其值指向 S3 bucket，並將 CloudFormation action 的 namespace 設為 StackVariables。選項 D 正確，因為 S3 deploy action reference 指出其 input 恰好為 1 個 artifact（要部署的檔案，即 build artifact），而其必填的 BucketName 設定欄位可用 namespace.key 語法 #{StackVariables.BucketName} 引用所產生的變數。B 與 D 一起把 CloudFormation stack Outputs 的 bucket 名稱傳遞給 S3 deploy action。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation Outputs cannot 'export to an AWS::SSM::Parameter resource.' Output exports use Export/Fn::ImportValue for cross-stack references, not SSM. CodePipeline consumes the value via action namespaces and the variable reference syntax, not by writing the output into an SSM parameter resource.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 的 Outputs 無法『匯出到 AWS::SSM::Parameter 資源』。Output 的 export 是用 Export/Fn::ImportValue 做跨 stack 參照，而非寫入 SSM。CodePipeline 透過 action namespace 與變數引用語法取用該值，而不是把 output 寫進 SSM 參數資源。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The CloudFormation action's output artifact is an S3-stored JSON file (the OutputFileName containing the stack Outputs section), not an SSM Parameter Store parameter. You cannot configure an output artifact to be an SSM parameter, and the S3 deploy action does not read bucket names from output artifacts.","why_zh":"CloudFormation action 的 output artifact 是存放於 S3 的 JSON 檔（即 OutputFileName，內含 stack Outputs 區段），並非 SSM Parameter Store 參數。無法把 output artifact 設定成 SSM 參數，且 S3 deploy action 也不會從 output artifact 讀取 bucket 名稱。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Per the S3 deploy action reference, the action accepts exactly 1 input artifact (the files to deploy), and an SSM parameter cannot be supplied as an input artifact. The bucket name is consumed through the BucketName configuration field via the #{StackVariables.BucketName} variable reference, not as a second input artifact.","why_zh":"依 S3 deploy action reference，該 action 恰好只接受 1 個 input artifact（要部署的檔案），而 SSM 參數無法作為 input artifact 提供。Bucket 名稱是透過 BucketName 設定欄位以 #{StackVariables.BucketName} 變數引用方式取用，而非作為第二個 input artifact。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CloudFormation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-variables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-S3Deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/reference-variables.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/tutorials-cloudformation-action.html"]}},{"id":328,"question_en":"A company used a lift and shift strategy to migrate a workload to AWS. The company has an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances. Each EC2 instance runs a web application, a database, and a Redis cache. Users are experiencing large variations in the web application's response times. Requests to the web application go to a single EC2 instance that is under significant load. The company wants to separate the application components to improve availability and performance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司采用“平移”策略将工作负载迁移到了 AWS。该公司有一个由亚马逊 EC2 实例组成的自动扩 展组。每个 EC2 实例都运行着一个网络应用程序、一个数据库和一个 Redis 缓存。 用户在使用网络应用程序时，发现其响应时间存在较大差异。向该网络应用程序发出的请求都发送到 了一台负载过重的 EC2 实例上。该公司希望将应用程序的各个组件分离，以提高可用性和性能。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a Network Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group for the web application. Migrate the database to an Amazon Aurora Serverless database. Create an Application Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group for the Redis cache.","B":"Create an Application Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group for the web application. Migrate the database to an Amazon Aurora database that has a Multi-AZ deployment. Create a Network Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group in a single Availability Zone for the Redis cache.","C":"Create a Network Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group for the web application. Migrate the database to an Amazon Aurora Serverless database. Create an Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster for the cache. Create a target group that has a DNS target type that contains the ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster hostname.","D":"Create an Application Load Balancer and an Auto Scaling group for the web application. Migrate the database to an Amazon Aurora database that has a Multi-AZ deployment. Create an Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) cluster for the cache."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 Web 应用程序创建一个网络负载均衡器和一个自动扩展组。将数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora Serverless 数据库。为 Redis 缓存创建一个应用负载均衡器和一个自动扩展组。","B":"为 Web 应用程序创建一个应用负载均衡器和一个自动扩展组。将数据库迁移到具有多可用区部署 的 Amazon Aurora 数据库。在单个可用区中为 Redis 缓存创建一个网络负载均衡器和一个自动扩 展组。","C":"为网络应用创建一个网络负载均衡器和一个自动扩展组。将数据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora 无服务 器数据库。创建一个 Amazon ElastiCache（Redis 开源软件） 为缓存创建一个集群。创建一个具有 DNS 目标类型的靶向组，其中包含 ElastiCache（Redis OSS） 集群的主机名。","D":"为 Web 应用程序创建应用负载均衡器和自动扩展组。将数据库迁移到具有多可用区部署的 Amazon Aurora 数据库。创建一个 Amazon ElastiCache（Redis OSS）集群用于缓存。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The task is to decompose the co-located web/database/cache stack into the architecturally correct, fully managed service for each tier. (1) Web tier: the web application serves HTTP/HTTPS, so an Application Load Balancer (Layer 7) plus an Auto Scaling group is the right choice, which eliminates options A and C that front the web tier with a Network Load Balancer (Layer 4). (2) Database: Amazon Aurora with a Multi-AZ deployment provides a synchronous standby and automatic failover for high availability, satisfying the availability requirement. (3) Cache: Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) is the managed Redis service; with replication groups it provides Multi-AZ failover. You do not place a stateful in-memory Redis store behind a load balancer and an Auto Scaling group (as in A and B). Option C is additionally wrong because it invents a 'DNS target type' target group pointing at the ElastiCache hostname; AWS docs confirm NLB target group types are only instance, ip, and alb (ALB supports instance, ip, lambda) and clients connect directly to the ElastiCache endpoint, not through a load balancer target group. Only option D pairs each component with the correct managed, highly available service: ALB plus Auto Scaling for the web tier, Aurora Multi-AZ for the database, and ElastiCache (Redis OSS) for the cache.","explanation_zh":"本題要將共置的 web/資料庫/快取 堆疊拆分為各層架構上正確且完全受管的服務。(1) Web 層：web 應用提供 HTTP/HTTPS 服務，因此 Application Load Balancer（第七層）加 Auto Scaling group 是正確選擇，這排除了以 Network Load Balancer（第四層）作為 web 層前端的選項 A 與 C。(2) 資料庫：具 Multi-AZ 部署的 Amazon Aurora 提供同步待命節點與自動故障轉移以達成高可用性，符合可用性需求。(3) 快取：Amazon ElastiCache (Redis OSS) 是受管的 Redis 服務，搭配 replication group 可提供 Multi-AZ 故障轉移。不應把有狀態的記憶體內 Redis 放在負載平衡器加 Auto Scaling group 之後（如 A 與 B）。選項 C 另外還錯在虛構了一個指向 ElastiCache 主機名稱的「DNS 目標類型」target group；AWS 文件確認 NLB target group 類型只有 instance、ip 與 alb（ALB 支援 instance、ip、lambda），且用戶端應直接連到 ElastiCache 端點，而非透過負載平衡器 target group。只有選項 D 為每個元件搭配正確、受管且高可用的服務：web 層用 ALB 加 Auto Scaling、資料庫用 Aurora Multi-AZ、快取用 ElastiCache (Redis OSS)。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses a Network Load Balancer (Layer 4) for an HTTP/HTTPS web application where an ALB (Layer 7) is appropriate, and incorrectly fronts the Redis cache with an ALB and an Auto Scaling group instead of using managed ElastiCache. Redis is a stateful in-memory data store, not a stateless load-balanceable web tier, so this design does not improve availability or performance correctly.","why_zh":"對 HTTP/HTTPS web 應用使用第四層的 Network Load Balancer（應使用第七層 ALB），並錯誤地以 ALB 加 Auto Scaling group 作為 Redis 快取前端，而非使用受管的 ElastiCache。Redis 是有狀態的記憶體內資料儲存，不是可負載平衡的無狀態 web 層，因此此設計無法正確提升可用性或效能。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Correctly uses an ALB for the web tier and Aurora Multi-AZ for the database, but tries to load-balance a self-managed Redis behind an NLB and an Auto Scaling group in a single Availability Zone. Single-AZ reduces availability, and self-managing Redis behind an NLB/ASG is architecturally wrong compared with the managed ElastiCache (Redis OSS) service.","why_zh":"正確使用 ALB 與 Aurora Multi-AZ，但試圖把自管的 Redis 放在單一可用區的 NLB 加 Auto Scaling group 之後做負載平衡。單一可用區降低可用性，且以 NLB/ASG 自管 Redis 在架構上不如使用受管的 ElastiCache (Redis OSS) 服務。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses an NLB for the HTTP/HTTPS web tier (ALB is the correct Layer-7 choice) and invents a 'DNS target type' target group pointing at the ElastiCache hostname. AWS docs confirm NLB target group types are only instance, ip, and alb (ALB target groups support instance, ip, lambda); there is no DNS target type, and clients connect directly to the ElastiCache endpoint rather than through a load balancer target group.","why_zh":"對 HTTP/HTTPS web 層使用 NLB（正確選擇是第七層 ALB），並虛構了一個指向 ElastiCache 主機名稱的「DNS 目標類型」target group。AWS 文件確認 NLB target group 類型只有 instance、ip 與 alb（ALB target group 支援 instance、ip、lambda）；並沒有 DNS 目標類型，且用戶端應直接連到 ElastiCache 端點，而非透過負載平衡器 target group。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/network/load-balancer-target-groups.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonElastiCache/latest/dg/Replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonElastiCache/latest/dg/disaster-recovery-resiliency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Concepts.AuroraHighAvailability.html"]}},{"id":329,"question_en":"A company is using AWS Organizations and wants to implement a governance strategy with the following requirements: • AWS resource access is restricted to the same two Regions for all accounts. • AWS services are limited to a specific group of authorized services for all accounts. • Authentication is provided by Active Directory. • Access permissions are organized by job function and are identical in each account. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS 组织，并希望实施一项具有以下要求的治理策略： • 所有账户对 AWS 资源的访问权限均仅限于相同的两个区域。 • 对于所有账户，AWS 服务仅限于特定的一组授权服务。 身份验证由 Active Directory 提供。 访问权限按工作职能进行组织，并且每个账户中的权限都相同。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Establish an organizational unit (OU) with group policies in the management account to restrict Regions and authorized services. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to provision roles with permissions for each job function, including an IAM trust policy for IAM identity provider authentication in each account.","B":"Establish a permission boundary in the management account to restrict Regions and authorized services. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to provision roles with permissions for each job function, including an IAM trust policy for IAM identity provider authentication in each account.","C":"Establish a service control policy in the management account to restrict Regions and authorized services. Use AWS Resource Access Manager (AWS RAM) to share management account roles with permissions for each job function, including AWS IAM Identity Center for authentication in each account.","D":"Establish a service control policy in the management account to restrict Regions and authorized services. Use AWS CloudFormation StackSets to provision roles with permissions for each job function, including an IAM trust policy for IAM identity provider authentication in each account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户中创建一个具有组策略的组织单位（OU），以限制区域和授权服务。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 为每个工作职能配置具有相应权限的角色，包括每个账户中用于 IAM 身份 提供商身份验证的 IAM 信任策略。","B":"在管理账户中设置权限边界，以限制区域和授权服务。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 为 每个工作职能配置具有相应权限的角色，包括为每个账户中的 IAM 身份提供商身份验证配置 IAM 信任策略。","C":"在管理账户中建立服务控制策略，以限制区域和授权服务。使用 AWS 资源访问管理器（AWS RAM） 与每个工作职能的权限共享管理账户角色，包括在每个账户中使用 AWS IAM 身份中心进行身份验 证。","D":"在管理账户中建立服务控制策略，以限制区域和授权服务。使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 为每个工作职能配置具有相应权限的角色，包括为每个账户中的 IAM 身份提供商身份验证配 置 IAM 信任策略。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"All four requirements map cleanly onto option D. (1)+(2) The org-wide guardrail that restricts AWS resource access to specific Regions and limits accounts to an authorized set of services is a service control policy (SCP) attached at the organization or OU level. AWS docs state an SCP 'offers central control over the maximum available permissions for the IAM users and IAM roles in your organization,' which is exactly a deny-based Region/service guardrail across every member account. (3)+(4) AWS CloudFormation StackSets deploys identical stacks across many accounts in a single operation, so it can provision the same per-job-function IAM roles into every account. Each role's IAM trust policy references an IAM SAML identity provider, enabling SAML 2.0 federation from Active Directory (via AD FS) and AssumeRoleWithSAML, which delivers the Active-Directory-based authentication. Option D is the only choice that uses the correct mechanism for all four requirements.","explanation_zh":"四項需求都能完整對應到選項 D。(1)+(2) 將 AWS 資源存取限制在特定 Region、並限制帳戶僅能使用授權服務的組織層級護欄，是在組織或 OU 層級附加 service control policy (SCP)。AWS 文件指出 SCP「為組織中的 IAM users 與 IAM roles 提供最大可用權限的集中控制」，正是橫跨所有成員帳戶的 Region/服務 deny 型護欄。(3)+(4) AWS CloudFormation StackSets 可在單一作業中跨多個帳戶部署相同的堆疊，因此能將各工作職能對應的相同 IAM roles 佈署到每個帳戶。每個 role 的 IAM trust policy 參照 IAM SAML identity provider，啟用從 Active Directory（透過 AD FS）進行的 SAML 2.0 聯合與 AssumeRoleWithSAML，提供以 Active Directory 為基礎的驗證。只有選項 D 對四項需求都採用正確機制。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Organizations has no feature called 'group policies.' OUs are merely containers in the org hierarchy; the org-wide guardrail used to restrict Regions and services is the SCP, not a 'group policy.' The mechanism/terminology for the restriction half is invalid, so the option cannot satisfy requirements (1) and (2).","why_zh":"AWS Organizations 並無所謂「group policies」功能。OU 只是組織階層中的容器，限制 Region 與服務的組織層級護欄是 SCP，而非「group policy」。限制部分的機制/用語無效，因此無法滿足需求 (1) 與 (2)。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Permission boundaries set the maximum permissions of a single IAM entity (a user or role) and are attached per-entity. They are not an organization-wide control you 'establish in the management account' to restrict Regions/services for all accounts. The correct org-wide guardrail is the SCP, so the restriction half fails requirements (1) and (2).","why_zh":"Permission boundary 設定的是單一 IAM 實體（user 或 role）的最大權限，並以個別實體為單位附加，無法在管理帳戶中「設定」以對所有帳戶限制 Region/服務。正確的組織層級護欄是 SCP，因此限制部分無法滿足需求 (1) 與 (2)。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The SCP half is correct, but AWS RAM cannot share IAM roles. RAM shares service-managed resources (for example VPC subnets, Transit Gateways, Route 53 rules, License Manager configs); IAM roles are not in the RAM shareable resource-type list. RAM can optionally share certain resources to IAM users/roles, but it cannot share the roles themselves, so you cannot use RAM to distribute management-account job-function roles to member accounts.","why_zh":"SCP 部分正確，但 AWS RAM 無法分享 IAM roles。RAM 分享的是由服務管理的資源（例如 VPC subnets、Transit Gateways、Route 53 規則、License Manager 設定）；IAM role 不在 RAM 可分享資源類型清單中。RAM 雖可選擇性地將某些資源分享給 IAM users/roles，但無法分享 role 本身，因此無法用 RAM 將管理帳戶的職能 role 散布到成員帳戶。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/what-is-cfnstacksets.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ram/latest/userguide/shareable.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/id_roles_providers_saml.html"]}},{"id":330,"question_en":"A company detects unusual login attempts in many of its AWS accounts. A DevOps engineer must implement a solution that sends a notification to the company's security team when multiple failed login attempts occur. The DevOps engineer has already created an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic and has subscribed the security team to the SNS topic. Which solution will provide the notification with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司发现其多个 AWS 账户出现了异常登录尝试。一位 DevOps 工程师必须实施一个解决方案，当多 次登录尝试失败时向公司的安全团队发送通知。该 DevOps 工程师已经创建了一个亚马逊简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题，并已将安全团队订阅到该 SNS 主题。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力提供通知？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send management events to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Create a CloudWatch Logs metric filter to match failed ConsoleLogin events. Create a CloudWatch alarm that is based on the metric filter. Configure an alarm action to send messages to the SNS topic.","B":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send management events to an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an Amazon Athena query that returns a failure if the query finds failed logins in the logs in the S3 bucket. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to periodically run the query. Create a second EventBridge rule to detect when the query fails and to send a message to the SNS topic.","C":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send data events to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. Create a CloudWatch logs metric filter to match failed ConsoleLogin events. Create a CloudWatch alarm that is based on the metric filter. Configure an alarm action to send messages to the SNS topic.","D":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send data events to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure an Amazon S3 event notification for the s3:ObjectCreated event type. Filter the event type by ConsoleLogin failed events. Configure the event notification to forward to the SNS topic."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将管理事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器以匹配失败的控制台登录事件。基于该指标筛选器创建一个 CloudWatch 警报。配置警报 操作以向 SNS 主题发送消息。","B":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将管理事件发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。创建一个 Amazon Athena 查询，如果在 S3 存储桶中的日志中发现登录失败，则该查询返回失败。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则以定期运行 该查询。创建第二个 EventBridge 规则以检测查询失败并向 SNS 主题发送消息。","C":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将数据事件发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。创建一个 CloudWatch 日志指 标过滤器以匹配失败的控制台登录事件。基于该指标过滤器创建一个 CloudWatch 警报。配置警报操作 以向 SNS 主题发送消息。","D":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将数据事件发送到 Amazon S3 存储桶。为 s3:ObjectCreated 事件类型配置 Amazon S3 事件通知。通过控制台登录失败事件筛选事件类型。配置事件通知将其转发到 SNS 主 题。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Failed console logins are captured by CloudTrail as the ConsoleLogin event. Per AWS docs, console sign-in events are non-API events logged alongside management events (eventType = AwsConsoleSignIn), and they are NOT data events. The canonical, fully managed, least-effort pattern is Option A: send CloudTrail management events to a CloudWatch Logs log group, create a metric filter that matches failed ConsoleLogin events, create a CloudWatch alarm on that metric, and configure the alarm action to publish to the existing SNS topic. This requires no custom code, no scheduling, and no extra services (it is the same approach the CIS AWS Benchmark uses for monitoring unauthorized console sign-in failures). Option C fails because data events are data-plane resource operations (S3 object-level activity, Lambda Invoke, SNS Publish), so the metric filter would never see ConsoleLogin and would never alarm. Option B is functional but adds S3, Athena, scheduled queries, and two EventBridge rules, which is far more operational effort. Option D is infeasible because S3 event notifications fire on object creation (s3:ObjectCreated) and cannot inspect or filter on the contents of the delivered log files.","explanation_zh":"失敗的主控台登入會被 CloudTrail 以 ConsoleLogin 事件記錄。依 AWS 文件，主控台登入事件屬於非 API 事件，與 management events 一起記錄（eventType 為 AwsConsoleSignIn），而非 data events。最標準、全託管且最省力的做法是選項 A：將 CloudTrail management events 送到 CloudWatch Logs log group，建立比對失敗 ConsoleLogin 事件的 metric filter，再對該 metric 建立 CloudWatch alarm，並把 alarm action 設定為發佈到既有的 SNS topic。此做法無需自訂程式、無需排程、也不需額外服務（與 CIS AWS Benchmark 監控未授權主控台登入失敗所用的方法相同）。選項 C 不可行，因為 data events 是資料層級的資源操作（S3 物件層級活動、Lambda Invoke、SNS Publish），metric filter 永遠看不到 ConsoleLogin，也就永遠不會觸發告警。選項 B 雖可運作，但加入 S3、Athena、排程查詢與兩條 EventBridge 規則，運維負擔明顯更高。選項 D 不可行，因為 S3 事件通知是在物件建立（s3:ObjectCreated）時觸發，無法檢視或依交付的 log 檔內容進行過濾。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Using Athena queries plus two EventBridge rules and a periodic scheduled query is functional but introduces many moving parts (S3 delivery, Athena, query scheduling, two separate rules), which is far more operational effort than a single metric-filter alarm. It violates the LEAST operational effort requirement.","why_zh":"使用 Athena 查詢加上兩條 EventBridge 規則與定期排程查詢雖可運作，但元件繁多（S3 交付、Athena、查詢排程、兩條獨立規則），運維負擔遠高於單一 metric filter 加 alarm，違反『最少運維』要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Identical to A but routes CloudTrail DATA events to the log group. AWS docs define data events as data-plane resource operations (S3 object-level, Lambda Invoke, SNS Publish); ConsoleLogin is a non-API/management-tier event, not a data event, so a metric filter on data events would never match failed ConsoleLogin and would never alarm. Technically broken.","why_zh":"與 A 相同，但把 CloudTrail DATA events 送到 log group。AWS 文件將 data events 定義為資料層級的資源操作（S3 物件層級、Lambda Invoke、SNS Publish）；ConsoleLogin 是非 API／management 層級事件而非 data event，因此對 data events 設的 metric filter 永遠比對不到失敗的 ConsoleLogin，永遠不會觸發告警，技術上不成立。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"S3 event notifications trigger on object lifecycle events (e.g., s3:ObjectCreated) and cannot inspect or filter on the contents of the delivered log files. There is no mechanism to 'filter by ConsoleLogin failed events' inside an S3 event notification, so this is not technically feasible.","why_zh":"S3 事件通知是針對物件生命週期事件（例如 s3:ObjectCreated）觸發，無法檢視或依交付的 log 檔內容過濾。S3 事件通知並無『依 ConsoleLogin 失敗事件過濾』的機制，技術上無法實現。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-non-api-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-event-reference-aws-console-sign-in-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/logging-management-events-with-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/logging-data-events-with-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/monitor-cloudtrail-log-files-with-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateMetricFilterProcedure.html"]}},{"id":331,"question_en":"A company has deployed a new REST API by using Amazon API Gateway. The company uses the API to access confidential data. The API must be accessed from only specific VPCs in the company. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司通过使用亚马逊 API 网关部署了一个新的 REST API。该公司使用此 API 访问机密数据。该 API 必须仅能从公司内部的特定虚拟私有云（VPC）进行访问。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create and attach a resource policy to the API Gateway API. Configure the resource policy to allow only the specific VPC IDs.","B":"Add a security group to the API Gateway API. Configure the inbound rules to allow only the specific VPC IP address ranges.","C":"Create and attach an IAM role to the API Gateway API. Configure the IAM role to allow only the specific VPC IDs.","D":"Add an ACL to the API Gateway API. Configure the outbound rules to allow only the specific VPC IP address ranges."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建并附加一个资源策略到 API 网关 API 上。配置该资源策略，使其仅允许特定的 VPC ID。","B":"将安全组添加到 API 网关 API 中。配置入站规则，仅允许特定的 VPC IP 地址范围。","C":"创建并向 API 网关 API 挂载一个 IAM 角色。将该 IAM 角色配置为仅允许特定的 VPC ID。","D":"在 API 网关 API 上添加访问控制列表（ACL）。配置出站规则，仅允许特定的 VPC IP 地址范围。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Amazon API Gateway resource policies are JSON policy documents that you attach directly to a REST API to control which principals can invoke it. The AWS documentation explicitly states that resource policies can allow an API to be invoked by 'Specified virtual private clouds (VPCs) or VPC endpoints (in any account).' The official resource policy examples page includes one titled 'Allow private API traffic based on source VPC or VPC endpoint' that uses the aws:SourceVpc condition key (e.g., vpc-1a2b3c4d) to restrict access to only specific VPCs. This is the native, intended mechanism for limiting access to confidential API data to specific VPCs, so option A is correct.","explanation_zh":"Amazon API Gateway resource policy 是直接附加到 REST API 上的 JSON 政策文件，用於控制哪些 principal 可以呼叫該 API。AWS 文件明確指出 resource policy 可以允許 API 被『指定的 virtual private clouds (VPCs) 或 VPC endpoints（任何帳戶）』呼叫。官方的 resource policy 範例頁面包含名為『Allow private API traffic based on source VPC or VPC endpoint』的範例，使用 aws:SourceVpc condition key（例如 vpc-1a2b3c4d）將存取限制為僅特定 VPC。這正是將機密 API 資料限制給特定 VPC 的原生且預期的機制，因此選項 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"API Gateway is a fully managed regional service; you cannot attach a security group to an API Gateway API. Security groups apply to ENIs and VPC resources (an interface VPC endpoint can have a security group, but the API itself cannot), and source-VPC restriction for the API is performed via a resource policy, not security group inbound rules.","why_zh":"API Gateway 是全託管的區域服務，無法為 API Gateway API 附加 security group。Security group 適用於 ENI 與 VPC 資源（介面 VPC endpoint 可有 security group，但 API 本身不行），對 API 的來源 VPC 限制是透過 resource policy 而非 security group inbound rules 完成。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"You do not 'attach an IAM role to the API' to grant invocation access by VPC. IAM identity-based policies control which principals (users/roles) can call the API via SigV4, and a role cannot allow or deny based on specific VPC IDs. The construct that filters by aws:SourceVpc is a resource policy, not an IAM role.","why_zh":"不能透過『將 IAM role 附加到 API』來依 VPC 授予呼叫權限。IAM 身分型政策控制哪些 principal（使用者/角色）能透過 SigV4 呼叫 API，且 role 無法依特定 VPC ID 允許或拒絕。能依 aws:SourceVpc 篩選的是 resource policy，而非 IAM role。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"API Gateway does not have ACLs with inbound/outbound rules; that concept belongs to VPC network ACLs, which operate on subnets, not on a managed API. Moreover, outbound rules would not control inbound API access from VPCs. This option conflates VPC networking constructs with API Gateway access control.","why_zh":"API Gateway 沒有具 inbound/outbound rules 的 ACL；該概念屬於 VPC network ACL，作用於 subnet 而非託管 API。此外，outbound rules 無法控制來自 VPC 的 inbound API 存取。此選項混淆了 VPC 網路結構與 API Gateway 存取控制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-resource-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-resource-policies-examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/apigateway/latest/developerguide/apigateway-private-apis.html"]}},{"id":332,"question_en":"A company runs a website by using an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) service that is connected to an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The service was in a steady state with tasks responding to requests successfully. A DevOps engineer updated the task definition with a new container image and deployed the new task definition to the service. The DevOps engineer noticed that the service is frequently stopping and starting new tasks because the ALB health checks are failing. What should the DevOps engineer do to troubleshoot the failed deployment?","question_zh":"一家公司通过使用与应用负载均衡器（ALB）相连接的亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）来运营其 网站。该服务一直保持稳定状态，任务能够成功响应请求。 一位 DevOps 工程师使用新的容器镜像更新了任务定义，并将新的任务定义部署到服务中。该 DevOps 工程师注意到，由于应用负载均衡器（ALB）的健康检查失败，服务频繁停止并启动新任务。 DevOps 工程师应该采取什么措施来排查部署失败的问题？","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that a security group associated with the service allows traffic from the ALB.","B":"Increase the ALB health check grace period for the service.","C":"Increase the service minimum healthy percent setting.","D":"Decrease the ALB health check interval."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保与服务相关联的安全组允许来自应用负载均衡器（ALB）的流量。","B":"延长该服务的 ALB 健康检查宽限期。","C":"提高服务最低健康百分比设置。","D":"减少 ALB 健康检查的间隔时间。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The service was already in a steady state with the old task definition, so networking, security groups, target groups, and the ALB health check configuration were all functioning. The only change was the new container image. A repeated stop/start cycle driven by failing ALB health checks immediately after deployment is the textbook symptom of a new image that needs more time to initialize before it can respond to ALB health checks. The ECS service parameter healthCheckGracePeriodSeconds is defined as 'the period of time, in seconds, that the Amazon ECS service scheduler ignores unhealthy Elastic Load Balancing, VPC Lattice, and container health checks after a task has first started' (default 0). Increasing this grace period makes ECS ignore the early failing ELB health checks while the new container finishes initializing, stopping ECS from prematurely killing tasks that just need more startup time. This is the correct ECS-specific troubleshooting lever for this exact deployment symptom, so the answer is B.","explanation_zh":"該 service 在使用舊 task definition 時已經處於 steady state，代表網路、security group、target group 以及 ALB health check 設定原本都正常運作；唯一的變更是新的 container image。部署後立即因 ALB health check 失敗而反覆停止/啟動 task，正是新映像在啟動初期還來不及回應 health check 的典型徵兆。ECS service 參數 healthCheckGracePeriodSeconds 的官方定義為「Amazon ECS service scheduler 在 task 首次啟動後忽略 unhealthy Elastic Load Balancing、VPC Lattice 與 container health check 的秒數」（預設為 0）。增加此 grace period 可讓 ECS 在新 container 完成初始化前忽略早期失敗的 ELB health check，避免 ECS 過早終止只是需要更多啟動時間的 task。因此正確答案為 B。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The service already reached a steady state with the same security groups before the new image was deployed. A security group blocking ALB traffic would have prevented the service from ever reaching steady state, so the security group cannot be the cause when the only change is the container image. The ECS load balancer troubleshooting doc lists security groups only for services that never reach steady state.","why_zh":"該 service 在部署新映像前，已用相同的 security group 達到 steady state。若 security group 阻擋 ALB 流量，原本就無法達到 steady state；既然唯一變更是 container image，security group 不會是原因。ECS 文件僅針對從未達到 steady state 的 service 才需檢查 security group。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"minimumHealthyPercent only controls how many existing tasks must stay running during a deployment to preserve availability; it does not change whether or when ALB health checks pass. Raising it does not give a slow-starting container more time to initialize and does not stop the stop/start cycle caused by failing health checks, so it does not address the root cause.","why_zh":"minimumHealthyPercent 只控制部署期間需保持運行的既有 task 數量以維持可用性，並不影響 ALB health check 是否或何時通過。提高它無法讓啟動較慢的 container 取得更多初始化時間，也無法停止因 health check 失敗造成的停止/啟動循環，未解決根本原因。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Decreasing the health check interval makes checks more frequent, which causes a task to reach the unhealthy threshold faster, not slower. AWS docs state that shorter health check intervals accelerate reaching the Unhealthy Threshold, so this would worsen the premature task termination, the opposite of what is needed.","why_zh":"縮短 health check interval 會使檢查更頻繁，讓 task 更快達到 unhealthy threshold，而非更慢。AWS 文件指出較短的 health check interval 會加速達到 Unhealthy Threshold，因此這只會加劇 task 被過早終止，與需求相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sdk-for-kotlin/api/latest/ecs/aws.sdk.kotlin.services.ecs.model/-create-service-request/health-check-grace-period-seconds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/troubleshoot-service-load-balancers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/load-balancer-healthcheck.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/service-unhealthy-event-messages.html"]}},{"id":333,"question_en":"A company that uses electronic patient health records runs a fleet of Amazon EC2 instances with an Amazon Linux operating system. The company must continuously ensure that the EC2 instances are running operating system patches and application patches that are in compliance with current privacy regulations. The company uses a custom repository to store application patches. A DevOps engineer needs to automate the deployment of operating system patches and application patches. The DevOps engineer wants to use both the default operating system patch repository and the custom patch repository. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST effort?","question_zh":"一家使用电子患者健康记录的公司运行着一批搭载亚马逊 Linux 操作系统的亚马逊 EC2 实例。该 公司必须持续确保这些 EC2 实例运行的操作系统补丁和应用程序补丁符合当前的隐私法规。该 公司使用一个自定义的存储库来存储应用程序补丁。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要实现操作系统补丁和应用程序补丁的自动化部署。该工程师希望同时使用 默认的操作系统补丁库和自定义补丁库。 哪种解决方案能以最少的努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager to create a new custom patch baseline that includes the default operating system repository and the custom repository. Run the AWS-RunPatchBaseline document by using the Run command to verify and install patches. Use the BaselineOverride API to configure the new custom patch baseline.","B":"Use AWS Direct Connect to integrate the custom repository with the EC2 instances. Use Amazon EventBridge events to deploy the patches.","C":"Use the yum-config-manager command to add the custom repository to the /etc/yum.repos.d configuration. Run the yum-config-manager-enable command to activate the new repository.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager to create a patch baseline for the default operating system repository and a second patch baseline for the custom repository. Run the AWS-RunPatchBaseline document by using the Run command to verify and install patches. Use the BaselineOverride API to configure the default patch baseline and the custom patch baseline."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 创建一个新的自定义补丁基准，该基准包含默认的操作系统存储库和自 定义存储库。使用“运行”命令运行 AWS-RunPatchBaseline 文档以验证并安装补丁。使用 BaselineOverride API 配置新的自定义补丁基准。","B":"使用 AWS Direct Connect 将自定义存储库与 EC2 实例集成。使用 Amazon EventBridge 事件部 署补丁。","C":"使用 yum-config-manager 命令将自定义存储库添加到 /etc/yum.repos.d 配置中。运行 yum- config-manager-enable 命令以激活新的存储库。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 为默认操作系统存储库创建一个补丁基准，为自定义存储库创建另一 个补丁基准。使用 Run 命令运行 AWS-RunPatchBaseline 文档以验证并安装补丁。使用 BaselineOverride API 配置默认补丁基准和自定义补丁基准。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Patch Manager (a tool in AWS Systems Manager) lets you specify alternative patch source repositories inside a single custom patch baseline for Linux managed nodes. The AWS docs explicitly state that specifying alternative repositories does NOT mean specifying additional repositories: 'you must also specify the default repositories as part of the alternative patch source configuration if you want their updates to be applied.' This is the documented pattern for the exact scenario in this question (alternative-source-repository 'Example 3 - Internal Corporate Applications on supported Amazon Linux versions' for industry regulatory compliance): create or update one custom baseline whose Sources include BOTH the default OS repository and your custom corporate repository, then use Run Command to run the AWS-RunPatchBaseline document with Scan/Install to verify and install patches. The BaselineOverride parameter applies a JSON list of baselines from Amazon S3 and selects the baseline whose OperatingSystem matches the host, so a single Amazon Linux baseline containing both repos is applied at runtime. Option A captures exactly this single-baseline, two-repo design and meets the requirement with the LEAST effort.","explanation_zh":"Patch Manager（AWS Systems Manager 的工具）允許你在 Linux 受管節點的「單一」custom patch baseline 中指定替代的 patch source repositories（alternative source repositories）。AWS 文件明確指出：指定替代 repositories 並不等於指定「額外」repositories，「如果你想套用預設 repositories 的更新，必須同時把預設 repositories 也列為替代 patch 來源設定的一部分」。這正是本題情境的官方建議做法（見 alternative-source-repository 文件中的 'Example 3 - Internal Corporate Applications on supported Amazon Linux versions'，用於產業法規合規）：建立或更新「一個」custom baseline，在其 Sources 中同時包含預設 OS repository 與自訂 custom repository，再用 Run command 執行 AWS-RunPatchBaseline document（Scan/Install）來驗證與安裝 patch。BaselineOverride 參數會從 Amazon S3 套用一份 baseline 的 JSON 清單，並挑選 OperatingSystem 與 host 相符的 baseline，因此在執行時會套用這個同時含兩個 repo 的單一 Amazon Linux baseline。選項 A 正是這種「單一 baseline、兩個 repo」設計，並以最少工作量滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Direct Connect is a dedicated physical network connection between on-premises and AWS; it has nothing to do with integrating a software/yum package repository or deploying patches. Amazon EventBridge can trigger automation but does not itself install patches. This option uses the wrong services, adds far more effort, and never touches patch baselines or compliance.","why_zh":"AWS Direct Connect 是地端與 AWS 之間的專用實體網路連線，與整合軟體/yum 套件 repository 或部署 patch 無關。Amazon EventBridge 可觸發自動化，但本身並不會安裝 patch。此選項用錯服務、工作量更大，也完全沒有觸及 patch baseline 或合規。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Manually using yum-config-manager to edit /etc/yum.repos.d only configures a repository at the OS level on each instance; it is a per-node, non-automated approach that bypasses Patch Manager entirely. It does not provide centralized, continuous compliance verification against current privacy regulations and does not scale across a fleet. (The actual syntax is also `yum-config-manager --enable`, not a `yum-config-manager-enable` command.) This is more effort and not continuous compliance.","why_zh":"手動用 yum-config-manager 編輯 /etc/yum.repos.d 只是在每台執行個體的 OS 層級設定 repository，是逐節點、非自動化的做法，完全繞過 Patch Manager。它無法針對隱私法規提供集中式、持續的合規驗證，也無法在整個機群擴展。（正確語法是 `yum-config-manager --enable`，並無 `yum-config-manager-enable` 指令。）這是更多工作量且非持續合規。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"BaselineOverride applies a JSON list of baselines and uses only the baseline whose OperatingSystem matches the host (the doc's example list holds one AMAZON_LINUX_2 and one SUSE baseline). Creating two separate baselines for the SAME Amazon Linux OS is redundant and conflicting because only one will be selected per host, so the second repo would not be applied. The supported design is a single baseline whose Sources include both the default and the custom repository, so D adds effort with no benefit and fails the LEAST-effort qualifier.","why_zh":"BaselineOverride 會套用一份 baseline 的 JSON 清單，且只使用 OperatingSystem 與 host 相符的那一個 baseline（文件範例清單中是一個 AMAZON_LINUX_2 與一個 SUSE baseline）。為「同一個」Amazon Linux OS 建立兩個分開的 baseline 是多餘且衝突的，因為每台 host 只會選到其中一個，第二個 repo 不會被套用。受支援的設計是「單一」baseline 並在其 Sources 同時包含預設與自訂 repository，因此 D 增加工作量卻無好處，不符合「最少工作量」的限定條件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-alternative-source-repository.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-baselineoverride-parameter.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-aws-runpatchbaseline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/patch-manager-create-a-patch-baseline-for-linux.html"]}},{"id":334,"question_en":"A company use an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The company has enabled all features enabled for the organization. The company configured the organization as a hierarchy of OUs under the root OU. The company recently registered all its OUs and enrolled all its AWS accounts in AWS Control Tower. The company needs to customize the AWS Control Tower managed AWS Config configuration recorder in each of the company's AWS accounts. The company needs to apply the customizations to both the existing AWS accounts and to any new AWS accounts that the company enrolls in AWS Control Tower in the future. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司已启用该组织的所有 功能。该公司将组织配置为在根组织单元（OU）下分层的多个 OU。该公司最近已注册其所有 OU， 并将所有 AWS 账户纳入 AWS Control Tower。 该公司需要在每个 AWS 账户中自定义 AWS Control Tower 管理的 AWS Config 配置记录器。该公司 需要将这些自定义设置应用于现有的 AWS 账户以及未来在 AWS Control Tower 中注册的任何新账户。 哪些步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a new AWS account. Create an AWS Lambda function in the new account to apply the customizations to the AWS Config configuration recorder in each AWS account in the organization.","B":"Create a new AWS account as an AWS Config delegated administrator. Create an AWS Lambda function in the delegated administrator account to apply the customizations to the AWS Config configuration recorder in the delegated administrator account.","C":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule in the AWS Control Tower management account to invoke an AWS Lambda function when the Organizations OU is registered or reregistered. Re-register the root Organizations OU.","D":"Configure the AWSControlTowerExecution IAM role in each AWS account in the organization to be assumable by an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to assume the AWSControlTowerExecution IAM role.","E":"Create an IAM role in the AWS Control Tower management account that an AWS Lambda function can assume. Grant the IAM role permission to assume the AWSControlTowerExecution IAM role in any account in the organization. Configure the Lambda function to use the new IAM role.","F":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule in the AWS Control Tower management account to invoke an AWS Lambda function when an AWS account is updated or enrolled in AWS Control Tower or when the landing zone is updated. Re-register each Organizations OU in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在新账户中创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，用于对组织中每个 AWS 账户的 AWS Config 配置记录器应用自定义设置。","B":"以 AWS Config 委托管理员的身份创建一个新的 AWS 账户。在委托管理员账户中创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以对委托管理员账户中的 AWS Config 配置记录器应用自定义设置。","C":"在 AWS 控制塔管理账户中配置 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在组织单位（OU）注册或重新注 册时调用 AWS Lambda 函数。重新注册根组织单位（OU）。","D":"在组织中的每个 AWS 账户中配置可由 AWS Lambda 函数承担的 AWSControlTowerExecution IAM 角色。配置 Lambda 函数以承担 AWSControlTowerExecution IAM 角色。","E":"在 AWS 控制塔管理账户中创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数可以承担的 IAM 角色。授予该 IAM 角色在组织内 任何账户中承担 AWSControlTowerExecution IAM 角色的权限。配置 Lambda 函数使用新创建的 IAM 角 色。","F":"在 AWS 控制塔管理账户中配置 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以便在 AWS 账户更新或注册到 AWS 控制 塔时，或者在着陆区更新时调用 AWS Lambda 函数。重新注册组织中的每个 Organizations 组织单元。"},"answer":["C","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["D","E","F"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"This scenario maps exactly to the AWS-documented solution in the blog 'Customize AWS Config resource tracking in AWS Control Tower environment', which AWS Prescriptive Guidance (designing-control-tower-landing-zone/config-mgmt) explicitly references as the supported, drift-free way to customize the Control Tower-managed AWS Config configuration recorder in every enrolled account. In that architecture a Lambda function runs in the AWS Control Tower management account and assumes the AWSControlTowerExecution IAM role that exists in each enrolled account to modify that account's Config recorder. The AWSControlTowerExecution role doc states the role 'must be present in all enrolled accounts' and is designed to 'create and enroll accounts, automatically, with scripts and Lambda functions' (option D, the target/assumed side). The Lambda also needs an execution role in the management account that is granted permission to assume AWSControlTowerExecution in any account (option E, the source side); D and E together form the complete cross-account assume-role chain. To apply the customization to both existing and future accounts, an EventBridge rule in the management account must invoke the Lambda. The blog states the rule 'initiates the Producer Lambda function on events like UpdateLandingZone, CreateManagedAccount, and UpdateManagedAccount' - which is precisely option F's wording ('when an AWS account is updated or enrolled... or when the landing zone is updated'). The lifecycle-events doc confirms enrolling or creating an account fires CreateManagedAccount/UpdateManagedAccount (not RegisterOrganizationalUnit), so option F is the only trigger that catches a NEW account later enrolled via Account Factory into an already-registered OU. Option C fires only on OU register/re-register and re-registers just the root OU, so it never fires for an individual future account enrollment and fails the requirement. Therefore the correct combination is D, E, F, and the dump's [C, D, E] is wrong on the trigger leg.","explanation_zh":"此情境正好對應 AWS 官方記載的解法，即部落格 'Customize AWS Config resource tracking in AWS Control Tower environment'；AWS Prescriptive Guidance（designing-control-tower-landing-zone/config-mgmt）明確將其引用為在每個 enrolled 帳戶中客製化 AWS Control Tower 管理的 AWS Config configuration recorder、且不造成 drift 的支援作法。該架構中，Lambda 在 AWS Control Tower management account 執行，並去 assume 每個 enrolled 帳戶內既有的 AWSControlTowerExecution IAM role 來修改該帳戶的 Config recorder。AWSControlTowerExecution role 文件指出此 role『必須存在於所有 enrolled 帳戶』，並明確設計給『以 script 與 Lambda function 自動建立與 enroll 帳戶』使用（選項 D，被 assume 的目標側）。Lambda 還需要一個位於 management account 的執行 role，被授權可 assume 任一帳戶的 AWSControlTowerExecution role（選項 E，來源側）；D 與 E 合起來構成完整的跨帳戶 assume-role 鏈。要同時套用到既有與未來帳戶，需在 management account 設定 EventBridge rule 觸發 Lambda。部落格明載該 rule『在 UpdateLandingZone、CreateManagedAccount、UpdateManagedAccount 等事件時 initiate Producer Lambda function』，這正是選項 F 的描述（『當 AWS 帳戶被更新或 enrolled… 或 landing zone 被更新時』）。lifecycle-events 文件確認 enroll 或建立帳戶會觸發 CreateManagedAccount/UpdateManagedAccount（而非 RegisterOrganizationalUnit），因此 F 是唯一能捕捉日後經 Account Factory enroll 進已 register OU 的新帳戶的觸發器。選項 C 只在 OU register/re-register 時觸發並只重新 register root OU，當有個別未來帳戶 enroll 時並不會觸發，無法滿足需求。所以正確組合為 D、E、F，dump 的 [C, D, E] 在觸發器這一項是錯的。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A brand-new account whose Lambda 'directly' applies changes to every account has no trust path into member accounts and ignores the AWSControlTowerExecution role; the documented mechanism runs the Lambda in the management account and assumes AWSControlTowerExecution, not in an arbitrary new account.","why_zh":"全新帳戶的 Lambda 要『直接』變更每個帳戶並無進入成員帳戶的信任路徑，且忽略了 AWSControlTowerExecution role；官方機制是 Lambda 在 management account 執行並 assume AWSControlTowerExecution，而非在任意新帳戶。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A Config delegated administrator Lambda that customizes the recorder only in the delegated administrator account fails the requirement to customize the recorder in EACH account; scope is far too narrow and is not how the Control Tower-managed recorders are reached.","why_zh":"Config delegated administrator 帳戶的 Lambda 只變更該帳戶本身的 recorder，無法滿足『每個帳戶』都要客製化的需求，範圍太窄，也不是觸及 Control Tower 管理 recorder 的方式。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Triggering only on OU register/re-register and re-registering just the root OU does not fire when a single new account is later enrolled into an already-registered OU via Account Factory - that enrollment fires CreateManagedAccount/UpdateManagedAccount, not RegisterOrganizationalUnit - so it misses future account enrollments. Option F covers both existing and future accounts.","why_zh":"僅在 OU register/re-register 時觸發並只重新 register root OU，當日後有個別新帳戶經 Account Factory enroll 進已 register 的 OU（觸發的是 CreateManagedAccount/UpdateManagedAccount 而非 RegisterOrganizationalUnit）時不會觸發，因此漏掉未來的帳戶 enrollment。選項 F 同時涵蓋既有與未來帳戶。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/designing-control-tower-landing-zone/config-mgmt.html","https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/mt/customize-aws-config-resource-tracking-in-aws-control-tower-environment/","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/awscontroltowerexecution.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/lifecycle-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-controltower.html"]}},{"id":335,"question_en":"A company runs an application in an Auto Scaling group of Amazon EC2 instances behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). The EC2 instances run Docker containers that make requests to a MySQL database that runs on separate EC2 instances. A DevOps engineer needs to update the application to use a serverless architecture. Which solution will meet this requirement with the FEWEST changes?","question_zh":"一家公司在应用负载均衡器（ALB）后面的亚马逊 EC2 实例的自动扩展组中运行一个应用程序。这些 EC2 实例运行的 Docker 容器会向运行在单独的 EC2 实例上的 MySQL 数据库发出请求。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要更新应用程序以采用无服务器架构。 哪种解决方案只需做最少的改动就能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Replace the containers that run on EC2 instances and the ALB with AWS Lambda functions. Replace the MySQL database with an Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 database that is compatible with MySQL.","B":"Replace the containers that run on EC2 instances with AWS Fargate. Replace the MySQL database with an Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 database that is compatible with MySQL.","C":"Replace the containers that run on EC2 instances and the ALB with AWS Lambda functions. Replace the MySQL database with Amazon DynamoDB tables.","D":"Replace the containers that run on EC2 instances with AWS Fargate. Replace the MySQL database with Amazon DynamoDB tables."},"options_zh":{"A":"用 AWS Lambda 函数替换在 EC2 实例上运行的容器和应用负载均衡器（ALB）。用与 MySQL 兼容的 Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 数据库替换 MySQL 数据库。","B":"将在 EC2 实例上运行的容器替换为 AWS Fargate。将 MySQL 数据库替换为与 MySQL 兼容的 Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 数据库。","C":"用 AWS Lambda 函数替换在 EC2 实例上运行的容器和应用负载均衡器（ALB）。用 Amazon DynamoDB 表替换 MySQL 数据库。","D":"将在 EC2 实例上运行的容器替换为 AWS Fargate。将 MySQL 数据库替换为 Amazon DynamoDB 表。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Database","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is a fully serverless architecture achieved with the FEWEST changes. Two workload components must become serverless: (1) the Docker containers on EC2 and (2) the self-managed MySQL database on EC2. AWS Fargate is a serverless compute engine for containers that runs your existing containers 'without having to manage servers or clusters of Amazon EC2 instances' and supports 'any language that can run in a container,' so the existing Docker images move over with little or no code change, and the ALB can remain in front of the ECS/Fargate service via service load balancing. Amazon Aurora Serverless v2 that is compatible with MySQL is a serverless, auto-scaling, MySQL-compatible engine, so it is effectively a drop-in replacement for the self-managed MySQL database (typically only a connection-string change), not a data-layer rewrite. By contrast, moving the containers to AWS Lambda (A, C) forces an event-driven, stateless re-architecture (Lambda is 'stateless by design' with a 15-minute execution limit) and removal/replacement of the ALB, and replacing MySQL with Amazon DynamoDB (C, D) is a relational-to-NoSQL migration that requires schema redesign and rewriting all data-access and query logic. Therefore Option B reaches serverless with the smallest amount of change.","explanation_zh":"需求是以「最少變更」達成完全 serverless 架構。需要 serverless 化的兩個元件是 (1) 在 EC2 上執行的 Docker 容器，以及 (2) 在 EC2 上自行管理的 MySQL 資料庫。AWS Fargate 是容器的 serverless 運算引擎，能在「無須管理伺服器或 Amazon EC2 叢集」的情況下執行現有容器，並支援「任何能在容器中執行的語言」，因此現有的 Docker 映像幾乎不需修改程式碼即可移轉，且 ALB 可透過 ECS/Fargate 的 service load balancing 繼續放在服務前端。Amazon Aurora Serverless v2（相容 MySQL）是 serverless、自動擴展且相容 MySQL 的引擎，因此基本上是可直接替換自行管理 MySQL 的方案（通常只需變更連線字串），而非重寫資料層。相對地，將容器改為 AWS Lambda（A、C）會迫使改成事件驅動、無狀態的重新架構（Lambda「本質上是無狀態」且有 15 分鐘執行上限）並移除/替換 ALB；而將 MySQL 改為 Amazon DynamoDB（C、D）是關聯式轉 NoSQL 的遷移，需重新設計結構並重寫所有資料存取與查詢邏輯。因此選項 B 以最小變更達成 serverless。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Replacing the containers and the ALB with Lambda functions requires re-architecting the application into an event-driven, stateless model (Lambda is stateless by design with a 15-minute limit) and removing the ALB. That is far more change than simply moving the same containers onto Fargate. The Aurora Serverless v2 part is fine, but the compute change is excessive.","why_zh":"以 Lambda 取代容器與 ALB 需把應用重構為事件驅動、無狀態模型（Lambda 本質無狀態且有 15 分鐘上限）並移除 ALB，遠比直接把相同容器移到 Fargate 變更更大。Aurora Serverless v2 部分沒問題，但運算層改動過多。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Combines two large rewrites: a Lambda event-driven re-architecture (plus ALB removal) and a MySQL-to-DynamoDB NoSQL migration that requires schema redesign and rewriting all queries. This is the most invasive option, not the fewest changes.","why_zh":"同時包含兩項大改寫：Lambda 事件驅動重新架構（並移除 ALB）以及 MySQL 轉 DynamoDB 的 NoSQL 遷移（需重新設計結構並重寫所有查詢）。這是侵入性最高的選項，並非最少變更。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Using Fargate for the containers is correct and minimal, but replacing MySQL with DynamoDB forces a relational-to-NoSQL migration: schema redesign and rewriting all data-access and query code. Aurora Serverless v2 MySQL-compatible (Option B) is a near drop-in replacement, so D involves more changes than B.","why_zh":"用 Fargate 取代容器是正確且變更最小，但把 MySQL 換成 DynamoDB 會迫使關聯式轉 NoSQL 遷移：需重新設計結構並重寫所有資料存取與查詢程式碼。Aurora Serverless v2（相容 MySQL，選項 B）近乎可直接替換，因此 D 的變更比 B 多。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/decision-guides/latest/fargate-or-lambda/fargate-or-lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/AWS_Fargate.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/aurora-serverless-v2.html"]}},{"id":336,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage 10 AWS accounts. All features are enabled, and trusted access for AWS CloudFormation is enabled. A DevOps engineer needs to use CloudFormation to deploy an IAM role to the Organizations management account and all member accounts in the organization. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织中的一个组织来管理 10 个 AWS 账户。所有功能均已启用，并且已为 AWS CloudFormation 启用受信任访问。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要使用 CloudFormation 将一个 IAM 角色部署到组织管理账户以及该组织中的所有成 员账户。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudFormation StackSet that has service-managed permissions. Set the root OU as a deployment target.","B":"Create a CloudFormation StackSet that has service-managed permissions. Set the root OU as a deployment target. Deploy a separate CloudFormation stack in the Organizations management account.","C":"Create a CloudFormation StackSet that has self-managed permissions. Set the root OU as a deployment target.","D":"Create a CloudFormation StackSet that has self-managed permissions. Set the root OU as a deployment target. Deploy a separate CloudFormation stack in the Organizations management account."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个具有服务管理权限的 CloudFormation 栈集。将根组织单位设置为部署目标。","B":"创建一个具有服务管理权限的 CloudFormation 栈集。将根组织单元设置为部署目标。在 Organizations 管理账户中部署单独的 CloudFormation 栈。","C":"创建一个具有自管理权限的 CloudFormation 栈集。将根组织单位设置为部署目标。","D":"创建一个具有自管理权限的 CloudFormation 栈集。将根组织单位设置为部署目标。在 Organizations 管理账户中部署单独的 CloudFormation 栈。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The role must reach BOTH the management account AND all member accounts with the least operational overhead. With service-managed permissions you can target the root OU, which automatically includes all child OUs and member accounts, and CloudFormation creates the execution roles for you instead of you provisioning them per account. However, the service-managed StackSets Considerations explicitly state: 'CloudFormation doesn't deploy stacks to the management account, even if that account is part of your organization or belongs to an organizational unit (OU).' So a root-OU StackSet covers every member account but skips the management account. To also deploy the IAM role to the management account, you add one separate CloudFormation stack in the management account, which is exactly Option B. Option A leaves the management account without the role. Options C and D are technically invalid because self-managed permissions deploy to explicit account IDs (accounts where you can create an IAM role), not to OUs, so you cannot 'set the root OU as a deployment target' with that model.","explanation_zh":"此題要求以最少維運負擔將 IAM role 同時部署到 management account 與所有 member accounts。採用 service-managed permissions 的 StackSet 可將 root OU 設為部署目標，root OU 會自動包含所有子 OU 與 member accounts，且 CloudFormation 會代為建立執行用的 IAM roles，無需逐一帳戶手動建立。不過官方 service-managed StackSets 的 Considerations 明確指出：「CloudFormation doesn't deploy stacks to the management account, even if that account is part of your organization or belongs to an organizational unit (OU).」因此 root OU 的 StackSet 雖能涵蓋所有 member accounts，卻會略過 management account。要同時覆蓋 management account，只需在 management account 另外部署一個獨立的 CloudFormation stack，這正是選項 B。選項 A 會讓 management account 缺少該 role；選項 C 與 D 在技術上無效，因為 self-managed permissions 只能針對明確的 account IDs（可建立 IAM role 的帳戶）部署，無法將 root OU 設為部署目標。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A service-managed StackSet targeting the root OU deploys to all member accounts but, per the official Considerations, never deploys to the management account. The requirement explicitly includes the management account, so this leaves the role missing there.","why_zh":"以 root OU 為目標的 service-managed StackSet 雖會部署到所有 member accounts，但依官方 Considerations 永遠不會部署到 management account。題目明確要求涵蓋 management account，故此選項會讓 management account 缺少該 role。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Self-managed permissions deploy to explicit account IDs (accounts where you can create an IAM role), not to OUs. OU/root-OU targeting is a service-managed-only capability, so you cannot 'set the root OU as a deployment target' with self-managed permissions, making this option technically invalid; it would also still miss the management account.","why_zh":"Self-managed permissions 只能針對明確的 account IDs（可建立 IAM role 的帳戶）部署，無法針對 OU。以 OU／root OU 為目標是 service-managed 專屬功能，因此 self-managed 無法『將 root OU 設為部署目標』，此選項技術上無效，且仍會遺漏 management account。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as C: self-managed permissions cannot target the root OU; OU targeting requires service-managed permissions. Adding a separate management-account stack doesn't fix the invalid OU-targeting step, and self-managed also forces you to provision administration/execution IAM roles in every account, increasing overhead.","why_zh":"與 C 相同的致命缺陷：self-managed permissions 無法以 root OU 為目標，OU 目標需要 service-managed。即使再額外部署 management account 的 stack 也無法修正無效的 OU 目標步驟，且 self-managed 還需在每個帳戶建立 administration/execution IAM roles，反而增加負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-getting-started-create-self-managed.html"]}},{"id":337,"question_en":"A company runs an application that stores artifacts in an Amazon S3 bucket. The application has a large user base. The application writes a high volume of objects to the S3 bucket. The company has enabled event notifications for the S3 bucket. When the application writes an object to the S3 bucket, several processing tasks need to be performed simultaneously. The company's DevOps team needs to create an AWS Step Functions workflow to orchestrate the processing tasks. Which combination of steps should the DevOps team take to meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司运行着一个应用程序，该程序将工件存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中。该应用程序拥有庞大的 用户群。该应用程序向 S3 存储桶写入大量对象。该公司已为该 S3 存储桶启用了事件通知功能。 当应用程序将对象写入 S3 存储桶时，需要同时执行多个处理任务。公司的 DevOps 团队需要创建 一个 AWS Step Functions 工作流来协调这些处理任务。 DevOps 团队应采取哪两种步骤组合才能以最低的运营开销满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a Standard workflow that contains a parallel state that defines the processing tasks. Create an Asynchronous Express workflow that contains a parallel state that defines the processing tasks.","B":"Create a Synchronous Express workflow that contains a map state that defines the processing tasks.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match when a new S3 object is created. Configure the EventBridge rule to invoke an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to start the processing workflow.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match when a new S3 object is created. Configure the EventBridge rule to start the processing workflow."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个标准工作流，其中包含一个并行状态，用于定义处理任务。创建一个异步快速工作流， 其中包含一个并行状态，用于定义处理任务。","B":"创建一个包含定义处理任务的映射状态的同步 Express 工作流。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于匹配新 S3 对象创建的事件。配置 EventBridge 规则 以调用 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数以启动处理工作流。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，用于匹配新 S3 对象创建的事件。配置 EventBridge 规则以启动处理工作流。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two independent decisions are being tested: how to trigger the workflow from the S3 event, and which construct runs several tasks simultaneously. For the trigger (D), AWS Step Functions is a native EventBridge target, so an EventBridge rule that matches the S3 'Object Created' event (S3 EventBridge notifications are already enabled) can start the state machine execution directly. The official tutorial 'Starting a Step Functions workflow in response to events' walks through exactly this: enable S3 EventBridge notifications, create an EventBridge rule on the S3 Object Created event, and select the Step Functions state machine as the target. For the construct (A), the Parallel state adds separate branches of execution that Step Functions runs as concurrently as possible, which matches 'several processing tasks need to be performed simultaneously.' Option C inserts an unnecessary Lambda function between EventBridge and Step Functions, adding code and IAM to build, secure, and maintain (more overhead). Option B uses a Map state, which runs the same set of steps for each item in a dataset (data-driven fan-out) rather than several distinct named tasks, and Synchronous Express blocks for a result that an asynchronous EventBridge trigger never consumes. Therefore A + D meet the requirement with the least operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"本題考兩個獨立決策：如何由 S3 事件觸發工作流程，以及用哪種構造同時執行多個任務。觸發方式（D）：AWS Step Functions 本身就是 EventBridge 的原生目標，因此 EventBridge 規則只要比對 S3 'Object Created' 事件（S3 已啟用 EventBridge 通知），即可直接啟動 state machine 執行。官方教學 'Starting a Step Functions workflow in response to events' 正是此情境：在 S3 啟用 EventBridge 通知、針對 S3 Object Created 事件建立 EventBridge 規則，並選擇 Step Functions state machine 作為目標。構造（A）：Parallel state 會加入多個獨立的執行分支，Step Functions 會盡可能同時執行，符合「多個處理任務需同時執行」。選項 C 在 EventBridge 與 Step Functions 之間多插入一個不必要的 Lambda，需額外建置與維護程式碼及 IAM 權限，營運負擔較高。選項 B 使用 Map state，是針對資料集中的每個項目執行相同步驟（資料驅動的 fan-out），而非多個彼此不同的具名任務；且 Synchronous Express 會阻塞等待回傳結果，但非同步的 EventBridge 觸發根本不會接收該結果。因此 A 加 D 以最少營運負擔滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A Map state runs the same set of workflow steps for each item in a dataset (data-driven, dynamic fan-out over an array or S3 source), not a fixed set of several distinct processing tasks; the Parallel state is the correct construct for running several named tasks simultaneously. Additionally, a Synchronous Express workflow blocks the caller and returns the result, but EventBridge starts executions asynchronously with no caller waiting on output, so Synchronous mode is the wrong fit for an EventBridge-triggered workflow.","why_zh":"Map state 是針對資料集中的每個項目執行相同的工作步驟（針對陣列或 S3 來源的資料驅動動態 fan-out），而非一組固定且彼此不同的處理任務；要同時執行多個具名任務應使用 Parallel state。此外 Synchronous Express 會讓呼叫端阻塞並回傳結果，但 EventBridge 是非同步啟動執行、沒有呼叫端等待輸出，因此同步模式不適合由 EventBridge 觸發的工作流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Inserting a Lambda function between EventBridge and Step Functions is unnecessary because Step Functions is a native EventBridge target that can start an execution directly. The extra Lambda adds code plus IAM/permissions to build, secure, and maintain, which is MORE operational overhead than letting the EventBridge rule start the workflow directly (option D).","why_zh":"在 EventBridge 與 Step Functions 之間插入 Lambda 是多餘的，因為 Step Functions 本身就是 EventBridge 的原生目標，可直接啟動執行。多出的 Lambda 需額外建置程式碼與 IAM 權限並加以維護，營運負擔比讓 EventBridge 規則直接啟動工作流程（選項 D）更高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/tutorial-cloudwatch-events-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/statemachine-starting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/state-parallel.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/state-map.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/step-functions/latest/dg/choosing-workflow-type.html"]}},{"id":338,"question_en":"A DevOps team supports an application that runs in an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Currently, the DevOps team uses AWS CodeDeploy to deploy the application by using a blue/green all-at-once strategy. Recently, the DevOps team had to roll back a deployment when a new version of the application dramatically increased response times for requests. The DevOps team needs use to a deployment strategy that will allow the team to monitor a new version of the application before the team shifts all traffic to the new version. If a new version of the application increases response times, the deployment should be rolled back as quickly as possible. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队支持一个在 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）集群中运行的应用程 序，该集群位于一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。目前，该 DevOps 团队使用 AWS CodeDeploy 通过蓝绿全量部署策略来部署应用程序。最近，由于应用程序的新版本大幅增加了请求的响应时间， DevOps 团队不得不回滚部署。 DevOps 团队需要采用一种部署策略，以便在将所有流量切换到新版本之前，能够对新版本的应用 程序进行监控。如果新版本的应用程序增加了响应时间，应尽快回滚部署。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Modify the CodeDeploy deployment to use the CodeDeployDefault.ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes configuration.","B":"Modify the CodeDeploy deployment to use the CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes configuration.","C":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to monitor the UnHealthyHostCount metric for the ALB. Set the alarm to activate if the metric is higher than the desired value. Associate the alarm with the CodeDeploy deployment group. Modify the deployment group to roll back when a deployment fails.","D":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to monitor the TargetResponseTime metric for the ALB. Set the alarm to activate if the metric is higher than the desired value. Associate the alarm with the CodeDeploy deployment group. Modify the deployment group to roll back when alarm thresholds are met.","E":"Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm to monitor the TargetConnectionErrorCount metric for the ALB. Set the alarm to activate if the metric is higher than the desired value. Associate the alarm with the CodeDeploy deployment group. Modify the deployment group to roll back when alarm thresholds are met."},"options_zh":{"A":"将 CodeDeploy 部署修改为使用 CodeDeployDefault.ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes 配置。","B":"将 CodeDeploy 部署修改为使用 CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes 配置。","C":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控 ALB 的 UnHealthyHostCount 指标。将警报设置为在该 指标高于期望值时触发。将警报与 CodeDeploy 部署组关联。修改部署组，使其在部署失败时 回滚。","D":"创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控 ALB 的 TargetResponseTime 指标。将警报设置为在该 指标高于期望值时触发。将警报与 CodeDeploy 部署组相关联。修改部署组，使其在达到警报 阈值时回滚。","E":"为应用负载均衡器（ALB）的 TargetConnectionErrorCount 指标创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 警 报。将警报设置为当该指标高于期望值时触发。将警报与 CodeDeploy 部署组关联。修改部署 组，使其在达到警报阈值时回滚。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements must be met: (1) monitor the new version with a small slice of traffic before shifting all traffic, and (2) automatically roll back fast if response times rise. Option A (CodeDeployDefault.ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes) is a predefined Amazon ECS deployment configuration that 'shifts 10 percent of traffic in the first increment' and deploys 'the remaining 90 percent five minutes later.' That single 10% bake window is exactly the 'monitor before shifting all traffic' pattern, and because only 10% of users are exposed during the window, an alarm-triggered rollback has the smallest blast radius and is the fastest to recover from. Option D is the correct alarm because the reported problem is increased response times, and per the ALB CloudWatch metrics docs TargetResponseTime is 'the time elapsed, in seconds, after the request leaves the load balancer until the target starts to send the response headers' the metric that directly measures request latency. D also uses the correct rollback trigger: CodeDeploy docs state a deployment group can be configured to automatically roll back 'when a monitoring threshold you specify is met,' and a deployment stops/rolls back whenever any associated CloudWatch alarm is activated (enters ALARM). The combination A+D detects the latency regression while only 10% of traffic is shifted and rolls back immediately.","explanation_zh":"需同時滿足兩個條件:(1) 在把全部流量切過去之前,先用一小部分流量監控新版本;(2) 若回應時間上升,要能快速自動回滾。選項 A (CodeDeployDefault.ECSCanary10Percent5Minutes) 是 Amazon ECS 的預定義 deployment configuration,『在第一階段切 10% 流量』,並在『5 分鐘後再切剩下的 90%』。這個 10% 的觀察視窗正是『在切換全部流量前先監控』的 canary 模式;因為視窗期間只有 10% 使用者受影響,由警示觸發的回滾影響範圍最小、復原最快。選項 D 是正確的警示,因為問題是回應時間增加;根據 ALB CloudWatch metrics 文件,TargetResponseTime 是『請求離開負載平衡器後,直到目標開始送出回應標頭所經過的秒數』,正是直接量測請求延遲的指標。D 也使用正確的回滾觸發方式:CodeDeploy 文件說明 deployment group 可設定『當所指定的監控閾值達到時』自動回滾,且只要任一所關聯的 CloudWatch 警示被觸發(進入 ALARM),部署就會停止/回滾。A+D 的組合能在僅切 10% 流量時就偵測到延遲退化並立即回滾。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes continuously shifts 10% every 3 minutes until all traffic is shifted, so traffic keeps moving in steps rather than holding at a small percentage to 'monitor before shifting all traffic.' The canary configuration's dedicated 10% bake window matches the requirement more precisely and exposes fewer users during evaluation, so A is preferred over B.","why_zh":"CodeDeployDefault.ECSLinear10PercentEvery3Minutes 每 3 分鐘持續切 10% 直到全部切完,流量是逐步不斷移動,而非保留在小比例『先監控再切全部流量』。canary 設定專屬的 10% 觀察視窗更精準符合需求,評估期間影響的使用者也更少,故 A 優於 B。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Doubly wrong. UnHealthyHostCount measures targets failing ALB health checks, not response latency; a version that responds slowly but still passes health checks would not change this metric, so it misses the latency regression. It also uses the trigger 'roll back when a deployment fails,' which only fires on deployment failure, not on a CloudWatch alarm state, so the alarm would not drive the rollback.","why_zh":"雙重錯誤。UnHealthyHostCount 量測的是未通過 ALB 健康檢查的目標數,而非回應延遲;回應變慢但仍通過健康檢查的版本不會改變此指標,因此會漏掉延遲退化。它還用『當部署失敗時回滾』的觸發方式,只在部署失敗時觸發,而非在 CloudWatch 警示狀態時觸發,因此警示無法驅動回滾。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"TargetConnectionErrorCount counts TCP connections that were not successfully established between the load balancer and the target, not request latency. A version that responds slowly but still accepts connections would not increase this metric, so it fails to detect the increased response times described in the scenario.","why_zh":"TargetConnectionErrorCount 計算的是負載平衡器與目標之間未能成功建立的 TCP 連線數,而非請求延遲。新版本若回應變慢但仍能接受連線,此指標不會上升,因此無法偵測情境中描述的回應時間增加。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/monitoring-create-alarms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployments-rollback-and-redeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-cloudwatch-metrics.html"]}},{"id":339,"question_en":"A security team must record the configuration of AWS resources, detect issues, and send notifications for findings. The main workload in the AWS account consists of an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group that scales in and out several times during the day. The team wants to be notified within 2 days if any Amazon EC2 security group allows traffic on port 22 for 0.0.0.0/0. The team also needs a snapshot of the configuration of the AWS resources to be taken routinely. The security team has already created and subscribed to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Which solution meets these requirements?","question_zh":"安全团队必须记录 AWS 资源的配置，检测问题，并为发现的情况发送通知。AWS 账户中的主要工 作负载由一个 Amazon EC2 自动扩展组构成，该组在一天内会进行多次扩展和收缩。 如果任何亚马逊 EC2 安全组允许 0.0.0.0/0 在 22 端口进行通信，团队希望在 2 天内得到通知。团队还 需要定期对 AWS 资源的配置进行快照。 安全团队已经创建并订阅了一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。 哪种解决方案符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS Config to use periodic recording for the AWS account. Deploy the vpc-sg-port- restriction-check AWS Config managed rule. Configure AWS Config to use the SNS topic as the target for notifications.","B":"Configure AWS Config to use configuration change recording for the AWS account. Deploy the vpc-sg- open-only-to-authorized-ports AWS Config managed rule. Configure AWS Config to use the SNS topic as the target for notifications.","C":"Configure AWS Config to use configuration change recording for the AWS account. Deploy the ssh- restricted AWS Config managed rule. Configure AWS Config to use the SNS topic as the target for notifications.","D":"Create an AWS Lambda function to evaluate security groups and publish a message to the SNS topic. Use an Amazon EventBridge rule to schedule the Lambda function to run once a day."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 AWS Config 以使用周期性记录方式记录 AWS 账户。部署 vpc-sg-portrestriction-check AWS Config 管理规则。配置 AWS Config 以使用 SNS 主题作为通知目标。","B":"配置 AWS Config 以使用配置更改记录功能记录 AWS 账户的配置更改。部署 vpc-sgopen-only-to- authorized-ports AWS Config 管理规则。配置 AWS Config 以将 SNS 主题用作通知的目标。","C":"配置 AWS Config 以对 AWS 账户使用配置更改记录功能。部署 sshrestricted AWS Config 管理规则。 配置 AWS Config 以将 SNS 主题用作通知目标。","D":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来评估安全组并向 SNS 主题发布消息。使用 Amazon EventBridge 规则安 排该 Lambda 函数每天运行一次。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Both restricted-ssh (C) and vpc-sg-port-restriction-check (A) technically detect a security group that allows port 22 from 0.0.0.0/0, and both can route compliance notifications to the existing SNS topic, so the rule choice alone does not decide the question. The deciding factor is the recording frequency, which the scenario frames with three converging clues: (1) an Auto Scaling group that scales in and out several times a day - AWS docs verbatim classify AWS Auto Scaling as an ephemeral workload that drives up Config recording and evaluation activity; (2) a generous 'within 2 days' window, so real-time detection (continuous recording's main benefit) is unnecessary; and (3) a 'routine snapshot' of configuration, which maps directly to periodic/daily recording that delivers a daily configuration item representing the most recent state. These clues point to periodic (daily) recording, which eliminates B and C because both specify configuration change (continuous) recording. Option A pairs periodic recording with vpc-sg-port-restriction-check, a Periodic-trigger managed rule that by default flags security groups allowing 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 on TCP/UDP ports 22/3389, making it the internally consistent design.","explanation_zh":"restricted-ssh（C）與 vpc-sg-port-restriction-check（A）在技術上都能偵測允許 port 22 對 0.0.0.0/0 開放的 security group，且兩者都能將合規通知送往既有的 SNS topic，因此單看規則無法決定答案。決定性因素是 recording frequency，題目用三個一致的線索框定：（1）每天多次擴縮的 Auto Scaling group——AWS 文件原文將 AWS Auto Scaling 歸類為 ephemeral workload，會推升 Config 記錄與評估活動；（2）寬鬆的「2 天內」時限，因此不需要即時偵測（即 continuous recording 的主要優勢）；（3）需要「例行」組態快照，這直接對應 periodic/daily recording，每 24 小時提供一個代表最新狀態的 configuration item。這些線索指向 periodic（daily）recording，因而排除 B 與 C，因為兩者皆指定 configuration change（continuous）recording。選項 A 將 periodic recording 與 vpc-sg-port-restriction-check 搭配，後者為 Periodic 觸發的 managed rule，預設會標記允許 0.0.0.0/0 或 ::/0 經 TCP/UDP port 22/3389 進入的 security group，是內部一致的設計。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"vpc-sg-open-only-to-authorized-ports uses an allowlist (authorized-ports) model and only evaluates SGs already open to 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0; it does not directly target port 22 without parameter configuration. More importantly, it specifies configuration change (continuous) recording, which conflicts with the routine-snapshot and 2-day framing and with AWS's guidance to avoid continuous recording churn for ephemeral Auto Scaling workloads.","why_zh":"vpc-sg-open-only-to-authorized-ports 採用允許清單（authorized-ports）模型，且僅評估已對 0.0.0.0/0 或 ::/0 開放的 SG；未設定參數時無法直接針對 port 22。更重要的是，它指定 configuration change（continuous）recording，與例行快照及 2 天的框架相牴觸，也違背 AWS 對 ephemeral Auto Scaling 工作負載應避免 continuous recording 雜訊的建議。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer. restricted-ssh does correctly check incoming SSH (port 22) and flags 0.0.0.0/0 or ::/0 as NON_COMPLIANT, but the option specifies configuration change (continuous) recording. AWS classifies an Auto Scaling group that churns several times a day as an ephemeral workload and recommends avoiding the increased continuous-recording activity; the routine-snapshot requirement and generous 2-day window both signal periodic (daily) recording instead, making C an inconsistent design.","why_zh":"此為題庫建議答案。restricted-ssh 確實檢查進入的 SSH（port 22），並將 0.0.0.0/0 或 ::/0 標記為 NON_COMPLIANT，但此選項指定 configuration change（continuous）recording。AWS 將每天多次擴縮的 Auto Scaling group 歸類為 ephemeral workload，建議避免其增加的 continuous-recording 活動；例行快照需求與寬鬆的 2 天時限皆指向 periodic（daily）recording，使 C 成為不一致的設計。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A custom Lambda plus EventBridge schedule carries high operational overhead and, critically, does not record the configuration of AWS resources or provide a routine configuration snapshot. It bypasses AWS Config entirely, so it fails the explicit 'record the configuration of AWS resources' and 'routine snapshot' requirements.","why_zh":"自訂 Lambda 加 EventBridge 排程的運維負擔高，且關鍵在於它不會記錄 AWS 資源的組態，也不提供例行組態快照。它完全繞過 AWS Config，因此無法滿足題目明確要求的「記錄 AWS 資源組態」與「例行快照」。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/vpc-sg-port-restriction-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/restricted-ssh.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/vpc-sg-open-only-to-authorized-ports.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/select-resources.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/select-resources-console.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/managing-recorder_console-change-recording-frequency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/notifications-for-AWS-Config.html"]}},{"id":340,"question_en":"A company has proprietary data available by using an Amazon CloudFront distribution. The company needs to ensure that the distribution is accessible by only users from the corporate office that have a known set of IP address ranges. An AWS WAF web ACL is associated with the distribution and has a default action set to Count. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司通过使用亚马逊 CloudFront 分发服务可获取专有数据。该公司需要确保只有来自公司办公 室且具有已知 IP 地址范围的用户才能访问该分发服务。已将 AWS WAF 网络访问控制列表（web ACL）与该分发服务相关联，并将默认操作设置为计数。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new regex pattern set. Add the regex pattern set to a new rule group. Create a new web ACL that has a default action set to Block. Associate the web ACL with the CloudFront distribution. Add a rule that allows traffic based on the new rule group.","B":"Create an AWS WAF IP address set that matches the corporate office IP address range. Create a new web ACL that has a default action set to Allow. Associate the web ACL with the CloudFront distribution. Add a rule that allows traffic from the IP address set.","C":"Create a new regex pattern set. Add the regex pattern set to a new rule group. Set the default action on the existing web ACL to Allow. Add a rule that has priority 0 that allows traffic based on the regex pattern set.","D":"Create a WAF IP address set that matches the corporate office IP address range. Set the default action on the existing web ACL to Block. Add a rule that has priority 0 that allows traffic from the IP address set."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的正则表达式模式集。将该正则表达式模式集添加到新的规则组中。创建一个新的 Web ACL 并将其默认操作设置为“阻止”。将 Web ACL 与 CloudFront 分发关联。添加一条基于新规则 组允许流量的规则。","B":"创建一个与公司办公室 IP 地址范围匹配的 AWS WAF IP 地址集。创建一个新的 Web ACL 并将其默认 操作设置为允许。将 Web ACL 与 CloudFront 分发关联。添加一条允许来自该 IP 地址集的流量的规 则。","C":"创建一个新的正则表达式模式集。将该正则表达式模式集添加到新的规则组。将现有 Web ACL 的默认 操作设置为允许。添加一个优先级为 0 的规则，该规则基于正则表达式模式集允许流量。","D":"创建一个与公司办公室 IP 地址范围匹配的 WAF IP 地址集。将现有 Web ACL 的默认操作设置为阻止。 添加一个优先级为 0 的规则，允许来自该 IP 地址集的流量。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to allow access to the CloudFront distribution ONLY from a known set of corporate IP ranges, with the least operational overhead. The AWS WAF IP set match statement is the documented mechanism that 'inspects the IP address of a web request against a set of IP addresses and address ranges... to allow or block web requests based on the IP addresses that the requests originate from' and supports IPv4/IPv6 CIDR ranges. The AWS WAF default-action documentation describes this exact 'block by default, allow specific IPs' pattern: choose Block for the web ACL default action when you want to prevent most users but allow access to requests that originate from specified IP addresses, then add rules that identify and allow those specific requests. Because Allow is a terminating action, requests from the corporate IP set are immediately allowed while every other request falls through to the default Block. Option D achieves this by reusing the EXISTING web ACL (just flipping the default action from Count to Block and adding one priority-0 Allow rule referencing the IP set), giving the least operational overhead.","explanation_zh":"需求是「只允許」來自已知公司辦公室 IP 範圍的使用者存取 CloudFront distribution，且要求最少的營運負擔。AWS WAF 的 IP set match statement 是官方文件記載用來比對來源 IP 的機制：它會「比對 web 請求的 IP 位址與一組 IP 位址及位址範圍」，用以根據請求來源 IP 來 allow 或 block，並支援 IPv4/IPv6 CIDR 範圍。AWS WAF 的 default action 文件描述了這個「預設 Block、只放行特定 IP」的標準模式：當你想阻擋大多數使用者、但允許來自指定 IP 位址的請求時，將 web ACL 的 default action 設為 Block，再新增 rules 來識別並放行那些特定請求。由於 Allow 是 terminating action，符合公司 IP set 的請求會被立即放行，其餘所有請求則落到 default Block。Option D 重複使用「現有」的 web ACL（只把 default action 從 Count 改為 Block，並新增一條 priority-0 的 Allow rule 參照該 IP set），因此營運負擔最小。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A regex pattern set match statement inspects a string request component (query string, body, headers, cookies), not the source IP address, so it cannot match corporate CIDR ranges. It also needlessly creates a new rule group AND a brand-new web ACL that must be re-associated with the distribution, increasing operational overhead rather than reusing the existing web ACL.","why_zh":"regex pattern set match statement 檢查的是字串型的請求元件（query string、body、headers、cookies），而非來源 IP 位址，因此無法比對公司的 CIDR 範圍。它還多此一舉地建立新的 rule group 與全新的 web ACL 並需重新關聯到 distribution，反而增加營運負擔，而非重用既有的 web ACL。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Setting the web ACL default action to Allow means all non-matching (non-corporate) traffic is allowed through, which directly defeats the 'accessible by only corporate IPs' requirement. It also wastefully creates a new web ACL and re-associates it instead of reusing the existing one, adding operational overhead.","why_zh":"將 web ACL default action 設為 Allow，代表所有未命中（非公司）的流量都會被放行，這直接違反「只有公司 IP 才能存取」的需求。它還多此一舉地建立新的 web ACL 並重新關聯，而非重用既有者，徒增營運負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Like option A, it relies on a regex pattern set, which inspects string request components rather than source IP addresses, so it cannot match IP ranges. Even though it reuses the existing web ACL, setting the default to Allow combined with the wrong match type would let non-corporate traffic through, failing the requirement.","why_zh":"與 option A 相同，它依賴 regex pattern set，檢查的是字串型請求元件而非來源 IP，無法比對 IP 範圍。即使它重用既有 web ACL，把 default 設為 Allow 再加上錯誤的比對類型，仍會放行非公司流量，無法滿足需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-ipset-match.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/web-acl-default-action.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-action.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/waf-rule-statement-type-regex-pattern-set-match.html"]}},{"id":341,"question_en":"A company runs several applications in the same AWS account. The applications send logs to Amazon CloudWatch. A data analytics team needs to collect performance metrics and custom metrics from the applications. The analytics team needs to transform the metrics data before storing the data in an Amazon S3 bucket. The analytics team must automatically collect any new metrics that are added to the CloudWatch namespace. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司在同一个 AWS 账户中运行多个应用程序。这些应用程序将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch。 一个数据分析团队需要从应用程序中收集性能指标和自定义指标。该团队需要在将数据存储到 Amazon S3 存储桶之前对指标数据进行转换。该团队必须自动收集添加到 CloudWatch 命名空间中的任何新指标。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a CloudWatch metric stream to include metrics from the application and the CloudWatch namespace. Configure the metric stream to deliver the metrics to an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream. Configure the Firehose delivery stream to invoke an AWS Lambda function to transform the data. Configure the delivery stream to send the transformed data to the S3 bucket.","B":"Configure a CloudWatch metrics stream to include all the metrics and to deliver the metrics to an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream. Configure the Firehose delivery stream to invoke an AWS Lambda function to transform the data. Configure the delivery stream to send the transformed data to the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure metric filters for the CloudWatch logs to create custom metrics. Configure a CloudWatch metric stream to deliver the application metrics to the S3 bucket.","D":"Configure subscription filters on the application log groups to target an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream. Configure the Firehose delivery stream to invoke an AWS Lambda function to transform the data. Configure the delivery stream to send the transformed data to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置一个 CloudWatch 指标流，使其包含来自应用程序和 CloudWatch 命名空间的指标。将指标流配 置为将指标传递到 Amazon Data Firehose 交付流。将 Firehose 交付流配置为调用 AWS Lambda 函 数来转换数据。将交付流配置为将转换后的数据发送到 S3 存储桶。","B":"配置一个 CloudWatch 指标流，使其包含所有指标，并将这些指标传递给 Amazon Data Firehose 交付 流。配置 Firehose 交付流以调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数来转换数据。配置交付流以将转换后的数 据发送到 S3 存储桶。","C":"为 CloudWatch 日志配置指标筛选器以创建自定义指标。配置 CloudWatch 指标流将应用程序指标 传递到 S3 存储桶。","D":"在应用程序日志组上配置订阅筛选器，以指向 Amazon Data Firehose 交付流。配置 Firehose 交付流以 调用 AWS Lambda 函数来转换数据。配置交付流将转换后的数据发送到 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"官方文件判定需斟酌","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"medium","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to collect the applications' performance metrics and custom metrics that are already published to CloudWatch, transform the data before storing it in S3, and automatically include any new metric that appears in the namespace, all with the LEAST operational overhead. A CloudWatch metric stream is the native, fully managed way to continuously stream CloudWatch metrics to an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream, which can invoke an AWS Lambda function for data transformation before delivering records to S3 (satisfying transform + S3). The CloudWatch docs confirm a metric stream can stream all metrics or use include/exclude filters scoped to namespaces or specific metrics, and that 'after a metric stream is created, if new metrics are created that match the filters in place, the new metrics are automatically included in the stream' - so an include filter scoped to the application namespace auto-collects new metrics. Option A mirrors the requirement exactly: it includes the application/CloudWatch namespace via a metric stream and uses the standard Firehose-to-Lambda-to-S3 transform pipeline, collecting precisely the metrics 'from the applications' that the question asks for. This eliminates C (metric filters derive brand-new metrics from log events rather than collecting the metrics the apps already publish, and its stream step delivers straight to S3 with no transformation) and D (subscription filters stream raw log events, not metric data, so they never collect the required performance/custom metrics). Compared with B, which streams ALL metrics in the account (including every unrelated AWS service metric), Option A is correctly scoped to the application metrics the requirement specifies and still auto-includes new matching metrics, so it is the best fit.","explanation_zh":"需求是收集應用程式已發布到 CloudWatch 的效能指標與自訂指標、在存入 S3 前轉換資料、並自動納入命名空間中出現的任何新指標,且要以「最少維運開銷」達成。CloudWatch metric stream 是將 CloudWatch 指標持續串流到 Amazon Data Firehose 的原生、全託管方式,而 Firehose 可在送入 S3 前呼叫 AWS Lambda 函式進行資料轉換(滿足轉換 + S3)。CloudWatch 文件確認 metric stream 可串流所有指標或使用以命名空間/特定指標為範圍的 include/exclude filter,且「metric stream 建立後,若新建立的指標符合既有 filter,新指標會自動納入串流」,因此以應用程式命名空間為範圍的 include filter 能自動收集新指標。選項 A 完全對應需求:透過 metric stream 納入應用程式/CloudWatch 命名空間,並使用標準的 Firehose → Lambda → S3 轉換流程,正好收集題目所要求「來自應用程式」的指標。據此排除 C(metric filters 是從 log 事件衍生全新指標,而非收集應用程式已發布的指標,且其串流步驟直接送到 S3 而無轉換)與 D(subscription filters 串流的是原始 log 事件而非指標資料,根本沒有收集到所需的效能/自訂指標)。相較於 B 串流帳戶內「所有指標」(含各種不相關的 AWS 服務指標),選項 A 正確聚焦於需求指定的應用程式指標,同時仍能自動納入符合的新指標,因此是最佳解。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses the same valid metric-stream-to-Firehose-to-Lambda-to-S3 pipeline, but streams ALL metrics in the account, including every unrelated AWS service metric. The requirement explicitly asks to collect metrics 'from the applications', so streaming everything over-collects, increases metric-update cost, and pushes more irrelevant data through the transform Lambda. Option A's namespace-scoped include filter matches the requirement more precisely while still auto-including new matching metrics.","why_zh":"採用相同有效的 metric stream → Firehose → Lambda → S3 流程,但串流帳戶內「所有指標」,包含各種不相關的 AWS 服務指標。需求明確要求收集「來自應用程式」的指標,串流全部會過度收集、增加 metric update 成本,並讓轉換 Lambda 處理更多無關資料。選項 A 以命名空間為範圍的 include filter 更精準符合需求,同時仍能自動納入符合的新指標。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Metric filters create brand-new metrics FROM log events, duplicating the custom metrics the applications already publish rather than collecting them. The metric-stream step also delivers directly to S3 with no Lambda transformation, failing the requirement to transform data before storing it.","why_zh":"Metric filters 是從 log 事件「建立」全新指標,等於重做應用程式已發布的自訂指標而非收集它們。其 metric stream 步驟也直接送到 S3 而無 Lambda 轉換,未滿足存入前需轉換資料的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Subscription filters on log groups stream raw log events to Firehose, not metric data. The requirement is to collect performance metrics and custom metrics that already exist in CloudWatch as metrics, so a log-based subscription pipeline does not collect the required metrics at all.","why_zh":"Log group 上的 subscription filters 串流的是原始 log 事件而非指標資料。需求是收集已存在於 CloudWatch 的效能指標與自訂指標,因此以 log 為基礎的 subscription 流程根本沒有收集到所需的指標。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch-Metric-Streams.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch-metric-streams-setup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/firehose/latest/dev/data-transformation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html"]}},{"id":342,"question_en":"A company uses an HPC platform to run analysis jobs for data. The company uses AWS CodeBuild to create container images and store the images on Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR). The images are then deployed on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). To maintain compliance, the company needs to ensure that the images are signed before the images are deployed on Amazon EKS. The signing keys must be rotated periodically and must be managed automatically. The company needs to track who generates the signatures. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司使用高性能计算（HPC）平台来运行数据的分析任务。该公司使用 AWS CodeBuild 来创建容器 镜像，并将这些镜像存储在亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中。随后，这些镜像会被部署到亚 马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）上。 为保持合规性，公司需要确保在将图像部署到亚马逊 EKS 之前对其进行签名。签名密钥必须定期轮换， 并且必须自动管理。公司需要追踪谁生成了签名。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use CodeBuild to retrieve the image that was previously pushed to Amazon ECR. Use AWS Signer to sign the image. Use AWS CloudTrail to track who generates the signatures.","B":"Use AWS Lambda to retrieve the image that was previously pushed to Amazon ECR. Use a Lambda function to sign the image. Use Amazon CloudWatch to track who generates the signatures.","C":"Use AWS Lambda to retrieve the image that was previously pushed to Amazon ECR. Use AWS Signer to sign the image. Use Amazon CloudWatch to track who generates the signatures.","D":"Use CodeBuild to build the image. Sign the image by using AWS Signer before pushing the image to Amazon ECR. Use AWS CloudTrail to track who generates the signatures."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 CodeBuild 检索先前推送到 Amazon ECR 的镜像。使用 AWS Signer 对镜像进行签名。使用 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪谁生成了签名。","B":"使用 AWS Lambda 检索先前推送到 Amazon ECR 的镜像。使用 Lambda 函数对镜像进行签名。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 跟踪生成签名的人员。","C":"使用 AWS Lambda 检索先前推送到 Amazon ECR 的镜像。使用 AWS Signer 对镜像进行签名。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 跟踪生成签名的人员。","D":"使用 CodeBuild 构建镜像。在将镜像推送到 Amazon ECR 之前，使用 AWS Signer 对其进行签名。使 用 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪谁生成了签名。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"AWS Signer is a fully managed code-signing service that 'manages the code-signing certificate's public and private keys, and enables central management of the code-signing lifecycle' (satisfying automatic key management and rotation), and its 'integration with AWS CloudTrail helps you track who is generating code signatures and to meet your compliance requirements' (satisfying 'track who generates the signatures'). For container images, AWS Signer uses the Notation CLI to sign images that are ALREADY stored in an Amazon ECR private repository: Step 3 of the Signer image-signing guide signs the image by repository name and SHA256 digest, then 'creates the signature and pushes it to the same Amazon ECR private repository that the image being signed is in,' and the ECR manual-signing prerequisites explicitly require you to 'have a container image stored in an Amazon ECR private repository to sign.' Option A reuses the company's existing CodeBuild tooling to handle the already-pushed image, signs it with AWS Signer, and uses CloudTrail to identify the signer, meeting every requirement with the least operational effort because no new compute (Lambda) and no custom signing logic is introduced. The dump's suggested answer D is invalid because you cannot 'sign the image using AWS Signer before pushing it to Amazon ECR' - the Signer/Notation workflow signs by digest and pushes the signature alongside the image that must already exist in ECR.","explanation_zh":"AWS Signer 是一項完全受管的程式碼簽署服務，它「管理程式碼簽署憑證的公鑰與私鑰，並支援程式碼簽署生命週期的集中管理」（滿足金鑰自動管理與輪替的需求），而且其「與 AWS CloudTrail 的整合協助您追蹤是誰產生程式碼簽章並滿足合規需求」（滿足「追蹤誰產生簽章」的需求）。對於容器映像，AWS Signer 透過 Notation CLI 對「已經」儲存在 Amazon ECR 私有儲存庫中的映像進行簽署：Signer 映像簽署指南的步驟 3 以儲存庫名稱與 SHA256 摘要來簽署映像，然後「產生簽章並將其推送到與被簽署映像相同的 Amazon ECR 私有儲存庫」，而 ECR 手動簽署的先決條件也明確要求你必須「擁有一個已儲存在 Amazon ECR 私有儲存庫中、要簽署的容器映像」。選項 A 重複使用公司既有的 CodeBuild 工具處理已推送的映像，使用 AWS Signer 簽署，並以 CloudTrail 識別簽署者；因為不需引入新的運算資源（Lambda）也不需自訂簽署邏輯，以最少的營運工作量滿足所有需求。題庫建議的答案 D 不成立，因為無法「在將映像推送到 Amazon ECR 之前使用 AWS Signer 簽署映像」 - Signer/Notation 工作流程是以摘要進行簽署，並將簽章與必須已存在於 ECR 的映像一起推送。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Using a custom Lambda function to sign the image means managing your own signing keys, which fails the 'keys must be rotated periodically and managed automatically' requirement and adds operational overhead and custom code to maintain. Amazon CloudWatch (Events) only reports 'Signer Job Status Change' state events for automation; it does not identify which user or account generated the signature - that identity tracking is CloudTrail's role.","why_zh":"使用自訂 Lambda 函式簽署映像意味著要自行管理簽署金鑰，無法滿足「金鑰必須定期輪替且自動管理」的需求，並增加營運負擔與需維護的自訂程式碼。Amazon CloudWatch (Events) 僅回報「Signer Job Status Change」狀態事件以供自動化，無法識別是哪個使用者或帳戶產生了簽章 - 該身分追蹤是 CloudTrail 的職責。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Although it correctly uses AWS Signer (managed, automatically rotated keys), it uses Amazon CloudWatch to track who generates signatures. CloudWatch Events only reports signing-job status changes; it does not capture the caller's identity. The requirement to 'track who generates the signatures' is met by CloudTrail, which captures the API calls and identifies the users/accounts. Adding Lambda also increases operational effort versus reusing the existing CodeBuild tooling.","why_zh":"雖然正確地使用了 AWS Signer（受管且自動輪替的金鑰），但它使用 Amazon CloudWatch 來追蹤誰產生簽章。CloudWatch Events 僅回報簽署工作的狀態變更，無法擷取呼叫者的身分。「追蹤誰產生簽章」的需求應由 CloudTrail 滿足，它會擷取 API 呼叫並識別使用者/帳戶。此外，引入 Lambda 相較於重複使用既有的 CodeBuild 工具也增加了營運工作量。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is technically invalid. AWS Signer/Notation signs container images that already exist in an Amazon ECR repository - the signing step references the image by SHA256 digest and pushes the signature into the same ECR repo as the image, and the ECR manual-signing prerequisites require the image to already be stored in ECR. You therefore cannot 'sign the image using AWS Signer before pushing it to Amazon ECR.' The image must be built and pushed to ECR first, then signed. The CloudTrail portion is correct, but the sign-before-push sequence is impossible with the Signer container-image workflow.","why_zh":"這是題庫建議的答案，但技術上不成立。AWS Signer/Notation 簽署的是「已經」存在於 Amazon ECR 儲存庫中的容器映像 - 簽署步驟以 SHA256 摘要參照映像，並將簽章推送到與映像相同的 ECR 儲存庫，而 ECR 手動簽署的先決條件要求映像必須已儲存於 ECR 中。因此你無法「在將映像推送到 Amazon ECR 之前使用 AWS Signer 簽署映像」。映像必須先建置並推送到 ECR，然後才能簽署。CloudTrail 部分正確，但「推送前先簽署」的順序在 Signer 容器映像工作流程中是不可能的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/signer/latest/developerguide/Welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/signer/latest/developerguide/image-signing-steps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/signer/latest/developerguide/monitoring-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-signing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-signing-manual.html"]}},{"id":343,"question_en":"A company uses an AWS CodeArtifact repository to store Python packages that the company developed internally. A DevOps engineer needs to use AWS CodeDeploy to deploy an application to an Amazon EC2 instance. The application uses a Python package that is stored in the CodeArtifact repository. A BeforeInstall lifecycle event hook will install the package. The DevOps engineer needs to grant the EC2 instance access to the CodeArtifact repository. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库来存储其内部开发的 Python 包。一位 DevOps 工程师需要使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将应用程序部署到 Amazon EC2 实例上。该应用程序使用存储在 CodeArtifact 存储库中 的 Python 包。在部署过程中，BeforeInstall 生命周期事件钩子将安装该包。 DevOps 工程师需要授予 EC2 实例访问 CodeArtifact 存储库的权限。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a service-linked role for CodeArtifact. Associate the role with the EC2 instance. Use the aws codeartifact get-authorization-token CLI command on the instance.","B":"Configure a resource-based policy for the CodeArtifact repository that allows the ReadFromRepository action for the EC2 instance principal.","C":"Configure ACLs on the CodeArtifact repository to allow the EC2 instance to access the Python package.","D":"Create an instance profile that contains an IAM role that has access to CodeArtifact. Associate the instance profile with the EC2 instance. Use the aws codeartifact login CLI command on the instance."},"options_zh":{"A":"为 CodeArtifact 创建一个服务关联角色。将该角色与 EC2 实例相关联。在实例上使用 aws codeartifact get-authorization-token CLI 命令。","B":"为 CodeArtifact 存储库配置基于资源的策略，允许 EC2 实例主体执行“从存储库读取”操作。","C":"在 CodeArtifact 存储库上配置访问控制列表（ACL），以允许 EC2 实例访问 Python 包。","D":"创建一个包含有权访问 CodeArtifact 的 IAM 角色的实例配置文件。将实例配置文件与 EC2 实例相 关联。在实例上使用 aws codeartifact login CLI 命令。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"To consume a package from CodeArtifact, the client (pip) must authenticate with an authorization token obtained from the GetAuthorizationToken API. AWS docs state that calling GetAuthorizationToken requires both codeartifact:GetAuthorizationToken and sts:GetServiceBearerToken, and these must come from an identity-based (IAM role/user) policy attached to the calling principal. For an EC2 instance, you supply those credentials by creating an instance profile that contains an IAM role with CodeArtifact access and associating it with the instance. The aws codeartifact login command (pip is an explicitly supported tool) then fetches the token with GetAuthorizationToken and configures pip with the token and the correct repository endpoint in a single step, which is exactly what the BeforeInstall hook needs. Option D matches the AWS-documented pattern precisely.","explanation_zh":"要從 CodeArtifact 取用套件，用戶端（pip）必須使用透過 GetAuthorizationToken API 取得的授權權杖進行驗證。AWS 文件指出呼叫 GetAuthorizationToken 需要同時具備 codeartifact:GetAuthorizationToken 與 sts:GetServiceBearerToken，且這些權限必須來自附加在呼叫主體上的 identity-based（IAM 角色/使用者）政策。對 EC2 執行個體而言，提供這些憑證的方式是建立一個包含具 CodeArtifact 存取權 IAM 角色的 instance profile，並將其關聯到執行個體。接著 aws codeartifact login 指令（pip 是明確支援的工具）會以 GetAuthorizationToken 擷取權杖，並一步到位地將該權杖與正確的儲存庫端點設定到 pip，這正是 BeforeInstall hook 所需。選項 D 完全符合 AWS 文件記載的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A service-linked role is a special role that the CodeArtifact service itself assumes to act on your behalf; it is not something you associate with an EC2 instance to grant the instance repository access. EC2 instances receive credentials via an ordinary IAM role wrapped in an instance profile, not an SLR. Although get-authorization-token is a real command, the role construct in this option is incorrect.","why_zh":"service-linked role 是 CodeArtifact 服務本身代您執行動作時所擔任的特殊角色，並非用來關聯到 EC2 執行個體以授予儲存庫存取權。EC2 執行個體是透過包在 instance profile 中的一般 IAM 角色取得憑證，而非 SLR。雖然 get-authorization-token 是真實指令，但此選項的角色構造是錯誤的。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A repository resource-based policy with ReadFromRepository targets account/IAM principals (e.g., arn:...:root) and is primarily for cross-account download access; an 'EC2 instance principal' is not a valid principal type. It also gives the instance no AWS credentials of its own. Critically, AWS docs say sts:GetServiceBearerToken (required to call GetAuthorizationToken) has no effect when placed in a CodeArtifact resource policy and must be in the caller's identity-based policy, so a resource policy alone cannot let the instance authenticate.","why_zh":"含 ReadFromRepository 的儲存庫 resource-based 政策是針對帳戶/IAM 主體（例如 arn:...:root），主要用於跨帳戶下載存取；『EC2 instance principal』並非有效的主體類型。它也不會給執行個體任何屬於自身的 AWS 憑證。關鍵在於 AWS 文件說明：呼叫 GetAuthorizationToken 所需的 sts:GetServiceBearerToken 若放在 CodeArtifact 資源政策中是無效的，必須放在呼叫者的 identity-based 政策上，因此僅靠資源政策無法讓執行個體完成驗證。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeArtifact does not support ACLs. Access is controlled exclusively through IAM identity-based policies and repository/domain resource-based policies, so 'configuring ACLs on the repository' is not a real CodeArtifact mechanism.","why_zh":"CodeArtifact 不支援 ACL。存取完全是透過 IAM identity-based 政策與儲存庫/網域 resource-based 政策控制，因此『在儲存庫上設定 ACL』並非真實的 CodeArtifact 機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/tokens-authentication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/python-configure-pip.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/get-set-up-provision-user.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repo-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/getting-started-create-iam-instance-profile.html"]}},{"id":344,"question_en":"A company has a file-reading application that saves files to a database that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. Regulations require the company to delete files from EC2 instances every day at a specific time. The company must delete database records that are older than 60 days. The database record deletion must occur after the file deletions. The company has created scripts to delete files and database records. The company needs to receive an email notification for any failure of the deletion scripts. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款文件读取应用程序，该程序会将文件保存到运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的数据库中。法 规要求该公司每天在特定时间从 EC2 实例中删除文件。公司必须删除超过 60 天的数据库记录。 数据库记录的删除必须在文件删除之后进行。该公司已创建了用于删除文件和数据库记录的脚本。公司 需要在删除脚本出现任何故障时收到电子邮件通知。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Systems Manager State Manager to automatically invoke a Systems Manager Automation document at the specified time each day. Configure the Automation document to use a run command to run the deletion scripts in sequential order. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to send failure notifications to the company.","B":"Use AWS Systems Manager State Manager to automatically invoke a Systems Manager Automation document at the specified time each day. Configure the Automation document to use a run command to run the deletion scripts in sequential order. Create a conditional statement inside the Automation document as the last step to check for errors. Use Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to send failure notifications as email messages to the company.","C":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function at the specified time. Add the necessary permissions for the invocation to the Lambda function's resource-based policy. Configure the Lambda function to run the deletion scripts in sequential order. Configure the Lambda function to use Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) to send failure notifications to the company.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that invokes an AWS Lambda function at the specified time. Add the necessary permissions for the invocation to the Lambda function's resource-based policy. Configure the Lambda function to run the deletion scripts in sequential order. Configure the Lambda function to use Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES) to send failure notifications as email messages to the company."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Systems Manager State Manager 每天在指定时间自动调用 Systems Manager Automation 文 档。配置 Automation 文档以使用运行命令按顺序运行删除脚本。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规 则，使用 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）向公司发送失败通知。","B":"使用 AWS Systems Manager State Manager 每天在指定时间自动调用 Systems Manager Automation 文 档。配置 Automation 文档以使用运行命令按顺序运行删除脚本。在 Automation 文档的最后一步创 建一个条件语句来检查错误。使用 Amazon Simple Email Service （Amazon SES） 将失败通知作为 电子邮件发送给公司。","C":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在指定时间调用 AWS Lambda 函数。向 Lambda 函数的基于资 源的策略添加必要的调用权限。配置 Lambda 函数按顺序运行删除脚本。配置 Lambda 函数使用 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）向公司发送失败通知。","D":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在指定时间调用 AWS Lambda 函数。向 Lambda 函数的基于资 源的策略添加必要的调用权限。配置 Lambda 函数按顺序运行删除脚本。配置 Lambda 函数使用 Amazon 简单电子邮件服务（Amazon SES）将失败通知以电子邮件形式发送给公司。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two deletion scripts must run daily, in order (files first, then 60-day-old DB records), on EC2 instances, with an email on any failure, at LEAST development effort. Options A and B are identical for the execution half: State Manager schedules an Automation runbook that uses Run Command to run the scripts in sequential order on the instances (an Automation runbook executes its mainSteps in defined order, so file deletion precedes DB-record deletion). The only difference is the failure-notification mechanism. Option A uses the native EventBridge 'EC2 Automation Execution Status-change Notification' event, which exposes a 'Failed' status, and routes it directly to an Amazon SNS topic (EventBridge natively supports SNS topics as targets); an SNS email subscription then delivers the email with zero custom code. Option B instead requires writing a custom conditional error-checking step inside the runbook AND integrating Amazon SES, which is sent only programmatically via the API/SDK and additionally requires identity verification and (typically) sandbox removal. That extra logic and SES setup is more development effort than A's all-configuration path. Options C and D put the scripts in a Lambda function, but the files and database live ON the EC2 instances, so Lambda cannot execute them directly without adding SSM Run Command code, making them the most effort, not the least. Therefore A meets the requirements with the least development effort.","explanation_zh":"需求是每天依序在 EC2 執行個體上執行兩個刪除腳本（先刪檔案，再刪超過 60 天的資料庫紀錄），並在任何失敗時寄送 email，且要以「最少開發工作量」完成。選項 A 與 B 在執行面完全相同：State Manager 排程一份 Automation runbook，透過 Run Command 在執行個體上依序執行腳本（Automation runbook 會依 mainSteps 的定義順序逐步執行，故檔案刪除會先於資料庫紀錄刪除）。兩者唯一差別在失敗通知機制。選項 A 使用原生的 EventBridge 'EC2 Automation Execution Status-change Notification' 事件，其包含 'Failed' 狀態，並直接路由到 Amazon SNS topic（EventBridge 原生支援 SNS topic 作為 target），再以 SNS email 訂閱寄送郵件，完全不需自訂程式碼。選項 B 則需在 runbook 內撰寫自訂的條件式錯誤檢查步驟，並整合 Amazon SES；SES 只能透過 API/SDK 以程式寄信，且需驗證身分並（通常）申請移出沙箱，這些額外邏輯與設定的開發量高於 A 的純設定路徑。選項 C 與 D 把腳本放進 Lambda，但檔案與資料庫位於 EC2 執行個體「上」，Lambda 無法直接執行，必須再加上 SSM Run Command 程式碼，開發量最高而非最少。因此 A 以最少開發工作量滿足需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Execution is identical to A (State Manager + Automation + Run Command), but the notification path is heavier: it requires writing a custom conditional error-checking step inside the Automation document AND using Amazon SES, which sends only programmatically via the API/SDK and requires verified identities (and typically sandbox removal). That is more development effort than A's native EventBridge 'Failed' Automation event routed to an SNS email subscription, which is pure configuration.","why_zh":"執行面與 A 完全相同（State Manager + Automation + Run Command），但通知路徑較重：需在 Automation document 內撰寫自訂的條件式錯誤檢查步驟，並使用 Amazon SES（只能透過 API/SDK 以程式寄信，需驗證身分且通常需移出沙箱）。這比 A 用原生 EventBridge Automation 'Failed' 事件直接路由到 SNS email 訂閱（純設定）開發量更高。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Lambda function cannot directly run scripts that delete files and DB records hosted ON the EC2 instances; it would need additional SSM Run Command code to invoke them on the instances, greatly increasing development effort. Building the full Lambda plus the resource-based-policy invocation wiring is more work than State Manager + Automation, even though SNS for notification is fine.","why_zh":"Lambda 函式無法直接執行針對 EC2 執行個體「上」檔案與資料庫紀錄的刪除腳本，必須額外撰寫 SSM Run Command 程式碼才能在執行個體上觸發，開發量大增。即使通知用 SNS 沒問題，撰寫完整 Lambda 並串接 resource-based policy 調用，仍比 State Manager + Automation 費工。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Has the same Lambda limitation as C (cannot directly run the on-EC2 deletion scripts without extra SSM Run Command code) and additionally relies on Amazon SES, which needs identity verification, sandbox removal, and programmatic API/SDK send. This is the highest development effort, not the least.","why_zh":"具有與 C 相同的 Lambda 限制（不寫額外 SSM Run Command 程式碼便無法直接執行 EC2 上的刪除腳本），又額外依賴 Amazon SES（需驗證身分、移出沙箱並透過 API/SDK 以程式寄信）。這是開發量最高的選項，而非最少。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/scheduling-automations-state-manager-associations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/reference-eventbridge-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-automation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sns/latest/dg/sns-email-notifications.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/ses/latest/dg/send-an-email-using-sdk-programmatically.html"]}},{"id":345,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations that has all features enabled to manage its AWS accounts. Amazon EQ instances run in the AWS accounts. The company requires that all current EC2 instances must use Instance Metadata Service Version 2 (IMDSv2). The company needs to block AWS API calls that originate from EC2 instances that do not use IMDSv2. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS 组织中的一个启用了所有功能的组织来管理其 AWS 资源。 账户。Amazon EQ 实例在 AWS 账户中运行。 公司要求所有当前的 EC2 实例必须使用实例元数据服务版本 2（IMDSv2）。公司需要阻止源自未使 用 IMDSv2 的 EC2 实例的 AWS API 调用。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new SCP statement that denies the ec2:RunInstances action when the ec2:MetadataHttpTokens condition key is not equal to the value of required. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","B":"Create a new SCP statement that denies the ec2:RunInstances action when the ec2:MetadataHttpPutResponseHopLimit condition key value is greater than two. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","C":"Create a new SCP statement that denies \"*\" when the ec2:RoleDelivery condition key value is less than two. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","D":"Create a new SCP statement that denies when the ec2:MetadataHttpTokens condition key value is not equal to required. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的 SCP 语句，MetadataHttpTokens 条件键不等于 required 值时，拒绝 ec2:RunInstances 操 作。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","B":"创建一个新的 SCP 语句，当 ec2:MetadataHttpPutResponseHopLimit 条件键值大于 2 时，拒绝 ec2: RunInstances 操作。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","C":"创建一个新的 SCP 语句，当 ec2:RoleDelivery 条件键值小于 2 时拒绝“*”。将该 SCP 附加到组织的 根目录。","D":"创建一个新的 SCP 语句，当 ec2:MetadataHttpTokens 条件键值不等于 required 时拒绝。将该 SCP 附 加到组织的根目录。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirement is to BLOCK AWS API calls that originate from EC2 instances not using IMDSv2 - that is, to stop role credentials obtained through IMDSv1 from actually being used. AWS's IMDSv2 transition documentation states that this access-management layer of protection is achieved with the ec2:RoleDelivery condition key: credentials delivered via IMDSv1 carry an ec2:RoleDelivery value of 1.0, while IMDSv2-delivered credentials carry 2.0. The documented SCP/IAM example 'Require role credentials to be retrieved from IMDSv2' is exactly: Deny Action '*' Resource '*' with Condition NumericLessThan ec2:RoleDelivery 2.0, so any API call signed with IMDSv1-obtained role credentials receives an UnauthorizedOperation error. That is precisely option C. Options A, B, and D rely on ec2:MetadataHttpTokens / ec2:MetadataHttpPutResponseHopLimit, which are only present in the request context of the ec2:RunInstances and ec2:ModifyInstanceMetadataOptions APIs (how an instance is configured at launch/modify time); they cannot block API calls made by already-running instances. The dump's suggested answer D is therefore wrong: ec2:MetadataHttpTokens governs instance configuration, not the blocking of API calls made by instances.","explanation_zh":"需求是「封鎖來自未使用 IMDSv2 之 EC2 instance 的 AWS API 呼叫」，也就是要阻止透過 IMDSv1 取得的 role 憑證被實際使用。AWS 官方 IMDSv2 transition 文件指出，這層 access-management 防護是用 ec2:RoleDelivery 這個 condition key 來達成：透過 IMDSv1 取得的憑證其 ec2:RoleDelivery 值為 1.0，透過 IMDSv2 取得的則為 2.0。文件中「Require role credentials to be retrieved from IMDSv2」的 SCP/IAM 範例正是：Deny Action '*'、Resource '*'，Condition 為 NumericLessThan ec2:RoleDelivery 2.0，因此任何以 IMDSv1 憑證簽署的 API 呼叫都會收到 UnauthorizedOperation 錯誤，這正是選項 C。選項 A、B、D 使用的是 ec2:MetadataHttpTokens / ec2:MetadataHttpPutResponseHopLimit，這些 key 只存在於 ec2:RunInstances 與 ec2:ModifyInstanceMetadataOptions API 的 request context（控制 instance 啟動/修改時的設定），無法封鎖已執行 instance 所發出的 API 呼叫。因此 dump 建議的答案 D 是錯的：ec2:MetadataHttpTokens 管的是 instance 的設定，而非封鎖 instance 發出的 API 呼叫。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"ec2:MetadataHttpTokens scoped to ec2:RunInstances only prevents launching new IMDSv1-enabled instances; this key is only available in the RunInstances/ModifyInstanceMetadataOptions request context. It does nothing to block API calls from existing instances that already run with IMDSv1 credentials, which is the stated requirement.","why_zh":"ec2:MetadataHttpTokens 套用在 ec2:RunInstances 只能阻止啟動新的啟用 IMDSv1 的 instance，且此 key 僅存在於 RunInstances/ModifyInstanceMetadataOptions 的 request context，無法封鎖既有 instance 以 IMDSv1 憑證發出的 API 呼叫，不符合需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"ec2:MetadataHttpPutResponseHopLimit controls the IMDS hop limit at instance launch time, not IMDSv2 enforcement; a hop limit greater than two does not even indicate IMDSv1 usage. Restricting it on RunInstances has nothing to do with blocking API calls from non-IMDSv2 instances.","why_zh":"ec2:MetadataHttpPutResponseHopLimit 控制的是 instance 啟動時的 IMDS hop limit，與強制 IMDSv2 無關，hop limit 大於二也不代表使用 IMDSv1。套在 RunInstances 上無法封鎖非 IMDSv2 instance 的 API 呼叫。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer but it is wrong. ec2:MetadataHttpTokens is only present in the request context of the RunInstances and ModifyInstanceMetadataOptions APIs (instance configuration), so a Deny based on it cannot block arbitrary AWS API calls made by already-running instances using IMDSv1-delivered credentials. The documented key for blocking those calls is ec2:RoleDelivery (option C).","why_zh":"這是 dump 建議的答案，但它是錯的。ec2:MetadataHttpTokens 只存在於 RunInstances 與 ModifyInstanceMetadataOptions API 的 request context（instance 設定），因此以它為條件的 Deny 無法封鎖既有 instance 以 IMDSv1 憑證發出的任意 AWS API 呼叫。文件指定用來封鎖這類呼叫的 key 是 ec2:RoleDelivery（選項 C）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/instance-metadata-transition-to-version-2.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/ExamplePolicies_EC2.html"]}},{"id":346,"question_en":"A DevOps team supports an application that runs on a large number of Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group. The DevOps team uses AWS CloudFormation to deploy the EC2 instances. The application recently experienced an issue. A single instance returned errors to a large percentage of requests. The EC2 instance responded as healthy to both Amazon EC2 and Elastic Load Balancing health checks. The DevOps team collects application logs in Amazon CloudWatch by using the embedded metric format. The DevOps team needs to receive an alert if any EC2 instance is responsible for more than half of all errors. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队支持的应用程序在 Auto Scaling 组中的大量 Amazon EC2 实例上运行。该团队使用 AWS CloudFormation 部署 EC2 实例。最近，该应用程序出现了一个问题。单个实例对大量请求返回错 误。该 EC2 实例对 Amazon EC2 和 Elastic Load Balancing 的健康检查均显示为正常。 DevOps 团队通过使用嵌入式指标格式在 Amazon CloudWatch 中收集应用程序日志。如果任何 EC2 实 例导致的错误超过所有错误的一半，DevOps 团队需要收到警报。 哪种步骤组合能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudWatch Contributor Insights rule that groups logs from the CloudWatch application logs based on instance ID and errors.","B":"Create a resource group in AWS Resource Groups. Use the CloudFormation stack to group the resources for the application. Add the application to CloudWatch Application Insights. Use the resource group to identify the application.","C":"Create a metric filter for the application logs to count the occurrence of the term \"Error.'' Create a CloudWatch alarm that uses the METRIC_COUNT function to determine whether errors have occurred. Configure the CloudWatch alarm to send a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify the DevOps team.","D":"Create a CloudWatch alarm that uses the INSIGHT_RULE_METRIC function to determine whether a specific instance is responsible for more than half of all errors reported by EC2 instances. Configure the CloudWatch alarm to send a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify the DevOps team.","E":"Create a CloudWatch subscription filter for the application logs that filters for errors and invokes an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to send the instance ID and error and in a notification to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify the DevOps team."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 CloudWatch 贡献者洞察规则，根据实例 ID 和错误对 CloudWatch 应用程序日志进行分组。","B":"在 AWS 资源组中创建一个资源组。使用 CloudFormation 堆栈对应用程序的资源进行分组。将应用程 序添加到 CloudWatch 应用程序洞察中。使用资源组来标识应用程序。","C":"为应用程序日志创建一个度量筛选器，用于计算“Error”（错误）一词出现的次数。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，该警报使用 METRIC_COUNT 函数来确定是否发生了错误。配置 CloudWatch 警 报，使其向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题发送通知，以告知 DevOps 团队。","D":"创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，该警报使用 INSIGHT_RULE_METRIC 函数来确定特定实例是否导致 了由 EC2 实例报告的所有错误中的超过一半。配置 CloudWatch 警报，使其向 Amazon 简单通知 服务（Amazon SNS）主题发送通知，以告知 DevOps 团队。","E":"为应用程序日志创建一个 CloudWatch 订阅过滤器，用于筛选错误并调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数。 配置该 Lambda 函数，使其将实例 ID 和错误信息发送到 Amazon Simple Notification Service （Amazon SNS）主题，以通知 DevOps 团队。"},"answer":["A","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to alert when a single EC2 instance is responsible for more than half of ALL errors, using application logs already in CloudWatch (embedded metric format), with the LEAST operational overhead. CloudWatch Contributor Insights (A) is purpose-built for this: the docs say it analyzes high-cardinality log data in real time to find 'bad hosts' and 'the URLs that generate the most errors' by grouping on a key such as instance ID, producing top-N contributor time series. You then attach a CloudWatch alarm using the INSIGHT_RULE_METRIC metric-math function (D). The docs document this exact pattern: INSIGHT_RULE_METRIC(ruleName, metricName) exposes MaxContributorValue (the top contributor's value) and Sum (the total across all contributors), and the AWS example builds e3 = (e1/e2)*100 to alarm on a percentage threshold (changing 100 to the desired percent), then notifies an SNS topic. Setting the threshold to 50 percent alarms when one instance drives more than half of all errors. This is fully managed with no custom code, meeting the LEAST operational overhead qualifier.","explanation_zh":"需求是：在單一 EC2 instance 造成超過一半的「所有」錯誤時發出警示，且要使用已存在於 CloudWatch（embedded metric format）的應用程式日誌，並以最少維運負擔達成。CloudWatch Contributor Insights（A）正是為此設計：文件說明它即時分析高基數日誌資料，用來找出 'bad hosts' 與 '產生最多錯誤的 URL'，可依 instance ID 等鍵分組，產生 top-N 貢獻者的時間序列。接著用 INSIGHT_RULE_METRIC metric math 函式建立 CloudWatch alarm（D）。文件記載了完全相同的範式：INSIGHT_RULE_METRIC(ruleName, metricName) 提供 MaxContributorValue（最大貢獻者的值）與 Sum（所有貢獻者的總和），AWS 範例以 e3 = (e1/e2)*100 對百分比門檻設警示（把 100 改為想要的百分比），並通知 SNS topic。將門檻設為 50% 即可在某一 instance 造成超過一半錯誤時觸發。此方案完全託管、無自訂程式碼，符合最少維運負擔的限定條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch Application Insights (with Resource Groups) provides SageMaker-powered automated detection of common application/infrastructure problems and auto-configures monitoring and dashboards for supported components. It does not analyze custom EMF application logs grouped by instance ID to compute which single instance contributes more than half of all errors, so it does not meet the contributor-ratio alerting requirement.","why_zh":"CloudWatch Application Insights（搭配 Resource Groups）透過 SageMaker 自動偵測常見的應用/基礎設施問題，並為支援的元件自動設定監控與儀表板。它不會依 instance ID 分組分析自訂的 EMF 應用程式日誌來計算哪一台 instance 造成超過一半的錯誤，因此無法滿足此貢獻者比例的警示需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A metric filter that counts the term 'Error' produces only a total error count with no per-instance breakdown, so it cannot determine whether a single instance causes more than half of the errors. There is also no METRIC_COUNT function in CloudWatch metric math, so the described alarm expression is invalid.","why_zh":"計數 'Error' 字詞的 metric filter 只會產生錯誤總數，沒有各 instance 的細分，因此無法判斷某一台 instance 是否造成超過一半的錯誤。CloudWatch metric math 也沒有 METRIC_COUNT 函式，所述警示運算式不成立。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"A subscription filter that invokes a Lambda function on each matching error and sends it to SNS is custom code that fires per error event and would also require stateful aggregation to compute the more-than-half-of-all-errors ratio. This adds significant operational overhead compared with the native Contributor Insights + INSIGHT_RULE_METRIC alarm approach.","why_zh":"由 subscription filter 對每筆符合的錯誤呼叫 Lambda 函式並送至 SNS，屬於自訂程式碼，會在每個錯誤事件觸發，且還需要具狀態的彙總來計算『超過一半錯誤』的比例，相較於原生的 Contributor Insights + INSIGHT_RULE_METRIC 警示方式增加了可觀的維運負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContributorInsights.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContributorInsights-GraphReportData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/using-metric-math.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/cloudwatch-application-insights.html"]}},{"id":347,"question_en":"A company is using AWS CloudFormation to perform deployments of its application environment. A deployment failed during a recent update to the existing CloudFormation stack. A DevOps engineer discovered that some resources in the stack were manually modified. The DevOps engineer needs a solution that detects manual modification of resources and sends an alert to the DevOps lead. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CloudFormation 来部署其应用程序环境。在最近对现有 CloudFormation 堆栈进行更新时，部署失败了。一位 DevOps 工程师发现堆栈中的某些资源被手动修改了。 DevOps 工程师需要一个解决方案，能够检测到对资源的手动修改，并向 DevOps 负责人发送警报。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the DevOps lead to the topic by using an email address. Create an AWS Config managed rule that has the CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK identifier. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is invoked on the NON_COMPLIANT resources status. Set the SNS topic as the rule target.","B":"Tag all CloudFormation resources with a specific tag. Create an AWS Config custom rule by using the AWS Config Rules Development Kit Library (RDKlib) that checks all resource changes that have the specific tag. Configure the custom rule to mark all the tagged resource changes as NON_COMPLIANT when the change is not performed by CloudFormation. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is invoked on the NON_COMPUANT resources status. Create an AWS Lambda function that sends an email message to the DevOps lead. Set the Lambda function as the rule target.","C":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Subscribe the DevOps lead to the topic by using an email address. Create an AWS Config managed rule that has the CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK identifier. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is invoked on the COMPLIANT resources status. Set the SNS topic as the rule target.","D":"Create an AWS Config managed rule that has the CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK identifier. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that is invoked on the NON_COMPLIANT resources status. Create an AWS Lambda function that sends an email message to the DevOps lead. Set the Lambda function as the rule target."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。使用电子邮件地址将 DevOps 负责人订阅到该 主题。创建一个具有 CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK 标识符的 AWS Config 管理规则。创建一个在资源状态为 NON_COMPLIANT 时被触发的 Amazon EventBridge 规 则。将 SNS 主题设置为规则目标。","B":"使用特定标签标记所有 CloudFormation 资源。通过使用 AWS Config 规则开发工具包库（RDKlib） 创建一个自定义规则，该规则检查所有带有特定标签的资源更改。配置自定义规则，当更改不是由 CloudFormation 执行时，将所有带有标签的资源更改标记为“不符合”。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在“不符合”资源状态时触发。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，向 DevOps 领导 发送电子邮件消息。将 Lambda 函数设置为规则目标。","C":"创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。使用电子邮件地址将 DevOps 负责人订阅到 该主题。创建一个具有 CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK 标识符的 AWS Config 管理规则。创建一个在资源状态为 COMPLIANT 时被调用的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。 将 SNS 主题设置为规则目标。","D":"创建一个具有以下特性的 AWS Config 管理规则： CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK 标识符。创建一个在资源状态为“不 合规”时被调用的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。创建一个向 DevOps 领导发送电子邮件消息的 AWS Lambda 函数。将 Lambda 函数设置为规则的目标。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to detect manual modification (drift) of CloudFormation stack resources and email the DevOps lead with the LEAST operational effort. The AWS Config managed rule CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK is purpose-built for this: it runs DetectStackDrift and is COMPLIANT when the stack drift status is IN_SYNC and NON_COMPLIANT when the stack has DRIFTED (i.e., a resource was manually modified). AWS Config emits a 'Config Rules Compliance Change' event directly to EventBridge, so an EventBridge rule matching the NON_COMPLIANT status fires precisely on drift. Option A targets that EventBridge rule at an SNS topic with a direct email subscription, delivering the alert with no custom code to author or maintain, which is the least operational effort. Option C is logically inverted (it triggers on COMPLIANT, the in-sync/no-drift state), Option D adds an unnecessary Lambda function to send email, and Option B builds a custom RDKlib rule plus tagging plus Lambda (highest effort).","explanation_zh":"需求是以最少維運成本偵測 CloudFormation 堆疊資源的手動修改（drift）並以 email 通知 DevOps lead。AWS Config 受管規則 CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK 正是為此設計：它執行 DetectStackDrift，當堆疊 drift 狀態為 IN_SYNC 時為 COMPLIANT，當堆疊為 DRIFTED（即資源被手動修改）時為 NON_COMPLIANT。AWS Config 會直接向 EventBridge 發送 'Config Rules Compliance Change' 事件，因此比對 NON_COMPLIANT 狀態的 EventBridge rule 會在發生 drift 時觸發。選項 A 將該 EventBridge rule 指向訂閱了 email 的 SNS topic，無需撰寫或維護任何自訂程式碼即可送出警示，維運成本最低。選項 C 邏輯相反（在 COMPLIANT／無 drift 狀態觸發）；選項 D 多加了不必要的 Lambda function 來寄信；選項 B 則需自訂 RDKlib 規則加上標籤與 Lambda，成本最高。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building a custom AWS Config rule with the RDKlib library, tagging every CloudFormation resource, and adding a Lambda function to send email is by far the highest operational effort. The purpose-built managed rule CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK already detects drift, so a custom rule is unnecessary and overengineered, and a generic tag-based custom rule cannot easily determine whether a change was performed by CloudFormation.","why_zh":"以 RDKlib 函式庫自建自訂 AWS Config 規則、為每個 CloudFormation 資源加標籤，並加上 Lambda function 寄信，是維運成本最高的做法。既有專用受管規則 CLOUDFORMATION_STACK_DRIFT_DETECTION_CHECK 已可偵測 drift，自訂規則屬多此一舉的過度設計，且以標籤為基礎的通用自訂規則也難以判斷變更是否由 CloudFormation 執行。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This triggers the EventBridge rule on the COMPLIANT status. For the drift-detection rule, COMPLIANT means the stack is IN_SYNC (no drift), so the DevOps lead would be alerted when there is NO manual modification and would receive no alert when drift actually occurs. The logic is inverted.","why_zh":"此選項在 COMPLIANT 狀態觸發 EventBridge rule。對於 drift 偵測規則，COMPLIANT 代表堆疊為 IN_SYNC（無 drift），因此會在沒有手動修改時通知 DevOps lead，而真正發生 drift 時反而不會發出警示，邏輯顛倒。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The detection logic (managed rule + EventBridge on NON_COMPLIANT) is correct, but routing the alert through a custom Lambda function to send email adds code to author, deploy, and maintain. Since EventBridge can target an SNS topic with an email subscription directly (as in A), the Lambda is unnecessary and increases operational effort, failing the LEAST-effort qualifier.","why_zh":"偵測邏輯（受管規則 + 在 NON_COMPLIANT 觸發 EventBridge）正確，但透過自訂 Lambda function 寄信會增加需撰寫、部署與維護的程式碼。由於 EventBridge 可直接以訂閱 email 的 SNS topic 作為 target（如選項 A），此 Lambda 屬多餘並提高維運成本，不符合「最少維運成本」的條件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/cloudformation-stack-drift-detection-check.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/event-bus-rule-get-started.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/notifications-for-AWS-Config.html"]}},{"id":348,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer deployed multiple AWS accounts by using AWS Control Tower to support different business, technical, and administrative units in a company. A security team needs the DevOps engineer to automate AWS Control Tower guardrails for the company. The guardrails must be applied to all accounts in an OU of the company's organization in AWS Organizations. The security team needs a solution that has version control and can be reviewed and rolled back if necessary. The security team will maintain the management of the solution in its OU. The security team wants to limit the type of guardrails that are allowed and allow only new guardrails that are approved by the security team. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师通过使用 AWS 控制塔部署了多个 AWS 账户，以支持公司内的不同业务、技术和 行政部门。安全团队要求该 DevOps 工程师为公司自动化 AWS 控制塔的防护措施。这些防护措施必须 应用于公司 AWS 组织中某个组织单元（OU）内的所有账户。 安全团队需要一个具备版本控制功能的解决方案，并且在必要时能够进行审查和回滚。安全团队将在其 组织单位中负责该解决方案的管理。安全团队希望限制允许的防护措施类型，并且只允许经过安全团队 批准的新防护措施。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create individual AWS CloudFormation templates that align to a guardrail. Store the templates in an AWS CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS::ControlTower::EnableControl logical resource in the template for each OU in the organization. Configure an AWS Code Build project that an Amazon EventBridge rule will invoke for the security team's AWS CodeCommit changes.","B":"Create individual AWS CloudFormation templates that align to a guardrail. Store the templates in an AWS CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS::ControlTower::EnableControl logical resource in the template for each account in the organization. Configure an AWS CodePipeline pipeline in the security team's account. Advise the security team to invoke the pipeline and provide these parameters when starting the pipeline.","C":"Create individual AWS CloudFormation templates that align to a guardrail. Store the templates in an AWS CodeCommit repository. Create an AWS::ControlTower::EnableControl logical resource in the template for each OU in the organization. Configure an AWS CodePipeline pipeline in the security team's account that an Amazon EventBridge rule will invoke for the security team's CodeCommit changes.","D":"Configure an AWS CodePipeline pipeline in the security team's account that an Amazon EventBridge rule will invoke for PutObject events to an Amazon S3 bucket. Create individual AWS CloudFormation templates that align to a guardrail. Store the templates in the S3 bucket. Create an AWS::ControlTower::EnableControl logical resource in the template for each OU in the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建与防护栏对齐的单独的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。将模板存储在 AWS CodeCommit 存储库中。 为组织中的每个组织单元（OU）在模板中ControlTower::EnableControl 逻辑资源。配置一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目，该项目将由 Amazon EventBridge 规则在安全团队对 AWS CodeCommit 进行更改时 调用。","B":"为每个防护栏创建单独的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。将模板存储在 AWS CodeCommit 存储库中。在组 织中的每个账户的模板中创建一个 AWS::ControlTower::EnableControl 逻辑资源。在安全团队的账户中 配置一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。建议安全团队启动管道时调用该管道，并提供以下参数。","C":"创建与防护栏对齐的单独的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。将模板存储在 AWS CodeCommit 存储库中。 为组织中的每个组织单元（OU）在模板中ControlTower::EnableControl 逻辑资源。在安全团队的账 户中配置一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道将由 Amazon EventBridge 规则在安全团队的 CodeCommit 更改时调用。","D":"在安全团队的账户中配置一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，该管道将由 Amazon EventBridge 规则在向 Amazon S3 存储桶写入对象时触发。为每条防护栏创建单独的 AWS CloudFormation 模板。将模板存储 在 S3 存储桶中。在模板中为组织中的每个组织单元（OU）创建一个 AWS::ControlTower:: EnableControl 逻辑资源。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Control Tower controls (guardrails) are enabled against an organizational unit, not individual accounts. The AWS::ControlTower::EnabledControl resource's TargetIdentifier is documented as 'The ARN of the organizational unit', and the resource 'creates AWS resources on the specified organizational unit and the accounts it contains.' This rules out option B, which defines a resource per account and additionally requires manual pipeline invocation. Among the remaining OU-level options, C is the most operationally efficient: it stores guardrail CloudFormation templates in AWS CodeCommit (a Git repo that provides version control, pull-request review, and clean rollback so the security team can gate and approve which guardrails are merged), keeps the AWS CodePipeline in the security team's own account so the team maintains management in its OU, and uses an Amazon EventBridge rule on CodeCommit changes to fully automate the release. CodePipeline (not CodeBuild as in A) gives an orchestrated, staged, approval-capable, and rollback-capable release workflow, and a Git repo (not an S3 bucket as in D) gives the pull-request review the requirement calls for. This matches the dump's suggested answer.","explanation_zh":"AWS Control Tower 的控制項（guardrails）是針對 organizational unit（OU）啟用，而非個別帳戶。AWS::ControlTower::EnabledControl 資源的 TargetIdentifier 在文件中明確定義為「OU 的 ARN」，且此資源會在指定的 OU 以及其所含的帳戶上建立資源。這排除了選項 B（為每個帳戶定義資源，且還需手動啟動 pipeline）。在其餘採用 OU 層級的選項中，C 最具營運效率：它將 guardrail 的 CloudFormation 範本存放在 AWS CodeCommit（以 Git 為基礎，提供版本控制、pull request 審查與乾淨的回溯，讓安全團隊把關並核准哪些 guardrails 被合併），把 AWS CodePipeline 放在安全團隊自己的帳戶中（讓團隊在其 OU 內維護管理），並以 Amazon EventBridge 規則在 CodeCommit 變更時完全自動化發佈。CodePipeline（而非 A 的 CodeBuild）提供可編排、階段化、可加核准關卡且可回溯的發佈流程；而 Git 儲存庫（而非 D 的 S3 儲存桶）提供需求所要求的 pull request 審查。此與題庫建議答案一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Targets each OU correctly, but uses AWS CodeBuild invoked by EventBridge instead of CodePipeline. CodeBuild alone is a single build/compute step with no orchestrated, staged release and no native manual approval action, so it is a weaker fit for a 'reviewed, approved, and rollback-capable' deployment and is less operationally efficient than a managed pipeline.","why_zh":"雖正確以每個 OU 為目標，但使用由 EventBridge 觸發的 AWS CodeBuild 取代 CodePipeline。CodeBuild 僅是單一建置/運算步驟，缺乏可編排、階段化的發佈與原生的手動核准動作，對於「可審查、核准且可回溯」的部署較不適合，營運效率也不如受管 pipeline。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Defines an EnableControl resource per account, but the resource's TargetIdentifier must be an OU ARN (controls are enabled at OU level and automatically apply to the contained accounts), so per-account targeting is not how this is implemented. It also requires the security team to manually invoke the pipeline with parameters every time, which is not automated and is operationally inefficient.","why_zh":"為每個帳戶定義 EnableControl 資源，但該資源的 TargetIdentifier 必須是 OU 的 ARN（控制項在 OU 層級啟用並自動套用至所含帳戶），因此以帳戶為目標並非正確做法。此外每次都需安全團隊手動以參數啟動 pipeline，並非自動化，營運效率低。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Uses CodePipeline and correct OU-level targeting, but stores the templates in an S3 bucket triggered by PutObject events instead of a Git repository. Although S3 supports object versioning, it does not provide the pull-request code review and Git-based rollback workflow the security team needs to limit and approve new guardrails; CodeCommit (as in C) is the more operationally efficient choice for version control, review, and rollback.","why_zh":"使用 CodePipeline 且正確以 OU 層級為目標，但將範本存放在由 PutObject 事件觸發的 S3 儲存桶，而非 Git 儲存庫。雖然 S3 支援物件版本控制，但無法提供安全團隊限制並核准新 guardrails 所需的 pull request 程式碼審查與以 Git 為基礎的回溯流程；CodeCommit（如選項 C）在版本控制、審查與回溯上更具營運效率。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-resource-controltower-enabledcontrol.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/enable-controls.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/triggering.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/approvals.html"]}},{"id":349,"question_en":"A company runs a web application on Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS). The company uses Amazon CloudFront to distribute the application. The company recently enabled AWS WAF. The company set up Amazon CloudWatch Logs to send logs to an aws-waf-logs log group. The company wants a DevOps engineer to receive alerts if there are sudden changes in blocked traffic. The company does not want to receive alerts for other changes in AWS WAF log behavior. The company will tune AWS WAF rules over time. The DevOps engineer is currently subscribed to an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic in the environment. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）上运行一个网络应用程序。该公司使用亚马逊云 分发服务（Amazon CloudFront）来分发该应用程序。该公司最近启用了 AWS WAF。该公司设置了亚马逊 云监控日志服务（Amazon CloudWatch Logs）将日志发送到一个名为“aws-waf-logs”的日志组。 该公司希望有一位 DevOps 工程师在出现突发的被阻断流量变化时收到警报。该公司不希望收到 AWS WAF 日志行为其他变化的警报。该公司会随着时间的推移调整 AWS WAF 规则。 该 DevOps 工程师当前已订阅了环境中的亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a CloudWatch Logs metrics filter for blocked requests on the AWS WAF log group to create a custom metric. Create a CloudWatch alarm by using CloudWatch anomaly detection and the published custom metric. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic to alert the DevOps engineer.","B":"Create a CloudWatch anomaly detector for the log group. Create a CloudWatch alarm by using metrics that the CloudWatch anomaly detector publishes. Use the high setting for the LogAnomalyPriority metric. Configure the alarm to go into alarm state if a static threshold of one anomaly is detected. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic to alert the DevOps engineer.","C":"Create a CloudWatch metrics filter for counted requests on the AWS WAF log group to create a custom metric. Create a CloudWatch alarm that activates when the sum of blocked requests in the custom metric during a period of 1 hour is greater than a static estimate for the acceptable number of blocked requests in 1 hour. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic to alert the DevOps engineer.","D":"Create a CloudWatch anomaly detector for the log group. Create a CloudWatch alarm by using metrics that the CloudWatch anomaly detector publishes. Use the medium setting for the LogAnomalyPriority metric. Configure the alarm to go into alarm state if a sum of anomalies over 1 hour is greater than an expected value. Configure the alarm to notify the SNS topic to alert the DevOps engineer."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS WAF 日志组上创建一个 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器，用于被阻止的请求，以创建自定义指标。 使用 CloudWatch 异常检测和发布的自定义指标创建 CloudWatch 警报。将警报配置为通知 SNS 主题， 以提醒 DevOps 工程师。","B":"为日志组创建一个 CloudWatch 异常检测器。使用 CloudWatch 异常检测器发布的指标创建一个 CloudWatch 警报。将 LogAnomalyPriority 指标设置为高。配置警报，使其在检测到一个异常的静态阈 值时进入警报状态。配置警报以通知 SNS 主题，从而提醒 DevOps 工程师。","C":"在 AWS WAF 日志组上创建一个 CloudWatch 指标筛选器，用于对计数请求创建自定义指标。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，当自定义指标中 1 小时内被阻止的请求数量之和超过 1 小时内可接受的被阻止请求 数量的静态估计值时激活该警报。将警报配置为通知 SNS 主题以提醒 DevOps 工程师。","D":"为日志组创建一个 CloudWatch 异常检测器。使用 CloudWatch 异常检测器发布的指标创建一个 CloudWatch 警报。将 LogAnomalyPriority 指标设置为中等。配置警报，使其在 1 小时内的异常总 和大于预期值时进入警报状态。配置警报以通知 SNS 主题，从而提醒 DevOps 工程师。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to alert ONLY on sudden changes in blocked traffic, not on other AWS WAF log-behavior changes, and the baseline of acceptable blocked requests will shift as WAF rules are tuned over time. Option A creates a CloudWatch Logs metric filter that matches the blocked-request pattern (e.g. action=BLOCK in the WAF log JSON) to produce a scoped custom metric, then builds a CloudWatch alarm using metric anomaly detection on that custom metric. Per the CloudWatch anomaly detection docs, anomaly detection works on custom metrics, generates a band of expected values, and continually re-trains the model as metric values evolve over time, so it flags only sudden deviations while adapting as rules are tuned, and the metric filter keeps the signal scoped to blocked traffic only. It notifies the existing SNS topic, satisfying all three requirements. Options B and D instead use a CloudWatch Logs anomaly detector (LogAnomalyPriority/AnomalyCount), which is ML pattern/token recognition over the entire log content and surfaces anomalies in ANY log behavior (error keywords, IPs, new request IDs, surges of any token) - exactly the other behavior changes the company does not want, and is not scoped to blocked requests. Option C filters for counted requests (not blocked) and uses a static threshold/estimate, which mis-targets the metric and breaks when rule tuning shifts the acceptable-blocked baseline.","explanation_zh":"需求是只在被封鎖流量（blocked traffic）出現突然變化時告警，而不是對 AWS WAF 日誌的其他行為變化告警；而且隨著 WAF rules 持續調整，可接受的封鎖請求基線會隨時間移動。選項 A 建立一個 CloudWatch Logs metric filter，比對被封鎖請求的模式（例如 WAF 日誌 JSON 中的 action=BLOCK）以產生一個範圍受限的 custom metric，然後對該 custom metric 用 CloudWatch metric anomaly detection 建立告警。依 CloudWatch anomaly detection 文件，anomaly detection 可用於 custom metrics，會產生一段預期值的帶狀範圍（band），並隨指標值隨時間演進而持續重新訓練模型，因此能在規則被調整時自動適應，只標記突然的偏離，而 metric filter 讓訊號僅限於被封鎖流量。它會通知既有的 SNS topic，滿足全部三項需求。選項 B 與 D 則使用 CloudWatch Logs anomaly detector（LogAnomalyPriority/AnomalyCount），那是針對整體日誌內容的 ML 模式/token 辨識，會對任何日誌行為（錯誤關鍵字、IP、新的 request ID、任何 token 的突增）標記異常，正是公司不想要的其他行為變化，且未限定在被封鎖請求。選項 C 過濾的是 counted requests（非 blocked），並使用靜態門檻/估計值，既鎖錯指標，也會在規則調整使可接受封鎖基線移動時失效。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses a CloudWatch Logs anomaly detector (LogAnomalyPriority), which is ML log pattern/token detection over the entire log content, so it flags anomalies in ANY WAF log behavior (errors, new tokens, surges) rather than specifically blocked traffic - violating the requirement to avoid alerts for other log-behavior changes. A static threshold of one anomaly is also extremely noisy.","why_zh":"使用 CloudWatch Logs anomaly detector（LogAnomalyPriority），是針對整體日誌內容的 ML 模式/token 偵測，會對任何 WAF 日誌行為（錯誤、新 token、突增）標記異常，而非專指被封鎖流量，違反了避免對其他日誌行為變化告警的需求；且「一個異常」的靜態門檻也極易產生雜訊。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Creates a metric filter for counted requests (Count action), not blocked requests, and uses a static estimate threshold over 1 hour. It mis-targets the metric, and a fixed static threshold cannot track the shifting baseline of acceptable blocked requests as WAF rules are tuned, producing false alarms or missing real spikes relative to a moving normal.","why_zh":"為 counted requests（Count 動作）而非 blocked requests 建立 metric filter，並使用 1 小時的靜態估計門檻。它鎖錯了指標，且固定的靜態門檻無法隨 WAF 規則調整而追蹤移動中的可接受封鎖請求基線，因而會產生誤報，或相對於移動的正常值漏掉真正的尖峰。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Like B, uses a CloudWatch Logs anomaly detector (medium LogAnomalyPriority), which is ML pattern detection across all WAF log content rather than scoped to blocked requests, so it alerts on other WAF log-behavior changes the company explicitly does not want.","why_zh":"與 B 相同，使用 CloudWatch Logs anomaly detector（medium LogAnomalyPriority），是針對所有 WAF 日誌內容的 ML 模式偵測，而非限定在被封鎖請求，因此會對公司明確不想要的其他 WAF 日誌行為變化告警。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Anomaly_Detection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/LogsAnomalyDetection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateMetricFilterProcedure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntaxForMetricFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging.html"]}},{"id":350,"question_en":"A video platform company is migrating its video catalog to AWS. The company will host MP4 videos files in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company will use Amazon CloudFront and Amazon EC2 instances to serve the video files. Users first connect to a frontend application that redirects to a video URL. The video URL contains an authorization token in CloudFront. The cache is activated on the CloudFront distribution. Authorization token check activity needs to be logged in Amazon CloudWatch. The company wants to prevent direct access to video files on CloudFront and Amazon S3 and wants to implement checks of the authorization token that the frontend application provides. The company also wants to perform regular rolling updates of the code that checks the authorization token signature. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家视频平台公司正在将其视频目录迁移到 AWS。该公司将在 Amazon S3 存储桶中托管 MP4 视频文件， 并使用 Amazon CloudFront 和 Amazon EC2 实例来提供视频文件。 用户首先连接到前端应用程序，该程序会重定向到视频 URL。视频 URL 中包含 CloudFront 中的授 权令牌。CloudFront 分发中的缓存已激活。授权令牌检查活动需要在 Amazon CloudWatch 中进行 记录。 该公司希望阻止对 CloudFront 和 Amazon S3 上视频文件的直接访问，并希望对前端应用程序提供的 授权令牌进行检查。该公司还希望定期滚动更新用于检查授权令牌签名的代码。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Implement an authorization token check in Lambda@Edge as a trigger on the CloudFront distribution. Enable CloudWatch logging for the Lambda@Edge function. Attach the Lambda@Edge function to the CloudFront distribution. Implement CloudFront continuous deployment to perform updates.","B":"Implement an authorization token check in CloudFront Functions. Enable CloudWatch logging for the CloudFront function. Attach the CloudFront function to the CloudFront distribution. Implement CloudFront continuous deployment to perform updates.","C":"Implement an authorization token check in the application code that is installed on the EC2 instances. Install the CloudWatch agent on the EC2 instances. Configure the application to log to the CloudWatch agent. Implement a second CloudFront distribution. Migrate the traffic from the first CloudFront distribution by using Amazon Route 53 weighted routing.","D":"Implement an authorization token check in CloudFront Functions. Enable CloudWatch logging for the CloudFront function. Attach the CloudFront function to the CloudFront distribution. Implement a second CloudFront distribution. Migrate the traffic from the first CloudFront distribution by using Amazon Route 53 weighted routing."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFront 分发上作为触发器在 Lambda@Edge 中实现授权令牌检查。为 Lambda@Edge 函数启 用 CloudWatch 日志记录。将 Lambda@Edge 函数附加到 CloudFront 分发。实现 CloudFront 持续部 署以执行更新。","B":"在 CloudFront 函数中实现授权令牌检查。为 CloudFront 函数启用 CloudWatch 日志记录。将 CloudFront 函数附加到 CloudFront 分发。实现 CloudFront 持续部署以执行更新。","C":"在安装于 EC2 实例上的应用程序代码中实现授权令牌检查。在 EC2 实例上安装 CloudWatch 代理。 将应用程序配置为向 CloudWatch 代理进行日志记录。实现第二个 CloudFront 分发。使用 Amazon Route 53 加权路由将流量从第一个 CloudFront 分发迁移到第二个。","D":"在 CloudFront 函数中实现授权令牌检查。为 CloudFront 函数启用 CloudWatch 日志记录。将 CloudFront 函数附加到 CloudFront 分发。实现第二个 CloudFront 分发。使用 Amazon Route 53 加权 路由将流量从第一个 CloudFront 分发迁移到第二个。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Migration","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: validate an authorization token at the CloudFront edge (so direct access to S3/CloudFront is blocked), log the check activity to CloudWatch, and perform regular rolling updates of the signature-checking code with the LEAST operational effort. AWS lists 'Request authorization - Validate hashed authorization tokens, such as JSON web tokens (JWT)' as a primary CloudFront Functions use case and publishes an official example 'Validate a simple token in a CloudFront Functions viewer request,' so CloudFront Functions is the lightweight, AWS-recommended choice for this exact task (sub-millisecond, no IAM execution role, no cross-Region replication, and it can be built/tested entirely within CloudFront). CloudFront Functions automatically sends console.log() output to CloudWatch Logs, satisfying the logging requirement. For rolling updates, CloudFront continuous deployment is purpose-built: a staging distribution plus a continuous deployment policy let you weight-route a percentage of production traffic to validate updated configuration, and the docs explicitly state you can update external resources referenced by the distribution 'such as ... a CloudFront function.' Option B combines the lightweight function, native CloudWatch logging, and the built-in deployment mechanism, so it meets every requirement with the least operational effort.","explanation_zh":"需求為：在 CloudFront 邊緣驗證授權 token（藉此阻擋對 S3/CloudFront 的直接存取）、將檢查活動記錄到 CloudWatch，並以「最少維運工作量」對簽章檢查程式碼進行定期滾動更新。AWS 將「Request authorization - 驗證雜湊授權 token，例如 JSON web token (JWT)」列為 CloudFront Functions 的主要使用情境，並發佈官方範例『Validate a simple token in a CloudFront Functions viewer request』，因此 CloudFront Functions 正是此任務輕量且為 AWS 推薦的選擇（次毫秒延遲、不需 IAM 執行角色、不需跨區複寫，且可完全在 CloudFront 內建置與測試）。CloudFront Functions 會自動把 console.log() 輸出送到 CloudWatch Logs，滿足日誌需求。至於滾動更新，CloudFront continuous deployment 正是為此設計：透過 staging distribution 加上 continuous deployment policy，可用加權方式把部分正式流量導向以驗證更新後的設定；文件明確指出可更新 distribution 所引用的外部資源，例如『a CloudFront function』。選項 B 結合輕量函式、原生 CloudWatch 日誌與內建部署機制，因此以最少維運工作量滿足所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Lambda@Edge can also validate tokens and log to CloudWatch, and it works with continuous deployment, but it is heavier than CloudFront Functions for simple token validation: it requires an IAM execution role, is replicated cross-Region, has higher latency/cost, and cannot be fully built/tested within CloudFront. AWS recommends CloudFront Functions for hashed-token authorization, so A involves more operational effort than B.","why_zh":"Lambda@Edge 同樣能驗證 token 並寫入 CloudWatch，也可搭配 continuous deployment，但對於簡單的 token 驗證它比 CloudFront Functions 笨重：需要 IAM 執行角色、會跨區複寫、延遲與成本較高，且無法完全在 CloudFront 內建置與測試。AWS 對雜湊 token 授權推薦使用 CloudFront Functions，因此 A 的維運工作量高於 B。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Performing the token check in EC2 application code happens at the origin/application layer, not at the CloudFront edge, so it does not prevent direct access to CloudFront or S3 content as required. It also relies on a second CloudFront distribution plus Route 53 weighted routing for updates, which is far more operational effort than native continuous deployment.","why_zh":"在 EC2 應用程式碼中做 token 檢查是發生在來源/應用層，而非 CloudFront 邊緣，因此無法依需求阻擋對 CloudFront 或 S3 內容的直接存取。它還需用第二個 CloudFront distribution 加 Route 53 加權路由來做更新，維運工作量遠高於原生 continuous deployment。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The function and logging parts are correct, but using a second CloudFront distribution with Route 53 weighted routing to roll out updates is substantially more operational effort than CloudFront's built-in continuous deployment, which natively supports weight-based traffic shifting and updating a referenced CloudFront function. This fails the 'LEAST operational effort' qualifier compared to B.","why_zh":"函式與日誌部分正確，但用第二個 CloudFront distribution 搭配 Route 53 加權路由來推送更新，比 CloudFront 內建的 continuous deployment（原生支援加權流量轉移與更新所引用的 CloudFront function）維運工作量大很多。相較 B，未能滿足「最少維運工作量」這個條件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/edge-functions-choosing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/edge-functions-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/example_cloudfront_functions_kvs_jwt_verify_section.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/understanding-continuous-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/working-with-staging-distribution-continuous-deployment-policy.html"]}},{"id":351,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts in a hierarchical structure. An SCP that is associated with the organization root allows IAM users to be created. A DevOps team must be able to create IAM users with any level of permissions. Developers must also be able to create IAM users. However, developers must not be able to grant new IAM users excessive permissions. The developers have the CreateAndManageUsers role in each account. The DevOps team must be able to prevent other users from creating IAM users. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来以分层结构管理多个 AWS 账户。与组织根关联的一个 服务控制策略（SCP）允许创建 IAM 用户。 DevOps 团队必须能够创建具有任何权限级别的 IAM 用户。开发人员也必须能够创建 IAM 用户。然而， 开发人员不得向新创建的 IAM 用户授予过多权限。开发人员在每个账户中都具有“创建和管理用户” 角色。DevOps 团队必须能够阻止其他用户创建 IAM 用户。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an SCP in the organization to deny users the ability to create and modify IAM users. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization. Attach the CreateAndManageUsers role to developers.","B":"Create an SCP in the organization to grant users that have the DeveloperBoundary policy attached the ability to create new IAM users and to modify IAM users. Configure the SCP to require users to attach the PermissionBoundaries policy to any new IAM user. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","C":"Create an IAM permissions policy named PermissionBoundaries within each account. Configure the PermissionBoundaries policy to specify the maximum permissions that a developer can grant to a new IAM user.","D":"Create an IAM permissions policy named PermissionBoundaries within each account. Configure PermissionsBoundaries to allow users who have the PermissionBoundaries policy to create new IAM users.","E":"Create an IAM permissions policy named DeveloperBoundary within each account. Configure the DeveloperBoundary policy to allow developers to create IAM users and to assign policies to IAM users of only if the developer includes the PermissionBoundaries policy as the permissions boundary. Attach the DeveloperBoundary policy to the CreateAndManageUsers role within each account."},"options_zh":{"A":"在组织中创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止用户创建和修改 IAM 用户。将该 SCP 附加到组织的 根目录。将 CreateAndManageUsers 角色附加到开发人员。","B":"在组织内创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），授予附加了“DeveloperBoundary”策略的用户创建新 IAM 用户以及修改 IAM 用户的权限。配置该 SCP，要求用户在创建任何新 IAM 用户时附加 “PermissionBoundaries”策略。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","C":"在每个账户中创建一个名为“PermissionBoundaries”的 IAM 权限策略。配置“PermissionBoundaries” 策略以指定开发人员可以授予新 IAM 用户的最大权限。","D":"在每个账户中创建一个名为“PermissionBoundaries”的 IAM 权限策略。配置“PermissionBoundarie s”，允许拥有“PermissionBoundaries”策略的用户创建新的 IAM 用户。","E":"在每个账户中创建一个名为“DeveloperBoundary”的 IAM 权限策略。将 DeveloperBoundary 策略配置 为仅当开发人员将“PermissionBoundaries”策略作为权限边界包含在内时，才允许开发人员创建 IAM 用户并向 IAM 用户分配策略。在每个账户中将 DeveloperBoundary 策略附加到 “CreateAndManageUsers”角色。"},"answer":["C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This question maps one-to-one onto the canonical 'Delegating responsibility to others using permissions boundaries' example in the IAM User Guide. Option C creates the PermissionBoundaries managed policy (the doc's XCompanyBoundaries) that defines the MAXIMUM permissions any new IAM user can be granted - this caps what a developer can hand to a new user. Option E creates the DeveloperBoundary policy (the doc's DelegatedUserBoundary) and attaches it to the developers' CreateAndManageUsers role; its CreateOrChangeOnlyWithBoundary statement allows iam:CreateUser, iam:AttachUserPolicy, iam:PutUserPolicy, etc. only when the request carries the StringEquals condition iam:PermissionsBoundary = the PermissionBoundaries ARN. Together this lets developers create users but never grant them more than the boundary allows, while the DevOps team (with its own broader identity policy and no such restricting boundary) can still create users with any level of permissions. The key distinction: a permissions boundary sets the maximum but never grants permissions on its own - the grant plus the iam:PermissionsBoundary condition must live in the delegate's identity policy (Option E), and the cap must live in the separate boundary policy (Option C).","explanation_zh":"本題與 IAM User Guide 中經典範例『Delegating responsibility to others using permissions boundaries』一一對應。Option C 建立 PermissionBoundaries 受管政策（即文件中的 XCompanyBoundaries），用來定義任何新 IAM user 可被授予的最大權限，藉此限制開發人員能交給新 user 的權限上限。Option E 建立 DeveloperBoundary 政策（即文件中的 DelegatedUserBoundary）並附加到開發人員的 CreateAndManageUsers role；其 CreateOrChangeOnlyWithBoundary 陳述只在請求帶有 StringEquals 條件 iam:PermissionsBoundary 等於 PermissionBoundaries ARN 時，才允許 iam:CreateUser、iam:AttachUserPolicy、iam:PutUserPolicy 等動作。兩者結合後，開發人員可建立 user，但無法授予超過 boundary 允許的權限；而 DevOps 團隊因為有自己較寬的 identity policy 且未受此限制性 boundary 約束，仍可建立任意權限等級的 user。關鍵區別：permissions boundary 只設定上限，本身不會授權，因此授權動作與 iam:PermissionsBoundary 條件必須放在委派者（delegate）的 identity policy（Option E），而上限則放在獨立的 boundary policy（Option C）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An SCP at the organization root that denies creating/modifying IAM users applies to ALL principals in the affected accounts, including the DevOps team - an explicit Deny in an SCP cannot be overridden by any IAM policy. This would block the DevOps team from creating users with any permissions, violating a core requirement. The 'Attach the CreateAndManageUsers role to developers' clause is also redundant since the developers already have that role in each account.","why_zh":"在組織 root 套用 SCP 拒絕建立/修改 IAM user 會作用於受影響帳戶中的所有 principal，包含 DevOps 團隊；SCP 中的明確 Deny 無法被任何 IAM policy 覆寫。這會使 DevOps 團隊無法建立任意權限的 user，違反核心需求。且『將 CreateAndManageUsers role 附加給開發者』也屬多餘，因為開發者在每個帳戶中已擁有該 role。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"SCPs never grant permissions - they only set guardrails (the maximum allowable permissions) and must be paired with IAM identity-based policies that actually grant access. The wording 'grant users the ability to create new IAM users' fundamentally misrepresents how SCPs work. The grant plus the iam:PermissionsBoundary requirement belongs in the developer's identity policy (Option E), not in an SCP.","why_zh":"SCP 從不授予權限，它只設定防護界限（允許的最大權限），必須搭配真正授權的 IAM identity-based policy。『grant users the ability to create new IAM users』的措辭根本性地誤解了 SCP 的運作方式。授權動作與強制 iam:PermissionsBoundary 的需求應放在開發人員的 identity policy（Option E），而非 SCP。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"This conflates the boundary policy with the delegate's grant. The PermissionBoundaries policy's job is to cap what a NEW user receives (the doc's XCompanyBoundaries / Task 1), not to allow the developer to create users. A permissions boundary does not grant permissions on its own, and the create-user delegation with the iam:PermissionsBoundary condition must live in the DeveloperBoundary/identity policy (Task 2), not in the boundary policy itself.","why_zh":"此選項混淆了 boundary policy 與委派者的授權。PermissionBoundaries 政策的作用是限制新 user 所獲得的權限上限（即文件的 XCompanyBoundaries / Task 1），而非允許開發人員建立 user。Permissions boundary 本身不會授權，且帶有 iam:PermissionsBoundary 條件的建立 user 委派必須放在 DeveloperBoundary/identity policy（Task 2），而非 boundary policy 本身。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies_boundaries.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/access_policies.html"]}},{"id":352,"question_en":"A company has deployed a landing zone that has a well-defined AWS Organizations structure and an SCP. The company's development team can create their AWS resources only by using AWS CloudFormation and the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK). A DevOps engineer notices that Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queues that are deployed in different CloudFormation stacks have different configurations. The DevOps engineer also notices that the application cost allocation tag is not always set. The DevOps engineer needs a solution that will enforce tagging and promote the reuse of code. The DevOps engineer needs to avoid different configurations for the deployed SQS queues. What should the DevOps engineer do to meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司已部署了一个着陆区，该着陆区具有明确的 AWS 组织结构和 SCP。该公司的开发团队只能 通过使用 AWS CloudFormation 和 AWS 云开发工具包（AWS CDK）来创建其 AWS 资源。 一位 DevOps 工程师注意到，部署在不同 CloudFormation 堆栈中的 Amazon Simple Queue Service （Amazon SQS）队列具有不同的配置。该 DevOps 工程师还发现，应用程序成本分配标签并非总是设置。 DevOps 工程师需要一个解决方案来强制执行标签使用并促进代码复用。DevOps 工程师需要避免为 部署的 SQS 队列设置不同的配置。 DevOps 工程师应如何做才能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Organizations tag policy to enforce the cost allocation tag in CloudFormation stacks. Instruct the development team to use CloudFormation to define SQS queues. Instruct the development team to deploy the SQS queues by using CloudFormation StackSets.","B":"Update the SCP to enforce the cost allocation tag in CloudFormation stacks. Instruct the development team to use CloudFormation modules to define SQS queues. Instruct the development team to deploy the SQS queues by using CloudFormation stacks.","C":"Use AWS CDK tagging to enforce the cost allocation tag in CloudFormation StackSets. Instruct the development team to use the AWS CDK to define SQS queues. Instruct the development team to deploy the SQS queues by using CDK stacks.","D":"Use AWS CDK tagging to enforce the cost allocation tag in CloudFormation stacks. Instruct the development team to use the AWS CDK to define SQS queues. Instruct the development team to deploy the SQS queues by using CDK feature flags."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个组织标签策略，以强制在 CloudFormation 堆栈中使用成本分配标签。指示开发团队使用 CloudFormation 来定义 SQS 队列。指示开发团队通过使用 CloudFormation 堆栈集来部署 SQS 队列。","B":"更新 SCP 以强制在 CloudFormation 堆栈中使用成本分配标签。指示开发团队使用 CloudFormation 模 块来定义 SQS 队列。指示开发团队通过使用 CloudFormation 堆栈来部署 SQS 队列。","C":"使用 AWS CDK 标签在 CloudFormation StackSets 中强制执行成本分配标签。指示开发团队使用 AWS CDK 定义 SQS 队列。指示开发团队通过使用 CDK 堆栈部署 SQS 队列。","D":"使用 AWS CDK 标签在 CloudFormation 堆栈中强制执行成本分配标签。指示开发团队使用 AWS CDK 定义 SQS 队列。指示开发团队通过使用 CDK 功能标志来部署 SQS 队列。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Two requirements must be satisfied: hard-enforce the cost-allocation tag and promote code reuse so SQS queues stop diverging. CloudFormation modules are purpose-built to 'package resource configurations for inclusion across stack templates, in a transparent, manageable, and repeatable way,' encapsulating one standard SQS configuration that every team reuses across templates and accounts; this directly fixes the divergent-configuration problem, and tags specified at the stack level are assigned to the resources derived from the module. Genuine enforcement of the tag in an Organizations landing zone is best done with an SCP Deny that uses an aws:RequestTag / aws:TagKeys (e.g., Null) condition to block resource creation when the cost-allocation tag is absent, because SCPs are the coarse-grained org-wide guardrail. Option B combines both correctly (SCP enforcement plus CloudFormation modules for reusable, consistent SQS definitions deployed via normal stacks). The dump's suggested C fails because CDK Tags.of().add() is opt-in code, not enforcement, and CDK alone does not stop teams from authoring divergent queues.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個需求：硬性強制套用成本分攤標籤，並促進程式碼重用以避免 SQS 設定持續分歧。CloudFormation modules 專門用來『以透明、可管理、可重複的方式封裝資源設定供多個 stack 範本引用』，把一套標準 SQS 設定封裝成可跨範本與帳戶重用的建構區塊，直接解決設定分歧問題；而在 stack 層級指定的標籤會傳遞到 module 產生的資源。在 Organizations landing zone 中，標籤的真正強制最好由 SCP 的 Deny 搭配 aws:RequestTag / aws:TagKeys（例如 Null）條件，在缺少成本分攤標籤時阻擋資源建立，因為 SCP 正是組織層級的粗粒度護欄。選項 B 正確結合兩者（SCP 強制 + CloudFormation modules 提供可重用且一致的 SQS 定義，以一般 stack 部署）。題庫建議的 C 不成立，因為 CDK Tags.of().add() 是可選的程式碼而非強制，且單靠 CDK 無法阻止各團隊撰寫分歧的佇列設定。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Organizations tag policies only standardize the case/values of tags that are already applied; the docs state 'Untagged resources or tags that aren't defined in the tag policy aren't evaluated for compliance,' so a tag policy cannot force the cost-allocation tag to be present. StackSets is for multi-account/Region replication of a template, not for standardizing a single resource configuration or promoting code reuse within stacks.","why_zh":"Organizations tag policy 只標準化已套用標籤的大小寫/值；文件明言『未加標籤的資源或未定義於 tag policy 的標籤不會被評估合規性』，因此無法強制成本分攤標籤必須存在。StackSets 用於跨帳戶/區域複製範本，並非用來標準化單一資源設定或在 stack 內促進程式碼重用。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CDK Tags.of().add() applies tags but is opt-in code, not enforcement: a developer who omits the call simply ships an untagged queue and nothing blocks it. 'CDK tagging to enforce the cost allocation tag in CloudFormation StackSets' is also a confused construction, and CDK by itself does not prevent divergent SQS configurations across teams. This is the dump's suggested answer, but it fails the 'enforce' requirement.","why_zh":"CDK 的 Tags.of().add() 會套用標籤，但屬於可選的程式碼而非強制：開發者若省略該呼叫，就會部署未加標籤的佇列且無任何阻擋。『用 CDK tagging 在 CloudFormation StackSets 中強制成本分攤標籤』也是混淆的說法，且單靠 CDK 無法防止各團隊出現分歧的 SQS 設定。此為題庫建議答案，但未滿足『強制』需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Deploying SQS queues 'by using CDK feature flags' is technically nonsensical: CDK feature flags are context values in cdk.json that toggle breaking/legacy CDK behaviors, not a deployment mechanism. CDK tagging is also non-enforcing opt-in code, so this fails the enforcement requirement too.","why_zh":"『用 CDK feature flags 部署 SQS 佇列』在技術上不成立：CDK feature flags 是 cdk.json 中用來切換破壞性/舊版 CDK 行為的 context 值，並非部署機制。CDK tagging 同樣是非強制的可選程式碼，因此同樣未滿足強制需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/modules.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/modules-using.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_tag-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/v2/guide/tagging.html"]}},{"id":353,"question_en":"A DevOps team manages a company's AWS account. The company wants to ensure that specific AWS resource configuration changes are automatically reverted. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队管理着一家公司的 AWS 账户。该公司希望确保特定的 AWS 资源配置更改能够自 动回滚。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS Config rules to detect changes in resource configurations. Configure remediation action that uses AWS Systems Manager Automation documents to revert the configuration changes.","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch alarms to monitor resource metrics. When an alarm is activated, use an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify an administrator to manually reverts the configuration changes.","C":"Use AWS CloudFormation to create a stack that deploys the necessary configuration changes. Update the stack when configuration changes need to be reverted.","D":"Use AWS Trusted Advisor to check for noncompliant configurations. Manually apply necessary changes based on Trusted Advisor recommendations."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Config 规则检测资源配置的变化。配置使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 文档来还 原配置更改的修复操作。","B":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch 警报来监控资源指标。当警报被触发时，使用 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）主题通知管理员手动还原配置更改。","C":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 创建一个堆栈来部署必要的配置更改。当需要撤销配置更改时，更新该堆 栈。","D":"使用 AWS 可信顾问检查不符合规定的配置。根据可信顾问的建议手动应用必要的更改。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to AUTOMATICALLY revert specific resource configuration changes, which requires both continuous DETECTION of the change and an UNATTENDED corrective action. AWS Config continuously records resource configuration changes and evaluates them with AWS Config rules to determine compliance. When a rule flags a resource as noncompliant, AWS Config applies remediation using AWS Systems Manager Automation documents; the AWS Config docs explicitly state these documents 'define the actions to be performed on noncompliant AWS resources.' By enabling Auto remediation on the rule, AWS Config runs the SSM Automation runbook with no human intervention (with optional retries) to revert the resource to the desired state. Option A is the only choice that both detects the change and automatically reverts it; every other option ends with a manual human action.","explanation_zh":"需求是要「自動還原」特定資源組態變更，這同時需要持續「偵測」變更，並執行無需人工介入的修正動作。AWS Config 會持續記錄資源組態變更，並透過 AWS Config rules 評估其合規性。當規則將資源標記為不合規時，AWS Config 會使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation documents 套用修正；AWS Config 文件明確指出這些 documents「定義要對不合規 AWS 資源執行的動作」。在規則上啟用 Auto remediation 後，AWS Config 會自動執行 SSM Automation runbook（可選擇重試），無需人工介入即可將資源還原為期望狀態。選項 A 是唯一同時能偵測變更並自動還原的方案；其餘選項最後都需人工手動操作。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CloudWatch alarms monitor metrics/thresholds, not resource configuration state, and the workflow ends by notifying an administrator to MANUALLY revert the change. This violates the 'automatically reverted' requirement, and an SNS notification has no built-in revert capability.","why_zh":"CloudWatch alarms 監控的是指標/閾值而非資源組態狀態，且流程最終是通知管理員「手動」還原變更，違反「自動還原」需求；SNS 通知本身也無內建還原功能。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CloudFormation deploys configuration but does not continuously detect out-of-band changes and auto-correct them. The option itself says you must UPDATE the stack to revert, which is a manual operator-initiated action; CloudFormation drift detection only reports drift, it does not automatically revert it.","why_zh":"CloudFormation 用於部署組態，但不會持續偵測帶外（out-of-band）變更並自動修正。選項本身說明需「更新」堆疊才能還原，屬由操作人員發起的人工動作；CloudFormation drift detection 僅回報偏移，並不會自動還原。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Trusted Advisor surfaces noncompliant or suboptimal configurations as recommendations on a limited set of checks, but the option explicitly says to 'Manually apply necessary changes,' which fails the 'automatically reverted' requirement. Trusted Advisor does not run revert automation on resources.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 會以建議形式呈現有限檢查項目的不合規或非最佳組態，但此選項明確指出要「手動套用必要變更」，不符合「自動還原」需求；Trusted Advisor 不會在資源上執行還原自動化。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/remediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/WhatIsConfig.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/how-does-config-work.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-automation.html"]}},{"id":354,"question_en":"A company hosts an application in its AWS account. The application uses an Amazon S3 bucket to store objects that contain sensitive information. The company needs to capture object-level S3 API calls, including calls that are rejected because the calls were made by using credentials that are not valid. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在其 AWS 账户中托管了一个应用程序。该应用程序使用一个 Amazon S3 存储桶来存储包含 敏感信息的对象。 该公司需要捕获对象级别的 S3 API 调用，包括因使用无效凭证而被拒绝的调用。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail in the account. Enable S3 data events logging. Configure the trail to log to Amazon CloudWatch.","B":"Create a new S3 bucket. Configure access logging on the application's S3 bucket. Deliver the access logs to the new S3 bucket.","C":"Configure Amazon GuardDuty with S3 protection enabled for the account. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that matches findings that are associated with the S3 bucket. Configure the rule to use an Amazon Simple Queue Service (Amazon SQS) queue as the target.","D":"Create an AWS CloudTrail trail and a new S3 bucket in the account. Configure the trail to log to the S3 new bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"在账户中创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪。启用 S3 数据事件日志记录。将跟踪配置为记录到 Amazon CloudWatch。","B":"创建一个新的 S3 存储桶。在应用程序的 S3 存储桶上配置访问日志记录。将访问日志传递到新的 S3 存储桶。","C":"为账户配置启用 S3 保护功能的 Amazon GuardDuty。创建一个与 S3 存储桶相关联的发现相匹配的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。将规则配置为使用 Amazon Simple Queue Service（Amazon SQS）队 列作为目标。","D":"在账户中创建一个 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪和一个新的 S3 存储桶。将跟踪配置为记录到新的 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to capture object-level S3 API calls, including calls rejected because they used invalid credentials. Object-level S3 operations such as GetObject, PutObject, and DeleteObject are CloudTrail data events, and by default a CloudTrail trail does not log data events (it logs only management/bucket-level events). CloudTrail records every API request, including attempts that fail authentication or authorization, and writes errorCode/errorMessage (for example AccessDenied) into the event, so rejected and invalid-credential calls are captured. Option A is the only choice that explicitly enables S3 data events, which is the decisive requirement for object-level capture; delivering the trail to CloudWatch Logs is a supported CloudTrail configuration. Option D uses the same CloudTrail pattern but never enables data events, so it would capture only bucket-level management events, not object-level activity, making it incomplete.","explanation_zh":"需求是擷取物件層級 (object-level) 的 S3 API 呼叫，包含因為使用無效憑證而被拒絕的呼叫。GetObject、PutObject、DeleteObject 等物件層級操作屬於 CloudTrail data events，而 trail 預設不會記錄 data events（只記錄 management／值區層級事件）。CloudTrail 會記錄每一個 API 請求，包括驗證或授權失敗的嘗試，並把 errorCode/errorMessage（例如 AccessDenied）寫入事件，因此被拒絕及無效憑證的呼叫都會被擷取。選項 A 是唯一明確啟用 S3 data events 的選項，而這正是物件層級擷取的關鍵需求；將 trail 傳送到 CloudWatch Logs 是 CloudTrail 支援的設定。選項 D 雖然同樣是 CloudTrail 模式，但沒有啟用 data events，所以只會記錄值區層級的 management 事件，無法涵蓋物件層級活動，因此不完整。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"S3 server access logging is best-effort (delivery is not guaranteed or complete) and is not the AWS-recommended mechanism for an auditable API record with identity attribution. It does not reliably capture object-level API calls rejected due to invalid credentials, unlike CloudTrail data events which record errorCode such as AccessDenied.","why_zh":"S3 server access logging 是 best-effort（傳遞不保證完整），並非 AWS 建議用來做帶有身分歸屬的可稽核 API 記錄機制。它無法可靠地擷取因憑證無效而被拒絕的物件層級 API 呼叫，而 CloudTrail data events 會記錄如 AccessDenied 的 errorCode。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"GuardDuty with S3 protection produces threat-detection findings by analyzing data events; it does not capture or store a complete record of every object-level S3 API call. It surfaces suspicious activity, not a comprehensive log of all calls including routine rejected ones.","why_zh":"啟用 S3 protection 的 GuardDuty 透過分析 data events 產生威脅偵測 findings，並不會擷取或保存每一個物件層級 S3 API 呼叫的完整記錄。它呈現的是可疑活動，而非包含一般被拒絕呼叫在內的完整呼叫記錄。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating a CloudTrail trail that logs to S3 without enabling S3 data events captures only management (bucket-level) events, not object-level operations like GetObject/PutObject/DeleteObject. The requirement explicitly demands object-level capture, so D is incomplete.","why_zh":"建立寫入 S3 的 CloudTrail trail 但沒有啟用 S3 data events，只會擷取 management（值區層級）事件，無法擷取 GetObject/PutObject/DeleteObject 等物件層級操作。需求明確要求物件層級擷取，因此 D 不完整。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/logging-data-events-with-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-logging-s3-info.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/enable-cloudtrail-logging-for-s3.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/send-cloudtrail-events-to-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-user-guide.html"]}},{"id":355,"question_en":"A DevOps administrator is responsible for managing the security of a company's Amazon CloudWatch Logs log groups. The company's security policy states that employee IDs must not be visible in logs except by authorized personnel. Employee IDs follow the pattern of Emp-XXXXXX, where each X is a digit. An audit discovered that employee IDs are found in a single log file. The log file is available to engineers, but the engineers are not authorized to view employee IDs. Engineers currently have an AWS IAM Identity Center permission that allows logs:* on all resources in the account. The administrator must mask the employee ID so that new log entries that contain the employee ID are not visible to unauthorized personnel. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"DevOps 管理员负责管理公司 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组的安全。公司的安全政策规定，员工 ID 除 授权人员外不得在日志中显示。员工 ID 的格式为 Emp-XXXXXX，其中每个 X 代表一位数字。 一次审计发现员工 ID 出现在一个单独的日志文件中。该日志文件可供工程师访问，但工程师无权查看 员工 ID。目前，工程师拥有一个 AWS IAM 身份中心权限，允许其对账户中的所有资源执行日志操作。 管理员必须对员工 ID 进行屏蔽，以确保包含员工 ID 的新日志条目不会被未经授权的人员看到。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new data protection policy on the log group. Add an Emp-\\d{6} custom data identifier configuration. Create an IAM policy that has a Deny action for the Action\":\"logs:Unmask\" permission on the resource. Attach the policy to the engineering accounts.","B":"Create a new data protection policy on the log group. Add managed data identifiers for the personal data category. Create an IAM policy that has a Deny action for the \"NotAction\":\"logs:Unmask\" permission on the resource. Attach the policy to the engineering accounts.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to parse a log file entry, remove the employee ID, and write the results to a new log file. Create a Lambda subscription filter on the log group and select the Lambda function. Grant the lambda:InvokeFunction permission to the log group.","D":"Create an Amazon Data Firehose delivery stream that has an Amazon S3 bucket as the destination. Create a Firehose subscription filter on the log group that uses the Firehose delivery stream. Remove the \"logs:*\" permission on the engineering accounts. Create an Amazon Macie job on the S3 bucket that has an Emp-\\d{6} custom identifier."},"options_zh":{"A":"在日志组上创建新的数据保护策略。添加一个 Emp-\\d{6} 自定义数据标识符配置。创建一个 IAM 策 略，该策略对资源上的“Action\":\"logs:Unmask\" 权限具有拒绝操作。将该策略附加到工程账户。","B":"在日志组上创建新的数据保护策略。为个人数据类别添加托管数据标识符。创建一个 IAM 策略， 该策略对资源具有“NotAction”为“logs:Unmask”的拒绝操作。将该策略附加到工程账户。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来解析日志文件条目，移除员工 ID，并将结果写入新的日志文件。在 日志组上创建一个 Lambda 订阅筛选器，并选择该 Lambda 函数。向日志组授予 lambda: InvokeFunction 权限。","D":"创建一个将 Amazon S3 存储桶作为目标的 Amazon Data Firehose 传输流。在日志组上创建一个使用 该 Firehose 传输流的订阅筛选器。移除工程账户上的“logs:*”权限。在具有 Emp-\\d{6} 自定义标 识符的 S3 存储桶上创建一个 Amazon Macie 任务。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Employee IDs in the form Emp-XXXXXX are a company-specific value, and AWS docs state explicitly that CloudWatch Logs custom data identifiers (a custom regex) are the way to detect 'company-specific employee IDs' that managed data identifiers cannot cover; the docs even give the parallel example regex EmployeeID-\\d{9}, so Emp-\\d{6} is the correct CDI. Once a data protection policy masks data, it is masked at all egress points (Logs Insights, metric filters, subscription filters) for newly ingested events, and only principals holding logs:Unmask can reveal it. Because the engineers already have logs:* (which includes logs:Unmask), the administrator attaches an IAM policy with an explicit Deny on the Action logs:Unmask; an explicit Deny always overrides an Allow, so engineers see only masked employee IDs. This is the native, lowest-overhead solution with no custom code or extra infrastructure, satisfying MOST operational efficiency.","explanation_zh":"Emp-XXXXXX（六位數字）是公司專屬的值，AWS 文件明確指出要偵測 managed data identifiers 無法涵蓋的「company-specific employee IDs」必須使用 CloudWatch Logs custom data identifier（自訂 regex），文件甚至給出對應範例 regex EmployeeID-\\d{9}，因此 Emp-\\d{6} 就是正確的 CDI。一旦 data protection policy 進行 masking，新攝取的事件會在所有 egress 點（Logs Insights、metric filters、subscription filters）被遮罩，只有具備 logs:Unmask 權限的 principal 才能還原。由於工程師已擁有 logs:*（包含 logs:Unmask），管理員加上一條對 Action logs:Unmask 明確 Deny 的 IAM policy；明確 Deny 永遠覆蓋 Allow，因此工程師只能看到被遮罩的 employee ID。這是原生、最低營運成本的方案，無需自訂程式碼或額外基礎設施，符合 MOST operational efficiency。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Managed data identifiers in the 'personal' category are predefined types (Address, EmailAddress, Name, SSN, driver's license, etc.) and do NOT include company-specific employee IDs; that requires a custom data identifier. Also, an IAM Deny statement with \"NotAction\":\"logs:Unmask\" denies every action EXCEPT logs:Unmask, which is inverted logic: it would still leave logs:Unmask allowed (so engineers could unmask) while breaking their other logs permissions.","why_zh":"personal 類別的 managed data identifiers 是預先定義的類型（Address、EmailAddress、Name、SSN、駕照等），並不包含公司專屬的 employee ID；這需要 custom data identifier。此外，IAM Deny 搭配 \"NotAction\":\"logs:Unmask\" 會拒絕除了 logs:Unmask 以外的所有動作，邏輯相反：仍會讓 logs:Unmask 被允許（工程師仍可 unmask），同時破壞其他 logs 權限。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A Lambda subscription filter that parses each entry, strips the employee ID, and writes to a new log group is high operational overhead (custom code to build, deploy, and maintain). It does not mask the original log group's new entries, and is far less efficient than the native data protection masking feature.","why_zh":"用 Lambda subscription filter 解析每筆項目、移除 employee ID 並寫到新 log group 屬於高營運成本（需建置、部署與維護程式碼）。它不會遮罩原始 log group 的新項目，效率遠低於原生的 data protection masking 功能。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Firehose to S3 plus an Amazon Macie job is heavy infrastructure that only inspects data copied to S3, not the CloudWatch log group itself; Macie audits/discovers sensitive data but does not mask it in place in CloudWatch Logs, so engineers viewing the live log group would still see employee IDs. Removing logs:* entirely is also overly broad. Highest operational overhead.","why_zh":"Firehose 到 S3 再加 Amazon Macie job 是龐大的基礎設施，只檢查複製到 S3 的資料，而非 CloudWatch log group 本身；Macie 會稽核/發現敏感資料但不會在 CloudWatch Logs 原地遮罩，因此工程師檢視即時 log group 仍會看到 employee ID。完全移除 logs:* 也過於廣泛。營運成本最高。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL-custom-data-identifiers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/mask-sensitive-log-data.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/data-protection-policy-permissions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CWL-managed-data-identifiers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_notaction.html"]}},{"id":356,"question_en":"A company uses an organization in AWS Organizations to manage many AWS accounts. The company has enabled all features for the organization. The company uses AWS CloudFormation StackSets to deploy configurations to the accounts. The company uses AWS Config to monitor an Amazon S3 bucket. The company needs to ensure that all object uploads to the S3 bucket use AWS Key Management Service (AWS KMS) encryption. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 中的一个组织来管理多个 AWS 账户。该公司已为该组织启用所有功 能。该公司使用 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 将配置部署到这些账户。该公司使用 AWS Config 来监 控一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。 该公司需要确保所有上传至 S3 存储桶的对象都使用 AWS 密钥管理服务（AWS KMS）进行加密。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Config conformance pack that includes the s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled rule. Deploy the conformance pack to the accounts. Configure the rule to target an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","B":"Create an SCP that includes a deny statement for the s3:createBucket action and a condition statement where s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption is not aws:kms. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization.","C":"Create an AWS CloudFormation stack set to enable an AWS CloudTrail trail to capture S3 data events for the organization. In the stack set, create an Amazon EventBridge rule to match S3 PutObject events that do not use AWS KMS encryption. Configure the rule to target an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic.","D":"Create an SCP that includes a deny statement for the s3:putObject action and a condition where s3:x- amz-server-side-encryption is not aws:kms. Attach the SCP to the root of the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个包含 s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled 规则的 AWS Config 合规性包。将合规性包部署 到各个账户。配置该规则以针对 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。","B":"创建一个 SCP，其中包含对 s3:createBucket 操作的拒绝声明以及一个条件声明，即 s3:x-amz-server- side-encryption 不为 aws:kms。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。","C":"创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 栈集，以启用 AWS CloudTrail 跟踪来捕获组织的 S3 数据事件。在该栈 集中，创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以匹配未使用 AWS KMS 加密的 S3 PutObject 事件。配 置该规则以指向一个 Amazon Simple Notification Service（Amazon SNS）主题。","D":"创建一个 SCP，其中包含针对 s3:putObject 操作的拒绝语句以及一个条件，即 s3:xamz-server-side- encryption 不为 aws:kms。将该 SCP 附加到组织的根目录。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to ENSURE (prevent) that all object uploads to the S3 bucket use AWS KMS encryption, which demands a preventive control. Option D creates an SCP with a Deny statement on the s3:PutObject action with a condition that the request's s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption value is not aws:kms, and attaches it to the organization root. Because the organization has all features enabled, SCPs are available and apply to all member accounts beneath the root, so the guardrail blocks any PutObject request that is not encrypted with SSE-KMS. This mirrors the documented enforcement pattern: the AWS S3 'Requiring encryption' bucket-policy examples use Effect Deny on s3:PutObject conditioned on the server-side-encryption header to require SSE-KMS, and the same s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption / aws:kms request condition keys are valid in an SCP. Options A and C are detective/notification controls (an AWS Config conformance pack, or CloudTrail data events + EventBridge + SNS) that only detect or alert after the fact and cannot prevent non-KMS uploads. Option B targets s3:CreateBucket, the wrong action, which does nothing to control the encryption of object uploads.","explanation_zh":"需求是要「確保」(預防) 所有上傳到 S3 bucket 的物件都使用 AWS KMS 加密,這需要的是預防型控制 (preventive control)。選項 D 建立一個 SCP,對 s3:PutObject 動作加上 Deny 陳述式,並以條件判斷請求的 s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption 值不等於 aws:kms,然後附加到組織根 (root)。由於組織已啟用所有功能 (all features),SCP 可用且套用至 root 之下所有成員帳戶,因此此 guardrail 可阻擋任何未使用 SSE-KMS 的 PutObject 請求。這正符合官方文件記載的強制做法:AWS S3「Requiring encryption」bucket policy 範例以 Effect Deny s3:PutObject 搭配 server-side-encryption 標頭條件來要求 SSE-KMS,而相同的 s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption / aws:kms 請求條件鍵在 SCP 中同樣適用。選項 A 與 C 是偵測/通知型控制 (AWS Config conformance pack,或 CloudTrail data events + EventBridge + SNS),只能事後偵測或告警,無法預防非 KMS 上傳。選項 B 針對 s3:CreateBucket(錯誤的動作),完全無法控制物件上傳的加密。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An AWS Config conformance pack with the s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled rule plus SNS notification is a detective control that only reports compliance status of the bucket's default encryption configuration; it does not block non-KMS object uploads, so it cannot 'ensure' enforcement.","why_zh":"使用 s3-bucket-server-side-encryption-enabled 規則的 AWS Config conformance pack 加 SNS 通知屬於偵測型控制,只回報 bucket 預設加密設定的合規狀態,無法阻止非 KMS 的物件上傳,因此無法『確保』強制執行。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"The SCP denies s3:CreateBucket, the wrong action. The s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption condition key applies to PutObject, not bucket creation, and restricting CreateBucket does nothing to enforce KMS encryption on object uploads, so the requirement is not met.","why_zh":"此 SCP 拒絕的是 s3:CreateBucket,動作錯誤。s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption 條件鍵適用於 PutObject 而非建立 bucket,限制 CreateBucket 完全無法對物件上傳強制 KMS 加密,因此不符合需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Enabling a CloudTrail trail for S3 data events with an EventBridge rule matching non-KMS PutObject events targeting SNS is a detective/alerting control. It notifies after an upload occurs but does not prevent unencrypted uploads.","why_zh":"為 S3 data events 啟用 CloudTrail trail,並以 EventBridge 規則比對非 KMS 的 PutObject 事件再送到 SNS,屬於偵測/告警型控制。它只在上傳發生後通知,無法預防未加密的上傳。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/example-bucket-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/accounts/latest/reference/using-orgs-example-scps.html"]}},{"id":357,"question_en":"A company uses an Amazon Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster and loads transactional data into the database every 5 hours. Data analysts use the Aurora PostgreSQL database to run short-running queries, create complex aggregated queries, and create simple reports that use the data. The data analysts also manually update the data, including deleting and inserting data. The data analysts have reported performance issues. The database team recently identified a long-running idle transaction connection that affected performance by blocking other queries and preventing VACUUM operations. The team wants to be proactively notified about these potential operational issues and about the recommended actions to fix the issues. The company's AWS account uses Amazon DevOps Guru to monitor all the applications in the account. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群，每 5 小时将事务数据加载到数据库中。数据分析师 使用 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库运行短时间查询、创建复杂的聚合查询，并生成使用这些数据的简单报告。 数据分析师还会手动更新数据，包括删除和插入数据。 数据分析师报告了性能问题。数据库团队最近发现了一个长时间空闲的事务连接，该连接阻塞了其他查 询并妨碍了 VACUUM 操作，从而影响了性能。团队希望在出现此类潜在运营问题时能主动收到通知，并 了解解决这些问题的建议措施。 该公司的 AWS 账户使用亚马逊 DevOps Guru 来监控账户中的所有应用程序。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Turn on Performance Insights and DevOps Guru in the existing Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster. Configure DevOps Guru to send notifications to the database team by using Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).","B":"Turn on Performance Insights in the existing Aurora PostrgreSQL DB cluster. Configure Amazon EventBridge to receive events from the existing Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster. Configure the Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster to send notifications to the database team by using Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS).","C":"Turn on Performance Insights and DevOps Guru in the existing Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster. Configure the Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster to send notifications to the database team by using Amazon Simple Email Service (Amazon SES).","D":"Turn on Performance Insights in the existing Aurora PostrgreSQL DB cluster. Configure Amazon EventBridge to receive events from the existing Aurora PostgreSQL DB cluster. Configure DevOps Guru to send notifications to the database team by using Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS)."},"options_zh":{"A":"在现有的 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群中启用性能洞察和 DevOps 专家。配置 DevOps 专家通 过使用亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）向数据库团队发送通知。","B":"在现有的 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群中启用性能洞察功能。配置 Amazon EventBridge 以接收来自现 有 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群的事件。配置 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群，通过使用 Amazon 简 单通知服务（Amazon SNS）向数据库团队发送通知。","C":"在现有的 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群中启用性能洞察和 DevOps 专家功能。配置 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群，通过使用亚马逊简单电子邮件服务（Amazon SES）向数据库团队发 送通知。","D":"在现有的 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群中启用性能洞察功能。配置 Amazon EventBridge 以接收来自 现有 Aurora PostgreSQL 数据库集群的事件。配置 DevOps Guru 使用 Amazon 简单通知服务 （Amazon SNS）向数据库团队发送通知。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is proactive ML-based detection of Aurora PostgreSQL operational issues (such as a long-running idle transaction that blocks queries and prevents VACUUM) together with recommended corrective actions and notifications. DevOps Guru for RDS delivers exactly this, but only when Performance Insights is enabled: AWS docs state that DevOps Guru for RDS 'applies machine learning to Performance Insights metrics for Amazon Aurora databases' and that 'If Amazon RDS DB instances have Performance Insights turned on, DevOps Guru for RDS provides detailed analysis and recommendations.' So you must turn on BOTH Performance Insights and DevOps Guru. For notifications, the only supported DevOps Guru channel is Amazon SNS ('The one supported notification channel is Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS)'), and the insights/recommendations are produced and sent by DevOps Guru itself, not by the Aurora cluster or raw EventBridge events. Option A is the only choice that enables both Performance Insights and DevOps Guru and routes DevOps Guru insights to the team via SNS.","explanation_zh":"需求是針對 Aurora PostgreSQL 的營運問題（例如長時間閒置交易會阻擋查詢並阻止 VACUUM）進行主動式、機器學習導向的偵測，並附上建議的修正動作與通知。Amazon DevOps Guru for RDS 正好能做到這點，但前提是必須啟用 Performance Insights：AWS 文件指出 DevOps Guru for RDS 會「對 Amazon Aurora 資料庫的 Performance Insights 指標套用機器學習」，且「若 Amazon RDS 執行個體已啟用 Performance Insights，DevOps Guru for RDS 會在異常中提供詳細分析與建議」。因此必須同時開啟 Performance Insights 與 DevOps Guru。在通知方面，DevOps Guru 唯一支援的通知通道是 Amazon SNS（「唯一支援的通知通道是 Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS)」），而且洞見與建議是由 DevOps Guru 本身產生並發送，而非 Aurora 叢集或原始 EventBridge 事件。選項 A 是唯一同時啟用 Performance Insights 與 DevOps Guru，並透過 SNS 將 DevOps Guru 洞見送達團隊的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"It turns on Performance Insights but never enables DevOps Guru, so no ML-based proactive insights or recommended corrective actions are produced. Forwarding raw Aurora events through EventBridge and having the Aurora cluster send SNS notifications only reports generic lifecycle/event changes, not the idle-transaction/VACUUM-blocking analysis with fixes that the requirement demands.","why_zh":"它啟用了 Performance Insights，但完全沒有啟用 DevOps Guru，因此不會產生機器學習導向的主動式洞見或修正建議。透過 EventBridge 轉送原始 Aurora 事件並由 Aurora 叢集自行發送 SNS 通知，只會回報一般生命週期/事件變更，無法提供需求所要求的閒置交易/阻擋 VACUUM 分析與修正措施。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"It correctly turns on both Performance Insights and DevOps Guru, but specifies Amazon SES as the notification channel. DevOps Guru's only supported notification channel is Amazon SNS; SES is not a valid DevOps Guru notification target, and the notifications must come from DevOps Guru, not the Aurora cluster.","why_zh":"它正確地同時啟用了 Performance Insights 與 DevOps Guru，但指定使用 Amazon SES 作為通知通道。DevOps Guru 唯一支援的通知通道是 Amazon SNS；SES 不是有效的 DevOps Guru 通知目標，且通知必須來自 DevOps Guru，而非 Aurora 叢集。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"It turns on Performance Insights and references DevOps Guru for SNS notifications, but it never actually enables DevOps Guru on the cluster, and it adds an unnecessary EventBridge-from-Aurora step. DevOps Guru for RDS consumes Performance Insights metrics directly rather than relying on cluster-emitted EventBridge events, so the design is incomplete and self-contradictory (asking DevOps Guru to notify via SNS without enabling DevOps Guru coverage).","why_zh":"它啟用了 Performance Insights 並提到由 DevOps Guru 發送 SNS 通知，但實際上從未在叢集上啟用 DevOps Guru，且加入了不必要的「Aurora 送到 EventBridge」步驟。DevOps Guru for RDS 是直接消耗 Performance Insights 指標，而非依賴叢集發出的 EventBridge 事件，因此此設計不完整且自相矛盾（要求 DevOps Guru 透過 SNS 發送通知卻未啟用 DevOps Guru 覆蓋）。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/devops-guru-for-rds.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/devops-guru/latest/userguide/working-with-rds.overview.definitions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-devopsguru-notificationchannel-notificationchannelconfig.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/devops-guru/latest/userguide/sns-required-permissions.html"]}},{"id":358,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is implementing governance controls for a company that requires its infrastructure to be housed within the United States. The company has many AWS accounts in an organization in AWS Organizations that has all features enabled. The engineer must restrict which AWS Regions the company can use. The engineer must also ensure that an alert is sent as soon as possible if any activity outside the governance policy occurs. The controls must be automatically enabled on any new Region outside the United States. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在为一家要求其基础设施必须部署在美国境内的公司实施治理控制措施。该公司 在 AWS 组织中拥有多个 AWS 账户，该组织已启用所有功能。 工程师必须限制公司可以使用的 AWS 区域。工程师还必须确保一旦出现任何违反治理策略的活动，能尽 快发送警报。对于美国以外的任何新区域，这些控制措施必须自动启用。 哪种步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an Organizations SCP deny policy that has a condition that the aws:RequestedRegion property does not match a list of all US Regions. Include an exception in the policy for global services. Attach the policy to the root of the organization.","B":"Configure AWS CloudTrail to send logs to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Enable CloudTrail for all Regions. Use a CloudWatch Logs metric filter to create a metric in non-US Regions. Configure a CloudWatch alarm to send an alert if the metric is greater than 0.","C":"Use an AWS Lambda function that checks for AWS service activity. Deploy the Lambda function to all Regions. Write an Amazon EventBridge rule that runs the Lambda function every hour. Configure the rule to send an alert if the Lambda function finds any activity in a non-US Region.","D":"Use an AWS Lambda function to query Amazon Inspector to look for service activity in non-US Regions. Configure the Lambda function to send alerts if Amazon Inspector finds any activity.","E":"Create an Organizations SCP allow policy that has a condition that the aws:RequestedRegion property matches a list of all US Regions. Include an exception in the policy for global services. Attach the policy to the root of the organization."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个组织 SCP 拒绝策略，该策略包含一个条件，即 aws:RequestedRegion 属性与所有美国区域列 表不匹配。在策略中为全球服务添加一个例外。将该策略附加到组织的根目录。","B":"配置 AWS CloudTrail 将日志发送到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。为所有区域启用 CloudTrail。在 非美国区域使用 CloudWatch Logs 指标筛选器创建一个指标。配置 CloudWatch 警报，如果该 指标大于 0 则发送警报。","C":"使用一个检查 AWS 服务活动的 AWS Lambda 函数。将该 Lambda 函数部署到所有区域。编写一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，每小时运行一次该 Lambda 函数。配置该规则，如果 Lambda 函数在非 美国区域发现任何活动，则发送警报。","D":"使用 AWS Lambda 函数查询 Amazon Inspector 以查找非美国区域的服务活动。配置 Lambda 函 数，以便在 Amazon Inspector 发现任何活动时发送警报。","E":"创建一个组织 SCP 允许策略，该策略包含一个条件，即 aws:RequestedRegion 属性与所有美国区域的列 表相匹配。在策略中为全球服务添加一个例外。将该策略附加到组织的根目录。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are: restrict usable AWS Regions to the US, automatically cover any newly launched non-US Region, and alert as soon as possible on out-of-policy activity. Option A is the AWS-documented Region deny pattern: an Organizations SCP Deny statement with a Condition of StringNotEquals on aws:RequestedRegion against the list of allowed US Regions, using NotAction exceptions for global services (IAM, Organizations, KMS, CloudFront, STS, Route 53, etc.), attached to the org root. Because it denies any action when the requested Region is not in the US allow-list, a newly launched non-US Region is automatically blocked with no policy change. This is exactly the pattern in the AWS Control Tower Region deny control. Option B provides the alerting: enable CloudTrail for all Regions (a multi-Region/organization trail automatically extends its configuration to any newly enabled Region) sending events to CloudWatch Logs, use a metric filter to count events that occur in non-US Regions, and a CloudWatch alarm that fires when the metric exceeds 0, giving near-real-time notification. Together A (enforcement) and B (prompt alerting) meet all requirements and both auto-extend to new Regions.","explanation_zh":"需求是：將可用的 AWS Region 限制在美國境內、自動涵蓋任何新啟用的非美國 Region、並在發生違反治理政策的活動時盡快發出警示。選項 A 是 AWS 文件記載的 Region 拒絕模式：一個 Organizations SCP Deny 陳述式，使用 StringNotEquals 條件比對 aws:RequestedRegion 與允許的美國 Region 清單，並以 NotAction 為全域服務（IAM、Organizations、KMS、CloudFront、STS、Route 53 等）設定例外，附加到組織 root。由於只要請求的 Region 不在美國允許清單內就拒絕所有動作，任何新推出的非美國 Region 都會自動被封鎖且不需修改政策，這正是 AWS Control Tower Region deny control 的模式。選項 B 提供警示機制：為所有 Region 啟用 CloudTrail（multi-Region/organization trail 會自動將設定延伸到任何新啟用的 Region），將事件送至 CloudWatch Logs，使用 metric filter 計算發生在非美國 Region 的事件數，並設定 CloudWatch alarm 在指標大於 0 時觸發，提供近即時通知。A（強制）與 B（即時警示）合在一起即可滿足所有需求，且兩者都會自動延伸到新 Region。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"An AWS Lambda function triggered by an EventBridge schedule that runs every hour is a polling approach that introduces up to roughly an hour of latency, so it does not alert 'as soon as possible.' Having Lambda generically 'check for AWS service activity' is also vague and far less reliable than the event-driven CloudTrail-to-CloudWatch metric-filter-and-alarm pattern, and it adds operational overhead to deploy/maintain Lambda in every Region.","why_zh":"由 EventBridge 排程每小時觸發一次的 Lambda 函式屬於輪詢方式，最多會有約一小時的延遲，因此無法『盡快』發出警示。讓 Lambda 概略地『檢查 AWS 服務活動』也很模糊，遠不如事件驅動的 CloudTrail 到 CloudWatch metric filter 加 alarm 模式可靠，而且還需在每個 Region 部署維護 Lambda，營運負擔大。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability and network-reachability assessment service for EC2, ECR container images, and Lambda functions. It does not detect or report cross-Region API or service activity, so it is the wrong tool for identifying activity occurring in non-US Regions.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector 是針對 EC2、ECR 容器映像與 Lambda 函式的弱點與網路可達性評估服務，它不會偵測或回報跨 Region 的 API 或服務活動，因此用來找出發生在非美國 Region 的活動是錯誤的工具。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"SCPs follow a deny-list strategy where FullAWSAccess grants the baseline and Deny statements carve out restrictions. The AWS-documented mechanism for Region restriction is a Deny statement with StringNotEquals on aws:RequestedRegion (Option A), not an Allow SCP scoped to US Regions. An allow-only SCP intersects with FullAWSAccess and is not the canonical pattern for auto-covering new Regions. A and E both target Region restriction, so only one can be the intended answer, and A matches official AWS guidance.","why_zh":"SCP 採用拒絕清單策略，由 FullAWSAccess 提供基準權限，再用 Deny 陳述式設限。AWS 文件記載的 Region 限制機制是使用 StringNotEquals 比對 aws:RequestedRegion 的 Deny 陳述式（選項 A），而非僅允許美國 Region 的 Allow SCP。Allow-only SCP 會與 FullAWSAccess 取交集，並非自動涵蓋新 Region 的標準模式。A 與 E 都是要做 Region 限制，因此只有一個是正解，而 A 符合 AWS 官方指引。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/controlreference/primary-region-deny-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/monitor-cloudtrail-log-files-with-cloudwatch-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/awscloudtrail/latest/userguide/cloudtrail-multi-region-trails.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Alarm-On-Logs.html"]}},{"id":359,"question_en":"A company runs applications on Amazon EC2 instances that are in an Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group. The EC2 instances are behind an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Users recently began to experience errors when traffic was directed to some of the EC2 instances. A DevOps engineer discovers that the Auto Scaling group reports the problematic instances are healthy despite the application errors. User experience returns to normal after the DevOps engineer resolves the application errors on the problematic instances. The company wants to ensure that traffic is routed only to healthy instances that are not experiencing application errors. The company also wants a support team to receive a notification if the traffic routing configuration changes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行应用程序，这些实例位于一个亚马逊 EC2 自动扩展组中。 EC2 实例位于应用负载均衡器（ALB）之后。最近，用户在流量被定向到某些 EC2 实例时开始遇到 错误。 一位 DevOps 工程师发现，尽管应用程序出现错误，但自动扩展组报告有问题的实例是健康的。在 DevOps 工程师解决了有问题的实例上的应用程序错误后，用户体验恢复正常。 该公司希望确保流量仅被路由到运行正常且未出现应用程序错误的实例。该公司还希望在流量路 由配置发生更改时，支持团队能够收到通知。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to use ELB health checks. Enable AWS Config. Create an AWS Config rule to ensure that any new Auto Scaling group will use ELB health checks. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify the support team if the traffic routing configuration changes. Configure the AWS Config rule to send a notification to the topic.","B":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to use EC2 health checks. Enable AWS Config. Create an AWS Config rule to ensure that any new Auto Scaling group will use EC2 health checks. Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic to notify the support team if the traffic routing configuration changes. Configure the AWS Config rule to send a notification to the topic.","C":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to use EC2 health checks. Create an Amazon CloudWatch synthetic canary to monitor the application. Create a CloudWatch alarm that is triggered when the CloudWatch canary fails. Configure the alarm to notify the support team when the alarm state is in alarm.","D":"Configure the Auto Scaling group to use ELB health checks. Create an Amazon CloudWatch synthetic canary to monitor the application. Create a CloudWatch alarm that is triggered when the CloudWatch canary fails. Configure the alarm to notify the support team when the alarm state is in alarm."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置自动扩展组以使用 ELB 健康检查。启用 AWS 配置。创建一个 AWS 配置规则，以确保任何新 的自动扩展组都将使用 ELB 健康检查。创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题， 以便在流量路由配置更改时通知支持团队。配置 AWS 配置规则，使其向该主题发送通知。","B":"将自动扩展组配置为使用 EC2 健康检查。启用 AWS 配置。创建一个 AWS 配置规则，以确保任何 新的自动扩展组都将使用 EC2 健康检查。创建一个 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题， 以便在流量路由配置更改时通知支持团队。将 AWS 配置规则配置为向该主题发送通知。","C":"将自动扩展组配置为使用 EC2 健康检查。创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 合成金丝雀来监控应用程 序。创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，当 CloudWatch 金丝雀出现故障时触发该警报。将警报配置为在 警报状态处于警报时通知支持团队。","D":"配置自动扩展组以使用 ELB 健康检查。创建一个 Amazon CloudWatch 合成金丝雀来监控应用程序。 创建一个 CloudWatch 警报，当 CloudWatch 金丝雀出现故障时触发该警报。配置警报，当警报状 态处于警报状态时通知支持团队。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two requirements decide this. (1) Route traffic only to healthy instances not experiencing application errors: Amazon EC2 status checks only confirm the instance is running and detect underlying hardware/software impairment; they cannot detect application-level errors, which is exactly why the Auto Scaling group reported the broken instances as healthy. Turning on Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) health checks makes Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling use the load balancer's health-check results (the application's response on the health-check path), so erroring instances are marked Unhealthy and replaced, and the ALB stops routing traffic to them. This eliminates options B and C, which use EC2 health checks. (2) Notify a support team if the traffic routing configuration changes: AWS Config provides the managed rule autoscaling-group-elb-healthcheck-required (identifier AUTOSCALING_GROUP_ELB_HEALTHCHECK_REQUIRED, resource type AWS::AutoScaling::AutoScalingGroup, trigger type 'Configuration changes'), which re-evaluates whenever an ASG's configuration (including its health-check type) changes and flags any ASG not using ELB health checks. AWS Config can stream configuration changes and compliance evaluations to an Amazon SNS topic for the support team. A CloudWatch synthetic canary (option D) only monitors application availability/errors at the endpoint, not changes to the traffic routing configuration, so it fails requirement 2. Therefore A satisfies both requirements.","explanation_zh":"本題由兩個需求決定。(1) 僅將流量導向沒有應用程式錯誤的健康執行個體：Amazon EC2 status checks 只確認執行個體正在執行並偵測底層硬體/軟體損壞，無法偵測應用程式層級的錯誤，這正是 Auto Scaling group 將故障執行個體回報為健康的原因。啟用 Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) health checks 後，Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling 會採用負載平衡器的健康檢查結果（應用程式在健康檢查路徑上的回應），因此發生錯誤的執行個體會被標記為 Unhealthy 並被替換，ALB 也會停止將流量導向它們。這排除了使用 EC2 health checks 的選項 B 與 C。(2) 當流量路由設定變更時通知支援團隊：AWS Config 提供受管規則 autoscaling-group-elb-healthcheck-required（識別碼 AUTOSCALING_GROUP_ELB_HEALTHCHECK_REQUIRED，資源類型 AWS::AutoScaling::AutoScalingGroup，觸發類型為 'Configuration changes'），每當 ASG 設定（包含其 health-check type）變更時都會重新評估，並標記任何未使用 ELB health checks 的 ASG。AWS Config 可將組態變更與合規評估串流至 Amazon SNS topic 通知支援團隊。CloudWatch synthetic canary（選項 D）僅在端點監控應用程式可用性/錯誤，無法偵測流量路由設定的變更，因此無法滿足需求 2。所以 A 同時滿足兩個需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses EC2 health checks, which only verify the instance is running and pass status checks; they cannot detect application errors. This is precisely the failure mode in the scenario (the ASG reported erroring instances as healthy), so traffic would keep routing to broken instances. It fails requirement 1.","why_zh":"使用 EC2 health checks，只能驗證執行個體在執行中並通過狀態檢查，無法偵測應用程式錯誤。這正是情境中的故障模式（ASG 將發生錯誤的執行個體回報為健康），流量仍會導向故障執行個體。無法滿足需求 1。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses EC2 health checks (fails requirement 1, same as B) and relies on a canary, which monitors application errors rather than traffic routing configuration changes (fails requirement 2). Doubly wrong.","why_zh":"使用 EC2 health checks（與 B 一樣無法滿足需求 1），且依賴 canary 監控應用程式錯誤而非流量路由設定變更（無法滿足需求 2）。雙重錯誤。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Correctly uses ELB health checks (meets requirement 1), but a CloudWatch synthetic canary only monitors the application endpoint for availability/errors; it does not detect or notify when the traffic routing configuration changes. It fails the explicit requirement to notify the support team if the routing configuration changes, which is what AWS Config (option A) provides.","why_zh":"正確使用 ELB health checks（滿足需求 1），但 CloudWatch synthetic canary 只監控應用程式端點的可用性/錯誤，無法偵測或在流量路由設定變更時通知。它無法滿足『路由設定變更時通知支援團隊』這項明確需求，而這正是 AWS Config（選項 A）所提供的功能。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/health-checks-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/autoscaling-group-elb-healthcheck-required.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/notifications-for-AWS-Config.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Synthetics_Canaries.html"]}},{"id":360,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to troubleshoot a pipeline that uses a GitHub code repository. The pipeline contains a source stage, a build stage, and a deploy stage. The pipeline also has an AWS CodeStar connection to the GitHub code repository. The build stage uses an AWS CodeBuild build project. The build project needs to perform a git clone of the repository as part of the build process. The DevOps engineer validates that the source stage is working properly. However, the build stage fails each time the pipeline runs. What is the reason that the build stage fails in the pipeline?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要排查使用 GitHub 代码库的流水线故障。该流水线包含源代码阶段、构建 阶段和部署阶段。该流水线还与 GitHub 代码库建立了 AWS CodeStar 连接。 构建阶段使用 AWS CodeBuild 构建项目。构建项目需要在构建过程中执行对存储库的 git 克隆操作。 开发运维工程师确认源代码阶段运行正常。然而，每次运行流水线时，构建阶段都会失败。 管道中的构建阶段失败的原因是什么？","options_en":{"A":"The build stage within the pipeline needs to use the AWS CodeStar connection action.","B":"The AWS CodeStar connection to GitHub contains incorrect credentials.","C":"The AWS CodePipeline service role does not have permission to use the AWS CodeStar connection.","D":"The AWS CodeBuild service role does not have permission to use the AWS CodeStar connection."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管道中的构建阶段需要使用 AWS CodeStar 连接操作。","B":"AWS CodeStar 与 GitHub 的连接包含错误的凭证。","C":"AWS CodePipeline 服务角色没有使用 AWS CodeStar 连接的权限。","D":"AWS CodeBuild 服务角色没有使用 AWS CodeStar 连接的权限。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This is the exact scenario from the AWS 'full clone' GitHub pipeline tutorial. When a CodePipeline source action uses a CodeStar/CodeConnections connection to GitHub with the Full clone output artifact format, the CodeBuild build project performs the git clone of the repository itself inside the build environment. For that clone to succeed, the CodeBuild service role must have the codestar-connections:UseConnection (now codeconnections:UseConnection) permission attached via a customer-managed policy. The tutorial states verbatim in Step 3: 'The initial pipeline run will fail because the CodeBuild service role must be updated with permissions to use connections.' Because the source stage already works, the CodePipeline service role already holds UseConnection for the source action; the only missing piece is the CodeBuild service role permission, so the failure is isolated to the build stage. That makes D the correct cause.","explanation_zh":"這正是 AWS 'full clone' GitHub pipeline 教學中的情境。當 CodePipeline 的 source action 透過 CodeStar/CodeConnections connection 連到 GitHub，且輸出 artifact 格式設為 Full clone 時，CodeBuild build project 會在 build 環境中自行對 repository 執行 git clone。要讓此 clone 成功，CodeBuild service role 必須透過 customer-managed policy 取得 codestar-connections:UseConnection（現為 codeconnections:UseConnection）權限。教學的 Step 3 原文寫道：'The initial pipeline run will fail because the CodeBuild service role must be updated with permissions to use connections.' 由於 source stage 已正常運作，代表 CodePipeline service role 已對 source action 擁有 UseConnection 權限；唯一缺少的是 CodeBuild service role 的權限，因此失敗只發生在 build stage。故 D 為正確原因。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The CodeStar connection action is a source-action type, not a build-action type. The build stage correctly uses a CodeBuild action; you do not add a separate connection action to the build stage. The CodeBuild action consumes the source via Full clone and just needs UseConnection permission on its service role.","why_zh":"CodeStar connection action 屬於 source action 類型，不是 build action 類型。Build stage 正確地使用 CodeBuild action，不會在 build stage 額外加入 connection action。CodeBuild action 透過 Full clone 取得原始碼，只需在其 service role 上具備 UseConnection 權限即可。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"If the connection had incorrect/invalid credentials or were not in an Available state, the source stage would fail first. The question states the source stage works properly, which proves the connection credentials are valid; therefore credentials are not the cause.","why_zh":"若 connection 的憑證錯誤或未處於 Available 狀態，source stage 會先失敗。題目指出 source stage 運作正常，證明 connection 憑證有效，因此憑證並非失敗原因。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The CodePipeline service role's UseConnection permission is what the source action needs. Since the source stage works properly, the CodePipeline service role already has the required connection permission. The build-stage failure is unrelated to the CodePipeline service role.","why_zh":"CodePipeline service role 的 UseConnection 權限是 source action 所需。既然 source stage 運作正常，代表 CodePipeline service role 已具備該 connection 權限。Build stage 失敗與 CodePipeline service role 無關。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/tutorials-github-gitclone.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/troubleshooting.html"]}},{"id":361,"question_en":"A company's DevOps team uses Node Package Manager (NPM) open source libraries to build applications. The DevOps team runs its application build process in an AWS CodeBuild project that downloads the NPM libraries from public NPM repositories. The company wants to host the NPM libraries in private NPM repositories. The company also needs to be able to run checks on new versions of the libraries before the DevOps team uses the libraries. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational effort?","question_zh":"一家公司的 DevOps 团队使用 Node 包管理器（NPM）开源库来构建应用程序。该 DevOps 团队在其 AWS CodeBuild 项目中运行应用程序构建流程，从公共 NPM 存储库下载 NPM 库。 该公司希望将 NPM 库托管在私有 NPM 仓库中。此外，公司还需要能够在 DevOps 团队使用这些库之前对 新版本的库进行检查。 哪种解决方案能以最少的操作努力满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeArtifact repository with an upstream repository named npm-store. Configure the application build process to use the CodeArtifact repository as the default source for NPM. Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline to perform the required checks on package versions in the CodeArtifact repository. Set the package status to unlisted if a failure occurs.","B":"Enable Amazon S3 caching in the CodeBuild project configuration. Add a step in the buildspec.yaml config file to perform the required checks on the package versions in the cache.","C":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository for each library. Clone the required NPM libraries to the appropriate CodeCommit repository. Modify the CodeBuild appspec.yaml config file to use the private CodeCommit repositories. Add a step to perform the required checks on the package versions.","D":"Create an AWS CodeCommit repository for each library. Clone the required NPM libraries to the appropriate CodeCommit repository. Modify the CodeBuild buildspec.yaml config file so that NPM uses the private CodeCommit repositories. Add an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that performs the required checks on the package versions for each new commit to the repositories. Configure the pipeline to revert to the most recent commit in the event of a failure."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个名为 npm-store 的上游仓库的 AWS CodeArtifact 仓库。配置应用程序构建过程，将 CodeArtifact 仓库设置为 NPM 的默认源。创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，对 CodeArtifact 仓库中 的软件包版本执行所需的检查。如果出现故障，则将软件包状态设置为未列出。","B":"在 CodeBuild 项目配置中启用 Amazon S3 缓存。在 buildspec.yaml 配置文件中添加一个步骤，对缓存中 的软件包版本执行所需的检查。","C":"为每个库创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库。将所需的 NPM 库克隆到相应的 CodeCommit 存储库。修 改 CodeBuild 的 appspec.yaml 配置文件以使用私有 CodeCommit 存储库。添加一个步骤来执行所需的包 版本检查。","D":"为每个库创建一个 AWS CodeCommit 存储库。将所需的 NPM 库克隆到相应的 CodeCommit 存储库中。 修改 CodeBuild 的 buildspec.yaml 配置文件，以便 NPM 使用私有 CodeCommit 存储库。添加一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，对每个存储库的新提交执行所需的包版本检查。配置管道在出现故障时回滚到最近 的提交。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS CodeArtifact is the managed, purpose-built private artifact repository for npm and other formats, so it directly satisfies hosting npm libraries privately with the least operational effort. Connecting the CodeArtifact repository to an upstream named npm-store (which has an external connection to npmjs.com) makes CodeArtifact transparently fetch and cache public open-source npm packages on demand and serve them privately as the default npm registry in CodeBuild; no servers or per-library plumbing are required. To gate new versions before developers use them, a CodePipeline pipeline can run the required checks and, on failure, call update-package-versions-status to set the version status to Unlisted. AWS docs explicitly state that an Unlisted version 'can still be downloaded as normal, but it will not appear in package version lists returned to commands such as npm view,' and Unlisted is a documented valid target status (alongside Published and Archived). This combination of managed services plus native package-status controls is the lowest-effort solution.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeArtifact 是專為 npm 等格式打造的受管私有 artifact repository，因此最能以最少維運成本滿足「私有託管 npm 函式庫」的需求。將 CodeArtifact repository 連接到名為 npm-store 的 upstream repository（該 upstream 具有對 npmjs.com 的 external connection），即可讓 CodeArtifact 在需要時自動抓取並快取公開的 open-source npm 套件，並在 CodeBuild 中作為預設 npm registry 私有提供，無需自行管理伺服器或為每個函式庫做額外設定。為了在開發團隊使用前對新版本進行檢查，可由 CodePipeline pipeline 執行所需檢查，若失敗則呼叫 update-package-versions-status 將該版本狀態設為 Unlisted。AWS 文件明確指出 Unlisted 版本「仍可正常下載，但不會出現在 npm view 等指令回傳的版本清單中」，且 Unlisted 是文件記載的有效 target status（與 Published、Archived 並列）。結合受管服務與原生套件狀態控制，這是維運成本最低的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Enabling Amazon S3 caching in CodeBuild only caches build dependencies between builds for speed; it does not host a private npm registry, does not replace the public npmjs source, and the cache is not a governed package store where you can run pre-use version checks. It meets neither core requirement.","why_zh":"在 CodeBuild 啟用 Amazon S3 快取只是為了加速、在建置間快取相依套件，並非私有 npm registry，無法取代公開 npmjs 來源，且快取也不是可治理、可在使用前檢查版本的套件儲存庫，無法滿足任一核心需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"CodeCommit is a Git source-control service, not an npm registry; npm cannot resolve and install packages from a CodeCommit Git repo the way it does from a registry. Cloning each library into a separate repo is high manual effort, and appspec.yaml is a CodeDeploy file, not the CodeBuild buildspec used to configure npm. It fails both the registry requirement and the LEAST-effort qualifier.","why_zh":"CodeCommit 是 Git 原始碼控管服務，不是 npm registry；npm 無法像對 registry 那樣從 CodeCommit Git 儲存庫解析並安裝套件。為每個函式庫各 clone 一個儲存庫是大量人工作業，且 appspec.yaml 屬於 CodeDeploy，並非用來在 CodeBuild 設定 npm 的 buildspec。不符合 registry 需求，也不符合維運最少的條件。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same fundamental flaw as C: CodeCommit is not an npm registry, so npm cannot consume libraries from it the way a package manager consumes a registry. Manually cloning every library into per-library Git repos and wiring revert-on-failure pipelines is far more operational effort than using managed CodeArtifact with native package-status controls.","why_zh":"與 C 有相同的根本缺陷：CodeCommit 不是 npm registry，npm 無法像套件管理工具消費 registry 那樣從中取用函式庫。為每個函式庫手動 clone 成各自的 Git 儲存庫，並建置失敗時回復提交的管線，維運成本遠高於使用受管的 CodeArtifact 搭配原生套件狀態控制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/external-connection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/update-package-version-status.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/APIReference/API_UpdatePackageVersionsStatus.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/using-npm-packages-in-codebuild.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repos-upstream.html"]}},{"id":362,"question_en":"A company has a search application that has a web interface. The company uses Amazon CloudFront, Application Load Balancers (ALBs), and Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group with a desired capacity of 3. The company uses prebaked AMIs. The application starts in 1 minute. The application queries an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster. The application is deployed to multiple Availability Zones. Because of compliance requirements, the application needs to have a disaster recovery (DR) environment in a separate AWS Region. The company wants to minimize the ongoing cost of the DR environment and requires an RTO and an RPO of under 30 minutes. The company has created an ALB in the DR Region. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款具备网络界面的搜索应用程序。该公司使用了亚马逊 CloudFront、应用负载均衡器 （ALB）以及处于自动扩展组中的 3 台亚马逊 EC2 实例，该组的期望容量为 3。该公司使用预配置的 AMI。该应用程序在 1 分钟内启动。该应用程序会查询亚马逊 OpenSearch 服务集群。 该应用程序已部署到多个可用区。由于合规性要求，该应用程序需要在单独的 AWS 区域中拥有一个灾 难恢复（DR）环境。该公司希望将 DR 环境的持续成本降至最低，并要求恢复时间目标（RTO）和恢 复点目标（RPO）均低于 30 分钟。该公司已在 DR 区域创建了一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Add the new ALB as an origin in the CloudFront distribution. Configure origin failover functionality. Copy the AMI to the DR Region. Create a launch template and an Auto Scaling group with a desired capacity of 0 in the DR Region. Create a new OpenSearch Service cluster in the DR Region. Set up cross-cluster replication for the cluster.","B":"Create a new CloudFront distribution in the DR Region and add the new ALB as an origin. Use Amazon Route 53 DNS for Regional failover. Copy the AMI to the DR Region. Create a launch template and an Auto Scaling group with a desired capacity of 0 in the DR Region. Reconfigure the OpenSearch Service cluster as a Multi-AZ with Standby deployment. Ensure that the standby nodes are in the DR Region.","C":"Create a new CloudFront distribution in the DR Region and add the new ALB as an origin. Use Amazon Route 53 DNS for Regional failover. Copy the AMI to the DR Region. Create a launch template and an Auto Scaling group with a desired capacity of 3 in the DR Region. Reconfigure the OpenSearch Service cluster as a Multi-AZ with Standby deployment. Ensure that the standby nodes are in the DR Region.","D":"Add the new ALB as an origin in the CloudFront distribution. Configure origin failover functionality. Copy the AMI to the DR Region. Create a launch template and an Auto Scaling group with a desired capacity of 3 in the DR Region. Create a new OpenSearch Service cluster in the DR Region. Set up cross-cluster replication for the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 CloudFront 分发中将新的 ALB 添加为源站。配置源站故障转移功能。将 AMI 复制到灾难恢复 区域。在灾难恢复区域创建一个启动模板和一个期望容量为 0 的自动扩展组。在灾难恢复区域创 建一个新的 OpenSearch 服务集群。为该集群设置跨集群复制。","B":"在灾难恢复区域创建一个新的 CloudFront 分发，并将新的应用负载均衡器（ALB）添加为源。使 用 Amazon Route 53 DNS 实现区域故障转移。将 AMI 复制到灾难恢复区域。在灾难恢复区域创 建一个启动模板和一个期望容量为 0 的自动扩展组。将 OpenSearch Service 集群重新配置为具有 备用节点的多可用区部署。确保备用节点位于灾难恢复区域。","C":"在灾难恢复区域创建一个新的 CloudFront 分发，并将新的 ALB 添加为源。使用 Amazon Route 53 DNS 实现区域故障转移。将 AMI 复制到灾难恢复区域。在灾难恢复区域创建一个启动模板和一 个期望容量为 3 的自动扩展组。将 OpenSearch Service 集群重新配置为多可用区带备用节点部署。 确保备用节点位于灾难恢复区域。","D":"在 CloudFront 分发中将新的 ALB 添加为源站。配置源站故障转移功能。将 AMI 复制到灾难恢复 区域。在灾难恢复区域创建一个启动模板和一个期望容量为 3 的自动扩展组。在灾难恢复区域创 建一个新的 OpenSearch 服务集群。为该集群设置跨集群复制。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Cost Optimization"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Two facts decide this question. First, OpenSearch Service Multi-AZ with Standby is a single-Region availability feature: the AWS docs state it 'creates a domain across three Availability Zones' within the same Region and activates standby nodes in under a minute. It cannot place standby nodes in a different (DR) Region, so options B and C are technically impossible. The correct cross-Region OpenSearch DR mechanism is cross-cluster replication, which 'helps to ensure disaster recovery if there is an outage, and allows you to replicate data across geographically distant data centers' using an active-passive (leader/follower) model with continuous replication, easily meeting an RPO under 30 minutes (options A and D). Second, CloudFront origin failover lets you add the DR ALB as a secondary origin in an origin group on the existing distribution, providing automatic Regional failover with no DNS or distribution changes. Between A and D, the only difference is the Auto Scaling group desired capacity: A uses 0 (pilot light) and D uses 3 (warm standby). Because the AMIs are prebaked and the application starts in 1 minute, scaling from 0 to 3 easily fits within the 30-minute RTO, while desired capacity 0 minimizes the ongoing DR cost, which is the explicit qualifier. Therefore A is correct.","explanation_zh":"兩個事實決定了答案。第一，OpenSearch Service Multi-AZ with Standby 是單一 Region 內的可用性功能：AWS 文件說明它是在同一個 Region 內「跨三個 Availability Zones 建立 domain」，並在不到一分鐘內啟用 standby 節點。它無法將 standby 節點放在不同的（DR）Region，因此選項 B 與 C 在技術上不可能。正確的跨 Region OpenSearch DR 機制是 cross-cluster replication，文件指出它「在發生中斷時有助於確保 disaster recovery，並可跨地理上分隔的資料中心複製資料」，採用 active-passive（leader/follower）模型持續複製，可輕易達到 RPO 低於 30 分鐘（選項 A 與 D）。第二，CloudFront origin failover 可將 DR ALB 加為現有 distribution 中 origin group 的次要 origin，提供自動的 Regional failover，且不需更改 DNS 或 distribution。A 與 D 的唯一差異是 Auto Scaling group 的 desired capacity：A 使用 0（pilot light），D 使用 3（warm standby）。由於 AMI 已預先製作（prebaked）且應用程式 1 分鐘即可啟動，從 0 擴展到 3 可輕易在 30 分鐘 RTO 內完成，而 desired capacity 0 可將 DR 的持續成本降至最低，這正是題目明確要求的限定條件。因此 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Multi-AZ with Standby is a single-Region feature that spreads nodes across three Availability Zones in one Region; it cannot put standby nodes in a separate DR Region, so 'Ensure that the standby nodes are in the DR Region' is impossible. Creating a whole new CloudFront distribution plus Route 53 failover is also unnecessary overhead compared to origin failover.","why_zh":"Multi-AZ with Standby 是單一 Region 功能，將節點分散在一個 Region 的三個 AZ，無法把 standby 節點放到另一個 DR Region，因此「讓 standby 節點位於 DR Region」不可能。另外建立全新的 CloudFront distribution 加 Route 53 容錯也比 origin failover 多餘。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Same fatal flaw as B: Multi-AZ with Standby cannot span Regions. Additionally a desired capacity of 3 keeps a full warm fleet running, increasing ongoing cost and violating the 'minimize the ongoing cost of the DR environment' requirement.","why_zh":"與 B 相同的致命缺陷：Multi-AZ with Standby 無法跨 Region。此外 desired capacity 設為 3 會持續維持完整的暖機機群，增加持續成本，違反「最小化 DR 環境持續成本」的需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The OpenSearch (cross-cluster replication) and CloudFront (origin failover) parts are correct, but a desired capacity of 3 runs a full warm fleet continuously in the DR Region, which does not minimize ongoing DR cost. With prebaked AMIs and a 1-minute startup, desired capacity 0 (option A) still meets the sub-30-minute RTO at much lower cost.","why_zh":"OpenSearch（cross-cluster replication）與 CloudFront（origin failover）部分正確，但 desired capacity 設為 3 會在 DR Region 持續執行完整暖機機群，無法最小化持續的 DR 成本。由於有預製 AMI 且 1 分鐘啟動，desired capacity 0（選項 A）仍能以更低成本滿足低於 30 分鐘的 RTO。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/managedomains-multiaz.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/opensearch-service/latest/developerguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/high_availability_origin_failover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/whitepapers/latest/disaster-recovery-workloads-on-aws/disaster-recovery-options-in-the-cloud.html"]}},{"id":363,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer uses AWS WAF to manage web ACLs across an AWS account. The DevOps engineer must ensure that AWS WAF is enabled for all Application Load Balancers (ALBs) in the account. The DevOps engineer uses an AWS CloudFormation template to deploy an individual ALB and AWS WAF as part of each application stack's deployment process. If AWS WAF is removed from the ALB after the ALB is deployed, AWS WAF must be added to the ALB automatically. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师使用 AWS WAF 来管理整个 AWS 账户中的网络访问控制列表（ACL）。该 DevOps 工程师必须确保账户中的所有应用负载均衡器（ALB）都启用了 AWS WAF。DevOps 工程师使 用 AWS CloudFormation 模板在每个应用堆栈的部署过程中部署单个 ALB 和 AWS WAF。如果在部署 ALB 后从 ALB 中移除了 AWS WAF，则必须自动将 AWS WAF 添加回 ALB。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Config. Add the alb-waf-enabled managed rule. Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation document to add AWS WAF to an ALB. Edit the rule to automatically remediate. Select the Systems Manager Automation document as the remediation action.","B":"Enable AWS Config. Add the alb-waf-enabled managed rule. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to send all AWS Config ConfigurationItemChangeNotification notification types to an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to call the AWS Config start-resource-evaluation API in detective mode.","C":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to periodically call an AWS Lambda function that calls the detect-stack-drift API on the CloudFormation template. Configure the Lambda function to modify the ALB attributes with waf.fail_open.enabled set to true if the AWS::WAFv2::WebACLAssociation resource shows a status of drifted.","D":"Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule to periodically call an AWS Lambda function that calls the detect-stack-drift API on the CloudFormation template. Configure the Lambda function to delete and redeploy the CloudFormation stack if the AWS::WAFv2::WebACLAssociation resource shows a status of drifted."},"options_zh":{"A":"启用 AWS Config。添加 alb-waf-enabled 管理规则。创建一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 文档 以将 AWS WAF 添加到 ALB。编辑规则以自动修复。选择 Systems Manager Automation 文档作为修 复操作。","B":"启用 AWS Config。添加 alb-waf-enabled 管理规则。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，将所有 AWS Config 的 ConfigurationItemChangeNotification 通知类型发送到一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配 置该 Lambda 函数以在检测模式下调用 AWS Config 的 start-resource-evaluation API。","C":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，定期调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 CloudFormation 模 板上的 detect-stack-drift API。如果 AWS::WAFv2::WebACLAssociation 资源的状态显示为“已偏离”， 则配置该 Lambda 函数将 ALB 属性修改为 waf.fail_open.enabled 设置为 true。","D":"配置一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，定期调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，该函数调用 CloudFormation 模板上的 detect-stack-drift API。如果 AWS::WAFv2::WebACLAssociation 资源的状态显示为“已偏 离”，则配置该 Lambda 函数删除并重新部署 CloudFormation 堆栈。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Config provides the managed rule alb-waf-enabled (identifier ALB_WAF_ENABLED, resource type AWS::ElasticLoadBalancingV2::LoadBalancer) whose trigger type is 'Configuration changes'. Because it is change-triggered, AWS Config re-evaluates the ALB the instant the WAF (Web ACL) association is removed and marks the load balancer NON_COMPLIANT. AWS Config natively supports automatic remediation by associating an AWS Systems Manager Automation document with the rule and turning on 'Automatic remediation' (PutRemediationConfigurations); the Automation document then re-associates AWS WAF to the ALB with no custom polling code or stack redeployment. This managed, event-driven flow with a built-in remediation action requires the least operational effort, which is exactly what option A describes.","explanation_zh":"AWS Config 提供受管規則 alb-waf-enabled（識別碼 ALB_WAF_ENABLED，資源類型 AWS::ElasticLoadBalancingV2::LoadBalancer），其觸發類型為「Configuration changes（組態變更）」。由於是變更觸發，一旦從 ALB 移除 WAF（Web ACL）關聯，AWS Config 會立即重新評估該 ALB 並標記為 NON_COMPLIANT。AWS Config 原生支援自動修復：將一份 AWS Systems Manager Automation document 關聯到該規則並開啟「Automatic remediation（自動修復）」（PutRemediationConfigurations），該 Automation document 便會自動把 AWS WAF 重新關聯到 ALB，無需自訂輪詢程式碼或重新部署堆疊。此受管、事件驅動且內建修復動作的流程所需的維運成本最低，正是選項 A 所描述的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Calling start-resource-evaluation in detective mode only re-evaluates and reports COMPLIANT/NON_COMPLIANT status; it performs no remediation, so AWS WAF is never re-added to the ALB. The design is also circular (re-triggering evaluation from evaluation notifications) and adds unnecessary Lambda code.","why_zh":"以 detective 模式呼叫 start-resource-evaluation 只會重新評估並回報 COMPLIANT/NON_COMPLIANT 狀態，完全不執行修復，因此永遠不會把 AWS WAF 重新加回 ALB。此設計也是循環的（用評估通知再次觸發評估），並增加不必要的 Lambda 程式碼。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Periodic detect-stack-drift is slower and less efficient than change-triggered Config, and the remediation is technically wrong: waf.fail_open.enabled only controls whether traffic is allowed through when the WAF is unavailable. It does not re-associate a Web ACL, so WAF is not actually restored on the ALB.","why_zh":"週期性的 detect-stack-drift 比變更觸發的 Config 更慢且效率更低，且其修復動作在技術上是錯的：waf.fail_open.enabled 僅控制當 WAF 不可用時是否放行流量，並不會重新關聯 Web ACL，因此實際上並未把 WAF 還原到 ALB。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Periodic detect-stack-drift is less timely than change-triggered Config, and deleting then redeploying the entire CloudFormation stack to restore a single Web ACL association is highly disruptive (it tears down the ALB and the whole application stack, causing downtime). This is the opposite of the MOST operationally efficient approach.","why_zh":"週期性的 detect-stack-drift 不如變更觸發的 Config 即時，且為了還原單一 Web ACL 關聯而刪除並重新部署整個 CloudFormation 堆疊極具破壞性（會拆掉 ALB 及整個應用程式堆疊並造成停機）。這與「最高維運效率」的要求恰恰相反。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/alb-waf-enabled.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/setup-autoremediation.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/evaluate-config_components.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-stack-drift.html"]}},{"id":364,"question_en":"A company is developing an ecommerce application on AWS. The company wants to make sure that the application can handle sudden increases in traffic. The company uses AWS CodePipeline for its CI/CD process. The company must implement a solution to integrate automated load testing into the CI/CD pipeline to validate the application's performance. The solution must perform production deployment only if the performance exceeds a threshold. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上开发一个电子商务应用程序。该公司希望确保该应用程序能够应对流量的突然增 加。 该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 来执行其持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）流程。该公司必须实施一个解决 方案，将自动化负载测试集成到 CI/CD 管道中，以验证应用程序的性能。只有在性能超过阈值的情况 下，该解决方案才能执行生产部署。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application by using AWS Elastic Beanstalk. Enable load balancing. Use Elastic Beanstalk to deploy tools for load tests. Run the tests during each deployment, and roll back the deployment if performance thresholds are unmet. Create an AWS Lambda function to monitor test metrics. Set up alarms for performance thresholds. Configure Amazon EventBridge to return an error if a test fails and to proceed with production deployment if a test passes.","B":"Implement AWS Fargate tasks to run tools for load tests. Use Amazon Elastic container Service (Amazon ECS) to manage the test containers. Create AWS Lambda functions to analyze the test results. Integrate the functions with CodePipeline by using custom actions to initiate and evaluate the tests. Program the functions to return an error if a test fails and to proceed with production deployment if a test passes.","C":"Launch Amazon EC2 instances to run tools for load tests. Store test scripts in a GitHub repository. Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate the tests and result analysis in the CodePipeline workflow. Use Amazon EventBridge to invoke an AWS Lambda function based on the test results. Program the function to return an error if a test fails and to proceed with production deployment if a test passes.","D":"Use AWS CodeBuild to run tools for load tests, store the test artifacts in Amazon S3, and configure a CodePipeline stage to invoke the CodeBuild project. Use Amazon CloudWatch to monitor the test metrics and to set up alarms for performance thresholds. Integrate an AWS Lambda function into the pipeline by using a custom action. Program the function to return an error if a test fails and to proceed with production deployment if a test passes."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 部署应用程序。启用负载均衡。使用 Elastic Beanstalk 部署负载测试工具。 在每次部署期间运行测试，如果未达到性能阈值则回滚部署。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来监控测 试指标。为性能阈值设置警报。配置 Amazon EventBridge，如果测试失败则返回错误，如果测试通 过则继续进行生产部署。","B":"实施 AWS Fargate 任务以运行负载测试工具。使用亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）管理测试容 器。创建 AWS Lambda 函数来分析测试结果。通过使用自定义操作将这些函数与 CodePipeline 集成， 以启动和评估测试。编写函数，使其在测试失败时返回错误，并在测试通过时继续进行生产部署。","C":"启动 Amazon EC2 实例以运行负载测试工具。将测试脚本存储在 GitHub 代码库中。使用 AWS Step Functions 在 CodePipeline 工作流中编排测试和结果分析。使用 Amazon EventBridge 根据测试结果调 用 AWS Lambda 函数。编写该函数，使其在测试失败时返回错误，在测试通过时继续进行生产部署。","D":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 运行负载测试工具，将测试工件存储在 Amazon S3 中，并配置 CodePipeline 阶 段以调用 CodeBuild 项目。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 监控测试指标，并为性能阈值设置警报。通过 自定义操作将 AWS Lambda 函数集成到管道中。编写函数，使其在测试失败时返回错误，并在测 试通过时继续进行生产部署。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The decisive qualifier is LEAST operational overhead for integrating automated load testing into CodePipeline so production deploys only when performance passes a threshold. AWS CodeBuild is a fully managed build/test service that plugs into CodePipeline as a native action (Category: Build or Test, Owner: AWS, Provider: CodeBuild). It runs arbitrary load-test tooling via a buildspec inside a managed container with no servers to provision, stores artifacts natively in Amazon S3, and a failing CodeBuild action automatically fails the stage, which blocks the pipeline from reaching the production deploy stage. CloudWatch is the native service for collecting CodeBuild test metrics and setting threshold alarms, and Lambda can be added directly as an invoke action to evaluate results and pass/fail the pipeline (via PutJobSuccessResult/PutJobFailureResult). Option D therefore relies only on fully managed services with native pipeline integration, giving the lowest overhead. Option C self-manages EC2 instances (most overhead); Option B requires defining and managing ECS+Fargate tasks plus custom-action job workers; Option A is architecturally incoherent because EventBridge does not gate a CodePipeline stage the way described.","explanation_zh":"決定性的限定詞是「最少維運負擔」(LEAST operational overhead),要在 CodePipeline 中整合自動化負載測試,並只在效能達標時才部署到正式環境。AWS CodeBuild 是全代管的 build/test 服務,可作為原生 action 直接整合進 CodePipeline(Category: Build 或 Test、Owner: AWS、Provider: CodeBuild)。它透過 buildspec 在代管容器中執行任意負載測試工具,不需自行佈建伺服器,artifacts 原生存放在 Amazon S3;當 CodeBuild action 失敗時會自動讓該 stage 失敗,進而阻止流程進入正式部署 stage。CloudWatch 是收集 CodeBuild 測試指標並設定門檻警示(alarm)的原生服務,而 Lambda 可作為 invoke action 直接加入,用以評估結果並透過 PutJobSuccessResult/PutJobFailureResult 決定流程通過或失敗。因此選項 D 全部採用具原生 pipeline 整合的全代管服務,維運負擔最低。選項 C 自管 EC2(負擔最高);選項 B 需定義與管理 ECS+Fargate 任務並建置自訂 action 的 job worker;選項 A 在架構上不一致,因為 EventBridge 並非以所述方式把關 CodePipeline 的 stage。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Elastic Beanstalk does not natively 'deploy tools for load tests', and gluing load testing onto EB deployments with a Lambda monitor plus EventBridge to gate the pipeline is convoluted. EventBridge does not directly gate CodePipeline stage progression; pipeline flow is controlled by action success/failure. This design adds operational overhead rather than reducing it.","why_zh":"Elastic Beanstalk 並不原生「部署負載測試工具」,把負載測試硬塞進 EB 部署、再用 Lambda 監控加 EventBridge 來把關流程的設計相當迂迴。EventBridge 無法直接把關 CodePipeline 的 stage 進度;流程是由 action 的成功/失敗控制。此設計反而增加維運負擔。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Requires building and managing ECS task definitions and container images for Fargate, plus a custom CodePipeline action whose job worker must poll (PollForJobs) and report results. Custom actions and self-managed containers add notably more operational overhead than the fully managed CodeBuild Build/Test action, which needs none of that.","why_zh":"需要為 Fargate 建立並管理 ECS task definition 與容器映像,還要建立自訂 CodePipeline action,其 job worker 必須輪詢(PollForJobs)並回報結果。自訂 action 與自管容器比起全代管的 CodeBuild Build/Test action(完全不需這些)明顯增加維運負擔。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Highest operational overhead: self-managed EC2 instances to run the load tools, an external GitHub repo for scripts, Step Functions orchestration, and EventBridge plus Lambda wiring. Managing EC2 patching, scaling, and the orchestration glue far exceeds what the LEAST-overhead requirement allows, and EventBridge again is not the mechanism that gates a CodePipeline stage.","why_zh":"維運負擔最高:需自管 EC2 執行負載工具、用外部 GitHub repo 存放腳本、Step Functions 編排,再加上 EventBridge 與 Lambda 串接。管理 EC2 的修補、擴縮與編排黏合,遠超過「最少負擔」的要求,且 EventBridge 同樣不是把關 CodePipeline stage 的機制。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CodeBuild.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-invoke-lambda-function.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-create-custom-action.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pipeline.html"]}},{"id":365,"question_en":"A company needs to update its order processing application to improve resilience and availability. The application requires a stateful database and uses a single-node Amazon RDS DB instance to store customer orders and transaction history. A DevOps engineer must make the database highly available. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司需要更新其订单处理应用程序以提高其弹性和可用性。该应用程序需要一个有状态的数据库， 并使用单节点的 Amazon RDS 数据库实例来存储客户订单和交易历史记录。一位 DevOps 工程师必须 使该数据库具备高可用性。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Migrate the database to Amazon DynamoDB global tables. Configure automatic failover between AWS Regions by using Amazon Route 53 health checks.","B":"Migrate the database to Amazon EC2 instances in multiple Availability Zones. Use Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) Multi-Attach to connect all the instances to a single EBS volume.","C":"Use the RDS DB instance as the source instance to create read replicas in multiple Availability Zones. Deploy an Application Load Balancer to distribute read traffic across the read replicas.","D":"Modify the RDS DB instance to be a Multi-AZ deployment. Verify automatic failover to the standby instance if the primary instance becomes unavailable."},"options_zh":{"A":"将数据库迁移到 Amazon DynamoDB 全球表。通过使用 Amazon Route 53 健康检查在 AWS 区域之间配 置自动故障转移。","B":"将数据库迁移到多个可用区的 Amazon EC2 实例上。使用 Amazon Elastic Block Store（Amazon EBS）多挂载功能将所有实例连接到单个 EBS 卷。","C":"使用 RDS 数据库实例作为源实例，在多个可用区创建只读副本。部署应用负载均衡器以将读取流量 分配到各个只读副本。","D":"将 RDS 数据库实例修改为多可用区部署。如果主实例不可用，验证是否能自动故障转移到备用实 例。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to make a single-node, stateful Amazon RDS relational database highly available with minimal change. Amazon RDS Multi-AZ DB instance deployments are purpose-built for exactly this: RDS automatically provisions and maintains a synchronous standby replica in a different Availability Zone, and if the primary instance fails (instance failure, AZ disruption, or maintenance), RDS automatically fails over to the standby by repointing the DB endpoint's DNS CNAME, with no application changes or manual intervention. You enable it by simply modifying the existing DB instance to specify Multi-AZ, so it keeps the managed relational engine and adds HA with the least operational overhead. The AWS docs state Multi-AZ 'provides high availability and failover support for DB instances' and 'automatically provisions and maintains a synchronous standby replica in a different Availability Zone,' and explicitly note the HA option is not a read-scaling solution. Read replicas (C) are asynchronous and read-only and do not provide automatic write failover, and DynamoDB (A) and EC2/EBS Multi-Attach (B) abandon the managed relational model entirely.","explanation_zh":"需求是讓單節點、有狀態的 Amazon RDS 關聯式資料庫達成高可用性，且改動最小。Amazon RDS Multi-AZ DB instance 部署正是為此設計：RDS 會在另一個 Availability Zone 自動佈建並維護一個同步的 standby replica，當主要執行個體故障（執行個體故障、AZ 中斷或維護）時，RDS 會透過重新指向 DB endpoint 的 DNS CNAME 自動容錯移轉至 standby，不需修改應用程式或人工介入。只要修改現有 DB instance 啟用 Multi-AZ 即可，因此保留受管的關聯式引擎，並以最低營運負擔加上 HA。AWS 文件明確指出 Multi-AZ「為 DB instance 提供高可用性與容錯移轉支援」，並會「在另一個 Availability Zone 自動佈建並維護一個同步的 standby replica」，同時明確說明此 HA 選項並非讀取擴展方案。Read replica（C）為非同步且唯讀，無法提供自動寫入容錯移轉；DynamoDB（A）與 EC2/EBS Multi-Attach（B）則完全捨棄受管關聯式模型。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"DynamoDB is a NoSQL key-value/document store, not a relational database; migrating an order/transaction relational schema to DynamoDB global tables is a major re-architecture, not a simple HA enablement, and introduces multi-Region eventual consistency. Route 53 cross-Region health-check failover is also unnecessary for AZ-level HA and adds complexity.","why_zh":"DynamoDB 是 NoSQL 鍵值/文件儲存，並非關聯式資料庫；把訂單/交易關聯式結構遷移到 DynamoDB global tables 是大規模重新架構，而非單純啟用 HA，且引入多區域最終一致性。Route 53 跨 Region 健康檢查容錯移轉對 AZ 層級 HA 也屬多餘並增加複雜度。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Running the database yourself on EC2 abandons the managed RDS service and adds large operational overhead. EBS Multi-Attach attaches one io1/io2 volume to multiple instances in the SAME Availability Zone (not across AZs) and does not provide write coordination without a cluster-aware filesystem, so the single shared volume is itself a single point of failure and provides no automatic database failover.","why_zh":"在 EC2 上自管資料庫等於放棄受管的 RDS 服務並大幅增加營運負擔。EBS Multi-Attach 是將單一 io1/io2 磁碟區掛載到「同一個」Availability Zone 內的多個執行個體（無法跨 AZ），且若無叢集感知檔案系統便無法協調寫入，因此該單一共用磁碟區本身就是單點故障，也不提供自動資料庫容錯移轉。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Read replicas use asynchronous replication and are read-only; an Application Load Balancer cannot route writes to a replica, and there is no automatic promotion/failover of the writer on primary failure. AWS docs explicitly state read replicas are a read-scaling feature, and that the Multi-AZ HA option (not replicas) provides failover; the single primary remains a single point of failure for writes.","why_zh":"Read replica 採非同步複寫且為唯讀；Application Load Balancer 無法將寫入導向 replica，主要執行個體故障時也沒有自動提升/容錯移轉寫入端的機制。AWS 文件明確指出 read replica 是讀取擴展功能，而提供容錯移轉的是 Multi-AZ HA 選項（而非 replica）；單一 primary 對寫入仍是單點故障。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Concepts.MultiAZSingleStandby.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Concepts.MultiAZ.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/USER_ReadRepl.html"]}},{"id":366,"question_en":"A company has application code in an AWS CodeConnections compatible Git repository. The company wants to configure unit tests to run when pull requests are opened. The company wants to ensure that the test status is visible in pull requests when the tests are completed. The company wants to save output data files that the tests generate to an Amazon S3 bucket after the tests are finished. Which combination of solutions will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司将其应用程序代码存放在与 AWS CodeCommit 兼容的 Git 代码库中。该公司希望在打开拉取请 求时运行单元测试，并确保测试完成后在拉取请求中显示测试状态。该公司还希望在测试结束后将测试生 成的输出数据文件保存到 Amazon S3 存储桶中。 哪种解决方案的组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create an IAM service role to allow access to the resources that are required to run the tests. B Create a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline that has a test stage. Create a trigger to run the pipeline when pull requests are created or updated. Add a source action to report test results.","B":"Create an AWS CodeBuild project to run the tests. Enable webhook triggers to run the tests when pull requests are created or updated. Enable build status reporting to report test results.","C":"Create a buildspec.yml file that has a reports section to upload output files when the tests have finished running.","D":"Create a buildspec.yml file that has an artifacts section to upload artifacts when the tests have finished running.","E":"Create an appspec.yml file that has a files section to upload output files when the tests have finished running."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 IAM 服务角色，以允许访问运行测试所需的资源。B. 在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个 具有测试阶段的管道。创建一个触发器，以便在创建或更新拉取请求时运行管道。添加一个源 操作以报告测试结果。","B":"创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来运行测试。启用网络钩子触发器，以便在创建或更新拉取请求时运 行测试。启用构建状态报告以报告测试结果。","C":"创建一个包含“reports”部分的 buildspec.yml 文件，以便在测试运行结束后上传输出文件。","D":"创建一个包含 artifacts（工件）部分的 buildspec.yml 文件，以便在测试完成后上传工件。","E":"创建一个 appspec.yml 文件，其中包含一个 files 部分，以便在测试运行结束后上传输出文件。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A","B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"Use a webhook-driven CodeBuild flow. (A) Create an IAM service role so CodeBuild can access the resources it needs (the source connection, CloudWatch Logs, and the S3 bucket it writes to). (B) Create a CodeBuild project to run the tests, enable webhook triggers so the build runs when pull requests are created or updated, and enable build status reporting so CodeBuild posts the result back to the source provider (reportBuildStatus), making the test status visible directly in the pull request - this covers requirements 1 and 2. (D) Add an artifacts section to buildspec.yml; the artifacts section is the general-purpose mechanism that uploads arbitrary build output files to an Amazon S3 bucket, which is exactly how you save the 'output data files that the tests generate.' Option C is the trap: the buildspec reports section is purpose-built only for structured test-result/code-coverage report files (JUnit XML, NUnit XML, Cucumber JSON, TestNG, Visual Studio TRX, code-coverage formats), which represent 'the raw data of test results' and flow into a report group, not arbitrary generated data files, so it does not meet the requirement the way the artifacts section does. Option E is wrong because appspec.yml is a CodeDeploy construct whose files section maps source files onto deployment targets; it neither runs CodeBuild tests nor uploads files to S3. The dump answer A/C/E is wrong on both C and E.","explanation_zh":"採用由 webhook 觸發的 CodeBuild 流程。(A) 建立 IAM service role,讓 CodeBuild 能存取所需資源(source connection、CloudWatch Logs,以及要寫入的 S3 bucket)。(B) 建立 CodeBuild project 來執行測試,啟用 webhook triggers,使 pull request 建立或更新時觸發建置,並啟用 build status reporting,讓 CodeBuild 透過 reportBuildStatus 把結果回報給 source provider,使測試狀態直接顯示在 pull request 中,涵蓋需求 1 和 2。(D) 在 buildspec.yml 加上 artifacts 區段;artifacts 區段是把任意建置輸出檔案上傳到 Amazon S3 bucket 的通用機制,正是用來儲存「測試產生的 output data files」的做法。選項 C 是陷阱:buildspec 的 reports 區段只用於結構化的測試結果/覆蓋率報告檔(JUnit XML、NUnit XML、Cucumber JSON、TestNG、Visual Studio TRX、覆蓋率格式),這些代表「測試結果的原始資料」並進入 report group,而非任意產生的資料檔,因此無法像 artifacts 區段那樣滿足需求。選項 E 錯誤,因為 appspec.yml 屬於 CodeDeploy,其 files 區段是把來源檔案對應到部署目標,既不會執行 CodeBuild 測試,也不會上傳檔案到 S3。dump 的 A/C/E 在 C 與 E 兩處都不正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"The buildspec reports section is purpose-built only for structured test-result/code-coverage report files (JUnit XML, NUnit XML, Cucumber JSON, TestNG, Visual Studio TRX) that flow into a CodeBuild report group; it represents 'the raw data of test results,' not the arbitrary output data files the tests generate, so it does not satisfy the S3 file-save requirement the way the generic artifacts section (D) does.","why_zh":"buildspec 的 reports 區段只用於結構化的測試結果/覆蓋率報告檔(JUnit XML、NUnit XML、Cucumber JSON、TestNG、Visual Studio TRX),這些會進入 CodeBuild report group,代表「測試結果的原始資料」,而非測試產生的任意 output data files,因此無法像通用的 artifacts 區段 (D) 那樣滿足儲存到 S3 的需求。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"appspec.yml is an AWS CodeDeploy construct, not a CodeBuild construct. Its files section copies source files onto deployment targets (EC2/on-prem/Lambda/ECS) during a deployment; it does not run tests, is not used by CodeBuild, and does not upload output files to an S3 bucket.","why_zh":"appspec.yml 是 AWS CodeDeploy 的構件,不是 CodeBuild 的構件。其 files 區段在部署期間把來源檔案複製到部署目標(EC2/地端/Lambda/ECS),它不執行測試、不被 CodeBuild 使用,也不會把輸出檔案上傳到 S3 bucket。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/sample-github-pull-request.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/github-webhook.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/test-reporting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/setting-up-service-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/reference-appspec-file.html"]}},{"id":367,"question_en":"A software development team is implementing a CI/CD pipeline for its web application. The team is using AWS CodeBuild to compile Java-based source code and to run unit tests. The team needs to store the artifacts that are created by the CodeBuild project. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一个软件开发团队正在为其网络应用程序实施持续集成/持续部署（CI/CD）流水线。该团队使用 AWS CodeBuild 来编译基于 Java 的源代码并运行单元测试。 团队需要存储由 CodeBuild 项目创建的工件。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the S3 bucket as an artifact output location in the project. Add the artifact locations to the project's buildspec file. Configure an S3 bucket policy that allows the CodeBuild project's resource access role to access the S3 bucket.","B":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure the S3 bucket as an artifact output location in the project's buildspec file. Add the artifact locations to the project's buildspec file. Configure an S3 bucket policy that allows the CodeBuild service role to access the S3 bucket.","C":"Configure an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system as a file system location for the project. Configure the EFS file system as the artifact output location in the project's buildspec file. Configure a file system policy that allows CodeBuild to access the file system.","D":"Create an Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volume. Configure the EBS volume as the artifact output location in the project's buildspec file. Configure an IAM role that allows CodeBuild to access the volume."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。在项目中将 S3 存储桶配置为工件输出位置。将工件位置添加到项目的 buildspec 文件中。配置一个 S3 存储桶策略，允许 CodeBuild 项目的资源访问角色访问该 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。在项目的 buildspec 文件中将 S3 存储桶配置为工件输出位置。将工件位 置添加到项目的 buildspec 文件中。 配置一个 S3 存储桶策略，允许 CodeBuild 服务角色访问该 S3 存储桶。","C":"为项目配置一个 Amazon 弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS）文件系统作为文件系统位置。在项目的 buildspec 文件中将 EFS 文件系统配置为构建输出位置。配置一个文件系统策略，允许 CodeBuild 访 问该文件系统。","D":"创建一个亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷。在项目的 buildspec 文件中将 EBS 卷配置为工件输出 位置。配置一个 IAM 角色，允许 CodeBuild 访问该卷。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS CodeBuild stores build output artifacts in an Amazon S3 bucket, so the team should create an S3 bucket and configure it as the project's artifact output location, while the buildspec file's 'artifacts' section declares which files to package. The decisive point is the IAM principal that needs bucket access: per the CodeBuild documentation, 'CodeBuild uses the service role for all operations that are performed on your behalf,' which includes uploading output artifacts to S3. Therefore the S3 bucket policy (and/or the service role's IAM policy) must grant access to the CodeBuild service role, exactly as Option B states. Option A is nearly identical but grants access to a 'CodeBuild project's resource access role,' which is not a real CodeBuild concept (the correct principal is the service role), so A fails on the decisive IAM-principal detail. Options C and D are invalid because Amazon EFS and Amazon EBS are not CodeBuild output-artifact targets (EFS can only be mounted as a file system location during a build, and EBS is not a CodeBuild artifact concept at all).","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeBuild 會將建置輸出 artifacts 儲存到 Amazon S3 bucket，因此團隊應建立一個 S3 bucket，並在專案中將其設定為 artifact 輸出位置，同時由 buildspec 檔案的 'artifacts' 區段宣告要打包哪些檔案。關鍵在於需要存取 bucket 的 IAM principal：根據 CodeBuild 文件，'CodeBuild 會使用 service role 執行代你執行的所有操作'，其中包含將輸出 artifacts 上傳到 S3。因此 S3 bucket policy（與／或 service role 的 IAM policy）必須授權給 CodeBuild service role，這正是選項 B 所描述的。選項 A 幾乎相同，但卻將存取權授予「CodeBuild 專案的 resource access role」，這並非真實存在的 CodeBuild 概念（正確的 principal 是 service role），因此 A 在關鍵的 IAM principal 細節上錯誤。選項 C 與 D 無效，因為 Amazon EFS 與 Amazon EBS 並非 CodeBuild 的輸出 artifact 目標（EFS 只能在建置期間作為 file system location 掛載，而 EBS 根本不是 CodeBuild 的 artifact 概念）。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"S3 is the correct artifact store, but the bucket policy grants access to a 'CodeBuild project's resource access role,' which is not a real CodeBuild concept. CodeBuild performs all on-your-behalf operations (including writing artifacts to S3) using its service role, so the principal must be the service role, not an invented 'resource access role.'","why_zh":"S3 是正確的 artifact 儲存位置，但其 bucket policy 將存取權授予「CodeBuild 專案的 resource access role」，這並非真實存在的 CodeBuild 概念。CodeBuild 是以其 service role 執行代你執行的所有操作（包含將 artifacts 寫入 S3），因此 principal 必須是 service role，而非虛構的「resource access role」。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon EFS is not a CodeBuild output-artifact destination. EFS can be mounted as a file system location for a build to read/write shared data during execution, but build output artifacts are uploaded to Amazon S3, not stored in EFS as an artifact output location.","why_zh":"Amazon EFS 並非 CodeBuild 的輸出 artifact 目的地。EFS 可作為 file system location 掛載，讓建置在執行期間讀寫共用資料，但建置輸出 artifacts 是上傳到 Amazon S3，而非以 EFS 作為 artifact 輸出位置。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Amazon EBS is not a CodeBuild artifact concept at all. CodeBuild does not let you attach an EBS volume as an artifact output location; output artifacts are written to Amazon S3.","why_zh":"Amazon EBS 根本不是 CodeBuild 的 artifact 概念。CodeBuild 不允許將 EBS volume 作為 artifact 輸出位置掛載；輸出 artifacts 是寫入 Amazon S3。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/setting-up-service-role.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/create-project.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-codebuild-project-artifacts.html"]}},{"id":368,"question_en":"A company uses AWS Organizations to manage multiple AWS accounts. The accounts are in an OU that has a policy attached to allow all actions. The company is migrating several Git repositories to a specified AWS CodeConnections supported Git provider. The Git repositories manage AWS CloudFormation stacks for application infrastructure that the company deploys across multiple AWS Regions. The company wants a DevOps team to integrate CodeConnections into the CloudFormation stacks. The DevOps team must ensure that company staff members can integrate only with the specified Git provider. The deployment process must be highly available across Regions. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS Organizations 来管理多个 AWS 账户。这些账户位于一个组织单元（OU）中，该组织单 元附有一个允许执行所有操作的策略。该公司正在将多个 Git 代码库迁移到指定的 AWS CodeCommit 支持 的 Git 提供商。这些 Git 代码库管理着公司跨多个 AWS 区域部署的应用程序基础设施的 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈。 该公司希望组建一个 DevOps 团队将 CodeConnections 集成到 CloudFormation 堆栈中。DevOps 团队必须确 保公司员工只能与指定的 Git 提供商进行集成。部署过程必须在各区域都具备高可用性。 哪种步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Add a new SCP statement to the OU that denies the CodeConnections CreatingConnections action where the provider type is not the specified Git provider.","B":"Add a new SCP statement to the OU that allows the CodeConnections CreatingConnections action where the provider type is the specified Git provider.","C":"Use CodeConnectlons to configure a single CodeConnections connection to each Git repository.","D":"Use CodeConnections to create a CodeConnections connection from each Region where the company operates to each Git repository.","E":"Use CodeConnections to create a CodeConnections repository link. Update each CfoudFormation stack to sync from the Git repository.","F":"For each Git repository, create a pipeline in AWS CodePipefine that has the Git repository set as the source and a CloudFormation deployment stage."},"options_zh":{"A":"向组织单位添加一个新的 SCP 语句，拒绝提供程序类型不是指定的 Git 提供程序的 CodeConnections CreatingConnections 操作。","B":"向该组织单位添加一个新的 SCP 语句，允许在提供程序类型为指定的 Git 提供程序时执行 CodeConnections 的 CreatingConnections 操作。","C":"使用 CodeConnectlons 为每个 Git 代码库配置一个 CodeConnections 连接。","D":"使用 CodeConnections 从公司运营的每个区域到每个 Git 代码库创建一个 CodeConnections 连接。","E":"使用 CodeConnections 创建一个 CodeConnections 代码库链接。更新每个 CloudFormation 堆栈以从 Git 代码库同步。","F":"对于每个 Git 代码库，在 AWS CodePipeline 中创建一个管道，将该 Git 代码库设置为源，并添加一 个 CloudFormation 部署阶段。"},"answer":["A","D","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":3,"diff_why":"複選・題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The integration uses CloudFormation Git sync: connect the Git provider with CodeConnections, create a repository link, and update each CloudFormation stack to sync from the Git repository (E). To restrict staff to only the specified provider, note the OU already has an allow-all (FullAWSAccess-style) policy. SCPs are deny-list guardrails, so an extra Allow statement subtracts nothing; you must add a Deny on the CreateConnection action where codeconnections:ProviderType is NOT the specified provider (A). The Service Authorization Reference confirms codeconnections:CreateConnection supports the codeconnections:ProviderType condition key, and the CreateConnection API takes a ProviderType parameter, so this Deny is enforceable. For high availability across Regions, the key fact is that AWS CodeConnections connections are GLOBAL resources: the AWS docs state a connection is replicated across all AWS Regions, you create it once and can use it in any Region, and if the creating Region has issues you can still use the connection in every other Region. Therefore a single connection per repository (C) is inherently highly available across Regions. The dump answer and first analyst chose D (a connection from each Region to each repository), but that is technically wrong: connections are not per-Region resources, so creating one per Region is unnecessary and contradicts the global-resource model. The correct combination is A, C, E.","explanation_zh":"整合方式為 CloudFormation Git sync：以 CodeConnections 連接 Git provider、建立 repository link，並更新每個 CloudFormation stack 從 Git repository 同步（E）。要限制員工只能整合指定的 Git provider，需注意該 OU 已套用 allow-all（等同 FullAWSAccess）政策。SCP 是 deny-list 護欄，額外再加 Allow 並不會減少任何權限；必須對 CreateConnection 動作加上 Deny，條件為 codeconnections:ProviderType 不等於指定 provider（A）。依 Service Authorization Reference，codeconnections:CreateConnection 支援 codeconnections:ProviderType 條件鍵，且 CreateConnection API 本身就帶 ProviderType 參數，故此 Deny 可強制執行。關於跨 Region 高可用，關鍵事實是 AWS CodeConnections 的 connection 屬於『全域（global）』資源：AWS 文件明載 connection 會複寫到所有 AWS Region，只需建立一次即可在任何 Region 使用；即使建立該 connection 的 Region 發生問題，仍可在其他所有 Region 正常使用該 connection。因此每個 repository 只建立單一 connection（C）本身即跨 Region 高可用。題庫答案與第一位分析師選了 D（從每個 Region 各對每個 repository 建立 connection），但這在技術上是錯的：connection 並非 Region 級資源，逐 Region 建立既無必要也與全域資源模型相矛盾。正確組合為 A、C、E。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Adding an Allow SCP statement does nothing when the OU already has FullAWSAccess (allow all). SCP Allow statements only define the permission ceiling and cannot subtract other providers; only an explicit Deny on CreateConnection with a codeconnections:ProviderType condition blocks unwanted provider types.","why_zh":"在 OU 已有 FullAWSAccess（允許所有動作）時，再加一條 Allow SCP 毫無作用。SCP 的 Allow 只界定權限上限，無法排除其他 provider；唯有對 CreateConnection 加上以 codeconnections:ProviderType 為條件的明確 Deny，才能封鎖不想要的 provider 類型。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CodeConnections connections are GLOBAL resources replicated across all Regions; per AWS docs you create a connection once and can use it in any Region, and it survives an outage of its creating Region. Creating a connection from each Region to each repository is unnecessary and contradicts how the service works, so it is not the HA mechanism the question wants.","why_zh":"CodeConnections 的 connection 屬於全域資源，會複寫至所有 Region；依 AWS 文件，只需建立一次即可在任何 Region 使用，且能在建立 Region 故障時於其他 Region 繼續使用。從每個 Region 各對每個 repository 建立 connection 既無必要、也與服務運作方式相矛盾，並非題目要求的高可用機制。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Creating a CodePipeline with a CloudFormation deployment stage integrates CodeConnections into a pipeline, not into the CloudFormation stacks themselves. The requirement is to integrate CodeConnections into the stacks via Git sync, which is option E; F also adds nothing toward the global-connection HA point.","why_zh":"建立含 CloudFormation 部署階段的 CodePipeline，是把 CodeConnections 整合進 pipeline，而非整合進 CloudFormation stacks 本身。題目要求透過 Git sync 整合進 stacks，對應選項 E；且 F 對全域 connection 帶來的高可用亦無幫助。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dtconsole/latest/userguide/welcome-connections-how-it-works-global.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/git-sync-concepts-terms.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/git-sync-prereq.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/service-authorization/latest/reference/list_awscodeconnections.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeconnections/latest/APIReference/API_CreateConnection.html"]}},{"id":369,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer updates an AWS CloudFormation stack to add a nested stack that includes several Amazon EC2 instances. When the DevOps engineer attempts to deploy the updated stack, the nested stack fails to deploy. What should the DevOps engineer do to determine the cause of the failure?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师更新了一个 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈，以添加一个包含多个 Amazon EC2 实例的 嵌套堆栈。当该 DevOps 工程师尝试部署更新后的堆栈时，嵌套堆栈部署失败。 DevOps 工程师应该怎么做才能确定故障的原因？","options_en":{"A":"Use the CloudFormation detect root cause capability for the failed stack to analyze the failure and return the event that is the most likely cause for the failure.","B":"Query failed stacks by specifying the root stack as the ParentId property. Examine the StackStatusReason property for all returned stacks to determine the reason the nested stack failed to deploy.","C":"Activate AWS Systems Manager for the AWS account where the application runs. Use the AWS Systems Manager Automation AWS-SupportTroubleshootCFNCustomResource runbook to determine the reason the nested stack failed to deploy.","D":"Configure the CloudFormation template to publish logs to Amazon CloudWatch. View the CloudFormation logs for the failed stack in the CloudWatch console to determine the reason the nested stack failed to deploy."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 CloudFormation 的检测根本原因功能来分析失败的堆栈，并返回最有可能导致失败的事件。","B":"通过将根堆栈指定为 ParentId 属性来查询失败的堆栈。检查所有返回堆栈的 StackStatusReason 属性， 以确定嵌套堆栈部署失败的原因。","C":"为运行应用程序的 AWS 账户激活 AWS Systems Manager。使用 AWS Systems Manager Automation 中 的 AWS-SupportTroubleshootCFNCustomResource 运行手册来确定嵌套堆栈部署失败的原因。","D":"配置 CloudFormation 模板以将日志发布到 Amazon CloudWatch。在 CloudWatch 控制台中查看失败堆 栈的 CloudFormation 日志，以确定嵌套堆栈部署失败的原因。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When a nested stack fails, the root (parent) stack rolls back with only a generic message such as \"Embedded stack ... was not successfully updated,\" so the real error lives on the failed nested stack itself. The CloudFormation DescribeStacks API returns Stack objects that include both a ParentId property (\"For nested stacks, the stack ID of the direct parent of this stack; for the first level of nested stacks, the root stack is also the parent stack\") and a StackStatusReason property that holds the human-readable failure message from CloudFormation or the underlying service (here, the EC2 error). By querying the failed stacks associated with the root stack as the parent and inspecting each StackStatusReason, the engineer pinpoints the actual cause. Option A is disqualified for a subtle reason: CloudFormation does have a real \"Detect root cause\" feature, but the AWS documentation explicitly states that \"Nested stacks don't support Detect root cause,\" so it cannot be used in this nested-stack scenario. Option C's AWSSupport-TroubleshootCFNCustomResource runbook only diagnoses custom-resource failures, not EC2 instances, and Option D references a non-existent capability to publish generic \"CloudFormation logs\" for a failed stack to CloudWatch from the template.","explanation_zh":"當 nested stack 部署失敗時，root（parent）stack 只會以類似 \"Embedded stack ... was not successfully updated\" 的籠統訊息回滾，真正的錯誤其實位於失敗的 nested stack 本身。CloudFormation 的 DescribeStacks API 回傳的 Stack 物件同時包含 ParentId 屬性（文件定義為「對 nested stack 而言是其直接 parent 的 stack ID；第一層 nested stack 的 root stack 同時也是 parent stack」）以及 StackStatusReason 屬性（內含來自 CloudFormation 或底層服務的可讀失敗訊息，本例即 EC2 錯誤）。透過以 root stack 作為 parent 查詢失敗的 stacks，並檢視每個 stack 的 StackStatusReason，工程師即可定位真正原因。選項 A 不成立的原因較細緻：CloudFormation 確實有真實的 Detect root cause 功能，但 AWS 文件明確指出「Nested stacks 不支援 Detect root cause」，因此無法用於此 nested stack 情境。選項 C 的 AWSSupport-TroubleshootCFNCustomResource runbook 只診斷 custom resource 失敗，不適用於 EC2 instances；選項 D 提到的「從 template 將失敗 stack 的通用 CloudFormation logs 發布到 CloudWatch」功能並不存在。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CloudFormation's 'Detect root cause' is a genuine console feature, but AWS documentation explicitly states 'Nested stacks don't support Detect root cause,' so it cannot diagnose this nested-stack failure. (It is also a console action, not an API 'capability.')","why_zh":"CloudFormation 的 Detect root cause 是真實的主控台功能，但 AWS 文件明確說明「Nested stacks 不支援 Detect root cause」，因此無法用於診斷此 nested stack 失敗（且它是主控台動作，並非 API『capability』）。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The AWSSupport-TroubleshootCFNCustomResource runbook is scoped to diagnosing CloudFormation custom-resource failures (checking the service token and custom-resource error message), not nested stacks that contain EC2 instances.","why_zh":"AWSSupport-TroubleshootCFNCustomResource runbook 的範圍是診斷 CloudFormation custom resource 失敗（檢查 service token 與 custom resource 錯誤訊息），並非含有 EC2 instances 的 nested stack。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"There is no CloudFormation template feature that publishes generic 'CloudFormation logs' for a failed stack to CloudWatch; CloudFormation surfaces failures through stack events and the Status reason (StackStatusReason). You can ship EC2 cfn-init/cloud-init logs to CloudWatch, but those reflect instance bootstrap, not why a nested stack failed to deploy.","why_zh":"CloudFormation template 並沒有將失敗 stack 的通用『CloudFormation logs』發布到 CloudWatch 的功能；CloudFormation 是透過 stack events 與 Status reason（StackStatusReason）呈現失敗。你可以把 EC2 的 cfn-init/cloud-init 日誌送到 CloudWatch，但那反映的是執行個體開機程序，而非 nested stack 部署失敗的原因。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/APIReference/API_Stack.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/APIReference/API_DescribeStacks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/determine-root-cause-for-stack-failures.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/using-cfn-nested-stacks.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-awssupport-TroubleshootCFNCustomResource.html"]}},{"id":370,"question_en":"A DevOps team operates an integration service that runs on an Amazon EC2 instance. The DevOps team uses Amazon Route 53 to manage the integration service's domain name by using a simple routing record. The integration service is stateful and uses Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) for data storage and state storage. The integration service does not support load balancing between multiple nodes. The DevOps team deploys the integration service on a new EC2 instance as a warm standby to reduce the mean time to recovery. The DevOps team wants the integration service to automatically fail over to the standby EC2 instance. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一个 DevOps 团队运营着一个在亚马逊 EC2 实例上运行的集成服务。该团队使用亚马逊 Route 53 通过简 单的路由记录来管理集成服务的域名。集成服务是有状态的，并使用亚马逊弹性文件系统（Amazon EFS） 进行数据存储和状态存储。该集成服务不支持在多个节点之间进行负载均衡。 DevOps 团队在新的 EC2 实例上部署集成服务作为热备，以减少平均恢复时间。DevOps 团队希望集成服 务能自动切换到备用的 EC2 实例。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the existing Route 53 DNS record's routing policy to weighted. Set the existing DNS record's weighting to 100. For the same domain, add a new DNS record that points to the standby EC2 instance. Set the new DNS record's weighting to 0. Associate an application health check with each record.","B":"Update the existing Route 53 DNS record's routing policy to weighted. Set the existing DNS record's weighting to 99. For the same domain, add a new DNS record that points to the standby EC2 instance. Set the new DNS record's weighting to 1. Associate an application health check with each record.","C":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Update the existing Route 53 record to point to the ALB. Create a target group for each EC2 instance. Configure an application health check on each target group. Associate both target groups with the same ALB listener. Set the primary target group's weighting to 100. Set the standby target group's weighting to 0.","D":"Create an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Update the existing Route 53 record to point to the ALB. Create a target group for each EC2 instance. Configure an application health check on each target group. Associate both target groups with the same ALB listener. Set the primary target group's weighting to 99. Set the standby target group's weighting to 1."},"options_zh":{"A":"将现有的 Route 53 DNS 记录的路由策略更新为加权策略。设置现有 DNS 记录的权重。 将权重设置为 100。对于相同的域，添加一个新的 DNS 记录，指向备用的 EC2 实例。将新 DNS 记 录的权重设置为 0。为每个记录关联一个应用程序健康检查。","B":"将现有的 Route 53 DNS 记录的路由策略更新为加权策略。将现有 DNS 记录的权重设置为 99。对于相同 的域名，添加一个新的 DNS 记录，指向备用的 EC2 实例。将新 DNS 记录的权重设置为 1。为每个记 录关联一个应用程序健康检查。","C":"创建一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。更新现有的 Route 53 记录以指向该 ALB。为每个 EC2 实例创建一 个目标组。在每个目标组上配置应用健康检查。将两个目标组都与同一个 ALB 监听器相关联。将主 目标组的权重设置为 100。将备用目标组的权重设置为 0。","D":"创建一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。更新现有的 Route 53 记录以指向该 ALB。为每个 EC2 实例创建一 个目标组。在每个目标组上配置应用健康检查。将两个目标组都与同一个 ALB 监听器相关联。将主 目标组的权重设置为 99。将备用目标组的权重设置为 1。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The integration service is stateful, stores state in EFS, and does NOT support load balancing between nodes, so the architecture must be active-passive (warm standby): the primary must receive 100% of traffic and the standby must receive traffic ONLY after the primary fails. Option A configures Route 53 weighted records with the primary at weight 100 and the standby at weight 0, with an application health check on each record. AWS documents this exact active-passive behavior: 'Route 53 initially considers only the nonzero weighted records' and 'if all the records that have a weight greater than 0 are unhealthy, then Route 53 considers the zero-weighted records.' The weighted-routing truth table confirms a healthy weight-0 record is NOT used while a nonzero-weight record is healthy, and is used only when all nonzero-weight records are unhealthy. This delivers automatic DNS failover with zero standby traffic during normal operation, preserving the single-node stateful service. Options B and D use weights 99/1, which continuously send ~1% of traffic to the standby and would break a stateful, non-load-balanceable service. Options C and D also add an ALB, which load-balances across targets (the service forbids that) and does not perform automatic active-passive promotion of a zero-weight target group when the primary's targets become unhealthy.","explanation_zh":"此整合服務為有狀態 (stateful)，狀態資料儲存於 EFS，且不支援多節點之間的負載平衡，因此架構必須為 active-passive（warm standby）：主要節點接收全部流量，待命節點僅在主要節點故障後才接收流量。選項 A 使用 Route 53 weighted 記錄，主要記錄權重為 100、待命記錄權重為 0，且每筆記錄都關聯 application health check。AWS 文件明確說明此 active-passive 行為：『Route 53 最初只考慮非零權重的記錄』，且『若所有權重大於 0 的記錄皆為 unhealthy，Route 53 才會考慮權重為 0 的記錄』。weighted routing 的真值表也證實：當某筆非零權重記錄健康時，健康的權重 0 記錄不會被使用，只有當所有非零權重記錄都 unhealthy 時才會啟用。如此即可達成自動 DNS 故障切換，且正常運作時待命節點不接收任何流量，符合單節點有狀態服務的需求。選項 B 與 D 使用 99/1 權重，會持續將約 1% 流量送往待命節點，破壞有狀態、不可負載平衡的服務。選項 C 與 D 另外加入 ALB，ALB 會在多個 target 之間做負載平衡（此服務禁止此行為），且在主要 target 變為 unhealthy 時，ALB 並不會自動把流量提升切換到權重為 0 的 target group。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Weights 99 and 1 are both nonzero, so Route 53 treats BOTH records as active and continuously splits ~1% of traffic (1/100) to the standby. The stateful service that does not support load balancing between nodes breaks because live traffic always reaches the standby. This is active-active, not the required active-passive warm-standby failover.","why_zh":"權重 99 與 1 皆為非零，Route 53 會將兩筆記錄都視為 active，並持續將約 1%（1/100）流量送往待命節點。不支援多節點負載平衡的有狀態服務會出問題，因為即時流量總會送達待命節點。這是 active-active，而非所需的 active-passive warm standby 故障切換。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"An ALB distributes traffic across registered targets, but the service explicitly does not support load balancing between nodes and is stateful (EFS state). Although weight 100/0 sends traffic only to the primary, ALB weighted target groups do not perform automatic active-passive promotion of a zero-weight target group when the primary's targets become unhealthy (it returns errors rather than failing over). The ALB is unnecessary infrastructure and does not deliver the automatic health-based failover that Route 53 weighted-plus-health-check records do.","why_zh":"ALB 會在已註冊的 target 之間分配流量，但此服務明確不支援多節點負載平衡且為有狀態 (EFS 狀態)。雖然 100/0 權重只把流量送到主要 target，但 ALB 的 weighted target group 並不會在主要 target 變為 unhealthy 時自動把流量提升切換到權重為 0 的 target group（會回傳錯誤而非故障切換）。ALB 屬多餘的基礎設施，也無法提供 Route 53 weighted 加 health check 記錄所達成的、以健康狀態為基礎的自動故障切換。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines two flaws: it adds an ALB (the service cannot be load balanced and ALB gives no automatic zero-weight failover), and uses weights 99/1 that continuously send ~1% of live traffic to the standby, breaking the stateful single-node service. Neither warm-standby isolation nor automatic failover is satisfied.","why_zh":"同時包含兩項缺陷：加入 ALB（該服務無法被負載平衡，且 ALB 不提供權重 0 的自動故障切換），又使用 99/1 權重持續將約 1% 即時流量送往待命節點，破壞有狀態的單節點服務。既不符合 warm standby 的隔離，也不符合自動故障切換。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-weighted.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/dns-failover-configuring.html"]}},{"id":371,"question_en":"A company hosts several applications in an AWS account. Each application sends logs to its own log group in Amazon CloudWatch. The company's CloudWatch costs for ingestion are increasing. A DevOps engineer needs to identify which applications are the source of the increased logging costs. Which solution will meet this requirement in the MOST operationally efficient way?","question_zh":"一家公司在 AWS 账户中托管了多个应用程序。每个应用程序都将日志发送到其在 Amazon CloudWatch 中自己的日志组。该公司在 CloudWatch 日志摄取方面的成本正在增加。 一位 DevOps 工程师需要确定哪些应用程序是导致日志记录成本增加的原因。 哪种解决方案能以最高效的操作方式满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use CloudWatch metrics to create a custom expression that identifies the CloudWatch log groups that receive the most data.","B":"Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights to create a query for the application log groups to identify the number of log groups that received data during a specific time period.","C":"Use AWS Cost Explorer to generate a cost report that details costs for CloudWatch usage.","D":"Use AWS CloudTrail to filter for CreateLogStream events for each application."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 CloudWatch 指标创建自定义表达式，以识别接收数据量最大的 CloudWatch 日志组。","B":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs Insights 为应用程序日志组创建查询，以确定在特定时间段内收到数据的 日志组数量。","C":"使用 AWS 成本管理器生成一份成本报告，详细列出 CloudWatch 使用的成本。","D":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 过滤每个应用程序的 CreateLogStream 事件。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Cost Optimization","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudWatch Logs ingestion is billed per GB of data ingested, so the application whose log group ingests the most data drives the rising cost. The AWS/Logs namespace automatically publishes the IncomingBytes metric every minute, and with the LogGroupName dimension it reports 'the volume of log events in uncompressed bytes uploaded to the log group.' Because this metric is already collected at no extra cost, a DevOps engineer can build a single CloudWatch metric math / search / Metrics Insights expression (for example SUM(IncomingBytes) GROUP BY LogGroupName ORDER BY descending) to instantly rank log groups by ingested volume and pinpoint the source applications. This native approach requires no new infrastructure, queries, or log parsing, making it the most operationally efficient solution.","explanation_zh":"CloudWatch Logs 的擷取（ingestion）費用是按每 GB 擷取的資料量計費，因此擷取資料量最大的應用程式（log group）就是費用上升的來源。AWS/Logs 命名空間每分鐘自動發佈 IncomingBytes 指標，當搭配 LogGroupName 維度時，它代表「上傳到該 log group 的 log 事件未壓縮位元組量」。由於此指標已自動收集且無額外費用，DevOps 工程師只需建立單一 CloudWatch metric math / search / Metrics Insights 運算式（例如 SUM(IncomingBytes) GROUP BY LogGroupName 並降冪排序），即可立即依擷取量排序各 log group 並找出來源應用程式。此原生方法不需新增基礎設施、查詢或 log 解析，因此是最具營運效率的做法。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The described Logs Insights query only counts the NUMBER of log groups that received data, not which ones ingested the most bytes, so it does not identify the cost driver. Logs Insights queries are also billed per GB of data scanned, adding cost while investigating cost.","why_zh":"此處描述的 Logs Insights 查詢只計算有收到資料的 log group 數量，而非哪個 log group 擷取最多位元組，無法找出費用來源。此外 Logs Insights 查詢還會按掃描的每 GB 資料計費，在調查費用時反而增加成本。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Cost Explorer can show that CloudWatch spend rose by service and usage type, but it does not break down ingestion cost per individual log group, so it cannot identify which application is the source without enabling resource-level cost data/tagging. It answers 'how much does CloudWatch cost' rather than 'which log group drives it,' adding overhead with less precise log-group attribution.","why_zh":"Cost Explorer 可依服務與使用類型顯示 CloudWatch 花費上升，但不會逐一拆解每個 log group 的擷取成本，因此在未啟用資源層級成本資料／標籤的情況下無法辨識來源應用程式。它回答的是「CloudWatch 花了多少」，而非「哪個 log group 造成成本」，營運負擔較高且對 log group 歸因較不精確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"CloudTrail CreateLogStream events only indicate that a log stream was created, not how much data was ingested. Ingestion cost is driven by data volume (bytes), not by the count of stream-creation API calls, so this signal is irrelevant to the cost question and also requires parsing CloudTrail logs.","why_zh":"CloudTrail 的 CreateLogStream 事件只表示建立了 log stream，並不代表擷取了多少資料。擷取費用由資料量（位元組）驅動，而非由建立 stream 的 API 呼叫次數決定，因此此訊號與費用問題無關，且還需要解析 CloudTrail logs。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CloudWatch-Logs-Monitoring-CloudWatch-Metrics.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/using-metric-math.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/query_with_cloudwatch-metrics-insights.html"]}},{"id":372,"question_en":"A company has an AWS account named PipelineAccount. The account manages a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline. The account uses an IAM role named CodePipeline_Service_Role and produces an artifact that is stored in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company uses a customer managed AWS KMS key to encrypt objects in the S3 bucket. A DevOps engineer wants to configure the pipeline to use an AWS CodeDeploy application in an AWS account named CodeDeployAccount to deploy the produced artifact. The DevOps engineer updates the KMS key policy to grant the CodeDeployAccount account permission to use the key. The DevOps engineer configures an IAM role named DevOps_Role in the CodeDeployAccount account that has access to the CodeDeploy resources that the pipeline requires. The DevOps engineer updates an Amazon EC2 instance role that operates within the CodeDeployAccount account to allow access to the S3 bucket and the KMS key that is in the PipelineAccount account. Which additional steps will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一个名为 PipelineAccount 的 AWS 账户。该账户在 AWS CodePipeline 中管理一条流水线。该 账户使用名为 CodePipeline_Service_Role 的 IAM 角色，并生成一个存储在 Amazon S3 存储桶中的工件。该 公司使用客户管理的 AWS KMS 密钥对 S3 存储桶中的对象进行加密。 一位 DevOps 工程师希望配置流水线，以便在名为 CodeDeployAccount 的 AWS 账户中使用 AWS CodeDeploy 应用程序来部署生成的工件。 DevOps 工程师更新 KMS 密钥策略，授予 CodeDeployAccount 账户权限以 使用该密钥。DevOps 工程师在 CodeDeployAccount 账户中配置了一个名为 DevOps_Role 的 IAM 角色，该 角色有权访问管道所需的 CodeDeploy 资源。DevOps 工程师更新了在 CodeDeployAccount 账户中运行的 Amazon EC2 实例角色，以允许其访问 PipelineAccount 账户中的 S3 存储桶和 KMS 密钥。 哪些额外的步骤能够满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the S3 bucket policy to grant the CodeDeployAccount account access to the S3 bucket. Configure the DevOps_Role IAM role to have an IAM trust policy that allows the PipelineAccount account to assume the role. Update the CodePipeline_Service_Role IAM role to grant permission to assume the DevOps_Role role.","B":"Update the S3 bucket policy to grant the CodeDeployAccount account access to the S3 bucket. Configure the DevOps_Role IAM role to have an IAM trust policy that allows the PipelineAccount account to assume the role. Update the DevOps_Role IAM role to grant permission to assume CodePipelfne_Service_Role role.","C":"Update the S3 bucket policy to grant the PipelineAccount account access to the S3 bucket. Configure the DevOps_Role IAM role to have an IAM trust policy that allows the PipelineAccount account to assume the role. Update the CodePipeline_Service_Role IAM to grant permission to assume the DevOps_Role role.","D":"Update the S3 bucket policy to grant the CodeDeployAccount account access to the S3 bucket. Configure the DevOps_Role IAM role to have an IAM trust policy that allows the CodeDeployAccount account to assume the role. Update the CodePipeline_Service_Role IAM role to grant permission to assume the DevOps_Role role."},"options_zh":{"A":"更新 S3 存储桶策略，授予 CodeDeployAccount 账户对 S3 存储桶的访问权限。配置 DevOps_Role IAM 角色，使其具有允许 PipelineAccount 账户承担该角色的 IAM 信任策略。更新 CodePipeline_Service_ Role IAM 角色，授予其承担 DevOps_Role 角色的权限。","B":"更新 S3 存储桶策略，授予 CodeDeployAccount 账户对 S3 存储桶的访问权限。配置 DevOps_Role IAM 角色，使其具有允许 PipelineAccount 账户承担该角色的 IAM 信任策略。更新 DevOps_Role IAM 角色，授予其承担 CodePipelfne_Service_Role 角色的权限。","C":"更新 S3 存储桶策略，授予 PipelineAccount 账户访问该 S3 存储桶的权限。配置 DevOps_Role IAM 角色， 使其具有允许 PipelineAccount 账户承担该角色的 IAM 信任策略。更新 CodePipeline_Service_Role IAM 角色，授予其承担 DevOps_Role 角色的权限。","D":"更新 S3 存储桶策略，授予 CodeDeployAccount 账户访问该 S3 存储桶的权限。配置 DevOps_Role IAM 角色，使其具有允许 CodeDeployAccount 账户承担该角色的 IAM 信任策略。更新 CodePipeline_ Service_Role IAM 角色，授予其承担 DevOps_Role 角色的权限。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"This maps exactly to the AWS CodePipeline cross-account walkthrough. PipelineAccount = AccountA (owns the S3 artifact bucket, the customer managed KMS key, and the CodePipeline_Service_Role); CodeDeployAccount = AccountB (owns the CodeDeploy application, the EC2 instance role, and the cross-account DevOps_Role). The doc lists three remaining setup steps: (1) AccountA creates an S3 bucket policy that grants AccountB (CodeDeployAccount) access to the artifact bucket; (2) AccountB configures the cross-account role (DevOps_Role) with a trust relationship that allows the CodePipeline service role in AccountA (PipelineAccount) to assume it; (3) AccountA attaches a policy to CodePipeline_Service_Role allowing it (AccountA) to assume the role in AccountB (DevOps_Role). Option A states all three correctly and in the right direction. Note the assume-role direction is one-way: the pipeline service role in PipelineAccount assumes DevOps_Role in CodeDeployAccount, never the reverse.","explanation_zh":"此情境完全對應 AWS CodePipeline 跨帳戶部署的官方教學。PipelineAccount = AccountA（擁有 S3 成品儲存桶、客戶受管 KMS 金鑰，以及 CodePipeline_Service_Role）；CodeDeployAccount = AccountB（擁有 CodeDeploy 應用程式、EC2 instance role，以及跨帳戶的 DevOps_Role）。文件列出剩餘三個設定步驟：(1) AccountA 建立 S3 儲存桶政策，授予 AccountB（CodeDeployAccount）存取成品桶；(2) AccountB 設定跨帳戶角色（DevOps_Role）的信任關係，允許 AccountA（PipelineAccount）中的 CodePipeline service role 擔任該角色；(3) AccountA 在 CodePipeline_Service_Role 上附加政策，允許其（AccountA）擔任 AccountB 的 DevOps_Role。選項 A 三個步驟皆正確且方向無誤。請注意擔任角色的方向是單向的：PipelineAccount 的 pipeline service role 擔任 CodeDeployAccount 的 DevOps_Role，絕非反向。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The first two steps are correct, but the third reverses the assume-role direction: it grants DevOps_Role permission to assume CodePipeline_Service_Role. The doc requires the opposite — AccountA's CodePipeline_Service_Role must be allowed to assume DevOps_Role in CodeDeployAccount (AccountB).","why_zh":"前兩步正確，但第三步把擔任角色的方向弄反：讓 DevOps_Role 取得擔任 CodePipeline_Service_Role 的權限。文件要求相反——AccountA 的 CodePipeline_Service_Role 必須被允許擔任 CodeDeployAccount（AccountB）的 DevOps_Role。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The S3 bucket policy must grant the foreign account (CodeDeployAccount / AccountB) access, not PipelineAccount. The bucket already resides in PipelineAccount (AccountA), so granting that account access is meaningless; per the doc, AccountA writes a bucket policy granting AccountB access.","why_zh":"S3 儲存桶政策必須授予外部帳戶（CodeDeployAccount / AccountB）存取，而非 PipelineAccount。該桶本就位於 PipelineAccount（AccountA），授予自身存取毫無意義；依文件，AccountA 撰寫的儲存桶政策應授予 AccountB 存取。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The trust policy on DevOps_Role must allow PipelineAccount / AccountA (where the CodePipeline service role lives) to assume it, not CodeDeployAccount. Trusting CodeDeployAccount (the role's own account) does not enable the pipeline's service role in PipelineAccount to assume the role.","why_zh":"DevOps_Role 的信任政策必須允許 PipelineAccount / AccountA（CodePipeline service role 所在帳戶）擔任，而非 CodeDeployAccount。信任 CodeDeployAccount（角色自身帳戶）無法讓 PipelineAccount 的 pipeline service role 擔任該角色。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/pipelines-create-cross-account.html"]}},{"id":373,"question_en":"A company has multiple development teams in separate business units that work in a single shared AWS account. All Amazon EC2 resources that users create in the account must include tags that specify which user created the resources. The tagging must occur within the first hour of resource creation. A DevOps engineer needs to add tags to new resources that include the ID of the user that created the resource and the appropriate cost center ID. The DevOps engineer configures an AWS Lambda function to use the cost center mappings to tag the resources. The DevOps engineer also sets up AWS CloudTrail in the shared AWS account. An Amazon S3 bucket stores the CloudTrail event logs. Which solution will meet the tagging requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有多个开发团队分布在不同的业务部门，这些团队在一个共享的 AWS 账户中工作。用户在该账 户中创建的所有 Amazon EC2 资源都必须包含指定创建资源的用户的标签。这些标签必须在资源创建后的 第一个小时内添加。 DevOps 工程师需要为新资源添加标签，标签中应包含创建资源的用户 ID 以及相应的成本中心 ID。DevOps 工程师配置了一个 AWS Lambda 函数，利用成本中心映射来为资源添加标签。DevOps 工程师还在共享的 AWS 账户中设置了 AWS CloudTrail。Amazon S3 存储桶用于存储 CloudTrail 事件日志。 哪种解决方案能满足标签要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an S3 event notification on the S3 bucket to invoke the Lambda function for s3:ObjectTagging:Put events. Enable bucket versioning on the S3 bucket.","B":"Enable server access logging on the S3 bucket. Create an S3 event notification on the S3 bucket for s3:ObjectTagging:* events.","C":"Enable AWS Config in the account. Configure the required-tags AWS managed rule to check and update the required tags. D Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses Amazon EC2 as the event source. Configure the rule to match events that CloudTrail delivers. Configure the rule to target the Lambda function.","D":"Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that uses Amazon EC2 as the event source. Configure the rule to match events that CloudTrail delivers. Configure the rule to target the Lambda function."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 S3 存储桶上创建 S3 事件通知，以便在发生 s3:ObjectTagging:Put 事件时调用 Lambda 函数。在 S3 存储桶上启用版本控制。","B":"在 S3 存储桶上启用服务器访问日志记录。在 S3 存储桶上为 s3:ObjectTagging:* 事件创建 S3 事件通知。","C":"在账户中启用 AWS Config。配置“所需标签”AWS 管理规则以检查并更新所需的标签。 D 创建一个使用 Amazon EC2 作为事件源的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则以匹配 CloudTrail 传 递的事件。配置该规则以将目标指向 Lambda 函数。","D":"创建一个使用 Amazon EC2 作为事件源的 Amazon EventBridge 规则。配置该规则以匹配 CloudTrail 传递 的事件。将该规则配置为指向 Lambda 函数。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Storage","Compute","Cost Optimization","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to tag newly created EC2 resources with the creating user's ID and a cost center ID within one hour of creation, using a Lambda function that already holds the cost-center mappings. The canonical AWS pattern is to create an Amazon EventBridge rule with EC2 as the event source that matches events delivered by CloudTrail (Event type 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail', e.g. RunInstances) and targets the Lambda function. CloudTrail records the creating user's identity in the event, EventBridge matches it in near real-time, and the Lambda applies the tags well within the one-hour window. This is exactly the workflow documented in the EventBridge tutorial 'Create an EventBridge rule that reacts to AWS API calls via CloudTrail', where the rule's Event source is set to EC2, Event type to 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail', and the target is a Lambda function. Option D is the only choice that triggers the engineer's tagging Lambda based on EC2 resource creation.","explanation_zh":"需求是在 EC2 資源建立後一小時內，使用已內含成本中心對應表的 Lambda 函式，為新建立的 EC2 資源加上建立者的使用者 ID 與成本中心 ID 標籤。標準的 AWS 模式是建立一個以 EC2 為事件來源的 Amazon EventBridge 規則，比對由 CloudTrail 傳遞的事件（Event type 為 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail'，例如 RunInstances），並以該 Lambda 函式為目標。CloudTrail 在事件中記錄了建立者的身分，EventBridge 近乎即時地比對，Lambda 即可在一小時內套用標籤。此流程正是 EventBridge 教學文件「Create an EventBridge rule that reacts to AWS API calls via CloudTrail」所描述的：規則的 Event source 設為 EC2、Event type 設為 'AWS API Call via CloudTrail'、目標設為 Lambda 函式。選項 D 是唯一能依 EC2 資源建立來觸發工程師標籤 Lambda 的方案。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"An s3:ObjectTagging:Put notification plus bucket versioning operate on S3 objects (the CloudTrail log files), not on EC2 resources. This never tags EC2 resources nor detects EC2 creation; it only reacts to tagging actions performed on objects already in the bucket.","why_zh":"s3:ObjectTagging:Put 通知加上儲存貯體版本控制是針對 S3 物件（CloudTrail 日誌檔），而非 EC2 資源。它完全無法為 EC2 資源加上標籤，也偵測不到 EC2 的建立，只會對貯體內既有物件的標籤動作做出反應。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Server access logging plus s3:ObjectTagging:* notifications again target S3 object tagging, not EC2 resource creation. There is no mechanism that ties an EC2 RunInstances event to the tagging Lambda.","why_zh":"伺服器存取記錄加上 s3:ObjectTagging:* 通知同樣是針對 S3 物件標籤，而非 EC2 資源建立。此處沒有任何機制能將 EC2 RunInstances 事件連結到標籤 Lambda。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The AWS Config required-tags managed rule only evaluates and reports compliance against required tag keys; the docs state it 'does not prevent you from creating resources with incorrect tags' and that the AWS-managed AWS-SetRequiredTags SSM document 'does not work as a remediation with this rule.' It cannot add or update tag values by itself and does not invoke the engineer's Lambda that holds the cost-center mappings, so it neither computes the correct cost center per user nor guarantees tagging within the one-hour window the way an event-driven trigger does.","why_zh":"AWS Config 的 required-tags 受管規則只會針對必要標籤鍵評估並回報合規性；文件明確指出它「無法防止你建立帶有錯誤標籤的資源」，且 AWS 受管的 AWS-SetRequiredTags SSM 文件「無法作為此規則的修復動作」。它本身無法新增或更新標籤值，也不會呼叫含成本中心對應表的工程師 Lambda，因此既無法依使用者計算正確的成本中心，也不像事件驅動觸發那樣保證在一小時內完成標籤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-log-api-call.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/userguide/eb-service-event-cloudtrail.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/config/latest/developerguide/required-tags.html"]}},{"id":374,"question_en":"A company is developing code and wants to use semantic versioning. The company's DevOps team needs to create a pipeline for compiling the code. The team also needs to manage versions of the compiled code. If the code uses any open source libraries, the libraries must also be cached in the build process. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发代码，并希望采用语义化版本控制。该公司的 DevOps 团队需要创建一个用于编译代码的 流水线。团队还需要管理编译代码的版本。如果代码使用了任何开源库，这些库也必须在构建过程中进行缓 存。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodeArtifact repository and associate the upstream repositories. Create an AWS CodeBuild project that builds the semantic version of the code artifacts. Configure the project to authenticate and connect to the CodeArtifact repository and publish the artifact to the repository.","B":"Use AWS CodeDeploy to upload the generated semantic version of the artifact to an Amazon Elastic File System (Amazon EFS) file system.","C":"Use an AWS CodeBuild project to build the code and to publish the generated semantic version of the artifact to AWS Artifact. Configure build caching in the CodeBuild project.","D":"Create a new AWS CodeArtifact repository. Create an AWS Lambda function that pulls open source packages from the internet and publishes the packages to the repository. Configure AWS CodeDeploy to build semantic versions of the code and publish the versions to the repository."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库并关联上游存储库。创建一个 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建代码 工件的语义版本。配置该项目以进行身份验证并连接到 CodeArtifact 存储库，并将工件发布到该 存储库。","B":"使用 AWS CodeDeploy 将生成的语义版本的工件上传到 Amazon Elastic File System（Amazon EFS）文 件系统。","C":"使用 AWS CodeBuild 项目来构建代码，并将生成的语义版本的工件发布到 AWS Artifact。在 CodeBuild 项目中配置构建缓存。","D":"创建一个新的 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，从互联网上拉取开源软件包并将 其发布到该存储库。配置 AWS CodeDeploy 以构建代码的语义版本，并将这些版本发布到存储库。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"Option A uses the correct AWS service for every requirement. AWS CodeArtifact is a managed artifact repository that stores and manages versions of software packages, which is exactly how you manage versions of the compiled, semantically versioned code (it works with package managers such as npm, Maven, Gradle, NuGet, pip, and twine, all of which use semantic versioning). Associating upstream repositories that have external connections to public repos (npmjs, Maven Central, NuGet Gallery, PyPI) makes CodeArtifact fetch and store the open-source packages on demand, so dependencies are cached for the build, satisfying the open-source caching requirement. AWS CodeBuild compiles the code, authenticates to CodeArtifact with an authorization token, and publishes the built semantic version to the repository, which is the documented 'Using CodeArtifact with CodeBuild' integration pattern. The distractors misuse services: AWS Artifact provides compliance reports (ISO/PCI/SOC), CodeDeploy deploys applications (it does not build or store package versions), and EFS is general file storage with no version management.","explanation_zh":"選項 A 為每一項需求都使用了正確的 AWS 服務。AWS CodeArtifact 是受管的軟體製品儲存庫，可儲存與管理軟體套件的版本，這正好用來管理已編譯且採用語意化版本的程式碼（它支援 npm、Maven、Gradle、NuGet、pip、twine 等套件管理工具，這些工具皆使用語意化版本）。將具有對公開儲存庫（npmjs、Maven Central、NuGet Gallery、PyPI）external connection 的 upstream repository 關聯後，CodeArtifact 會按需擷取並儲存開源套件，使相依套件在建置時被快取，滿足開源函式庫快取需求。AWS CodeBuild 編譯程式碼、使用授權權杖向 CodeArtifact 進行驗證，並將建置好的語意化版本發布至儲存庫，這正是官方文件「Using CodeArtifact with CodeBuild」所描述的整合模式。其餘選項誤用了服務：AWS Artifact 提供合規報告（ISO/PCI/SOC），CodeDeploy 用於部署應用程式（不建置也不儲存套件版本），而 EFS 只是一般檔案儲存，沒有版本管理功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"CodeDeploy deploys applications to compute targets; it does not compile code or build/version artifacts. Amazon EFS is a general-purpose file system, not a versioned package/artifact repository, so it provides no semantic version management and nothing caches the open-source libraries.","why_zh":"CodeDeploy 用於將應用程式部署到運算目標，並不編譯程式碼或建置／管理製品版本。Amazon EFS 是通用檔案系統，而非版本化的套件／製品儲存庫，因此無法提供語意化版本管理，也沒有任何元件快取開源函式庫。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Artifact is a portal for downloading AWS security and compliance reports and agreements (ISO, PCI, SOC) — it is NOT an artifact repository and you cannot publish your compiled software to it. The similar name is a deliberate trap. CodeBuild build caching alone also does not provide versioned package management.","why_zh":"AWS Artifact 是用於下載 AWS 安全與合規報告及協議（ISO、PCI、SOC）的入口網站，並非製品儲存庫，無法將你編譯出的軟體發布到其中。相似的名稱是刻意設下的陷阱。僅靠 CodeBuild 的建置快取也無法提供有版本管理的套件儲存。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A custom Lambda that pulls open-source packages reinvents what CodeArtifact upstream/external connections do natively and on demand, adding operational overhead. More fundamentally, it relies on CodeDeploy to 'build' semantic versions and publish them, but CodeDeploy is a deployment service that cannot build code or publish to CodeArtifact, so the build/publish step is invalid.","why_zh":"自訂 Lambda 去擷取開源套件，等於重造 CodeArtifact upstream／external connection 原生且按需提供的功能，徒增營運負擔。更關鍵的是它依賴 CodeDeploy 來『建置』語意化版本並發布，但 CodeDeploy 是部署服務，無法建置程式碼，也無法發布到 CodeArtifact，因此其建置與發布步驟並不成立。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repos-upstream.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/codebuild.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/external-connection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/artifact/latest/ug/what-is-aws-artifact.html"]}},{"id":375,"question_en":"A company uses a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline to deploy an application. The company created an AWS Fault Injection Service (AWS FIS) experiment template to test the resiliency of the application. A DevOps engineer needs to integrate the experiment into the pipeline. Which solution will meet this requirement?","question_zh":"一家公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 中的管道来部署应用程序。该公司创建了一个 AWS 故障注入服务（AWS FIS）实验模板来测试应用程序的弹性。一位 DevOps 工程师需要将该实验集成到管道中。 哪种解决方案能满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Configure a new stage in the pipeline that includes an AWS FIS action. Configure the action to reference the AWS FIS experiment template. Grant the pipeline access to start the experiment.","B":"Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduler. Grant the scheduler permission to start the AWS FIS experiment. Configure a new stage in the pipeline that includes an action to invoke the EventBridge scheduler.","C":"Create an AWS Lambda function to start the AWS FIS experiment. Grant the Lambda function permission to start the experiment. Create a new stage in the pipeline that has a Lambda action. Set the action to invoke the Lambda function.","D":"Export the AWS FIS experiment template to an Amazon S3 bucket. Create an AWS CodeBuild unit test project that has a buildspec that starts the AWS FIS experiment. Grant the CodeBuild project access to start the experiment. Configure a new stage in the pipeline that includes an action to run the CodeBuild unit test project."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管道中配置一个新的阶段，其中包含一个 AWS FIS 操作。配置该操作以引用 AWS FIS 实验模 板。授予管道启动实验的权限。","B":"创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 调度器。授予该调度器启动 AWS FIS 实验的权限。在管道中配置一个 新阶段，其中包括调用 EventBridge 调度器的操作。","C":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来启动 AWS FIS 实验。授予该 Lambda 函数启动实验的权限。在管道中创 建一个新阶段，该阶段包含一个 Lambda 操作。将操作设置为调用该 Lambda 函数。","D":"将 AWS FIS 实验模板导出到 Amazon S3 存储桶。创建一个具有启动 AWS FIS 实验的构建规范的 AWS CodeBuild 单元测试项目。授予 CodeBuild 项目启动实验的权限。在管道中配置一个新阶段，其中包括 运行 CodeBuild 单元测试项目的操作。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"CodePipeline has no native AWS FIS action provider. The authoritative \"Valid action providers in CodePipeline\" table lists every provider across the Source, Build, Test, Deploy, Approval, Invoke, and Compute categories, and AWS FIS appears in none of them. In particular, the Invoke category contains only the CodePipeline Invoke action, AWS Lambda, AWS Step Functions, and InspectorScan. Therefore Option A (configure an \"AWS FIS action\" in a stage) is technically impossible. The standard, integrated, lowest-overhead way to call an arbitrary AWS API such as fis:StartExperiment from a pipeline is the Invoke category's AWS Lambda action: the Lambda function calls StartExperiment (which starts an experiment from the specified experimentTemplateId) and then reports the outcome back to the pipeline via the PutJobSuccessResult or PutJobFailureResult API. Per the Lambda invoke action reference, the action hangs (waits) until one of those calls is made or it times out, so the pipeline genuinely gates on the experiment result. That is exactly Option C.","explanation_zh":"CodePipeline 沒有原生的 AWS FIS action provider。權威的「Valid action providers in CodePipeline」清單列出了 Source、Build、Test、Deploy、Approval、Invoke 與 Compute 各類別下的所有 provider，當中完全沒有 AWS FIS。特別是 Invoke 類別只包含 CodePipeline Invoke action、AWS Lambda、AWS Step Functions 與 InspectorScan。因此選項 A（在 stage 內設定一個「AWS FIS action」）在技術上不可行。要從 pipeline 呼叫像 fis:StartExperiment 這類任意 AWS API，標準、整合且開銷最低的方式就是 Invoke 類別的 AWS Lambda action：Lambda function 呼叫 StartExperiment（依指定的 experimentTemplateId 啟動實驗），再透過 PutJobSuccessResult 或 PutJobFailureResult API 將結果回報給 pipeline。根據 Lambda invoke action reference，該 action 會一直等待，直到其中一個 API 被呼叫或逾時為止，因此 pipeline 確實會以實驗結果作為通過與否的關卡。這正是選項 C。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodePipeline does not offer a native 'AWS FIS action' provider. The Valid action providers table (Source/Build/Test/Deploy/Approval/Invoke/Compute) contains no FIS provider in any category, so an action that 'references the AWS FIS experiment template' cannot be configured. This option is technically impossible.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 沒有原生的『AWS FIS action』provider。Valid action providers 清單（Source/Build/Test/Deploy/Approval/Invoke/Compute）在任何類別中都沒有 FIS provider，因此無法設定一個「參照 AWS FIS experiment template」的 action。此選項在技術上不可行。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"EventBridge Scheduler can start FIS experiments, but it is not a CodePipeline action provider and is time/cron based, not a synchronous in-pipeline step. There is no 'invoke EventBridge scheduler' pipeline action, and Scheduler would not return success/failure to gate the pipeline, so this cannot be wired as a stage action.","why_zh":"EventBridge Scheduler 可以啟動 FIS 實驗，但它不是 CodePipeline 的 action provider，且是以時間/cron 觸發，並非 pipeline 內的同步步驟。並沒有「invoke EventBridge scheduler」這種 pipeline action，而且 Scheduler 也不會回報成功/失敗來控管 pipeline，因此無法接成 stage action。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A CodeBuild buildspec could technically call fis:StartExperiment, but the premise is wrong: FIS experiments start from the experimentTemplateId via StartExperiment, not by exporting the template to S3 and importing it. Adding an S3 export and a contrived 'unit test' build project introduces needless steps and overhead and misrepresents the FIS workflow, making it inferior to the native Lambda invoke action.","why_zh":"CodeBuild buildspec 技術上可呼叫 fis:StartExperiment，但前提是錯的：FIS 實驗是透過 StartExperiment 依 experimentTemplateId 啟動，而非把 template 匯出到 S3 再匯入。加入 S3 匯出與牽強的「unit test」build project 增加了不必要的步驟與維運開銷，且誤解 FIS 工作流程，因此劣於原生的 Lambda invoke action。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/actions-valid-providers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-Lambda.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/fis/latest/APIReference/API_StartExperiment.html"]}},{"id":376,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer is creating a CI/CD pipeline to build container images. The engineer needs to store container images in Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) and scan the images for common vulnerabilities. The CI/CD pipeline must be resilient to outages in upstream source container image repositories. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师正在创建一个 CI/CD 管道来构建容器镜像。该工程师需要将容器镜像存储在亚马逊弹 性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中，并对这些镜像进行常见漏洞扫描。CI/CD 管道必须能够抵御上游源容 器镜像仓库中断的影响。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an ECR private repository in the private registry to store the container images and scan images when images are pushed to the repository. Configure a replication rule in the private registry to replicate images from upstream repositories.","B":"Create an ECR public repository in the public registry to cache images from upstream source repositories. Create an ECR private repository to store images. Configure the private repository to scan images when images are pushed to the repository.","C":"Create an ECR public repository in the public registry. Configure a pull through cache rule for the repository. Create an ECR private repository to store images. Configure the ECR private registry to perform basic scanning.","D":"Create an ECR private repository in the private registry to store the container images. Enable basic scanning for the private registry, and create a pull through cache rule."},"options_zh":{"A":"在私有注册表中创建一个 ECR 私有存储库来存储容器镜像，并在将镜像推送到该存储库时扫描镜像。在 私有注册表中配置一个复制规则，以从上游存储库复制镜像。","B":"在公共注册表中创建一个 ECR 公共存储库以缓存来自上游源存储库的镜像。创建一个 ECR 私有存储库来 存储镜像。配置私有存储库，使其在将镜像推送到存储库时扫描镜像。","C":"在公共注册表中创建一个 ECR 公共存储库。为该存储库配置一个拉取缓存规则。创建一个 ECR 私有 存储库来存储镜像。配置 ECR 私有注册表执行基本扫描。","D":"在私有注册表中创建一个 ECR 私有存储库以存储容器镜像。为私有注册表启用基本扫描，并创建一 个拉取缓存规则。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements are to store images in an ECR private repository, scan them for common vulnerabilities, and stay resilient to outages in upstream source image repositories. ECR pull through cache rules are created in the ECR private registry and sync content from upstream registries (Docker Hub, ECR Public, Quay, Kubernetes, etc.) into that private registry, auto-creating repositories as images are pulled. Crucially, the AWS docs state that if Amazon ECR is unable to update an image from the upstream registry for any reason, the last cached image is still served on pull, which is exactly the upstream-outage resilience the question demands. ECR basic scanning uses AWS native technology with the CVE database to scan images for OS vulnerabilities and is enabled at the private registry/repository level with scan-on-push. Option D combines all three correctly: a private repository for storage, basic scanning for vulnerabilities, and a pull through cache rule for upstream resilience.","explanation_zh":"需求是將映像存放於 ECR private repository、掃描常見漏洞，並能在上游 (upstream) 來源映像 repository 發生中斷時維持韌性。ECR pull through cache rule 建立在 ECR private registry 上，會把上游 registry（Docker Hub、ECR Public、Quay、Kubernetes 等）的內容同步到該 private registry，並在拉取映像時自動建立 repository。關鍵在於 AWS 文件明確指出：若 Amazon ECR 因任何原因無法從上游 registry 更新映像，拉取時仍會提供最後一次快取的映像，這正是題目要求的上游中斷韌性。ECR basic scanning 使用 AWS 原生技術搭配 CVE 資料庫掃描映像的 OS 漏洞，可在 private registry/repository 層級啟用並支援 scan-on-push。選項 D 正確結合三者：private repository 儲存、basic scanning 掃描漏洞、pull through cache rule 提供上游韌性。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"ECR replication rules only copy images between Amazon ECR private registries (cross-Region or cross-account ECR-to-ECR). They cannot replicate from arbitrary upstream third-party source repositories such as Docker Hub or Quay, so they do not provide resilience to outages in upstream source image repositories. Pull through cache, not replication, is the feature designed for ingesting and caching upstream sources.","why_zh":"ECR replication rule 只在 Amazon ECR private registry 之間複製映像（跨 Region 或跨帳號的 ECR 對 ECR），無法從 Docker Hub、Quay 等任意第三方上游來源 repository 複製，因此無法對上游來源映像 repository 的中斷提供韌性。用來擷取並快取上游來源的功能是 pull through cache，而非 replication。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Pull through cache rules cache upstream images into the ECR private registry, not into an ECR public repository. ECR public repositories are for publishing/sharing your own images publicly; there is no mechanism that makes a public repository cache upstream third-party source repositories. The caching layer described does not exist.","why_zh":"Pull through cache 會把上游映像快取到 ECR private registry，而非 ECR public repository。ECR public repository 是用來公開發佈/分享自己的映像，並沒有讓 public repository 快取第三方上游來源 repository 的機制，所述的快取層並不存在。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A pull through cache rule is created on and targets the ECR private registry, not an ECR public repository. Configuring a pull through cache rule 'for the repository' in the public registry is mechanically incorrect, so the architecture is inverted and will not work even though the basic scanning portion is on the correct (private) side.","why_zh":"Pull through cache rule 是在 ECR private registry 上建立且以其為目標，而非 ECR public repository。在 public registry 為其 repository 設定 pull through cache rule 在機制上是錯的，因此即使 basic scanning 設在正確的 private 側，整體架構仍是顛倒且無法運作。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/pull-through-cache.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/image-scanning-basic-enabling.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/replication.html"]}},{"id":377,"question_en":"A company is running its ecommerce website on AWS. The website is currently hosted on a single Amazon EC2 instance in one Availability Zone. A MySQL database runs on the same EC2 instance. The company needs to eliminate single points of failure in the architecture to improve the website's availability and resilience. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST configuration changes to the website?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上运行其电子商务网站。该网站目前托管在单个可用区的一个 Amazon EC2 实例 上。MySQL 数据库也运行在同一个 EC2 实例上。 该公司需要消除架构中的单点故障，以提高网站的可用性和弹性。 哪种解决方案会 以对网站进行最少的配置更改来满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy the application by using AWS Fargate containers. Migrate the database to Amazon DynamoDB. Use Amazon API Gateway to route requests.","B":"Deploy the application on EC2 instances across multiple Availability Zones. Put the EC2 instances into an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer. Migrate the database to Amazon Aurora Multi-AZ. Use Amazon CloudFront for content delivery.","C":"Use AWS Elastic Beanstalk to deploy the application across multiple AWS Regions. Migrate the database to Amazon Redshift. Use Amazon ElastiCache for session management.","D":"Migrate the application to AWS Lambda functions. Use Amazon S3 for static content hosting. Migrate the database to Amazon DocumentDB (with MongoDB compatibility)."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS Fargate 容器部署应用程序。将数据库迁移到 Amazon DynamoDB。使用 Amazon API Gateway 路由请求。","B":"在多个可用区的 EC2 实例上部署应用程序。将 EC2 实例置于应用负载均衡器后面的自动扩展组中。将数 据库迁移到 Amazon Aurora 多可用区。使用 Amazon CloudFront 进行内容分发。","C":"使用 AWS Elastic Beanstalk 在多个 AWS 区域部署应用程序。将数据库迁移到 Amazon Redshift。 使用 Amazon ElastiCache 进行会话管理。","D":"将应用程序迁移到 AWS Lambda 函数。使用 Amazon S3 来托管静态内容。将数据库迁移到具有 MongoDB 兼容性的 Amazon DocumentDB。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Storage","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The architecture has two single points of failure: a single EC2 instance in one AZ (compute) and a co-located MySQL database. The qualifier is LEAST configuration changes to the website. Option B addresses both: deploying EC2 instances across multiple AZs in an Auto Scaling group behind an Application Load Balancer removes the compute/AZ single point of failure, and Amazon Aurora removes the database single point of failure by synchronously replicating data across Availability Zones to six storage nodes with automatic failover. Critically, AWS docs state Aurora is MySQL-compatible and that the code, tools, and applications you use today with existing MySQL databases can be used with Aurora without requiring changes to most existing applications, so the website keeps the same drivers, connection strings, and SQL; CloudFront is purely additive for content delivery. The other options all force a major application rewrite (containers/DynamoDB NoSQL, Lambda/DocumentDB, or Redshift which is an analytics warehouse rather than an OLTP transactional store), so they fail the 'least changes' qualifier.","explanation_zh":"此架構有兩個單點故障：位於單一 AZ 的單一 EC2 instance（運算層），以及與其同機的 MySQL 資料庫。題目限定條件為對網站做「最少的設定變更」。選項 B 同時解決兩者：將 EC2 instances 跨多個 AZ 部署於 Auto Scaling group 中並置於 Application Load Balancer 之後，消除運算/AZ 單點故障；Amazon Aurora 透過跨 AZ 同步複製資料至六個儲存節點並自動 failover，消除資料庫單點故障。關鍵在於 AWS 文件明載 Aurora 與 MySQL 相容，且現有 MySQL 資料庫所用的程式碼、工具與應用程式可直接用於 Aurora，多數現有應用程式無需變更，因此網站可沿用相同的 driver、連線字串與 SQL；CloudFront 則為純粹附加的內容傳遞。其他選項都迫使大幅改寫應用程式（容器/DynamoDB NoSQL、Lambda/DocumentDB，或 Redshift 這個分析型資料倉儲而非 OLTP 交易型資料庫），因此不符合「最少變更」的限定條件。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Migrating to Fargate containers, rewriting all data access for Amazon DynamoDB (a NoSQL key-value store incompatible with relational MySQL schemas/joins/transactions), and fronting with API Gateway requires a substantial application rewrite, violating the LEAST changes qualifier.","why_zh":"改用 Fargate 容器、將所有資料存取改寫為 Amazon DynamoDB（NoSQL 鍵值儲存，與關聯式 MySQL 的 schema/join/交易不相容），並以 API Gateway 作為前端，需大幅改寫應用程式，違反「最少變更」限定條件。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Redshift is a columnar OLAP data warehouse for analytics, not an OLTP transactional database for an ecommerce website, so it is the wrong database choice; deploying Elastic Beanstalk across multiple Regions also adds far more complexity than needed for HA within one Region.","why_zh":"Amazon Redshift 是用於分析的欄式 OLAP 資料倉儲，並非電商網站所需的 OLTP 交易型資料庫，屬錯誤的資料庫選擇；且跨多個 Region 部署 Elastic Beanstalk 對單一 Region 內的高可用性而言增加了過多不必要的複雜度。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Re-architecting the website into Lambda functions plus S3 static hosting is a full serverless rewrite, and Amazon DocumentDB is MongoDB-compatible (document/NoSQL), not MySQL-compatible, forcing a complete data-layer rewrite, which contradicts the LEAST changes requirement.","why_zh":"將網站重構為 Lambda 函式加上 S3 靜態託管屬於完整的無伺服器改寫，且 Amazon DocumentDB 與 MongoDB 相容（文件型/NoSQL），並非與 MySQL 相容，會迫使資料層完全改寫，與「最少變更」要求相牴觸。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/CHAP_AuroraOverview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/AuroraUserGuide/Concepts.AuroraHighAvailability.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/ec2-auto-scaling-availability-zone-balanced.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/autoscaling/ec2/userguide/attach-load-balancer-asg.html"]}},{"id":378,"question_en":"A company is developing a microservices-based application on AWS. The application consists of AWS Lambda functions and Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) services that need to be deployed frequently. A DevOps engineer needs to implement a consistent deployment solution across all components of the application. The solution must automate the deployments, minimize downtime during updates, and manage configuration data for the application. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST development effort?","question_zh":"一家公司正在 AWS 上开发一个基于微服务的应用程序。该应用程序由 AWS Lambda 函数和需要频 繁部署的 Amazon Elastic Container Service（Amazon ECS）服务组成。 一名 DevOps 工程师需要在应用程序的所有组件中实施一致的部署方案。该方案必须实现部署自动化， 将更新期间的停机时间降至最低，并管理应用程序的配置数据。 哪种解决方案能以最少的开发工作量满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudFormation to define and provision the Lambda functions and ECS services. Implement stack updates with resource replacement for all components. Use AWS Secrets Manager to manage the configuration data.","B":"Use AWS CodeDeploy to manage deployments for the Lambda functions and ECS services. Implement canary deployments for the Lambda functions. Implement blue/green deployments for the ECS services. Use AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to manage the configuration data.","C":"Use AWS Step Functions to orchestrate deployments for the Lambda functions and ECS services. Use canary deployments for the Lambda functions and ECS services in a different AWS Region. Use AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store to manage the configuration data.","D":"Use AWS Systems Manager to manage deployments for the Lambda functions and ECS services. Implement all-at-once deployments for the Lambda functions. Implement rolling updates for the ECS services. Use AWS Secrets Manager to manage the configuration data."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudFormation 来定义和配置 Lambda 函数以及 ECS 服务。对所有组件实施堆栈更新时采 用资源替换的方式。使用 AWS Secrets Manager 来管理配置数据。","B":"使用 AWS CodeDeploy 来管理 Lambda 函数和 ECS 服务的部署。为 Lambda 函数实施金丝雀部署。 为 ECS 服务实施蓝/绿部署。使用 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储来管理配置数据。","C":"使用 AWS Step Functions 来编排 Lambda 函数和 ECS 服务的部署。在不同的 AWS 区域对 Lambda 函 数和 ECS 服务使用金丝雀部署。使用 AWS Systems Manager 参数存储来管理配置数据。","D":"使用 AWS Systems Manager 来管理 Lambda 函数和 ECS 服务的部署。对 Lambda 函数实施一次性部 署。对 ECS 服务实施滚动更新。使用 AWS Secrets Manager 来管理配置数据。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"AWS CodeDeploy is the purpose-built, fully managed deployment service that automates application deployments across all three required compute platforms, including AWS Lambda functions and Amazon ECS services, so it provides one consistent solution with the least development effort and no custom orchestration code. For Lambda, CodeDeploy offers predefined canary traffic-shifting deployment configurations (for example CodeDeployDefault.LambdaCanary10Percent5Minutes) that move traffic in increments with automatic rollback to minimize downtime. For ECS, CodeDeploy performs blue/green deployments that route Application Load Balancer traffic to a replacement task set with zero downtime. AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store is designed to store, organize, and retrieve application configuration data hierarchically and cost-effectively, which exactly fits the requirement to manage configuration data without paying for Secrets Manager's secret-rotation features. Because every capability in option B is a managed service requiring no custom code, it meets all requirements with the least effort.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeDeploy 是專為部署而設計的全代管服務，可自動化部署到全部三種運算平台，包含 AWS Lambda 函數與 Amazon ECS 服務，因此能以最少的開發工作提供一致的部署方案，且無需自行撰寫編排程式碼。對 Lambda，CodeDeploy 提供預先定義的 canary 流量轉移部署設定（例如 CodeDeployDefault.LambdaCanary10Percent5Minutes），逐步移轉流量並可自動回復，以將停機時間降到最低。對 ECS，CodeDeploy 執行 blue/green 部署，將 Application Load Balancer 流量導向替換的 task set，達成零停機。AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store 專為以階層方式且具成本效益地儲存、組織與擷取應用程式組態資料而設計，正好符合『管理組態資料』的需求，且無須支付 Secrets Manager 的機密輪替功能費用。由於選項 B 的每項能力都是代管服務、無須自訂程式碼，因此能以最少工作量滿足所有需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Defining stack updates with resource replacement for all components forces resources to be deleted and recreated, which causes downtime and directly violates the minimize-downtime requirement. CloudFormation alone does not provide native incremental canary/blue-green traffic shifting without additional CodeDeploy hooks, and Secrets Manager is intended for secrets and rotation rather than general application configuration data.","why_zh":"對所有元件以資源取代（replacement）方式進行堆疊更新，會導致資源被刪除並重建而造成停機，直接違反『最小化停機時間』的需求。單靠 CloudFormation 在沒有額外 CodeDeploy hooks 的情況下無法提供原生的逐步 canary/blue-green 流量轉移，且 Secrets Manager 是用於機密與輪替，而非一般應用程式組態資料。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS Step Functions requires you to build and maintain custom deployment orchestration logic, which is far more development effort, not the least. Running canary deployments 'in a different AWS Region' is technically nonsensical because canary deployments shift traffic incrementally within the same environment, not across Regions, and it does nothing to minimize production downtime.","why_zh":"AWS Step Functions 需要自行建立並維護自訂的部署編排邏輯，開發工作量遠高於其他方案，並非最少。將 canary 部署放在『不同 AWS 區域』在技術上說不通，因為 canary 部署是在同一環境中逐步轉移流量、而非跨區域進行，對於降低生產環境停機時間也毫無幫助。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Systems Manager does not provide a native managed service to deploy Lambda function versions or ECS application revisions the way CodeDeploy does, so it cannot serve as the deployment engine here. All-at-once Lambda deployments shift 100% of traffic immediately and can cause downtime, contradicting the requirement, and Secrets Manager again targets secrets rather than configuration data.","why_zh":"AWS Systems Manager 並未像 CodeDeploy 那樣提供原生的代管服務來部署 Lambda 函數版本或 ECS 應用程式修訂，因此無法作為此處的部署引擎。Lambda 的 all-at-once 部署會立即轉移 100% 流量並可能造成停機，與需求相牴觸；且 Secrets Manager 同樣是針對機密而非組態資料。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployment-configurations.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/deployment-type-bluegreen.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager/latest/userguide/systems-manager-parameter-store.html"]}},{"id":379,"question_en":"A company is implementing a CI/CD pipeline for an application by using AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild. The company needs a solution to run unit tests and automatically generate code coverage reports before any code is deployed to production. The CI/CD pipeline execution must fail if the code coverage is less than 80%. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在使用 AWS CodePipeline 和 AWS CodeBuild 为一个应用程序实施持续集成/持续部署 （CI/CD）流水线。该公司需要一个解决方案，在任何代码部署到生产环境之前运行单元测试并自 动生成代码覆盖率报告。如果代码覆盖率低于 80%，CI/CD 流水线的执行必须失败。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS Lambda function to run unit tests and generate code coverage reports. Add a Lambda invoke action to a stage in the CodePipeline pipeline. Create an Amazon EventBridge scheduled rule to run hourly to monitor the Lambda function's output. Configure the rule to fail the pipeline if coverage is less than 80%.","B":"Create an AWS Step Functions workflow to run unit tests and generate code coverage reports. Add a Step Functions test action to a stage in the CodePipeline pipeline to invoke the workflow. Configure the workflow to fail if the code coverage is less than 80%.","C":"Create a CodeBuild project with a buildspec.yml file that includes commands to run unit tests and generate code coverage reports. Add a CodeBuild test action to a stage in the CodePipeline pipeline. Configure the CodeBuild test action to use the source artifacts from the source action as input. Modify the buildspec.yml file to fail the build if coverage is less than 80%.","D":"Create a CodeBuild project with Jenkins installed. Configure Jenkins to run unit tests and generate code coverage reports. Add a Jenkins test action to a stage in the CodePipeline pipeline. Configure the Jenkins test action to output the coverage report as an output artifact. Configure an approval action to fail the pipeline if code coverage is less than 80%."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数来运行单元测试并生成代码覆盖率报告。在 CodePipeline 管道的某个阶段 添加一个 Lambda 调用操作。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 定时规则，每小时运行一次以监控 Lambda 函数的输出。配置该规则，如果覆盖率低于 80%，则使管道失败。","B":"创建一个 AWS Step Functions 工作流来运行单元测试并生成代码覆盖率报告。在 CodePipeline 管道的 某个阶段添加一个 Step Functions 测试操作以调用该工作流。配置工作流，使其在代码覆盖率低于 80% 时失败。","C":"创建一个带有 buildspec.yml 文件的 CodeBuild 项目，该文件包含运行单元测试和生成代码覆盖率报 告的命令。在 CodePipeline 管道的某个阶段添加一个 CodeBuild 测试操作。配置 CodeBuild 测试操 作，使其将源操作的源工件作为输入。修改 如果覆盖率低于 80%，则让 buildspec.yml 文件使构建失败。","D":"创建一个安装了 Jenkins 的 CodeBuild 项目。配置 Jenkins 运行单元测试并生成代码覆盖率报告。在 CodePipeline 管道的某个阶段添加一个 Jenkins 测试操作。配置 Jenkins 测试操作将覆盖率报告输出为输 出工件。配置一个审批操作，如果代码覆盖率低于 80%，则使管道失败。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS CodeBuild is the native, purpose-built service for running unit tests and generating code coverage reports inside a CodePipeline. A buildspec.yml runs the test commands, and a 'reports:' section emits a code coverage report (line/branch coverage from JaCoCo XML, Clover XML, Cobertura XML, LCOV INFO, or SimpleCov JSON). CodeBuild is a first-class CodePipeline test action category, so it slots directly into a stage and consumes the source action's source artifacts as input. Because CodeBuild runs each buildspec command in a shell, any command that exits with a non-zero status (for example, a coverage-threshold gate that exits 1 when line coverage < 80%) fails the build phase; a failed CodeBuild action fails the pipeline stage and therefore the entire pipeline execution, preventing the deploy/production stage from running. This satisfies all requirements (run unit tests, generate coverage reports, fail the pipeline below 80%) with the least operational overhead and a fully native, deterministic fail mechanism. The other options bolt on extra services (Lambda, Step Functions, Jenkins) and rely on indirect, non-existent, or non-deterministic gating.","explanation_zh":"AWS CodeBuild 是在 CodePipeline 中執行單元測試並產生程式碼覆蓋率報告的原生、專用服務。buildspec.yml 可執行測試指令，而 'reports:' 區段可產生覆蓋率報告（支援 JaCoCo XML、Clover XML、Cobertura XML、LCOV INFO 或 SimpleCov JSON 的行/分支覆蓋率）。CodeBuild 是 CodePipeline 的一等 test action 類別，因此可直接放入某個 stage，並以 source action 的 source artifacts 作為輸入。由於 CodeBuild 在 shell 中執行每個 buildspec 指令，任何以非零狀態結束的指令（例如當行覆蓋率低於 80% 時 exit 1 的覆蓋率門檻檢查）都會使該 build 階段失敗；CodeBuild action 失敗會使 pipeline stage 失敗，進而使整個管線執行失敗，阻止部署/正式環境階段執行。這以最少的維運負擔滿足了所有需求（執行單元測試、產生覆蓋率報告、低於 80% 時讓管線失敗），且為完全原生、可確定地讓管線失敗的機制。其他選項硬塞了額外服務（Lambda、Step Functions、Jenkins），並依賴間接、不存在或不確定的把關方式。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A Lambda invoke action that fails already fails the pipeline on its own, so adding an hourly EventBridge scheduled rule to 'monitor the output and fail the pipeline' is decoupled and architecturally broken. Scheduled rules run on a fixed cron cadence and cannot reliably or synchronously fail the specific in-flight pipeline execution based on coverage, so they do not deterministically gate the deploy. Lambda is also not the purpose-built tool for running test suites and generating coverage reports, and this adds operational overhead.","why_zh":"失敗的 Lambda invoke action 本身就會使 pipeline 失敗，因此再加一個每小時的 EventBridge 排程規則去『監控輸出並使 pipeline 失敗』是脫鉤且架構錯誤的。排程規則以固定 cron 週期執行，無法可靠或同步地根據覆蓋率使該次進行中的管線執行失敗，因此無法確定性地把關部署。Lambda 也非執行測試套件與產生覆蓋率報告的專用工具，且此做法增加維運負擔。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"There is no native CodePipeline 'Step Functions test action.' CodePipeline integrates Step Functions only via an Invoke action (StepFunctions provider), not as a test-category action. Step Functions is an orchestration service and does not natively run test frameworks or generate code coverage reports; you would still need CodeBuild or another compute. This option is invalid as described and over-engineered.","why_zh":"CodePipeline 並沒有原生的『Step Functions test action』。CodePipeline 只透過 Invoke action（StepFunctions 供應商）整合 Step Functions，而非測試類別的 action。Step Functions 是流程編排服務，本身不會執行測試框架或產生程式碼覆蓋率報告；仍需 CodeBuild 或其他運算資源。此選項如所述無效且過度設計。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Running Jenkins inside a CodeBuild project is a contradiction and adds heavy operational overhead versus native CodeBuild. More importantly, an approval action is a manual human gate that pauses for action; it cannot automatically evaluate a coverage percentage and fail the pipeline. Coverage gating must be an automated, deterministic check, which an approval action does not provide.","why_zh":"在 CodeBuild 專案內執行 Jenkins 自相矛盾，且相較於原生 CodeBuild 增加沉重的維運負擔。更重要的是，approval action 是需要人工操作的手動門檻；它無法自動評估覆蓋率百分比並使管線失敗。覆蓋率把關必須是自動化、可確定的檢查，而 approval action 無法提供。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/code-coverage-report.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/build-spec-ref.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-CodeBuild.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pipeline-add-test.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html"]}},{"id":380,"question_en":"A company has a web application that publishes logs that contain metadata for transactions, with a status of success or failure for each log. The logs are in JSON format. The application publishes the logs to an Amazon CloudWatch Logs log group. The company wants to create a dashboard that displays the number of successful transactions. Which solution will meet this requirement with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个网络应用程序，该程序会发布包含交易元数据的日志，每个日志都有成功或失败的状态。 这些日志采用 JSON 格式。该应用程序将日志发布到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 日志组。 该公司希望创建一个仪表板来显示成功交易的数量。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster and an OpenSearch Service subscription filter to send the log group data to the cluster. Create a dashboard within the Dashboards feature in the OpenSearch Service cluster by using a search query for transactions that have a status of success.","B":"Create a CloudWatch subscription filter for the log group that uses an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to parse the JSON logs and publish a custom metric to CloudWatch for transactions that have a status of success. Create a CloudWatch dashboard by using a metric graph that displays the custom metric.","C":"Create a CloudWatch metric filter for the log groups with a filter pattern that matches the transaction status property and a value of success. Create a CloudWatch dashboard by using a metric graph that displays the new metric.","D":"Create an Amazon Kinesis data stream that is subscribed to the log group. Configure the data stream to filter incoming log data based on a status of success and to send the filtered logs to an AWS Lambda function. Configure the Lambda function to publish a custom metric to CloudWatch. Create a CloudWatch dashboard by using a metric graph that displays the custom metric."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个 Amazon OpenSearch Service 集群和一个 OpenSearch Service 订阅筛选器，将日志组数据发送到该 集群。在 OpenSearch Service 集群的“仪表板”功能中，使用搜索查询创建一个仪表板，该查询针对状 态为“成功”的交易。","B":"为日志组创建一个使用 AWS Lambda 函数的 CloudWatch 订阅筛选器。配置 Lambda 函数以解析 JSON 日 志，并为状态为成功的交易向 CloudWatch 发布自定义指标。使用显示自定义指标的指标图创建 CloudWatch 仪表板。","C":"为日志组创建一个 CloudWatch 指标筛选器，筛选模式匹配事务状态属性且值为“成功”。使用显示新 指标的指标图表创建一个 CloudWatch 仪表板。","D":"创建一个订阅了日志组的 Amazon Kinesis 数据流。配置数据流，使其根据成功状态过滤传入的日志数据， 并将过滤后的日志发送到一个 AWS Lambda 函数。配置 Lambda 函数，使其向 CloudWatch 发布自定 义指标。使用显示自定义指标的指标图创建一个 CloudWatch 仪表板。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"CloudWatch Logs metric filters natively support JSON filter patterns. A pattern such as { $.status = \"success\" } uses a property selector ($.) plus an equality operator (=) to match only log events whose JSON status property equals \"success\"; the AWS docs give the identical example { $.eventType = \"UpdateTrail\" }. The docs also state metric filters 'turn log data into numerical CloudWatch metrics that you can graph or set an alarm on,' and by default each matching event increments the metric, so graphing it on a CloudWatch dashboard directly shows the count of successful transactions. This is a fully managed, configuration-only feature: no code to write, no clusters or streams to provision, and no Lambda to maintain. Therefore option C meets the requirement with the LEAST operational overhead. The other options all add managed infrastructure (OpenSearch cluster, Kinesis stream) or custom Lambda code that merely re-implements what a metric filter does natively.","explanation_zh":"CloudWatch Logs 的 metric filter 原生支援 JSON filter patterns。像 { $.status = \"success\" } 這樣的模式使用 property selector ($.) 加上 equality operator (=)，只比對 JSON status 屬性等於 \"success\" 的日誌事件；AWS 文件給出完全相同形式的範例 { $.eventType = \"UpdateTrail\" }。文件也指出 metric filters 會「把 log data 轉成可繪圖或設警示的數值 CloudWatch metrics」，且每個符合的事件預設使 metric 加 1，因此在 CloudWatch dashboard 上繪製此 metric 即可直接顯示成功交易的數量。這是完全託管、僅需設定的功能：不需撰寫程式碼、不需建置叢集或串流、也不需維護 Lambda，因此營運負擔最低。其他選項都額外引入託管基礎設施（OpenSearch cluster、Kinesis stream）或自訂 Lambda 程式碼，只是重新實作 metric filter 原生就能完成的事。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Provisioning and operating an Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster (plus a subscription filter pipeline and dashboards) means cluster sizing, patching, and scaling, which is far more operational overhead than a native metric filter for simply counting successful transactions.","why_zh":"建置並維運 Amazon OpenSearch Service cluster（外加 subscription filter 管線與儀表板）需處理叢集規模、修補與擴展，只為計算成功交易數，營運負擔遠高於原生 metric filter。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A subscription filter invoking a Lambda function to parse JSON and PutMetricData requires writing, deploying, and maintaining custom code plus Lambda error handling and IAM; this is unnecessary because metric filters already match JSON properties natively, so it only adds overhead.","why_zh":"用 subscription filter 觸發 Lambda function 解析 JSON 並 PutMetricData，需撰寫、部署、維護自訂程式碼，外加 Lambda 錯誤處理與 IAM；由於 metric filter 已原生支援 JSON 屬性比對，這屬多餘且只增加負擔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Kinesis data streams cannot content-filter log records by a status value, so this still needs a Lambda function plus a stream to provision, shard-manage, and pay for; it is the most operationally complex option and duplicates the native metric filter capability.","why_zh":"Kinesis data streams 無法依 status 值過濾日誌記錄，因此仍需 Lambda function 加上要佈建、管理分片並付費的串流；這是營運上最複雜的選項，且重複了 metric filter 的原生能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/MonitoringLogData.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntax.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntaxForMetricFilters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateMetricFilterProcedure.html"]}},{"id":381,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon API Gateway and AWS Lambda functions to implement an API. The company uses a pipeline in AWS CodePipeline to build and deploy the API. The pipeline contains a source stage, build stage, and deployment stage. The company deploys the API without performing smoke tests. Soon after the deployment, the company observes multiple issues with the API. A security audit finds security vulnerabilities in the production code. The company wants to prevent these issues from happening in the future. Which combination of steps will meet this requirement? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用亚马逊 API 网关和 AWS Lambda 函数来实现一个 API。该公司使用 AWS CodePipeline 中的 管道来构建和部署该 API。该管道包含源代码阶段、构建阶段和部署阶段。 该公司在未进行冒烟测试的情况下就部署了 API。部署后不久，该公司就发现 API 存在多个问题。一次安 全审计发现生产代码中存在安全漏洞。 该公司希望防止此类问题在未来再次发生。 哪两种步骤的组合能满足这一要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a smoke test script that returns an error code if the API code fails the test. Add an action in the deployment stage to run the smoke test script after deployment. Configure the deployment stage for automatic rollback.","B":"Create a smoke test script that returns an error code if the API code fails the test. Add an action in the deployment stage to run the smoke test script after deployment. Configure the deployment stage to fail if the smoke test script returns an error code.","C":"Add an action in the build stage that uses Amazon Inspector to scan the Lambda function code after the code is built. Configure the build stage to fail if the scan returns any security findings.","D":"Add an action in the build stage to run an Amazon CodeGuru code scan after the code is built. Configure the build stage to fail if the scan returns any security findings.","E":"Add an action in the deployment stage to run an Amazon CodeGuru code scan after deployment. Configure the deployment stage to fail if the scan returns any security findings."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个冒烟测试脚本，如果 API 代码未通过测试则返回错误代码。在部署阶段添加一个操作，在 部署完成后运行冒烟测试脚本。为部署阶段配置自动回滚功能。","B":"创建一个冒烟测试脚本，如果 API 代码未通过测试则返回错误代码。在部署阶段添加一个操作，在部 署完成后运行该冒烟测试脚本。配置部署阶段，如果冒烟测试脚本返回错误代码则部署失败。","C":"在构建阶段添加一个操作，在代码构建完成后使用 Amazon Inspector 扫描 Lambda 函数代码。如果 扫描返回任何安全问题，则配置构建阶段失败。","D":"在构建阶段添加一个操作，在代码构建完成后运行 Amazon CodeGuru 代码扫描。配置构建阶 段，如果扫描返回任何安全问题则构建失败。","E":"在部署阶段添加一个操作，在部署完成后运行 Amazon CodeGuru 代码扫描。配置部署阶段，如 果扫描返回任何安全问题则部署失败。"},"answer":["B","D"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["B","D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"Two distinct problems must be solved: functional issues observed after deployment (need a smoke test gate) and security vulnerabilities reaching production (need a pre-deployment SAST scan). For the smoke test, Option B matches the native CodePipeline mechanism exactly: a script that returns a non-zero error code is run as an action in the deployment stage, and a failed action fails the stage, halting the pipeline and signaling the bad deployment so it does not proceed. Option A (automatic rollback) is a CodeDeploy deployment-group construct that, per AWS docs, triggers 'when a deployment fails or when a monitoring threshold you specify is met' (CloudWatch alarms), not directly off an arbitrary smoke-test script's exit code; the scenario is a generic API Gateway/Lambda pipeline with no CodeDeploy mentioned, so A does not fit the described script-exit-code mechanism. For security, Option D is correct: Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer performs program-analysis-based 'security analysis' (security detectors plus secrets detection) during the code-review/build stage, so failing the build on findings keeps vulnerable code out of production. Option C is wrong because Amazon Inspector Lambda code scanning scans 'application code in a Lambda function'—an already-deployed function via continuous, event-driven assessment—not a build-stage gate on a freshly built artifact. Option E (CodeGuru after deployment) fails the requirement because vulnerable code would already be in production before it is scanned. Therefore B and D meet the requirement.","explanation_zh":"本題有兩個獨立問題要解決：部署後才發現的功能性問題（需要 smoke test 把關），以及進入正式環境的安全漏洞（需要部署前的 SAST 掃描）。針對 smoke test，選項 B 正好對應 CodePipeline 的原生機制：在 deployment stage 加入一個 action 執行會回傳非零錯誤碼的腳本，當 action 失敗時整個 stage 失敗、pipeline 停止，明確標示這次部署有問題而不會繼續。選項 A（automatic rollback）是 CodeDeploy 的 deployment group 機制，依 AWS 文件其觸發條件是『部署失敗或達到你指定的監控門檻（CloudWatch alarm）』，並不是直接依任意 smoke test 腳本的退出碼觸發；而本題是一般的 API Gateway/Lambda pipeline，完全沒有提到 CodeDeploy，故 A 不符合題目描述的腳本退出碼機制。針對安全，選項 D 正確：Amazon CodeGuru Reviewer 透過程式分析在 code review/build 階段進行『security analysis』（security detectors 加上 secrets detection），在 build stage 發現問題即讓 build 失敗，可把有漏洞的程式擋在正式環境之外。選項 C 錯誤，因為 Amazon Inspector Lambda code scanning 掃描的是『Lambda function 內的應用程式碼』，也就是已部署函式上的持續、事件驅動評估，並非針對剛建置出的 artifact 在 build stage 做把關。選項 E（部署後才用 CodeGuru 掃描）不符合需求，因為漏洞程式在被掃描前就已進入正式環境。因此 B 與 D 符合需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Automatic rollback is a CodeDeploy deployment-group feature triggered when a deployment fails or a CloudWatch monitoring threshold is met, not directly by an arbitrary smoke-test script's exit code; the scenario is a generic API Gateway/Lambda pipeline with no CodeDeploy, so configuring 'the deployment stage for automatic rollback' does not match the described mechanism of a script returning an error code.","why_zh":"Automatic rollback 是 CodeDeploy deployment group 的功能，由部署失敗或 CloudWatch 監控門檻觸發，並非直接由任意 smoke test 腳本的退出碼觸發；本題是一般 API Gateway/Lambda pipeline 且未使用 CodeDeploy，故『將 deployment stage 設為自動回復』不符合題目描述的腳本回傳錯誤碼機制。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon Inspector Lambda code scanning scans application code in an already-deployed Lambda function via continuous, event-driven assessment of AWS resources. It is not a build-stage action that gates a freshly built artifact before deployment, so it cannot fail the build on findings to keep vulnerable code out of production in the way described.","why_zh":"Amazon Inspector Lambda code scanning 掃描的是已部署 Lambda function 內的應用程式碼，屬於對 AWS 資源的持續、事件驅動評估，並非在部署前對剛建置 artifact 把關的 build-stage action，因此無法依題意以發現項目使 build 失敗來阻擋漏洞程式進入正式環境。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Running the CodeGuru scan after deployment means the vulnerable code has already reached production before being scanned, which directly violates the requirement to prevent security vulnerabilities in production code. Security scanning must gate the build before deployment, not run post-deployment.","why_zh":"在部署後才執行 CodeGuru 掃描，代表漏洞程式在被掃描前就已進入正式環境，直接違反『避免正式環境程式存在安全漏洞』的需求。安全掃描必須在部署前的 build 階段把關，而不是部署後才執行。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeguru/latest/reviewer-ug/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/inspector/latest/user/scanning_resources_lambda_code.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployments-rollback-and-redeploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codebuild/latest/userguide/how-to-create-pipeline-add-test.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html"]}},{"id":382,"question_en":"A company is implementing a standardized security baseline across its AWS accounts. The accounts are in an organization in AWS Organizations. The company must deploy consistent IAM roles and policies across all existing and future accounts in the organization. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司正在其所有的 AWS 账户中实施标准化的安全基线。这些账户都属于 AWS 组织中的一个组织。 该公司必须在其组织内所有现有及未来的账户中部署一致的身份和访问管理（IAM）角色及策略。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Enable AWS Control Tower in the management account. Configure AWS Control Tower Account Factory customization to deploy the required IAM roles and policies to all accounts.","B":"Activate trusted access for AWS CloudFormation StackSets in Organizations. In the management account, create a stack set that has service-managed permissions to deploy the required IAM roles and policies to all accounts. Enable automatic deployment for the stack set.","C":"In each member account, create IAM roles that have permissions to create and manage resources. In the management account, create an AWS CloudFormation stack set that has self-managed permissions to deploy the required IAM roles and policies to all accounts. Enable automatic deployment for the stack set.","D":"In the management account, create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline. Configure the pipeline to use AWS CloudFormation to automate the deployment of the required IAM roles and policies. Set up cross- account IAM roles to allow CodePipeline to deploy resources in the member accounts."},"options_zh":{"A":"在管理账户中启用 AWS Control Tower。配置 AWS Control Tower 账户工厂自定义设置，以便将 所需的 IAM 角色和策略部署到所有账户。","B":"在组织中为 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 启用受信任访问。在管理账户中创建一个具有服务管理权 限的堆栈集，以便将所需的 IAM 角色和策略部署到所有账户。启用堆栈集的自动部署。","C":"在每个成员账户中，创建具有创建和管理资源权限的 IAM 角色。在管理账户中，创建一个具有自我 管理权限的 AWS CloudFormation 堆栈集，以便将所需的 IAM 角色和策略部署到所有账户。启用 堆栈集的自动部署。","D":"在管理账户中，创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。配置该管道以使用 AWS CloudFormation 自动部署 所需的 IAM 角色和策略。设置跨账户 IAM 角色，以允许 CodePipeline 在成员账户中部署资源。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to deploy consistent IAM roles and policies to all existing AND future accounts in an AWS Organizations org with the MOST operational efficiency. CloudFormation StackSets with service-managed permissions is purpose-built for this. After activating trusted access with Organizations, a service-managed stack set created in the management account can target the entire organization (or an OU, which automatically includes all child OUs and accounts). AWS docs state that with service-managed permissions 'you don't have to create the necessary IAM roles; StackSets creates the IAM roles on your behalf' and 'you can also turn on automatic deployments to accounts that you add to your organization in the future.' Enabling automatic deployment means any account later added to the organization or target OU automatically receives the stack, satisfying the 'future accounts' requirement with zero ongoing effort. This is exactly Option B (activate trusted access, create a service-managed stack set, enable automatic deployment), giving the least operational overhead for both existing and future accounts.","explanation_zh":"需求是以最高的營運效率，將一致的 IAM roles 與 policies 部署到 AWS Organizations 中所有現有及未來的帳戶。CloudFormation StackSets 搭配 service-managed permissions 正是為此設計。在啟用與 Organizations 的 trusted access 後，於 management account 建立的 service-managed stack set 可針對整個組織（或某個 OU，會自動包含所有子 OU 與帳戶）進行部署。AWS 文件明確指出，使用 service-managed permissions 時『你不需要自行建立必要的 IAM roles；StackSets 會代你建立 IAM roles』，且『你也可以開啟 automatic deployments，讓未來加入組織的帳戶自動部署』。啟用 automatic deployment 後，任何之後加入組織或目標 OU 的新帳戶都會自動收到該 stack，滿足『未來帳戶』需求且無需任何後續維護。這正好對應選項 B（啟用 trusted access、建立 service-managed stack set、啟用 automatic deployment），對現有與未來帳戶都提供最低的營運開銷。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS Control Tower Account Factory Customization (AFC) can deploy blueprints, but it first requires a fully deployed Control Tower landing zone and OUs registered/baselined (AWSControlTowerBaseline), which is much heavier setup. AFC is oriented around per-account blueprints applied at provisioning time; applying to existing accounts requires per-account 'Update account' actions. Adopting Control Tower solely to push a set of IAM roles/policies is far more operational overhead than a single service-managed stack set with automatic deployment.","why_zh":"AWS Control Tower Account Factory Customization (AFC) 雖可部署 blueprints，但需先完整部署 Control Tower landing zone 並註冊/baseline OU（AWSControlTowerBaseline），設定成本高很多。AFC 以每個帳戶於佈建時套用 blueprint 為主；要套用到現有帳戶需逐一執行『Update account』。僅為推送一組 IAM roles/policies 而導入 Control Tower，營運開銷遠高於單一 service-managed stack set 搭配 automatic deployment。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Self-managed permissions require you to manually create the StackSet administration and execution IAM roles in every member account (the option even states this), which is significant manual setup. Critically, self-managed StackSets do NOT support automatic deployment to newly added organization accounts (that feature belongs to service-managed permissions), so future accounts would not be covered automatically.","why_zh":"Self-managed permissions 需要你在每個 member account 手動建立 StackSet 的管理與執行 IAM roles（此選項本身也這麼描述），屬大量手動設定。更關鍵的是，self-managed StackSets 不支援對新加入組織帳戶的自動部署（該功能屬於 service-managed permissions），因此未來帳戶不會被自動涵蓋。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A CodePipeline + CloudFormation + cross-account IAM roles approach is a custom build requiring you to maintain the pipeline, account lists, and per-account deploy roles. It does not natively integrate with Organizations to auto-discover or auto-enroll future accounts, so you would have to update the pipeline and roles for every new account. This is the most operational overhead of all options.","why_zh":"CodePipeline + CloudFormation + 跨帳戶 IAM roles 屬於自建方案，需自行維護 pipeline、帳戶清單與每個帳戶的部署角色。它不原生整合 Organizations 來自動發現或自動納入未來帳戶，每新增一個帳戶都需更新 pipeline 與 roles，是所有選項中營運開銷最高的。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-associate-stackset-with-org.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-activate-trusted-access.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/af-customization-page.html"]}},{"id":383,"question_en":"A company is migrating its web application to AWS. The application uses WebSocket connections for real- time updates and requires sticky sessions. A DevOps engineer must implement a highly available architecture for the application. The application must be accessible to users worldwide with the least possible latency. Which solution will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"一家公司正在将其网络应用程序迁移到 AWS。该应用程序使用 WebSocket 连接来实现实时通信。 时间更新并需要保持会话持久。 DevOps 工程师必须为应用程序实现高可用性架构。该应用程序必须能以尽可能低的延迟为全球用户 提供访问服务。 哪种解决方案能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB). Deploy another ALB in a different AWS Region. Enable cross-zone load balancing and sticky sessions on the ALBs. Integrate the ALBs with Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing.","B":"Deploy a Network Load Balancer (NLB). Deploy another NLB in a different AWS Region. Enable cross- zone load balancing and sticky sessions on the NLBs. Integrate the NLBs with Amazon Route 53 geolocation routing.","C":"Deploy a Network Load Balancer (NLB) with cross-zone load balancing enabled. Configure the NLB with IP-based targets in multiple Availability Zones. Use Amazon CloudFront for global content delivery. Implement sticky sessions by using source IP address preservation on the NLB.","D":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) for HTTP traffic. Deploy a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in each of the company’s AWS Regions for WebSocket connections. Enable sticky sessions on the ALB. Configure the ALB to forward requests to the NLB."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。在另一个 AWS 区域部署另一个 ALB。在 ALB 上启用跨区负载 均衡和粘性会话。将 ALB 与基于延迟的 Amazon Route 53 路由集成。","B":"部署一个网络负载均衡器（NLB）。在不同的 AWS 区域部署另一个 NLB。在 NLB 上启用跨区负载均 衡和粘性会话。将 NLB 与 Amazon Route 53 地理位置路由集成。","C":"部署一个启用了跨区域负载均衡的网络负载均衡器（NLB）。在多个可用区中使用基于 IP 的目标配置 NLB。使用 Amazon CloudFront 进行全球内容分发。通过在 NLB 上保留源 IP 地址来实现粘性会话。","D":"部署一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）来处理 HTTP 流量。在公司的每个 AWS 区域部署一个网络负载均 衡器（NLB）来处理 WebSocket 连接。在 ALB 上启用粘性会话。配置 ALB 将请求转发到 NLB。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The application needs native WebSocket support, cookie-based sticky sessions, multi-Region high availability, lowest-latency global access, and the least operational overhead. An Application Load Balancer operates at Layer 7, natively handles the HTTP-to-WebSocket protocol upgrade, and provides true cookie-based stickiness (duration-based AWSALB cookie or application-based cookie) — the correct stickiness mechanism for a web application. Deploying an ALB in two AWS Regions gives cross-Region high availability, and Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing serves each user from the Region that provides the lowest latency, which the docs state explicitly: 'serving their requests from the AWS Region that provides the lowest latency.' Because ALB and Route 53 are fully managed, this design has the least operational overhead, so option A is correct. The NLB options fail on stickiness (NLB stickiness is Layer-4 flow/source-IP based, not cookie-based), and geolocation routing (B) routes by location rather than measured latency.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式需要原生 WebSocket 支援、以 cookie 為基礎的 sticky sessions、跨 Region 高可用性、全球最低延遲存取，且操作負擔最低。Application Load Balancer 運作於第 7 層，原生處理 HTTP 到 WebSocket 的協定升級，並提供真正以 cookie 為基礎的黏著（duration-based 的 AWSALB cookie 或 application-based cookie），這正是 Web 應用程式適用的黏著機制。在兩個 AWS Region 部署 ALB 可提供跨 Region 高可用性，而 Amazon Route 53 latency-based routing 會由延遲最低的 Region 為每位使用者提供服務，文件明確指出『serving their requests from the AWS Region that provides the lowest latency』。由於 ALB 與 Route 53 皆為全託管服務，此設計操作負擔最低，因此選項 A 正確。NLB 選項在黏著機制上不符（NLB 黏著屬第 4 層 flow/source-IP 基礎，而非 cookie 基礎），而 geolocation routing（B）依位置導流而非實測延遲。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A Network Load Balancer operates at Layer 4, and its 'sticky sessions' are flow/source-IP based, not cookie-based, which is improper for web-application stickiness and unreliable behind NAT or proxies. Route 53 geolocation routing directs queries by the user's geographic location, not by measured latency, so it does not satisfy the 'least possible latency' requirement.","why_zh":"Network Load Balancer 運作於第 4 層，其 sticky sessions 以 flow/source IP 為基礎而非 cookie，不適合 Web 應用程式的黏著需求，在 NAT/代理後方也不可靠。Route 53 geolocation routing 依使用者地理位置導流，而非實測延遲，無法滿足『最低延遲』需求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"A single NLB spanning AZs in one Region is not multi-Region highly available, and there is no Route 53 layer to fail over or latency-route across Regions. 'Source IP address preservation' is a client-IP visibility feature, not a sticky-session mechanism, and an NLB cannot do cookie-based stickiness. CloudFront accelerates delivery but does not by itself provide cross-Region failover, so the HA requirement is not met.","why_zh":"單一 NLB 僅跨單一 Region 的多個 AZ，並非跨 Region 高可用，且缺少 Route 53 層做跨 Region 故障轉移或延遲導流。『Source IP address preservation』是用戶端 IP 可見性功能，並非 sticky session 機制，且 NLB 無法做 cookie-based 黏著。CloudFront 可加速傳遞但本身不提供跨 Region 故障轉移，因此不滿足高可用需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Chaining an ALB to forward to per-Region NLBs for WebSocket is architecturally redundant and complex; an ALB already natively handles WebSocket and provides cookie-based stickiness. This stacked design increases operational overhead and provides no clean global latency-routing layer, violating the LEAST operational overhead qualifier.","why_zh":"讓 ALB 轉發到各 Region 的 NLB 來處理 WebSocket 在架構上多餘且複雜；ALB 本身已原生支援 WebSocket 並提供 cookie-based 黏著。此堆疊式設計增加操作負擔，且未提供乾淨的全球延遲導流層，違反『操作負擔最低』的限定條件。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-latency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-geo.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/introduction.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/load-balancer-listeners.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/sticky-sessions.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/elasticloadbalancing/latest/application/edit-target-group-attributes.html"]}},{"id":384,"question_en":"A company has a workflow that generates a file for each of the company's products and stores the files in a production environment Amazon S3 bucket. The company's users can access the S3 bucket. Each file contains a product ID. Product IDs for products that have not been publicly announced are prefixed with a specific UUID. Product IDs are 12 characters long. IDs for products that have not been publicly announces begin with the letter P. The company does not want information about products that have not been publicly announced to be available in the production environment S3 bucket. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个工作流程，为公司的每种产品生成一个文件，并将这些文件存储在生产环境的亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。该公司的用户可以访问此 S3 存储桶。 每个文件都包含一个产品 ID。尚未公开宣布的产品的产品 ID 以特定的 UUID 作为前缀。产品 ID 长 度为 12 个字符。尚未公开宣布的产品的 ID 以字母 P 开头。 该公司不希望尚未公开发布的产品信息出现在生产环境的 S3 存储桶中。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a new staging S3 bucket. Generate all files in the new staging bucket. Create an Amazon Macie custom data identifier to identify product IDs in the new bucket that begin with the specific UUID. Launch an Amazon Macie sensitive data discovery job with the custom data identifier. Copy all files that do not have a Macie finding to the production S3 bucket.","B":"Create an Amazon Macie custom data identifier to identify product IDs in the production bucket that begin with the specific UUID. Launch an Amazon Macie sensitive data discovery job with the custom data identifier. Remove all files that have a Macie finding from the production S3 bucket.","C":"Create a new staging S3 bucket. Generate all files in the new staging bucket. Launch an Amazon Macie sensitive data discovery job with a managed data identifier. Copy all files that do not have a Macie finding to the production S3 bucket.","D":"Create an Amazon Macie sensitive data discovery job with a managed data identifier. Remove all files that have a Macie finding from the production S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个新的暂存 S3 存储桶。在新的暂存存储桶中生成所有文件。创建一个 Amazon Macie 自定义数 据标识符，用于识别新存储桶中以特定 UUID 开头的产品 ID。使用自定义数据标识符启动 Amazon Macie 敏感数据发现任务。将所有没有 Macie 发现结果的文件复制到生产 S3 存储桶。","B":"创建一个 Amazon Macie 自定义数据标识符，用于识别生产存储桶中以特定 UUID 开头的产品 ID。 使用该自定义数据标识符启动 Amazon Macie 敏感数据发现任务。从生产 S3 存储桶中删除所有被 Macie 发现存在问题的文件。","C":"创建一个新的暂存 S3 存储桶。在新的暂存存储桶中生成所有文件。使用托管数据标识符启动 Amazon Macie 敏感数据发现任务。将所有没有 Macie 发现结果的文件复制到生产 S3 存储桶。","D":"使用托管数据标识符创建一个 Amazon Macie 敏感数据发现任务。从生产 S3 存储桶中移除所有被 Macie 标记出问题的文件。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The product ID with a UUID prefix is a proprietary, organization-specific pattern, not a built-in sensitive data type. Amazon Macie managed data identifiers detect only a fixed set of built-in types (credentials, financial information, PII/PHI such as AWS secret keys, credit card numbers, and passport numbers), so they cannot match a custom product-ID/UUID pattern. Detecting an organization-defined pattern requires a custom data identifier, where you supply a regex (the AWS doc cites employee IDs and customer account numbers as examples). This eliminates options C and D, which both rely on a managed data identifier. The deciding qualifier is that unannounced-product information must NOT be available in the production bucket at all. A Macie sensitive data discovery job scans objects that already exist in a bucket, so it is an after-the-fact detection mechanism, not a preventive gate. Option B generates files directly in production and only removes flagged files after the job runs, leaving a window where user-accessible production data exposes unannounced products. Option A generates all files in a separate staging bucket, scans them there with a custom data identifier, and copies only files with no Macie finding into production, so unannounced-product data never reaches production. Therefore A is correct.","explanation_zh":"帶有 UUID 前綴的產品 ID 是公司專有、組織自訂的模式，並非內建的敏感資料類型。Amazon Macie 的 managed data identifier 只能偵測固定的內建類型（憑證、財務資訊、PII/PHI，例如 AWS secret key、信用卡號、護照號碼），因此無法比對自訂的產品 ID/UUID 模式。要偵測組織自訂的模式必須使用 custom data identifier，由你提供 regex（AWS 文件以員工 ID、客戶帳號為範例）。這排除了同樣只用 managed data identifier 的選項 C 與 D。決定性的限定條件是：未公開產品的資訊絕對不可出現在 production bucket。Macie sensitive data discovery job 掃描的是已存在於 bucket 中的物件，屬於事後偵測機制，並非預防性的閘門。選項 B 直接在 production 產生檔案，僅在 job 執行後才移除被標記的檔案，期間會留下使用者可存取且暴露未公開產品的空窗。選項 A 在獨立的 staging bucket 產生所有檔案，於該處以 custom data identifier 掃描，僅將沒有 Macie finding 的檔案複製到 production，因此未公開產品資料永遠不會進入 production。故 A 正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Uses the correct custom data identifier, but generates files directly in the user-accessible production bucket and only removes flagged files after the discovery job completes. Because the job is a post-write scan, unannounced-product data is exposed in production during the scan window, violating the requirement that it never be available there.","why_zh":"雖使用正確的 custom data identifier，但直接在使用者可存取的 production bucket 產生檔案，僅在 discovery job 完成後才移除被標記的檔案。由於 job 屬於寫入後掃描，在掃描空窗期間未公開產品資料會暴露於 production，違反「絕不可出現於 production」的要求。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses only a managed data identifier, which detects built-in sensitive data types (credentials, financial, PII/PHI) and cannot match the company's custom UUID-prefixed product-ID pattern. The job would produce no relevant findings, so unannounced-product files would be copied to production undetected.","why_zh":"只使用 managed data identifier，僅能偵測內建敏感資料類型（憑證、財務、PII/PHI），無法比對公司自訂的 UUID 前綴產品 ID 模式。該 job 不會產生相關 finding，導致未公開產品檔案未被偵測就被複製到 production。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Combines both failures: a managed data identifier cannot detect the custom UUID pattern, and the scan runs against the production bucket after the fact and then removes. It fails to detect the proprietary pattern and also leaves the data exposed in production, so it doubly fails the requirements.","why_zh":"結合兩個缺陷：managed data identifier 無法偵測自訂 UUID 模式，且在 production bucket 事後掃描後才移除。既無法偵測專有模式，又讓資料暴露於 production，因此雙重不符合要求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/custom-data-identifiers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/managed-data-identifiers.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/discovery-jobs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/macie/latest/user/cdis-create.html"]}},{"id":385,"question_en":"A company uses Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server as its primary database for applications. The company needs to ensure high availability within and across AWS Regions. An Amazon Route 53 CNAME record is configured for the database endpoint. The applications connect to the database endpoint. The company must redirect application traffic to a standby database during a failover event. The company must maintain an RPO of less than 1 minute and an RTO of less than 10 minutes. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"该公司将其应用程序的主要数据库托管在 Amazon RDS for Microsoft SQL Server 上。该公司需要确 保在 AWS 区域内部以及跨区域的高可用性。 亚马逊 Route 53 的 CNAME 记录已针对数据库端点进行配置。应用程序连接到数据库端点。在故障转移 事件期间，公司必须将应用程序流量重定向到备用数据库。公司必须保持小于 1 分钟的恢复点目标 （RPO）和小于 10 分钟的恢复时间目标（RTO）。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Amazon RDS for SQL Server Multi-AZ DB cluster deployment that uses cross-Region read replicas. Use automation to promote the read replica to a standalone instance and to update the Route 53 record.","B":"Deploy an Amazon RDS for SQL Server Multi-AZ DB cluster deployment. Set up automated snapshots to be copied to another Region every 5 minutes. Use AWS Lambda to restore the latest snapshot in the secondary Region during failover.","C":"Deploy an Amazon RDS for SQL Server Single-AZ DB instance. Use AWS Database Migration Service (AWS DMS) to replicate data continuously to an RDS DB instance in another Region. Use Amazon CloudWatch alarms to notify the company about failover events.","D":"Deploy an Amazon RDS for SQL Server Single-AZ DB instance. Configure AWS Backup to create cross-Region backups every 30 seconds. Use automation to restore the latest backup and to update the Route 53 record during failover."},"options_zh":{"A":"部署一个使用跨区域读取副本的 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 多可用区数据库集群。使用自动化将读 取副本提升为独立实例，并更新 Route 53 记录。","B":"部署一个 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 多可用区数据库集群。设置每 5 分钟将自动快照复制到另一个区 域。使用 AWS Lambda 在故障转移期间在辅助区域恢复最新的快照。","C":"部署一个 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 单可用区数据库实例。使用 AWS 数据库迁移服务（AWS DMS） 将数据持续复制到另一个区域的 RDS 数据库实例。使用 Amazon CloudWatch 警报在发生故障转移事 件时通知公司。","D":"部署一个 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 单可用区数据库实例。配置 AWS Backup 每 30 秒创建一次跨 区域备份。使用自动化在故障转移期间恢复最新备份并更新 Route 53 记录。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Migration","Compute","Database","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The requirement is cross-Region HA for RDS for Microsoft SQL Server with RPO < 1 minute and RTO < 10 minutes, redirecting traffic via a Route 53 CNAME during failover. Options A and B are both architecturally impossible because Amazon RDS for SQL Server does NOT support Multi-AZ DB cluster deployments. The AWS documentation explicitly states Multi-AZ DB clusters 'aren't available' for RDS for Db2, RDS for MariaDB, RDS for Oracle, and RDS for SQL Server (only RDS for MySQL and RDS for PostgreSQL are supported). Option D is infeasible because AWS Backup schedules backups by frequency (hourly at the smallest standard cron interval), not 'every 30 seconds,' and restoring a backup into a brand-new DB instance in another Region during failover would far exceed the 10-minute RTO. Option C is the only valid choice: AWS DMS supports ongoing replication (CDC) from a SQL Server source, continuously streaming low-latency changes to a pre-provisioned, warm-standby RDS instance in the secondary Region, achieving RPO < 1 minute. Because the standby already exists and is running, failover is simply updating the Route 53 record, easily meeting RTO < 10 minutes, while CloudWatch alarms provide failover notifications. The dump's suggested answer (A) is wrong because it relies on a Multi-AZ DB cluster feature that does not exist for SQL Server.","explanation_zh":"需求是為 RDS for Microsoft SQL Server 提供跨 Region 的高可用性，RPO < 1 分鐘、RTO < 10 分鐘，並在故障切換時透過 Route 53 CNAME 重新導向流量。選項 A 與 B 在架構上根本不可行，因為 Amazon RDS for SQL Server 不支援 Multi-AZ DB cluster 部署。AWS 文件明確指出 Multi-AZ DB clusters 對 RDS for Db2、RDS for MariaDB、RDS for Oracle 與 RDS for SQL Server 都『不可用』（只有 RDS for MySQL 與 RDS for PostgreSQL 支援）。選項 D 不可行，因為 AWS Backup 是以頻率排程備份（透過 cron 的標準最小間隔為每小時），無法『每 30 秒』備份，且故障切換時將備份還原成另一個 Region 的全新 DB instance 會遠超過 10 分鐘的 RTO。選項 C 是唯一有效的方案：AWS DMS 支援從 SQL Server 來源進行持續複寫（CDC），將低延遲變更持續串流到次要 Region 中已預先佈建、處於暖待命（warm standby）的 RDS instance，達成 RPO < 1 分鐘。由於待命實例已存在且持續運行，故障切換只需更新 Route 53 記錄，可輕鬆滿足 RTO < 10 分鐘，並由 CloudWatch alarms 提供故障切換通知。題庫建議答案（A）是錯的，因為它依賴 SQL Server 並不存在的 Multi-AZ DB cluster 功能。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Amazon RDS for SQL Server does NOT support Multi-AZ DB cluster deployments; AWS docs explicitly list SQL Server (with Db2, MariaDB, Oracle) as engines for which Multi-AZ DB clusters aren't available. The 'Multi-AZ DB cluster deployment that uses cross-Region read replicas' configuration cannot be created for SQL Server at all, so the premise is invalid even though the promote-replica + Route 53 update pattern is otherwise reasonable.","why_zh":"Amazon RDS for SQL Server 不支援 Multi-AZ DB cluster 部署；AWS 文件明確將 SQL Server（連同 Db2、MariaDB、Oracle）列為 Multi-AZ DB clusters 不可用的引擎。『使用跨 Region read replica 的 Multi-AZ DB cluster 部署』這個組態根本無法為 SQL Server 建立，因此前提無效，即使提升 replica 加更新 Route 53 的模式本身合理。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Same fatal flaw: Multi-AZ DB cluster is not available for RDS for SQL Server. Additionally, snapshot copies cannot be scheduled every 5 minutes (which would also breach RPO < 1 minute), and restoring the latest snapshot in the secondary Region during failover cannot meet RTO < 10 minutes.","why_zh":"同樣的致命缺陷：Multi-AZ DB cluster 不適用於 RDS for SQL Server。此外，快照複製無法每 5 分鐘排程（也會違反 RPO < 1 分鐘），且故障切換時於次要 Region 還原最新快照無法滿足 RTO < 10 分鐘。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Backup schedules backups by frequency (hourly at the smallest standard cron interval), not 'every 30 seconds,' so RPO < 1 minute is impossible. Restoring the latest backup into a brand-new DB instance in another Region during failover takes far longer than the 10-minute RTO, and it updates Route 53 only after a lengthy restore rather than cutting over to a warm standby.","why_zh":"AWS Backup 以頻率排程備份（透過標準 cron 的最小間隔為每小時），無法『每 30 秒』備份，因此不可能達成 RPO < 1 分鐘。故障切換時將最新備份還原成另一個 Region 的全新 DB instance 所需時間遠超過 10 分鐘 RTO，且它只在漫長還原後才更新 Route 53，而非切換到暖待命。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/Concepts.RDS_Fea_Regions_DB-eng.Feature.MultiAZDBClusters.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonRDS/latest/UserGuide/multi-az-db-clusters-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/CHAP_Source.SQLServer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/dms/latest/userguide/CHAP_Source.SQLServer.CDC.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/creating-a-backup-plan.html"]}},{"id":386,"question_en":"A company wants to build a pipeline to update the standard AMI monthly. The AMI must be updated to use the most recent patches to ensure that launched Amazon EC2 instances are up to date. Each new AMI must be available to all AWS accounts in the company's organization in AWS Organizations. The company needs to configure an automated pipeline to build the AMI. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司希望构建一条管道，每月更新标准的 AMI。AMI 必须更新为使用最新的补丁，以确保所启动的 Amazon EC2 实例保持最新状态。每个新的 AMI 都必须可供公司组织中 AWS 组织内的所有 AWS 账户使 用。 该公司需要配置一个自动化流水线来构建 AMI。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that uses AWS CodeBuild. Create an AWS Lambda function to run the pipeline every month. Create an AWS CloudFormation template. Share the template with all AWS accounts in the organization.","B":"Create an AMI pipeline by using EC2 Image Builder. Configure the pipeline to distribute the AMI to the AWS accounts in the organization. Configure the pipeline to run monthly.","C":"Create an AWS CodePipeline pipeline that runs an AWS Lambda function to build the AMI. Configure the pipeline to share the AMI with the AWS accounts in the organization. Configure Amazon EventBridge Scheduler to invoke the pipeline every month.","D":"Create an AWS Systems Manager Automation runbook. Configure the automation to run in all AWS accounts in the organization. Create an AWS Lambda function to run the automation every month."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个使用 AWS CodeBuild 的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，每月运行一 次该管道。创建一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板。将该模板与组织中的所有 AWS 账户共享。","B":"使用 EC2 Image Builder 创建 AMI 管道。配置管道将 AMI 分发到组织中的 AWS 账户。配置管道每月 运行一次。","C":"创建一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道，运行一个 AWS Lambda 函数来构建 AMI。配置管道与组织中的 AWS 账户共享 AMI。配置 Amazon EventBridge 调度程序每月调用一次该管道。","D":"创建一个 AWS Systems Manager Automation 运行手册。配置自动化以在组织中的所有 AWS 账户中 运行。创建一个 AWS Lambda 函数，每月运行一次该自动化。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"EC2 Image Builder is the AWS purpose-built, fully managed service for automating AMI builds, so it meets all requirements with the least operational overhead. An Image Builder AMI pipeline includes a schedule that configures when and how often the pipeline automatically creates a new image, so it can rebuild the AMI monthly without custom Lambda/EventBridge code. The build process uses AWSTOE components to bake in OS patching, ensuring each new AMI contains the most recent patches. Image Builder's distribution settings natively define AMI launch permissions and support cross-account/AWS Organizations sharing, so each new AMI is automatically made available to all member accounts. The other options require hand-built orchestration (custom Lambda build logic, CodePipeline glue, manual CloudFormation/AMI sharing, or per-account Systems Manager runbooks) that adds significant overhead and does not match Image Builder's native scheduling, patching, and organization-wide distribution.","explanation_zh":"EC2 Image Builder 是 AWS 專為自動化 AMI 建置打造的全代管服務，因此能以最低營運負擔滿足所有需求。Image Builder 的 AMI pipeline 內建排程（Schedule），可設定 pipeline 自動建立新映像的時間與頻率，因此無需自訂 Lambda 或 EventBridge 程式碼即可每月重建 AMI。建置流程透過 AWSTOE components 將作業系統修補納入映像，確保每個新 AMI 都包含最新的修補程式。Image Builder 的 distribution settings 原生定義 AMI 啟動權限，並支援跨帳戶／AWS Organizations 共用，因此每個新 AMI 都能自動提供給所有成員帳戶。其他選項都需要手動拼湊的協調流程（自訂 Lambda 建置邏輯、CodePipeline 串接、手動 CloudFormation／AMI 共用，或每帳戶的 Systems Manager runbook），會增加大量營運負擔，且不及 Image Builder 原生的排程、修補與組織範圍散布能力。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"CodePipeline + CodeBuild + a custom Lambda scheduler + a CloudFormation template is a build-it-yourself approach. CodeBuild does not natively produce or patch AMIs, and sharing a CloudFormation template does not distribute an AMI's launch permissions to organization accounts. This is far more operational overhead than Image Builder.","why_zh":"CodePipeline + CodeBuild + 自訂 Lambda 排程器 + CloudFormation 範本屬於自行打造的做法。CodeBuild 本身不會產生或修補 AMI，而分享 CloudFormation 範本也無法將 AMI 的啟動權限散布給組織帳戶。其營運負擔遠高於 Image Builder。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Using a Lambda function inside CodePipeline to build the AMI plus EventBridge Scheduler to trigger it requires writing and maintaining all the AMI-build, patch, and cross-account sharing logic by hand. AMI builds are also long-running and resource-intensive, which is a poor fit for Lambda. Image Builder provides all of this as managed features, so this option has much higher operational overhead.","why_zh":"在 CodePipeline 中以 Lambda 建置 AMI、再用 EventBridge Scheduler 觸發，需自行撰寫並維護所有 AMI 建置、修補與跨帳戶共用邏輯。AMI 建置耗時且資源密集，並不適合 Lambda。Image Builder 已將這些功能以代管方式提供，因此此選項營運負擔高出許多。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"A Systems Manager Automation runbook run in every account plus a Lambda monthly trigger means each account independently builds its own AMI, rather than producing one standard AMI shared org-wide. This multiplies maintenance across accounts and does not satisfy the single standard-AMI-distributed requirement as cleanly as Image Builder.","why_zh":"在每個帳戶執行 Systems Manager Automation runbook 並以 Lambda 每月觸發，代表每個帳戶各自獨立建置自己的 AMI，而非產生一個在組織內共享的標準 AMI。這會在各帳戶間倍增維護成本，且無法像 Image Builder 那樣乾淨地滿足單一標準 AMI 散布的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/what-is-image-builder.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/how-image-builder-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/cross-account-dist.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/schedule-pipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/TemplateReference/aws-properties-imagebuilder-imagepipeline-schedule.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/imagebuilder/latest/userguide/manage-shared-resources.html"]}},{"id":387,"question_en":"A company has an application that uses an Amazon API Gateway REST API, AWS Lambda functions, and an Amazon DynamoDB table. The application currently runs in a single AWS Region. The company wants to make the application highly available across two Regions. User traffic must be routed to the Region that provides the least latency. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司拥有一款应用程序，该程序使用了亚马逊 API 网关 REST API、AWS Lambda 函数以及亚马逊 DynamoDB 表。目前该应用程序仅在一个 AWS 区域运行。该公司希望使应用程序在两个区域都具备高可 用性。用户流量必须被路由到延迟最小的区域。 哪种步骤组合能满足这些要求？（选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Create a replica of the DynamoDB table in a second Region.","B":"Create a global secondary index for the DynamoDB table.","C":"Create copies of the REST API and the Lambda functions in a second Region.","D":"Create health checks in Amazon Route 53. Create DNS records that include a failover routing policy.","E":"Create health checks in Amazon Route 53. Create DNS records that include a latency routing policy.","F":"Create DNS records in Amazon Route 53 that include a multivalue answer routing policy."},"options_zh":{"A":"在第二个区域创建 DynamoDB 表的副本。","B":"为 DynamoDB 表创建一个全局二级索引。","C":"在第二个区域创建 REST API 和 Lambda 函数的副本。","D":"在 Amazon Route 53 中创建健康检查。创建包含故障转移路由策略的 DNS 记录。","E":"在 Amazon Route 53 中创建健康检查。创建包含延迟路由策略的 DNS 记录。","F":"在 Amazon Route 53 中创建包含多值答案路由策略的 DNS 记录。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"both","explanation_en":"The requirement is a two-Region, highly available, active-active application where user traffic is routed to the Region with the LOWEST latency. (A) Replicating the DynamoDB table to a second Region with global tables creates a multi-active, multi-Region data tier where any replica can serve reads and writes, delivering the required high availability and a local data store in each Region. (C) Creating copies of the REST API and Lambda functions in the second Region provides the independent compute/API stack each Region needs to serve requests on its own. (E) The Route 53 latency routing policy is defined precisely for the case where you have resources in multiple AWS Regions and want to route traffic to the Region that provides the best (lowest) latency; adding Route 53 health checks ensures traffic is only sent to healthy endpoints, providing the failover/high-availability behavior. Together, A+C+E deliver both least-latency routing and high availability across two Regions.","explanation_zh":"需求是跨兩個 Region 的高可用、主動-主動應用程式，並將使用者流量導向延遲最低的 Region。(A) 以 DynamoDB global tables 將資料表複寫到第二個 Region，建立多主動、多 Region 的資料層，任一 replica 皆可讀寫，提供所需的高可用性與每個 Region 的本地資料存放區。(C) 在第二個 Region 建立 REST API 與 Lambda functions 的副本，提供每個 Region 各自獨立的運算/API 堆疊以獨立處理請求。(E) Route 53 latency routing policy 正是為「在多個 AWS Region 擁有資源並希望將流量導向延遲最佳（最低）Region」的情境而設計；再加上 Route 53 health checks 可確保流量只送往健康的端點，提供 failover/高可用性行為。A+C+E 同時達成最低延遲路由與跨兩個 Region 的高可用性。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A global secondary index provides an alternate query key schema within a single table/Region; it does nothing for cross-Region replication, high availability, or latency-based routing, so it is irrelevant to a multi-Region resilience requirement.","why_zh":"global secondary index 僅在單一資料表/Region 內提供替代查詢鍵結構，對跨 Region 複寫、高可用或延遲路由毫無幫助，與多 Region 韌性需求無關。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"The failover routing policy implements active-passive failover, sending all traffic to a primary endpoint and only switching to the secondary on failure. It does NOT consider latency and cannot route users to the lowest-latency Region, which is the explicit requirement; latency routing (E) is the correct policy.","why_zh":"failover routing policy 實作主動-被動 failover，所有流量先送主要端點，僅在故障時切換到次要端點；它不考量延遲，無法將使用者導向延遲最低的 Region（題目明確要求），正確策略是 latency routing（E）。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"The multivalue answer routing policy returns up to eight healthy records selected at random; it improves availability but selects records randomly rather than by lowest latency, so it fails the least-latency requirement.","why_zh":"multivalue answer routing policy 隨機回傳最多八筆健康記錄，雖可提升可用性，但為隨機選取而非依最低延遲挑選，因此不符合最低延遲需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-latency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/GlobalTables.html"]}},{"id":388,"question_en":"A company has a web application that is hosted on Amazon EC2 instances. The company is deploying the application into multiple AWS Regions. The application consists of dynamic content such as WebSocket-based real-time product updates. The company uses Amazon Route 53 to manage all DNS records. Which solution will provide multi-Region access to the application with the LEAST latency?","question_zh":"一家公司有一个托管在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的网络应用程序。该公司正在将该应用程序部署到多个 AWS 区域。 该应用程序包含诸如基于 WebSocket 的实时产品更新之类的动态内容。该公司使用亚马逊 Route 53 来管理所有 DNS 记录。 哪种解决方案能以最低的延迟为应用程序提供多区域访问？","options_en":{"A":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of the EC2 instances in each Region. Create a Route 53 A record with a latency-based routing policy. Add IP addresses of the ALBs as the value of the record.","B":"Deploy an Application Load Balancer (ALB) in front of the EC2 instances in each Region. Deploy an Amazon CloudFront distribution with an origin group that contains the ALBs as origins. Create a Route 53 alias record that points to the CloudFront distribution's DNS address.","C":"Deploy a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in front of the EC2 instances in each Region. Create a Route 53 A record with a multivalue answer routing policy. Add IP addresses of the NLBs as the value of the record.","D":"Deploy a Network Load Balancer (NLB) in front of the EC2 instances in each Region. Deploy an AWS Global Accelerator standard accelerator with an endpoint group for each NLB. Create a Route 53 alias record that points to the accelerator's DNS address."},"options_zh":{"A":"在每个区域的 EC2 实例前部署一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。创建一个具有基于延迟的路由策略的 Route 53 A 记录。将 ALB 的 IP 地址作为该记录的值。","B":"在每个区域的 EC2 实例前部署一个应用负载均衡器（ALB）。部署一个 Amazon CloudFront 分发，其 源组包含这些 ALB 作为源。创建一个指向 CloudFront 分发的 DNS 地址的 Route 53 别名记录。","C":"在每个区域的 EC2 实例前部署网络负载均衡器（NLB）。创建一个具有多值响应路由策略的 Route 53 A 记录。将 NLB 的 IP 地址作为该记录的值添加进去。","D":"在每个区域的 EC2 实例前部署网络负载均衡器（NLB）。为每个 NLB 部署一个 AWS 全球加速器标 准加速器及一个端点组。创建一个指向加速器 DNS 地址的 Route 53 别名记录。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Compute"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The application serves dynamic, WebSocket-based real-time traffic that must reach the nearest Region with the lowest latency. An AWS Global Accelerator standard accelerator gives you static anycast IPs that ingest client traffic at the nearest AWS edge location and route it over the congestion-free AWS global network to the optimal, nearest healthy Regional endpoint. The AWS docs explicitly state that a standard accelerator 'directs traffic over the AWS global network to endpoints in the nearest Region to the client' and routes to 'the optimal regional endpoint based on health, client location, and policies.' Global Accelerator supports TCP/WebSocket traffic and NLB endpoints, and you point a Route 53 alias record at the accelerator's DNS name. Option D is therefore the lowest-latency multi-Region design. The dump-suggested answer A is technically invalid because ALBs do not have static IP addresses, so you cannot place ALB IPs in a Route 53 A record; AWS requires an alias record (not a hard-coded A record) to route to any ELB.","explanation_zh":"此應用程式提供動態、以 WebSocket 為基礎的即時流量，必須以最低延遲送達最近的 Region。AWS Global Accelerator standard accelerator 提供靜態 anycast IP，將用戶端流量在最近的 AWS edge location 接收，並透過無壅塞的 AWS 全球網路路由到最佳、最近的健康 Regional endpoint。AWS 文件明確指出 standard accelerator 會『將流量透過 AWS 全球網路導向最接近用戶端的 Region 內的 endpoint』，並依『健康狀態、用戶端位置與您設定的政策』路由到最佳 regional endpoint。Global Accelerator 支援 TCP/WebSocket 流量與 NLB endpoint，並可用 Route 53 alias record 指向 accelerator 的 DNS 名稱。因此 D 是延遲最低的多 Region 設計。題庫建議答案 A 在技術上無效，因為 ALB 沒有靜態 IP，無法將 ALB 的 IP 放進 Route 53 A record；AWS 要求使用 alias record（而非寫死的 A record）才能路由到任何 ELB。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"ALBs do not have static IP addresses, so you cannot 'add IP addresses of the ALBs as the value' of an A record. AWS requires a Route 53 alias record (not a hard-coded A record) to route to an ELB. Even if it worked, latency-based routing resolves at DNS and then traverses the public internet to the origin, so it cannot match the latency of Global Accelerator routing over the AWS global network.","why_zh":"ALB 沒有靜態 IP，因此無法『把 ALB 的 IP 當作 A record 的值』。AWS 要求使用 Route 53 alias record（而非寫死的 A record）才能路由到 ELB。即使可行，latency-based routing 只在 DNS 層解析，之後仍走公網到來源，無法達到 Global Accelerator 透過 AWS 全球網路的低延遲。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"A CloudFront origin group provides active-passive origin failover: CloudFront always sends requests to the fixed primary origin and only uses the secondary on failure (and only for GET/HEAD/OPTIONS). It is not latency-based multi-Region routing to the viewer's nearest Region, so all dynamic/WebSocket traffic is pinned to one Region regardless of client location and latency is not minimized.","why_zh":"CloudFront origin group 提供的是 active-passive 來源故障轉移：CloudFront 一律將請求送到固定的 primary origin，只有在失敗時才使用 secondary（且僅限 GET/HEAD/OPTIONS）。這並非依觀看者最近 Region 的延遲式多 Region 路由，因此所有動態/WebSocket 流量都被固定在單一 Region，無法將延遲最小化。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Multivalue answer routing returns up to eight random healthy records and lets the client pick one; it provides availability and simple distribution, not routing to the lowest-latency or nearest Region. It is not latency-aware, so it fails the LEAST-latency requirement even though NLBs do have static IPs that can be used in an A record.","why_zh":"Multivalue answer routing 會回傳最多八筆隨機的健康紀錄並由用戶端自行選擇，提供的是可用性與簡單的流量分散，而非導向延遲最低或最近的 Region。它不感知延遲，因此即使 NLB 具備可用於 A record 的靜態 IP，仍無法滿足最低延遲的需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/what-is-global-accelerator.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/global-accelerator/latest/dg/introduction-how-it-works.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-to-elb-load-balancer.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudFront/latest/DeveloperGuide/high_availability_origin_failover.html"]}},{"id":389,"question_en":"A company manages its multi-account environment by using AWS Organizations and AWS Control Tower. The company must deploy standardized security controls and compliance policies across all of its AWS accounts and AWS Regions. Any changes to these controls must be automatically applied to all accounts simultaneously. The company has the required security controls and compliance policies defined in AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) as a security controls construct. Which solution will deploy these controls across all accounts and Regions with the LEAST operational overhead?","question_zh":"该公司通过使用 AWS 组织和 AWS 控制塔来管理其多账户环境。该公司必须在其所有的 AWS 账户和 AWS 区域中部署标准化的安全控制措施和合规性策略。对这些控制措施所做的任何更改都必须同时自 动应用于所有账户。 该公司已在 AWS 云开发工具包（AWS CDK）中定义了所需的安全部署和合规策略，作为 安全控制结构的一部分。 哪种解决方案能在所有账户和地区部署这些控制措施，且操作开销最小？","options_en":{"A":"Create an AWS CDK app that includes an AWS CloudFormation StackSets construct. Configure the StackSets construct to use the security controls construct as its template. Specify the target accounts and Regions. Create automation to deploy the CDK app to create and manage the CloudFormation stack set.","B":"Create an AWS CDK app that synthesizes an AWS CloudFormation template from the security controls construct. Use Amazon EventBridge to invoke an AWS Lambda function to update a CloudFormation stack set when changes are made to the security controls construct.","C":"Convert the security controls construct to an AWS CloudFormation macro. Create a CloudFormation stack set that references the macro and deploys the macro to all target accounts. Use Organizations to automatically add new accounts to the stack set’s list of target accounts.","D":"Use AWS Control Tower to create a customized landing zone that includes configurations from the security controls construct. Configure AWS Control Tower to automatically enroll new accounts and to apply the landing zone template."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个包含 AWS CloudFormation StackSets 构造的 AWS CDK 应用程序。将 StackSets 构造配置 为使用安全控制构造作为其模板。指定目标账户和区域。创建自动化流程以部署 CDK 应用程序 来创建和管理 CloudFormation 堆栈集。","B":"创建一个 AWS CDK 应用程序，该程序从安全控制构造中合成一个 AWS CloudFormation 模板。使用 Amazon EventBridge 调用一个 AWS Lambda 函数，在对安全控制构造进行更改时更新 CloudFormation 堆栈集。","C":"将安全控制结构转换为 AWS CloudFormation 宏。创建一个引用该宏的 CloudFormation 堆栈集，并 将该宏部署到所有目标账户。使用 Organizations 自动将新账户添加到堆栈集的目标账户列表中。","D":"使用 AWS Control Tower 创建一个包含安全控制结构配置的自定义着陆区。配置 AWS Control Tower 以自动注册新账户并应用着陆区模板。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Compute","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The controls are already authored in CDK as a security controls construct, so the lowest-overhead path is to keep everything in CDK and let a CloudFormation StackSet handle the cross-account/cross-Region distribution. AWS CDK provides a first-class CfnStackSet construct (with an AutoDeploymentProperty), so you can synthesize the security controls construct into the StackSet template, target the organization's accounts and Regions, and use service-managed permissions. Service-managed StackSets natively support automatic deployment to accounts that are added to the organization in the future, and the docs state that when you update a StackSet 'all associated stack instances update throughout all accounts and Regions' - satisfying both 'changes automatically applied to all accounts simultaneously' and auto-onboarding of new accounts without custom glue. Option A relies entirely on native CDK + StackSets capabilities, which is the least operational overhead; the other options add bespoke automation, use a technically unsupported mechanism, or misrepresent what Control Tower can do.","explanation_zh":"這些安全控制已經以 CDK 的 security controls construct 形式撰寫，因此維運負擔最低的做法是讓一切留在 CDK 中，並由 CloudFormation StackSet 負責跨帳號、跨區域的部署。AWS CDK 提供原生的 CfnStackSet construct（含 AutoDeploymentProperty），可將 security controls construct 合成為 StackSet 範本，鎖定組織的帳號與區域，並使用 service-managed permissions。Service-managed StackSets 原生支援對日後新加入組織的帳號自動部署；文件並指出更新 StackSet 時『所有相關的 stack instances 會在所有帳號與區域中一併更新』，正好同時滿足『變更自動同時套用到所有帳號』與新帳號自動納管，且無需自訂膠合程式。選項 A 完全仰賴 CDK 與 StackSets 的原生能力，維運負擔最低；其餘選項不是加入額外自訂自動化，就是使用技術上不支援的機制，或誤述 Control Tower 的能力。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Building an EventBridge rule plus a Lambda function to update the stack set when the construct changes is unnecessary custom plumbing. The CDK app can define and manage the StackSet natively (Option A), and 'changes to the construct' (source code) is not even a native EventBridge event source. The event-driven Lambda glue adds operational overhead you must build, secure, and maintain rather than reducing it.","why_zh":"建立 EventBridge 規則加 Lambda 函式在 construct 變更時更新 stack set 是多餘的自訂機制。CDK app 可原生定義並管理 StackSet（選項 A），且『construct 的變更』（原始碼）本身也不是 EventBridge 的原生事件來源。這套事件驅動的 Lambda 膠合反而增加你必須自建、保護與維護的維運負擔，而非降低。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Converting the construct to a CloudFormation macro is both inappropriate and unsupported here. The CloudFormation docs explicitly state StackSets does not support creating or updating stack sets with service-managed permissions from templates that reference macros, so the organization-wide auto-deployment and auto-onboarding of new accounts simply cannot work. A macro is a template transform (Lambda), not a deployment mechanism for security controls, making this technically broken.","why_zh":"將 construct 轉成 CloudFormation macro 既不合適也不被支援。CloudFormation 文件明確指出 StackSets 不支援從引用 macro 的範本建立或更新使用 service-managed permissions 的 stack sets，因此組織層級的自動部署與新帳號自動納管根本無法運作。此外 macro 是範本轉換（Lambda），並非安全控制的部署機制，技術上行不通。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS Control Tower's managed landing zone does not consume an arbitrary CDK security controls construct as a 'landing zone template'. Console customization is limited (Regions, optional controls, Region Deny, Security Hub), and broader infrastructure-as-code customization requires the separate Customizations for AWS Control Tower (CfCT) framework, not embedding a CDK construct in the landing zone. This misrepresents Control Tower's capability and adds overhead.","why_zh":"AWS Control Tower 的受管 landing zone 不會將任意 CDK security controls construct 當成『landing zone 範本』使用。主控台的客製化有限（區域、選用控制、Region Deny、Security Hub），更廣泛的基礎設施即程式碼客製化需另外使用 Customizations for AWS Control Tower（CfCT）框架，而非把 CDK construct 嵌進 landing zone。此選項誤述了 Control Tower 的能力並增加負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/stacksets-orgs-manage-auto-deployment.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cdk/api/v2/docs/aws-cdk-lib.aws_cloudformation.CfnStackSet.AutoDeploymentProperty.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSCloudFormation/latest/UserGuide/template-macros-overview.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/controltower/latest/userguide/customize-landing-zone.html"]}},{"id":390,"question_en":"A company needs to manage shared libraries for various projects across its development AWS account and production AWS account. The company has configured IAM roles for developers and has defined an AWS CodePipeline pipeline by using the AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK). A DevOps engineer must implement a solution to ensure that only developers can access the latest versions of the libraries. The solution must test shared packages independently before the shared packages are consumed by other applications and before they go to production. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司需要在其开发 AWS 账户和生产 AWS 账户之间管理多个项目的共享库。该公司已为开发人 员配置了 IAM 角色，并使用 AWS 云开发工具包（AWS CDK）定义了一个 AWS CodePipeline 管道。 DevOps 工程师必须实施一项解决方案，以确保只有开发人员能够访问库的最新版本。该解决方 案必须在其他应用程序使用这些共享包以及这些包投入生产之前，对共享包进行独立测试。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a single AWS CodeArtifact repository for development and production in a central account. Use IAM policies for the developer roles to allow only developers to access the shared libraries. Create an Amazon EventBridge role to start an AWS CodeBuild project and to test each package before the package is copied to the production repository.","B":"Create an AWS CodeArtifact repository in the development account. Create another CodeArtifact repository in the production account. For the development repository, add a repository policy that allows only developers to access the shared libraries. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to start the CodePipeline pipeline and to test each package before the package is copied to the production repository.","C":"Create a single Amazon S3 bucket with versioning enabled for development and production in a central account. Use IAM policies for the developer roles to allow only the developers to access the shared libraries. Create an Amazon EventBridge rule to start an AWS CodeBuild project and to test each package before the package is copied to production.","D":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket with versioning enabled in the development account. Create another S3 bucket with versioning enabled in the production account. For the development S3 bucket, add a bucket policy that allows only developers to access the shared libraries. Create an Amazon EventBridge role to start the CodePipeline pipeline. Configure the role to test each package when the package is copied to production and to revert the changes if the tests fail."},"options_zh":{"A":"在中央账户中为开发和生产创建一个单一的 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。使用 IAM 策略为开发人员 角色设置权限，仅允许开发人员访问共享库。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 角色，用于启动 AWS CodeBuild 项目，并在将每个软件包复制到生产存储库之前对其进行测试。","B":"在开发账户中创建一个 AWS CodeArtifact 存储库。在生产账户中创建另一个 CodeArtifact 存储库。 对于开发存储库，添加一个存储库策略，仅允许开发人员访问共享库。创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，以启动 CodePipeline 管道，并在将软件包复制到生产存储库之前对每个软件包 进行测试。","C":"在一个中央账户中创建一个启用版本控制功能的单一 Amazon S3 存储桶，用于开发和生产环境。使 用 IAM 策略为开发人员角色授权，仅允许开发人员访问共享的存储桶。 创建一个 Amazon EventBridge 规则，在将每个软件包复制到生产环境之前启动 AWS CodeBuild 项目并对其进行测试。","D":"在开发账户中创建一个启用了版本控制的 Amazon S3 存储桶。在生产账户中创建另一个启用了版本 控制的 S3 存储桶。对于开发 S3 存储桶，添加一个仅允许开发人员访问共享库的存储桶策略。创建 一个 Amazon EventBridge 角色以启动 CodePipeline 管道。配置该角色，以便在将软件包复制到生产 环境时对其进行测试，并在测试失败时回滚更改。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Storage","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is to manage versioned, shared software libraries (packages) for npm/Maven/pip-style projects, restrict access to developers, and test each package independently before it is promoted to production. AWS CodeArtifact is the purpose-built managed artifact repository for exactly this: it stores and shares versioned private packages and integrates with package managers, so it can expose the latest versions of libraries (Amazon S3 is plain object storage with no package/version semantics or package-manager integration, ruling out C and D). Option B creates a development repository in the development account and a separate production repository in the production account, applies a repository (resource-based) policy on the dev repo so that only developers can access the shared libraries, and uses an EventBridge rule to start the existing CDK-defined CodePipeline pipeline to test each package before it is copied into the production repository. This matches documented CodeArtifact behavior: repository policies use resource-based permissions to control who has access to a repository, and CodeArtifact emits a 'CodeArtifact Package Version State Change' EventBridge event on publish that can directly start a CodePipeline execution, enabling test-then-promote. Two separate repositories enforce the independent-test-before-production gate, and reusing the existing CodePipeline (rather than spinning up a separate CodeBuild project) fits the stated environment.","explanation_zh":"需求是管理具版本控制、可共享的軟體函式庫（套件，類似 npm/Maven/pip），限制只有開發人員可存取，並在套件升級到生產環境前先獨立測試。AWS CodeArtifact 正是為此設計的受管 artifact repository：它儲存與共享有版本的私有套件、整合各種 package manager，因此能提供函式庫的最新版本（Amazon S3 僅為物件儲存，沒有套件/版本語意，也不整合 package manager，因此排除 C 與 D）。選項 B 在開發帳戶建立開發 repository、在生產帳戶建立另一個生產 repository，於開發 repository 套用 repository policy（resource-based policy）使只有開發人員能存取共享函式庫，並以 EventBridge rule 觸發既有以 CDK 定義的 CodePipeline，在套件被複製到生產 repository 之前先測試每個套件。這符合文件描述：repository policy 以 resource-based 權限控制誰能存取 repository，且 CodeArtifact 在發佈套件時會發出 'CodeArtifact Package Version State Change' EventBridge 事件，可直接啟動 CodePipeline 執行，實現先測試後升級。使用兩個分離的 repository 落實了進入生產前的獨立測試關卡，並沿用既有的 CodePipeline（而非另起一個 CodeBuild 專案）符合題目所述的環境。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A single shared dev/prod repository defeats the requirement to test packages independently before they go to production, because there is no separation to promote between. It also relies on IAM identity-based policies for the developer roles rather than the repository (resource-based) policy that CodeArtifact uses to control repository access, and it spins up a separate CodeBuild project via EventBridge instead of reusing the existing CDK-defined CodePipeline.","why_zh":"單一同時用於開發與生產的 repository 無法滿足在進入生產前獨立測試的需求，因為沒有可供升級的分隔。它還依賴開發人員角色的 IAM 身分原則，而非 CodeArtifact 用來控制 repository 存取的 repository（resource-based）policy，並以 EventBridge 另起一個 CodeBuild 專案，而非沿用既有以 CDK 定義的 CodePipeline。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Amazon S3 is plain object storage with no package or version-resolution semantics and no package-manager integration, so it cannot serve npm/Maven/pip-style shared libraries or expose the latest versions the way a package repository does. A single bucket for both dev and prod also fails the independent-test-before-production separation.","why_zh":"Amazon S3 只是物件儲存，沒有套件或版本解析語意，也不整合 package manager，無法像套件儲存庫那樣提供 npm/Maven/pip 類共享函式庫或最新版本。單一桶同時供開發與生產也無法滿足進入生產前的獨立測試分隔。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Even with two versioned buckets, Amazon S3 still lacks package/version semantics and package-manager integration, so it is the wrong store for shared libraries. The option is also incoherent: it describes an 'EventBridge role' (not a rule) that tests packages only when they are copied to production and reverts on failure, which is not the independent test-before-promotion gate the requirement demands, and the described revert behavior is not a native S3/EventBridge capability.","why_zh":"即使使用兩個啟用版本控制的桶，Amazon S3 仍缺乏套件/版本語意與 package manager 整合，因此不適合作為共享函式庫的儲存。此選項描述也不一致：它提到一個 'EventBridge role'（而非 rule），只在套件被複製到生產時才測試並在失敗時還原，這並非需求所要求的進入生產前獨立測試關卡，且所述的還原行為也不是 S3/EventBridge 原生能力。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/repo-policies.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/configure-service-events-codepipeline.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/monitoring-events.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/copy-package.html"]}},{"id":391,"question_en":"A company manages environments for its application in multiple AWS accounts. Each environment account is in a different OU in AWS Organizations. A DevOps team is responsible for the application deployment process across the environments. The deployment process uses an AWS CodePipeline pipeline in a Shared Services account. The DevOps team members are in the same user group. The team members have administrative access to all accounts through AWS IAM Identity Center. A recent deployment problem in the development environment required the DevOps team to perform manual steps. The deployment to the production environment then resulted in an incident that caused the pipeline to fail, which blocked new deployments for several hours. A DevOps engineer needs to ensure that only the pipeline can perform deployments in the production environment. The DevOps engineer must have access to the environment in case of an emergency. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司在多个 AWS 账户中为其应用程序管理环境。每个环境账户都在 AWS 组织中的不同组织 单元（OU）中。 DevOps 团队负责跨环境的应用程序部署流程。部署流程使用共享服务账户中的 AWS CodePipeline 管道。 DevOps 团队成员处于同一用户组。团队成员通过 AWS IAM 身份中心对所有账户拥有管理权限。 最近开发环境出现了一个部署问题，导致 DevOps 团队不得不执行手动操作。随后在生产环境的部署又 引发了一起事故，致使流水线中断，新部署也因此停滞了数小时。 DevOps 工程师需要确保只有流水线能够在生产环境中执行部署操作。在紧急情况下，DevOps 工程 师必须能够访问该环境。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Update the DevOps group to have the ReadOnlyAccess permission set for the production accounts. Configure the DevOps engineer user with a new permission set that has AdministratorAccess permissions and that allows the user to assume the pipeline role. Add an SCP that denies modification of resources by any entity other than the pipeline role.","B":"Create an SCP that denies all write actions for the DevOps team members on the production OU. Configure a new user in IAM Identity Center for the DevOps engineer with a new permission set that has AdministratorAccess permissions. Add an SCP that denies modification of resources by any entity other than the pipeline role.","C":"Update the DevOps group to be able to assume the pipeline role for the production accounts. Configure a new user in IAM Identity Center for the DevOps engineer with a new permission set that has AdministratorAccess permissions. Add an SCP that denies modification of resources by any entity other than the DevOps engineer.","D":"Create an SCP that denies all write actions for the DevOps team members on the production OU. Use a specific tag to tag the resources that CodePipeline provisions. Add an SCP that denies modification of tagged resources by any entity other than the DevOps engineer."},"options_zh":{"A":"将开发运维团队的权限集更新为对生产账户具有只读访问权限。为开发运维工程师用户配置一个新的 权限集，该权限集具有管理员访问权限，并允许该用户承担管道角色。添加一个服务控制策略 （SCP），禁止除管道角色之外的任何实体修改资源。","B":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止开发运维团队成员对生产组织单位（OU）执行所有写入操作。 在 IAM 身份中心为开发运维工程师配置一个新用户，并为其分配一个具有管理员访问权限的新权限 集。添加一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止除管道角色之外的任何实体修改资源。","C":"更新 DevOps 团队，使其能够承担生产账户的管道角色。在 IAM 身份中心为 DevOps 工程师配置一个 新用户，并为其分配一个具有管理员访问权限的新权限集。添加一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止 除 DevOps 工程师之外的任何实体修改资源。","D":"创建一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止 DevOps 团队成员对生产组织单位（OU）执行所有写入操作。 使用特定标签标记 CodePipeline 部署的资源。添加一个服务控制策略（SCP），禁止除 DevOps 工程 师以外的任何实体修改已标记的资源。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirement is that ONLY the pipeline role can deploy to production while the DevOps engineer keeps an emergency (break-glass) path, with the MOST operational efficiency. The decisive guardrail is an SCP that denies modification of resources by any entity other than the pipeline role (a Deny on write actions with a condition such as aws:PrincipalArn ArnNotLike <pipeline-role-arn>). Because an SCP is a permission boundary that affects every IAM user and role in the member accounts and never grants permission, this guardrail blocks every principal in the production accounts except the pipeline role. Option A is the only choice whose emergency path is logically consistent with that SCP: the DevOps engineer's new permission set has AdministratorAccess AND lets the user assume the pipeline role, so in an emergency the engineer operates AS the pipeline role and the SCP exclusion permits the action. The rest of the DevOps group is reduced to ReadOnlyAccess, which prevents the manual-intervention problem from recurring, and everything reuses existing IAM Identity Center permission-set and SCP constructs, satisfying operational efficiency.","explanation_zh":"需求是只有 pipeline role 能部署到 production，同時 DevOps engineer 仍保有緊急（break-glass）存取路徑，並且要最具營運效率。決定性的防護欄是一條 SCP，拒絕除 pipeline role 以外任何主體修改資源（對寫入動作的 Deny，搭配 aws:PrincipalArn ArnNotLike <pipeline-role-arn> 之類的條件）。由於 SCP 是權限邊界、影響成員帳戶中所有 IAM user 與 role 且本身從不授權，此防護欄會封鎖 production 帳戶中除 pipeline role 以外的所有主體。選項 A 是唯一其緊急路徑與該 SCP 邏輯一致的方案：DevOps engineer 的新 permission set 不只有 AdministratorAccess，還允許該使用者 assume pipeline role，因此緊急時工程師以 pipeline role 身分操作，SCP 的排除條件即放行該動作。DevOps group 其餘成員則降為 ReadOnlyAccess，避免再次發生人為手動介入的問題，且全部沿用既有的 IAM Identity Center permission set 與 SCP 構件，符合營運效率。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"The engineer's new permission set only has AdministratorAccess; it does NOT let the engineer assume the pipeline role. The same SCP that denies modification by any entity other than the pipeline role would therefore ALSO block the engineer's emergency AdministratorAccess (the engineer's principal ARN is not the pipeline role), so the engineer has no real emergency write access. It also stacks a redundant first SCP (deny write for team members on the production OU) on top of the second SCP, which is less efficient than A.","why_zh":"工程師的新 permission set 只有 AdministratorAccess，並未允許其 assume pipeline role。那條拒絕除 pipeline role 以外任何主體修改的 SCP 也會一併封鎖工程師的緊急 AdministratorAccess（工程師的 principal ARN 並非 pipeline role），工程師等於沒有真正的緊急寫入存取。此外它在第二條 SCP 之上又疊一條多餘的第一條 SCP（對團隊成員在 production OU 拒絕寫入），效率不如 A。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The SCP denies modification by any entity other than the DevOps engineer, which makes the ENGINEER (not the pipeline) the privileged deployer and, worse, would block the pipeline role itself from deploying. This directly violates the core requirement that only the pipeline can perform deployments.","why_zh":"該 SCP 拒絕除 DevOps engineer 以外任何主體修改，等於讓工程師（而非 pipeline）成為特權部署者，更糟的是會封鎖 pipeline role 本身的部署。這直接違反了只有 pipeline 能執行部署的核心需求。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Tag-based control that denies modification of tagged resources by anyone except the DevOps engineer again makes the engineer the privileged actor rather than restricting deployment to the pipeline, and does not guarantee pipeline-only deployments. Tag-based guardrails are fragile (untagged resources are unprotected, tags can be altered) and add operational overhead, so it is the least operationally efficient and fails the requirement.","why_zh":"以標籤為基礎、拒絕除 DevOps engineer 以外任何主體修改有標籤資源的做法，同樣讓工程師成為特權主體，而非將部署限制於 pipeline，也無法保證只有 pipeline 部署。標籤式防護欄脆弱（未標記資源不受保護、標籤可被竄改）且增加營運負擔，因此營運效率最低且不符需求。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/organizations/latest/userguide/orgs_manage_policies_scps_examples.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/IAM/latest/UserGuide/reference_policies_elements_principal.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/singlesignon/latest/userguide/emergency-access-planning.html"]}},{"id":392,"question_en":"A company builds container images and stores them on Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) in the company's primary AWS Region. A DevOps engineer wants to replicate all the company's ECR repository images to a secondary Region. The DevOps engineer creates a new ECR repository in the secondary Region and configures permission on the new repository to allow replication. Which solution will meet these requirements with the MOST operational efficiency?","question_zh":"一家公司构建容器镜像，并将其存储在公司主要 AWS 区域的亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）中。 一位 DevOps 工程师想要将公司所有的 ECR 仓库镜像复制到一个备用区域。该 DevOps 工程师在备用 区域创建了一个新的 ECR 仓库，并在新仓库上配置了权限以允许复制。 哪种解决方案能在运营效率方面最符合这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Pull the existing primary ECR images and then push the images to the secondary ECR repository. Create a replication rule on the primary ECR registry to replicate the images to the secondary ECR registry.","B":"Pull the existing primary ECR images and then push the images to the secondary ECR repository. Configure permission on the primary ECR registry to allow access from the secondary Region.","C":"Configure permission on the primary ECR registry to allow access from the secondary Region. Create a replication rule on the primary ECR registry to replicate the images to the secondary ECR registry.","D":"Configure an AWS Lambda function to automatically save the ECR images to an Amazon S3 bucket. Configure cross-Region replication for the S3 bucket. Configure a second Lambda function to push the images to ECR repositories in the replication destination Region when images are replicated to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"拉取现有的主 ECR 镜像，然后将这些镜像推送到辅助 ECR 存储库。在主 ECR 注册表上创建一 个复制规则，将镜像复制到辅助 ECR 注册表。","B":"拉取现有的主 ECR 镜像，然后将这些镜像推送到辅助 ECR 仓库。在主 ECR 注册表上配置权限， 以允许从辅助区域访问。","C":"在主 ECR 注册表上配置权限，允许从辅助区域访问。在主 ECR 注册表上创建复制规则，将镜像复 制到辅助 ECR 注册表。","D":"配置一个 AWS Lambda 函数，以自动将 ECR 镜像保存到 Amazon S3 存储桶。为该 S3 存储桶配置跨 区域复制。配置第二个 Lambda 函数，在镜像复制到 S3 存储桶时将镜像推送到复制目标区域的 ECR 仓库。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The scenario has images that ALREADY exist in the primary Region and asks to replicate ALL of them to a secondary Region with the most operational efficiency. The decisive Amazon ECR replication rule is documented explicitly: 'Only repository content pushed or restored to a repository after replication is configured is replicated. Any preexisting content in a repository isn't replicated.' Therefore a replication rule alone cannot move the existing images. Option A is the correct, most operationally efficient native solution: pull the existing primary images and push them to the secondary repository (the only supported way to move preexisting content), AND create a replication rule on the primary registry so every future push is automatically replicated. This covers both existing and future images using built-in ECR features with no custom code. Option C (the dump's suggested answer) only creates the replication rule and would silently skip all preexisting images, so it fails the 'replicate ALL images' requirement.","explanation_zh":"情境中映像『已經存在』於主要 Region，且要求以最高營運效率把『所有』映像複寫到次要 Region。決定性的 Amazon ECR replication 規則在文件中明確記載：『只有在設定 replication 之後才 push 或 restore 到 repository 的內容才會被複寫；repository 中任何既有(preexisting)內容都不會被複寫。』因此單靠 replication rule 無法搬移既有映像。Option A 是正確且最具營運效率的原生方案：先把既有的主要 Region 映像 pull 下來再 push 到次要 repository（這是搬移既有內容的唯一支援方式），同時在主要 registry 上建立 replication rule，讓之後每次 push 都自動複寫。這樣同時涵蓋既有與未來的映像，且全部使用 ECR 內建功能、無需自訂程式碼。Option C（dump 建議答案）只建立 replication rule，會默默略過所有既有映像，無法滿足『複寫所有映像』的需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Pulling and pushing handles the existing images, but with no replication rule, future image pushes are NOT automatically replicated, so the secondary Region does not stay in sync. It also misplaces the permission policy: for ECR cross-Region replication the registry permissions policy belongs on the DESTINATION registry, not the source, and same-account cross-Region replication needs no extra registry policy at all.","why_zh":"pull/push 處理了既有映像，但沒有 replication rule，未來 push 的映像不會自動複寫，次要 Region 無法持續同步。它也放錯權限政策：ECR 跨 Region 複寫需要的是目的端 registry 的權限政策(非來源端)，而同帳號跨 Region 複寫根本不需額外的 registry 政策。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"This is the dump's suggested answer, but it is wrong. A replication rule only replicates content pushed or restored AFTER the rule is configured; AWS docs state preexisting content is not replicated. Since the company already has existing images, the rule alone leaves all of them unreplicated, failing 'replicate ALL the company's images.' (The permission step is also misstated; the registry policy belongs on the destination registry.)","why_zh":"這是 dump 的建議答案，但是錯的。replication rule 只會複寫在規則設定『之後』才 push 或 restore 的內容；AWS 文件明載既有內容不會被複寫。由於公司已有既有映像，僅靠規則會讓所有既有映像未被複寫，無法達成『複寫公司的所有映像』。（權限步驟描述也不正確，registry 政策應位於目的端 registry。）"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Building a custom pipeline with two Lambda functions plus S3 cross-Region replication to extract, copy, and re-push container images is heavy, error-prone, and requires significant ongoing maintenance. ECR provides native cross-Region replication, so this custom solution has the highest operational overhead, the opposite of 'MOST operational efficiency.'","why_zh":"用兩個 Lambda 函式加上 S3 跨 Region 複寫來擷取、複製並重新 push 容器映像，屬於繁重、易出錯且需持續維護的自建方案。ECR 已提供原生跨 Region replication，因此這個自建方案營運負擔最高，與『最高營運效率』背道而馳。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/registry-settings-configure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/registry-permissions.html"]}},{"id":393,"question_en":"A company is experiencing failures in its AWS CodeDeploy deployments for a critical application. The application is deployed on Amazon EC2 instances. A DevOps engineer must analyze the failed deployments to identify the root cause of the failures. Which solution will provide the appropriate information to troubleshoot the deployment issues?","question_zh":"一家公司发现其关键应用程序在 AWS CodeDeploy 上的部署出现故障，该应用程序部署在 Amazon EC2 实例上。一位 DevOps 工程师必须分析这些失败的部署，以找出故障的根本原因。 哪种解决方案能提供适当的信息来排查部署问题？","options_en":{"A":"Configure VPC Flow Logs to monitor network traffic. Use Amazon Inspector to detect non-network deployment issues. Use Amazon Detective to analyze the findings.","B":"Enable detailed monitoring on the EC2 instances. Use AWS Systems Manager Run Command to run troubleshooting scripts on all the EC2 instances simultaneously. Analyze the results in AWS CloudTrail logs.","C":"Use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to review application logs. Analyze CodeDeploy deployment logs in the /opt/codedeploy-agent/deployment-root/ directory on the EC2 instances. Use AWS X-Ray to trace requests through the application components.","D":"Examine AWS Trusted Advisor checks for the CodeDeploy deployments. Use the AWS Health Dashboard to monitor application health. Analyze performance metrics in Amazon CloudWatch dashboards."},"options_zh":{"A":"配置 VPC 流日志以监控网络流量。使用 Amazon Inspector 检测非网络部署问题。使用 Amazon Detective 分析发现的结果。","B":"在所有 EC2 实例上启用详细监控。使用 AWS Systems Manager Run Command 同时在所有 EC2 实例 上运行故障排除脚本。在 AWS CloudTrail 日志中分析结果。","C":"使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 查看应用程序日志。分析 EC2 实例上 /opt/codedeploy-agent/deployment- root/ 目录中的 CodeDeploy 部署日志。使用 AWS X-Ray 跟踪请求在应用程序组件中的路径。","D":"检查 AWS 可信顾问针对 CodeDeploy 部署的检查结果。使用 AWS 健康控制面板来监控应用 程序的运行状况。在 Amazon CloudWatch 控制面板中分析性能指标。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"To root-cause CodeDeploy deployment failures on EC2, you review the log files the CodeDeploy agent writes during the deployment process. AWS documentation states deployment logs are stored on Amazon Linux/RHEL/Ubuntu instances at /opt/codedeploy-agent/deployment-root/deployment-logs/codedeploy-agent-deployments.log (with the agent log and per-deployment scripts.log alongside), and the EC2/On-Premises troubleshooting guide explicitly notes that 'the causes of many deployment failures can be identified by reviewing the log files created during the deployment process' and recommends using Amazon CloudWatch Logs to centrally monitor those log files instead of inspecting each instance individually. Option C captures exactly this purpose-built workflow: CloudWatch Logs for application/agent logs, the deployment logs in /opt/codedeploy-agent/deployment-root/, and X-Ray as a defensible add-on for tracing application requests. The other options propose unrelated or misapplied services (VPC Flow Logs, Inspector, Detective, Trusted Advisor, Health Dashboard, CloudTrail/Run Command) that do not surface CodeDeploy lifecycle-event hook output or deployment script errors.","explanation_zh":"要找出 EC2 上 CodeDeploy 部署失敗的根本原因，必須檢視 CodeDeploy agent 在部署過程中寫入的記錄檔。AWS 文件指出，在 Amazon Linux/RHEL/Ubuntu 執行個體上，部署記錄儲存於 /opt/codedeploy-agent/deployment-root/deployment-logs/codedeploy-agent-deployments.log（並有 agent 記錄檔與各部署的 scripts.log 一同存在），而 EC2/On-Premises 疑難排解指南明確指出「許多部署失敗的原因可透過檢視部署過程中建立的記錄檔來辨識」，並建議使用 Amazon CloudWatch Logs 集中監控這些記錄檔，而非逐一登入各執行個體檢視。選項 C 正好涵蓋此專為此用途設計的流程：以 CloudWatch Logs 檢視應用程式/agent 記錄、檢視 /opt/codedeploy-agent/deployment-root/ 中的部署記錄，並以 X-Ray 作為追蹤應用程式請求的合理輔助。其他選項提出的服務（VPC Flow Logs、Inspector、Detective、Trusted Advisor、Health Dashboard、CloudTrail/Run Command）皆無關或誤用，無法呈現 CodeDeploy 生命週期事件掛鉤輸出或部署指令碼錯誤。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"VPC Flow Logs only capture IP traffic metadata and reveal nothing about CodeDeploy lifecycle-event or script failures. Amazon Inspector is a vulnerability/CVE assessment service, not a deployment-troubleshooting tool, and Amazon Detective analyzes security findings (GuardDuty/VPC/CloudTrail), not deployment errors.","why_zh":"VPC Flow Logs 只記錄 IP 流量中繼資料，完全無法揭露 CodeDeploy 生命週期事件或指令碼失敗。Amazon Inspector 是漏洞/CVE 評估服務，並非部署疑難排解工具；Amazon Detective 分析的是安全發現（GuardDuty/VPC/CloudTrail），而非部署錯誤。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Detailed EC2 monitoring provides metrics at finer granularity, not deployment error context. Running ad-hoc Run Command scripts is reactive guesswork, and CloudTrail records API calls (who invoked CreateDeployment), not the agent's lifecycle-event/script error output that explains why a deployment failed.","why_zh":"EC2 詳細監控只提供更細粒度的指標，並非部署錯誤內容。臨時用 Run Command 執行指令碼只是被動猜測；CloudTrail 記錄的是 API 呼叫（誰呼叫了 CreateDeployment），而非說明部署為何失敗的 agent 生命週期事件/指令碼錯誤輸出。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Trusted Advisor performs cost/security/limit best-practice checks and has no CodeDeploy deployment checks. The AWS Health Dashboard reports AWS service/account events, not your deployment's failure cause, and CloudWatch performance metric dashboards do not contain CodeDeploy script/lifecycle error logs.","why_zh":"Trusted Advisor 執行成本/安全/限額等最佳實務檢查，並無 CodeDeploy 部署檢查項目。AWS Health Dashboard 回報的是 AWS 服務/帳戶事件，而非你部署的失敗原因；CloudWatch 效能指標儀表板也不包含 CodeDeploy 指令碼/生命週期錯誤記錄。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/deployments-view-logs.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/troubleshooting-deployments.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/codedeploy-agent-operations-cloudwatch-agent.html"]}},{"id":394,"question_en":"A company has developed a web application that conducts seasonal sales on public holidays. The web application is deployed on AWS and uses AWS services for storage, database, computing, and encryption. During seasonal sales, the company expects high network traffic from a large number of users. The company must receive insights regarding any unexpected behavior during the sale. A DevOps team wants to review the insights upon detecting anomalous behaviors during the sale. The DevOps team wants to receive recommended actions to resolve the anomalous behaviors. The recommendations must be provided on the provisioned infrastructure to address the issues that might occur in the future. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the LEAST operational overhead? (Choose two.)","question_zh":"一家公司开发了一个在公共假日进行季节性促销的网络应用程序。该应用程序部署在 AWS 上，并使用 AWS 的服务进行存储、数据库、计算和加密。在季节性促销期间，公司预计会有大量用户访问，从而 产生高网络流量。公司必须获取有关促销期间任何意外行为的洞察信息。 DevOps 团队希望在销售期间检测到异常行为时审查相关见解。该团队希望收到解决异常行为的建 议措施。这些建议必须在已配置的基础设施上提供，以解决未来可能出现的问题。 哪种步骤组合能在操作开销最小的情况下满足这些要求？（选择两项。）","options_en":{"A":"Enable Amazon DevOps Guru in the AWS account. Determine the coverage for DevOps Guru for all supported AWS resources in the account. Use the DevOps Guru dashboard to find the analysis, recommendations, and related metrics.","B":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Configure Amazon DevOps Guru to send notifications about important events to the company when anomalies are identified.","C":"Create an Amazon S3 bucket. Store Amazon CloudWatch logs, AWS CloudTrail data, and AWS Config data in the S3 bucket. Use Amazon Athena to generate insights on the data. Create a dashboard by using Amazon QuickSight.","D":"Configure email message reports for an Amazon QuickSight dashboard. Schedule and send the email reports to the company.","E":"Create an Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS) topic. Configure Amazon Athena to send query results about important events to the company when anomalies are identified."},"options_zh":{"A":"在 AWS 账户中启用 Amazon DevOps Guru。确定 DevOps Guru 对账户中所有受支持的 AWS 资源 的覆盖范围。使用 DevOps Guru 控制面板查找分析结果、建议及相关指标。","B":"创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。配置亚马逊 DevOps Guru，在检测到异常时向 公司发送有关重要事件的通知。","C":"创建一个 Amazon S3 存储桶。将 Amazon CloudWatch 日志、AWS CloudTrail 数据和 AWS Config 数 据存储在该 S3 存储桶中。使用 Amazon Athena 对数据进行分析。通过 Amazon QuickSight 创建一个 仪表板。","D":"为 Amazon QuickSight 控制面板配置电子邮件消息报告。安排并发送电子邮件报告给公司。","E":"创建一个亚马逊简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）主题。配置 Amazon Athena，在发现异常情况时向公司 发送有关重要事件的查询结果。"},"answer":["A","B"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The requirements map directly onto Amazon DevOps Guru, a fully managed, ML-powered operations service. DevOps Guru analyzes operational data and metrics to identify behaviors that deviate from normal operating patterns (anomalous behavior during the sale), creates reactive insights for current issues and proactive insights to avoid future problems, and presents intelligent recommendations to address current and predicted future operational issues on the provisioned infrastructure. Option A is correct: the documented setup Step 2 is 'Determine coverage for DevOps Guru,' which sets the boundary of AWS resources analyzed for anomalous behavior, and the DevOps Guru dashboard surfaces the analysis, recommendations, and related metrics for the DevOps team to review. Option B is correct: setup Step 3 is 'Identify your Amazon SNS notifications topic,' and DevOps Guru publishes notifications (for example NEW_INSIGHT and NEW_RECOMMENDATION) to an SNS topic when anomalies/insights are identified, so the team is alerted during the sale. This pairing has the LEAST operational overhead because DevOps Guru is fully managed and requires only enablement plus an SNS topic. Options C, D, and E require building and maintaining a custom analytics pipeline (S3 + Athena + QuickSight) that does not natively perform ML anomaly detection or generate remediation recommendations for future issues, so they fail the recommended-actions and least-overhead requirements.","explanation_zh":"本題需求直接對應 Amazon DevOps Guru，一個全託管、以機器學習驅動的維運服務。DevOps Guru 分析維運資料與指標，找出偏離正常模式的行為（促銷期間的異常行為），產生針對當前問題的 reactive insights 以及避免未來問題的 proactive insights，並針對已佈建的基礎設施提供智慧建議以解決當前與預測的未來維運問題。選項 A 正確：官方設定流程的 Step 2 為 'Determine coverage for DevOps Guru'，用以設定要被分析異常行為的 AWS 資源邊界；DevOps Guru 儀表板則呈現分析結果、建議與相關指標供 DevOps 團隊檢視。選項 B 正確：設定流程 Step 3 為 'Identify your Amazon SNS notifications topic'，當偵測到異常或 insight 時，DevOps Guru 會發佈通知（例如 NEW_INSIGHT、NEW_RECOMMENDATION）到 SNS topic，使團隊在促銷期間獲得告警。此組合維運負擔最低，因為 DevOps Guru 為全託管，僅需啟用並建立 SNS topic。選項 C、D、E 需要建置並維護自訂分析管線（S3 + Athena + QuickSight），本質上無法執行 ML 異常偵測或針對未來問題產生修復建議，因此不符合『建議行動』與『最低維運負擔』的要求。","distractors":[{"letter":"C","why_en":"Building an S3 data store fed by CloudWatch Logs, CloudTrail, and AWS Config, queried with Athena and visualized in QuickSight, is a heavy custom analytics pipeline. It can show dashboards but does NOT use ML to detect anomalies nor generate recommended remediation actions for future issues, and it has far higher operational overhead than the managed DevOps Guru.","why_zh":"建置由 CloudWatch Logs、CloudTrail 與 AWS Config 餵入資料的 S3 儲存，再用 Athena 查詢、QuickSight 視覺化，是沉重的客製化分析管線。它能呈現儀表板，但不會用機器學習偵測異常，也不會針對未來問題產生建議的修復動作，且營運負擔遠高於託管的 DevOps Guru。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Scheduling emailed QuickSight dashboard reports only delivers periodic static snapshots; it is not anomaly-triggered and provides no ML insights, no real-time anomaly notifications, and no recommended remediation actions. It also depends on the high-overhead pipeline in C.","why_zh":"排程寄送 QuickSight 儀表板的 email 報表只能定期提供靜態快照；並非由異常觸發，也不提供 ML insight、即時異常通知或建議的修復動作，且還依賴選項 C 那條高負擔的管線。"},{"letter":"E","why_en":"Amazon Athena is an interactive SQL query service; it cannot autonomously detect anomalies and push results to SNS. There is no native mechanism for Athena to send query results to SNS upon anomaly detection, so this does not meet the detection/notification requirement and would require extra custom orchestration that increases overhead.","why_zh":"Amazon Athena 是互動式 SQL 查詢服務，無法自主偵測異常並將結果推送到 SNS。Athena 並沒有在偵測到異常時將查詢結果發送到 SNS 的原生機制，因此無法滿足偵測/通知需求，還需額外的客製化協調，反而增加負擔。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/devops-guru/latest/userguide/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/devops-guru/latest/userguide/setting-up.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/devops-guru/latest/userguide/notification-types.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/devops-guru/latest/userguide/concepts.html"]}},{"id":395,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer needs to design a cloud-based solution to standardize deployment artifacts for AWS Cloud deployments and on-premises deployments. There is currently no routing traffic between the on- premises data center and the AWS environment. The solution must be able to consume downstream packages from public repositories and must be highly available. Data must be encrypted in transit and at rest. The solution must store the deployment artifacts in object storage and deploy the deployment artifacts into Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). The deployment artifacts must be encrypted in transit if the deployment artifacts travel across the public internet. The DevOps engineer needs to deploy this solution in less than two weeks. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师需要设计一个基于云的解决方案，以统一 AWS 云部署和本地部署的部署工件。 目前，本地数据中心与 AWS 环境之间没有路由流量。 该解决方案必须能够从公共存储库中获取下游软件包，并且必须具有高可用性。数据在传输过程中和静 止时都必须进行加密。该解决方案必须将部署工件存储在对象存储中，并将部署工件部署到亚马逊弹性 容器服务（Amazon ECS）。如果部署工件通过公共互联网传输，则必须对其进行加密。 这位 DevOps 工程师需要在不到两周的时间内部署此解决方案。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use a third-party software VPN appliance to connect the on-premises data center and AWS. Use AWS CodeArtifact to store the deployment artifacts.","B":"Use an AWS Direct Connect connection and a VPN connection to connect the on-premises data center to AWS. Deploy third-party artifact management software on Amazon EC2 instances.","C":"Use two AWS VPN connections to connect the on-premises data center to AWS. Use AWS CodeArtifact to store the deployment artifacts.","D":"Use parallel AWS Direct Connect connections to connect the on-premises data center to AWS. Deploy third-party artifact management software on Amazon EC2 instances."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用第三方软件 VPN 设备将本地数据中心与 AWS 连接起来。使用 AWS CodeArtifact 来存储部署工 件。","B":"使用 AWS Direct Connect 连接和 VPN 连接将本地数据中心连接到 AWS。在 Amazon EC2 实例上部署 第三方工件管理软件。","C":"使用两个 AWS VPN 连接将本地数据中心连接到 AWS。使用 AWS CodeArtifact 存储部署 工件。","D":"使用多个并行的 AWS Direct Connect 连接将本地数据中心连接到 AWS。在 Amazon EC2 实例上部署 第三方工件管理软件。"},"answer":["C"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The solution must connect on-premises to AWS with no existing routing, be highly available, encrypt in transit and at rest, store artifacts in object storage, consume packages from public repositories, deploy to ECS, and ship in under two weeks. AWS CodeArtifact is a fully managed, highly scalable artifact repository that encrypts all stored assets at rest with AWS KMS and protects all communication in transit with TLS, and it natively creates external connections to public repositories such as npmjs, Maven Central, PyPI, and NuGet to fetch and store downstream packages on demand. This eliminates B and D, which require self-managed third-party artifact software on EC2 where you must build HA and encryption yourself. For connectivity, AWS documents redundant Site-to-Site VPN as the HA pattern: a second VPN connection plus a second customer gateway protects against a customer-gateway-device failure, so option C's two AWS VPN connections deliver documented failover. Direct Connect (B, D) requires a partner, an LOA-CFA, and a physical cross-connect at a Direct Connect location, which cannot reliably be provisioned in under two weeks, while a Site-to-Site VPN can be set up in hours. Option A uses a single third-party software VPN appliance, which is a single point of failure and not highly available. Therefore C is the only option meeting every requirement, agreeing with the marked answer.","explanation_zh":"此方案需要在無現有路由的情況下連接地端與 AWS、具備高可用性、傳輸中與靜態皆加密、以物件儲存存放成品、從公開儲存庫取得套件、部署至 ECS,並在兩週內完成。AWS CodeArtifact 是全託管且高度可擴展的成品儲存庫,會以 AWS KMS 對所有靜態資產加密,並以 TLS 保護所有傳輸中的通訊,且原生支援與 npmjs、Maven Central、PyPI、NuGet 等公開儲存庫的 external connection,可依需求抓取並儲存下游套件。這排除了 B 與 D,因為它們需要在 EC2 上自行管理第三方成品軟體,HA 與加密都得自行建置。在連線方面,AWS 文件以冗餘 Site-to-Site VPN 作為 HA 模式:第二條 VPN 連線加上第二個 customer gateway 可防範 customer gateway 裝置故障,因此選項 C 的兩條 AWS VPN 連線提供文件記載的故障切換。Direct Connect(B、D)需要合作夥伴、LOA-CFA 以及在 Direct Connect 據點的實體 cross-connect,無法在兩週內穩定佈建,而 Site-to-Site VPN 數小時即可建立。選項 A 使用單一第三方軟體 VPN 設備,為單點故障且不具高可用性。因此 C 是唯一滿足所有需求的選項,與標記答案一致。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"A single third-party software VPN appliance is a single point of failure and does not satisfy the high-availability requirement; even though CodeArtifact is the correct artifact store, the connectivity layer fails HA.","why_zh":"單一第三方軟體 VPN 設備是單點故障,無法滿足高可用性需求;即使 CodeArtifact 是正確的成品儲存選擇,連線層仍不符合 HA。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"AWS Direct Connect requires a partner, an LOA-CFA, and a physical cross-connect, which cannot be reliably provisioned in under two weeks; deploying self-managed third-party artifact software on EC2 also forces you to build HA, encryption, and object storage yourself.","why_zh":"AWS Direct Connect 需要合作夥伴、LOA-CFA 與實體 cross-connect,無法在兩週內穩定佈建;在 EC2 上自管第三方成品軟體還需自行建置 HA、加密與物件儲存。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Parallel Direct Connect connections still require physical cross-connect provisioning that exceeds the two-week deadline, and self-managed third-party artifact software on EC2 is not a managed, inherently HA, KMS/TLS-encrypted, object-storage-backed solution.","why_zh":"並聯的 Direct Connect 仍需實體 cross-connect 佈建,超過兩週期限;且在 EC2 上自管第三方成品軟體並非全託管、原生 HA、KMS/TLS 加密且以物件儲存為後端的方案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/welcome.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/external-connection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codeartifact/latest/ug/security-encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/vpn/latest/s2svpn/vpn-redundant-connection.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/directconnect/latest/UserGuide/dedicated_connection.html"]}},{"id":396,"question_en":"A DevOps engineer successfully creates an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster that includes managed node groups. When the DevOps engineer tries to add node groups to the cluster, the cluster returns an error that states, \"NodeCreationFailure: Instances failed to join the Kubernetes cluster.\" The DevOps engineer confirms that the EC2 worker nodes are running and that the EKS cluster is in an active state. How should the DevOps engineer troubleshoot this issue?","question_zh":"一位 DevOps 工程师成功创建了一个包含托管节点组的亚马逊弹性 Kubernetes 服务（Amazon EKS）集 群。当该 DevOps 工程师尝试向集群添加节点组时，集群返回一个错误，内容为：“NodeCreationFailu re：实例未能加入 Kubernetes 集群。” DevOps 工程师确认 EC2 工作节点正在运行，并且 EKS 集群处于活动状态。 DevOps 工程师应如何排查此问题？","options_en":{"A":"Ensure that the EKS cluster's VPC subnets do not overlap with the 172.17.0.0/16 CIDR range.","B":"Use kubectl to update the kubeconfig file to use the credentials that created the cluster.","C":"Run the AWSSupport-TroubleshootEKSWorkerNode runbook.","D":"Create an AWS Identity and Access Management (IAM) OpenID Connect (OIDC) provider for the cluster."},"options_zh":{"A":"确保 EKS 集群的 VPC 子网不与 172.17.0.0/16 的 CIDR 范围重叠。","B":"使用 kubectl 更新 kubeconfig 文件以使用创建集群时的凭证。","C":"运行 AWSSupport-TroubleshootEKSWorkerNode 运行手册。","D":"为集群创建一个 AWS 身份和访问管理 （IAM） 开放身份连接 （OIDC） 提供程序。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"題庫與社群皆錯","research":{"verdict":["C"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"neither","explanation_en":"The error 'NodeCreationFailure: Instances failed to join the Kubernetes cluster' is exactly the scenario the AWSSupport-TroubleshootEKSWorkerNode runbook is built to diagnose. The official EKS 'Troubleshoot problems with Amazon EKS clusters and nodes' page, in its 'Nodes fail to join cluster' section, explicitly says: 'To identify and troubleshoot common causes that prevent worker nodes from joining a cluster, you can use the AWSSupport-TroubleshootEKSWorkerNode runbook.' The runbook reference page states its prerequisites: the EC2 worker node must be in a running state and the EKS cluster must be ACTIVE - precisely the two conditions the engineer has already confirmed. The runbook runs a Python script that checks the documented set of common root causes (node IAM role / aws-auth mapping, ownership tags, security groups, subnet routing / NAT, DHCP options, STS endpoint, etc.), so it is the documented next action rather than guessing one cause. The dump's suggested answer A (172.17.0.0/16 CIDR overlap) is not listed among the official node-join failure causes and is a Docker-bridge red herring.","explanation_zh":"錯誤訊息 'NodeCreationFailure: Instances failed to join the Kubernetes cluster' 正是 AWSSupport-TroubleshootEKSWorkerNode runbook 設計用來診斷的情境。官方 EKS『Troubleshoot problems with Amazon EKS clusters and nodes』頁面在『Nodes fail to join cluster』段落明確指出：要找出並排除導致 worker node 無法加入叢集的常見原因，可使用 AWSSupport-TroubleshootEKSWorkerNode runbook。該 runbook 參考頁面列出的前置條件為：EC2 worker node 必須處於 running 狀態、且 EKS cluster 必須為 ACTIVE 狀態——正是題目中工程師已確認的兩項條件。此 runbook 會執行 Python 腳本，檢查文件記載的各項常見根因（node IAM role / aws-auth 對應、ownership 標籤、security group、子網路由 / NAT、DHCP options、STS endpoint 等），因此是文件指定的下一步動作，而非猜測單一原因。題庫建議答案 A（172.17.0.0/16 CIDR 重疊）並未列在官方的 node 加入失敗原因清單中，屬於與 Docker bridge 相關的誤導選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"The official 'Nodes fail to join cluster' guidance lists the common causes (node IAM role/aws-auth mapping, ClusterName mismatch, missing kubernetes.io/cluster ownership tag, no public IP or NAT route, disabled STS endpoint, DHCP options) - a 172.17.0.0/16 CIDR overlap is not among them. 172.17.0.0/16 is Docker's default bridge subnet, not a documented EKS node-join failure cause; this is the dump's narrow single-cause guess.","why_zh":"官方『Nodes fail to join cluster』指南列出的常見原因（node IAM role/aws-auth 對應、ClusterName 不符、缺少 kubernetes.io/cluster ownership 標籤、無 public IP 或 NAT 路由、STS endpoint 未啟用、DHCP options）並不包含 172.17.0.0/16 CIDR 重疊。172.17.0.0/16 是 Docker 預設 bridge 子網，並非文件記載的 EKS node 加入失敗原因，屬於題庫的狹隘單一原因猜測。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Updating the local kubeconfig credentials addresses 'Unauthorized or access denied (kubectl)' errors - a different troubleshooting section. Whether worker nodes register with the cluster does not depend on the engineer's local kubectl credentials, so this does not resolve a NodeCreationFailure.","why_zh":"更新本機 kubeconfig 憑證是針對『Unauthorized or access denied (kubectl)』錯誤，屬於不同的排錯段落。worker node 能否註冊到叢集與工程師本機的 kubectl 憑證無關，因此無法解決 NodeCreationFailure。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"An IAM OIDC provider enables IAM Roles for Service Accounts (IRSA) so that pods can assume IAM roles. It has no bearing on whether EC2 worker nodes successfully join the Kubernetes cluster, so it does not address the NodeCreationFailure error.","why_zh":"IAM OIDC provider 用於啟用 IAM Roles for Service Accounts (IRSA)，讓 pod 能取得 IAM 角色，與 EC2 worker node 能否成功加入 Kubernetes 叢集無關，因此無法解決 NodeCreationFailure 錯誤。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eks/latest/userguide/troubleshooting.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/systems-manager-automation-runbooks/latest/userguide/automation-awssupport-troubleshooteksworkernode.html"]}},{"id":397,"question_en":"A company is developing an ecommerce application that has a backend that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The application has a static frontend website that is hosted in an Amazon S3 bucket. The company uses a GitHub repository for version control and must automate builds and deployments whenever code is pushed to the main branch. The company must deploy changes to the frontend and backend independently of each other. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司正在开发一个电子商务应用程序，其后端运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上。该应用程序有一 个静态的前端网站，托管在亚马逊 S3 存储桶中。 该公司使用 GitHub 代码库进行版本控制，并且每当代码被推送到主分支时，必须自动执行构建和部 署操作。公司还必须将前端的更改部署到位。 后端彼此独立。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create a single AWS CodePipeline pipeline to use for the frontend and the backend. Specify the GitHub repository as the source. Configure two build stages that use AWS CodeBuild as the action provider to build the frontend components and backend components, respectively. Configure two deployment stages that use AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider to deploy the frontend and backend, respectively.","B":"Create a single AWS CodePipeline pipeline to use for the frontend and the backend. Specify the GitHub repository as the source. Configure two build stages that use AWS CodeBuild as the action provider to build the frontend components and backend components, respectively. Configure two deployment stages. For the backend stage, use AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider to deploy the backend to the EC2 instances. For the frontend stage, use Amazon S3 as the action provider to deploy the frontend to the S3 bucket.","C":"Create two AWS CodePipeline pipelines: one for the frontend and one for the backend. Specify the GitHub repository as the source. Configure a build stage that uses AWS CodeBuild as the action provider for each pipeline to build the frontend and the backend. Configure a deployment stage that uses AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider for each pipeline to deploy the frontend and the backend.","D":"Create two AWS CodePipeline pipelines: one for the frontend and one for the backend. Specify the GitHub repository as the source. Configure a build stage that uses AWS CodeBuild as the action provider for each pipeline to build the frontend and the backend. For the backend pipeline, use AWS CodeDeploy as the action provider to deploy the backend to the EC2 instances. For the frontend pipeline, use Amazon S3 as the action provider to deploy the frontend to the S3 bucket."},"options_zh":{"A":"创建一个用于前端和后端的单一 AWS CodePipeline 管道。将 GitHub 代码库指定为源。配置两个构建 阶段，分别使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来构建前端组件和后端组件。配置两个部署阶 段，分别使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序来部署前端和后端。","B":"创建一个用于前端和后端的单一 AWS CodePipeline 管道。将 GitHub 代码库指定为源。配置两个构建阶段， 分别使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来构建前端组件和后端组件。配置两个部署阶段。对于后 端阶段，使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序将后端部署到 EC2 实例。对于前端阶段，使用 Amazon S3 作为操作提供程序将前端部署到 S3 存储桶。","C":"创建两个 AWS CodePipeline 管道：一个用于前端，一个用于后端。将 GitHub 代码库指定为源。为每 个管道配置一个构建阶段，使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来构建前端和后端。为每个管道 配置一个部署阶段，使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序来部署前端和后端。","D":"创建两个 AWS CodePipeline 管道：一个用于前端，一个用于后端。将 GitHub 代码库指定为源。为每 个管道配置一个构建阶段，使用 AWS CodeBuild 作为操作提供程序来构建前端和后端。对于后端管 道，使用 AWS CodeDeploy 作为操作提供程序将后端部署到 EC2 实例。对于前端管道，使用 Amazon S3 作为操作提供程序将前端部署到 S3 存储桶。"},"answer":["D"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Storage","Compute","Monitoring/Ops"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["D"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The two decisive requirements are (1) deploy the static frontend to an S3 bucket and (2) deploy frontend and backend independently of each other. CodePipeline provides a native Amazon S3 deploy action (Category: Deploy, Owner: AWS, Provider: S3) whose purpose is to deploy files to an S3 bucket for static website hosting. CodeDeploy, by contrast, only deploys to compute targets (EC2/on-premises, Lambda, ECS) and cannot deploy a static website into an S3 bucket (it uses S3 only as a source revision location, not a deploy target). That eliminates A and C, which both use CodeDeploy for the frontend S3 deployment. Between B and D, the 'deploy changes to the frontend and backend independently of each other' qualifier requires two separate pipelines: a single pipeline (B) couples both into one execution that runs end to end on every push, so they cannot be released independently. D uses two pipelines (independent triggers/releases), CodeDeploy to deploy the backend to EC2, and the Amazon S3 deploy action to deploy the frontend to the S3 bucket, satisfying both requirements.","explanation_zh":"兩個關鍵需求是 (1) 將靜態前端部署到 S3 bucket，以及 (2) 前端與後端要能各自獨立部署。CodePipeline 提供原生的 Amazon S3 deploy action（Category: Deploy、Owner: AWS、Provider: S3），用途正是將檔案部署到設定為靜態網站託管的 S3 bucket。相對地，CodeDeploy 只能部署到運算目標（EC2/地端、Lambda、ECS），無法將靜態網站部署到 S3 bucket（它僅將 S3 當作來源版本位置，而非部署目標）。因此可排除 A 與 C，這兩者都用 CodeDeploy 部署前端到 S3。在 B 與 D 之間，「前端與後端各自獨立部署」這個限定條件需要兩條獨立的 pipeline：單一 pipeline（B）會把兩者耦合在同一次執行中，每次 push 都整條跑完，無法獨立發佈。D 使用兩條 pipeline（觸發與發佈各自獨立），以 CodeDeploy 將後端部署到 EC2，並以 Amazon S3 deploy action 將前端部署到 S3 bucket，同時滿足兩項需求。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses CodeDeploy to deploy the frontend to S3, but CodeDeploy cannot deploy a static website to an S3 bucket (it targets EC2/Lambda/ECS). Also a single pipeline couples frontend and backend, breaking the independent-deployment requirement.","why_zh":"用 CodeDeploy 將前端部署到 S3，但 CodeDeploy 無法把靜態網站部署到 S3 bucket（其目標為 EC2/Lambda/ECS）。且單一 pipeline 將前後端耦合，違反獨立部署需求。"},{"letter":"B","why_en":"Correctly uses the S3 deploy action for the frontend, but a single pipeline runs both build/deploy stages in one execution on every push, so frontend and backend cannot be deployed independently of each other.","why_zh":"前端正確使用 S3 deploy action，但單一 pipeline 在每次 push 時於同一次執行跑完所有 build/deploy stage，前後端無法各自獨立部署。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Uses two pipelines (good for independence) but deploys the frontend to S3 via CodeDeploy, which is not a supported CodeDeploy target. CodeDeploy deploys to EC2/Lambda/ECS, not to an S3 static-hosting bucket.","why_zh":"使用兩條 pipeline（獨立性正確），但以 CodeDeploy 將前端部署到 S3，而 S3 並非 CodeDeploy 支援的部署目標。CodeDeploy 只能部署到 EC2/Lambda/ECS，無法部署到 S3 靜態託管 bucket。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/action-reference-S3Deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/integrations-action-type.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codepipeline/latest/userguide/tutorials-s3deploy.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/codedeploy/latest/userguide/welcome.html"]}},{"id":398,"question_en":"A company has an RPO of 24 hours and an RTO of 10 minutes for a critical web application that runs on Amazon EC2 instances. The company uses AWS Organizations to manage its AWS account. The company wants to set up AWS Backup for its AWS environment. A DevOps engineer configures AWS Organizations for AWS Backup. The DevOps engineer creates a new centralized AWS account to store the backups. Each EC2 instance has four Amazon Elastic Block Store (Amazon EBS) volumes attached. Which solution will meet this requirement MOST securely?","question_zh":"一家公司对其运行在亚马逊 EC2 实例上的关键网络应用程序设定了 24 小时的恢复点目标（RPO）和 10 分钟的恢复时间目标（RTO）。该公司使用 AWS 组织来管理其 AWS 账户。该公司希望为其 AWS 环境设 置 AWS 备份服务。 一位 DevOps 工程师为 AWS 备份配置了 AWS 组织。该 DevOps 工程师创建了一个新的集中式 AWS 账户来 存储备份。每个 EC2 实例都附加了四个亚马逊弹性块存储（Amazon EBS）卷。 哪种解决方案能最安全地满足这一要求？","options_en":{"A":"Create encrypted backup vaults and customer managed AWS KMS keys in both accounts. Configure AWS Backup to create full EC2 backups as AMIs. Copy the backups to the centralized vault.","B":"Create encrypted vaults in both accounts by using the source account's AWS KMS key. Configure AWS Backup to create EC2 AMIs. Copy the AMIs to the centralized vault.","C":"Create backup vaults in both accounts. Use AWS managed keys for encryption. Configure AWS Backup to create EC2 AMIs. Copy the AMIs to the centralized vault.","D":"Create encrypted vaults in both accounts. Use a customer managed KMS key in the source account. Use an AWS managed key in the centralized account. Configure AWS Backup to create EC2 AMIs. Copy the AMIs to the centralized vault."},"options_zh":{"A":"在两个账户中创建加密备份库和客户管理的 AWS KMS 密钥。配置 AWS 备份以创建完整的 EC2 备份 作为 AMI。将备份复制到集中式备份库。","B":"使用源账户的 AWS KMS 密钥在两个账户中创建加密存储库。配置 AWS Backup 以创建 EC2 AMI。 将 AMI 复制到集中式存储库。","C":"在两个账户中创建备份库。使用 AWS 管理的密钥进行加密。配置 AWS 备份以创建 EC2 AMI。将 AMI 复制到集中式备份库。","D":"在两个账户中创建加密存储库。在源账户中使用客户管理的 KMS 密钥。在集中账户中使用 AWS 管理 的密钥。配置 AWS 备份以创建 EC2 AMI。将 AMI 复制到集中存储库。"},"answer":["A"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Disaster Recovery/HA","Organizations/Governance","Security/IAM","Storage","Compute"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["A"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"When AWS Backup backs up an EC2 instance it produces an AMI plus encrypted EBS snapshots that capture the instance and all four attached volumes, so 'full EC2 backups as AMIs' is the correct backup type. EC2/AMI/EBS are resources that are NOT fully managed by AWS Backup, so they do not support independent backup encryption (the AWS Backup encryption table lists EC2 AMIs and EBS as 'Not supported'). The decisive constraint is the cross-account copy to the centralized account: for a recovery point of a resource that is not fully managed by AWS Backup, the destination vault's KMS key must be a customer managed key (CMK) or the owning service's AWS managed key (aws/ebs) - the aws/backup managed key cannot be used. AWS explicitly states 'Cross-account copy with AWS managed keys isn't supported for resources that aren't fully managed by AWS Backup' because an AWS managed key's policy is immutable and cannot be shared cross-account. Option A uses encrypted vaults with customer managed KMS keys in BOTH the source and the centralized destination account, which both succeeds for the cross-account copy and is the MOST secure choice because CMKs give full control over key policy, rotation, sharing, and auditability in both accounts. The 24-hour RPO and 10-minute RTO are satisfied by any of these backup approaches and do not change the encryption decision.","explanation_zh":"AWS Backup 對 EC2 instance 做備份時會產生一個 AMI 加上加密的 EBS 快照，涵蓋該 instance 與其全部四個附掛的 volumes，因此「以 AMI 形式建立完整 EC2 備份」是正確的備份類型。EC2/AMI/EBS 屬於「非」由 AWS Backup 完整管理（not fully managed）的資源，因此不支援獨立備份加密（AWS Backup 加密表將 EC2 AMIs 與 EBS 列為 'Not supported'）。關鍵限制在於跨帳號複製到集中帳號：對於非完整管理資源的 recovery point，目的端 vault 的 KMS key 必須是 customer managed key（CMK）或擁有該底層資源服務的 AWS managed key（aws/ebs），不能使用 aws/backup managed key。AWS 明確指出『Cross-account copy with AWS managed keys isn't supported for resources that aren't fully managed by AWS Backup』，因為 AWS managed key 的 key policy 不可變更、無法跨帳號分享。選項 A 在來源帳號與集中式目的帳號「兩端」都使用加密 vault 搭配 customer managed KMS keys，既能成功完成跨帳號複製，且因 CMK 在兩個帳號都提供對 key policy、輪替、分享與稽核的完整控制而是「最安全」的選擇。24 小時 RPO 與 10 分鐘 RTO 在這些備份方式下皆可滿足，不影響加密決策。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"A backup vault is encrypted with a KMS key that resides in the vault's own account; you cannot encrypt the centralized (destination) account's vault with the source account's KMS key. Configuring 'both vaults by using the source account's KMS key' is an invalid configuration for a cross-account setup and is also less secure than dedicated CMKs per account.","why_zh":"備份 vault 是以位於該 vault 所屬帳號內的 KMS key 加密；你無法用來源帳號的 KMS key 來加密集中（目的）帳號的 vault。將「兩個 vault 都以來源帳號的 KMS key」加密在跨帳號架構下是無效組態，安全性也不如每個帳號各自的 CMK。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"AWS managed keys cannot be used for cross-account copy of resources that are not fully managed by AWS Backup (such as EC2). AWS docs state cross-account copy with AWS managed keys isn't supported because the key policy is immutable, so the copy to the centralized vault would fail. It is also less secure than CMKs because customers cannot control the key policy.","why_zh":"AWS managed keys 無法用於非完整管理之資源（如 EC2）的跨帳號複製。AWS 文件指出因 key policy 不可變更，故不支援以 AWS managed keys 進行跨帳號複製，複製到集中 vault 會失敗。其安全性也低於 CMK，因為客戶無法控制 key policy。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"For a cross-account copy of a not-fully-managed resource, the DESTINATION vault key must be a CMK (or the service's aws/ebs key). Using an AWS managed key (e.g. aws/backup) in the centralized destination account fails because AWS managed keys cannot be shared cross-account, and even otherwise a CMK is more secure, so this is not the MOST secure answer.","why_zh":"對於非完整管理資源的跨帳號複製，「目的端」vault 金鑰必須是 CMK（或服務的 aws/ebs 金鑰）。在集中目的帳號使用 AWS managed key（例如 aws/backup）會因 AWS managed keys 無法跨帳號分享而失敗；即便可行，CMK 也更安全，故此非「最安全」的答案。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/encryption.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/create-cross-account-backup.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/aws-backup/latest/devguide/backup-feature-availability.html"]}},{"id":399,"question_en":"A company wants to proactively monitor and respond to AWS service issues that might affect an application. The company must correlate AWS Health events with application performance metrics and must set up automated alerts. The solution must give the company the ability to archive events, test the application's latency in different scenarios, and create custom metrics. Which solution will meet these requirements?","question_zh":"一家公司希望主动监控并响应可能影响应用程序的 AWS 服务问题。该公司必须将 AWS Health 事件 与应用程序性能指标相关联，并且必须设置自动警报。该解决方案必须使公司能够存档事件、测试 应用程序在不同场景下的延迟，并创建自定义指标。 哪种解决方案能满足这些要求？","options_en":{"A":"Use AWS CloudTrail to log all AWS Health events. Use Amazon Athena to query the logs and to correlate the logs with application metrics stored in Amazon Timestream for LiveAnalytics. Set up AWS Chatbot for real-time notifications.","B":"Use Amazon EventBridge to route AWS Health events to Amazon CloudWatch Logs. Create a metric filter for AWS Health events. Create custom metrics in CloudWatch that are based on application performance data. Set up CloudWatch alarms that correlate AWS Health events with the custom metrics.","C":"Configure the AWS Health Dashboard to send notifications to Amazon Simple Notification Service (Amazon SNS). Use AWS Lambda to correlate the notifications with metrics and to update custom metrics in Amazon CloudWatch. Set up CloudWatch alarms for the custom metrics. Use AWS Systems Manager for automated remediation.","D":"Configure AWS X-Ray to trace AWS Health events and application performance. Use Amazon QuickSight to visualize the correlations between events and metrics. Use Amazon GuardDuty to detect anomalies in the application's behavior and to provide alerts."},"options_zh":{"A":"使用 AWS CloudTrail 记录所有 AWS Health 事件。使用 Amazon Athena 查询日志，并将日志与存储 在 Amazon Timestream 中的 LiveAnalytics 应用程序指标相关联。设置 AWS Chatbot 以实现实时通 知。","B":"使用 Amazon EventBridge 将 AWS Health 事件路由到 Amazon CloudWatch Logs。为 AWS Health 事 件创建指标过滤器。在 CloudWatch 中基于应用程序性能数据创建自定义指标。设置 CloudWatch 警报，将 AWS Health 事件与自定义指标相关联。","C":"配置 AWS 健康仪表板，使其向 Amazon 简单通知服务（Amazon SNS）发送通知。使用 AWS Lambda 将通知与指标相关联，并更新 Amazon CloudWatch 中的自定义指标。为自定义指标设置 CloudWatch 警报。使用 AWS 系统管理器进行自动修复。","D":"配置 AWS X-Ray 来追踪 AWS 健康事件和应用程序性能。使用 Amazon QuickSight 来可视化事件与 指标之间的关联。使用 Amazon GuardDuty 来检测应用程序行为中的异常情况并提供警报。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Security/IAM","Compute","Database","Serverless/Integration","Monitoring/Ops","Analytics"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"AWS Health sends service events directly to Amazon EventBridge (source aws.health) on a durable basis, and EventBridge is the AWS-documented mechanism to detect and react to AWS Health events by routing them to targets, sending notifications, and taking automated action. Option B routes AWS Health events through EventBridge to CloudWatch Logs (log retention provides the archive), uses a CloudWatch metric filter on those logs plus custom application performance metrics, and uses CloudWatch alarms to correlate Health events with the custom metrics and fire automated alerts. Every component in B is a valid, supported AWS pattern, and it makes no false service claims. Option A fails because AWS CloudTrail only records AWS Health API calls (for example DescribeEvents) on a best-effort basis, not the Health events themselves, so it cannot log all AWS Health events; Amazon Timestream for LiveAnalytics is also being deprecated and is not the recommended correlation store. Option C is built on a false premise: the AWS Health Dashboard is a console/viewing surface that does not natively publish notifications to Amazon SNS (the documented path is EventBridge to SNS), and it adds Systems Manager remediation that was never required. Option D is invalid because AWS X-Ray traces application request paths and cannot trace AWS Health events, and Amazon GuardDuty is a security threat-detection service, not an application-performance anomaly detector. B is therefore the only choice built entirely on the correct AWS-recommended EventBridge integration that satisfies the achievable requirements.","explanation_zh":"AWS Health 會以持久 (durable) 方式將服務事件直接傳送到 Amazon EventBridge (source 為 aws.health)，而 EventBridge 正是 AWS 官方文件用來偵測並回應 AWS Health 事件的機制：可將事件路由到各種目標、發送通知並執行自動化動作。選項 B 透過 EventBridge 把 AWS Health 事件路由到 CloudWatch Logs (以 log retention 達成封存)，在這些日誌上建立 CloudWatch metric filter 並搭配自訂的應用程式效能 custom metrics，再用 CloudWatch alarms 將 Health 事件與 custom metrics 做關聯並觸發自動化警示。B 的每一個元件都是有效且受支援的 AWS 模式，且沒有任何不實的服務宣稱。選項 A 不成立，因為 AWS CloudTrail 只會以 best-effort 方式記錄 AWS Health 的 API 呼叫 (例如 DescribeEvents)，而非 Health 事件本身，因此無法記錄所有 AWS Health 事件；而且 Amazon Timestream for LiveAnalytics 正在被淘汰，並非建議的關聯存放區。選項 C 建立在錯誤前提上：AWS Health Dashboard 只是主控台/檢視介面，本身並不會原生地把通知發布到 Amazon SNS (官方路徑是 EventBridge 到 SNS)，且額外加上題目從未要求的 Systems Manager 修復。選項 D 無效，因為 AWS X-Ray 是追蹤應用程式請求路徑，無法追蹤 AWS Health 事件，而 Amazon GuardDuty 是安全威脅偵測服務，並非應用程式效能異常偵測器。因此 B 是唯一完全建立在正確的 AWS 建議 EventBridge 整合上、且能滿足可達成需求的選項。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"AWS CloudTrail records AWS Health API calls (e.g., DescribeEvents) on a best-effort basis, not the Health events themselves, so it cannot log all AWS Health events. Querying CloudTrail logs in Athena is not the recommended near-real-time event-correlation pattern, and Amazon Timestream for LiveAnalytics is being deprecated.","why_zh":"AWS CloudTrail 以 best-effort 方式記錄 AWS Health 的 API 呼叫 (如 DescribeEvents)，而非 Health 事件本身，因此無法記錄所有 AWS Health 事件。用 Athena 查詢 CloudTrail 日誌並非建議的近即時事件關聯模式，且 Amazon Timestream for LiveAnalytics 正在被淘汰。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"The AWS Health Dashboard is a console/viewing interface and does not natively publish notifications to Amazon SNS; the documented programmatic path is EventBridge to SNS. It also adds AWS Systems Manager automated remediation that the question never required, making it an over-engineered and technically inaccurate option.","why_zh":"AWS Health Dashboard 是主控台/檢視介面，本身並不會原生地把通知發布到 Amazon SNS；官方的程式化路徑是 EventBridge 到 SNS。它又加上題目從未要求的 AWS Systems Manager 自動化修復，屬於過度設計且技術上不正確的選項。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"AWS X-Ray traces application request paths and cannot trace AWS Health events. Amazon GuardDuty is a security threat-detection service for accounts/workloads, not an application-performance anomaly detector, so it cannot provide the required performance correlation or alerts.","why_zh":"AWS X-Ray 追蹤的是應用程式請求路徑，無法追蹤 AWS Health 事件。Amazon GuardDuty 是針對帳號/工作負載的安全威脅偵測服務，並非應用程式效能異常偵測器，因此無法提供所需的效能關聯或警示。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/cloudwatch-events-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/eventbridge/latest/ref/events-ref-health.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/health/latest/ug/aws-health-dashboard-status.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/CreateMetricFilterProcedure.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/logs/FilterAndPatternSyntaxForMetricFilters.html"]}},{"id":400,"question_en":"A company uses a CI/CD pipeline to deploy its workload in the ap-southeast-2 Region. The company receives images through a Network Load Balancer (NLB) and processes the images in AWS Fargate tasks on an Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS) cluster. An Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) repository stores the images as Docker images. The company uses Amazon Route 53 to configure DNS. The company saves the images in an Amazon S3 bucket and saves the metadata from the images in an Amazon DynamoDB table. The company wants to expand the workload to a second Region. A DevOps engineer needs to build a highly available and resilient design to expand the workload to the eu-west-2 Region. Which combination of steps will meet these requirements with the FEWEST configuration changes? (Choose three.)","question_zh":"一家公司使用 CI/CD 管道在 ap-southeast-2 区域部署其工作负载。该公司通过网络负载均衡器（NLB） 接收图像，并在 Amazon ECS 集群上的 AWS Fargate 任务中处理这些图像。 亚马逊弹性容器注册表（Amazon ECR）存储库将镜像存储为 Docker 镜像。该公司使用亚马逊路由 53 来配置 DNS。该公司将镜像保存在 Amazon S3 存储桶中，并将镜像的元数据保存在 Amazon DynamoDB 表中。 该公司希望将工作负载扩展到第二个区域。一名 DevOps 工程师需要构建一个高可用且具有弹性的 设计，以将工作负载扩展到 eu-west-2 区域。 哪种组合的 哪些步骤能以最少的配置更改满足这些要求？ （选择三项。）","options_en":{"A":"Configure ECR replication to eu-west-2 on the repository. Configure an NLB in eu-west-2 that resolves to Fargate tasks in an ECS cluster in eu-west-2. Configure a latency routing policy in Route 53 for the two workloads.","B":"Configure the DynamoDB table as a global table with a replica in eu-west-2. Configure the Fargate tasks to interact with the DynamoDB table in ap-southeast-2.","C":"Configure the DynamoDB table as a global table with a replica in eu-west-2. Configure the Fargate tasks to interact with the DynamoDB table in the same Region that the tasks run in.","D":"Configure a new S3 bucket in eu-west-2. Configure data replication between the S3 bucket in ap- southeast-2 and the S3 bucket in eu-west-2. Configure the Fargate tasks to use the S3 bucket in the same Region that the tasks run in to perform S3 PUT operations and GET operations.","E":"Configure an S3 Multi-Region Access Point for the S3 bucket in ap-southeast-2 and a new S3 bucket in eu-west-2. Configure two-way replication on the S3 buckets. Configure the workloads to use the Multi- Region Access Point for S3 PUT operations and GET operations.","F":"Configure the CI/CD pipeline to deploy ECR images to both Regions. Configure an NLB in eu-west-2 that resolves to Fargate tasks in an ECS cluster in eu-west-2. Configure a failover routing policy in Route 53 for the two workloads."},"options_zh":{"A":"在该存储库中配置 ECR 复制到 eu-west-2 区域。在 eu-west-2 区域配置一个网络负载均衡器（NLB），使 其解析到 eu-west-2 区域中 ECS 集群内的 Fargate 任务。在 Route 53 中为这两个工作负载配置延迟路由 策略。","B":"将 DynamoDB 表配置为全局表，并在 eu-west-2 区域设置一个副本。将 Fargate 任务配置为与 ap- southeast-2 区域的 DynamoDB 表进行交互。","C":"将 DynamoDB 表配置为全局表，并在 eu-west-2 区域设置一个副本。将 Fargate 任务配置为与任务运 行所在区域的 DynamoDB 表进行交互。","D":"在 eu-west-2 区域配置一个新的 S3 存储桶。在 apsoutheast-2 区域的 S3 存储桶与 eu-west-2 区域的 S3 存 储桶之间配置数据复制。配置 Fargate 任务使用其所在区域的 S3 存储桶来执行 S3 的 PUT 操作和 GET 操作。","E":"为位于 ap-southeast-2 区域的 S3 存储桶和位于 eu-west-2 区域的新 S3 存储桶配置 S3 多区域访问点。在两 个 S3 存储桶上配置双向复制。配置工作负载使用 S3 多区域访问点执行 S3 PUT 操作和 GET 操作。","F":"配置 CI/CD 管道以将 ECR 镜像部署到两个区域。在 eu-west-2 区域配置一个网络负载均衡器（NLB）， 使其解析到 eu-west-2 区域中 ECS 集群内的 Fargate 任务。在 Route 53 中为这两个工作负载配置故障 转移路由策略。"},"answer":["A","C","E"],"multi":true,"vote":{},"tags":["Networking/DNS","Disaster Recovery/HA","Storage","Compute","Database","Containers"],"difficulty":2,"diff_why":"複選","research":{"verdict":["A","C","E"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The goal is an active-active, highly available, resilient two-Region expansion with the FEWEST configuration changes. (A) Amazon ECR supports native cross-Region replication configured as a single registry/repository setting, so no CI/CD re-plumbing is needed (option F instead rewrites the pipeline to push to both Regions, which is more configuration). A Route 53 latency routing policy serves each user from the lowest-latency Region, keeping both Regions actively serving traffic (active-active). F's failover routing is active-passive (the secondary is used only when the primary is unhealthy), which does not deliver the active-active HA pattern. (C) A DynamoDB global table is multi-active and replicates automatically with no application changes; the AWS prescriptive-guidance routing doc explicitly states the compute layer 'should do that by using the local endpoint for that Region' and calls a single-stack design that makes remote calls to a secondary Region's DynamoDB endpoint 'not best practice.' So having each Region's Fargate tasks talk to their local replica (C) is correct and resilient; option B forces all tasks back to ap-southeast-2, adding latency and a single point of failure. (E) An S3 Multi-Region Access Point gives one global endpoint and automatically routes PUT to the closest bucket and GET to the closest active bucket; combined with bidirectional (two-way) CRR, all buckets stay synchronized so any request succeeds. The MRAP request-routing doc describes exactly this pattern (PUT to the closest bucket, two-way CRR for global GET availability). Option D requires the application to select a specific bucket per Region and uses one-way replication, which is more configuration and less resilient. Thus A, C, and E together give active-active HA with the fewest changes.","explanation_zh":"目標是以最少的設定變更建立 active-active、高可用且具韌性的雙 Region 擴展。(A) Amazon ECR 支援原生跨 Region replication，只需在 registry/repository 上設定單一規則，不必改動 CI/CD pipeline（選項 F 反而要改寫 pipeline 以推送到兩個 Region，設定更多）。Route 53 latency routing policy 會把每位使用者導向延遲最低的 Region，讓兩個 Region 同時提供服務（active-active）。F 的 failover routing 屬於 active-passive（次要 Region 僅在主要 Region 不健康時才使用），無法達成 active-active 高可用模式。(C) DynamoDB global table 為 multi-active 且自動複寫、無需修改應用程式；AWS prescriptive-guidance 路由文件明確指出運算層『應使用該 Region 的本地 endpoint』，並將『單一堆疊在發生問題時遠端呼叫次要 Region 的 DynamoDB endpoint』的設計列為『非最佳實務』。因此讓各 Region 的 Fargate tasks 與其所在 Region 的本地 replica 互動（C）才正確且具韌性；選項 B 強迫所有 tasks 連回 ap-southeast-2，增加延遲並形成單點故障。(E) S3 Multi-Region Access Point 提供單一全域 endpoint，PUT 自動導向最近的 bucket、GET 導向最近的有效 bucket；搭配雙向（two-way）CRR 讓所有 bucket 保持同步，任何請求都能成功。MRAP 請求路由文件正是描述此模式（PUT 寫入最近 bucket，two-way CRR 確保全球 GET 可用）。選項 D 需要應用程式依 Region 選擇特定 bucket 且使用單向複寫，設定更多且韌性較低。因此 A、C、E 合起來以最少變更提供 active-active 高可用。","distractors":[{"letter":"B","why_en":"Forcing all Fargate tasks to call the ap-southeast-2 DynamoDB table defeats the purpose of a global table: the AWS routing best-practice doc explicitly calls remote cross-Region DynamoDB calls 'not best practice' and recommends using the local Region endpoint. It adds cross-Region latency and makes eu-west-2 dependent on ap-southeast-2 (single point of failure), undermining HA and resiliency.","why_zh":"強迫所有 Fargate tasks 呼叫 ap-southeast-2 的 DynamoDB table，違背 global table 的用意：AWS 路由最佳實務文件明確將跨 Region 遠端呼叫列為『非最佳實務』，並建議使用本地 Region endpoint。此作法增加跨 Region 延遲，且使 eu-west-2 依賴 ap-southeast-2（單點故障），破壞高可用與韌性。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Creating a separate bucket with one-way replication requires the application to explicitly target a Region-specific bucket for PUT/GET (more configuration changes) and only replicates in one direction, so objects written in eu-west-2 are not propagated back to ap-southeast-2. This is less resilient and more complex than the single global endpoint of option E.","why_zh":"建立獨立 bucket 並使用單向複寫，需要應用程式明確指定 Region 專屬 bucket 來做 PUT/GET（設定變更更多），且只單向複寫，因此在 eu-west-2 寫入的物件不會回傳到 ap-southeast-2。相較於選項 E 的單一全域 endpoint，此作法韌性較低且更複雜。"},{"letter":"F","why_en":"Configuring the CI/CD pipeline to deploy ECR images to both Regions is more configuration than ECR's native cross-Region replication (a single registry setting), and a Route 53 failover routing policy is active-passive (secondary used only on primary failure), which does not match the active-active highly available design the question requires.","why_zh":"設定 CI/CD pipeline 將 ECR 映像部署到兩個 Region，比 ECR 原生跨 Region replication（單一 registry 設定）需要更多設定；且 Route 53 failover routing policy 屬 active-passive（次要僅在主要故障時使用），不符合題目要求的 active-active 高可用設計。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECR/latest/userguide/replication.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-latency.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/Route53/latest/DeveloperGuide/routing-policy-failover.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/bp-global-table-design.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/amazondynamodb/latest/developerguide/bp-global-table-design.prescriptive-guidance.request-routing.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/MultiRegionAccessPoints.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/MultiRegionAccessPointRequestRouting.html"]}},{"id":401,"question_en":"A company has deployed a microservices-based application on Amazon Elastic Container Service (Amazon ECS). The application is experiencing performance issues. The company needs to identify which microservices are causing the issues. Which solution will provide this information?","question_zh":"一家公司已在亚马逊弹性容器服务（Amazon ECS）上部署了一个基于微服务的应用程序。该应用程序正遭 遇性能问题。该公司需要确定是哪些微服务导致了这些问题。 哪种解决方案能提供这些信息？","options_en":{"A":"Configure AWS X-Ray for each ECS task. Create an X-Ray group for each microservice. Implement custom X-Ray subsegments in each microservice to capture detailed timing information. Use an X-Ray service map to visualize and identify slow microservices and requests.","B":"Configure AWS X-Ray for each ECS task. Use an X-Ray service map to visualize the application's architecture and request flow. Filter the X-Ray traces by response time and error rate. Identify the microservices that have high latency or high error rates. Analyze individual traces to identify slow microservices and requests.","C":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights for each ECS task. Analyze Container Insights metrics to identify slow microservices. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to filter the Container Insights log data by response time and error rate. Analyze the log data to identify slow requests.","D":"Configure Amazon CloudWatch Container Insights for each ECS task. Use the CloudWatch automatic dashboard for Amazon ECS to identify slow microservices. Use CloudWatch Logs Insights to analyze the Container Insights performance logs for each ECS task to identify slow requests."},"options_zh":{"A":"为每个 ECS 任务配置 AWS X-Ray。为每个微服务创建一个 X-Ray 组。在每个微服务中实现自定义 X- Ray 子段以捕获详细的计时信息。使用 X-Ray 服务映射来可视化并识别运行缓慢的微服务和请求。","B":"为每个 ECS 任务配置 AWS X-Ray。使用 X-Ray 服务映射来可视化应用程序的架构和请求流程。按 响应时间和错误率筛选 X-Ray 跟踪。识别出延迟高或错误率高的微服务。分析单个跟踪以找出运 行缓慢的微服务和请求。","C":"为每个 ECS 任务配置 Amazon CloudWatch 容器洞察功能。分析容器洞察指标以识别运行缓慢的微服务。 使用 CloudWatch 日志洞察功能按响应时间和错误率筛选容器洞察日志数据。分析日志数据以识别运行 缓慢的请求。","D":"为每个 ECS 任务配置 Amazon CloudWatch 容器洞察功能。使用 Amazon ECS 的 CloudWatch 自动仪表板 来识别运行缓慢的微服务。使用 CloudWatch Logs Insights 分析每个 ECS 任务的容器洞察性能日志，以 识别运行缓慢的请求。"},"answer":["B"],"multi":false,"vote":{},"tags":["Compute","Monitoring/Ops","Containers"],"difficulty":1,"diff_why":"社群共識高、單選","research":{"verdict":["B"],"confidence":"high","agrees_with":"marked","explanation_en":"The goal is to identify which microservice in a distributed ECS application is causing latency/errors across request paths. AWS X-Ray is the AWS-native distributed tracing service for this: it groups segments from all services sharing a trace ID into a single service graph (service map), where each microservice appears as a separate node showing health, latency, error, and fault data. Option B is the standard, minimal-effort workflow: enable X-Ray per task, use the service map to visualize architecture and request flow, filter traces by response time and error rate to find high-latency or high-error microservices, then drill into individual traces. Option A also uses X-Ray but adds inaccurate/unnecessary steps: X-Ray groups are filter-expression-based trace collections, not a per-microservice construct (the service map already separates microservices into nodes automatically), and mandating custom subsegments in every microservice is extra implementation not needed to answer 'which microservice is slow.' Options C and D rely on CloudWatch Container Insights, which collects infrastructure telemetry (CPU, memory, disk, network) aggregated at the cluster/service/task/container level; it cannot trace a request across microservices, and its performance log events are resource-utilization records, not per-request response-time data, so filtering log data 'by response time' is technically inaccurate.","explanation_zh":"目標是找出分散式 ECS 應用程式中哪個 microservice 造成跨請求路徑的延遲或錯誤。AWS X-Ray 是 AWS 原生的分散式追蹤服務，正適合此情境：它將共用同一 trace ID 的所有服務 segment 組成單一 service graph（service map），每個 microservice 顯示為獨立節點，呈現健康狀態、延遲、error 與 fault 資料。選項 B 是標準且最省工的流程：為每個 task 啟用 X-Ray，用 service map 視覺化架構與請求流程，依 response time 與 error rate 過濾 traces 以找出高延遲或高錯誤率的 microservice，再深入分析個別 trace。選項 A 雖也使用 X-Ray，但加入不正確且不必要的步驟：X-Ray group 是以 filter expression 為基礎的 trace 集合，並非為每個 microservice 設立的構造（service map 本來就自動將各 microservice 分成節點），且要求在每個 microservice 中加入自訂 subsegment 是回答「哪個 microservice 較慢」並不需要的額外實作。選項 C 與 D 依賴 CloudWatch Container Insights，它收集的是基礎設施遙測資料（CPU、記憶體、磁碟、網路），於 cluster/service/task/container 層級彙總；它無法跨 microservice 追蹤單一請求，其 performance log 事件是資源使用率記錄而非每請求的 response time 資料，因此宣稱可依 response time 過濾 log 資料在技術上並不正確。","distractors":[{"letter":"A","why_en":"Uses X-Ray (correct tool) but adds inaccurate/unnecessary steps: an X-Ray group is a filter-expression-based trace collection, not a per-microservice construct, and the service map already separates microservices into nodes automatically. Mandating custom subsegments in every microservice is extra implementation not required to identify the slow microservice, making B the cleaner correct workflow.","why_zh":"使用 X-Ray（正確工具）但加入不正確或不必要的步驟：X-Ray group 是以 filter expression 為基礎的 trace 集合，並非每個 microservice 的構造，而 service map 本來就自動將各 microservice 分為節點。要求在每個 microservice 加入自訂 subsegment 是找出慢速 microservice 並不需要的額外實作，故 B 才是更精簡正確的流程。"},{"letter":"C","why_en":"Container Insights collects infrastructure telemetry (CPU, memory, disk, network) aggregated at cluster/service/task level; it cannot trace a request across microservices. Its performance log events are resource-utilization records, not per-request response-time data, so filtering Container Insights logs 'by response time and error rate' to find slow requests is technically inaccurate.","why_zh":"Container Insights 收集基礎設施遙測（CPU、記憶體、磁碟、網路），於 cluster/service/task 層級彙總，無法跨 microservice 追蹤單一請求。其 performance log 事件是資源使用率記錄，而非每請求的 response time 資料，因此宣稱可依 response time 與 error rate 過濾 Container Insights log 來找出慢速請求在技術上並不正確。"},{"letter":"D","why_en":"Same flaw as C: relies on Container Insights and its automatic ECS dashboard, which surface resource-utilization metrics, not distributed per-request traces. Container Insights performance logs contain infrastructure telemetry, not per-request response times, so they cannot identify which microservice is slow at the request level the way an X-Ray service map and traces can.","why_zh":"與 C 相同的缺陷：依賴 Container Insights 及其 ECS 自動儀表板，呈現的是資源使用率指標而非分散式的每請求 trace。Container Insights 的 performance log 包含基礎設施遙測而非每請求的 response time，因此無法像 X-Ray service map 與 trace 那樣在請求層級辨識哪個 microservice 較慢。"}],"sources":["https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/aws-xray.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/xray/latest/devguide/xray-concepts.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonECS/latest/developerguide/cloudwatch-container-insights.html","https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContainerInsights.html"]}}];
